{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Hidradenitis suppurativa (HS) is associated with an increased prevalence of cardiovascular diseases compared with the general population. Any association between polygenic risk for HS, risk of incident cardiometabolic outcomes, and the plasma proteome is unclear. OBJECTIVE: To investigate the genetic correlation between HS and cardiometabolic disease. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: This cohort study used a polygenic risk score (PRS) for HS to examine the risks of coronary artery disease (CAD) and diabetes and identify changes in the plasma proteome in individuals of European ancestry from the UK Biobank. Participants were enrolled from January 1, 2006, to December 31, 2010. End of follow-up was January 1, 2023. Correlations were assessed between HS susceptibility and cardiometabolic traits using linkage disequilibrium score regression. Odds ratios were assessed in logistic regressions. The risk of incident CAD and diabetes was estimated in cause-specific survival models designed as time-to-event analyses. EXPOSURE: The PRS for HS. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: Main outcomes were CAD and diabetes diagnosis measured by logistic regressions and incident disease measured by Cox proportional hazards regression models adjusted for sex, age, body mass index, and smoking status. RESULTS: The study included 391 481 individuals (median [IQR] age, 58 [51-64] years; 209 235 [53%] female). Genetic variants for HS correlated significantly with variants associated with CAD, diabetes, and plasma levels of high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, triglycerides, and C-reactive protein. Compared with the low-risk group, a high PRS for HS (≥75th percentile) conferred odds ratios of 1.09 (95% CI, 1.06-1.12; P < .001) for CAD and 1.13 (95% CI, 1.10-1.17; P < .001) for diabetes. Estimates remained consistent when examining only incident CAD and diabetes. The PRS for HS was significantly associated with altered expression of 58 plasma proteins. Integrating this proteomic profile and the PRS for HS in a machine learning model improved prediction of CAD and diabetes compared with a reference model based on sex, age, and body mass index. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: These findings suggest that a high genetic risk of HS is associated with increased risk of subsequent CAD and diabetes and altered composition of the plasma proteome. Additional investigation into the identified proteins and their potential roles as drug targets is warranted.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nielsen, Valdemar Wendelboe","Vad, Oliver B.","Holgersen, Nikolaj","Paludan-Müller, Christian","Monfort, Laia Meseguer","Beyer, Astrid Filt","Jemec, Gregor B E","Andersen, Rune Kjærsgaard","Egeberg, Alexander","Thyssen, Jacob P.","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Rosenø, Nana Aviaaja Lippert","Hansen, Peter Riis","Thomsen, Simon Francis","Olesen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798976"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LEO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-LEO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic susceptibility to hidradenitis suppurativa and predisposition to cardiometabolic disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-798976","identifier":[{"id":"85209232473","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39382891","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11465120","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-16735bac-a713-4e9b-9201-f60331c14cc3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-227AD34F9C41CB39887DABD490D89012"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"leo pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LEO","l3nl":"LEO Pharma","l3nn":"LEO Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LEO Pharma","namevar":["LEO Pharma"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LEO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Valdemar Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Valdemar Wendelboe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Oliver Bundgaard","key":"vadpau","last":"Vad","locid":"28b00ca5-e5b4-40f3-adab-83b905677652","name":"Vad, Oliver B.","name_org":"Vad, Oliver Bundgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nikolaj","key":"holgersenpau","last":"Holgersen","name":"Holgersen, Nikolaj","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christian","key":"paludanmüllerpau","last":"Paludan-Müller","locid":"efbe85eb-0b49-4ffe-832a-740b383c77a1","name":"Paludan-Müller, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laia Meseguer","key":"monfortpau","last":"Monfort","name":"Monfort, Laia Meseguer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Astrid Filt","key":"beyerpau","last":"Beyer","name":"Beyer, Astrid Filt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Gregor Borut Ernst","key":"jemecpau","last":"Jemec","locid":"b963b007-18b6-4432-897f-28b6a08275be","name":"Jemec, Gregor B E","name_org":"Jemec, Gregor Borut Ernst","orcid":"0000-0002-0712-2540","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Rune","key":"kjærsgaardandersenpau","last":"Kjærsgaard Andersen","locid":"b9ecd15a-cf83-41cc-8898-9fd38d6b4490","name":"Andersen, Rune Kjærsgaard","name_org":"Kjærsgaard Andersen, Rune","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Alexander","key":"egebergpau","last":"Egeberg","name":"Egeberg, Alexander","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jacob P.","key":"thyssenpau","last":"Thyssen","name":"Thyssen, Jacob P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nana Aviaaja Lippert","key":"rosenøpau","last":"Rosenø","name":"Rosenø, Nana Aviaaja Lippert","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Peter Riis","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9ab3e639-a02a-4ab7-9bde-d1d64cc7ecae","name":"Hansen, Peter Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-9056-535X","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Simon Francis","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"sallingolesenpau","last":"Salling Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","name_org":"Salling Olesen, Morten","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39382891"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamadermatol.2024.3779","issn":["11301910","21686068"],"issn_org":["21686068"],"issue":"1","journal":"JAMA Dermatology","pages":"22-30","status":"p","title":"JAMA Dermatology","volume":"161"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209232473"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","LEO Pharma","Private Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-16735bac-a713-4e9b-9201-f60331c14cc3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic Susceptibility to Hidradenitis Suppurativa and Predisposition to Cardiometabolic Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798976","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Today, Germanic languages, including German, English, Frisian, Dutch and the Nordic languages, are widely spoken in northwest Europe. However, key aspects of the assumed arrival and diversification of this linguistic group remain contentious1–3. By adding 712 new ancient human genomes we find an archaeologically elusive population entering Sweden from the Baltic region by around 4000 BP. This population became widespread throughout Scandinavia by 3500 BP, matching the contemporaneous distribution of Palaeo-Germanic, the Bronze Age predecessor of Proto-Germanic4–6. These Baltic immigrants thus offer a new potential vector for the first Germanic speakers to arrive in Scandinavia, some 800 years later than traditionally assumed7–12. Following the disintegration of Proto-Germanic13–16, we find by 1650 BP a southward push from Southern Scandinavia into presumed Celtic-speaking areas, including Germany, Poland and the Netherlands. During the Migration Period (1575–1375 BP), we see this ancestry representing West Germanic Anglo-Saxons in Britain, and Langobards in southern Europe. We find a related large-scale northward migration into Denmark and South Sweden corresponding with historically attested Danes and the expansion of Old Norse. These movements have direct implications for multiple linguistic hypotheses. Our findings show the power of combining genomics with historical linguistics and archaeology in creating a unified, integrated model for the emergence, spread and diversification of a linguistic group.","author_count":115,"contributors":["McColl, Hugh","Kroonen, Guus","Moreno Mayar, José Victor","Seersholm, Frederik Valeur","Scorrano, Gabriele","Pinotti, Thomaz","Vimala, Tharsika","Sindbæk, Søren M.","Ethelberg, Per","Fyfe, Ralph","Gaillard, Marie-José","Larsen, Hanne M. Ellegr ard","Mortensen, Morten Fischer","Demeter, Fabrice","Jørkov, M L S","Bergerbrant, Sophie","Damgaard, Peter de Barros","Allentoft, Morten E.","Vinner, Lasse","Gaunitz, Charleen","Ramsøe, Abigail","Altinkaya, Isin","Amund Henriksen, Rasmus","Irving-Pease, Evan K.","Sabatini, Serena","Fischer, Anders","Barrie, William","Ingason, Andrés","Rosengren, Anders","Vaughn, Andrew","Cao, Jialu","Staring, Jacqueline","Stenderup, Jesper","Yediay, Fulya Eylem","Ahlström, Torbjörn","Albris, Sofie Laurine","Atabiev, Biyaslan","Bangsgaard, Pernille","Belcastro, Maria Giovanna","Card, Nick","Charlier, Philippe","Chernykh, Elizaveta","Christiansen, Torben Trier","Coppa, Alfredo","De Coster, Maura","Denham, Sean Dexter","Desenne, Sophie","Downes, Jane","Frei, Karin Margarita","Gábor, Olivér","Gr ardsvoll, Johan Zakarias","Glørstad, Zanette Tsigaridas","Hansen, Jesper","Heeren, Stijn","Henriksen, Merete","Heyd, Volker","Høj, Mette","Holst, Mads Kähler","Jankauskas, Rimantas","Janson, Henrik","Jessen, Mads Dengsø","Johannsen, Jens Winther","Johansen, Torkel","Kastholm, Ole Thirup","Kern, Anton","Khaskhanov, Ruslan","Kjær, Katrine","Kolosov, Vladimir","Kootker, Lisette M.","Larsen, Anne Christine","Lejars, Thierry","Løvschal, Mette","Lynnerup, Niels","Magnusson, Yvonne","Mannermaa, Kristiina","Masyakin, Vyacheslav","Melheim, Anne Lene","Merkyte, Inga","Moiseyev, Vyacheslav","Møller, Stig Bergmann","Molnár, Erika","Mortensen, Nadja","Murphy, Eileen","Nielsen, Bjarne Henning","Pany-Kucera, Doris","Paulsson, Bettina Schulz","Ponce de León, Marcia S","Reiersen, Hr akon","Reinhard, Walter","Sajantila, Antti","Skar, Birgitte","Slavchev, Vladimir","Smrčka, Václav","Sørensen, Lasse","Tiefengraber, Georg","Uldum, Otto Christian","Vega, Jorge","Vitali, Daniele","Voloshinov, Alexey","Wr ahlin, Sidsel","Wendling, Holger","Wessman, Anna","Wilhelmson, Helene","Wiltschke, Karin","Zilhao, João","Zollikofer, Christoph PE","Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","Chaume, Bruno","Demoule, Jean-Paul","Werge, Thomas","Nielsen, Rasmus","Hedeager, Lotte","Kristiansen, Kristian","Sikora, Martin","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800889"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches F