iljø og Energi, No. 652","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-097857c7-9bb9-4e86-bc42-1adf002f10a1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Vildtbestande og jagttider i Danmark : Det biologiske grundlag for jagttidsrevisionen 2026","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805808","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Perforation of a major epicardial coronary artery during percutaneous coronary interventions (PCIs) is potentially lethal. Here the authors present a novel treatment strategy for managing a perforation in the bifurcation core with a complex 2-stent technique using polyurethane-covered stents. Specialized equipment for chronic total occlusion (CTO) interventions was used for recanalization of the main vessel and side branch. The procedure was tested in a bench setting and validated using 3-dimensional optical coherence tomography and micro-computed tomography. Discussion: The case emphasizes the need for complex CTO-PCI techniques in the treatment of acute non-CTO PCI. Novelty: To the best of our knowledge, this is the first report of a complex bifurcation technique for treatment of an epicardial perforation. Take-Home Message: It is feasible to treat an epicardial perforation in the bifurcation core with an advanced 2-stent technique. Ex vivo training for rare and severe complications may improve procedural outcome.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Holck, Emil Nielsen","Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","Hansen, Emilie Kjær","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Brüel, Annemarie","Johansen, Peter","Christiansen, Evald Høj","Jakobsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806666"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Holck, Emil Nielsen"],"keyword":["Chronic total occlusion","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complex treatment of a coronary bifurcation perforation with a dual covered stent strategy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2025.103382","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806666","identifier":[{"id":"105000514237","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40185573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12046829","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6c62164d-7403-4bc0-bb33-39791ec7b644"],"keyword":["chronic total occlusion","coronary perforation","percutaneous coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FB5D132DF4A1B266A42967926347741"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2025.103382","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil Nielsen","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","locid":"8e9383af-7f88-4fa3-bbbc-35641f5cbf8e","name":"Holck, Emil Nielsen","orcid":"0009-0009-6697-1073","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Nyhus","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"4dcde74a-8de8-4b84-b795-c9d84cfc7af7","name":"Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","orcid":"0000-0002-9891-7890","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emilie Kjær","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"da5c3a7f-5eca-4a73-9f67-a72c3810633f","name":"Hansen, Emilie Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Skovhus","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"924ef2ac-827c-4260-9cd7-fbe300bbafeb","name":"Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0001-9386-6679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annemarie","key":"brüelpau","last":"Brüel","locid":"aba2a94b-2aea-46c0-bdde-8b821e0f9d3f","name":"Brüel, Annemarie","orcid":"0000-0003-4833-0888","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"a2880dd0-b5a9-400e-9ee2-69fc3ce3761a","name":"Johansen, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evald Høj","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"06b04feb-3d2f-402d-b211-7ad5fd0387f1","name":"Christiansen, Evald Høj","orcid":"0000-0002-8740-4862","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"8da74392-7299-4ef1-bd97-faad1809c71d","name":"Jakobsen, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40185573"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jaccas.2025.103382","issn":["26660849"],"issue":"7","journal":"JACC: Case Reports","paperid":"103382","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Case Reports","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000514237"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6c62164d-7403-4bc0-bb33-39791ec7b644"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Complex Treatment of a Coronary Bifurcation Perforation With a Dual-Covered Stent Strategy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806666","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We investigate parametric decay instabilities (PDIs) of electron cyclotron waves due to a rotating neoclassical tearing mode (NTM) in ASDEX Upgrade. Strong scattering characteristic of PDIs is observed in a discharge where a (2,1) NTM has been identified. By mapping out the structure of the NTM toroidally, it is possible to determine the phases of the NTM which enable the decay to occur. Signatures of PDIs are seen when the edges of the magnetic island intersect the gyrotron beam path, but not when the O-point of the magnetic island is located directly in front of the gyrotron launcher. We propose an explanation using a simplified model, which reproduces features of the scattering in 1D particle-in-cell (PIC) simulations. The simulations show that a density perturbation caused by an NTM can give rise to a lowered PDI power threshold. The threshold is lowest in an intermediate density perturbation region where certain waves excited in PDIs can become trapped. The PIC simulations show that several decay and combination events involving approximately half frequency waves produce waves slightly downshifted from the main pump frequency of 140 GHz. This is the first time PIC simulations based on experimental profiles reproduce signals close to the pump frequency, which result from interactions with half frequency waves. The numerical results support previous observations from the tokamak TEXTOR.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Senstius, M. G.","Ragona, R.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Rasmussen, Jesper","Hansen, S. K.","Stober, J.","Salewski, Mirko","Akers, R.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808610"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["the ASDEX Upgrade Team","the MST1 Team"],"corresponding_author":["Senstius, M. G."],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Electron Bernstein wave","Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Parametric decay instability","Particle in cell","Upper hybrid layer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parametric decay of a gyrotron beam due to a rotating magnetic island in asdex upgrade","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ad9847","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808610","identifier":[{"id":"85219750162","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-937d5281-ab8c-4383-a850-496b3ffc71f3"],"keyword":["Electron bernstein wave","Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Neoclassical tearing mode","Parametric decay instability","Particle-in-cell","Upper hybrid layer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B104C88D9BF530D462A1688438FE8D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ad9847","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/400046735/Senstius_2025_Nucl._Fusion_65_026004.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"united kingdom atomic energy authority","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","used":1},{"affno":6,"key":"the mst1 team","name":"the MST1 Team","role":"oau"},{"affno":7,"key":"the asdex upgrade team","name":"the ASDEX Upgrade Team","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. G.","key":"senstiuspau","last":"Senstius","name":"Senstius, M. G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"ragonapau","last":"Ragona","locid":"6d50cb6b-b871-4b57-9536-210bf639b883","name":"Ragona, R.","orcid":"0000-0002-3225-5732","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A. S.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","name_org":"Jacobsen, A. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"S. K.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, S. K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"stoberpau","last":"Stober","name":"Stober, J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","name_org":"Salewski, M.","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"akerspau","last":"Akers","name":"Akers, R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/ad9847","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"026004","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219750162"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-937d5281-ab8c-4383-a850-496b3ffc71f3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Parametric decay of a gyrotron beam due to a rotating magnetic island in ASDEX Upgrade","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808610","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background/Aims: Several prognostic gene signatures have been proposed as predictors of the prognosis of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC), yet none are implemented in the clinical setting. We aimed to validate two gene scores previously derived from European cohorts. Methods: The patients who underwent liver resection for HCC at Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet from 2014 to 2018 were included. RNA sequencing determined the expression of genes in the ‘5-gene score’ (HN1, RAN, RAMP3, KRT19, TAF9B) and ‘HepatoPredict’ (CLU, DPT, SPRY2, CAPSN1). Univariable Cox regression assessed associations with overall and disease-free survival. These parameters were also analyzed in the The Cancer Genome Atlas Liver Hepatocellular Carcinoma (TCGA-LIHC) (n = 359) and National Institute of Health (NIH) (n = 178) cohorts. Results: Among 51 patients (88% male), 59% had no underlying liver disease and 25% had cirrhosis. No individual genes were significantly associated with overall survival in the Danish cohort. In the TCGA-LIHC cohort, CLU was linked to better overall survival, and in the NIH cohort, high expression of SPRY2 was associated with poorer overall survival. In the TCGA-LIHC cohort, HN1, RAN, and TAF9B were associated with poorer overall survival, while RAMP3 was linked to better overall survival. No genes were associated with disease-free survival. Conclusion: Few individual genes significantly predicted survival in the larger cohorts, and none in the Danish cohort. However, the clinical implication of this needs further investigation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Schnabl, Stinna D.","Klubien, Jeanett","O'Rourke, Colm J","Bull Nordkild, Sophie","Kugler, Jan Michael","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Andersen, Jesper B","Pommergaard, Hans Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810084"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomarker","Gene signature","Liver cancer","Liver resection","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of two prognostic gene scores in patients undergoing liver resection for hepatocellular carcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jceh.2025.102544","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810084","identifier":[{"id":"105001696785","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12002650","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40248345","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-719a13ea-e298-40d4-b374-94279359846f"],"keyword":["biomarker","gene signature","liver cancer","liver resection","prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-024F77390AEAAA6D813D1CC582DB40EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jceh.2025.102544","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/447738031/1-s2.0-S0973688325000441-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Andersen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stinna D.","key":"schnablpau","last":"Schnabl","name":"Schnabl, Stinna D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeanett","key":"klubienpau","last":"Klubien","name":"Klubien, Jeanett","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Colm J.","key":"orourkepau","last":"O'Rourke","locid":"891b9753-0ac7-4050-8599-8a1bff701efc","name":"O'Rourke, Colm J","name_org":"O'Rourke, Colm J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie","key":"bullnordkildpau","last":"Bull Nordkild","name":"Bull Nordkild, Sophie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jan Michael","key":"kuglerpau","last":"Kugler","name":"Kugler, Jan Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Susanne","key":"damnielsenpau","last":"Dam Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","name_org":"Dam Nielsen, Susanne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper B.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"fc0b6e89-065a-421e-b98a-cc9d328be76d","name":"Andersen, Jesper B","name_org":"Andersen, Jesper B.","orcid":"0000-0003-1760-5244","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hans Christian","key":"pommergaardpau","last":"Pommergaard","locid":"07936b89-5cc5-46bc-9488-e6b37feb9c44","name":"Pommergaard, Hans Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40248345"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jceh.2025.102544","issn":["09736883","22133453"],"issn_org":["09736883"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Clinical and Experimental Hepatology","paperid":"102544","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical and Experimental Hepatology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001696785"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-719a13ea-e298-40d4-b374-94279359846f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validation of Two Prognostic Gene Scores in Patients Undergoing Liver Resection for Hepatocellular Carcinoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-810084","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
