{"abstract":"Background: Remodelling of the extracellular matrix (ECM) is a continuous process necessary for maintaining skin tissue architecture and function. Disruption of type VII and XVII collagen turnover within the ECM is a contributing factor in the pathogenesis of skin conditions such as atopic dermatitis (AD). Objectives: To investigate the turnover of type VII and XVII collagens in AD using novel biomarkers of ECM turnover. Materials & Methods: Type VII (C7M) and XVII (PRO-C17) collagen turnover were measured using ELISAs. The cohort comprised 158 AD patients and 20 matched healthy donors (HD), with 53 of the AD patients treated with topical calcineurin inhibitors. Disease severity was assessed using the SCORAD index, categorizing patients into mild (SCORAD < 25), moderate (SCORAD: 25-50), and severe (SCORAD > 50) groups. Results: AD patients across all severity groups had higher C7M levels (all: p < 0.0001), while the levels of PRO-C17 were higher in mild AD patients versus HD (p = 0.0399). The C7M marker demonstrated an AUC of 0.96, and its levels were decreased in AD patients undergoing topical calcineurin inhibitor treatment (p=0.0073). Conclusion: The turnover of type VII and XVII collagens, measured by the biomarkers C7M and PRO-C17, is elevated in patients with AD. The biomarker C7M may have the potential to serve as a diagnostic and treatment response biomarker in AD.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andelic, Matej","Groen, Solveig Skovlund","Holm, Jesper Grønlund","Egeberg, Alexander","Thyssen, Jacob P.","Nielsen, Valdemar W.","Karsdal, Morten","Bay-Jensen, Anne Christine","Nielsen, Signe Holm","Thomsen, Simon Francis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819171"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atopic dermatitis","Biomarker","ECM","type VII collagen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel biomarker of type vii collagen degradation increases in patients with atopic dermatitis and decreases upon treatment with immunosuppressants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-819171","identifier":[{"id":"105006857010","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40417888","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5a486261-6986-4d09-a403-89088f8192dc"],"keyword":["ECM","ECM remodelling","atopic dermatitis","biomarker","type VII collagen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A9432290AF83B387F4E45957BB566EF8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Matej","key":"andelicmatejpau","last":"Andelic","locid":"5a85efeb-a09c-47e8-8aa9-d2597036c463","name":"Andelic, Matej","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Solveig Skovlund","key":"groensolveigskovlundpau","last":"Groen","locid":"c3ed8d9e-938e-4f49-a455-50b597700222","name":"Groen, Solveig Skovlund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Grønlund","key":"holmjespergrønlundpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jesper Grønlund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Alexander","key":"egebergalexanderpau","last":"Egeberg","locid":"e4445a48-c228-4507-b47c-a83175478f82","name":"Egeberg, Alexander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Jacob P.","key":"thyssenjacobppau","last":"Thyssen","locid":"c02c08ab-10c1-4ce8-bec3-447154952fc2","name":"Thyssen, Jacob P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Valdemar W.","key":"nielsenvaldemarwpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Valdemar W.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"karsdalmortenpau","last":"Karsdal","name":"Karsdal, Morten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Christine","key":"bayjensenannechristinepau","last":"Bay-Jensen","name":"Bay-Jensen, Anne Christine","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Signe Holm","key":"nielsensigneholmpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Signe Holm","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Simon Francis","key":"thomsensimonfrancispau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40417888"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1684/ejd.2025.4854","issn":["11671122","19524013"],"issn_org":["11671122"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Dermatology","pages":"91-97","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Dermatology","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105006857010"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a486261-6986-4d09-a403-89088f8192dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A novel biomarker of type VII collagen degradation increases in patients with atopic dermatitis and decreases upon treatment with immunosuppressants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819171","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Purpose Patients in temporary stays are typically older individuals with frailty and multimorbidity. However, limited knowledge exists about their medication use. This study aimed to describe prescription drug use among patients in temporary stays in Denmark. Methods We conducted a drug utilisation study on 11,424 patients in public healthcare-operated temporary stay units across 14 Danish municipalities between 2016 and 2023 (median age 81 years; 54% women). Prescription data were sourced from the Danish National Prescription Registry. Results Patients used a median of six drug classes (interquartile range [IQR] 4-10) in the four months before moving into a temporary stay facility; 68% used ≥ 5 drug classes, and 26% used ≥ 10. The most commonly used drug classes were paracetamol (49%), statins (30%), and proton pump inhibitors (29%). The monthly rate of new drug use increased from 23/100 patients six months before move-in to a peak of 262/100 patients in the first month after move-in, driven primarily by laxatives, analgesics, and antibiotics. High-risk drug use increased from 70 to 83% following move-in, with 49% of patients initiating at least one new high-risk drug, most commonly opioids (28%), potassium (17%), and anticoagulants and platelet inhibitors (15%). General practitioners initiated 60-70% of treatments and maintained 80-90%. Hospital physician prescriptions increased around move-in, peaking at 55% for initiation and 25% for maintenance in the first month after move-in. Conclusion Patients in temporary stays in Denmark demonstrate high medication use, including high-risk drugs, with a notable increase in treatment initiations around the time of move-in.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Harbi, Hanin","Lundby, Carina","Jensen, Peter Bjødstrup","Larsen, Søren Post","Rørbæk, Linda Grouleff","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Ryg, Jesper","Reilev, Mette","Edwards, Kasper","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827648"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pottegård, Anton"],"keyword":["Aged","Drug Utilization","Epidemology","Intermediate care facilities","Polypharmacy","Skilled nursing facilities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["REAGENS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"medication use patterns among older patients in temporary stays in denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827648","identifier":[{"id":"105004475411","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40332658","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-662de66a-77de-408c-a8e9-8efcd7bd46a9"],"keyword":["Aged","Drug utilization","Epidemology","Intermediate care facilities","Polypharmacy","Skilled nursing facilities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D6654C14DA6D6B3411E0126A442E8128"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/411359356/s41999-025-01210-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["REAGENS"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Strategy and Leadership Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanin","key":"harbipau","last":"Harbi","name":"Harbi, Hanin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","name":"Lundby, Carina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Bjødstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Peter Bjødstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Post","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Søren Post","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Linda Grouleff","key":"rørbækpau","last":"Rørbæk","name":"Rørbæk, Linda Grouleff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Vestergaard","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn-Nielsen","name":"Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","name":"Ryg, Jesper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"reilevpau","last":"Reilev","name":"Reilev, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","locid":"e713de29-a31d-4da0-ba3d-a21f6525c79d","name":"Edwards, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6328-1765","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","name":"Pottegård, Anton","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40332658"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","issn":["18787649"],"journal":"European Geriatric Medicine","pages":"1427-1435","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Geriatric Medicine","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004475411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-662de66a-77de-408c-a8e9-8efcd7bd46a9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Medication use patterns among older patients in temporary stays in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827648","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Nanolasers operating at low power levels are strongly affected by intrinsic quantum noise, influencing both intensity fluctuations and laser coherence. Starting from semiclassical rate equations and making a simple hypothesis for the phase of the laser field, a simple stochastic model for the laser quantum noise is suggested. The model is shown to agree quantitatively with quantum master equations for microscopic lasers with a small number of emitters and with classical Langevin equations for macroscopic systems. In contrast, neither quantum master equations nor classical Langevin equations adequately address the mesoscopic regime. The stochastic approach is used to calculate the linewidth throughout the transition to lasing, where the linewidth changes from being dominated by the particlelike nature of photons below threshold to the wavelike nature above threshold, where it is strongly influenced by index fluctuations enhancing the linewidth.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bundgaard-Nielsen, Matias","Saldutti, Marco","Gøtzsche, Benjamin Falkenberg","Grovn, Emil","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828094"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mørk, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple yet accurate stochastic approach to the quantum phase noise of nanolasers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105007100734","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828094","identifier":[{"id":"40531042","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105007100734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f4d76221-a3b4-4de1-90ff-e884ec7f1598"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8DDD7B5A01F4152548022605AAD95CA4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, NanoPhoton – Center for Nanophotonics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matias","key":"bundgaardnielsenpau","last":"Bundgaard-Nielsen","locid":"ec5fab64-bf0d-495e-b3fb-8c53ad2dcb0f","name":"Bundgaard-Nielsen, Matias","orcid":"0000-0003-2941-6643","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"salduttipau","last":"Saldutti","locid":"f7860a91-f9be-400d-8987-99ed508ee7b4","name":"Saldutti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0003-1834-4672","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin Falkenberg","key":"gøtzschepau","last":"Gøtzsche","locid":"cab04d69-7b60-48a7-86fa-2b95bd2c5ae6","name":"Gøtzsche, Benjamin Falkenberg","orcid":"0000-0002-2319-7462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"grovnpau","last":"Grovn","locid":"1f42528e-cce4-4f81-a0fb-203899afb4eb","name":"Grovn, Emil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40531042"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.134.213804","issn":["00319007","10797114"],"issn_org":["00319007"],"issue":"21","journal":"Physical Review Letters","paperid":"213804","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Letters","volume":"134"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007100734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f4d76221-a3b4-4de1-90ff-e884ec7f1598"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simple yet Accurate Stochastic Approach to the Quantum Phase Noise of Nanolasers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828094","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: In 2019, an initiative to reduce sickness absence in public sector workplaces in Denmark was introduced. The initiative involved appointing a sickness absence coordinator (SA coordinator) to oversee the implementation of workplace-based sickness absence interventions. Since the role of the SA coordinator is a novel concept introduced as part of the initiative, this study investigates the responsibilities of SA coordinators and the challenges they experienced in fulfilling this role during the implementation process. METHODS: Semi-structured interviews with and observations of SA coordinators from four public sector workplaces were carried out. We collected the first four interviews and observations during the implementation process with follow-up interviews collected at the end of the process. The data were analyzed using thematic analysis. RESULTS: The SA coordinators all experienced challenges in terms of lack of commitment among the line managers to participate in the intervention. They experienced being seen as a burden rather than a helping hand, and felt that the line managers might have difficulty recognizing the value of the SA coordinators. Potential ways to improve the collaboration between the SA coordinators and the line managers include considering hiring the SA coordinator in-house and incorporation of intervention components into existing activities to accommodate the busyness of the line managers. CONCLUSIONS: To support the SA coordinators in carrying out their role and responsibilities, this study suggests that it is important to ensure commitment to the role, especially among the line managers in order to enhance good working relationships.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Lene","Nielsen, Maj Britt Dahl","Garde, Anne Helene","Kristiansen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-093.26-793962"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Lene"],"keyword":["Absenteeism","Denmark","Female","Humans","Implementation","Implementering","Intervention","Interviews as Topic","Male","Professional Role","Public Sector organization administration","Qualitative Research","Rehabilitation","Return to work","Sick Leave","Sygefravær","Workplace","Workplace organization administration"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the role of sickness absence coordinators in implementing interventions to reduce sickness absence in public sector workplaces in denmark","src":["nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10926-024-10183-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.26-793962","identifier":[{"id":"85188341688","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38519778","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11839793","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["nfa-5e8c1b3b-316f-4910-8cb7-4a6b0b50d017","sdu-efd5e25b-2974-42e2-b9f9-42f329eaaa21"],"keyword":["Absenteeism","Denmark","Female","Humans","Implementation","Intervention","Interviews as Topic","Male","Professional Role","Public Sector/organization & administration","Qualitative Research","Rehabilitation","Return to work","Sick Leave","Sygefravær","Workplace","Workplace/organization & administration","implementering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-58C221D14EEA68E2E2D26FBC0C4B78F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10926-024-10183-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/285722763/s10926-024-10183-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Mental health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0d8ad03f-8294-49a2-8bb7-fea40eccf25a","name":"Rasmussen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-7864-4178","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj Britt Dahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9dfb8e84-90f3-4531-b486-2df21e9ecd3a","name":"Nielsen, Maj Britt Dahl","orcid":"0000-0002-5758-8031","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"8e894baf-467c-45d3-8abe-41a805b30b22","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38519778"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10926-024-10183-1","issn":["10530487","15733688"],"issn_org":["10530487"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Occupational Rehabilitation","pages":"78-87","publisher":"Springer New York","status":"p","title":"Journal of Occupational Rehabilitation","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188341688"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-5e8c1b3b-316f-4910-8cb7-4a6b0b50d017","sdu-efd5e25b-2974-42e2-b9f9-42f329eaaa21"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exploring the Role of Sickness Absence Coordinators in Implementing Interventions to Reduce Sickness Absence in Public Sector Workplaces in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.26-793962","year":2025,"yearsub":2025}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate the proportion of running-related injuries that can be classified as (i) being based on overload with an acute mechanism with a sudden onset, (ii) being overuse in the sense they are based on a repetitive mechanism with a sudden onset; and (iii) being overuse in the sense that runners gradually develop problems that lead to an injury. DESIGN: Cohort study with an 18-month follow-up. METHODS: English-speaking runners aged at least 18 years who were tracking running activities were included. Running-related injury during follow-up categorized into three groups: (i) those with overload injury; (ii) those with a running-related problem 7 to 28 days prior to reporting a running-related injury and (iii) those sustaining a running-related injury without any preceding problems. RESULTS: Overload injury accounted for 467 of 1,666 injuries (28%), while 1,199 injuries were overuse (72%). Among overuse injuries, the proportion of runners having a problem prior to injury occurrence was 6.9% [9.4%; 13.0%] 28 days prior to injury. CONCLUSION: Most of the overuse injuries occurring in adult runners may be classified as sudden repetitive overuse injuries rather than injuries that are based on a gradual onset.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Frandsen, Jesper Schuster Brandt","Simonsen, Nina Sjoerup","Hulme, Adam","Jacobsen, Julie Sandell","Nielsen, Rasmus Oestergaard"],"cuid":["S02-097.22-804174"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Frandsen, Jesper Schuster Brandt"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NHMRC Centre for Clinical Research Excellence in Spinal Pain, Injury and Health, University of Queensland","University of Queensland"],"keyword":["Injuries","Overuse","Running","health nutrition and quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis i Aarhus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a paradigm shift in understanding overuse running related injuries findings from the garmin runsafe study point to a sudden not gradual onset","src":["au","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2519/josptopen.2024.0075","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.22-804174","ids":["au-a4f07b73-d345-4665-8118-e5c850f1bf9d","via-9ac38e12-d246-4cd4-ac3a-fc60cf108ea3"],"keyword":["health, nutrition and quality of life","injuries","overuse","running"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33171DDD87BFBF00EAAE9DDA4ECA202C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.jospt.org/doi/10.2519/josptopen.2024.0075","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2519/josptopen.2024.0075","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Institute of Environmental and Occupational Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis i Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","c