{"abstract":"Background: Cardiovascular disease (CVD) preventive medications are recommended for patients at high short-term CVD risk. As most younger people with multiple raised CVD risk factors levels have low short-term risk, they could be falsely reassured to take no action. Heart age-the chronological age of a hypothetical person with the same short-term absolute CVD risk as the patient being assessed, but with an 'ideal' risk profile-is a complementary relative CVD risk metric developed to encourage these younger patients to make long-term lifestyle changes. However, clinicians sometimes use heart age to inform medication decisions. We assessed the appropriateness of this practice by comparing heart age and short-term CVD risk. Methods: New Zealand primary care patients are recruited to the PREDICT cohort when their CVD risk is assessed. PREDICT is an ongoing prospective study in one-third of New Zealand general practices, designed to derive CVD risk prediction algorithms. Five-year CVD risk was calculated for 35-74-year-old PREDICT participants using published equations. Heart age was calculated using non-smoking, systolic blood pressure of 120 mm Hg and total cholesterol/high-density lipoprotein ratio of 3.5, as the 'ideal' risk profile. CVD risk and heart age gaps (difference between chronological age and heart age) were compared. Results: Among 371 676 PREDICT participants, 5-year CVD risk increased with age, approximately doubling every 10 years, whereas heart age gaps decreased with increasing age, approximately halving between 35 and 44-year olds and 65-74-year olds. There were 5-40-year heart age gap differences between groups with similar 5-year CVD risks, but different ages. Conclusion: Short-term CVD risk and heart age are not interchangeable risk metrics. Short-term risk increases with increasing age whereas heart age gaps generally decline, with major differences between younger and older people with similar short-term risk. If heart age is used to inform medication decisions rather than encourage long-term lifestyle changes, older people at high short-term risk could be undertreated and younger people at low short-term risk could be unnecessarily medicated.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Stjernholm, Kathrine","Kerr, Andrew","Poppe, Katrina K","Jensen, Anders Elkær","Mehta, Suneela","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Jackson, Rod","Wells, Susan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-802745"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Stjernholm, Kathrine"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Auckland"],"keyword":["Adult","Age Factors","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases epidemiology","Coronary artery disease","Epidemiology","Female","Heart Disease Risk Factors","Humans","Hyperlipidemias","Hypertension","Male","Middle Aged","New Zealand epidemiology","Primary Health Care","Prospective Studies","Risk Assessment methods","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"age stratified comparison of heart age and predicted cardiovascular risk in 000000000370 000000000000 primary care patients","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/heartjnl-2024-324156","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-802745","identifier":[{"id":"39658197","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85214565166","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11874366","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-b4178785-9285-4737-be20-7a4757b8a572"],"keyword":["Adult","Age Factors","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases/epidemiology","Coronary Artery Disease","Epidemiology","Female","Heart Disease Risk Factors","Humans","Hyperlipidemias","Hypertension","Male","Middle Aged","New Zealand/epidemiology","Primary Health Care","Prospective Studies","Risk Assessment/methods","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51620409AAAA6F77E04C2CB651A0DE2A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/282987421/166.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/heartjnl-2024-324156","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Auckland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathrine","key":"stjernholmpau","last":"Stjernholm","locid":"f3e9c7ce-a03a-4747-a0ee-112c1481f176","name":"Stjernholm, Kathrine","orcid":"0000-0003-1198-2022","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"kerrpau","last":"Kerr","name":"Kerr, Andrew","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrina K","key":"poppepau","last":"Poppe","name":"Poppe, Katrina K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Elkær","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c03a32e8-161e-45b7-82ff-bd93d460de3c","name":"Jensen, Anders Elkær","orcid":"0000-0002-9056-9326","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Suneela","key":"mehtapau","last":"Mehta","name":"Mehta, Suneela","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rod","key":"jacksonpau","last":"Jackson","name":"Jackson, Rod","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan","key":"wellspau","last":"Wells","name":"Wells, Susan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39658197"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/heartjnl-2024-324156","issn":["13556037","1468201X"],"issn_org":["13556037"],"issue":"4","journal":"Heart","pages":"166-171","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Heart","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214565166"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b4178785-9285-4737-be20-7a4757b8a572"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Age-stratified comparison of heart age and predicted cardiovascular risk in 370 000 primary care patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-802745","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Sodium glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitors lower blood pressure. The underlying mechanisms are multifactorial and include effects on vascular function. We examined the systemic hemodynamic effects of empagliflozin in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM2) with and without chronic kidney disease (CKD) and in patients with nondiabetic CKD. Methods: Three double-blinded, randomized, placebo-controlled cross-over trials, including patients with DM2 and preserved renal function (n = 16), DM2 and CKD (n = 17) and nondiabetic CKD (n = 16). Participants were randomized to 4 weeks of empagliflozin 10 mg or placebo and crossed over after a 2-week washout. We measured brachial and central 24-h ambulatory blood pressure (ABP), pulse wave velocity (PWV), augmentation index (AIx@75), markers of nitric oxide and erythrocyte sodium sensitivity (ESS), a marker of endothelial glycocalyx function. Results: Empagliflozin reduced PWV [-0.16 m/s, 95% confidence interval (95% CI): -0.26; -0.06, P = 0.002], AIx@75 (-2.17%, 95% CI: -3.31; -1.02, P < 0.001) and brachial and central ABP in the combined study population (n = 49). Changes in PWV and AIx@75 correlated to changes in systolic brachial ABP. Markers of nitric oxide did not increase, but empagliflozin decreased ESS, which was correlated to an increase in haematocrit. Conclusion: Empagliflozin decreased arterial stiffness, mediated partly by a decrease in brachial ABP. We found no increase in nitric oxide activity, but ESS decreased. While this may be explained partly by a change in haematocrit, it could indicate an improvement in endothelial glycocalyx function.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Steffen Flindt","Duus, Camilla Lundgreen","Buus, Niels Henrik","Bech, Jesper N.","Mose, Frank Holden"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805930"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Steffen Flindt"],"keyword":["Augmentation index","Blood Pressure","Chronic kidney disease","Endothelium","Nitric oxide","Pulse wave velocity","Sodium glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitors","Type 2 diabetes mellitus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of empagliflozin on systemic haemodynamic function three randomized placebo controlled trials","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105001718369","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-805930","identifier":[{"id":"40156337","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105001718369","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-18c37fb1-06d2-41fa-930f-b40cf50e8ce7"],"keyword":["augmentation index","blood pressure","chronic kidney disease","endothelium","nitric oxide","pulse wave velocity","sodium glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitors","type 2 diabetes mellitus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D605B8321BA6347BA1AAB2744DCC75C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen F.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"040ca6cf-cd77-4f21-8512-8cb0130c7f09","name":"Nielsen, Steffen Flindt","name_org":"Nielsen, Steffen F.","orcid":"0009-0002-5410-1088","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla L.","key":"duuspau","last":"Duus","locid":"dd95ffa8-c453-4af1-8bc5-f08e62c18b6c","name":"Duus, Camilla Lundgreen","name_org":"Duus, Camilla L.","orcid":"0009-0007-2241-5791","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"buuspau","last":"Buus","locid":"cb682ed6-2fe3-4664-90d6-0690462e8f80","name":"Buus, Niels Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper N.","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","locid":"ada3ab11-5e6a-4f8c-8c03-c9e09fcb18be","name":"Bech, Jesper N.","orcid":"0000-0002-0605-1277","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank H.","key":"mosepau","last":"Mose","locid":"2743ec13-0199-4678-9480-a5c65172749f","name":"Mose, Frank Holden","name_org":"Mose, Frank H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40156337"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/hjh.0000000000004007","issn":["02636352","09521178"],"issn_org":["02636352"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Hypertension","pages":"1021-1029","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hypertension","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001718369"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-18c37fb1-06d2-41fa-930f-b40cf50e8ce7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effects of empagliflozin on systemic haemodynamic function : three randomized, placebo-controlled trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805930","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: This study examines trends in paracetamol overdoses among Danish adolescents during and following the COVID-19 pandemic. Methods: A retrospective observational study was conducted using data from the national databases, covering all paediatric departments in Denmark from January 2016 to December 2023. Patients between 10 and 19 years of age diagnosed with paracetamol overdose were stratified by sex, age and number of hospital admissions. As the dataset covers the entire population, observed values reflect true parameters. A one-sample t-test compared post-COVID-19 values to the pre-COVID-19 mean. Results: A total of 4.448 patients accounted for 5.794 hospital admissions due to paracetamol overdoses, with a majority being girls. During the second year of the pandemic (2021), a rise in overdose cases (26.5%) and hospital admissions (30.3%) was observed, especially among girls. The average number of admissions per patient increased, indicating repeated self-harm attempts. Cases of severe overdoses leading to acute liver failure increased at Rigshospitalet. These trends reversed post-pandemic. Conclusion: The findings suggest an association between pandemic-related isolation and an increase in adolescent paracetamol overdoses. While rates began to normalise after restrictions were lifted, further research is needed to assess the long-term mental health impact of such restrictions.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Kempf, Oliver Nørholm","Helt, Thora Wesenberg","Herrche-Petersen, Jens Jakob","Søndergaard, Charlotte","Longin, Elke","Ellerman, Annie","Frederiksen, Marianne Sjølin","Lundby-Christensen, Louise","Andersen, Jesper","Petersen, Thomas Houmann","Nielsen, Rasmus G.","Nielsen, Bent Windelborg","Trier, Cæcilie","Jürgensen, Louise","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Reynskor, Magnus Ove","Kvistgaard, Helene","Boas, Malene","Jeppesen, Eva Mosfeldt","Christensen, Vibeke Brix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807416"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kempf, Oliver Nørholm"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paracetamol overdoses among danish adolescents a covid 000000000019 perspective","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.70037","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807416","identifier":[{"id":"85219668959","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39968885","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c0904405-1bbd-4900-9db7-8644ae118ccf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-38943F00CF62526B653688DC67503462"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.70037","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Børn og Unge, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["North Denmark Regional Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Pediatric Department, Holbæk Hospital, Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver Nørholm","key":"kempfolivernørholmpau","last":"Kempf","name":"Kempf, Oliver Nørholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thora Wesenberg","key":"heltthorawesenbergpau","last":"Helt","name":"Helt, Thora Wesenberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Jakob","key":"herrchepetersenjensjakobpau","last":"Herrche-Petersen","name":"Herrche-Petersen, Jens Jakob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"søndergaardcharlottepau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"8212a0d4-6fa3-4a7f-8c4c-cafe9a630582","name":"Søndergaard, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Elke","key":"