b-f6771b13329c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Spatial and Temporal Summation on Histaminergic and Non-Histaminergic Itch","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-815020","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs) are being tested in numerous clinical trials, yet the limited progression of these trials to advanced stages indicates unresolved translational challenges. Expanding MSCs is a critical step in most therapeutic applications, and bioreactor-based culture offers large-scale production compared to monolayer cultures. Nevertheless, since MSCs sense their microenvironment, it is crucial to understand how these systems affect their properties. We expanded human adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells (AD-MSCs) from the same donors in both small- and large-scale platforms. Bulk-RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) and mass spectrometry analysis demonstrated that small-scale culture had a broader range of differentially expressed genes (DEGs) and proteins within immunomodulatory, cell migration, and cell adhesion pathways. In contrast, the large-scale culture showed a lower amount of DEGs and proteins associated mainly with extracellular matrix synthesis. Our findings demonstrate that expansion platforms significantly impact MSCs’ properties, highlighting the need to optimize expansion conditions to obtain high cell yield without compromising MSCs’ attributes.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Galera, Marina Ramírez","Oikonomou, Athanasios","Elsborg, Jonas D.","Harth, Lisa","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Løvendorf, Marianne Bengtson","Dyring-Andersen, Beatrice","Iorio, Francesco","Fog, Lea Munthe","Woetmann, Anders","Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819499"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Computational Biology Research Centre, Human Technopole","Fondazione Human Technopole"],"keyword":["Bioreactor","Cell expansion","Immunomodulation","MSCs","Transcriptomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Celcore"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of cell culture transition on adipose derived mesenchymal stromal cells multi omics analysis of small vs large scale production","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819499","identifier":[{"id":"105009437769","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-81449c79-bbd7-4424-b5b0-e2fec4552837"],"keyword":["AD-MSCs","MSCs","adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells","bioreactor","cell expansion","culture platform","immunomodulation","large-scale cell production","transcriptomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-17CBF9A86E6B581F086477A500705DD5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456083625/Impact_of_cell_culture_transition.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Skin Immunology Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"computational biology research centre human technopole","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Computational Biology Research Centre, Human Technopole","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Celcore"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"it","key":"fondazione human technopole","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fondazione Human Technopole","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marina Ramírez","key":"galerapau","last":"Galera","locid":"51a1f4a2-848d-4817-936a-adede4a4070f","name":"Galera, Marina Ramírez","orcid":"0000-0001-9797-8512","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Athanasios","key":"oikonomoupau","last":"Oikonomou","name":"Oikonomou, Athanasios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas D.","key":"elsborgpau","last":"Elsborg","locid":"dbd544fa-a21d-4a87-b5ff-226aa2f424b6","name":"Elsborg, Jonas D.","orcid":"0000-0002-1506-4280","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lisa","key":"harthpau","last":"Harth","locid":"07113df3-377c-4814-8bd2-ca1ad73ad2fb","name":"Harth, Lisa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","first":"Marianne Bengtson","key":"løvendorfpau","last":"Løvendorf","locid":"c2444ac6-8300-4e66-9b0a-c5a153a7ea30","name":"Løvendorf, Marianne Bengtson","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Beatrice","key":"dyringandersenpau","last":"Dyring-Andersen","locid":"8d2c8b9b-81bb-458e-aad4-4653e0ace0d6","name":"Dyring-Andersen, Beatrice","orcid":"0000-0002-3012-2645","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Francesco","key":"ioriopau","last":"Iorio","name":"Iorio, Francesco","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lea Munthe","key":"fogpau","last":"Fog","name":"Fog, Lea Munthe","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"woetmannpau","last":"Woetmann","locid":"18df0978-d38c-4ffb-985d-b544e22fa387","name":"Woetmann, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-3008-735X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Dyrendom","key":"svalgaardpau","last":"Svalgaard","name":"Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","issn":["23290501"],"issue":"3","journal":"Molecular Therapy Methods and Clinical Development","paperid":"101512","status":"p","title":"Molecular Therapy Methods and Clinical Development","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009437769"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-81449c79-bbd7-4424-b5b0-e2fec4552837"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of cell culture transition on adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells : Multi-omics analysis of small- vs large-scale production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819499","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Public transport (PT) users spend considerable time reaching, waiting and transferring at stations, finding these trip legs highly cumbersome. Improving travellers’ experiences during these legs is pivotal for satisfaction with door-to-door PT and, hence, long-term ridership. Further attention to the design of stations and their urban surroundings, considering the travel experience holistically, is therefore necessary. This study investigates the relationship between (i) street- and station-level built environment features at both trip ends, perceived safety and travel environment satisfaction, (ii) travel environment satisfaction and trip satisfaction, using data from a tailor-made survey (N=3,085) on train trips in East Denmark. Findings from structural equation model highlight that safe, attractive environments at home and activity ends can boost satisfaction. Key improvements include better maintenance, lighting, and wayfinding and reducing isolated areas around stations. The results encourage researchers to factor in urban surroundings in PT studies and practitioners to design safe and attractive travel environments.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Başaran, Gülin Göksu","Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827487"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Başaran, Gülin Göksu"],"keyword":["Perceived safety","Security","Train station","Transit","Urban design","structural equation modelling SEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a holistic view of safe attractive travel environments for public transport satisfaction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trd.2025.104768","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827487","identifier":[{"id":"105004560913","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3726ec89-dd2b-40c9-b874-b9c6e99d8c1b"],"keyword":["Perceived safety","Security","Station design","Structural equation modelling (SEM)","Train station","Transit","Urban design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-4BA5980CCA9E41181D51F86B29DABB1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/409419553/1-s2.0-S1361920925001786-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trd.2025.104768","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science, Transportation Systems Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gülin Göksu","key":"başaranpau","last":"Başaran","locid":"bbde6a42-a32a-403c-a9d4-e739aec4d6a3","name":"Başaran, Gülin Göksu","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-5715","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.trd.2025.104768","issn":["13619209","18792340"],"issn_org":["13619209"],"journal":"Transportation Research. Part D: Transport & Environment","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Transportation Research. Part D: Transport & Environment","title_org":"Transportation Research, Part D: Transport and Environment","volume":"144"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004560913"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3726ec89-dd2b-40c9-b874-b9c6e99d8c1b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A holistic view of safe, attractive travel environments for public transport satisfaction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827487","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Acute respiratory infections (ARIs) are frequent reasons for medical consultations in general practice and can lead to unnecessary recontacts. Introducing new point-of-care (POC) polymerase chain reaction (PCR) diagnostic equipment may offer an attractive and efficient way of providing a more precise and exact microbial diagnosis. Successful uptake of POC PCR equipment could potentially lead to a reduction in recontacts with benefits for both staff and patients. However, introducing new diagnostic technology is a complex intervention and several contextual factors may impact the implementation. Objective: This study aims to evaluate the effect of POC PCR test availability in general practice on the subsequent (1) number of recontacts to the general practitioner (GP) for patients with symptoms of ARIs (primary outcome) and (2) hospital admissions, deaths, antibiotic prescriptions, health-related quality of life, GP and patient satisfaction, costs, cost-effectiveness, and contextual facilitators and barriers conditioning the implementation process (secondary outcomes). Methods: This study is a cluster-randomized, crossover, nonblinded superiority trial with a 1:1 allocation ratio between usual care (control) and POC PCR test availability (intervention). Questionnaire data are collected at day 0, 7, 14, and 28 after the initial contact (health-related quality of life, absenteeism and presentism among patients, and patient satisfaction) and after finalization of the study period (GP satisfaction). Data on recontacts, hospital admissions, redeemed antibiotic prescriptions, costs, and deaths will be retrieved from the Danish national registries. The implementation process will be evaluated based on data from interviews with users of POC PCR tests (i.e., GPs, staff, and patients) and from observations in the clinics in line with Medical Research Council guidelines. Results: As per the randomized crossover design carried out during September 2023 to March 2024 investigating a sample of 100 GP clinics, we expect to obtain an in-depth and multifaceted understanding of the effects of the availability of the POC PCR test equipment in general practice. Conclusions: This study will provide valuable information about the diagnostic conditions and possibilities in general practice and provide insights into the organization of primary health care. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT06120153; https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT06120153 International Registered Report Identifier (IRRID): DERR1-10.2196/72842","author_count":13,"contributors":["Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","Simonsen, Line Maria","Kongstad, Line Planck","Thilsing, Trine","Wehberg, Sonja","Hallas, Jesper","Sopina, Liza","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Overbeck, Gritt","Hvidt, Elisabeth Assing","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Rasmussen, Tina Lein","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828362"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute respiratory infections","General practice","Point of care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluating the effect of a molecular point of care test on acute respiratory infections in general practice protocol for a cluster randomized trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/72842","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828362","identifier":[{"id":"40921063","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-12629eb2-6afe-49eb-82ca-1f1b7c2628ed"],"keyword":["acute respiratory infections","general practice","point-of-care"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E11E8AA467C9ABBD00D2391E1F93D1FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/72842","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/475111040/resprot-2025-1-e72842.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirubakaran","key":"balasubramaniampau","last":"Balasubramaniam","name":"Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Maria","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Line Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Planck","key":"kongstadpau","last":"Kongstad","name":"Kongstad, Line Planck","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","name":"Thilsing, Trine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sonja","key":"wehbergpau","last":"Wehberg","name":"Wehberg, Sonja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","name":"Hallas, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liza","key":"sopinapau","last":"Sopina","name":"Sopina, Liza","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gritt","key":"overbeckpau","last":"Overbeck","locid":"6af8fc11-7218-4c13-8094-1138e1b4e523","name":"Overbeck, Gritt","orcid":"0000-0002-1740-1148","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth Assing","key":"hvidtpau","last":"Hvidt","name":"Hvidt, Elisabeth Assing","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina Lein","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Tina Lein","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40921063"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/72842","issn":["19290748"],"journal":"JMIR Research Protocols","paperid":"e72842","status":"p","title":"JMIR Research Protocols","title_org":"J M I R Research Protocols","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-12629eb2-6afe-49eb-82ca-1f1b7c2628ed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluating the Effect of a Molecular Point-of-Care Test on Acute Respiratory Infections in General Practice : Protocol for a Cluster Randomized Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828362","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Despite significant advancements in diabetes care, many individuals with type 2 diabetes (T2D) do not receive optimal care and treatment. Digital interventions promoting behavioral changes have shown promising long-term results in supporting healthier lifestyles but are not implemented in most healthcare offerings, maybe due to lack of general practice support and collaboration. This study evaluates the efficacy of the Digital, Individualized, and Collaborative Treatment of T2D in General Practice Based on Decision Aid (DICTA), a randomized controlled trial integrating a patient-centered smartphone application for lifestyle support in conjunction with a clinical decision support (CDS) tool to assist general practitioners (GPs) in optimizing antidiabetic treatment. Methods: The present randomized controlled trial aims to recruit 400 individuals with T2D from approximately 70 GP clinics (GPCs) in Denmark. The GPCs will be cluster-randomized in a 2:3 ratio to intervention or control groups. The intervention group will receive one year of individualized eHealth lifestyle coaching via a smartphone application, guided by patient-reported outcomes (PROs). Alongside this, the GPCs will have access to the CDS tool to optimize pharmacological decision-making through electronic health records. The control group will receive usual care for one year, followed by the same intervention in the second year. Results: The primary outcome is the one-year change in estimated ten-year cardiovascular risk, assessed by SCORE2-Diabetes calculated from age, smoking status, systolic blood pressure, total and high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, age at diabetes diagnosis, HbA1c, and eGFR. Conclusions: If effective, DICTA could offer a scalable, digital-first approach for improving T2D management in primary care by combining patient-centered lifestyle coaching with real-time pharmacological clinical decision support.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Kristoffersen, Sofie Frigaard","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Jeremiassen, Louise Munk Ramo","Kylkjær, Lea Bolette","Christensen, Nanna Reffstrup","Jørgensen, Sally Wulff","Kristensen, Jette Kolding","Wehberg, Sonja","Raymond, Ilan Esra","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Olsen, Michael Hecht","Nielsen, Jens Steen","Brandt, Carl Joakim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-831258"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kristoffersen, Sofie Frigaard"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for the digital individualized and collaborative treatment of type 000000000002 diabetes in general practice based on decision aid dicta a randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu17152494","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-831258","identifier":[{"id":"40806079","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105013197447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8c06aa28-c0fb-4874-8186-1b978a26d247"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7F77DDB0502C71DF903162D4D3E11DD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/294339266/nutrients-17-02494.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu17152494","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Research Unit of General Practice in Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Copenhagen University Hospital Amager and Hvidovre, Hvidovre, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Holbæk Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"