{"abstract":"Selective breeding has been proposed as an effective mean to enhance the production of insects used for food and feed. Despite advantages of incorporating pedigree information in selective breeding schemes no studies have yet explored this approach for insects farmed for food and feed. Here we performed a multi-trait selective breeding experiment aimed at increasing larval size and decreasing egg-to-adult development time in a pedigreed house fly (Musca domestica) population. Estimated breeding values (EBVs) based on family average phenotypic records were used as the primary selection criterion, and selection responses were evaluated over the seven generations of the selective breeding experiment. Following termination of selection, larval size, egg-to-adult development time, larval heat stress tolerance, and egg-to-adult survival were compared between the selection line and a non-selected control line when reared in a mass-rearing setup on a standard and a low-quality diet. The selection line had higher larval size compared to the control line, while no differences were found for egg-to-adult development time, larval heat stress tolerance and egg-to-adult survival. The larger larval size of the selection line compared to the control line was most evident when larvae were reared on the low-quality diet, indicating that the selection line copes better with nutritionally stressful conditions. The selection line exhibited genetic improvement throughout the selective breeding experiment, but those effects were not reflected in the phenotype, possibly indicating negative and accumulative environmental influences on the traits.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Laursen, Stine Frey","Nielsen, Hanne Marie","Bahrndorff, Simon","Sahana, Goutam","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Kristensen, Torsten Nygaard","Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813305"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Laursen, Stine Frey"],"keyword":["Development time","Musca domestica","estimated breeding values EBVs","larval size","selection trade offs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi trait pedigree based selective breeding to optimise farmed insects evidence from a house fly population","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/784712811/accepted_author_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark (DFF-0136-00171B)."],"id":"S02-100.00-813305","identifier":[{"id":"105009830089","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-17d066d9-df1e-4893-886b-8c0bca929c43","au-6b67d2e0-689c-410e-abf1-d2d078f0e760"],"keyword":["Musca domestica","development time","estimated breeding values (EBVs)","larval size","selection trade-offs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-664C21B1B9EBF9237D73301A09232802"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/784712811/accepted_author_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Functional Ecology and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Frey","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"1a898d84-89ba-4f9d-b176-c6658e075581","name":"Laursen, Stine Frey","orcid":"0000-0002-7879-8660","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Marie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4557ab69-42a2-40e1-9c55-66bb9f9aad50","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"bahrndorffpau","last":"Bahrndorff","locid":"a270f01e-03d6-473b-8cd1-ab444b299416","name":"Bahrndorff, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-0838-4008","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Goutam","key":"sahanapau","last":"Sahana","locid":"bb375f9c-4103-4460-80cc-ec53d0cd03d5","name":"Sahana, Goutam","orcid":"0000-0001-7608-7577","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Nygård","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"48974411-cbd8-4785-8336-315ac8080f15","name":"Kristensen, Torsten Nygaard","name_org":"Kristensen, Torsten Nygård","orcid":"0000-0001-6204-8753","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura Skrubbeltrang","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5fd29cd8-360a-461a-b205-b81e0ac76c23","name":"Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang","orcid":"0000-0002-4270-6365","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1163/23524588-bja10247","issn":["23524588"],"journal":"Journal of Insects as Food and Feed","publisher":"Wageningen Academic Publishers","status":"e","title":"Journal of Insects as Food and Feed"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009830089"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["aau-17d066d9-df1e-4893-886b-8c0bca929c43","au-6b67d2e0-689c-410e-abf1-d2d078f0e760"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Multi-trait pedigree-based selective breeding to optimise farmed insects : Evidence from a house fly population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-813305","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To explore modifications of the 2021 European Resuscitation Council/European Society of Intensive Care Medicine (ERC/ESICM) guideline algorithm for neuroprognostication after cardiac arrest to improve its prognostic accuracy. Methods: Post-hoc analysis of four prospective multicentre studies (TTM, TTM2, KORHN and ProNeCA). We raised the Glasgow Coma Scale motor (GCS-M) inclusion threshold at 72 h after cardiac arrest from the current GCS-M < 4 to GCS-M < 6 (all unconscious patients). Secondly, we included good outcome predictors (GCS-M 4–5, neuron-specific enolase < 17 µg/L, benign electroencephalography patterns ≤ 72 h post-arrest and normal magnetic resonance imaging at 72–168 h post-arrest) in the algorithm. Functional outcome was assessed dichotomously at six months, including modified Rankin Scale 0–3, Cerebral Performance Category 1–2 or Glasgow Outcome Scale 4–5 (no symptoms to moderate disability) as good outcome. Results: We analysed 3,388 patients, of whom 2,079 had GCS-M < 4 at ≥ 72 h. Of the 874 patients identified by the 2021 ERC/ESICM poor outcome criteria, 870 had poor functional outcome (specificity: 99.6% [95%CI 99.0–99.9]). Using the GCS-M < 6 threshold, 366 more patients entered the algorithm (N = 2,445). Seven more patients with poor outcomes were identified, with close to identical specificity. Good outcome predictors thereafter identified 673 patients with potential recovery, of whom 411 (61%) had a good functional outcome at six months. With the updated algorithm, the number of prognosticated patients with an indeterminate prognosis decreased from 1,205/2,079 (58%) to 891/2,445 (36%). Conclusion: Raising the GCS-M inclusion threshold and adding favourable predictors to the 2021 ERC/ESICM prognostication algorithm reduced prognostic uncertainty without increasing falsely pessimistic predictions.","author_count":42,"contributors":["Lagebrant, Alice","Sandroni, Claudio","Nolan, Jerry P.","Bělohlávek, Jan","Cariou, Alain","Carrai, Riccardo","Dankiewicz, Josef","Grejs, Anders Morten","Grippo, Antonello","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Haenggi, Matthias","Jakobsen, Janus C.","Keeble, Thomas R.","Kirkegaard, Hans","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael A.","Lee, Byung Kook","Lee, Dong Hun","Levin, Helena","Lilja, Gisela","Lundin, Andreas","Nielsen, Niklas","Oh, Sang Hoon","Park, Kyu Nam","Pellis, Tommaso","Robba, Chiara","Rylander, Christian","Ryu, Seok Jin","Saxena, Manoxj","Scarpino, Maenia","Schrag, Claudia","Stammet, Pascal","Storm, Christian","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Thomas, Matthew","Westhall, Erik","Wise, Matt P.","Youn, Chun Song","Young, Paul","Cronberg, Tobias","Moseby-Knappe, Marion"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-813800"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, Central","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lagebrant, Alice"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Cuba","Czechia","France","Germany","Italy","Luxembourg","Netherlands","New Zealand","Poland","Slovakia","South Korea","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","ARU School of Medicine & MTRC","All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Anglia Ruskin University","Azienda Ospedaliera Careggi","Cantonal Hospital St. Gallen","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Cardiff University","Careggi University Hospital","Catholic University in Ruzomberok","Catholic University of Korea","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Centre Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Charles University","Chonnam National University","Chonnam National University Hospital","Chonnam National University Medical School","ETH Zürich","Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli IRCCS","Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Gemelli","Free University of Brussels","General Teaching Hospital","Graduate School of Health Economics and Management","Helsingborg Hospital","Hospital Cochin","Hôpital Universitaire de Bruxelles","Hôpital Universitaire de Bruxelles (HUB)","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST","IRCCS Ospedale Policlinico San Martino","Kantonsspital St. Gallen","Kantonsspital St. Gallen, St. Gallen, Switzerland.","Lund University","MSE Trust","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Mid and South Essex NHS Foundation Trust","Monash University","Ospedale Santa Maria degli Angeli Pordenone","Paris-Cité University","Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli","Pordenone Hospital","Royal United Hospital Bath NHS Trust","Royal United Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Royal United Hospitals Bath NHS Foundation Trust","San Martino Hospital Genoa","Skåne University Hospital","St. George Hospital","The Catholic University of Korea Seoul St. Mary's Hospital","The George Institute for Global Health","The St George Hospital","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital Zurich","University Hospital Zürich","University Hospital of Wales","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospitals Brussels (UZB)","University of Amsterdam","University of Genoa","University of Gothenburg","University of Luxembourg","University of Melbourne","University of Warwick","Université Libre de Bruxelles","Uppsala University","Wellington Hospital","Wroclaw Medical University","Wrocław Medical University"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Functional outcome","Good Outcome Prediction","Indeterminate Prognosis","Neurological Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediction of good functional outcome decreases diagnostic uncertainty in unconscious survivors after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2025.110686","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-813800","identifier":[{"id":"40533052","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105009304366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c12ee8d1-87f8-497d-91fa-f802144a0418","ku-8c095f8d-600b-417d-b491-b653312dbd52","sdu-424ab98b-4262-4d34-9242-b367473649ff"],"keyword":["Cardiac Arrest","Functional Outcome","Good Outcome Prediction","Indeterminate Prognosis","Neurological Prognostication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5CDB00571186C053E4366886C82CCAEA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2025.110686","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456080702/1-s2.0-S0300957225001984-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/292917922/Prediction_of_good_functional_outcome_decreases_diagnostic_uncertainty_in_unconscious_survivors_after_out-of-hospital_cardiac_arrest.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"fondazione policlinico universitario agostino gemelli irccs","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli IRCCS","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"sk","key":