inty in unconscious survivors after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-813800","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Remote ischemic conditioning (RIC) is a simple and low-cost intervention that is thought to increase collateral blood flow through the vasodilatory effects of nitric oxide (NO) produced by the endothelium and red blood cells (RBCs). This study aims to investigate whether RIC affects RBC deformability and levels of NO and nitrite in patients with ischemic stroke. METHODS: This is a predefined substudy to the RESIST (Remote Ischemic Conditioning in Patients With Acute Stroke Trial) randomized clinical trial conducted in Denmark. RIC was started in the ambulance and continued at the hospital for seven days. Blood samples were collected at different time points: prehospital in the ambulance, in-hospital upon arrival, 2 hours postadmission, and 24 hours postadmission. RBC deformability and erythrocyte aggregation rate were assessed using ektacytometry, NO using flowcytometry, and nitrite content using ozone chemiluminescence. RESULTS: Of 1500 prehospital randomized patients, 486 patients were included in this study between July 28, 2020, and November 11, 2023, and had blood samples taken. Of these, 249 (51%) had AIS, and here RIC treatment was not associated with increased RBC maximal deformability (RIC, 0.549; sham, 0.548; P=0.31), RBC NO (RIC, 35 301 median fluorescence intensity; sham, 34979 median fluorescence intensity; P=0.89), or nitrite (RIC, 0.036 µmol/L; sham, 0.034 µmol/L; P=0.38), but RIC treatment was associated with a significantly reduced aggregation pressure and a slower erythrocyte aggregation rate (RIC, 323.76 millipascal; sham, 352.74 millipascal; P=0.0113). CONCLUSIONS: Prehospital and in-hospital RIC significantly reduced erythrocyte aggregation rate in patients with acute ischemic stroke, while there was no change in RBC deformability, NO content, or whole blood nitrite levels.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Blauenfeldt, Rolf Ankerlund","Waller, Jennifer","Drasbek, Kim Ryun","Bech, Jesper N.","Hvas, Anne-Mette","Larsen, Julie Brogaard","Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","Nielsen, Marlene Christina","Kjølhede, Maria","Kjeldsen, Mathilde","Gude, Martin Faurholdt","Khan, Mohammad Badruzzaman","Baban, Babak","Andersen, Grethe","Hess, David Charles"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-795984"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Blauenfeldt, Rolf Ankerlund"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Augusta University"],"keyword":["Erythrocytes","Ischemic stroke","Nitric oxide","Nitrites"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of remote ischemic conditioning on the form and function of red blood cells in patients with acute ischemic stroke","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85216954742","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-795984","identifier":[{"id":"85216954742","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39882626","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11850200","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-3c472d57-0708-40c7-bc75-39e781b1f9e7"],"keyword":["erythrocytes","ischemic stroke","nitric oxide","nitrites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9801DE675D8DECE19D307D2033AF577D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"augusta university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Augusta University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rolf Ankerlund","key":"blauenfeldtrolfankerlundpau","last":"Blauenfeldt","locid":"2cc4cfa1-de55-413c-b008-6b5d1c275888","name":"Blauenfeldt, Rolf Ankerlund","orcid":"0000-0002-4846-9516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer","key":"wallerjenniferpau","last":"Waller","name":"Waller, Jennifer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Ryun","key":"drasbekkimryunpau","last":"Drasbek","locid":"de170443-bbbb-46ff-ad6c-077e42b64468","name":"Drasbek, Kim Ryun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Nørgaard","key":"bechjespernpau","last":"Bech","locid":"ada3ab11-5e6a-4f8c-8c03-c9e09fcb18be","name":"Bech, Jesper N.","name_org":"Bech, Jesper Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0605-1277","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Mette","key":"hvasannemettepau","last":"Hvas","locid":"b4362b49-6deb-4c2c-9027-48dc6cdbd5e6","name":"Hvas, Anne-Mette","name_org":"Hvas, Anne Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie Brogaard","key":"larsenjuliebrogaardpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fee13d4e-8051-4767-8da1-6590b1dd7022","name":"Larsen, Julie Brogaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2978-5185","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Nørgaard","key":"andersenmortennørgaardpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5820fa2e-0f0e-4429-badc-9e264f102231","name":"Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0820-7789","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marlene Christina","key":"nielsenmarlenechristinapau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2ab8f88c-9bf7-4e6f-9b37-10090f38fff5","name":"Nielsen, Marlene Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"kjølhedemariapau","last":"Kjølhede","name":"Kjølhede, Maria","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde","key":"kjeldsenmathildepau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Mathilde","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Faurholdt","key":"gudemartinfaurholdtpau","last":"Gude","locid":"433e9619-b61e-4860-ad8d-c816e4db4eed","name":"Gude, Martin Faurholdt","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Badruzzaman","key":"khanmohammadbadruzzamanpau","last":"Khan","name":"Khan, Mohammad Badruzzaman","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Babak","key":"babanbabakpau","last":"Baban","name":"Baban, Babak","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Grethe","key":"andersengrethepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"97e157c9-4cb4-4690-a971-06e4699b50fe","name":"Andersen, Grethe","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-2500","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David Charles","key":"hessdavidcharlespau","last":"Hess","name":"Hess, David Charles","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39882626"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/strokeaha.124.048976","issn":["00392499","15244628"],"issn_org":["00392499"],"issue":"3","journal":"Stroke","pages":"603-612","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Stroke","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216954742"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3c472d57-0708-40c7-bc75-39e781b1f9e7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of Remote Ischemic Conditioning on the Form and Function of Red Blood Cells in Patients with Acute Ischemic Stroke","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-795984","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"AIM: This study examines trends in paracetamol overdoses among Danish adolescents during and following the COVID-19 pandemic. METHODS: A retrospective observational study was conducted using data from the national databases, covering all paediatric departments in Denmark from January 2016 to December 2023. Patients between 10 and 19 years of age diagnosed with paracetamol overdose were stratified by sex, age and number of hospital admissions. As the dataset covers the entire population, observed values reflect true parameters. A one-sample t-test compared post-COVID-19 values to the pre-COVID-19 mean. RESULTS: A total of 4.448 patients accounted for 5.794 hospital admissions due to paracetamol overdoses, with a majority being girls. During the second year of the pandemic (2021), a rise in overdose cases (26.5%) and hospital admissions (30.3%) was observed, especially among girls. The average number of admissions per patient increased, indicating repeated self-harm attempts. Cases of severe overdoses leading to acute liver failure increased at Rigshospitalet. These trends reversed post-pandemic. CONCLUSION: The findings suggest an association between pandemic-related isolation and an increase in adolescent paracetamol overdoses. While rates began to normalise after restrictions were lifted, further research is needed to assess the long-term mental health impact of such restrictions.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Kempf, Oliver Nørholm","Helt, Thora Wesenberg","Herrche-Petersen, Jens Jakob","Søndergaard, Charlotte","Longin, Elke","Ellerman, Annie","Frederiksen, Marianne Sjølin","Lundby-Christensen, Louise","Andersen, Jesper","Petersen, Thomas Houmann","Nielsen, Rasmus G.","Nielsen, Bent Windelborg","Trier, Cæcilie","Jürgensen, Louise","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Reynskor, Magnus Ove","Kvistgaard, Helene","Boas, Malene","Jeppesen, Eva Mosfeldt","Christensen, Vibeke Brix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805168"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kempf, Oliver Nørholm"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paracetamol overdoses among danish adolescents a covid 000000000019 perspective","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.70037","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-805168","identifier":[{"id":"39968885","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85219668959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7bd0dea7-847e-4102-98c4-f59a6bd21503"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-38943F00CF62526B653688DC67503462"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.70037","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"D