{"abstract":"Objectives Approximately half of individuals with suspected PMR initiate prednisolone before rheumatological evaluation, but it is unknown if prednisolone reduces the ability to diagnose PMR. This study evaluated the clinical assessment of a PMR diagnosis before and after prednisolone initiation and after short-term prednisolone discontinuation. Methods Data from a prospective cohort of treatment-naïve patients with PMR (n = 66) and non-PMR (n = 27) were used to create case report forms (CRFs). All patients were assessed at baseline and patients with PMR were reassessed after 8 weeks of prednisolone treatment (n = 57) and after short-term prednisolone discontinuation at week 10 (n = 48). In total, 198 CRFs were created containing patient demographics, current symptoms, physical examination and blood test results. Six rheumatologists, blinded to diagnosis, prednisolone treatment and visit timing, assessed each CRF, rating the probability of a PMR diagnosis from 0 to 10 and classifying them as PMR or non-PMR. Results At baseline, CRF assessors effectively distinguished PMR from non-PMR, demonstrating median probabilities of PMR of 7.8 and 2.8, respectively, and a sensitivity/specificity of 85.9%/82.7% for the PMR diagnosis. After prednisolone initiation, the median probability of PMR was 1.0 and sensitivity was 3.5%, followed by a median probability of PMR of 2.3 and a sensitivity of 25% after short-term prednisolone discontinuation. Conclusion This study shows that clinically assessing PMR becomes challenging after prednisolone initiation, and that short-term prednisolone discontinuation does not improve clinical assessment to pre-treatment levels. Consequently, the study supports recommendations of deferring prednisolone initiation until after specialist evaluation in individuals suspected of having PMR.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Våben, Christoffer","Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","Nielsen, Marc K","Moll, Line Thorndal","Mørk, Christoffer","Dalgaard, Emil Barner","Rasmussen, Tue Kruse","Østgård, René Drage","Hansen, Ib Tønder","Nielsen, Berit Dalsgaard","Sørensen, Christian Møbjerg","Blegvad-Nissen, Jesper","Kjær, Søren Geill","Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","Keller, Kresten Krarup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807061"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diagnostic accuracy","Glucocorticoids","Polymyalgia rheumatica","Prednisolone"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of prednisolone initiation and short term discontinuation on the clinical assessment of polymyalgia rheumatica","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105012482538","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807061","identifier":[{"id":"105012482538","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40131424","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-981cf1b1-8fe3-4a18-936b-740fb4fd02e9"],"keyword":["diagnostic accuracy","diagnostic taper","glucocorticoids","polymyalgia rheumatica","prednisolone"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-60F894F202579D199090F3B9DE24988D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Section for Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer S","key":"våbenchristofferpau","last":"Våben","locid":"d0eeb26e-f0e5-4c8c-ae7c-b0d846bc03ec","name":"Våben, Christoffer","name_org":"Våben, Christoffer S","orcid":"0000-0003-2704-4081","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas W","key":"nielsenandreaswiggerspau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dc3ce48a-c47a-46ef-beac-360aec95aacc","name":"Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","name_org":"Nielsen, Andreas W","orcid":"0000-0001-8180-6871","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc K","key":"nielsenmarckpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Marc K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line T","key":"molllinethorndalpau","last":"Moll","locid":"1ef45a8e-4b1c-4271-9c6e-5ea93e0f8ac8","name":"Moll, Line Thorndal","name_org":"Moll, Line T","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"mørkchristofferpau","last":"Mørk","name":"Mørk, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil B","key":"dalgaardemilbarnerpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"d433cfa3-ddda-4ee0-b783-82d95b62029f","name":"Dalgaard, Emil Barner","name_org":"Dalgaard, Emil B","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tue K","key":"rasmussentuekrusepau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0b1018e8-2ad6-4f8d-8413-5c10a8db586d","name":"Rasmussen, Tue Kruse","name_org":"Rasmussen, Tue K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René D","key":"østgårdrenédragepau","last":"Østgård","locid":"55d0f083-27c9-4d6b-95d4-92ec4d785e87","name":"Østgård, René Drage","name_org":"Østgård, René D","orcid":"0000-0001-6124-8972","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib T","key":"hansenibtønderpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"81d0b2cc-7b1e-46a1-a233-5ac2e412721b","name":"Hansen, Ib Tønder","name_org":"Hansen, Ib T","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Berit D","key":"nielsenberitdalsgaardpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d039e19c-8101-423b-a89a-414f0f95f793","name":"Nielsen, Berit Dalsgaard","name_org":"Nielsen, Berit D","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian M","key":"sørensenchristianmøbjergpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5b9d2f3e-1fac-4e1c-a295-2d5bddba8362","name":"Sørensen, Christian Møbjerg","name_org":"Sørensen, Christian M","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"blegvadnissenjesperpau","last":"Blegvad-Nissen","locid":"8b75f4b8-75e5-48e7-bf81-e65a57a2160d","name":"Blegvad-Nissen, Jesper","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren G","key":"kjærsørengeillpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"5076f30c-8b9f-4765-b494-a263c944e96b","name":"Kjær, Søren Geill","name_org":"Kjær, Søren G","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen-Margrethe","key":"haugeellenmargrethepau","last":"Hauge","locid":"6e0e979f-48d6-40bd-89ec-a2502b1cefd4","name":"Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","name_org":"Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kresten K","key":"kellerkrestenkraruppau","last":"Keller","locid":"a13c7405-9555-41cf-9bc3-311bb925bb9c","name":"Keller, Kresten Krarup","name_org":"Keller, Kresten K","orcid":"0000-0003-2474-3389","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40131424"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/rheumatology/keaf170","issn":["14620324","14620332"],"issn_org":["14620324"],"issue":"8","journal":"Rheumatology","pages":"4756-4760","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Rheumatology","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012482538"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-981cf1b1-8fe3-4a18-936b-740fb4fd02e9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effect of prednisolone initiation and short-term discontinuation on the clinical assessment of polymyalgia rheumatica","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807061","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Encouraging walking is essential for creating healthy and liveable cities. While research shows that walking environments influence walking frequency, less is known about how the built environment influences the emotional experience of walking. The circumplex model of affect (CM) is a well-established psychological framework for structuring emotions but has been applied in few studies of the built environment. This study applies the CM as a framework to understand how urban walking environments influence emotions. Methods: An expert panel evaluated ten videos of walking environments based on urban indicators. The same environments were rated by participants of an online survey (N = 311) in terms of pleasantness, excitement, stress, and complexity. Principal component analysis combined these variables into valence and activation, the two dimensions of the CM. According to valence and activation levels, we identified participants' emotional states (stressed, bored, excited, relaxed) for the walking environments. We estimated mixed logit models to investigate how the emotional states change with different urban features. Results: Urban features were significantly related to the identified emotions: mixed-use streets with varied facades and pedestrian spaces evoke excitement, modern residential streets with greenery and reduced traffic promote relaxation, monotonous streets with closed facades and traffic cause boredom, and streets with underpasses, high traffic, poor accessibility or litter cause stress. Improving features such as facades and urban surroundings most significantly increase the likelihood of feeling excited. Conclusions: Our findings highlight the importance of urban design features that encourage engagement with the environment and create exciting and relaxing experiences. By showing how features such as varied facades, greenery and pedestrianisation evoke positive emotions, this study highlights the critical role of well-designed urban environments in shaping emotional experiences. For future research, the application of CM to the built environment provides a systematic way of analysing pedestrians' emotions and well-being.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Brunner, Lisa Marie","Başaran, Gülin Göksu","Haustein, Sonja","Klöckner, Christian A.","Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker","Hillnhütter, Helge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808386"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Brunner, Lisa Marie"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"emotional experiences of urban walking environments an application of the circumplex model of affect","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jth.2025.102008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808386","identifier":[{"id":"85219560587","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-42e49787-626e-4a83-bba9-2022d6e2f26b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5F8B4E91BC7E089C595ADA6309F038E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/394828926/1-s2.0-S2214140525000283-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jth.2025.102008","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science, Transportation Systems Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa Marie","key":"brunnerpau","last":"Brunner","name":"Brunner, Lisa Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gülin Göksu","key":"başaranpau","last":"Başaran","locid":"bbde6a42-a32a-403c-a9d4-e739aec4d6a3","name":"Başaran, Gülin Göksu","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-5715","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sonja","key":"hausteinpau","last":"Haustein","locid":"5888f456-a8b8-4d2e-b759-47c34d58c68c","name":"Haustein, Sonja","orcid":"0000-0001-5219-0115","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian A.","key":"klöcknerpau","last":"Klöckner","name":"Klöckner, Christian A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"hillnhütterpau","last":"Hillnhütter","name":"Hillnhütter, Helge","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jth.2025.102008","issn":["22141405","22141413"],"issn_org":["22141405"],"journal":"Journal of Transport & Health","paperid":"102008","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Transport & Health","title_org":"Journal of Transport and Health","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219560587"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-42e49787-626e-4a83-bba9-2022d6e2f26b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Emotional experiences of urban walking environments : an application of the circumplex model of affect","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808386","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Acanthamoeba keratitis (AK) is a severe corneal infection with potential detrimental effects on visual outcome and quality of life, primarily affecting young contact lens wearers. We report Acanthamoeba genotypes, subtypes and clinical outcome from Danish patients with AK. METHODS: Thirty-nine PCR-positive AK cases diagnosed and treated at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, from 2002 to 2022 were included. Corneal samples underwent next-generation sequencing (NGS) for Acanthamoeba genotyping. These data were compared with clinical data and results from PCR. RESULTS: Acanthamoeba T4 was the most frequent genotype (n = 35), with four subtypes identified (T4A, T4B, T4D and T4G); three cases of the T3 genotype were observed. Three samples showed evidence of two distinct Acanthamoeba sequences. The median patient age was 35 years, genders were equally represented and the median time from symptom onset to diagnosis was 26 days. Ninety per cent had identifiable risk factors in addition to contact lens wear. Corticosteroid treatment prior to AK diagnosis, moderate-to-severe pain, male gender, older age, ring infiltration and infiltrate size >3 mm were associated with poor visual outcome. No significant correlation was found between Acanthamoeba genotype or subtype and clinical outcomes. CONCLUSION: We reveal the genetic diversity of Acanthamoeba involved in AK in Denmark. However, genotype or subtype did not predict clinical outcome. Further research is needed to clarify the role of specific genotypes and subtypes in disease progression and treatment response.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skovdal, Sandra Maria","Stensvold, Christen Rune","Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","Nielsen, Stine Elkjær","Hjortdal, Jesper","Ivarsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816230"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acanthamoeba Keratitis","Clinical microbiology","Genetic diversity","Molecular epidemiology","Next generation sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic diversity of acanthamoeba and clinical outcome predictors in danish patients with acanthamoeba keratitis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.17527","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816230","identifier":[{"id":"105005601212","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40387241","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-942e15b4-1bfd-4e39-9361-f6de0b0a7859"],"keyword":["Acanthamoeba keratitis","clinical microbiology","contact lens wear","genetic diversity","infectious keratitis","molecular epidemiology","next-generation sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EA91F505688C522540BC1A1CE2F9EEBA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.17527","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra M","key":"skovdalsandramariapau","last":"Skovdal","locid":"8e6b7c72-2732-402b-940c-ca02967599bd","name":"Skovdal, Sandra Maria","name_org":"Skovdal, Sandra M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christen Rune","key":"stensvoldchristenrunepau","last":"Stensvold","name":"Stensvold, Christen Rune","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Vedel","key":"nielsenhenrikvedelpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Elkjær","key":"nielsenstineelkjærpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Stine Elkjær","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdaljesperpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"ivarsenanderspau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"072c0ad1-1c62-4539-8b63-868ff8422866","name":"Ivarsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1466-4804","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40387241"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.17527","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"e","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005601212"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["au-942e15b4-1bfd-4e39-9361-f6de0b0a7859"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Genetic diversity of Acanthamoeba and clinical outcome predictors in Danish patients with Acanthamoeba keratitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816230","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We study blockchain-based provably anonymous payment systems between light clients. Such clients interact with the blockchain through full nodes, which can see what the light clients read and write. The goal of our work is to enable light clients to perform anonymous payments, while maintaining privacy even against the full nodes through which they interact with the blockchain. We formalize the problem in the UC model and present a provably secure solution. We show that a varia-tion of tree ORAM gives obliviousness even when an adversary can follow how its own data elements move in the tree. We use this for anonymity via shuffling of payments on the blockchain, while at the same time allowing the light client to know a few positions among which to find its payment without knowing the current state of the blockchain. In comparison to existing works, we are the first ones that simultaneously provide strong anonymity guarantees, provable security, and anonymity with respect to full nodes. Along the way, we make several contributions that may be of independent interest. We define and construct anonymous-coin friendly encryption schemes and show how they can be used within anonymous payment systems. We define and construct efficient compressible random-ness beacons, which produce unpredictable values in regular intervals and allow for storing all published values in a short digest.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Blatchley Hansen, Adam","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Simkin, Mark"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816764"],"event":{"end":"2025-05-15","place":"Røros, no","start":"2025-05-12","title":"28th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public Key Cryptography, PKC 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Flashbots"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ocash fully anonymous payments between blockchain light clients","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105005936130","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816764","identifier":[{"id":"105005936130","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-da776398-51b8-483a-b490-7d04f6ebe6b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6CF9375BF7E05485F5565081C0D84BA9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Flashbots"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Adam Blatchley","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d0a5a0c7-21aa-4e62-bf5c-2014d56e32c7","name":"Blatchley Hansen, Adam","name_org":"Hansen, Adam Blatchley","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"simkinpau","last":"Simkin","name":"Simkin, Mark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tibor","key":"jagerpedh","last":"Jager","name":"Jager, Tibor","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jiaxin","key":"panpedh","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Jiaxin","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-91832-2_6","isbn":["9783031918315"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"169-202","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Public-Key Cryptography – PKC 2025 - 28th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public-Key Cryptography, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005936130"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-da776398-51b8-483a-b490-7d04f6ebe6b5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"OCash : Fully Anonymous Payments Between Blockchain Light Clients","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816764","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"A central challenge in movement neuroscience is developing methods for non-invasive spatiotemporal imaging of brain activity during natural, whole-body movement. We test the utility of a new brain imaging modality, optically pumped magnetoencephalography (OP-MEG), as an instrument to study the spatiotemporal dynamics of human walking. Specifically, we ask whether known physiological signals can be recovered during discrete steps involving large-scale, whole-body translation. Our findings show that by using OP-MEG, we can image the brain during large-scale, natural movements. We provide proof-of-principle evidence for movement-related changes in beta band activity during stepping vs. standing, which are source-localized to the sensorimotor cortex. This work supports the significant potential of the OP-MEG modality for addressing fundamental questions in human gait research relevant to both the physiological and pathological mechanisms of walking.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Spedden, Meaghan E.","O’Neill, George C.","West, Timothy O.","Tierney, Tim M.","Mellor, Stephanie","Alexander, Nicholas A.","Seymour, Robert","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Farmer, Simon F.","Bestmann, Sven","Barnes, Gareth R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819356"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Balgrist University Hospital","Hospital Los Madroños","Imperial College London","University College London","University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","University of Oxford","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["Naturalistic neuroimaging","Sensorimotor control"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using wearable meg to study the neural control of human stepping","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s25134160","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819356","identifier":[{"id":"105010323614","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12252452","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"001527558100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"40648415","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-71f70d11-e6eb-4ac9-a7f6-601b480f66d8"],"keyword":["OP-MEG","naturalistic neuroimaging","sensorimotor control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-55F5EC24330768A561463293AE85DC67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/457506714/sensors-25-04160.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s25134160","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"balgrist university hospital","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Balgrist University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university college london hospitals nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"es","key":"hospital los madroños","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Los Madroños","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Meaghan E.","key":"speddenpau","last":"Spedden","name":"Spedden, Meaghan E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"George C.","key":"oneillpau","last":"O’Neill","name":"O’Neill, George C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Timothy O.","key":"westpau","last":"West","name":"West, Timothy O.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tim M.","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Tim M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","first":"Stephanie","key":"mellorpau","last":"Mellor","name":"Mellor, Stephanie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicholas A.","key":"alexanderpau","last":"Alexander","name":"Alexander, Nicholas A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Robert","key":"seymourpau","last":"Seymour","name":"Seymour, Robert","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Simon F.","key":"farmerpau","last":"Farmer","name":"Farmer, Simon F.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8","first":"Sven","key":"bestmannpau","last":"Bestmann","name":"Bestmann, Sven","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gareth R.","key":"barnespau","last":"Barnes","name":"Barnes, Gareth R.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40648415"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/s25134160","issn":["14248220","14248239"],"issn_org":["14243210"],"issue":"13","journal":"Sensors","paperid":"4160","status":"p","title":"Sensors","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010323614"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-71f70d11-e6eb-4ac9-a7f6-601b480f66d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Wearable MEG to Study the Neural Control of Human Stepping","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819356","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Tumor necrosis factor (TNF) is highly upregulated after ischemic stroke and plays a crucial role in shaping the neuroinflammatory response that follows. Therapies aimed at inhibiting detrimental soluble (sol)TNF-TNF receptor 1 (TNFR1) signaling are gaining interest as new treatment options for neuroinflammatory conditions. We previously demonstrated that XPro1595, a selective solTNF inhibitor, decreased inflammation and improved functional outcome in the acute phase of experimental stroke. Here, we extended these studies by investigating the effects of solTNF inhibition on inflammation, functional outcome, and cognitive impairments in the subacute phases after stroke onset. We observed that in mice treated with XPro1595, glial cell responses were altered 7 and 14 days after experimental stroke, with changes in microglial morphology, as well as astrocyte and oligodendrocyte cell populations, pointing to altered reactive states. While the number of pre-myelinating oligodendrocytes was decreased in the ipsilateral cortex, XPro1595 upregulated oligodendrocyte lipid levels and improved myelin integrity. Similarly, the number of astrocytes in the ipsilateral cortex was decreased with XPro1595 treatment, followed by changes to their lipid profile. Moreover, the treatment led to a decrease in systemic immune cell numbers, indicative of a dampened peripheral inflammatory response. These changes were followed by increased hippocampal pro-brain-derived neurotrophic factor levels and an improvement in cognitive function, seen as better recognition memory, as well as improved motor asymmetry. In conclusion, these findings support a long-term protective effect of inhibiting solTNF in experimental ischemic stroke.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Pedersen, Estrid Thougaard","Nielsen, Pernille Vinther","Raffaele, Stefano","Nielsen, Ann-Sofie Nyboe","Larsen, Lea Lydolph","Corradini, Silvia","Havelund, Jesper F","Becirovic, Lejla Vahl","Bowman, Elisabeth Margriet","Fumagalli, Marta","Færgeman, Nils J.","Brambilla, Roberta","Clausen, Bettina Hjelm","Wlodarczyk, Agnieszka","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821014"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lambertsen, Kate Lykke"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Miami","University of Milan"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GUB"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-PR-GUB","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systemic inhibition of soluble tnf significantly changes glial cell populations leading to improved myelin integrity and better functional outcome after experimental stroke","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopha.2025.118334","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-821014","identifier":[{"id":"105010024134","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40645014","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-1111f7fd-8aef-4880-9e4a-65d6d1438f90"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4B05CD2C8982389DB6C714F4980BD713"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopha.2025.118334","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/293095216/1-s2.0-S0753332225005281-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"gubra","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GUB","l3nl":"Gubra","l3nn":"Gubra","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Gubra","namevar":["Gubra"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GUB","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of miami","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Miami","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Estrid Thougaard","key":"pedersenestridthougaardpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d68bc422-5767-457d-8f5e-936d7ecefa88","name":"Pedersen, Estrid Thougaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4270-3535","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Vinther","key":"nielsenpernillevintherpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"197f08b3-ec1b-47c3-9de7-e43cf6d6206b","name":"Nielsen, Pernille Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-1996-063X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefano","key":"raffaelestefanopau","last":"Raffaele","name":"Raffaele, Stefano","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corres