R/EULAR Classification Criteria","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.31-804018","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Økonomiske teorier udfolder sig ikke isoleret fra deres hi­storiske kontekst, men er ofte en reaktion på presserende udfordringer i deres samtid. De reflekterer nye strømnin­ger i et foranderligt samfund og vil typisk afspejle nye po­litiske udfordringer, f.eks. arbejdsløshed, inflation, ulig­hed og klimaforandringer. Disse udfordringer kalder på udvikling af de eksisterende teorier i en proces, hvori der kan forekomme en betydelig uenighed blandt deltagerne. Tilgangen i DEN ØKONOMISKE TEORIS HISTORIE er derfor først og fremmest pluralistisk, idet de forskellige økonomiske teorier så vidt muligt beskrives på egne præ­misser, og diverse stridigheder mellem økonomer frem­stilles med respekt for forskellighed i deres samtid. Spørgsmålet om videnskabelighed betragtes heller ikke som givet. Der eksisterer konkurrerende perspektiver på, hvad der kendetegner videnskabelighed, og disse er i høj grad på spil i spændingsfelterne mellem forskellige øko­nomiske teorier. Bogen giver dermed en bred og nuanceret fremstilling af økonomiske teorier før og nu med det formål, at læseren kan orientere sig og vurdere dem i lyset af den historiske kontekst. JESPER JESPERSEN er ph.d., dr.scient.adm. og professor(em.) i samfundsøkonomi ved Roskilde Universitet. PETER NIELSEN er ph.d. og lektor i politisk økonomi ved Roskilde Universitet. RUNE MØLLER STAHL er ph.d. og adjunkt i politisk øko­nomi ved Copenhagen Business School.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jespersen, Jesper","Nielsen, Peter","Stahl, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S02-094.17-813885"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"den økonomiske teoris historie","src":["cbs","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://djoefforlag.dk/products/den-okonomiske-teoris-historie-2?variant=54350488174917","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.17-813885","ids":["cbs-ec3cabeb-8934-4e01-9e5d-5b0a62d4fb76","ruc-6318474f-ca44-489a-9329-839817cd287b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-FC800531FA9E579D9AD06732ADDB329A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business","Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business, Economic Policy, Institutions and Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper B.","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"32688fb3-c5d5-4cd1-a4aa-8c134535f417","name":"Jespersen, Jesper","name_org":"Jespersen, Jesper B.","orcid":"0000-0003-4973-2854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c51b09ae-d8f6-4af0-9ccd-df683fd46e3d","name":"Nielsen, Peter","orcid":"0009-0004-6566-1544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rune Møller","key":"stahlpau","last":"Stahl","locid":"254f80ac-8068-4bd4-884d-f48cc107f2b4","name":"Stahl, Rune Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-8235-8377","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"3","eisbn":["9788757464757"],"isbn":["9788757460759"],"pages":"242","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-ec3cabeb-8934-4e01-9e5d-5b0a62d4fb76","ruc-6318474f-ca44-489a-9329-839817cd287b"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Den økonomiske teoris historie","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.17-813885","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"How do differences in the constraints of a practiced motor task affect oscillatory functional connectivity between the motor cortex and muscle? Here, we investigate corticomuscular (CM) and intermuscular (IM) coherence during the hold-phase of a dynamic position control (PC) and isometric force control (FC) task. We also investigate the effects of PC motor practice requiring precise wrist flexions to designated target positions, and effects of FC motor practice involving isometric wrist flexions to designated target force levels or rest in a control group. In 46 young healthy adults (aged 20–30 yr), full-cap electroencephalography (EEG) and electromyography (EMG) were recorded from the flexor and extensor carpi radialis muscles during the tasks. Beta-band (15–35 Hz) CM and IM coherence were investigated as a task-related marker of oscillatory activity in the corticospinal system. At baseline, higher CM coupling was demonstrated during position control compared with force control. Following PC motor practice, CM b-band coherence increased (P ¼ 0.038), whereas it remained unchanged for participants who practiced FC or rested. This pattern was also found for IM coherence. The increased oscillatory synchronization following PC practice was driven by greater descending signaling (P ¼ 0.025). We speculate that the observed differences between position and force control relate to task differences in corticomuscular control-strategy and the influence of different sensory modalities during motor practice. We interpret the results as indicating increased coupling between the motor cortex and the motoneuron pool of the contracting muscle following dynamic motor practice emphasizing requirements for position control in motor learning. NEW & NOTEWORTHY We present the effects of different types of motor practice on functional connectivity in the corticomuscular system. We present differences in corticomuscular connectivity between tasks with position versus force control emphasis and evidence for increased functional and directed connectivity within the network specifically following position-control motor practice. These findings support using different control strategies based on task constraints and emphasize the importance of dynamic motor practice focused on position control for increasing coherence.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, August Lomholt","Stolpe, Malene Norup","Bjørndal, Jonas Rud","Wiegel, Patrick","Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-096.43-813965"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Corticomuscular coherence","Directionality","Intermuscular coherence","Motor learning","health nutrition and quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased functional and directed corticomuscular connectivity after dynamic motor practice but not isometric motor practice","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00061.2024","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["A.L.N. and J.L.-J. are supported by a grant from Team Danmark through the Novo Nordisk Foundation under Grant Number NNF.22SA0078293."],"id":"S02-096.43-813965","identifier":[{"id":"86000758140","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39951554","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["kp-338951ec-140c-4c6c-8cb0-6ba8f92f4079","ku-807e7c27-cd5d-47fd-91e8-a2dc7a690f78"],"keyword":["corticomuscular coherence","directionality","health, nutrition and quality of life","intermuscular coherence","motor control, motor learning","motor learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-164C9633726FA4ACF97F802124AC4706"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/437782331/nielsen-et-al-2025-increased-functional-and-directed-corticomuscular-connectivity-after-dynamic-motor-practice-but-not.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00061.2024","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Psykomotorikuddannelsen","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Børneliv - Sund tilknytning og aktiv livsstil for børn og unge"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"August Lomholt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"babf098d-97c8-434c-9345-40a30817d332","name":"Nielsen, August Lomholt","orcid":"0009-0008-0543-2220","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene","key":"noruppau","last":"Norup","locid":"62c7e795-b6ae-4246-96ba-48c2e3fdfd80","name":"Stolpe, Malene Norup","name_org":"Norup, Malene","orcid":"0000-0002-5150-9048","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Norup","key":"stolpepau","last":"Stolpe","locid":"0da93143-5e45-49b4-9b1f-86163381d0e9","name":"Stolpe, Malene Norup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Rud","key":"bjørndalpau","last":"Bjørndal","locid":"a08cffa6-ec3c-4626-bea4-09e99fa2cbc6","name":"Bjørndal, Jonas Rud","orcid":"0000-0003-0710-7129","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"wiegelpau","last":"Wiegel","locid":"b9f5e627-b733-4139-960d-6736db58523d","name":"Wiegel, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0001-5034-7174","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Meaghan Elizabeth","key":"speddenpau","last":"Spedden","locid":"e96259a8-d793-4586-903e-cbf824fa8021","name":"Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6854-2226","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39951554"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/jn.00061.2024","issn":["00223077","15221598"],"issn_org":["00223077"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Neurophysiology","pages":"930-943","publisher":"American Physiological Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neurophysiology","volume":"133"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000758140"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-338951ec-140c-4c6c-8cb0-6ba8f92f4079","ku-807e7c27-cd5d-47fd-91e8-a2dc7a690f78"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increased functional and directed corticomuscular connectivity after dynamic motor practice but not isometric motor practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.43-813965","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Insect production for food and feed presents a promising supplement to ensurefood safety and address the adverse impacts of agriculture on climate and environ-ment in the future. However, optimisation is required for insect production to realiseits full potential. This can be by targeted improvement of traits of interest throughselective breeding, an approach which has so far been underexplored and underu-tilised in insect farming. Here, we present a comprehensive review of the selectivebreeding framework in the context of insect production. We systematically evaluateadjustments of selective breeding techniques to the realm of insects and highlightthe essential components integral to the breeding process. The discussion coversevery step of a conventional breeding scheme, such as formulation of breeding objec-tives, phenotyping, estimation of genetic parameters and breeding values, selectionof appropriate breeding strategies, and mitigation of issues associated with geneticdiversity depletion and inbreeding. This review combines knowledge from diversedisciplines, bridging the gap between animal breeding, quantitative genetics, evolu-tionary biology and entomology, offering an integrated view of the insect breedingresearch area and uniting knowledge which has previously remained scattered acrossdiverse fields of expertise.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang","Laursen, Stine Frey","Bahrndorff, Simon","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Sahana, Goutam","Kristensen, Torsten Nygaard","Nielsen, Hanne Marie"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767021"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang"],"keyword":["Artificial selection","Breeding values","Domestication","G × E interactions","Genetic improvement","Genetic parameters","Insect breeding","Phenotyping","Review","breeding programme","production insects"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the unpaved road towards efficient selective breeding in insects for food and feed a review","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85208981226&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark (DFF\\u20100136\\u201000171B and DFF\\u20101127\\u201000081B) and the Novo Nordic Foundation (NNF21OC0070910)."],"id":"S02-100.00-767021","identifier":[{"id":"85208981226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c948fa65-7f87-4b08-ab44-7e783c248ba4","au-571fdbf3-3ca7-4260-bd8e-cf5099311fb6"],"keyword":["G × E interactions","artificial selection","breeding programme","breeding values","domestication","genetic improvement","genetic parameters","insect breeding","phenotyping","production insects","review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-55F98F74FA1D83FCB93F54A8AD7C1CCA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Genetics, Ecology and Evolution","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Functional Ecology and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura Skrubbeltrang","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5fd29cd8-360a-461a-b205-b81e0ac76c23","name":"Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang","orcid":"0000-0002-4270-6365","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Frey","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"1a898d84-89ba-4f9d-b176-c6658e075581","name":"Laursen, Stine Frey","orcid":"0000-0002-7879-8660","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"bahrndorffpau","last":"Bahrndorff","locid":"a270f01e-03d6-473b-8cd1-ab444b299416","name":"Bahrndorff, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-0838-4008","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Goutam","key":"sahanapau","last":"Sahana","locid":"bb375f9c-4103-4460-80cc-ec53d0cd03d5","name":"Sahana, Goutam","orcid":"0000-0001-7608-7577","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Nygaard","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"48974411-cbd8-4785-8336-315ac8080f15","name":"Kristensen, Torsten Nygaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6204-8753","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Marie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4557ab69-42a2-40e1-9c55-66bb9f9aad50","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Marie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/eea.13526","issn":["00138703","15707458"],"issn_org":["00138703"],"issue":"6","journal":"Entomologia Experimentalis et Applicata","pages":"498-521","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Entomologia Experimentalis et Applicata","volume":"173"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208981226"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c948fa65-7f87-4b08-ab44-7e783c248ba4","au-571fdbf3-3ca7-4260-bd8e-cf5099311fb6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The unpaved road towards efficient selective breeding in insects for food and feed—A review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767021","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present findings from a qualitative ethnographic study investigating the experiences and perceptions of general practitioners and other practice staff when introducing a new point of care diagnostic test technology (point of care polymerase chain reaction (POC PCR)) in general practice in Denmark. The ethnographic study was conducted in five general practice clinics, involving observations in four of the clinics and interviews with general practitioners and practice staff in all five clinics. Following an initial analytic phase in which barriers and facilitators in the implementation process of the Point-of-Care test were identified, we developed theoretically informed themes, drawing upon Hartmut Rosa’s social theory of technological acceleration. These themes included ambiguous experiences and perceptions of: (i) diagnostic specification and inflation embedded in diagnostic practices; (ii) empowerment and erosion of professional judgment; (iii) strategies of security and insecurity in communication; (iv) the interdependence between professional autonomy and economic structures associated with organizational power; and (v) subjective and organizational time. We discuss how diagnostic technologies simultaneously contribute to and disrupt treatment safety, efficiency, and medical decision-making. Using Rosa’s sociological concepts of alienation and resonance, this article furthermore explores how these ambiguous dynamics are experienced in general practice settings. It also examines the implications of navigating a heterogeneous socio-technical and medical landscape and what it means to be a health professional in a contemporary general practice environment that is increasingly shaped by diagnostic technologies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Simonsen, Line Maria","Eilerskov, Natasja","Andersen, Rikke Sand","Soendergaard, Jens","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Thilsing, Trine","Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767922"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Simonsen, Line Maria"],"keyword":["Patient physician relationship","Primary care","Technology in Healthcare","Theory","profession and professionalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing point of care pcr technology in general practice ambiguities experiences and perceptions among health care professionals","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85194967226","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-767922","identifier":[{"id":"38818659","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85194967226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-db769655-9d20-4ccb-8eea-cf8513b330ec","ruc-e5cfe034-2966-497a-927f-6ceaf9332909"],"keyword":["Patient-physician relationship","primary care","profession and professionalization","technology in healthcare","theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9B9323D8414B4E18ECCFE4FCFFE8A226"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Health and Society Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Maria","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Line Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Natasja","key":"eilerskovpau","last":"Eilerskov","locid":"ad341867-2ff2-417e-800c-c06aed6199b8","name":"Eilerskov, Natasja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Sand","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"616d8687-d6a1-4e6d-9886-8415286adaff","name":"Andersen, Rikke Sand","orcid":"0000-0003-2450-5866","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"soendergaardpau","last":"Soendergaard","name":"Soendergaard, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","name":"Thilsing, Trine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirubakaran","key":"balasubramaniampau","last":"Balasubramaniam","name":"Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"assinghvidtpau","last":"Assing Hvidt","name":"Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38818659"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/13634593241254988","issn":["13634593","14617196"],"issn_org":["13634593"],"issue":"3","journal":"Health","pages":"427-446","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Health","title_org":"Health (United Kingdom)","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194967226"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-db769655-9d20-4ccb-8eea-cf8513b330ec","ruc-e5cfe034-2966-497a-927f-6ceaf9332909"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Introducing Point-of-Care PCR technology in general practice : Ambiguities, experiences, and perceptions among health care professionals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767922","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: It has been hypothesized that 2-[18F]fluoro-2-deoxy-D-glucose ([18F]FDG) positron emission tomography (PET) computed tomography (CT) can distinguish polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR) from non-PMR patients based on the [18F]FDG-uptake patterns. Nevertheless, a comprehensive assessment of whole-body [18F]FDG-patterns across all uptaking musculoskeletal sites, as well as site-specific [18F]FDG-uptake patterns, has not been conducted. Therefore, this study aimed to investigate both the overall whole-body [18F]FDG-uptake patterns and the specific uptake patterns at individual sites in patients suspected of having PMR. Methods: Two distinct cohorts of patients with suspected PMR from Denmark and the Netherlands were prospectively included, encompassing 66/27 and 36/21 PMR/non-PMR patients, respectively. The cohorts consisted of treatment-naïve patients, who underwent pre-treatment [18F]FDG-PET/CT scans. The [18F]FDG-uptake was then assessed across 34 different anatomical sites. Furthermore, the site-specific [18F]FDG-uptake pattern within each anatomical site was categorized according to its shape. Results: Patients with PMR were more likely than non-PMR patients to have bilateral [18F]FDG-uptake equal to or above liver compared at the ischial tuberosities (91%/41%), shoulder joints (86%/45%), hip joints (83%/52%), and along the lumbar spinal processes (70%/30%). However, a subgroup analysis comparing non-PMR patients with other inflammatory conditions to patients with PMR revealed that several non-PMR patients exhibited a similar whole-body [18F]FDG-uptake pattern. Furthermore, site-specific [18F]FDG-uptake patterns were similar in patients with PMR and non-PMR. Conclusion: Assessing whole-body or site-specific [18F]FDG-uptake patterns does not improve the diagnostic accuracy in distinguishing PMR from other inflammatory diseases. Consequently, [18F]FDG-PET/CT should mainly be used to rule out a clinical diagnosis of PMR. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT04519580). Registered 17th of August 2020.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","van Praagh, Gijs D.","van der Geest, Kornelis S.M.","Hansen, Ib Tønder","Nielsen, Berit Dalsgaard","Kjær, Søren Geill","Blegvad-Nissen, Jesper","Rewers, Kate","Møller Sørensen, Christian","Brouwer, Elisabeth","Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","Gormsen, Lars Christian","Slart, Riemer H.J.A.","Keller, Kresten Krarup"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-804127"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Groningen","University of Groningen","University of Twente"],"keyword":["Diagnostic imaging","FDG PET CT","Pattern recognition","Polymyalgia rheumatica"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"whole body and site specific sup 000000000018 sup f fdg uptake patterns on pet ct have limited value in differentiating between polymyalgia rheumatica and other inflammatory diseases two cohorts of treatment naïve suspected polymyalgia rheumatica","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13550-025-01233-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-804127","identifier":[{"id":"40307615","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003882847","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12044134","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-89478a28-4041-4d54-87b4-8889fdfcb46a","sdu-bd28a449-cea3-4587-9624-a6ff04fc436c"],"keyword":["Diagnostic imaging","FDG-PET/CT","Pattern recognition","Polymyalgia rheumatica"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A36364D8A103D70D4D852F21BFDBE2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289726493/s13550-025-01233-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13550-025-01233-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Diagnostical Center, HEM","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Section for Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university medical center groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital","Regionshospitalet Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Departm