,"publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"EJNMMI Research","title_org":"EJNMMI research","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003882847"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-89478a28-4041-4d54-87b4-8889fdfcb46a","sdu-bd28a449-cea3-4587-9624-a6ff04fc436c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Whole-body and site specific [<sup>18</sup>F]FDG uptake patterns on PET/CT have limited value in differentiating between polymyalgia rheumatica and other inflammatory diseases : two cohorts of treatment-naïve suspected polymyalgia rheumatica","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-804127","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims To assess the reproducibility of interpreting hypoattenuated thickening (HAT) and peridevice leak (PDL) using cardiac computed tomography (CT) imaging following Watchman FLX left atrial appendage closure (LAAC) Methods In this multicentre retrospective reproducibility study, 100 anonymized post-LAAC cardiac CT scans were evaluated within and results the same cardiac phase by an experienced and a novice rater blinded to prior evaluations. All scans were evaluated twice by each rater, assessing overall HAT and PDL categories as well as specific associated findings based on suggested algorithms for post-LAAC interpretation. Inter- and intra-rater agreement and reliability were evaluated using absolute agreement, Cohen’s kappa, and Kendall’s tau for categorical variables, and mean difference, Bland–Altman plots, limits of agreement (lower and upper), and intra-class correlation coefficients (ICCs) for continuous variables. Within overall categories of both HAT and PDL, substantial agreement (kappa ≥0.61) and reliability (Kendall’s tau-b ≥ 0.75) were observed. Specifically, identifying high-grade HAT (kappa ≥0.78) and distal patency (kappa ≥0.85) displayed the highest agreement within HAT and PDL interpretation. Meanwhile, measuring the height of the proximal screw hub cove represented the least reliable HAT assessment among both inter- and intra-rater comparisons (ICC < 0.75), while suspected leak mechanism represented the least reproducible PDL measure Conclusion Despite only minimal training of one rater, overall high levels of inter- and intra-rater agreement and reliability were observed across the chosen algorithms for interpretation of HAT and PDL following Watchman FLX LAAC. The prognostic implications of the included variables are to be explored in future trials and registries.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kramer, Anders","Lo Russo, Gerardo","Alarouri, Hasan S","Collins, Jeremy D","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Alkhouli, Mohamad","Korsholm, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757681"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Korsholm, Kasper"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","University of Milan"],"keyword":["Cardiac computed tomography","Device related thrombosis","Left atrial appendage closure","Watchman FLX","peridevice leak"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reproducibility of cardiac computed tomography classifications of hypoattenuated thickening and peridevice leak following left atrial appendage closure","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85214318524","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-757681","identifier":[{"id":"85214318524","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39225186","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1addd0e4-6f09-4b54-9577-ffb6bb2a475d"],"keyword":["Watchman FLX","cardiac computed tomography","device-related thrombosis","left atrial appendage closure","peridevice leak"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28E72A47328EDBECD23B06EBF1429F4B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"mayo clinic rochester mn","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"kramerpau","last":"Kramer","locid":"be3123b5-5f55-4c8a-930c-f0f39cbc2981","name":"Kramer, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5546-8693","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerardo","key":"lorussopau","last":"Lo Russo","name":"Lo Russo, Gerardo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasan S","key":"alarouripau","last":"Alarouri","name":"Alarouri, Hasan S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeremy D","key":"collinspau","last":"Collins","name":"Collins, Jeremy D","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"møllerjensenpau","last":"Møller Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","name_org":"Møller Jensen, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohamad","key":"alkhoulipau","last":"Alkhouli","name":"Alkhouli, Mohamad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39225186"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/jeae236","issn":["15252167","15322114"],"issn_org":["15252167"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"62-71","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214318524"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1addd0e4-6f09-4b54-9577-ffb6bb2a475d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reproducibility of Cardiac Computed Tomography Classifications of Hypoattenuated Thickening and Peridevice Leak Following Left Atrial Appendage Closure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-757681","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Diabetes affects approximately 6% of the population, with 20% developing foot ulcers. Gout affects about 3% of the population, but <40% receive sufficient urate-lowering therapy to prevent or dissolve urate crystal (tophi) deposition in the feet, which can ulcerate and become infected. Among patients with diabetes, 20% also have gout. This study aimed to assess adherence to recommended gout treatment in patients with diabetes and to compare usual care with initial care provided by a nurse-led gout care program. In patients with diabetes, gout is frequently undertreated, particularly when not initially managed in a nurse-led gout care program.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Claus","Larsen, Jesper Walther","Holm, Peter C. W.","Nielsen, Gunnar Lauge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-785984"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Claus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gout an overlooked disease in patients with diabetes a danish prospective cohort study with 000000000002 years of follow up","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105003129000&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-785984","identifier":[{"id":"40290813","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003129000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7546241e-9b28-4782-898a-cfa247018fd8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A23406529B657ABB41B3C03A871F5D11"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Clinical Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, North Denmark Regional Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"16534364-e0f1-4da9-adc4-97ddf1b44140","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Walther","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f16603b1-2671-4f5a-a354-bc4e48963534","name":"Larsen, Jesper Walther","orcid":"0009-0000-3794-0942","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter C. W.","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"dde58cc9-fb65-463a-952e-cc7d9cbd4d7c","name":"Holm, Peter C. W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunnar Lauge","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7e984c06-4032-4a3f-8fa7-fc532cb2549b","name":"Nielsen, Gunnar Lauge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40290813"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/cd24-0082","issn":["08918929","19454953"],"issn_org":["19454953"],"issue":"2","journal":"Clinical Diabetes","pages":"282-290","paperid":"cd240082","publisher":"American Diabetes Association","status":"p","title":"Clinical Diabetes","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003129000"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7546241e-9b28-4782-898a-cfa247018fd8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Gout: An Overlooked Disease in Patients With Diabetes? A Danish Prospective Cohort Study With 2 Years of Follow-Up","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-785984","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Plasmacytoid dendritic cells (pDCs) play a pivotal role in immune responses, particularly against viral infections. pDCs exhibit diverse functions, including interferon production, cytokine secretion, and antigen presentation. Here, we investigate the antigen cross-presentation capacity of pDCs and their role in CD8 + T cell activation. Utilizing a culturing system with CD8 + T cells and autologous pDCs derived from circulating CD34 + hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells, we demonstrate that pDCs efficiently activate CD8 + T cells via cross-presentation, promoting T cell expansion and cytotoxic activity. The antigen presentation capacity of pDCs is comparable to that of monocyte-derived dendritic cells (moDCs) and myeloid dendritic cells, which are known for their efficient antigen-presentation capacity. Transcriptomic analysis reveals genetic signatures in CD8 + T cells activated by pDCs distinct from moDCs, suggesting different activation mechanisms. These findings underscore the importance of pDCs in antigen presentation and their contribution to CD8 + T cell activation.","author_count":17,"contributors":["van der Sluis, Renée Marije","García-Rodríguez, Juan Luis","Nielsen, Ian Helstrup","Gris-Oliver, Albert","Becker, Jennifer","Costa, Bibiana","Chaudhry, M Zeeshan","Werner, Marvin","Laustsen, Anders","Pedersen, Jesper Geert","Jakobsen, Kristine Raaby","Mogensen, Trine H","Kalinke, Ulrich","Cicin-Sain, Luka","Bak, Rasmus O","Kristensen, Lasse Sommer","Jakobsen, Martin Roelsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796507"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jakobsen, Martin Roelsgaard","van der Sluis, Renée Marije"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research (HZI)","TWINCORE, Centre for Experimental and Clinical Infection Research"],"keyword":["Antigen Presentation","CD8 T cell","CP Immunology","Dendritic cell","Immunity","Inflammation","Plasmacytoid dendritic cell","pDC"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distinctive cd000000000008 sup sup t cell activation by antigen presenting plasmacytoid dendritic cells compared to conventional dendritic cells","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2025.115413","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-796507","identifier":[{"id":"86000635547","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40073016","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8059bc31-c09d-47f2-8efa-9efe75cc725e"],"keyword":["CD8 T cell","CP: Immunology","IFNa","antigen presentation","dendritic cell","immunity","inflammation","pDC","plasmacytoid dendritic cell"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-45D3CD1CFB588E353B026C42C41E5855"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2025.115413","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"twincore centre for experimental and clinical infection research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TWINCORE, Centre for Experimental and Clinical Infection Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"helmhol