 Bech Jellesmark","orcid":"0000-0002-4533-1642","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Sofia","key":"korremanstinesofiapau","last":"Korreman","locid":"2ea90767-c414-4d74-9eb1-d4587dfcb9eb","name":"Korreman, Stine Sofia","orcid":"0000-0002-3523-382X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte Vrou","key":"offersenbirgittevroupau","last":"Offersen","locid":"8e07074b-b750-43e0-93ec-b63086536def","name":"Offersen, Birgitte Vrou","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39725067"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.radonc.2024.110705","issn":["01678140"],"journal":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","paperid":"110705","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","title_org":"Radiotherapy and Oncology","volume":"204"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214306106"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-95f83d7a-f4d1-4583-96a8-4b8d90bd62e3","au-de70e2ce-4d1c-4d6f-be0d-237ddf319c5e","sdu-11b22898-e366-4ac1-95db-aaeff518e14f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The effect of coronary artery calcifications and radiotherapy on the risk of coronary artery disease in high-risk breast cancer patients in the DBCG RT-Nation cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-792962","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"On August 29 and 30, 2024, eight researchers and six expert practitioners within wellbeing and youth sport were gathered in Copenhagen to reach evidence-based consensus on how to promote wellbeing in and through youth sports. The consensus process integrated international research-based knowledge with practice-based knowledge into statements about key factors influencing wellbeing in youth sport. Based on this knowledge, practice and policy directed statements on how wellbeing in and through sport can be promoted were formulated. The consensus process and the resulting statements were based on a system approach to wellbeing in youth sport and how it can be promoted. Four system levels (the individual, interpersonal, community, and policy levels) were addressed in answering the following questions: (1) What characterizes wellbeing in sport for children and adolescents? (2) What characterizes sport environments that promote children and adolescents’ wellbeing? (3) Which factors are important to consider in efforts to develop wellbeing promoting youth sport environments? (4) How can wellbeing in youth sport be promoted? In total, 19 consensus statement sentences were formulated on how young sports participants (3), parents/caretakers (5), coaches and leaders/managers (5), local sport communities (3) and sports federations (3) can promote wellbeing in youth sport.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Nielsen, Glen","Krustrup, Peter","Rossing, Niels Nygaard","Elsborg, Peter Juul","Nøddesbo, Jesper","Krabbe, Annemette","Rashid, Imran","Høj, Bodil Borg","Mortensen, Janne","Østergaard, Søren","Skovgaard, Thomas","Ryom, Knud","Aggerholm, Kenneth","Agergaard, Sine"],"cuid":["S04-098.69-822247"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Glen"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for Digital Health","Norwegian School of Sport Sciences"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Club sports","Consensus","Denmark","Health Promotion methods","Humans","Leisure","Mental health","Physical activity","Thriving","Wellbeing","Young people","Youth Sports"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Jesper Noeddesbo Coaching and Consulting"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to promote wellbeing in youth sport recommendations from the 000000002024 copenhagen consensus conference","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.70121","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: The authors received no specific funding for this work. The authors would like to thank the hosts of the conference: Charlotte Sandager Aggestrup is a consultant, FIBU, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark; Karin Ingemann is the head of development, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark; Liselotte Byrnak is a program manager, FIBU, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark; Louise Briand Thomsen is a facilitator, Academic Staff, The Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Active Living, University of Southern Denmark; Maiken Ziebell is a project manager, FIBU, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark; Signe Henningsen is a student assistant, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark; Stephanie Hougaard is a consultant, the National Olympic Committee and Sports Confederation of Denmark.","The authors received no specific funding for this work."],"id":"S04-098.69-822247","identifier":[{"id":"105013192835","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12341447","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40793750","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001547610400001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-16c45af1-08b5-49d4-ae53-1e1270500f57","au-ed76529e-e060-445b-bae3-6deded25a24e","ku-1df1acda-04a7-4e5f-99c6-0a2cb5e83a57","sdu-12210e75-270a-4733-8d65-c4a36841ea03"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Consensus","Denmark","Health Promotion/methods","Humans","Youth Sports","club sports","leisure","mental health","physical activity","thriving","wellbeing","young people"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A707838ACFD5C26E74956DF9A750BB47"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/460696207/Scandinavian_Med_Sci_Sports_-_2025_-_Nielsen_-_How_to_Promote_Wellbeing_in_Youth_Sport_Recommendations_From_the_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.70121","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/791359952/Scandinavian_Med_Sci_Sports_-_2025_-_Nielsen_-_How_to_Promote_Wellbeing_in_Youth_Sport_Recommendations_From_the_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/295074630/Scandinavian_Med_Sci_Sports_-_2025_-_Nielsen_-_How_to_Promote_Wellbeing_in_Youth_Sport_Recommendations_From_the_2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of