{"abstract":"In this paper, we present the design and commissioning results of the upgraded collective Thomson scattering diagnostic at the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator. The diagnostic has a new radiometer designed to operate between the second and third harmonics of the electron cyclotron emission from the plasma at 171-177 GHz, where the emission background has a minimum and is of order 10-100 eV. It allows us to receive the scattered electromagnetic field with a significantly improved signal-to-noise ratio and extends the set of possible scattering geometries compared to the case of the original instrument operated at 140 GHz. The elements of the diagnostic are a narrowband notch filter and a frequency stabilized probing gyrotron that will allow measuring scattered radiation spectra very close to the probing frequency. Here, we characterize the microwave components applied to the radiometer and demonstrate the performance of the complete system that was achieved during the latest experimental campaign, OP2.1.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Ponomarenko, S.","Moseev, D.","Stange, T.","Krier, L.","Stordiau, P.","Braune, H.","Gantenbein, G","Jelonnek, J.","Kuleshov, A.","Laqua, H. P.","Lechte, C.","Marsen, S.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Oosterbeek, J. W.","Plaum, B.","Ragona, R.","Rasmussen, Jesper","Ruess, T.","Salewski, Mirko","Thumm, M.","Zimmermann, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712116"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["W7-X Team"],"corresponding_author":["Ponomarenko, S."],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Ukraine"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","NASU - Institute of Radiophysics and Electronics","University of Stuttgart"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of the 000000000174 ghz collective thomson scattering diagnostics at wendelstein 000000000007 x","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0174444","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712116","identifier":[{"id":"38180346","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181796288","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cbbbf9af-8c5a-40ff-9c5f-517541236fe0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-97AAC225917BB445D6A43656CBFAD78B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/348830450/013501_1_5.0174444.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0174444","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ua","key":"nasu institute of radiophysics and electronics","loc":["Ukraine","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"NASU - Institute of Radiophysics and Electronics","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"university of stuttgart","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Stuttgart","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"