{"abstract":"The article examine the analytical potentials of the concepts of the dispositive, assemblage, and actor-network developed by Foucault, Deleuze, and Latour, respectively. We do so by engaging with a selected empirical case concerning an intervention in the Danish educational landscape–the Assessment of Educational Readiness (AER). Regarding the dispositive, the ambition of problematizing and destabilizing the status quo is pursued with genealogy as an analytical tool, and by analysing the heterogeneous constitutive complexities in order to illuminate how that which is regarded as natural comprises specific forms of power/knowledge. This analytical strategy we describe as a reality- and subjectivity-problematizing reconfiguration. With the analytical strategy imbricated in the concept of assemblage, the-taken-for-granted is disrupted by examining processes of becoming and the production of differences associated with these processes, as well as unpacking potentialities in the form of fractures, cracks, or tentative attempts to develop alternative ways of becoming. It allows us to engage with the complex nature of a phenomenon by focusing on virtuality in the form of the not yet realized or that which is yet to come, which is why we term this analytical strategy a virtual reality reconfiguration. Finally, the actor-network as an analytical strategy examines the ways in which the social is constructed through the joining together of heterogeneous actors in networks and by mapping events with the aim of providing insight into how heterogeneous human and non-human actors are networked together and create new realities. We term this analytical strategy a heterogeneous reality reconfiguration.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Stilling Olesen, Jesper","Plauborg, Helle","Simovska, Venka","Søndergaard, Dorte Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-141807"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"keyword":["Actor network","Aktørnetværk","Analytical strategies","Assemblage","Deleuze","Dispositiv","Dispositive","Forskningsmetode","Foucault","Latour","Reconfigurations","Uddannelsesparathedsvurdering","Uddannelsespolitik"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring educational un readiness through the concepts of dispositive assemblage and actor network","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85127262183","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-141807","identifier":[{"id":"85127262183","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1589b6e1-ecc0-4c83-9ebd-cc18de02dbbe"],"keyword":["Analytical strategies","Deleuze","Forskningsmetode","Foucault","Latour","Reconfigurations","Uddannelsesparathedsvurdering","Uddannelsespolitik","actor-network","aktørnetværk","assemblage","dispositiv","dispositive"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22BD54C3BCB25C62A265E5D39956E326"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"plauborgpau","last":"Plauborg","locid":"1fed98e7-1fbe-4b19-adcb-043de327af58","name":"Plauborg, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-2285-9372","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Venka","key":"simovskapau","last":"Simovska","locid":"3fa7b3d7-0f48-4529-b978-d667187bf858","name":"Simovska, Venka","orcid":"0000-0003-1391-9182","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Marie","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"c938db5d-8b6d-4c0c-98e0-c4a0800b3a3e","name":"Søndergaard, Dorte Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-8859-8590","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s42087-022-00284-9","issn":["25225790","25225804"],"issn_org":["25225790"],"issue":"4","journal":"Human Arenas","pages":"761-777","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Human Arenas","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127262183"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1589b6e1-ecc0-4c83-9ebd-cc18de02dbbe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Exploring educational (un)readiness through the concepts of dispositive, assemblage and actor-network","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-141807","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with psychotic disorders (PD) often have comorbid alcohol use disorder (AUD), which is typically treated pharmacologically. Up till now, no systematic review has examined the effectiveness and safety of AUD treatment in PD patients. Objectives: This study aimed to systematically review the literature on (1) the effects of pharmacological treatments for AUD on drinking outcomes, (2) the side effects of the drugs, and (3) the effects of polypharmacy in patients with comorbid AUD and PD. Methods: Bibliographic searches were conducted in MEDLINE, Embase, Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials, and PsycINFO. At least two reviewers extracted the data, assessed the risk of bias, and performed the qualitative synthesis of the collected evidence. Results: Twelve eligible studies were identified, half being randomized controlled trials (RCTs). Three studies examined disulfiram, nine naltrexone, two acamprosate, and one nalmefene by comparing the effects of treatment to placebo, baseline, or pharmacological agents. Disulfiram and naltrexone were shown to reduce alcohol intake. Regarding acamprosate, the findings were mixed. Nalmefene decreased alcohol intake. All pharmacological agents appeared safe to use as AUD monotherapy, but cardiac events were reported when combining naltrexone and disulfiram. Nine studies had a high risk of bias, and three had some other concerns. Conclusion: The studies provide tentative support for the use of naltrexone and disulfiram in this population, although combinations of pharmacological AUD treatments and other polypharmacy remain unexplored. The studies had high adherence rates that are hardly replicable in real-world settings. Thus, the findings should be confirmed in larger high quality efficacy and effectiveness RCTs with longer follow-ups.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rosenstand, Niels Jørgen","Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","Skøt, Lotte","Anhøj, Simon Jesper","Nielsen, Dorthe Grüner","Højlund, Mikkel","Mellentin, Angelina Isabella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-703170"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mellentin, Angelina Isabella"],"keyword":["Acamprosate therapeutic use","Alcohol Drinking","Alcohol use disorder","Alcoholism complications","Disulfiram therapeutic use","Dual diagnosis","Humans","Naltrexone therapeutic use","Pharmacological agents","Polypharmacy","Psychotic Disorders","Psychotic Disorders complications","Side effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pharmacological treatment of alcohol use disorder in patients with psychotic disorders a systematic review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10964102/pdf/CN-22-1129.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-703170","identifier":[{"id":"85184453753","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10964102","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36582063","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b3fa5bc3-22ba-476e-9796-7f2659ba28e9"],"keyword":["Acamprosate/therapeutic use","Alcohol Drinking","Alcoholism/complications","Disulfiram/therapeutic use","Humans","Naltrexone/therapeutic use","Pharmacological agents","Psychotic Disorders/complications","alcohol use disorder","dual diagnosis","polypharmacy","psychotic disorders","side effects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-34607A8695388FA91276A33299E883F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10964102/pdf/CN-22-1129.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Jørgen","key":"rosenstandnielsjørgenpau","last":"Rosenstand","name":"Rosenstand, Niels Jørgen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Søgaard","key":"nielsenanettesøgaardpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"63429b82-37e7-4fc5-84dd-f73ef3f5658a","name":"Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8569-4165","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"skøtlottepau","last":"Skøt","locid":"4902df5a-0988-4535-9480-434af6b26352","name":"Skøt, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1762-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"anhøjsimonjesperpau","last":"Anhøj","locid":"3aa8cfdb-307a-4253-ae68-db56e7107d17","name":"Anhøj, Simon Jesper","name_org":"Anhøj, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-8903-499X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Grüner","key":"nielsendorthegrünerpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"45c544fc-760e-4676-9179-794ecaec78a4","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Grüner","orcid":"0000-0003-1235-8336","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"højlundmikkelpau","last":"Højlund","locid":"1a78b498-c531-4ec8-9415-8702b8f0dce8","name":"Højlund, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-5786-5203","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Angelina Isabella","key":"mellentinangelinaisabellapau","last":"Mellentin","locid":"354a18df-b9f8-4eb2-b0f3-b815c1a6dfe0","name":"Mellentin, Angelina Isabella","orcid":"0000-0002-6515-2852","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36582063"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1570159x21666221229160300","issn":["1570159X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Current Neuropharmacology","pages":"1129-1143","publisher":"Bentham Science Publishers","status":"p","title":"Current Neuropharmacology","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184453753"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b3fa5bc3-22ba-476e-9796-7f2659ba28e9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Pharmacological treatment of alcohol use disorder in patients with psychotic disorders : A systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-703170","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate associations between hormone levels and corneal parameters in patients with keratoconus (KC), before and after photooxidative corneal collagen crosslinking (CXL). Design: Prospective, observational cohort study. Participants: Twenty-eight patients with KC who were scheduled for CXL at Aarhus University Hospital in Denmark. Methods: Androgen (dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate [DHEA-S]) and estrogen (estrone and estriol) plasma levels were measured and clinical assessments were performed before CXL and 2 to 3 months post-CXL, comparing the CXL eye with the control eye from the same participant. Main Outcome Measures: Associations between hormone levels and maximum corneal curvature (K max) and minimum central corneal thickness (CCt min) before and after CXL. Results: Corneal collagen crosslinking was associated with a 2% reduction in K max values in the CXL eye, post-CXL, from baseline (median, 56.8 diopters [D]; 95% confidence interval [CI], 50.4–60.3) to the second visit (55.7 D; 95% CI, 50.4–58.8; P < 0.001). Systemic DHEA-S levels were 5 to 6 orders of magnitude higher than estriol or estrone concentrations in plasma. Importantly, estriol levels, rather than DHEA-S or estrone levels, were more closely correlated with K max before CXL (Spearman's r = 0.55, P = 0.01). Post-CXL K max and CCt min were not associated with DHEA-S, estrone, or estriol plasma levels at the same timepoint. Conclusions: This study provides supporting evidence based on a KC clinical population that systemic estrogen levels may influence corneal parameters (curvature and thickness) pre-CXL. Further studies evaluating the interplay between the therapeutic benefits of CXL and systemic hormone distributions are needed to determine if perturbation of the local corneal microenvironment influences endocrine function. Financial Disclosure(s): The authors have no proprietary or commercial interest in any materials discussed in this article.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Van, Lyly","Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","Nicholas, Sarah E","Hjortdal, Jesper","McKay, Tina B","Karamichos, Dimitrios"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-707621"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Karamichos, Dimitrios"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","University of Oklahoma","University of Texas"],"keyword":["Cornea","Corneal crosslinking","Estrogen","Hormones","Keratoconus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prospective observational study evaluating systemic hormones and corneal crosslinking effects in keratoconus","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xops.2023.100364","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-707621","identifier":[{"id":"37868794","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10585634","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85174027553","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4e9b64ae-43a7-49c2-8dea-eb6af4564cc1"],"keyword":["Cornea","Corneal crosslinking","Estrogen","Hormones","Keratoconus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F954189EB79AAE7DFBF7CE7D48B960A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xops.2023.100364","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of texas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lyly","key":"vanpau","last":"Van","name":"Van, Lyly","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sashia","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","locid":"4d778acb-8da2-45ce-a916-232721f4c529","name":"Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","name_org":"Bennett, Sashia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah E","key":"nicholaspau","last":"Nicholas","name":"Nicholas, Sarah E","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina B","key":"mckaypau","last":"McKay","name":"McKay, Tina B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dimitrios","key":"karamichospau","last":"Karamichos","name":"Karamichos, Dimitrios","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37868794"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.xops.2023.100364","issn":["26669145"],"issue":"2","journal":"Ophthalmology Science","paperid":"100364","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Ophthalmology Science","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174027553"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4e9b64ae-43a7-49c2-8dea-eb6af4564cc1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prospective Observational Study Evaluating Systemic Hormones and Corneal Crosslinking Effects in Keratoconus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-707621","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Automated Fare Collection (AFC) data for public transport analyses has received much research interest recently, including its use for the estimation of passenger route choice preferences. However, an important problem persists since AFC data only includes information about the trip within the public transport system, that is stop-to-stop (tap-in to tap-out). Not knowing the full trip from door-to-door might lead to estimation bias, especially when estimating route choice models based on only the chosen stops, which is common practice in current research using AFC data. To avoid this, we propose an improved method for estimating route choice models in public transport using AFC data. The method is based on randomly generating pseudo origin (and destination) points in close vicinity of the actually chosen origin (and destination) stops, thus allowing pseudo access and egress times to be incorporated into the route choice model. The framework is compatible with any probability density function. We suggest using the Beta distribution for generating points when knowledge about access and egress distances are available, whereas the Uniform distribution is suggested when no knowledge is available. The method was applied on replicated AFC data based on traditional travel survey data from the Greater Copenhagen area in Denmark. The results of the model estimations confirm estimation bias in parameter estimates when not correcting for the lack of access/egress information. The proposed method notably improves in-vehicle-time parameter estimates of the route choice model compared to estimation assuming AFC stop-to-stop data, whereas access/egress time and hidden waiting time parameters are still biased, although to a lesser extent than a traditional naïve estimation based on stop-to-stop data.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Thorhauge, Mikkel","Nielsen, Otto Anker","Eltved, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712107"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choice set","Discrete choice modelling","Estimation bias","Public transport","Route choice modelling","Smart card data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Movia Public Transport"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public transport route choice modelling reducing estimation bias when using smart card data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tra.2023.103929","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712107","identifier":[{"id":"85179761035","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ca895095-4bbd-49f1-8e52-49ceebca860d"],"keyword":["Choice Set","Discrete choice modelling","Estimation bias","Public transport","Route choice modelling","Smart card data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD7E2BDC0FAA375BBA6BCB7745C184A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tra.2023.103929","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/345596723/1-s2.0-S096585642300349X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science, Transportation Systems Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Movia Public Transport"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"thorhaugepau","last":"Thorhauge","locid":"17be4255-2d6a-412f-a6c4-5d82af55dc57","name":"Thorhauge, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-1887-7527","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"eltvedpau","last":"Eltved","name":"Eltved, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tra.2023.103929","issn":["09658564","18792375"],"issn_org":["09658564"],"journal":"Transportation Research Part A: Policy and Practice","paperid":"103929","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Transportation Research Part A: Policy and Practice","title_org":"Transportation Research Part A","volume":"179"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179761035"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ca895095-4bbd-49f1-8e52-49ceebca860d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Public transport route choice modelling: Reducing estimation bias when using smart card data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712107","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Protein identification and quantification is an important tool for biomarker discovery. With the increased sensitivity and speed of modern mass spectrometers, sample preparation remains a bottleneck for studying large cohorts. To address this issue, we prepared and evaluated a simple and efficient workflow on the Opentrons OT-2 robot that combines sample digestion, cleanup, and loading on Evotips in a fully automated manner, allowing the processing of up to 192 samples in 6 h. Analysis of 192 automated HeLa cell sample preparations consistently identified ∼8000 protein groups and ∼130,000 peptide precursors with an 11.5 min active liquid chromatography gradient with the Evosep One and narrow-window data-independent acquisition (nDIA) with the Orbitrap Astral mass spectrometer providing a throughput of 100 samples per day. Our results demonstrate a highly sensitive workflow yielding both reproducibility and stability at low sample inputs. The workflow is optimized for minimal sample starting amount to reduce the costs for reagents needed for sample preparation, which is critical when analyzing large biological cohorts. Building on the digesting workflow, we incorporated an automated phosphopeptide enrichment step using magnetic titanium-immobilized metal ion affinity chromatography beads. This allows for a fully automated proteome and phosphoproteome sample preparation in a single step with high sensitivity. Using the integrated digestion and Evotip loading workflow, we evaluated the effects of cancer immune therapy on the plasma proteome in metastatic melanoma patients.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kverneland, Anders H.","Harking, Florian S.","Vej-Nielsen, Joel Mario","Huusfeldt, Magnus","Bekker-Jensen, Dorte B.","Svane, Inge Marie","Bache, Nicolai","Olsen, Jesper V."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747881"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully automated workflow for integrated sample digestion and evotip loading enabling high throughput clinical proteomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100790","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747881","identifier":[{"id":"38777088","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85199934306","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11251069","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3d7b6045-b2ea-43e4-b1b9-f44ade9d4146"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F712A42150F2FF2623483267E499DD66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397985292/1_s2.0_S153594762400080X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100790","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Olsen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Evosep Biosystems"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anders H.","key":"kvernelandpau","last":"Kverneland","locid":"cb8e2dcf-c2ad-494b-8ce5-6946f0f4bb24","name":"Kverneland, Anders H.","orcid":"0000-0002-9883-936X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Florian","key":"harkingpau","last":"Harking","locid":"7e90d979-2e7f-465d-8771-5cb2458940ee","name":"Harking, Florian S.","name_org":"Harking, Florian","orcid":"0000-0001-5553-1421","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Joel Mario","key":"vejnielsenpau","last":"Vej-Nielsen","name":"Vej-Nielsen, Joel Mario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Magnus","key":"huusfeldtpau","last":"Huusfeldt","name":"Huusfeldt, Magnus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Dorte B.","key":"bekkerjensenpau","last":"Bekker-Jensen","name":"Bekker-Jensen, Dorte B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge Marie","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Inge Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Nicolai","key":"bachepau","last":"Bache","name":"Bache, Nicolai","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper V.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"16f5cd56-244f-4fe8-bebd-13ee7bd17822","name":"Olsen, Jesper V.","orcid":"0000-0002-4747-4938","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38777088"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100790","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"7","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","paperid":"100790","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","title_org":"Molecular & cellular proteomics : MCP","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199934306"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","evosep biosystems"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3d7b6045-b2ea-43e4-b1b9-f44ade9d4146"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fully Automated Workflow for Integrated Sample Digestion and Evotip Loading Enabling High-Throughput Clinical Proteomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747881","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denne rapport opsummerer hovedresultaterne fra forskningsprojektet ”Udviklingsinitiativer for marine virkemidler”, der er besluttet og finansieret af ”Aftale om grøn omstilling af dansk landbrug” fra 2021 og udmøntet via Miljøstyrelsen. Projektet skal danne grundlag for beslutning om, og i givet fald hvordan de marine virkemidler ”reetablering af ålegræs” og ”dyrkning af tang” kan anvendes i vandplanlægningen til at opsamle næringsstoffer og/eller opnå andre positive miljøeffekter, som kan bidrage til hurtigere opnåelse af god økologisk tilstand i danske kystvandområder i overensstemmelse med vandrammedirektivet.Forskningsprojektet og nærværende opsummerende rapport er ledet af DTU Aqua ved projektleder Karen Timmermann og udført i samarbejde med Syddansk Universitet (SDU), Københavns Universitet (KU), Aarhus Universitet (AU) og DHI. Rapporten er en del af rapportserien ”Udviklingsinitiativer for marine virkemidler”, som udover den opsummerende rapport omfatter en række baggrundsrapporter med videnskabelig dokumentation for projektets resultater.Baggrundsrapporterne i serien udgives i løbet af 2024 og udgøres af:• En dybdegående projektsynteserapport.• Vidensyntese om ålegræstransplantering.• Videnssyntese om tangdyrkning.• Rapporten ”Muligheder for at indregne marine virkemidler i den nationale drivhusgasopgørelse”.• Rapporten ”Retlige rammer for marine virkemidler og marin natur”.• Arbejdspakkerapporter med videnskabelig dokumentation for resultaterne fra hver af projektets centrale faglige arbejdspakker omhandlende ”Ålegræstransplantering”, ”Dyrkning af sukkertang” og \"Modellering af virkemiddeleffekter”.Miljøstyrelsen har haft rapportudkast til kommentering undervejs i projektgruppens arbejde, men valg af metoder og konklusioner er alene projektgruppens ansvar.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Timmermann, Karen","Mostovaya, Alina","Barnewitz, Anders","Erichsen, Anders","Petersen, Anders Høker","Holbach, Andreas","Bruhn, Annette","Nielsen, Benjamin","Taylor, Daniel","Hansen, Flemming Thorbjørn","Hansen, Frederik H.","Christensen, Freja","Anker, Helle Tegner","Christensen, Jesper","Holding, Johnna","Baaner, Lasse","Hermannsen, Line","Callisen, Lærke W.","Nielsen, Mette Møller","Gommesen, Mia","Lees, Mikkel Keller","Flindt, Mogens","Holst, Niels","Canal-Vergés, Paula","Schmedes, Peter Søndergaard","Kjær, Rasmus Ambus","Steinfurth, Rune","Stæhr, Sanjina Upadhyay","Pedersen, Sidsel Gurholt","Vinbæk, Sidsel Juul","Gyldenkerne, Steen","Andersen, Søren Stig","Boderskov, Teis","Jørgensen, Thor S.","Banke, Timi Løvholt","Andersen, Trine A.","Larsen, Trine C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750732"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Timmermann, Karen"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ålegræstransplantering og tangdyrkning som marine virkemidler potentialer effekter og juridiske aspekter opsummering af hovedresultater fra projektet","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/dtu.000003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750732","ids":["sdu-98125997-674b-4af1-91f2-b7f798a4aed8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-488C91DA458711B6B97768BBB7818586"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/dtu.000003","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/265798208/457-2024-Aalegraestransplantering-og-tangdyrkning-som-marine-virkemidler_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"