{"abstract":"Over the past decade, treatment with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) has been implemented in cancer treatment. It has led to a significant improvement in the prognosis for many types of cancer. ICIs work by inducing the body's immune response against cancer cells. Unfortunately, they can also cause immune-related adverse events in most organ systems, with skin-related adverse events being among the most common. This review provides an overview of existing evidence and clinical experience regarding managing dermatological adverse events associated with ICIs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kaae, Jeanette","Carlsen, Berit Christina","Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","Palshof, Jesper","Svane, Inge Marie","Vestergaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757588"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kutane bivirkninger ved behandling med immuncheckpointinhibitorer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V03240216","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-757588","identifier":[{"id":"39115212","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85200939176","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0318b7c1-df56-4371-a8cd-e1ce7311cdc5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D051B5CA2060EA67D72864C79BF178AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V03240216","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Dermatology and Venereology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev and Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"kaaepau","last":"Kaae","name":"Kaae, Jeanette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Berit Christina","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","name":"Carlsen, Berit Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aska","key":"drljevicnielsenpau","last":"Drljevic-Nielsen","locid":"10a1cade-abdc-4a12-821b-9c94f3f7ddfd","name":"Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"palshofpau","last":"Palshof","name":"Palshof, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge Marie","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Inge Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"1e1f8aeb-17cb-488a-8a3d-2d377ffa668e","name":"Vestergaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6485-3158","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39115212"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v03240216","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"29","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V03240216","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200939176"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0318b7c1-df56-4371-a8cd-e1ce7311cdc5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Kutane bivirkninger ved behandling med immuncheckpointinhibitorer","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-757588","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: In Denmark, the primary responsibility for treatment of patients with diabetes has shifted from hospitals to primary care. Thus, general practice has assumed responsibility for a complex and multifaceted disease. To address this situation a stratification tool to assist the nurses in primary care in their work with diabetes patients was developed. Aim: In the present study we evaluated this stratification tool. Method: The evaluation was based on 18 semi-structured interviews conducted with nurses employed in primary care across Denmark, and who had experience with the stratification tool. The data was subsequently analyzed by content and thematic analyses. Results: The interviewees were generally positive towards the stratification tool. The analyses established three themes 1. Treatment, 2. Resources, and 3. Points of critique. Conclusions: Our study indicates that a combined tool for risk stratification of patients with T2D and for subsequent risk communication is perceived as positive and supportive for quality in care. It is seen to potentially reduce the resources presently allocated to well-regulated and stable T2D patients. These resources will eventually be available for other patients. The positive reception by nurses supports that tools like the Diabetes Control Support Tool could be developed and implemented in general practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nissen, Ricko Damberg","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783099"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nissen, Ricko Damberg"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Primary care","Qualitative study","Resource allocation","Risk communication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of a support tool for diabetes control in primary care a qualitative study with primary care staff","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.deman.2024.100228","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783099","identifier":[{"id":"85197514792","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-50c56f64-4f31-45d7-b3f5-53395c27513e"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Primary care","Qualitative study","Resource allocation","Risk communication","Stratification tool"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7569EF852AE83D3BFFAD09C866ADCEA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/277070200/1-s2.0-S2666970624000337-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.deman.2024.100228","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ricko Damberg","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"b345345d-ba8d-4b18-b5c0-1f0398ae6843","name":"Nissen, Ricko Damberg","orcid":"0000-0001-5590-374X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.deman.2024.100228","issn":["26669706"],"journal":"Diabetes Epidemiology and Management","paperid":"100228","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Epidemiology and Management","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197514792"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-50c56f64-4f31-45d7-b3f5-53395c27513e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of a Support Tool for Diabetes Control in primary care – A Qualitative study with primary care staff","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783099","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Both vestibular neuronitis (VN) and Meniere's disease (MD) have great impact on quality of life and are associated with a significant number of sick leave days absent from work. The aim was to assess labor market participation rate one year after hospital diagnosis of VN and MD and the use of rehabilitation measures. STUDY DESIGN: Nationwide register-based cohort study including patients with VN (n = 1,341) and MD (n = 843) and control persons matched in 1:5 with a VN cohort control (n = 6,683) and MD cohort control (n = 4,209). RESULTS: Compared to control persons, VN patients were more likely to be single, have higher income, and a higher Charlson comorbidity index score. MD patients had a higher level of education and a higher Charlson index compared to control persons. One year after patients were diagnosed with VN, no significant difference in labor market participation was observed (p = 0.88). However, MD patients had a 10.4% reduced probability of possessing a full-time job one year after diagnosis compared to matched control persons (58.1 ± 0.5% vs. 68.5 ± 0.5%, p < 0.001). Both VN and MD patients consulted otorhinolaryngologists, general practitioners, and physiotherapists more than control persons both before and after the initial diagnosis (p < 0.01). In addition, MD patients also consulted psychologists more frequently before and after diagnosis of the disease (p < 0.01). CONCLUSION: Intrahospital diagnosed MD increases the risk of leaving the labor market in opposition to VN. Both MD and VN are associated with significant expenses to the Danish health care system from the use of public rehabilitation measures and medical consultations.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tønnesen, Emil Severin","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Rose Olsen, Kim","Wanscher, Jens Højberg","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","Sørensen, Jesper Roed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783391"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Jesper Roed"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Case Control Studies","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Dizziness","Employment statistics numerical data","Female","Humans","Labor market","Male","Meniere s disease","Middle Aged","Quality of Life","Register based","Registries","Rehabilitation","Sick Leave statistics numerical data","Vestibular Neuronitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"labor market effects of rehabilitation for patients diagnosed with dizziness a danish nationwide register based cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00405-024-08871-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783391","identifier":[{"id":"85200422978","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11564300","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39098958","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-889456b8-bf92-4c0e-bcc6-cb387361118d"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Case-Control Studies","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Dizziness","Dizziness/rehabilitation","Employment/statistics & numerical data","Female","Humans","Labor market","Male","Meniere Disease/rehabilitation","Meniere’s disease","Middle Aged","Quality of Life","Registerø-based","Registries","Rehabilitation","Sick Leave/statistics & numerical data","Vestibular Neuronitis/rehabilitation","Vestibular neuronitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87398221D9B6E7BDBD4C191A33C62B9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00405-024-08871-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/277567217/s00405-024-08871-y.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Severin","key":"tønnesenpau","last":"Tønnesen","name":"Tønnesen, Emil Severin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"rosepau","last":"Rose","locid":"529d9463-bb6c-4c8a-9114-eb7c45358642","name":"Rose Olsen, Kim","name_org":"Rose, Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-0473-4736","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Højberg","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","locid":"33130a0a-a7b5-4e60-b090-5a6e43f3396a","name":"Wanscher, Jens Højberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hvass","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"db84fc4e-28da-45af-a608-13ce8f4ec719","name":"Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","orcid":"0000-0001-7683-1407","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Roed","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"df2f67c9-1538-4bd8-82fb-79cd5c6b6814","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Roed","name_org":"Sorensen, Jesper Roed","orcid":"0000-0003-4351-8873","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39098958"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00405-024-08871-y","issn":["09374477","09428992"],"issn_org":["09374477"],"issue":"12","journal":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","pages":"6353-6358","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","volume":"281"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200422978"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-889456b8-bf92-4c0e-bcc6-cb387361118d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Labor market effects of rehabilitation for patients diagnosed with dizziness - a Danish nationwide register-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783391","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background Sarcopenia and sarcopenic obesity (SO) are age-related syndromes that may compromise physical and mental health among older adults. The Nordic countries differ from other regions on prevalence of disease, life-style behavior, and life expectancy, which may impact prevalence of sarcopenia and SO. Therefore, the aim of this study is to review the available evidence and gaps within this field in the Nordic countries. Methods PubMed, Embase, and Web of science (WOS) were searched up to February 2023. In addition, grey literature and reference lists of included studies were searched. Two independent researcher assessed papers and extracted data. Results Thirty-three studies out of 6,363 searched studies were included in this scoping review. Overall prevalence of sarcopenia varied from 0.9 to 58.5%. A wide prevalence range was still present for community-dwelling older adults when definition criteria and setting were considered. The prevalence of SO ranged from 4 to 11%, according to the only study on this field. Based on the included studies, potential risk factors for sarcopenia include malnutrition, low physical activity, specific diseases (e.g., diabetes), inflammation, polypharmacy, and aging, whereas increased levels of physical activity and improved dietary intake may reduce the risk of sarcopenia. The few available interventions for sarcopenia were mainly focused on resistance training with/without nutritional supplements (e.g., protein, vitamin D). Conclusion The findings of our study revealed inadequate research on SO but an increasing trend in the number of studies on sarcopenia. However, most of the included studies had descriptive cross-sectional design, small sample size, and applied different diagnostic criteria. Therefore, larger well-designed cohort studies that adhere to uniform recent guidelines are required to capture a full picture of these two age-related medical conditions in Nordic countries, and plan for prevention/treatment accordingly.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Baygi, Fereshteh","Buhl, Sussi Friis","Thilsing, Trine","Søndergaard, Jens","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783765"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Baygi, Fereshteh"],"keyword":["Age","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Humans","Nordic countries","Obesity epidemiology","Prevalence","Risk Factors","Sarcopenia","Sarcopenia epidemiology","Sarcopenic obesity","Scandinavian and Nordic Countries epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sarcopenia and sarcopenic obesity among older adults in the nordic countries a scoping review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-024-04970-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783765","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11092005","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85192951483","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38741067","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-d25488d1-2963-4e7c-b0e0-b29da45f660f"],"keyword":["Age","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Humans","Nordic countries","Obesity/epidemiology","Prevalence","Risk Factors","Sarcopenia","Sarcopenia/epidemiology","Sarcopenic obesity","Scandinavian and Nordic Countries/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-19C5A1F4479CC65E050268323BE99A63"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/278604860/s12877-024-04970-x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-024-04970-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fereshteh","key":"baygipau","last":"Baygi","locid":"82ac54a3-f35a-4ee6-85dc-362c9e160ee9","name":"Baygi, Fereshteh","orcid":"0000-0002-9260-2281","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sussi Friis","key":"buhlpau","last":"Buhl","locid":"3d9fcc5f-51ba-43d9-865f-8084e9a4fb92","name":"Buhl, Sussi Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-9145-9770","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","locid":"6ae25242-1e96-48cf-ab01-cbac26690f6b","name":"Thilsing, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-2041-2219","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38741067"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12877-024-04970-x","issn":["14712318"],"journal":"BMC Geriatrics","paperid":"421","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Geriatrics","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192951483"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d25488d1-2963-4e7c-b0e0-b29da45f660f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sarcopenia and sarcopenic obesity among older adults in the nordic countries: a scoping review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783765","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We model and measure the Brillouin power spectrum of Brillouin OTDR assisted by Raman amplification. We show how Raman pump depletion leads to measurement errors due to spectral translation of the Brillouin spectrum.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Vandborg, Mads Holmark","Mathew, Neethu Mariam","Christensen, Jesper","Joy, Tomin","Allousch, M. Ali","Marx, Benjamin","Jostmeier, Thorben","Grüner-Nielsen, Lars","Rishøj, Lars Søgaard","Rottwitt, Karsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789075"],"event":{"end":"2023-11-24","place":"Hamamatsu, jp","start":"2023-11-20","title":"28<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Optical Fiber Sensor","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Vandborg, Mads Holmark"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luna Innovations Germany GmbH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DFM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DFM","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling the brillouin spectrum in raman amplifier assisted brillouin otdr","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/345585490/Tu3.19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789075","ids":["dtu-78bcf332-db7e-4eb2-aac9-33e508334e81"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC0535922F3CB4E9C5B5FE31789A9528"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/345585490/Tu3.19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Fiber Optics, Devices and Non-linear Effects"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dfm danish national metrology institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DFM","l3nn":"DFM Danish National Metrology Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DFM Danish National Metrology Institute","namevar":["DFM - Dansk Fundamental Metrologi A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DFM","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"luna innovations germany gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Luna Innovations Germany GmbH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Holmark","key":"vandborgpau","last":"Vandborg","locid":"46883988-1b9e-487e-9c18-3604cf49e349","name":"Vandborg, Mads Holmark","orcid":"0000-0003-2513-2424","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Neethu","key":"mariammathewpau","last":"Mariam Mathew","locid":"a54eb883-5d36-4ea3-924e-3f8b6fe76deb","name":"Mathew, Neethu Mariam","name_org":"Mariam Mathew, Neethu","orcid":"0000-0002-1180-5811","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomin","key":"joypau","last":"Joy","name":"Joy, Tomin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M. Ali","key":"allouschpau","last":"Allousch","name":"Allousch, M. Ali","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin","key":"marxpau","last":"Marx","name":"Marx, Benjamin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorben","key":"jostmeierpau","last":"Jostmeier","name":"Jostmeier, Thorben","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"grünernielsenpau","last":"Grüner-Nielsen","locid":"d446bb16-12b9-4482-8c11-d4892cdb57e5","name":"Grüner-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0001-7974-8385","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Søgaard","key":"rishøjpau","last":"Rishøj","locid":"d4d25864-403d-4f3c-99b3-0b3193883b1f","name":"Rishøj, Lars Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0810-3859","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karsten","key":"rottwittpau","last":"Rottwitt","locid":"08d1b850-4e34-46e1-9f77-ee3f84163a4c","name":"Rottwitt, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0001-6738-5847","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Optica Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 28<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Optical Fiber Sensors"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-78bcf332-db7e-4eb2-aac9-33e508334e81"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modelling the Brillouin spectrum in Raman amplifier assisted Brillouin OTDR","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789075","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this symposium, the ongoing Danish project \"Scientific Reading – Learning with Texts in Science Education\" (2022-2026) is presented. The symposium focuses on Danish science teachers' use of learning materials as well as their understanding of and approaches to literacy in science. In Denmark, research on literacy and use of learning materials in science teaching is scarce, underpinning the significance of this project. Unlike the traditional ‘content area literacy’ approach that has dominated Danish science education, this project adopts a contemporary ‘disciplinary literacy’ framework. The symposium comprises three presentations exploring specific aspects of the project: Presentation 1 delves into a survey study mapping literacy and learning material use in Danish primary and lower secondary science education; Presentation 2 lays forth and discusses preliminary findings from qualitative classroom studies exploring learning with texts in science teaching; Presentation3 offers a comparative analysis of recent trends in disciplinary literacy in science education based on an international research review and Danish findings from the survey study introduced in presentation 1, emphasizing among others the prominence of multimodality. The symposium aims to bridge connections between actual trends in literacy research (multimodality and disciplinary literacy) and the increasing emphasis on models and modeling in science education research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bremholm, Jesper","Sillassen, Martin Krabbe","Buch, Bettina","Nielsen, Therese Malene","Oksbjerg, Marianne","Pagaard, Ditte Marie","Kragholm Knudsen, Stine","Ejdrup, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-792422"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-07","place":"Reykjavik, is","start":"2024-06-05","title":"NFSUN 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Nationalt Videnscenter for læsning"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"læremiddelbrug og literacyforståelser i naturfagene i danmark","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://nfsun2024.hi.is/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/NFSUN2024-Collection-of-abstracts.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-792422","ids":["ucn-2a5878c0-c24e-4304-9a8f-f3e7c0c0ec9e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6FE1CC309E83693FD0D2ED0C4E88AC3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://nfsun2024.hi.is/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/NFSUN2024-Collection-of-abstracts.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Nationalt Videnscenter for læsning"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA University College"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["University College Absalon"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Læreruddannelsen Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["University College Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bremholmpau","last":"Bremholm","name":"Bremholm, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Krabbe","key":"sillassenpau","last":"Sillassen","name":"Sillassen, Martin Krabbe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"buchpau","last":"Buch","name":"Buch, Bettina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Therese Malene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"44a19526-9e4b-4a3d-966c-875d06e6e22a","name":"Nielsen, Therese Malene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"oksbjergpau","last":"Oksbjerg","locid":"4db12419-a7dc-4e7b-ac4d-27105acc1244","name":"Oksbjerg, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-5618-9987","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Marie","key":"pagaardpau","last":"Pagaard","name":"Pagaard, Ditte Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"kragholmknudsenpau","last":"Kragholm Knudsen","name":"Kragholm Knudsen, Stine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"ejdruppau","last":"Ejdrup","name":"Ejdrup, Tine","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University College Absalon","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-2a5878c0-c24e-4304-9a8f-f3e7c0c0ec9e"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Læremiddelbrug og literacyforståelser i naturfagene i Danmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-792422","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This report summarizes the outcome of the project “Improved knowledge for management of flatfish stocks in Danish waters”, funded by the European Maritime and Fisheries Fund and the Danish Fisheries Agency (“Fiskeri, natur og miljø - Marin biodiversitet”). The project focused on improving the biological data to support advice and sustainable management of three flatfish species in Denmark: turbot (Scophthalmus maximus), common sole (Solea solea) and European plaice (Pleuronectes platessa). These species are important to Danish fisheries, and they currently suffer from a lack of information on a number of questions of importance for proper stock assessment and management. While there were differences between knowledge gaps of species, there were also common themes, such as the identification of biological populations, their geographical distributions and migration between areas which are currently challenging a sustainable management, in particular in the Skagerrak/Kattegat, which was a focus area in all species in the current study. In turbot, we reviewed how available evidence for population structure matches current stock assessment and management units for the species. Importantly, Kattegat and Skagerrak are currently merged into one management unit. However, merging Kattegat and Skagerrak did not seem to match available biological evidence, suggesting the presence of two different biological populations within the management unit, with interaction between North Sea/Atlantic and Baltic Sea populations mainly occurring in the Kattegat. This is based on substantial data, including genetic evidence and long-term data series. However, more information on the distribution of these populations in and outside spawning periods will be needed to refine current stock assessment and management practices to better match underlying biological variation (e.g. geographical distribution of populations across life stages). In addition, we addressed issues related to data quality for the stock assessment and confirmed the validity of catch data series and survey design in relation to the distribution of fishing efforts. In sole, we used genetic data in combination with otolith microchemistry to identify populations and their migrations in the North Sea-Baltic Sea transition zone, with a particular focus on Kattegat/Skagerrak. In this area, previous work had indicated evidence for population mixing not well aligned with current assessment units, where Skagerrak and Kattegat are merged with the rest of the Baltic Sea transition zone. We found evidence for the presence of two biological populations in our data, with a strong degree of mixing in particular in the Skagerrak, with indications of the presence of spawning individuals from both populations. In addition, we found stronger mixing outside spawning season and also found mixing in other areas (e.g. northern part of the North Sea). Migration data and larval origin supported a hypothesis of extended distribution into the Skagerrak of a Baltic Sea population, and hence recruits to the western Baltic Sea may have been spawned as far north as the Skagerrak, where our current study indicates that both Baltic Sea and North Sea/Atlantic populations may reproduce. However, data also indicated that common sole, once recruited to a specific geographical area within the distribution of the two populations, are fairly stationary and do not migrate to a notable extent. Collectively, the results have provided an improved understanding of biological variability and population dynamics in the management areas, supporting a change in management procedures towards a population based assessment rather than the present area based assessment. However, while such population based stock assessment and management have been implemented in other species, further work, in particular related to more fine scale and quantitative estimation of population presence and migration will be needed to implement this change for sole. In plaice, we focused on issues related to an apparent mis-match between stock assessment and quotas and the perception of the stock status by fishermen. In particular, in the Skagerrak where fishermen since 2017 are far from utilizing the quota that is based on the advice. In the project, we found distribution shifts possibly resulting in the availability of fewer plaice in the Skagerrak, matching the perception from the fishery. While the underlying reasons for these changes are unknown at present, we discuss potential sources of this variability, in particular in relation to potential local depletion and environmental changes that may have driven distribution changes in the Skagerrak. Collectively, the project has improved our knowledge on stock dynamics and biological parameters to support the quality of stock assessment and management in all three species significantly. While there are still open questions, the results have also shown interesting common patterns across species, such as the identification of specific geographical areas with high level of interaction between biological populations in several species. As such, and in addition to improving single species biological advice, our project could also have broader impacts, for example in relation to future ecosystem based approaches to management, where an integrated understanding across species will be needed to secure an implementation on a sustainable basis. In addition, climate change will also challenge current management procedures and the balance of quota allocation between countries through changes in distributions and migrations of exploited populations. As such, an improved understanding and quantification of these changes will provide crucial decision support for future management.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hansen, Jakob Hemmer","Hüssy, Karin","Jimenez-Mena, Belen","Svendsen, Jon Christian","Krüger-Johnsen, Maria","Støttrup, Josianne","Kokkalis, Alexandros","Brown, Elliot John","Mosegaard, Henrik","Nielsen, Anders","Berg, Casper Willestofte","Boje, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798050"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved knowledge for management of flatfish stocks in danish waters forflad","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/60e738ef-cc68-424f-9c49-14411651757e","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798050","ids":["dtu-60e738ef-cc68-424f-9c49-14411651757e"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-216B51FEB22B3AE4E332A3E13D607D73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/60e738ef-cc68-424f-9c49-14411651757e","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/387878532/473-2024-Improved-knowledge-for-management-of-flatfish-stocks-FORFLAD.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Marine Living Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"hemmerhansenpau","last":"Hemmer-Hansen","locid":"a9fbe122-035f-40d7-b5af-d1ed7caf2d2b","name":"Hansen, Jakob Hemmer","name_org":"Hemmer-Hansen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-1033-2565","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin","key":"hüssypau","last":"Hüssy","locid":"95c8d929-52bf-4c36-b1c1-974515d3410b","name":"Hüssy, Karin","orcid":"0000-0002-1993-6146","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Belen","key":"jimenezmenapau","last":"Jimenez-Mena","locid":"62c7e696-f38a-4c6d-8d86-115f16cebfaa","name":"Jimenez-Mena, Belen","orcid":"0000-0001-8458-5533","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon C.","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"2208c455-c4d1-4ba7-a638-9062097f640b","name":"Svendsen, Jon Christian","name_org":"Svendsen, Jon C.","orcid":"0000-0002-0273-0985","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"krügerjohnsenpau","last":"Krüger-Johnsen","locid":"6bd81274-c87b-44a3-8d49-93e759f0f27c","name":"Krüger-Johnsen, Maria","orcid":"0000-0001-6684-1716","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josianne Gatt","key":"støttruppau","last":"Støttrup","locid":"cf999b24-fb74-420b-b42b-d48a114d16b1","name":"Støttrup, Josianne","name_org":"Støttrup, Josianne Gatt","orcid":"0000-0002-0921-8773","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexandros","key":"kokkalispau","last":"Kokkalis","locid":"b058635a-8085-42bd-91e2-2e8f47f01885","name":"Kokkalis, Alexandros","orcid":"0000-0002-9662-6272","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elliot John","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","locid":"6e9adf26-4e21-4d56-9ac8-2676ad255957","name":"Brown, Elliot John","orcid":"0000-0003-0862-1904","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"mosegaardpau","last":"Mosegaard","locid":"01482533-590c-4ffd-b236-9baf6fe84c8d","name":"Mosegaard, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7045-9456","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b954c930-484f-4d22-8431-f896942080ec","name":"Nielsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9683-9262","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Casper W.","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"ac57118e-9cfd-4e2f-aeb4-bcdb72c529a8","name":"Berg, Casper Willestofte","name_org":"Berg, Casper W.","orcid":"0000-0002-3812-5269","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"bojepau","last":"Boje","locid":"06dba873-ab1b-4838-9d60-25ae7de754c8","name":"Boje, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-9034-4605","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.11581/60e738ef-cc68-424f-9c49-14411651757e","issn":["13958216"],"issue":"473-2024","pages":"74","place":"Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark","publisher":"DTU Aqua","repno":"DTU Aqua-rapport, 473-2024","series":"DTU Aqua-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-60e738ef-cc68-424f-9c49-14411651757e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved knowledge for management of flatfish stocks in Danish waters (FORFLAD)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798050","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Patients with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) associated interstitial lung disease (ILD) or emphysema have an increased mortality compared to RA patients without respiratory disease. The study aimed to determine the diagnostic accuracy of thoracic ultrasound (TUS) for detecting ILD in RA patients with respiratory symptoms. Methods: Patients with RA were systematically screened for pre-defined respiratory symptoms during routine outpatient follow-up. TUS was performed before high-resolution computed tomography (HRCT) and pulmonary function tests (PFT). TUS indicated ILD if either ≥10 B-lines or bilateral thickened and fragmented pleura were present. A blinded TUS expert evaluated the TUS clips. An ILD subspecialized radiologist assessed HRCT, and an experienced pulmonologist determined clinical diagnosis based on HRCT, PFT, journal audit, and MDT. Results: 77 participants (mean age 64.6 years (SD: 11.2 years), 52 (68 females) received HRCT <30 days after TUS. ILD was verified in 23 (30 and 13 (17 had emphysema. TUS had a sensitivity of 82.695 61.2 to 95.0) and a specificity of 51.995 37.8 to 65.7) for detecting ILD. In patients with emphysema, 10 out of 13 (77 had TUS findings indicating ILD. On HRCT, these emphysema patients had findings such as basal and sub-pleural bullae, bronchiolitis with peribronchiolar inflammation and/or oedema of the visceral pleura. Conclusions: TUS had a high sensitivity for detection of ILD in RA patients with respiratory symptoms. However, it had a low specificity. The clinical role of TUS in RA patients may be as a screening tool for detecting patients who should receive an HRCT.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sofíudóttir, Bjørk Khaliqi","Laursen, Christian B","Harders, Stefan","Lage-Hansen, Philip Rask","Nielsen, Sabrina Mai","Just, Søren Andreas","Christensen, Robin","Ellingsen, Torkell","Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-803120"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-11","place":"Wien, at","start":"2024-09-07","title":"European Respiratory Society Congress 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thoracic ultrasound findings and pulmonary diagnosis in rheumatoid arthritis with respiratory symptoms","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/13993003.congress-2024.OA1081","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-803120","ids":["sdu-ec821cb5-b155-41e7-b29a-bacf6c918fdf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BC1541B8797952BD88E839CD0D811A6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/13993003.congress-2024.OA1081","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Rheumatology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Frederiksberg Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørk Khaliqi","key":"sofíudóttirpau","last":"Sofíudóttir","locid":"510e357e-598e-486f-812f-951673410110","name":"Sofíudóttir, Bjørk Khaliqi","orcid":"0000-0002-5918-3206","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Borbjerg","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"333fc524-a408-42f4-885a-0fee79e488b9","name":"Laursen, Christian B","name_org":"Laursen, Christian Borbjerg","orcid":"0000-0001-6382-9906","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"harderspau","last":"Harders","name":"Harders, Stefan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"lagehansenpau","last":"Lage-Hansen","locid":"254f7e2c-8d35-4fea-8d87-19ddaf5afe9f","name":"Lage-Hansen, Philip Rask","name_org":"Lage-Hansen, Philip","orcid":"0000-0002-1449-254X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabrina Mai","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Sabrina Mai","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Andreas","key":"justpau","last":"Just","locid":"94aaa5ff-430a-4bdf-8d84-3248f247a78f","name":"Just, Søren Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-3946-5919","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Robin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torkell","key":"ellingsenpau","last":"Ellingsen","locid":"12189359-9c0f-4bf1-8b75-be844c75b85b","name":"Ellingsen, Torkell","orcid":"0000-0003-0426-4962","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Rømhild","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"bfd91489-501f-49d3-aa3b-d9e8ea9a77f0","name":"Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-4014","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/13993003.congress-2024.oa1081","issn":["09031936","13993003"],"issn_org":["09031936"],"issue":"suppl. 68","journal":"European Respiratory Journal","paperid":"OA1081","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"European Respiratory Journal","volume":"64"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ec821cb5-b155-41e7-b29a-bacf6c918fdf"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Thoracic ultrasound findings and pulmonary diagnosis in rheumatoid arthritis with respiratory symptoms","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-803120","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Ingrown toenail is a common condition with many different treatment options. This review finds evidence that mild cases can be treated safely with non-surgical methods like change of ill-fitted shoes and nail brace. With failure in non-surgical treatment or in more severe cases surgical methods can be performed with note to the risk of complications - most frequently infection and the risk of recurrence at 3-13%. This review does not find evidence to use oral antibiotics in the treatment in general.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Jerry Schou","Grim, Rasmus","Mortensen, Jakob Fyhring","Obionu, Kenneth Chukwuemeka","Overgaard, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810288"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nedgroet tånegl","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V01240046","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810288","identifier":[{"id":"39530441","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209480984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-85816144-54d3-4749-bf52-b426b5e4a3d7"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E614692FDBD3F100FD8C655BD1886BFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446773605/V01240046_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V01240046","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – Nykøbing F,"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Jerry Schou","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Jerry Schou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"grimpau","last":"Grim","name":"Grim, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Fyhring","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Jakob Fyhring","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kenneth Chukwuemeka","key":"obionupau","last":"Obionu","name":"Obionu, Kenneth Chukwuemeka","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"34af3e7b-4d90-4f73-8d48-711a386f47ae","name":"Overgaard, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39530441"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v01240046","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"39","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-85816144-54d3-4749-bf52-b426b5e4a3d7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nedgroet tånegl","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-810288","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background  Childhood obesity can have significant negative consequences for children’s wellbeing and long-term health. Prior school-based interventions to prevent child overweight and obesity have shown limited effects, highlighting the necessity for comprehensive approaches addressing complex drivers of childhood obesity. “Generation Healthy Kids” (GHK) is a multi-setting, multi-component intervention to promote healthy weight development, health and wellbeing in Danish children aged 6–11 years. This protocol describes the GHK main trial, which is a cluster-randomized trial evaluating effectiveness and implementation of the GHK intervention.  Methods  Twenty-four schools from the Capital, Zealand and Southern Denmark Regions are randomly allocated 1:1 to intervention or control. The intervention will run for two school years (18–20 months) from October 2023 to June 2025 and will include children in 1st–3rd grade (approx. n = 1,600). The intervention targets multiple settings, including families, schools, after-school clubs, and local communities. Within four focus areas–diet, physical activity, screen media use, and sleep habits–the intervention incorporates several fixed elements, including a school lunch program and three weekly sessions of physical activity at school. Furthermore, building on whole-systems thinking, the intervention encompasses co-created elements developed in collaboration with local stakeholders, e.g. municipalities, sports clubs and supermarkets. This part of the intervention emphasizes building local capacity and engagement to promote child health. Effectiveness data will be collected from participating children and families at baseline, and at the end of school year one (after 6–8 months) and school year two (after 18–20 months). The primary outcome is the change in fat mass, measured by air-displacement plethysmography, from baseline to end-of-study in the intervention group compared to the control group. This is supplemented with numerous secondary outcomes and other prespecified outcomes related to child health and wellbeing. Furthermore, thorough process evaluation will be performed.  Discussion  GHK combines evidence-based intervention elements targeting multiple settings with a whole-systems approach focusing on capacity building and stakeholder involvement. This novel approach holds promise as an innovative way to promote child health and wellbeing and prevent childhood obesity.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Thomsen, Louise T.","Pedersen, Jesper","Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","Krustrup, Peter","Grøntved, Anders","Krølner, Rikke","Nielsen, Glen","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Skovgaard, Thomas","Mølgaard, Christian","Hansen, Anders Blædel Gottlieb","Hoeeg, Didde","Larsen, Malte Nejst","Lund, Line","Melby, Paulina Sander","Pedersen, Natascha Holbæk","Troelsen, Jens","Nordsborg, Nikolai Baastrup","Toft, Ulla"],"cuid":["S02-089.25-785442"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Toft, Ulla"],"keyword":["Body Weight","Child","Denmark","Diet","Exercise","Female","Health Promotion methods","Humans","Male","Pediatric Obesity prevention control","School Health Services","Schools"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generation healthy kids protocol for a cluster randomized controlled trial of a multi component and multi setting intervention to promote healthy weight and wellbeing in 000000000006 000000000011 year old children in denmark","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0308142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.25-785442","identifier":[{"id":"39636875","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85211601181","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11620443","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4cba273c-a716-405a-950b-e36e3a599085","sdu-0639595b-d3d3-4b45-99e3-fec5b7c392d4"],"keyword":["Body Weight","Child","Denmark","Diet","Exercise","Female","Health Promotion/methods","Humans","Male","Pediatric Obesity/prevention & control","School Health Services","Schools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B56D166F0EEE16722CD2A1589F1A8932"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0308142","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/279228860/journal.pone.0308142.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416314140/journal.pone.0308142.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Mi