{"abstract":"This report constitutes a follow-up to the International Evaluation of the Scientific and Legal Basis for Nitrogen Reduction in the 3rd Danish River Basin Management Plan (RBMP3), which was finalised in October 2023. Two of the issues identified by the international evaluation panel included 1) the use of Chl-a target values in open intercalibrated water bodies and 2) the applicability of eelgrass depth limit in shallow water bodies leading to alternative methods for estimating Maximum Allowable nutrient Inputs (MAI) to Danish coastal waters. In addition, the methods for estimating riverine nutrient inputs to coastal waters have been revised, resulting in updated data for nitrogen loadings. In this report we assess the implications of updates for the MAI estimations and revise the MAI estimations used for the RBMP3 taking into account the scientific updates and alternative solutions resulting from the international evaluation. This report is financially supported by the Danish Environmental Protection Agency (DEPA) under the project “Second opinion phase III, strengthen model foundation”. While DEPA has commented a previous draft of the report, the content and recommendations are the sole responsibility of the authors.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Timmermann, Karen","Nielsen, Sophia Elisabeth Bardram","Christensen, Jesper","Erichsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-094.32-767452"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revision of maximum allowable nitrogen inputs applicable for the danish river basin management plan 000000002021 000000002027 rbmp000000000003 a follow up on the international evaluation","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/DTU.00000359","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.32-767452","ids":["au-538b75c4-ba64-4213-b929-ee268098c5ae","dtu-a9fe7591-ff32-4c9b-abe3-e00f0f85f285"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D32C887C6801E2FA719E63704A454941"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376174330/467-2024-Revision-of-maximum-allowable-nitrogen-inputs-applicable-for-RBMP3-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.11581/DTU.00000359","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aqua.dtu.dk/-/media/institutter/aqua/publikationer/rapporter-451-500/467-2024-revision-of-maximum-allowable-nitrogen-inputs-applicable-for-rbmp3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Coastal Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Applied Marine Ecology and Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"timmermannpau","last":"Timmermann","locid":"abfd7b7d-0497-46ec-a26c-ba1772c111df","name":"Timmermann, Karen","orcid":"0000-0001-5989-4692","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sophia E. B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"23ea2744-bcac-4e4f-b350-491426793334","name":"Nielsen, Sophia Elisabeth Bardram","name_org":"Nielsen, Sophia E. B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Philip Aagaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"147cb218-7cf3-41b6-9c16-3d636c6fe518","name":"Christensen, Jesper Philip Aagaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"erichsenpau","last":"Erichsen","name":"Erichsen, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.11581/dtu.00000359","issn":["13958216"],"issue":"467-2024","pages":"93","place":"Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark","publisher":"DTU Aqua","repno":"DTU Aqua-rapport, 467-2024","series":"DTU Aqua-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-538b75c4-ba64-4213-b929-ee268098c5ae","dtu-a9fe7591-ff32-4c9b-abe3-e00f0f85f285"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Revision of maximum allowable nitrogen inputs applicable for the Danish River Basin Management Plan 2021-2027 (RBMP3): A follow-up on the international evaluation","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.32-767452","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To determine the diagnostic accuracy of thoracic ultrasound (TUS) for detecting interstitial lung disease (ILD) in rheumatoid arthritis (RA) with respiratory symptoms. Methods: Individuals with RA visiting rheumatologic outpatient clinics in the Region of Southern Denmark were systematically screened for dyspnea, cough, recurrent pneumonia, prior severe pneumonia, or a chest x-ray indicating interstitial abnormalities. Eighty participants with a positive screening were consecutively included. Individuals were not eligible if they had a chest high-resolution computed tomography (HRCT) less than 12 months ago or were already diagnosed with ILD. A blinded TUS expert evaluated TUS, and TUS was registered as positive for ILD if at least 10 B-lines or bilateral thickened and fragmented pleura were present. The primary outcomes were TUS's sensitivity, specificity, and positive predictive value and negative predictive value. An ILD-specialized thoracic radiologist assessed HRCT, followed by a multidisciplinary team discussion, which was the reference standard. The accepted window of HRCT was less than 30 days after TUS was performed. Results: A total of 77 participants received HRCT less than 30 days after TUS, and 23 (30%) were diagnosed with ILD. TUS had a sensitivity of 82.6% (95% confidence interval [CI] 61.2%–95.0%) and a specificity of 51.9% (95% CI 37.8%–65.7%), corresponding to a positive predictive value of 42.2% (95% CI 27.7%–57.8%) and a negative predictive value of 87.5% (95% CI 71.0%–96.5%). Conclusion: To our knowledge, this prospective study is the first to use respiratory symptoms in RA as inclusion criteria. Systematic screening for respiratory symptoms combined with TUS can reduce the diagnostic delay of ILD in RA. (Figure presented.).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sofíudóttir, Bjørk K.","Harders, Stefan Walbom","Laursen, Christian B.","Lage-Hansen, Philip R.","Nielsen, Sabrina M.","Just, Søren A.","Christensen, Robin","Davidsen, Jesper R.","Ellingsen, Torkell"],"cuid":["S02-096.43-761746"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sofíudóttir, Bjørk K.","Sofíudóttir, Bjørk Khaliqi"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Arthritis Rheumatoid diagnostic imaging","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Lung Diseases Interstitial diagnostic imaging","Lung diagnostic imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Prospective Studies","Reproducibility of Results","Tomography X Ray Computed","Ultrasonography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detection of interstitial lung disease in rheumatoid arthritis by thoracic ultrasound a diagnostic test accuracy study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/acr.25351","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.43-761746","identifier":[{"id":"38622106","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85196661333","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5d8a7cfb-2dc6-417d-8f44-8b3b16ba16ff","sdu-7a3038ff-e952-4838-a28c-812d5445da22"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Arthritis, Rheumatoid/diagnostic imaging","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Lung Diseases, Interstitial/diagnostic imaging","Lung/diagnostic imaging","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Prospective Studies","Reproducibility of Results","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","Ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2AB5D702766CBEA44635E7910A3394BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"htt