{"abstract":"AIMS: The three correlated environmental exposures (air pollution, road traffic noise, and green space) have all been associated with the risk of myocardial infarction (MI). The present study aimed to analyse their independent and cumulative association with MI. METHODS AND RESULTS: In a cohort of all Danes aged 50 or older in the period 2005-17, 5-year time-weighted average exposure to fine particles (PM2.5), ultrafine particles, elemental carbon, nitrogen dioxide (NO2), and road traffic noise at the most and least exposed façades of residence was estimated. Green space around residences was estimated from land use maps. Cox proportional hazard models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) and 95% confidence interval (CI), and cumulative risk indices (CRIs) were calculated. All expressed per interquartile range. Models were adjusted for both individual and neighbourhood-level socio-demographic covariates. The cohort included 1 964 702 persons. During follow-up, 71 285 developed MI. In single-exposure models, all exposures were associated with an increased risk of MI. In multi-pollutant analyses, an independent association with risk of MI was observed for PM2.5 (HR: 1.026; 95% CI: 1.002-1.050), noise at most exposed façade (HR: 1.024; 95% CI: 1.012-1.035), and lack of green space within 150 m of residence (HR: 1.018; 95% CI: 1.010-1.027). All three factors contributed significantly to the CRI (1.089; 95% CI: 1.076-1.101). CONCLUSION: In a nationwide cohort study, air pollution, noise, and lack of green space were all independently associated with an increased risk of MI. The air pollutant PM2.5 was closest associated with MI risk.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Massling, Andreas","Khan, Jibran","Münzel, Thomas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-741948"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","University Medical Center Mainz","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Green space","Myocardial Infarction","Traffic noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concomitant exposure to air pollution green space and noise and risk of myocardial infarction a cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181263003","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research described in this article was conducted under contract to the Health Effects Institute (HEI), an organization jointly funded by the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) (Assistance Award No. R-82811201) and certain motor vehicle and engine manufacturers. The contents of this article do not necessarily reflect the views and policies of the EPA or the vehicle and engine manufacturers. The study funder was not involved in the design of the study; the collection, analysis, and interpretation of the data; and writing the paper and did not impose any restrictions regarding the publication of the paper."],"id":"S02-100.00-741948","identifier":[{"id":"37738461","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181263003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-95b579f1-7240-4635-b9dc-aa48f0eeb221","ruc-f976f81f-8473-42fe-a770-713dc80ef875"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Green space","Myocardial infarction","Traffic noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B4A9B0477937E18FA616957998092504"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"university medical center mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Mainz","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla A.","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise M.","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","name_org":"Frohn, Lise M.","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"masslingpau","last":"Massling","locid":"5bb9394c-7de2-4cb2-a79d-a5e2af778523","name":"Massling, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-8046-2798","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"münzelpau","last":"Münzel","name":"Münzel, Thomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37738461"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurjpc/zwad306","issn":["20474873","20474881"],"issn_org":["20474873"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","pages":"131-141","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181263003"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-95b579f1-7240-4635-b9dc-aa48f0eeb221","ruc-f976f81f-8473-42fe-a770-713dc80ef875"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Concomitant exposure to air pollution, green space and noise, and risk of myocardial infarction : a cohort study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-741948","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Prevalence of pulmonary embolism (PE) in patients referred to diagnostic imaging is decreasing, indicating a need for improving patient selection. The aim of this study was to assess reduction in referral to diagnostic imaging by integrating a bespoke ultrasound protocol and describe associated failure rate and adverse events in patients with suspected PE. Methods: In a randomized open-label multicentre trial spanning June 18, 2021, through Feb 1, 2023, adult patients with suspected PE and 1) a Wells score of 0–6 and elevated age-adjusted D-dimer or 2) Wells score >6 were randomly assigned 1:1 to direct diagnostic imaging (controls) or focused lung, cardiac, and deep venous ultrasound by unblinded investigators. Ultrasound could: 1) dismiss PE if no signs of PE and low clinical suspicion or an alternate diagnosis, 2) confirm PE in case of visible venous thrombus, ≥2 subpleural infarctions, McConnell's, or D-sign, or 3) refer to diagnostic imaging if neither category was fulfilled or a patient with confirmed PE by ultrasound required admission. Primary endpoint was proportion of patients referred to diagnostic imaging. Outcome assessors were not blinded to group assignment. All included participants were included in safety analyses. The trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov (NCT04882579). Findings: A total of 150 patients were recruited, of whom 73 were randomized to ultrasound. Among 77 controls referred to diagnostic imaging, 26 patients had PE confirmed. In the ultrasound group, 40 patients were referred to diagnostic imaging of whom 20 had PE, reducing referral for diagnostic imaging by 45.2% (95% CI: 34.3–56.6, p < 0.0001). Three further PEs were diagnosed by presence of a DVT. During 3-month follow-up, the number of patients who did not receive anticoagulation but was diagnosed with PE was two (4%; 95% CI: 1.1–13.5) and none (0%; 95% CI: 0.0–7.0) in the ultrasound and control group, respectively. Interpretation: Ultrasound substantially reduced referral to diagnostic imaging in suspected PE. Albeit with an unacceptable failure rate. Funding: University of Southern Denmark, Odense University Hospital, Master Carpenter Sophus Jacobsen and wife's foundation, Engineer K. A. Rhode and wife foundation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Falster, Casper","Mørkenborg, Mads Damgaard","Thrane, Mikkel","Clausen, Jesper","Arvig, Michael Dan","Brockhattingen, Kristoffer","Biesenbach, Peter","Paludan, Lasse","Nielsen, Rune Wiig","Huynh, Thi Anh Nhi","Poulsen, Mikael K.","Brabrand, Mikkel","Møller, Jacob E.","Posth, Stefan","Laursen, Christian B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-756225"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Falster, Casper"],"keyword":["Cardiology","Diagnosis","Emergency medicine","Pulmonary embolism","Pulmonology","Radiology","Respiratory medicine","Ultrasonography","Ultrasound","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"utility of ultrasound in the diagnostic work up of suspected pulmonary embolism an open label multicentre randomized controlled trial the prime study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lanepe.2024.100941","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-756225","identifier":[{"id":"85194415363","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39070742","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11281927","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-236295c2-6e94-4a98-ba0f-9ce31c7230cb","sdu-d9c0a8ff-6f06-49ec-8654-119ab153a57c"],