ull,"first":"Christian B.","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"333fc524-a408-42f4-885a-0fee79e488b9","name":"Laursen, Christian B","name_org":"Laursen, Christian B.","orcid":"0000-0001-6382-9906","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39070742"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lanepe.2024.100941","issn":["26667762"],"journal":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","paperid":"100941","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Regional Health - Europe","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194415363"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-236295c2-6e94-4a98-ba0f-9ce31c7230cb","sdu-d9c0a8ff-6f06-49ec-8654-119ab153a57c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Utility of ultrasound in the diagnostic work-up of suspected pulmonary embolism : an open-label multicentre randomized controlled trial (the PRIME study)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-756225","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Transportation noise has been linked with cardiometabolic outcomes, yet whether it is a risk factor for atrial fibrillation (AF) remains inconclusive. We aimed to assess whether transportation noise was associated with AF in a large, pooled Nordic cohort. Methods: We pooled data from 11 Nordic cohorts, totaling 161,115 participants. Based on address history from five years before baseline until end of follow-up, road, railway, and aircraft noise was estimated at a residential level. Incident AF was ascertained via linkage to nationwide patient registries. Cox proportional hazards models were utilized to estimate associations between running 5-year time-weighted mean transportation noise (Lden) and AF after adjusting for sociodemographics, lifestyle, and air pollution. Findings: We identified 18,939 incident AF cases over a median follow-up of 19.6 years. Road traffic noise was associated with AF, with a hazard ratio (HR) and 95% confidence interval (CI) of 1.02 (1.00–1.04) per 10-dB of 5-year mean time-weighted exposure, which changed to 1.03 (1.01–1.06) when implementing a 53-dB cut-off. In effect modification analyses, the association for road traffic noise and AF appeared strongest in women and overweight and obese participants. Compared to exposures ≤40 dB, aircraft noise of 40.1–50 and > 50 dB were associated with HRs of 1.04 (0.93–1.16) and 1.12 (0.98–1.27), respectively. Railway noise was not associated with AF. We found a HR of 1.19 (1.02–1.40) among people exposed to noise from road (≥45 dB), railway (>40 dB), and aircraft (>40 dB) combined. Interpretation: Road traffic noise, and possibly aircraft noise, may be associated with elevated risk of AF. Funding: NordForsk.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Thacher, Jesse D.","Roswall, Nina","Ögren, Mikael","Pyko, Andrei","Åkesson, Agneta","Oudin, Anna","Rosengren, Annika","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Eriksson, Charlotta","Segersson, David","Rizzuto, Debora","Helte, Emilie","Andersson, Eva M.","Aasvang, Gunn Marit","Engström, Gunnar","Gudjonsdottir, Hrafnhildur","Selander, Jenny","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Leander, Karin","Overvad, Kim","Mattisson, Kristoffer","Eneroth, Kristina","Stucki, Lara","Barregard, Lars","Stockfelt, Leo","Albin, Maria","Simonsen, Mette K.","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Jousilahti, Pekka","Tiittanen, Pekka","Ljungman, Petter L.S.","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Gustafsson, Susanna","Yli-Tuomi, Tarja","Cole-Hunter, Thomas","Lanki, Timo","Lim, Youn Hee","Andersen, Zorana J.","Pershagen, Göran","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-767987"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thacher, Jesse D."],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Biomedicum Helsinki","Center for Occupational and Environmental Medicine","City of Malmö","Danderyds Hospital","Environment and Health Administration","Environmental Department of the City of Malmö","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","National Institute for Health and Welfare","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Region Stockholm","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Svensk kommun","Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute","Swedish National Board of Health and Welfare","Umeå University","University of Eastern Finland","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Aircraft noise","Arrhythmia","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac","Pooled cohort","Railway noise","Road traffic noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"revi