","Private Research","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","smv company (denmark)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-36e20316-953f-4b7e-8bf8-7d9b68312937","dtu-51f0d451-d77c-4b97-a324-cf22ebf8cf7f","ku-a31b4a17-dfc3-4b86-bc27-997244bc73ab","kum-f9506713-be49-427d-b3e5-d6d262522f75"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"100 ancient genomes show repeated population turnovers in Neolithic Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.15-793206","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Proton radiotherapy offers a dosimetric advantage compared to photon therapy in sparing normal tissue, but the clinical evidence for toxicity reductions in the treatment of head and neck cancer is limited. The Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA) has initiated the DAHANCA 35 randomised trial to clarify the value of proton therapy (NCT04607694). The DAHANCA 35 trial is performed in an enriched population of patients selected by an anticipated benefit of proton therapy to reduce the risk of late dysphagia or xerostomia based on normal tissue complication probability (NTCP) modelling. We present our considerations on the trial design and a test of the selection procedure conducted before initiating the randomised study.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Friborg, Jeppe","Jensen, Kenneth","Eriksen, Jesper Grau","Samsøe, E.","Maare, C.","Farhadi, M.","Sibolt, P.","Nielsen, M.","Andersen, M.","Holm, Anne Ivalu Sander","Skyt, Peter Sandegaard","Smulders, Bob","Johansen, J.","Overgaard, Jens","Grau, Cai","Hansen, Christian Rønn"],"cuid":["S04-095.74-793092"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Friborg, J.","Friborg, Jeppe"],"keyword":["Head and Neck Neoplasms radiotherapy","Head and neck cancer","Humans","Probability","Proton Therapy methods","Proton radiotherapy","Protons","Radiotherapy Dosage","Radiotherapy Intensity Modulated methods","Radiotherapy Planning Computer Assisted","Trial design"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"considerations for study design in the dahanca 000000000035 trial of protons versus photons for head and neck cancer","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.radonc.2023.109958","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The DAHANCA 35 trial is supported by Novo Nordisk Foundation, Denmark NNF18OC0034612"],"id":"S04-095.74-793092","identifier":[{"id":"85176078117","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37871751","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f69ba38d-a32b-4362-a016-e7647093ffcb","au-0379fed6-4f8c-428a-82ef-e1d0a72814a6","ku-b305d7a3-294b-42da-be94-f5d85e782045","sdu-e0a57462-37bf-4c86-8b77-ca70ebf21d7a"],"keyword":["Head and Neck Neoplasms/radiotherapy","Head and neck cancer","Humans","Photons/therapeutic use","Probability","Proton Therapy/methods","Proton radiotherapy","Protons","Radiotherapy Dosage","Radiotherapy Planning, Computer-Assisted","Radiotherapy, Intensity-Modulated/methods","Trial design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-D4C93378FD9AE55EC19616FD5AE585F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/676431244/Friborg_et_al._2024_._Considerations_for_study_design_in_the_DAHANCA_35_trial_of_protons_versus_photons_for_head_and_neck_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/427576440/1_s2.0_S0167814023898528_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.radonc.2023.109958","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/255333385/1-s2.0-S0167814023898528-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU