79-4021-b35e-b6138c984590"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Luftkvalitet 2022 : Status for den nationale luftkvalitetsovervågning","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736991","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Metalenses are flat lenses, where sub-wavelength, so-called meta-atoms manipulate the electric field to perform a given lens function. Compared to traditional lenses, the two main drawbacks of metalenses are their achromatic limitations and low efficiencies. While an abundance of simulations show that efficiencies above 90% are attainable for low numerical apertures (NA), experimental reports showing such high efficiencies are limited. Here, we use electron-beam lithography (EBL) to realize a set of lenses with varying NA from 0.08 to 0.93. The low NAs were expected to fit the model, and the higher NAs determine the validity range of the model. We find that measured efficiencies above 92% for NA = 0.24 are achievable, and that a slight modification of the simulation model extends its validility to NA = 0.6. Based on our results, we discuss that the lower efficiencies reported in the literature are caused by low-fidelity manufacturing, closing the efficiency gap between measurements and simulation in metalens fabrication.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Egede Johansen, Villads","Gür, Uǧur Meriç","Martínez-Llinás, Jade","Fly Hansen, Jesper","Samadi, Akbar","Skak Vestergaard Larsen, Maria","Nielsen, Theodor","Mattinson, Fredrik","Schmidlin, Moritz","Mortensen, N. Asger","Quaade, Ulrich J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-740761"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Quaade, Ulrich J."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nanoscale precision brings experimental metalens efficiencies on par with theoretical promises","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42005-024-01598-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-740761","identifier":[{"id":"85189933354","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a36b4ef4-e0ea-4d2b-94f8-7404e6f2dcd5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FB4C55254007DA9AADC8D09A1FB98142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42005-024-01598-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/259245553/s42005-024-01598-6_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["NIL Technology ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Danish Institute for Advanced Study","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), Center for Polariton-driven Light-Matter Interactions (POLIMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Villads","key":"egedejohansenpau","last":"Egede Johansen","name":"Egede Johansen, Villads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uǧur Meriç","key":"gürpau","last":"Gür","name":"Gür, Uǧur Meriç","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jade","key":"martínezllináspau","last":"Martínez-Llinás","name":"Martínez-Llinás, Jade","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"flyhansenpau","last":"Fly Hansen","name":"Fly Hansen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Akbar","key":"samadipau","last":"Samadi","name":"Samadi, Akbar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"skakvestergaardlarsenpau","last":"Skak Vestergaard Larsen","name":"Skak Vestergaard Larsen, Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Theodor","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Theodor","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrik","key":"mattinsonpau","last":"Mattinson","name":"Mattinson, Fredrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Moritz","key":"schmidlinpau","last":"Schmidlin","name":"Schmidlin, Moritz","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"N. Asger","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f3505872-a266-4e19-a0fe-6ce190dd9eca","name":"Mortensen, N. Asger","orcid":"0000-0001-7936-6264","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrich J.","key":"quaadepau","last":"Quaade","name":"Quaade, Ulrich J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s42005-024-01598-6","issn":["23993650"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications Physics","paperid":"123","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Communications Physics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189933354"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","nil technology aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a36b4ef4-e0ea-4d2b-94f8-7404e6f2dcd5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Nanoscale precision brings experimental metalens efficiencies on par with theoretical promises","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-740761","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) is performed increasingly, but long-term follow-up imaging data are lacking. AIMS: The aim of this study was to evaluate the safety and durability of the Amplatzer Amulet device >4 years after LAAO. METHODS: This was a prospective observational cohort study including 52 patients implanted with the Amplatzer Amulet device at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark. A >4-year follow-up cardiac computed tomography (CT) scan after LAAO was performed and compared with the results from the 2-month and 12-month scans. The primary outcome was left atrial appendage (LAA) sealing based on distal LAA contrast patency and peridevice leakage (PDL), stratified into complete occlusion (grade 0 [G0]) and grade 1-3 leakage (G1-3), respectively. Secondary outcomes were low- and high-grade hypoattenuated thickening (HAT), device-related thrombosis (DRT) and device durability. RESULTS: The median (interquartile range [IQR]) follow-up time from LAAO to the latest CT scan was 5.8 years (4.5; 6.3). At 2-month (n=52), 12-month (n=27) and >4-year CT follow-ups (n=52), rates of both complete occlusion (33%, 37%, 35%) and G2 leaks (52%, 52%, 48%) remained stable. Rates of G1 leaks varied (14%, 4%, 6%) and G3 leaks rose (2%, 7%, 12%) from earliest to latest follow-up. The median left atrial (LA) volume increased from 127 mL (96; 176) to 144 mL (108; 182) and 147 mL (107; 193). No DRT was found. The structural device integrity was preserved. CONCLUSIONS: This study indicates a stable LAA sealing status throughout the follow-up period, emphasising the importance of the procedural result in avoiding PDL. Few patients displayed PDL progression, which might partly be related to LA remodelling with increasing volume. The long-term device durability appears excellent. Larger studies are warranted to confirm these findings.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Tiroke, Lasse Hubertus","Kramer, Anders","Poulsen, Mette Wørmer","Jensen, Caroline Damsgaard","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Korsholm, Kasper","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743550"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Atrial Appendage diagnostic imaging","Atrial Fibrillation surgery","Cardiac Catheterization methods","Female","Femoral","Follow Up Studies","Humans","LAA closure","MSCT","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Septal Occluder Device","Stroke","Tomography X Ray Computed","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term cardiac computed tomography follow up after left atrial appendage occlusion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4244/EIJ-D-23-00802","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-743550","identifier":[{"id":"38840576","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11145311","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195333602","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-02eede37-c828-4bb5-9c33-7463ea4b9da1"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Atrial Appendage/diagnostic imaging","Atrial Fibrillation/surgery","Cardiac Catheterization/methods","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","LAA closure","MSCT","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Septal Occluder Device","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","Treatment Outcome","femoral","stroke","transseptal"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB1F3BA0B2A4DFD2E44C40FD0F5554BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4244/EIJ-D-23-00802","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse Hubertus","key":"tirokelassehubertuspau","last":"Tiroke","locid":"ad27c457-bb57-44b1-a4bc-948e569ac971","name":"Tiroke, Lasse Hubertus","orcid":"0000-0002-2659-9598","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"krameranderspau","last":"Kramer","locid":"be3123b5-5f55-4c8a-930c-f0f39cbc2981","name":"Kramer, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5546-8693","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Wørmer","key":"poulsenmettewørmerpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"399ca143-b3ab-4fea-b78e-6ec1bf588a9e","name":"Poulsen, Mette Wørmer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Caroline Damsgaard","key":"jensencarolinedamsgaardpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"186c85b9-a5e8-4300-9f40-9c04d03c5ddb","name":"Jensen, Caroline Damsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenjespermøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardbjarnelindepau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmkasperpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskjenserikpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38840576"],"pub":{"doi":"10.4244/eij-d-23-00802","issn":["1774024X","19696213"],"issn_org":["1774024X"],"issue":"11","journal":"EuroIntervention","publisher":"Europa Group","status":"p","title":"EuroIntervention","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195333602"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-02eede37-c828-4bb5-9c33-7463ea4b9da1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long-term cardiac computed tomography follow-up after left atrial appendage occlusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743550","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Accessory mitral valve tissue (AMVT) is a rare congenital cardiac anomaly often diagnosed in childhood and is associated with left ventricular outflow tract obstruction. We present a case of an asymptomatic adult man in his 60s with an incidental finding of AMVT. A transthoracic echocardiography and transesophageal echocardiography initially raised suspicion of AMVT, but the precise origin of the anomaly was established using a dynamic 4-dimensional cardiac computed tomography scan, ultimately confirming the diagnosis. This case highlights the potential value of multimodality imaging in the diagnosis of AMVT and rules out other differential diagnoses.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Christian Byskov","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","Jensen, Morten Kvistholm","Tang, Mariann","Løgstrup, Brian Bridal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745701"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Christian Byskov"],"keyword":["Aortic Valve","Aortic regurgitation","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac magnetic resonance","Cardiac surgery","Congenital heart disease","Diagnostic techniques","Direct oral anticoagulant","Echocardiography","Left ventricular outflow tract","Transesophageal echocardiography","Transthoracic echocardiography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimodal imaging for the diagnosis of accessory mitral valve tissue","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7326/AIMCC.2023.0738","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745701","identifier":[{"id":"85196662516","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au