{"abstract":"This case report describes laryngeal oedema occurring in a 35-year-old woman with chronic bowel-associated dermatosis-arthritis syndrome, and stenosis of the left main bronchus. The oedema was attributed to persistent cough exacerbated by delayed treatment and intubation-related irritation. Evaluations ruled out inflammatory, autoimmune, and malignant causes. Literature lacks on specific descriptions of cough-induced laryngeal oedema, emphasizing the need for a multidisciplinary approach and early intervention in complex cases to prevent severe hospitalizations in patients with known serious conditions and symptom exacerbation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Martine S.","Borup, Maria Bisgaard","Kjeldsen, Jens","Stenger, Michael","Madsen, Anders Rørbæk","Schmidt, Henrik","Ellingsen, Torkell","Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782975"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Martine S."],"keyword":["Adult","Cough etiology","Female","Humans","Intubation Intratracheal adverse effects","Respiration Artificial adverse effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hosteinduceret respiratorkrævende larynxødem","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V12230792","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782975","identifier":[{"id":"85197724780","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38953687","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-3a0575f7-ecec-42ce-8446-f180b3e8b543"],"keyword":["Adult","Cough/etiology","Female","Humans","Intubation, Intratracheal/adverse effects","Laryngeal Edema/etiology","Respiration, Artificial/adverse effects"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55603C18DCD1064A8BCD922625944783"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275077110/V12230792_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V12230792","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Odense Respiratory Research Unit (ODIN)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martine Siw","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a37263da-160f-410f-84ee-d565008e7134","name":"Nielsen, Martine S.","name_org":"Nielsen, Martine Siw","orcid":"0000-0002-5999-3372","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Bisgaard","key":"boruppau","last":"Borup","locid":"2279e795-daa2-4b2e-8310-9876fb1698b2","name":"Borup, Maria Bisgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"4893b496-ebc1-4498-92aa-836500b4cb45","name":"Kjeldsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8148-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"stengerpau","last":"Stenger","locid":"736bd795-eb91-41ee-ad81-fdf944151b2d","name":"Stenger, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3605-1785","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rørbækmadsenpau","last":"Rørbæk Madsen","locid":"686fd288-67ef-4a05-9e17-01d4cef47b86","name":"Madsen, Anders Rørbæk","name_org":"Rørbæk Madsen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torkell Juulsgaard","key":"ellingsenpau","last":"Ellingsen","locid":"12189359-9c0f-4bf1-8b75-be844c75b85b","name":"Ellingsen, Torkell","name_org":"Ellingsen, Torkell Juulsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0426-4962","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Rømhild","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"bfd91489-501f-49d3-aa3b-d9e8ea9a77f0","name":"Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-4014","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38953687"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v12230792","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"20","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V12230792","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197724780"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3a0575f7-ecec-42ce-8446-f180b3e8b543"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hosteinduceret respiratorkrævende larynxødem","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782975","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background and Aim: In the Nordic countries, about one in five children aged 5-18 years are affected by obesity. This review study analyses the patterns of the scientific publications on childhood obesity in the Nordic region to offer insights into the scientific progress and guide future strategic decisions for researchers and policymakers. Material and Methods: Using Python version 3.12, we conducted a visualization analysis of Nordic childhood obesity literature from Scopus, covering publication up to February 2024. This analysis included trends of scientific outputs, citations, patterns, and collaboration network, and leading institutions. Results: In Nordic countries 4,990 documents were published from 1963-2024. A consistent increase was identified in publication, with a notable rise in collaborative studies since 1981. A strong partnership was noted between Denmark and Sweden, as well as between Sweden and Finland. Iceland showed fewer collaborations compared to its Nordic counterparts. Top contributing institutions included Karolinska Institute (Sweden) and University of Copenhagen (Denmark), with significant centrality forming across the region. Denmark, Sweden, and Finland emerge as the most central countries in international collaborations. The research themes included understanding the prevalence, determinants, and outcomes associated with obesity, while recent years showed a shift toward exploring lifestyle factors contributing to childhood obesity and strategies for prevention and management. Highly cited publications primarily focused on public health interventions and policies, indicating a growing impact in these fields. However, areas such as \"sedentary behavior\" and \"diet\" in connection with long-term health outcomes received less attention, suggesting opportunities for future research to explore these links. Conclusion: Despite the ascending trends in research outputs within this field, there is a need to enhance collaborative efforts and explore the above gaps related to behavior change and food. We encourage policymakers to allocate resources that fills these gaps to better support future health preventive interventions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Baygi, Fereshteh","Gohari, Kimiya","Djalalinia, Shirin","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783284"],"event":{"end":"2024-11-02","place":"Nyborg , dk","start":"2024-11-01","title":"Annual Obesity Meeting: The Danish Association for the Study of Obesity","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Baygi, Fereshteh"],"country":["Iran","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Ministry of Health and Medical Education","Non-Communicable Diseases Research Center","Tehran University of Medical Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"past present and future of nordic research on childhood obesity","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-783284","ids":["sdu-74607f58-c0d3-4cd4-a913-c78cebace72d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-29FDA34745E2162128836ABAC33EAD5F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ir","key":"tehran university of medical sciences","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Tehran University of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ir","key":"ministry of health and medical education","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Ministry of Health and Medical Education","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ir","key":"non communicable diseases research center","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Non-Communicable Diseases Research Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fereshteh","key":"baygipau","last":"Baygi","locid":"82ac54a3-f35a-4ee6-85dc-362c9e160ee9","name":"Baygi, Fereshteh","orcid":"0000-0002-9260-2281","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kimiya","key":"goharipau","last":"Gohari","name":"Gohari, Kimiya","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Shirin","key":"djalaliniapau","last":"Djalalinia","name":"Djalalinia, Shirin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Reffstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7b0b955e-4090-479a-8bef-6fd6ad983680","name":"Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2412-5989","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-74607f58-c0d3-4cd4-a913-c78cebace72d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Past, Present, and Future of Nordic Research on Childhood Obesity","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783284","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to establish a porcine model of urinary tract infection (UTI) with gram-positive uropathogens. Ten female domestic pigs were experimentally inoculated with human UTI isolates of Enterococcus faecalis (n = 3), Staphylococcus saprophyticus (n = 3), or Staphylococcus aureus (n = 4) and followed with regular urine samples. Bladders and kidneys were aseptically removed at termination (5-7 days post infection) and assessed by gross pathology and bacterial enumeration. Enterococcus faecalis (n = 3 of 3) and S. aureus (n = 2 of 4) successfully colonized the pig bladders. Inoculation with S. saprophyticus never resulted in detectable bacteriuria. All infected pigs had cleared the infection spontaneously before termination. Surprisingly, three (of four) pigs inoculated with S. aureus led to spontaneous infection with opportunistic pathogens. Also, one pig colonized with E. faecalis resulted in spontaneous infection with E. coli. In conlusion, the pig supports experimental UTI with E. faecalis for up to 24 h but not prolonged infection. S. aureus and S. saprophyticus fails to cause UTI in pigs and other animals should be considered for studying these pathogens.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Stærk, Kristian","Heidtmann, Christoffer Vogsen","Hjelmager, Janni Søvsø","Ewald, Jesper Dupont","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","Nielsen, Poul","Andersen, Thomas Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783479"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stærk, Kristian"],"keyword":["Animals","Disease Models Animal","Enterococcus faecalis isolation purification","Female","Gram Positive Bacterial Infections microbiology","Kidney microbiology","Staphylococcal Infections microbiology","Staphylococcus aureus pathogenicity","Swine","Swine Diseases microbiology","Urinary Bladder microbiology","Urinary Tract Infections microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the infectious capacity of enterococcus faecalis staphylococcus aureus and staphylococcus saprophyticus in a porcine model of urinary tract infection","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apm.13469","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783479","identifier":[{"id":"39295304","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85204474034","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-99598dc0-69b6-48dc-a122-3de6d74426f9"],"keyword":["Animals","Disease Models, Animal","Enterococcus faecalis/isolation & purification","Female","Gram-Positive Bacterial Infections/microbiology","Kidney/microbiology","Staphylococcal Infections/microbiology","Staphylococcus aureus/pathogenicity","Staphylococcus saprophyticus/isolation & purification","Swine","Swine Diseases/microbiology","Urinary Bladder/microbiology","Urinary Tract Infections/microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D1F5B936AC2C09592148330AF48D0258"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275033312/APMIS_-_2024_-_St_rk_-_The_infectious_capacity_of_Enterococcus_faecalis_Staphylococcus_aureus_and_Staphylococcus.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apm.13469","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkkristianpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer Vogsen","key":"heidtmannchristoffervogsenpau","last":"Heidtmann","locid":"10aa0c3f-5e74-4c93-80c5-b714c11ea6f0","name":"Heidtmann, Christoffer Vogsen","orcid":"0000-0002-2579-3938","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janni Søvsø","key":"hjelmagerjannisøvsøpau","last":"Hjelmager","locid":"1a2acd4a-2a00-44d0-9c18-279cadb1e28d","name":"Hjelmager, Janni Søvsø","orcid":"0000-0001-7486-2023","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Dupont","key":"ewaldjesperdupontpau","last":"Ewald","locid":"d73bb185-6ab0-4185-86db-157f56301f5a","name":"Ewald, Jesper Dupont","orcid":"0000-0002-3452-2291","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Uhd","key":"nielsencarstenuhdpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"69a90973-6315-4248-a49e-c6e0413b526a","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","orcid":"0000-0001-5776-6865","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"nielsenpoulpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a0f6be7e-096f-4971-bc4c-6f83a2ed85f2","name":"Nielsen, Poul","orcid":"0000-0001-7946-311X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Emil","key":"andersenthomasemilpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"87fae7cd-ed6a-4d21-80cc-e13da9f91099","name":"Andersen, Thomas Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-9453-1141","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39295304"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apm.13469","issn":["09034641","0903465X"],"issn_org":["09034641"],"issue":"11","journal":"APMIS","pages":"807-813","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":