{"abstract":"This paper presents the application of a recently developed framework for nonlinear input-state estimation, namely a Finite Element (FE)-aided Kalman Filter, for the estimation of the nonlinear response of an offshore jacket structure subjected to strong waves and experiencing structural damage. The outcome of the framework consists of estimated dynamic responses and of nonlinear FE analysis outputs. The latter can be used for the identification of the structural damage, which can then be compared with the true one. Two applications are presented in this paper: one considering only acceleration measurements and one considering acceleration and velocity measurements.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Caglio, Luigi","Sadeqi, Amirali","Stang, Henrik","Tychsen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jurgen Svejgaard","Katsanos, Evangelos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789299"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Damage identification","Nonlinear finite element model","Nonlinear system","State estimation","Structural health monitoring","Unknown input"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"damage identification for offshore structure via fe aided kalman filter","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17736/ijope.2024.jc917","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789299","identifier":[{"id":"85216204265","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001382147000001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-bad3ec5a-ed9e-4d52-b5d9-d9f15d5c549a"],"keyword":["Augmented Extended Kalman Filter","Damage identification","Nonlinear finite element model","Nonlinear system","State estimation","Structural health monitoring","Unknown input"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9497D303F66A6847C424671A2AD92CB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17736/ijope.2024.jc917","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering and Structural Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Total Energies EP Danmark A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luigi","key":"cagliopau","last":"Caglio","locid":"970db115-af4f-4368-b3a3-70bd7b206146","name":"Caglio, Luigi","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-2490","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amirali","key":"sadeqipau","last":"Sadeqi","locid":"0db09fbe-c91a-4442-b988-999f6de405d2","name":"Sadeqi, Amirali","orcid":"0000-0001-6443-2425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"stangpau","last":"Stang","locid":"57fe0e89-5130-43bb-a270-b38b7f8b885e","name":"Stang, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5812-4028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"tychsenpau","last":"Tychsen","name":"Tychsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jurgen Svejgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jurgen Svejgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evangelos","key":"katsanospau","last":"Katsanos","locid":"66c07f61-0ded-4f95-aa15-239b7f0b7480","name":"Katsanos, Evangelos","orcid":"0000-0003-2574-5327","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17736/ijope.2024.jc917","issn":["10535381"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Offshore and Polar Engineering","pages":"344-351","publisher":"International Society of Offshore and Polar Engineers","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Offshore and Polar Engineering","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216204265"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","total energies ep danmark a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bad3ec5a-ed9e-4d52-b5d9-d9f15d5c549a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Damage Identification for Offshore Structure via FE-aided Kalman Filter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789299","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A tool for increasing the range of Brillouin optical time domain reflectometry (BOTDR) is distributed in-line Raman amplification. In this article, we model and experimentally verify how a combination of Raman pump depletion, pump-probe walk-off and self- and cross-phase modulation lead to a shift of the Brillouin spectrum, ultimately inducing an error in the sensor reading. The induced error is up to approximately 7 MHz (approx. 7 $^{\\circ }$C) for standard BOTDR parameters. We numerically model the propagation of the fields in the fiber using standard propagation equations, and by considering only spontaneous Brillouin scattering as the source of the back-scattered field, we find an expression of the Brillouin spectrum. By using standard parameters of a BOTDR setup, we show how there is a tradeoff between Raman amplifier gain and the spectrally induced error. By comparing the model to experiments, we find that the measurements show the same trend as the simulated spectra.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Vandborg, Mads Holmark","Mathew, Neethu Mariam","Christensen, Jesper","Joy, Tomin","Allousch, M. Ali","Marx, Benjamin","Grüner-Nielsen, Lars","Rishøj, Lars Søgaard","Rottwitt, Karsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789404"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luna Innovations Germany GmbH"],"keyword":["Optical fiber amplifiers","Optical fiber sensors","Optical fibers","Probes","Raman scattering","Stimulated emission","Temperature measurement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DFM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DFM","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling the brillouin spectrum in raman amplifier assisted brillouin otdr","src":["dtu"