{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION. In 2021, administration of β&;-agonist in the ambulance changed from nebuliser to spacer in the North Denmark Region. We aimed to quantify the effectiveness of the switch by comparing 1) dyspnoea score, 2) median pCO2 , pH, and paO2 and 3) vital signs. METHODS. We conducted a quality assessment study including adults treated in the ambulance with a β&;-agonist from 2018 to 2022 in the North Denmark Region. Prehospital vital signs, dyspnoea scores (0-10) and medicine administration data were collected from the electronic prehospital medical record. Blood gas analyses were collected from the clinical laboratory information system. RESULTS. A total of 6,521 patient encounters were included, 70% received β&;-agonist by nebuliser and 30% by spacer. Dyspnoea scores were recorded in 45%, arterial blood gas analysis in 62%. The median (interquartile range) last dyspnoea score was 4 (3-6) in both groups, p = 0.79. The nebuliser group had a higher median paCO2 (6.0 versus 5.8, p < 0.001), a lower pH (7.38 versus 7.40, p < 0.001), a higher paO2 (9.20 versus 9.00, p < 0.001), and a higher last measured mean pulse (99 versus 97, p = 0.001) than the spacer group. CONCLUSIONS. Patients receiving β&;-agonist by spacer had similar relief of dyspnoea as those who received the medicine by nebuliser. Patients using the nebuliser had a higher median paCO2 , a lower pH and a higher pulse rate than patients using the spacer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","Nielsen, Marc Trunjer Kusk","Søltoft, Jesper Lolk","Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","Krarup, Anne Lund","Gamst, Jacob Kjær"],"cuid":["S02-095.71-751600"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","Dahl Christiansen, Charlotte"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Emergency Medical Services, North Denmark Region"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prehospital β agonist administration via spacer versus nebuliser","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A01240041","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.71-751600","identifier":[{"id":"85201665337","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40116450","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8e556739-8863-46d3-91ae-3063ce7ee2a5","sdu-773bf179-852a-4738-9c2e-32e224efd802"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E28A6827AA5D8E56B42CAF6A53C47F4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A01240041","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/734251076/Christiansen_et_al._2024_._Prehospital_-agonist_administration_via_spacer_versus_nebuliser.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/268778257/A01240041_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Emergency Medicine and Trauma Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Clinical Microbiology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Emergency Medical Services, North Denmark Region"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Dahl","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"4e6c73fe-0a4e-4ed3-a073-63c990b8bd27","name":"Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"dahlchristiansenpau","last":"Dahl Christiansen","name":"Dahl Christiansen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"trunjerkusknielsenpau","last":"Trunjer Kusk Nielsen","locid":"1f7690d9-c93e-4437-8890-83f03f03f528","name":"Trunjer Kusk Nielsen, Marc","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Lolk","key":"søltoftpau","last":"Søltoft","locid":"9be6dfbf-45ef-4cee-b0b4-cbd9ddbdaaef","name":"Søltoft, Jesper Lolk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erika Frischknecht","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c27dead8-d244-4565-b33a-c15f420f389b","name":"Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","orcid":"0000-0003-3673-9694","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Lund","key":"kraruppau","last":"Krarup","locid":"05957add-3c70-4106-9e06-6db64be7129f","name":"Krarup, Anne Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2228-7132","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Kjær","key":"gamstpau","last":"Gamst","locid":"f231c1bd-c358-4261-a6dd-d640a584a246","name":"Gamst, Jacob Kjær","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40116450"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/a01240041","issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"8","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A01240041","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201665337"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8e556739-8863-46d3-91ae-3063ce7ee2a5","sdu-773bf179-852a-4738-9c2e-32e224efd802"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prehospital β₂-agonist administration via spacer versus nebuliser","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.71-751600","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD) are susceptible to vascular calcification and vitamin K deficiency. Matrix gla protein (MGP) is a potent inhibitor of calcification requiring vitamin K for activation. Inactive MGP, i.e. dephosphorylated uncarboxylated MGP (dp-ucMGP), is frequently elevated in CKD along with protein induced by vitamin K absence (PIVKA-II). We investigated whether dp-ucMGP and PIVKA-II are useful markers of aortic calcification in CKD. Methods: Patients with normal or reduced kidney function underwent a non-contrast computed tomography scan of the entire aorta with subsequent blinded standard calcification scoring of the aortic wall ad modum Agatston. Blood samples were analyzed for plasma concentrations of dp-ucMGP and PIVKA-II. Results: 141 patients (104 with CKD stage 3–5) were included. In patients with/without CKD median (interquartile range) were dp-ucMGP 543 (503–744)/1078 (835–1682) pmol/l (P < 0.01); PIVKA-II 19.3 (16.3–23.5)/21.8 (17.2–36.8) ng/ml (P = 0.33) and aortic Agatston scores 1644 (729–4138)/7172 (2834–15360) (P < 0.01). Agatston score was positively associated with PIVKA-II (β = 0.71, P = 0.014, r2 = 0.04) and tended to be so with dp-ucMGP (β = 0.44, P = 0.08, r2 = 0.02). Age, estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) and smoking status were also associated with Agatston score and remained so, along with PIVKA-II, when adjusted for potential confounders. However, the association between age and aortic Agatston score was stronger than for PIVKA-II, eGFR and smoking-status. Conclusion: Vitamin K deficiency, as estimated through PIVKA-II, but not dp-ucMGP, is weakly associated with aortic Agatston score. Yet, as markers of aortic calcification, both were outperformed substantially by age, and neither surpassed smoking nor eGFR. ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT04114695.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nyvad, Jakob","Christensen, Kent Lodberg","Andersen, Gratien","Reinhard, Mark","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Madsen, Jonna Skov","Nielsen, Sebastian","Thomsen, Martin Bjergskov","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Peters, Christian Daugaard","Buus, Niels Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.72-767185"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nyvad, Jakob"],"keyword":["Aged","Ageing","Aorta","Aortic Diseases diagnostic imaging","Atherosclerosis","Biomarkers blood","Calcification","Calcium Binding Proteins blood","Chronic kidney disease","Extracellular Matrix Proteins blood","Female","Humans","Male","Matrix Gla protein","Middle Aged","Protein Precursors blood","Prothrombin","Renal Insufficiency Chronic blood","Vascular Calcification diagnostic imaging","Vitamin K dependent proteins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pivka ii but not dp ucmgp is associated with aortic calcification in chronic kidney disease","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12882-024-03876-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.72-767185","identifier":[{"id":"85210387139","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39604863","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11600904","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-035fef5c-353f-47fd-8dfd-80a6322e0c15","sdu-539d3abc-b597-430d-b29b-e76e1482b375"],"keyword":["Aged","Ageing","Aorta","Aortic Diseases/diagnostic imaging","Atherosclerosis","Biomarkers/blood","Calcification","Calcium-Binding Proteins/blood","Chronic kidney disease","Extracellular Matrix Proteins/blood","Female","Humans","Male","Matrix Gla Protein","Middle Aged","Protein Precursors/blood","Prothrombin","Renal Insufficiency, Chronic/blood","Vascula