ty of Southern Denmark"],"title":"An Albumin-Holliday Junction Biomolecular Modular Design for Programmable Multifunctionality and Prolonged Circulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735103","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Excess abdominal visceral adipose tissue (VAT) is associated with metabolic diseases and poor survival in colon cancer (CC). We assessed the impact of different types of CC surgery on changes in abdominal fat depots. Material and methods: Computed tomography (CT)-scans performed preoperative and 3 years after CC surgery were analyzed at L3-level for VAT, subcutaneous adipose tissue (SAT) and total adipose tissue (TAT) areas. We assessed changes in VAT, SAT, TAT and VAT/SAT ratio after 3 years and compared the changes between patients who had undergone left-sided and right-sided colonic resection in the total population and in men and women separately. Results: A total of 134 patients with stage I-III CC undergoing cancer surgery were included. Patients who had undergone left-sided colonic resection had after 3 years follow-up a 5% (95% CI: 2–9%, p < 0.01) increase in abdominal VAT, a 4% (95% CI: 2–6%, p < 0.001) increase in SAT and a 5% increase (95% CI: 2–7%, p < 0.01) in TAT. Patients who had undergone right-sided colonic resection had no change in VAT, but a 6% (95% CI: 4–9%, p < 0.001) increase in SAT and a 4% (95% CI: 1–7%, p < 0.01) increase in TAT after 3 years. Stratified by sex, only males undergoing left-sided colonic resection had a significant VAT increase of 6% (95% CI: 2–10%, p < 0.01) after 3 years. Conclusion: After 3 years follow-up survivors of CC accumulated abdominal adipose tissue. Notably, those who underwent left-sided colonic resection had increased VAT and SAT, whereas those who underwent right-sided colonic resection demonstrated solely increased SAT. [Figure not available: see fulltext.]","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kays Mohammed Ali, Younes","Dolin, Troels Gammeltoft","Damm Nybing, Janus","Lykke, Jakob","Hvid Linden, Frederik","Høgh-Schmidt, Erik","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Christensen, Jesper Frank","Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","Stenfatt Larsen, Jim","Madsbad, Sten","Johansen, Julia S.","Svane, Maria Saur","Lang Lehrskov, Louise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735598"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lang Lehrskov, Louise"],"keyword":["Colonic Neoplasms surgery","Female","Humans","Intra Abdominal Fat diagnostic imaging","Male","Obesity Abdominal complications","Obesity complications","Subcutaneous Fat","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"change in abdominal obesity after colon cancer surgery effects of left sided and right sided colonic resection","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41366-023-01445-8","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish Diabetes Association and the Danish Diabetes Academy, which is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation under grant number NNF17SA0031406. The Centre for Physical Activity Research (CFAS) is supported by TrygFonden (grants ID 101390, ID 20045, and ID 125132). The VELUX foundation (Grant project number 00018310, salary to TGD) is acknowledged. Chief physician Benny Vittrup is acknowledged for his important contribution to the REBECCA study."],"id":"S02-100.00-735598","identifier":[{"id":"85181255445","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38172335","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10978490","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-f7f4fd90-9076-4045-86d4-03a69ec6b7f9","sdu-408343ea-e949-4153-8514-7d19d8a2a3e6"],"keyword":["Colonic Neoplasms/surgery","Female","Humans","Intra-Abdominal Fat/diagnostic imaging","Male","Obesity, Abdominal/complications","Obesity/complications","Subcutaneous Fat","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB21E8039B6233FD240FFD8A60567ACD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/259713451/s41366-023-01445-8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387384947/s41366_023_01445_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41366-023-01445-8","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Younes","key":"kays