{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Aliotta, Giulia Erica","Tanaka, Ryusuke","Elberling, Jesper","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Lo Vecchio, Silvia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786219"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-09","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2024-08-05","title":"IASP 2024 World Congress on Pain","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antipruritic and anti inflammatory effect of ketamine cream on itch a pilot study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://posters.worldcongress2024.org/poster/antipruritic-and-anti-inflammatory-effect-of-ketamine-cream-on-itch-a-pilot-study/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-786219","ids":["aau-aeef4b98-0583-45ea-bcb1-4bb100f9b36e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-38BCED8DF152DBCDC0D0375B451AC72A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://posters.worldcongress2024.org/poster/antipruritic-and-anti-inflammatory-effect-of-ketamine-cream-on-itch-a-pilot-study/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Pain Neuroscience and Precision Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giulia Erica","key":"aliottapau","last":"Aliotta","locid":"efb82db6-80bc-4a13-8fda-f95c91b88a94","name":"Aliotta, Giulia Erica","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryusuke","key":"tanakapau","last":"Tanaka","locid":"eb208fdf-04e2-4043-941a-b40918f1a048","name":"Tanaka, Ryusuke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aeef4b98-0583-45ea-bcb1-4bb100f9b36e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Antipruritic and anti-inflammatory effect of ketamine cream on itch, a pilot study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786219","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Up to 20% of patients develop chronic pain after total knee arthroplasty (TKA), yet there is a scarcity of effective interventions for this population. Objective: To evaluate whether neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education were superior to pain neuroscience education alone for patients with chronic pain after TKA. Design, Setting, and Participants: A superiority randomized clinical trial was conducted at 3 outpatient clinics at Aalborg University Hospital in Denmark. Participants with moderate-to-severe average daily pain intensity and no signs of prosthesis failure at least 1 year after primary TKA were included. Participant recruitment was initiated on April 12, 2019, and completed on October 31, 2022. The 12-month follow-up was completed on March 21, 2023. Interventions: The study included 24 sessions of supervised neuromuscular exercise (2 sessions per week for 12 weeks) and 2 total sessions of pain neuroscience education (6 weeks between each session) or the same pain neuroscience education sessions alone. The interventions were delivered in groups of 2 to 4 participants. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was change from baseline to 12 months using the mean score of the Knee Injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score, covering the 4 subscales pain, symptoms, activity of daily living, and knee-related quality of life (KOOS 4; scores range from 0 to 100, with higher scores indicating better outcomes). The outcome assessors and statistician were blinded. All randomized participants were included in the intention-to-treat analysis. Results: Among the 69 participants (median age, 67.2 years [IQR, 61.2-71.9 years]; 40 female [58%]) included in the study, 36 were randomly assigned to the neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education group, and 33 to the pain neuroscience education-alone group. The intention-to-treat analysis showed no between-group difference in change from baseline to 12 months for the KOOS 4 (7.46 [95% CI, 3.04-11.89] vs 8.65 [95% CI, 4.67-12.63] points; mean difference, -1.33 [95% CI, -7.59 to 4.92]; P =.68). Among the 46 participants who participated in the 12-month assessment in the 2 groups, 16 (34.8%) experienced a clinically important improvement (a difference of ≥10 points on the KOOS 4) with no between-group difference. No serious adverse events were observed. Conclusions and Relevance: In this randomized clinical trial, the results demonstrated that neuromuscular exercises and pain neuroscience education were not superior to pain neuroscience education alone in participants with chronic pain after TKA. Approximately one-third of the participants, regardless of intervention, experienced clinically important improvements. Future studies should investigate which patient characteristics indicate a favorable response to exercises and/or pain neuroscience education. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT03886259.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper B.","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Laursen, Mogens","Bruun, Niels Henrik","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S02-099.76-741512"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jesper B."],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee adverse effects","Chronic Pain etiology","Denmark","Exercise Therapy methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neurosciences education","Osteoarthritis Knee surgery","Pain Management methods","Pain Measurement","Pain Postoperative etiology","Patient Education as Topic methods","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exercise and pain neuroscience education for patients with chronic pain after total knee arthroplasty a randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.12179","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding/Support: This work was supported by grant R168-A5619 from the Danish Rheumatism Association and by the Svend Andersen Foundation and the Lions Club Danmark (Dr Larsen) and by grants 801790 for payment to the University of Southern Denmark and 945377 for payment to the N\\u00E6stved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospital from the European Union\\u2019s Horizon 2020 research and innovati on program (Prof Skou).","This work was supported by grant R168-A5619 from the Danish Rheumatism Association and by the Svend Andersen Foundation and the Lions Club Danmark (Dr Larsen) and by grants 801790 for payment to the University of Southern Denmark and 945377 for payment to the Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospital from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovati on program (Prof Skou)."],"id":"S02-099.76-741512","identifier":[{"id":"38787559","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85194129295","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11127128","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-b3afe817-3ff7-423d-b49a-e93a3080002a","sdu-60df1a86-fd91-40d2-82e4-1128c56cc5f0"],"keyword":["Aged","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/adverse effects","Chronic Pain/etiology","Denmark","Exercise Therapy/methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neurosciences/education","Osteoarthritis, Knee/surgery","Pain Management/methods","Pain Measurement","Pain, Postoperative/etiology","Patient Education as Topic/methods","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8D28B029F8E8CA10A072B5D497DFE72B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/f