twork open","paperid":"e2412179","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","title_org":"JAMA NETWORK OPEN","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194129295"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b3afe817-3ff7-423d-b49a-e93a3080002a","sdu-60df1a86-fd91-40d2-82e4-1128c56cc5f0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exercise and Pain Neuroscience Education for Patients With Chronic Pain After Total Knee Arthroplasty: A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.76-741512","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Squamous cell carcinoma of unknown primary in the head and neck (HNSCCUP) remains a diagnostic challenge. Tongue base mucosectomy by transoral robotic surgery (TORS-TBM) can increase the diagnostic yield and de-intensify treatment. However, the added value of TORS-TBM as an adjunct to work-up programs for HNSCCUP is unclear. Furthermore, the optimal extent of the procedure and selection criteria remain to be established. AIM: The primary aim of the present study was to assess the diagnostic yield of TORS-TBM as a supplement to a standardized work-up program, using the Danish national guidelines as an example. Secondary aims include predictive values of HPV-testing and PET/CT. METHODS: This was a national multicenter observational cohort study including all patients diagnosed with HNSCCUP from January 2013 to December 2019, who subsequently underwent TORS-TBM. In most cases HPV status was based on dual testing (p16 and HPV-DNA). Predictive values of PET/CT and HPV status were calculated. RESULTS: A total of 100 consecutive patients underwent TORS-TBM; 93 total TBMs and 7 unilateral TBMs. The primary tumor was detected in 49 % (49/100) of patients. The detection rate was 58 % (47/81) in patients with HPV-associated disease (PPV of HPV status) and 11 % (2/19) in patients with HPV-independent disease. The NPV of HPV status was 89 %. The PPV and NPV of PET/CT was 53 % and 52 %, respectively. CONCLUSION: Adding total TORS-TBM to the current Danish guideline-based work-up program on HNCCCUP patients with HPV-associated disease significantly improved the diagnostic yield.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Signe Bergliot","Holm Larsen, Mikkel Hjordt","Channir, Hani Ibrahim","Kiss, Katalin","Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","Godballe, Christian","Eriksen, Jesper Grau","Rubek, Niclas","Kjærgaard, Thomas","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767379"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Signe Bergliot"],"keyword":["Diagnostic techniques","Head and neck cancer","Human papillomavirus","Robotic Surgical Procedures","Squamous cell carcinoma","Tongue base mucosectomy","Unknown primary tumor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the value of tongue base mucosectomy in the work up of squamous cell carcinoma of unknown primary a danish national cohort study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oraloncology.2024.107083","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-767379","identifier":[{"id":"39476631","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85207805295","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3bbaca46-5835-408a-b4b7-5ce2398ddba3","sdu-60ca2936-d656-4d5f-aa43-ffbf0dc4f4fb"],"keyword":["Diagnostic techniques","Head and neck cancer","Human papillomavirus","Robotic surgical procedures","Squamous cell carcinoma","Tongue base mucosectomy","Unknown primary tumor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-18E337A2E4B2CD0FC058A9D518461213"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oraloncology.2024.107083","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276665373/1-s2.0-S1368837524004019-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oto Rhino Laryngology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe Bergliot","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"19df8d18-bee6-42d8-9d29-93c30adf1377","name":"Nielsen, Signe Bergliot","orcid":"0000-0002-3004-3103","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Hjordt","key":"holmlarsenpau","last":"Holm Larsen","name":"Holm Larsen, Mikkel Hjordt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hani Ibrahim","key":"channirpau","last":"Channir","name":"Channir, Hani Ibrahim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Katalin","key":"kisspau","last":"Kiss","name":"Kiss, Katalin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedicte","key":"parmulhøipau","last":"Parm Ulhøi","locid":"5077458c-a838-4374-b064-47a320ea5de4","name":"Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","name_org":"Parm Ulhøi, Benedicte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"godballepau","last":"Godballe","locid":"ff9e9b81-947f-4b49-be93-3467ee6937e3","name":"Godballe, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-7639-6337","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"graueriksenpau","last":"Grau Eriksen","locid":"8c1cfe12-4441-494c-a8b7-8abfbf7aa48c","name":"Eriksen, Jesper Grau","name_org":"Grau Eriksen, Jesper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niclas","key":"rubekpau","last":"Rubek","name":"Rubek, Niclas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"5c2179b1-a9d4-45cf-bf72-8149849d6b5a","name":"Kjærgaard, Thomas","name_org":"Kjaergaard, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39476631"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oraloncology.2024.107083","issn":["13688375","17419409"],"issn_org":["13688375"],"journal":"Oral Oncology","paperid":"107083","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Oral Oncology","volume":"159"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207805295"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3bbaca46-5835-408a-b4b7-5ce2398ddba3","sdu-60ca2936-d656-4d5f-aa43-ffbf0dc4f4fb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The value of tongue base mucosectomy in the work-up of squamous cell carcinoma of unknown primary : A Danish national cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767379","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Hearing loss has been suggested as a risk factor for dementia, but there is still a need for high-quality research to better understand the association between these 2 conditions and the underlying causal mechanisms and treatment benefits using larger cohorts and detailed data. OBJECTIVE: To investigate the association between hearing loss and incident dementia, as well as how hearing aid use contributes to this association. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: This population-based cohort study was conducted in Southern Denmark between January 2003 and December 2017 and included all residents 50 years and older. We excluded all persons with dementia before baseline as well as those who did not live in the region 5 years before baseline, with incomplete address history, or who had missing covariate information. EXPOSURES: Individual hearing status based on the Hearing Examinations in Southern Denmark database, which contains data on all pure-tone audiometry examinations performed at public hearing rehabilitation clinics in Southern Denmark. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: Incident cases of dementia and Alzheimer disease as identified from national registries. RESULTS: The study population comprised 573 088 persons (298 006 women [52%]; mean [SD] age, 60.8 [11.3] years) with 23 023 cases of dementia and mean (SD) follow-up of 8.6 (4.3) years. Having a hearing loss was associated with an increased risk of dementia, with an adjusted hazard ratio (HR) of 1.07 (95% CI, 1.04-1.11) compared with having no hearing loss. Severe hearing loss in the better and worse ear was associated with a higher dementia risk, with an HR of 1.20 (95% CI, 1.09-1.32) and 1.13 (95% CI, 1.06-1.20), respectively, compared with having no hearing loss in the corresponding ear. Compared with people without hearing loss, the risk of dementia was higher among people with hearing loss who were not using hearing aids than those who had hearing loss and were using hearing aids, with HRs of 1.20 (95% CI, 1.13-1.27) and 1.06 (95% CI, 1.01-1.10), respectively. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: The results of this cohort study suggest that hearing loss was associated with increased dementia risk, especially among people not using hearing aids, suggesting that hearing aids might prevent or delay the onset and progression of dementia. The risk estimates were lower than in previous studies, highlighting the need for more high-quality longitudinal studies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech","Pedersen, Ellen Raben","Waldorff, Frans Boch","Wermuth, Lene","Pedersen, Kjeld Møller","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Sørensen, Mette","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass"],"cuid":["S04-096.24-742135"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech"],"keyword":["Aged","Alzheimer Disease","Audiometry Pure Tone","Cohort Studies","Deafness","Female","Hearing Loss complications","Hearing aids","Humans","Middle Aged","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hearing loss hearing aid use and risk of dementia in older adults","src":["au","ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamaoto.2023.3509","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-096.24-742135","identifier":[{"id":"38175662","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10767640","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85183044366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ffbb8637-7f10-4d5c-a398-a0aea9302a42"