y of Denmark"],"title":"Repeaterless Brillouin OTDR Sensing over 250 km using Erbium doped Fiber Amplifier","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747103","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Cable bacteria are filamentous bacteria that couple the oxidation of sulfide in sediments to the reduction of oxygen via long-distance electron transport over centimeter distances through periplasmic wires. However, the capability of cable bacteria to perform extracellular electron transfer to acceptors, such as electrodes, has remained elusive. In this study, we demonstrate that living cable bacteria actively move toward electrodes in different bioelectrochemical systems. Carbon felt and carbon fiber electrodes poised at +200 mV attracted live cable bacteria from the sediment. When the applied potential was switched off, cable bacteria retracted from the electrode. qPCR and scanning electron microscopy corroborated this finding and revealed cable bacteria in higher abundance present on the electrode surface compared with unpoised controls. These experiments raise new possibilities to study metabolism of cable bacteria and cultivate them in bioelectrochemical devices for bioelectronic applications, such as biosensing and bioremediation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bonné, Robin","Marshall, Ian P.G.","Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","Marzocchi, Ugo","Manca, Jean","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Aiyer, Kartik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-753189"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Aiyer, Kartik"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hasselt University"],"keyword":["Bioelectrochemical system","Cable bacteria","Electrode","Extracellular electron transfer","Microscopy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interaction of living cable bacteria with carbon electrodes in bioelectrochemical systems","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/aem.00795-24","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-753189","identifier":[{"id":"85201771724","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11337825","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39082847","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bcad4e19-0a84-439b-a5ae-6102caf69161"],"keyword":["bioelectrochemical system","cable bacteria","electrode","extracellular electron transfer","microscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA20483861E0B6EC2B5AA26998C9AFA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/aem.00795-24","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Electromicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"bonnépau","last":"Bonné","locid":"ebd8f627-bf23-4be3-96fb-13c93e9cbe28","name":"Bonné, Robin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ian P.G.","key":"marshallpau","last":"Marshall","locid":"25504f0f-4132-4611-8697-0019cedc5d5d","name":"Marshall, Ian P.G.","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-4687","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper J.","key":"bjergpau","last":"Bjerg","locid":"682ae3d8-d830-4101-b5a3-494ea2e4e0be","name":"Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","name_org":"Bjerg, Jesper J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ugo","key":"marzocchipau","last":"Marzocchi