{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Atrial fibrillation (AF) has a substantial genetic component. The importance of polygenic risk is well established, while the contribution of rare variants to disease risk warrants characterization in large cohorts. OBJECTIVE: To identify rare predicted loss-of-function (pLOF) variants associated with AF and elucidate their role in risk of AF, cardiomyopathy (CM), and heart failure (HF) in combination with a polygenic risk score (PRS). DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: This was a genetic association and nested case-control study. The impact of rare pLOF variants was evaluated on the risk of incident AF. HF and CM were assessed in cause-specific Cox regressions. End of follow-up was July 1, 2022. Data were analyzed from January to October 2023. The UK Biobank enrolled 502 480 individuals aged 40 to 69 years at inclusion in the United Kingdom between March 13, 2006, and October 1, 2010. UK residents of European ancestry were included. Individuals with prior diagnosis of AF were excluded from analyses of incident AF. EXPOSURES: Rare pLOF variants and an AF PRS. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: Risk of AF and incident HF or CM prior to and subsequent to AF diagnosis. RESULTS: A total of 403 990 individuals (218 489 [54.1%] female) with a median (IQR) age of 58 (51-63) years were included; 24 447 were diagnosed with incident AF over a median (IQR) follow-up period of 13.3 (12.4-14.0) years. Rare pLOF variants in 6 genes (TTN, RPL3L, PKP2, CTNNA3, KDM5B, and C10orf71) were associated with AF. Of these, TTN, RPL3L, PKP2, CTNNA3, and KDM5B replicated in an external cohort. Combined with high PRS, rare pLOF variants conferred an odds ratio of 7.08 (95% CI, 6.03-8.28) for AF. Carriers with high PRS also had a substantial 10-year risk of AF (16% in female individuals and 24% in male individuals older than 60 years). Rare pLOF variants were associated with increased risk of CM both prior to AF (hazard ratio [HR], 3.13; 95% CI, 2.24-4.36) and subsequent to AF (HR, 2.98; 95% CI, 1.89-4.69). CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: Rare and common genetic variation were associated with an increased risk of AF. The findings provide insights into the genetic underpinnings of AF and may aid in future genetic risk stratification.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Vad, Oliver B.","Monfort, Laia M","Paludan-Müller, Christian","Kahnert, Konstantin","Diederichsen, Søren Z","Andreasen, Laura","Lotta, Luca A","Nielsen, Jonas B","Lundby, Alicia","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Olesen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759643"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corpau":["Geisinger MyCode Community Health Initiative and the Regeneron Genetics Center (RGC) Research Team"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Regeneron Genetics Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rare and common genetic variation underlying atrial fibrillation risk","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamacardio.2024.1528","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759643","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11209175","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85200946268","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38922602","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1dc0cdc0-5eed-4c3e-ab79-091b34d934cc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-20056C9E2AB2B4651FB7D807740DD310"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/403624162/Rare_and_Common_Genetic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamacardio.2024.1528","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"regeneron genetics center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Regeneron Genetics Center","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"geisinger mycode community health initiative and the regeneron genetics center research team","name":"Geisinger MyCode Community Health Initiative and the Regeneron Genetics Center (RGC) Research Team","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Oliver B","key":"vadpau","last":"Vad","locid":"28b00ca5-e5b4-40f3-adab-83b905677652","name":"Vad, Oliver B.","name_org":"Vad, Oliver B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laia M","key":"monfortpau","last":"Monfort","name":"Monfort, Laia M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christian","key":"paludanmüllerpau","last":"Paludan-Müller","locid":"efbe85eb-0b49-4ffe-832a-740b383c77a1","name":"Paludan-Müller, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Konstantin","key":"kahnertpau","last":"Kahnert","locid":"77a3e046-4f95-41a7-a845-66b57df67a5c","name":"Kahnert, Konstantin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren Z","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","name":"Diederichsen, Søren Z","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Laura","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"058fca60-48be-4703-beca-c144879aa2d0","name":"Andreasen, Laura","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Luca A","key":"lottapau","last":"Lotta","name":"Lotta, Luca A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jonas B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alicia","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","locid":"6273cf1f-1ae6-4abd-ab98-68d9299e0632","name":"Lundby, Alicia","orcid":"0000-0002-1612-6041","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jesper H","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","name_org":"Svendsen, Jesper H","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten S","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38922602"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamacardio.2024.1528","issn":["23806583","23806591"],"issn_org":["23806583"],"issue":"8","journal":"JAMA Cardiology","pages":"732-740","status":"p","title":"JAMA Cardiology","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200946268"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1dc0cdc0-5eed-4c3e-ab79-091b34d934cc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rare and Common Genetic Variation Underlying Atrial Fibrillation Risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759643","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Fast digitizers are employed in a variety of experimental contexts, including for microwave measurements from fusion plasma diagnostics. However, most existing commercial digitizers used for this purpose are severely limited by their onboard memory. Here we present a system developed from mostly commercially available hardware components capable of acquiring essentially indefinitely (here ∼10 s) while meeting the target performance of 5 GHz analog bandwidth with a rate of 10 billion samples per second and 8 bits per sample. At its core is a field-programmable gate array (FPGA) receiving data from a high-performance analog-to-digital converter (ADC). The data are continuously streamed with a maximum throughput of 120 Gb/s from the FPGA to a computer over optical fiber in the form of raw Ethernet packets, allowing the use of entirely standard networking hardware in the PC. Whilst this technology is transferable to a range of applications, we are motivated by the demands of microwave scattering measurements, for which the new digitizer increased the acquisition duty cycle from 6% to 100%. In this paper we describe our digitization system, demonstrate its capability, and then use it to acquire data from microwave diagnostics at the ASDEX Upgrade and Wendelstein 7-X fusion experiments.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Verdier, T.","Vann, R. G.L.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Jensen, T.","Rasmussen, Jesper","Ragona, R.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764426"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["ASDEX Upgrade Team","W7-X Team"],"corresponding_author":["Verdier, T."],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of York"],"keyword":["ADC","Continuous","FPGA","Fast digitizer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an ultrafast digitizer for continuous measurements from microwave fusion diagnostics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fusengdes.2024.114597","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764426","identifier":[{"id":"85198937953","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d2733863-c8d1-41ca-881c-109a47917363"],"keyword":["ADC","Continuous","FPGA","Fast digitizer","GHz bandwidth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-668DBD125946F0C993351DB82DF044FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/375793224/1-s2.0-S0920379624004484-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fusengdes.2024.114597","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"asdex upgrade team","name":"ASDEX Upgrade Team","role":"oau"},{"affno":4,"key":"w7 x team","name":"W7-X Team","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T.","key":"verdierpau","last":"Verdier","locid":"b03e7c15-4650-45b0-b64e-03ceabe0c7ff","name":"Verdier, T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"R. G.L.","key":"vannpau","last":"Vann","name":"Vann, R. G.L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. S.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","name_org":"Jacobsen, A. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e840242d-2592-40b7-bc0b-02995c8fe6ba","name":"Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9801-1530","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"ragonapau","last":"Ragona","locid":"6d50cb6b-b871-4b57-9536-210bf639b883","name":"Ragona, R.","orcid":"0000-0002-3225-5732","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fusengdes.2024.114597","issn":["09203796","18737196"],"issn_org":["09203796"],"journal":"Fusion Engineering and Design","paperid":"114597","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fusion Engineering and Design","volume":"206"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198937953"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d2733863-c8d1-41ca-881c-109a47917363"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"An ultrafast digitizer for continuous measurements from microwave fusion diagnostics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764426","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Knowledge about medieval iron production in Denmark is very limited. However, recent excavations in the area around Silkeborg in central Jutland, Denmark, have led to the discovery of several slag heaps and furnaces testifying to considerable iron production in this part of the country. Charcoal from slag heaps at six sites has been analysed to learn about fuel use in iron production. At two sites from the 12th-13th century, many species were used as fuel. Only 50–63% of the fuel consisted of high-density wood with a high caloric value, which at these sites included species such as birch, elm and pomaceous fruit. At the other four sites from the 14th-15th century, species diversity was smaller, and species with a high caloric value constituted 85–93% of the fuel, with beech, oak and birch being most common. Thus, a change in fuel use over time, which possibly could be related to access rights to the high forest, is indicated in the study. Some horizontal and vertical variations within the slag heaps were also recorded. A detailed analysis of vertically sampled charcoal at Gødvad Bygade III showed that the tree species used for fuel changed slightly at some point during the period of iron production, and that the accumulation period was likely 5–60 years. The study demonstrates that there is a great potential in analysing charcoal from iron production sites, as this approach can provide not only information about fuel use but in some cases even about organizational aspects of the production.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Jannie Koster","Nielsen, Nina Helt","Olsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-774158"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jannie Koster"],"keyword":["Bayesian analysis","Denmark","Medieval period"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Moesgaard"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fuel use in medieval iron production in central jutland denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206384054","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-774158","identifier":[{"id":"85206384054","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ff80f6cb-79ce-4491-a61a-2e6541e04f31"],"keyword":["Bayesian analysis","Charcoal analysis","Denmark","Iron production","Medieval period","Slag heaps"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E0ECC50776D09CAAFA2BAD2D7A2E356F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Moesgaard"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Archeology and Heritage Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannie Koster","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3c00c8fa-c3bd-49c4-bb2a-c4c1ebcf0d36","name":"Larsen, Jannie Koster","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina Helt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Nina Helt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12520-024-02087-1","issn":["18669557","18669565"],"issn_org":["18669557"],"issue":"11","journal":"Archaeological and Anthropological Sciences","paperid":"177","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Archaeological and Anthropological Sciences","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206384054"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ff80f6cb-79ce-4491-a61a-2e6541e04f31"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fuel use in medieval iron production in central Jutland, Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-774158","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Parallel Factor Analysis 2 (PARAFAC2) is a multimodal factor analysis model suitable for analyzing multi-way data when one of the modes has incomparable observation units, for example, because of differences in signal sampling or batch sizes. A fully probabilistic treatment of the PARAFAC2 is desirable to improve robustness to noise and provide a principled approach for determining the number of factors, but challenging because direct model fitting requires that factor loadings be decomposed into a shared matrix specifying how the components are consistently co-expressed across samples and sample-specific orthogonality-constrained component profiles. We develop two probabilistic formulations of the PARAFAC2 model along with variational Bayesian procedures for inference: In the first approach, the mean values of the factor loadings are orthogonal leading to closed form variational updates, and in the second, the factor loadings themselves are orthogonal using a matrix Von Mises–Fisher distribution. We contrast our probabilistic formulations to the conventional direct fitting algorithm based on maximum likelihood on synthetic data and real fluorescence spectroscopy and gas chromatography–mass spectrometry data showing that the probabilistic formulations are more robust to noise and model order misspecification. The probabilistic PARAFAC2, thus, forms a promising framework for modeling multi-way data accounting for uncertainty.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Philip Johan Havemann","Nielsen, Søren Føns Vind","Hinrich, Jesper Løve","Schmidt, Mikkel Nørgaard","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Mørup, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-774949"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mørup, Morten"],"keyword":["PARAFAC2","Tensor decomposition","Variational inference"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probabilistic parafac000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/e26080697","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-774949","identifier":[{"id":"001305806100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85202599971","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11354162","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39202167","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-09122d83-6bf6-4b7f-9f4d-d261809165cf"],"keyword":["Multi-way modeling","Orthogonality constraint","PARAFAC2","Tensor decomposition","Variational inference"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1EA9868181CB7B1819A3490C1F20414"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/377918895/entropy-26-00697-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/e26080697","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip J.H.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"c50537ce-d98e-475f-96f3-90db25281943","name":"Jørgensen, Philip Johan Havemann","name_org":"Jørgensen, Philip J.H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren F.","key":"nielse