{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Marie","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Hammel, Stephanie Cheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-780226"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-08","place":"København, dk","start":"2024-05-08","title":"Arbejdsmiljøforskningsfondens Årskonference 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Institut for Sundhedstjenesteforskning, Syddansk Universitet, Danmark."]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eksponering for klorerede paraffiner på danske arbejdspladser","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-780226","ids":["nfa-2ad7731a-3377-497c-8f7a-fff2078a820d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D55672A8758E365F5E70F23EC298349F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut for Sundhedstjenesteforskning, Syddansk Universitet, Danmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"682bbcfb-b19f-4bc1-a542-0c8cae7deb94","name":"Frederiksen, Marie","name_org":"Frederiksen, M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1553-5414","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephanie Cheng","key":"hammelpau","last":"Hammel","locid":"889bb52d-c835-43d1-80d0-1aef2d9553c6","name":"Hammel, Stephanie Cheng","orcid":"0000-0001-5334-2045","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-2ad7731a-3377-497c-8f7a-fff2078a820d"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Eksponering for klorerede paraffiner på danske arbejdspladser","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-780226","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Increasing melanoma incidence with less increasing mortality is observed in several countries. This discrepancy is not well understood. Objectives: In this study, our aim was to discuss factors [ultraviolet radiation (UVR) exposure, melanoma treatment, diagnostic activity, overdiagnosis, pathologists' diagnostic threshold and clinicians' propensity to remove suspect skin lesions] that might influence melanoma incidence and mortality in Denmark. Methods: This was a register study with the number of melanocyte-related lesions and melanoma mortality based on comprehensive national pathology and mortality databases for the period 1999-2019. We investigated melanocyte-related diagnoses and mortality in a population of 5.5 million with a national healthcare system. Age-adjusted melanoma mortality and age-adjusted incidence of benign naevi, atypical lesion, or melanoma in situ and of invasive melanoma were computed for data analysis. Results: In total, 1 434 798 biopsies were taken from 704 682 individuals (65% female). The mean age at biopsy was 39.8 years in males and 37.6 in females. In males and females, the incidence of invasive melanoma increased by 87% during the period 1999-2011. During the subsequent period it increased by 9% in males but remained unchanged in females. The incidence of melanoma in situ increased by 476% in males and 357% in females during the study period, while the increases for atypical melanocytic lesions were 1928% and 1686%, respectively. Biopsy rates increased by 153% in males and 118% in females from 1999 through 2011 but fell by 20% in males and 22% in females during the subsequent period. Mortality varied slightly from year to year without any significant time trend for males or females. We identified no evidence of increased UVR exposure over the latest 30 years in Denmark. Immunotherapy of advanced melanoma was introduced in Denmark in 2010 and came into general use in 2014. Conclusions: Comprehensive national data demonstrate increasing melanoma incidence correlated with increasing biopsy rates, but with no change in mortality. Previously suggested explanations for such a trend are a lowered threshold of melanoma diagnosis among pathologists, increased diagnostic activity in the presence of overdiagnosis and improved melanoma treatment. Because the study is observational and we have more explanatory factors than outcomes, the findings do not warrant conclusions about causal relationships.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","Thapa, Subash"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783876"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"country":["Australia","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charles Sturt University","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Biopsy","Child","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Melanoma mortality","Middle Aged","Overdiagnosis statistics numerical data","Registries statistics numerical data","Skin Neoplasms mortality","Sunlight adverse effects","Ultraviolet Rays adverse effects","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increasing melanoma incidence with unchanged mortality more sunshine better treatment increased diagnostic activity overdiagnosis or lowered diagnostic threshold","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bjd/ljae175","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783876","identifier":[{"id":"38655629","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85201413819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e4976060-c1ba-41e5-8a76-a86ff1cd6bef"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Biopsy","Child","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Melanoma/mortality","Middle Aged","Overdiagnosis/statistics & numerical data","Registries/statistics & numerical data","Skin Neoplasms/mortality","Sunlight/adverse effects","Ultraviolet Rays/adverse effects","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A68393B4F05B0B068F825C15F14D3167"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/277566174/ljae175.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bjd/ljae175","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"charles sturt university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Charles Sturt University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivar Sønbø","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2bcec001-e6b0-48e7-bc80-904ee8c535ae","name":"Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Subash","key":"thapapau","last":"Thapa","locid":"a271bef3-0a7e-4c8d-b6b7-28a6a21e9480","name":"Thapa, Subash","orcid":"0000-0002-1182-8511","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38655629"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/bjd/ljae175","issn":["00070963","13652133"],"issn_org":["00070963"],"issue":"3","journal":"British Journal of Dermatology","pages":"365-374","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Dermatology","volume":"191"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201413819"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e4976060-c1ba-41e5-8a76-a86ff1cd6bef"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Increasing melanoma incidence with unchanged mortality : more sunshine, better treatment, increased diagnostic activity, overdiagnosis or lowered diagnostic threshold?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783876","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
