 G.","key":"eriksenjespergpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, jesper G.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"farhadimohammadpau","last":"Farhadi","name":"Farhadi, Mohammad","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"andersenmariapau","last":"Andersen","locid":"6da3e480-13a0-4b96-9c64-d739bd7ba6fe","name":"Andersen, Maria","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"maarechristianpau","last":"Maare","name":"Maare, Christian","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"overgaardjenspau","last":"Overgaard","name":"Overgaard, Jens","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Cai","key":"graucaipau","last":"Grau","name":"Grau, Cai","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe","key":"friborgjeppepau","last":"Friborg","name":"Friborg, Jeppe","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian R.","key":"hansenchristianrpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Christian R.","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s0167-8140(24)01426-9","issn":["01678140"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","title_org":"Radiotherapy and Oncology","volume":"194"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a57f3e68-502d-4264-b140-ad87aaff4adc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Investigating treatment plan quality for photon and proton RT in the clinical trial DAHANCA 35","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786174","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Concomitant type 2 diabetes (T2DM) and cardiovascular disease (CVD) is frequent with a poor prognosis with high risk of comorbidities. Strict risk factor control reduces the risk for complications – yet many people do not achieve treatment targets. The complexity and fragmentation of the healthcare system may, together with the vulnerability of these patients, be a reason. Objective: The purpose of this paper is to describe the protocol of a non-randomized interventional pilot study testing the feasibility and effect of a multidisciplinary, shared care clinic using personalized medicine and coordinated care in people living with concomitant T2D and CVD. Methods: Participants were included from the Holbaek area in Denmark. People suffered from T2DM and CVD and were dysregulated regarding to HbA1c, cholesterol, micro/macroalbuminuaria or blood pressure. Participants went through a thorough evaluation to identify their needs and resources and received consultations every three months for one year. Results: A total of 63 participants with T2DM and CVD were enrolled in the clinic. The participants had a mean age of 69 years and a BMI of 30.9 kg/m2. Almost 50 % had heart failure, 95 % dyslipidemia and 91 % hypertension. Around 54 % received GLP-1 agonists and 39 % received SGLT-2-inhibitors. Perspectives: To our knowledge, a similar study with a multidisciplinary, shared care, outpatient clinic treating people living with concomitant T2DM and CVD, has not been performed previously. This study will provide information about the feasibility and efficacy of a multidisciplinary clinic based on changes in cardiovascular risk factors and medication.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Pontoppidan, Julie Rye Noer","Nielsen, Emil Eik","Olsen, Michael Hecht","Skjødt, Michael Kriegbaum","Christensen, Jesper Olund","Raymond, Ilan Esra","Møller, Sara Hedlund","Soja, Anne Merete Boas","Gæde, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-792166"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pontoppidan, Julie Rye Noer"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular Diseases","Comorbidity","Diabetes mellitus","Pilot Projects","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Type 2","Vulnerable Patients"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a multidisciplinary shared care clinic using personalized medicine and coordinated care in patients with concomitant type 000000000002 diabetes and cardiovascular disease protocol and baseline characteristics","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pmedr.2024.102594","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the local research committee at NSR Hospitals, by Holbaek and Slagelse hospital and by research grant from Steno Diabetes Center Sjælland."],"id":"S01-000.00-792166","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10821603","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85182383593","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38283962","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-ce6fe717-0060-4ecb-b9b0-c13b7f23a17a"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular Diseases","Comorbidity","Diabetes Mellitus","Pilot Projects","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Type 2","Vulnerable Patients"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-036810522A5946F00622875CA01E6375"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281035717/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pmedr.2024.102594","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"aff