boratory Press","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-3e301dca-c617-4d51-8329-6a00d9256a6f"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Steppe Ancestry in western Eurasia and the spread of the Germanic Languages","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811617","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION. Healthcare databases are a valuable source for epidemiological research in obstructive sleep apnoea, but accurately registered diagnoses are pivotal in contributing quality evidence. We examined positive predictive values (PPV) of the International Classification of Diseases, tenth version (ICD-10) diagnosis for “obstructive sleep apnoea” and “sleep apnoea” in the Danish National Patient Register. METHODS. Using the Danish National Patient Registry, we randomly sampled 100 patients from the North Denmark Region diagnosed with “obstructive sleep apnoea” (ICD-10 code DG4732) and 100 patients diagnosed with “sleep apnoea” (DG473*) during the year 2020. We calculated the PPV using a documented Apnea-Hypopnea Index (AHI) ≥ 5 to confirm the recorded diagnosis. A total of 70 patients were referred to the private sector for assessment of the AHI and excluded due to limited access to their data. RESULTS. The study population included 130 patients, among whom 64 were diagnosed with “obstructive sleep apnoea”, and 66 patients were registered with “sleep apnoea”. The PPV for “obstructive sleep apnoea” was 93.8% (95% confidence interval (CI): 85.0-97.5%), and the PPV for “sleep apnoea” was 80.3% (95% CI: 69.2-88.1%). CONCLUSIONS. Our findings indicated a high validity of the ICD-10 code DG4732 with a PPV of 93.8% and a lower PPV (80.3%) for the ICD-10 code DG473* for identifying patients with obstructive sleep. The “obstructive sleep apnoea” diagnosis is a suitable source of data for epidemiological research to identify patients with the disease.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ofverlind, Emilia Colding","Bille, Jesper","Overvad, Thure Filskov","Nielsen, Per Brønnum","Albertsen, Ida Ehlers"],"cuid":["S02-087.40-741335"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Albertsen, Ida Ehlers"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","International Classification of Diseases","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Registries","Reproducibility of Results","Sleep Apnea Obstructive diagnosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity of obstructive sleep apnoea diagnoses","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A11230701","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.40-741335","identifier":[{"id":"85195439306","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38847413","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-3b64dccc-930b-41cb-86f5-70387fef533a","au-a6e38942-a137-436d-bb47-770be612247d"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","International Classification of Diseases","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Registries","Reproducibility of Results","Sleep Apnea, Obstructive/diagnosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B42BFD8A7E2F249E855F48B8D7F2F08F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/718560688/Ofverlind_et_al._2024_._Validity_of_obstructive_sleep_apnoea_diagnoses.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A11230701","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Otorhinolaryngology, Head and Neck Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilia Colding","key":"ofverlindpau","last":"Ofverlind","locid":"2d750007-1e26-4842-bebb-611a52ccbe44","name":"Ofverlind, Emilia Colding","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"billepau","last":"Bille","locid":"e01ad509-1441-4201-8840-77490d3099c8","name":"Bille, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thure Filskov","key":"overvadpau","last":"Overvad","locid":"63d282a2-85c6-4f40-a01b-f4cc59ec37f5","name":"Overvad, Thure Filskov","orcid":"0000-0001-8096-0236","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brønnum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ce5c24a-cc41-4e4c-a071-9a41f036faf8","name":"Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","orcid":"0000-0003-2922-6970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Ehlers","key":"albertsenpau","last":"Albertsen","locid":"394af010-709e-4604-b3af-99886d850b79","name":"Albertsen, Ida Ehlers","orcid":"0000-0002-3460-8116","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38847413"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/a11230701","issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["16039629"],"issue":"6","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A11230701","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195439306"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3b64dccc-930b-41cb-86f5-70387fef533a","au-a6e38942-a137-436d-bb47-770be612247d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Validity of obstructive sleep apnoea diagnoses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.40-741335","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background Upfront primary tumor resection (PTR) has been associated with longer overall survival (OS) in patients with synchronous unresectable metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC) in retrospective analyses. The aim of the CAIRO4 study was to investigate whether the addition of upfront PTR to systemic therapy resulted in a survival benefit in patients with synchronous mCRC without severe symptoms of their primary tumor. Patients and methods This randomized phase III trial was conducted in 45 hospitals in The Netherlands and Denmark. Eligibility criteria included previously untreated mCRC, unresectable metastases, and no severe symptoms of the primary tumor. Patients were randomized (1 : 1) to upfront PTR followed by systemic therapy or systemic therapy without upfront PTR. Systemic therapy consisted of first-line fluoropyrimidine-based chemotherapy with bevacizumab in both arms. Primary endpoint was OS in the intention-to-treat population. The study was registered at ClinicalTrials.gov , NCT01606098. Results Between August 2012 and February 2021, 206 patients were randomized. In the intention-to-treat analysis, 204 patients were included (n = 103 without upfront PTR, n = 101 with upfront PTR) of whom 116 were men (57%) with median age of 65 years (interquartile range 59-71 years). Median follow-up was 69.4 months. Median OS in the arm without upfront PTR was 18.3 months (95% confidence interval 16.0-22.2 months) compared with 20.1 months (95% confidence interval 17.0-25.1 months) in the upfront PTR arm (P = 0.32). The number of grade 3-4 events was 71 (72%) in the arm without upfront PTR and 61 (65%) in the upfront PTR arm (P = 0.33). Three deaths (3%) possibly related to treatment were reported in the arm without upfront PTR and four (4%) in the upfront PTR arm. Conclusions Addition of upfront PTR to palliative systemic therapy in patients with synchronous mCRC without severe symptoms of the primary tumor does not result in a survival benefit. This practice should no longer be considered standard of care.","author_count":30,"contributors":["van der Kruijssen, D. E. W.","Elias, S. G.","van de Ven, P. M.","van Rooijen, K. L.","Lam-Boer, J. 't","Mol, L.","Punt, C. J. A.","Sommeijer, D. W.","Tanis, P. J.","Nielsen, Jesper Dan","Yilmaz, Mette Karen","Van Riel, J. M. G. H.","Wasowiz-Kemps, D. K.","Loosveld, O. J. L.","van der Schelling, G. P.","de Groot, J. W. B.","van Westreenen, H. L.","Jakobsen, H. L.","Fromm, A. L.","Hamberg, P.","Verseveld, M.","Jaensch, C.","Liposits, G. I.","van Duijvendijk, P.","Hadj, J. Oulad","van der Hoeven, J. A. B.","Trajkovic, M.","de Wilt, J. H. W.","Koopman, M."],"cuid":["S02-090.97-755916"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corpau":["CAIRO4 working group"],"corresponding_author":["Koopman, M."],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["Albert Schweitzer Ziekenhuis","All Global Affiliations","Amphia Hospital","Amsterdam UMC","ETZ Elisabeth","ETZ Elisabeth - Tweesteden Ziekenhuis","Erasmus University Medical Center","Flevoziekenhuis Almere","Franciscus Gasthuis & Vlietland","Franciscus Gasthuis Zuyderland","Gelre Ziekenhuizen","Isala Clinics","Netherlands Association of Comprehensive Cancer Centres","Netherlands Cancer Institute","Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation","Radboud University Medical Center","University Hospital Muenster","University Medical Center Utrecht","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols therapeutic use","Bevacizumab administration dosage","Colorectal Neoplasms pathology","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Metastatic colorectal cancer","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Metastasis","Netherlands epidemiology","Survival Rate","Systemic therapy","primary tumor resection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["