me":"Thomsen, Jacob Bay","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolaj","key":"valstednicolajpau","last":"Valsted","name":"Valsted, Nicolaj","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vestergaardannapau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Anna","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"karoffchristofferpau","last":"Karoff","locid":"b71daf07-cedf-42bb-bd7c-b0af441e57cd","name":"Karoff, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0003-2009-7965","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/frsen.2024.1474560","issn":["26736187"],"journal":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","paperid":"1474560","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208798743"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ca4b833d-fa44-4572-9b87-8dda8c791fee","sdu-c53e86ae-0f83-4d4c-b84c-dc476842298f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"DISCO-2 – an ambitious earth observing student CubeSat for arctic climate research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767862","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Current guidelines recommend implantable cardioverter-defibrillator (ICD) therapy in patients with heart failure, a left ventricular ejection fraction of ≤35%, and New York Heart Association (NYHA) class II-III. However, the evidence regarding the benefit of primary prevention ICD is less consistent in patients with NYHA class III. We investigated the long-term effects of primary prevention ICD implantation according to NYHA class in an extended follow-up study of the DANISH trial. METHODS AND RESULTS: The DANISH trial randomized 1116 patients with non-ischaemic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF) to ICD implantation or usual care. Outcomes were analysed according to NYHA class at baseline (NYHA class II and III/IV). The primary outcome was all-cause mortality. Of the 1116 patients randomized in the DANISH trial, 597 (53.5%) were in NYHA class II at baseline, 505 (45.3%) in NYHA class III, and 14 (1.3%) in NYHA class IV. During a median follow-up of 9.5 years, NYHA class III/IV, compared with NYHA class II, were associated with a greater long-term rate of all-cause mortality (hazard ratio [HR] 1.52, 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.20-1.93) and cardiovascular death (HR 1.95 [1.47-2.60]). ICD implantation, compared with usual care, did not reduce the long-term rate of all-cause mortality (all participants: HR 0.89 [95% CI 0.74-1.08]; NYHA class II: HR 0.85 [0.64-1.13]; NYHA class III/IV: HR 0.89 [0.69-1.14]; pinteraction = 0.78) or cardiovascular death (all participants: HR 0.87 [95% CI 0.70-1.09]; NYHA class II: HR 0.78 [0.54-1.12]; NYHA class III/IV: HR 0.89 [0.67-1.19]; pinteraction = 0.58), irrespective of NYHA class. Similarly, NYHA class did not modify the beneficial effects of ICD implantation on sudden cardiovascular death (all participants: HR 0.60 [95% CI 0.40-0.92]; NYHA class II: HR 0.73 [0.40-1.36]; NYHA class III/IV: HR 0.52 [0.29-0.94]; pinteraction = 0.39). CONCLUSIONS: In patients with non-ischaemic HFrEF, ICD implantation, compared with usual care, did not reduce the overall mortality rate, but it did reduce sudden cardiovascular death, regardless of baseline NYHA class. CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00542945.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Karacan, Munise N","Doi, Seiko N","Yafasova, Adelina","Thune, Jens Jakob","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Haarbo, Jens","Bruun, Niels E","Gustafsson, Finn","Eiskjær, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper H","Høfsten, Dan E","Pehrson, Steen","Køber, Lars","Butt, Jawad H"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-741549"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Butt, Jawad H."],"keyword":["Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Clinical trial","Heart failure","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","NYHA functional class"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new york heart association functional class and implantable cardioverter defibrillator in non ischaemic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction extended follow up of the danish trial","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejhf.3239","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The DANISH trial was supported by unrestricted grants from Medtronic, St. Jude Medical, TrygFonden, and the Danish Heart Foundation. No further funding was obtained for this follow\\u2010up study. Dr. Karacan was supported by a research grant from Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"id":"S03-100.00-741549","identifier":[{"id":"85192903969","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38733253","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-d25f4a1f-3f1a-4a5e-a7dc-cee2ee9a4dc0","au-57d91822-e2aa-416a-9eaf-e19251e43ce3","ku-e0271c8f-2ad8-411d-9c3b-9eb0e2a63ab8"],"keyword":["Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Clinical trial","Heart failure","Implantable cardioverter-defibrillator","NYHA functional class"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F01BBAAF6FED9485FEC7980920DDCA24"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/721076153/Karacan_et_al._2024_._New_York_Heart_Association_functional_class_and_implantable_cardioverter-defibrillator_in_non-ischaemic_heart_failure_with_reduced_ejection_fraction_-_Extended_follow-up_of_the_DANISH_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397982181/European_J_of_Heart_Fail_2024_Karacan_New_York_Heart_Association_functional_class_and_implantable.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejhf.3239","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-