ascular interventions","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205520444"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c365d5e1-76c9-4d15-a389-a73ce7ac12e3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Left Atrial Appendage Closure : What Is Fabric Edge Leak and How Can It Be Treated?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-763569","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Data fusion modeling can identify common features across diverse data sources while accounting for source-specific variability. Here we introduce the concept of a coupled generator decomposition and demonstrate how it generalizes sparse principal component analysis (SPCA) for data fusion. Leveraging data from a multisubject, multimodal (electro- and magnetoencephalography (EEG and MEG)) neuroimaging experiment, we demonstrate the efficacy of the framework in identifying common features in response to face perception stimuli, while accommodating modality- and subject-specific variability. Through split-half cross-validation of EEG/MEG trials, we investigate the optimal model order and regularization strengths for models of varying complexity, comparing these to a group-level model assuming shared brain responses to stimuli. Our findings reveal altered ~ 170ms fusiform face area activation for scrambled faces, as opposed to real faces, particularly evident in the multimodal, multisubject model. Model parameters were inferred using stochastic optimization in PyTorch, demonstrating comparable performance to conventional quadratic programming inference for SPCA but with considerably faster execution. We provide an easily accessible toolbox for coupled generator decomposition that includes data fusion for SPCA, archetypal analysis and directional archetypal analysis. Overall, our approach offers a promising new avenue for data fusion.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Olsen, Anders S.","Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","Mørup, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775396"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2024-08-26","title":"2024 32nd European Signal Processing Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mørup, Morten"],"keyword":["Data fusion","Sparse principal component analysis","Spatiotemporal variability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coupled generator decomposition for fusion of electro and magnetoencephalography data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85208445617","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-775396","identifier":[{"id":"85208445617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-599153b7-8d1e-44ee-b45d-97788bf3397f"],"keyword":["Data fusion","Mag- netoencephalography","Sparse principal component analysis","Spatiotemporal variability","lectroencephalography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B37D4F3F4190C719583D50774611878B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders S.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"1aef1538-3aa1-4dfa-8cf2-21e17a440f09","name":"Olsen, Anders S.","orcid":"0000-0002-1275-6660","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"72984c53-aee6-47e3-80d7-3f973e5aa18d","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper D.","orcid":"0000-0003-3697-1012","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","locid":"7ffdfaca-76bd-44ec-a98f-13fe4f033b71","name":"Mørup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-4985-4368","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eusipco63174.2024.10715032","eisbn":["9789464593617"],"isbn":["9798331519773"],"pages":"1357-1361","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 32nd European Signal Processing Conference (EUSIPCO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208445617"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-599153b7-8d1e-44ee-b45d-97788bf3397f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Coupled Generator Decomposition for Fusion of Electro- and Magnetoencephalography Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-775396","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: To investigate patients with disorders of consciousness (DoC) for residual awareness, guidelines recommend quantifying glucose brain metabolism using positron emission tomography. However, this is not feasible in the intensive care unit (ICU). Cerebral blood flow (CBF) assessed by arterial spin labeling magnetic resonance imaging (ASL-MRI) could serve as a proxy for brain metabolism and reflect consciousness levels in acute DoC. We hypothesized that ASL-MRI would show compromised CBF in coma and unresponsive wakefulness states (UWS) but relatively preserved CBF in minimally conscious states (MCS) or better. Methods: We consecutively enrolled ICU patients with acute DoC and categorized them as being clinically unresponsive (i.e., coma or UWS [≤ UWS]) or low responsive (i.e., MCS or better [≥ MCS]). ASL-MRI was then acquired on 1.5 T or 3 T. Healthy controls were investigated with both 1.5 T and 3 T ASL-MRI. Results: We obtained 84 ASL-MRI scans from 59 participants, comprising 36 scans from 35 patients (11 women [31.4%]; median age 56 years, range 18–82 years; 24 ≤ UWS patients, 12 ≥ MCS patients; 32 nontraumatic brain injuries) and 48 scans from 24 healthy controls (12 women [50%]; median age 50 years, range 21–77 years). In linear mixed-effects models of whole-brain cortical CBF, patients had 16.2 mL/100 g/min lower CBF than healthy controls (p = 0.0041). However, ASL-MRI was unable to discriminate between ≤ UWS and ≥ MCS patients (whole-brain cortical CBF: p = 0.33; best hemisphere cortical CBF: p = 0.41). Numerical differences of regional CBF in the thalamus, amygdala, and brainstem in the two patient groups were statistically nonsignificant. Conclusions: CBF measurement in ICU patients using ASL-MRI is feasible but cannot distinguish between the lower and the upper ends of the acute DoC spectrum. We suggest that pilot testing of diagnostic interventions at the extremes of this spectrum is a time-efficient approach in the continued quest to develop DoC neuroimaging markers in the ICU.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Grønlund, Elisabeth Waldemar","Lindberg, Ulrich","Fisher, Patrick M.","Othman, Marwan H.","Amiri, Moshgan","Sølling, Christine","Nielsen, Rune Damgaard","Capion, Tenna","Ciochon, Urszula Maria","Hauerberg, John","Sigurdsson, Sigurdur Thor","Thomsen, Gerda","Knudsen, Gitte Moos","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","Møller, Kirsten","Hansen, Adam Espe","Kondziella, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778037"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Brain injury","Cerebral blood flow","Coma","Disorders of consciousness","Functional neuroimaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"arterial spin labeling magnetic resonance imaging for acute disorders of consciousness in the intensive care unit","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12028-024-02031-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778037","identifier":[{"id":"38918338","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85196804143","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11599417","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-710f0353-06b1-4ae2-b48a-5e849e9507d9"],"keyword":["Brain injury","Cerebral blood flow","Coma","Disorders of consciousness","Functional neuroimaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B76E566F942B31C78F2FE585CAF7E9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12028-024-02031-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414302339/s12028_024_02031_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Molecular and Cellular Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth Waldemar","key":"grønlundpau","last":"Grønlund","name":"Grønlund, Elisabeth Waldemar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrich","key":"lindbergpau","last":"Lindberg","name":"Lindberg, Ulrich","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Patrick M.","key":"fisherpau","last":"Fisher","locid":"7fa3f6fa-fbc3-44b3-8c1b-742ca63b8547","name":"Fisher, Patrick M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marwan H.","key":"othmanpau","last":"Othman","name":"Othman, Marwan H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Moshgan","key":"amiripau","last":"Amiri","name":"Amiri, Moshgan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christine","key":"søllingpau","last":"Sølling","name":"Sølling, Christine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rune Damgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rune Damgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tenna","key":"capionpau","last":"Capion","name":"Capion, Tenna","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Urszula Maria","key":"ciochonpau","last":"Ciochon","name":"Ciochon, Urszula Maria","rank":9,"role