{"abstract":"Background/Objectives: A recent retrospective study conducted by our team identified a high percentage of postoperative pneumonia in children with neuromuscular scoliosis. Based on the findings in that study and our clinical experience, we aimed to assess the effectiveness of an optimized perioperative care protocol. Methods: As part of a prospective study, a multidisciplinary team developed a protocol that included preoperative nutritional and respiratory optimization, intra- and postoperative intravenous glucose infusion, early extubation, and postoperative nutritional optimization. Non-ambulant children between 6 and 18 years of age with neuromuscular scoliosis were eligible for inclusion in the study. The primary outcome was the rate of postoperative pneumonia within 30 days of surgery. The secondary outcome measures were the rate of postoperative complications, including readmissions. All the outcomes were compared to a retrospective control group that was receiving standard care during the same period. Results: Eleven children were included in the intervention group and 14 in the control group. In regard to the intervention group, the nutritional and respiratory assessment before surgery resulted in optimized treatment in 8/11 patients (73%) and 9/11 patients (82%), respectively. One patient (9%) in the intervention group and three patients (21%) in the control group developed postoperative pneumonia (relative risk 0.42, 95% confidence interval 0.05–3.50). The intervention and control groups did not differ significantly in terms of postoperative complications or readmission rates. Conclusions: The multidisciplinary care protocol is feasible, with a high compliance rate in regard to study procedures. A numerical reduction in the 30-day pneumonia rate did occur in the intervention group; however, this reduction did not reach statistical significance.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Naume, Marie Mostue","Hoei-Hansen, Christina Engel","Born, Alfred Peter","Brekke, Ghita","Høj, Astrid","Nielsen, Maja Risager","Borgwardt, Lise","Vissing, John","Dirks, Jesper","Staehr-Rye, Anne Kathrine","Møller, Morten Hylander","Andersen, Thomas Borbjerg","Ørngreen, Mette Cathrine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-791233"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Neuromuscular scoliosis","Nutrition","Pneumonia","Respiration"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a prospective study on the feasibility and effect of an optimized perioperative care protocol in pediatric neuromuscular scoliosis surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm13247848","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-791233","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11676504","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39768771","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85213251255","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f6ef0336-bb7d-4dfa-a706-1a6f6370f4b3"],"keyword":["neuromuscular scoliosis","nutrition","optimized perioperative care protocol","pneumonia","respiration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6936EF33A1949AE38982224A913AAE1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm13247848","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/417004285/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Mostue","key":"naumepau","last":"Naume","name":"Naume, Marie Mostue","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christina Engel","key":"hoeihansenpau","last":"Hoei-Hansen","locid":"7dfbdd44-09ef-4e29-96f1-0a120709865b","name":"Hoei-Hansen, Christina Engel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alfred Peter","key":"bornpau","last":"Born","name":"Born, Alfred Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ghita","key":"brekkepau","last":"Brekke","name":"Brekke, Ghita","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Astrid","key":"højpau","last":"Høj","name":"Høj, Astrid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Risager","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Maja Risager","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","name":"Borgwardt, Lise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"John","key":"vissingpau","last":"Vissing","locid":"7a69ec3d-d580-4028-af4e-36350ccafa06","name":"Vissing, John","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"dirkspau","last":"Dirks","name":"Dirks, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anne Kathrine Stæhr","key":"ryepau","last":"Rye","locid":"85751109-1f92-4d74-9fcc-b5807dbd963a","name":"Staehr-Rye, Anne Kathrine","name_org":"Rye, Anne Kathrine Stæhr","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten Hylander","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"9463b017-3c43-470d-b95b-cf3cba8a27d4","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Borbjerg","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Thomas Borbjerg","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Cathrine","key":"ørngreenpau","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Mette Cathrine","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39768771"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/jcm13247848","issn":["20770383"],"issue":"24","journal":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","paperid":"7848","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213251255"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f6ef0336-bb7d-4dfa-a706-1a6f6370f4b3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Prospective Study on the Feasibility and Effect of an Optimized Perioperative Care Protocol in Pediatric Neuromuscular Scoliosis Surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-791233","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Indo-European languages are among the most widely spoken in the world, yet their early diversification remains contentious1–5. It is widely accepted that the spread of this language family across Europe from the 5th millennium BP correlates with the expansion and diversification of steppe-related genetic ancestry from the onset of the Bronze Age6,7. However, multiple steppe-derived populations co-existed in Europe during this period, and it remains unclear how these populations diverged and which provided the demographic channels for the ancestral forms of the Italic, Celtic, Greek, and Armenian languages8,9. To investigate the ancestral histories of Indo-European-speaking groups in Southern Europe, we sequenced genomes from 314 ancient individuals from the Mediterranean and surrounding regions, spanning from 5,200 BP to 2,100 BP, and co-analysed these with published genome data. We additionally conducted strontium isotope analyses on 224 of these individuals. We find a deep east-west divide of steppe ancestry in Southern Europe during the Bronze Age. Specifically, we show that the arrival of steppe ancestry in Spain, France, and Italy was mediated by Bell Beaker (BB) populations of Western Europe, likely contributing to the emergence of the Italic and Celtic languages. In contrast, Armenian and Greek populations acquired steppe ancestry directly from Yamnaya groups of Eastern Europe. These results are consistent with the linguistic Italo-Celtic10,11 and Graeco-Armenian1,12,13 hypotheses accounting for the origins of most Mediterranean Indo-European languages of Classical Antiquity. Our findings thus align with specific linguistic divergence models for the Indo-European language family while contradicting others. This underlines the power of ancient DNA in uncovering prehistoric diversifications of human populations and language communities.","author_count":91,"contributors":["Yediay, Fulya Eylem","Kroonen, Guus","Sabatini, Serena","Frei, Karin Margarita","Frank, Anja B.","Pinotti, Thomaz","Wigman, Andrew","Thorsø, Rasmus","Vimala, Tharsika","McColl, Hugh","Moutafi, Ioanna","Altinkaya, Isin","Ramsøe, Abigail","Gaunitz, Charleen","Renaud, Gabriel","Mederos Martin, Alfredo","Demeter, Fabrice","Scorrano, Gabriele","Canci, Alessandro","Fischer, Peter","Duyar, Izzet","Serhal, Claude","Varzari, Alexander","Türkteki, Murat","O’Shea, John","Rahmstorf, Lorenz","Polat, Gürcan","Atamtürk, Derya","Vinner, Lasse","Omura, Sachihiro","Matsumura, Kimiyoshi","Cao, Jialu","Seersholm, Frederik Valeur","Morillo Leon, Jose Miguel","Voutsaki, Sofia","Orgeolet, Raphaël","Burke, Brendan","Herrmann, Nicholas P","Recchia, Giulia","Corazza, Susi","Borgna, Elisabetta","Cipolloni Sampò, Mirella","Trucco, Flavia","Pando, Ana Pajuelo","Jørkov, M L S","Courtaud, Patrice","Peake, Rebecca","Bao, Juan Francisco Gibaja","Parditka, Györgyi","Stenderup, Jesper","Sjögren, Karl-Göran","Staring, Jacqueline","Olsen, Line","Deyneko, Igor V.","Pálfi, György","Aldana, Pedro Manuel López","Burns, Bryan","Paja, László","Mühlenbock, Christian","Cavazzuti, Claudio","Cazzella, Alberto","Lagia, Anna","Lambrinoudakis, Vassilis","Kolonas, Lazaros","Rambach, Jörg","Sava, Eugen","Agulnikov, Sergey","Fernández, Vicente Castañeda","Broné, Mia","Romo, Victoria Peña","González, Fernando Molina","Serrano, Juan Antonio Cámara","Brobeil, Sylvia Jiménez","Molino, Trinidad Nájera","Ariza, Maria Oliva Rodriguez","Saulnier, Catalina Galán","Martin, Armando González","Cauwe, Nicolas","Mordant, Claude","Roscio, Mafalda","Staniaszek, Luc","Tafuri, Mary Anne","Yildirim, Tayfun","Salzani, Luciano","Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","Moreno Mayar, José Victor","Allentoft, Morten E.","Sikora, Martin","Nielsen, Rasmus","Kristiansen, Kristian","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800563"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe