{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Patients with hypothalamic pathology often develop hypothalamic obesity, causing severe metabolic alterations resulting in increased morbidity and mortality. Treatments for hypothalamic obesity have not proven very effective, although the glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist semaglutide has been shown to have positive effects. We examined semaglutide's effect on weight loss in a sample of patients with hypothalamic obesity. METHODS: Four female patients with hypothalamic obesity resulting from treatment of craniopharyngiomas were treated with semaglutide for six months. Whole Body Dual-energy x-ray absorptiometry scans were performed, and blood samples drawn at baseline and after six months. Semaglutide dosages were increased monthly along with tracking of body weight and eating behavior (Three Factor Eating Questionnaire, TFEQ-R18). RESULTS: BMI was reduced in all cases, with an average of 7.9 BMI (range: 6.7 to 10.1) corresponding to a weight loss of 17.0% (range: 11.3-22.4%) or 20.2 kg (range 16.2 kg to 23.4 kg). We found a comparable reduction in total fat mass (17.2%, p = 0.006) and lean mass (16.0%, p = 0.05), whereas bone mass was unchanged (2.6%, p = 0.12). All cases reported an increase in energy levels, improved mobility and physical activity. Unfavorable eating behaviors were reduced after 1 month of treatment (emotional eating - 41 points, p = 0.02, uncontrolled eating - 23 points, p = 0.11). HbA1c and total cholesterol were significantly reduced (p = 0.014 for both). CONCLUSION: Semaglutide is a promising and safe treatment option for HO, that improves eating behavior, reduces weight, and improves metabolic markers.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Gjersdal, Erlend","Larsen, Liva Bundgaard","Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt","Vestergaard, Peter","Nielsen, Eigil Husted","Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","Müller, Hermann L.","Dal, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-814423"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-15","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2024-06-14","title":"Dansk Endokrinologisk Selskabs Årsmøde 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Klinikum Oldenburg","University of Oldenburg"],"keyword":["Craniopharyngioma","GLP1RA","Hypothalamic obesity","Semaglutide","TFEQ"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"semaglutide as a promising treatment for hypothalamic obesity a six month case series on four females with craniopharyngioma","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"funding_acknowledgement":["E.G., L.B.L., E.H.N., J.S.K. and K.S.E. have no competing interests to declare that are relevant to the content of this article. P.V. is head of research at the Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark, funded by an unrestricted grant by the Novo Nordisk Foundation. H.L.M. has received reimbursement of participation fees for scientific meetings and continuing medical education events from the following companies: Ferring, Pfizer, Sandoz/Hexal, Novo Nordisk, IPSEN, Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, and Merck Serono. He has also received reimbursement of travel expenses from Merck Serono, Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, and IPSEN and a lecture honoraria from Pfizer. J.D. has received unrestricted research grants from IPSEN and Pfizer."],"id":"S01-000.00-814423","ids":["aau-49a6bf5f-6dd9-4195-86af-80b91b83101a"],"keyword":["Craniopharyngioma","GLP1RA","Hypothalamic obesity","Semaglutide","TFEQ"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DB6FC2A7C01EB6E988A12948886FCCAD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, The Department of Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"klinikum oldenburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Klinikum Oldenburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of oldenburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oldenburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erlend","key":"gjersdalpau","last":"Gjersdal","locid":"729ebfe6-28fd-442a-8997-b46491942a6a","name":"Gjersdal, Erlend","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liva Bundgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"55d6ec02-548d-48fa-8a36-39a3496886c6","name":"Larsen, Liva Bundgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kåre Schmidt","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","locid":"2bdb42e7-d104-4bd2-9d0d-718e033a883d","name":"Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"ad223cc8-3f85-4cdf-9da5-5ec44f6a1714","name":"Vestergaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9046-2967","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eigil Husted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2b197b9e-4971-4a2d-84de-96e9e59e461b","name":"Nielsen, Eigil Husted","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Scott","key":"karmisholtpau","last":"Karmisholt","locid":"410922f0-294c-4d56-b758-b30fffef3a49","name":"Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hermann L.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Hermann L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"dalpau","last":"Dal","locid":"2e86cdf8-de5b-4bcf-b705-d5ac5f184cf2","name":"Dal, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-0610-7867","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-49a6bf5f-6dd9-4195-86af-80b91b83101a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Semaglutide as a promising treatment for hypothalamic obesity: a six-month case series on four females with craniopharyngioma","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814423","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The purpose of this study is to explore line managers’ perspectives on data as tool in the management of sickness absence in public sector workplaces in Denmark.  Methods: The study is a qualitative study based on 19 semi-structured interviews with line managers from four public sector workplaces characterized by high levels of sickness absence or poor work environment. The interviews were analysed inductively using thematic analysis.  Results: The findings show that line managers primarily use data to identify employees at risk of sickness absence. The experiences highlighted related to how and when data are perceived as a valuable tool by the line managers, and that nuances in the data, accessibility of the data and how data are presented are important factors to ensure appropriate follow-up on sickness absence.  Conclusions: The findings suggest that for line managers to use data to manage sickness absence appropriately, the data must be easily accessible, simple for line managers to understand and provide line managers with a sufficient overview of sickness absence in their work units. It is also important to consider other factors affecting sickness absence, such as the work environment, when aiming to reduce sickness absence.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Lene","Nielsen, Maj Britt Dahl","Garde, Anne Helene","Kristiansen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-099.91-769608"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Lene"],"keyword":["Absenteeism","Adult","Data","Denmark","Female","Humans","Intervention","Interviews as Topic","Ledelse","Line manager","Male","Middle Aged","Occupational health","Public sector","Qualitative Research","Sick Leave","Sickness absence","Sygefravær","Workplace"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring line managers perspectives on using data in managing sickness absence a qualitative study","src":["nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12961-024-01224-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.91-769608","identifier":[{"id":"85204309138","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39289710","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11407000","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["nfa-e5ad2344-43d1-44ce-b941-662f849e123d","sdu-a7b3735a-b3b1-4ad2-8860-891376ded312"],"keyword":["Absenteeism","Adult","Data","Denmark","Female","Humans","Intervention","Interviews as Topic","Ledelse","Line manager","Male","Middle Aged","Occupational Health","Public Sector","Qualitative Research","Sick Leave","Sickness absence","Sygefravær","Workplace"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F9994482C0AE135A3B552772F92855EA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12961-024-01224-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/272664999/s12961-024-01224-5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Mental health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0d8ad03f-8294-49a2-8bb7-fea40eccf25a","name":"Rasmussen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-7864-4178","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj Britt Dahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9dfb8e84-90f3-4531-b486-2df21e9ecd3a","name":"Nielsen, Maj Britt Dahl","orcid":"0000-0002-5758-8031","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"8e894baf-467c-45d3-8abe-41a805b30b22","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39289710"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12961-024-01224-5","issn":["14784505"],"issue":"1","journal":"Health Research Policy and Systems","pages":"126","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Health Research Policy and Systems","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204309138"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-e5ad2344-43d1-44ce-b941-662f849e123d","sdu-a7b3735a-b3b1-4ad2-8860-891376ded312"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exploring line managers’ perspectives on using data in managing sickness absence : a qualitative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.91-769608","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Robust data on changes in pulmonary valve replacement (PVR) procedural volume and predictors of bioprosthetic pulmonary valve (BPV) durability in patients with tetralogy of Fallot (TOF) are scarce. Objectives: This study sought to assess temporal trends in PVR procedural volume and BPV durability in a nationwide, retrospective TOF cohort. Methods: Data were obtained from patient records. Robust linear regression was used to assess temporal trends in PVR procedural volume. Piecewise exponential additive mixed models were used to estimate BPV durability, defined as the time from implantation to redo PVR with death as a competing risk, and to assess risk factors for reduced durability. Results: In total, 546 PVR were performed in 384 patients from 1976 to 2021. The annual number of PVR increased from 0.4 to 6.0 per million population (P < 0.001). In the last decade, the transcatheter PVR volume increased by 20% annually (P < 0.001), whereas the surgical PVR volume did not change significantly. The median BPV durability was 17 years (Q1: 10-Q3: 10 years-not applicable). There was no significant difference in the durability of different BPV after adjustment for confounders. Age at PVR (HR: 0.78 per 10 years from <1 year; 95% CI: 0.63-0.96; P = 0.02) and true inner valve diameter (9-17 mm vs 18-22 mm HR: 0.40; 95% CI: 0.22-0.73; P = 0.003 and 18-22 mm vs 23-30 mm HR: 0.59; 95% CI: 0.25-1.39; P = 0.23) were associated with reduced BPV durability in multivariate models. Conclusions: The PVR procedural volume has increased over time, with a greater increment in transcatheter than surgical PVR during the last decade. Younger patient age at PVR and a smaller true inner valve diameter predicted reduced BPV durability.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Gröning, Mathis","Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","Munk, Kim","Andersen, Helle","Nielsen, Dorte Guldbrand","Nissen, Henrik","Mortensen, Ulrik Markus","Jensen, Annette Schophuus","Bække, Pernille Steen","Bjerre, Jesper","Engholm, Morten","Vejlstrup, Niels","Juul, Klaus","Søndergaard, Eva","Thyregod, Hans Gustav Hørsted","Andersen, Henrik Ørbæk","Helvind, Morten","De Backer, Ole","Jøns, Christian","Schmidt, Michael Rahbek","Jørgensen, Troels Højsgaard","Sondergaard, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-724713"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gröning, Mathis"],"keyword":["Child","Durability","Heart Valve Prosthesis Implantation adverse effects","Humans","Pulmonary Valve diagnostic imaging","Pulmonary valve replacement","Retrospective Studies","Tetralogy of Fallot","Tetralogy of Fallot diagnostic imaging","Treatment Outcome","bioprosthetic pulmonary valves","procedural volume"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pulmonary valve replacement in tetralogy of fallot procedural volume and durability of bioprosthetic pulmonary valves","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcin.2023.10.070","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank Bente Birgitte Brodersen, Anne Ankerstjerne Rasmussen, and Sussie Faxøe for their assistance with the acquisition of data."],"id":"S02-100.00-724713","identifier":[{"id":"38127022","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181934062","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7ceaa106-00ba-4e24-8fdc-34c021627557","sdu-12b20f6d-4e7d-4204-96ac-1b562be6ef87"],"keyword":["Child","Heart Valve Prosthesis Implantation/adverse effects","Humans","Pulmonary Valve Insufficiency/diagnostic imaging","Pulmonary Valve/diagnostic imaging","Retrospective Studies","Tetralogy of Fallot/diagnostic imaging","Treatment Outcome","bioprosthetic pulmonary valves","durability","procedural volume","pulmonary valve replacement","tetralogy of Fallot"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-392B518EAB759D1BD626ECEBA38AE004"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcin.2023.10.070","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/253608860/1-s2.0-S1936879823015054-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital