ne and a short-term prednisolone discontinuation for the diagnostic accuracy of FDG-PET/CT in polymyalgia rheumatica-a prospective study of 101 patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-751779","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Since the COVID-19 pandemic, the use of video consultation (VC) in primary care has expanded considerably in many countries. VC and other telehealth formats are often touted as a solution to improved health care access, with numerous studies showing high satisfaction with this care format among health professionals and patients. However, operationalization and measurement of patient satisfaction with VC varies across studies and often lacks consideration of dynamic contextual factors (eg, convenience, ease-of-use, or privacy) and doctor-patient relational variables that may influence patient satisfaction. OBJECTIVE: We aim to develop a comprehensive and evidence-based questionnaire for assessing patient satisfaction with VC in general practice. METHODS: The vCare Patient-Satisfaction Questionnaire (the vCare-PSQ) was developed according to the COSMIN (Consensus-Based Standards for the Selection of Health Measurement Instruments) guidelines. To achieve our overall objective, we pursued three aims: (1) a validation analysis of an existing patient-satisfaction scale (the PS-14), (2) an assessment of extrinsic contextual factors that may impact patient satisfaction, and (3) an assessment of pertinent intrinsic and relational satisfaction correlates (eg, health anxiety, information technology literacy, trust in the general practitioner, or convenience). For validation purposes, the questionnaire was filled out by a convenience sample of 188 Danish adults who had attended at least 1 VC. RESULTS: Our validation analysis of the PS-14 in a Danish population produced reliable results, indicating that the PS-14 is an appropriate measure of patient satisfaction with VC in Danish patient populations. Regressing situational and doctor-patient relational factors onto patient satisfaction further suggested that patient satisfaction is contingent on several factors not measured by the PS-14. These include information technology literacy and patient trust in the general practitioner, as well as several contextual pros and cons. CONCLUSIONS: Supplementing the PS-14 with dynamic measures of situational and doctor-patient relational factors may provide a more comprehensive understanding of patient satisfaction with VC. The vCare-PSQ may thus contribute to an enhanced methodological approach to assessing patient satisfaction with VC. We hope that the vCare-PSQ format may be useful for future research and implementation efforts regarding VC in a general practice setting.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larrabee Sonderlund, Anders","Bang van Sas, Tessa Quirina","Wehberg, Sonja","Huibers, Linda","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-785198"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larrabee Sonderlund, Anders"],"keyword":["ADULTS","Adult","COSMIN","Covid 19","Danish","General practice","Health professional","Health professionals","Healthcare","IT literacy","Methodological","Pandemic","Patient Satisfaction","Patient physician relationship","Primary care","SARS CoV 2","Telehealth","Video consultation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a video consultation patient satisfaction questionnaire vcare psq a cross sectional explorative study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/58928","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-785198","identifier":[{"id":"85201753145","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11329851","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39094110","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c34008bd-d131-4d95-94ed-d64929f141d7","sdu-3ba60462-6bd2-4f58-882f-d2bb54ed8011"],"keyword":["COSMIN","COVID-19","Danish","IT-literacy","SARS-CoV-2","adult","adults","general practice","health professional","health professionals","healthcare","methodological","pandemic","patient satisfaction","patient-physician relationship","pilot-testing","primary care","telehealth","vCare-PSQ","video consultation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EECBEE1C63954C84BA03CE15A6BAA99E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276864638/formative-2024-1-e58928_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/58928","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"larrabeesonderlundpau","last":"Larrabee Sonderlund","locid":"052e950e-ab44-4d41-869d-4a3d4a37c62e","name":"Larrabee Sonderlund, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6627-3322","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tessa","key":"quirinabangvansaspau","last":"Quirina Bang Van Sas","locid":"d81a4043-9997-47e6-b1aa-c662fe81ce78","name":"Bang van Sas, Tessa Quirina","name_org":"Quirina Bang Van Sas, Tessa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonja","key":"wehbergpau","last":"Wehberg","locid":"2a11b516-c573-4a93-88f1-4a86a858b664","name":"Wehberg, Sonja","orcid":"0000-0003-1503-2649","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda","key":"huiberspau","last":"Huibers","locid":"999be5c2-cd8d-477c-96d5-f9916c1c5bac","name":"Huibers, Linda","orcid":"0000-0002-5048-3026","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"assinghvidtpau","last":"Assing Hvidt","locid":"8c678f9e-b6bc-401c-b9ca-561b04c3ec2b","name":"Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0003-3762-8478","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39094110"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/58928","issn":["2561326X"],"journal":"JMIR Formative Research","paperid":"e58928","publisher":"JMIR Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"JMIR Formative Research","title_org":"JMIR formative research","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201753145"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c34008bd-d131-4d95-94ed-d64929f141d7","sdu-3ba60462-6bd2-4f58-882f-d2bb54ed8011"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Development of a Video Consultation Patient-Satisfaction Questionnaire (vCare-PSQ) : A Cross-Sectional Explorative Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785198","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: To assess the effect of long-term isolation on the mental state of Danish youth. This study aimed to investigate trends in paracetamol overdoses among people under 18 years of age in Denmark during Covid-19 restrictions as an indicator of mental health. METHODS: All patients under the age of 18 years presenting with paracetamol overdose at one of the 18 paediatric departments in Denmark from 2016 to 2021 were included. They were identified in all Danish hospital databases using specific diagnostic codes. RESULTS: From 2016 to 2021, a total of 3,217 people under 18 years of age were admitted for paracetamol overdose. Among these, 86% (n = 2,755) were girls and 14% (n = 462) were boys. During 2020, a slight (7%) decrease in admissions was observed among both boys and girls compared with the preceding four-year mean value. In 2021, the number of overdoses among girls exceeded by 35% the former all-time high from 2016. Furthermore, the number of overdoses among girls exceeded the pre-four-year period mean value by 43%. Among boys, an 8% increase was seen from the highest ever previous value recorded in 2019 and a 23% increase compared with the previous four-year mean value. CONCLUSIONS: During the first year of restrictions, a slight decrease in paracetamol overdoses was observed, possibly associated with limited accessibility. The second year showed a considerable increase in paracetamol overdoses, which may imply an affected mental state among youth during the prolonged lockdown restrictions as seen in previous epidemics. Therefore, further studies are warranted to develop a pandemic preparedness plan to protect general mental health. FUNDING: None. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Not relevant.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Kempf, Oliver Nørholm","Helt, Thora Wesenberg","Johansen, Klaus Birkelund","Rittig, Charlotte","Lundby-Christensen, Louise","Frederiksen, Marianne Sjølin","Mathiesen, Pernille","Boas, Malene","Nielsen, Preben Berg","Ellermann, Annie","Børch, Klaus","Petersen, Jens Jakob","Petersen, Thomas Houmann","Sønderskov, Cæcilie Trier","Andersen, Jesper","Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskær","Jeppesen, Eva Mosfeldt","Christensen, Vibeke Brix"],"cuid":["S03-099.87-741546"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Vibeke Brix","Kempf, Oliver Nørholm"],"keyword":["Acetaminophen poisoning","Adolescent","Analgesics Non Narcotic poisoning","COVID 19 epidemiology","Child","Child Preschool","Denmark epidemiology","Drug Overdose epidemiology","Female","Humans","Infant","Male","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paracetamol overdose in danish children and adolescents during the covid 000000000019 restrictions","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A08230494","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.87-741546","identifier":[{"id":"38704838","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85192290189","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d0dd82c2-e9a2-4bf1-ad33-34e22ed5b9eb","au-8f6c3dc4-f71e-41f0-895d-dcb8e3808150","sdu-ffed2b70-68be-4b24-8c2f-8c9e5aaa13c1"],"keyword":["Acetaminophen/poisoning","Adolescent","Analgesics, Non-Narcotic/poisoning","COVID-19/epidemiology","Child","Child, Preschool","Denmark/epidemiology","Drug Overdose/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Infant","Male","SARS-CoV-2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Loc