"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jawad H","key":"buttpau","last":"Butt","name":"Butt, Jawad H","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38293926"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.123.031977","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e031977","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184296262"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ea2d9685-773b-4578-b047-8d86959e630e","au-9978bdba-8050-4112-88fd-1919127b050c","ku-1e6e4add-ef18-4d7f-b6dd-c266784d3d21","sdu-661a4141-c40a-4910-bc3d-faeab988cb52"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate and Implantable Cardioverter-Defibrillator in Nonischemic Systolic Heart Failure : Extended Follow-Up of DANISH","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.45-724383","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: There is strong observational evidence that respirators are highly effective in protecting the users from being infected with Middle East respiratory syndrome and severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus (SARS-CoV), but the evidence for SARS-CoV-2 during daily work is limited. This study utilized a subset of healthcare workers' temporary use of a new brand respirator with frequent defects when caring for coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) patients to assess the protective effect of regular respirators against SARS-CoV-2 infection. METHODS: We retrospectively followed 463 participants wearing a regular respirator and 168 wearing the new brand respirator day-by-day when caring for COVID-19 patients until testing polymerase chain reaction positive for SARS-CoV-2 between 27th December 2020 and 14th January 2021. RESULTS: We observed seven and eight incident SARS-CoV-2-infected cases. This corresponded with daily infection rates of 0.2 and 0.5%, an incidence rate ratio of 0.4 [95% confidence interval (CI) 0.1; 1.0], and an incidence rate difference of 0.3% (95% CI -0.1; 0.8) when comparing a regular with the new brand respirator. DISCUSSION: We regard the new brand respirator a sham intervention, and this study thus provides further evidence for the protective effect of respirators when exposed to SARS-CoV-2 virus.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Kolstad, Henrik A.","Frydenberg, Morten","Nielsen, Kent Jacob","Schlünssen, Vivi","Biering, Karin","Kjærsgaard, Mona","Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","Würtz, Else Toft","Pugdahl, Kirsten","Würtz, Anne Mette Lund","Hansen, Karoline Kærgaard","Jespersen, Sanne","Thomsen, Marianne Kragh","Sørensen, Mette Marie","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Dvinge Redder, Jacob","Storgaard, Merete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161025"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Follow Up Studies","Follow up study","Healthcare worker","Humans","Incidence rate ratio","Occupational Exposure adverse effects","Respirator","Retrospective Studies","SARS CoV 2","Sham","Ventilators Mechanical"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sars cov 000000000002 infection rates following use of regular compared with defective respirators when caring for covid 000000000019 patients a retrospective follow up study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85139446061","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161025","identifier":[{"id":"35488370","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139446061","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-377c850d-374e-4218-8715-1502baaaf540"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Occupational Exposure/adverse effects","Retrospective Studies","SARS-CoV-2","Ventilators, Mechanical","follow-up study","healthcare worker","incidence rate ratio","respirator","sham"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47F5779A7F6B2BD553CFCB4DDC6F4349"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Occupational and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik A","key":"kolstadhenrikapau","last":"Kolstad","locid":"287e6e28-266e-42e8-aa6d-10dffb6dc51e","name":"Kolstad, Henrik A.","name_org":"Kolstad, Henrik A","orcid":"0000-0002-6535-4323","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten