{"abstract":"Contemporary capabilities in timber fabrication have encouraged the advancement of robotic manufacturing and assembly. In this paper, the ReconWoodjoint, a new type of reversible joint conceived for robotic timber assembly is investigated. Thejoint use CNC milled shear-keys to ensure enhanced shear capacity and more ductile behaviour over the conventional dowel-type connection. More specifically, we here establish a method for the modelling and structural analysis of such joint where the complex nature of timber is tackled by using material laws which are readily available in most commercial FE software. The paper presents a hybrid material model using the Hill Criterion in combination with fracture mechanics (CZM) to appropriately describe these behaviours. The material model is implemented in a three-dimensional FEM model to simulate the joint's mechanical behaviour, and a test series is presented to validate the modelling approach. The results show that the model is able to predict the mechanical response with great precision, both in relation to the stiffness, ultimate strength, and failure mode.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hansen, Jesper Kierkegaard","Nielsen, Mads Friborg","Gustenhoff Hansen, Søren","Kunic, Anja","Naboni, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697401"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-22","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2023-06-19","title":"13th World Conference on Timber Engineering: Timber for a Livable Future, WCTE 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gustenhoff Hansen, Søren"],"keyword":["Anisotropy","Experiments","Fracture mechanics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fracture mechanical and anisotropic fem model of the reconwood joint and experimental verification","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85171625496","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697401","identifier":[{"id":"85171625496","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e114212a-fac5-4ad3-b83c-6d40a7e58ee1"],"keyword":["Anisotropy","Experiments","Fracture mechanics","Solid 3D F E M","Timberjoint"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A10AE467B8D839E9502686DE7DDF53FB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Civil and Architectural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kierkegaard","key":"hansenjesperkierkegaardpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper Kierkegaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Friborg","key":"nielsenmadsfriborgpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Mads Friborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Seren Gustenhoff","key":"gustenhoffhansensørenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"53420b1f-1a7f-4447-b6f3-4cd3f0c5b30a","name":"Gustenhoff Hansen, Søren","name_org":"Hansen, Seren Gustenhoff","orcid":"0000-0003-3424-0216","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"kunicanjapau","last":"Kunic","locid":"1276ce2a-fb47-42cb-9c43-2e848bb969df","name":"Kunic, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-4677-4859","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"nabonirobertopau","last":"Naboni","locid":"21bb63b6-a718-4604-a80b-07e0724aef27","name":"Naboni, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0001-9647-0426","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Q.","key":"nyrudandersqpedh","last":"Nyrud","name":"Nyrud, Anders Q.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kjell Arne","key":"malokjellarnepedh","last":"Malo","name":"Malo, Kjell Arne","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristine","key":"norekristinepedh","last":"Nore","name":"Nore, Kristine","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Knut Werner Lindeberg","key":"alsenknutwernerlindebergpedh","last":"Alsen","name":"Alsen, Knut Werner Lindeberg","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Saule","key":"tulebekovasaulepedh","last":"Tulebekova","name":"Tulebekova, Saule","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Efthymia Ratsou","key":"staehrefthymiaratsoupedh","last":"Staehr","name":"Staehr, Efthymia Ratsou","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gabrielle","key":"berghgabriellepedh","last":"Bergh","name":"Bergh, Gabrielle","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Wendy","key":"wuytswendypedh","last":"Wuyts","name":"Wuyts, Wendy","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.52202/069179-0171","eisbn":["9781713873297"],"pages":"1252-1260","publisher":"World Conference on Timber Engineering (WCTE)","status":"p","title":"13th World Conference on Timber Engineering, WCTE 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171625496"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e114212a-fac5-4ad3-b83c-6d40a7e58ee1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Fracture mechanical and anisotropic fem model of the \"Reconwood Joint\" and experimental verification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697401","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To evaluate the value of the thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH) test in the diagnosis of central hypothyroidism (CH) in patients with pituitary disease. Methods: Systematic evaluation of 359 TRH tests in patients with pituitary disease including measurements of thyroxine (T4), TBG-corrected T4 (T4 corr), baseline TSH (TSH 0) and relative or absolute TSH increase (TSH fold, TSH absolute). Results: Patients diagnosed with CH (n=39) show comparable TSH 0 (p-value 0.824) but lower T4 corr (p-value <0.001) and lower TSH increase (p-value <0.001) compared to patients without CH. In 54% (42 of 78 cases) of patients with low T4 corr, the CH diagnosis was rejected based on a high TSH fold. In these cases, a spontaneous increase and mean normalization in T4 corr (from 62 to 73 nmol/L, p-value <0.001) was observed during the follow-up period (7.6 ± 5.0 years). Three of the 42 patients (7%) were started on replacement therapy due to spontaneous deterioration of thyroid function after 2.8 years. Patients diagnosed with CH reported significantly more symptoms of hypothyroidism (p-value 0.005), although, symptoms were reported in most patients with pituitary disease. The TRH test did not provide clinical relevant information in patients with normal T4 or patients awaiting pituitary surgery (78%, 281 of 359). There were only mild and reversible adverse effects related to the TRH test except for possibly one case (0.3%) experiencing a pituitary apoplexy. Conclusion: The TRH test could be reserved to patients with pituitary disease, low T4 levels without convincing signs of CH. Approximately 50% of patients with a slightly decreased T4 were considered to have normal pituitary thyroid function based on the TRH test results.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christensen, Sara Ellegaard","Smith, Liv Norma","Rosendal, Christian Alexander Helleshøj","Gulisano, Helga Angela","Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt","Vestergaard, Peter","Nielsen, Eigil Husted","Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","Dal, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-698496"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rosendal, Christian Alexander Helleshøj"],"keyword":["Central hypothyroidism","Humans","Hyperthyroidism drug therapy","Hypopituitarism","Hypothyroidism drug therapy","Pituitary Diseases drug therapy","Thyrotropin","Thyroxine therapeutic use","pituitary disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the trh test provides valuable information in the diagnosis of central hypothyroidism in patients with known pituitary disease and low t000000000004 levels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2023.1226887","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-698496","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10577283","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85174261244","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37850100","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-28d68056-27cb-4431-98f0-e59d8145ffbd"],"keyword":["Humans","Hyperthyroidism/drug therapy","Hypothyroidism/drug therapy","Pituitary Diseases/drug therapy","TRH test","Thyrotropin","Thyrotropin-Releasing Hormone/therapeutic use","Thyroxine/therapeutic use","central hypothyroidism","hypopituitarism","pituitary disease","thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9C9BB7C5A8C47DCD9FAD89AFC7681B2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/558699415/Christensen_et_al._2023_._The_TRH_test_provides_valuable_information_in_the_diagnosis_of_central_hypothyroidism_in_patients_with_known_pituitary_disease_and_low_T4_levels.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2023.1226887","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, The Department of Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Ellegaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"db7022d2-baf8-4756-837f-683a31f10248","name":"Christensen, Sara Ellegaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liv Norma","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","locid":"6c7aba20-cdd9-4504-9485-98a15c0fb230","name":"Smith, Liv Norma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Alexander H.","key":"rosendalpau","last":"Rosendal","locid":"eef249b8-63dd-4949-b661-485ae602bc4f","name":"Rosendal, Christian Alexander Helleshøj","name_org":"Rosendal, Christian Alexander H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helga Angela","key":"gulisanopau","last":"Gulisano","locid":"ae8bea20-91de-46dd-a5cf-a3f0e1579aec","name":"Gulisano, Helga Angela","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kåre Schmidt","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","locid":"2bdb42e7-d104-4bd2-9d0d-718e033a883d","name":"Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"ad223cc8-3f85-4cdf-9da5-5ec44f6a1714","name":"Vestergaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9046-2967","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eigil Husted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2b197b9e-4971-4a2d-84de-96e9e59e461b","name":"Nielsen, Eigil Husted","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Scott","key":"karmisholtpau","last":"Karmisholt","locid":"410922f0-294c-4d56-b758-b30fffef3a49","name":"Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"dalpau","last":"Dal","locid":"2e86cdf8-de5b-4bcf-b705-d5ac5f184cf2","name":"Dal, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-0610-7867","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37850100"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fendo.2023.1226887","issn":["16642392"],"journal":"Frontiers in Endocrinology","paperid":"1226887","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Endocrinology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174261244"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-28d68056-27cb-4431-98f0-e59d8145ffbd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The TRH test provides valuable information in the diagnosis of central hypothyroidism in patients with known pituitary disease and low T4 levels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-698496","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Many single- and multi-channel speech enhancement techniques, old and new, rely in one way or another on estimates of the noise power spectral density (PSD). For example, the classical Wiener filter requires that either the speech or noise PSD be estimated. Typically, the noise PSD is estimated, as it is often easier to model and estimate than the speech. As a result, much attention has been paid to this important problem over the past couple of decades, with important scientific milestones being the minimum statistics (MS), the minima controlled recursive averaging (IMCRA), and the minimum mean squared (MMSE) estimators. Despite leading to major progress, these estimators are rather ad hoc, making them difficult to tune and improve in a systematic manner. In this article, we analyse some of the common heuristics employed in such noise PSD estimators to put them on firmer mathematical ground. More specifically, we use the Gaussian stochastic volatility model and show that the MMSE noise PSD estimator can be interpreted as a special case thereof. Moreover, we analyze the related problem of speech presence probability (SPP) estimation and show that the SPP estimation performed in the MMSE noise PSD estimator can be interpreted as an SNR estimator in the context of the Gaussian stochastic volatility model.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Boldt, Jesper Bunsow"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705325"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"keyword":["Noise PSD estimation","Speech enhancement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an analysis of traditional noise power spectral density estimators based on the gaussian stochastic volatility model","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85161612803&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Innovation Fund Denmark under Grant 99-2014-1."],"id":"S01-000.00-705325","identifier":[{"id":"85161612803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-64a3bdb4-2fc1-4dc2-96bc-8b383f21610c"],"keyword":["Noise PSD estimation","speech enhancement","speech presence probabilities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE9C60A4BF9F1F5E9FF4FD7246100E48"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Artificial Intelligence and Sound","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Audio Analysis Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Gn Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjaer","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjaer","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Graesboll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","name_org":"Christensen, Mads Graesboll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bunsow","key":"boldtpau","last":"Boldt","name":"Boldt, Jesper Bunsow","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/taslp.2023.3282107","issn":["23299290"],"journal":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","pages":"2299-2313","publisher":"IEEE Advancing Technology for Humanity","status":"p","title":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","title_org":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio Speech and Language Processing","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161612803"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","gn group"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-64a3bdb4-2fc1-4dc2-96bc-8b383f21610c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An Analysis of Traditional Noise Power Spectral Density Estimators Based on the Gaussian Stochastic Volatility Model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705325","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A common assumption in many speech and acoustic processing methods is that the noise is white and Gaussian (WGN). Although making this assumption results in simple and computationally attractive methods, the assumption is often too simple and crude in many applications. In this paper, we introduce a general purpose and online pre-whitener which can be used as a pre-processor with methods based on the WGN assumption, improving their reliability and performance in applications with colored noise. The pre-whitener is a time-varying filter whose coefficients are found using a parametric non-negative matrix factorization (NMF), based on autoregressive (AR) mixture modeling of both the noise component and the signal component constituting the noisy signal. Compared to other types of pre-whiteners, we show that the proposed pre-whitener has the best performance, especially in applications with non-stationary noise. We also perform a large number of experiments to quantify the benefits of using a pre-whitener as a pre-processor for methods based on the WGN-assumption. The applications of interest were pitch estimation and time-of-arrival (TOA) estimation, where the WGN assumption is very popular.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jaramillo, Alfredo Esquivel","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705416"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jaramillo, Alfredo Esquivel"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Enhancement","NMF","Pitch","Pre whitening"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an adaptive autoregressive pre whitener for speech and acoustic signals based on parametric nmf","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.specom.2023.04.002","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by the National Council of Science and Technology (CONACYT), Mexico under grant 418437 ."],"id":"S01-000.00-705416","identifier":[{"id":"85159592944","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-72c7bb7e-da93-4615-b8d1-63765ec76fa8"],"keyword":["Colored","Enhancement","NMF","Pitch","Pre-whitening","TOA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C8F18B5379AA49AB57E9E42E484DD40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.specom.2023.04.002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/698856416/1-s2.0-S0167639323000572-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo Esquivel","key":"jaramillopau","last":"Jaramillo","name":"Jaramillo, Alfredo Esquivel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.specom.2023.04.002","issn":["01676393","18727182"],"issn_org":["01676393"],"journal":"Speech Communication","pages":"9-23","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Speech Communication","volume":"151"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159592944"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-72c7bb7e-da93-4615-b8d1-63765ec76fa8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An adaptive autoregressive pre-whitener for speech and acoustic signals based on parametric NMF","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705416","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper Bie","Madeleine, Pascal","Sørensen, Line Bay","Sachau, Juliane","Otto, J. C.","Baron, R.","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705545"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-22","place":"Budapest, hu","start":"2023-09-20","title":"13th Congress of the European Pain Federation EFIC","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jesper Bie"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["AMEOS Gruppe","All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"individual conditioned pain modulation responses in patients with chronic pain explorative findings from a multicenter trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-705545","ids":["aau-89bb78e4-3ca2-4660-a1c2-9e58b8a04fa1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B96373D70BCA0F590FC3968F2B27A602"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Musculoskeletal Health and Implementation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university medical center schleswig holstein","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ameos gruppe","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"AMEOS Gruppe","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"16d35f43-63eb-473e-a466-4f5a12d5f43f","name":"Larsen, Jesper Bie","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-7913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Bay","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"70e36cd9-caf8-4dba-bf93-8c21a28383e0","name":"Sørensen, Line Bay","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juliane","key":"sachaupau","last":"Sachau","name":"Sachau, Juliane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"J. C.","key":"ottopau","last":"Otto","name":"Otto, J. C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"baronpau","last":"Baron","name":"Baron, R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-89bb78e4-3ca2-4660-a1c2-9e58b8a04fa1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Individual conditioned pain modulation responses in patients with chronic pain : Explorative findings from a multicenter trial","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705545","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In his landmark paper at TCC 2008 Paul Valiant introduced the notion of “incrementally verifiable computation” which enables a prover to incrementally compute a succinct proof of correct execution of a (potentially) long running process. The paper later won the 2019 TCC test of time award. The construction was proven secure in the random oracle model without any further computational assumptions. However, the overall proof was given using a non-standard version of the random-oracle methodology where sometimes the hash function is a random oracle and sometimes it has a short description as a circuit. Valiant clearly noted that this model is non-standard, but conjectured that the standard random oracle methodology would not suffice. This conjecture has been open for 14 years. We prove that if the proof system can receive a long witness as input in an incremental manner and is also zero-knowledge then the conjecture is true. Valiant’s original construction does not have these properties but can easily be extended to have them in his model. We relate our result to recent possibility and impossibility results for SNARKs and incrementally verifiable computation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hall-Andersen, Mathias Nørup","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-709137"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lower bounds","Proof systems","Zero knowledge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on valiant s conjecture impossibility of incrementally verifiable computation from random oracles","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85161673756","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-709137","identifier":[{"id":"85161673756","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bffb55d3-5f4a-4315-ab7d-18f780338522"],"keyword":["Idealized Models","Lower Bounds","Proof Systems","Separations and Impossibility Results","Zero-Knowledge"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E7D3FCA68611214D7B866BABC8466278"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Nørup","key":"hallandersenpau","last":"Hall-Andersen","locid":"9037f5a8-e72e-4d59-a56b-8d20df254102","name":"Hall-Andersen, Mathias Nørup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carmit","key":"hazaypedh","last":"Hazay","name":"Hazay, Carmit","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Martijn","key":"stampedh","last":"Stam","name":"Stam, Martijn","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-30617-4_15","eisbn":["9783031306174"],"isbn":["9783031306167"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"438-469","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"42nd Annual International Conference on the Theory and Applications of Cryptographic Techniques, Lyon, France, April 23–27, 2023, Proceedings, Part II","title":"Advances in Cryptology – EUROCRYPT 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161673756"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bffb55d3-5f4a-4315-ab7d-18f780338522"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"On Valiant's Conjecture : Impossibility of Incrementally Verifiable Computation from Random Oracles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-709137","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the use of colour and brightness for feedback from sound zone systems. User interaction with sound zones suffer from them being invisible. Hence, spatial properties such as volume, size, and overlaps need to be represented through, e.g., light. Two studies were conducted. In the first study (N27), participants experienced different colour and brightness values shown on an LED strip attached to a volume controller and related those to sound zone volume, size, and overlaps. In the second study (N36), participants created an overlap between two sound zones by turning up the volume, triggering 12 animated light patterns. Our findings show that brightness reflects well the size of a sound zone, and that instant patterns are better indicators of overlaps compared to gradual patterns. These contributions are useful for designing sound zone visualisations.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Johansen, Stine S.","Nielsen, Peter Axel","Stec, Kashmiri","Kjeldskov, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-716620"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-01","place":"York, gb","start":"2023-08-28","title":"19th IFIP TC 13 International Conference on Human-Computer Interaction, INTERACT 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Johansen, Stine S."],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queensland University of Technology"],"keyword":["Brightness","Colour","Light","Sound zone"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-BOO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-BOO","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using colour and brightness for sound zone feedback","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85171445600&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-716620","identifier":[{"id":"85171445600","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-10546d57-9308-4c99-acf3-221086a4c4bf"],"keyword":["Brightness","Colour","Light","Sound zone"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF5247F85DC816826FD0112EAAEE9375"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"queensland university of technology","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Queensland University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"bang olufsen","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-BOO","l3nl":"Bang & Olufsen","l3nn":"Bang & Olufsen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bang & Olufsen","namevar":["Bang & Olufsen A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-BOO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Stine S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Axel","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d5302c36-a512-42d6-8ab5-32d3f7da115e","name":"Nielsen, Peter Axel","orcid":"0000-0002-0282-7445","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kashmiri","key":"stecpau","last":"Stec","name":"Stec, Kashmiri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"kjeldskovpau","last":"Kjeldskov","locid":"90f5514b-34fa-4d01-98dd-ed6166dd1489","name":"Kjeldskov, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7990-4229","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"abdelnournocerapedh","last":"Abdelnour Nocera","name":"Abdelnour Nocera, José","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marta","key":"kristínlárusdóttirpedh","last":"Kristín Lárusdóttir","name":"Kristín Lárusdóttir, Marta","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Helen","key":"petriepedh","last":"Petrie","name":"Petrie, Helen","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonio","key":"piccinnopedh","last":"Piccinno","name":"Piccinno, Antonio","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"wincklerpedh","last":"Winckler","name":"Winckler, Marco","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-42280-5_15","eisbn":["9783031422805"],"isbn":["9783031422799"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"247-272","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"19th IFIP TC13 International Conference, York, UK, August 28 – September 1, 2023, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Human-Computer Interaction – INTERACT 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171445600"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Bang & Olufsen","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-10546d57-9308-4c99-acf3-221086a4c4bf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Using Colour and Brightness for Sound Zone Feedback","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-716620","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Thyroid autoimmunity is the most prevalent autoimmune disorder among women of reproductive age and has been suggested as a risk factor in recurrent pregnancy loss (RPL)—a condition in which couples suffer several consecutive pregnancy losses, but where a cause can be identified in less than half of the cases. Most studies have focused on thyroid peroxidase antibodies (TPOAbs), not considering the presence of thyroglobulin antibodies (TgAbs). The aim of this study was to systematically assess the prevalence of TgAb positivity in women with RPL, and whether TgAb positivity was associated with the outcome of the next pregnancy. Methods: A systematic literature search of PubMed and Embase (from inception to April 29, 2023) was performed for studies reporting on TgAbs in women with RPL. The primary outcome was TgAb positivity in women with RPL compared with women without RPL, with a secondary outcome of association between TgAb positivity and the outcome of the next pregnancy. Pooled effect estimates were expressed as odds ratios (ORs) with confidence intervals [CI] using a random-effects model. The study was registered with PROSPERO (No. CRD42022310232) and adhered to the PRISMA guidelines. Results: A total of 770 studies were screened, 28 of which could be included reporting data from a total of 6868 women. The prevalence of TgAb positivity in women with RPL ranged from 3.6% to 28% compared with 2.4% to 29% in women without RPL. The OR for TgAb positivity was 1.93 ([CI 1.27–2.92]; I2 = 63%) compared with women without RPL, and for TgAbs and/or TPOAbs 2.66 ([CI 1.75–4.05]; I2 = 69%). Four studies reported on the outcome of the next pregnancy after antibody measurement with highly heterogeneous results (OR for pregnancy loss ranging from 0.99 in one study to 10.0 in the other study, and two studies reported no data eligible for meta-analysis). Consequently, a meta-analysis could not be performed. Conclusions: Women with RPL were significantly more often TgAb-positive than women without RPL. Although there was a lack of studies reporting prospective outcomes, the findings of this study support the significance of awareness about the strong association between RPL and thyroid autoimmunity.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Huisman, Perrine","Krogh, Jesper","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Bliddal, Sofie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719781"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University"],"keyword":["Meta analysis","Pregnancy","Recurrent pregnancy loss","Systematic review","thyroglobulin antibodies","thyroid autoimmunity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thyroglobulin antibodies in women with recurrent pregnancy loss a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-719781","identifier":[{"id":"85175485657","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37725583","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-33cb2789-55f2-4484-8cf4-66d365187df7"],"keyword":["meta-analysis","pregnancy","recurrent pregnancy loss","systematic review","thyroglobulin antibodies","thyroid autoimmunity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E96F09C619809401E7FA5DF17B031B4B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"leiden university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leiden University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark",