:"19","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise M","key":"thomapau","last":"Thoma","name":"Thoma, Louise M","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","corresponding":null,"first":"Elizabeth","key":"wellsandtpau","last":"Wellsandt","name":"Wellsandt, Elizabeth","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"21","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel K","key":"whitepau","last":"White","name":"White, Daniel K","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie A","key":"holdenpau","last":"Holden","name":"Holden, Melanie A","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36631968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/msc.1732","issn":["14782189","15570681"],"issn_org":["14782189"],"issue":"2","journal":"Musculoskeletal Care","pages":"545-555","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Musculoskeletal Care","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146154502"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6eab739b-467b-40a3-88b8-9559588d01b8","sdu-b914a9e3-e4d2-4202-9d36-ac7ed14b6b83"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"What should a toolkit to aid the delivery of therapeutic exercise for hip and knee osteoarthritis look like? : Qualitative analysis of an international survey of 318 researchers, clinicians, and consumers by the OARSI Rehabilitation Discussion Group","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.89-672347","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To assess temporal changes in the surgical management of patients with tetralogy of Fallot including the timing of interventions, surgical techniques, reinterventions and survival in a nationwide cohort. METHODS: Patients with tetralogy of Fallot in Denmark were divided into 3 eras based on their year of birth: early (1977–1991), intermediate (1992–2006) and late (2007–2021). RESULTS: The cohort consisted of 745 patients. Median follow-up was 21.2 years (13.7–30.5). There was a temporal trend towards less shunt palliation (–0.3% per year, 95% CI –0.05 to –0.1). Median age at intracardiac repair was 2.9 years (1.8–5.0), 0.8 years (0.5–1.3) and 0.5 years (0.4–0.7) (P < 0.001) in the early, intermediate and late era, respectively. There was a temporal trend towards less valve-sparing repair (–0.7% per year, 95% CI –0.5 to –1.0) and more repair with transannular patches (0.7% per year, 95% CI 0.5–1.0). Survival at 10 years was 79% (64–76), 90% (87–93) and 95% (92–98) (P < 0.001) and pulmonary valve replacement within the first 10 years after intracardiac repair was performed in 3% (1–6), 12% (8–16) and 21% (13–29) (P < 0.001) in the early, intermediate and late era, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: There was a temporal trend towards less shunt palliation and intracardiac repair at a younger age with more use of transannular patches. While survival throughout childhood and adolescence has improved, more patients undergo pulmonary valve replacement during the first 10 years after intracardiac repair.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Gröning, Mathis","Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","Nielsen, Dorte Guldbrand","Nissen, Henrik","Munk, Kim","Mortensen, Ulrik Markus","Andersen, Helle","Engholm, Morten","Bjerre, Jesper","Vejlstrup, Niels","Juul, Klaus","Søndergaard, Eva","Jensen, Annette Schophuus","Jørgensen, Troels Højsgaard","Thyregod, Hans Gustav Hørsted","Andersen, Henrik Ørbæk","Jøns, Christian","Helvind, Morten","Sondergaard, Lars"],"cuid":["S03-092.50-685938"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Gröning, Mathis"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Cardiac Surgical Procedures methods","Child","Child Preschool","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Infant","Intracardiac repair","Palliative shunt","Pulmonary valve replacement","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Survival","Tetralogy of Fallot","Tetralogy of Fallot surgery","Transannular patch","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal changes in the surgical management of patients with tetralogy of fallot in denmark a nationwide cohort study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85158103697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-092.50-685938","identifier":[{"id":"85158103697","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36617167","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-61ee8d70-de8b-47e1-94ea-272d9f38bd08","ku-4b4ef31c-3243-4ae2-bd40-ddeecac3f26d","sdu-6d6524c0-4bf6-4fef-93b1-4e58b374d5c1"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Cardiac Surgical Procedures/methods","Child","Child, Preschool","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Infant","Intracardiac repair","Palliative shunt","Pulmonary Valve/surgery","Pulmonary valve replacement","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Survival","Tetralogy of Fallot","Tetralogy of Fallot/surgery","Transannular patch","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-771AFF364ECEBA2CB8004266431901F4"],"org":