,"first":"Lars","key":"søndergaardlarspau","last":"Sondergaard","locid":"6a064e1f-1f3e-480c-a5a2-53086732b169","name":"Søndergaard, Lars","name_org":"Sondergaard, Lars","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36617167"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ejcts/ezad007","issn":["10107940","1873734X"],"issn_org":["10107940"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","paperid":"ezad007","publisher":"European Association for Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85158103697"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-61ee8d70-de8b-47e1-94ea-272d9f38bd08","ku-4b4ef31c-3243-4ae2-bd40-ddeecac3f26d","sdu-6d6524c0-4bf6-4fef-93b1-4e58b374d5c1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Temporal Changes in the Surgical Management of Patients with Tetralogy of Fallot in Denmark - A Nationwide Cohort Study.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.50-685938","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims Insights into subclinical atrial fibrillation (AF) development are warranted to inform the strategies of screening and subsequent clinical management upon AF detection. Hence, this study sought to characterize the onset and progression of subclinical AF with respect to 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG) parameters. Methods We included AF-naïve individuals aged 70–90 years with additional stroke risk factors who underwent implantable loop re- and results corder (ILR) monitoring in the LOOP Study. Using data from daily ILR recordings and the computerized analysis of baseline ECG, we studied empirically selected ECG parameters for AF detection (≥6 min), cumulative AF burden, long-lasting AF (≥24 h), and AF progression. Of 1370 individuals included, 419 (30.6%) developed AF during follow-up, with a mean cumulative AF burden of 1.5% [95% CI: 1.2–1.8]. Several P-wave-related and ventricular ECG parameters were associated with new-onset AF and with cumulative AF burden in AF patients. P-wave duration (PWD), P-wave terminal force in Lead V 1, and interatrial block (IAB) further demonstrated significant associations with long-lasting AF. Among AF patients, we observed an overall reduction in cumulative AF burden over time (IRR 0.70 [95% CI: 0.51–0.96]), whereas IAB was related to an increased risk of progression to AF ≥24 h (HR 1.86 [95% CI: 1.02–3.39]). Further spline analysis also revealed longer PWD to be associated with this progression in AF duration. Conclusion We identified several ECG parameters associated with new-onset subclinical AF detected by ILR. Especially PWD and IAB were robustly related to the onset and the burden of AF as well as progression over time.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Xing, Lucas Yixi","Diederichsen, Søren Zöga","Højberg, Søren","Krieger, Derk W","Graff, Claus","Olesen, Morten S","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Brandes, Axel","Køber, Lars","Haugan, Ketil Jørgen","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S03-095.46-715742"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dubai Hospital","Mediclinic City Hospital","Mohammed Bin Rashid University of Medicine and Health Sciences"],"keyword":["Association","Atrial Fibrillation diagnosis","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac arrhythmias","Duration","Electrocardiography","Electrocardiography Ambulatory","Electrocardiography methods","Electrodes Implanted adverse effects","Humans","Individuals","Interatrial Block","P wave","PR interval","Risk","Risk Factors","Stroke","Stroke prevention control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrocardiographic markers of subclinical atrial fibrillation detected by implantable loop recorder insights from the loop study","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euad014","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Christian Kronborg (University of Southern Denmark, Denmark) for his contribution to the trial steering committee of the LOOP Study. We thank Dan Atar (Oslo University Hospital Ullevål, Norway), Gregory Y. H. Lip (The University of Liverpool, UK), and Mårten Rosenqvist (Karolinska Institutet and Danderyd Hospital, Sweden) for their contribution in the international advisory committee of the LOOP Study. We thank our colleagues at Rigshospitalet, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital, Zealand University Hospital, and Odense University Hospital who assisted with the conduct of the LOOP Study. The LOOP Study was supported by Innovation Fund Denmark [grant number 12-1352259], The Research Foundation for the Capital Region of Denmark, The Danish Heart Foundation [grant number 11-04-R83-A3363-22625], Aalborg University Talent Management Program, Arvid Nilssons Fond, Skibsreder Per Henriksen, R og Hustrus Fond, Horizon 2020 [grant number 847770 to the AFFECT-EU consortium], Læge Sophus Carl Emil Friis og hustru Olga Doris Friis’ Legat, and an unrestricted grant from Medtronic. The employment of the first author, L.Y.X., is funded by the AFFECT-EU consortium and thereby the Horizon 2020 programme."],"id":"S03-095.46-715742","identifier":[{"id":"85166172682","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10227658","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000973636400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"37068888","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a06a64b6-ed1f-404d-9faa-7f96d43cde03","ku-a5ef67e5-780a-48a7-aae1-86b3c867b01b","sdu-04622e5e-5f10-48fd-af44-70545d3d47f9"],"keyword":["ASSOCIATION","Atrial Fibrillation/diagnosis","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac arrhythmias","DURATION","Electrocardiography","Electrocardiography, Ambulatory","Electrocardiography/methods","Electrodes, Implanted/adverse effects","Humans","INDIVIDUALS","Interatrial Block","P-wave","PR INTERVAL","RISK","Risk Factors","Stroke","Stroke/prevention & control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-9-3005EE4FC19AA196A87A78699F701286"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/254743262/euad014.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/532401240/euad014.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359315142/Electrocardiographic_markers.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","t