{"abstract":"During spring 2021, AZD1222 and BNT162b2 were used as prime and BNT162b2 as booster COVID-19 vaccines in Denmark. We obtained self-reported information on systemic reactogenicity day-by-day during two weeks for 2862 healthcare workers vaccinated with heterologous AZD1222+BNT162b2 or homologous BNT162b2+BNT162b2 regimens and compared prevalences of symptoms with unvaccinated healthcare workers. We found comparable systemic reactogenicity during the first week in the two vaccine regimens and no reactogenicity during the second week. Most of the symptoms returned to a level equal to the control population four days after booster vaccination.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Tabatabaeifar, Sorosh","Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","Würtz, Else Toft","Hansen, Karoline Kærgaard","Nielsen, Kent Jacob","Schlünssen, Vivi","Kolstad, Henrik A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-200260"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COVID 19 vaccine","Cohort study","Healthcare workers","Vaccine safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systemic reactogenicity following homologues and heterologous prime boost azd000000001222 and bnt000000000162b000000000002 covid 000000000019 vaccination of 000000002862 healthcare workers compared with an unvaccinated population","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jvacx.2023.100280","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-200260","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10010832","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36945661","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85150465960","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7bf73839-c43a-47ed-893a-76400b427429"],"keyword":["COVID-19 vaccine","Cohort study","Healthcare workers","Systemic reactogenicity","Vaccine safety"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C1E7ABFBBCEFF8438452D675E839626"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jvacx.2023.100280","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Occupational and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sorosh","key":"tabatabaeifarpau","last":"Tabatabaeifar","locid":"1d3658a5-f16f-4310-a3bb-4cf94dfdcf5c","name":"Tabatabaeifar, Sorosh","orcid":"0000-0001-8635-6523","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Medom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f2a2e103-1293-4370-b308-c4427f184a75","name":"Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-6566","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Else Toft","key":"würtzpau","last":"Würtz","locid":"34d10331-97e4-447e-9b2d-c7b956b06e91","name":"Würtz, Else Toft","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karoline Kærgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c915b720-5c0e-418a-8f3b-7a578ddee804","name":"Hansen, Karoline Kærgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3508-6727","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent Jacob","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b11fecf5-8895-4034-a7b1-d5eb0399ea93","name":"Nielsen, Kent Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-4643-5697","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vivi","key":"schlünssenpau","last":"Schlünssen","locid":"422d1a4f-145b-4418-b776-7450d942d03e","name":"Schlünssen, Vivi","orcid":"0000-0003-4915-1734","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik A.","key":"kolstadpau","last":"Kolstad","locid":"287e6e28-266e-42e8-aa6d-10dffb6dc51e","name":"Kolstad, Henrik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6535-4323","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36945661"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jvacx.2023.100280","issn":["25901362"],"journal":"Vaccine: X","paperid":"100280","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Vaccine: X","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150465960"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7bf73839-c43a-47ed-893a-76400b427429"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Systemic reactogenicity following homologues and heterologous prime-boost AZD1222 and BNT162b2 COVID-19 vaccination of 2862 healthcare workers compared with an unvaccinated population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-200260","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims Beyond 1 year after percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI), guidelines recommend anticoagulant monotherapy in patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) rather than dual therapy with an anticoagulant and an antiplatelet drug. The risks and benefits of this strategy, however, remain uncertain. We examined hospitalization for bleeding and ischaemic risk beyond 1 year after PCI in patients with AF treated with monotherapy vs. dual therapy. Furthermore, among patients treated with monotherapy, we compared direct oral anticoagulant (DOAC) therapy and vitamin K antagonist (VKA) therapy. Methods and results We included all patients with AF undergoing first-time PCI between 2003 and 2017 from the Western Denmark Heart Registry and followed them for up to 4 years. Follow-up started 15 months after PCI to enable assessment of medical treatment after 12 months. Using a Cox regression model, we computed weighted hazard ratios (HR w) of hospitalization for bleeding and major adverse cardiac events (MACEs). Analyses comparing monotherapy vs. dual therapy included 3331 patients, and analyses comparing DOAC vs. VKA monotherapy included 1275 patients. Risks of hospitalization for bleeding [HR w 0.90, 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.75–1.09] and MACE (HR w 1.04, 95% CI 0.90–1.19) were similar with monotherapy and dual therapy. Similarly, risks of hospitalization for bleeding (HR w 1.27, 95% CI 0.84–1.92) and MACE (HR w 1.15, 95% CI 0.87–1.50) were equal with DOAC and VKA monotherapy. Conclusion Our results support long-term OAC monotherapy beyond 1 year after PCI in patients with atrial fibrillation and suggest that DOAC monotherapy is as safe and effective as VKA monotherapy.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Jensen, Thomas","Thrane, Pernille Gro","Olesen, Kevin Kris Warnakula","Würtz, Morten","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Gyldenkerne, Christine","Thim, Troels","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Kristensen, Steen Dalby","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Eikelboom, John W","Maeng, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-219738"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Maeng, Michael"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","McMaster University"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding","Cohort study","Coronary intervention","Percutaneous","Thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antithrombotic treatment beyond 000000000001 year after percutaneous coronary intervention in patients with atrial fibrillation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85159050997","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-219738","identifier":[{"id":"36269306","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85159050997","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9eb5a09e-3167-42a4-abfa-095dd6fb12e6"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding","Cohort study","Percutaneous","Thromboembolism","coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3BA4C8610F86077F7E1D7667006BFF37"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"mcmaster university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McMaster University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"jensenthomaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f3739755-fb40-406e-b577-af166c82442a","name":"Jensen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-5054-4108","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Gro","key":"thranepernillegropau","last":"Thrane","locid":"02268f3c-db36-4f53-b023-98dd3d2df60d","name":"Thrane, Pernille Gro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kevin Kris Warnakula","key":"olesenkevinkriswarnakulapau","last":"Olesen","locid":"3042515e-4af3-4545-987c-15f6276c0fae","name":"Olesen, Kevin Kris Warnakula","orcid":"0000-0002-0560-3615","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"würtzmortenpau","last":"Würtz","locid":"b5e070b9-ecf1-43ae-83c2-164d5eeccfc5","name":"Würtz, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7150-7704","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bødtker","key":"mortensenmartinbødtkerpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f995af52-018b-4fa9-a398-c1bdc7ab1bd0","name":"Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christine","key":"gyldenkernechristinepau","last":"Gyldenkerne","locid":"b1e91a98-3e63-492f-a378-0372c7d3b958","name":"Gyldenkerne, Christine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Troels","key":"thimtroelspau","last":"Thim","locid":"1d4a89fa-3b3a-498e-8507-d387d518e83c","name":"Thim, Troels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardbjarnelindepau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenjespermøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Dalby","key":"kristensensteendalbypau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenjenscosedispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"John W","key":"eikelboomjohnwpau","last":"Eikelboom","name":"Eikelboom, John W","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"maengmichaelpau","last":"Maeng","locid":"e4bc8bdc-eeb6-419f-94dc-5eb69e03a564","name":"Maeng, Michael","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36269306"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjcvp/pvac058","issn":["20556837"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Heart Journal - Cardiovascular Pharmacotherapy","pages":"208-219","paperid":"208-219","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal - Cardiovascular Pharmacotherapy","title_org":"European heart journal - Cardiovascular pharmacotherapy","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159050997"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9eb5a09e-3167-42a4-abfa-095dd6fb12e6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Antithrombotic treatment beyond 1 year after percutaneous coronary intervention in patients with atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-219738","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The left atrial appendage (LAA) sealing properties of the Amplatzer Amulet and Watchman FLX devices were compared using cardiac computed tomography (CT) follow-up. METHODS: Single-center cohort study of patients undergoing LAAO between 2017 and 2020. Two consecutive cohorts were enrolled, one treated with the Amplatzer Amulet (n = 150) up till 2019, and a second cohort treated with the Watchman FLX (n = 150) device from 2019. Cardiac CT was performed 2 months postprocedure. The primary outcome was complete LAA occlusion defined as no visible peri-device leak (PDL) and absence of contrast patency in the distal LAA. Secondary outcomes included PDL, contrast patency without visible PDL, PDL area, and periprocedural complications. RESULTS: Complete occlusion was achieved in 39 (30.5%) of the Amulet group, compared to 89 (71.8%) of the FLX group, p < 0.001. A PDL at the Amulet disc was present in 65 (50.8%), at the lobe in 16 (12.5%), and at both the disc and lobe in 13 (10.2%). For FLX, a PDL was present in 20 (16.1%). Contrast patency without visible PDL was observed in 24 (18.8%) and 15 (12.1%) of the Amulet and FLX group, respectively. The PDL area at the Amulet mid-lobe was 92 mm2 (59-158) and 32 mm2 (IQR 28-96) for FLX, p = 0.019. Device-related thrombosis occurred in 1 (0.7%) and 2 (1.3%), respectively (p = 0.99), with periprocedural adverse events occurring in 6 (4%) and 8 (5.3%) of the Amulet and FLX group (p = 0.79). CONCLUSION: Complete LAA occlusion was achieved in a significantly higher proportion treated with the Watchman FLX compared to the Amulet device. PDL was smaller with the FLX than the Amulet. Conceptual device design differences make interpretation of results complex, and additional studies with clinical outcomes are needed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Korsholm, Kasper","Kramer, Anders","Andersen, Asger","Saw, Jacqueline","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-223190"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vancouver General Hospital"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Computed tomography","Left atrial appendage occlusion","Watchman"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"left atrial appendage sealing performance of the amplatzer amulet and watchman flx device","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10840-022-01336-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-223190","identifier":[{"id":"35951214","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135857205","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9977851","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-a4b7d13d-e44f-41fd-b490-b28446e5a833"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Computed tomography","Left atrial appendage occlusion","Watchman"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9608DE9B6FDB84F6CBD37E6D88977712"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/401963338/Left_atrial_appendage_sealing_performance_of_the_Amplatzer_Amulet_and_Watchman_FLX_device.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10840-022-01336-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"vancouver general hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Vancouver General Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"kramerpau","last":"Kramer","locid":"be3123b5-5f55-4c8a-930c-f0f39cbc2981","name":"Kramer, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5546-8693","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a87aec57-562e-4950-b4cf-6741aae86cf1","name":"Andersen, Asger","orcid":"0000-0002-9102-3130","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacqueline","key":"sawpau","last":"Saw","name":"Saw, Jacqueline","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35951214"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10840-022-01336-4","issn":["1383875X","15728595"],"issn_org":["1383875X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","pages":"391-401","publisher":"Spr