{"abstract":"A practical estimation methodology of the mean added resistance in irregular waves is shown, and the present paper provides statistical analyses of estimates for ships in actual conditions. The study merges telemetry data of more than 200 in-service container vessels with ocean re-analysis data from ERA5. Theoretical estimates relying on spectral calculations of added resistance are made for both long- and short-crested waves and are based on a combination of a parametric expression for the wave spectrum and a semi-empirical formula for the added resistance transfer function. The theoretical estimates are compared to predictions from an indirect calculation of added resistance relying on shaft power measurements and empirical estimates of the remaining resistance components. Overall, the comparison reveals a bias in bow oblique waves and higher sea states of the spectral estimates as well as the large variance of the empirically derived predictions — particularly in beam-to-following waves. One of the study’s main findings, confirming previous studies but based on a much larger dataset than in earlier similar studies, is that added resistance assessment based on in-service data is complex due to significant associated uncertainties.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mittendorf, Malte","Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","Bingham, Harry B.","Dietz, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308204"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mittendorf, Malte"],"keyword":["Added resistance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of added resistance estimates based on monitoring data from a fleet of container vessels","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oceaneng.2023.113892","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-308204","identifier":[{"id":"85147926612","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0c0ef3fc-0617-43d4-bcce-409aea4b772c"],"keyword":["Added resistance","Fleet performance data","Metocean hindcast data","Parametric wave spectrum","Resistance decomposition","Spectral calculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7B12CAE6BB00B06F20C212732BAD2CF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oceaneng.2023.113892","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/309701986/1_s2.0_S0029801823002767_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"a p moller maersk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-MAE","l3nl":"A.P. Møller – Mærsk","l3nn":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","namevar":["Maersk Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-MAE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malte","key":"mittendorfpau","last":"Mittendorf","locid":"ae77e558-e392-4fcf-a5c8-696a8e5f97f3","name":"Mittendorf, Malte","orcid":"0000-0002-0529-0962","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Harry B.","key":"binghampau","last":"Bingham","locid":"ce245728-e918-4e11-90de-d143c2403110","name":"Bingham, Harry B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7263-442X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oceaneng.2023.113892","issn":["00298018","18735258"],"issn_org":["00298018"],"journal":"Ocean Engineering","paperid":"113892","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ocean Engineering","volume":"272"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147926612"],"search":{"DAF":["A.P. Møller – Mærsk","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0c0ef3fc-0617-43d4-bcce-409aea4b772c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assessment of added resistance estimates based on monitoring data from a fleet of container vessels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308204","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Extracellular matrix (ECM) remodeling of the skin is a continuous process necessary for maintaining tissue homeostasis. Type VI collagen (COL6) is characterized as a beaded filament, located in the dermal ECM, where COL6-α6-chain has been demonstrated upregulated in atopic dermatitis. The aim of this study was to develop and validate a competitive ELISA, targeting the N-terminal of COL6-α6-chain, named C6A6, and evaluate its associations with the dermatological condition’s atopic dermatitis, psoriasis, hidradenitis suppurativa, systemic lupus erythematosus, systemic sclerosis, urticaria, vitiligo, and cutaneous malignant melanoma in comparison, to healthy controls. A monoclonal antibody was raised and employed in an ELISA assay. The assay was developed, technically validated, and evaluated in two independent patient cohorts. Cohort 1 showed C6A6 was significantly elevated in patients with atopic dermatitis (p < 0.0001), psoriasis (p < 0.0001), hidradenitis suppurativa (p = 0.0095), systemic lupus erythematosus (p = 0.0032) and melanoma (p < 0.0001) compared to healthy donors. Cohort 2 confirmed C6A6 being upregulated in atopic dermatitis compared to healthy controls (p < 0.0001), but also associated with disease severity (SCORAD, p = 0.046) and lowered in patients receiving calcineurin inhibitors (p = 0.014). These findings are hypothesis generating, and the utility of the C6A6 biomarker for disease severity and treatment response needs to be validated in larger cohorts and longitudinal studies.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Holm Nielsen, Signe","Port, Helena","Møller Hausgaard, Cecilie","Holm, Jesper Grønlund","Thyssen, Jacob P.","Groen, Solveig Skovlund","Karsdal, Morten","Nielsen, Valdemar Wendelboe","Egeberg, Alexander","Bay-Jensen, Anne Christine","Thomsen, Simon Francis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436997"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fragment of type vi collagen alpha 000000000006 chain is elevated in serum from patients with atopic dermatitis psoriasis hidradenitis suppurativa systemic lupus erythematosus and melanoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-28746-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-436997","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9945456","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36810294","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85148551029","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-48f6949a-d381-49c6-a081-425895fe593d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-93875E08B4D0F6A34E0134CA53F23655"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/337994023/A_fragment_of_type_VI_collagen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-28746-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Signe","key":"holmnielsenpau","last":"Holm Nielsen","name":"Holm Nielsen, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Helena","key":"portpau","last":"Port","name":"Port, Helena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie","key":"møllerhausgaardpau","last":"Møller Hausgaard","name":"Møller Hausgaard, Cecilie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Grønlund","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jesper Grønlund","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Jacob P.","key":"thyssenpau","last":"Thyssen","locid":"c02c08ab-10c1-4ce8-bec3-447154952fc2","name":"Thyssen, Jacob P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Solveig Skovlund","key":"groenpau","last":"Groen","locid":"c3ed8d9e-938e-4f49-a455-50b597700222","name":"Groen, Solveig Skovlund","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"karsdalpau","last":"Karsdal","name":"Karsdal, Morten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Valdemar Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Valdemar Wendelboe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Alexander","key":"egebergpau","last":"Egeberg","locid":"e4445a48-c228-4507-b47c-a83175478f82","name":"Egeberg, Alexander","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Christine","key":"bayjensenpau","last":"Bay-Jensen","name":"Bay-Jensen, Anne Christine","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Simon Francis","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36810294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-023-28746-2","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"3056","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148551029"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-48f6949a-d381-49c6-a081-425895fe593d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A fragment of type VI collagen alpha-6 chain is elevated in serum from patients with atopic dermatitis, psoriasis, hidradenitis suppurativa, systemic lupus erythematosus and melanoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436997","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Little is known about the combined effect of several risk factors occurring simultaneously, and the perspectives of patients with language barriers or dementia are lacking because these patients are often excluded as research participants. This study aimed at investigating medication safety among older migrants with cognitive disorders who use five or more medications daily from the perspective of older patients and their relatives. Eight semi-structured interviews with patients and relatives were conducted in their homes. The study adopted an inductive hermeneutic phenomenological approach and used both 'Analyzing the present' and 'Systematic text condensation' as inspiration for the analysis. Three main themes were identified: (i) potential medication safety and threats, (ii) communication and missing medication information, and (iii) everyday life with medication. Threats to medication safety included medication perceptions, health perceptions, and cognitive impairment of the patient as well as miscommunication amongst departments, wrong diagnosis and medication, and unlocked medication cabinets. However, most families expressed having no problems concerning medication, which could be a result of limited engagement of the patient and relatives in the medical treatment and limited medication information provided to the families by health care professionals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lynnerup, Camilla","Rossing, Charlotte","Sodemann, Morten","Ryg, Jesper","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600813"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lynnerup, Camilla"],"keyword":["Health perception","Medication information","Migrant health","Qualitative Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pharmakon"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perspectives on medication safety from vulnerable older migrants and their relatives a qualitative explorative study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13842","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-600813","identifier":[{"id":"36750434","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85148455043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-608744d8-52cb-45ea-af08-fdcb2e1586fb"],"keyword":["health perception","medication information","migrant health","qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E0DFBEF25377C0ED36385341E077160F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13842","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/226230188/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_2023_Lynnerup_Perspectives_on_medication_safety_from_vulnerable_older_migrants_and_their.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pharmakon"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"lynneruppau","last":"Lynnerup","locid":"4e3683f0-d2f5-4fd0-ba5e-0f4654f745d3","name":"Lynnerup, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0002-8242-846X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","name":"Rossing, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannpau","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36750434"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.13842","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"5","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"392-402","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","volume":"132"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148455043"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-608744d8-52cb-45ea-af08-fdcb2e1586fb"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Perspectives on medication safety from vulnerable older migrants and their relatives - a qualitative explorative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-600813","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Determining patients' cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) preferences in the emergency department (ED) is common practice but the stability of these preferences and their recollection by patients has been questioned. Therefore, this study assessed the stability and recall of CPR preferences of older patients at and following ED discharge. METHODS: This survey-based cohort study was conducted between February and September 2020 at three EDs in Denmark. It consecutively asked mentally competent patients aged 65 years or older who were admitted to hospital through the ED and then one and six months later \"In your current state of health, do you wish that physicians should try to intervene if your heart stops beating?\" Possible responses were confined to \"definitely yes\", \"definitely no\", \"uncertain\", and \"prefer not to answer\". RESULTS: In total, 3688 patients admitted to hospital via the ED patients were screened, 1766 were eligible and 491 (27.8%) were included: median age was 76 (IQR 71-82) years, and 257 (52.3%) were men. One third of patients who expressed definite yes or no preferences in ED had changed their preference at one month follow-up. Only 90 (27.4%) and 94 (35.7%) patients recalled their preferences at one and six months follow-up, respectively. CONCLUSION: and Relevance In this study, one-in-three older ED patients who initially expressed definite resuscitation preferences had changed their minds at one month follow-up. Preferences were more stable at six months but only a minority were able to recall their preferences.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hanson, Stine","Lassen, Annmarie Touborg","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","Ryg, Jesper","Forero, Roberto","Brabrand, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-685244"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Hanson, Stine"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ingham Institute for Applied Medical Research","Western Sydney University"],"keyword":["Aged","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Cohort Studies","Emergency department","End of life","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Independence","Male","Physicians","Preferences","Recall","Resuscitation","Resuscitation Orders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resuscitation preferences of older acutely admitted medical and mentally competent patients with one and six months follow up","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109836","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-685244","identifier":[{"id":"37196801","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85161493617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8bebedef-842c-4156-891b-7914701e15c7"],"keyword":["Aged","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Cohort Studies","Emergency department","End of life","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Independence","Male","Physicians","Preferences","Recall","Resuscitation","Resuscitation Orders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-06C6F5356E5B98C50F84EFC4D340E4FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/237796846/PIIS0300957223001491.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109836","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"western sydney university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Western Sydney University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"ingham institute for applied medical research","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Ingham Institute for Applied Medical Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"bba8709c-7b49-489b-ad24-64d9019447a9","name":"Hanson, Stine","orcid":"0000-0002-7699-8001","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annmarie","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"80e651b5-e70f-43e0-baf8-e88335ac10b8","name":"Lassen, Annmarie Touborg","name_org":"Lassen, Annmarie","orcid":"0000-0003-4942-6152","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"foreropau","last":"Forero","name":"Forero, Roberto","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"96dae706-4310-46de-ac4f-447df19289f6","name":"Brabrand, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-3340-8251","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37196801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109836","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","paperid":"109836","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","t