{"abstract":"Background and aims: Chronic itch is a common symptom of several pathological conditions with a lifetime prevalence of about 20%. In most conditions chronic itch follows a histamine-independent pathway, involving a subgroup of polymodal C-fibers that can be experimentally activated by the application of BAM8-22, an agonist of Mas-related G protein-coupled receptor X1 (MrgprX1). Moreover, the TRPA1 receptor downstream activation can likewise be involved in non-histaminergic itch generation. This study aimed to evaluate the interaction between MrgprX1 and TRPA1 by modulating BAM8-22-induced non-histaminergic itch by TRPA1 antagonist A-967079. Methods: Twenty-two healthy subjects were randomized, using a single-blinded protocol. Four areas on the forearms were selected and treated as follows: vehicle+BAM8-22, A-967079+BAM8-22, A-967079+BAM8-22 (applied after 5 minutes), and A-967079+inactivated cowhage spicules. A-967079 (0.5 mg/ml) and vehicle were intradermally injected (0.1 ml), while BAM8-22 was applied through inactivated cowhage spicules coated with while BAM8-22 (2 mg/ml). After spicules application, itch intensity was scored with a visual analog scale for 9 minutes followed by the assessment of the mechanically evoked itch. Results: Itch evoked by ‘A-967079+BAM8-22 (after 5 min)’ resulted in a lower intensity than ‘vehicle+BAM8-22’ (p<0.05). Moreover, the mechanically evoked itch was lower in ‘A-967079+BAM8-22 (after 5 min)’ and ‘A-967079+inativated spicules’ areas compared to ‘vehicle+BAM8-22’ (p<0.05). Conclusions: A-967079 reduced the itch intensity and the mechanically evoked itch in BAM8-22-induced non-histaminergic itch. This study confirmed the involvement of TRPA1 receptors in the signal pathway of non-histaminergic itch generation and hence the block of TRPA1 receptors can be a promising option for treating chronic itch.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aliotta, Giulia Erica","Elberling, Jesper","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Lo Vecchio, Silvia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692985"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-22","place":"Budapest, hu","start":"2023-09-20","title":"13th Congress of the European Pain Federation EFIC","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Aliotta, Giulia Erica"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antagonizing trpa000000000001 receptors counteracts non histaminergic itch in humans","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-692985","ids":["aau-c1c2c8e9-a699-4a53-9f83-fb0de2f1b266"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E24CD5BB9D85435F26D9D7C72C885E0C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giulia Erica","key":"aliottapau","last":"Aliotta","locid":"efb82db6-80bc-4a13-8fda-f95c91b88a94","name":"Aliotta, Giulia Erica","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c1c2c8e9-a699-4a53-9f83-fb0de2f1b266"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Antagonizing trpa1 receptors counteracts non-histaminergic itch in humans","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-692985","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Spontaneous pregnancy loss occurs in approximately 1 in 4 pregnancies; however, diagnostic workup is mostly restricted to women with recurrent pregnancy loss. The lack of workup on first pregnancy loss is likely a result of the high de novo fetal aneuploidy rate; however, this ignores the association of euploid pregnancy loss with an increased risk of future losses. Diagnosis of ploidy is advantageous but requires collection of pregnancy tissue. Cell-free fetal DNA (cffDNA) has revolutionized prenatal screening and has shown evidence in 2 small studies of diagnostic utility in pregnancy loss. The prospective Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss (COPL) study is a large initiative with the overall aim to explore the causes of pregnancy loss. This prospective cohort study of women from the COPL aimed to investigate the clinical utility of cffDNA-based testing in women with pregnancy loss. Adult women with a pregnancy loss before gestational age 22 weeks seen between November 2020 and May 2022 at 1 of the 3 participating COPL sites were invited to participate. Blood samples for cffDNA analysis were obtained before treatment to remove pregnancy tissue or within 24 hours of passage of pregnancy tissue. Pregnancy tissue was collected for direct sequencing and comparison to cffDNA results. Aneuploidy was assessed for all chromosomes, and discordant results were considered false-positive if the cffDNA result was aneuploid and false-negative if the cffDNA result was euploid. A total of 1000 women were recruited and underwent cffDNA blood draws, and 32% of women either did not manage to collect pregnancy tissue or collected a sample classified as unknown tissue. The cffDNA result was inconclusive in 112 (11%) of initial cases due to a low fetal fraction or low sequencing quality and were excluded from sensitivity and specificity analysis. The association between inconclusive results and gestational age was approximately 10% from gestational age 7 weeks on, whereas results were inconclusive approximately 50% of the time at earlier gestational ages. The final cohort for analysis thus included 888 cases, 446 (50%) of which were euploid, 405 (46%) aneuploid, and 37 (4%) contained multiple aneuploidies. The sensitivity of cffDNA testing compared with direct sequencing of pregnancy tissue was 85% (95% confidence interval [CI], 79–90), specificity was 93% (CI, 88–96), and accuracy was 89% (95% CI, 85–92). The results of this study demonstrate that cffDNA-based testing has a high sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy for the diagnosis of ploidy when compared with direct sequencing of pregnancy tissue. In addition, approximately a third of women were not able to collect true pregnancy tissue, illustrating the importance of introducing a pregnancy tissue-independent alternative for diagnostics in pregnancy loss.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","Ambye, Louise","Gruhn, Jennifer R.","Petersen, Jesper Friis","Wrønding, Tine","Amato, Letizia","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Ji, Boyang","Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","Werge, Lene","Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","Brinkmann, Clara","Petersen, Julie Birch","Dunø, Morten","Bache, Iben","Herrgård, Markus J.","Jørgensen, Finn Stener","Hoffmann, Eva R.","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695912"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["BioInnovation Institute"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell free fetal dna for genetic evaluation in copenhagen pregnancy loss study copl a prospective cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695912","identifier":[{"id":"85163829377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6d784b63-fedb-4c4a-bda3-748b17b691d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C42CB7D39CA0DAFB4598A6F5400CD037"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["BioInnovation Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja Schlaikjær","key":"hartwigtanjaschlaikjærpau","last":"Hartwig","name":"Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"ambyelouisepau","last":"Ambye","name":"Ambye, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jennifer R.","key":"gruhnjenniferrpau","last":"Gruhn","locid":"d1b8c69f-7bff-4210-b193-5391514106df","name":"Gruhn, Jennifer R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jesper Friis","key":"petersenjesperfriispau","last":"Petersen","locid":"41d7917c-a9f8-4765-9057-1fed4304173d","name":"Petersen, Jesper Friis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine","key":"wrøndingtinepau","last":"Wrønding","name":"Wrønding, Tine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Letizia","key":"amatoletiziapau","last":"Amato","name":"Amato, Letizia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andrew Chi-Ho","key":"chanandrewchihopau","last":"Chan","locid":"3f0f0aa0-3dfa-4793-a731-62781e5135c6","name":"Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","name_org":"Chan, Andrew Chi-Ho","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Boyang","key":"jiboyangpau","last":"Ji","name":"Ji, Boyang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maiken Hemme","key":"brojørgensenmaikenhemmepau","last":"Bro-Jørgensen","name":"Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"wergelenepau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Lene","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","key":"petersenmettemariebabielschmidtpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Clara","key":"brinkmannclarapau","last":"Brinkmann","name":"Brinkmann, Clara","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie Birch","key":"petersenjuliebirchpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Julie Birch","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"dunømortenpau","last":"Dunø","name":"Dunø, Morten","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Iben","key":"bacheibenpau","last":"Bache","name":"Bache, Iben","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Markus J.","key":"herrgårdmarkusjpau","last":"Herrgård","name":"Herrgård, Markus J.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Finn Stener","key":"jørgensenfinnstenerpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"af103a51-0399-4d0c-8377-db0260a8c6c8","name":"Jørgensen, Finn Stener","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva R.","key":"hoffmannevarpau","last":"Hoffmann","locid":"463cbfab-40b4-48fc-afd5-d95c1506f24f","name":"Hoffmann, Eva R.","orcid":"0000-0002-2588-0652","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henriette Svarre","key":"nielsenhenriettesvarrepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0dbb49-ded3-4607-aca2-08fd68b6a558","name":"Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ogx.0000000000001163","issn":["00297828","15339866"],"issn_org":["00297828"],"issue":"6","journal":"Obstetrical and Gynecological Survey","pages":"345-346","status":"p","title":"Obstetrical and Gynecological Survey","volume":"78"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163829377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6d784b63-fedb-4c4a-bda3-748b17b691d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cell-Free Fetal DNA for Genetic Evaluation in Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss Study (COPL) : A Prospective Cohort Study","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695912","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To evaluate two user-operated audiometry methods, the AMTASTM PC-based audiometry and a low-cost smartphone audiometry research application (R-App). DESIGN: A repeated-measures within-subject study design was used to compare both user-operated methods to traditional manual audiometry and to evaluate test-retest reliability of each method. STUDY SAMPLE: 58 subjects were recruited in the study of which 83 ears had normal hearing thresholds and 33 ears had hearing loss (pure-tone average > 25 dB HL). Average age of participants was 44.8 years, with an age range of 11-85. RESULTS: Standard deviation of absolute differences ranged between 3.9-6.9 dB on AMTASTM and 4.5-6.8 dB on the R-App. The highest variability was found at the 8000 Hz frequency (R-App and AMTASTM test) and 3000 Hz frequency (AMTASTM retest). Evaluation of test-retest reliability of AMTASTM and R-App showed SD of absolute differences ranging between 3.5-5.8 dB and 3.1-5.0 dB, respectively. The mean threshold difference between test and retest was within ±1.5 dB on AMTASTM and ±1 dB on the R-App. CONCLUSION: Accuracy of AMTASTM and the R-App was within acceptable limits for audiometry and comparable to traditional manual audiometry on all tested frequencies (250-8000 Hz). Evaluation of test-retest reliability showed acceptable variation on both AMTASTM and R-App. Both user-operated methods could be reliably performed in a quiet non-soundproofed environment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Chris Bang","Adams, Thomas Bording","Pedersen, Ellen Raben","Nielsen, Jacob","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697369"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Chris Bang"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"amtastm and user operated smartphone research application audiometry an evaluation study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0291412","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697369","identifier":[{"id":"85171341444","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10501612","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37708125","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-d5daf94c-472f-4d6c-9261-e9e514f8f14e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B345E2F5C866EC82944EFDBDB6B033CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/240953565/journal.pone.0291412.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0291412","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Metaverse Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chris Bang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"d99e9d61-082b-402c-9764-1deb459c7110","name":"Sørensen, Chr