{"abstract":"Background It is not clearly known how well Danes estimate their chances of reaching the average life expectancy and whether identifiable population subgroups misestimate their life expectancy, and potentially also investments and savings in health and pensions. Therefore, in this study, we examined on the individual level whether subjective life expectancy is in line with the statistically calculated chance of reaching age 85, and further explored the psychological and behavioral factors associated with under or overestimation. Methods We opted for a cross-sectional survey design based on a sample of 5,379 Danish citizens aged 50–70 years, returning a web-based questionnaire with socio-demographic data supplemented from a national registry. Average participant estimates of their chance of reaching age 85 for each age range and sex group were compared with actuarial data. We then performed multiple linear regression analyses to examine factors associated with the subjective expectancy of reaching age 85 years. Results We found that 32% of females and 23% of males reported 100% certainty of reaching age 85, and average expected survival chance exceeded the statistically predicted survival chance for 23% of males and 16% for females in age-ranges 50–60 and 61–70. Our multivariable analysis found that health literacy, internal health locus of control, willingness to take health risks, self-rated health, and health and life satisfaction all showed a significant positive association with expectation of reaching age 85. Moreover, those on daily medications, ex- or current smokers, and heavy drinkers were significantly less optimistic about reaching age 85. Conclusions Particularly for the population groups with inaccurate life expectancies, the significant associations with psychological and behavioral factors open a way for initiatives based on behavior change theories to reach a better agreement between subjective and statistical life expectancy.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thapa, Subash","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713764"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thapa, Subash"],"keyword":["Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Health literacy","Healthy aging","Humans","Life Expectancy","Male","Motivation","Optimism","Pensions","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subjective expectation of reaching age 000000000085 agreement with population statistics and association with behavioral and psychological factors","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-03951-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713764","identifier":[{"id":"85153448269","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10120199","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37081423","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2d787e70-da9d-47cf-b2ed-044f51830c13"],"keyword":["Biopsychosocial framework","Cross-Sectional Studies","Decade of healthy aging","Decade of healthy aging; healthy aging;","Female","Health literacy","Healthy aging","Humans","Internal locus of control","Life expectancy","Male","Motivation","Optimism","Pensions","Pensions and saving","Subjective life expectation","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E9D09446DAD1461B76939E42B0A76C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-03951-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252865908/s12877-023-03951-w.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Subash","key":"thapapau","last":"Thapa","locid":"a271bef3-0a7e-4c8d-b6b7-28a6a21e9480","name":"Thapa, Subash","orcid":"0000-0002-1182-8511","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37081423"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12877-023-03951-w","issn":["14712318"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Geriatrics","paperid":"240","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Geriatrics","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153448269"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2d787e70-da9d-47cf-b2ed-044f51830c13"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Subjective expectation of reaching age 85 : agreement with population statistics and association with behavioral and psychological factors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713764","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
