{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Helmke, Christophe","Nielsen, Jesper","Rivera Guzmán, Angel Iván"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778940"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making the transient eternal on the stone effigies of i xiuhmolpilli i among central mexican cultures","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mesoweb.com/pari/publications/journal/2304/Xiuhmolpilli.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778940","ids":["ku-c04b9a19-45e7-417b-a9b3-d43e017e05f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-06CD7340CF67EFCB017E78D8841F6769"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mesoweb.com/pari/publications/journal/2304/Xiuhmolpilli.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Angel Iván","key":"riveraguzmánpau","last":"Rivera Guzmán","name":"Rivera Guzmán, Angel Iván","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15315398"],"issue":"4","journal":"The PARI Journal","pages":"1-19","status":"p","title":"The PARI Journal","title_org":"The P A R I Journal","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c04b9a19-45e7-417b-a9b3-d43e017e05f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Making the Transient Eternal : On the Stone Effigies of <i>xiuhmolpilli </i>among Central Mexican Cultures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-778940","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this study, we investigated the effects of motor practice with an emphasis on either position or force control on motor performance, motor accuracy and variability in preadolescent children. Furthermore, we investigated corticomuscular coherence and potential changes following motor practice.  We designed a setup allowing discrete wrist flexions of the non-dominant hand and tested motor accuracy and variability when the task was to generate specific movement endpoints (15-75 deg) or force levels (5-25% MVC). All participants were tested in both tasks at baseline and post motor practice without augmented feedback on performance. Following baseline assessment, participants (44 children aged 9-11 years) were randomly assigned to either position (PC) or force control (FC) motor practice or a resting control group (CON). The PC and FC groups performed four blocks of 40 trials motor practice with augmented feedback on performance.  Following practice, improvements in movement accuracy were significantly greater in the PC group compared to the FC and CON groups (p < 0.001). None of the groups displayed changes in force task performance indicating no benefits of force control motor practice and low transfer between tasks (p-values:0.08-0.45). Corticomuscular coherence (C4-FCR) was demonstrated during the hold phase in both tasks with no difference between tasks. Corticomuscular coherence did not change from baseline to post practice in any group. Our findings demonstrate that preadolescent children improve position control following dynamic accuracy motor practice. Contrary to previous findings in adults, preadolescent children displayed smaller or no improvements in force control following isometric motor practice, low transfer between tasks and no changes in corticomuscular coherence.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Stolpe, Malene Norup","Nielsen, August Lomholt","Bjørndal, Jonas Rud","Wiegel, Patrick","Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-081.27-704542"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London"],"keyword":["Coherence","Faculty of Science","Force control","Motor control","Motor learning","Position control","Sensory motor training","Visual feedback"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of dynamic and isometric motor practice on position control force control and corticomuscular coherence in preadolescent children","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.humov.2023.103114","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.27-704542","identifier":[{"id":"37354890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85163158644","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-cd77d1bd-40b0-4985-b9b4-9306f9071ef8","ku-bf6862a7-4530-4a51-9de9-005c9eed3377"],"keyword":["Coherence","Faculty of Science","Force control","Motor control","Motor learning","Position control","Sensory-motor training","Visual feedback"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B9FFA48F14F306BC4889DECB92F69A40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.humov.2023.103114","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/358726151/Norup_et_al_Human_Movement_Science_2023_Vol_90_e103114.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["University College Copenhagen (KP)"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Malene","key":"noruppau","last":"Norup","locid":"62c7e795-b6ae-4246-96ba-48c2e3fdfd80","name":"Stolpe, Malene Norup","name_org":"Norup, Malene","orcid":"0000-0002-5150-9048","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Norup","key":"stolpepau","last":"Stolpe","locid":"0da93143-5e45-49b4-9b1f-86163381d0e9","name":"Stolpe, Malene Norup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"August Lomholt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"babf098d-97c8-434c-9345-40a30817d332","name":"Nielsen, August Lomholt","orcid":"0009-0008-0543-2220","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Rud","key":"bjørndalpau","last":"Bjørndal","locid":"a08cffa6-ec3c-4626-bea4-09e99fa2cbc6","name":"Bjørndal, Jonas Rud","orcid":"0000-0003-0710-7129","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"wiegelpau","last":"Wiegel","locid":"b9f5e627-b733-4139-960d-6736db58523d","name":"Wiegel, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0001-5034-7174","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Meaghan Elizabeth","key":"speddenpau","last":"Spedden","locid":"e96259a8-d793-4586-903e-cbf824fa8021","name":"Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6854-2226","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37354890"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.humov.2023.103114","issn":["01679457","18727646"],"issn_org":["01679457"],"journal":"Human Movement Science","paperid":"103114","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Human Movement Science","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163158644"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-cd77d1bd-40b0-4985-b9b4-9306f9071ef8","ku-bf6862a7-4530-4a51-9de9-005c9eed3377"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of dynamic and isometric motor practice on position control, force control and corticomuscular coherence in preadolescent children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.27-704542","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Recently, time-based primitives such as time-lock puzzles (TLPs) and verifiable delay functions (VDFs) have received a lot of attention due to their power as building blocks for cryptographic protocols. However, even though exciting improvements on their efficiency and security (e.g. achieving non-malleability) have been made, most of the existing constructions do not offer general composability guarantees and thus have limited applicability. Baum et al. (EUROCRYPT 2021) presented in TARDIS the first (im)possibility results on constructing TLPs with Universally Composable (UC) security and an application to secure two-party computation with output-independent abort (OIA-2PC), where an adversary has to decide to abort before learning the output. While these results establish the feasibility of UC-secure TLPs and applications, they are limited to the two-party scenario and suffer from complexity overheads. In this paper, we introduce the first UC constructions of VDFs and of the related notion of publicly verifiable TLPs (PV-TLPs). We use our new UC VDF to prove a folklore result on VDF-based randomness beacons used in industry and build an improved randomness beacon from our new UC PV-TLPs. We moreover construct the first multiparty computation protocol with punishable output-independent aborts (POIA-MPC), i.e. MPC with OIA and financial punishment for cheating. Our novel POIA-MPC both establishes the feasibility of (non-punishable) OIA-MPC and significantly improves on the efficiency of state-of-the-art OIA-2PC and (non-OIA) MPC with punishable aborts.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Baum, Carsten","David, Bernardo","Dowsley, Rafael","Kishore, Ravi","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Oechsner, Sabine"],"cuid":["S02-083.97-761792"],"event":{"end":"2023-05-10","place":"Atlanta, us","start":"2023-05-07","title":"26th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public-Key Cryptography, PKC 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["David, Bernardo"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Monash University","University of Edinburgh"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"craft composable randomness beacons and output independent abort mpc from time","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85161388341","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-083.97-761792","identifier":[{"id":"85161388341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8e68394a-bc06-4369-a030-6ad3d449f78f","dtu-bfefc779-f751-42b4-997b-9736c7550e79"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-7EB052631900461BFB41ECC6C0D473D6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cybersecurity Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"baumpau","last":"Baum","locid":"ac00f0e9-1985-4767-922a-d55e5df81c29","name":"Baum, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-7905-0198","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo","key":"davidpau","last":"David","name":"David, Bernardo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"dowsleypau","last":"Dowsley","name":"Dowsley, Rafael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ravi","key":"kishorepau","last":"Kishore","name":"Kishore, Ravi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabine","key":"oechsnerpau","last":"Oechsner","name":"Oechsner, Sabine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandra","key":"boldyrevapedh","last":"Boldyreva","name":"Boldyreva, Alexandra","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Vladimir","key":"kolesnikovpedh","last":"Kolesnikov","name":"Kolesnikov, Vladimir","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-31368-4_16","eisbn":["9783031313684"],"isbn":["9783031313677"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"439-470","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"26th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public-Key Cryptography, Atlanta, GA, USA, May 7–10, 2023, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Public-Key Cryptography – PKC 2023","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161388341"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8e68394a-bc06-4369-a030-6ad3d449f78f","dtu-bfefc779-f751-42b4-997b-9736c7550e79"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"CRAFT: Composable Randomness Beacons and Output-Independent Abort MPC From Time","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.97-761792","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with stage II seminoma have traditionally been treated with photons to the retroperitoneal and iliac space, which leads to a substantial dose bath to abdominal and pelvic organs at risk (OAR). As these patients are young and with excellent prognosis, reducing dose to OAR and thereby the risk of secondary cancer is of utmost importance. We compared IMPT to opposing IMRT fields and VMAT, assessing dose to OAR and both overall and organ-specific secondary cancer risk. Material and methods: A comparative treatment planning study was conducted on planning CT-scans from ten patients with stage II seminoma, treated with photons to a ‘dog-leg’ field with doses ranging from 20 to 25 Gy and a 10 Gy sequential boost to the metastatic lymph node(s). Photon plans were either 3–4 field IMRT (Eclipse) or 1–2 arc VMAT (Pinnacle). Proton plans used robust (5 mm; 3.5%) IMPT (Eclipse), multi field optimization with 3 posterior fields supplemented by 2 anterior fields at the level of the iliac vessels. Thirty plans were generated. Mean doses to OARs were compared for IMRT vs IMPT and VMAT vs IMPT. The risk of secondary cancer was calculated according to the model described by Schneider, using excess absolute risk (EAR, per 10,000 persons per year) for body outline, stomach, duodenum, pancreas, bowel, bladder and spinal cord. Results: Mean doses to all OARs were significantly lower with IMPT except similar kidney (IMRT) and spinal cord (VMAT) doses. The relative EAR for body outline was 0.59 for IMPT/IMRT (p <.05) and 0.33 for IMPT/VMAT (p <.05). Organ specific secondary cancer risk was also lower for IMPT except for pancreas and duodenum. Conclusion: Proton therapy reduced radiation dose to OAR compared to both IMRT and VMAT plans, and potentially reduce the risk of secondary cancer both overall and for most OAR.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rønde, Heidi S.","Kronborg, Camilla","Høyer, Morten","Hansen, Jolanta","Bak, Malene Eppler","Agergaard, Søren Nielsen","Als, Anne Birgitte","Agerbæk, Mads","Lauritsen, Jakob","Meidahl Petersen, Peter","Dysager, Lars","Kallehauge, Jesper F."],"cuid":["S02-088.46-761834"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rønde, Heidi S."],"keyword":["Animals","Dogs","Humans","IMPT","Male","Organs at Risk","Proton Therapy adverse effects","Proton therapy","Radiotherapy Dosage","Radiotherapy Intensity Modulated adverse effects","Radiotherapy Planning Computer Assisted","Secondary cancer","Seminoma radiotherapy","Testicular Neoplasms radiotherapy","Testis cancer","testicular seminoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dose comparison of robustly optimized intensity modulated proton therapy impt vs imrt and vmat photon plans for testicular seminoma","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/0284186X.2023.2254925","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.46-761834","identifier":[{"id":"85170559125","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37683054","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c295a9d9-74b9-49d8-945c-7164acb5815c","sdu-e0d727ec-e9c2-4d25-b7ee-02b58c4c7832"],"keyword":["Animals","Dogs","Humans","IMPT","Male","Organs at Risk","Proton Therapy/adverse effects","Proton therapy","Radiotherapy Dosage","Radiotherapy Planning, Computer-Assisted","Radiotherapy, Intensity-Modulated/adverse effects","Seminoma/radiotherapy","Testicular Neoplasms/radiotherapy","secondary cancer","testicular seminoma","testis cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Tech