n global brain metabolism after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.00-686229","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We investigated the association between SARS-CoV-2 infection and new-onset type 1 diabetes (T1D) in children and adolescents in a nationwide, matched cohort study. The hazard ratio of new-onset T1D within 6 months after SARS-CoV-2 infection was 1.22 (0.58-2.58). The risk of new-onset T1D in children and adolescents was not significantly increased after SARS-CoV-2 infection.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bering, Louise","Christensen, Anne Vinggaard","Birk, Nina Marie","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Bundgaard, Henning","Benfield, Thomas","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Johannesen, Jesper","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Berg, Selina Kikkenborg"],"cuid":["S02-092.97-716465"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bering, Louise"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Freiburg"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Children","Covid 19","SARS CoV 2","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of new onset type 000000000001 diabetes in danish children and adolescents after sars cov 000000000002 infection a nationwide matched cohort study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85175194859","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the A.P. Møller and Chastine Mc-Kinney Møller Foundation [2021-00661]. The study funder was not involved in the study."],"id":"S02-092.97-716465","identifier":[