"All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-12b0f377-6066-4456-b4ef-d59af3697e28","sdu-9657a765-ad55-4f18-91a6-73fa2c37f09b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Physical activity impacts resting skeletal muscle myosin conformation and lowers its ATP consumption","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-673051","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Multi-component psychological interventions may mitigate overweight and obesity in children and adolescents. Evidence is, however, scattered on the effectiveness of such interventions. This study aims to review the available evidence on the effectiveness of multi-component psychological interventions on anthropometric measures of school-aged children with overweight or obesity. Methods: We systematically searched international databases/search engines including PubMed and NLM Gateway (for MEDLINE), Web of Science, SCOPUS, and Google Scholar up to November 2022 for relevant articles pertaining to psychological weight-loss interventions targeting school-aged children. Two reviewers screened and extracted pertinent data. The quality of included studies was assessed using the Cochrane Risk of Bias Tool for Randomized Trials. Random effect meta-analysis was used to calculate, and pool standardized mean differences (SMD). We distinguished between intervention and maintenance effects. Intervention effects were defined as the mean change in outcome measurement detected between baseline and post-treatment. Maintenance effects were defined as the mean change in outcome measurement between post-treatment and last follow-up. Results: Of 3,196 studies initially identified, 54 and 30 studies were included in the qualitative and quantitative syntheses, respectively. Most studies reported on group-based interventions. The significant effects of intervention on BMI z-score (SMD -0.66, 95% CI: -1.15, -0.17) and WC (SMD -0.53, 95% CI: -1.03, -0.04) were observed for interventions that centered on motivational interviewing and cognitive behavioral therapy, respectively. Mean BMI and WC did not differ significantly between post-treatment and last follow-up measurement (maintenance effect), indicating that an initial weight loss obtained through the intervention period could be maintained over time. Conclusions: Findings indicate that motivational interviewing and cognitive behavioral therapy as interventions to reduce BMI z-score (generalized obesity) and waist circumference (abdominal obesity) are effective and durable. However, detailed analyses on individual components of the interventions are recommended in future effectiveness studies.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Baygi, Fereshteh","Djalalinia, Shirin","Qorbani, Mostafa","Larrabee Sonderlund, Anders","Kousgaard Andersen, Merethe Kirstine","Thilsing, Trine","Heitmann, Berit Lilienthal","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-704574"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Baygi, Fereshteh"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["Alborz University of Medical Sciences","All Global Affiliations","Iranian Ministry of Health and Medical Education","Ministry of Health and Medical Education"],"keyword":["Meta analysis","Obesity","Overweight","Psychological interventions","School aged children"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of psychological interventions targeting overweight and obesity in school aged children a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-023-16339-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This article is dedicated to “Professor Carsten Lyng Obel”- who passed away in February 2022- in memory of his contribution to the conception of this study."],"id":"S02-100.00-704574","identifier":[{"id":"37537523","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10398924","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85166539276","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-794cc22d-ce30-4727-8258-fdedc194253d","sdu-04adf715-d675-41a4-b6ff-575450a9ba2c"],"keyword":["Meta-analysis","Obesity","Overweight","Psychological Interventions","School-aged Children"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-72FF54D1C1DA1780ECD4D30E2E13E489"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-023-16339-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/362680486/s12889_023_16339_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252096831/s12889-023-16339-7_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"iranian ministry of health and medical education","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Iranian Ministry of Health and Medical Education","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ir","key":"ministry of health and medical education","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Ministry of Health and Medical Education","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ir","key":"alborz university of medical sciences","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Alborz University of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fereshteh","key":"baygipau","last":"Baygi","locid":"82ac54a3-f35a-4ee6-85dc-362c9e160ee9","name":"Baygi, Fereshteh","orcid":"0000-0002-9260-2281","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Shirin","key":"djalaliniapau","last":"Djalalinia","name":"Djalalinia, Shirin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mostafa","key":"qorbanipau","last":"Qorbani","name":"Qorbani, Mostafa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"larrabeesonderlundpau","last":"Larrabee Sonderlund","locid":"052e950e-ab44-4d41-869d-4a3d4a37c62e","name":"Larrabee Sonderlund, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6627-3322","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merethe Kirstine","key":"kousgaardandersenpau","last":"Kousgaard Andersen","locid":"c6a8bf7f-78bf-4e29-a55d-5c1771a197f9","name":"Andersen, Merethe Kirstine Kousgaard","name_org":"Kousgaard Andersen, Merethe Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-4833-1867","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","locid":"6ae25242-1e96-48cf-ab01-cbac26690f6b","name":"Thilsing, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-2041-2219","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6 1","first":"Berit Lilienthal","key":"heitmannpau","last":"Heitmann","locid":"b644e477-0a57-40f2-b0a7-71e52f624356","name":"Heitmann, Berit Lilienthal","orcid":"0000-0002-6809-4504","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37537523"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12889-023-16339-7","issn":["14712458"],"journal":"BMC Public Health","paperid":"1478","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166539276"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-794cc22d-ce30-4727-8258-fdedc194253d","sdu-04adf715-d675-41a4-b6ff-575450a9ba2c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The effect of psychological interventions targeting overweight and obesity in school-aged children : a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-704574","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Long-Term air pollution is a risk factor for stroke. Which types and sources of air pollution contribute most to stroke in populations is unknown. We investigated whether risk of stroke differed by type and source of air pollution. Methods: We selected all persons aged >50 years and living in Denmark in the period 2005-17. We estimated running 5-year mean residential air-pollution concentrations of particulate matter <2.5 μm (PM2.5), ultrafine particles (UFP), elemental carbon (EC) and nitrogen dioxide (NO2). Pollutants were modelled as total air pollution from all emission sources, as well as apportioned into contributions from non-Traffic and traffic sources. Hazard ratios (HRs) and CIs were estimated by using Cox proportional hazards models, adjusting for area-level and personal demographic and socio-economic covariates. We identified all primary strokes from hospital and mortality registers. Results: The cohort numbered 2 million people and 94-256 cases of stroke. Interquartile ranges (IQR) of air pollution were associated with risk of stroke with HRs of 1.077 (95% CI: 1.061-1.094, IQR: 1.85 μg/m3) for PM2.5, 1.039 (1.026-1.052, IQR: 4248 particles/cm3) for UFP, 1.009 (1.001-1.018, IQR: 0.28 μg/m3) for EC and 1.028 (1.017-1.040, IQR: 7.15 μg/m3) for NO2. Traffic sources contributed little to the total exposure. HRs associated with air pollution from traffic were close to the null, whereas non-Traffic sources tended to be associated with HRs higher than those for total air pollution, e.g. for non-Traffic PM2.5, the HR was 1.091 (1.074-1.108). Conclusions: Air pollution, including UFP, was associated with risk of stroke. The risk appeared attributable mainly to air pollution from non-Traffic sources.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Im, Ulas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716029"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cohort study","Epidemiology","Stroke","Ultrafine particles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"source specific air pollution and risk of stroke in denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85154618667","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716029","identifier":[{"id":"36921285","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85154618667","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-87ed83bd-4c9b-48cd-a4fb-76b2a9be1e9e","ruc-dc335edf-4894-4f99-848f-60dd3420c03d"],"keyword":["Air pollution","cohort study","epidemiology","stroke","ultrafine particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB10ECDACBE01D4CEAC9B201D7531E7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank"