Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2f7c851a-459a-4345-87ec-17127b5232ac"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"La pirámide de las serpientes emplumadas. : Nuevas acercamientos","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421743","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background/Aim: Signs of hypoxic ischaemic encephalopathy (HIE) on head computed tomography (CT) predicts poor neurological outcome after cardiac arrest. We explore whether levels of brain injury markers in blood could predict the likelihood of HIE on CT. Methods: Retrospective analysis of CT performed at 24–168 h post cardiac arrest on clinical indication within the Target Temperature Management after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest-trial. Biomarkers prospectively collected at 24- and 48 h post-arrest were analysed for neuron specific enolase (NSE), neurofilament light (NFL), total-tau and glial fibrillary acidic protein (GFAP). HIE was assessed through visual evaluation and quantitative grey-white-matter ratio (GWR) was retrospectively calculated on Swedish subjects with original images available. Results: In total, 95 patients were included. The performance to predict HIE on CT (performed at IQR 73–116 h) at 48 h was similar for all biomarkers, assessed as area under the receiving operating characteristic curve (AUC) NSE 0.82 (0.71–0.94), NFL 0.79 (0.67–0.91), total-tau 0.84 (0.74–0.95), GFAP 0.79 (0.67–0.90). The predictive performance of biomarker levels at 24 h was AUC 0.72–0.81. At 48 h biomarker levels below Youden Index accurately excluded HIE in 77.3–91.7% (negative predictive value) and levels above Youden Index correctly predicted HIE in 73.3–83.7% (positive predictive value). NSE cut-off at 48 h was 48 ng/ml. Elevated biomarker levels irrespective of timepoint significantly correlated with lower GWR. Conclusion: Biomarker levels can assess the likelihood of a patient presenting with HIE on CT and could be used to select suitable patients for CT-examination during neurological prognostication in unconscious cardiac arrest patients.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Lagebrant, Alice","Lang, Margareta","Nielsen, Niklas","Blennow, Kaj","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Mikael A.","Mattsson-Carlgren, Niklas","Pellis, Tommaso","Rylander, Christian","Sigmund, Roger","Stammet, Pascal","Undén, Johan","Zetterberg, Henrik","Wise, Matt P.","Cronberg, Tobias","Moseby-Knappe, Marion"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-424812"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Luxembourg","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Academic Medical Centre","All Global Affiliations","Azienda Sanitaria Friuli Occidentale","Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Lund University","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","University College London","University Hospital of Wales","University of Gothenburg","University of Luxembourg","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brain injury markers in blood predict signs of hypoxic ischaemic encephalopathy on head computed tomography after cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2022.12.006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-424812","identifier":[{"id":"36563954","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146604323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-34d2a5c4-095a-4bdf-a93a-43918d63acc3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-34F22DF19FDDC626877B62D7CE8216CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2022.12.006","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341279937/1_s2.0_S0300957222007407_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"sahlgrenska university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Sahlgrenska University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"academic medical centre","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Academic Medical Centre","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nl","key":"medical centre leeuwarden","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical Centre Leeuwarden","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"it","key":"azienda sanitaria friuli occidentale","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Azienda Sanitaria Friuli Occidentale","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"lu","key":"center hospitalier de luxembourg","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"lu","key":"university of luxembourg","loc":["