2","first":"Christoffer Tandrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"90277fe6-5d9e-4795-9b75-352465ebeea1","name":"Nielsen, Christoffer Tandrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jesper","key":"lindhardsenpau","last":"Lindhardsen","locid":"a8dcf7b1-332a-456e-b0b8-72a67eaf4ce6","name":"Lindhardsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37003283"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2213-2600(23)00130-3","issn":["22132600","22132619"],"issn_org":["22132600"],"issue":"6","journal":"The Lancet Respiratory Medicine","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Respiratory Medicine","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85156235992"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-50db9d70-70e2-4c72-8b15-b9e9e5ab1cfc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pirfenidone in rheumatoid arthritis-associated interstitial lung disease","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701670","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: On average, older patients use five or more medications daily. A consequence is an increased risk of adverse drug reactions, interactions, or medication errors. Therefore, it is important to understand the challenges experienced by the patients, relatives, and healthcare professionals pertinent to the concomitant use of many drugs. Methods: We conducted a qualitative study using focus group interviews to collect information from patients, relatives, and healthcare professionals regarding older patients' management of prescribed medicine. We interviewed seven patients using five or more medications daily, three relatives, three general practitioners, nine nurses from different healthcare sectors, one home care assistant, two hospital physicians, and four pharmacists. Results: The following themes were identified: (1) Unintentional non-adherence, (2) Intentional non-adherence, (3) Generic substitution, (4) Medication lists, (5) Timing and medication schedule, (6) Medication reviews and (7) Dose dispensing/pill organizers. Conclusion: Medication is the subject of concern among patients and relatives. They become confused and insecure about information from different actors and the package leaflets. Therefore, patients often request a thorough medication review to provide an overview, knowledge of possible side effects and interactions, and a clarification of the medication's timing. In addition, patients, relatives and nurses all request an indication of when medicine should be taken, including allowable deviations from this timing. Therefore, prescribing physicians should prioritize communicating information regarding these matters when prescribing.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Thorbjørn Hougaard","Søndergaard, Jens","Kjær, Niels Kristian","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Ryg, Jesper","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Mogensen, Christian Backer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713873"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Thorbjørn Hougaard"],"keyword":["Continuity of care","Experiences","Focus group interviews","Medication Errors","Non adherence","Older people","Polypharmacy","Qualitative Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling polypharmacy a qualitative study using focus group interviews with older patients their relatives and healthcare professionals","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-04131-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by a grant from VELUX FONDEN grant no. 34175. VELUX FONDEN did not participate in or influence the design of the study as well as the collection, analysis, and interpretation of data nor in writing the manuscript."],"id":"S01-000.00-713873","identifier":[{"id":"85167371702","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10410867","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37553585","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-3e6d2251-4191-4e6e-b226-b096b46b8f02"],"keyword":["Adverse drug interactions","Continuity of care","Experiences","Focus group interviews","Medication errors","Non-adherence","Older people","Polypharmacy","Qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-70413FBBAC1427146547DA023FAC187F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-04131-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/253008747/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU