{"abstract":"NSD2 is a histone methyltransferase predominantly catalyzing di-methylation of histone H3 on lysine K36. Increased NSD2 activity due to mutations or fusion-events affecting the gene encoding NSD2 is considered an oncogenic event and a driver in various cancers, including multiple myelomas carrying t(4;14) chromosomal translocations and acute lymphoblastic leukemia‘s expressing the hyperactive NSD2 mutant E1099 K. Using DNA-encoded libraries, we have identified small molecule ligands that selectively and potently bind to the PWWP1 domain of NSD2, inhibit NSD2 binding to H3K36me2-bearing nucleosomes, but do not inhibit the methyltransferase activity. The ligands were subsequently converted to selective VHL1-recruiting NSD2 degraders and by using one of the most efficacious degraders in cell lines, we show that it leads to NSD2 degradation, decrease in K3 K36me2 levels and inhibition of cell proliferation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["LegaardAndersson, Jan","Christensen, Jesper","Kleine-Kohlbrecher, Daniela","Comet, Itys","Støier, Jonatan Fullerton","Antoku, Yasuko","Poljak, Visnja","Moretti, Loris","Dolberg, Johannes","Jacso, Tomas","Jensby Nielsen, Søren","Nørregaard-Madsen, Mads","Franch, Thomas","Helin, Kristian","Cloos, Paul Andreas Compare"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720681"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Cancer Research"],"keyword":["PROTACs","Selectivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovery of nsd000000000002 degraders from novel and selective del hits","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373619717/MJAC_ChemBioChem_2023_Andersson_Discovery_of_NSD2_degraders_from_Novel_and_Selective_DEL_hits.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720681","identifier":[{"id":"85174632148","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37807669","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-726f404c-b29c-4b9d-9681-309cb86824e1"],"keyword":["DEL","NSD2","PROTACS","VHL1","selectivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09570999DB9E999EB5D05F81066C6A9F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373619717/MJAC_ChemBioChem_2023_Andersson_Discovery_of_NSD2_degraders_from_Novel_and_Selective_DEL_hits.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Nuevolution A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Helin Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"institute of cancer research","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Cancer Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"legaardanderssonpau","last":"LegaardAndersson","name":"LegaardAndersson, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"d1168701-7281-4e81-96fc-0758e89c075e","name":"Christensen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniela","key":"kleinekohlbrecherpau","last":"Kleine-Kohlbrecher","locid":"ce9f1e81-b07c-4d9c-81ef-8ce760bfbbb1","name":"Kleine-Kohlbrecher, Daniela","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Itys","key":"vachercometpau","last":"Vacher Comet","locid":"f7b26174-625b-4ad3-af1e-3b6433f86c23","name":"Comet, Itys","name_org":"Vacher Comet, Itys","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jonatan","key":"fullertonstøierpau","last":"Fullerton Støier","locid":"8d6dc76f-03c9-46d0-b5b1-4639067d06e9","name":"Støier, Jonatan Fullerton","name_org":"Fullerton Støier, Jonatan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yasuko","key":"antokupau","last":"Antoku","locid":"11d34f12-8c17-44fe-b734-4eeef023e0b5","name":"Antoku, Yasuko","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Visnja","key":"poljakpau","last":"Poljak","name":"Poljak, Visnja","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Loris","key":"morettipau","last":"Moretti","name":"Moretti, Loris","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johannes","key":"dolbergpau","last":"Dolberg","name":"Dolberg, Johannes","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tomas","key":"jacsopau","last":"Jacso","name":"Jacso, Tomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"jensbynielsenpau","last":"Jensby Nielsen","name":"Jensby Nielsen, Søren","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"nørregaardmadsenpau","last":"Nørregaard-Madsen","name":"Nørregaard-Madsen, Mads","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"franchpau","last":"Franch","name":"Franch, Thomas","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Kristian","key":"helinpau","last":"Helin","locid":"b95e097b-b1b4-44db-b097-0c3990dadf63","name":"Helin, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-1975-6097","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul A.C.","key":"cloospau","last":"Cloos","locid":"b5ab484f-a101-4534-97fd-b9a4846928a6","name":"Cloos, Paul Andreas Compare","name_org":"Cloos, Paul A.C.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37807669"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cbic.202300515","issn":["14394227","14397633"],"issn_org":["14394227"],"issue":"24","journal":"ChemBioChem","paperid":"e202300515","status":"p","title":"ChemBioChem","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174632148"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","bioorigin aps","nuevolution a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-726f404c-b29c-4b9d-9681-309cb86824e1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovery of NSD2-Degraders from Novel and Selective DEL Hits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720681","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Sub-classification of hidradenitis suppurativa (HS) may allow for a better understanding of disease aetiology and disease burden, and eventually permit a more personalised treatment for patients. Objective: To identify patient subtypes of HS based on comorbidity patterns and clinical characteristics, and to examine their inflammatory and metabolic blood profiles and associated levels of experienced distress, pain, quality of life, employment status and prescribed treatments. Methods: Cluster analysis of clinical data from consecutive, newly referred adult HS patients attending a dermatological hospital department. Results: A total of 534 patients (338 women and 196 men) with a mean age of 40.5 years (SD = 13.7) were included; 35.4% had Hurley stage I, 50.4% had Hurley stage II, and 14.8% had Hurley stage III. In total, six disease subtypes were identified: ‘female subtype’ (n = 182, 34.1%), ‘familial subtype’ (n = 144, 27.0%), ‘diabetes subtype’ (n = 107, 20.0%), ‘psychiatric disease subtype’ (n = 49, 9.2%), ‘Crohn's disease subtype’ (n = 29, 5.4%) and ‘asthma subtype’ (n = 23, 4.3%). Patients with ‘Crohn's disease subtype’ and ‘diabetes subtype’ had highest levels of systemic inflammation (C-reactive protein, erythrocyte sedimentation rate, leucocytes and neutrophils), blood glucose and lipids (triglycerides), p < 0.001. The highest boil-associated pain score, p < 0.001, overall disease-related distress, p = 0.008 and lowest quality of life, p = 0.015, was reported by patients with ‘familial subtype’, whereas highest rates of unemployment were observed among patients with ‘diabetes subtype’ and ‘psychiatric disease subtype’, p < 0.001. Treatment patterns differed significantly between the subtypes, with biologics being most often prescribed to patients with ‘Crohn's disease subtype’ (21.1%), p < 0.001. Conclusion: This study identified six subtypes of HS based on comorbidity patterns, clinical characteristics, blood profiles, patient-reported outcomes and treatment patters, supporting the concept of heterogeneity within HS.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Astrid Helene R.","Arildsen, Nicolai Skovbjerg","Yao, Yiqiu","Holm, Jesper G.","Nielsen, Valdemar W.","Ring, Hans C.","Woetmann, Anders","Thomsen, Simon Francis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-722572"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cluster Analysis","Comorbidities","Hidradenitis suppurativa","Subtypes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cluster analysis identifies six clinical subtypes of hidradenitis suppurativa characterised by distinct comorbidities inflammatory and metabolic profiles patient reported outcomes and treatment patterns","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jvc2.89","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-722572","identifier":[{"id":"85170664818","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ffcdfa36-3c1a-4adf-a037-9829d90af65c"],"keyword":["cluster analysis","comorbidities","hidradenitis suppurativa","subtypes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-248965CF9E14842D8D7E54ED5BF54A08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379716018/Cluster_analysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jvc2.89","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Skin Immunology Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Astrid Helene R.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Astrid Helene R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicolai S.","key":"arildsenpau","last":"Arildsen","locid":"b5e33658-6558-45b8-a127-be6059430303","name":"Arildsen, Nicolai Skovbjerg","name_org":"Arildsen, Nicolai S.","orcid":"0000-0002-1596-3120","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yiqiu","key":"yaopau","last":"Yao","name":"Yao, Yiqiu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper G.","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jesper G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Valdemar W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Valdemar W.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans C.","key":"ringpau","last":"Ring","name":"Ring, Hans C.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"woetmannpau","last":"Woetmann","locid":"18df0978-d38c-4ffb-985d-b544e22fa387","name":"Woetmann, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-3008-735X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Simon F.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","name_org":"Thomsen, Simon F.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jvc2.89","issn":["27686566"],"issue":"1","journal":"JEADV Clinical Practice","pages":"80-91","status":"p","title":"JEADV Clinical Practice","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170664818"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ffcdfa36-3c1a-4adf-a037-9829d90af65c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cluster analysis identifies six clinical subtypes of hidradenitis suppurativa characterised by distinct comorbidities, inflammatory and metabolic profiles, patient-reported outcomes and treatment patterns","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722572","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Transitioning urban drainage systems to serve water-smart societies requires the involvement of different disciplines and stakeholders. However, stakeholders have different visions and needs from the transitioning process (e.g in terms of financing, policy adaptation and system management) these also vary between regions and countries. Identifying such different needs for stakeholders is necessary to propose practical adaptation strategies. Therefore, evidence of needs as reflected in policy papers and legislation in seven European countries was collected. Knowledgeable individuals in the urban drainage community were asked about their visions. Results show that whilst there is consensus on the challenges, visions on how to transition are diverse, indicating that more interaction between the different stakeholder groups is required to develop consensus. Additionally, organisational and legislative structures often slow down the necessary change processes.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Tondera, Katharina","Brelot, Elodie","Fontanel, Fanny","Cherqui, Frédéric","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Brüggemann, Thomas","Naismith, Iain","Goerke, Marcel","Suárez López, Joaquín","Rieckermann, Jörg","Leitão, João P.","Clemens-Meyer, François H.L.R.","Moreno-Rodenas, Antonio","Tait, Simon","Anta, José"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-725551"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tondera, Katharina"],"country":["France","Germany","Netherlands","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deltares","Groupe de Recherche, Animation technique et Information sur l'Eau","IKT - Institute for Underground Infrastructure GmbH","Swiss Federal Institute of Aquatic Science and Technology","Universite Claude Bernard Lyon 1","University of A Coruna","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Europe","Guidelines","Legislation","Stormwater","Transition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"european stakeholders visions and needs for stormwater in future urban drainage systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1573062X.2023.2211559","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was carried out within the Collaborative Urban Drainage research labs communities - Co-UDlabs Project. Co-UDlabs has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under Grant Agreement No. 101008626. In France, this research was performed within the framework of the OTHU (Field Observatory for Urban Water Management–www.othu.org) and the Graduate School H2O’Lyon (ANR-17-EURE-0018). We thank the participants of the Rennes workshop and the individuals that responded to the online survey for their valuable input to the project."],"id":"S01-000.00-725551","identifier":[{"id":"85161444022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2af40abb-8bcd-44c5-a6ed-c8eaa944bbee"],"keyword":["Europe","Transition","adaptation to climate change","guidelines","legislation","stormwater"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85AD814FDDB297FF9322FA89DC1D8F53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/693806800/European_stakeholders_visions_and_needs_for_stormwater_in_future_urban_drainage_systems.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1573062X.2023.2211559","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"universite claude bernard lyon 1","loc":["France","Europe, 