{"abstract":"Offshore structures, functioning in harsh and extreme environmental conditions, may experience structural damages that can be challenging to reliably identify with conventional methods, especially if the damages do not correspond to a permanent change in the modal properties. In this study, a state-of-the-art Kalman Filter (KF) framework aided by a Finite Element (FE) analysis is employed for nonlinear state estimation and, consequently, structural damage identification of an offshore steel jacket structure subjected to unknown extreme wave loads. The outcome of this approach enables the estimation of the nonlinear structural response that, in turn, allows the localization and quantification of the damage.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Caglio, Luigi","Sadeqi, Amirali","Stang, Henrik","Tychsen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jørgen Svejgaard","Katsanos, Evangelos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-729656"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-23","place":"Ottawa, ca","start":"2023-06-19","title":"33<sup>rd</sup> International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Damage identification","Kalman filter","Nonlinear finite element model","Nonlinear system","State estimation","Structural health monitoring","Unknown input"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["TotalEnergies EP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"damage identification of offshore jacket structure via a kalman filter based nonlinear state estimation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85188693470","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-729656","identifier":[{"id":"85188693470","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6adba504-528b-4550-90ef-8910cecf4620"],"keyword":["Damage identification","Kalman Filter","Nonlinear finite element model","Nonlinear system","State estimation","Structural Health Monitoring","Unknown input"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-29B33EDCF0AC8E1EA3280B96697C176D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering and Structural Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["TotalEnergies EP"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luigi","key":"cagliopau","last":"Caglio","locid":"970db115-af4f-4368-b3a3-70bd7b206146","name":"Caglio, Luigi","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-2490","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amirali","key":"sadeqipau","last":"Sadeqi","locid":"0db09fbe-c91a-4442-b988-999f6de405d2","name":"Sadeqi, Amirali","orcid":"0000-0001-6443-2425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"stangpau","last":"Stang","locid":"57fe0e89-5130-43bb-a270-b38b7f8b885e","name":"Stang, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5812-4028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"tychsenpau","last":"Tychsen","name":"Tychsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Svejgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Svejgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evangelos","key":"katsanospau","last":"Katsanos","locid":"66c07f61-0ded-4f95-aa15-239b7f0b7480","name":"Katsanos, Evangelos","orcid":"0000-0003-2574-5327","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781880653807"],"issn":["10986189"],"pages":"3289-3295","publisher":"International Society of Offshore and Polar Engineers (ISOPE)","series":"Proceedings of the International Offshore and Polar Engineering Conference","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 33rd (2023) International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188693470"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6adba504-528b-4550-90ef-8910cecf4620"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Damage Identification of Offshore Jacket Structure via a Kalman Filter Based Nonlinear State Estimation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-729656","year":"2023","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background. Itch can be transmitted by two parallel pathways, histaminergic and nonhistaminergic. Histaminergic itch is transmitted by a subgroup of mechano-insensitive C-fibers, while nonhistaminergic itch by a subgroup of polymodal C-fibers. Experimental models are used to study pruritus: histamine for the histaminergic itch by antagonizing the histamine H1-receptors, and BAM8-22 and cowhage for the nonhistaminergic by activating Mas-related G protein-coupled receptors and protease-activated receptors, respectively. This study aims to evaluate the antipruritic effects of topical doxepin (H1-receptor antagonistic effect) on histaminergic and nonhistaminergic itch induced by histamine, BAM8-22, and cowhage. Methods. This study was conducted on 22 healthy subjects. Histamine, BAM8-22, cowhage, and vehicle were applied to 4 areas on the forearms. After 7 days, the same substances were applied after  hour-pretreatment with doxepin. After the application of pruritogens, itch and pain intensities were assessed for 9 minutes, followed by the measurement of superficial blood perfusion (SBP), mechanical and thermal sensitivities. Results. Application of histamine, BAM8-22, and cowhage all induced itch as compared to a vehicle. The pretreatment with doxepin almost abolished the histamine-induced itch and modestly reduced BAM8-22- and cowhage-induced itch. Histamine induced a higher SBP compared to the other conditions. Doxepin reduced SBP induced by each pruritogen, even though SBP of histamine remains the highest. Conclusion. Doxepin cream abolished histaminergic itch by antagonizing the peripheral H1-histamine receptors. Moreover, doxepin reduced nonhistaminergic itch and related neurogenic inflammation. Further studies are needed to elucidate the molecular mechanisms underlying this peripheral modulation of nonhistaminergic itch by a topically applied H1-antagonist. This trial is registered with NCT04588532.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aliotta, Giulia Erica","Lo Vecchio, Silvia","Elberling, Jesper","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-086.67-724330"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lo Vecchio, Silvia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antipruritic effects of doxepin cream on experimentally induced histaminergic and nonhistaminergic itch","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2023/9926108","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.67-724330","identifier":[{"id":"85205786040","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c266bced-0c57-4cab-8a5a-10f252397194","ku-cb3b3ca7-faa5-411c-8bec-c301a6a9342b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-511CB891738A0CD893078925A2321FEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/545316702/9926108.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/386576430/9926108.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2023/9926108","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giulia Erica","key":"aliottapau","last":"Aliotta","locid":"efb82db6-80bc-4a13-8fda-f95c91b88a94","name":"Aliotta, Giulia Erica","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Jesper Vraamark","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","name_org":"Elberling, Jesper Vraamark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2023/9926108","issn":["13960296","15298019"],"issn_org":["13960296"],"journal":"Dermatologic Therapy","paperid":"9926108","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Dermatologic Therapy","volume":"2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205786040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c266bced-0c57-4cab-8a5a-10f252397194","ku-cb3b3ca7-faa5-411c-8bec-c301a6a9342b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antipruritic Effects of Doxepin Cream on Experimentally Induced Histaminergic and Nonhistaminergic Itch","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.67-724330","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: One in four pregnancies end in a pregnancy loss. Although the effect on couples is well documented, evidence-based treatments and prediction models are absent. Fetal aneuploidy is associated with a higher chance of a next successful pregnancy compared with euploid pregnancy loss in which underlying maternal conditions might be causal. Ploidy diagnostics are therefore advantageous but challenging as they require collection of the pregnancy tissue. Cell-free fetal DNA (cffDNA) from maternal blood has the potential for evaluation of fetal ploidy status, but no large-scale validation of the method has been done. METHODS: In this prospective cohort study, women with a pregnancy loss were recruited as a part of the Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss (COPL) study from three gynaecological clinics at public hospitals in Denmark. Women were eligible for inclusion if older than 18 years with a pregnancy loss before gestational age 22 weeks (ie, 154 days) and with an intrauterine pregnancy confirmed by ultrasound (including anembryonic sac), and women with pregnancies of unknown location or molar pregnancies were excluded. Maternal blood was collected while pregnancy tissue was still in situ or within 24 h after pregnancy tissue had passed and was analysed by genome-wide sequencing of cffDNA. Direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue was done as reference. FINDINGS: We included 1000 consecutive women, at the time of a pregnancy loss diagnosis, between Nov 12, 2020, and May 1, 2022. Results from the first 333 women with a pregnancy loss (recruited between Nov 12, 2020, and Aug 14, 2021) were used to evaluate the validity of cffDNA-based testing. Results from the other 667 women were included to evaluate cffDNA performance and result distribution in a larger cohort of 1000 women in total. Gestational age of fetus ranged from 35-149 days (mean of 70·5 days [SD 16·5], or 10 weeks plus 1 day). The cffDNA-based test had a sensitivity for aneuploidy detection of 85% (95% CI 79-90) and a specificity of 93% (95% CI 88-96) compared with direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue. Among 1000 cffDNA-based test results, 446 (45%) were euploid, 405 (41%) aneuploid, 37 (4%) had multiple aneuploidies, and 112 (11%) were inconclusive. 105 (32%) of 333 women either did not manage to collect the pregnancy tissue or collected a sample classified as unknown tissue giving a high risk of being maternal. INTERPRETATION: This validation of cffDNA-based testing in pregnancy loss shows the potential and feasibility of the method to distinguish euploid and aneuploid pregnancy loss for improved clinical management and benefit of future reproductive medicine and women's health research. FUNDING: Ole Kirks Foundation, BioInnovation Institute Foundation, and the Novo Nordisk Foundation.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Schlaikjær Hartwig, Tanja","Ambye, Louise","Gruhn, Jennifer R.","Petersen, Jesper Friis","Wrønding, Tine","Amato, Letizia","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Ji, Boyang","Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","Werge, Lene","Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","Brinkmann, Clara","Petersen, Julie Birch","Dunø, Morten","Bache, Iben","Herrgård, Markus J.","Jørgensen, Finn Stener","Hoffmann, Eva R.","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","Freiesleben, Nina la Cour","Bliddal, Sofie","Søndergaard, Therese Juhlin","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Sørensen, Erik","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Herregård, Markus J.","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Kolte, Astrid Marie","Westergaard, David","þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Stefánsson, Kári","Jónsson, Hákon","Magnússon, Ólafur","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Schmidt, Lone","Kristiansen, Karsten","Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","Nyegaard, Mette","Krog, Maria Christine","Løkkegaard, Ellen","Bredkjær, Helle Ejdrup","Wilken-Jensen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-094.13-005502"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["COPL consortium"],"level":"sci","mr