"37083042"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euad088","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"5","journal":"Europace","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160876373"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-23b5d20b-ef10-4f64-9c0a-375361e9f828","ku-f1af99b3-eb71-4ec6-bf9a-4638c2f73396"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ventricular rate in atrial fibrillation and the risk of heart failure and death","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.03-672257","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Corn bran is exceptionally rich in substituted glucuronoarabinoxylan polysaccharides, which are monoferuloylated and cross-linked by diferulic acid moieties. Here, we assessed the potential prebiotic activity of three enzymatically solubilized corn bran glucuronoarabinoxylans: medium feruloylated (FGAX-M), laccase cross-linked FGAX-M (FGAX-H), and alkali-treated FGAX-M devoid of feruloyl substitutions (FGAX-B). We examined the influence of these soluble FGAX samples on the gut microbiome composition and functionality during in vitro simulated colon fermentations, determined by 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing and assessment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFAs) production. All FGAX samples induced changes in the relative composition of the microbiota and the SCFA levels after 24 h of in vitro fermentation. The changes induced by FGAX-M and FGAX-H tended to be more profound and more similar to the changes induced by inulin than changes conferred by FGAX-B. The microbiota changes induced by FGAX-M and FGAX-H correlated with an increase in the relative abundance of Anaerostipes and with increased butyric acid production, while the changes induced by the FGAX-B sample were less compelling. The results imply that solubilized, substituted diferuloylated corn bran glucuronoarabinoxylans may be potential prebiotic candidates and that both single feruloylations and diferuloyl cross-links influence the prebiotic potential of these arabinoxylan compounds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lin, Shang","Xu, Xinming","Holck, Jesper","Wittrup Agger, Jane","Wilkens, Casper","Xie, Zhuqing","Khakimov, Bekzod","Nielsen, Dennis S.","Meyer, Anne S."],"cuid":["S02-098.70-036902"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Anne S."],"keyword":["16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing","Diferuloyl cross links","In vitro colon fermentation","Potential prebiotic","Short chain fatty acids"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"soluble diferuloylated corn bran glucuronoarabinoxylans modulate the human gut microbiota i in vitro i","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85148368678","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.70-036902","identifier":[{"id":"85148368678","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36787634","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-be1ca4ad-33f1-46a8-96f5-598d41aea19d","ku-f6d96b41-b54d-4fd9-954a-1f8ee2ecb4da"],"keyword":["16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing","Cooccurence network analysis","Diferuloyl cross-links","In vitro colon fermentation","Potential prebiotic","Short-chain fatty acids","cooccurrence network analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A62F82D634AB9A586B2F020E175F2651"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, Enzyme Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shang","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","locid":"d2976ee3-62db-4372-bf42-dbf93ec2215a","name":"Lin, Shang","orcid":"0000-0003-0359-1179","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinming","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"3343a165-8f3f-4342-a8bf-df6bb281219f","name":"Xu, Xinming","orcid":"0000-0002-3203-4526","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","locid":"d444e5ac-34d3-487b-9327-7ae08138d861","name":"Holck, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8072-1101","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane","key":"wittrupaggerpau","last":"Wittrup Agger","locid":"c8d024fd-be76-4aa3-a266-0cbc3e2b36db","name":"Wittrup Agger, Jane","orcid":"0000-0002-7796-3089","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Casper","key":"wilkenspau","last":"Wilkens","locid":"d26028c1-6ef8-48e2-8810-cb3db9f32c14","name":"Wilkens, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-7692-067X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhuqing","key":"xiepau","last":"Xie","locid":"e87a296c-61aa-4e2e-82ab-50ead83b8bd2","name":"Xie, Zhuqing","orcid":"0000-0002-8323-4472","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bekzod","key":"khakimovpau","last":"Khakimov","locid":"deffc914-4694-4caa-92e2-b9c5ad41eb86","name":"Khakimov, Bekzod","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dennis S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","name_org":"Nielsen, Dennis S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne S.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"1e9f4759-72d8-4d52-94ec-ce192ffca184","name":"Meyer, Anne S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8910-9931","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36787634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jafc.2c08338","issn":["00218561","15205118"],"issn_org":["00218561"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","pages":"3885-3897","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148368678"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-be1ca4ad-33f1-46a8-96f5-598d41aea19d","ku-f6d96b41-b54d-4fd9-954a-1f8ee2ecb4da"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Soluble, Diferuloylated Corn Bran Glucuronoarabinoxylans Modulate the Human Gut Microbiota <i>In Vitro</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.70-036902","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Air pollution is negatively associated with cardiovascular health. Impediments to efficient regulation include lack of knowledge about which sources of air pollution contributes most to health burden and few studies on effects of the potentially more potent ultrafine particles (UFP). OBJECTIVE: The authors aimed to investigate myocardial infarction (MI) morbidity and specific types and sources of air pollution. METHODS: We identified all persons living in Denmark in the period 2005–2017, age >50 y and never diagnosed with MI. We quantified 5-y running time-weighted mean concentrations of air pollution at residencies, both total and apportioned to traffic and nontraffic sources. We evaluated particulate matter (PM) with aerodynamic diameter ≤2:5 lm (PM 2:5), <0:1 lm (UFP), elemental carbon (EC), and nitrogen dioxide (NO 2). We used Cox pro-portional hazards models, with adjustment for time-varying exposures, and personal and area-level demographic and socioeconomic covariates from high-quality administrative registers. RESULTS: In this nationwide cohort of 1,964,702 persons (with 18 million person-years of follow-up and 71,285 cases of MI), UFP and PM 2:5 were associated with increased risk of MI with hazard ratios (HRs) per interquartile range (IQR) of 1.040 [95% confidence interval (CI): 1.025, 1.055] and 1.053 (95% CI: 1.035, 1.071), respectively. HRs per IQR of UFP and PM 2:5 from nontraffic sources were similar to the total (1.034 and 1.051), whereas HRs for UFP and PM 2:5 from traffic sources were smaller (1.011 and 1.011). The HR for EC from traffic sources was 1.013 (95% CI: 1.003, 1.023). NO 2 from nontraffic sources was associated with MI (HR = 1:048; 95% CI: 1.034, 1.062) but not from traffic sources. In general, nontraffic sources contributed more to total air pollution levels than national traffic sources. CONCLUSIONS: PM 2:5 and UFP from traffic and nontraffic sources were associated with increased risk of MI, with nontraffic sources being the domi-nant source of exposure and morbidity. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10556.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Christensen, Jesper H.","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Andersen, Christopher","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.48-686005"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Aslak Harbo"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"source specific air pollution including ultrafine particles and risk of myocardial infarction a nationwide cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10556","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.48-686005","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10217353","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37235386","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85160288285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9fff1b69-ed01-4355-82a7-2cb721d5e9e7","ruc-33a3a092-599e-4077-b4d7-feb73956c1be"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8E14E706013A2E62AB30DBC8206341CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10556","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/95109377/EHP10556.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christopher","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3cb895d7-5de5-421e-a12f-ce9982a1cdeb","name":"Andersen, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-2337-8239","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37235386"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp10556","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"5","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","paperid":"057010","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"131"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160288285"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9fff1b69-ed01-4355-82a7-2cb721d5e9e7","ruc-33a3a092-599e-4077-b4d7-feb73956c1be"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Source-Specific Air Pollution Including Ultrafine Particles and Risk of Myocardial Infarction : A Nationwide Cohort Study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.48-686005","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Targeted temperature management (TTM) may moderate the injury from out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Slowing the metabolism has been a suggested effect. Nevertheless, studies have found higher lactate levels in patients cooled to 33°C compared with 36°C even days from TTM cessation. Larger studies have not been performed on the TTM's effect on the metabolome. Accordingly, to explore the effect of TTM, we used ultra-performance liquid-mass spectrometry in a substudy of 146 patients randomized in the TTM trial to either 33°C or 36°C for 24 hours and quantified 60 circulating metabolites at the time of hospital arrival (T0) and 48 hours later (T48). From T0 to T48, profound changes to the metabolome were observed: tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle metabolites, amino acids, uric acid, and carnitine species all decreased. TTM significantly modified these changes in nine metabolites (Benjamini-Hochberg corrected false discovery rate <0.05): branched amino acids valine and leucine levels dropped more in the 33°C arm (change [95% confidence interval]: -60.9 μM [-70.8 to -50.9] vs. -36.0 μM [-45.8 to -26.3] and -35.5 μM [-43.1 to -27.8] vs. -21.2 μM [-28.7 to -13.6], respectively), whereas the TCA metabolites including malic acid and 2-oxoglutaric acid remained higher for the first 48 hours (-7.7 μM [-9.7 to -5.7] vs. -10.4 μM [-12.4 to -8.4] and -3 μM [-4.3 to -1.7] vs. -3.7 μM [-5 to -2.3]). Prostaglandin E2 only dropped in the TTM 36°C group. The results show that TTM affects the metabolism hours after normothermia have been reached. Clinical Trial Number: NCT01020916.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Beske, Rasmus Paulin","Obling, Laust Emil Roelsgaard","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Nielsen, Niklas","Meyer, Martin Abild Steengaard","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Johansson, Pär Ingemar","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-715892"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Metabolism","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Targeted temperature management"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of targeted temperature management on the metabolome following out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85178650405","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-715892","identifier":[{"id":"37219970","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85178650405","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2190d8c3-ffa0-4cad-a866-d38a0f567fc3","ku-5b9c6e0f-1f2d-432b-a125-ec148a2f27fd"],"keyword":["metabolism","out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","targeted temperature management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DA6E0D0BF51F8ADC4F0FA5A50B62BCCA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Cardiology, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Paulin","key":"beskepau","last":"Beske","name":"Beske, Rasmus Paulin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laust Emil Roelsgaard","key":"oblingpau","last":"Obling","name":"Obling, Laust Emil Roelsgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","locid":"43823b29-f095-4817-baab-275e6758259f","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","orcid":"0000-0001-7187-5734","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abild Steengaard","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Martin Abild Steengaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"10ffadd9-ed9c-4251-954a-a2c12ce83aca","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Pär Ingemar","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","locid":"658264ad-0ef0-4939-9515-9ef0cee85995","name":"Johansson, Pär I.","name_org":"Johansson, Pär Ingemar","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37219970"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/ther.2022.0065","issn":["21537658","21537933"],"issn_org":["21537658"],"issue":"4","journal":"Therapeutic Hypothermia and Temperature Management","pages":"208-215","publisher":"Mary Ann Liebert Inc.","status":"p","title":"Therapeutic Hypothermia and Temperature Management","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178650405"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2190d8c3-ffa0-4cad-a866-d38a0f567fc3","ku-5b9c6e0f-1f2d-432b-a125-ec148a2f27fd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Effect of Targeted Temperature Management on the Metabolome Following Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-715892","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Air pollution, road traffic noise, and green space are correlated factors, associated with risk of stroke. We investigated their independent relationship with stroke in multi-exposure analyses and estimated their cumulative stroke burden. Methods: For all persons, ≥50 years of age and living in Denmark from 2005 to 2017, we established complete address histories and estimated running 5-year mean exposure to fine particles (PM2.5), ultrafine particles, elemental carbon, nitrogen dioxide (NO2), and road traffic noise at the most, and least exposed façade. For air pollutants, we estimated total, and non-traffic contributions. Green space around the residence was estimated from land use maps. Hazard ratios (HR) and 95% confidence limits (CL) were estimated with Cox proportional hazards models and used to calculate cumulative risk indices (CRI). We adjusted for the individual and sociodemographic covariates available in our dataset (which did not include information about individual life styles and medical conditions). Findings: The cohort accumulated 18,344,976 years of follow-up and 94,256 cases of stroke. All exposures were associated with risk of stroke in single pollutant models. In multi-pollutant analyses, only PM2.5 (HR: 1.058, 95% CI: 1.040–1.075) and noise at most exposed façade (HR: 1.033, 95% CI: 1.024–1.042) were independently associated with a higher risk of stroke. Both noise and air pollution contributed substantially to the CRI (1.103, 95% CI: 1.092–1.114) in the model with noise, green space, and total PM2.5 concentrations. Interpretation: Environmental exposure to air pollution and noise were both independently associated with risk of stroke. Funding: Health Effects Institute (HEI) (Assistance Award No. R-82811201).","author_count":11,"contributors":["Poulsen, Aslak H.","Sørensen, Mette","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Andersen, Christopher","Jensen, Ste