{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: There is a growing body of evidence linking residential exposure to transportation noise with several nonauditory health outcomes. However, auditory outcomes, such as tinnitus, are virtually unexplored. OBJECTIVES: We aimed to investigate the association between residential transportation noise and risk of incident tinnitus. METHODS: We conducted a nationwide cohort study including all residents in Denmark age ≥30 y, of whom 40,692 were diagnosed with tinnitus. We modeled road traffic and railway noise at the most (L denmax) and least (L denmin) exposed façades of all Danish addresses from 1990 until 2017. For all participants, we calculated 1-, 5-, and 10-y time-weighted mean noise exposure and retrieved detailed information on individual-and area-level socioeconomic covariates. We conducted analyses using Cox proportional hazards models. RESULTS: We found positive associations between exposure to road traffic noise and risk of tinnitus, with hazard ratios of 1.06 [95% confidence interval (CI): 1.04, 1.08] and 1.02 (95% CI: 1.01, 1.03) per 10-dB increase in 10-y L denmin and L denmax, respectively. Highest risk estimates were found for women, people without a hearing loss, people with high education and income, and people who had never been in a blue-collar job. The association with road L denmin followed a positive, monotonic exposure–response relationship. We found no association between railway noise and tinnitus. DISCUSSION: To our knowledge, this is the first study to show that residential exposure to road traffic noise may increase risk of tinnitus, suggesting noise may negatively affect the auditory system. If confirmed, this finding adds to the growing evidence of road traffic noise as a harmful pollutant with a substantial health burden. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP11248.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech","Pedersen, Ellen Raben","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Levin, Gregor","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-099.35-028010"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech"],"keyword":["Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Environmental Exposure adverse effects","Female","Humans","Male","Noise Transportation adverse effects","Risk","Tinnitus epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transportation noise and risk of tinnitus a nationwide cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP11248","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.35-028010","identifier":[{"id":"85147317778","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9891135","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36722980","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d3c07942-6a51-4970-8cef-c3905a48fab5","ruc-100b0271-51e0-438d-8925-e2d9e5565316","sdu-5a1e5507-9a18-418b-93b2-8c6e138025c8"],"keyword":["Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Environmental Exposure/adverse effects","Female","Humans","Male","Noise, Transportation/adverse effects","Risk","Tinnitus/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-26FC5770BB03070619667CECBF2AF2BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/89347327/EHP11248.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP11248","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Applied AI and Data Science","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Kræftens Bekæmpelse"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuella Lech","key":"cantuariapau","last":"Cantuaria","locid":"8f037fd9-8e4b-4926-ad07-466bc021a3da","name":"Cantuaria, Manuella Lech","orcid":"0000-0003-3201-9606","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen Raben","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b7a104b3-f660-4af6-a5eb-aa39f455e89f","name":"Pedersen, El