rst":"Rene Ernst","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"689bbd5c-f16d-4316-9717-29e68172bb57","name":"Nielsen, René Ernst","name_org":"Nielsen, Rene Ernst","orcid":"0000-0002-7982-6352","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"kragholmpau","last":"Kragholm","locid":"052ee38b-92bc-47d4-a37d-13fa99e39ddb","name":"Kragholm, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0001-9629-8670","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"fleischerpau","last":"Fleischer","name":"Fleischer, Jesper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"laugesenpau","last":"Laugesen","name":"Laugesen, Esben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"polcwiartekpau","last":"Polcwiartek","locid":"3e199cab-8236-49a9-a5a9-35daa24f991b","name":"Polcwiartek, Christoffer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38510185"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahjo.2023.100252","issn":["26666022"],"journal":"American Heart Journal Plus: Cardiology Research and Practice","paperid":"100252","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal Plus: Cardiology Research and Practice","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153883051"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-349c2443-2b47-4c3b-9918-68089cbb3516"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Cardiovascular autonomic reflex tests using a handheld device in the diagnosis of cardiovascular autonomic neuropathy in patients with schizophrenia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673509","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The presence of electrocardiogram (ECG) abnormalities is high in patients with end-stage kidney disease, but no studies have examined the prevalence of ECG abnormalities according to different strata of estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) in a population-based setting.This was a retrospective cross-sectional study including 310,060 individuals from the Copenhagen General Practitioners' Laboratory who had an available digital ECG recorded between 2001 and 2015 and a creatinine measurement within 7 days of the ECG. eGFR was calculated using the The Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration equation. ECG abnormalities were categorized as no, minor or major, as done previously [1]. Patients with both minor and major ECG abnormalities were assigned as major ECG abnormalities. The prevalence of ECG abnormalities was examined according to different strata of renal function [eGFR (ml/min/1.73 m2) \\gt;90, 61–90, 46–60, 31–45, 30-16 and ≤15]. Ordinal logistic regression was used to illustrate the probability of ECG abnormalities as a function of eGFR.The median age was 55 [IQR, 41-69] years and 46\\7,249 (17.9\\ of the included patients had an eGFR \\lt;60. The prevalence of major ECG abnormalities increased with declining eGFR: \\gt;90 (16.5\\, 61–90 (21.6\\, 46–60 (36.5\\ 31–45 (52.1\\, 30-16 (57.9\\ and ≤15 (60.1\\. In ordinal logistic regression, the risk of having major ECG abnormalities compared to minor/no abnormalities significantly decreased pr. 5 ml/min increase in eGFR, OR 0.90 (95\\ 0.85-0.90), Fig. 1. The most common major ECG abnormalities were left ventricular hypertrophy and ST-T deviations. The prevalence of all ECG abnormalities is shown in Table 1.Figure 1:Predicted probability of ECG abnormalities according to eGFR.Table 1:Prevalence of ECG abnormalities.eGFR (ml/min/1.73 m2)\\gt;90n = 105,10561-90n = 153,98446-60n = 36,20931-45n = 11,60616-30n = 2732≤15n = 424Age, yrs (median, iqr)42 (30-53)57 (46-68)75 (66-82)83 (76-88)84 (78-89)82 (70-89)Males53,221 (50.6)73,157 (47.5)11,630 (32.1)3504 (30.2)962 (35.2)197 (46.5)Heart rate, bpm (median, iqr)69 (61-78)69 (61-78)72 (63-82)73 (64-84)73 (64-85)76 (66-86)No ECG abnormality82,968 (78.9)111,962 (72.7)20,717 (57.2)4714 (40.6)901 (33.0)132 (31.1)Minor ECG abnormality4782 (4.5)8744 (5.7)2280 (6.3)846 (7.3)248 (9.1)37 (8.7) First-degree atrioventricular block1736 (1.7)5748 (3.7)2628 (7.3)1306 (11.3)385 (14.1)63 (14.9) Incomplete bundle branch block2420 (2.3)3734 (2.4)790 (2.2)260 (2.2)75 (2.7)9 (2.1) Left fascicular block1212 (1.2)1836 (1.2)649 (1.8)260 (2.2)63 (2.3)18 (4.2) QTcF prolongation1854 (1.8)5554 (3.6)2212 (6.1)1141 (9.8)385 (14.1)79 (18.6)Major ECG abnormality17,355 (16.5)33,278 (21.6)13,212 (36.5)6046 (52.1)1583 (57.9)255 (60.1) Left ventricular hyperthrophy9822 (9.3)14,438 (9.4)4930 (13.6)2061 (17.8)535 (19.6)100 (23.6) Atrial fibrillation663 (0.6)4257 (2.8)2907 (8.0)1628 (14.0)428 (15.7)54 (12.7) Bundle branch block1160 (1.1)4663 (3.0)2412 (6.7)1324 (11.4)380 (13.9)54 (12.7) Intraventricular conduction disorder725 (0.7)1149 (0.7)322 (0.9)171 (1.5)48 (1.8)10 (2.4) Q waves3560 (3.4)8115 (5.3)2911 (8.0)1186 (10.2)293 (10.7)40 (9.4) ST-T deviations2802 (2.7)5729 (3.7)3247 (9.0)1853 (16.0)552 (20.2)86 (20.3)ECG abnormalities are common in patients with chronic kidney disease, and the probability of major ECG abnormalities increases with declining eGFR.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Carlson, Nicholas","Nelveg-Kristensen, Karl-Emil","Rantanen, Jesper Moesgaard","Madsen, Bo","Graff, Claus","Nielsen, Jonas","Pietersen, Adrian","Torp, Christian","Riahi, Sam","Svensson, My","Gregersen, Jon Waarst","Polcwiartek, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673586"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-18","place":"Milan, it","start":"2023-06-15","title":"60th ERA Congress","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of electrocardiographic abnormalities in patients with chronic kidney disease","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-673586","ids":["aau-4592bb99-8ea3-42fb-a9ed-1b9968102189"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6D7C39D387B11D5D3FF2372443498107"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen General Practitioners’ Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"carlsonpau","last":"Carlson","name":"Carlson, Nicholas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl-Emil","key":"nelvegkristensenpau","last":"Nelveg-Kristensen","name":"Nelveg-Kristensen, Karl-Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Moesgaard","key":"rantanenpau","last":"Rantanen","locid":"96c9206c-9b16-48ab-9d7f-9fa31b658bcb","name":"Rantanen, Jesper Moesgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"4193ceab-cd08-4355-836a-5fd0b7563981","name":"Madsen, Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"pietersenpau","last":"Pietersen","name":"Pietersen, Adrian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","name":"Torp, Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sam","key":"riahipau","last":"Riahi","locid":"9e5489d8-981a-469c-bd84-20b2e24832de","name":"Riahi, Sam","orcid":"0000-0003-1849-9463","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"My","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"0ed91c60-a2c2-44d5-b7f5-c17fb1318c47","name":"Svensson, My","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon Waarst","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"4d228f34-6d50-4c26-ac0e-26b28eba788c","name":"Gregersen, Jon Waarst","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"polcwiartekpau","last":"Polcwiartek","locid":"3e199cab-8236-49a9-a5a9-35daa24f991b","name":"Polcwiartek, Christoffer","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ndt/gfad063c_4750","issn":["09310509","14602385"],"issn_org":["09310509"],"issue":"Supplement_1","journal":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","paperid":"gfad063c_4750","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","title_org":"Nephrology, Dialysis, Transplantation","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","copenhagen general practitioners’ laboratory"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4592bb99-8ea3-42fb-a9ed-1b9968102189"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Prevalence of electrocardiographic abnormalities in patients with chronic kidney disease","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673586","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Electrocardiogram (ECG) abnormalities are associated with adverse cardiovascular outcomes in patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD), but their prognostic relevance according to estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) categories remains unexplored. This study investigated the associations between no, minor, and major ECG abnormalities and fatal cardiovascular disease (CVD) according to different strata of renal function.This was a retrospective cohort study including 310.060 individuals aged ≥16 years from the Copenhagen General Practitioners' Laboratory that had an available digital ECG and creatinine measurement within 7 days from 2001–2015. eGFR was calculated using The Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration equation, and data were cross-linked with Danish nation-wide healthcare registries to gain information on medication, comorbidity, and fatal CVD. ECG abnormalities were categorized as either no abnormalities, minor (first‐degree atrioventricular block, incomplete bundle branch block or corrected QT prolongation) or major (left ventricular hypertrophy, atrial fibrillation/flutter, bundle branch block, Q waves, or ST‐T deviations), as done previously [1]. Patients with both minor and major ECG abnormalities were assigned as major ECG abnormalities. ECG abnormalities and their association with fatal CVD were compared across strata of renal function [eGFR (ml/min/1.73m2) \\gt;90, 61–90, 46–60, 31–45, 16–30 and ≤15] based on multivariable Cox-regression analysis adjusted for age, sex, and comorbidities. Counterfactual G-estimation of Hazard Ratios (HRs) standardized to age and sex was performed to estimate 5-year absolute risk of fatal CVD.The median age was 55 [IQR, 41-69] years and 46\\up time was 10.3 [IQR, 6.7-14.4] years. A total of 47,249 (17.9\\ of the included patients had an eGFR \\lt;60. The rate of fatal CVD according to ECG abnormalities and their adjusted HRs is shown in Fig. 1, while 5-year standardized risk of fatal CVD is depicted in Fig. 2. Generally, having minor or major ECG abnormalities, conferred a worse prognosis across all eGFR strata, with the highest 5-year absolute risk of fatal CVD being observed among patients with major ECG abnormalities and an eGFR between 31–45 [19\\95\\ 18–20\\], eGFR 16–30 [25\\95\\ 24–26\\] or an eGFR ≤15 [27.5\\95\\ 24–31\\], Fig. 1–2.Figure 1:Multivariable Cox-regression of the association between fatal cardiovascular disease and eGFR categories across no, minor and major ECG abnormalities. Adjusted for age, sex, heart failure, coronary artery disease, atrial fibrillation/flutter, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, diabetes, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and QT-prolonging medications.Figure 2:Standardized 5-year absolute risk of fatal cardiovascular disease across no, minor and major ECG abnormalities. Absolute risks are depicted with error bars representing ± standard error.In a population-based setting, having minor or major ECG abnormalities were associated with an increased risk of fatal CVD across all strata of renal function. Patients with an eGFR ≤45 and major ECG abnormalities represent a high-risk population, that might benefit from careful monitoring and cardiovascular risk management.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Carlson, Nicholas","Nelveg-Kristensen, Karl-Emil","Rantanen, Jesper Moesgaard","Madsen, Bo","Graff, Claus","Nielsen, Jonas","Pietersen, Adrian","Torp, Christian","Riahi, Sam","Svensson, My","Gregersen, Jon Waarst","Polcwiartek, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674106"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-18","place":"Milan, it","start":"2023-06-15","title":"60th ERA Congress","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic relevance of electrocardiographic abnormalities according to egfr categories","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-674106","ids":["aau-c8898545-6cb8-46f0-87a1-078c40969b2f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E3510E334D4E201A14AEF5C2B94101A3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen General Practitioners’ Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"carlsonpau","last":"Carlson","name":"Carlson, Nicholas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl-Emil","key":"nelvegkristensenpau","last":"Nelveg-Kristensen","name":"Nelveg-Kristensen, Karl-Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Moesgaard","key":"rantanenpau","last":"Rantanen","locid":"96c9206c-9b16-48ab-9d7f-9fa31b658bcb","name":"Rantanen, Jesper Moesgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"4193ceab-cd08-4355-836a-5fd0b7563981","name":"Madsen, Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"pietersenpau","last":"Pietersen","name":"Pietersen, Adrian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","name":"Torp, Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sam","key":"riahipau","last":"Riahi","locid":"9e5489d8-981a-469c-bd84-20b2e24832de","name":"Riahi, Sam","orcid":"0000-0003-1849-9463","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"My","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"0ed91c60-a2c2-44d5-b7f5-c17fb1318c47","name":"Svensson, My","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon Waarst","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"4d228f34-6d50-4c26-ac0e-26b28eba788c","name":"Gregersen, Jon Waarst","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"polcwiartekpau","last":"Polcwiartek","locid":"3e199cab-8236-49a9-a5a9-35daa24f991b","name":"Polcwiartek, Christoffer","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ndt/gfad063c_4771","issn":["09310509","14602385"],"issn_org":["09310509"],"issue":"Supplement_1","journal":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","paperid":"gfad063c_4771","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","title_org":"Nephrology, Dialysis, Transplantation","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","copenhagen general practitioners’ laboratory"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c8898545-6cb8-46f0-87a1-078c40969b2f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Prognostic relevance of electrocardiographic abnormalities according to EGFR categories","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674106","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Burst abdomen is a serious complication requiring immediate surgical treatment. This study aimed to investigate the association between rectus diastasis and burst abdomen in patients undergoing emergency midline laparotomy. Methods: A single-center, retrospective, matched case–control study of patients undergoing emergency midline laparotomy from May 2016 to August 2021 was conducted. Cases (patients who suffered from burst abdomen) were matched 1:4 with controls based on age and sex. Rectus diastasis was evaluated on CT imaging and was defined as a distance of at least three centimeters between the rectus abdominis muscles, three centimeters above the umbilicus. Midline laparotomy aponeurosis closure was standardized during the study period, using a slowly absorbable suture, sutured continuously with small bites of five millimeters and a minimum suture-to-wound ratio of 4:1. The primary outcome was the association between rectus diastasis and burst abdomen, evaluated against other suspected risk factors including obesity, liver cirrhosis, previous laparotomy, midline hernias and active smoking in a multivariate analysis. Results: A total of 465 patients were included in the study, with 93 cases matched to 372 controls. Eighty-four patients had rectus diastasis (35.5% cases vs. 13.7% controls; p = < 0.001). Multivariate analysis found rectus diastasis significantly associated with burst abdomen (OR 3.06, 95% CI 1.71–5.47; p = < 0.001). No other suspected risk factors showed a significant association with burst abdomen. Conclusion: Rectus diastasis was highly associated with an increased risk of burst abdomen after emergency midline laparotomy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kvist, M.","Henriksen, Nadia A.","Burcharth, Jakob","Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","Jensen, Thomas Korgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-678835"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Burst abdomen","Laparotomy","Rectus diastasis","Wound Healing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rectus diastasis increases risk of burst abdomen in emergency midline laparotomies a matched case control study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381240141/pdf24_merged_Rectus.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-678835","identifier":[{"id":"85142437705","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36422726","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a43df9f5-9e05-4793-96d9-68325a2ac7c0"],"keyword":["Burst abdomen","Laparotomy","Midline hernia","Rectus diastasis","Wound healing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B251BE0B6D85AEC03D513A25D5B6243"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381240141/pdf24_merged_Rectus.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"M.","key":"kvistpau","last":"Kvist","name":"Kvist, M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"N. A.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"aaaa2bff-9d81-462f-bcdd-15a0e71470ea","name":"Henriksen, Nadia A.","name_org":"Henriksen, N. A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J.","key":"burcharthpau","last":"Burcharth","locid":"cefbcb72-ea12-46e2-8fee-9b67d7fc9ff2","name":"Burcharth, Jakob","name_org":"Burcharth, J.","orcid":"0000-0001-8367-7831","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Y. W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"41cd192a-a0fd-4fd8-9361-cbedd07691f9","name":"Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","name_org":"Nielsen, Y. W.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"T. K.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a01d2365-97ed-4689-9cbc-9d2fcb6466cc","name":"Jensen, Thomas Korgaard","name_org":"Jensen, T. K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36422726"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10029-022-02719-2","issn":["12489204","12654906"],"issn_org":["12654906"],"journal":"Hernia","pages":"353-361","status":"p","title":"Hernia","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142437705"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a43df9f5-9e05-4793-96d9-68325a2ac7c0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rectus diastasis increases risk of burst abdomen in emergency midline laparotomies : a matched case–control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678835","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Galectins are a group of carbohydrate-binding proteins with a presumed immunomodulatory role and an elusive function on antigen-presenting cells. Here we analyzed the expression of galectin-1 and found upregulation of galectin-1 in the extracellular matrix across multiple tumors. Performing an in-depth and dynamic proteomic and phosphoproteomic analysis of human macrophages stimulated with galectin-1, we show that galectin-1 induces a tumor-associated macrophage phenotype with increased expression of key immune checkpoint protein programmed cell death 1 ligand 1 (PD-L1/CD274) and immunomodulator indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase-1 (IDO1). Galectin-1 induced IDO1 and its active metabolite kynurenine in a dose-dependent manner through JAK/STAT signaling. In a 3D organotypic tissue model system equipped with genetically engineered tumorigenic epithelial cells, we analyzed the cellular source of galectin-1 in the extracellular matrix and found that galectin-1 is derived from epithelial and stromal cells. Our results highlight the potential of targeting galectin-1 in immunotherapeutic treatment of human cancers.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Levann, Asha Maria Rudjord","Ye, Zilu","Hafkenscheid, Lise","Horn, Sabrina","Wiegertjes, Renske","Nielsen, Mathias I.","Song, Ming","Madsen, Caroline B","Stoop, Jesse","Stowell, Sean","thor Straten, Per","Leffler, Hakon","Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","Dabelsteen, Sally","Olsen, Jesper V.","Wandall, Hans H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684122"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Immunology and Glycobiology"],"keyword":["Cancer","Immunology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"galectin 000000000001 induces a tumor associated macrophage phenotype and upregulates indoleamine 000000000002 000000000003 dioxygenase 000000000001","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106984","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-684122","identifier":[{"id":"85161718499","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10391608","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37534161","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001056896500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-748fa7c0-e498-4bfa-83fb-6e065a7d0475"],"keyword":["Cancer","Immunology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4AC1588A07867CBB9BBC281FC7CAB949"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360682647/1_s2.0_S2589004223010611_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106984","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","nameva