ten Salling","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","name_org":"Olesen, Morten Salling","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Bille","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Bille","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"brandespau","last":"Brandes","locid":"de0996e3-b51d-4ce2-9dc0-380aee6329e9","name":"Brandes, Axel","orcid":"0000-0001-9145-6887","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ketil Jørgen","key":"hauganpau","last":"Haugan","name":"Haugan, Ketil Jørgen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37666019"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amjcard.2023.08.042","issn":["00029149","18791913"],"issn_org":["00029149"],"journal":"American Journal of Cardiology","pages":"457-464","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Cardiology","title_org":"The American Journal of Cardiology","volume":"205"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170037861"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8a60e7ab-7a7b-4ce4-beb5-a2b77c2293fd","ku-cd6b869e-9728-4e99-ae78-ab696823134d","sdu-bf620fcd-c5ee-4122-8057-91dbebe0812d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Electrocardiographic Morphology-Voltage-P-Wave-Duration (MVP) Score to Select Patients for Continuous Atrial Fibrillation Screening to Prevent Stroke","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-685699","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Patients with Brugada syndrome (BrS) are recommended to avoid drugs that may increase their risk of arrhythmic events. We examined treatment with such drugs in patients with BrS after their diagnosis. Methods and Results All Danish patients diagnosed with BrS (2006-2018) with >12 months of follow-up were identified from nationwide registries. Nonrecommended BrS drugs were grouped into drugs to \"avoid\" or \"preferably avoid\" according to http://www.brugadadrugs.org. Cox proportional hazards analyses were performed to identify factors associated with any nonrecommended BrS drug use, and logistic regression analyses were performed to examine associated risk of appropriate implantable cardioverter defibrillator therapy, mortality, and a combined end point indicating an arrhythmic event of delayed implantable cardioverter defibrillator implantation, appropriate implantable cardioverter defibrillator therapy, and mortality. During a median follow-up of 6.8 years, 93/270 (34.4%) patients with BrS (70.4% male, median age at diagnosis 46.1 years [interquartile range, 32.6-57.4]) were treated with ≥1 nonrecommended BrS drugs. No difference in any nonrecommended BrS drug use was identified comparing time before BrS diagnosis (12.6%) with each of the 5 years following BrS diagnosis (P>0.05). Factors associated with any nonrecommended BrS drug use after diagnosis were female sex (hazard ratio [HR]) 1.83 [95% CI, 1.15-2.90]), psychiatric disease (HR, 3.63 [1.89-6.99]), and prior use of any nonrecommended BrS drug (HR, 4.76 [2.45-9.25]). No significant association between any nonrecommended BrS drug use and implantable cardioverter defibrillator therapy (n=20/97, odds ratio [OR], 0.7 [0.2-2.4]), mortality (n=10/270, OR, 3.4 [0.7-19.6]), or the combined end point (n=38/270, OR, 1.7 [0.8-3.7]) was identified. Conclusions One in 3 patients with BrS were treated with a nonrecommended BrS drug after BrS diagnosis, and a BrS diagnosis did not change prescription patterns. More awareness of nonrecommended drug use among patients with BrS is needed.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Jespersen, Camilla H B","Krøll, Johanna","Bhardwaj, Priya","Hansen, Carl Johann","Svane, Jesper","Winkel, Bo G","Jøns, Christian","Jacobsen, Peter Karl","Haarbo, Jens","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Johansen, Jens Brock","Philbert, Berit T","Riahi, Sam","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Køber, Lars","Hansen, Jacob Tfelt","Weeke, Peter E"],"cuid":["S04-099.96-665745"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Jespersen, Camilla H B"],"keyword":["Adverse drug events","BrS","Brugada Syndrome diagnosis","Cohort Studies","Death Sudden Cardiac","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark epidemiology","Electrocardiography methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pharmacotherapy","Ventricular arrhythmia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of nonrecommended drugs in patients with brugada syndrome a danish nationwide cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.122.028424","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.96-665745","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10122907","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85152159310","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36942759","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2b0eeedb-6e61-4ce1-84ec-69e93099cbf5","au-fcba79c4-68df-489c-95e9-16d2db53dcdf","ku-ecaff382-ebc1-4600-b1cc-f12c33e13965","sdu-9c24ceca-cff1-4118-ac56-188574e8c6d4"],"keyword":["BrS","Brugada Syndrome/diagnosis","Cohort Studies","Death, Sudden, Cardiac","Defibrillators, Implantable","Denmark/epidemiology","Electrocardiography/methods","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","adverse drug events","pharmacotherapy","ventricular arrhythmia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-3775B5F6B9B60E781BCA31AA912FF2D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/227196293/JAHA.122.028424.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/527474024/Jespersen_et_al._2023_._Use_of_Nonrecommended_Drugs_in_Patients_With_Brugada_Syndrome_A_Danish_Nationwide_Cohort_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/344709804/JAHA.122.028424.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.122.028424","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Section of Forensic Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus