{"abstract":"Antigen binding by B cell receptors (BCR) on cognate B cells elicits a response that eventually leads to production of antibodies. However, it is unclear what the distribution of BCRs is on the naïve B cell and how antigen binding triggers the first step in BCR signaling. Using DNA-PAINT super-resolution microscopy, we find that most BCRs are present as monomers, dimers, or loosely associated clusters on resting B cells, with a nearest-neighbor inter-Fab distance of 20–30 nm. We leverage a Holliday junction nanoscaffold to engineer monodisperse model antigens with precision-controlled affinity and valency, and find that the antigen exerts agonistic effects on the BCR as a function of increasing affinity and avidity. Monovalent macromolecular antigens can activate the BCR at high concentrations, whereas micromolecular antigens cannot, demonstrating that antigen binding does not directly drive activation. Based on this, we propose a BCR activation model determined by the antigen footprint.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ferapontov, Alexey","Omer, Marjan","Baudrexel, Isabelle","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Dupont, Daniel Miotto","Juul-Madsen, Kristian","Steen, Philipp","Eklund, Alexandra S.","Thiel, Steffen","Vorup-Jensen, Thomas","Jungmann, Ralf","Kjems, Jørgen","Degn, Søren Egedal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164455"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Degn, Søren Egedal"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antigen footprint governs activation of the b cell receptor","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-36672-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164455","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9947222","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36813795","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85148719985","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3da81cd5-dd9c-41b8-977f-45433eca27dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C61AE4DCF55B05BE2A21578A31EA444A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-36672-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexey","key":"ferapontovpau","last":"Ferapontov","locid":"92124ba7-b3a7-4739-bda0-09e7239be58d","name":"Ferapontov, Alexey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marjan","key":"omerpau","last":"Omer","locid":"07128923-a361-4afe-9c16-91c1f1b9a5df","name":"Omer, Marjan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabelle","key":"baudrexelpau","last":"Baudrexel","name":"Baudrexel, Isabelle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sejrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"fir