{"abstract":"The cortical mechanisms underlying the act of taking a step-including planning, execution, and modification - are not well understood. We hypothesized that oscillatory communication in a parieto-frontal and corticomuscular network is involved in the neural control of visually guided steps. We addressed this hypothesis using source reconstruction and lagged coherence analysis of electroencephalographic and electromyographic recordings during visually guided stepping and 2 control tasks that aimed to investigate processes involved in (i) preparing and taking a step and (ii) adjusting a step based on visual information. Steps were divided into planning, initiation, and execution phases. Taking a step was characterized by an upregulation of beta/gamma coherence within the parieto-frontal network during planning followed by a downregulation of alpha and beta/gamma coherence during initiation and execution. Step modification was characterized by bidirectional modulations of alpha and beta/gamma coherence in the parieto-frontal network during the phases leading up to step execution. Corticomuscular coherence did not exhibit task-related effects. We suggest that these task-related modulations indicate that the brain makes use of communication through coherence in the context of large-scale, whole-body movements, reflecting a process of flexibly fine-tuning inter-regional communication to achieve precision control during human stepping.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Beck, Mikkel Malling","West, Timothy O","Farmer, Simon F","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-497500"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Hospital for Neurology and Neurosurgery, London","University College London","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Coherence","EEG","EMG","Faculty of Science","Stepping","Walking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamics of cortical and corticomuscular connectivity during planning and execution of visually guided steps in humans","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/302544750/Spedden_et_al_Cerebral_Cortex_2022_bhac066_Coherence_during_stepping_Accepted_manuscript_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-497500","identifier":[{"id":"35238339","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7614067","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85136487824","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ae33d163-0d1f-4359-a370-60c1f829dc88"],"keyword":["Coherence","EEG","EMG","Faculty of Science","Stepping","Walking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D00E7D892BD6F4E4C4371D4250D06D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7614067/pdf/EMS144170.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/302544750/Spedden_et_al_Cerebral_Cortex_2022_bhac066_Coherence_during_stepping_Accepted_manuscript_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"national hospital for neurology and neurosurgery london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"National Hospital for Neurology and Neurosurgery, London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Meaghan Elizabeth","key":"speddenpau","last":"Spedden","locid":"e96259a8-d793-4586-903e-cbf824fa8021","name":"Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6854-2226","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Malling","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"a2e41a51-30c1-4e2a-b435-eefa69465a83","name":"Beck, Mikkel Malling","orcid":"0000-0002-8006-2580","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Timothy O","key":"westpau","last":"West","name":"West, Timothy O","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Simon F","key":"farmerpau","last":"Farmer","name":"Farmer, Simon F","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35238339"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cercor/bhac066","issn":["10473211","14602199"],"issn_org":["10473211"],"issue":"2","journal":"Cerebral Cortex","pages":"258-277","status":"p","title":"Cerebral Cortex","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136487824"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ae33d163-0d1f-4359-a370-60c1f829dc88"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamics of cortical and corticomuscular connectivity during planning and execution of visually guided steps in humans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-497500","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Hearing loss is a widespread problem while treatment is not always accessible, mainly because of the limited availability of hearing care professionals and clinics. In this work, part of the User-Operated Audiometry project, we investigate the acoustic environment of inexpensive non-sound-treated rooms that could be used for unsupervised audiometric testing. Measurements of 10 min of ambient noise were taken from 20 non-sound-treated rooms in libraries and private and public clinics, nine of which were measured twice. Ambient noise was compared against two traditional audiometric sound-treated rooms and Maximum Permissible Ambient noise levels by ISO 8231-1, while factoring for the attenuation by the DD450 circumaural headphones provided. In most non-sound-treated rooms, MPAs were violated only by transient sounds, while the floor-noise level was below MPAs. Non-sound-treated rooms’ ambient noise levels presented with much larger fluctuations compared to sound-treated rooms. Almost all violations occurred at low to mid-low frequencies. Our results suggest that large-scale implementation of user-operated audiometry outside traditional audiometric rooms is possible, at least under some realizable conditions. Circumaural headphones’ attenuation is probably a necessary condition for all cases. Depending on the room, an online system making decisions based on ambient noise might also be included in combination with active attenuation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sidiras, Christos","Nielsen, Jacob","Sørensen, Chris Bang","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","Pedersen, René Gyldenlund","Pedersen, Ellen Raben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587049"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sidiras, Christos"],"country":["Greece"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aristotle University of Thessaloniki"],"keyword":["Acoustic environment","Ambient noise","User operated"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ambient noise in candidate rooms for user operated audiometry","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/healthcare11060889","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-587049","identifier":[{"id":"36981546","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10048149","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85151132688","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-304f0529-782f-4d87-be58-1e012db7ed96"],"keyword":["acoustic environment","ambient noise","pure-tone audiometry","sound treated","user-operated"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B404E70DC39EFEC5F49A5B7194D8DF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/224372547/healthcare_11_00889_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/healthcare11060889","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gr","key":"aristotle university of thessaloniki","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aristotle University of Thessaloniki","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christos","key":"sidiraschristospau","last":"Sidiras","locid":"f7ef18da-9b53-4020-a432-01c656098a8f","name":"Sidiras, Christos","rank":1,"