{"abstract":"In the Arctic, the spatiotemporal variation of net methane uptake in upland soils depends on unresolved interactive controls between edaphic and microbial factors not yet included in current models, underpinning the uncertainty of upscaling the Arctic methane budget. Here we show that upland soils in Greenland are consistent methane sinks (−1.83 ± 0.19 nmol methane g−1 dw d−1) across a N-S (64–83 °N) pedoclimatic transect. We demonstrate that methane oxidizers abundance, soil pH, and available soil copper are important controls on the spatial variation in methane oxidation. We revised a soil biogeochemical model with a high-resolution land classification and meteorological data for Greenland and tested it against our methane uptake measurements. The model simulated well the magnitudes of observed methane uptake but not the spatial variation across all sites. This work provides novel insights into the controls of methane uptake, which are critical for the accuracy of methane budgets.","author_count":12,"contributors":["D'Imperio, Ludovica","Li, Bing-Bing","Tiedje, James M.","Oh, Youmi","Christiansen, Jesper Riis","Kepfer-Rojas, Sebastian","Westergaard-Nielsen, Andreas","Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","Holm, Peter Engelund","Wang, Peiyan","Ambus, Per Lennart","Elberling, Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721932"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anhui Agricultural University","Michigan State University","NOAA Earth System Research Laboratory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatial controls of methane uptake in upland soils across climatic and geological regions in greenland","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-023-01143-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721932","identifier":[{"id":"85178950607","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cf8db244-7208-43a5-a301-4967a7cfa032"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA966C4BD0A1B0AC2CB7680BA1FC748E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375549855/s43247_023_01143_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-023-01143-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Landscape Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"michigan state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Michigan State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"anhui agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Anhui Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"noaa earth system research laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NOAA Earth System Research Laboratory","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ludovica","key":"dimperiopau","last":"D’imperio","locid":"263da3e2-52fc-4757-9389-ef42bf5a0a49","name":"D'Imperio, Ludovica","name_org":"D’imperio, Ludovica","orcid":"0000-0002-6751-145X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Bing-Bing","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bing-Bing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"James M.","key":"tiedjepau","last":"Tiedje","name":"Tiedje, James M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Youmi","key":"ohpau","last":"Oh","name":"Oh, Youmi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Riis","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"54e64b51-5eca-4922-b031-9f0f6e1b85e4","name":"Christiansen, Jesper Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-3277-0734","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"kepferrojaspau","last":"Kepfer-Rojas","locid":"a679d0ef-f122-4f30-8cbe-b2cdd103c29e","name":"Kepfer-Rojas, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0002-1681-2877","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"westergaardnielsenpau","last":"Westergaard-nielsen","locid":"c0c1cbc7-3866-4719-87f1-78a224ee2e5a","name":"Westergaard-Nielsen, Andreas","name_org":"Westergaard-nielsen, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0003-1021-0530","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Koefoed","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"c196f0ea-2378-4bc3-bf49-2e64410cbabf","name":"Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","orcid":"0000-0001-7886-9708","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter E.","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"cc41fec2-bb93-4070-abe0-b4f120b183a8","name":"Holm, Peter Engelund","name_org":"Holm, Peter E.","orcid":"0000-0003-1233-0843","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peiyan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"589e8e24-b024-4c2a-ba26-3d2bc194db28","name":"Wang, Peiyan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"ambuspau","last":"Ambus","locid":"e3fc10b5-9fcd-494b-a3bc-dcfbede40f90","name":"Ambus, Per Lennart","name_org":"Ambus, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-7580-524X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"e12e4d80-dea0-424d-82bf-4dc019f65547","name":"Elberling, Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-6023-885X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s43247-023-01143-3","issn":["26624435"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications Earth and Environment","paperid":"461","status":"p","title":"Communications Earth and Environment","title_org":"Communications Earth & Environment","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178950607"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cf8db244-7208-43a5-a301-4967a7cfa032"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spatial controls of methane uptake in upland soils across climatic and geological regions in Greenland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721932","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Infectious diseases are major health care challenges globally and a prevalent cause of admission to emergency departments. Epidemiologic characteristics and outcomes based on population level data are limited. The Database of Community Acquired Infections in Eastern Denmark (DCAIED) 2018–2021 was established with the aim to explore and estimate the population characteristics, and outcomes of patients suffering from community acquired infections at the emergency departments in the Capital Region and the Zealand Region of Denmark using data from electronic medical records. Adult patients (≥18 years) presenting to the emergency department with suspected or confirmed infection are included in the cohort. Presence of sepsis and organ failure are assessed using modified criteria from the Third International Consensus Definitions for Sepsis and Septic Shock (Sepsis-3). During the inclusion period from January 2018 to January 2022, 2,241,652 adult emergency department visits have been registered. Of these, 451,825 were unique encounters of which 60,316 fulfilled criteria of suspected infection and 28,472 fulfilled sepsis criteria and 8,027 were defined as septic shock. The database covers the entire Capital and Zealand Region of Denmark with an uptake area of 2.6 million inhabitants and includes demographic, laboratory and outcome indicators, with complete follow-up. The database is well-suited for epidemiological research for future national and international collaborations.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Holler, Jon Gitz","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Engsig, Frederik Neess","Bestle, Morten H.","Lindegaard, Birgitte","Rasmussen, Jens Henning","Bundgaard, Henning","Nielsen, Finn Erland","Iversen, Kasper","Larsen, Jesper Juul","Holzknecht, Barbara Juliane","Boel, Jonas","Sivapalan, Pradeesh","Itenov, Theis Skovsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732349"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyw