+Business Media","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","volume":"280"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152550275"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-44803a3b-fa80-4b8d-b9f6-0a978ad8540c","au-95b8f6c9-e92c-4b83-aa93-07baa994c6e9","ku-d4c75388-e478-4351-94b6-607fac95b090","sdu-06657385-42cc-4ef0-acec-3a572de5226c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Epidemiology, outcomes, and prognostic factors in submandibular gland carcinomas : a national DAHANCA study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-094.00-685629","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Many patients with heart failure and a reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF) with an indication for cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT) are also eligible for prophylactic implantation of an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD) for the prevention of sudden cardiac death (SCD). However, it is unclear whether patients who are eligible for CRT should routinely receive an ICD. In addition, the risk of SCD has declined in patients with HFrEF, a finding that is consistent with a cumulative benefit of disease-modifying pharmacological therapies and CRT on this cause of death.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Butt, Jawad H.","Yafasova, Adelina","Doi, Seiko N.","Nielsen, Jens C.","Haarbo, Jens","Eiskjær, Hans","Brandes, Axel","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Gustafsson, Finn","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper H.","Høfsten, Dan E.","Videbæk, Lars","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Pehrson, Steen","Thune, Jens Jakob","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S04-094.74-697721"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Butt, Jawad H."],"keyword":["Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Clinical trial","Death Sudden Cardiac","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark","Follow Up Studies","Heart Failure Systolic therapy","Heart Failure therapy","Heart failure","Humans","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Mortality","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implantable cardioverter defibrillator in patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure with and without cardiac resynchronization therapy exte