,"pmid":["37812653"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.123.065560","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"issue":"15","journal":"Circulation","pages":"1179-1181","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"148"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175170609"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-662efac9-32f3-409f-b057-c3aef2aff8c4","au-597ae34c-8048-4377-946d-e7a9e2d21475","ku-36abd17b-9245-4835-b224-433138ed78b4","sdu-65bd66b5-19ab-4039-8695-f90c5359f443"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillator in Patients With Nonischemic Systolic Heart Failure With and Without Cardiac Resynchronization Therapy: Extended Follow-Up Study of the DANISH Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-094.74-697721","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Active acromegaly is subject to sex differences in growth hormone (GH) and Insulin like growth factor 1 (IGF-I) patterns as well as clinical features but whether this also pertains to controlled disease is unclear. DESIGN: In a cross-sectional, multi-centre study, 84 patients with acromegaly (F = 43, M = 41), who were considered controlled after surgery alone (n = 23) or during continued somatostatin receptor ligand (SRL) treatment (n = 61), were examined. METHODS: Serum concentrations of GH, insulin, glucose and free fatty acid (FFA) were measured during an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) together with baseline serum IGF-I and completion of two HR-Qol questionnaires (acromegaly quality of life questionnaire [AcroQol] and Patient-assessed Acromegaly Symptom Questionnaire [PASQ]). RESULTS: The mean age at the time of the study was 57 (±1.1) years and the majority of females (were postmenopausal. Females had significantly higher fasting GH but comparable IGF-I standard deviation scores (SDS). Using fasting GH < 1.0 µg/L as cut off, disease control was less prevalent in females (F: 56% vs. M: 83%, p = .007) whereas a comparable figure was observed using IGF-I SDS < 2 (F:79% vs. M:76%, p = .71). Compared with males, female patients showed impaired AcroQol physical score (p = .05), higher fasting FFA (p = .03) and insulin concentrations during the OGTT (p = .04). CONCLUSION: In patients with acromegaly considered controlled, postmenopausal females exhibited higher GH levels than males despite comparable IGF-I levels, which also translated into impaired metabolic health and well-being. Our findings point to the relevance of including GH measurements in the assessment of disease control and suggest that disease-specific sex differences prevail after treatment.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dal, Jakob","Rosendal, Christian Alexander Helleshøj","Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Andersen, Marianne S.","Klose, Marianne","Feltoft, Claus","Heck, Ansgar","Nielsen, Eigil Husted","Jørgensen, Jens O. L."],"cuid":["S04-099.96-003951"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dal, Jakob"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo University Hospital","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Acromegaly","Age","Cross Sectional Studies","FFA","Female","GH","Humans","IGF I","Insulin","Insulin Like Growth Factor I","Male","Pituitary adenoma","Quality of Life","Sex","Sex Characteristics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetic Center Northjutland"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex difference in patients with controlled acromegaly a multicentre survey","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cen.14750","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Jakob Dal: unrestricted research grants and lecture fee from Pfizer and IPSEN, Jens O L Jørgensen: Grants and lecture fees from Pfizer, IPSEN and Novartis, Claus feldttoft: Lecture fee from Bristol Myers Squibb, UFR: Grants, advisory board honoraria and lecture fees from Pfizer, IPSEN and Novartis, advisory board honoraria from Recordati, Ansgar Heck: speaker fees from Ipsen and Recordati."],"id":"S04-099.96-003951","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10083986","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85129330780","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35474467","type":"pmi