wed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131514543"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aaa577f7-578d-4cff-99d0-4ca8c1116219","sdu-125a3d3b-ac35-4f47-b521-0c3a33d9c8cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Protocol for an individual patient data meta-analysis on blood pressure targets after cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045201","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) is a leading cause of death. Even if successfully resuscitated, mortality remains high due to ischemic and reperfusion injury (I/R). The oxygen deprivation leads to a metabolic derangement amplified upon reperfusion resulting in an uncontrolled generation of reactive oxygen species in the mitochondria triggering cell death mechanisms. The understanding of I/R injury in humans following OHCA remains sparse, with no existing treatment to attenuate the reperfusion injury. Aim: To describe metabolic derangement in patients following resuscitated OHCA. Methods: Plasma from consecutive resuscitated unconscious OHCA patients drawn at hospital admission were analyzed using ultra-performance-liquid-mass-spectrometry. Sixty-one metabolites were prespecified for quantification and studied. Results: In total, 163 patients were included, of which 143 (88%) were men, and the median age was 62 years (53–68). All measured metabolites from the tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle were significantly higher in non-survivors vs. survivors (180-days survival). Hierarchical clustering identified four clusters (A-D) of patients with distinct metabolic profiles. Cluster A and B had higher levels of TCA metabolites, amino acids and acylcarnitine species compared to C and D. The mortality was significantly higher in cluster A and B (A:62% and B:59% vs. C:21 % and D:24%, p < 0.001). Cluster A and B had longer time to return of spontaneous circulation (A:33 min (21–43), B:27 min (24–35), C:18 min (13–28), and D:18 min (12–25), p < 0.001). Conclusion: Circulating levels of metabolites from the TCA cycle best described the variance between survivors and non-survivors. Four different metabolic phenotypes with significantly different mortality were identified.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Paulin Beske, Rasmus","Henriksen, Hanne H.","Obling, Laust","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Nielsen, Niklas","Johansson, Pär I.","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-741724"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Paulin Beske, Rasmus"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Lipid metabolites","Metabolomics","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Tricarboxylic acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeted plasma metabolomics in resuscitated comatose out of hospital cardiac arrest patients","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2022.06.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-741724","identifier":[{"id":"85133399006","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35753507","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-22fc9b46-b8bc-4f0a-9896-fdc2035364da","ku-a7fc15cc-4184-4d9e-99f8-33654efa1307"],"keyword":["Lipid metabolites","Metabolomics","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Tricarboxylic acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A9B22663DAB7BA91F5CF4F7A1BBE175D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2022.06.010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323996831/1_s2.0_S0300957222005731_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-H