null,"first":"M.N.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"bbd320a7-9c17-4062-a6d9-76a1bbed24bf","name":"Johansen, Martin Berg","name_org":"Johansen, M.N.","orcid":"0000-0001-9790-0985","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.S.","key":"rathleffpau","last":"Rathleff","locid":"90c1260f-4cd4-497f-88ca-a98f412bbe7b","name":"Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","name_org":"Rathleff, M.S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1173-0335","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","name_org":"Arendt-Nielsen, L.","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","name_org":"Rasmussen, S.","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Thorgaard","key":"skoupau","last":"Skou","locid":"656a59cf-32bc-4190-b072-4adf47d954c1","name":"Skou, Søren Thorgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.joca.2022.02.252","issn":["10634584","15229653"],"issn_org":["10634584"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","publisher":"W. B. Saunders Company","status":"p","title":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-681953ed-2b6d-4aec-a65e-6ae2ac1bd4e7","sdu-26e1c408-e628-43b8-b62e-ee1cc329a0fc","sdu-39d91c69-92c1-481e-ab97-416298e71424"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"5-year follow-up of patients with knee osteoarthritis receiving non-surgical treatment: Results from a randomized controlled trial.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-090.06-005047","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Identification of patients with nonischemic cardiomyopathy who may benefit from prophylactic implantation of a cardioverter-defibrillator. We hypothesized that periodic repolarization dynamics (PRD), a marker of repolarization instability associated with sympathetic activity, could be used to identify patients who will benefit from prophylactic implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD) implantation. Methods: We performed a post hoc analysis of DANISH (Danish ICD Study in Patients With Dilated Cardiomyopathy), in which patients with nonischemic cardiomyopathy, left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤35%, and elevated NT-proBNP (N-terminal probrain natriuretic peptides) were randomized to ICD implantation or control group. Patients were included in the PRD substudy if they had a 24-hour Holter monitor recording at baseline with technically acceptable ECG signals during the night hours (00:00-06:00). PRD was assessed using wavelet analysis according to previously validated methods. The primary end point was all-cause mortality. Cox regression models were adjusted for age, sex, NT-proBNP, estimated glomerular filtration rate, LVEF, atrial fibrillation, ventricular pacing, diabetes, cardiac resynchronization therapy, and mean heart rate. We proposed PRD ≥10 deg 2as an exploratory cut-off value for ICD implantation. Results: A total of 748 of the 1116 patients in DANISH qualified for the PRD substudy. During a mean follow-up period of 5.1±2.0 years, 82 of 385 patients died in the ICD group and 85 of 363 patients died in the control group (P=0.40). In Cox regression analysis, PRD was independently associated with mortality (hazard ratio [HR], 1.28 [95% CI, 1.09-1.50] per SD increase; P=0.003). PRD was significantly associated with mortality in the control group (HR, 1.51 [95% CI, 1.25-1.81]; P<0.001) but not in the ICD group (HR, 1.04 [95% CI, 0.83-1.54]; P=0.71). There was a significant interaction between PRD and the effect of ICD implantation on mortality (P=0.008), with patients with higher PRD having greater benefit in terms of mortality reduction. ICD implantation was associated with an absolute mortality reduction of 17.5% in the 280 patients with PRD ≥10 deg 2(HR, 0.54 [95% CI, 0.34-0.84]; P=0.006; number needed to treat=6), but not in the 468 patients with PRD <10 deg 2(HR, 1.17 [95% CI, 0.77-1.78]; P=0.46; P for interaction=0.01). Conclusions: Increased PRD identified patients with nonischemic cardiomyopathy in whom prophylactic ICD implantation led to significant mortality reduction.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Boas, Rune","Sappler, Nikolay","von Stülpnagel, Lukas","Klemm, Mathias","Dixen, Ulrik","Thune, Jens Jakob","Pehrson, Steen","Køber, Lars","Nielsen, Jens C.","Videbæk, Lars","Haarbo, Jens","Korup, Eva","Bruun, Niels Eske","Brandes, Axel","Eiskjær, Hans","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Philbert, Berit T.","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","Bauer, Axel","Rizas, Konstantinos D"],"cuid":["S04-090.45-004649"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Boas, Rune"],"country":["Austria","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","Innsbruck Medical University","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","University of Innsbruck"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Cardiomyopathies diagnosis","Death Sudden","Death Sudden Cardiac prevention control","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Risk","Stroke Volume","Ventricular Function Left","cardiomyopath","ies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"periodic repolarization dynamics identifies icd responders in non ischemic cardiomyopathy a danish substudy","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85125965728","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-090.45-004649","identifier":[{"id":"85125965728","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34889650","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-5fb2c356-5210-4d73-af5d-8a45efaeebfa","au-574b8331-3f0e-4f61-8611-4ae5c33ce9b4","ku-fb985b8a-d5cc-4036-9564-7fc213ed682c","sdu-21b7a4d6-8c33-4edc-aaf7-975c57b4fe48"],"keyword":["Atrial Fibrillation","Cardiomyopathies/diagnosis","Death, Sudden, Cardiac/prevention & control","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Stroke Volume","Ventricular Function, Left","cardiomyopath","death, sudden","defibrillators, implantable","ies","risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-0CDC869C119906DB5E376EAE4B2379ED"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"innsbruck medical university","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Innsbruck Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"german centre for cardiovascular research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Centre for Cardiovascular Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian