{"abstract":"The aim of this study is to evaluate the adequacy of treatment, and to identify factors influencing treatment of hypothyroidism. Patients newly diagnosed with overt hypothyroidism ( n=345) were identified via a register linked to a laboratory database. In selected periods with staff available, 165 patients were invited, and 113 (68.5 %) accepted participating in a comprehensive program including blood tests and completion of questionnaires. We performed a longitudinal follow-up on thyroid function tests 10 years after the diagnosis. Time to reach a serum TSH level of 0.2-10 mU/L (termed as clinically acceptable) and biochemical normalization (TSH: 0.2-5.0 mU/L), respectively, were analyzed using Kaplan Meier survival analysis. Predictors for longer duration to reach the normal TSH range were identified using cox proportional hazards regression. Only 67.7 % of the patients were in the euthyroid range on the long term after diagnosis of overt hypothyroidism (2 years: 59.4 %; 10 years: 67.7 %). Median time to the first normal TSH was 8.9 months (95 % CI: 7.6-10.2 months). The factors associated with longer duration until normalization of TSH after multivariate analysis were age (HR 0.79 per 10 years; 95 % CI: 0.66-0.94; P = <0.01), smoking (HR 0.47; 95 % CI: 0.26-0.83; P = <0.01), serum TSH at diagnosis (HR 0.96 per 10 mU/L; 95 % CI: 0.93-0.99; P = 0.02) and BMI (HR 0.96 per kg/m 2; 95 % CI: 0.91-0.99; P = 0.03). A considerable number of hypothyroid patients remained inadequately treated. When treating hypothyroid patients, special attention should be addressed to those patients who never or lately obtain euthyroid status.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Julie Lindgard","Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","Pedersen, Inge Bülow","Carlé, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-098902"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Julie Lindgard"],"keyword":["Hypothyroidism","Overt hypothyroidism","Population based study","Treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence and predictors of adequate treatment of overt hypothyroidism a population based study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17179/excli2021-4291","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-098902","identifier":[{"id":"85127700488","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35145368","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a85d53d2-6abc-4ea6-9ecc-51393e7777f0"],"keyword":["Treatment","hypothyroidism","overt hypothyroidism","population-based study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F5B7CD2BE3E6CDAFC14DE136077554F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17179/excli2021-4291","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/460203045/Nielsen_et_al._2022_._PREVALENCE_AND_PREDICTORS_OF_ADEQUATE_TREATMENT_OF_OVERT_HYPOTHYROIDISM_A_POPULATION_BASED_STUDY.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, The Department of Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Lindgard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a834f5c1-1548-4f74-afc9-6088ffd316f7","name":"Nielsen, Julie Lindgard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"karmisholtpau","last":"Karmisholt","locid":"410922f0-294c-4d56-b758-b30fffef3a49","name":"Karmisholt, Jesper Scott","name_org":"Karmisholt, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge Bulow","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0b17bcdf-70d8-459d-a188-1d38f12a4664","name":"Pedersen, Inge Bülow","name_org":"Pedersen, Inge Bulow","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"carlepau","last":"Carle","locid":"302be08f-b6cb-46ad-9253-645a50ba4072","name":"Carlé, Allan","name_org":"Carle, Allan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35145368"],"pub":{"doi":"10.17179/excli2021-4291","issn":["16112156"],"journal":"EXCLI Journal","pages":"104-116","publisher":"Leibniz Research Centre for Working Environment and Human Factors","status":"p","title":"EXCLI Journal","title_org":"EXCLI journal","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127700488"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a85d53d2-6abc-4ea6-9ecc-51393e7777f0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Prevalence and predictors of adequate treatment of overt hypothyroidism – a population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-098902","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This study compared metabolic power (MP) and time trial (TT) running performance between Adidas Adizero Adios (AAA) and Nike VaporFly 4% (NVP). Thirty-seven runners completed three laboratory sessions and two field sessions (n=30). After familiarization (visit 1), participants completed eight 6-min treadmill running bouts (four with each shoe, counterbalanced) at their preferred pace, and MP was assessed using indirect calorimetry (visits 2 and 3). During visits 4 and 5, participants completed two outdoor TTs (~3.5 km) in NVP and AAA (counterbalanced). Compared with AAA, NVP exhibited superior MP (NVP: median=13.88 (Q1-Q3=12.90-15.08 W/kg; AAA: median=14.08 (Q1-Q3=13.12-15.44 W/kg; z=-4.81, p<.001, effect size=.56) and TT (NVP=793±98 s; AAA=802±100 s, p=.001; effect size=.09). However, there was no relationship between changes in MP and changes in TT between shoes (r=.151 p=.425, 95% confidence interval=[-.22;.48]). Our results demonstrate that NVP, compared with AAA, improves MP and TT in recreational runners. The lack of correlation between changes in MP and TT indicates that factors other than improved MP contribute to faster short-distance TT with NVP.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders","Franch, Jesper","Heyde, Christian","de Zee, Mark","Kersting, Uwe G.","Larsen, Ryan Godsk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116315"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Ryan Godsk"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["Adidas Group","All Global Affiliations","German Sport University Cologne"],"keyword":["Biomechanical Phenomena","Carbon","Exercise Test","Humans","Oxygen Consumption","Running","Running economy","Running performance","Running shoes","Shoes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carbon plate shoes improve metabolic power and performance in recreational runners","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85130567673&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-116315","identifier":[{"id":"85130567673","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35523201","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e3fa9d84-5912-45bd-bb89-63e07b791319"],"keyword":["Biomechanical Phenomena","Carbon","Exercise Test","Humans","Oxygen Consumption","Running","Shoes","adidas adios","nike vaporfly","running economy","running performance","running shoes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C39EC757148001409F637CDB9CE8711A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"adidas group","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Adidas Group","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german sport university cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Sport University Cologne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"56136ff8-3354-4fe5-9d96-ab0a3b6e4c6b","name":"Nielsen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"franchpau","last":"Franch","locid":"9f5ebab9-2344-4c4d-aae9-7dc7d0dfa5fd","name":"Franch, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8668-2385","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"heydepau","last":"Heyde","name":"Heyde, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"dezeepau","last":"de Zee","locid":"25caa881-65a0-4f66-9d65-b760fc4787b3","name":"de Zee, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0584-271X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uwe","key":"kerstingpau","last":"Kersting","locid":"8faf2c1f-3363-4159-9cff-910f59b77406","name":"Kersting, Uwe G.","name_org":"Kersting, Uwe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryan Godsk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"86d31e60-1de1-4284-a688-596cc17dca1c","name":"Larsen, Ryan Godsk","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-1453","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35523201"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1055/a-1776-7986","issn":["01724622","0943917X"],"issn_org":["01724622"],"issue":"9","journal":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"804-810","publisher":"Georg Thieme Verlag","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130567673"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e3fa9d84-5912-45bd-bb89-63e07b791319"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Carbon Plate Shoes Improve Metabolic Power and Performance in Recreational Runners","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-116315","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This article presents an evaluation of the performance of two different approaches for beamforming (BF) in a fifth generation (5G) handset, based on measured channels from a dual-polarized transmitter (Tx) to a mockup handset with a seven-element receiver (Rx) array. The measurements at 21.5 GHz include both small-scale and large-scale channel changes and were conducted for different users holding the mockup at different locations in an indoor corridor environment. The unique measurements enable novel results based on the statistics of the power achieved with BF, using channel state information (CSI) measured at a 90 Hz rate, and both when using beam scanning (BS) and the equal gain combining (EGC) reference case. For the case of ideal CSI knowledge, BF gains of up to about 18 dB were found. However, when the density of the angle scanning grid is reduced and the CSI is delayed to realistic values, the average performance decreases by 8 dB. More results are given in the article.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-119241"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antenna arrays","Antenna measurements","Beamforming","Cellular communications","Channel sounding","Directive antennas","Gain","Loss measurement","Power measurement","Telephone sets","User Impact","radio propagation measurements"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance of beamforming for a handheld device in measured 000000000021 000000000005 ghz indoor channels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/481222629/Nielsen_etal_Perf_of_Beamforming_TAP_2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-119241","identifier":[{"id":"85127505117","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ee04e0b0-efd9-4227-aa3f-d69596827e94"],"keyword":["Antenna arrays","Antenna measurements","Beamforming (BF)","Cellular communications","Directive antennas","Gain","Loss measurement","Power measurement","Telephone sets","beamforming","channel sounding","mm-wave propagation","radio propagation measurements","user impact"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1268326600D1A3D2C9B54D648DB79BA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/481222629/Nielsen_etal_Perf_of_Beamforming_TAP_2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Wireless propagation and Over the Air testing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert Frølund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tap.2022.3161567","issn":["0018926X"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","pages":"5725-5735","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127505117"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ee04e0b0-efd9-4227-aa3f-d69596827e94"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Performance of Beamforming for a Handheld Device in Measured 21.5 GHz Indoor Channels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-119241","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Albæk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146777"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the folketing s role and tasks","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-146777","ids":["au-1e6fb215-ae7c-4341-a997-b9ba44725b5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AA3297E6C451476AF061B4306D54C171"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Albæk","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d2f53b93-a268-48a0-9a4e-cfc74b91705e","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Albæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4528-2884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Aagaard","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Peter Aagaard","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpedh","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788741277981"],"pages":"211-236","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Insights into Danish Constitutional and Administrative Law","title":"Public Law"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1e6fb215-ae7c-4341-a997-b9ba44725b5f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Folketing's Role and Tasks","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146777","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The rapid life cycle of most insects allows for the direct comparison of simulated and realised genetic gain from insect breeding schemes, enabling real-time optimisation of the breeding scheme design. However, rearing and maintenance of insects gives rise to major challenges due to specific dietary and environmental requirements, complex life cycles and reproductive patterns and this adds complexity to all aspects of the breeding plan implementation. We have developed an experimental design for large-scale individual phenotyping and tracing pedigree records and applied this to estimate genetic parameters for larval size and egg-to-adult development time using the housefly (Musca domestica) as a model species. These parameters contribute valuable information on the potentials for genetic improvement in this species and the methods and results presented can be used more generally in the process of insect breeding scheme implementation and optimisation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang","Laursen, Stine Frey","Bahrndorff, S.","Kargo, Morten","Kristensen, T.N.","Sahana, Goutam","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Nielsen, Hanne Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198818"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-08","place":"Rotterdam, nl","start":"2022-07-03","title":"World Congress on Genetics Applied to Livestock Production","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards selective breeding in insects estimating genetic parameters with individual level phenotypes and pedigree","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.wageningenacademic.com/pb-assets/wagen/WCGALP2022/53_010.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-198818","ids":["au-79788609-dcd6-4a74-9dee-1402435b626c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0834A1B64A74E4E22CB756CBC1D150AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.wageningenacademic.com/pb-assets/wagen/WCGALP2022/53_010.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University (AAU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura Skrubbeltrang","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5fd29cd8-360a-461a-b205-b81e0ac76c23","name":"Hansen, Laura Skrubbeltrang","orcid":"0000-0002-4270-6365","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Frey","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Stine Frey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"bahrndorffpau","last":"Bahrndorff","name":"Bahrndorff, S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"kargopau","last":"Kargo","locid":"a3522626-c405-4303-9d68-3e5f12599c31","name":"Kargo, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T.N.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, T.N.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Goutam","key":"sahanapau","last":"Sahana","locid":"bb375f9c-4103-4460-80cc-ec53d0cd03d5","name":"Sahana, Goutam","orcid":"0000-0001-7608-7577","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Marie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4557ab69-42a2-40e1-9c55-66bb9f9aad50","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Wageningen Academic Publishers","status":"p","title":"WCGALP 2022 Programme book"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-79788609-dcd6-4a74-9dee-1402435b626c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Towards selective breeding in insects – estimating genetic parameters with individual-level phenotypes and pedigree","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-198818","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Isolated tricuspid valve (TV) surgery is rarely performed and has been associated with high mortality and morbidity. The aim of this study was to describe the clinical outcome and functional capacity following isolated TV surgery in contemporary practice. METHODS: We conducted a retrospective cohort study including all patients who underwent isolated TV surgery at our institution from 2013 to 2019. Our cohort was identified using the Western Denmark Heart Registry. Postoperative outcomes were evaluated using patients' medical records. The clinical and echocardiographic status was reported for patients who survived beyond 1 year. RESULTS: We included 43 patients [mean age 65.2 ± 13.8, median European System for Cardiac Operative Risk Evaluation II 1.8 (interquartile range 2.0)]. Twelve (27.9%) had prior cardiac surgery. Up to 90-day follow-up, no patient died and major morbidity was limited to 4 patients (9.3%) requiring pacemaker implantation and 1 patient requiring 2 reoperations. Within 1 year, 4 patients (9.3%) died. Nine patients (20.1%) required single readmission for cardiac reasons during the median follow-up of 38.4 months (interquartile range 30.9 months). All patients who survived beyond 1 year (n = 39) completed clinical follow-up. At follow-up, 38/39 (97.4%) patients were New York Heart Association I or II compared to 12/39 (30.8%) preoperatively (P = 0.001). The presence of oedema and intensity of diuretic treatment were significantly reduced (P = 0.005 and P = 0.008, respectively). Echocardiographic follow-up showed significant improvement of TV dysfunction in all patients. CONCLUSIONS: Our results suggest that isolated TV surgery can be performed safely and greatly improve patients' functional status. Our findings support the importance of optimal surgical timing and patient selection.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Weiss, Thomas","Villadsen, Peter Ryom","Jensen, Jesper Khedri","Lehnert, Per","Nielsen, Per Hostrup","Modrau, Ivy Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218506"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Modrau, Ivy Susanne"],"keyword":["Outcome","Tricuspid regurgitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcomes of isolated tricuspid valve surgery in contemporary practice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85135376090","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-218506","identifier":[{"id":"000756760800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85135376090","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35138382","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9c9380b3-8ecd-4b80-90c7-7f9f8e6df86c"],"keyword":["Outcome","Tricuspid regurgitation","Tricuspid valve repair","Tricuspid valve replacement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-94F143B1E1224EDA4C351CB339045082"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"weisspau","last":"Weiss","locid":"09cd2e5b-5108-4366-96d5-ea90b3f6d570","name":"Weiss, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Ryom","key":"villadsenpau","last":"Villadsen","locid":"3a687d56-3b20-49d8-989b-f03b1af5ff2e","name":"Villadsen, Peter Ryom","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Khedri","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"766add66-79cf-4c28-9035-0f267ff5f494","name":"Jensen, Jesper Khedri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"lehnertpau","last":"Lehnert","locid":"db34a568-9d8f-4174-bcf9-1e948e6f5db8","name":"Lehnert, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Hostrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f7d1db00-47c2-4afc-b82c-805fa4372e91","name":"Nielsen, Per Hostrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivy Susanne","key":"modraupau","last":"Modrau","locid":"00ab336f-ed78-4c39-ba27-ad2be0fc345f","name":"Modrau, Ivy Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-2812-6591","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35138382"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ejcts/ezac077","issn":["10107940","1873734X"],"issn_org":["10107940"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","paperid":"ezac077","publisher":"European Association for Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135376090"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c9380b3-8ecd-4b80-90c7-7f9f8e6df86c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Outcomes of isolated tricuspid valve surgery in contemporary practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-218506","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Long-term weight loss can reduce the risk of type 2 diabetes for people living with obesity and reduce complications for patients diagnosed with type 2 diabetes. We investigated whether a telehealth lifestyle-coaching program (Liva) leads to long-term (24 months) weight loss compared to usual care. In a randomized controlled trial, n = 340 participants living with obesity with or without type 2 diabetes were enrolled and randomized via an automated computer algorithm to an intervention group (n = 200) or to a control group (n = 140). The telehealth lifestyle-coaching program comprised of an initial one-hour face-to-face motivational interview followed by asynchronous telehealth coaching. The behavioural change techniques used were enabled by individual live monitoring. The primary outcome was a change in body weight from baseline to 24 months. Data were assessed for n = 136 participants (40%), n = 81 from the intervention group and n = 55 from the control group, who completed the 24-month follow-up. After 24 months mean body weight and body mass index were reduced significantly for completers in both groups, but almost twice as much was registered for those in the intervention group which was not significant between groups −4.4 (CI −6.1; −2.8) kg versus −2.5 (CI −3.9; −1.1) kg, P = 0.101. Haemoglobin A1c was significantly reduced in the intervention group −3.1 (CI −5.0; −1.2) mmol/mol, but not in the control group −0.2 (CI −2.4; −2.0) mmol/mol without a significant between group difference (P = 0.223). Low completion was partly due to coronavirus disease 2019. Telehealth lifestyle coaching improve long-term weight loss (> 24 months) for obese people with and without type 2 diabetes compared to usual care.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Hesseldal, Laura","Bastholm Olesen, Thomas","Olsen, Michael Hecht","Jakobsen, Pernille Ravn","Laursen, Ditte Hjorth","Lauridsen, Jørgen T.","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Brandt, Carl Joakim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-254307"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coaching","Obesity","Primary care","Randomized Controlled Trial","Telehealth","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term weight loss in a 000000000024 month primary care anchored telehealth lifestyle coaching program randomized controlled trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85141728805","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-254307","identifier":[{"id":"85141728805","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-daee50f1-2b38-44e5-80a3-7fda9ca81fb4"],"keyword":["Obesity","coaching","primary care","randomized controlled trial","telehealth","weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-7-934CFBAFC98CF948A594E9CF360A51C6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Pediatric Department, Holbæk Hospital, Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeanette Reffstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"4a0d4268-48b4-4669-94a0-9b554f559330","name":"Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"hesseldalpau","last":"Hesseldal","name":"Hesseldal, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"bastholmolesenpau","last":"Bastholm Olesen","name":"Bastholm Olesen, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Hecht","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Michael Hecht","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Ravn","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Pernille Ravn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Hjorth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Ditte Hjorth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen T.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, Jørgen T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl Joakim","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Carl Joakim","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1357633x22112341","issn":["1357633X","17581109"],"issn_org":["1357633X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Telemedicine and Telecare","pages":"764-770","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Telemedicine and Telecare","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141728805"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-daee50f1-2b38-44e5-80a3-7fda9ca81fb4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long-term Weight Loss in a 24 Month Primary Care-Anchored Telehealth Lifestyle Coaching Program : Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254307","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Accurate position measurements are extremely valuable in the shipping industry for various reasons such as safety (collision avoidance), security (situational awareness), fuel-saving (weather identification), punctuality (route prediction), etc. Although GNSS (Global Navigation Satellite System) receivers installed on-board the ships are proven to be highly accurate, the data logging process may occasionally be problematic, mainly due to the complexity of the measurements and the decimal precision that is required. Data were collected from 3 years of operations of 228 Maersk Line container vessels and an analysis reveals that there is a substantial amount (≈20%) of historical position measurements sent to shore that does not reflect reality. In the study, the sources of the faulty logged position measurements are categorized and an interpolation methodology is proposed to validate and correct them by using AIS (Automatic Identification System) data.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ikonomakis, Angelos","Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","Holst, Klaus Kähler","Dietz, Jesper","Galeazzi, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-326432"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ikonomakis, Angelos"],"keyword":["Measurement error","Sensor accuracy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation and correction of auto logged position measurements","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.commtr.2022.100051","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-326432","identifier":[{"id":"85132269027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4987fb7a-d5e2-4046-94b7-7c3b788c784e"],"keyword":["AIS coordinates","GNSS coordinates","Linear interpolation","Measurement error","Sensor accuracy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3AE8C1D536AD3B1AD9D5FD4C0E0F0922"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.commtr.2022.100051","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/271651640/ikonomakis2022_a_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"a p moller maersk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-MAE","l3nl":"A.P. Møller – Mærsk","l3nn":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","namevar":["Maersk R&D"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-MAE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Angelos","key":"ikonomakispau","last":"Ikonomakis","locid":"92af5f16-83f5-4a32-af27-6a70b500f2dd","name":"Ikonomakis, Angelos","orcid":"0000-0002-1571-8782","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus Kähler","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Klaus Kähler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzipau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.commtr.2022.100051","issn":["27724247"],"journal":"Communications in Transportation Research","paperid":"100051","publisher":"Tsinghua University Press","status":"p","title":"Communications in Transportation Research","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132269027"],"search":{"DAF":["A.P. Møller – Mærsk","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4987fb7a-d5e2-4046-94b7-7c3b788c784e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Validation and correction of auto-logged position measurements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-326432","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Energy transfer from confined fast ions will play a key role in maintaining the core plasma at fusion-relevant conditions in future fusion devices such as ITER. The dynamics of such ions is experimentally well characterized in low-density plasmas, owing to good fast-ion coverage with diagnostics such as fast-ion D-α spectroscopy (FIDA), neutron/γ-ray spectrometry, and collective Thomson scattering. In contrast, this applies much less to highdensity discharges, in which the relevant diagnostic performance is more limited by the shorter slowing-down time of energetic particles, the reduced neutral beam (NBI) penetration, and the significantly increased Bremsstrahlung emission. Collective Thomson scattering (CTS) is less hampered by the latter of these limitations and will be the main diagnostic for measuring confined fast ions in ITER across their full energy range [1, 2, 3]. Although ITER will achieve a combination of high density n and low core collisionality ν ∝ nT −3/2 that cannot be accessed in present devices, it remains relevant to experimentally test predictions of energetic-ion dynamics at high density as a step in preparing for ITER operation. Here we present the first CTS measurements of fast-ion dynamics in ASDEX Upgrade (AUG) performed at a local density of ne ≈ 9×1019 m−3 , i.e., similar to projections for the high-density ITER baseline scenario [4].","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Verdier, T.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Kappatou, A.","Jensen, T.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Salewski, Mirko","Garcia-Muñoz, M.","Vallar, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334564"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-01","place":"Online","start":"2022-06-27","title":"48<sup>th</sup> EPS Conference on Plasma Physics","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","University of Seville"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast ion dynamics at iter relevant densities in asdex upgrade measured with collective thomson scattering","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-334564","ids":["dtu-649ab15d-45b7-4f65-8baa-15b2cbba5aa9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7E84C993EA977EB3DC283BF764A61F84"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T.","key":"verdierpau","last":"Verdier","locid":"b03e7c15-4650-45b0-b64e-03ceabe0c7ff","name":"Verdier, T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S.K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"kappatoupau","last":"Kappatou","name":"Kappatou, A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e840242d-2592-40b7-bc0b-02995c8fe6ba","name":"Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9801-1530","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.B.","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","name_org":"Korsholm, S.B.","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"garciamuñozpau","last":"Garcia-Muñoz","name":"Garcia-Muñoz, M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"vallarpau","last":"Vallar","name":"Vallar, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-649ab15d-45b7-4f65-8baa-15b2cbba5aa9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fast-ion dynamics at ITER-relevant densities in ASDEX Upgrade measured with collective Thomson scattering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334564","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"An overview of recent results obtained at the tokamak ASDEX Upgrade (AUG) is given. A work flow for predictive profile modelling of AUG discharges was established which is able to reproduce experimental H-mode plasma profiles based on engineering parameters only. In the plasma center, theoretical predictions on plasma current redistribution by a dynamo effect were confirmed experimentally. For core transport, the stabilizing effect of fast ion distributions on turbulent transport is shown to be important to explain the core isotope effect and improves the description of hollow low-Z impurity profiles. The L–H power threshold of hydrogen plasmas is not affected by small helium admixtures and it increases continuously from the deuterium to the hydrogen level when the hydrogen concentration is raised from 0 to 100%. One focus of recent campaigns was the search for a fusion relevant integrated plasma scenario without large edge localised modes (ELMs). Results from six different ELM-free confinement regimes are compared with respect to reactor relevance: ELM suppression by magnetic perturbation coils could be attributed to toroidally asymmetric turbulent fluctuations in the vicinity of the separatrix. Stable improved confinement mode plasma phases with a detached inner divertor were obtained using a feedback control of the plasma β. The enhanced Dα H-mode regime was extended to higher heating power by feedback controlled radiative cooling with argon. The quasi-coherent exhaust regime was developed into an integrated scenario at high heating power and energy confinement, with a detached divertor and without large ELMs. Small ELMs close to the separatrix lead to peeling-ballooning stability and quasi continuous power exhaust. Helium beam density fluctuation measurements confirm that transport close to the separatrix is important to achieve the different ELM-free regimes. Based on separatrix plasma parameters and interchange-drift-Alfvén turbulence, an analytic model was derived that reproduces the experimentally found important operational boundaries of the density limit and between L- and H-mode confinement. Feedback control for the X-point radiator (XPR) position was established as an important element for divertor detachment control. Stable and detached ELM-free phases with H-mode confinement quality were obtained when the XPR was moved 10 cm above the X-point. Investigations of the plasma in the future flexible snow-flake divertor of AUG by means of first SOLPS-ITER simulations with drifts activated predict beneficial detachment properties and the activation of an additional strike point by the drifts.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Stroth, U.","Aguiam, D.","Alessi, E.","Angioni, C.","Arden, N.","Parra, R. Arredondo","Artigues, V.","Asunta, O.","Balden, M.","Bandaru, V.","Banon-Navarro, A.","Behler, K.","Bergmann, A.","Bergmann, M.","Bernardo, J.","Bernert, M.","Biancalani, A.","Bielajew, R.","Bilato, R.","Birkenmeier, G.","Blanken, T.","Bobkov, V.","Bock, A.","Body, T.","Bolzonella, T.","Bonanomi, N.","Bortolon, A.","Böswirth, B.","Bottereau, C.","Bottino, A.","van den Brand, H.","Brenzke, M.","Brezinsek, S.","Brida, D.","Brochard, F.","Bruhn, C.","Buchanan, J.","Buhler, A.","Burckhart, A.","Camenen, Y.","Holm, John Hammer","Jensen, T.","Madsen, Jens","Naulin, Volker","Nem, R. D.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Olsen, J.","Rasmussen, Jesper","Salewski, Mirko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337809"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["EUROfusion MST1 Team"],"corresponding_author":["Stroth, U."],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Portugal","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aalto University","Aix-Marseille Université","All Global Affiliations","Consorzio RFX","EURATOM Association","Eindhoven University of Technology","Forschungszentrum Jülich GmbH","Institute for Magnetic Fusion Research","Instituto Superior Técnico","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","Plasma Science & Fusion Center at MIT","Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","Université de Lorraine"],"keyword":["ASDEX Upgrade","Confinement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"progress from asdex upgrade experiments in preparing the physics basis of iter operation and demo scenario development","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ac207f","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-337809","identifier":[{"id":"85117123924","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6f565446-da2e-4443-a5f1-2188f78b44db"],"keyword":["Asdex upgrade","Confinement","ELLM-free discharges"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-23B9AA369B87EFB2BE6DE372F06E6CB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1741-4326/ac207f","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277168772/Stroth_2022_Nucl._Fusion_62_042006.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"instituto superior técnico","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Instituto Superior Técnico","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"euratom association","loc":