{"abstract":"This article investigates the types of relationship that develop among athletes and coaches and how interactions between coaches and athletes influence how talent is performed. Inspired by new materialist theory, we challenge the common understanding of talent as something an athlete either is or has by examining talent as a relational phenomenon, residing in the dynamic relationship between athlete and coach. The article is based on interviews with 60 talented athletes aged 13–16 years from a Danish talent development programme. We found three key practices that shape the coach-athlete-relationship: practices that render the talent visible, practices that build or disrupt agency and practices that affect the athletes’ commitment. The analysis shows that coaches have a position that can either promote or inhibit access to and participation in talent development environments. A relational approach to talent opens for ethical discussions of power and responsibility in talent development.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Olesen, Jesper S.","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S02-098.80-011383"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"keyword":["Agential Realism New Materialism","Coaching","Dual career","Experiences","Idrætstalenter","New materialism","Nymaterialisme","Soccer","Talent","Talent development","Talentudvikling","Trænerrelationer","athlete coach relationships","talent in the making","talenttilblivelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the coach as gatekeeper distributor of resources and partner for sports talents","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85115675292&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.80-011383","identifier":[{"id":"85115675292","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000699892100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-ee680f1d-d0f6-4cb4-809a-06283a950495","au-de049351-89d1-4189-b286-b1ddf65c7a01"],"keyword":["Agential Realism-New Materialism","EXPERIENCES","SOCCER","Talent","athlete-coach-relationships","coaching","dual career","idrætstalenter","new materialism","nymaterialisme","talent development","talent in the making","talenttilblivelse","talentudvikling","trænerrelationer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-65E9A7CB2CF675191FADB13408CD1EFF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)","Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":2021},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Active Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte S.","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","name_org":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte S.","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/21640629.2021.1978730","issn":["21640629","21640637"],"issn_org":["21640629"],"issue":"2","journal":"Sports Coaching Review","pages":"233-251","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Sports Coaching Review","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115675292"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ee680f1d-d0f6-4cb4-809a-06283a950495","au-de049351-89d1-4189-b286-b1ddf65c7a01"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Coach as Gatekeeper, distributor of Resources and Partner for Sports Talents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.80-011383","year":"2022","yearsub":2022}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: COVID-19 infection has been hypothesized to affect left ventricular function; however, the underlying mechanisms and the association to clinical outcome are not understood. The global work index (GWI) is a novel echocardiographic measure of systolic function that may offer insights on cardiac dysfunction in COVID-19. We hypothesized that GWI was associated with disease severity and all-cause death in patients with COVID-19. METHODS AND RESULTS: In a multicenter study of patients admitted with COVID-19 (n=305), 249 underwent pressure-strain loop analyses to quantify GWI at a median time of 4 days after admission. We examined the association of GWI to cardiac biomarkers (troponin and NT-proBNP [N-terminal pro-B-type natriuretic peptide]), disease severity (oxygen requirement and CRP [C-reactive protein]), and all-cause death. Patients with elevated troponin (n=71) exhibited significantly reduced GWI (1508 versus 1707 mm Hg%; P=0.018). A curvilinear association to NT-proBNP was observed, with increasing NT-proBNP once GWI decreased below 1446 mm Hg%. Moreover, GWI was significantly associated with a higher oxygen requirement (relative increase of 6% per 100– mm Hg% decrease). No association was observed with CRP. Of the 249 patients, 37 died during follow-up (median, 58 days). In multivariable Cox regression, GWI was associated with all-cause death (hazard ratio, 1.08 [95% CI, 1.01–1.15], per 100– mm Hg% decrease), but did not increase C-statistics when added to clinical parameters. CONCLUSIONS: In patients admitted with COVID-19, our findings indicate that NT-proBNP and troponin may be associated with lower GWI, whereas CRP is not. GWI was independently associated with all-cause death, but did not provide prognostic information beyond readily available clinical parameters. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT04377035.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Olsen, Flemming Javier","Lassen, Mats Christian Højbjerg","Skaarup, Kristoffer Grundtvig","Christensen, Jacob","Davidovski, Filip Soeskov","Alhakak, Alia Saed","Sengeløv, Morten","Nielsen, Anne Bjerg","Johansen, Niklas Dyrby","Graff, Claus","Bundgaard, Henning","Hassager, Christian","Jabbari, Reza","Carlsen, Jørn","Kirk, Ole","Lindholm, Matias Greve","Wiese, Lothar","Kristiansen, Ole Peter","Nielsen, Olav W.","Lindegaard, Birgitte","Tønder, Niels","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Lamberts, Morten","Sivapalan, Pradeesh","Gislason, Gunnar","Iversen, Kasper","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Schou, Morten","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Aalen, John Moene","Smiseth, Otto Armin","Remme, Espen Wattenberg","Biering‐Sørensen, Tor"],"cuid":["S02-099.63-002223"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo University Hospital","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["COVID","Corona","Myocardial work","Pressure strain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"myocardial work in patients hospitalized with covid 000000000019 relation to biomarkers covid 000000000019 severity and all cause mortality","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/jaha.122.026571","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.63-002223","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9673715","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139403704","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36129046","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2c2322f9-ebe6-43c9-82de-f4441a2a2de2","ku-fda0220a-c05e-4e6f-97ad-3ae68c8aa933"],"keyword":["COVID","corona","myocardial work","pressure-strain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9D8D626CB6F973E3970BDEFAC1C94F17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.122.026571","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323854920/Myocardial_Work_in_Patients_Hospitalized_With_COVID_19.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/489312275/JAHA.122.026571.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalb