"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Otto Armin","key":"smisethottoarminpau","last":"Smiseth","name":"Smiseth, Otto Armin","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Tor","key":"bieringsørensentorpau","last":"Biering-Sørensen","locid":"2a25298f-30d3-4b37-b20b-646684a29fd8","name":"Biering-Sørensen, Tor","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Espen Wattenberg","key":"remmeespenwattenbergpau","last":"Remme","name":"Remme, Espen Wattenberg","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36129046"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.122.026571","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"19","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e026571","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139403704"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2c2322f9-ebe6-43c9-82de-f4441a2a2de2","ku-fda0220a-c05e-4e6f-97ad-3ae68c8aa933"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Myocardial Work in Patients Hospitalized With COVID‐19 : Relation to Biomarkers, COVID‐19 Severity, and All‐Cause Mortality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.63-002223","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Chronic itch is a socioeconomic burden with limited management options. Non-histaminergic itch, involved in problematic pathological itch conditions, is transmitted by a subgroup of polymodal C-fibres. Cowhage is traditionally used for studying experimentally induced non-histaminergic itch in humans but encounters some limitations. The present study, therefore, aims to design a new human, experimental model of non-histaminergic itch based on the application of bovine adrenal medulla (BAM)8-22, an endogenous peptide that activates the MrgprX1 receptor. Twenty-two healthy subjects were recruited. Different concentrations (0.5, 1 and 2 mg/ml) of BAM8-22 solution and vehicle, applied by a single skin prick test (SPT), were tested in the first session. In the second session, the BAM8-22 solution (1 mg/ml) was applied by different number of SPTs (1, 5 and 25) and by heat-inactivated cowhage spicules coated with BAM8-22. Provoked itch and pain intensities were monitored for 9 min, followed by the measurement of superficial blood perfusion (SBP) and mechanical and thermal sensitivities. BAM8-22 induced itch at the concentration of 1, 2 mg/ml (p < 0.05) and with the significantly highest intensity when applied through BAM8-22 spicules (p < 0.001). No concomitant pain sensation or increased SBP was observed. SBP increased only in the 25 SPTs area probably due to microtrauma from the multiple skin penetrations. Mechanical and thermal sensitivities were not affected by any of the applications. BAM8-22 applied through heat-inactivated spicules was the most efficient method to induce itch (without pain or changes in SBP and mechanical and thermal sensitivities) suggesting BAM8-22 as a novel non-histaminergic, human, experimental itch model.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aliotta, Giulia Erica","Lo Vecchio, Silvia","Elberling, Jesper","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001265"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lo Vecchio, Silvia"],"keyword":["BAM8 22","Itch","Pain","cowhage spicules","non histaminergic itch"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of itch and pain induced by bovine adrenal medulla bam 000000000008 000000000022 a new human model of non histaminergic itch","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/exd.14611","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001265","identifier":[{"id":"85131080472","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10286652","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35587729","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-18a65483-6de3-48d0-9436-1e0e40b2b4bf","ku-6da8f69a-6fc0-45fd-935e-519ba1943e40"],"keyword":["BAM8-22","cowhage spicules","itch","non-histaminergic itch","pain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D62DD89350D9196D8A16253C7CABB424"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320657782/Experimental_Dermatology_2022_Aliotta_Evaluation_of_itch_and_pain_induced_by_bovine_adrenal_medulla_BAM_8_22_a_new.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/509697879/Experimental_Dermatology_2022_Aliotta_Evaluation_of_itch_and_pain_induced_by_bovine_adrenal_medulla_BAM_8_22_a_new.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/exd.14611","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giulia Erica","key":"aliottapau","last":"Aliotta","locid":"efb82db6-80bc-4a13-8fda-f95c91b88a94","name":"Aliotta, Giulia Erica","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35587729"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/exd.14611","issn":["09066705","14791250"],"issn_org":["09066705"],"issue":"9","journal":"Experimental Dermatology","pages":"1402-1410","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Experimental Dermatology","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131080472"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-18a65483-6de3-48d0-9436-1e0e40b2b4bf","ku-6da8f69a-6fc0-45fd-935e-519ba1943e40"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluation of itch and pain induced by bovine adrenal medulla (BAM)8-22, a new human model of non-histaminergic itch","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-001265","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The administration of broadly neutralising anti-HIV-1 antibodies before latency reversal could facilitate elimination of HIV-1-infected CD4 T cells. We tested this concept by combining the broadly neutralising antibody 3BNC117 in combination with the latency-reversing agent romidepsin in people with HIV-1 who were taking suppressive antiretroviral therapy (ART). Methods: We did a randomised, open-label, phase 2A trial at three university hospital centres in Denmark, Germany, and the USA. Eligible participants were virologically suppressed adults aged 18–65 years who were infected with HIV-1 and on ART for at least 18 months, with plasma HIV-1 RNA concentrations of less than 50 copies per mL for at least 12 months, and a CD4 T-cell count of greater than 500 cells per μL. Participants were randomly assigned (1:1) to receive 3BNC117 plus romidepsin or romidepsin alone in two cycles. All participants received intravenous infusions of romidepsin (5 mg/m2 given over 120 min) at weeks 0, 1, and 2 (treatment cycle 1) and weeks 8, 9, and 10 (treatment cycle 2). Those in the 3BNC117 plus romidepsin group received an intravenous infusion of 3BNC117 (30 mg/kg given over 60 min) 2 days before each treatment cycle. An analytic treatment interruption (ATI) of ART was done at week 24 in both groups. Our primary endpoint was time to viral rebound during analytic treatment interruption, which was assessed in all participants who completed both treatment cycles and ATI. We used a log-rank test to compare time to viral rebound during analytic treatment interruption between the two groups. This trial is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT02850016. It is closed to new participants, and all follow-up is complete. Findings: Between March 20, 2017, and Aug 14, 2018, 22 people were enrolled and randomly assigned, 11 to the 3BNC117 plus romidepsin group and 11 to the romidepsin group. 19 participants completed both treatment cycles and the ATI: 11 in the 3BNC117 plus romidepsin group and 8 in the romidepsin group. The median time to viral rebound during ATI was 18 days (IQR 14–28) in the 3BNC117 plus romidepsin group and 28 days (21–35) in the romidepsin group B (p=0·0016). Although this difference was significant, prolongation of time to viral rebound was not clinically meaningful in either group. All participants in both groups reported adverse events, but overall the combination of 3BNC117 and romidepsin was safe. Two severe adverse events were observed in the romidepsin group during 48 weeks of follow-up, one of which—increased direct bilirubin—was judged to be related to treatment. Interpretation: The combination of 3BNC117 and romidepsin was safe but did not delay viral rebound during analytic treatment interruptions in individuals on long-term ART. The results of our trial could serve as a benchmark for further optimisation of HIV-1 curative strategies among people with HIV-1 who are taking suppressive ART. Funding: amfAR, German Center for Infection Research.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Gruell, Henning","Gunst, Jesper D","Cohen, Yehuda Z","Pahus, Marie H","Malin, Jakob J","Platten, Martin","Millard, Katrina G","Tolstrup, Martin","Jones, R Brad","Conce Alberto, Winnifer D","Lorenzi, Julio C C","Oliveira, Thiago Y","Kümmerle, Tim","Suárez, Isabelle","Unson-O'Brien, Cecilia","Nogueira, Lilian","Olesen, Rikke","Østergaard, Lars","Nielsen, Henrik","Lehmann, Clara","Nussenzweig, Michel C","Fätkenheuer, Gerd","Klein, Florian","Caskey, Marina","Søgaard, Ole S"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001757"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Søgaard, Ole S","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","German Center for Infection Research (DZIF)","Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research","Howard Hughes Medical Institute","Praxis am Ebertplatz","Rockefeller University","University Hospital Cologne","University of Cologne","Weill Cornell Medical College","Wisplinghoff Laboratories"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of 000000000003bnc000000000117 and romidepsin on the hiv 000000000001 reservoir in people taking suppressive antiretroviral therapy roadmap a randomised open label phase 000000000002a trial","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2666-5247(21)00239-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001757","identifier":[{"id":"85125493340","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35544074","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10293654","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-22ea2bc7-5828-47e7-b590-67999e670298","au-7c6928fe-3cc7-425c-8be8-33a09ee7c80c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11381F0954DAB4B0B5C899F5CD69C66E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2666-5247(21)00239-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/465410694/Gruell_et_al._2022_._Effect_of_3BNC117_and_romidepsin_on_the_HIV_1_reservoir_in_people_taking_suppressive_antiretroviral_therapy_ROADMAP_a_randomised_open_label_phase_2A_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cologne","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university hospital cologne","lo