{"abstract":"AIMS: This study aims to investigate the long-term occurrence of the composite endpoint of heart failure (HF) hospitalization or all-cause death (primary endpoint) in patients randomized to cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT) using individualized multimodality imaging-guided left ventricular (LV) lead placement compared with a routine fluoroscopic approach. Furthermore, this study aims to evaluate whether inter-lead electrical delay (IED) is associated with improved response rate of this endpoint. METHODS AND RESULTS: We reviewed follow-up data until November 2020 for all 182 patients included in the ImagingCRT trial for the occurrence of HF hospitalization and all-cause death. During median (inter-quartile range) time to primary endpoint/censuring of 6.7 (3.3-7.9) years, the rate of the primary endpoint was 60% (n = 53) in the imaging group compared with 52% (n = 48) in the control group [hazard ratio (HR) 1.22, 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.83-1.81, P = 0.31]. Neither the risk of HF hospitalization (HR 1.11, 95% CI 0.62-1.99, P = 0.72) nor of all-cause death differed between treatment groups (HR 1.23, 95% CI 0.82-1.85, P = 0.32). The risk of the primary endpoint was significantly reduced among those with IED ≥100 ms when compared with those with IED <100 ms (HR 0.62, 95% CI 0.39-0.98, P = 0.04). CONCLUSIONS: In this study, an individualized multimodality imaging-guided strategy targeting LV lead placement towards the latest mechanically activated non-scarred myocardial segment during CRT implantation did not reduce HF hospitalization or all-cause death when compared with routine LV lead placement during long-term follow-up. Targeting the latest electrical activation should be studied as an alternative individualized strategy for optimizing LV lead placement in CRT recipients.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin","Sommer, Anders","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Kronborg, Mads Brix","Kristensen, Jens","Gerdes, Christian","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002777"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin"],"keyword":["Cardiac Resynchronization Therapy Devices","Cardiac Resynchronization Therapy adverse effects","Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Echocardiography","Heart Failure diagnostic imaging","Heart Ventricles diagnostic imaging","Heart failure patients","Humans","Left ventricular lead placement","Long term follow up","Mortality","Position","Survival","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term outcomes in a randomized controlled trial of multimodality imaging guided left ventricular lead placement in cardiac resynchronization therapy","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85127305040&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002777","identifier":[{"id":"000791518600017","type":"wos"},{"id":"85127305040","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35041000","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-38084d63-1cf5-4a92-a2f8-3dd317a6a87e","au-662d8005-c9ff-4ba0-b63b-d1fac7a3cb79"],"keyword":["Cardiac Resynchronization Therapy Devices","Cardiac Resynchronization Therapy/adverse effects","Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Echocardiography","HEART-FAILURE PATIENTS","Heart Failure/diagnostic imaging","Heart Ventricles/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Left ventricular lead placement","Long-term follow-up","MORTALITY","POSITION","SURVIVAL","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-35173CD46955C96B555D0CA5A3F75E9D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Benjamin","key":"fyenbodanielbenjaminpau","last":"Fyenbo","locid":"90f4115a-ffcf-4502-8461-34533e634242","name":"Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin","orcid":"0000-0001-5898-1743","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"sommeranderspau","last":"Sommer","locid":"310abbc0-d3b1-4351-9e62-e77454fb14fa","name":"Sommer, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardbjarnelindepau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Brix","key":"kronborgmadsbrixpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"76c15c18-4786-4b38-93b3-91afbc1ea875","name":"Kronborg, Mads Brix","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kristensenjenspau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"ede439bf-3ff5-4519-9c5b-5c2e1a1daea0","name":"Kristensen, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"gerdeschristianpau","last":"Gerdes","locid":"43704ceb-b5ba-49ac-bff8-5e26e3b9d419","name":"Gerdes, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenhenrikkjærulfpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenjespermøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenjenscosedispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35041000"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euab314","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"5","journal":"Europace","pages":"828-834","paperid":"euab314","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127305040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-38084d63-1cf5-4a92-a2f8-3dd317a6a87e","au-662d8005-c9ff-4ba0-b63b-d1fac7a3cb79"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long-term outcomes in a randomized controlled trial of multimodality imaging-guided left ventricular lead placement in cardiac resynchronization therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-002777","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Decisions about resuscitation preference is an essential part of patient-centered care but a prerequisite is having an idea about which questions to ask and understand how such questions may be clustered in dimensions. The European Resuscitation Council Guidelines 2021 encourages resuscitation shared decision making in emergency care treatment plans and needs and experiences of people approaching end-of-life have been characterized within the physical, psychological, social, and spiritual dimensions. We aimed to develop, test, and validate the dimensionality of items that may influence resuscitation preference in older Emergency Department (ED) patients. Methods: A 36-item questionnaire was designed based on qualitative interviews exploring what matters and what may influence resuscitation preference and existing literature. Items were organized in physical, psychological, social, and spiritual dimensions. Initial pilot-testing to assess content validity included ten older community-dwelling persons. Field-testing, confirmatory factor analysis and post-hoc bifactor analysis was performed on 269 older ED patients. Several model fit indexes and reliability coefficients (explained common variance (ECV) and omega values) were computed to evaluate structural validity, dimensionality, and model-based reliability. Results: Items were reduced from 36 to 26 in field testing. Items concerning religious beliefs from the spiritual dimension were misunderstood and deemed unimportant by older ED patients. Remaining items concerned physical functioning in daily living, coping, self-control in life, optimism, overall mood, quality of life and social participation in life. Confirmatory factor analysis displayed poor fit, whereas post-hoc bifactor analysis displayed satisfactory goodness of fit (χ2 =562.335 (p<0.001); root mean square error of approximation=0.063 (90% CI [0.055;0.070])). The self-assessed independence may be the bifactor explaining what matters to older ED patients’ resuscitation preference. Conclusions: We developed a questionnaire and investigated the dimensionality of what matters and may influence resuscitation preference among older ED patients. We could not confirm a spiritual dimension. Also, in bifactor analysis the expected dimensions were overruled by an overall explanatory general factor suggesting independence to be of particular importance for clinicians practicing resuscitation discussions in EDs. Studies to investigate how independence may relate to patients’ choice of resuscitation preference are needed.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hanson, Stine","Nissen, Søren Kabell","Nielsen, Dorthe","Lassen, Annmarie","Brabrand, Mikkel","Forero, Roberto","Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","Ryg, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014112"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Hanson, Stine"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ingham Institute for Applied Medical Research","Liverpool Hospital, Australia","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Affect","Aged","Bifactor analysis","Emergency Service Hospital","Emergency department","End of life","Humans","Independence","Preferences","Psychometrics methods","Quality of Life psychology","Reproducibility of Results","Resuscitation","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what matters and influence resuscitation preference development field testing and structural validation of items among older patients in the emergency department","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-022-03707-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Region of Southern Denmark [16/42004], the Health Foundation [17-B-0072], and the Karola Jorgensens Foundation. None of the funders played a role in the design, execution, analyses, interpretation of the data, or writing of the study."],"id":"S02-100.00-014112","identifier":[{"id":"36564759","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85144637152","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9783719","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-150a641c-d13e-4fcd-9d1e-7c8d97facc7d","sdu-f06e6680-3e38-4931-9830-7dd8885a517e"],"keyword":["Affect","Aged","Bifactor analysis","Emergency Service, Hospital","Emergency department","End of life","Humans","Independence","Preferences","Psychometrics/methods","Quality of Life/psychology","Reproducibility of Results","Resuscitation","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-02D421142FC77A56CD52F5D6AACFAB12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-022-03707-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/217338828/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of new south wales","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD