{"abstract":"Objective: Recent studies on air pollution and disease have been based on millions of participants within a region or country, relying entirely on register-based confounder adjustment. We aimed to investigate the effects of increasing adjustment for register- and questionnaire-based covariates on the association between air pollution and cardiometabolic diseases. Methods: In a population-based cohort of 246,766 eligible participants randomly selected across Denmark in 2010 and 2013 and followed up until December 31, 2017, we identified 3,247 myocardial infarction (MI) cases, 4,166 stroke cases and 6,366 type 2 diabetes cases. Based on historical address-information, we calculated 5-year time-weighted exposure to PM 2.5 and NO 2 modelled using a validated air pollution model. We used Cox proportional hazards models to calculate hazard ratios (HR) with increasing adjustment for a number of individual- and area-level register-based covariates as well as lifestyle covariates assessed through questionnaires. Results: We found that a 5 μg/m 3 higher PM 2.5 was associated with HRs (95% CI) for MI, stroke and diabetes, of respectively, 1.18 (0.91–1.52), 1.11 (0.88–1.40) and 1.24 (1.03–1.50) in the fully adjusted models. For all three diseases, adjustment for either individual-level, area-level or lifestyle covariates, or combinations of these resulted in higher HRs compared to HRs adjusted only for age, sex and calendar-year, most marked for MI and diabetes. Further adjustment for lifestyle in models with full register-based individual- and area-level adjustment resulted in only minor changes in HRs for all three diseases. Conclusions: Our findings suggest that in studies of air pollution and cardiometabolic disease, which use an adjustment strategy with a broad range of register-based socioeconomic variables, there is no effect on risk estimates from subsequent lifestyle adjustment.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Arthur Hvidtfeldt, Ulla","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Thygesen, Lau Caspar","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Khan, Jibran","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-098.81-022129"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Mette"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Cardiometabolic disease","Cohort study","Confounders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of adjustment to register based and questionnaire based covariates on the association between air pollution and cardiometabolic disease","src":["au","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85112857154","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research described in this article was conducted under contract to the Health Effects Institute (HEI), an organization jointly funded by the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) (Assistance Award No. R-82811201) and certain motor vehicle and engine manufacturers. The contents of this article do not necessarily reflect the views of HEI, or its sponsors, nor do they necessarily reflect the views and policies of the EPA or motor vehicle and engine manufacturers."],"id":"S03-098.81-022129","identifier":[{"id":"85112857154","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34411546","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-81914484-e1fa-4131-8587-53dc7b8b0ac3","ruc-18f2aa9c-1a87-4fd0-a387-70bcd9d19a0a","sdu-8f96d6b7-61f8-4883-a94e-fa7b1386fb47"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Air pollution Cardiometabolic disease Cohort study Confounders","Cardiometabolic disease","Cohort study","Confounders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4C39788CDEACFAAC04154FA8F58A50DE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"arthurhvidtfeldtpau","last":"Arthur Hvidtfeldt","name":"Arthur Hvidtfeldt, Ulla","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lau Caspar","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"1932f287-552d-4539-8153-b2fc204a703b","name":"Thygesen, Lau Caspar","orcid":"0000-0001-8375-5211","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34411546"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2021.111886","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"111886","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"203"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112857154"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-81914484-e1fa-4131-8587-53dc7b8b0ac3","ruc-18f2aa9c-1a87-4fd0-a387-70bcd9d19a0a","sdu-8f96d6b7-61f8-4883-a94e-fa7b1386fb47"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The effect of adjustment to register-based and questionnaire-based covariates on the association between air pollution and cardiometabolic disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.81-022129","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The goal of this trial was to investigate whether an eHealth lifestyle coaching programme led to significant weight loss and decreased Haemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) in patients with type 2 diabetes. In an RCT, 170 patients were enrolled from 2018 to 2019 for intervention or control. Inclusion criteria were diagnosed with type 2 diabetes, BMI 30-45 kg/m2, and aged 18-70 years. Exclusion criteria were lacks internet access, pregnant or planning a pregnancy, or has a serious disease. Primary and secondary outcomes were a reduction in body weight and HbA1c. At six months, 75 (75%) patients in the intervention group and 53 (76%) patients in the control group remained in the trial. The mean body weight loss was 4.2 kg (95% CI, -5.49; -2.98) in the intervention group and 1.5 kg (95% CI, -2.57; -0.48) in the control group (p = 0.005). In the intervention group, 24 out of 62 patients with elevated HbA1c at baseline (39%) had a normalized HbA1c &lt; 6.5% at six months, compared to 8 out of 40 patients with elevated HbA1c at baseline (20%) in the control group (p = 0.047). The eHealth lifestyle coaching programme can lead to significant weight loss and decreased HbA1c among patients with type 2 diabetes, compared to standard care.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Laursen, Ditte Hjorth","Lauridsen, Jørgen T.","Hesseldal, Laura","Jakobsen, Pernille Ravn","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Brandt, Carl J"],"cuid":["S03-099.78-021932"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup"],"keyword":["Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 therapy","Glycated Hemoglobin A analysis","Humans","Interactive advice","Intervention","Life Style","Lifestyle change","Management","Mentoring","Obesity","Participant engagement","Primary Health Care","Quality of Life","Telemedicine","Weight loss","digital behavioural coaching","health behaviour change","mobile intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reversing type 000000000002 diabetes in a primary care anchored ehealth lifestyle coaching programme in denmark a randomised controlled trial","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu14163424","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.78-021932","identifier":[{"id":"36014930","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000845781200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85136633609","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9414066","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-7ef4b70e-67ce-4f4d-bf21-639f8349fdbb","ku-063e16f5-964a-4a6c-a7ea-65c17398453b","sdu-6495f782-b28a-4ec0-affc-7125a719ffea"],"keyword":["Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/therapy","Glycated Hemoglobin A/analysis","Humans","INTERVENTION","Life Style","MANAGEMENT","Mentoring","Primary Health Care","WEIGHT-LOSS","digital behavioural coaching","health behaviour change","interactive advice","lifestyle change","mobile intervention","obesity","participant engagement","quality of life","telemedicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-235249D7CFA4BB645A8976BDE6B6BA14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/209473772/nutrients_14_03424_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu14163424","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318707825/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Re