{"abstract":"Oligonucleotides are increasingly being used as a programmable connection material to assemble molecules and proteins in well-defined structures. For the application of such assemblies for in vivo diagnostics or therapeutics it is crucial that the oligonucleotides form highly stable, non-toxic, and non-immunogenic structures. Only few oligonucleotide derivatives fulfil all of these requirements. Here we report on the application of acyclic l-threoninol nucleic acid (aTNA) to form a four-way junction (4WJ) that is highly stable and enables facile assembly of components for in vivo treatment and imaging. The aTNA 4WJ is serum-stable, shows no non-targeted uptake or cytotoxicity, and invokes no innate immune response. As a proof of concept, we modify the 4WJ with a cancer-targeting and a serum half-life extension moiety and show the effect of these functionalized 4WJs in vitro and in vivo, respectively.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Märcher, Anders","Kumar, Vipin","Andersen, Veronica Liv","El-Chami, Kassem","Nguyen, Thuy Jane Dinh","Skaanning, Mads Koch","Rudnik-Jansen, Imke","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Howard, Ken","Kjems, Jørgen","Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154785"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager"],"keyword":["Amino Alcohols chemistry","Butylene Glycols","CELLS","DNA","Delivery","Nanobodies","Nanostructures","Nucleic Acid Conformation","Nucleic Acids chemistry","Oligonucleotides","Proteins","RNA chemistry","aTNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functionalized acyclic l threoninol nucleic acid four way junction with high stability in vitro and in vivo","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.202115275","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154785","identifier":[{"id":"000782301200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35352451","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128196548","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9324938","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-2c7f5436-6060-4d45-9a07-53de17409047"],"keyword":["Amino Alcohols/chemistry","Butylene Glycols","CELLS","DELIVERY","DNA","DNA NANOSTRUCTURES","Holliday Junction","NANOBODIES","Nanostructures","Nucleic Acid Conformation","Nucleic Acids/chemistry","Oligonucleotides","PROTEINS","RNA/chemistry","aTNA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E71E81536C2E44A0B238A952024C958"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.202115275","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9324938/pdf/ANIE-61-0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"märcherpau","last":"Märcher","locid":"f5efd690-60d9-4541-a917-5ffcee8d32f0","name":"Märcher, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vipin","key":"kumarpau","last":"Kumar","locid":"33f9e911-c747-44ed-a408-0823fc96aa83","name":"Kumar, Vipin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronica L.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"de7beb69-fdb9-4569-822b-ba1a3dd1cf79","name":"Andersen, Veronica Liv","name_org":"Andersen, Veronica L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kassem","key":"elchamipau","last":"El-Chami","locid":"afc2d632-fe29-4e5f-a0f0-831c2e754237","name":"El-Chami, Kassem","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thuy J.D.","key":"nguyenpau","last":"Nguyen","locid":"68332a51-9167-4f03-937b-e01b4894a7aa","name":"Nguyen, Thuy Jane Dinh","name_org":"Nguyen, Thuy J.D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads K.","key":"skaanningpau","last":"Skaanning","locid":"a15e9849-b3d9-404a-9190-bd3d6a9d5aa0","name":"Skaanning, Mads Koch","name_org":"Skaanning, Mads K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Imke","key":"rudnikjansenpau","last":"Rudnik-Jansen","locid":"3f6ac569-ea82-49fd-810f-f76af5dc4024","name":"Rudnik-Jansen, Imke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth A.","key":"howardpau","last":"Howard","locid":"8ecf79c2-bb52-4f69-9438-72a69a44a0c9","name":"Howard, Ken","name_org":"Howard, Kenneth A.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemspau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kurt V.","key":"gothelfpau","last":"Gothelf","locid":"8ca43d09-e887-432e-8775-ab2f38db1e6d","name":"Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","name_org":"Gothelf, Kurt V.","orcid":"0000-0003-2399-3757","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35352451"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.202115275","issn":["14337851","15213773"],"issn_org":["14337851"],"issue":"24","journal":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","paperid":"202115275","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","title_org":"Angewandte Chemie - International Edition","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128196548"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2c7f5436-6060-4d45-9a07-53de17409047"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Functionalized Acyclic (l)-Threoninol Nucleic Acid Four-Way Junction with High Stability In Vitro and In Vivo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154785","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR) can be treated by retinal photocoagulation, but in some cases, the treatment is initiated too late or is insufficient so that the disease advances to a stage requiring vitrectomy. There is a need to identify risk factors that can predict if patients with PDR will develop complications in need for vitrectomy. Methods: Survival analysis with death as competing risk was used to study systemic risk factors for PDR progression to a complication in need for vitrectomy in right eyes of all 1288 diabetic patients from the Aarhus area, Denmark, who had developed proliferative retinopathy in the right eye during the 25 years period from 1 July 1994 until 1 July 2019. Results: The overall cumulative incidence of reaching a vitrectomy end point in the right eye was 24.1% (n = 311). In 9.3% (n = 120) of the patients where vitrectomy had been performed together with the first photocoagulation, the age of onset of diabetes was significantly higher (p < 0.0001), the diabetes duration longer (p < 0.035) and BMI higher (p < 0.01) than in the patients who had been vitrectomized later than the first photocoagulation. The risk for vitrectomy was significantly increased by high variability of HbA1c before the development of PDR (p < 0.0001), but not by other parameters known to increase the risk for developing PDR. Conclusion: Increasing variability of HbA1c before the development of PDR increases the risk for progression to a complication in need of vitrectomy. The need for vitrectomy is unaffected by other risk factors known to increase the risk for developing PDR.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bek, Toke","Nielsen, Mette Slot","Klug, Sidsel Ehlers","Eriksen, Jesper Engholt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-159025"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bek, Toke"],"keyword":["Diabetic retinopathy","Photocoagulation","Risk Factors","Survival Analysis","Vitrectomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increasing metabolic variability increases the risk for vitrectomy in proliferative diabetic retinopathy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85116534240","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-159025","identifier":[{"id":"85116534240","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34625890","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-33f00625-fb56-45b8-bd28-f51dd4a8383f"],"keyword":["Diabetic retinopathy","Photocoagulation","Risk factors","Survival analysis","Vitrectomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9054DAB31C9790C55838CA485D4A7699"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Slot","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bb29c970-ea2d-4334-b42e-6d692dbd6ecf","name":"Nielsen, Mette Slot","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidsel Ehlers","key":"klugpau","last":"Klug","locid":"f771504c-ad0d-4b79-bfce-1b6c8b66e3bf","name":"Klug, Sidsel Ehlers","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Engholt","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Jesper Engholt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34625890"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10792-021-02041-3","issn":["01655701","15732630"],"issn_org":["01655701"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Ophthalmology","pages":"757-763","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Ophthalmology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116534240"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-33f00625-fb56-45b8-bd28-f51dd4a8383f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Increasing metabolic variability increases the risk for vitrectomy in proliferative diabetic retinopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-159025","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: This study investigates whether individuals who have sustained an electrical injury (EI) are diagnosed with unspecified pain or pain related to the musculoskeletal system in the years following the injury. METHODS: Individuals listed in Danish registers as having sustained EIs were matched for sex, age, and year of injury in a cohort study with individuals having experienced dislocations/sprains (match 1), eye injuries (match 2), and a sample of individuals with the same occupation without a history of electrical injuries (match 3). Outcomes were unspecified pain and unspecified soft tissue disorders. Conditional logistic regression and conditional Cox regression were applied. RESULTS: We identified 14,112 individuals who sustained EIs. A higher risk of both outcomes was observed for all three matches, and was highest at the 6- and 12-month follow-ups. The risk of both outcomes was considerably higher for match 3. CONCLUSIONS: This study confirms that exposure to EIs increases the risk of being diagnosed with unspecified pain or unspecified soft tissue disorders both at short and long terms. Our results also showed that the risk of unspecified pain as sequelae is related to the severity of the injury.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Poulsen, Per Hoegh","Carstensen, Ole","Kærgaard, Anette","Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","Nielsen, Kent Jacob","Biering, Karin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230818"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Per Hoegh"],"keyword":["Matched cohort study","Pain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unspecified pain and other soft tissue disorders following electrical injuries a register based matched cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-021-01802-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230818","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9038797","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000705132300003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85116760134","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34628524","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b1d8e63e-39a5-4fbb-8bb9-a95487ecea1a"],"keyword":["Electrical injury","Electrical shock","Matched cohort study","Pain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8608EF837A94EE3C907466C2DE609BBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-021-01802-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/330163433/Unspecified_pain_and_other_soft_tissue_disorders_following_electrical_injuries_a_register_based_matched_cohort_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Occupational and Environmental Medicine, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Hoegh","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"19e68b21-16df-4011-9fe2-e3d8a39c1187","name":"Poulsen, Per Hoegh","orcid":"0000-0002-0196-2290","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"f3192717-9366-4b48-9462-782288954025","name":"Carstensen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette","key":"kærgaardpau","last":"Kærgaard","locid":"97dbcdfa-9288-42b8-960e-47568add33e3","name":"Kærgaard, Anette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Medom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f2a2e103-1293-4370-b308-c4427f184a75","name":"Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-6566","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent J","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b11fecf5-8895-4034-a7b1-d5eb0399ea93","name":"Nielsen, Kent Jacob","name_org":"Nielsen, Kent J","orcid":"0000-0002-4643-5697","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin","key":"bieringpau","last":"Biering","locid":"747fb3a4-9438-4f99-b7c3-d13deeb4442f","name":"Biering, Karin","orcid":"0000-0001-7038-9566","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34628524"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00420-021-01802-y","issn":["03400131","14315777"],"issn_org":["03400131"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","pages":"799-809","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116760134"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b1d8e63e-39a5-4fbb-8bb9-a95487ecea1a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Unspecified pain and other soft tissue disorders following electrical injuries : a register-based matched cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230818","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Instructing newly diagnosed sleep apnoea patients in the use of continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) machines is time consuming for healthcare workers and patients alike. Our aim was to test the feasibility of video instruction as an alternative to physical attendance in the clinic. METHODS: In this randomised controlled trial, we enrolled 120 patients who were randomised to either classic instruction by a nurse or video instruction at home. Both patients and doctors answered questionnaires at the time of inclusion. Follow-up was 1-3 months. RESULTS: No significant difference was recorded between the two groups on any measured parameter. CONCLUSIONS: Video instruction is feasible and should be considered as an alternative to physical attendance for the CPAP start-up.none. TRIAL REGISTRATION: clinicaltrials.gov (NCT number 15022020).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fuglsang, Milos","Duez, Christophe Henri Valdemar","Dahl, Line Borreskov","Nielsen, Marianne Bach","Bille, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-236780"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ambulatory Care Facilities","Continuous positive airway pressure","Humans","Sleep Apnea Obstructive therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in person versus video instruction of patients with sleep apnoea in the use of continuous positive airway pressure cpap","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/346085573/In-person_versus_video_instruction_of_patients_with_sleep_apnoea_in_the_use_of_continuous_positive_airway_pressure_CPAP_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-236780","identifier":[{"id":"85122842884","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34913431","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bc2e9540-e8cf-458a-b2e1-5fdafb3794da"],"keyword":["Ambulatory Care Facilities","Continuous Positive Airway Pressure","Humans","Sleep Apnea Syndromes/therapy","Sleep Apnea, Obstructive/therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BCB360FE1613B9B5B72CCA8055E2BB3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/dmj/person-versus-video-instruction-patients-sleep-apnoea-use-continuous-positive-airway-pressure-cpap","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/346085573/In-person_versus_video_instruction_of_patients_with_sleep_apnoea_in_the_use_of_continuous_positive_airway_pressure_CPAP_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital of Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Milos","key":"fuglsangpau","last":"Fuglsang","locid":"7238b441-d227-44d9-a807-81eed8314f9a","name":"Fuglsang, Milos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christophe","key":"duezpau","last":"Duez","locid":"c83d9eab-d5e9-4efd-9525-2f8a2c35c52b","name":"Duez, Christophe Henri Valdemar","name_org":"Duez, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0001-7560-9214","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Borreskov","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"9139884e-08f5-46f3-a71d-ede866c23450","name":"Dahl, Line Borreskov","orcid":"0000-0002-3913-3076","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Bach","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Marianne Bach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"billepau","last":"Bille","locid":"e01ad509-1441-4201-8840-77490d3099c8","name":"Bille, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34913431"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"1","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A07210549","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bc2e9540-e8cf-458a-b2e1-5fdafb3794da"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"In-person versus video instruction of patients with sleep apnoea in the use of continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-236780","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Understanding the molecular pathways driving the acute antiviral and inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2 infection is critical for developing treatments for severe COVID-19. Here, we find decreasing number of circulating plasmacytoid dendritic cells (pDCs) in COVID-19 patients early after symptom onset, correlating with disease severity. pDC depletion is transient and coincides with decreased expression of antiviral type I IFNα and of systemic inflammatory cytokines CXCL10 and IL-6. Using an in vitro stem cell-based human pDC model, we further demonstrate that pDCs, while not supporting SARS-CoV-2 replication, directly sense the virus and in response produce multiple antiviral (interferons: IFNα and IFNλ1) and inflammatory (IL-6, IL-8, CXCL10) cytokines that protect epithelial cells from de novo SARS-CoV-2 infection. Via targeted deletion of virus-recognition innate immune pathways, we identify TLR7-MyD88 signaling as crucial for production of antiviral interferons (IFNs), whereas Toll-like receptor (TLR)2 is responsible for the inflammatory IL-6 response. We further show that SARS-CoV-2 engages the receptor neuropilin-1 on pDCs to selectively mitigate the antiviral interferon response, but not the IL-6 response, suggesting neuropilin-1 as potential therapeutic target for stimulation of TLR7-mediated antiviral protection.","author_count":26,"contributors":["van der Sluis, Renée Marije","Cham, Lamin B.","Gris-Oliver, Albert","Jakobsen, Kristine Raaby","Pedersen, Jesper Geert","Idorn, Manja","Ahmadov, Ulvi","Hernández, Sabina Sánchez","Cemalovic, Ena","Godsk, Stine Høvring","Thyrsted, Jacob","Gunst, Jesper D.","Nielsen, Silke D.","Jørgensen, Janni J.","Bjerg, Tobias Wang","Laustsen, Anders","Reinert, Line S.","Olagnier, David","Bak, Rasmus O","Kjolby, Mads","Holm, Christian K","Tolstrup, Martin","Paludan, Søren R","Kristensen, Lasse Sommer","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","Jakobsen, Martin Roelsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255335"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","al