{"abstract":"We present novel experimental evidence of parametric decay instability of microwave beams in the plasma edge of the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator. We propose that the instability is sustained by trapping of only one daughter wave in the non-monotonic density profile measured with high spatial resolution within a stationary magnetic island. The power levels and spectral shapes of the detected microwave signal are reproduced by numerical modelling and a theoretical power threshold is predicted around 300 kW, comparable with observations. We predict a fraction of power drained by daughter waves around 4% in the experiments, potentially increasing above 50% for more hollow edge density profiles. Such absorption levels could significantly reduce the efficiency of the microwave heating and current-drive system in tokamaks and stellarators.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Tancetti, A.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Gusakov, E. Z.","Popov, A. Yu","Moseev, D.","Stange, T.","Senstius, M. G.","Killer, C.","Vecséi, M.","Jensen, T.","Zanini, M.","Abramovic, I.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Anda, G.","Dunai, D.","Zoletnik, S.","Laqua, H. P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353562"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tancetti, A."],"country":["Germany","Hungary","Netherlands","Russia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for Energy Research","Eindhoven University of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","RAS - Ioffe Physico Technical Institute"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Parametric decay instability","Upper hybrid wave","Wendelstein 7 X stellarator"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nonlinear decay of high power microwaves into trapped modes in inhomogeneous plasma","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/299101790/Paper_w_changes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has been supported by research Grant 15483 from VILLUM FONDEN and the Enabling Research Grant ENR-MFE19.DTU-03 from the EUROfusion Consortium. The work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014–2018 and 2019–2020 under Grant No. 633053. The views and opinions expressed herein do not necessarily reflect those of the European Commission. The analytical theoretical treatment is supported under the Ioffe Institute state contract 0040-2019-0023, whereas the numerical modeling is supported under the Ioffe Institute state contract 0034-2021-0003."],"id":"S01-000.00-353562","identifier":[{"id":"85129433166","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a430d223-10df-4755-aaa2-e63dfa6d1cdf"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Ion Bernstein waves","Parametric decay instability","Upper hybrid wave","Wendelstein 7-X stellarator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F84B5AE060F9D3DEB4775FD7888DC04C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/299101790/Paper_w_changes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denm