{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Motzfeldt, Hanne Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397803"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transformation automated decisions and decision support based on machine learning in public administration","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://publiclaw.digi.hansreitzel.dk/?id=152","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-397803","ids":["ku-0736a5c9-9630-40c2-b1f0-2c2aa89ea03e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6F303FD9CD63F605FCB9ABBD9BBAD6C1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre for Information and Innovation Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Marie","key":"motzfeldtpau","last":"Motzfeldt","locid":"c9e7c3da-e2e2-44df-84e7-3de82aa9c8e8","name":"Motzfeldt, Hanne Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-3112-6760","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Aagaard","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Peter Aagaard","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"jesper","key":"olsenpedh","last":"olsen","name":"olsen, jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788741277981"],"isbn":["9788702388206"],"pages":"445-462","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Insights into Danish Constitutional and Administrative Law","title":"Public Law"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0736a5c9-9630-40c2-b1f0-2c2aa89ea03e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transformation : Automated Decisions and Decision Support Based on Machine Learning in Public Administration","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-397803","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and ObjectivesEEG is widely used for prediction of neurologic outcome after cardiac arrest. To better understand the relationship between EEG and neuronal injury, we explored the association between EEG and neurofilament light (NfL) as a marker of neuroaxonal injury, evaluated whether highly malignant EEG patterns are reflected by high NfL levels, and explored the association of EEG backgrounds and EEG discharges with NfL.MethodsWe performed a post hoc analysis of the Target Temperature Management After Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest trial. Routine EEGs were prospectively performed after the temperature intervention ≥36 hours postarrest. Patients who awoke or died prior to 36 hours postarrest were excluded. EEG experts blinded to clinical information classified EEG background, amount of discharges, and highly malignant EEG patterns according to the standardized American Clinical Neurophysiology Society terminology. Prospectively collected serum samples were analyzed for NfL after trial completion. The highest available concentration at 48 or 72 hours postarrest was used.ResultsA total of 262/939 patients with EEG and NfL data were included. Patients with highly malignant EEG patterns had 2.9 times higher NfL levels than patients with malignant patterns and NfL levels were 13 times higher in patients with malignant patterns than those with benign patterns (95% CI 1.4-6.1 and 6.5-26.2, respectively; effect size 0.47; p < 0.001). Both background and the amount of discharges were independently strongly associated with NfL levels (p < 0.001). The EEG background had a stronger association with NfL levels than EEG discharges (R2 = 0.30 and R2 = 0.10, respectively). NfL levels in patients with a continuous background were lower than for any other background (95% CI for discontinuous, burst-suppression, and suppression, respectively: 2.26-18.06, 3.91-41.71, and 5.74-41.74; effect size 0.30; p < 0.001 for all). NfL levels did not differ between suppression and burst suppression. Superimposed discharges were only associated with higher NfL levels if the EEG background was continuous.DiscussionBenign, malignant, and highly malignant EEG patterns reflect the extent of brain injury as measured by NfL in serum. The extent of brain injury is more strongly related to the EEG background than superimposed discharges. Combining EEG and NfL may be useful to better identify patients misclassified by single methods.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Grindegård, Linnéa","Cronberg, Tobias","Backman, Sofia","Blennow, Kaj","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Kjaer, Troels W.","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Mattsson-Carlgren, Niklas","Nielsen, Niklas","Van Rootselaar, Anne Fleur","Rossetti, Andrea O.","Stammet, Pascal","Ullén, Susann","Zetterberg, Henrik","Westhall, Erik","Moseby-Knappe, Marion"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430783"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Hong Kong","Luxembourg","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Center Hospitalier de Luxembourg","Faculty of Medicine","Hong Kong Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases","Lund University","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","University College London","University of Amsterdam","University of Luxembourg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between eeg patterns and serum neurofilament light after cardiac arrest a post hoc analysis of the ttm trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/WNL.0000000000200335","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-430783","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9231840","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35470143","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85131903308","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3e8017ff-be78-4656-bab9-0c339fbeac64"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1E6870B724ABE8574505148A9576775A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1212/WNL.0000000000200335","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/330473120/Association_Between_EEG_Patterns.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"sahlgrenska university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Sahlgrenska University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet