{"abstract":"Recent improvements in the analysis of ancient biomolecules from human remains and associated dental calculus have provided new insights into the prehistoric diet and genetic diversity of our species. Here we present a multi-omics study, integrating metagenomic and proteomic analyses of dental calculus, and human ancient DNA analysis of the petrous bones of two post-Last Glacial Maximum (LGM) individuals from San Teodoro cave (Italy), to reconstruct their lifestyle and the post-LGM resettlement of Europe. Our analyses show genetic homogeneity in Sicily during the Palaeolithic, representing a hitherto unknown Italian genetic lineage within the previously identified Villabruna cluster. We argue that this lineage took refuge in Italy during the LGM, followed by a subsequent spread to central-western Europe. Analysis of dental calculus showed a diet rich in animal proteins which is also reflected on the oral microbiome composition. Our results demonstrate the power of this approach in the study of prehistoric humans and will enable future research to reach a more holistic understanding of the population dynamics and ecology.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Scorrano, Gabriele","Nielsen, Sofie Holtsmark","Vetro, Domenico Lo","Sawafuji, Rikai","Mackie, Meaghan","Margaryan, Ashot","Fotakis, Anna K.","Martínez-Labarga, Cristina","Fabbri, Pier Francesco","Allentoft, Morten E.","Carra, Marialetizia","Martini, Fabio","Rickards, Olga","Olsen, Jesper V.","Pedersen, Mikkel Winther","Cappellini, Enrico","Sikora, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432861"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Curtin University","University of Florence","University of Rome La Sapienza","University of Rome Tor Vergata","University of Salento"],"keyword":["Genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomic ancestry diet and microbiomes of upper palaeolithic hunter gatherers from san teodoro cave sicily italy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-022-04190-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-432861","identifier":[{"id":"85142044894","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9674856","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000885318600009","type":"wos"},{"id":"36400919","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-41f1efa4-f7d1-45c5-8efb-5b7e4baa70e2"],"keyword":["genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2718C542F3B005C6655D04D2AEBC4CF5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-022-04190-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/327143255/s42003_022_04190_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of florence","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Florence","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of rome tor vergata","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rome Tor Vergata","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of salento"