{"abstract":"Designing, building, and testing new adaptable automation equipment for the discrete manufacturing industry is becoming a still more complex discipline where static Technical Product Specifications are no longer the situation in a dynamic and changing environment. Therefore, computer simulation tools at different abstraction levels become very important in designing and building automation solutions. This paper investigates how to develop and test machines effectively, taking offset in a practical industry case. The paper proposes a methodology from the first simulation models to a digital twin environment. The result is a practical-based framework that helps machine builders and end-customers identify the appropriate simulation methods in advance, ensuring faster and simpler development of automation equipment that will lower the overall costs.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hansen, Jesper Puggaard de Oliveira","Ribeiro da Silva, Elias","Bilberg, Arne","Bro, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579655"],"event":{"acronym":"CARV","end":"2021-11-02","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2021-11-01","title":"8th Changeable, Agile, Reconﬁgurable and Virtual Production Conference and the World Mass Customization &amp; Personalization Conference","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Jesper Puggaard de Oliveira"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Siemens"],"keyword":["Digital twin","Machine Building","Simulation","Smart automation","Virtual Commissioning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agile machine development from virtual to real","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"f