{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Møller","Christoffersen, Mette","Møllenbach, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749592"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-23","place":"Bellevue , us","start":"2022-07-20","title":"The society for theriogenology and the american college of theriogenologists Annual meeting","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel sperm filtration system based on microfluidics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://clinicaltheriogenology.net/index.php/CT/article/view/9971/15963","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749592","ids":["ku-ff8895b5-110d-4335-afb5-f7508e3372af"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-836B3853A2E3D84F3DB614B8486C9545"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://clinicaltheriogenology.net/index.php/CT/article/view/9971/15963","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Ansager Large Animal Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Veterinary Reproduction and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Motility Count ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Møller","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mette","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"ec5ca085-ed96-4bae-8e16-3db5263fc80d","name":"Christoffersen, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8160-8856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jacob","key":"møllenbachpau","last":"Møllenbach","name":"Møllenbach, Jacob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"260-261","status":"p","title":"Clinical Theriogenology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Other Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","ansager large animal hospital","motility count aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ff8895b5-110d-4335-afb5-f7508e3372af"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A novel sperm filtration system based on microfluidics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749592","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Management of phenylketonuria (PKU) is mainly achieved through dietary control with limited intake of phenylalanine (Phe) from food, supplemented with low protein (LP) food and a mixture of free synthetic (FS) amino acids (AA) (FSAA). Casein glycomacropeptide (CGMP) is a natural peptide released in whey during cheese making by the action of the enzyme chymosin. Because CGMP in its pure form does not contain Phe, it is nutritionally suitable as a supplement in the diet for PKU when enriched with specific AAs. Lacprodan (R) CGMP-20 (= CGMP) used in this study contained only trace amounts of Phe due to minor presence of other proteins/peptides. Objective The aims were to address the following questions in a classical PKU mouse model: Study 1, off diet: Can pure CGMP or CGMP supplemented with Large Neutral Amino Acids (LNAA) as a supplement to normal diet significantly lower the content of Phe in the brain compared to a control group on normal diet, and does supplementation of selected LNAA results in significant lower brain Phe level?. Study 2, on diet: Does a combination of CGMP, essential (non-Phe) EAAs and LP diet, provide similar plasma and brain Phe levels, growth and behavioral skills as a formula which alone consist of FSAA, with a similar composition?. Material and methods 45 female mice homozygous for the Pah(enu2 )mutation were treated for 12 weeks in five different groups; G1(N-CGMP), fed on Normal (N) casein diet (75%) in combination with CGMP (25%); G2 (N-CGMP-LNAA), fed on Normal (N) casein diet (75%) in combination with CGMP (19,7%) and selected LNAA (5,3% Leu, Tyr and Trp); G3 (N), fed on normal casein diet (100%); G4 (CGMP-EAA-LP), fed on CGMP (70,4%) in combination with essential AA (19,6%) and LP diet; G5 (FSAA-LP), fed on FSAA (100%) and LP diet. The following parameters were measured during the treatment period: Plasma AA profiles including Phe and Tyr, growth, food and water intake and number of teeth cut. At the end of the treatment period, a body scan (fat and lean body mass) and a behavioral test (Barnes Maze) were performed. Finally, the brains were examined for content of Phe, Tyr, Trp, dopamine (DA), 3,4dihydroxyphenylacetic acid (DOPAC), serotonin (5-HT) and 5-hydroxyindole-acetic acid (5HIAA), and the bone density and bone mineral content were determined by dual-energy xray absorptiometry. Results Study 1: Mice off diet supplemented with CGMP (G1 (N-CGMP)) or supplemented with CGMP in combination with LNAA (G2 (N-CGMP-LNAA)) had significantly lower Phe in plasma and in the brain compared to mice fed only casein (G3 (N)). Extra LNAA (Tyr, Trp and Leu) to CGMP did not have any significant impact on Phe levels in the plasma and brain, but an increase in serotonin was measured in the brain of G2 mice compared to G1. Study 2: PKU mice fed with mixture of CGMP and EAA as supplement to LP diet (G4 (CGMP-EAA-LP)) demonstrated lower plasma-Phe levels but similar brain- Phe levels and growth as mice fed on an almost identical combination of FSAA (G5 (FSAA-LP)). Conclusion CGMP can be a relevant supplement for the treatment of PKU.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Ahring, Kirsten K.","Dagnæs-Hansen, Frederik","Brüel, Annemarie","Christensen, Mette","Jensen, Erik","Jensen, Thomas G.","Johannsen, Mogens","Johansen, Karen Singers","Lund, Allan M.","Madsen, Jesper Guldsmed","Brøndum-Nielsen, Karen","Pedersen, Michael","Sørensen, Lambert Kristiansen","Kjolby, Mads","Møller, Lisbeth B."],"cuid":["S02-082.65-029146"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ahring, Kirsten K."],"keyword":["Amino Acids blood","Animals","Barnes maze","Bone Density","Bone and Bones diagnostic imaging","Brain","Brain metabolism","Diet","Dietary Supplements","Disease Models Animal","Female","Maze Learning","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","PKU","Peptide Fragments therapeutic use","Plasma","Protein","Serotonin blood","Spatial memory"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of casein glycomacropeptide versus free synthetic amino acids for early treatment of phenylketonuria in a mice model","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0261150","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.65-029146","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8751992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85122635820","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000814820600002","type":"wos"},{"id":"35015767","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e3729999-5996-45fb-b7e6-58ac73919dab","ku-ace6656c-1cab-4d0f-ad43-f4e972fe1818"],"keyword":["Amino Acids/blood","Animals","BARNES MAZE","BRAIN","Bone Density","Bone and Bones/diagnostic imaging","Brain/metabolism","Caseins/therapeutic use","DIET","Dietary Supplements","Disease Models, Animal","Female","GENETIC MOUSE MODEL","Maze Learning","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","PHENYLALANINE-HYDROXYLASE","PKU","PLASMA","PROTEIN","Peptide Fragments/therapeutic use","Phenylalanine Hydroxylase/deficiency","Phenylalanine/analysis","Phenylketonurias/diet therapy","SPATIAL MEMORY","SUPPORTS GROWTH","Serotonin/blood","Tyrosine/blood"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-49ACFDF4C1BAF011B6CEC567549CEF3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/315850235/journal.pone.0261150.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0261150","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Dyrestald"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten K.","key":"ahringkirstenkpau","last":"Ahring","name":"Ahring, Kirsten K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"dagnæshansenfrederikpau","last":"Dagnæs-Hansen","locid":"a8bfdfa1-6563-4519-a5a2-6a0732d549c7","name":"Dagnæs-Hansen, Frederik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annemarie","key":"brüelannemariepau","last":"Brüel","locid":"aba2a94b-2aea-46c0-bdde-8b821e0f9d3f","name":"Brüel, Annemarie","orcid":"0000-0003-4833-0888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mette","key":"christensenmettepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"47671170-00da-4dce-91dd-bc09c06624e3","name":"Christensen, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"jensenerikpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas G.","key":"jensenthomasgpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"13925c3d-69bb-4a6a-b6df-dc8b777d98ce","name":"Jensen, Thomas G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"johannsenmogenspau","last":"Johannsen","locid":"75805917-240a-47fb-8c5f-ef88bb000b43","name":"Johannsen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-2548-7025","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen S.","key":"johansenkarensingerspau","last":"Johansen","locid":"187c523e-58d4-482a-aa24-a86fda46ddf2","name":"Johansen, Karen Singers","name_org":"Johansen, Karen S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan M.","key":"lundallanmpau","last":"Lund","locid":"0ef3787e-801e-4874-b2cd-e1eab5fc2c85","name":"Lund, Allan M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper G.","key":"madsenjesperguldsmedpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"572ce995-a83c-4112-99f0-d1ff626e3582","name":"Madsen, Jesper Guldsmed","name_org":"Madsen, Jesper G.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper G.","key":"madsenjespergpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Jesper G.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen","key":"brondumnielsenkarenpau","last":"Brondum-Nielsen","name":"Brondum-Nielsen, Karen","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"pedersenmichaelpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"871199c4-33bb-4fac-95ef-9a2266f30695","name":"Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1146-0382","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lambert K.","key":"sørensenlambertkristiansenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8cf45c89-ac2d-4ef2-a97c-20eec9f71a8e","name":"Sørensen, Lambert Kristiansen","name_org":"Sørensen, Lambert K.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"kjolbymadspau","last":"Kjolby","locid":"e465630d-67af-43cc-8608-821049586fd8","name":"Kjolby, Mads","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisbeth B.","key":"mollerlisbethbpau","last":"Moller","name":"Moller, Lisbeth B.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35015767"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0261150","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"1","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0261150","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122635820"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e3729999-5996-45fb-b7e6-58ac73919dab","ku-ace6656c-1cab-4d0f-ad43-f4e972fe1818"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of casein glycomacropeptide versus free synthetic amino acids for early treatment of phenylketonuria in a mice model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.65-029146","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Pulmonary congestion is a key component of heart failure (HF) that chest computed tomography (CT) can detect. However, no guideline describes which of many anticipated CT signs are most associated with HF in patients with undifferentiated dyspnea. METHODS: In a prospective observational single-center study, we included consecutive patients ≥ 50 years admitted with acute dyspnea to the emergency department. Patients underwent immediate clinical examination, blood sampling, echocardiography, and CT. Two radiologists independently evaluated all images. Acute HF (AHF) was adjudicated by an expert panel blinded to radiology images. Lasso and logistic regression identified the independent CT signs of AHF. RESULTS: Among 232 patients, 102 (44%) had AHF. Of 18 examined CT signs, 5 were associated with AHF (multivariate odds ratio, 95% confidence interval): enlarged heart (20.38, 6.86-76.16), bilateral interlobular thickening (11.67, 1.78-230.99), bilateral pleural effusion (6.39, 1.98-22.85), and increased vascular diameter (4.49, 1.08-33.92). Bilateral ground-glass opacification (2.07, 0.95-4.52) was a consistent fifth essential sign, although it was only significant in univariate analysis. Eighty-eight (38%) patients had none of the five CT signs corresponding to a 68% specificity and 86% sensitivity for AHF, while two or more of the five CT signs occurred in 68 (29%) patients, corresponding to 97% specificity and 67% sensitivity. A weighted score based on these five CT signs had an 0.88 area under the curve to detect AHF. CONCLUSIONS: Five CT signs seem sufficient to assess the risk of AHF in the acute setting. The absence of these signs indicates a low probability, one sign makes AHF highly probable, and two or more CT signs mean almost certain AHF.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Miger, Kristina Cecilia","Fabricius-Bjerre, Andreas","Overgaard Olesen, Anne Sophie","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Høst, Nis","Køber, Nanna","Abild, Annemette","Winkler Wille, Mathilde Marie","Wamberg, Jesper","Pedersen, Lars","Lawaetz Schultz, Hans Henrik","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Wendelboe Nielsen, Olav"],"cuid":["S02-097.92-000048"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Miger, Kristina Cecilia"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Acute heart failure","Dyspnea","Dyspnea complications","Emergency Service Hospital","Emergency department","Heart Failure diagnosis","Humans","Prospective Studies","Pulmonary congestion","Tomography X Ray Computed","chest computed tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chest computed tomography features of heart failure a prospective observational study in patients with acute dyspnea","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5603/CJ.a2022.0004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.92-000048","identifier":[{"id":"35146729","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128488787","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9007481","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-00bf52dc-6934-45ce-9de9-2fc5d1fe50da","ku-5057fb49-34c6-4fd2-8cbf-a44c9f9a88ea"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Dyspnea/complications","Emergency Service, Hospital","Heart Failure/diagnosis","Humans","Prospective Studies","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","acute heart failure","chest computed tomography","dyspnea","emergency department","pulmonary congestion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A22DAD5B5D8E13A58E04B6A7E36119EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5603/