{"abstract":"Background: Fascicular heart blocks can progress to complete heart blocks, but this risk has not been evaluated in a large general population. Objective: The purpose of this study was to investigate the association between various types of fascicular blocks diagnosed by electrocardiographic (ECG) readings and the risk of incident higher degree atrioventricular block (AVB), syncope, pacemaker implantation, and death. Methods: We studied primary care patients referred for ECG recording between 2001 and 2015. Cox regression models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) as well as absolute risks of cardiovascular outcomes. Results: Of 358,958 primary care patients (median age 54 years; 55% women), 13,636 (3.8%) had any type of fascicular block. Patients were followed up to 15.9 years. We found increasing HRs of incident syncope, pacemaker implantation, and third-degree AVB with increasing complexity of fascicular block. Compared with no block, isolated left anterior fascicular block (LAFB) was associated with 0%–2% increased 10-year risk of developing third-degree AVB (HR 1.6; 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.25–2.05), whereas right bundle branch block combined with LAFB and first-degree AVB was associated with up to 23% increased 10-year risk (HR 11.0; 95% CI 7.7–15.7), depending on age and sex group. Except for left posterior fascicular block (HR 2.09; 95% CI 1.87–2.32), we did not find any relevant associations between fascicular block and death. Conclusion: We found that higher degrees of fascicular blocks were associated with increasing risk of syncope, pacemaker implantation, and complete heart block, but the association with death was negligible.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Nyholm, Benjamin Chris","Ghouse, Jonas","Ji-Young Lee, Christina","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","Pietersen, Adrian","Hansen, Steen Møller","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Køber, Lars","Haunso, Stig","Olesen, Morten Salling","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Graff, Claus","Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Skov, Morten Wagner"],"cuid":["S02-097.96-007317"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nyholm, Benjamin Chris"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Complete heart block","Electrocardiography","Fascicular heart block","Pacemaker implantation","Risk prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fascicular heart blocks and risk of adverse cardiovascular outcomes results from a large primary care population","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85118526253&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.96-007317","identifier":[{"id":"34673253","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85118526253","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-96fde0f7-9e23-4b60-8249-460caa1e8ed7","ku-5b44f1da-1bd3-49f8-9cdd-3ff06053e316"],"keyword":["Complete heart block","Electrocardiography","Fascicular heart block","Pacemaker implantation","Risk prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0BEC459A939B3F385E04683B6978F6B8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen General Practitioners’ Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Benjamin Chris","key":"nyholmpau","last":"Nyholm","locid":"085147aa-512d-4a62-a591-3d6158c03529","name":"Nyholm, Benjamin","name_org":"Nyholm, Benjamin Chris","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"ghousepau","last":"Ghouse","name":"Ghouse, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"jiyoungleepau","last":"Ji-Young Lee","name":"Ji-Young Lee, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina Ji Young","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Christina Ji Young","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter Vibe","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca186b96-3318-42e7-8fe1-34aa087a51b0","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"pietersenpau","last":"Pietersen","name":"Pietersen, Adrian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Steen Møller","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"f71bedc6-3736-4559-b937-6a18e770616e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Salling","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","name_org":"Olesen, Morten Salling","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Gaarsdal","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Bille","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Bille","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Wagner","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Morten Wagner","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34673253"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hrthm.2021.09.041","issn":["15475271","15563871"],"issn_org":["15475271"],"issue":"2","journal":"Heart Rhythm","pages":"252-259","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Heart Rhythm","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118526253"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","copenhagen general practitioners’ laboratory"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-96fde0f7-9e23-4b60-8249-460caa1e8ed7","ku-5b44f1da-1bd3-49f8-9cdd-3ff06053e316"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fascicular heart blocks and risk of adverse cardiovascular outcomes : Results from a large primary care population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.96-007317","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Grazing herbivores may affect soil microbial communities indirectly by impacting soil structure and vegetation composition. In high arctic environments, this impact is poorly elucidated, while having potentially wide-reaching effects on the ecosystem. This study examines how a key arctic herbivore, the muskox Ovibos moschatus, affects the soil microbial community in a high arctic fen. Environmental DNA was extracted from soil samples taken from grazed control plots and from muskox exclosures established 5 years prior. We sequenced amplicons of the 16S rRNA gene to provide insight into the microbial communities. We found that in the grazed control plots, microbial communities exhibited high evenness and displayed highly similar overall diversity. In plots where muskoxen had been excluded, microbial diversity was significantly reduced, and had more uneven intra-sample populations and overall lower ecological richness and evenness. We observed that the composition of microbial communities in grazed soils were significantly affected by the presence of muskoxen, as seen by elevated relative abundances of Bacteroides and Firmicutes, two major phyla found in muskox faeces. Furthermore, an increase in relative abundance of bacteria involved in degradation of recalcitrant carbohydrates and cycling of nitrogen was observed in grazed soil. Ungrazed soils displayed increased abundances of bacteria potentially involved in anaerobic oxidation of methane, whereas some methanogens were more abundant in grazed soils. This corroborates a previous finding that methane emissions are higher in arctic fens under muskox grazing. Our results show that the presence of large herbivores stimulates soil microbial diversity and has a homogenizing influence on the inter-species dynamics in soil microbial communities. The findings of this study, thus, improve our understanding of the effect of herbivore grazing on arctic ecosystems and the derived methane cycling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aggerbeck, Marie Rønne","Nielsen, Tue Kjærgaard","Mosbacher, Jesper Bruun","Schmidt, Niels Martin","Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-017123"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["16S amplicon sequencing","Arctic ecology","Environmental Microbiology","Methane emission","Microbial diversity","Muskox","muskox Ovibos moschatus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"muskoxen homogenise soil microbial communities and affect the abundance of methanogens and methanotrophs","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.153877","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-017123","identifier":[{"id":"000790354600006","type":"wos"},{"id":"85126509355","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35218841","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3cdf86d0-f1b9-45ff-b057-c4c8debf4109","ku-80c0f300-575f-41cc-8677-581ef7b60997"],"keyword":["16S amplicon sequencing","Arctic ecology","Environmental microbiology","Methane emission","Microbial diversity","Muskox ()","Muskox (Ovibos moschatus)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CBCA0A9394C628A292DF99452EF2F4A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/333666310/1_s2.0_S004896972200969X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/306148191/1_s2.0_S004896972200969X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.153877","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Rønne","key":"aggerbeckpau","last":"Aggerbeck","locid":"a3fe8d55-895e-4b1e-b308-548f83b5ee98","name":"Aggerbeck, Marie Rønne","orcid":"0000-0003-4851-2091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tue Kjærgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a3eb9b69-4a4e-4ab6-9921-b2b3f4abfbd7","name":"Nielsen, Tue Kjærgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6610-8450","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bruun","key":"mosbacherpau","last":"Mosbacher","locid":"9c13fa64-c01e-45a5-a610-91a95c7c080b","name":"Mosbacher, Jesper Bruun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Hestbjerg","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2e041f09-bf9d-434a-b82a-d6e2763bb262","name":"Hansen, Lars H.","name_org":"Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","orcid":"0000-0003-0027-1524","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35218841"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.153877","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"153877","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"827"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126509355"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3cdf86d0-f1b9-45ff-b057-c4c8debf4109","ku-80c0f300-575f-41cc-8677-581ef7b60997"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Muskoxen homogenise soil microbial communities and affect the abundance of methanogens and methanotrophs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-017123","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Air pollution, road traffic noise and lack of greenness coexist in urban environments and have all been associated with type 2 diabetes. We aimed to investigate how these co-exposures were associated with type 2 diabetes in a multi-exposure perspective. Methods: We estimated 5-year residential mean exposure to fine particles (PM2.5), ultrafine particles (UFP), elemental carbon (EC), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and road traffic noise at the most (LdenMax) and least (LdenMin) exposed facade for all persons aged > 50 years living in Denmark in 2005 to 2017. For each air pollutant, we estimated total concentrations and traffic contributions. Based on land use maps, we estimated proportion of green and non-green space within 150 and 1000 m of all residences. In total, 1.9 million persons were included and 128,358 developed type 2 diabetes during follow-up. We performed analyses using Cox proportional hazards models, with adjustment for individual and neighborhood-level sociodemographic co-variates. Results: In single-pollutant models, all air pollutants, noise and lack of green space were associated with higher risk of diabetes. In two-, three- and four-pollutant analyses of the air pollutants, only UFP and NO2 remained associated with higher diabetes risk in all models. LdenMax, LdenMin and the two proxies of green space remained associated with diabetes in two-pollutant models of, respectively, noise and green space. In a multi-pollutant analysis, we found hazard ratios (95 % confidence intervals) per interquartile range of 1.021 (1.005; 1.038) for UFP, 1.012 (0.996; 1.028) for NO2, 1.022 (1.012; 1.033) for LdenMin, 1.013 (1.004; 1.022) for LdenMax, and 1.038 (1.031; 1.044) and 1.018 (1.010; 1.025) for lack of green space within, respectively, 150 m and 1000 m, and a cumulative risk index of 1.131 (1.113; 1.149). Conclusions: Air pollution, road traffic noise and lack of green space were independently associated with higher risk of type 2 diabetes.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Sørensen, Mette","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Brandt, Jørgen","Frohn, Lise Marie","Ketzel, Matthias","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Im, Ulas","Khan, Jibran","Münzel, Thomas","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-027275"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Mette"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","University Medical Center Mainz","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Green space","Multi pollutant","Road traffic noise","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollution road traffic noise and lack of greenness and risk of type 000000000002 diabetes a multi exposure prospective study covering denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2022.107570","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-027275","identifier":[{"id":"85142429625","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36334460","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c95d54a7-28aa-4059-9960-3e806709ae25","ruc-16cbdf8a-7824-469d-bc07-cae374953ef3"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Green space","Multi-pollutant","Road traffic noise","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C7D2036146DA1E9B8394686AFFEEFBC4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2022.107570","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/86012089/1_s2.0_S0160412022004974_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"university medical center mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Mainz","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla A.","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise M.","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","name_org":"Frohn, Lise M.","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"münzelpau","last":"Münzel","name":"Münzel, Thomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36334460"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2022.107570","issn":["01604120","18736750"],"issn_org":["01604120"],"journal":"Environment International","paperid":"107570","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Environment International","volume":"170"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142429625"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c95d54a7-28aa-4059-9960-3e806709ae25","ruc-16cbdf8a-7824-469d-bc07-cae374953ef3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Air pollution, road traffic noise and lack of greenness and risk of type 2 diabetes : A multi-exposure prospective study covering Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-027275","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"(1) The current literature contains several studies investigating the correlation between dual-energy-derived iodine concentration (IC) and positron emission tomography (PET)-derived Flourodeoxyglucose (18F-FDG) uptake in patients with non-small-cell lung cancer (NSCLC). In previously published studies, either the entire tumor volume or a region of interest containing the maximum IC or 18F-FDG was assessed. However, the results have been inconsistent. The objective of this study was to correlate IC with FDG both within the entire volume and regional sub-volumes of primary tumors in patients with NSCLC. (2) In this retrospective study, a total of 22 patients with NSCLC who underwent both dual-energy CT (DE-CT) and 18F-FDG PET/CT were included. A region of interest (ROI) encircling the entire primary tumor was delineated, and a rigid registration of the DE-CT, iodine maps and FDG images was performed for the ROI. The correlation between tumor measurements and area-specific measurements of ICpeak and the peak standardized uptake value (SUVpeak) was found. Finally, a correlation between tumor volume and the distance between SUVpeak and ICpeak centroids was found. (3) For the entire tumor, moderate-to-strong correlations were found between SUVmax and ICmax (R = 0.62, p = 0.002), and metabolic tumor volume vs. total iodine content (R = 0.91, p < 0.001), respectively. For local tumor sub-volumes, a negative correlation was found between ICpeak and SUVpeak (R = −0.58, p = 0.0046). Furthermore, a strong correlation was found between the tumor volume and the distance in millimeters between SUVpeak and ICpeak centroids (R = 0.81, p < 0.0001). (4) In patients with NSCLC, high FDG uptakes and high DE-CT-derived iodine concentrations correlated on a whole-tumor level, but the peak areas were positioned at different locations within the tumor. 18F-FDG PET/CT and DE-CT provide complementary information and might represent different underlying patho-physiologies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Andersen, Michael Brun","Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","Thygesen, Jesper","Kruis, Matthijs Ferdinand","Hjorthaug, Karin","Rasmussen, Finn","Nijkamp, Jasper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-666147"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Michael Brun"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Koninklijke Philips N.V.","Philips B.V. (Netherlands)"],"keyword":["Computed tomography","F Flourodeoxyglucose PET CT","Lung cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of correlation between dual energy ct de ct derived iodine concentration and local flourodeoxyglucose fdg uptake in patients with primary non small cell lung cancer","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/tomography8040149","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-666147","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9326656","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135106198","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35894014","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2b999df0-d78f-4df0-a6fc-deb711e76f43","ku-bce3538a-a989-43c4-80d1-37c9a5794e01"],"keyword":["F-Flourodeoxyglucose PET/CT","computed tomography","lung cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7D31CD27FC0376173D18D66640949A08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/tomography8040149","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"philips b v","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Philips B.V. (Netherlands)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"koninklijke philips n v","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Koninklijke Philips N.V.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Brun","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f1d3f9b4-8b12-4c15-b083-e46d121b1d6d","name":"Andersen, Michael Brun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aska","key":"drljevicnielsenpau","last":"Drljevic-Nielsen","locid":"10a1cade-abdc-4a12-821b-9c94f3f7ddfd","name":"Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"1ec56c42-5347-4630-9296-8c9e260a862d","name":"Thygesen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthijs Ferdinand","key":"kruispau","last":"Kruis","name":"Kruis, Matthijs Ferdinand","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"hjorthaugpau","last":"Hjorthaug","locid":"4051e1c3-8359-4005-b185-25bd7e89fe9c","name":"Hjorthaug, Karin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1c4dadf5-d001-4c6c-9f23-347af298c53d","name":"Rasmussen, Finn","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jasper Albertus","key":"nijkamppau","last":"Nijkamp","locid":"673da4a7-e330-498b-bbb8-52f6505b637a","name":"Nijkamp, Jasper","name_org":"Nijkamp, Jasper Albertus","orcid":"0000-0001-7523-5881","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35894014"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/tomography8040149","issn":["23791381","2379139X"],"issn_org":["23791381"],"issue":"4","journal":"Tomography","pages":"1770-1780","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Tomography","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135106198"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2b999df0-d78f-4df0-a6fc-deb711e76f43","ku-bce3538a-a989-43c4-80d1-37c9a5794e01"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Assessment of Correlation between Dual-Energy Ct (De-Ct)-Derived Iodine Concentration and Local Flourodeoxyglucose (Fdg) Uptake in Patients with Primary Non-Small-Cell Lung Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-666147","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Night shift work often implies shorter sleep duration and this can lead to sleepiness, which has been associated with an increased risk of accidents and injuries. The aim is to study how the number of consecutive night shifts affects self-reported sleepiness. PARTICIPANTS AND METHODS: The study was a quasi-experimental, within-subject crossover study with 73 police officers. Three work schedules of two, four, and seven consecutive night shifts followed by the same number of recovery days, i.e., days worked or days off, was performed by all participants. Sleepiness was self-reported using the Karolinska sleepiness scale (KSS) every fourth hour on the last night shift and the last recovery day in each sequence. RESULTS: We observed differences in the level of sleepiness between recovery days and night shift days but no differences in the pattern of sleepiness levels on night shift days in the different work schedules. The highest levels of KSS were observed before bedtime (at 07:00 after a night shift and 23:00 on a recovery day). CONCLUSION: The number of consecutive night shifts did not affect the self-reported levels of self-reported sleepiness among Danish police officers.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","Nielsen, Helena Breth","Sallinen, Mikael","Kristiansen, Jesper","Hansen, Åse Marie","Garde, Anne Helene"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-769015"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Institute of Occupational Health","Finnish Institute of Occupational Health, Helsinki, Finland."],"keyword":["Arbejdstid","Søvn"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Department of Public Health, Centre for Health and Society, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self reported sleepiness after 000000000002 000000000004 and 000000000007 consecutive night shifts and recovery days in danish police officers","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph191710527","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-769015","identifier":[{"id":"36078243","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9518407","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85137543175","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8694441e-210d-40f3-a2b2-5f76078f6f5b","nfa-3c5e7603-7b19-452a-9a23-e63375c86608"],"keyword":["Arbejdstid","Søvn"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C5741F2CCC9A224433212CE31EC9D7A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/319119928/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph191710527","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"finnish institute of occupational health","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Institute of Occupational Health","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"finnish institute of occupational health helsinki finland","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Institute of Occupational Health, Helsinki, Finland.","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Public Health, Centre for Health and Society, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Aarrebo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena Breth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"47ae35e5-47cc-47ff-b81d-12e2a0f4145d","name":"Nielsen, Helena Breth","orcid":"0000-0001-6409-5166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Mikael","key":"sallinenpau","last":"Sallinen","name":"Sallinen, Mikael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5b151ef4-abb8-4673-9522-abc399e62fea","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4075-3918","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"64b13e21-4e8a-4454-b945-766da6180377","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36078243"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijerph191710527","issn":["16604601","16617827"],"issn_org":["16617827"],"issue":"17","journal":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","pages":"10527","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137543175"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8694441e-210d-40f3-a2b2-5f76078f6f5b","nfa-3c5e7603-7b19-452a-9a23-e63375c86608"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Self-Reported Sleepiness after 2, 4, and 7 Consecutive Night Shifts and Recovery Days in Danish Police Officers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-769015","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Management decisions are considered important for the performance of public organizations, but how does information about performance influence management decision-making? Developed from Simon's notion of bounded rationality, the behavioral model of performance-based learning suggests that managers adjust their understanding of organizational problems, search for information, and consider initiating change when their organization performs below aspirations. In this paper, we offer experimental evidence of how performance information affects the attitudes and decision-making of public managers. We leverage two experiments conducted among managers in public education. Study 1 uses a question-order experiment to prime only treated respondents to consider performance, whereas study 2 uses treatments with high- and low-performance signals. We find that low performance affects problem focus but not managers' intention to conduct innovative search. We also find that low-performance signals increase preferences for immediate performance-oriented changes but not for other types of changes. We discuss the implications for management decision-making. Evidence for Practice: Performance information holds the potential to generate organizational learning and inform public managers' decisions about important problems, priorities, and organizational change. Public managers become more focused on direct performance-oriented changes when performance is low, whereas high performance lets them engage in other types of changes. Performance information alone does not ensure that public managers are focused on generating innovative solutions to performance problems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Jesper Asring Jessen","Nielsen, Poul Aaes"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-792888"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Poul Aaes"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how do public managers learn from performance information experimental evidence on problem focus innovative search and change","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/puar.13533","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-792888","identifier":[{"id":"85134201140","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-63246923-7487-4724-be39-15287d084a4a","au-b619926d-9c36-45ab-88e5-4a00b3174dee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E923D74E2DCFC65FBDAA5582710B0A5B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/puar.13533","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/365088502/Public_Administration_Review_-_2022_-_Hansen_-_How_Do_Public_Managers_Learn_from_Performance_Information_Experimental.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Public Administration & Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Asring Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5262d709-71df-4ec8-a779-78de00d7eb9c","name":"Hansen, Jesper Asring Jessen","orcid":"0000-0003-0267-1222","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Aaes","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"652b9905-c3dd-43c8-83f5-138251df217d","name":"Nielsen, Poul Aaes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/puar.13533","issn":["00333352","15406210"],"issn_org":["00333352"],"issue":"5","journal":"Public Administration Review","pages":"946-957","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Public Administration Review","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134201140"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-63246923-7487-4724-be39-15287d084a4a","au-b619926d-9c36-45ab-88e5-4a00b3174dee"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How Do Public Managers Learn from Performance Information? Experimental Evidence on Problem Focus, Innovative Search, and Change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-792888","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND. New therapies have emerged for metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), though corresponding imaging markers are lacking. Dual-layer spectral-detector CT (DLCT) can quantify iodine concentration (IC) and effective atomic number (Zeffective), providing information beyond attenuation that may indicate mRCC prognosis. OBJECTIVE. The purpose of our study was to assess the utility of the DLCT-derived parameters IC and Zeffective for predicting mRCC treatment response and survival. METHODS. This prospective study enrolled 120 participants with mRCC from January 2018 to January 2020 who underwent DLCT, with reconstruction of IC and Zeffective maps, before treatment initiation. Final analysis included 115 participants (86 men, 29 women; median age, 65.1 years), incorporating 313 target lesions that were clinically selected using RECIST version 1.1 on arterial phase acquisitions of the chest and abdomen. Semiautomatic volumetric segmentation was performed of the target lesions. Voxels from all lesions were combined to a single histogram per patient. The median IC and Zeffective of the combined histograms were recorded. Measurements above and below the cohort median values were considered high and low, respectively. Univariable associations were explored between IC and Zeffective with objective response rate (ORR), progression-free survival (PFS), and overall survival (OS). Multivariable associations were explored between IC and ORR, PFS, and OS, adjusting for treatment (tyrosine kinase inhibitor vs checkpoint immunotherapy) and significant univariable predictors (including tumor histology and International Metastatic Renal Cell Carcinoma Database Consortium [IMDC] risk factors). RESULTS. At baseline, median IC was 2.26 mg/mL, and median Zeffective was 8.49. In univariable analysis, high IC and high Zeffective were associated with better ORR (both, odds ratio [OR] = 4.35; p = .001), better PFS (both, hazard ratio [HR] = 0.51; p = .004), and better OS (both, HR = 0.38; p < .001). In multivariable models, high IC independently predicted better ORR (OR = 4.35, p = .001), better PFS (HR = 0.51, p = .004), and better OS (HR = 0.37, p < .001); neutrophilia independently predicted worse PFS (HR = 2.10, p = .004) and worse OS (HR = 2.28, p = .003). The estimated C-index for predicting OS using IMDC risk factors alone was 0.650 versus 0.687 when incorporating high attenuation and 0.692 when incorporating high IC or high Zeffective. CONCLUSION. High IC and high Zeffective are significant predictors of better treatment response and survival in mRCC. CLINICAL IMPACT. Baseline DLCT parameters may improve current mRCC prognostic models. TRIAL REGISTRATION. ClinicalTrials.gov NCT03616951","author_count":7,"contributors":["Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","Donskov, Frede","Mains, Jill Rachel","Andersen, Michael Brun","Thorup, Kennet","Thygesen, Jesper","Rasmussen, Finn"],"cuid":["S03-099.37-672581"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska"],"keyword":["Aged","Carcinoma Renal Cell diagnostic imaging","Disease Free Survival","Female","Hounsfield units HU","Humans","Iodine concentration","Kidney Neoplasms diagnostic imaging","Male","Metastatic renal cell carcinoma","Prognosis","Prognostic factor","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Tomography X Ray Computed","Treatment Outcome","effective atomic number Z","spectral dual layer CT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic utility of parameters derived from pretreatment dual layer spectral detector ct in patients with metastatic renal cell carcinoma","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85129345145","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.37-672581","identifier":[{"id":"34910540","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129345145","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-23e48e58-111b-4b02-8a2c-c3e161d93e3b","ku-69ba1d2b-2223-42ad-b2e5-b314784edb97","sdu-3b3cd72b-cbd6-46d6-bc29-6832566efbea"],"keyword":["Aged","Carcinoma, Renal Cell/diagnostic imaging","Disease-Free Survival","Female","Hounsfield units (HU)","Humans","Kidney Neoplasms/diagnostic imaging","Male","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","Treatment Outcome","effective atomic number (Z)","iodine concentration","metastatic renal cell carcinoma","prognostic factor","spectral dual-layer CT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-CCCA591F13F1D0642FC38EC28DD60AD6"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev og Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aska","key":"drljevicnielsenpau","last":"Drljevic-Nielsen","locid":"10a1cade-abdc-4a12-821b-9c94f3f7ddfd","name":"Drljevic-Nielsen, Aska","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frede","key":"donskovpau","last":"Donskov","locid":"51fdc715-1b4d-4639-9b26-5dbf474dbec7","name":"Donskov, Frede","orcid":"0000-0002-8449-863X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jill Rachel","key":"mainspau","last":"Mains","locid":"aa8803bb-8cbb-44dc-ad98-039b03101780","name":"Mains, Jill Rachel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Michael Brun","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2011438d-efaa-4cd0-a092-8e9970e0b885","name":"Andersen, Michael Brun","rank":4,"rol