orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"haarbopau","last":"Haarbo","name":"Haarbo, Jens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Margrethe","key":"thøgersenpau","last":"Thøgersen","locid":"040c49e1-e9f1-4e74-8cd0-4a9ef9fb7006","name":"Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Jakob","key":"thunepau","last":"Thune","name":"Thune, Jens Jakob","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35106935"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ehf2.13810","issn":["20555822"],"issue":"2","journal":"ESC Heart Failure","pages":"1287-1293","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"ESC Heart Failure","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124032505"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-78a9e5d1-20ed-40a2-a12b-497798fc2644","au-18066e0c-1b25-4ce2-a98e-17bec6432e5f","ku-41a7e3e1-bf37-4025-a696-d98f023368bc","sdu-3c187a6f-78f7-474f-994d-4b9561ed682d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of implantable cardioverter-defibrillators in patients with non-ischaemic systolic heart failure and concurrent coronary atherosclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.64-005863","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: In this extended follow-up study of the DANISH (Danish Study to Assess the Efficacy of Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillators in Patients with Non-ischemic Systolic Heart Failure on Mortality) trial, adding 4 years of additional follow-up, we examined the effect of implantable cardioverter-defibrillator (ICD) implantation according to baseline N-terminal pro–B-type natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) level. Background: In the DANISH trial, NT-proBNP level at baseline appeared to modify the response to ICD implantation. Methods: In the DANISH trial, 1,116 patients with nonischemic systolic HF were randomized to receive an ICD (N = 556) or usual clinical care (N = 550). Outcomes were analyzed according to NT-proBNP levels (below/above median) at baseline. The primary outcome was death from any cause. Results: All 1,116 patients in the DANISH trial had an available NT-proBNP measurement at baseline (median: 1,177 pg/mL; range: 200-22,918 pg/mL). There was a trend toward a reduction in all-cause death with ICD implantation, compared with usual clinical care, in patients with NT-proBNP levels lower than the median (HR: 0.75 [95% CI: 0.55-1.03]), but not in those with higher NT-proBNP levels (HR: 0.95 [95% CI: 0.74-1.21]) (Pinteraction = 0.28). Similarly, ICD implantation significantly reduced the rate of cardiovascular (CV) and sudden cardiovascular death (SCD) in patients with NT-proBNP levels lower than the median (CV death, HR: 0.69 [95% CI: 0.47-1.00]; SCD, HR: 0.37 [95% CI: 0.19-0.75]), but not in those with higher levels (CV death, HR: 0.94 [95% CI: 0.70-1.25]; SCD, HR: 0.86 [95% CI: 0.49-1.51]) (Pinteraction = 0.20 and 0.08 for CV death and SCD, respectively). Conclusions: Lower baseline NT-proBNP levels could identify patients with nonischemic systolic HF who may derive benefit from ICD implantation. (Danish Study to Assess the Efficacy of Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillators in Patients with Non-ischemic Systolic Heart Failure on Mortality [DANISH]; NCT00542945)","author_count":21,"contributors":["Butt, Jawad H.","Yafasova, Adelina","Elming, Marie B.","Dixen, Ulrik","Nielsen, Jens C.","Haarbo, Jens","Videbæk, Lars","Korup, Eva","Bruun, Niels Eske","Eiskjær, Hans","Brandes, Axel","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Gustafsson, Finn","Egstrup, Kenneth","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Høfsten, Dan E.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Pehrson, Steen","Thune, Jens Jakob","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S04-099.98-011917"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Butt, Jawad H."],"keyword":["Heart failure","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Mortality","N terminal pro B type natriuretic peptide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nt probnp and icd in nonischemic systolic heart failure extended follow up of the danish trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381636495/Manuscript_JACC_HF_2_clean1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Dr Butt has received advisory board honoraria from Bayer, outside the submitted work. Dr Nielsen is supported by a grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF16OC0018658) outside this work. Dr Bruun has received funding from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, the Augustinus Foundation, the Kaj Hansen Foundation, and from Health Insurance Denmark outside this work. Dr Brandes has received a research grant from Theravance and the Regions of Southern Denmark and Zealand; has received speaker honoraria from Bayer, Boehringer Ingelheim, and Bristol-Myers Squibb; and has received a travel grant from Biotronik outside this work. Dr Gustafsson has received speaker honorarium from Orion, Novartis, and Vifor Pharma; and has received advisory board honorarium from Abott, Bayer, Alnylam, Ionis, Pfizer, Corvia, and Pharmacosmos. Dr Hassager has received speaker honorarium from Abiomed. Dr Svendsen has received speaker honorarium from Medtronic. Dr Pehrson has received lecture fees from Abbott, Bristol Myers Squibb, and AstraZeneca. Dr Køber has received speaker honorarium from Novartis, AstraZeneca, Boehringer, and Novo Nordisk. All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose."],"id":"S04-099.98-011917","identifier":[{"id":"85124773259","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35241243","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-fa16bdcd-91a1-4f57-9b40-6ec101935df0","au-ea6d2c19-75ac-4f78-9f8f-aed30242bc06","ku-0bc6aaa2-5cc1-48d8-9cc2-bd29d0784163","sdu-0bd12924-ad05-4f46-9843-fc50ef434101"],"keyword":["N-terminal pro–B-type natriuretic peptide","heart failure","implantable cardioverter-defibrillator","mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-7175900B58B2AEBB1F4067D9BA7EAE8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381636495/Manuscript_JACC_HF_2_clean1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"]