{"abstract":"Sound zone technology has been actively developed for more than two decades with a promise to provide users with personal sound without wearing headphones. In this paper, we build on this development from the perspective of interaction design in two ways. First, we explore the relation between sound zones and the acoustic environment, referred to as a soundscape, through a theoretical exploration of related research in both areas. Second, we present eight interaction design challenges resulting from this. Four different interaction approaches to potentially take on the challenges are sketched and discussed in a workshop and collecting qualitative data from the process. These approaches include tangible representation, light projections, familiar objects, and handheld devices. We group the approaches as visual displays, and user-centred and sound zone-centred interfaces. Overall, our research provides a new perspective on interaction with sound zone technology with specific outlines for further research in this area.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Stine Schmieg","Nielsen, Peter Axel","Kjeldskov, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091500"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Handheld","Interaction design","Projection","Sound zone","Sound zones","Soundscape","Tangible","Wearable"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for domestic sound zone interaction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85082102471&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091500","identifier":[{"id":"85082102471","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8ea0a32e-3a05-4c33-9697-b05704f8d7fc"],"keyword":["Handheld","Interaction Design","Projection","Sound Zones","Sound zone","Soundscape","Tangible","Wearable"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F210ED10AD075E7E0EE66EEA84C62A0D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Schmieg","key":"lundgaardpau","last":"Lundgaard","locid":"04546f61-a1e4-4f11-90db-a305c42e53b4","name":"Johansen, Stine Schmieg","name_org":"Lundgaard, Stine Schmieg","orcid":"0000-0002-8451-5444","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Axel","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d5302c36-a512-42d6-8ab5-32d3f7da115e","name":"Nielsen, Peter Axel","orcid":"0000-0002-0282-7445","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"kjeldskovpau","last":"Kjeldskov","locid":"90f5514b-34fa-4d01-98dd-ed6166dd1489","name":"Kjeldskov, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7990-4229","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00779-020-01387-2","issn":["16174909","16174917"],"issn_org":["16174917"],"issue":"4","journal":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","pages":"1225-1236","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082102471"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8ea0a32e-3a05-4c33-9697-b05704f8d7fc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Designing for domestic sound zone interaction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091500","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Camelid single-domain antibody fragments, also called nanobodies, constitute a class of binders that are small in size (~15 kDa) and possess antigen-binding properties similar to their antibody counterparts. Facile production of recombinant nanobodies in several microorganisms has made this class of binders attractive within the field of molecular imaging. Particularly, their use in super-resolution microscopy has improved the spatial resolution of molecular targets due to a smaller linkage error. In single-molecule localization microscopy techniques, the effective spatial resolution can be further enhanced by site-specific fluorescent labeling of nanobodies owing to a more homogeneous protein-to-fluorophore stoichiometry, reduced background staining and a known distance between dye and epitope. Here, we present a protocol for site-specific bioconjugation of DNA oligonucleotides to three distinct nanobodies expressed with an N- or C-terminal unnatural amino acid, 4-azido-L-phenylalanine (pAzF). Using copper-free click chemistry, the nanobody-oligonucleotide conjugation reactions were efficient and yielded highly pure bioconjugates. Target binding was retained in the bioconjugates, as demonstrated by bio-layer interferometry binding assays and the super-resolution microscopy technique, DNA points accumulation for imaging in nanoscale topography (PAINT). This method for site-specific protein-oligonucleotide conjugation can be further extended for applications within drug delivery and molecular targeting where site-specificity and stoichiometric control are required.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Teodori, Laura","Omer, Marjan","Märcher, Anders","Skaanning, Mads Koch","Andersen, Veronica Liv","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Oldenburg, Emil","Lin, Yuchen","Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","Kjems, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137088"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kjems, Jørgen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"site specific nanobody oligonucleotide conjugation for super resolution imaging","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14440/jbm.2022.381","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137088","identifier":[{"id":"35510035","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9058258","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0d88efd5-6a1f-4c48-a7e7-c0f7ac148932"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2B06741609BC8E443CDDA8BF3FB85679"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14440/jbm.2022.381","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335432874/MS381.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura","key":"teo