"Agriculture, Ecosystems & Environment","paperid":"107746","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Agriculture, Ecosystems & Environment","volume":"325"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118536071"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a210c720-cf80-4ac8-9431-a03531560204"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Barnacle goose <i>Branta leucopsis </i>derogation shooting effort in relation to abundance and vulnerable crops","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-221691","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Anthropogenic airborne pollution has lowered soil pH for decades, while partial chemical recovery has been documented in recent years in northwest Europe; however, it remains uncertain how naturally acidic ecosystems, such as dry heaths, have responded. Here, we attempt to elucidate scale changes over decades in surface soil pH in dry heath ecosystems by encompassing 1336 historic measurements from 120 sites covering a time span from 1920 to 2015, an unmatched timespan. The data set had soil pH (1:1 soil–water) ranging from 3.06 to 6.38 with a mean of 3.86 ± 0.01. When analyzing the data in a change point model, initially a minor non-significant drop in pH (0.99) was seen before the change point followed by a weak non-significant positive trend. This may indicate that either there was a drop from the 1920s to 1942, after which soil pH probably increased, or that there has been no change in the entire period. We propose that the change is related to either (1) that the sulphur deposition peaked in the early 1980s and, as result, sulphur deposition decreased, which caused a small recovery of soil pH, or (2) that anthropogenic acidification did not significantly change soil pH in this naturally very acidic ecosystem.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kaae, Mathias Emil","Petersen, Asger Ryge","Kristiansen, Søren Munch","Nielsen, Knud Erik","Bak, Jesper Leth","Damgaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232277"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Damgaard, Christian"],"keyword":["Change point model","Heathlands","Soil acidification","Soil pH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"soil acidification on dry heaths in jutland denmark trends in ph over a century","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85122919785","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-232277","identifier":[{"id":"85122919785","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000742647700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-b472c288-1392-45cb-b5cb-e2b3360dd9fd"],"keyword":["Change point model","Dry heaths","Heathlands","Soil acidification","Soil pH"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5EA8424C32818C76A5CAA868D2BA78CD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Emil","key":"kaaepau","last":"Kaae","locid":"f7670497-1fbd-486f-9538-57ec5c75156b","name":"Kaae, Mathias Emil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Ryge","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"f21a5883-ff16-4b2d-8a47-562a5ec51f48","name":"Petersen, Asger Ryge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Munch","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Erik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b349ca79-38d0-4c9b-84d2-7eb4defb1240","name":"Nielsen, Knud Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Leth","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"72bda0b4-7b42-