{"abstract":"AIMS: The aim of this study was to compare short- and long-term risk of sudden cardiac death (SCD) among persons aged 18-49 years with and without chronic kidney disease (CKD). METHODS AND RESULTS: Using Danish nationwide health registries, all persons aged 18-49 years diagnosed with earlier stages of CKD or chronic kidney failure from 1 July 1995 through 2009 were identified. Non-exposed subjects matched on sex and birth-year were identified. All SCD in the Danish population aged 18-49 years in 2000-2009 have previously been identified using information from the Danish nationwide health registries, death certificates, and autopsy reports. In total, 9308 incident cases of earlier stage CKD and 1233 incident cases of chronic kidney failure were included. Among patients with earlier stage CKD, the absolute risk of SCD 1, 5, and 10 years after diagnosis was 0.14%, 0.37%, and 0.68%, respectively. Compared with age- and sex-matched subjects the corresponding relative risk (RR) was 20.3 [95% confidence interval (CI) 8.4-48.8], 7.1 (95% CI 4.2-12.0), and 6.1 (95% CI 3.8-9.7), respectively. Among patients with chronic kidney failure, the absolute 1-, 5-, and 10-year risk of SCD was 0.17%, 0.56%, and 2.07%, respectively. The corresponding RR was 12.5 (95% CI 1.4-111.6), 7.9 (95% CI 2.3-27.0), and 10.1 (95% CI 4.5-22.6). CONCLUSION: Persons with earlier stage CKD and chronic kidney failure had increased risk of SCD compared with the background population with a 6- to 20-fold increased risk of SCD. These findings underline the importance of early cardiovascular risk monitoring and assessment in persons with CKD.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Svane, Jesper","Nielsen, Jakob Lund","Stampe, Niels Kjær","Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","Garcia, Rodrigue","Risgaard, Bjarke","Gislason, Gunnar","Winkel, Bo Gregers","Lynge, Thomas Hadberg","Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-766359"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Svane, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nationwide study of mortality and sudden cardiac death in young persons diagnosed with chronic kidney disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85168611543","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-766359","identifier":[{"id":"35373838","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85168611543","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-edd1cf95-6db1-4d02-8125-b38a671e1e59"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B465C21857EA5F9E3DE905DB0D5E83BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-HJER","l3nn":"Danish Heart Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Heart Foundation","namevar":["Hjerteforeningen"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-HJER","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Lund","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jakob Lund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Kjær","key":"stampepau","last":"Stampe","name":"Stampe, Niels Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rodrigue","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","name":"Garcia, Rodrigue","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke","key":"risgaardpau","last":"Risgaard","name":"Risgaard, Bjarke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar Hilmar","key":"gislasonpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"4d541da8-6a3b-4dbc-a5b8-d7576a86790d","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","name_org":"Gislason, Gunnar Hilmar","orcid":"0000-0002-0548-402X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo Gregers","key":"winkelpau","last":"Winkel","name":"Winkel, Bo Gregers","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Hadberg","key":"lyngepau","last":"Lynge","name":"Lynge, Thomas Hadberg","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35373838"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euac032","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"10","journal":"Europace","pages":"1599-1607","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","title_org":"EP - Europace","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168611543"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-edd1cf95-6db1-4d02-8125-b38a671e1e59"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Nationwide study of mortality and sudden cardiac death in young persons diagnosed with chronic kidney disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-766359","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Organ preserving treatment strategies based on chemoradiotherapy may spare rectal cancer patients of major surgery and stoma. We suggest substantially improved tumor control by increasing the radiotherapy dose, without significant increase in the rate of late effects. We designed a prospective phase II trial to test high-dose radiotherapy of low rectal cancer for organ preservation in a multicenter setting. Methods: We enrolled patients with localized T1-3 N0-1 M0 rectal cancer within 6 cm from the anal verge and in performance status 0-2. Any N1-nodes had to be at the level of the tumor and included in the primary tumor-volume. Radiotherapy consisted of 62 Gy to the tumor and 50.4 Gy to the regional lymph nodes, delivered in 28 fractions using intensity modulated radiation therapy and daily image guidance. Capecitabine 825 mg/m2 BID. Patients with clinical complete response (cCR) 6–12 weeks after end of treatment were allocated to follow-up. Surgery was offered only in case of residual cancer or later re-growth. The primary endpoint was the proportion of patients with locoregional tumor control after two years by chemoradiation alone. Secondary endpoints included long-term side effects (CTCAE grading), cCR, rate of distant metastases, and overall survival. Results: Three Danish centers enrolled 107 patients between 2015 and 2019. Baseline classifications were T1/T2/T3 and N1 in 15%/54%/31% and 29%, respectively. The median age was 71 years and 64% were male. 92 (86.0%) had cCR and were allocated to observation. Four patients drew consent or died leaving 103 observed for at least 2 years. 23 had regrowth after cCR, five of whom had organ preserving transanal endoscopic microsurgery, 15 other curative surgery, and three palliation. 63 had no locoregional regrowth. Thus 61% (63/103) of patients with 2 years of follow-up had locoregional tumor control with chemoradiation alone. The actuarial estimate of locoregional control at 2 years from start of observation was 73.8% (95%CI 63.2-81.8). Calculated from time of enrollment, metastasis-free and overall survival at 30 months was 85.4% (95%CI 76.5-91.1) and 94.8% (95%CI 87.8-97.8). In the 63 patients with complete response at 2 years, ‘Low Anterior Resection Syndrome-score’ was None=37%, Minor=28%, and Major=35%. The most severe toxicity was erectile dysfunction grade 3 (n=3), grade 2 (n=4), grade 1 (n=6), and grade 0 (n=26). Grade 2 diarrhea, constipation, fecal incontinence, rectal bleeding and decreased libido were each reported in one case, while urinary frequency grade 2 was seen in four patients. Conclusions: The vast majority of patients with low rectal cancer can be cured by modern radiotherapy 62 Gy in 28 fractions with excellent patient-reported outcomes, toxicity, tumor control, and survival. The treatment is feasible in a multicenter setting. We suggest this approach as a standard of care option. Clinical trial information: NCT02438839.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Jensen, Lars Henrik","Risum, Signe","Nielsen, Jesper Dan","Mynster, Tommie","Ploeen, John","Rahr, Hans B","Havelund, Birgitte Mayland","Appelt, Ane L","Lindebjerg, Jan","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Jakobsen, Anders","Poulsen, Laurids"],"cuid":["S02-096.15-000632"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-07","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2022-06-03","title":"2022 ASCO annual meeting","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"curative chemoradiation for low rectal cancer primary clinical outcomes from a multicenter phase ii trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ascopubs.org/doi/abs/10.1200/JCO.2022.40.17_suppl.LBA3514","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.15-000632","ids":["aau-0c1153e5-060c-4ac9-b084-08a95f4cb7c2","sdu-711d7320-c37e-4319-91fa-9e2c7004c4ef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7D2777DE8244C04A25554DDECBCD78F3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Regional Hospital Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalbo