":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129770063"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","prehospital emergency medical services"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2f4d42f1-7e14-4934-a12b-0c2f1b103f55","au-ca4e2548-c968-4347-929e-d3dc08d3e5bb","ku-b3e35d64-a999-4717-9cd5-0186b3394885","sdu-11604bf5-280e-45a2-bd13-340fdf50ad90"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of Vasopressin and Methylprednisolone vs. Placebo on Long-Term Outcomes in Patients with In-Hospital Cardiac Arrest A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.05-002368","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Men and women may respond differently to certain therapies for heart failure with reduced ejection fraction, including implantable cardioverter defibrillators (ICD). In an extended follow-up study of the DANISH trial (Danish Study to Assess the Efficacy of ICDs in Patients With Non-Ischemic Systolic Heart Failure on Mortality), adding 4 years of additional follow-up, we examined the effect of ICD implantation according to sex. METHODS: In the DANISH trial, 1116 patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure were randomized to receive an ICD (N=556) or usual clinical care (N=550). The primary outcome was all-cause mortality. RESULTS: Of the 1116 patients randomized in the DANISH trial, 307 (27.5%) were women. During a median follow-up of 9.5 years, women had a lower associated rate of all-cause mortality (hazard ratio [HR], 0.60 [95% CI, 0.47-0.78]) cardiovascular death (HR, 0.62 [95% CI, 0.46-0.84]), nonsudden cardiovascular death (HR, 0.59 [95% CI, 0.42-0.85]), and a numerically lower rate of sudden cardiovascular death (HR, 0.70 [95% CI, 0.40-1.25]), compared with men. Compared with usual clinical care, ICD implantation did not reduce the rate of all-cause mortality, irrespective of sex (men, HR, 0.85 [95% CI, 0.69-1.06]; women, HR, 0.98 [95% CI, 0.64-1.50]; Pinteraction=0.51). In addition, sex did not modify the effect of ICD implantation on sudden cardiovascular death (men, HR, 0.57 [95% CI, 0.36-0.92]; women, HR, 0.68 [95% CI, 0.26-1.77]; Pinteraction=0.76). CONCLUSIONS: In patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure, ICD implantation did not provide an overall survival benefit, but reduced sudden cardiovascular death, irrespective of sex. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www. CLINICALTRIALS: gov; Unique identifier: NCT00542945.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Butt, Jawad H.","Yafasova, Adelina","Elming, Marie B.","Dixen, Ulrik","Nielsen, Jens C.","Haarbo, Jens","Videbæk, Lars","Korup, Eva","Bruun, Niels Eske","Eiskjær, Hans","Brandes, Axel","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Gustafsson, Finn","Egstrup, Kenneth","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Høfsten, Dan E.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Pehrson, Steen","Thune, Jens Jakob","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S04-099.65-000970"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Butt, Jawad H."],"keyword":["Clinical trial","Death Sudden Cardiac etiology","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark","Female","Follow Up Studies","Heart Failure Systolic etiology","Heart Failure therapy","Heart failure","Humans","Male","Mortality","Risk Factors","Women","defibrillator implantable"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy of implantable cardioverter defibrillator in nonischemic systolic heart failure according to sex extended follow up study of the danish trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381636378/Manuscript_Circ_HF_FINAL1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S04-099.65-000970","identifier":[{"id":"35942877","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138458179","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-127e8f9b-bad2-455e-a161-e0201eebcb86","au-6c9039ca-78da-4d9b-9760-dc9fb116ef43","ku-06aee99d-389f-4307-9fcf-458cbb836a86","sdu-414b5a56-5b11-4d56-88be-77f146d2c89f"],"keyword":["Death, Sudden, Cardiac/etiology","Defibrillators, Implantable","Denmark","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Heart Failure, Systolic/etiology","Heart Failure/t