{"abstract":"Postcoital vaginal cuff dehiscence is a rare but well documented complication of hysterectomy. Common symptoms are vaginal bleeding and abdominopelvic pain with or without evisceration of the intraperitoneal contents through the separated vaginal cuff, which can lead to bowel injury, necrosis and sepsis. This potentially life-threatening condition usually occurs during the first postoperative act of intercourse or within the first few months of surgery. This case report presents the unusual case of vaginal cuff dehiscence in a 59-year-old woman 14 years after a total abdominal hysterectomy.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gibrael, Hevy Sadraddin","Ærenlund, Mia Prindahl","Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","Weltz, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407779"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Female","Humans","Hysterectomy adverse effects","Intestinal Perforation etiology","Laparoscopy adverse effects","Middle Aged","Vagina surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fri luft i abdomen skyldes ikke altid tarmperforation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/358719118/v03220166_web.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-407779","identifier":[{"id":"85136341653","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35959821","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-18093f71-9c3b-441d-aa1b-13f4c613f2fc"],"keyword":["Female","Humans","Hysterectomy/adverse effects","Intestinal Perforation/etiology","Laparoscopy/adverse effects","Middle Aged","Pneumoperitoneum/diagnostic imaging","Surgical Wound Dehiscence/complications","Vagina/surgery"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B4CA1E307ADD63F486645C971C58B51A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/358719118/v03220166_web.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://content.ugeskriftet.dk/sites/default/files/scientific_article_files/2022-06/v03220166_web.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hevy Sadraddin","key":"gibraelpau","last":"Gibrael","name":"Gibrael, Hevy Sadraddin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mia Prindahl","key":"ærenlundpau","last":"Ærenlund","name":"Ærenlund, Mia Prindahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"41cd192a-a0fd-4fd8-9361-cbedd07691f9","name":"Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke","key":"weltzpau","last":"Weltz","name":"Weltz, Vibeke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35959821"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"29","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V03220166","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"184"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-18093f71-9c3b-441d-aa1b-13f4c613f2fc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fri luft i abdomen skyldes ikke altid tarmperforation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407779","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"AIM & METHODS: Extreme endurance exercise provides a valuable research model for understanding the adaptive metabolic response of older and younger individuals to intense physical activity. Here, we compare a wide range of metabolic and physiologic parameters in two cohorts of seven trained men, age 30±5 years or age 65±6 years, before and after the participants travelled ≈3000 km by bicycle over 15 days. RESULTS: Over the 15-day exercise intervention, participants lost 2-3 kg fat mass with no significant change in body weight. V̇O 2 max did not change in younger cyclists, but decreased (p=0.06) in the older cohort. The resting plasma FFA concentration decreased markedly in both groups, and plasma glucose increased in the younger group. In the older cohort, plasma LDL-cholesterol and plasma triglyceride decreased. In skeletal muscle, fat transporters CD36 and FABPm remained unchanged. The glucose handling proteins GLUT4 and SNAP23 increased in both groups. Mitochondrial ROS production decreased in both groups and ADP sensitivity increased in skeletal muscle in the older but not in the younger cohort. CONCLUSION: In summary, these data suggest that older but not younger individuals experience a negative adaptive response affecting cardiovascular function in response to extreme endurance exercise, while a positive response to the same exercise intervention is observed in peripheral tissues in younger and older men. The results also suggest that the adaptive thresholds differ in younger and old men, and this difference primarily affects central cardiovascular functions in older men after extreme endurance exercise.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Frandsen, Jacob","Sahl, Ronni Eg","Rømer, Tue","Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","Nielsen, Andreas Blaaholm","Lie-Olesen, Michelle Munk","Rasmusen, Hanne Kruuse","Søgaard, Ditte","Ingersen, Arthur","Rosenkilde, Mads","Westerterp, Klaas","Holst, Jens Juul","Andersen, Jesper L.","Markowski, Adam Roman","Blachnio-Zabielska, Agnieszka","Clemmensen, Christoffer","Sacchetti, Massimo","Cataldo, Angelo","Traina, Marcello","Larsen, Steen","Dela, Flemming","Helge, Jørn Wulff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418866"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Netherlands","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Maastricht University","Medical University of Białystok","University of Palermo","University of Rome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extreme duration exercise affects old and younger men differently","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apha.13816","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-418866","identifier":[{"id":"35347845","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000783285100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9287057","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85128271666","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2aa79046-5223-4ff0-bc70-548b394abaa0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBB89722F3B78E9348872E2E6C43C5A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apha.13816","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/311613695/Acta_Physiologica_2022_Frandsen_Extreme_duration_exercise_affects_old_and_younger_men_differently.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"maastricht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Maastricht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pl","key":"medical university of białystok","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Białystok","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of rome","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rome","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of palermo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Palermo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"259020bb-ca39-4937-9668-1e15ba972196","name":"Frandsen, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ronni Eg","key":"sahlpau","last":"Sahl","locid":"df8ae78f-67cf-4af7-a03d-baf172608d07","name":"Sahl, Ronni Eg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tue","key":"rømerpau","last":"Rømer","locid":"32b26587-2ba1-4451-b564-da70a76f4712","name":"Rømer, Tue","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thunestvedthansenpau","last":"Thunestvedt Hansen","locid":"58070c3b-ed1e-4859-9467-29b512cdea42","name":"Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","name_org":"Thunestvedt Hansen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-3879-2192","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Blaaholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Andreas Blaaholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michelle Munk","key":"lieolesenpau","last":"Lie-Olesen","name":"Lie-Olesen, Michelle Munk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Kruuse","key":"rasmusenpau","last":"Rasmusen","locid":"6dbffce3-fd8e-4415-a2ba-f1158cfbbac3","name":"Rasmusen, Hanne Kruuse","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ditte","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"915036b6-f8f0-47f4-a841-bd20b96245ee","name":"Søgaard, Ditte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arthur","key":"ingersenpau","last":"Ingersen","locid":"a135c9d1-97f5-41e6-806b-a7d1c51d4ecb","name":"Ingersen, Arthur","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"rosenkildepau","last":"Rosenkilde","locid":"46abef02-cc20-45ab-bc2c-262c81050cc3","name":"Rosenkilde, Mads","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Klaas","key":"westerterppau","last":"Westerterp","name":"Westerterp, Klaas","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Løvind","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"bc09ab83-a612-43e6-9e37-a1d43dc2b1db","name":"Andersen, Jesper L.","name_org":"Andersen, Jesper Løvind","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Adam Roman","key":"markowskipau","last":"Markowski","name":"Markowski, Adam Roman","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Agnieszka","key":"blachniozabielskapau","last":"Blachnio-Zabielska","name":"Blachnio-Zabielska, Agnieszka","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"cb6d6cab-88bf-4650-9bd9-7759c2dc0be6","name":"Clemmensen, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0003-2456-9667","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Massimo","key":"sacchettipau","last":"Sacchetti","name":"Sacchetti, Massimo","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Angelo","key":"cataldopau","last":"Cataldo","name":"Cataldo, Angelo","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Marcello","key":"trainapau","last":"Traina","name":"Traina, Marcello","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Steen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d4c64c4e-1edf-41cf-890e-aba81d9e35f7","name":"Larsen, Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-5170-4337","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørn Wulff","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35347845"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apha.13816","issn":["17481708","17481716"],"issn_org":["17481708"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Physiologica","paperid":"e13816","status":"p","title":"Acta Physiologica","volume":"235"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128271666"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2aa79046-5223-4ff0-bc70-548b394abaa0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extreme duration exercise affects old and younger men differently","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418866","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The primary aim was to investigate the diagnostic performance of an Artificial Intelligence (AI) algorithm for pneumoperitoneum detection in patients with acute abdominal pain who underwent an abdominal CT scan. Method: This retrospective diagnostic test accuracy study used a consecutive patient cohort from the Acute High-risk Abdominal patient population at Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Denmark between January 1, 2019 and September 25, 2019. As reference standard, all studies were rated for pneumoperitoneum (subgroups: none, small, medium, and large amounts) by a gastrointestinal radiology consultant. The index test was a novel AI algorithm based on a sliding window approach with a deep recurrent neural network at its core. The primary outcome was the area under the curve (AUC) of the receiver operating characteristic (ROC). Results: Of 331 included patients (median age 68 years (Range 19–100; 180 women)) 31 patients (9%) had pneumoperitoneum (large: 16, moderate: 7, small: 8). The AUC was 0.77 (95% CI 0.66–0.87). At a specificity of 99% (297/300, 95% CI: 97–100%), sensitivity was 52% (16/31, 95% CI 29–65%), and positive likelihood ratio was 52 (95% CI 16–165). When excluding cases with smaller amounts of free air (<0.25 mL) the AUC increased to 0.96 (95% CI 0.89–1.0). At 99% specificity, sensitivity was 81% (13/16) and positive likelihood ratio was 82 (95% CI 27 – 254). Conclusions: An AI algorithm identified pneumoperitoneum on CT scans in a clinical setting with low sensitivity but very high specificity, supporting its role for ruling in pneumoperitoneum.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","Taubmann, Oliver","Eibenberger, Eva","Müller, Felix C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436334"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Siemens"],"keyword":["Acute abdomen","Artificial intelligence","CT","Detection","Diagnostic test accuracy","Pneumoperitoneum"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"artificial intelligence based detection of pneumoperitoneum on ct scans in patients presenting with acute abdominal pain a clinical diagnostic test accuracy study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2022.110216","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-436334","identifier":[{"id":"85125643885","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35259709","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-47d5ad85-3f1f-46eb-b7f1-7b9d3480cf75"],"keyword":["Acute Abdomen","Artificial Intelligence","CT","Detection","Diagnostic Test Accuracy","Pneumoperitoneum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D66BAFDB99717ADF9595D825343CAC5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2022.110216","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313654351/Artificial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital regi