{"abstract":"This chapter studies compromise and bargaining in Danish legislative politics. While it does point out a democratic tradition of inclusion and consensus norms, it also highlights that bargained compromises often result from competition between political parties over policy influence, votes, and government office. In particular a special form of bargained legislative compromises (politiske forlig), is important. The chapter studies the historical background, and democratic thinking concerning these agreements. It shows the degree of consensus in legislative votes, the share of legislative agreements made within and across the political blocs in Denmark and the importance of a number of legislative norms of consensus.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christiansen, Flemming Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-564964"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish consensus democracy legislative competition and cooperation","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://hansreitzel.dk/soeg/public-law-bog-52114-9788741277981","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-564964","ids":["ruc-85b56b7e-1da8-486b-b22b-fe08e64e06dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2B3EB83F411749AE206AFEC2B935DB4A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Social Sciences and Business"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affn