ary Care-Anchored eHealth Lifestyle Coaching Program : Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598826","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"High-efficient and power-dense ac/dc power electronic converters are demanded for a wide range of applications such as motor drives and active rectifiers. The utilization of wide bandgap (WBG) devices, such as gallium-nitride (GaN) transistors, is a key feature to improve both the efficiency and the power density of power electronic converters. Owing to the superiority of GaN switches, this paper achieves a high efficiency three-level active-neutral-point-clamped (ANPC) converter. However, using GaN transistors is critically dependent on the layout configuration to achieve smooth switching transient and, as equally important, efficient cooling. Therefore, this paper presents layout optimization and considers different layout configurations to achieve a low power loop inductance and as efficient heatsink assembly/performance. Two configurations of the switch boards are built by GaN/Si MOSFETs, and a power loop inductance comparison is presented. Furthermore, a comprehensive loss model is performed to fine-tune the switching frequency from the efficiency and the size point of view. A 10kW laboratory prototype voltage source converter, including an EMI filter, is built with the switching frequency of 140kHz. The efficiency measurement is performed and confirmed the full load efficiency of 99% and peak efficiency of 99.34%. Moreover, the CISPR11 Class A conducted EMI standard is fulfilled.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Najjar, Mohammad","Kouchaki, Alireza","Nielsen, Jesper","Lazar, Radu","Nymand, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602491"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Najjar, Mohammad"],"keyword":["Active neutral point clamped ANPC","Capacitors","EMI filter","Efficiency","Electromagnetic interference","Modulation","Multilevel converter","Power factor correction PFC","Power harmonic filters","Switches","Switching frequency","Switching loss","Volume minimization","electromagnetic interference EMI filter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-DFS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-PR-DFS","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design procedure and efficiency analysis of a 000000000099 000000000003 efficient 000000000010 kw three phase three level hybrid gan si active neutral point clamped converter","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85120579963","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-602491","identifier":[{"id":"85120579963","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-66474e05-e65f-440c-bcb3-a58490458ef7"],"keyword":["Active neutral point clamped (ANPC)","Capacitors","EMI filter","Efficiency","Electromagnetic interference","Modulation","Multilevel converter","Power harmonic filters","Power-factor correction (PFC)","Switches","Switching frequency","Switching loss","Volume minimization","electromagnetic interference (EMI) filter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF9BBC62DFB172AFD764E2F02A1CB01F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, SDU Microelectronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"danish technological inst