{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Hoeck, Bente","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","Ryg, Jesper","Delmar, Charlotte","Andersen, H. E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-609505"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-10","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2022-06-08","title":"26th Nordic Congress of Gerontology","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blurred lines of caring responsibility older ill persons and their adult children s experiences with primary healthcare","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-609505","ids":["sdu-7ef1b001-a6c9-482c-a390-86e574e6e9ac"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-662D01738C5F7CAE3EC410FE9FF2D679"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og professionshøjskole"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ukendt"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"hoeckpau","last":"Hoeck","locid":"ed8ce3c5-4f5e-4dba-a104-b73d77a095e5","name":"Hoeck, Bente","orcid":"0000-0001-7647-5641","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"delmarpau","last":"Delmar","name":"Delmar, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"H. E.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, H. E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7ef1b001-a6c9-482c-a390-86e574e6e9ac"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Blurred lines of caring responsibility : Older ill persons and their adult children's experiences with primary healthcare.","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-609505","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim of the present analysis is to identify the reasons for accepting or rejecting the invitation to be screened by the Faecal Immunochemical Test as part of the free Danish screening programme for colorectal cancer (CRC). Study design: A cross-sectional representative survey of 15,072 Danish citizens aged 50–80 years was collected in 2019 via a Web-based questionnaire administered by Statistics Denmark. Among the net sample of 6807 respondents (45%), 177 were excluded because of current treatment for colorectal disease. Methods: To determine the reasons for accepting or refusing the invitation to be screened for CRC, a latent class analysis was conducted, which allowed participants to provide several reasons for acceptance or rejection of screening. Results: The most important reason for participating in CRC screening was the active public programme. A further reason for participation was the perceived risk for CRC, mainly in combination with the public programme. The reasons for participation did not differ between individuals who had participated and those who intended to participate when offered. Among participants who declined screening, the most frequent reasons were that they forgot to participate or that they were concerned about the unpleasant test procedure. Among individuals who intended to decline screening, a perceived low risk for CRC was the most frequently cited reason. Conclusions: Recommendation from a general practitioner (GP) was not given as a frequent reason for CRC screening participation which is discussed as a challenge to participation rates in population based screening program The main reasons reported for non-participation in CRC screening (i.e. forgot to participate or the unpleasant test procedure) might be addressed by a stronger endorsement from GPs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","Leppin, Anja","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-619690"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele"],"keyword":["Cross sectional study","Non participation","Participation","Population based"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reasons for participation and non participation in colorectal cancer screening","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.puhe.2022.01.010","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["In the present study, recommendation from GPs to participate in the screening programme was not a major reason to participate. This result is in contrast with findings reported by other studies that report inadequate health provider counselling, rather than poor patient acceptance, to be a factor that hampers screening.14 Also, complete absence of a screening recommendation from physicians is often mentioned as a major barrier to participation.19,20 However, these results cannot be directly compared with the present data. The current results only provide information about whether respondents perceived a physician recommendation as subjectively relevant to their participation decision. An explanation of the apparent missing association might be that the Danish mail-based screening invitation basically cuts out the GP as the patients' counsellor. With this exclusion, the impact of GPs on CRC screening participation via support and involvement in recruiting participants5 was precluded. In other studies, it is well documented that a patient-specific reminder or endorsement from a GP has a positive impact on participation rates.21,22 Furthermore, GPs who support screening programmes are regional promoters to improve participation.23 In support of this observation, a study on non-participants in CRC screening found that an endorsement letter or text message from their own GP did encourage participation in individuals who otherwise forgot, procrastinated or were reluctant to collect a stool sample.24 To enhance knowledge about screening and allow evidence-based decisions about participation, it is important to consider GPs in the process. One possibility would be to inform GPs when patients are invited for CRC screening. In addition, patients? invitations to CRC screening should more clearly suggest that they can contact their GP if they are in doubt about what to do."],"id":"S01-000.00-619690","identifier":[{"id":"85125530373","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35248951","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-a26f08d1-ac89-4e84-a94b-51d2d1ac420d"],"keyword":["Colon cancer screening","Cross-sectional study","Non-participation","Participation","Population based"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26B628FAB1B0D54D608D3E50F823A4A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.puhe.2022.01.010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/200008709/1_s2.0_S0033350622000117_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Health Promotion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriele","key":"bergbeckhoffpau","last":"Berg-Beckhoff","locid":"df22cacd-c8b4-440c-8c16-aecbc139d9b6","name":"Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","orcid":"0000-0003-1614-938X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"leppinpau","last":"Leppin","locid":"6bef1637-e9f4-44e0-902e-6c92974c8711","name":"Leppin, Anja","orcid":"0000-0001-6203-6162","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35248951"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.puhe.2022.01.010","issn":["00333506","14765616"],"issn_org":["00333506"],"journal":"Public Health","pages":"83-89","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Public Health","volume":"205"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125530373"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a26f08d1-ac89-4e84-a94b-51d2d1ac420d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Reasons for participation and non-participation in colorectal cancer screening","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-619690","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The prolongation of disease-free life (PODL) required by people to be willing to accept an offer of a preventive treatment is unknown. Quantifying the required benefits could guide information and discussions about preventive treatment. In this study, we investigated how large the benefit in prolongation of a disease-free life (PODL) should be for individuals aged 50-80 years to accept a preventive treatment offer. We used a cross-sectional survey design based on a representative sample of 6847 Danish citizens aged 50-80 years. Data were collected in 2019 through a web-based standardized questionnaire administered by Statistics Denmark, and socio-demographic data were added from a national registry. We analyzed the data with chi-square tests and stepwise multinomial logistic regression. The results indicate that the required minimum benefit from the preventive treatment varied widely between individuals (1-week PODL = 14.8%, ≥4 years PODL = 39.2%), and that the majority of individuals (51.1%) required a PODL of ≥2 years. The multivariable analysis indicate that education and income were independently and negatively associated with requested minimum benefit, while age and smoking were independently and positively associated with requested minimum benefit to accept the preventive treatment. Most individuals aged 50-80 years required larger health benefits than most preventive medications on average can offer. The data support the need for educating patients and health care professionals on how to use average benefits when discussing treatment benefits, especially for primary prevention.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","Thapa, Subash"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642240"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Non communicable disease","Preventive treatment","Primary prevention","Risk communication","Secondary prevention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prolongation of disease free life when is the benefit sufficient to warrant the effort of taking a preventive medicine","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ypmed.2021.106867","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-642240","identifier":[{"id":"34740678","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85118572413","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f124d25a-35fe-4cb8-8ce0-445adb02c7f3"],"keyword":["Benefit perception","Non-communicable disease","Preventive treatment","Primary prevention","Prolongation of disease-free life","Risk communication","Secondary prevention","Treatment benefit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C4962F3271C98AB52A032085384A76B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ypmed.2021.106867","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/194477390/Prolongation_of_disease.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper B","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivar S","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2bcec001-e6b0-48e7-bc80-904ee8c535ae","name":"Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø","name_org":"Kristiansen, Ivar S","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Subash","key":"thapapau","last":"Thapa","locid":"a271bef3-0a7e-4c8d-b6b7-28a6a21e9480","name":"Thapa, Subash","orcid":"0000-0002-1182-8511","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34740678"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ypmed.2021.106867","issn":["00917435","10960260"],"issn_org":["00917435"],"journal":"Preventive Medicine","paperid":"106867","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Preventive Medicine","volume":"154"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118572413"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f124d25a-35fe-4cb8-8ce0-445adb02c7f3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prolongation of disease-free life : When is the benefit sufficient to warrant the effort of taking a preventive medicine?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-642240","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Active Healthy Kids – Danmark 2022 indeholder en opdateret præsentation af i alt ti indikatorer om børn og unges fysiske aktivitet. Formålet er at opsamle og vurdere bedst tilgængelig viden, der kan inspirere til øget indsats og aktivt samarbejde mellem offentlige, private og civile aktører. Den overordnede ambition er at bidrage til, at flere børn og unge bevæger sig mere og oplever fysisk aktivitet som en integreret del af deres hverdagsliv.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Christiansen, Lars Breum","Toftager, Mette","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Møller, Niels Christian","Larsen, Malte Nejst","Schipperijn, Jasper","Høyer-Kruse, Jens","Skovgaard, Thomas","Rask, Steffen","Baagø-Rasmussen, Thomas","Rasmussen, Mette","Have Nielsen, Jacob","Ninn Sandfeld Melcher, Jesper","Præstholm, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671884"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christiansen, Lars Breum"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Idrættens Analyseinstitut"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"active healthy kids danmark 000000002022","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://fiibl.dk/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Active-Healthy-Kids-2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671884","ids":["sdu-d41943f8-4acc-4eb4-bd2a-a3089f17dafa"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-728807AA2F962A1B73519C591F26F30E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://fiibl.dk/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Active-Healthy-Kids-2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmar