ull,"first":"Jesper","key":"ninnsandfeldmelcherpau","last":"Ninn Sandfeld Melcher","name":"Ninn Sandfeld Melcher, Jesper","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"præstholmpau","last":"Præstholm","name":"Præstholm, Søren","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"32","publisher":"FIIBL","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d41943f8-4acc-4eb4-bd2a-a3089f17dafa"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"ACTIVE HEALTHY KIDS - DANMARK 2022","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671884","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we show how collaboration between Danish municipal primary and lower secondary schools (folkeskoler) and elite sports clubs to establish SportsClasses enables schools to set parameters that align student-athletes’ attitudes and behavior towards school and academic performance. Using neo-institutional theory, we show how two separate institutional domains–education and sport–come to agree on common purposes and practices for an endeavor that takes place on the ‘home field’ of education. We apply the theoretical concepts of ‘contractualisation’ and ‘accountability’ to understand what these learning agreements or implicit social contracts involve, how they are made, and how they are enforced. These concepts capture the empirical governance mechanisms that produce the integration of athletes into school norms and practices as well as how these norms and practises are re-configured as an effect of the cooperation. The article is based on an ethnographic study of the admissions process for SportsClasses. We discuss the benefits and risks for the publicly funded school system in entering into such social learning contracts.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Olesen, Jesper Stilling","Karen, David"],"cuid":["S02-099.88-007667"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bryn Mawr College"],"keyword":["Accountability","Dual career","Elite sports","Grundskole","Lower Secondary School","Neo institutional theory","Talent","Talent development","contractualisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cooperation between schools and elite sports how are schools affected from engaging in athletic talent development","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85096135167&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.88-007667","identifier":[{"id":"000588506900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85096135167","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9e0931ad-7b54-4d20-91b0-704826a54272","au-185316c6-e7ab-4333-bfec-c0e0232e8422"],"keyword":["Grundskole","Talent","Talent development","accountability","contractualisation","contractualisation and accountability","dual career","elite sports","lower secondary school","neo-institutional theory","school and elitesport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7E673339698DEB434FD6B5BBE5EC9DBC"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Active Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"bryn mawr college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Bryn Mawr College","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"karenpau","last":"Karen","name":"Karen, David","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09620214.2020.1847167","issn":["09620214","17475066"],"issn_org":["09620214"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Studies in Sociology of Education","pages":"325-346","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"International Studies in Sociology of Education","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096135167"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9e0931ad-7b54-4d20-91b0-704826a54272","au-185316c6-e7ab-4333-bfec-c0e0232e8422"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cooperation between schools and elite sports. How are schools affected from engaging in athletic talent development?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.88-007667","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To evaluate the association between different right ventricular (RV) lead positions as assessed by cardiac computed tomography (CT) and echocardiographic and clinical outcomes in patients receiving cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT). METHODS: We reviewed patient records of all 278 patients included in two randomized controlled trials (ImagingCRT and ElectroCRT) for occurrence of heart failure (HF) hospitalization or all-cause death (primary endpoint) during long-term follow-up. Outcomes were compared between RV lead positions using adjusted Cox regression analysis. Six months after CRT implantation, we estimated left ventricular (LV) reverse remodeling by measuring LV end-systolic and end-diastolic volumes by echocardiography. Changes from baseline to 6 months follow-up were compared between RV lead positions. Device-related complications were recorded at 6-month follow-up. RESULTS: During median (interquartile range) follow-up of 4.7 (2.9-7.1) years, the risk of meeting the primary endpoint was similar for patients with non-apical vs. apical RV lead position (adjusted hazard ratio (HR) 0.78, 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.54-1.12, p = 0.17) and free wall vs. septal RV lead position (adjusted HR 1.03, 95% CI 0.72-1.47, p = 0.86). Changes in LV ejection fraction and dimensions were similar with the different RV lead positions. We observed no differences in device-related complications relative to the RV lead position. CONCLUSIONS: In patients receiving CRT, the risk of HF hospitalization or all-cause death during long-term follow-up, and LV remodeling and incidence of device-related complications after 6 months are not associated with different anatomical RV lead position as assessed by cardiac CT.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin","Sommer, Anders","Stephansen, Charlotte","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Kronborg, Mads Brix","Kristensen, Jens","Gerdes, Christian","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010174"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin"],"keyword":["Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Clinical outcomes","Left ventricular reverse remodeling","Right ventricular lead position"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiac computed tomography verified right ventricular lead position and outcomes in cardiac resynchronization therapy","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85127338037&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-010174","identifier":[{"id":"35348998","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85127338037","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000776325200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d4baf0e7-aceb-4b35-ba49-e969a05ccfc0","au-c6312775-6de5-4ff8-bf09-6d473768c2de"],"keyword":["Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Clinical outcomes","Left ventricular reverse remodeling","Right ventricular lead position"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-897DE4981E9E0174BCF11B260B8E255C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Benjamin","key":"fyenbodanielbenjaminpau","last":"Fyenbo","locid":"90f4115a-ffcf-4502-8461-34533e634242","name":"Fyenbo, Daniel Benjamin","orcid":"0000-0001-5898-1743","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"sommeranderspau","last":"Sommer","locid":"310abbc0-d3b1-4351-9e62-e77454fb14fa","name":"Sommer, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"stephansencharlottepau","last":"Stephansen","locid":"bc398e00-bb58-4ef9-b28a-70f693ee6928","name":"Stephansen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3272-2115","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardbjarnelindepau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Brix","key":"kronborgmadsbrixpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"76c15c18-4786-4b38-93b3-91afbc1ea875","name":"Kronborg, Mads Brix","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kristensenjenspau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"gerdeschristianpau","last":"Gerdes","locid":"43704ceb-b5ba-49ac-bff8-5e26e3b9d419","name":"Gerdes, Christian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenhenrikkjærulfpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenjespermøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenjenscosedispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35348998"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10840-022-01193-1","issn":["1383875X","15728595"],"issn_org":["1383875X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","pages":"783-792","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127338037"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d4baf0e7-aceb-4b35-ba49-e969a05ccfc0","au-c6312775-6de5-4ff8-bf09-6d473768c2de"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cardiac computed tomography-verified right ventricular lead position and outcomes in cardiac resynchronization therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-010174","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: The incidence rate risk of testicular cancer has increased over the last four decades, and the most significant increase has been among Caucasian men in Nordic countries. Second-generation immigrant studies indicate a significant role of environmental exposure in testicular cancer. Methods: We conducted a nationwide register-based case- control study including 6,390 testicular cancer cases registered in the Danish Cancer Registry between 1989 and 2014. Up to four agematched controls for each case (n 18,997) were randomly selected fromthe Civil Registration System.Ambient air pollution levels were estimated at addresses of cases and controls with a state-of-the-art air pollution modeling system. Results: We mostly found ORs close to 1.00 and with 95% confidence intervals (CI) spanning 1.00. Exposure during the year preceding birth was associated with ORs for nitrogen dioxide (NO2) of 0.87 (95% CI, 0.77-0.97) per 10 mg/m3 and for organic carbon of 0.84 (95% CI, 0.72-0.98) per 1 mg/m3. Exposure during the first 10 years of life was associated with ORs for organic carbon of 0.79 (95% CI, 0.67-0.93) per 1 mg/m3, for ozone (O3) of 1.20 (95% CI, 1.07-1.34) per 10 mg/m3, and for secondary inorganic aerosols of 1.07 (95% CI, 1.00-1.15) per 1 mg/m3. Conclusions: Early-life exposure to NO2 and organic carbon (OC) was associated with lower risk for testicular cancer whereas early-life exposure to O3 and secondary inorganic aerosols (SIA) was associated with higher risk.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Taj, Tahir","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Ketzel, Matthias","Geels, Camilla","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","Sørensen, Mette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013864"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Taj, Tahir"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term residential exposure to air pollution and risk of testicular cancer in denmark a population based case control study","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aacrjournals.org/cebp/article/31/4/744/694018/Long-term-Residential-Exposure-to-Air-Pollution","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013864","identifier":[{"id":"85128481893","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35131880","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-11c0d305-c187-483e-b86a-2111046c1901","ruc-9ae2c98b-6fca-456a-add2-2030ab81c361"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C2FB11BF821F3F49FF5A6016DE324BE9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"tajpau","last":"Taj","name":"Taj, Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla Arthur","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla Arthur","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35131880"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1158/1055-9965.epi-21-0961","issn":["10559965","15387755"],"issn_org":["10559965"],"issue":"4","journal":"Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers & Prevention","pages":"744-750","publisher":"American Association for Cancer Research Inc.","status":"p","title":"Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers & Prevention","title_org":"Cancer Epidemiology Biomarkers and Prevention","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128481893"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-11c0d305-c187-483e-b86a-2111046c1901","ruc-9ae2c98b-6fca-456a-add2-2030ab81c361"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term Residential Exposure to Air Pollution and Risk of Testicular Cancer in Denmark : A Population-Based Case-Control Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013864","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Transportation noise increases the risk of ischemic heart disease (IHD), but few studies have investigated subtypes of IHD, such as myocardial infarction (MI), angina pectoris, or heart failure. We aimed to study whether exposure to road, railway and aircraft noise increased risk for ischemic heart disease (IHD), IHD subtypes, and heart failure in the entire adult Danish population, investigating exposures at both maximum exposed and silent façades of each residence. Methods: We modelled road, railway, and aircraft noise at the most and least exposed façades for the period 1995–2017 for all addresses in Denmark and calculated 10-year time-weighted running means for 2.5 million individuals age ≥50 years, of whom 122,523 developed IHD and 79,358 developed heart failure during follow-up (2005–2017). Data were analyzed using Cox proportional hazards models, adjusted for individual and area-level sociodemographic covariates and air pollution. Results: We found road traffic noise at the most exposed façade (Lden) to be associated with higher risk of IHD, myocardial infarction (MI), angina pectoris, and heart failure, with hazard ratios (HRs) (95% confidence intervals (CI)) of 1.052 (1.044–1.059), 1.041 (1.032–1.051), 1.095 (1.071–1.119), and 1.039 (1.033–1.045) per 10 dB higher 10-year mean exposure, respectively. These associations followed a near-linear exposure-response relationship and were robust to adjustment for air pollution with PM2.5. Railway noise at the least exposed façade was associated with heart failure (HR 1.28; 95% CI: 1.004–1.053), but not the other outcomes. Exposure to aircraft noise (>45 dB) seemed associated with increased risk for MI and heart failure. Conclusions: We found road traffic noise and potentially railway and aircraft noise to increase risk of various major cardiovascular outcomes, highlighting the importance of preventive actions towards transportation noise.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Thacher, Jesse D.","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Khan, Jibran","Levin, Gregor","Münzel, Thomas","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026283"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thacher, Jesse D."],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","University Medical Center Mainz"],"keyword":["Aircraft noise","Angina pectoris","Heart failure","Myocardial Infarction","Railway noise","Road noise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposure to transportation noise and risk for cardiovascular disease in a nationwide cohort study from denmark","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85126510881","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026283","identifier":[{"id":"85126510881","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35304113","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bb4e8ae2-fcdc-43f6-9221-540ef13a9c55","ruc-380f6031-b9d9-404f-ae1a-c99c4e14890d"],"keyword":["Aircraft noise","Angina pectoris","Heart failure","Myocardial infarction","Railway noise","Road noise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C37A8FE36769AD83D5CCFCD65840709D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university medical center mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesse D.","key":"thacherpau","last":"Thacher","name":"Thacher, Jesse D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla A.","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregor","key":"levinpau","last":"Levin","locid":"64497988-a46c-415b-bcfe-9b09efad5289","name":"Levin, Gregor","orcid":"0000-0002-5223-914X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"münzelpau","last":"Münzel","name":"Münzel, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35304113"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2022.113106","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"113106","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"211"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126510881"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bb4e8ae2-fcdc-43f6-9221-540ef13a9c55","ruc-380f6031-b9d9-404f-ae1a-c99c4e14890d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Exposure to transportation noise and risk for cardiovascular disease in a nationwide cohort study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026283","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: DANISH (The Danish Study to Assess the Efficacy of Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillators [ICDs] in Patients With Nonischemic Systolic Heart Failure on Mortality) found that primary-prevention ICD implantation was not associated with an overall survival benefit in patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure during a median follow-up of 5.6 years, although there was a beneficial effect on all-cause mortality in patients ≤70 years. This study presents an additional 4 years of follow-up data from DANISH. METHODS: In DANISH, 556 patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure were randomized to receive an ICD and 560 to receive usual clinical care and followed until June 30, 2016. In this long-term follow-up study, patients were followed until May 18, 2020. Analyses were conducted for the overall population and according to age (≤70 and >70 years). RESULTS: During a median follow-up of 9.5 years (25th-75th percentile, 7.9-10.9 years), 208/556 patients (37%) in the ICD group and 226/560 patients (40%) in the control group died. Compared with the control group, the ICD group did not have significantly lower all-cause mortality (hazard ratio [HR] 0.89, [95% CI, 0.74-1.08]; P = 0.24). In patients ≤70 years (n = 829), all-cause mortality was lower in the ICD group than the control group (117/389 [30%] versus 158/440 [36%]; HR, 0.78 [95% CI, 0.61-0.99]; P = 0.04), whereas in patients >70 years (n = 287), all-cause mortality was not significantly different between the ICD and control group (91/167 [54%] versus 68/120 [57%]; HR, 0.92 [95% CI, 0.67-1.28]; P = 0.75). Cardiovascular death showed similar trends (overall, 147/556 [26%] versus 164/560 [29%]; HR, 0.87 [95% CI, 0.70-1.09]; P = 0.20; ≤70 years, 87/389 [22%] versus 122/440 [28%]; HR, 0.75 [95% CI, 0.57-0.98]; P = 0.04; >70 years, 60/167 [36%] versus 42/120 [35%]; HR, 0.97 [95% CI, 0.65-1.45]; P = 0.91). The ICD group had a significantly lower incidence of sudden cardiovascular death in the overall population (35/556 [6%] versus 57/560 [10%]; HR, 0.60 [95% CI, 0.40-0.92]; P = 0.02) and in patients ≤70 years (19/389 [5%] versus 49/440 [11%]; HR, 0.42 [95% CI, 0.24-0.71]; P = 0.0008), but not in patients >70 years (16/167 [10%] versus 8/120 [7%]; HR, 1.34 [95% CI, 0.56-3.19]; P = 0.39). CONCLUSIONS: During a median follow-up of 9.5 years, ICD implantation did not provide an overall survival benefit in patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure. In patients ≤70 years, ICD implantation was associated with a lower incidence of all-cause mortality, cardiovascular death, and sudden cardiovascular death. Registration: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT00542945.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Yafasova, Adelina","Butt, Jawad H.","Elming, Marie B.","Nielsen, Jens C.","Haarbo, Jens","Videbæk, Lars","Olesen, Line L","Steffensen, Flemming H","Bruun, Niels Eske","Eiskjær, Hans","Brandes, Axel","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Egstrup, Kenneth","Gustafsson, Finn","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Høfsten, Dan E","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Pehrson, Steen","Thune, Jens Jakob","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S04-095.17-007536"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Køber, Lars Valeur","Yafasova, Adelina","Yafasova, Adelina Henney"],"keyword":["Follow up","Heart failure","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Long term","Systolic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term follow up of danish the danish study to assess the efficacy of icds in patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure on mortality","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195380229/2021_Circulation_Yafasova_LT_FU_of_the_Danish_study_to_assess_efficacy_of_ICDs_in_pts_with_non_ischemic_syst_HF_DANISH.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S04-095.17-007536","identifier":[{"id":"85124438154","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34882430","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-9b5c02a0-339f-46f0-9fd2-83ceb9c4aa6d","au-c9edb320-f479-4116-8600-a7bf22366475","ku-bbc594ed-592e-497e-b21f-fbb4bf57ee03","sdu-84813efa-1ce5-487c-862b-f82e68230adb"],"keyword":["follow-up","heart failure","implantable cardioverter defibrillator","long-term","systolic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-D2E9D9FD4658D27F76125A0815EA2AEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/380207209/2021_Circulation_Yafasova_LT_FU_of_the_Danish_study_to_assess_efficacy_of_ICDs_in_pts_with_non_ischemic_syst_HF_DANISH_2_36.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195380229/2021_Circulation_Yafasova_LT_FU_of_the_Danish_study_to_assess_efficacy_of_ICDs_in_pts_with_non_ischemic_syst_HF_DANISH.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Regi