{"abstract":"This paper examines the statistical properties and the quality of the speed through water (STW) measurement based on data extracted from almost 200 container ships of Maersk Line’s fleet for 3 years of operation. The analysis uses high-frequency sensor data along with additional data sources derived from external providers. The interest of the study has its background in the accuracy of STW measurement as the most important parameter in the assessment of a ship’s performance analysis. The paper contains a thorough analysis of the measurements assumed to be related with the STW error, along with a descriptive decomposition of the main variables by sea region including sea state, vessel class, vessel IMO number and manufacturer of the speed-log installed in each ship. The paper suggests a semi-empirical method using a threshold to identify potential error in a ship’s STW measurement. The study revealed that the sea region is the most influential factor for the STW accuracy and that 26% of the ships of the dataset’s fleet warrant further investigation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ikonomakis, Angelos","Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","Holst, Klaus Kähler","Dietz, Jesper","Galeazzi, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349506"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Dietz, Jesper","Galeazzi, Roberto","Holst, Klaus Kähler","Ikonomakis, Angelos","Nielsen, Ulrik Dam"],"keyword":["Measurement error","Regression Analysis","Sea currents","Speed through water"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how good is the stw sensor an account from a larger shipping company","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jmse9050465","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-349506","identifier":[{"id":"85105536652","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-969faa43-9854-4a64-9fd3-8faf4d2642c9"],"keyword":["Measurement error","Regression analysis","Sea currents","Sensor readings","Speed through water"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2FD9DA757A4BBD6F68A69562F54E34D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jmse9050465","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/245222870/jmse_09_00465_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"a p moller maersk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-MAE","l3nl":"A.P. Møller – Mærsk","l3nn":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","namevar":["Maersk Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-MAE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Angelos","key":"ikonomakispau","last":"Ikonomakis","locid":"92af5f16-83f5-4a32-af27-6a70b500f2dd","name":"Ikonomakis, Angelos","orcid":"0000-0002-1571-8782","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus Kähler","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Klaus Kähler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzipau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/jmse9050465","issn":["20771312"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Marine Science and Engineering","paperid":"465","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Journal of Marine Science and Engineering","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105536652"],"search":{"DAF":["A.P. Møller – Mærsk","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-969faa43-9854-4a64-9fd3-8faf4d2642c9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"How Good is the STW Sensor? An Account from a Larger Shipping Company","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349506","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Travel behavior adaptations resulting from international temporary relocation is understudied, despite their increasing relevance. The scarce published literature on the subject overlooks the local contexts and ignores aspects related to the adaptation processes and motivations. This study aims to partially fill this gap by addressing the travel behavior adaptation of international students and researchers, focusing on public transport (PT) frequency of use and satisfaction. To investigate this, a Bayesian Structural Equation Model was estimated using data collected from a tailor-made online survey answered by temporary international exchange students and researchers. The model confirms that (i) travel behavior habit in the city of origin influences the residential location choice in the host city; (ii) the higher the frequency of PT use in the city of origin, the higher the PT use in the host city; (iii) the residential location in the host city affects individuals’ frequency of PT use and satisfaction; (iv) perceiving technology as helpful to move around leads to perceiving the PT system as easier to use at the beginning of the stay; (v) perceiving the PT as easier to use, leads to a higher frequency of its use and a higher level of satisfaction with the PT system.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Moraes Monteiro, Mayara","E Silva, João de Abreu","Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker","de Sousa, Jorge Pinho"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351750"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon","University of Porto"],"keyword":["ICT","International students"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public transport use and satisfaction by international students and researchers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su13158417","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351750","identifier":[{"id":"85111767963","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000682152200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-9e31fb7f-a66f-498f-9f14-cdb9523af053"],"keyword":["ICT","International students","Satisfaction with public transport","Temporary residents","Transnational relocation","Travel behavior adaptation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0A952E4A93FE39C285FF98D14945B3B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258984221/Sustainability_Public_Transport_Use_and_Satisfaction_by_International_Students_and_Researchers.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su13158417","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mayara Moraes","ke