arsen, Klaus Steenberg","orcid":"0000-0002-1421-6182","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"vesterdalpau","last":"Vesterdal","locid":"55c9aca9-8d2d-46ca-85b2-a61e5a2c6154","name":"Vesterdal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0309-3735","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"gundersenpau","last":"Gundersen","locid":"0e6a960c-07ea-4a4c-aadd-9fd6d1596244","name":"Gundersen, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-9199-4033","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Riis","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"54e64b51-5eca-4922-b031-9f0f6e1b85e4","name":"Christiansen, Jesper Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-3277-0734","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-72a10575-02c0-45fd-bea1-52d3d158c591"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Abandoned Peatland Ecosystem Response to Secondary Succession","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-461936","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The cultural tradition of stuccoed and polychromatic murals in central Mexico dates back to Early Classic Teotihuacan and continued into the subsequent Epiclassic period, with the stunning murals from Cacaxtla as the most famous and well-studied example. In this paper, we present three examples of stuccoed and richly painted benches or thrones from the mayor Epiclassic site of Xochicalco in the Mexican state of Morelos. A careful iconographic and epigraphic analysis of the imagery, as well as the associated hieroglyphic signs from one of the benches, leads us to suggest that these benches played a pivotal role in displaying the religious, mythological, and historical underpinnings of hierarchical power at Xochicalco. Based on comparisons with benches and seats from Classic Maya culture and, in particular, the contemporaneous Terminal Classic city of Chichen Itza, which was deeply involved in interregional relations with central Mexico, we also suggest that the Xochicalco benches may even have served as royal seats or thrones.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Alvarado León, Claudia","Helmke, Christophe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503557"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","OECD"],"country":["Mexico"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Instituto Nacional de Antropología e Historia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the stuccoed and painted benches of xochicalco morelos mexico","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-503557","identifier":[{"id":"85088960794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b8770aed-eff5-41a4-a73f-07e46b685bbd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACB6F3E1331FC64B240487ECA62C9531"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"mx","key":"instituto nacional de antropología e historia","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"Instituto Nacional de Antropología e Historia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Claudia","key":"alvaradoleónpau","last":"Alvarado León","name":"Alvarado León, Claudia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0956536120000012","issn":["09565361","14691787"],"issn_org":["09565361"],"issue":"2","journal":"Ancient Mesoamerica","pages":"249-268","status":"p","title":"Ancient Mesoamerica","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088960794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b8770aed-eff5-41a4-a73f-07e46b685bbd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Stuccoed and Painted Benches of Xochicalco, Morelos, Mexico","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503557","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Targeted temperature management (TTM) exerts substantial impact on hemodynamic function in out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) patients. Whole-body oxygen consumption (VO) and delivery (DO) have not previously been investigated in a clinical setting during TTM at different levels of temperature after OHCA. A substudy of 151 patients randomized at a single center in the TTM-trial, where patients were randomly assigned TTM at 33°C (TTM33) or 36°C (TTM36) for 24 hours. We calculated VO according to the principle of Fick (VO = cardiac output∗arteriovenous oxygen content difference). DO was calculated as cardiac output∗arterial oxygen content. Cardiac output was measured by pulmonary artery catheter with thermodilution. Arteriovenous oxygen content difference was calculated from arterial and mixed venous oxygen saturation and hemoglobin. Oxygen extraction ratio = VO/DO. At 24 hours, the VO was 169 ± 59 mL O per minute in TTM33 and 217 ± 53 mL O per minute in TTM36 (p < 0.0001). During 24 hours of TTM, the overall difference was 53 mL O minute (95% confidence interval [CI]: 31-74, p < 0.0001). After rewarming at 36 and 48 hours, there was no difference in VO between the groups. DO was overall 277 mL O per minute (95% CI: 175-379, p < 0.0001) higher in the TTM36-group during TTM. Oxygen extraction ratio during TTM was not significantly different between the two groups (2% [95% CI: -0.1 to 5, p = 0.09]). VO during the first 36 hours after OHCA correlated significantly with temperature, and VO was 19 mL O per minute lower per degree reduction in temperature (95% CI: 15-22), p < 0.0001. TTM at 33°C compared to 36°C after OHCA is associated with significantly lower VO and DO, however, oxygen extraction ratio was not significantly different. For each degree lower body temperature, the VO fell by 19 mL O per minute.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Grand, Johannes","Hassager, Christian","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Gustafsson, Finn","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Boesgaard, Søren","Nielsen, Niklas","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524989"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helsingborg Hospital"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Cardiac index","Hemodynamic parameters","Oxygen Consumption","Targeted temperature management","postcardiac arrest syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of hypothermia on oxygenation variables and metabolism in survivors of out of hospital cardiac arrest undergoing targeted temperature management at 000000000033 c versus 000000000036 c","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-524989","identifier":[{"id":"32584698","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114862306","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dc3e20e6-c912-4eef-99ef-ad4eb08d9fba"],"keyword":["cardiac arrest","cardiac index","hemodynamic parameters","oxygen consumption","oxygen extraction ratio","postcardiac arrest syndrome","targeted temperature management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39D07F77E43CD2A20B3EFC12AF84A82F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology","University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"helsingborg hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Helsingborg Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren","key":"boesgaardpau","last":"Boesgaard","name":"Boesgaard, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7f5e02f9-db74-437d-a29e-60baae07f850","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"10ffadd9-ed9c-4251-954a-a2c12ce83aca","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32584698"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/ther.2020.0013","issn":["21537658","21537933"],"issn_org":["21537658"],"issue":"3","journal":"Therapeutic Hypothermia and Temperature Management","pages":"170-178","status":"p","title":"Therapeutic Hypothermia and Temperature Management","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114862306"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dc3e20e6-c912-4eef-99ef-ad4eb08d9fba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of Hypothermia on Oxygenation Variables and Metabolism in Survivors of Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest Undergoing Targeted Temperature Management at 33°C Versus 36°C","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524989","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
