,"All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-29583ca3-14b7-4632-8950-227a7f363dc7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Associations between left bundle branch block with different PR intervals, QRS durations, heart rates and the risk of heart failure : a register-based cohort study using ECG data from the primary care setting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-062006","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Personal sound zones provide users to experience independent listening and quiet areas in the same acoustic environment using multiple loudspeakers. The generalized eigenvalue decomposition (GEVD) has been proposed for sound zones generation, allowing user to control the trade-off between acoustic contrast and signal distortion by adjusting some parameters. Unfortunately, these parameters are not physically meaningful, and the user has to tune them for different source materials and acoustic environments. Moreover, performing a high dimensional GEVD is computational complex. In this article, we first propose various strategies to control the reproduced sound zones as precisely and accurately as possible by reformulating the problem using physically meaningful constraints using regularization approach. Then, a hybrid approach of combining the conjugate gradient method and GEVD is proposed to reduce the computational complexity and signal distortion when the subspace dimension is small. The proposed methods show precise control over the reproduced sound zone via extensive numerical simulations in reverberant environments for different physically meaningful constraints.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shi, Liming","Lee, Taewoong","Zhang, Lijun","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069840"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian"],"keyword":["Generalized eigenvalue decomposition","Personal sound zones"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generation of personal sound zones with physical meaningful constraints and conjugate gradient method","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/465187577/SZG_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-069840","identifier":[{"id":"85099732594","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-445bdc9a-92ac-49c1-9853-125f41de24ff"],"keyword":["Conjugate gradient method","Generalized eigenvalue decomposition","Personal sound zones","Physically meaningful constraints","Subspace-based approach"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5505EE5727B578ADD4EF5D4D46E67714"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/465187577/SZG_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liming","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","locid":"e44b1378-1291-46be-b76a-fd0e196e2d46","name":"Shi, Liming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Taewoong","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","locid":"d1eeade6-8e75-427d-9c1f-1a4ac5464576","name":"Lee, Taewoong","orcid":"0000-0002-6669-0820","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Lijun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/taslp.2021.3052564","issn":["23299290"],"journal":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","pages":"823-837","paperid":"9328283","publisher":"IEEE Advancing Technology for Humanity","status":"p","title":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099732594"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-445bdc9a-92ac-49c1-9853-125f41de24ff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Generation of Personal Sound Zones With Physical Meaningful Constraints and Conjugate Gradient Method","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069840","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The aim of this study was to assess clinical pain, pain sensitization and physical performances to profile patients with chronic painful knee osteoarthritis (OA) or pain after total knee arthroplasty (TKA). Examining the interactions between pain mechanisms and physical performances would enable us to investigate the underlying explanatory relationships between these parameters. Methods: In this explorative study, 70 patients with chronic painful knee OA (N = 46) or chronic pain after TKA (N = 24) were assessed for clinical pain, quantitative sensory profiling (mechanical pinprick pain sensitivity, temporal summation (TS) and conditioned pain modulation), physical performances (chair stand, walk and stair climb tests) and self-reported outcomes. Between-group comparisons were made using ANCOVA tests and associations between outcomes were analysed using multivariate linear regression models. Results: Overall, no differences between groups regarding clinical pain and quantitative sensory profiling outcomes were observed. Physical performances were lower in the TKA group compared with the OA group with moderate-to-large effect sizes, and a tendency towards better scores in self-reported outcomes for the OA group was observed with small-to-moderate effect sizes. Self-reported function seems to be associated with physical performances in the TKA group. Sensitization (TS) appears to be associated with poorer physical performances in the OA group. Conclusions: Similar profiles for pain intensity, signs of sensitization and conditioned pain modulation were observed. Patients with TKA seems to have impaired physical performances compared with the OA group, underlining the importance of targeting physical performances. Only the OA patients showed an association between sensitization (TS) and physical performance. Significance: Quantitative pain profiling assessment was used to assess pain intensities and pain mechanisms. We observed associations between physical performances and temporal summation in the OA group underlining the importance of assessing motor functions and pain mechanisms in the same trial. We observed lower levels of physical performances in the TKA group compared with the OA group, suggesting that examination and rehabilitation of physical performances is essential for TKA patients with chronic pain.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper Bie","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Simonsen, Ole","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072333"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain sensitization and physical performances in patients with chronic painful knee osteoarthritis or chronic pain following total knee arthroplasty an explorative study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/359472653/ejp.1663.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-072333","identifier":[{"id":"85092199124","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4cd8cb6a-e549-4d9a-800b-cc1afa7f5f71"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0C669CE2F588E2A403522861CF885C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/359472653/ejp.1663.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"16d35f43-63eb-473e-a466-4f5a12d5f43f","name":"Larsen, Jesper Bie","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-7913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"dc7f061c-65a2-47fc-901a-38fac8019f1f","name":"Simonsen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal Max","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","name_org":"Madeleine, Pascal Max","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejp.1663","issn":["10903801","15322149"],"issn_org":["10903801"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Pain","pages":"213-224","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pain","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092199124"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4cd8cb6a-e549-4d9a-800b-cc1afa7f5f71"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Pain, Sensitization, and physical performances in patients with chronic painful knee osteoarthritis or chronic pain following total knee arthroplasty : an explorative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072333","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Åben komposition til undervisningsbrug","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bergstrøm-Nielsen, Carl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095515"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Musikpædagogik"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lydsamlespil","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://butik.dansksang.dk/produkt/lydformning","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095515","ids":["aau-9cc0c30b-a98d-4d01-b341-24b989a3d25c"],"keyword":["Musikpædagogik"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4708AA2772E78E7D8D6075D9BB2E4D93"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music Therapy - CEDOMUS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carl","key":"bergstrømnielsenpau","last":"Bergstrøm-Nielsen","locid":"e284f0d5-04c9-4fa1-9d72-aa087c0313b0","name":"Bergstrøm-Nielsen, Carl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"adrianpedh","last":"Adrian","name":"Adrian, Signe","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"juellundjensenpedh","last":"Juellund Jensen","name":"Juellund Jensen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771781533"],"pages":"136-37","place":"Skive","publisher":"Dansk Sang, Musiklærerforeningens forlag","status":"p","title":"Lydformning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9cc0c30b-a98d-4d01-b341-24b989a3d25c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Lydsamlespil","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-095515","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background Patient and stakeholder engagements in research have increasingly gained attention in healthcare and healthcare-related research. A common and rigorous approach to establish research priorities based on input from people and stakeholders is the James Lind Alliance Priority Setting Partnership (JLA-PSP). The aim of this study was to establish research priorities for chronic musculoskeletal (MSK) pain by engaging with humans living with chronic MSK pain, relatives to humans living with chronic MSK pain, healthcare professionals (HCP), and researchers working with chronic MSK pain. Methods This JLA-PSP included a nation-wide survey in Denmark, an interim prioritisation, and an online consensus building workshop. The information gained from this was the basis for developing the final list of specific research priorities within chronic MSK pain. Results In the initial survey, 1010 respondents (91% people living with chronic MSK pain/relatives, 9% HCPs/researchers) submitted 3121 potential questions. These were summarised into 19 main themes and 36 sub-themes. In the interim prioritisation exercise, 51% people living with pain/relatives and 49% HCPs/researchers reduced the list to 33 research questions prior to the final priority setting workshop. 23 participants attended the online workshop (12 people/relatives, 10 HCPs, and 1 researcher) who reached consensus for the most important research priorities after two rounds of discussion of each question. Conclusion This study identified several specific research questions generated by people living with chronic MSK pain, relatives, HCPs, and researchers. The stakeholders proposed prioritization of the healthcare system’s ability to support patients, focus on developing coherent pathways between sectors and education for both patients and HCP. These research questions can form the basis for future studies, funders, and be used to align research with end-users’ priorities","author_count":19,"contributors":["Lyng, Kristian Damgaard","Larsen, Jesper Bie","Birnie, K","Stinson, J","Hoegh, Morten","Olesen, Anne Estrup","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Ehlers, Lars Holger","Fonager, Kirsten","Jensen, Martin Bach","Würtzen, H","Palsson, Thorvaldur Skuli","Poulin, P","Handberg, G","Ziegler, C","Møller, LB","Olsen, J","Heise, L","Rathleff, Michael Skovdal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-105530"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hospital for Sick Children","McGill University","Ottawa Hospital","University of Calgary","University of Toronto"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Gigtforeningen"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participatory research a priority setting partnership for chronic musculoskeletal pain in denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.12.17.21267948","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-105530","ids":["aau-bf62b7e0-40e0-4ed0-ace5-64f14c7ae135"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3E48F0516DA02D84DCD3B38002B10612"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.12.17.21267948","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalb