{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To estimate the incidence of COVID-19 hospitalization in patients with inflammatory rheumatic disease (IRD); in patients with RA treated with specific DMARDs; and the incidence of severe COVID-19 infection among hospitalized patients with RA. METHODS: A nationwide cohort study from Denmark between 1 March and 12 August 2020. The adjusted incidence of COVID-19 hospitalization was estimated for patients with RA; spondyloarthritis including psoriatic arthritis; connective tissue disease; vasculitides; and non-IRD individuals. Further, the incidence of COVID-19 hospitalization was estimated for patients with RA treated and non-treated with TNF-inhibitors, HCQ or glucocorticoids, respectively. Lastly, the incidence of severe COVID-19 infection (intensive care, acute respiratory distress syndrome or death) among hospital-admitted patients was estimated for RA and non-IRD sp - individudals. RESULTS: Patients with IRD (n = 58 052) had an increased partially adjusted incidence of hospitalization with COVID-19 compared with the 4.5 million people in the general population [hazard ratio (HR) 1.46, 95% CI: 1.15, 1.86] with strongest associations for patients with RA (n = 29 440, HR 1.72, 95% CI: 1.29, 2.30) and vasculitides (n = 4072, HR 1.82, 95% CI: 0.91, 3.64). There was no increased incidence of COVID-19 hospitalization associated with TNF-inhibitor, HCQ nor glucocorticoid use. COVID-19 admitted patients with RA had a HR of 1.43 (95% CI: 0.80, 2.53) for a severe outcome. CONCLUSION: Patients with IRD were more likely to be admitted with COVID-19 than the general population, and COVID-19 admitted patients with RA could be at higher risk of a severe outcome. Treatment with specific DMARDs did not affect the risk of hospitalization.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Cordtz, René","Lindhardsen, Jesper","Soussi, B. G.","Vela, Jonathan","Uhrenholt, Line","Westermann, Rasmus","Kristensen, Salome","Nielsen, Henrik","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Dreyer, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-106631"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cordtz, René"],"keyword":["DMARDs","Epidemiology","Rheumatoid arthritis","Viruses","biological therapies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence and severeness of covid 000000000019 hospitalization in patients with inflammatory rheumatic disease a nationwide cohort study from denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7798558/pdf/keaa897.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-106631","identifier":[{"id":"33369663","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85118285908","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c2fd9541-bb6f-4a88-800b-34643f3b1652"],"keyword":["DMARDs","biological therapies","epidemiology","immunosupressants","rheumatoid arthritis","viruses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6DA0FEFB51A990BEA17C5C3F758880B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7798558/pdf/keaa897.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Rheumatology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["DANBIO"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"cordtzpau","last":"Cordtz","locid":"49fa43fa-cc2f-4876-bf14-868a1e2288a5","name":"Cordtz, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"lindhardsenpau","last":"Lindhardsen","name":"Lindhardsen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bolette G","key":"soussipau","last":"Soussi","locid":"1519256e-5063-4f58-834f-d41fd732c466","name":"Soussi, B. G.","name_org":"Soussi, Bolette G","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"velapau","last":"Vela","locid":"d37a71fc-d46e-4ea6-b522-4b4f649c44d7","name":"Vela, Jonathan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"uhrenholtpau","last":"Uhrenholt","locid":"38226050-d395-4ab2-aade-b2477bbf4ae0","name":"Uhrenholt, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-4047-7175","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"westermannpau","last":"Westermann","locid":"735a00e6-b313-4ca9-b7fa-11723d85cc21","name":"Westermann, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-8148-9658","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Salome","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"9b80939c-06cf-4c5f-8a04-3107ac4426db","name":"Kristensen, Salome","orcid":"0000-0001-5812-5234","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"b12f9d3c-1fa5-4513-8002-c9fd87d60d53","name":"Dreyer, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-5156-2922","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33369663"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/rheumatology/keaa897","issn":["14620324","14620332"],"issn_org":["14620324"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Rheumatology","paperid":"keaa897","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Rheumatology","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118285908"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","danbio"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c2fd9541-bb6f-4a88-800b-34643f3b1652"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Incidence and severeness of COVID-19 hospitalization in patients with inflammatory rheumatic disease : a nationwide cohort study from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-106631","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Longitudinal studies in HCI research have the potential to increase our understanding of how human–technology interactions evolve over time. Potentially, longitudinal studies eliminate learning or novelty effects by considering change through repeated measurements of interaction and use. However, there seems to exist no agreement of how longitudinal HCI study designs are characterized. We conducted an analysis of 106 HCI papers published at the CHI conference from 1982 to 2019 where longitudinal studies were explicitly reported. We analysed these papers using classical longitudinal study metrics, e.g. duration, metrics, methods, change or stability. We illustrate that longitudinal studies in HCI research are highly diverse in terms of duration lasting from few days to several years and different metrics are applied. It appears that the paper contribution type highly influences study design, while only a little more than half of the papers discuss or illustrate change/stability during their studies. We further underline considerations of durations versus saturation, identifying points of measurements and matching contribution types with research questions. Finally, we urge researchers to extend implications presented on perceiving duration as a singular attribute, as well as longitudinal systematic approaches to ‘in situ’ studies and ethnography in HCI.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kjærup, Maria","Skov, Mikael B.","Nielsen, Peter Axel","Kjeldskov, Jesper","Gerken, Jens","Reiterer, Harald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116770"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gelsenkirchen University of Applied Sciences","University of Konstanz"],"keyword":["Change","Duration","Human Computer Interaction","Literature review","Longitudinal","Study design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"longitudinal studies in hci research a review of chi publications from 000000001982 000000002019","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/414964186/Review_Longitudinal_HCI_chapter_Author_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-116770","ids":["aau-e585f4eb-68c3-4818-abf1-71d1c48ccb0e"],"keyword":["Change","Duration","Human-Computer Interaction","Literature Review","Longitudinal","Study design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-475CCDA9BB6724FE61453B886242F2E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/414964186/Review_Longitudinal_HCI_chapter_Author_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"gelsenkirchen university of applied sciences","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Gelsenkirchen University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of konstanz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Konstanz","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria","key":"kjæruppau","last":"Kjærup","locid":"40515b28-4