{"abstract":"Private information retrieval (PIR) lets a client retrieve an entry from a database without the server learning which entry was retrieved. Here we study a weaker variant that we call random-index PIR (RPIR), where the retrieved index is an output rather than an input of the protocol, and is chosen at random. RPIR is clearly weaker than PIR, but it suffices for some interesting applications and may be realized more efficiently than full-blown PIR. We report here on two lines of work, both tied to RPIR but otherwise largely unrelated. The first line of work studies RPIR as a primitive on its own. Perhaps surprisingly, we show that RPIR is in fact equivalent to PIR when there are no restrictions on the number of communication rounds. On the other hand, RPIR can be implemented in a “noninteractive” setting (with pre-processing), which is clearly impossible for PIR. For two-server RPIR we even show a truly noninteractive solution, offering information-theoretic security without any pre-processing. The other line of work, which was the original motivation for our work, uses RPIR to improve on the recent work of Benhamouda et al. (TCC’20) for maintaining secret values on public blockchains. Their solution depends on a method for selecting many random public keys from a PKI while hiding most of the selected keys from an adversary. However, the method they proposed is vulnerable to a double-dipping attack, limiting its resilience. Here we observe that a RPIR protocol, where the client is implemented via secure MPC, can eliminate that vulnerability. We thus get a secrets-on-blockchain protocol (and more generally large-scale MPC) which is resilient to any fraction f&lt; 1 / 2 of corrupted parties, resolving the main open problem left from the work of Benhamouda et al. As the client in this solution is implemented via secure MPC, it really brings home the need to make it as efficient as possible. We thus strive to explore whatever efficiency gains we can get by using RPIR rather than PIR. We achieve more gains by using batch RPIR where multiple indexes are retrieved at once. Lastly, we observe that this application can make do with a weaker security guarantee than full RPIR, and show that this weaker variant can be realized even more efficiently. We discuss one protocol in particular that may be attractive for practical implementations.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gentry, Craig","Halevi, Shai","Magri, Bernardo","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Yakoubov, Sophia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-133262"],"event":{"acronym":"TCC","end":"2021-11-11","place":"Raleigh, us","start":"2021-11-08","title":"19th International Conference on Theory of Cryptography, TCC 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gentry, Craig"],"keyword":["Private information retrieval"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"random index pir and applications","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/archive/2020/1248/1623511579.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-133262","identifier":[{"id":"85120076697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-06e32e05-2280-4fcc-af36-8fd2d1fdeb32"],"keyword":["Batch PIR","Large-scale MPC","Private information retrieval","Random ORAM","Random PIR","Secrets on blockchain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-444E09747D14AA407C88AFDEC9CD981C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/archive/2020/1248/1623511579.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Craig","key":"gentrypau","last":"Gentry","name":"Gentry, Craig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shai","key":"halevipau","last":"Halevi","name":"Halevi, Shai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo","key":"magripau","last":"Magri","locid":"2e4b2471-3423-4eac-a276-f6670afa1f76","name":"Magri, Bernardo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sophia","key":"yakoubovpau","last":"Yakoubov","locid":"818cd271-6e5e-4980-b248-4a337b7c0603","name":"Yakoubov, Sophia","orcid":"0000-0001-7958-8537","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kobbi","key":"nissimpedh","last":"Nissim","name":"Nissim, Kobbi","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brent","key":"waterspedh","last":"Waters","name":"Waters, Brent","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-90456-2_2","isbn":["9783030904555"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"32-61","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"19th International Conference, TCC 2021, Proceedings","title":"Theory of Cryptography"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120076697"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-06e32e05-2280-4fcc-af36-8fd2d1fdeb32"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Random-Index PIR and Applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-133262","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Modelling of ambient particle number concentrations (PNC) has been implemented in the Danish air quality modelling system DEHM/UBM/AirGIS and evaluated with long-term measurements. We implemented particle dynamical processes in the regional scale model DEHM using the M7 aerosol dynamics module (presented in the accompanying article by Frohn et al., 2021), and we developed models for PNC at the local scale (UBM) and street scale (OSPM), in a first approximation without including the particle dynamics as presented in this article. Outdoor concentration estimates are provided at the front door of all residential address locations in Denmark for the past 40 years (1979–2018) with a spatial resolution of 1 km × 1 km taking all emission sectors in Denmark into account and additionally at the street location, with significant traffic (>500 vehicles/day). We evaluated our model with up to 18-year long measurement time series of particle number size distributions (PNSD) at Danish street, urban and rural background stations. Two particle size ranges were used for evaluation: PNC >10 (count of particles with diameter larger than 10 nm) and PNC 30_250 (diameter range 30–250 nm), in order to exclude nucleation events from the measurements and to obtain a consistent long-term measured time series. When comparing our model estimates with PNC 30_250 measurements, we obtain Pearson correlation coefficients (R p) in the range 0.39–0.95 depending on station location (street, urban background, rural) and averaging time (hour, day, month, year). The highest correlations were found for yearly averages at a monitoring station located at a street with dense traffic (R p = 0.95) whereas shorter time averages and comparisons with monitoring stations at urban and rural background locations provided lower correlations. The model performance for PNC in terms of correlation coefficients with respect to measurements is comparable to the performance for other pollutants such as NO X, PM 2.5 and better than the performance for PM 10. The model generally overestimated the observed concentrations, Normalized Mean Bias (NMB) was in the range 6%–190% compared to PNC >10 and 90%–290% compared to PNC 30_250. These relatively high NMBs are probably caused by uncertainties in the modelling process, especially the estimation of particle number emissions, which largely determine the ambient concentrations of PNC. Furthermore, uncertainties might as well originate from the complexity of modelling particle dynamical processes accurately and the great challenges in performing long-term PNC measurements. The presented model can estimate PNC at all Danish addresses over the last 40 years with a 1-h time resolution. The data seem to provide a good indication of the relative differences in PNC at Danish addresses.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ketzel, Matthias","Frohn, Lise Marie","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Massling, Andreas","Andersen, Christopher","Im, Ulas","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Khan, Jibran","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Manders, Astrid","Dernier van der Gon, Hugo","Kumar, Prashant","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154423"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ketzel, Matthias"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Netherlands Organization for Applied Scientific Research (TNO)","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling ultrafine particle number concentrations at address resolution in denmark from 000000001979 to 000000002018 part 000000000002 local and street scale modelling and evaluation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2021.118633","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154423","identifier":[{"id":"85114771391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2be307b0-6348-4a61-8b4e-bc8a73d6490d"],"keyword":["Particle numer concentration Local-scale air pollution modelling Ultrafine particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-8-08A58D8A7AA30E12EE38614B1DEED9B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273780527/1_s2.0_S1352231021004556_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2021.118633","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"netherlands organization for applied scientific research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Netherlands Organization for Applied Scientific Research (TNO)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Marie","key":"frohnpau","last":"Frohn","locid":"1db55612-df02-4189-ab0d-5c62193e1afc","name":"Frohn, Lise Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4236-5708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"masslingpau","last":"Massling","locid":"5bb9394c-7de2-4cb2-a79d-a5e2af778523","name":"Massling, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-8046-2798","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christopher","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3cb895d7-5de5-421e-a12f-ce9982a1cdeb","name":"Andersen, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-2337-8239","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Solvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0d52f91a-4eaa-46f9-ab5f-d7fd3c31440d","name":"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0