address resolution in Denmark from 1979 to 2018 - Part 2: : Local and street scale modelling and evaluation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154423","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Cable bacteria are multicellular filamentous bacteria within the Desulfobulbaceae that couple the oxidation of sulfide to the reduction of oxygen over centimeter distances via long distance electron transport (LDET). So far, none of the freshwater or marine cable bacteria species have been isolated into pure culture. Here we describe a method for establishing a stable single-strain cable bacterium culture in partially sterilized sediment. By repeated transfers of a single cable bacterium filament from freshwater pond sediment into autoclaved sediment, we obtained strain GS, identified by its 16S rRNA gene as a member of Ca. Electronema. This strain was further propagated by transferring sediment clumps, and has now been stable within its semi-natural microbial community for several years. Its metagenome-assembled genome was 93% complete, had a size of 2.76 Mbp, and a DNA G + C content of 52%. Average Nucleotide Identity (ANI) and Average Amino Acid Identity (AAI) suggest the affiliation of strain GS to Ca. Electronema as a novel species. Cell size, number of outer ridges, and detection of LDET in the GS culture are likewise consistent with Ca. Electronema. Based on these combined features, we therefore describe strain GS as a new cable bacterium species of the candidate genus Electronema, for which we propose the name Candidatus Electronema aureum sp.nov. Although not a pure culture, this stable single-strain culture will be useful for physiological and omics-based studies; similar approaches with single-cell or single-filament transfers into natural medium may also aid the characterization of other difficult-to-culture microbes.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thorup, Casper","Petro, Caitlin","Bøggild, Andreas","Ebsen, Tine Sneibjerg","Brokjær, Signe","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Schramm, Andreas","Bjerg, Jesper Jensen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-185914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schramm, Andreas"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Antwerp"],"keyword":["Cable bacteria","Cultivation","Filament","Freshwater sediment","Genome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to grow your cable bacteria establishment of a stable single strain culture in sediment and proposal of candidatus electronema aureum gs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.syapm.2021.126236","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-185914","identifier":[{"id":"34332367","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000697699400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85111286198","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-631826a1-2ad9-4eb0-a7b0-e7fe0094117c"],"keyword":["Autoclave","Cable bacteria","Cultivation","Filament","Freshwater sediment","Genome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-41B089A2A1C156AE15D1309DF3DA03CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/285206996/1_s2.0_S072320202100059X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.syapm.2021.126236","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Electromicrobiology","Aarhus Unive