{"abstract":"NORTH is a small-sized tokamak located at the Technical University of Denmark. It can be operated both as a spherical tokamak and a simple magnetized torus (SMT). Here we show first experimental results. We discuss the setup of the device, including the layout of the vacuum vessel, the magnetic field coils, the power supply systems, the heating sources, diagnostics, and the control system. We present measurements in discharges that have been heated by electron cyclotron resonance heating at the fundamental resonance. The waves have been injected both from the low-field side and the high-field side, and rich fluctuation spectra in Langmuir probe and Rogowski coil signals are presented during the different plasma phases. Finally, we discuss research plans and further installations to be made on NORTH.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Gryaznevich, M. P.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Jensen, T.","Jessen, Martin","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Rasmussen, Jesper","Salewski, Mirko","Senstius, M. G.","Naulin, Volker","Nem, R. D.","Korsgaard, M.L.H.","Nilsson, A. C.","Dam, F.","Goltermann, A.","Pedersen, A. C.","Sutherland, M. T.","Aalto, T.","Hokkanen, A.","Salmi, A.","Tala, T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368800"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Stefan Kragh"],"country":["Finland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tokamak Energy Ltd","VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland Ltd."],"keyword":["Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Plasma diagnostics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"first results from the north tokamak","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85101576338","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank Tokamak Energy for providing essential equipment. This work was supported by a research grant (15483) from VILLUM FONDEN. This work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014?2018 and 2019?2020 under grant agreement no. 633053. The views and opinions expressed herein do not necessarily reflect those of the European Commission. The authors would like to thank Tokamak Energy for providing essential equipment. This work was supported by a research grant ( 15483 ) from VILLUM FONDEN . This work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014–2018 and 2019–2020 under grant agreement no. 633053 . The views and opinions expressed herein do not necessarily reflect those of the European Commission."],"id":"S01-000.00-368800","identifier":[{"id":"85101576338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d6f17d2f-b3bb-4b37-83b7-4021babccd33"],"keyword":["Electron Bernstein wave heating","Electron cyclotron resonance heating","Plasma diagnostics","Tokamak operation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA140113B80EBFC6F2575425E38C7191"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"tokamak energy ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Tokamak Energy Ltd","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"vtt technical research centre of finland ltd","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland Ltd.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. P.","key":"gryaznevichpau","last":"Gryaznevich","name":"Gryaznevich, M. P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. S.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","name_org":"Jacobsen, A. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e840242d-2592-40b7-bc0b-02995c8fe6ba","name":"Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9801-1530","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"697d9805-d9c6-46ba-a045-8bb3467320f6","name":"Jessen, Martin","name_org":"Jessen, M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. B.","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","name_org":"Korsholm, S. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","name_org":"Salewski, M.","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. G.","key":"senstiuspau","last":"Senstius","locid":"81cb5107-081b-4ec9-aa8c-c7d1c565a07e","name":"Senstius, M. G.","orcid":"0000-0001-9596-7457","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"V.","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","name_org":"Naulin, V.","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R. D.","key":"nempau","last":"Nem","locid":"01ae5d52-705b-4557-a300-a13378847e1c","name":"Nem, R. D.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.L.H.","key":"korsgaardpau","last":"Korsgaard","name":"Korsgaard, M.L.H.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. C.","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, A. C.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","name":"Dam, F.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"goltermannpau","last":"Goltermann","name":"Goltermann, A.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. C.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c556b4ff-2212-4156-97bc-38f155bedae7","name":"Pedersen, A. C.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. T.","key":"sutherlandpau","last":"Sutherland","name":"Sutherland, M. T.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"aaltopau","last":"Aalto","name":"Aalto, T.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"hokkanenpau","last":"Hokkanen","name":"Hokkanen, A.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"salmipau","last":"Salmi","name":"Salmi, A.","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"talapau","last":"Tala","name":"Tala, T.","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fusengdes.2021.112288","issn":["09203796","18737196"],"issn_org":["09203796"],"journal":"Fusion Engineering and Design","paperid":"112288","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fusion Engineering and Design","volume":"166"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101576338"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d6f17d2f-b3bb-4b37-83b7-4021babccd33"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"First results from the NORTH tokamak","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-368800","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Tumor-associated macrophages often correlate with tumor progression, and therapies targeting immune cells in tumors have emerged as promising treatments. To select effective therapies, we established an in vitro 3D multicellular spheroid model including cancer cells, fibroblasts, and monocytes. We analyzed monocyte infiltration and differentiation in spheroids generated from fi-broblasts and either of the cancer cell lines MCF-7, HT-29, PANC-1, or MIA PaCa-2. Monocytes rapidly infiltrated spheroids and differentiated into mature macrophages with diverse phenotypes in a cancer cell line-dependent manner. MIA PaCa-2 spheroids polarized infiltrating monocytes to M2-like macrophages with high CD206 and CD14 expression, whereas monocytes polarized by MCF-7 spheroids displayed an M1-like phenotype. Monocytes in HT-29 and PANC-1 primarily obtained an M2-like phenotype but also showed upregulation of M1 markers. Analysis of the secretion of 43 soluble factors demonstrated that the cytokine profile between spheroid cultures differed con-siderably depending on the cancer cell line. Secretion of most of the cytokines increased upon the addition of monocytes resulting in a more inflammatory and pro-tumorigenic environment. These multicellular spheroids can be used to recapitulate the tumor microenvironment and the phenotype of tumor-associated macrophages in vitro and provide more realistic 3D cancer models allowing the in vitro screening of immunotherapeutic compounds.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Madsen, Natasha Helleberg","Nielsen, Boye Schnack","Nhat, Son Ly","Skov, Søren","Gad, Monika","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-410577"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Drug screening","In vitro assay","Multicellular spheroids","Tumor associated macrophages","Tumor microenvironment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-BION"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-BION","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monocyte infiltration and differentiation in 000000000003d multicellular spheroid cancer models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pathogens10080969","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-410577","identifier":[{"id":"34451433","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8399809","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85112626190","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1cbffae8-270e-4583-b576-d81b113d406b"],"keyword":["3D cancer cell models","Drug screening","In vitro assay","Multicellular spheroids","Tumor microenvironment","Tumor-associated macrophages"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81ED153B2DF3CEFE7CFACD5490D43E34"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pathogens10080969","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/276901457/pathogens_10_00969_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"bioneer","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-BION","l3nn":"Bioneer","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bioneer","namevar":["Bioneer"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-BION","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Natasha Helleberg","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Natasha Helleberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Boye Schnack","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Boye Schnack","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Son Ly","key":"nhatpau","last":"Nhat","name":"Nhat, Son Ly","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"c1c333fb-a9e9-4c7b-8d50-ef83a755fa41","name":"Skov, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Monika","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","name":"Gad, Monika","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34451433"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/pathogens10080969","issn":["20760817"],"issue":"8","journal":"Pathogens","paperid":"969","status":"p","title":"Pathogens","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112626190"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1cbffae8-270e-4583-b576-d81b113d406b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Monocyte infiltration and differentiation in 3d multicellular spheroid cancer models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-410577","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Buch-Hansen, Gitte","Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-420177"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forord bibelske konfigurationer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-420177","ids":["ku-2cd96beb-9a24-4717-916b-753c10e03ef1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1003CC9F24DD9AD0308513368240B6EA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Gitte","key":"buchhansenpau","last":"Buch-Hansen","locid":"82ed8803-3d7a-407d-a479-597c890bbd76","name":"Buch-Hansen, Gitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"7-24","publisher":"Eksistensen Akademisk","status":"p","title":"Bibelske konfigurationer i kunst og kultur"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2cd96beb-9a24-4717-916b-753c10e03ef1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forord. Bibelske konfigurationer","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-420177","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Mapping the within-field variability of crop status is of great importance in precision agriculture, which seeks to balance agronomic inputs with spatial crop demands. Satellite imagery and the delineation of management zones based on remote sensing plays a key role. However, satellite imagery is dependent on a cloud-free view, which is especially challenging in temperate regions such as Northern Europe. This disadvantage can be overcome with unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV), which provide an alternative to satellites. An investigation was conducted to establish whether UAV imagery can generate similar crop heterogeneity maps to satellites (Sentinel 2) and the extent to which crop heterogeneity and management zones can be reproduced by repeated data collection within short time intervals. Three winter wheat fields were monitored during the growing season. Two vegetation indices (NDVI and MSAVI2) based on red and near-infrared (NIR) reflectance were calculated to delineate fields into five management zones based on NDVI raster maps using quintiles. The Pearson correlation coefficient, the Nash-Sutcliffe agreement coefficient and the smallest real difference coefficient (SRD), also called the reproducibility coefficient were used to evaluate the reproducibility. NDVI and MSAVI2 gave similar results, but NDVI was a slightly better descriptor of crop heterogeneity after canopy closure and NDVI was used for the remainder of the study. The results showed that substitution of satellite data with UAV data resulted in an average reclassification of 10 m by 10 m management zones corresponding to 58% of the total field area. Reclassification means that management pixels were classified differently according to origin of images. Repeated satellite and UAV imagery resulted in 39% and 47% reclassification, respectively. The results showed that the reproduction of remote sensing data with different sensor systems added more measurement error to measurements than was the case with repeated measurements using the same sensor systems. In this study, SRD averaged 2.5 management zones, which means that differences up to 2.5 management zones were within the measurement error. This paper discusses the practical aspects of these findings and clarifies that the reclassification of management zones is depending on the heterogeneity of the studied fields. Therefore, the achieved results may not be generalized but the presented methodology can be used in future studies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Azim, Saiful","Boldsen, Søren Kjærgaard","Nitschke, Thomas","Jensen, Signe Marie","Nielsen, Jon","Christensen, Svend"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444992"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm","Cameras","GROWTH","Imagery","Management zones","Reproducibility","Sensors","Sentinel 2","Site specific management","Systems","Technology","Wheat"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the challenge of reproducing remote sensing data from satellites and unmanned aerial vehicles uavs in the context of management zones and precision agriculture","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-444992","identifier":[{"id":"85092928963","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000582299600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-564b190d-7e49-44ba-a71e-fd0677a6a4c1"],"keyword":["ALGORITHM","CAMERAS","Crop heterogeneity","CropSAT","GROWTH","IMAGERY","Management zones","Reproducibility","SENSORS","SITE-SPECIFIC MANAGEMENT","SYSTEMS","Sentinel 2","TECHNOLOGY","Variable rate application (VRA)","WHEAT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52853BE83B698CEFCFF5FAEAA381E3B9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["AgroTech AS"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Saiful","key":"azimpau","last":"Azim","locid":"6fdcaa54-993e-45e1-9976-cfd74fac0c12","name":"Azim, Saiful","orcid":"0000-0002-2686-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren Kjærgaard","key":"boldsenpau","last":"Boldsen","name":"Boldsen, Søren Kjærgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"nitschkepau","last":"Nitschke","name":"Nitschke, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe M.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"14cef501-7495-4c75-8c0f-28057dd3fcc0","name":"Jensen, Signe Marie","name_org":"Jensen, Signe M.","orcid":"0000-0002-7738-5231","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d45561f-3e81-41e1-8310-03bdb7abbad0","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c284dfaf-4015-461e-9604-be