{"abstract":"Background: The breeding prognosis for a mare with fungal (yeast or mold) endometritis is generally considered poor. To our knowledge, however, no reports have been published on the expected pregnancy rate for mares diagnosed with a fungal infection. Study design: Insemination records from 3,223 mares inseminated at two stud farms were retrospectively examined. Mares diagnosed with fungal endometritis were all treated with uterine lavage using physiological saline, intrauterine deposition of 100 mg Clotrimazole vagitorial tablets and oxytocin (10 i.e., i.m.) for three consecutive days. Methods: From mares with signs of endometritis microbiological culture and cytological assessment were performed on endometrial biopsies. The per season pregnancy results were compared between affected and unaffected mares. Results: A total of 686 mares out of 3,223 mares were considered to have endometritis. Based on the endometrial biopsies obtained, 377 (55%) had no growth, 50 (7.2%) had growth of yeast, 2 (0.3%) had growth of mold and 257 (37.4%) had growth of bacteria recorded. Positive cytology was found in 78.0% of samples diagnosed with yeast endometritis whereas that was the case in 65.6% of samples showing growth of mold or bacteria (P = 0.12). The per-season pregnancy rate was 48% in mares diagnosed with yeast endometritis. The overall per season pregnancy rate in the two stud farms was 76.4% (P < 0.0001, Odds ratio = 3.59, confidence interval 95% = 2.04–6.29). Conclusions: Yeast can make up a considerable cause of endometritis. The breeding prognosis of a mare with yeast endometritis must be considered worse than that of a normal mare. Following management of the condition approximately 50% of the mares previously diagnosed with an endometrial yeast infection got in foal rendering the breeding prognosis better than initially anticipated.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Møller","Fog, Peter","Bojesen, Anders Miki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-510455"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Candida","Clotrimazole","Endometritis","Fungus","Horse","Yeast"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of yeast endometritis on fertility in the mare","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-510455","identifier":[{"id":"85101888093","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33781433","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c409df0c-0880-4ec1-b825-c83e826cbac9"],"keyword":["Candida","Clotrimazole","Endometritis","Fungus","Horse","Yeast"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2D683FDB0145948A86B1B5695769EA4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Ansager Hestehospital"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Møller","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"fogpau","last":"Fog","name":"Fog, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Miki","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"404f5838-4d57-4c72-809d-ba35461a74e8","name":"Bojesen, Anders Miki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33781433"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jevs.2021.103409","issn":["07370806","15427412"],"issn_org":["07370806"],"journal":"Journal of Equine Veterinary Science","paperid":"103409","status":"p","title":"Journal of Equine Veterinary Science","volume":"99"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101888093"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","ansager hestehospital"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c409df0c-0880-4ec1-b825-c83e826cbac9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of Yeast Endometritis on Fertility in the Mare","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510455","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Adaptive introgression - the flow of adaptive genetic variation between species or populations - has attracted significant interest in recent years and it has been implicated in a number of cases of adaptation, from pesticide resistance and immunity, to local adaptation. Despite this, methods for identification of adaptive introgression from population genomic data are lacking. Here, we present Ancestry-HMM-S, a hidden Markov model-based method for identifying genes undergoing adaptive introgression and quantifying the strength of selection acting on them. Through extensive validation, we show that this method performs well on moderately sized data sets for realistic population and selection parameters. We apply Ancestry-HMM-S to a data set of an admixed Drosophila melanogaster population from South Africa and we identify 17 loci which show signatures of adaptive introgression, four of which have previously been shown to confer resistance to insecticides. Ancestry-HMM-S provides a powerful method for inferring adaptive introgression in data sets that are typically collected when studying admixed populations. This method will enable powerful insights into the genetic consequences of admixture across diverse populations. Ancestry-HMM-S can be downloaded from https://github.com/jesvedberg/Ancestry-HMM-S/.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Svedberg, Jesper","Shchur, Vladimir","Reinman, Solomon","Nielsen, Rasmus","Corbett-Detig, Russell"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511323"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Russia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Higher School of Economics","University of California at Santa Cruz"],"keyword":["Adaptive","Adaptive introgression","Admixture","Evolution","HMM","Hybridisation","Population genomics","Selection","pesticide resistance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inferring adaptive introgression using hidden markov models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msab014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511323","identifier":[{"id":"85106068919","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8097282","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33502512","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c5811e6c-4281-46cc-aa24-76d883d47e86"],"keyword":["HMM","adaptive","adaptive introgression","admixture","evolution","hybridisation","pesticide resistance","population genomics","selection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8565E614D12B3D03F58A19442F6A001"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msab014","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273072592/Inferring_Adaptive_Introgression_Using_Hidden_Markov_Models.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california at santa cruz","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Santa Cruz","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ru","key":"higher school of economics","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Higher School of Economics","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"svedbergpau","last":"Svedberg","name":"Svedberg, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vladimir","key":"shchurpau","last":"Shchur","name":"Shchur, Vladimir","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Solomon","key":"reinmanpau","last":"Reinman","name":"Reinman, Solomon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"68905e51-280a-4c0b-bc94-469bb52de9b6","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-0513-6591","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Russell","key":"corbettdetigpau","last":"Corbett-Detig","name":"Corbett-Detig, Russell","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33502512"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/molbev/msab014","issn":["07374038","15371719"],"issn_org":["07374038"],"issue":"5","journal":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","pages":"2152-2165","status":"p","title":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106068919"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c5811e6c-4281-46cc-aa24-76d883d47e86"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Inferring Adaptive Introgression Using Hidden Markov Models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511323","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
