{"abstract":"Use of medications of questionable benefit is common in end of life care. In order to effectively carry out deprescribing, it is important to gain insight into the perspectives of patients and their relatives. Thus, our objective was to explore perspectives on deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives. We conducted semi-structured interviews with ten nursing home residents and nine relatives. Interviews were analysed using systematic text condensation. Four main themes were identified: “Medication as a necessity and to feel well,” “Frailty as a barrier for taking responsibility,” “Patient autonomy and faith in authority” and “A wish for being involved.” Most participants had not considered the possibility of deprescribing but were open towards medication change if proposed by a healthcare professional. Most participants did not have in-depth knowledge about medication but would like to be informed or involved in decisions. The participants generally had faith in healthcare professionals despite limited contact. Our study implies that older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives are generally interested in deprescribing activities; however, the initiative of deprescribing lies with the healthcare professionals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Graabæk, Trine","Lundby, Carina","Ryg, Jesper","Søndergaard, Jens","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-085.00-049485"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Graabæk, Trine"],"keyword":["Deprescribing","End of life","Frailty","Interview","Perspectives"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i simply don t know because i don t know which drugs i get perspectives on deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13476","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.00-049485","identifier":[{"id":"32770703","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85089886760","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c5e5dcd7-d530-4a23-9e5d-0724fadff61b","ucl-dee6f323-56aa-48a4-827d-029257625d8e"],"keyword":["deprescribing","end of life","frailty","interview","perspectives"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8149D1337E690857BB0C07ABAABFEB98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13476","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/172886545/Manuscript_pt_rel_accepted_20200904.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["University College Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"graabækpau","last":"Graabæk","locid":"67e97b89-6918-4950-9557-f5e3939a3c57","name":"Graabæk, Trine","orcid":"0000-0001-6848-3107","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carina","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","locid":"ef58a4be-0ffe-42f3-80ec-7f6cecf96102","name":"Lundby, Carina","orcid":"0000-0002-2121-6252","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32770703"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.13476","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"1","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"115-127","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089886760"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c5e5dcd7-d530-4a23-9e5d-0724fadff61b","ucl-dee6f323-56aa-48a4-827d-029257625d8e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"“I simply don't know, because I don't know which drugs I get” : Perspectives on deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.00-049485","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hearing loss is the third leading cause of years lived with disability. It is estimated that 430 million people worldwide are affected, and the number of cases is expected to increase in the future. There is therefore increased pressure on hearing health systems around the world to improve efficiency and reduce costs to ensure increased access to quality hearing health care. Here, we describe the User-Operated Audiometry project, the goal of which is to introduce an automated system for user-operated audiometric testing into everyday clinic practice as a means to relieve part of this pressure. The alternative to the existing referral route is presented in which examination is executed via the user-operated system. This route is conceptualized as an interaction between the patient, the system, and the hearing care professional (HCP). Technological requirements of the system and challenges that are related to the interaction between patients, the user-operated system, and the HCPs within the specific medical setting are discussed. Lastly, a strategy for the development and implementation of user-operated audiometry is presented, which includes initial investigations, a validation study, and implementation in a real-life clinical situation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sidiras, Christos","Sanchez Lopez, Raul","Pedersen, Ellen Raben","Sørensen, Chris Bang","Nielsen, Jacob","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass"],"cuid":["S02-095.56-037752"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sidiras, Christos"],"keyword":["Audiometry","Automated","Hearing aid","Hearing loss","Telehealth","User operated"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user operated audiometry project uaud introducing an automated user operated system for audiometric testing into everyday clinic practice","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdgth.2021.724748","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.56-037752","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8529271","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34713194","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85131240867","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e72f8411-8969-4ca6-aa9b-6cb9f8d91c5a","sdu-dd0778f7-7c09-4a47-8f16-4d7e1b8bab34"],"keyword":["Audiometry","Hearing aid","Hearing loss","Hearing test","Telehealth","User-operated","automated"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9AC245DCB945E4C0E06FA2136446198E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258407323/fdgth_03_724748.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/193774453/User_Operated_Audiometry.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdgth.2021.724748","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Health Informatics and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Hearing Systems Section","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Hearing Systems Section, Hearing Systems Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christos","key":"sidiraspau","last":"Sidiras","locid":"f7ef18da-9b53-4020-a432-01c656098a8f","name":"Sidiras, Christos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Raul","key":"sanchezlopezpau","last":"Sanchez-Lopez","locid":"2fec602c-d244-46d1-85bc-5f29334a659c","name":"Sanchez Lopez, Raul","name_org":"Sanchez-Lopez, Raul","orcid":"0000-0002-5239-2339","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen Raben","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b7a104b3-f660-4af6-a5eb-aa39f455e89f","name":"Pedersen, Ellen Raben","orcid":"0000-0001-9917-9837","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chris Bang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"d99e9d61-082b-402c-9764-1deb459c7110","name":"Sørensen, Chris Bang","orcid":"0000-0002-2279-2091","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6b7d9868-eaae-40aa-a71f-f4839698f60f","name":"Nielsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-5134-8950","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"db84fc4e-28da-45af-a608-13ce8f4ec719","name":"Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","name_org":"Schmidt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7683-1407","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34713194"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fdgth.2021.724748","issn":["2673253X"],"issn_org":["2673253x"],"journal":"Frontiers in Digital Health","paperid":"724748","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Digital Health","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131240867"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e72f8411-8969-4ca6-aa9b-6cb9f8d91c5a","sdu-dd0778f7-7c09-4a47-8f16-4d7e1b8bab34"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"User-Operated Audiometry Project (UAud) – Introducing an Automated User-Operated System for Audiometric Testing Into Everyday Clinic Practice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.56-037752","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The term dementia-friendly hospital is increasingly used to describe a variety of initiatives and strategies that are implemented to meet the challenges faced by patients with dementia during hospitalization. However, no definition of the dementia-friendly hospital currently exists. This qualitative focus group study aimed to describe stakeholders' perspectives of the dementia-friendly hospital. Four stakeholder groups were included: people with dementia, relatives, hospital staff, and representatives from the Danish Alzheimer Association. The thematic analysis suggests that a person-centered approach is a key feature. This approach is described as a continuously reflexive awareness of how to see the person behind the dementia diagnosis. We discuss possible revision of the current dementia discourse and the implications of the findings for future practice and research.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ginnerup Toubøl, Annemarie","Moestrup, Lene","Ryg, Jesper","Thomsen, Katja","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-096.88-742466"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ginnerup Toubøl, Annemarie"],"keyword":["Dementia","Dementia Friendly Hospital","Focus Groups","Qualitative description","Thematic analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stakeholder perspectives of the dementia friendly hospital a qualitative descriptive focus group study","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85091016505","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.88-742466","identifier":[{"id":"85091016505","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32930603","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-afaf834a-c021-4c9d-a3be-cc8c088fbb6c","ucl-02842158-7fc9-4f2a-b35d-1cdc689704b8"],"keyword":["dementia","dementia-friendly hospital","focus groups","qualitative description","stakeholders’ perspective","thematic analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E901A17FE20E25415401BDF3C22B96E5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen i Vejle"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Geriatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annemarie Ginnerup","key":"toubølpau","last":"Toubøl","locid":"28296f4e-241d-4748-bb8e-5364a07e3d11","name":"Toubøl, Annemarie Ginnerup","orcid":"0000-0003-4794-8862","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"moestruppau","last":"Moestrup","locid":"b5ec9bc0-552c-4f92-9dd2-df00a997660c","name":"Moestrup, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-0978-664X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katja","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"26fcee0e-9fd1-47db-847b-ba123b840681","name":"Thomsen, Katja","orcid":"0000-0002-0454-836X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32930603"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1471301220947848","issn":["14713012","17412684"],"issn_org":["14713012"],"issue":"5","journal":"Dementia","pages":"1501-1517","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Dementia","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091016505"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-afaf834a-c021-4c9d-a3be-cc8c088fbb6c","ucl-02842158-7fc9-4f2a-b35d-1cdc689704b8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Stakeholder perspectives of the dementia-friendly hospital : A qualitative descriptive focus group study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.88-742466","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Targeted temperature management (TTM) following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) prolongs the QT-interval but our knowledge of different temperatures and risk of arrhythmia is incomplete. Objective: To assess whether the QTc, QT-peak (QTp) and T-peak to T-end interval (TpTe) may be useful markers of ventricular arrhythmia in contemporary post cardiac arrest treatment. Methods: An ECG-substudy of the TTM-trial (TTM at 33 °C vs. 36 °C) with serial ECGs from 680 (94%) patients. Bazett's (B) and Fridericia's (F) formula were used for heart rate correction of the QT, QTp and TpTe. Ventricular arrhythmia (VT/VF) were registered during the first three days of post cardiac arrest care. Results: The QT, QTc and QTp intervals were prolonged more at 33 °C compared to 36 °C and restored to similar and lower levels after rewarming. The TpTe-interval remained between 92–100 ms throughout TTM in both groups. The QTc intervals were associated with ventricular arrhythmia, but not after adjustment for cardiac arrest characteristics. The QTp-interval was not associated with risk of ventricular arrhythmia. Heart rate corrected TpTe-intervals were associated with higher risk of arrhythmia (Odds ratio (OR): TpTe(B): 1.12 (1.02–1.23, p = 0.01 TpTe(F): 1.12 (1.02–1.23, p = 0.02) per 20 ms). Further a prolonged TpTe-interval ≥ 90 ms was consistently associated with higher risk (OR adjusted: TpTe(B): 2.05 (1.25–3.37), p < 0.01, TpTe(F): 2.14 (1.32–3.49), p < 0.01). Conclusions: TTM prolongs the QT-interval by prolongation of the QTp-interval without association to increased risk. The TpTe-interval is not significantly affected by core temperature, but heart rate corrected TpTe intervals are robustly associated with risk of ventricular arrhythmia. Trial registration: The TTM-trial is registered and accessible at ClinicalTrials.gov (Identifier: NCT01020916).","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hartvig Thomsen, Jakob","Hassager, Christian","Erlinge, David","Nielsen, Niklas","Greve Lindholm, Matias","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Grand, Johannes","Pehrson, Steen","Graff, Claus","Køber, Lars V.","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-097.86-006478"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hartvig Thomsen, Jakob"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helsingborg Hospital","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Comatose","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","QT interval","QT peak","QTp","T peak T end interval","Targeted temperature management","Therapeutic hypothermia","TpTe","Ventricular arrhythmia","Ventricular fibrillation","Ventricular tachycardia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"repolarization and ventricular arrhythmia during targeted temperature management post cardiac arrest","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85114332751&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.86-006478","identifier":[{"id":"34271131","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114332751","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-86040800-9f96-419c-8adb-73430eb85ec7","ku-191d2397-aba9-4a5a-bda7-98e2b3d1669b"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Comatose","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","QT interval","QT peak","QTp","T-peak T-end interval","Targeted temperature management","Therapeutic hypothermia","TpTe","Ventricular arrhythmia","Ventricular fibrillation","Ventricular tachycardia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1557AC11DE97A5113E73DDE1E26D49AB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"helsingborg hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Helsingborg Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"hartvigthomsenpau","last":"Hartvig Thomsen","name":"Hartvig Thomsen, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Hartvig","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matias","key":"grevelindholmpau","last":"Greve Lindholm","name":"Greve Lindholm, Matias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matias Greve","key":"lindholmpau","last":"Lindholm","name":"Lindholm, Matias Greve","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"pehrsonpau","last":"Pehrson","name":"Pehrson, Steen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lars V.","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","name_org":"Køber, Lars V.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"10ffadd9-ed9c-4251-954a-a2c12ce83aca","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34271131"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2021.07.004","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"74-82","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"166"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114332751"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-86040800-9f96-419c-8adb-73430eb85ec7","ku-191d2397-aba9-4a5a-bda7-98e2b3d1669b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Repolarization and ventricular arrhythmia during targeted temperature management post cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.86-006478","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Wood ash is a by-product from energy production that can be recycled to forests to regain nutrients and prevent acidification. However, low concentrations of nitrogen (N) in wood ash may reduce its potential positive effect on plant growth. In addition, wood ash can have a high content of toxic heavy metals such as Cd, thus there are concerns that it may increase Cd accumulation in plants. We grew Deschampsia flexuosa (Wavy hair-grass) in pots in acidic nutrient poor forest soil fertilized with different concentrations of wood ash (corresponding to field application of 0, 1.1, 3.3, 11 and 33 t ha −1). Additionally, to disentangle the pH and nutrient effects of wood ash application, we included treatments with either CaO, to simulate pH effects of wood ash, or potassium (K) + phosphorus (P) fertilizer to mimic the nutrient effects. After 4.5 months of growth, we measured soil pH, plant biomass, Cd accumulation in shoots and N concentration in the various compartments of the system. Wood ash addition stimulated plant growth, whereas CaO and K + P addition resulted in more moderate increases in biomass. Despite the low concentration of N in the wood ash, plant uptake of N increased in wood ash amendments, probably because wood ash stimulated mineralization of soil organic N. Plant Cd content significantly increased at the highest dose of wood ash. Our results suggest that addition of wood ash significantly stimulates plant growth due to the combined effect of increased pH, elevated nutrient levels and increased N mineralization. Furthermore, despite the rather high Cd content in used wood ash (16.3 mg kg −1), wood ash amendments up to 11 t ha −1 did not result in significantly increased plant uptake of Cd.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Johansen, Jesper L.","Nielsen, Maiken L.","Madsen, Mette Vestergård","Mortensen, Louise Hindborg","Cruz-Paredes, Carla","Rønn, Regin","Kjøller, Rasmus","Hovmand, Mads Frederik","Christensen, Søren","Ekelund, Flemming"],"cuid":["S02-098.76-013072"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Johansen, Jesper L."],"keyword":["Cadmium","Circular economy","Plant growth","Plant nutrients","Soil pH","Sustainability","Wood ash"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the complexity of wood ash fertilization disentangled effects on soil ph nutrient status plant growth and cadmium accumulation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/317372350/The_complexity_of_wood_ash_fertilization_disentangled.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.76-013072","identifier":[{"id":"85101337157","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000642458900003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-06740d3d-35b0-4f67-9642-9e527371a7f5","ku-45d90c36-b522-41c5-9679-2cc17f1ce493"],"keyword":["Cadmium","Circular economy","Plant growth","Plant nutrients","Soil pH","Sustainability","Wood ash"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-95AB5E60C2CBF7528FF3D8F00A0AEB3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/317372350/The_complexity_of_wood_ash_fertilization_disentangled.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Univer