{"abstract":"Dysregulation of interleukin 33 (IL-33) has been implicated in the pathogenesis of several autoimmune and inflammatory diseases, but few studies have examined transcriptional regulation of the IL33 gene. In the intestines, gene regulation is controlled by a transcription factor network of which the intestinal-specific transcription factor CDX2 is a key component. In this study, we investigated whether CDX2 regulates IL33 mRNA expression. We examined IL33 mRNA expression in primary colonic epithelial cells from healthy humans and epithelial cell lines, revealing high expression levels in primary colonic and LS174T cells. Combining genomics data (ChIP-Seq, RNA-Seq) and IL33 promoter analyses in LS174T cells revealed intronic enhancer activity in the IL33 gene that is dependent on CDX2 expression. Western blotting and qRT-PCR confirmed that IL33 expression is upregulated in a CDX2 concentration-dependent manner, thereby providing the first evidence that CDX2 regulates the expression of IL33.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Sylvester","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Davidsen, Johanne","Dahlgaard, Katja","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Bennett, Eric P","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Coskun, Mehmet","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045994"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Gene regulation","Inflammatory bowel disease","Interleukin 33","transcriptional control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cdx000000000002 regulates interleukin 000000000033 gene expression in intestinal epithelial cells ls000000000174t","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2211-5463.13161","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045994","identifier":[{"id":"85104865410","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8167865","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33838073","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c3ab6e3a-c765-4d4f-80ca-d1dbe9458023","ruc-ec415210-fc06-4263-8c89-11b765a72d8e"],"keyword":["Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2","gene regulation","inflammatory bowel disease","interleukin-33","intestinal regulation","transcriptional control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E87C42FF75451E4463E2F83B02087DEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273587073/2211_5463.13161.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2211-5463.13161","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/78158996/2211_5463.13161.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved, Slagelse, Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Gastroenterology and Hepatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Sylvester","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ec07d30c-2417-4f63-a00a-af298dda69bd","name":"Larsen, Sylvester","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Johanne","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"5f273e10-a1e5-4ba7-ba9d-7ab1c51636d5","name":"Davidsen, Johanne","orcid":"0000-0003-4655-1513","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Katja","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"bd84257d-f62e-4de3-b1f4-aa6253e79f76","name":"Dahlgaard, Katja","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Claus Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8caf59ab-44ff-4d9a-a722-8dd317bbd8b9","name":"Nielsen, Claus Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7543-9016","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Eric Paul","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","locid":"985ebfda-1253-424b-8e7d-d5918fa165bf","name":"Bennett, Eric P","name_org":"Bennett, Eric Paul","orcid":"0000-0002-4976-0647","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ole Birger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Thorvald","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","name_org":"Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33838073"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/2211-5463.13161","issn":["22115463"],"issue":"6","journal":"FEBS Open Bio","pages":"1638-1644","status":"p","title":"FEBS Open Bio","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104865410"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c3ab6e3a-c765-4d4f-80ca-d1dbe9458023","ruc-ec415210-fc06-4263-8c89-11b765a72d8e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"CDX2 regulates interleukin-33 gene expression in intestinal epithelial cells (LS174T)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045994","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: It is unknown whether screening for atrial fibrillation and subsequent treatment with anticoagulants if atrial fibrillation is detected can prevent stroke. Continuous electrocardiographic monitoring using an implantable loop recorder (ILR) can facilitate detection of asymptomatic atrial fibrillation episodes. We aimed to investigate whether atrial fibrillation screening and use of anticoagulants can prevent stroke in individuals at high risk. Methods: We did a randomised controlled trial in four centres in Denmark. We included individuals without atrial fibrillation, aged 70–90 years, with at least one additional stroke risk factor (ie, hypertension, diabetes, previous stroke, or heart failure). Participants were randomly assigned in a 1:3 ratio to ILR monitoring or usual care (control) via an online system in permuted blocks with block sizes of four or eight participants stratified according to centre. In the ILR group, anticoagulation was recommended if atrial fibrillation episodes lasted 6 min or longer. The primary outcome was time to first stroke or systemic arterial embolism. This study is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT02036450. Findings: From Jan 31, 2014, to May 17, 2016, 6205 individuals were screened for inclusion, of whom 6004 were included and randomly assigned: 1501 (25·0%) to ILR monitoring and 4503 (75·0%) to usual care. Mean age was 74·7 years (SD 4·1), 2837 (47·3%) were women, and 5444 (90·7%) had hypertension. No participants were lost to follow-up. During a median follow-up of 64·5 months (IQR 59·3–69·8), atrial fibrillation was diagnosed in 1027 participants: 477 (31·8%) of 1501 in the ILR group versus 550 (12·2%) of 4503 in the control group (hazard ratio [HR] 3·17 [95% CI 2·81–3·59]; p<0·0001). Oral anticoagulation was initiated in 1036 participants: 445 (29·7%) in the ILR group versus 591 (13·1%) in the control group (HR 2·72 [95% CI 2·41–3·08]; p<0·0001), and the primary outcome occurred in 318 participants (315 stroke, three systemic arterial embolism): 67 (4·5%) in the ILR group versus 251 (5·6%) in the control group (HR 0·80 [95% CI 0·61–1·05]; p=0·11). Major bleeding occurred in 221 participants: 65 (4·3%) in the ILR group versus 156 (3·5%) in the control group (HR 1·26 [95% CI 0·95–1·69]; p=0·11). Interpretation: In individuals with stroke risk factors, ILR screening resulted in a three-times increase in atrial fibrillation detection and anticoagulation initiation but no significant reduction in the risk of stroke or systemic arterial embolism. These findings might imply that not all atrial fibrillation is worth screening for, and not all screen-detected atrial fibrillation merits anticoagulation. Funding: Innovation Fund Denmark, The Research Foundation for the Capital Region of Denmark, The Danish Heart Foundation, Aalborg University Talent Management Program, Arvid Nilssons Fond, Skibsreder Per Henriksen, R og Hustrus Fond, The AFFECT-EU Consortium (EU Horizon 2020), Læge Sophus Carl Emil Friis og hustru Olga Doris Friis' Legat, and Medtronic.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Svendsen, Jesper H","Diederichsen, Søren Z","Højberg, Søren","Krieger, Derk W","Graff, Claus","Kronborg, Christian","Olesen, Morten S","Nielsen, Jonas B","Holst, Anders G","Brandes, Axel","Haugan, Ketil J","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-002756"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Svendsen, Jesper H"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mediclinic City Hospital","Mohammed Bin Rashid University of Medicine and Health Sciences"],"keyword":["Aged","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation diagnosis","Brain Ischemia prevention control","Denmark","Female","Humans","Male","Risk Factors","Stroke prevention control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implantable loop recorder detection of atrial fibrillation to prevent stroke the loop study a randomised controlled trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85115135080&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-002756","identifier":[{"id":"85115135080","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34469766","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-378c6c30-3f9a-45c1-9d04-2961866e5941","ku-6a77ca56-e985-4f69-930b-5aae6c399f8e","sdu-c51238be-654a-48ff-9a4e-6478543a3161"],"keyword":["Aged","Anticoagulants/therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation/diagnosis","Brain Ischemia/prevention & control","Denmark","Electrocardiography, Ambulatory/instrumentation","Female","Humans","Male","Risk Factors","Stroke/prevention & control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3875085164836CCC789AB5BABB128B0A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-C