{"abstract":"Point-source pollutions in Denmark are typically investigated solely by drilling a number of boreholes in close vicinity or at the landfill. In the presented study a novel towed transient electromagnetic system was used in an early stage of investigation, providing a detailed 3D image of the geological structures to 100 m depth on a scale of several hundreds of hectares downstream the landfill. Furthermore, the geophysics provided insight on possible pollution flow paths along with an accurate image of the plume itself. The water managers responsible for the remediation consequently gained a unique understanding of the task at hand by using the transient electromagnetic system in an early stage of the study. In some locations the pollution plume is located in a depth of 50 meters and the width of the plume is more than 400 meters. Drilling to these depths and getting information on the plume architecture would have been a costly and time-consuming exercise by means of boreholes alone. The geophysics was used to select sites for deep investigation boreholes and chemical water analysis of the pollution plume, saving both time and money, by providing an educated answer to the optimal locations.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jesper Bjergsted","Maurya, Pradip Kumar","Kraghede, R.","Christiansen, Anders Vest","Nielsen, O. F.","Pedersen, J. K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745753"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-02","place":"Bordeaux, Virtual, fr","start":"2021-08-29","title":"1st Conference on Hydrogeophysics: Contribution to Exploration and Management of Groundwater, Land-Use and Natural Hazards under a Changing Climate, Held at Near Surface Geoscience Conference and Exhibition 2021, NSG 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized management of point source polluted sites by using 000000000003d geophysics","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85125186829","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745753","identifier":[{"id":"85125186829","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f935bdf8-75e7-4c4e-b998-ae0002efec33"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-79D7ED6E2583816D888813315BCDC500"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. B.","key":"pedersenjesperbjergstedpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"80edede7-62b3-4e07-be17-1c8a6863677b","name":"Pedersen, Jesper Bjergsted","name_org":"Pedersen, J. B.","orcid":"0000-0003-4094-4017","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P. K.","key":"mauryapradipkumarpau","last":"Maurya","locid":"bea76afd-a8ef-4a35-a472-0f2da3bf4d26","name":"Maurya, Pradip Kumar","name_org":"Maurya, P. K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"kraghederpau","last":"Kraghede","locid":"5d0aab74-8b6f-4443-8361-7f750f34cee4","name":"Kraghede, R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. V.","key":"christiansenandersvestpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"aeed4a08-2ff5-46e8-8270-64980a54d32f","name":"Christiansen, Anders Vest","name_org":"Christiansen, A. V.","orcid":"0000-0001-5829-2913","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"O. F.","key":"nielsenofpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, O. F.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J. K.","key":"pedersenjkpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, J. K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3997/2214-4609.202120174","eisbn":["9789462823877"],"publisher":"EAGE Publishing BV","series":"1st Conference on Hydrogeophysics: Contribution to Exploration and Management of Groundwater, Land-Use and Natural Hazards under a Changing Climate, Held at Near Surface Geoscience Conference and Exhibition 2021, NSG","status":"p","subtitle":"Contribution to Exploration and Management of Groundwater, Land-Use and Natural Hazards under a Changing Climate, Held at Near Surface Geoscience Conference and Exhibition 2021, NSG 2021","title":"1st Conference on Hydrogeophysics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125186829"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f935bdf8-75e7-4c4e-b998-ae0002efec33"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Optimized management of point-source polluted sites by using 3D geophysics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745753","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"EQ-5D is a generic instrument to measure health-related quality of life. In 2009, a new version, EQ-5D-5L, was introduced as an attempt to reduce ceiling effects and improve sensitivity to small changes over time. The objective of this study was to assess the measurement properties of the EQ-5D-5L instrument compared to the EQ-5D-3L instrument in an elderly general population with a moderate to a high degree of comorbidity. A subgroup of participants in a large clinical trial completed the EQ-5D-3L and the EQ-5D-5L questionnaires. Based on the collected data, we tested for feasibility and ceiling and floor effects. Furthermore, we assessed the redistribution properties of the responses and examined the level of inconsistency, informativity, and convergent validity. A total of 1002 persons diagnosed with hypertension, diabetes, heart failure, and/or previous stroke completed both the EQ-5D-3L and the EQ-5D-5L questionnaires. The overall ceiling effect decreased from 46% with the EQ-5D-3L to 30% with the EQ-5D-5L and absolute and relative informativity were higher for EQ-5D-5L, and there was a stronger correlation between EQ-5D-5L and EQ VAS. The EQ-5D-5L seemed to perform better than the EQ-5D-3L in terms of feasibility, ceiling effect, discriminatory power, and convergent validity. The overall ceiling effect was higher than that found in patient samples in previous studies but lower than the one found in population studies.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Christiansen, Anne Simone Juhl","Møller, Marie Louise Sletskov","Kronborg, Christian","Haugan, Ketil Jørgen","Køber, Lars","Højberg, Søren","Brandes, Axel","Graff, Claus","Diederichsen, Søren Zöga","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Krieger, Derk","Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S02-086.01-011465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kronborg, Christian"],"country":["Norway","Switzerland","United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mediclinic City Hospital","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","University Hospital Zurich","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["EQ 5D 3L","EQ 5d 5L","Health related quality of life","Measurement properties"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of the three level and the five level versions of the eq 000000000005d","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180400880/Manuskript_Jan2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-086.01-011465","identifier":[{"id":"85102920101","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33733344","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-effdf377-3a4b-463f-a877-fa648be20c12","sdu-f5b66d64-561a-44b0-bedb-343053005243"],"keyword":["EQ-5D-3L","EQ-5D-5L","Health-related quality of life","Measurement properties"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-F975B95EB4FE060699AE666F4FE42674"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180400880/Manuskript_Jan2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517562474/Manuskript_Jan2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U