gometry","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-079427","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this chapter we focus on the challenges faced by labour market policy from technological change, including the demands made on the skills of the labour force, in relation to automation in the fourth industrial revolution. We document recent changes in the Danish labour market, and we argue that labour market policy needs to be for the employed as well as the unemployed, the latter are the traditional target of labour market policy. We highlight this policy need by referring instead to ‘work policy’, and we focus on how such policy can future-proof the competence development of the workforce.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Peter","Holm, Jacob Rubæk","Lorenz, Edward"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088961"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","South Africa"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Johannesburg","Université Côte d'Azur"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"work policy and automation in the fourth industrial revolution","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-088961","identifier":[{"id":"85104749455","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8598a6d7-39dc-47e9-980e-9f84c97847f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2D5AEFD63F9769283DD6A543844E1E77"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, CARMA - Centre for Labour Market Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"za","key":"university of johannesburg","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of Johannesburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"université côte d azur","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Côte d'Azur","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1fc84531-8fbf-476e-8b6b-d61e53b810fe","name":"Nielsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7752-9514","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Rubæk","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"c8a8c5ad-0329-49b6-9858-9e9170b68d3b","name":"Holm, Jacob Rubæk","orcid":"0000-0003-1110-1918","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Edward","key":"lorenzpau","last":"Lorenz","name":"Lorenz, Edward","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper L.","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jesper L.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"gregersenpedh","last":"Gregersen","name":"Gregersen, Birgitte","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob R.","key":"holmpedh","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jacob R.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Edward","key":"lorenzpedh","last":"Lorenz","name":"Lorenz, Edward","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9781003037750-14","eisbn":["9781000368727"],"isbn":["9780367480479"],"pages":"189-207","publisher":"Routledge","series":"Routledge Studies in Innovation, Organizations and Technology","status":"p","subtitle":"The Danish Innovation System in Transition","title":"Globalisation, New and Emerging Technologies, and Sustainable Development"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104749455"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8598a6d7-39dc-47e9-980e-9f84c97847f0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Work policy and automation in the fourth industrial revolution","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088961","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"As Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) have achieved state-of- the-art performance in various scientific fields and applica- tions, the memory and computational complexity of DNNs have increased concurrently. The increased complexity re- quired by DNNs prohibits them from running on platforms with limited computational resources. This has sparked a re- newed interest in parameter pruning. We propose to replace the standard cross-entropy objective – typically used in clas- sification problems – with the Nonlinear Information Bottle- neck (NIB) objective to improve the accuracy of a pruned net- work. We demonstrate, that our proposal outperforms cross- entropy combined with global magnitude pruning for high compression rates on VGG-nets trained on CIFAR10. With approximately 97% of the parameters pruned, we obtain an accuracy of 87.63% and 88.22% for VGG-16 and VGG-19, respectively, where the baseline accuracy is 91.5% for the un- pruned networks. We observe that the majority of biases are pruned completely, and pruning parameters globally outper- forms layer-wise pruning.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Morten Østergaard","Østergaard, Jan","Jensen, Jesper","Tan, Zheng-Hua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101795"],"event":{"acronym":"MLSP","end":"2021-10-28","place":"Gold Coast, au","start":"2021-10-25","title":"2021 IEEE 31st International Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing (MLSP)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Mutual information"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTI","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"compression of dnns using magnitude pruning and nonlinear information bottleneck training","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85122838283&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-101795","identifier":[{"id":"85122838283","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b238dbf2-8328-4574-a61c-26dab69d86ac"],"keyword":["deep learning","mutual information","parameter pruning","variational bottleneck"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F94C601AF872C7E03A08F596E7991A1D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Artificial Intelligence and Sound","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"oticon","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTI","l3nl":"Oticon A/S","l3nn":"Oticon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oticon","namevar":["Oticon Danmark AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Østergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc3a0656-8a5d-479d-b8f5-4d77ce5807b1","name":"Nielsen, Morten Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3233-207X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"c8522a16-6640-4463-8bc4-016e43e2b342","name":"Østergaard, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-3724-6114","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"215c2d1c-5a1a-4d5e-a638-75e8ee0eec13","name":"Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-1478-622X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheng-Hua","key":"tanpau","last":"Tan","locid":"a1a8624f-e408-42a6-b2dc-f4f1a46476ed","name":"Tan, Zheng-Hua","orcid":"0000-0001-6856-8928","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mlsp52302.2021.9596128","eisbn":["9781728163383"],"isbn":["9781665411844"],"issn":["15512541"],"pages":"1-6","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing","status":"p","title":"2021 IEEE 31st International Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing (MLSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122838283"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Oticon A/S","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b238dbf2-8328-4574-a61c-26dab69d86ac"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Compression of dnns using magnitude pruning and nonlinear information bottleneck training","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101795","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To externally validate recent prognostic models that predict independent gait following stroke. Study Design and Setting: A systematic search identified recent models (<10 years) that predicted independent gait in adult stroke patients, using easily obtainable predictors. Predictors from the original models were assigned proxies when required, and model performance was evaluated in the validation cohort (n = 957). Models were updated to determine if performance could be improved. Results: Three prognostic models met our criteria, all with high Risk of Bias. Validation data was only available for the Australian model. This model used National Institute of Health Stroke Scale (NIHSS) and age to predict independent gait, using Motor Assessment Scale (MAS) walking item. For validation, Scandinavian Stroke Scale (SSS) was a proxy for NIHSS, and Functional Independence Measure (FIM) locomotion item was a proxy for MAS. The Area Under the Curve was 0.77 (0.74–0.80) and had good calibration in the validation dataset. Adjustment of the intercept and regression coefficients slightly improved discrimination. By adding paretic leg strength, the model further improved (AUC 0.82). Conclusion: External validation of the Australian model with proxies showed fair discrimination and good calibration. Updating the model by adding paretic leg strength further improved model performance.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Langerak, Anthonia J.","McCambridge, Alana B.","Stubbs, Peter W.","Mortensen, Jesper","Rogers, Kris","Quel de Oliveira, Camila","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Verhagen, Arianne P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-160439"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Verhagen, Arianne P."],"country":["Australia","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Technology Sydney","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["External validation","Gait","Model performance","Prediction","Prognostic model","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"externally validated model predicting gait independence after stroke showed fair performance and improved after updating","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclinepi.2021.03.022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-160439","identifier":[{"id":"85105833780","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33812010","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-36696e05-9f2a-485a-8a4b-5f7897210ebd"],"keyword":["External validation","Gait","Model performance","Prediction","Prognostic model","Stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-21B4D65684CD3CBA7098FC6BE9E9522B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/277442900/1_s2.0_S0895435621001049_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclinepi.2021.03.022","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of technology sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Technology Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hammel Neurocenter, Universitetsklinik for Neurorehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anthonia J.","key":"langerakpau","last":"Langerak","name":"Langerak, Anthonia J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alana B.","key":"mccambridgepau","last":"McCambridge","name":"McCambridge, Alana B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter W.","key":"stubbspau","last":"Stubbs","name":"Stubbs, Peter W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"fabriciuspau","last":"Fabricius","locid":"2b929317-14ec-499f-b8bd-f392162e2e65","name":"Mortensen, Jesper","name_org":"Fabricius, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7285-3422","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kris","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","name":"Rogers, Kris","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camila","key":"queldeoliveirapau","last":"Quel de Oliveira","name":"Quel de Oliveira, Camila","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen F.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Jørgen F.","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arianne P.","key":"verhagenpau","last":"Verhagen","name":"Verhagen, Arianne P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33812010"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jclinepi.2021.03.022","issn":["08954356","18785921"],"issn_org":["08954356"],"journal":"Journal of Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"73-82","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Epidemiology","volume":"137"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105833780"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-36696e05-9f2a-485a-8a4b-5f7897210ebd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Externally validated model predicting gait independence after stroke showed fair performance and improved after updating","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-160439","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We propose a framework for building Nakamoto-style proof-of-work blockchains where blocks are treated differently in the ``longest chain rule''. The crucial parameter is a weight function assigning different weights to blocks according to their hash value. Our framework enables the analysis of different weight functions while proving all statements at the appropriate level of abstraction. This allows us to quickly derive protocol guarantees for different weight functions. We exemplify the usefulness of our framework by capturing the classical Bitcoin protocol as well as exponentially growing functions as special cases. We show the typical properties---chain growth, chain quality and common prefix---for both, and further show that the latter provide an additional guarantee, namely a weak form of optimistic responsiveness. More precisely, we prove for a certain class of exponentially growing weight functions that in periods without corruption, the confirmation time only depends on the unknown actual network delay instead of the known upper bound.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kamp, Simon Holmgaard","Magri, Bernardo","Matt, Christian","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Thomsen, Søren Eller","Tschudi, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161054"],"event":{"acronym":"LATINCRYPT","end":"2021-10-08","place":"Bogotá, co","start":"2021-10-06","title":"7th International Conference on Cryptology and Information Security in Latin America<br/>","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Proof of work"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weight based nakamoto style blockchains","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85116943119","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161054","identifier":[{"id":"85116943119","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-378b38f7-ef4f-469b-a03b-4dd02f6140e9"],"keyword":["Block weight","Blockchain","Chain-selection rule","Optimistic responsiveness","Proof of work"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5824784F701F870460D898D21971409E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Holmgaard","key":"kamppau","last":"Kamp","locid":"605890de-dee5-4779-bc6c-6b76966639ba","name":"Kamp, Simon Holmgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3356-1827","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo","key":"magripau","last":"Magri","locid":"2e4b2471-3423-4eac-a276-f6670afa1f76","name":"Magri, Bernardo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"mattpau","last":"Matt","name":"Matt, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Eller","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"703f2983-8d52-4409-a4d5-18f0b7acdd42","name":"Thomsen, Søren Eller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"tschudipau","last":"Tschudi","locid":"0ee91524-821e-4add-bb6d-ca09a03888d5","name":"Tschudi, Daniel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patrick","key":"longapedh","last":"Longa","name":"Longa, Patrick","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carla","key":"ràfolspedh","last":"Ràfols","name":"Ràfols, Carla","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-88238-9_15","isbn":["9783030882389"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"299-319","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer International Publishing","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"7th International Conference on Cryptology and Information Security in Latin America Bogotá, Colombia, October 6–8, 2021, Proceedings","title":"Progress in Cryptology – LATINCRYPT 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116943119"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-378b38f7-ef4f-469b-a03b-4dd02f6140e9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Weight-Based Nakamoto-Style Blockchains","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-161054","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: This study aimed to investigate cardiac computed tomography (CT) and transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) peridevice leak (PDL) assessments, and the clinical relevance of PDL. BACKGROUND: PDL assessment is integral during follow-up after left atrial appendage (LAA) occlusion. Comparative studies of TEE and cardiac CT are sparse, and the clinical relevance of PDL is uncertain. METHODS: This was a single-center observational study of consecutive patients undergoing LAA occlusion with Amplatzer devices (Amplatzer Cardiac Plug/Amulet) between 2010 and 2018 (N = 415). Patients with both 8-week CT and TEE were included for analysis (n = 346). Images were analyzed by blinded investigators (K.K. and A.S.). PDL on cardiac CT was classified from grade 1 to 3, based on PDL at the device disc, device lobe, and LAA contrast patency. Primary clinical outcome was a composite of ischemic stroke, transient ischemic attack, systemic embolism, or all-cause death. RESULTS: PDL was present in 110 patients (32%) by TEE, with 29 (8%) >3 mm. By cardiac CT, 210 patients (61%) had PDL at the disc, with contrast patency in 204 patients (59%). A grade 3 PDL (gap at disc, lobe, and LAA contrast patency) was present in 63 patients (18%). Bland-Altman analysis showed poor agreement between CT and TEE for leak sizing. CT and TEE detected PDL was not significantly associated with worse outcome, hazard ratio: 1.82 (95 % confidence interval: 0.95 to 3.50); p = 0.07 and hazard ratio: 1.43 (95% confidence interval: 0.74 to 2.76); p = 0.28, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: PDL occurrence is substantially higher with CT compared with TEE, with a large discrepancy between modalities in leak quantification. A novel CT-based classification is proposed, yet PDL was not associated with worse clinical outcome.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Korsholm, Kasper","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Samaras, Athanasios","Saw, Jacqueline","Berti, Sergio","Tzikas, Apostolos","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-166336"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Korsholm, Kasper"],"country":["Canada","Greece"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aristotle University of Thessaloniki","Vancouver General Hospital"],"keyword":["Amplatzer","Left atrial appendage","Left atrial appendage occlusion","peridevice leak"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"peridevice leak following amplatzer left atrial appendage occlusion cardiac computed tomography classification and clinical outcomes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85098049459","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-166336","identifier":[{"id":"85098049459","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33413869","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-40ffe47f-96c3-40d1-80fb-0a0587c9b446"],"keyword":["Amplatzer","left atrial appendage","left atrial appendage occlusion","peridevice leak"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FAD16E7DAC2A9E1F4E05FEADE415A75F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Cardiac research clinic, West","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"vancouver general hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Vancouver General Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gr","key":"aristotle university of thessaloniki","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aristotle University of Thessaloniki","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Athanasios","key":"samaraspau","last":"Samaras","locid":"6a4a79d3-94eb-48b5-9e1f-87718ebe5376","name":"Samaras, Athanasios","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacqueline","key":"sawpau","last":"Saw","name":"Saw, Jacqueline","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergio","key":"bertipau","last":"Berti","name":"Berti, Sergio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Apostolos","key":"tzikaspau","last":"Tzikas","name":"Tzikas, Apostolos","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33413869"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcin.2020.10.034","issn":["18767605","19368798"],"issn_org":["19368798"],"issue":"1","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","pages":"83-93","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","title_org":"JACC. Cardiovascular interventions","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098049459"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-40ffe47f-96c3-40d1-80fb-0a0587c9b446"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Peridevice Leak Following Amplatzer Left Atrial Appendage Occlusion : Cardiac Computed Tomography Classification and Clinical Outcomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-166336","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Long-distance extracellular electron transfer has been observed in Gram-negative bacteria and plays roles in both natural and engineering processes. The electron transfer can be mediated by conductive protein appendages (in short unicellular bacteria such as Geobacter species) or by conductive cell envelopes (in filamentous multicellular cable bacteria). Here we show that Lysinibacillus varians GY32, a filamentous unicellular Gram-positive bacterium, is capable of bidirectional extracellular electron transfer. In microbial fuel cells, L. varians can form centimetre-range conductive cellular networks and, when grown on graphite electrodes, the cells can reach a remarkable length of 1.08 mm. Atomic force microscopy and microelectrode analyses suggest that the conductivity is linked to pili-like protein appendages. Our results show that long-distance electron transfer is not limited to Gram-negative bacteria.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Yang, Yonggang","Wang, Zegao","Gan, Cuifen","Klausen, Lasse Hyldgaard","Bonné, Robin","Kong, Guannan","Luo, Dizhou","Meert, Mathijs","Zhu, Chunjie","Sun, Guoping","Guo, Jun","Ma, Yuxin","Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","Manca, Jean","Xu, Meiying","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Dong, Mingdong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240885"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dong, Mingdong","Xu, Meiying"],"country":["Belgium","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangdong Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Guangdong Academy of Sciences","Hasselt University","Sichuan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long distance electron transfer in a filamentous gram positive bacterium","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-21709-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240885","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7969598","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33731718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85102678311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c37e164d-7c57-4986-8551-0b11db9f7dd7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FBE2C8BAC707CE1D8922AA71DA0F17A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-21709-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"guangdong academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"guangdong academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt U