{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Screening programs for colorectal cancer (CRC) exist in many countries, and with varying participation rates. The present study aimed at identifying socio-demographic factors for accepting a cost-free screening offer for CRC in Denmark, and to study if more people would accept the screening offer if the present fecal test was replaced by a blood test. METHODS: We used a cross-sectional survey design based on a representative group of 6807 Danish citizens aged 50-80 years returning a fully answered web-based questionnaire with socio-demographic data added from national registries. Data were analyzed in STATA and based on bivariate analyses followed by regression models. RESULTS: Danes in general have a high level of lifetime participation (+ 80%) in the national CRC screening program. The results of the stepwise logistic regression model to predict CRC screening participation demonstrated that female gender, higher age, higher income, and moderate alcohol intake were positively associated with screening participation, whereas a negative association was observed for higher educational attainment, obesity, being a smoker, and higher willingness to take health risks. Of the 1026 respondents not accepting the screening offer, 61% were willing to reconsider their initial negative response if the fecal sampling procedure were replaced by blood sampling. CONCLUSION: The CRC screening program intends to include the entire population within a certain at-risk age group. However, individual factors (e.g. sex, age obesity, smoking, risk aversity) appear to significantly affect willingness to participate in the screening program. From a preventive perspective, our findings indicate the need for a more targeted approach trying to reach these groups.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","Leppin, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-575577"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"to do or not to do a survey study on factors associated with participating in the danish screening program for colorectal cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-020-06023-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-575577","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7792101","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85098891743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33413310","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-085ad384-572f-4641-ac4a-cefd4fd4075d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6C9DB8EA2C8C16B24F4E08E36E2A8EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178643035/s12913_020_06023_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12913-020-06023-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriele","key":"bergbeckhoffpau","last":"Berg-Beckhoff","locid":"df22cacd-c8b4-440c-8c16-aecbc139d9b6","name":"Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","orcid":"0000-0003-1614-938X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"leppinpau","last":"Leppin","locid":"6bef1637-e9f4-44e0-902e-6c92974c8711","name":"Leppin, Anja","orcid":"0000-0001-6203-6162","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33413310"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12913-020-06023-6","issn":["14726963"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Health Services Research","paperid":"43","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Health Services Research","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098891743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-085ad384-572f-4641-ac4a-cefd4fd4075d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"To do or not to do - a survey study on factors associated with participating in the Danish screening program for colorectal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-575577","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Kluge, Sofie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-582713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fortællingens mysterium bogstavelighed og allegori i jorge luis borges el evangelio según marcos","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.eksistensen.dk/boger/teologi/bibelske-konfigurationer-i-kunst-og-kultur.html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-582713","ids":["sdu-214d7e05-5940-4172-a0e2-9aaf5604f03d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EE64E83A971302B8237D9BCA3A725883"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Literature"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"klugepau","last":"Kluge","locid":"35f66034-0c80-4312-ad37-6e85abc812cd","name":"Kluge, Sofie","orcid":"0000-0003-4701-5448","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gitte","key":"buchhansenpedh","last":"Buch-Hansen","name":"Buch-Hansen, Gitte","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"tangnielsenpedh","last":"Tang Nielsen","name":"Tang Nielsen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","isbn":["9788741000251"],"pages":"201-220","place":"København","publisher":"Eksistensen Akademisk","status":"p","title":"Bibelske konfigurationer i kunst og litteratur"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-214d7e05-5940-4172-a0e2-9aaf5604f03d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Fortællingens mysterium. Bogstavelighed og allegori i Jorge Luis Borges' El evangelio según Marcos","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-582713","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The adoption rate of digital health in the health care sector is low in many countries. A facilitating factor for successful implementation and adoption of digital health is acceptance by current and future health care professionals. OBJECTIVE: This study was conducted to identify factors associated with willingness to use digital health tools in patient care among health care professionals and students. METHODS: This was a quantitative cross-sectional survey study conducted among health care professionals and students at a university hospital in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia. A nonprobability convenience sampling procedure was used to recruit participants. Data were collected using a self-completed e-questionnaire that was distributed by email. Chi-square tests, t tests, and logistic regression were used to analyze the data. RESULTS: We found that 181 out of 218 health care professionals (83.0%; 75.6% [59/78] physicians; 87.1% [122/140] nurses) and 115 out of 154 students (74.7%; 80.0% [76/95] medical students and 66.1% [39/59] nursing students) were willing to use digital tools in patient care. Willingness to use digital tools was significantly associated with attitude (Adjusted Odds Ratios [AOR] 1.96; 95% CI 1.14-3.36) and self-efficacy (AOR 1.64; 95% CI 1.17-2.30) among health care professionals, and with current year of study (AOR 2.08; 95% CI 1.18-3.68) and self-efficacy (AOR 1.77; 95% CI 1.17-2.69) among students. No significant difference in willingness to use digital tools was found between physicians and nurses (P=.113), and between medical and nursing students (P=.079). CONCLUSIONS: The findings of this study should encourage policy makers and hospital managers to implement relevant eHealth interventions within routine health care systems in Saudi Arabia. For successful implementation, digital health education programs should be implemented simultaneously, so that current and future health care professionals are able to develop required positive attitudes as well as practical skills and competencies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thapa, Subash","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Aldahmash, Abdullah M","Qadri, Fatima R","Leppin, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586016"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Thapa, Subash"],"country":["Saudi Arabia"],"glorg":["Alfarabi Colleges","All Global Affiliations","King Saud University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"willingness to use digital health tools in patient care among health care professionals and students at a university hospital in saudi arabia quantitative cross sectional survey","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/18590","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586016","identifier":[{"id":"85101235018","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33605896","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8081256","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-2cbeeb38-97c5-45d3-aa62-aedf7cb14f72"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-309DD8BFA236A35D897BFDB293B19839"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/179652391/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/18590","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denma