 Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Peter","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b1e70d8a-0883-480d-8c07-5a7775417377","name":"Andersen, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2444-6210","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mathias W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d5b2521-2997-4092-9bb9-f5cb8abb4bc8","name":"Nielsen, Mathias Wullum","name_org":"Nielsen, Mathias W.","orcid":"0000-0001-8759-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Wiborg","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"8fcbf953-b83f-4fe7-b698-d4aec218e1f5","name":"Schneider, Jesper Wiborg","orcid":"0000-0001-5556-0919","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/qss_a_00119","issn":["26413337"],"issue":"1","journal":"Quantitative Science Studies","pages":"254-262","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Quantitative Science Studies","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117751943"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b427864-61ba-4621-8a4d-35db70204743","ku-a50e2471-e442-430d-a474-46865688d6e0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selective referencing and questionable evidence in Strumia’s paper on “Gender issues in fundamental physics”","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-022817","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The facultative bacterium Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans (Aa) is strongly associated with periodontitis and is occasionally found in periodontally healthy subjects. We aimed to determine the prevalence of salivary Aa among patients with either periodontitis Grade B (periodontitis-B) or Grade C (periodontitis-C), periodontally healthy controls (HCs), and to determine if systemic antibodies against Aa or its virulence factor leukotoxin A (LtxA) may serve as biomarkers that reveal the oral presence of the bacterium and discriminate subjects with periodontitis-C, periodontitis-B, or no periodontitis from each other. Methods: Serum and unstimulated saliva samples were collected from patients with periodontitis-C (n = 27), patients with periodontitis-B (n = 34), and HCs (n = 28). Serum level of immunoglobulin G antibodies to fragmented whole Aa and to LtxA were quantified using a bead-based assay. Aa was identified in saliva using quantitative polymerase chain reaction (qPCR). All analyses were adjusted for age, sex, and current smoking status. Results: Aa was present in saliva from 11% of HCs, in 32% of patients with periodontitis-B (P = 0.04 versus HCs), and in 37% of patients with periodontitis-C (P = 0.02 versus HCs). Serum antibodies to fragments of Aa associated significantly with periodontitis-C (P = 0.03), while serum anti-LtxA antibodies associated with both periodontitis-B and periodontitis-C (P = 0.002 and P = 9×10−4, respectively). Moreover, a significant association between serum anti-LtxA antibodies and Aa count in saliva was observed (P = 0.001). On the basis of serum anti-LtxA antibody levels, patients with periodontitis could be discriminated from HCs (AUC = 0.74 in ROC curve-analysis, P = 0.0003), and carriers of Aa could be discriminated from non-carriers (AUC = 0.78, P <0.0001). Conclusions: Aa is highly prevalent in saliva of patients with periodontitis-B or periodontitis-C. Systemic immunoglobulin G antibodies against LtxA distinguish patients with periodontitis, regardless of grade, from HCs, while their quantity reflects the concurrent bacterial burden in the oral cavity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Damgaard, Christian","Danielsen, Anne Katrine","Enevold, Christian","Reinholdt, Jesper","Holmstrup, Palle","Nielsen, Claus H.","Massarenti, Laura"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024230"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Damgaard, Christian"],"keyword":["Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans","Antibodies","Periodontitis","Saliva","Serum"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating antibodies against leukotoxin a as marker of periodontitis grades b and c and oral infection with i aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85104391362","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024230","identifier":[{"id":"85104391362","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33749825","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9e374d3d-a5bd-4232-9fde-1e342f327474","ku-0c71fa95-06e8-4616-ba86-5c4681c70cfa"],"keyword":["Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans","antibodies","periodontitis","saliva","serum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8342932519CC52356677D6E45C7DA75C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 03 - Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"166c1339-46eb-42f4-ab74-f84615ac1706","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2394-746X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Katrine","key":"danielsenpau","last":"Danielsen","locid":"1a5843c8-ad77-42d1-987e-a55881e54dde","name":"Danielsen, Anne Katrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"enevoldpau","last":"Enevold","name":"Enevold, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"reinholdtpau","last":"Reinholdt","locid":"03ef8acb-f581-45e7-9dd2-3cb6bb520c9a","name":"Reinholdt, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Palle","key":"holmstruppau","last":"Holmstrup","locid":"70e9b4ab-ebee-4ee2-9356-87e935612e99","name":"Holmstrup, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-1563-1089","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8caf59ab-44ff-4d9a-a722-8dd317bbd8b9","name":"Nielsen, Claus Henrik","name_org":"Nielsen, Claus H.","orcid":"0000-0001-7543-9016","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laura","key":"massarentipau","last":"Massarenti","name":"Massarenti, Laura","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33749825"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jper.20-0895","issn":["00223492","19433670"],"issn_org":["00223492"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Periodontology","pages":"1795-1804","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Periodontology","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104391362"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9e374d3d-a5bd-4232-9fde-1e342f327474","ku-0c71fa95-06e8-4616-ba86-5c4681c70cfa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Circulating antibodies against leukotoxin A as marker of periodontitis Grades B and C and oral infection with Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024230","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A crucial process in the production of industrial enzymes is recombinant gene expression, which aims to induce enzyme overexpression of the genes in a host microbe. Current approaches for securing overexpression rely on molecular tools such as adjusting the recombinant expression vector, adjusting cultivation conditions, or performing codon optimizations. However, such strategies are time-consuming, and an alternative strategy would be to select genes for better compatibility with the recombinant host. Several methods for predicting soluble expression are available; however, they are all optimized for the expression host Escherichia coli and do not consider the possibility of an expressed protein not being soluble. We show that these tools are not suited for predicting expression potential in the industrially important host Bacillus subtilis. Instead, we build a B. subtilis-specific machine learning model for expressibility prediction. Given millions of unlabelled proteins and a small labeled dataset, we can successfully train such a predictive model. The unlabeled proteins provide a performance boost relative to using amino acid frequencies of the labeled proteins as input. On average, we obtain a modest performance of 0.64 area-under-the-curve (AUC) and 0.2 Matthews correlation coefficient (MCC). However, we find that this is sufficient for the prioritization of expression candidates for high-throughput studies. Moreover, the predicted class probabilities are correlated with expression levels. A number of features related to protein expression, including base frequencies and solubility, are captured by the model.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Martiny, Hannah-Marie","Armenteros, Jose Juan Almagro","Johansen, Alexander Rosenberg","Salomon, Jesper","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-034183"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Martiny, Hannah-Marie"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep protein representations enable recombinant protein expression prediction","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compbiolchem.2021.107596","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-034183","identifier":[{"id":"85118856902","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34775287","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-469595cd-9340-4a5d-be9e-77552007c948","ku-7750ba0c-20c6-4b2d-af80-a0495ecf4e75"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C2206A12C45EC312EA631C367EB57248"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/263983078/1_s2.0_S1476927121001663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/285449464/1_s2.0_S1476927121001663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compbiolchem.2021.107596","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Genomic Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Brunak Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hannah-Marie","key":"martinypau","last":"Martiny","locid":"b24c2fb0-4ad8-4d0a-ae44-354d812e060f","name":"Martiny, Hannah-Marie","orcid":"0000-0001-6733-7888","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jose Juan Almagro","key":"armenterospau","last":"Armenteros","locid":"2ef303c4-c8c5-4339-8254-9ea0f5545752","name":"Armenteros, Jose Juan Almagro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Rosenberg","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Alexander Rosenberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"salomonpau","last":"Salomon","name":"Salomon, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fc3a367c-2f88-43ad-a5a9-24919f4470ec","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9412-9643","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34775287"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.compbiolchem.2021.107596","issn":["14769271","1476928X"],"issn_org":["14769271"],"journal":"Computational Biology and Chemistry","paperid":"107596","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Computational Biology and Chemistry","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118856902"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-469595cd-9340-4a5d-be9e-77552007c948","ku-7750ba0c-20c6-4b2d-af80-a0495ecf4e75"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep protein representations enable recombinant protein expression prediction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-034183","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Work in greenhouses entails exposure to airborne fungi and bacteria. The aims of this study are to obtain knowledge about whether exposure to fungal and bacterial genera and species during work in a cucumber greenhouse is affected by work tasks, and whether a cohort of greenhouse workers' serum levels of serum amyloid A (SAA) and C-reactive protein (CRP), biomarkers of systemic inflammation, are associated with this. Data on personal exposure to airborne fungal and bacterial species measured over four years as well as serum levels of SAA and CRP sampled over two years were analyzed. For data analysis, the main work tasks were grouped into three different groups, called 'grouped work task'. Microorganisms were identified using matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization time-of-flight (MALDI-TOF MS) and next-generation sequencing (NGS). The 'daily exposure' of greenhouse workers' were as follows: 4.8 × 104 CFU bacteria/m3, 1.4 × 106 CFU fungi/m3, and 392 EU/m3 of endotoxin. Workers were exposed to many different microbial species including several species within the genera Acinetobacter, Bacillus, Microbacterium, Pseudomonas, Staphylococcus, and Streptomyces. The genera Ralstonia and Cladosporium were found in most samples. The exposure levels as well as the microbial composition were associated significantly with grouped work task and season with high exposures during tasks in close contact with mature and old plants and in the autumn. CRP and SAA levels were also associated with exposure level and grouped work tasks. The Shannon-Wiener indices were not different in the 3 'grouped work tasks'. Several specific species including e.g. Halomonas elongata, Stenotrophomonas maltophilia, Podosphaera fusca, and Wallemia spp. were found frequently or in high concentrations in the exposures associated with the highest levels of CRP and SAA. The microorganisms S. maltophilia, P. fusca, and Wallemia spp. were also found on the cucumber plant leaves. In conclusion, both exposure level and the species composition seem to have an effect on the serum levels of CRP and SAA of exposed workers. The greenhouse workers were exposed to only a few species characterized as human pathogens.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Madsen, Anne Mette","White, John Kerr","Markouch, Amal","Kadhim, Sarah","de Jonge, Nadieh","Thilsing, Trine","Hansen, Vinni M","Bælum, Jesper","Nielsen, Jeppe Lund","Vogel, Ulla","Tendal, Kira"],"cuid":["S03-097.06-767080"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Anne Mette"],"keyword":["Acute phase response","Biodiversity","Fungal exposure","Mikrobiologi","Occupational Exposure","Serum amyloid A","Toksikologi"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a cohort study of cucumber greenhouse workers exposure to microorganisms as measured using ngs and maldi tof ms and biomarkers of systemic inflammation","src":["aau","nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envres.2020.110325","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-097.06-767080","identifier":[{"id":"33068575","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85093652669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dee0164d-9d7b-4cb1-98b3-f193d767a91f","nfa-1a58aeb0-9440-4e3c-8dc0-91f431548e51","sdu-73c0c8bb-441c-40bf-9143-a7c9b9300513"],"keyword":["Acute-phase response","Biodiversity","Drivhuse","Fungal exposure","Mikrobiologi","Occupational exposure","Serum amyloid A","Toksikologi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4130BC3CB4297776A231FF99832E2380"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/174648680/1_s2.0_S0013935120312226_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envres.2020.110325","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/459359104/1_s2.0_S0013935120312226_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Center for Microbial Communities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Mette","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"8b9c4389-8c90-43c9-9939-2e4bbce318db","name":"Madsen, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-5895-7521","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Kerr","key":"whitepau","last":"White","locid":"cbfb9922-9b01-4a87-b193-f7863d78607e","name":"White, John Kerr","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amal","key":"markouchpau","last":"Markouch","name":"Markouch, Amal","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"kadhimpau","last":"Kadhim","locid":"eebc341e-e81b-409d-988b-91ec38453a1d","name":"Kadhim, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nadieh","key":"dejongepau","last":"de Jonge","locid":"05e48ce2-1165-45bc-b4bf-7248af29ff43","name":"de Jonge, Nadieh","orcid":"0000-0003-0891-0837","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","locid":"6ae25242-1e96-48cf-ab01-cbac26690f6b","name":"Thilsing, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-2041-2219","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vinni M","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"52c67f06-7ebe-44ce-baf9-fa5a0e1f619e","name":"Hansen, Vinni Mona","name_org":"Hansen, Vinni M","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bælumpau","last":"Bælum","locid":"c8e0780b-a76a-4aef-be25-d870d305b527","name":"Bælum, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8221-4664","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Lund","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"452a0716-2a15-4423-9cd3-dcafdbb367b0","name":"Nielsen, Jeppe Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-8747-6938","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"vogelpau","last":"Vogel","locid":"157e7e7e-7506-4f84-8087-ccc586d5d13c","name":"Vogel, Ulla Birgitte","name_org":"Vogel, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-1524","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kira","key":"tendalpau","last":"Tendal","name":"Tendal, Kira","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33068575"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2020.110325","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"journal":"Environmental Research","pages":"110325","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"192"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85093652669"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dee0164d-9d7b-4cb1-98b3-f193d767a91f","nfa-1a58aeb0-9440-4e3c-8dc0-91f431548e51","sdu-73c0c8bb-441c-40bf-9143-a7c9b9300513"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A cohort study of cucumber greenhouse workers' exposure to microorganisms as measured using NGS and MALDI-TOF MS and biomarkers of systemic inflammation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.06-767080","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with colorectal cancer were examined to determine (1) whether elevated carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) levels, either before treatment or after surgery, was associated with an increased risk of overall or colorectal cancer-specific mortality or recurrence, and (2) whether high intensity follow-up would benefit those patients. Materials and methods: Post-hoc analysis based on 2509 patients that underwent surgery for colorectal cancer, stage II or III, in the COLOFOL randomized trial with 5-year follow-up. Serum CEA levels were ascertained before treatment and one month after surgery. Follow-up examinations included computed tomography of the thorax and abdomen and serum CEA sampling. Patients were randomized to examinations at either 6, 12, 18, 24, and 36 months (high-intensity group) or at 12 and 36 months after surgery (low-intensity group). Levels of CEA >5 μg/l were defined as elevated. Results: Elevated CEA levels before treatment were associated with increased risk of recurrence (hazard ratio [HR], 1.49; 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.22–1.83), colorectal cancer-specific mortality (HR, 1.44; 95% CI: 1.08–1.91), and overall mortality (HR, 1.38; 95% CI: 1.07–1.78). Elevated CEA levels after surgery were associated with increased colorectal cancer-specific mortality (HR, 1.68; 95% CI: 1.08–2.61) and overall mortality (HR, 1.79; 95% CI: 1.22–2.63). The intensity of the follow-up regimen had no effect on 5-year outcomes in patients with elevated CEA levels. Conclusion: Both pre-treatment and post-surgery elevated serum CEA levels were associated with increased overall and cancer-specific mortality. Intensified follow-up showed no benefit over low-intensity follow-up in this high-risk group of patients with elevated CEA levels.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Egenvall, Monika","Martling, Anna","Veres, Katalin","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Wille-Jørgensen, Peer","Høirup Petersen, Sune","Laurberg, Søren","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Syk, Ingvar","Nielsen, Jesper Dan"],"cuid":["S03-098.53-011297"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["COLOFOL Study Group","The COLOFOL Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Egenvall, Monika"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["Carcinoembryonic antigen","Clinical trial","Colorectal cancer","Follow up","Post hoc analysis","Prognostic value","Recurrence","stage II"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no benefit of more intense follow up after surgery for colorectal cancer in the risk group with elevated cea levels an analysis within the colofol randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejso.2021.03.235","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by unrestricted grants from the Nordic Cancer Union (Finland), A. P. M?ller Foundation (Denmark), Beckett Foundation (Denmark), Grosserer Chr. Andersen and wife bursary (Denmark), Sigvald and Edith Rasmussens Memorial Fund (Denmark), Martha Margrethe and Christian Hermansens Fund (Denmark), Danish Medical Association (Denmark), Danish Cancer Society (Denmark), Danish Council for Independent Research/Medical Sciences (Denmark, all awarded to Dr Wille-J?rgensen), and by an unrestricted grant (CAN 2013/553) from the Swedish Cancer Foundation (Sweden, awarded to Dr P?hlman). This study was funded by unrestricted grants from the Nordic Cancer Union (Finland), A. P. Møller Foundation (Denmark), Beckett Foundation (Denmark), Grosserer Chr. Andersen and wife bursary (Denmark), Sigvald and Edith Rasmussens Memorial Fund (Denmark), Martha Margrethe and Christian Hermansens Fund (Denmark), Danish Medical Association (Denmark) , Danish Cancer Society (Denmark) , Danish Council for Independent Research/Medical Sciences (Denmark, all awarded to Dr Wille-Jørgensen), and by an unrestricted grant ( CAN 2013/553 ) from the Swedish Cancer Foundation (Sweden, awarded to Dr Påhlman)."],"id":"S03-098.53-011297","identifier":[{"id":"000723107300033","type":"wos"},{"id":"33846037","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85103983480","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-eca44f17-7fc7-41fb-ab40-58451024d10a","au-9aec3cc8-59be-439f-84d3-7d7ac4066709","sdu-6913d4b5-b9a8-4f17-a1ff-73ccb3541fb6"],"keyword":["Carcinoembryonic antigen","Clinical trial","Colorectal cancer","Follow-up","PROGNOSTIC VALUE","Post-hoc analysis","RECURRENCE","STAGE-II"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B9C28E88C984B332008B33EF3C2B4C8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184489622/PIIS0748798321003772.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejso.2021.03.235","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517893594/1_s2.0_S0748798321003772_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/274448392/1_s2.0_S0748798321003772_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["