ab40-58451024d10a","au-9aec3cc8-59be-439f-84d3-7d7ac4066709","sdu-6913d4b5-b9a8-4f17-a1ff-73ccb3541fb6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"No benefit of more intense follow-up after surgery for colorectal cancer in the risk group with elevated CEA levels – An analysis within the COLOFOL randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.53-011297","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Alzheimer's Disease (AD) is a complex and multifactorial disease and novel approaches are needed to illuminate the underlying pathology. Metabolites comprise the end-product of genes, transcripts, and protein regulations and might reflect disease pathogenesis. Blood is a common biofluid used in metabolomics; however, since extracellular vesicles (EVs) hold cell-specific biological material and can cross the blood-brain barrier, their utilization as biological material warrants further investigation. We aimed to investigate blood- and EV-derived metabolites to add insigts to the pathological mechanisms of AD. Methods: Blood samples were collected from 10 AD and 10 Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) patients, and 10 healthy controls. EVs were enriched from plasma using 100,000×g, 1 h, 4 °C with a wash. Metabolites from serum and EVs were measured using liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (LC-MS) and nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy. Multivariate and univariate analyses were employed to identify altered metabolites in cognitively impaired individuals. Results: While no significant EV-derived metabolites were found differentiating patients from healthy individuals, six serum metabolites were found important; valine (p = 0.001, fold change, FC = 0.8), histidine (p = 0.001, FC = 0.9), allopurinol riboside (p = 0.002, FC = 0.2), inosine (p = 0.002, FC = 0.3), 4-pyridoxic acid (p = 0.006, FC = 1.6), and guanosine (p = 0.004, FC = 0.3). Pathway analysis revealed branched-chain amino acids, purine and histidine metabolisms to be downregulated, and vitamin B6 metabolism upregulated in patients compared to controls. Conclusion: Using a combination of LC-MS and NMR methodologies we identified several altered mechanisms possibly related to AD pathology. EVs require additional optimization prior to their possible utilization as a biological material for AD-related metabolomics studies.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jonas Ellegaard","Maltesen, Raluca","Havelund, Jesper F","Færgeman, Nils J","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Vestergaard, Karsten","Kristensen, Søren Risom","Pedersen, Shona"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-009240"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Shona"],"country":["Australia","Qatar"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qatar University","Westmead Hospital","Westmead Millennium Institute for Medical Research"],"keyword":["Alzheimer","Blood","Mass spectrometry","Metabolites","Nuclear magnetic resonance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterising alzheimer s disease through integrative nmr and lc ms based metabolomics","src":["aau","dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.metop.2021.100125","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-009240","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8479251","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34622190","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-bfae88e6-f1b4-4376-ac72-dff03b1d57f9","dtu-d2f32605-355b-4692-848a-70769fd343c8","sdu-b5ac984e-f190-40b3-8004-75f46fe139d4"],"keyword":["Alzheimer","Blood","Extracellular vehicles","Mass spectrometry","Metabolites","Nuclear magnetic resonance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-14D549CCABA42E40F96808F6E721D1D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258590612/1_s2.0_S2589936821000499_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/192804086/1_s2.0_S2589936821000499_main_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/450517182/Ellegaard_Nielsen_2021_Characterising_Alzheimer_s_disease_through_integrative_NMR_and_LC_MS_based_metabolomics.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.metop.2021.100125","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Biochemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"westmead millennium institute for medical research","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Westmead Millennium Institute for Medical Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"westmead hospital","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Westmead Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","us