{"abstract":"We present a unified view of the two-party and multi-party computation protocols based on oblivious transfer first outlined in Nielsen et al. (CRYPTO 2012) and Larraia et al. (CRYPTO 2014). We present a number of modifications and improvements to these earlier presentations, as well as full proofs of the entire protocol. Improvements include a unified pre-processing and online MAC methodology, mechanisms to pass between different MAC variants and fixing a minor bug in the protocol of Larraia et al. in relation to a selective failure attack. It also fixes a minor bug in Nielsen et al. resulting from using Jensen’s inequality in the wrong direction in an analysis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Burra, Sai Sheshank","Larraia, Enrique","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Nordholt, Peter Sebastian","Orlandi, Claudio","Orsini, Emmanuela","Scholl, Peter","Smart, Nigel P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-167205"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Smart, Nigel P."],"country":["Belgium","India"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indian Institute of Technology, Guwahati","KU Leuven"],"keyword":["Multi party computation","Oblivious transfer","Secret sharing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high performance multi party computation for binary circuits based on oblivious transfer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2015/472.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-167205","identifier":[{"id":"85109080750","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-42836a26-8a27-4f32-9d96-8a5e2331a937"],"keyword":["Multi-party computation","Oblivious transfer","Secret sharing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E9A1FF165D021875783EAB8BD55ACE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2015/472.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"indian institute of technology guwahati","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Technology, Guwahati","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"ku leuven","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"KU Leuven","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sai Sheshank","key":"burrapau","last":"Burra","name":"Burra, Sai Sheshank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Enrique","key":"larraiapau","last":"Larraia","name":"Larraia, Enrique","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Sebastian","key":"nordholtpau","last":"Nordholt","name":"Nordholt, Peter Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claudio","key":"orlandipau","last":"Orlandi","locid":"393c3898-d32f-431e-aea6-ee1e79c535ef","name":"Orlandi, Claudio","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanuela","key":"orsinipau","last":"Orsini","name":"Orsini, Emmanuela","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schollpau","last":"Scholl","locid":"7b93a5ba-5c9f-406e-9190-58367dc70087","name":"Scholl, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nigel P.","key":"smartpau","last":"Smart","name":"Smart, Nigel P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00145-021-09403-1","issn":["09332790","14321378"],"issn_org":["09332790"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Cryptology","paperid":"34","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cryptology","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109080750"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-42836a26-8a27-4f32-9d96-8a5e2331a937"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"High-Performance Multi-party Computation for Binary Circuits Based on Oblivious Transfer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-167205","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Proteinuria is a well-established marker and predictor of kidney disease. The receptors megalin and cubilin reabsorb filtered proteins and thereby proteinuria is avoided. It is unknown if all segments of the proximal tubule are involved in clearing the filtrate or if there exists a reserve capacity in case of increased glomerular protein filtration. To determine this, we performed serial sectioning of rat kidney and used stereology to quantify the endolysosomal system of the three segments of cortical and juxtamedullary nephrons by electron microscopy. Immunohistochemistry was applied to analyze the adaptor protein Dab2, which assists in megalin mediated endocytosis, megalin, and endocytic uptake of two endogenous megalin ligands; retinol binding protein and β2-microglobulin at exact tubular positions. Proteinuric rats (puromycin-treated) and mice (podocin knock-out) were analyzed to clarify the response of the tubule to increased protein filtration. We found that the endolysosomal system was most prominent in segment 1 and 2, whereas segment 3 was less developed. The depth of ligand uptake varied among nephrons, but it descended into segment 2 although uptake was lower than in segment 1 and it was never observed in segment 3. This was supported by prominent expression of Dab2 in segment 1 and 2. When protein filtration increased, segment 3 was included in the reabsorption process in proteinuric animals. Thus, segment 1 and 2 are responsible for clearing the filtrate for protein during normal physiological conditions, but the tubule exhibits plasticity and is able to include segment 3 under proteinuric stress.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Erik Ilsø","Kristoffersen, Inger B.","Grann, Birgitte","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Andreasen, Arne","Nielsen, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-187547"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a well developed endolysosomal system reflects protein reabsorption in segment 000000000001 and 000000000002 of rat proximal tubules","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85101569778","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-187547","identifier":[{"id":"85101569778","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33340516","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-65e38aab-26d1-45c0-90a7-299da3fcf648"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-04A8AD35FD25968B9A1B04C7B19CF714"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Syd"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik I","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"02cd5f81-741b-46d7-817c-03908de2b830","name":"Christensen, Erik Ilsø","name_org":"Christensen, Erik I","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inger B","key":"kristoffersenpau","last":"Kristoffersen","locid":"eb6ca3b8-ebb2-43d4-85b8-1ed31b3b5b8f","name":"Kristoffersen, Inger B.","name_org":"Kristoffersen, Inger B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"grannpau","last":"Grann","locid":"e350ff33-8ae2-42dd-8f46-4eb8b8d5a2b4","name":"Grann, Birgitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J