 of Mathematics - Science Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Haslund","key":"hansenannehaslundped","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Anne Haslund","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"harbsmeiermichaelped","last":"Harbsmeier","name":"Harbsmeier, Michael","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Sune","key":"pedersenchristiansuneped","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Christian Sune","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kurt","key":"nielsenjesperkurtped","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kurt","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter A.","key":"toftpeteraped","last":"Toft","name":"Toft, Peter A.","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Hvidtfelt","key":"nielsenkristianhvidtfeltped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b3e227f2-dc63-4a9b-b77f-efdc7798c83f","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Hvidtfelt","orcid":"0000-0002-6192-400X","rank":6,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788712065876"],"place":"København","publisher":"Gad","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b442086-c588-40cf-88f8-99e65ad57b38"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dansk Ekspeditionshistorie 1-3","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-208776","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Accurate age estimates are key life history parameters for understanding growth, reproduction and susceptibility to exploitation. Using a combination of fin spine growth increments and bomb radiocarbon dating, we provide minimum age estimates for the small Atlantic squaloid shark, black dogfish (Centroscyllium fabricii) sampled in Greenland waters. Age estimates based on growth increments in the fin spine, just distal to the end of the pulp cavity, were obtained from males (N = 64) and females (N = 70), and von Bertalanffy growth curves were fitted. The maximum growth increment count was 36 in males and 35 in females. Males and females had similar growth rates, but females grew larger (Linf, females = 68 cm, Linf, males = 61 cm). To evaluate the fin spine age estimates, bomb radiocarbon dating on eye lenses were done on a selection of females. All individuals larger than 65 cm (total length) were older than the bomb pulse corresponding to an age of at least 53 years, while those smaller than 55 cm were younger. Therefore, we observe a discrepancy between age estimates obtained from fin spines and bomb radiocarbon dating, indicating that fin spines are unsuitable for ageing black dogfish, at least for the oldest individuals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hedeholm, R.","Qvist, Trine","Frausing, Marie Hartlev","Olsen, Jesper","Nielsen, J.","Grønkjær, P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-209709"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Hedeholm, R."],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources"],"keyword":["Ageing","Elasmobranch","Greenland","Radiocarbon dating"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"age of black dogfish i centroscyllium fabricii i estimated from fin spines growth bands and eye lens bomb radiocarbon dating","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85102313565","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-209709","identifier":[{"id":"85102313565","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000626360800002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-8cf415ae-0d66-4903-9185-97bdf239fc7a"],"keyword":["Ageing","Elasmobranch","Fin spine","Greenland","Radiocarbon dating"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9068B77A76C7C4B33FCB36556A0EEDE0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"hedeholmpau","last":"Hedeholm","name":"Hedeholm, R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"qvistpau","last":"Qvist","locid":"a8b43ff5-96d4-48ad-954e-6ed4c1ff81ba","name":"Qvist, Trine","name_org":"Qvist, T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"frausingpau","last":"Frausing","locid":"b3551f1e-4907-485b-be4c-364336728646","name":"Frausing, Marie Hartlev","name_org":"Frausing, M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","name_org":"Olsen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"grønkjærpau","last":"Grønkjær","locid":"d3a6e508-4f46-4954-b906-b78aa74617ef","name":"Grønkjær, P.","orcid":"0000-0003-1337-4661","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00300-021-02832-5","issn":["07224060","14322056"],"issn_org":["07224060"],"issue":"4","journal":"Polar Biology","pages":"751-759","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Polar Biology","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102313565"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8cf415ae-0d66-4903-9185-97bdf239fc7a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Age of black dogfish (<i>Centroscyllium fabricii</i>) estimated from fin spines growth bands and eye lens bomb radiocarbon dating","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-209709","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Profound biogeochemical responses of anoxic sediments to the fluctuation of dissolved oxygen (DO) concentration in overlaying water are often observed, despite oxygen having a limited permeability in sediments. This contradiction is indicative of previously unrecognized mechanism that bridges the oxic and anoxic sediment layers. Using sediments from an urban river suffering from long-term polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) contamination, we analyzed the physicochemical and microbial responses to artificially elevated DO (eDO) in the overlying water over 9 weeks of incubation. Significant changes in key environmental parameters and microbial diversity were detected over the 0-6 cm sediment depth, along with accelerated degradation of PAHs, despite that eDO only increased the porewater DO in the millimeter subfacial layer. The dynamics of physicochemical and microbial properties coincided well with significantly increased presence of centimeter-long sulfide-oxidizing cable bacteria filaments under eDO, and were predominantly driven by cable bacteria metabolic activities. Phylogenetic ecological network analyses further revealed that eDO reinforced cable bacteria associated interspecific interactions with functional microorganisms such as sulfate reducers, PAHs degraders, and electroactive microbes, suggesting enhanced microbial syntrophy taking advantage of cable bacteria metabolism for the regeneration of SO42- and long-distance electron transfer. Together, our results suggest cable bacteria may mediate the impacts of eDO in anaerobic sediments by altering sediment physiochemical properties and by reinforcing community interactions. Our findings highlight the ecological importance of cable bacteria in sediments.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Liu, Feifei","Wang, Zhenyu","Wu, Bo","Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","Hu, Wenzhe","Guo, Xue","Guo, Jun","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Qiu, Rongliang","Xu, Meiying"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Qiu, Rongliang","Xu, Meiying"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central South University","Guangdong Academy of Sciences","Sun Yat-Sen University","Tsinghua University"],"keyword":["Biodegradation","COOCCURRENCE PATTERNS","Carbon","Community","DISTANCE ELECTRON TRANSPORT","Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons","Reduction","SP NOV","Succession","Sulfur oxidation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cable bacteria extend the impacts of elevated dissolved oxygen into anoxic sediments","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8114917/pdf/41396_2020_Article_869.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-218545","identifier":[{"id":"000609401600004","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC8114917","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85099573519","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33479492","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9ca53cda-e92f-4871-9a83-0acf1f7a6ce6"],"keyword":["BIODEGRADATION","CARBON","COMMUNITY","COOCCURRENCE PATTERNS","DISTANCE ELECTRON-TRANSPORT","POLYCYCLIC AROMATIC-HYDROCARBONS","REDUCTION","SP NOV.","SUCCESSION","SULFUR OXIDATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA61C30B1E2FF81F875AF614E1C30655"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8114917/pdf/41396_2020_Article_869.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"guangdong academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Electromicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"central south university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Central South University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Feifei","key":"liufeifeipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Feifei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenyu","key":"wangzhenyupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zhenyu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"wubopau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper T","key":"bjergjesperjensenpau","last":"Bjerg","locid":"682ae3d8-d830-4101-b5a3-494ea2e4e0be","name":"Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","name_org":"Bjerg, Jesper T","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenzhe","key":"huwenzhepau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Wenzhe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue","key":"guoxuepau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xue","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"guojunpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Jun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Peter","key":"nielsenlarspeterpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b1f70e1-663b-4a12-b10c-a12dfc320c81","name":"Nielsen, Lars Peter",