{"abstract":"Development of outreach skills is critical for researchers when communicating their work to non-expert audiences. However, due to the lack of formal training, researchers are typically unaware of the benefits of outreach training and often under-prioritize outreach. We present a training programme conducted with an international network of PhD students in quantum physics, which focused on developing outreach skills and an understanding of the associated professional benefits by creating an outreach portfolio consisting of a range of implementable outreach products. We describe our approach, assess the impact, and provide a list of guidelines for designing similar programmes across scientific disciplines in the future.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ahmed, Shaeema Zaman","Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","Rafner, Janet Frances","Weidner, Carrie Ann","Kragh, Gitte","Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","Bobroff, Julien","Nielsen, Kristian Hvidtfelt","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237511"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Outreach"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a training programme for early stage researchers that focuses on developing personal science outreach portfolios","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.03109","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-237511","ids":["au-bd7bed94-0299-4869-9192-9c17ae519887"],"keyword":["Outreach","Outreach training","Training courses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0B0ED4C2B645030BF2914514475C075B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shaeema Zaman","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","locid":"31688a7f-4d2f-424b-91fa-4324335ebe9f","name":"Ahmed, Shaeema Zaman","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arthur","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"b6da5c3f-dc2f-4376-a964-cec167d512e6","name":"Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","name_org":"Hjorth, Arthur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janet Frances","key":"rafnerpau","last":"Rafner","locid":"6eb09423-83bf-4190-94a5-a3f472891daa","name":"Rafner, Janet Frances","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-3334","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carrie Ann","key":"weidnerpau","last":"Weidner","locid":"68b2603f-044e-4a2a-8121-327ceae816b4","name":"Weidner, Carrie Ann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"kraghpau","last":"Kragh","locid":"50786e62-94f6-4627-ac2c-ea689c8e8595","name":"Kragh, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0003-1792-2098","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"90e2a5b6-a5b4-46be-b61b-3e1140888954","name":"Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Julien","key":"bobroffpau","last":"Bobroff","name":"Bobroff, Julien","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Hvidtfelt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b3e227f2-dc63-4a9b-b77f-efdc7798c83f","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Hvidtfelt","orcid":"0000-0002-6192-400X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Friis","key":"shersonpau","last":"Sherson","locid":"3d8e1590-c4fa-495b-81b4-588fe374b36c","name":"Sherson, Jacob","name_org":"Sherson, Jacob Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-6048-587X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2103.03109","issn":["10755470"],"series":"Science Communication","status":"s"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["au-bd7bed94-0299-4869-9192-9c17ae519887"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A training programme for early-stage researchers that focuses on developing personal science outreach portfolios","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-237511","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Exposure to electrical current may cause injury with both mental and physiological consequences. This may lead to increased contacts with general practitioners (GP) and the injured person may develop reduced ability to work. We aimed to examine these outcomes in terms of work-participation, long-term sick leave and contacts with GPs. METHODS: In a matched cohort design, we identified 14 112 electrical injuries in two registries and matched these with both patients with distorsion injuries or eye injuries, and with persons from the same occupation, using year of injury, sex and age for matching. We defined the outcomes based on register information regarding contacts with GPs and public transfer income. After the injury, we determined if the person had a long-term sick leave episode during the first 6, 12 months and 5 years. We calculated work participation during the year and 5 years and the number of GP contacts in the year of the injury, the year after and 5 years after the injury and dichotomised this at twice the mean number of contacts in the study population. The associations were analysed using conditional logistic regression. RESULTS: We found increased risk for all defined outcomes, with the highest estimates in the occupation match. The risk estimates were similar over time. Adjusting for previous work participation increased the estimates slightly, whereas adjusting for previous contacts with GPs reduced the estimates. Restricting to those with at longer hospitalisation increased the estimates. CONCLUSION: Electrical injuries increase risk of long-term sick leave, low work participation and increased contacts with GPs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Biering, Karin","Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","Nielsen, Kent Jacob","Carstensen, Ole","Kærgaard, Anette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-247598"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Biering, Karin"],"keyword":["Health and safety","Health services research","Public health","Sickness absence","occupational health practice"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contacts with general practitioner sick leave and work participation after electrical injuries a register based matched cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85096026748","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-247598","identifier":[{"id":"33139345","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85096026748","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cef64e15-cf8e-4412-a248-89a3b6723f55"],"keyword":["health and safety","health services research","occupational health practice","public health","sickness absence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4382CB927346E6B3F73FE79AEC841F0E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Occupational and Environmental Medicine, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Dansk Ramazzini Center"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin","key":"bieringpau","last":"Biering","locid":"747fb3a4-9438-4f99-b7c3-d13deeb4442f","name":"Biering, Karin","orcid":"0000-0001-7038-9566","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Medom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f2a2e103-1293-4370-b308-c4427f184a75","name":"Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-6566","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent Jacob","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b11fecf5-8895-4034-a7b1-d5eb0399ea93","name":"Nielsen, Kent Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-4643-5697","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"f3192717-9366-4b48-9462-782288954025","name":"Carstensen, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette","key":"kærgaardpau","last":"Kærgaard","locid":"97dbcdfa-9288-42b8-960e-47568add33e3","name":"Kærgaard, Anette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33139345"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/oemed-2020-106858","issn":["13510711","14707926"],"issn_org":["13510711"],"issue":"1","journal":"Occupational and Environmental Medicine","pages":"54-60","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Occupational and Environmental Medicine","title_org":"Occupational & Environmental Medicine","volume":"78"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096026748"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","dansk ramazzini center"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cef64e15-cf8e-4412-a248-89a3b6723f55"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Contacts with general practitioner, sick leave and work participation after electrical injuries : a register-based, matched cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-247598","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Prognostication of neurological outcome in patients who remain comatose after cardiac arrest resuscitation is complex. Clinical variables, as well as biomarkers of brain injury, cardiac injury, and systemic inflammation, all yield some prognostic value. We hypothesised that cumulative information obtained during the first three days of intensive care could produce a reliable model for predicting neurological outcome following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) using artificial neural network (ANN) with and without biomarkers. Methods: We performed a post hoc analysis of 932 patients from the Target Temperature Management trial. We focused on comatose patients at 24, 48, and 72 h post-cardiac arrest and excluded patients who were awake or deceased at these time points. 80% of the patients were allocated for model development (training set) and 20% for internal validation (test set). To investigate the prognostic potential of different levels of biomarkers (clinically available and research-grade), patients’ background information, and intensive care observation and treatment, we created three models for each time point: (1) clinical variables, (2) adding clinically accessible biomarkers, e.g., neuron-specific enolase (NSE) and (3) adding research-grade biomarkers, e.g., neurofilament light (NFL). Patient outcome was the dichotomised Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) at six months; a good outcome was defined as CPC 1–2 whilst a poor outcome was defined as CPC 3–5. The area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) was calculated for all test sets. Results: AUROC remained below 90% when using only clinical variables throughout the first three days in the ICU. Adding clinically accessible biomarkers such as NSE, AUROC increased from 82 to 94% (p < 0.01). The prognostic accuracy remained excellent from day 1 to day 3 with an AUROC at approximately 95% when adding research-grade biomarkers. The models which included NSE after 72 h and NFL on any of the three days had a low risk of false-positive predictions while retaining a low number of false-negative predictions. Conclusions: In this exploratory study, ANNs provided good to excellent prognostic accuracy in predicting neurological outcome in comatose patients post OHCA. The models which included NSE after 72 h and NFL on all days showed promising prognostic performance.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Andersson, Peder","Johnsson, Jesper","Björnsson, Ola","Cronberg, Tobias","Hassager, Christian","Zetterberg, Henrik","Stammet, Pascal","Undén, Johan","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Friberg, Hans","Blennow, Kaj","Lilja, Gisela","Wise, Matt P.","Dankiewicz, Josef","Nielsen, Niklas","Frigyesi, Attila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400221"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Luxembourg","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiff & Vale University Health Board","Lund University","National Rescue Services","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","University College London","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Artificial neural networks","Cardiac arrest","Cerebral performance category","Critical care","Intensive care","Machine learning","Neural networks","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prediction","Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting neurological outcome after out of hospital cardiac arrest with cumulative information development and internal validation of an artificial neural network algorithm","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-021-03505-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-400221","identifier":[{"id":"33632280","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85101674034","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7905905","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-0b47ab6b-4d41-4dd0-89f7-d17031350151"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Artificial neural networks","Cardiac arrest","Cerebral performance category","Critical care","Intensive care","Machine learning","Neural networks","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Prediction","Prognostication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C27B20582A8EA17AAD8F446D32ABA3C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/259045653/s13054_021_03505_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-021-03505-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","u