{"abstract":"Artisanal and small-scale mining (ASM) is a vital livelihood practice around the world, especially in the Global South. In Tanzania, millions of people depend on artisanal and small-scale gold mining and many of these people are in Geita, the main gold mining region of Tanzania. Based on qualitative research conducted in this region, this paper engages the artisanal and small-scale miners? experiences of gold mining. It highlights how extracting gold is experienced as increasingly difficult and how miners worry that gold reserves will be exhausted in the near future. Academic attention and policy making have focused on formalization and sustainable management of ASM, addressing current practices and their social and environmental impacts. However, a knowledge gap remains in the understanding of livelihood implications that emerge when mineral sources are nearing exhaustion and they become harder to extract. In Geita, this has led miners to diversify their investments and consider alternative livelihood strategies. With a focus on the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), this paper calls for a broader sustainability discussion on ASM, as well as a better integration of ASM into the SDG agenda. This integration should consider exit strategies for miners as their livelihoods depend upon non-renewable resources.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Anna Frohn","Nielsen, Jonas Østergaard","Friis, Cecilie","Jonsson, Jesper Bosse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437775"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Tanzania"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","RSK Environment (East Africa) Limited"],"keyword":["Livelihood diversification","SDGs","Sustainable development goals","Tanzania"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mineral exhaustion and its livelihood implications for artisanal and small scale miners","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsci.2021.02.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-437775","identifier":[{"id":"85101389435","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000631907500003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-4a3dd0af-cd9c-4610-9969-35fe183306c5"],"keyword":["Artisanal and small-scale mining","Livelihood diversification","Mineral decline","SDGS","Sustainable development goals","Tanzania"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-457E3B7C26B9417C9F1E65582095CB56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsci.2021.02.002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321962818/Mineral_exhaustion_and_its_livelihood_implications_for_artisanal_and_small_scale_miners.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"tz","key":"rsk environment limited","loc":["Tanzania","Africa"],"name":"RSK Environment (East Africa) Limited","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Frohn","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anna Frohn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Østergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Østergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Cecilie","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"47b8753d-2b36-4561-9162-bb13b509e74f","name":"Friis, Cecilie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Bosse","key":"jonssonpau","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Jesper Bosse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envsci.2021.02.002","issn":["14629011","18736416"],"issn_org":["14629011"],"journal":"Environmental Science & Policy","pages":"34-43","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Policy","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101389435"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4a3dd0af-cd9c-4610-9969-35fe183306c5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mineral exhaustion and its livelihood implications for artisanal and small-scale miners","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437775","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Teotihuacan, the great metropolis of the Central Mexican highlands, has often been characterized as a state without a writing system. This paper redresses this notion and provides an overview of the city’s writing system and weighs in on its state of decipherment. The corpus of texts is defined and outlined as are its media and contexts. The geographical distribution of the writing system is considered, identifying the localities that define the heartland of Teotihuacan writing and culture, as well as more distant sites and enclaves elsewhere in Mesoamerica where examples of Teotihuacan writing have been found. The temporal distribution is also appraised before going on to present the underlying graphic characteristics of the writing system, leading to an appraisal of the sign inventory, showing clear correspondences to other Mesoamerican logophonetic writing systems. A synopsis of previous work on the writing system is presented in a historical précis, before considering candidate languages of the script and features of the underlying language recorded in the writing system.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Helmke, Christophe","Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446017"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teotihuacan writing where are we now","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34314/vl.v55i2.4607","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446017","identifier":[{"id":"105007453806","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-57efe513-2a3d-435b-b426-4e1723199744"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A33E23A92543412FAC3F93D53B0B399F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/283915060/2021_VL_55_2_029_073.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34314/vl.v55i2.4607","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34314/vl.v55i2.4607","issn":["00222224"],"issue":"2","journal":"Visible Language","pages":"29-73","status":"p","title":"Visible Language","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007453806"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-57efe513-2a3d-435b-b426-4e1723199744"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Teotihuacan Writing : Where are we now?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446017","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Photoswitchable small molecules, such as N , N'- disubstituted indigos, have received great interest within fields such as pharmacology, energy storage, and functional materials, as they represent key building blocks for reversible and non-invasive control of chemical processes. However, to ensure applicability of photochromic systems it is of paramount importance to manipulate the photostationary state. In this work, we achieved this by tethering two redox-active indenofluorene-extended tetrathiafulvalene units to an N , N' -disubstituted indigo photoswitch. Upon two-electron oxidation, we observe significantly enhanced stability of the Z -isomer, compared to the neutral compound, illustrated by a substantial increase in the half-life from 0.48 seconds to 22 hours. This remarkable stabilization is ascribed to formation of strong, intramolecular pi-dimers between the oxidized subunits.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Broløs, Line","Klaue, Kristin","Bendix, Jesper","Grubert, Lutz","Hecht, Stefan","Nielsen, Mogens Brøndsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446046"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross coupling","Fused ring systems","Photochromism","Sulfur heterocycles","Supramolecular chemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stabilizing indigo z isomer via intramolecular associations of redox active appendages","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/279650658/Stabilizing_Indigo_Z_isomer_via_Intramolecular_Associations_of_Redox_Active_Appendages_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446046","identifier":[{"id":"85115879830","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-57f