{"abstract":"Purpose: The majority of unconscious patients after cardiac arrest (CA) do not fulfill guideline criteria for a likely poor outcome, their prognosis is considered “indeterminate”. We compared brain injury markers in blood for prediction of good outcome and for identifying false positive predictions of poor outcome as recommended by guidelines. Methods: Retrospective analysis of prospectively collected serum samples at 24, 48 and 72 h post arrest within the Target Temperature Management after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (TTM)-trial. Clinically available markers neuron-specific enolase (NSE) and S100B, and novel markers neurofilament light chain (NFL), total tau, ubiquitin carboxy-terminal hydrolase L1 (UCH-L1) and glial fibrillary acidic protein (GFAP) were analysed. Normal levels with a priori cutoffs specified by reference laboratories or defined from literature were used to predict good outcome (no to moderate disability, Cerebral Performance Category scale 1–2) at 6 months. Results: Seven hundred and seventeen patients were included. Normal NFL, tau and GFAP had the highest sensitivities (97.2–98% of poor outcome patients had abnormal serum levels) and NPV (normal levels predicted good outcome in 87–95% of patients). Normal S100B and NSE predicted good outcome with NPV 76–82.2%. Normal NSE correctly identified 67/190 (35.3%) patients with good outcome among those classified as “indeterminate outcome” by guidelines. Five patients with single pathological prognostic findings despite normal biomarkers had good outcome. Conclusion: Low levels of brain injury markers in blood are associated with good neurological outcome after CA. Incorporating biomarkers into neuroprognostication may help prevent premature withdrawal of life-sustaining therapy.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Moseby-Knappe, Marion","Mattsson-Carlgren, Niklas","Stammet, Pascal","Backman, Sofia","Blennow, Kaj","Dankiewicz, Josef","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Lilja, Gisela","Rylander, Christian","Ullén, Susann","Undén, Johan","Westhall, Erik","Wise, Matt P.","Zetterberg, Henrik","Nielsen, Niklas","Cronberg, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541183"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Luxembourg","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","National Fire and Rescue Corps","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","University College London","University Hospital of Wales","University of Gothenburg","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Blood biomarkers","Cardiac arrest","Neurofilament light","Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"serum markers of brain injury can predict good neurological outcome after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-021-06481-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-541183","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8421280","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34417831","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85113165680","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f77a035f-cfc8-4260-93e4-84db1c42f2a6"],"keyword":["Blood biomarkers","Cardiac arrest","ERC/ESICM guidelines","Good neurological outcome","Neurofilament light","Prognostication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-174656F07D8BBDE704DD95249E49F8E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-021-06481-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280240942/Moseby_Knappe2021_Article_SerumMarkersOfBrainInjuryCanPr.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"lu","key":"national fire and rescue corps","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Fire and Rescue Corps","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"sahlgrenska university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Sahlgrenska University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nl","key":"vrije universiteit amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","l