{"abstract":"We investigate vortex pair interactions at low Reynolds numbers. We base our analysis on the Q-criterion, where a vortex is defined as a region where the local rotation dominates the strain, and we make use of a topological approach to describe the qualitative changes of the vortex structure. In order to give a complete description of vortex pair interactions we further develop a general bifurcation theory for-vortices and prove that a threshold for vortex merging may occur when we allow two parameters to vary. To limit the number of free parameters, we study the interactions with two point vortices as the initial condition and show that the threshold is a codimension two bifurcation that appears as a cusp singularity on a bifurcation curve. We apply the general theory to the analytically tractable core growth model and conclude that a pair of co-rotating vortices merge only if their strength ratio, is less than. Below this threshold value, we observe two different regimes in which the merging processes can be described with different sequences of bifurcations. By comparison with Navier-Stokes simulations at different Reynolds numbers, we conclude that the merging threshold varies only slightly for Reynolds numbers up to. Furthermore, we observe an excellent agreement between the core growth model and the numerical simulations for Reynolds numbers below 10. We therefore conclude that, instead of solving the Navier-Stokes equation numerically we can, for sufficiently small Reynolds numbers, apply the core growth model as a simple, analytically tractable model with a low dimension.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anne R.","Andersen, Morten","Hansen, Jesper S.","Brøns, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038098"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bifurcation","Topological fluid dynamics","Vortex interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"topological bifurcations of vortex pair interactions","src":["dtu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262409171/Revision_of_second_submission_6_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Financial support from Independent Research Fund Denmark, grant no. 6108-00246B, is gratefully acknowledged."],"id":"S02-100.00-038098","identifier":[{"id":"85104871820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f800b697-99f0-4d17-b8eb-26868bf307be","ruc-dfd92169-65d0-4ebf-82fe-80cb89aa474d"],"keyword":["Bifurcation","Topological fluid dynamics","Vortex interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D5984685DA6C6FFB1A07A09F83A425FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262409171/Revision_of_second_submission_6_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77611730/Main_document.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne R.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08f659f4-035d-4e85-950a-0d4feb85ab96","name":"Nielsen, Anne R.","orcid":"0000-0001-7144-8978","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c3e27de5-fa0e-4dde-9dd5-249374492239","name":"Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7582-0685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schmidt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"413f2c94-d35d-4ae4-89f2-361d8fc3ccc3","name":"Hansen, Jesper Schmidt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"brønspau","last":"Brøns","locid":"b364a278-ce14-4e88-be21-7d0cd7ea6a7a","name":"Brøns, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-5522-3410","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/jfm.2021.191","issn":["00221120","14697645"],"issn_org":["00221120"],"journal":"Journal of Fluid Mechanics","paperid":"2100191","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Fluid Mechanics","volume":"917"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104871820"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f800b697-99f0-4d17-b8eb-26868bf307be","ruc-dfd92169-65d0-4ebf-82fe-80cb89aa474d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Topological bifurcations of vortex pair interactions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038098","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Severity and extent of coronary artery disease (CAD) assessed by invasive coronary angiography (ICA) guide treatment and may predict clinical outcome in patients with non–ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome (NSTEACS). Objectives: This study tested the hypothesis that coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA) is equivalent to ICA for risk assessment in patients with NSTEACS. Methods: The VERDICT (Very Early Versus Deferred Invasive Evaluation Using Computerized Tomography in Patients With Acute Coronary Syndromes) trial evaluated timing of treatment in relation to outcome in patients with NSTEACS and included a clinically blinded coronary CTA conducted prior to ICA. Severity of CAD was defined as obstructive (coronary stenosis ≥50%) or nonobstructive. Extent of CAD was defined as high risk (obstructive left main or proximal left anterior descending artery stenosis and/or multivessel disease) or non–high risk. The primary endpoint was a composite of all-cause death, nonfatal recurrent myocardial infarction, hospital admission for refractory myocardial ischemia, or heart failure. Results: Coronary CTA and ICA were conducted in 978 patients. During a median follow-up time of 4.2 years (interquartile range: 2.7 to 5.5 years), the primary endpoint occurred in 208 patients (21.3%). The rate of the primary endpoint was up to 1.7-fold higher in patients with obstructive CAD compared with in patients with nonobstructive CAD as defined by coronary CTA (hazard ratio [HR]: 1.74; 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.22 to 2.49; p = 0.002) or ICA (HR: 1.54; 95% CI: 1.13 to 2.11; p = 0.007). In patients with high-risk CAD, the rate of the primary endpoint was 1.5-fold higher compared with the rate in those with non–high-risk CAD as defined by coronary CTA (HR: 1.56; 95% CI: 1.18 to 2.07; p = 0.002). A similar trend was noted for ICA (HR: 1.28; 95% CI: 0.98 to 1.69; p = 0.07). Conclusions: Coronary CTA is equivalent to ICA for the assessment of long-term risk in patients with NSTEACS. (Very Early Versus Deferred Invasive Evaluation Using Computerized Tomography in Patients With Acute Coronary Syndromes [VERDICT]; NCT02061891)","author_count":41,"contributors":["Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Engstrøm, Thomas","Sigvardsen, Per E.","Linde, Jesper J.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","de Knegt, Martina","Hansen, Peter Riis","Fritz-Hansen, Thomas","Bech, Jan","Heitmann, Merete","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Høfsten, Dan E.","Kühl, Jørgen T.","Raymond, Ilan E.","Kristiansen, Ole P.","Svendsen, Ida H.","Domínguez Vall-Lamora, M. H.","Kragelund, Charlotte","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Jørgensen, Tem","Fornitz, Gitte Gleerup","Steffensen, Rolf","Jurlander, Birgit","Abdulla, Jawdat","Lyngbæk, Stig","Elming, Hanne","Therkelsen, Susette Krohn","Jørgensen, Erik","Kløvgaard, Lene","Bang, Lia E.","Helqvist, Steffen","Galatius, Søren","Pedersen, Frants","Abildgaard, Ulrik","Clemmensen, Peter","Saunamäki, Kari","Holmvang, Lene","Gislason, Gunnar","Kelbæk, Henning","Køber, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047273"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kofoed, Klaus F."],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Angiography","Cardiac computed tomography","Prognosis","Risk stratification"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic value of coronary ct angiography in patients with non st segment elevation acute coronary syndromes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacc.2020.12.037","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by the Danish Agency for Science, Technology, and Innovation and the Danish Council for Strategic Research (grant 09–066994) and the Research Council of Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen, Denmark. Dr. Kofoed has received grants from the Danish Research Foundation during the conduct of the study, in addition to grants from the Research Council of Rigshospitalet, AP Moller og Hustru Chastine McKinney Mollers Fond, the Danish Heart Foundation, and Canon Medical Corporation, outside the submitted work. Dr. Engstrom has received personal fees from Abbott, AstraZeneca, Bayer, Boston Scientific, and Novo, outside the submitted work. Dr. Linde has received grants from the Danish Research Foundation and the Research Council of Rigshospitalet during the conduct of the study. Dr. Torp-Pedersen has received grants from Bayer, outside the submitted work. Dr. Abdulla has received personal fees from Novartis Healthcare, outside the submitted work. Dr. Kober has received grants from the Danish Research Foundation during the conduct of the study. All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose."],"id":"S02-100.00-047273","identifier":[{"id":"85101040952","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33632478","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f0400315-d16a-485f-a2ed-08ef0613f7e3","sdu-6061b4a7-30ad-408f-a803-5fa4f1c48163"],"keyword":["acute coronary syndrome","angiography","cardiac computed tomography","prognosis","risk stratification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D9ACEDD8931E902C5A18F03E30864262"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacc.2020.12.037","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"