{"abstract":"The inherent difficulty of maintaining stateful environments over long periods of time gave rise to the paradigm of serverless computing, where mostly stateless components are deployed on demand to handle computation tasks, and are torn down once their task is complete. Serverless architecture could offer the added benefit of improved resistance to targeted denial-of-service attacks, by hiding from the attacker the physical machines involved in the protocol until after they complete their work. Realizing such protection, however, requires that the protocol only uses stateless parties, where each party sends only one message and never needs to speaks again. Perhaps the most famous example of this style of protocols is the Nakamoto consensus protocol used in Bitcoin: A peer can win the right to produce the next block by running a local lottery (mining) while staying covert. Once the right has been won, it is executed by sending a single message. After that, the physical entity never needs to send more messages. We refer to this as the You-Only-Speak-Once (YOSO) property, and initiate the formal study of it within a new model that we call the YOSO model. Our model is centered around the notion of roles, which are stateless parties that can only send a single message. Crucially, our modelling separates the protocol design, that only uses roles, from the role-assignment mechanism, that assigns roles to actual physical entities. This separation enables studying these two aspects separately, and our YOSO model in this work only deals with the protocol-design aspect. We describe several techniques for achieving YOSO MPC; both computational and information theoretic. Our protocols are synchronous and provide guaranteed output delivery (which is important for application domains such as blockchains), assuming honest majority of roles in every time step. We describe a practically efficient computationally-secure protocol, as well as a proof-of-concept information theoretically secure protocol.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gentry, Craig","Halevi, Shai","Krawczyk, Hugo","Magri, Bernardo","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Rabin, Tal","Yakoubov, Sophia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-215104"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-20","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-08-16","title":"41st Annual International Cryptology Conference, CRYPTO 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gentry, Craig"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at Berkeley"],"keyword":["Blockchains","secure MPC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"yoso you only speak once secure mpc with stateless ephemeral roles","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85115333209","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-215104","identifier":[{"id":"85115333209","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-969a631b-46e1-4453-aedd-b356199e20bf"],"keyword":["Blockchains","Secure MPC","Stateless Parties","YOSO"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-981983861CDDE13F90AB10A12BB1F82A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Craig","key":"gentrypau","last":"Gentry","name":"Gentry, Craig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shai","key":"halevipau","last":"Halevi","name":"Halevi, Shai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo","key":"krawczykpau","last":"Krawczyk","name":"Krawczyk, Hugo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo","key":"magripau","last":"Magri","locid":"2e4b2471-3423-4eac-a276-f6670afa1f76","name":"Magri, Bernardo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tal","key":"rabinpau","last":"Rabin","name":"Rabin, Tal","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sophia","key":"yakoubovpau","last":"Yakoubov","locid":"818cd271-6e5e-4980-b248-4a337b7c0603","name":"Yakoubov, Sophia","orcid":"0000-0001-7958-8537","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tal","key":"malkinpedh","last":"Malkin","name":"Malkin, Tal","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chris","key":"peikertpedh","last":"Peikert","name":"Peikert, Chris","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-84245-1_3","isbn":["9783030842444"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"64-93","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Annual International Cryptology Conference","title":"Advances in Cryptology – CRYPTO 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115333209"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-969a631b-46e1-4453-aedd-b356199e20bf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"YOSO: You Only Speak Once : Secure MPC with Stateless Ephemeral Roles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-215104","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The SARS-CoV-2 pandemic currently prevails worldwide. To understand the immunological signature of SARS-CoV-2 infections and aid the search and evaluation of new treatment modalities and vaccines, comprehensive characterization of adaptive immune responses towards SARS-CoV-2 is needed. Methods: We included 203 recovered SARS-CoV-2 infected patients in Denmark between April 3rd and July 9th 2020, at least 14 days after COVID-19 symptom recovery. The participants had experienced a range of disease severities from asymptomatic to severe. We collected plasma, serum and PBMC's for analysis of SARS-CoV-2 specific antibody response by Meso Scale analysis including other coronavirus strains, ACE2 competition, IgA ELISA, pseudovirus neutralization capacity, and dextramer flow cytometry analysis of CD8+ T cells. The immunological outcomes were compared amongst severity groups within the cohort, and 10 pre-pandemic SARS-CoV-2 negative controls. Findings: We report broad serological profiles within the cohort, detecting antibody binding to other human coronaviruses. 202(>99%) participants had SARS-CoV-2 specific antibodies, with SARS-CoV-2 neutralization and spike-ACE2 receptor interaction blocking observed in 193(95%) individuals. A significant positive correlation (r=0.7804) between spike-ACE2 blocking antibody titers and neutralization potency was observed. Further, SARS-CoV-2 specific CD8+ T-cell responses were clear and quantifiable in 95 of 106(90%) HLA-A2+ individuals. Interpretation: The viral surface spike protein was identified as the dominant target for both neutralizing antibodies and CD8+ T-cell responses. Overall, the majority of patients had robust adaptive immune responses, regardless of their disease severity. Funding: This study was supported by the Danish Ministry for Research and Education (grant# 0238-00001B) and The Danish Innovation Fund (grant# 0208-00018B)","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nielsen, Stine Sofie Frank","Vibholm, Line K.","Monrad, Ida","Olesen, Rikke","Frattari, Giacomo","Pahus, Marie Høst","Højen, Jesper Falkesgaard","Damsgaard Gunst, Jesper","Erikstrup, Christian","Holleufer, Andreas","Hartmann, Rune","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","Schleimann, Mariane Høgsbjerg","Tolstrup, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-241176"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Stine Sofie Frank"],"keyword":["Adaptive","Antibody","Asymptomatic","CD8 T cell","Corona","Covid 19","Immune response","SARS CoV 2","Severe","Virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sars cov 000000000002 elicits robust adaptive immune responses regardless of disease severity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2021.103410","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-241176","identifier":[{"id":"000668948400019","type":"wos"},{"id":"34098342","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8176920","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85108696247","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c3f947ab-2a8b-4233-bf4c-902b6b2de478"],"keyword":["Adaptive","Antibody","Asymptomatic","CD8 T-cell","COVID-19","Corona","Immune response","SARS-CoV-2","Severe","Virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5FD926D6C23AB4A4CF59BF375E489EC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2021.103410","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Sofie Frank","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"725719a2-01c0-4e6d-af64-6204e4f0ed35","name":"Nielsen, Stine Sofie Frank","orcid":"0000-0002-3313-5900","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Khalidan","key":"vibholmpau","last":"Vibholm","locid":"6ec0dcc4-c4ed-4c71-b983-f6ffa62883b4","name":"Vibholm, Line K.","name_org":"Vibholm, Line Khalidan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ida Monrad","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","locid":"8407b9b1-9bad-4f93-994b-e104ac211a7b","name":"Monrad, Ida","name_org":"Johannsen, Ida Monrad","orcid":"0009-0005-2610-8751","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"0c7b0a09-5f82-49ba-a6c3-5c7702fc3d4c","name":"Olesen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-5157-080X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giacomo","key":"frattaripau","last":"Frattari","locid":"cd6d85ae-d931-45bd-b1b0-118f6f88f4d4","name":"Frattari, Giacomo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Høst","key":"pahuspau","last":"Pahus","locid":"23f86c71-bc37-4c73-b0b4-5975230f738c","name":"Pahus, Marie Høst","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Falkesgaard","key":"højenpau","last":"Højen","locid":"1e68165f-6a55-4a88-80e5-eaf54214dcec","name":"Højen, Jesper Falkesgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"damsgaardgunstpau","last":"Damsgaard Gunst","name":"Damsgaard Gunst, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"523ae417-65a9-46aa-b665-0d88271dc0b9","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6551-6647","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"holleuferpau","last":"Holleufer","locid":"f12763af-3b6c-4cdc-a71f-2276b9b75692","name":"Holleufer, Andreas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"693cef7b-e116-4613-a5ca-bc538cab5b9f","name":"Hartmann, Rune","orcid":"0000-0003-1159-066X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Jørgen","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"fb8358a6-187a-4d5f-8187-06051ed74173","name":"Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-2459-0511","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Schmeltz","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"1939f653-c3a3-482e-a947-b1a7501b3986","name":"Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","orcid":"0000-0001-9107-2023","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariane Høgsbjerg","key":"schleimannpau","last":"Schleimann","locid":"9ff961ea-e475-4bab-bb80-f620961dace1","name":"Schleimann, Mariane Høgsbjerg","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"tolstruppau","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"36e9f1d5-608c-46b7-8d41-2505c02086fc","name":"Tolstrup, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7020-5173","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34098342"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ebiom.2021.103410","issn":["23523964"],"journal":"EBioMedicine","paperid":"103410","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"EBioMedicine","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108696247"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c3f947ab-2a8b-4233-bf4c-902b6b2de478"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"SARS-CoV-2 elicits robust adaptive immune responses regardless of disease severity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-241176","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Electrical injuries happen every day in homes and workplaces. Not only may these injuries cause physical damage and disability, they may also cause mental disorders. The aim of this study was to investigate if persons with an electrical injury suffer from mental disorders in the following years. MATERIAL AND METHODS: In a prospective matched cohort design, we identified 14.112 electrical injuries in two Danish registries and matched these with persons with dislocation/sprain injuries or eye injuries, respectively, as well as with persons from the workforce from the same occupation, using year of injury, sex and age as matching variables. We identified possible outcomes in terms of mental diagnoses in the Danish National Patient registry, based on literature, including reviews, original studies and case-reports as well as experiences from clinical praxis. The associations were analyzed using conditional cox- and logistic regression. RESULTS: We found that the following of the examined outcomes were associated with exposure to an electrical injury compared to the matched controls. Some of the outcomes showed the strongest associations shortly after the injury, namely 'mental disorders due to known physiological condition', 'anxiety and adjustment disorders', and especially the 'Post Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD)' subgroup. The same pattern was seen for 'Depression' although the associations were weaker. Other conditions took time to develop ('Somatoform disorders'), or were only present in the time to event analysis ('other non-psychotic mental disorders' and 'sleep disorders'). The findings were consistent in all three matches, with the highest risk estimates in the occupation match. CONCLUSION: Electrical injuries may result in mental disorders, both acute and several years after. However, the absolute risk is limited as most of the outcomes are rare.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Biering, Karin","Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","Kærgaard, Anette","Carstensen, Ole","Nielsen, Kent Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255508"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Biering, Karin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mental disorders following electrical injuries a register based matched cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0247317","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255508","identifier":[{"id":"33617562","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85101948275","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7899322","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-dd11afa7-2136-4ae7-b02d-3691e0d08d94"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78512C11EF09EE8595D89E6E7F31B2A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0247317","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Occupational and Environmental Medicine, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin","key":"bieringpau","last":"Biering","locid":"747fb3a4-9438-4f99-b7c3-d13deeb4442f","name":"Biering, Karin","orcid":"0000-0001-7038-9566","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Medom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f2a2e103-1293-4370-b308-c4427f184a75","name":"Vestergaard, Jesper Medom","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-6566","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette","key":"kærgaardpau","last":"Kærgaard","locid":"97dbcdfa-9288-42b8-960e-47568add33e3","name":"Kærgaard, Anette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"f3192717-9366-4b48-9462-782288954025","name":"Carstensen, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent J","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b11fecf5-8895-4034-a7b1-d5eb0399ea93","name":"Nielsen, Kent Jacob","name_org":"Nielsen, Kent J","orcid":"0000-0002-4643-5697","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33617562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0247317","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"2","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0247317","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101948275"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dd11afa7-2136-4ae7-b02d-3691e0d08d94"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mental disorders following electrical injuries-A register-based, matched cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255508","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Phonon interactions are inevitable in cavity quantum electrodynamical systems based on solid-state emitters or fluorescent molecules, where vibrations of the lattice or chemical bonds couple to the electronic degrees of freedom. Due to the non-Markovian response of the vibrational environment, it remains a significant theoretical challenge to describe such effects in a computationally efficient manner. This is particularly pronounced when the emitter-cavity coupling is comparable with or larger than the typical phonon energy range, and polariton formation coincides with vibrational dressing of the optical transitions. In this paper, we consider four non-Markovian perturbative master equation approaches to describe such dynamics over a broad range of light-matter coupling strengths and compare them with numerically exact reference calculations using a tensor network. The master equations are derived using different basis transformations, and a perturbative expansion in the transformed basis is subsequently introduced and analyzed. We find that two approaches are particularly successful and robust. The first of these is suggested and developed in this paper and is based on a vibrational dressing of the exciton-cavity polaritons. This enables the description of distinct phonon-polariton sidebands that appear when the polariton splitting exceeds the typical phonon frequency scale in the environment. The second approach is based on a variationally optimized polaronic vibrational dressing of the electronic state. Both of these approaches demonstrate good qualitative and quantitative agreement with reference calculations of the emission spectrum and are numerically robust, even at elevated temperatures, where the thermal phonon population is significant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bundgaard-Nielsen, Matias","Mørk, Jesper","Denning, Emil Vosmar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373812"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bundgaard-Nielsen, Matias"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non markovian perturbation theories for phonon effects in strong coupling cavity quantum electrodynamics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.103.235309","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This paper was supported by the Danish National Research Foundation through NanoPhoton—Center for Nanophotonics, Grant No. DNRF147, and Villum Fonden through the NATEC Center (Grant No. 8692). E.V.D. acknowledges support from Independent Research Fund Denmark through an International Postdoc fellowship."],"id":"S01-000.00-373812","identifier":[{"id":"85108021734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e7994e6c-aac0-47ff-ae50-53892f0a5999"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F24AB9AB078304CA12CE3BC1A314DFA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258975975/PhysRevB.103.235309.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.103.235309","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matias","key":"bundgaardnielsenpau","last":"Bundgaard-Nielsen","name":"Bundgaard-Nielsen, Matias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Vosmar","key":"denningpau","last":"Denning","locid":"22939a2d-b8f5-4324-99f9-d1debfe5ce2d","name":"Denning, Emil Vosmar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.103.235309","issn":["1550235X","24699950"],"issn_org":["24699950"],"issue":"23","journal":"Physical Review B","paperid":"235309","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108021734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e7994e6c-aac0-47ff-ae50-53892f0a5999"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Non-Markovian perturbation theories for phonon effects in strong-coupling cavity quantum electrodynamics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373812","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Taube, Karl","Helmke, Christophe","Escobedo, Héctor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413053"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blowgunners and the great bird at teotihuacan mesoamerican myths in a comparative perspective","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctv1z52356?refreqid=excelsior%3Ad1f162ac0261c891b0176c05829e9789","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-413053","ids":["ku-20e20d03-bc12-4136-a9c5-d4f77e0780f2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-60702887B60A3B4F9C0343AB23EF8661"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karl","key":"taubepau","last":"Taube","name":"Taube, Karl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Héctor","key":"escobedopau","last":"Escobedo","name":"Escobedo, Héctor","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Holley","key":"moyespedh","last":"Moyes","name":"Moyes, Holley","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Allen","key":"christensonpedh","last":"Christenson","name":"Christenson, Allen","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Frauke","key":"sachsepedh","last":"Sachse","name":"Sachse, Frauke","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781646421985"],"pages":"295-314","place":"Louisville","publisher":"University Press of Colorado","status":"p","title":"The Myths of the Popol Vuh in Cosmology, Art and Ritual"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-20e20d03-bc12-4136-a9c5-d4f77e0780f2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blowgunners and the Great Bird at Teotihuacan : Mesoamerican Myths in a Comparative Perspective","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-413053","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To describe burden and health-related quality of life amongst caregivers of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest survivors and explore the potential association with cognitive function of the survivors. Caregivers of patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction were used as controls. Methods: Data were collected from the cognitive substudy of the Targeted Temperature Management-trial. Caregiver burden was assessed with the 22-item Zarit Burden Interview, with scores ≤20 considered as no burden. Health-related quality of life was assessed with the SF-36v2®, with T-scores 47–53 representing the norm. Cardiac arrest survivors were categorized based on the results from cognitive assessments as having “no cognitive impairment” or “cognitive impairment”. Results: Follow-up 6 months post event was performed for caregivers of 272 cardiac arrest survivors and 108 matched myocardial infarction controls, included at an intended ratio of 2:1. In general, caregivers of cardiac arrest survivors and controls reported similar caregiver burden. The overall scores for quality of life were within normative levels and similar for caregivers of cardiac arrest survivors and control patients. Compared to those with no cognitive impairment, caregivers of cognitively impaired cardiac arrest survivors (n = 126) reported higher levels of burden (median 18 versus 8, p < 0.001) and worse quality of life in five of eight domains, particularly “Role-Emotional” (mean 45.7 versus 49.5, p = 0.002). Conclusions: In general, caregivers of cardiac arrest survivors and myocardial infarction controls reported similar levels of burden and quality of life. Cognitive outcome and functional dependency of the cardiac arrest survivor impact burden and quality of life of the caregiver.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bohm, Mattias","Cronberg, Tobias","Årestedt, Kristofer","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Ullén, Susann","Undén, Johan","Wise, Matt P.","Lilja, Gisela"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-448735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Linnaeus University","Lund University","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","Skåne University Hospital","University Hospital of Wales"],"keyword":["Caregiver burden","Cross Sectional Studies","Health related quality of life","Out of hospital cardiac arrest"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caregiver burden and health related quality of life amongst caregivers of out of hospital cardiac arrest survivors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2021.08.025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-448735","identifier":[{"id":"34437997","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114162556","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5c5b5da6-fd78-42c4-9c00-1371e03efe4c"],"keyword":["Caregiver burden","Cross-sectional studies","Health-related quality of life","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CAF2CA7749627728E8135C1B9C606F08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2021.08.025","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/281705884/1_s2.0_S0300957221003257_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"linnaeus university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linnaeus University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"medical centre leeuwarden","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical Centre Leeuwarden","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university hospital of wales","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital of Wales","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mattias","key":"bohmpau","last":"Bohm","name":"Bohm, Mattias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristofer","key":"årestedtpau","last":"Årestedt","name":"Årestedt, Kristofer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"d2d434a4-22