{"abstract":"This paper presents design and layout considerations for a high efficient GaN converter on two-layer cost-effective PCB. The fast switching capabilities of GaN FETs requires very low power loop inductance. The proposed method of embedding the input capacitors to minimize loop inductance is analyzed and tested on a non-isolated buck converter using GaN switches. Ultra low power loop inductance (418 pH) was achieved by placing the bypass capacitors vertically through the board. The proposed converter has reached a maximum measured conversion efficiency of 98.6 percentage in both buck and boost mode.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Ramachandran, Rakesh","Nymand, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580043"],"event":{"acronym":"EPE/ECCE","end":"2021-09-10","place":"Ghent, be","start":"2021-09-06","title":"23rd European Conference on Power Electronics and Applications, EPE 2021 ECCE Europe","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper"],"keyword":["DC DC converter","Efficiency","Gallium Nitride GaN","Optimization","Parasitic inductance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"demonstration of ultra low loop inductance on a high efficient gan converter using pcb embedded capacitors","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85119051459","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580043","identifier":[{"id":"85119051459","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-17db999f-9f12-477c-87de-b19849cb1766"],"keyword":["Efficiency","Finiteelement analysis","Gallium Nitride (GaN)","Optimization","Parasitic inductance","dc-dc Converter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39EED57ABB4016E31C01269E0DE7E641"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, SDU Microelectronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a2c86e37-f396-4b5e-9e63-19af9641cc04","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1469-7684","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rakesh","key":"ramachandranpau","last":"Ramachandran","locid":"09aad359-07e8-434e-9dc6-a305e06d055b","name":"Ramachandran, Rakesh","orcid":"0000-0003-0487-7857","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"nymandpau","last":"Nymand","locid":"3f0c9441-e312-42bb-bb24-490c2ab76c9d","name":"Nymand, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-1470-5621","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789075815375"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2021 23rd European Conference on Power Electronics and Applications, EPE 2021 ECCE Europe"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119051459"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-17db999f-9f12-477c-87de-b19849cb1766"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Demonstration of Ultra Low Loop Inductance on a High Efficient GaN Converter Using PCB Embedded Capacitors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580043","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Adipose tissues display a remarkable ability to adapt to the dietary status. Here, we have applied single-nucleus RNA-seq to map the plasticity of mouse epididymal white adipose tissue at single-nucleus resolution in response to high-fat-diet-induced obesity. The single-nucleus approach allowed us to recover all major cell types and to reveal distinct transcriptional stages along the entire adipogenic trajectory from preadipocyte commitment to mature adipocytes. We demonstrate the existence of different adipocyte subpopulations and show that obesity leads to disappearance of the lipogenic subpopulation and increased abundance of the stressed lipid-scavenging subpopulation. Moreover, obesity is associated with major changes in the abundance and gene expression of other cell populations, including a dramatic increase in lipid-handling genes in macrophages at the expense of macrophage-specific genes. The data provide a powerful resource for future hypothesis-driven investigations of the mechanisms of adipocyte differentiation and adipose tissue plasticity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Sárvári, Anitta Kinga","Van Hauwaert, Elvira Laila","Markussen, Lasse Kruse","Gammelmark, Ellen","Marcher, Ann-Britt","Ebbesen, Morten Frendø","Nielsen, Ronni","Brewer, Jonathan R.","Madsen, Jesper Grud Skat","Mandrup, Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605453"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Jesper Grud Skat","Mandrup, Susanne"],"keyword":["Adipocyte differentiation","adipose tissue plasticity","fibro adipogenic progenitors","snRNA seq"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasticity of epididymal adipose tissue in response to diet induced obesity at single nucleus resolution","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85099682151","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-605453","identifier":[{"id":"33378646","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85099682151","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-70c1b945-6eff-47e0-a4d0-6a8ac646681b"],"keyword":["adipocyte differentiation","adipocyte subpopulations","adipose tissue plasticity","fibro-adipogenic progenitors","in vivo adipogenesis","lipid-associated macrophages","snRNA-seq"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-43C1E25B9847FD61FC62F98B6BC32FAF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, ATLAS - Center for Functional Genomics and Tissue Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anitta Kinga","key":"sárváripau","last":"Sárvári","locid":"067c0118-3b2f-4943-991d-54a19815bd23","name":"Sárvári, Anitta Kinga","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elvira Laila","key":"vanhauwaertpau","last":"Van Hauwaert","locid":"ca4ec6e6-c3d5-4158-b0b9-bd7a125cf8de","name":"Van Hauwaert, Elvira Laila","orcid":"0000-0002-6248-0025","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Kruse","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","locid":"fcf00872-7de3-4a0a-a178-e253cb975d0e","name":"Markussen, Lasse Kruse","orcid":"0000-0002-8655-3719","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen","key":"gammelmarkpau","last":"Gammelmark","locid":"ff07fdc8-20b8-401a-85b5-2dc69788d6ee","name":"Gammelmark, Ellen","orcid":"0000-0003-1486-5219","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Britt","key":"marcherpau","last":"Marcher","locid":"11d5c9d9-4b44-4171-bd3b-7b1312bef200","name":"Marcher, Ann-Britt","orcid":"0000-0002-4799-8870","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Frendø","key":"ebbesenpau","last":"Ebbesen","locid":"07660920-3df1-47cb-a21e-29b6ca47c917","name":"Ebbesen, Morten Frendø","orcid":"0000-0001-5416-7429","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ronni","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fd12718-04a0-4664-882c-8213d3b5291b","name":"Nielsen, Ronni","orcid":"0000-0001-6331-7660","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonathan Richard","key":"brewerpau","last":"Brewer","locid":"11e75201-0423-4774-a4e1-81bdb75933bc","name":"Brewer, Jonathan R.","name_org":"Brewer, Jonathan Richard","orcid":"0000-0002-3444-1715","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Grud Skat","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"f3263ff0-108b-4afd-a88b-27fd259db777","name":"Madsen, Jesper Grud Skat","orcid":"0000-0002-0518-0800","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne","key":"mandruppau","last":"Mandrup","locid":"6e8c29d6-da8a-4ef0-ab1a-03efe2e3d9e5","name":"Mandrup, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-0961-5787","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33378646"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cmet.2020.12.004","issn":["15504131","19327420"],"issn_org":["15504131"],"issue":"2","journal":"Cell Metabolism","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Cell Metabolism","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099682151"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-70c1b945-6eff-47e0-a4d0-6a8ac646681b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Plasticity of Epididymal Adipose Tissue in Response to Diet-Induced Obesity at Single-Nucleus Resolution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605453","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Although prevention of incidents leading to evacuations at sea is of vital importance, little is known about its causal patterns and demographic determinants. We investigated therefore relationships between age, occupation and nationality and causes of evacuations. The data were obtained from the Telemedical Assistance Service (TMAS) in Denmark between 2004 and 2014 supplemented with data on all seafarers from the Danish Maritime Authority (N = 73,344). These data included information on broad age groups, occupational position and nationality. The outcomes were evacuations from any cause and in four broad categories of causes leading to evacuations. A total of 403 evacuations were reported in the 11-year study period. 27% of the evacuations were due to external causes, 19% due to diseases of the circulatory system, 14% due diseases of the digestive system and 40% from other or undetermined causes. Age-adjusted all-cause evacuation rates varied between 1.4 and 3.4 incidents per 1000 person-years in 2004–2014 for officers and between 3.3 and 20.2 incidents for non-officers. An elevated risk of evacuations was found among both officers and non-officers aged ≥50 years, compared with those aged 30–49 years with odds ratios of 2.73 (95% confidence intervals 1.66, 4.50) and 2.59 (2.03, 3.31), respectively. The odds ratios for non-officers from non-Danish European Union and from non-European Union countries compared with Danish non-officers were 1.51 (1.12, 2.04) and 0.55 (0.42, 0.71), respectively. In conclusion, working as non-officer, older age and non-Danish EU nationality were associated with a higher risk of evacuations irrespective of the cause leading to evacuation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Herttua, Kimmo","Vork, Jan","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605598"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Herttua, Kimmo"],"keyword":["Demographic determinants"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations of age occupation and nationality of seafarers with risk of evacuations at sea a register based study on danish flagged merchant ships","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175235690/ms_evacuations_R2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-605598","identifier":[{"id":"85084056936","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-713d1d0e-3be1-49c8-8dd5-a2fbdd7d0815"],"keyword":["Demographic determinants","Evacuations","Tele-medical assistance service"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C5A5049247FC61F15C2D69AEBAF4D950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175235690/ms_evacuations_R2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit for Maritime Health and Technology (MHT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kimmo","key":"herttuapau","last":"Herttua","locid":"52a35c53-4c7a-48e8-85c4-fce9540bb153","name":"Herttua, Kimmo","orcid":"0000-0003-2004-779X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"vorkpau","last":"Vork","locid":"cc62e730-1e61-49dc-b3ce-2b5e9ea3987a","name":"Vork, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marpol.2020.103989","issn":["0308597X","18729460"],"issn_org":["0308597X"],"journal":"Marine Policy","paperid":"103989","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Marine Policy","volume":"130"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084056936"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-713d1d0e-3be1-49c8-8dd5-a2fbdd7d0815"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations of age, occupation and nationality of seafarers with risk of evacuations at sea : A register-based study on Danish-flagged merchant ships","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605598","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: COVID-19 is associated with a risk of severe pneumonia and acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), requiring treatment at an intensive care unit (ICU). Since clinical deterioration may occur rapidly, a simple, fast, bedside, non-invasive method for assessment of lung changes is warranted. The primary aim of this study was to investigate whether lung ultrasonography findings within 72 hours of admission were predictive of clinical deterioration in hospitalized patients with confirmed Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2).Methods: Patients admitted to a dedicated COVID-19 unit were subject to daily lung ultrasonography examinations. Number of present consolidations and pleural effusions were registered and a Mongodi score was calculated. These findings were correlated with initial chest x-ray and clinical deterioration, defined as ICU-admission, ARDS diagnosis, death.Results: In total, 29 of 83 patients had lung ultrasonography performed during admission, 18 within 72 hours of admission. Of these, four patients died during admission, six were transferred to the ICU and 13 were diagnosed with ARDS. Initial Mongodi-score did not differ significantly between patients with and without clinical deterioration (p=0.95). Agreement between initial LUS and chest x-ray findings were fair with Cohen’s Kappa at 0.21.Conclusion: LUS performed within 72 hours in patients admitted to a dedicated COVID-19 unit could not predict ARDS, ICU admission or death. However, consecutive investigations may be of value, as sudden substantial changes may herald disease progression, enabling earlier supplementary diagnostics and treatment initiation.FootnotesCite this article as: European Respiratory Journal 2021; 58: Suppl. 65, PA3682.This abstract was presented at the 2021 ERS International Congress, in session textquotedblleftPrediction of exacerbations in patients with COPDtextquotedblright.This is an ERS International Congress abstract. No full-text version is available. Further material to accompany this abstract may be available at www.ers-education.org (ERS member access only).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Falster, Casper","Jacobsen, Niels","Madsen, Lone Wulff","Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","Knudtzen, Fredrikke Christie","Nielsen, Stig Lønberg","Johansen, Isik Somuncu","Laursen, Christian B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613893"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-08","start":"2021-09-05","title":"ERS International Congress 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lung ultrasound may be a valuable aid in decision making for patients admitted with covid 000000000019 disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://erj.ersjournals.com/content/58/suppl_65/PA3682","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-613893","ids":["sdu-8df822ad-ec1a-4221-a4a2-7063884b0f63"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6B9A00CAF3168976D8FCFFC64D266A2C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Odense Respiratory Research Unit (ODIN)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"falsterpau","last":"Falster","locid":"9a1037d1-3f52-4104-8591-444959dd5a1a","name":"Falster, Casper","orcid":"0000-0002-0389-5386","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"8bbc2496-9df4-4000-8737-0a2ec7b794f2","name":"Jacobsen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6189-2290","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Wulff","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"026c10be-bdc3-4a65-b5e9-96d10650d8dc","name":"Madsen, Lone Wulff","orcid":"0000-0002-7864-1268","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Dahlerup","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a0349aeb-56d9-4984-86b0-4829aee2a04b","name":"Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","orcid":"0000-0003-0853-0893","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rømhild","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"bfd91489-501f-49d3-aa3b-d9e8ea9a77f0","name":"Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-4014","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrikke Christie","key":"knudtzenpau","last":"Knudtzen","locid":"7d403c4d-7658-46ab-9ea1-94da06513969","name":"Knudtzen, Fredrikke Christie","orcid":"0000-0001-8348-7819","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Lønberg","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"acf3ca2e-c3e9-46f6-a531-51cfc6ff0112","name":"Nielsen, Stig Lønberg","orcid":"0000-0002-7780-7131","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isic Somuncu","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"d7a439ff-f0ad-43c9-80d8-a269647e1886","name":"Johansen, Isik Somuncu","name_org":"Johansen, Isic Somuncu","orcid":"0000-0002-2189-9823","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Borbjerg","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"333fc524-a408-42f4-885a-0fee79e488b9","name":"Laursen, Christian B","name_org":"Laursen, Christian Borbjerg","orcid":"0000-0001-6382-9906","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/13993003.congress-2021.pa3682","issn":["09031936","13993003"],"issn_org":["09031936"],"issue":"suppl 65","journal":"European Respiratory Journal","paperid":"PA3682","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"European Respiratory Journal","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8df822ad-ec1a-4221-a4a2-7063884b0f63"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Lung ultrasound may be a valuable aid in decision making for patients admitted with COVID-19 disease","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613893","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVE: There is limited evidence on the clinical effects of statins in older persons. We aimed to explore statin use and discontinuation patterns in Danes age 70 and older. DESIGN: Register-based drug utilisation study. SETTING: Danish nationwide health registries. SUBJECTS: All Danish persons aged ≥70 years between 2011 and 2016. MEASUREMENTS: (1) Monthly prevalence and (2) quarterly incidence of statin use, (3) characteristics of new users, (4) total amount of statin redeemed, (5) statin discontinuation rate between 2014 and 2016 in long-term statin users and (6) factors associated with discontinuation. RESULTS: We identified 395,279 unique older statin users between 2011 and 2016. The prevalence increased from 30% in 2011 to 33% in 2016 (23% for primary prevention and 56% for secondary prevention in 2016). The quarterly incidence fell from 11 per 1,000 persons in 2011 to 7 per 1,000 persons in 2016. The prevalence was generally stable in those 70 to 79 years. In those aged ≥80 years, the prevalence increased despite decreasing incidence. The proportion of persons initiating for primary prevention decreased from 58% in 2011 to 52% in 2016. Approximately 19% of long-term statin users discontinued therapy between 2014 and 2016. Increasing age was the strongest predictor of statin discontinuation. CONCLUSIONS: Approximately one in three Danes age ≥ 70 years were taking statins in 2016. The characteristics of incident users shifted between 2011 and 2016, with less people age 80 and older starting on statins and fewer people starting for primary prevention.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thompson, Wade","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Haastrup, Peter","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-629644"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thompson, Wade"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statin use and discontinuation in danes age 000000000070 and older a nationwide drug utilisation study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178945421/Statins_DUS_revised_CLEAN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-629644","identifier":[{"id":"85102657832","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32936863","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-c4fb99a6-4d79-46fd-ada2-da19ec92f01a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFE739EC5D34DA5DF28DBCEA053E010E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178945421/Statins_DUS_revised_CLEAN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wade","key":"thompsonpau","last":"Thompson","locid":"3d654d06-5597-4de2-9f88-e0913ad14d60","name":"Thompson, Wade","orcid":"0000-0002-8268-4092","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"03dbf65e-75df-4540-b951-0d05e7a60cde","name":"Haastrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7265-743X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32936863"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ageing/afaa160","issn":["00020729","14682834"],"issn_org":["14682834"],"issue":"2","journal":"Age and Ageing","pages":"554-558","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Age and Ageing","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102657832"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c4fb99a6-4d79-46fd-ada2-da19ec92f01a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Statin use and discontinuation in Danes age 70 and older : a nationwide drug utilisation study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-629644","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
