{"abstract":"Background: An increasing number of countries legalise the use of medical cannabis or allow it for a narrow range of medical conditions. Physicians, and often the patients’ general practitioner, play a major role in implementing this policy. Many of them, however, perceive a lack of evidence-based knowledge and are not confident with providing patients with medical cannabis. The objectives of this review are to synthesise findings about hospital physicians’ and GPs’ experiences, attitudes, and beliefs towards the use of medical cannabis with the purpose of identifying barriers and facilitators towards providing it to their patients. Methods: Peer-reviewed articles addressing hospital physicians’ and GPs’ experiences, attitudes, and beliefs towards the use of medical cannabis were searched systematically in PubMed, Scopus, EMBASE, and the Cochrane Library. Results: Twenty-one articles were included from five different countries in which the medical cannabis laws varied. The studied physicians experienced frequent inquiries about medical cannabis from their patients (49–95%), and between 10 and 95% of the physicians were willing to prescribe and/or provide it to the patients, depending on setting, specialty and experience among the physicians. This review found that physicians experienced in prescribing medical cannabis were more convinced of its benefits and less worried about adverse effects than non-experienced physicians. However, physicians specialized in addiction treatment and certain relevant indication areas seemed more sceptical compared to physicians in general. Nevertheless, physicians generally experienced a lack of knowledge of clinical effects including both beneficial and adverse effects. Conclusion: This review indicates that GPs and hospital physicians from various specialties frequently experience patient demands for medical cannabis and to some degree show openness to using it, although there was a wide gap between studies in terms of willingness to provide. Hospital physicians and GPs’ experienced in prescribing are more convinced of effects and less worried of adverse effects. However, most physicians experience a lack of knowledge of beneficial effects, adverse effects and of how to advise patients, which may comprise barriers towards prescribing. More research, including larger studies with cohort designs and qualitative studies, is needed to further examine facilitators and barriers to physicians’ prescribing practices.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ronne, Sabrina Trappaud","Rosenbaek, Frederik","Pedersen, Line Bjørnskov","Waldorff, Frans Boch","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Riisgaard, Helle","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-087.18-041505"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rosenbæk, Frederik"],"keyword":["Attitudes","Barriers","Experiences","Facilitators","Medical cannabis","Physicians"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physicians experiences attitudes and beliefs towards medical cannabis a systematic literature review","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-021-01559-w","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by The Region of Southern Denmark. The funding source was not involved in the choice of study design; analysis and interpretation of the results of the study; in the writing of the article; and in the decision to submit the article for publication."],"id":"S02-087.18-041505","identifier":[{"id":"34674661","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8532330","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000710274300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85117700381","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-37a97977-668e-4a60-9747-823d4d428a21","sdu-97e4a4c3-7926-4aaf-ac03-15035d201796"],"keyword":["Attitudes","Barriers","Experiences","Facilitators","Medical cannabis","Physicians"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9B6F7A739D5DDC53F8015A8B8C961CE3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-021-01559-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/283407003/Physicians_experiences_attitudes_and_beliefs_towards_medical_cannabis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/194159967/Rnne_2021_Physicians_experiences_attitudes_an.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, External Centres, Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabrina Trappaud","key":"rønnepau","last":"Rønne","locid":"f0ef3941-f355-4a82-92fd-e6a7812bbc9a","name":"Rønne, Sabrina Trappaud","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"rosenbækpau","last":"Rosenbæk","locid":"ddb48549-0a16-43ea-ace9-298bbf7a8c49","name":"Rosenbæk, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0003-0214-1539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Bjørnskov","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b2346680-b60a-41e8-9332-304171fab9be","name":"Pedersen, Line Bjørnskov","orcid":"0000-0001-6804-2045","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Frans Boch","key":"waldorffpau","last":"Waldorff","locid":"895410ef-1771-4e1d-a0a7-94ccef842d76","name":"Waldorff, Frans Boch","orcid":"0000-0002-7859-633X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"riisgaardpau","last":"Riisgaard","locid":"7bb4b4dd-cbd6-4c4c-b99e-aa3c6eee7d11","name":"Riisgaard, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-1985-6808","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34674661"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12875-021-01559-w","issn":["14712296"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Family Practice","paperid":"212","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Family Practice","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117700381"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-37a97977-668e-4a60-9747-823d4d428a21","sdu-97e4a4c3-7926-4aaf-ac03-15035d201796"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Physicians' experiences, attitudes, and beliefs towards medical cannabis : a systematic literature review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.18-041505","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Type 1 diabetes is an immune-driven disease, where the insulin-producing beta cells from the pancreatic islets of Langerhans becomes target of immune-mediated destruction. Several studies have highlighted the implication of circulating and exosomal microRNAs (miRNAs) in type 1 diabetes, underlining its biomarker value and novel therapeutic potential. Recently, we discovered that exosome-enriched extracellular vesicles carry altered levels of both known and novel miRNAs in breast milk from lactating mothers with type 1 diabetes. In this study, we aimed to characterize exosomal miRNAs in the circulation of lactating mothers with and without type 1 diabetes, hypothesizing that differences in type 1 diabetes risk in offspring from these groups are reflected in the circulating miRNA profile. We performed small RNA sequencing on exosome-enriched extracellular vesicles extracted from plasma of 52 lactating mothers around 5 weeks postpartum (26 with type 1 diabetes and 26 age-matched controls), and found a total of 2,289 miRNAs in vesicles from type 1 diabetes and control libraries. Of these, 176 were differentially expressed in plasma from mothers with type 1 diabetes (167 upregulated; 9 downregulated, using a cut-off of abs(log2FC) >1 and FDR adjusted p-value <0.05). Extracellular vesicles were verified by nanoparticle tracking analysis, transmission electron microscopy and immunoblotting. Five candidate miRNAs were selected based on their involvement in diabetes and immune modulation/beta-cell functions: hsa-miR-127-3p, hsa-miR-146a-5p, hsa-miR-26a-5p, hsa-miR-24-3p and hsa-miR-30d-5p. Real-time qPCR validation confirmed that hsa-miR-146a-5p, hsa-miR-26a-5p, hsa-miR-24-3p, and hsa-miR-30d-5p were significantly upregulated in lactating mothers with type 1 diabetes as compared to lactating healthy mothers. To determine possible target genes and affected pathways of the 5 miRNA candidates, computational network-based analyses were carried out with TargetScan, mirTarBase, QIAGEN Ingenuity Pathway Analysis and PantherDB database. The candidates showed significant association with inflammatory response and cytokine and chemokine mediated signaling pathways. With this study, we detect aberrant levels of miRNAs within plasma extracellular vesicles from lactating mothers with type 1 diabetes during the postpartum period, including miRNAs with associations to disease pathogenesis and inflammatory responses.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Frørup, Caroline","Mirza, Aashiq H.","Yarani, Reza","Nielsen, Lotte B.","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Damm, Peter","Svare, Jens","Engelbrekt, Christian","Størling, Joachim","Johannesen, Jesper","Mortensen, Henrik B.","Pociot, Flemming","Kaur, Simranjeet"],"cuid":["S02-095.84-036649"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kaur, Simranjeet"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"keyword":["Exosomes","Extracellular vesicles","Plasma","Small RNA Seq","Type 1 diabetes","miRNAs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma exosome enriched extracellular vesicles from lactating mothers with type 000000000001 diabetes contain aberrant levels of mirnas during the postpartum period","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2021.744509","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.84-036649","identifier":[{"id":"34691048","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85117596531","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8531745","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-b31f8934-3229-476b-8940-ae10cb8dfb26","ku-3b8ccdd7-2720-49f9-92af-caa09d3111be"],"keyword":["Exosomes","Extracellular vesicles","Plasma","Small RNA-Seq","Type 1 diabetes","miRNAs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-10231EC5FCE8D7B613EF71D0E2713C8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2021.744509","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/259141760/fimmu_12_744509.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284101472/fimmu_12_744509.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev a