{"abstract":"Most parametric fundamental frequency estimators make the implicit assumption that any corrupting noise is additive, white Gaussian. Under this assumption, the maximum likelihood (ML) and the least squares estimators are the same, and statistically efficient. However, in the coloured noise case, the estimators differ, and the spectral shape of the corrupting noise should be taken into account. To allow for this, we here propose two schemes that refine the noise statistics and parameter estimates in an iterative manner, one of them based on an approximate ML solution and the other one based on removing the periodic signal obtained from a linearly constrained minimum variance (LCMV) filter. Evaluations on real speech data indicate that the iteration steps improve the estimation accuracy, therefore offering improvement over traditional non-parametric fundamental frequency methods.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Esquivel Jaramillo, Alfredo","Jakobsson, Andreas","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059759"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2020-05-08","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2020-05-04","title":"2020 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing, ICASSP 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Fundamental frequency","Least squares","Maximum likelihood","Pre whitening"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust fundamental frequency estimation in coloured noise","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321346849/icassp2020AAJM_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059759","identifier":[{"id":"85089237075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-215f394a-b412-4f7e-a50c-fa348153777e"],"keyword":["LCMV filter","coloured noise","fundamental frequency","least-squares","maximum likelihood","pre-whitening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-079C057D01E9307006DC75DEE99B066A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321346849/icassp2020AAJM_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"esquiveljaramillopau","last":"Esquivel Jaramillo","locid":"a9286a43-363b-461d-adcf-9cd2b30e97ea","name":"Esquivel Jaramillo, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-8994-9479","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"jakobssonpau","last":"Jakobsson","name":"Jakobsson, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp40776.2020.9053018","eisbn":["9781509066315"],"isbn":["9781509066322"],"issn":["15206149"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2020 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing, ICASSP 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089237075"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-215f394a-b412-4f7e-a50c-fa348153777e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Robust Fundamental Frequency Estimation in Coloured Noise","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059759","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Sound zone control enables different users to enjoy different audio contents in the same acoustic environment. Generalized eigenvalue decomposition (GEVD)-based methods allow us to control the tradeoff between the acoustic contrast (AC) and signal distortion (SD). However, such methods have a high computational complexity. In this paper, we propose a fast reduced-rank sound zone control algorithm using the conjugate gradient (CG) method. Instead of using the eigenvectors as the basis for the solution space, the search directions in the CG method are used to reduce the computational complexity. Then, a low dimensional EVD is applied to obtain the sub-optimal control filter coefficients. The dark zone power can be adjusted by a parameter, which implicitly controls the trade-off between the AC and SD. Compared with GEVD-based methods, experimental results show that the proposed algorithm has a degradation of performance (4–5 dB) in terms of AC or SD but a high improvement on computational efficiency. Index Terms— Computational complexity, conjugate gradient, reduced-rank, sound zone control, variable span trade-off filter","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shi, Liming","Lee, Taewoong","Zhang, Lijun","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059926"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2020-05-08","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2020-05-04","title":"ICASSP 2020 - 2020 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Conjugate gradient","Reduced rank","Sound zone control","Variable Span Trade Off Filter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fast reduced rank sound zone control algorithm using the conjugate gradient method","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320787750/RR_CG_6.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059926","identifier":[{"id":"85091132381","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-21fdc4be-8c8e-4421-a5d3-8f2ff851803f"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Conjugate gradient","Reduced-rank","Sound zone control","Variable span trade-off filter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-250A6D1F594ADB54DD34AEFCE36602CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320787750/RR_CG_6.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liming","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","locid":"e44b1378-1291-46be-b76a-fd0e196e2d46","name":"Shi, Liming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Taewoong","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","locid":"d1eeade6-8e75-427d-9c1f-1a4ac5464576","name":"Lee, Taewoong","orcid":"0000-0002-6669-0820","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Lijun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp40776.2020.9054461","eisbn":["9781509066315"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"436-440","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091132381"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-21fdc4be-8c8e-4421-a5d3-8f2ff851803f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A fast reduced-rank sound zone control algorithm using the conjugate gradient method","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059926","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Reverse firewalls were introduced at Eurocrypt 2015 by Miro-nov and Stephens-Davidowitz, as a method for protecting cryptographic protocols against attacks on the devices of the honest parties. In a nutshell: a reverse firewall is placed outside of a device and its goal is to “sanitize” the messages sent by it, in such a way that a malicious device cannot leak its secrets to the outside world. It is typically assumed that the cryptographic devices are attacked in a “functionality-preserving way” (i.e. informally speaking, the functionality of the protocol remains unchanged under this attacks). In their paper, Mironov and Stephens-Davidowitz construct a protocol for passively-secure two-party computations with firewalls, leaving extension of this result to stronger models as an open question. In this paper, we address this problem by constructing a protocol for secure computation with firewalls that has two main advantages over the original protocol from Eurocrypt 2015. Firstly, it is a multiparty computation protocol (i.e. it works for an arbitrary number n of the parties, and not just for 2). Secondly, it is secure in much stronger corruption settings, namely in the active corruption model. More precisely: we consider an adversary that can fully corrupt up to n-1 parties, while the remaining parties are corrupt in a functionality-preserving way. Our core techniques are: malleable commitments and malleable non-interactive zero-knowledge, which in particular allow us to create a novel protocol for multiparty augmented coin-tossing into the well with reverse firewalls (that is based on a protocol of Lindell from Crypto 2001).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Chakraborty, Suvradip","Dziembowski, Stefan","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130365"],"event":{"acronym":"CRYPTO","end":"2020-08-21","place":"Santa Barbara, us","start":"2020-08-17","title":"40th Annual International Cryptology Conference, CRYPTO 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chakraborty, Suvradip"],"country":["Austria","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Science and Technology Austria","University of Warsaw"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reverse firewalls for actively secure mpcs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089715435","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130365","identifier":[{"id":"85089715435","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-01f3c15f-3a30-497e-b445-e885108d36dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01B773208453EFE193543661BD94D302"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"institute of science and technology austria","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Science and Technology Austria","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pl","key":"university of warsaw","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warsaw","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Suvradip","key":"chakrabortypau","last":"Chakraborty","name":"Chakraborty, Suvradip","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"dziembowskipau","last":"Dziembowski","name":"Dziembowski, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniele","key":"miccianciopedh","last":"Micciancio","name":"Micciancio, Daniele","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"ristenpartpedh","last":"Ristenpart","name":"Ristenpart, Thomas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-56880-1_26","eisbn":["9783030568801"],"isbn":["9783030568795"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"732-762","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advances in Cryptology - CRYPTO 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089715435"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-01f3c15f-3a30-497e-b445-e885108d36dd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reverse firewalls for actively secure mpcs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-130365","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
