:"Rasmussen, Torben Valdbjørn","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels-Jørgen","key":"aagaardnielsjørgenpau","last":"Aagaard","locid":"8849ede5-0d46-45c4-b8fe-2e4f06f65e3e","name":"Aagaard, Niels-Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-3230-5533","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit","key":"rasmussenbirgitpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Birgit","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"johnsenkjeldpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Kjeld","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Christian","key":"bergsøenielschristianpau","last":"Bergsøe","name":"Bergsøe, Niels Christian","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"2","eisbn":["9788756319355"],"isbn":["9788756319348"],"issn":["01066757"],"issue":"272","publisher":"Statens Byggeforskningsinstitut","series":"SBi-anvisning","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2b4bbada-1ea1-4f8a-ac67-b20be8bde499"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Anvisning om Bygningsreglement 2018","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-317458","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Lytic polysaccharide monooxygenases (LPMOs) are often studied in simple models involving activity measurements of a single LPMO or a blend thereof with hydrolytic enzymes towards an insoluble substrate. However, the contribution of LPMOs to polysaccharide breakdown in complex cocktails of hydrolytic and oxidative enzymes, similar to fungal secretomes, remains elusive. Typically, two starch-specific AA13 LPMOs are encoded by mainly Ascomycota genomes. Here, we investigate the impact of LPMO loss on the growth and degradation of starches of varying resistance to amylolytic hydrolases by Aspergillus nidulans. Deletion of the genes encoding AnAA13A that possesses a CBM20 starch-binding module, AnAA13B (lacking a CBM20) or both AA13 genes resulted in reduced growth on solid media with resistant, but not soluble processed potato starch. Larger size and amount of residual starch granules were observed for the AA13-deficient strains as compared to the reference and the impairment of starch degradation was more severe for the strain lacking AnAA13A based on a microscopic analysis. After 5 days of growth on raw potato starch in liquid media, the mount of residual starch was about fivefold higher for the AA13 gene deletion strains compared to the reference, which underscores the importance of LPMOs for degradation of especially resistant starches. Proteomic analyses revealed substantial changes in the secretomes of the double AA13 gene deletion, followed by the AnAA13A-deficient strain, whereas only a single protein was significantly different in the proteome of the AnAA13B-deficient strain as compared to the reference. This study shows that the loss of AA13, especially the starch-binding AnAA13A, impairs degradation of resistant potato starch, but has limited impact on less-resistant wheat starch and no impact on processed solubilized starch. The effects of LPMO loss are more pronounced at the later stages of fungal growth, likely due to the accumulation of the less-accessible regions of the substrate. The striking impairment in granular starch degradation due to the loss of a single LPMO from the secretome offers insight into the crucial role played by AA13 in the breakdown of resistant starch and presents a methodological framework to analyse the contribution of distinct LPMOs towards semi-crystalline polysaccharides under in vivo conditions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Haddad Momeni, Majid","Leth, Maria Louise","Sternberg, Claus","Schoof, Erwin M.","Nielsen, Maike Wennekers","Holck, Jesper","Workman, Christopher","Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg","Abou Hachem, Maher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343800"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Abou Hachem, Maher"],"keyword":["Ascomycota","Biomass","Biorefinery","Carbohydrate oxidation","Functional genomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"loss of aa000000000013 lpmos impairs degradation of resistant starch and reduces the growth of i aspergillus nidulans i","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13068-020-01775-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343800","identifier":[{"id":"85089378572","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32774456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7405360","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-8353fee5-d077-4266-9599-c9401cec990d"],"keyword":["Ascomycota","Aspergilius nidulans","Biomass","Biorefinery","Carbohydrate oxidation","Functional genomics","Recalcitrant polysaccharides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4EE9AAB45A38A0D4880ABC87FFA98192"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13068-020-01775-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/217961209/s13068_020_01775_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, Protein Glycoscience and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Majid","key":"haddadmomenipau","last":"Haddad Momeni","locid":"a153cbb6-ac92-48f1-9190-509c8d2bd791","name":"Haddad Momeni, Majid","orcid":"0000-0001-9653-1380","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Louise","key":"lethpau","last":"Leth","locid":"5c4c23c9-6b7f-43d5-9172-3df4c1acc0f2","name":"Leth, Maria Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-5668-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"sternbergpau","last":"Sternberg","locid":"1a361d9b-bd73-4de8-80d9-df1a209d5898","name":"Sternberg, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-2572-0288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erwin","key":"schoofpau","last":"Schoof","locid":"0fb8f624-dabf-435e-89e3-9afe6cf0c231","name":"Schoof, Erwin M.","name_org":"Schoof, Erwin","orcid":"0000-0002-3117-7832","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maike Wennekers","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"40a5b18b-782d-4378-a2a8-24aa70149a6d","name":"Nielsen, Maike Wennekers","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","locid":"d444e5ac-34d3-487b-9327-7ae08138d861","name":"Holck, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8072-1101","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher T.","key":"workmanpau","last":"Workman","locid":"e77ea2ce-8446-4d11-aa31-c985ef7be24f","name":"Workman, Christopher","name_org":"Workman, Christopher T.","orcid":"0000-0002-2210-3743","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Blæsbjerg","key":"hoofpau","last":"Hoof","locid":"339ce5a8-3232-410d-9484-abbc0f5b81b3","name":"Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-7650-9300","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maher","key":"abouhachempau","last":"Abou Hachem","locid":"a81cbffb-ca6f-44ca-8a7d-4211cea18ca1","name":"Abou Hachem, Maher","orcid":"0000-0001-8250-1842","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32774456"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13068-020-01775-z","issn":["17546834"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biotechnology for Biofuels","paperid":"135","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Biotechnology for Biofuels","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089378572"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8353fee5-d077-4266-9599-c9401cec990d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Loss of AA13 LPMOs impairs degradation of resistant starch and reduces the growth of <i>Aspergillus nidulans</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343800","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We present a code for the large-scale data analysis of electron cyclotron emission (ECE) measurements from magnetized plasmas called ECRad – the Electron Cyclotron Radiation transport model for Advanced Data analysis. Its key features are low computational cost, high robustness and the capability to predict ECE spectra of plasmas with non-thermal electron populations. This is accomplished by combining the absorption coefficient given by Albajar et al. (2007) and a corresponding emissivity for the radiation transport with geometrical optics ray tracing for the computation of the diagnostic line of sight. Another important aspect of ECRad is that it has passed a large amount of verification tests against real measurements by conventional, oblique and ECE imaging diagnostics. This paper explains the physical model of ECRad and its implementation. Furthermore, it is discussed how the code can be used for the inference of the electron temperature from ECE measurements and how an oblique ECE diagnostic can be cross-calibrated with ECRad.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Denk, S. S.","Fischer, R.","Poli, E.","Maj, O.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Willensdorfer, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-355318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Denk, S. S."],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics"],"keyword":["Data analysis","Electron cyclotron emission","Radiation transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ecrad an electron cyclotron radiation transport solver for advanced data analysis in thermal and non thermal fusion plasmas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/211183345/ECRad_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-355318","identifier":[{"id":"85079775311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a9dd0519-09e7-4a93-8321-874da180047a"],"keyword":["Data analysis","Electron cyclotron emission","Radiation transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10DB89CF6DFA87FCB3AA770098AC8152"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/211183345/ECRad_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S. S.","key":"denkpau","last":"Denk","name":"Denk, S. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"polipau","last":"Poli","name":"Poli, E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"O.","key":"majpau","last":"Maj","name":"Maj, O.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"stejnerpau","last":"Stejner","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Stejner, M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"willensdorferpau","last":"Willensdorfer","name":"Willensdorfer, M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cpc.2020.107175","issn":["00104655","13869485"],"issn_org":["00104655"],"journal":"Computer Physics Communications","paperid":"107175","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Computer Physics Communications","volume":"253"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079775311"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a9dd0519-09e7-4a93-8321-874da180047a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ECRad: An electron cyclotron radiation transport solver for advanced data analysis in thermal and non-thermal fusion plasmas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-355318","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a study focused on sea state estimation along the route of an in-service container ship. The paper is concerned with the wave buoy analogy in which wave-induced motions of the ship are processed and analysed together with corresponding motion transfer function to give the directional wave spectrum exactly at the point of operation. In this study, a simple and inexpensive instrumentation of the vessel is considered, and wave spectrum estimation is based on measurements from one motion response unit mounted close to the forward perpendicular of the ship. The estimates by the wave buoy analogy are compared with two sets of results from third generation spectral wave models, with one set provided by a commercial supplier and with another set obtained from the Copernicus Climate Change Service Information. Motion measurements from a seven-days voyage across the Pacific Ocean are studied, and it is shown that the wave buoy analogy estimates wave conditions, in terms of sea state parameters, in good agreement with the reports by the sets of ocean wave hindcasts. Along with the comparisons, the paper discusses some of the inherent drawbacks of the wave buoy analogy, notably the fact that a ship acts as a low-pass filter.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","Dietz, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365145"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Ulrik Dam"],"keyword":["ERA5","In service data","Ship motions","Wave buoy analogy","Wave spectrum estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of sea state parameters by the wave buoy analogy with comparisons to third generation spectral wave models","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235977117/OE_2020_Vol216_pp107781_PostPrint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365145","identifier":[{"id":"85089702892","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cad79dbf-0745-43b1-84bf-4cb1f8357856"],"keyword":["(ERA5)","Copernicus climate change service information","In-service data","Ship motions","Spectral wave models","Wave buoy analogy","Wave spectrum estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-242065D8DFB2830201244D580282FBC3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235977117/OE_2020_Vol216_pp107781_PostPrint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","name_org":"Nielsen, Ulrik D.","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","locid":"8daf5efe-5eb2-419d-a2ff-a8fe2b93e45f","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oceaneng.2020.107781","issn":["00298018","18735258"],"issn_org":["00298018"],"journal":"Ocean Engineering","paperid":"107781","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ocean Engineering","volume":"216"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089702892"],"sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cad79dbf-0745-43b1-84bf-4cb1f8357856"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Estimation of sea state parameters by the wave buoy analogy with comparisons to third generation spectral wave models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365145","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Electron cyclotron resonance heating (ECRH) can drive large current densities through electron cyclotron current drive (ECCD). ECCD is expected to be crucial for high-performance plasmas in future fusion reactors like ITER and DEMO, making the current drive efficiency of ECCD a critical design parameter for future reactors. In present-day devices, good agreement between measured and predicted current drive efficiency has been found. However, to ensure the reliability in future machines, a direct validation of the electron momentum distribution function is needed. As a first step towards this goal, we present in this paper oblique electron cyclotron emission (ECE) measurements of a low-density plasma in the ASDEX Upgrade tokamak. Two oblique ECE diagnostics are used to allow the simultaneous measurements of electrons streaming co- and counter-directionally with the plasma current. Predictions for the distribution function are computed with the bounce-averaged Fokker-Planck code RELAX.9 To allow direct comparison with the measurements, synthetic radiation temperatures are computed with the code ECRad.10 Good agreement is found if radial transport occurring predominantly at low electron energies is included. We demonstrate that oblique ECE diagnostics measure the electron distribution function directly at the ECRH deposition site in phase space. Furthermore, they are sensitive to the abundance of pitch-angle scattered electrons that reduce the ECCD efficiency. Limitations and uncertainties of the measurements and the modeling are discussed.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Denk, S. S.","Fischer, R.","Westerhof, E.","Luda Di Cortemiglia, T.","Hobirk, J.","Maj, O.","Poli, E.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner, M.","Stober, J.","Stroth, U.","Suttrop, W.","Willensdorfer, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Denk, S. S."],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Electron cyclotron emission"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"momentum space resolved measurements using oblique electron cyclotron emission for the validation of the quasi linear theory of electron cyclotron current drive","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-6587/abc1bd","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379403","identifier":[{"id":"85103214799","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fa127a15-83b2-4dfb-b7a5-7bab415a8170"],"keyword":["Electron cyclotron current drive","Electron cyclotron emission","Non-thermal electron velocity distribution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-34481054A6CB308A70BFC5222C7104DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-6587/abc1bd","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/264101550/Denk_2020_Plasma_Phys._Control._Fusion_63_015003.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"dutch institute for fundamental energy research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S. S.","key":"denkpau","last":"Denk","name":"Denk, S. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"westerhofpau","last":"Westerhof","name":"Westerhof, E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"ludadicortemigliapau","last":"Luda Di Cortemiglia","name":"Luda Di Cortemiglia, T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"hobirkpau","last":"Hobirk","name":"Hobirk, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"O.","key":"majpau","last":"Maj","name":"Maj, O.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"polipau","last":"Poli","name":"Poli, E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"stejnerpau","last":"Stejner","name":"Stejner, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"stoberpau","last":"Stober","name":"Stober, J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"U.","key":"strothpau","last":"Stroth","name":"Stroth, U.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"W.","key":"suttroppau","last":"Suttrop","name":"Suttrop, W.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"willensdorferpau","last":"Willensdorfer","name":"Willensdorfer, M.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1361-6587/abc1bd","issn":["07413335","13616587"],"issn_org":["07413335"],"issue":"1","journal":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","paperid":"015003","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103214799"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fa127a15-83b2-4dfb-b7a5-7bab415a8170"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Momentum-space-resolved measurements using oblique electron cyclotron emission for the validation of the quasi-linear theory of electron cyclotron current drive","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379403","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Consolidation leading to retention of motor memory following motor practice involves activity-dependent plastic processes in the corticospinal system. To investigate whether beta-band transcranial alternating current stimulation (tACS) applied immediately following skill acquisition can enhance ongoing consolidation processes and thereby motor skill retention 20 adults participated in a randomized, double-blinded, sham-controlled study. Participants received tACS at peak beta-band corticomuscular coherence (CMC) frequency or sham tACS for 10 min following practice of a visuomotor ankle dorsiflexion task. Performance was measured as the average percentage time on target. Electroencephalograhy (EMG) was measured at Cz and EMG from the right tibialis anterior muscle. CMC and intramuscular coherence (IMC) were estimated during 2-min tonic dorsiflexion. Motor skill retention was tested 1 and 7 days after motor practice. From the end of motor practice to the retention tests, motor performance improved more in the tACS group compared with the sham tACS group after 1 (P = 0.05) and 7 days (P < 0.001). At both retention tests, beta-band IMC increased in the tACS group compared with post-tACS. Beta-band CMC increased in the tACS group at retention day 1 compared with post-tACS. Changes in CMC but not IMC were correlated with performance 1 and 7 days following practice. This study shows that tACS applied at beta-band CMC frequency improves consolidation following visuomotor practice and increases beta-band CMC and IMC. We propose that oscillatory beta activity in the corticospinal system may facilitate consolidation of the motor skill.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Yamaguchi, Tomofumi","Svane, Christian","Forman, Christian Riis","Beck, Mikkel Malling","Geertsen, Svend Sparre","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-435554"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Juntendo University"],"keyword":["Corticomuscular coherence","Faculty of Science","Transcranial alternating current stimulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Elsass Instituttet, Charlottenlund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcranial alternating current stimulation of the primary motor cortex after skill acquisition improves motor memory retention in humans a double blinded sham controlled study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/texcom/tgaa047","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-435554","identifier":[{"id":"34296115","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8152838","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-46893ba8-95b5-40ed-9f3a-697de29d1a1b"],"keyword":["Beta-band stimulation","Corticomuscular coherence","Faculty of Science","Intramuscular coherence","Motor memory consolidation","Transcranial alternating current stimulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A54F3F972A06EA76037B6C12C94A5534"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275375023/Yamaguchi_et_al_Cerebral_Cortex_Communications_2020_Vol_1_1_tgaa047.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/texcom/tgaa047","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Motor Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"juntendo university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Juntendo University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Elsass Instituttet, Charlottenlund"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Tomofumi","key":"yamaguchipau","last":"Yamaguchi","locid":"1b5b0528-87e6-4273-91f7-b60b12fbfdd5","name":"Yamaguchi, Tomofumi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"f572838b-fce0-499b-8d0b-c67564c8b3d2","name":"Svane, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Riis","key":"formanpau","last":"Forman","locid":"fd013703-4944-4356-aa45-65bfacebb786","name":"Forman, Christian Riis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Malling","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"a2e41a51-30c1-4e2a-b435-eefa69465a83","name":"Beck, Mikkel Malling","orcid":"0000-0002-8006-2580","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend Sparre","key":"geertsenpau","last":"Geertsen","locid":"9b71cea0-a6d4-47bd-91ca-e969fd3e3af0","name":"Geertsen, Svend Sparre","orcid":"0000-0003-4497-3616","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34296115"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/texcom/tgaa047","issn":["26327376"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cerebral Cortex Communications","paperid":"tgaa047","status":"p","title":"Cerebral Cortex Communications","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-46893ba8-95b5-40ed-9f3a-697de29d1a1b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transcranial alternating current stimulation of the primary motor cortex after skill acquisition improves motor memory retention in humans: A double-blinded sham-controlled study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-435554","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Pre-hospital circumstances, cardiac arrest characteristics, comorbidities and clinical status on admission are strongly associated with outcome after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Early prediction of outcome may inform prognosis, tailor therapy and help in interpreting the intervention effect in heterogenous clinical trials. This study aimed to create a model for early prediction of outcome by artificial neural networks (ANN) and use this model to investigate intervention effects on classes of illness severity in cardiac arrest patients treated with targeted temperature management (TTM). Methods: Using the cohort of the TTM trial, we performed a post hoc analysis of 932 unconscious patients from 36 centres with OHCA of a presumed cardiac cause. The patient outcome was the functional outcome, including survival at 180 days follow-up using a dichotomised Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) scale with good functional outcome defined as CPC 1-2 and poor functional outcome defined as CPC 3-5. Outcome prediction and severity class assignment were performed using a supervised machine learning model based on ANN. Results: The outcome was predicted with an area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC) of 0.891 using 54 clinical variables available on admission to hospital, categorised as background, pre-hospital and admission data. Corresponding models using background, pre-hospital or admission variables separately had inferior prediction performance. When comparing the ANN model with a logistic regression-based model on the same cohort, the ANN model performed significantly better (p = 0.029). A simplified ANN model showed promising performance with an AUC above 0.852 when using three variables only: age, time to ROSC and first monitored rhythm. The ANN-stratified analyses showed similar intervention effect of TTM to 33 °C or 36 °C in predefined classes with different risk of a poor outcome. Conclusion: A supervised machine learning model using ANN predicted neurological recovery, including survival excellently, and outperformed a conventional model based on logistic regression. Among the data available at the time of hospitalisation, factors related to the pre-hospital setting carried most information. ANN may be used to stratify a heterogenous trial population in risk classes and help determine intervention effects across subgroups.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Johnsson, Jesper","Björnsson, Ola","Andersson, Peder","Jakobsson, Andreas","Cronberg, Tobias","Lilja, Gisela","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Kjaergard, Jesper","Wise, Matt","Nielsen, Niklas","Frigyesi, Attila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485182"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helsingborg Hospital","Lund University","University Hospital of Wales"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Artificial neural networks","Cerebral performance category","Critical care","Intensive care","Machine learning","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prediction","Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"artificial neural networks improve early outcome prediction and risk classification in out of hospital cardiac arrest patients admitted to intensive care","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-03103-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485182","identifier":[{"id":"85088908579","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7394679","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32731878","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-99735c58-5034-4f15-8fa2-0b76b1af74a3"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Artificial neural networks","Cerebral performance category","Critical care","Intensive care","Machine learning","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Prediction","Prognostication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6EDA0ACC856AF1750CEF0CF828A3F53D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-03103-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250973386/s13054_020_03103_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"helsingborg hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Helsingborg Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university hospital of wales","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital of Wales","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jesper","key":"johnssonpau","last":"Johnsson","name":"Johnsson, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ola","key":"björnssonpau","last":"Björnsson","name":"Björnsson, Ola","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peder","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Peder","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"jakobssonpau","last":"Jakobsson","name":"Jakobsson, Andreas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergardpau","last":"Kjaergard","name":"Kjaergard, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Matt","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Attila","key":"frigyesipau","last":"Frigyesi","name":"Frigyesi, Attila","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32731878"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13054-020-03103-1","issn":["1466609X"],"issn_org":["13648535"],"issue":"1","journal":"Critical Care","paperid":"474","status":"p","title":"Critical Care","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088908579"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-99735c58-5034-4f15-8fa2-0b76b1af74a3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Artificial neural networks improve early outcome prediction and risk classification in out-of-hospital cardiac arrest patients admitted to intensive care","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485182","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Cerebral venous sinus thrombosis (CVST) is a rare cause of stroke. We report the case of a patient with acute CVST, showing perfusion abnormalities on computed tomography perfusion with perfusion defect in the relevant hemisphere. The defect was found in a region adjacent to the occluded sinus and was not corresponding to an arterial territory. To the best of our knowledge this is the first ever report on CT perfusion abnormalities few hours after acute symptom onset in CVST.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Van Hooff, Robbert Jan","Gyllenborg, Jesper","Jesuratnam-Nielsen, Kayal","Wienecke, Troels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CT perfusion","Cerebral hypoperfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computed tomography perfusion showing cerebral hypoperfusion in a patient with acute cerebral venous sinus thrombosis a case report","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-493964","identifier":[{"id":"85079770256","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32085940","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a845c1eb-086b-4fd9-bbe1-5b36a1257886"],"keyword":["Acute cerebral venous sinus thrombosis","CT perfusion","cerebral hypoperfusion","rare acute stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9462226C2969C95E79C6E670203D904"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Robbert Jan","key":"vanhooffpau","last":"van Hooff","locid":"a4d9de7e-a1fc-46c9-948c-d2c9fb26a968","name":"Van Hooff, Robbert Jan","name_org":"van Hooff, Robbert Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"gyllenborgpau","last":"Gyllenborg","name":"Gyllenborg, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kayal","key":"jesuratnamnielsenpau","last":"Jesuratnam-Nielsen","name":"Jesuratnam-Nielsen, Kayal","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Troels","key":"wieneckepau","last":"Wienecke","locid":"f9d29f3f-0c60-486c-91f0-b23e140a9486","name":"Wienecke, Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-5389-1105","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32085940"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jstrokecerebrovasdis.2020.104681","issn":["10523057","15328511"],"issn_org":["10523057"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Stroke & Cerebrovascular Diseases","paperid":"104681","status":"p","title":"Journal of Stroke & Cerebrovascular Diseases","title_org":"Journal of Stroke and Cerebrovascular Diseases","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079770256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a845c1eb-086b-4fd9-bbe1-5b36a1257886"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computed Tomography Perfusion Showing Cerebral Hypoperfusion in a Patient with Acute Cerebral Venous Sinus Thrombosis—A Case Report","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493964","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Optimization of motor performance is of importance in daily life, in relation to recovery following injury as well as for elite sports performance. The present study investigated whether transcutaneous spinal direct current stimulation (tsDCS) may enhance voluntary ballistic activation of ankle muscles and descending activation of spinal motor neurons in able-bodied adults. Forty-one adults (21 men; 24.0 ± 3.2 years) participated in the study. The effect of tsDCS on ballistic motor performance and plantar flexor muscle activation was assessed in a double-blinded sham-controlled cross-over experiment. In separate experiments, the underlying changes in excitability of corticospinal and spinal pathways were probed by evaluating soleus (SOL) motor evoked potentials (MEPs) following single-pulse transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) over the primary motor cortex, SOL H-reflexes elicited by tibial nerve stimulation and TMS-conditioning of SOL H-reflexes. Measures were obtained before and after cathodal tsDCS over the thoracic spine (T11-T12) for 10 min at 2.5 mA. We found that cathodal tsDCS transiently facilitated peak acceleration in the ballistic motor task compared to sham tsDCS. Following tsDCS, SOL MEPs were increased without changes in H-reflex amplitudes. The short-latency facilitation of the H-reflex by subthreshold TMS, which is assumed to be mediated by the fast conducting monosynaptic corticomotoneuronal pathway, was also enhanced by tsDCS. We argue that tsDCS briefly facilitates voluntary motor output by increasing descending drive from corticospinal neurones to spinal plantar flexor motor neurons. tsDCS can thus transiently promote within-session CNS function and voluntary motor output and holds potential as a technique in the rehabilitation of motor function following central nervous lesions.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yamaguchi, Tomofumi","Beck, Mikkel Malling","Therkildsen, Eva Rudjord","Svane, Christian","Forman, Christian Riis","Lorentzen, Jakob","Conway, Bernard A","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Geertsen, Svend Sparre","Nielsen, Jens Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-495615"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Japan","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","JSPS Postdoctoral Fellow for Research Abroad, Tokyo","Juntendo University","University of Strathclyde"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Movement","Transcranial magnetic stimulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Elsass Institute, Charlottenlund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcutaneous spinal direct current stimulation increases corticospinal transmission and enhances voluntary motor output in humans","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.14531","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-495615","identifier":[{"id":"32812363","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85089629743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7435034","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ab152c57-a1bb-424c-8ff2-3ac7af4f9679"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Movement","Spinal stimulation","Transcranial magnetic stimulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7CEF7406621DB4978AC5E041BB795016"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.14531","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/247387400/Yamaguchi_et_al_Physiological_Reports_2020_Vol_8_16_e14531.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Motor Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"juntendo university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Juntendo University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"jsps postdoctoral fellow for research abroad tokyo","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"JSPS Postdoctoral Fellow for Research Abroad, Tokyo","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Elsass Institute, Charlottenlund"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of strathclyde","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Strathclyde","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Tomofumi","key":"yamaguchipau","last":"Yamaguchi","locid":"1b5b0528-87e6-4273-91f7-b60b12fbfdd5","name":"Yamaguchi, Tomofumi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Malling","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"a2e41a51-30c1-4e2a-b435-eefa69465a83","name":"Beck, Mikkel Malling","orcid":"0000-0002-8006-2580","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eva Rudjord","key":"therkildsenpau","last":"Therkildsen","locid":"6ca8e598-ba75-41c7-9080-41fdb7be24e8","name":"Therkildsen, Eva Rudjord","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"f572838b-fce0-499b-8d0b-c67564c8b3d2","name":"Svane, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Riis","key":"formanpau","last":"Forman","locid":"fd013703-4944-4356-aa45-65bfacebb786","name":"Forman, Christian Riis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jakob","key":"lorentzenpau","last":"Lorentzen","locid":"70660ba7-a635-4350-b486-ea6a118a0d3b","name":"Lorentzen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-7634-0218","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Bernard A","key":"conwaypau","last":"Conway","name":"Conway, Bernard A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend Sparre","key":"geertsenpau","last":"Geertsen","locid":"9b71cea0-a6d4-47bd-91ca-e969fd3e3af0","name":"Geertsen, Svend Sparre","orcid":"0000-0003-4497-3616","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32812363"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14814/phy2.14531","issn":["2051817X"],"issue":"16","journal":"Physiological Reports","paperid":"e14531","status":"p","title":"Physiological Reports","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089629743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab152c57-a1bb-424c-8ff2-3ac7af4f9679"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transcutaneous spinal direct current stimulation increases corticospinal transmission and enhances voluntary motor output in humans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-495615","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Admixture is increasingly being recognized as an important factor in evolutionary genetics. The distribution of genomic admixture tracts, and the resulting effects on admixture linkage disequilibrium, can be used to date the timing of admixture between species or populations. However, the theory used for such prediction assumes selective neutrality despite the fact that many famous examples of admixture involve natural selection acting for or against admixture. In this paper, we investigate the effects of positive selection on the distribution of tract lengths. We develop a theoretical framework that relies on approximating the trajectory of the selected allele using a logistic function. By numerically calculating the expected allele trajectory, we also show that the approach can be extended to cases where the logistic approximation is poor due to the effects of genetic drift. Using simulations, we show that the model is highly accurate under most scenarios. We use the model to show that positive selection on average will tend to increase the admixture tract length. However, perhaps counter-intuitively, conditional on the allele frequency at the time of sampling, positive selection will actually produce shorter expected tract lengths. We discuss the consequences of our results in interpreting the timing of the introgression ofEPAS1from Denisovans into the ancestors of Tibetans.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shchur, Vladimir","Svedberg, Jesper","Medina, Paloma","Corbett-Detig, Russell","Nielsen, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Russia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Higher School of Economics","University of California at Santa Cruz"],"keyword":["Adaptation","Adaptive introgression","Admixture","Coalescent","Disequilibrium","EPAS1","Hitchhiking","Linkage","Selection","UNIT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the distribution of tract lengths during adaptive introgression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1534/g3.120.401616","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511157","identifier":[{"id":"32763953","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85092561621","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000578420600019","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7534438","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-c5490615-1e04-4b15-9993-78157278ee2a"],"keyword":["COALESCENT","DISEQUILIBRIUM","EPAS1","HITCHHIKING","HUMAN-POPULATIONS","LINKAGE","SELECTION MODELS","UNIT","adaptation","adaptive introgression","admixture","selection","tract length"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0A95C10347A3FDED6384671675D5E65"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1534/g3.120.401616","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250539563/3663.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ru","key":"higher school of economics","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Higher School of Economics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at santa cruz","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Santa Cruz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vladimir","key":"shchurpau","last":"Shchur","name":"Shchur, Vladimir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"svedbergpau","last":"Svedberg","name":"Svedberg, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paloma","key":"medinapau","last":"Medina","name":"Medina, Paloma","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Russell","key":"corbettdetigpau","last":"Corbett-Detig","name":"Corbett-Detig, Russell","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"68905e51-280a-4c0b-bc94-469bb52de9b6","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-0513-6591","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32763953"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1534/g3.120.401616","issn":["21601836"],"issue":"10","journal":"G3: Genes, Genomes, Genetics","pages":"3663-3673","status":"p","title":"G3: Genes, Genomes, Genetics","title_org":"G3: Genes, Genomes, Genetics (Bethesda)","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092561621"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c5490615-1e04-4b15-9993-78157278ee2a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the Distribution of Tract Lengths During Adaptive Introgression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511157","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Arginine vasopressin has complex actions in critically ill patients, involving vasoregulatory status, plasma volume, and cortisol levels. Copeptin, a surrogate marker for arginine vasopressin, has shown promising prognostic features in small observational studies and is used clinically for early rule out of acute coronary syndrome. The objective of this study was to explore the association between early measurements of copeptin, circulatory status, and short-term survival after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Methods: Serial blood samples were collected at 24, 48, and 72 h as part of the target temperature management at 33 °C versus 36 °C after cardiac arrest trial, an international multicenter randomized trial where unconscious survivors after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest were allocated to an intervention of 33 or 36 °C for 24 h. Primary outcome was 30-day survival with secondary endpoints circulatory cause of death and cardiovascular deterioration composite; in addition, we examined the correlation with extended the cardiovascular sequential organ failure assessment (eCvSOFA) score. Results: Six hundred ninety patients were included in the analyses, of whom 203 (30.3%) developed cardiovascular deterioration within 24 h, and 273 (39.6%) died within 30 days. Copeptin measured at 24 h was found to be independently associated with 30-day survival, hazard ratio 1.17 [1.06-1.28], p = 0.001; circulatory cause of death, odds ratio 1.03 [1.01-1.04], p = 0.001; and cardiovascular deterioration composite, odds ratio of 1.05 [1.02-1.08], p < 0.001. Copeptin at 24 h was correlated with eCvSOFA score with rho 0.19 [0.12-0.27], p < 0.001. Conclusion: Copeptin is an independent marker of severity of the post cardiac arrest syndrome, partially related to circulatory failure. Trial registration: Clinical Trials, NCT01020916. Registered November 26, 2009.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Düring, Joachim","Annborn, Martin","Cronberg, Tobias","Dankiewicz, Josef","Devaux, Yvan","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Nikoukhah, Homa Rafi","Stammet, Pascal","Undén, Johan","Wanscher, Michael Jaeger","Wise, Matt","Friberg, Hans","Nielsen, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-520217"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Luxembourg","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiff & Vale University Health Board","Lund University","Luxembourg Institute of Health","Medical Centre Leeuwarden","National Rescue Services","Thermo Fisher Scientific, Inc.","University of Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Arginine Vasopressin","Biomarkers","Copeptin","Critical Illness","Humans","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prognosis","Survivors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"copeptin as a marker of outcome after cardiac arrest a sub study of the ttm trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-02904-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-520217","identifier":[{"id":"32345356","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084107249","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7189642","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d43c41d9-6289-4441-9582-f605c1afbb73"],"keyword":["AVP protein human","Arginine vasopressin","Biomarkers","Copeptin","Critical illness","Humans","Out-of hospital cardiac arrest","Prognosis","Survivors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F85A67053D182FCCDE425F9536F8378"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-02904-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/242716474/Copeptin_as_a_marker_of_outcome_after_cardiac_arrest.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"lu","key":"luxembourg institute of health","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Luxembourg Institute of Health","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"medical centre leeuwarden","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical Centre Leeuwarden","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"thermo fisher scientific inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Thermo Fisher Scientific, Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"lu","key":"national rescue services","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Rescue Services","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"cardiff vale university health board","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardiff & Vale University Health Board","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"düringpau","last":"Düring","name":"Düring, Joachim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"annbornpau","last":"Annborn","name":"Annborn, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josef","key":"dankiewiczpau","last":"Dankiewicz","name":"Dankiewicz, Josef","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yvan","key":"devauxpau","last":"Devaux","name":"Devaux, Yvan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Homa Rafi","key":"nikoukhahpau","last":"Nikoukhah","name":"Nikoukhah, Homa Rafi","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johan","key":"undénpau","last":"Undén","name":"Undén, Johan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael Jaeger","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","locid":"65a697e9-1889-4bed-8159-c0323cf425bc","name":"Wanscher, Michael Jaeger","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Matt","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32345356"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13054-020-02904-8","issn":["1466609X"],"issn_org":["13648535"],"journal":"Critical Care","paperid":"185","status":"p","title":"Critical Care","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084107249"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d43c41d9-6289-4441-9582-f605c1afbb73"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Copeptin as a marker of outcome after cardiac arrest : a sub-study of the TTM trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-520217","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: During targeted temperature management after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest infusion of vasoactive drugs is often needed to ensure cerebral perfusion pressure. This study investigated mean arterial pressure after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest and the association with brain injury and long-term cognitive function. METHODS: Post-hoc analysis of patients surviving at least 48 hours in the biobank substudy of the targeted temperature management trial with available blood pressure data. Patients were stratified in three groups according to mean arterial pressure during targeted temperature management (4-28 hours after admission; <70 mmHg, 70-80 mmHg, >80 mmHg). A biomarker of brain injury, neuron-specific enolase, was measured and impaired cognitive function was defined as a mini-mental state examination score below 27 in 6-month survivors. RESULTS: Of the 657 patients included in the present analysis, 154 (23%) had mean arterial pressure less than 70 mmHg, 288 (44%) had mean arterial pressure between 70 and 80 mmHg and 215 (33%) had mean arterial pressure greater than 80 mmHg. There were no statistically significant differences in survival (P=0.35) or neuron-specific enolase levels (P=0.12) between the groups. The level of target temperature did not statistically significantly interact with mean arterial pressure regarding neuron-specific enolase (Pinteraction_MAP*TTM=0.58). In the subgroup of survivors with impaired cognitive function (n=132) (35%) mean arterial pressure during targeted temperature management was significantly higher (Pgroup=0.03). CONCLUSIONS: In a large cohort of comatose out-of-hospital cardiac arrest patients, low mean arterial pressure during targeted temperature management was not associated with higher neuron-specific enolase regardless of the level of target temperature (33°C or 36°C for 24 hours). In survivors with impaired cognitive function, mean arterial pressure during targeted temperature management was significantly higher.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Grand, Johannes","Lilja, Gisela","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Friberg, Hans","Wanscher, Michael","Cronberg, Tobias","Nielsen, Niklas","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"arterial blood pressure during targeted temperature management after out of hospital cardiac arrest and association with brain injury and long term cognitive function","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527186","identifier":[{"id":"31246109","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164551956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dfe09ce5-4442-4704-8098-7fe41f0c20fc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB9E62550B30DE2AD270B7CE6384DF88"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J