cial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"IL","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","locid":"3ef0a37d-85b9-40e5-9a89-9e2f67171ffb","name":"Karlsen, IL","orcid":"0000-0002-7923-5800","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","name_org":"Kristiansen, J","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Østergaard","key":"jasperspau","last":"Jaspers","locid":"665181a1-f77e-4aa2-b70c-a928e41447d9","name":"Jaspers, Sofie Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0292-9660","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0d8ad03f-8294-49a2-8bb7-fea40eccf25a","name":"Rasmussen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-7864-4178","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Leonhardt","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Line Leonhardt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Kauffeldt","key":"hammelsvangpau","last":"Hammelsvang","name":"Hammelsvang, Sofie Kauffeldt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"bengtsenpau","last":"Bengtsen","name":"Bengtsen, E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette Bjørn","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henriette Bjørn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B","key":"austpau","last":"Aust","locid":"76cc2658-db81-44f2-86ba-5568b6196df7","name":"Aust, Birgit","name_org":"Aust, B","orcid":"0000-0002-4184-6577","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"København","publisher":"Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Arbejdsmiljø","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-60caf951-08af-4515-9331-1ee951b554c0","nfa-f7efc582-e25c-4a59-996f-49dbbf5c0957"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Afdækning af eksisterende viden, metoder og praksis ift. at forebygge, håndtere og lære af udadreagerende adfærd i ældreplejen i et arbejdsmiljøperspektiv. Minirapport","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.82-769494","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"It is not known how effective specific types of motor-enriched activities are at improving academic learning and early reading skills in children. The aim of this study was to investigate whether fine or gross motor enrichment during a single session of recognizing letters “b”/“d” can improve within-session performance or delayed retention the following day in comparison to letter recognition practice without movement. Furthermore, the aim was to investigate children’s motivation to perform the specific tasks. We used a randomized controlled intervention study-design to investigate the effect of 10-min motor-enriched “b”/“d” letter training on children’s ability to recognize the letters “b” and “d” (n = 127, mean age = 7.61 ± SD = 0.44 years) acutely, and in a delayed retention test. Three groups were included: a fine motor-enriched group (FME), a gross motor-enriched group (GME), that received 10 min of “b” and “d” training with enriched gestures (fine or gross motor movements, respectively), and a control group (CON), which received non motor-enriched “b”/“d” training. The children’s ability to recognize “b” and “d” were tested before (T0), immediately after (T1), and one day after the intervention (T2) using a “b”/“d” Recognition Test. Based on a generalized linear mixed model a significant group-time interaction was found for accuracy in the “b”/“d” Recognition Test. Specifically, FME improved their ability to recognize “b”/“d” at post intervention (T0→T1, p = 0.008) and one-day retention test (T0→T2, p < 0.001) more than CON. There was no significant difference in change between GME and CON. For reaction time there were no significant global interaction effects observed. However, planned post hoc comparisons revealed a significant difference between GME and CON immediately after the intervention (T0→T1, p = 0.03). The children’s motivation-score was higher for FME and GME compared to CON (FME-CON: p = 0.01; GME-CON: p = 0.01). The study demonstrated that fine motor-enriched training improved children’s letter recognition more than non motor activities. Both types of motor training were accompanied by higher intrinsic motivation for the children compared to the non motor training group. The study suggests a new method for motor-enriched letter learning and future research should investigate the underlying mechanisms.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Damsgaard, Linn","Elleby, Sofie Rejkjær","Gejl, Anne Kær","Malling, Anne Sofie Bøgh","Bugge, Anna","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Poulsen, Mads","Nielsen, Glen","Wienecke, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-098.57-039655"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Academic learning","Children","Cognition","Faculty of Science","Letter recognition","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motor enriched encoding can improve children s early letter recognition","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2020.01207","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.57-039655","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7333458","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85087784980","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32676043","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["kp-fbccf34a-eb96-4ac3-81a1-af676b04d617","ku-1327634e-312a-4dab-8854-9cce8843c72f"],"keyword":["Academic learning","Children","Cognition","Faculty of Science","Letter recognition","Motor-enriched","disease, health science and nursing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D1349E35491624666433DC1D1F275ADD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250088765/fpsyg_11_01207.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2020.01207","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Inst. for Terapeut- og Jordemoderudd. - Inst.chef","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Børneliv - Sund tilknytning og aktiv livsstil for børn og unge"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Linn","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"5bdec78f-e12e-4255-adc0-fa9106f19066","name":"Damsgaard, Linn","orcid":"0000-0001-6705-1142","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie Rejkjær","key":"ellebypau","last":"Elleby","locid":"9972dd0f-3d82-42f2-83cb-dfc9a149ded8","name":"Elleby, Sofie Rejkjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Kær","key":"gejlpau","last":"Gejl","locid":"fb0b6f35-0081-44d4-81ad-8c0039ac6833","name":"Gejl, Anne Kær","orcid":"0000-0001-6781-2263","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Sofie Bøgh","key":"mallingpau","last":"Malling","locid":"68fba531-0cb2-4767-8d39-9c14f4456618","name":"Malling, Anne Sofie Bøgh","orcid":"0000-0002-9267-9334","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"buggepau","last":"Bugge","locid":"2fbb1755-9b3d-4ea9-a3f4-c5f90cde1102","name":"Bugge, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-8345-1434","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"34318492-fd18-47e9-98ae-0c68092712ee","name":"Poulsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0001-6573-6332","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Glen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fc1c711b-5125-48cd-93a1-8267cba52968","name":"Nielsen, Glen","orcid":"0000-0003-2854-7182","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"wieneckepau","last":"Wienecke","locid":"2a2e95d8-1954-4b89-ac54-2add081560a1","name":"Wienecke, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-9786-4689","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32676043"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fpsyg.2020.01207","issn":["16641078"],"journal":"Frontiers in Psychology","paperid":"1207","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Psychology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087784980"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-fbccf34a-eb96-4ac3-81a1-af676b04d617","ku-1327634e-312a-4dab-8854-9cce8843c72f"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Motor-Enriched Encoding Can Improve Children's Early Letter Recognition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.57-039655","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To assess the impact of ESBL production on mortality and length of hospital stay (LOS) of community-onset infections due to Escherichia coli or Klebsiella pneumoniae. METHODS: A population-based cohort study including all adult patients hospitalized with a first-time community-onset E. coli or K. pneumoniae bacteraemia or urinary tract infection in the North Denmark Region between 2007 and 2017. For each bacterial agent, we computed 1 year Kaplan-Meier survival curves and cumulative incidence functions of LOS, and by use of Cox proportional hazard regression we computed HRs as estimates of 30 day and 1 year mortality rate ratios (MRRs) and LOS among patients with and without ESBL-producing infections. RESULTS: We included 24 518 cases (among 22 350 unique patients), of whom 1018 (4.2%) were infected by an ESBL-producing bacterium. The 30 day cumulative mortality and adjusted MRR (aMRR) in patients with and without ESBL-producing isolates was as follows: E. coli bacteraemia (n = 3831), 15.8% versus 14.0%, aMRR = 1.01 (95% CI = 0.70-1.45); E. coli urinary tract infection (n = 17 151), 9.5% versus 8.7%, aMRR = 0.97 (95% CI = 0.75-1.26); K. pneumoniae bacteraemia (n = 734), 0% versus 17.2%, aMRR = not applicable; and K. pneumoniae urinary tract infection (n = 2802), 13.8% versus 10.7%, aMRR = 1.13 (95% CI = 0.73-1.75). The 1 year aMRR remained roughly unchanged. ESBL-producing E. coli bacteraemia was associated with an increased LOS compared with non-ESBL production. CONCLUSIONS: ESBL production was not associated with an increased short- or long-term mortality in community-onset infections due to E. coli or K. pneumoniae, yet ESBL-producing E. coli bacteraemia was associated with an increased LOS.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Richelsen, Rasmus","Smit, Jesper","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Laxsen Anru, Pavithra","Gutiérrez-Gutiérrez, Belen","Rodríguez-Bãno, Jesús","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.78-002752"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Hospital Virgen Macarena"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Unidad Clínica de Enfermedades Infecciosas, Microbiología y Medicina Preventiva, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena/Departamento de Medicina, Universidad de Sevilla/Instituto de Biomedicina de Sevilla (IBiS), Sevilla, Spain"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcome of community onset esbl producing escherichia coli and klebsiella pneumoniae bacteraemia and urinary tract infection a population based cohort study in denmark","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85096152308","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.78-002752","identifier":[{"id":"85096152308","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32862220","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-3779c5ca-a104-414d-ad78-e6c177a9febd","sdu-19993b6e-84e5-4050-bfb0-2764d7ef3268"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C528AFB1D85C9663014F407E4DB5F51F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalbo