homa in Denmark : A Nationwide Register-Based Case-Control Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.93-019288","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The aim was to compare the diagnostic accuracy of 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT with conventional cross-sectional imaging and diffusion-weighted MRI (DW-MRI) for detecting lymph node metastasis (LNM) to stage prostate cancer patients. Twenty consecutive, newly- diagnosed prostate cancer patients were prospectively enrolled and underwent 68Ga-PSMA-11 PET/CT, anatomical MRI or contrast-enhanced CT, and DW-MRI prior to laparoscopic, template-based, extended lymph node dissection. Histopathological findings served as the reference test. RESULTS: Histopathology showed LNM in 13 of 20 patients (19 high-risk, 1 intermediate risk). Five patients had metastasis-suspected lymph nodes on 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT. Patient-based analysis showed that the sensitivity and specificity for detecting LNM were 39% and 100% with 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT, 8% and 100% with MRI/CT, and 36% and 83% with DW-MRI, respectively. The positive and negative predictive values were 100% and 49% with 68Ga-PSMA PET/C, 100% and 37% with MRI/CT, and 80% and 42% with DW-MRI. Of 573 dissected lymph nodes, 33 were LNM from 26 regions. True-positive LNM on 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT was 9-11 mm in diameter, whereas false-negative LNM had a median diameter of 4 mm, with only 3 of 30 lymph nodes being larger than 10 mm. LNM were positive for PSMA by immunostaining. CONCLUSIONS: The sensitivity of 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT was notably better than that of MRI/CT and comparable to that of DW-MRI. Some false positive findings with DW-MRI reduced its specificity and positive predictive value compared with those of 68Ga-PSMA PET/CT and MRI/CT.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Petersen, Lars Jelstrup","Nielsen, Julie B","Langkilde, Niels-Christian","Petersen, Astrid Christine","Afshar-Oromieh, Ali","De Souza, Nandita M","De Paepe, Katja","Fisker, Rune Vincents","Arp, Dennis Tideman","Hansen, Jesper Carl","Haberkorn, Uwe","Zacho, Helle D"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056792"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital Bern"],"keyword":["Diagnostic accuracy","PSMA PET CT","Prostatic neoplasm","Staging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sup 000000000068 sup ga psma pet ct compared with mri ct and diffusion weighted mri for primary lymph node staging prior to definitive radiotherapy in prostate cancer a prospective diagnostic test accuracy study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85067043164&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-056792","identifier":[{"id":"31190153","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85067043164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-16ef59ea-6526-47bf-9083-e6b239751947"],"keyword":["Anatomical cross-sectional imaging","Diagnostic accuracy","PSMA PET/CT","Prostatic neoplasm","Staging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-962B6DB3A7A99E0DF44528B267292820"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of 