ast":"Klenø Nøjgaard","locid":"9454305f-22e1-49a1-ab38-254379892e41","name":"Nøjgaard, Jacob Klenø","name_org":"Klenø Nøjgaard, Jacob","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"omstedtpau","last":"Omstedt","name":"Omstedt, Gunnar","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Camilla","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertil","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","name":"Forsberg, Bertil","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/acp-20-4333-2020","issn":["16807316","16807324"],"issn_org":["16807316"],"issue":"7","journal":"Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics","pages":"4333-4365","publisher":"Copernicus Publications","status":"p","title":"Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083510725"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-74f8f262-0a98-410b-ba10-79a4504d7f34"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The influence of residential wood combustion on the concentrations of PM2.5 in four Nordic cities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-196127","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This article is about the use of measured wave-induced vessel motions for estimation of ocean wave spectra by application of the wave buoy analogy. In the study, data from a larger, in-service container ship is considered. The estimation of wave spectra, equivalently sea state parameters, is based on measurements from, respectively, a gyro and two accelerometers leading to the simultaneous use of the pitching motion together with the horizontal and vertical accelerations in a position close to the forward perpendicular. The study of in-service data leads to contemplations about the vessel’s advance speed, as the possible existence of sea current means that speed-over-ground (SOG) and speed-through-water (STW) will be dfferent. The article discusses aspects related to advance speed in the context of the wave buoy analogy, and a smaller sensitivity study is conducted. Preceding to the sensitivity study, a comparison is made between sea state estimates by the wave buoy analogy and estimates obtained from a hindcast study. The article shows an acceptable agreement between the two sets of estimates. Following, the main conclusion from the sensitivity study on advance speed is that errors and uncertainties in the speed log have an effect on the estimates of the wave buoy analogy. In fact, the effect can be severe if reliable STW measurements are not available. In the final part, the article includes a few discussions about (non)stationary conditions in the context of the wave buoy analogy, and, although the effect on results is not necessarily detrimental, care must be shown when the wave buoy analogy is applied during in-service conditions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","Dietz, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335026"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Container ship","Directional wave spectrum","In service data","Ship motions","Speed through water","Wave spectrum estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ocean wave spectrum estimation using measured vessel motions from an in service container ship","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195102554/WaveEstimClementine_PostPrint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335026","identifier":[{"id":"85073719264","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-66053706-2252-479e-ab78-34240467b77e"],"keyword":["Container ship","Directional wave spectrum","In-service data","Ship motions","Speed-through-water","Wave spectrum estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86FAAE93D52191923CBCFCA71F04C2E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195102554/WaveEstimClementine_PostPrint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"a p moller maersk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-MAE","l3nl":"A.P. Møller – Mærsk","l3nn":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","namevar":["Maersk Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-MAE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","name_org":"Nielsen, Ulrik D.","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marstruc.2019.102682","issn":["09518339","18734170"],"issn_org":["09518339"],"journal":"Marine Structures","paperid":"102682","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Marine Structures","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073719264"],"search":{"DAF":["A.P. Møller – Mærsk","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-66053706-2252-479e-ab78-34240467b77e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Ocean wave spectrum estimation using measured vessel motions from an in-service container ship","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335026","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Activation of the voltage-gated Kv7 channels holds therapeutic promise in several neurological and psychiatric disorders, including epilepsy, schizophrenia, and depression. Here, we present a pharmacological characterization of Lu AA41178, a novel, pan-selective Kv7.2-7.5 opener, using both in vitro assays and a broad range of in vivo assays with relevance to epilepsy, schizophrenia, and depression. Electrophysiological characterization in Xenopus oocytes expressing human Kv7.2-Kv7.5 confirmed Lu AA41178 as a pan-selective opener of Kv7 channels by significantly left-shifting the activation threshold. Additionally, Lu AA41178 was tested in vitro for off-target effects, demonstrating a clean Kv7-selective profile, with no impact on common cardiac ion channels, and no potentiating activity on GABAA channels. Lu AA41178 was evaluated across preclinical in vivo assays with relevance to neurological and psychiatric disorders. In the maximum electroshock seizure threshold test and PTZ seizure threshold test, Lu AA41178 significantly increased the seizure thresholds in mice, demonstrating anticonvulsant efficacy. Lu AA41178 demonstrated antipsychotic-like activity by reducing amphetamine-induced hyperlocomotion in mice as well as lowering conditioned avoidance responses in rats. In the mouse forced swim test, a model with antidepressant predictivity, Lu AA41178 significantly reduced immobility. Additionally, behavioral effects typically observed with Kv7 openers was also characterized. In vivo assays were accompanied by plasma and brain exposures, revealing minimum effective plasma levels Lu AA41178, a potent opener of neuronal Kv7 channels demonstrate efficacy in assays of epilepsy, schizophrenia and depression and might serve as a valuable tool for exploring the role of Kv7 channels in both neurological and psychiatric disorders.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Grupe, Morten","Bentzen, Bo Hjorth","Benned-Jensen, Tau","Nielsen, Vibeke","Frederiksen, Kristen","Jensen, Henrik Sindal","Jacobsen, Anne-Marie","Skibsbye, Lasse","Sams, Anette Graven","Grunnet, Morten","Rottlander, Mario","Bastlund, Jesper Frank"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460447"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animal models","Anticonvulsant","Epilepsy","Excitability","KCNQ","KCNQ2","Kv7","Neurons","Social defeat","Susceptibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vitro and in vivo characterization of lu aa000000041178 a novel brain penetrant pan selective kv000000000007 potassium channel opener with efficacy in preclinical models of epileptic seizures and psychiatric disorders","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-460447","identifier":[{"id":"85089519699","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32745603","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000582725000008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-7028f5b2-5a14-440d-ae91-5130650925da"],"keyword":["ANIMAL-MODELS","ANTICONVULSANT","EXCITABILITY","Epilepsy","ICA-27243","KCNQ","KCNQ2","Kv7","Kv7 opener","Lu AA41178","N-(6-CHLORO-PYRIDIN-3-YL)-3,4-DIFLUORO-BENZAMIDE","NEURONS","RETIGABINE EZOGABINE","Retigabine","SOCIAL DEFEAT","SUSCEPTIBILITY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BEABEFB5995DD9533C17BB9818205405"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"grupepau","last":"Grupe","name":"Grupe, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bo Hjorth","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","locid":"59e5d901-5519-4467-870f-b60d716e9b6f","name":"Bentzen, Bo Hjorth","orcid":"0000-0002-0253-4992","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tau","key":"bennedjensenpau","last":"Benned-Jensen","name":"Benned-Jensen, Tau","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vibeke","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Vibeke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristen","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Kristen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Sindal","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Henrik Sindal","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne-Marie","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Anne-Marie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lasse","key":"skibsbyepau","last":"Skibsbye","name":"Skibsbye, Lasse","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette Graven","key":"samspau","last":"Sams","name":"Sams, Anette Graven","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"grunnetpau","last":"Grunnet","name":"Grunnet, Morten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mario","key":"rottlanderpau","last":"Rottlander","name":"Rottlander, Mario","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Frank","key":"bastlundpau","last":"Bastlund","name":"Bastlund, Jesper Frank","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32745603"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejphar.2020.173440","issn":["00142999","18790712"],"issn_org":["00142999"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmacology","paperid":"173440","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmacology","volume":"887"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089519699"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7028f5b2-5a14-440d-ae91-5130650925da"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In vitro and in vivo characterization of Lu AA41178 : A novel, brain penetrant, pan-selective Kv7 potassium channel opener with efficacy in preclinical models of epileptic seizures and psychiatric disorders","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460447","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE. The purpose of this study is to establish whether texture analysis and densitometry are complementary quantitative measures of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in a lung cancer screening setting. MATERIALS AND METHODS. This was a retrospective study of data collected prospectively (in 2004-2010) in the Danish Lung Cancer Screening Trial. The texture score, relative area of emphysema, and percentile density were computed for 1915 baseline low-dose lung CT scans and were evaluated, both individually and in combination, for associations with lung function (i.e., forced expiratory volume in 1 second as a percentage of predicted normal [FEV1% predicted]), diagnosis of mild to severe COPD, and prediction of a rapid decline in lung function. Multivariate linear regression models with lung function as the outcome were compared using the likelihood ratio test or the Vuong test, and AUC values for diagnostic and prognostic capabilities were compared using the DeLong test. RESULTS. Texture showed a significantly stronger association with lung function (p < 0.001 vs densitometric measures), a significantly higher diagnostic AUC value (for COPD, 0.696; for Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GOLD) grade 1, 0.648; for GOLD grade 2, 0.768; and for GOLD grade 3, 0.944; p < 0.001 vs densitometric measures), and a higher but not significantly different association with lung function decline. In addition, only texture could predict a rapid decline in lung function (AUC value, 0.538; p < 0.05 vs random guessing). The combination of texture and both densitometric measures strengthened the association with lung function and decline in lung function (p < 0.001 and p < 0.05, respectively, vs texture) but did not improve diagnostic or prognostic performance. CONCLUSION. The present study highlights texture as a promising quantitative CT measure of COPD to use alongside, or even instead of, densitometric measures. Moreover, texture may allow early detection of COPD in subjects who undergo lung cancer screening.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Lauge","Nielsen, Mads","Petersen, Jens","Pedersen, Jesper H","Dirksen, Asger","de Bruijne, Marleen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic obstructive pulmonary disease quantification using ct texture analysis and densitometry results from the danish lung cancer screening trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-515220","identifier":[{"id":"32255690","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085536223","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cbeb36df-3330-49ad-8a2b-c46f1a57fc30"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE65B96912A778117AFD9125DD893FD5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lauge","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"330d1478-c602-4767-8d45-30063bff33ea","name":"Sørensen, Lauge","orcid":"0000-0002-1181-7150","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52f8d6fb-fd83-4d11-ad65-3e183ca401f2","name":"Nielsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-1535-068X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0fcef7de-bc0f-463f-b539-bc02ae09e0e5","name":"Petersen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-0138-0693","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper H","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jesper H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Asger","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","name":"Dirksen, Asger","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marleen","key":"debruijnepau","last":"de Bruijne","locid":"988d3493-ffac-4b50-99ff-e91d85774b0d","name":"de Bruijne, Marleen","orcid":"0000-0002-6328-902X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32255690"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2214/ajr.19.22300","issn":["0361803X","15463141"],"issn_org":["0361803X"],"issue":"6","journal":"American Journal of Roentgenology","pages":"1269-1279","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Roentgenology","volume":"214"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085536223"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cbeb36df-3330-49ad-8a2b-c46f1a57fc30"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease Quantification Using CT Texture Analysis and Densitometry : Results From the Danish Lung Cancer Screening Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515220","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To show the prevalence of selected infectious diseases among internationally adopted children (IAC) in Denmark. Background: Each year approximately 200 IAC arrive in Denmark. These are at increased risk of infectious diseases rarely seen in Danish children. Studies from the 1990s showed that 60% of IAC had infectious diseases and that the majority of these were undetected without screening. Methods: The study is a prospective study of medical records from children seen in the adoption clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital in the period 2009-2013. Screening was done for hepatitis A (HAV), B (HBV) and C (HCV), syphilis, HIV, tuberculosis (TB) and intestinal parasites. Results: In 245 IAC tested, 2% had evidence of recent HAV infection, 3% with HBV and one child with HCV, and no cases of HIV were found. One child had antibodies against syphilis (anti-Trpa AB positivity), and 2% were latently infected with tuberculosis. We found 30% infected with pathogenic intestinal parasites. Only 46% had serologic evidence of immunisation against HBV. Conclusion: The prevalence of infections in IAC was lower than previously reported but compared to the general population, a higher prevalence of intestinal parasites, hepatitis and tuberculosis was found. We recommend that IAC are offered screening shortly after arrival.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Agnethe Vale","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Pedersen, Tine Marie","Helmuth, Ida Glode","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Nielsen, Helle Winter","Christensen, Vibeke Brix","Kurtzhals, Jørgen A L","Poulsen, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adoptees","Hepatitis A","Hepatitis B","Infectious diseases","Intestinal parasites","Tuberculosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infectious diseases detected by screening after arrival to denmark in internationally adopted children","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-521528","identifier":[{"id":"31580515","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85074750525","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d6637442-6fc6-4a45-af01-e5a00dbd81d8"],"keyword":["adoptees","hepatitis A","hepatitis B","infectious diseases","intestinal parasites","tuberculosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE9E582445C1A748AC598597134B2FBC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Agnethe Vale","key":"nielsenagnethevalepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Agnethe Vale","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"kjærgaardjesperpau","last":"Kjærgaard","name":"Kjærgaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tine Marie","key":"pedersentinemariepau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Tine Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida Glode","key":"helmuthidaglodepau","last":"Helmuth","name":"Helmuth, Ida Glode","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardulrikkapau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle Winter","key":"nielsenhellewinterpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Helle Winter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke Brix","key":"christensenvibekebrixpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Vibeke Brix","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jørgen Anders Lindholm","key":"kurtzhalsjørgenalpau","last":"Kurtzhals","locid":"e0731c1b-1543-4836-bb5a-6f05c9795754","name":"Kurtzhals, Jørgen A L","name_org":"Kurtzhals, Jørgen Anders Lindholm","orcid":"0000-0003-2760-8713","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja","key":"poulsenanjapau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Anja","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31580515"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.15045","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"5","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"1004-1010","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","title_org":"Acta Paediatrica, International Journal of Paediatrics","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074750525"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d6637442-6fc6-4a45-af01-e5a00dbd81d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infectious diseases detected by screening after arrival to Denmark in internationally adopted children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521528","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Udgaven rummer et nyskrevet kapitel (Kapitel 9) om koppeepidemiernes betydning for den spanske erobring af Mexico.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-538469"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opdaget mødet mellem indianere og europæere i 000000001500 tallets mexico","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://opdaget.ibog.forlagetcolumbus.dk/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-538469","ids":["ku-f3058670-b807-42b3-9c37-541b88bb79c9"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D1189C606CE0B1EA717A33E6014533F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","place":"København","publisher":"Forlaget Columbus","publisher_org":"forlaget columbus","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f3058670-b807-42b3-9c37-541b88bb79c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Opdaget? : Mødet mellem indianere og europæere i 1500-tallets Mexico","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-538469","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The adipose tissue-derived stromal vascular fraction (SVF) is a promising candidate for use in cell therapy and tissue engineering due to its regenerative and immunomodulatory properties. Some therapies are based on using the complete SVF product, whereas others depend on the expansion of adipose-derived stromal cells (ASCs) in culture. The latter application often involves a time delay between adipose tissue harvest and SVF isolation. This study investigated how storage time and temperature affected cell quality and composition. Aliquots of lipoaspirate were stored cold (4°C), at room temperature (18-20°C), or at 37°C. SVF was isolated on sequential time points over a period of 48 h, and the following were assessed: Cell viability, vitality, composition, and the proliferative potential of the ASCs. When the lipoaspirate was stored cold, the viability of the SVF remained stable for up to 48 h; however, the vitality of the SVF decreased significantly after 24 h. When stored at higher temperatures (room temperature or 37°C), the vitality of the SVF decreased after 8 h. The ASC fraction in the SVF decreased rapidly after 8 h when stored at higher temperatures, whereas this change was delayed significantly when the lipoaspirate was stored cold. Tendencies towards increases in the lag phase, population doubling time (PDt), and time to reach confluency were observed when the lipoaspirate was stored at higher temperatures. The vitality of the SVF was correlated significantly with the time of the lag phase and the time required to reach confluence, whereas no correlation was observed with the PDt. Both prolonged storage time and increased temperature during lipoaspirate storage negatively affected the quality of the obtained SVF. Our results suggest that lipoaspirate should be stored for no longer than 24 h at 4°C to maintain the optimal quality for the isolation of SVF and the expansion of ASCs.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom","Juul, Sarah","Vester-Glovinski, Peter Viktor","Haastrup, Eva Kannik","Ballesteros, Olga Rivera","Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","Jensen, Andreas Kryger","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Herly, Mikkel","Munthe-Fog, Lea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541046"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adipose derived stromal cells","Endothelial Cells","Endothelial progenitor cells","Stromal vascular fraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lipoaspirate storage time and temperature effects on stromal vascular fraction quality and cell composition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-541046","identifier":[{"id":"32580198","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85087631792","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f7418082-94db-4996-9c46-242efb5a439e"],"keyword":["Adipose-derived stromal cells","Colony-forming unit fibroblast","Endothelial cells","Endothelial progenitor cells","Nucleated cells","Stromal vascular fraction"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9ED47B3F8AD14A3070928353A7917E9D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Dyrendom","key":"svalgaardpau","last":"Svalgaard","name":"Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Viktor","key":"vesterglovinskipau","last":"Vester-Glovinski","name":"Vester-Glovinski, Peter Viktor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva Kannik","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","name":"Haastrup, Eva Kannik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olga Rivera","key":"ballesterospau","last":"Ballesteros","name":"Ballesteros, Olga Rivera","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Duch","key":"lynggaardpau","last":"Lynggaard","name":"Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Kryger","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c165a0cc-b45c-485e-bfda-70d124e46012","name":"Jensen, Andreas Kryger","orcid":"0000-0002-8233-9176","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","locid":"af37e8db-0c68-4da1-9b25-5625d241b9ca","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikkel","key":"herlypau","last":"Herly","name":"Herly, Mikkel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea","key":"munthefogpau","last":"Munthe-Fog","name":"Munthe-Fog, Lea","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32580198"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000507825","issn":["03650332","14226405"],"issn_org":["14226405"],"journal":"Cells, Tissues, Organs","pages":"54-63","status":"p","title":"Cells, Tissues, Organs","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087631792"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f7418082-94db-4996-9c46-242efb5a439e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lipoaspirate Storage Time and Temperature : Effects on Stromal Vascular Fraction Quality and Cell Composition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541046","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To investigate the effect of diabetes duration on glycaemic control, measured according to mean glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c) level, and mortality risk within different age, sex and clinically relevant, comorbidity-defined subgroups in an elderly population with type 2 diabetes (T2D). METHODS: We studied older (≥ 65 years) primary care patients with T2D, who had three successive annual measurements of HbA1c taken between 2005 and 2013. The primary exposure was the mean of all three HbA1c measurements. Follow-up began on the date of the third measurement. Individual mean HbA1c levels were categorized into clinically relevant groups (<48 mmol/mol [<6.5%]; 48-52 mmol/mol [6.5%-6.9 %]; 53-63 mmol/mol [7%-7.9%]; 64-74 mmol/mol [8%-8.9%]; and ≥ 75 mmol/mol [≥ 9%]). We used multiple Cox regression to study the effect of glycaemic control on the hazard of all-cause mortality, adjusted for age, sex, use of concomitant medication, and age- and disease-related comorbidities. RESULTS: A total of 9734 individuals were included. During a median (interquartile range) follow-up of 7.3 (4.6-8.7) years, 3320 individuals died. We found that the effect of mean HbA1c on all-cause mortality depended on the duration of diabetes (P for interaction <0.001). For individuals with short diabetes duration (<5 years), the risk of death increased with poorer glycaemic control (increasing HbA1c), whereas for individuals with longstanding diabetes (≥ 5 years), we found a J-shaped association, where a mean HbA1c level between 48 and 63 mmol/mol (6.5% and 7.9%) was associated with the lowest risk of death. For individuals with longstanding diabetes, both low (< 48 mmol/mol [<6.5 %]; hazard ratio [HR] 1.21, 95 % confidence interval [CI] 1.07-1.37, P = 0.002), and high mean HbA1c levels ( ≥ 75 mmol/mol [≥9.0 %]; HR 1.60, 95 % CI 1.28-1.99, P < 0.001) were associated with an increased risk of death. We also calculated 5-year absolute risks of all-cause mortality, separately for short and long diabetes duration, and found similar risk patterns across different age groups, sex and comorbidity strata. CONCLUSIONS: In elderly individuals with T2D, the effect of glycaemic control (measured by HbA1c) on all-cause mortality depended on the duration of diabetes. Of particular clinical importance, we found that strict glycaemic control was associated with an increased risk of death among individuals with long (>5 years) diabetes duration. This was not the case for individuals with short diabetes duration where strict glycaemic control was associated with the lowest risk of death. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ghouse, Jonas","Isaksen, Jonas L.","Skov, Morten W","Lind, Bent","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Olesen, Morten S","Holst, Anders G.","Nielsen, Jonas B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543831"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of diabetes duration on the relationship between glycaemic control and risk of death in older adults with type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/dom.13891","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-543831","identifier":[{"id":"31596048","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075168302","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fbf0dda3-9527-495d-b667-978330b0a3c0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-605EAD3C117314FD3BCA61D540BA236D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","u