versities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["sdu-8d80826d-4a75-4849-8bb8-c1882055e949"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Fokuseret lungeultralydskanning","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613758","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Mitochondrial dysfunction after transient cerebral ischemia can be monitored by cerebral microdialysis (CMD) using changes in the lactate and pyruvate concentrations and ratio. Other metabolites associated with mitochondrial (dys)function are, e.g., tricyclic acid (TCA) and purine metabolites. Ethyl pyruvate (EP) is a putative neuroprotectant, supposedly targeting mitochondrial energy metabolism, but its effect on cerebral energy metabolism has never been described using microdialysis. In this study we monitored the metabolic effects of EP in the endothelin-1 (ET-1) rat model using perfusion with13 C-succinate and analysis of endogenous and13 C-labeled metabolites in the dialysates by liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (LC-MS). Adult Sprague Dawley rats (n = 27 of which n = 11 were included in the study) were subjected to the microdialysis experiments. Microdialysis probes were perfused with13C-labeled succinate (1 mM), and striatal dialysates were collected at 30 min intervals before induction of the insult, during intracerebral application of ET-1, and during intravenous treatment with either EP (40 mg/kg) or placebo, which was administered immediately after the insult. The rats were subjected to transient cerebral ischemia by unilateral microinjection of ET-1 in the piriform cortex, causing vasoconstriction of the medial cerebral artery. Monitoring was continued for 5 h after reperfusion, and levels of endogenous and13C-labeled energy metabolites before and after ischemia-reperfusion were compared in EP-treated and control groups. Infarct volumes were assessed after 24 h. In both the EP-treated and placebo groups, ET-1-induced vasoconstriction resulted in a transient depression of interstitial glucose and elevation of lactate in the ipsilateral striatum. In the reperfusion phase, the concentrations of labeled malate, isocitrate, and lactate as well as endogenous xanthine were significantly higher in the EP-group than in the placebo-group: (mean ± SEM) labeled malate: 39.5% ± 14.9, p = 0.008; labeled isocitrate: 134.8% ± 67.9, p = 0.047; labeled lactate: 61% ± 22.0, p = 0.007; and endogenous xanthine: 93.9% ± 28.3, p = 0.0009. In the placebo group, significantly elevated levels of uridine were observed (mean ± SEM) 32.5% ± 12.7, p = 0.01. Infarct volumes were not significantly different between EP-treated and placebo groups, p = 0.4679. CMD labeled with13 C-succinate enabled detection of ischemic induction and EP treatment effects in the ET-1 rat model of transient focal cerebral ischemia. EP administered as a single intravenous bolus in the reperfusion-phase after transient cerebral ischemia increased de novo synthesis of several key intermediate energy metabolites (13 C-malate,13 C-isocitrate, and endogenous xanthine). In summary, mitochondria process13 C-succinate more effectively after EP treatment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nygaard, Kevin Heebøll","Havelund, Jesper F","Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","Nordström, Carl-Henrik","Færgeman, Nils J.","Poulsen, Frantz Rom","Gramsbergen, Jan Bert","Forsse, Axel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616248"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Forsse, Axel","Færgeman, Nils J.","Gramsbergen, Jan Bert","Havelund, Jesper F","Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","Nordström, Carl-Henrik","Nygaard, Kevin Heebøll","Poulsen, Frantz Rom"],"keyword":["Cerebral metabolism","Liquid chromatography mass spectrometry","Mitochondrial dysfunction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ethyl pyruvate increases post ischemic levels of mitochondrial energy metabolites a sup 000000000013 sup c labeled cerebral microdialysis study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/metabo10070287","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research received financial support from the Lundbeck Foundation—Danish Neurosurgical Society (DNKS) scholarship."],"id":"S01-000.00-616248","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7407637","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85087988514","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32668656","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-964cfa01-9409-4c61-9d59-7dd4c943c300"],"keyword":["Cerebral metabolism","Labeled succinate","Liquid chromatography—mass spectrometry","Mitochondrial dysfunction","Transient ischemia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E5D74BE7E3ADCC4B965418C77FC660B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/metabo10070287","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171437550/metabolites_10_00287_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin H.","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"214161cd-3a84-4d16-b05d-1406c746355d","name":"Nygaard, Kevin Heebøll","name_org":"Nygaard, Kevin H.","orcid":"0000-0002-9205-2005","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper F.","key":"havelundpau","last":"Havelund","locid":"89a02ac8-5f47-4c65-9d0b-1557a63aabf2","name":"Havelund, Jesper F","name_org":"Havelund, Jesper F.","orcid":"0000-0002-9797-5431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"18f40b9c-d8d6-4d6b-b3af-374f6221676a","name":"Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","name_org":"Nielsen, Troels H.","orcid":"0000-0002-3943-8128","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl Henrik","key":"nordströmpau","last":"Nordström","locid":"832530b4-9bf3-4eb3-bbda-ad9fad3cae33","name":"Nordström, Carl-Henrik","name_org":"Nordström, Carl Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nils J.","key":"færgemanpau","last":"Færgeman","locid":"448a164d-523a-4d91-923c-fc5536371b95","name":"Færgeman, Nils J.","orcid":"0000-0002-9281-5287","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frantz R.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"b50645f6-f0c4-4356-9f63-d44290b0dfd9","name":"Poulsen, Frantz Rom","name_org":"Poulsen, Frantz R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5715-6901","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Bert","key":"gramsbergenpau","last":"Gramsbergen","locid":"15eac9a5-253f-41bb-b320-0ae643f4ec30","name":"Gramsbergen, Jan Bert","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"forssepau","last":"Forsse","locid":"110773c8-4c8f-4048-8908-23e7fa21cdb0","name":"Forsse, Axel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32668656"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/metabo10070287","issn":["22181989"],"issue":"7","journal":"Metabolites","paperid":"287","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Metabolites","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087988514"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-964cfa01-9409-4c61-9d59-7dd4c943c300"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ethyl pyruvate increases post-ischemic levels of mitochondrial energy metabolites : A<sup>13</sup>c-labeled cerebral microdialysis study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616248","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper demonstrates the reduction of intra-winding capacitance in a high efficiency copper foil transformer. High efficiency transformer have low ac-resistance and low leakage inductance due to extensive interleaving of the transformer winding. Often high interleaving in a transformer winding leads to an increase in the intra-winding capacitance. This paper analyze how to estimate the intra-winding capacitance in a copper foil transformer. Two transformers are designed for a 2.4 kW, 50 kHz isolated dc-dc converter and presented in this paper. By changing the winding configuration, the intra-winding capacitance of the transformer has been reduced from 692pF to 150pF without increasing the leakage inductance and the ac-resistance. Efficiency measurement for the 2.4 kW converter utilizing the proposed low intra-winding capacitance transformer is also presented in this paper.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ramachandran, Rakesh","Nymand, Morten","Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-625283"],"event":{"acronym":"APEC","end":"2020-03-19","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2020-03-15","title":"35th Annual IEEE Applied Power Electronics Conference and Exposition, APEC 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Capacitance","High efficiency","Isolated DC DC converter","Transformer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis and experimental verification of reducing intra winding capacitance in a copper foil transformer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85087763956","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["ACKNOWLEDGMENT The project is supported by the Innovation Fund Denmark under the project Advanced Power Electronic Technology and Tools (APETT)."],"id":"S01-000.00-625283","identifier":[{"id":"85087763956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b5b957a8-2f1a-4aab-8017-1158b37f09ec"],"keyword":["capacitance","high efficiency","isolated dc-dc converter","transformer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7220F26AAADC6B5DAA55911473602474"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Institute of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, SDU Microelectronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rakesh","key":"ramachandranpau","last":"Ramachandran","locid":"09aad359-07e8-434e-9dc6-a305e06d055b","name":"Ramachandran, Rakesh","orcid":"0000-0003-0487-7857","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"nymandpau","last":"Nymand","locid":"3f0c9441-e312-42bb-bb24-490c2ab76c9d","name":"Nymand, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-1470-5621","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a2c86e37-f396-4b5e-9e63-19af9641cc04","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1469-7684","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/apec39645.2020.9124388","eisbn":["9781728148298","9781728148281"],"isbn":["9781728148304"],"issn":["10482334"],"pages":"2653-2657","publisher":"IEEE","series":"IEEE Applied Power Electronics Conference and Exposition (APEC) Proceedings","status":"p","title":"APEC 2020 - 35th Annual IEEE Applied Power Electronics Conference and Exposition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087763956"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b5b957a8-2f1a-4aab-8017-1158b37f09ec"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Analysis and Experimental Verification of Reducing Intra-winding Capacitance in a Copper Foil Transformer","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-625283","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Obesity is linked to a number of chronic health conditions, such as type 2 diabetes, heart disease, and cancer, and weight loss interventions are often expensive. Recent systematic reviews concluded that app and web-based interventions can improve lifestyle behaviors and weight loss at a reasonable cost, but long-term sustainability needs to be demonstrated. Objective: This study protocol is for a 2-year randomized controlled trial that aims to evaluate the clinical and economic effects of a primary care, anchored, collaborative, electronic health (eHealth) lifestyle coaching program (long-term Lifestyle change InterVention and eHealth Application [LIVA] 2.0) in obese participants with and without type 2 diabetes. The program’s primary outcome is weight loss. Its secondary outcome is the hemoglobin A 1c (HbA 1c) level, and its tertiary outcomes are retention rate, quality of life (QOL), and cost effectiveness. Analytically, the focus is on associations of participant characteristics with outcomes and sustainability. Methods: We conduct a multicenter trial with a 1-year intervention and 1-year retention. LIVA 2.0 is implemented in municipalities within administrative regions in Denmark, specifically eight municipalities located within the Region of Southern Denmark and two municipalities located within the Capital Region of Denmark. The participants are assessed at baseline and at 6-, 12-, and 24-month follow-ups. Individual data from the LIVA 2.0 platform are combined with clinical measurements, questionnaires, and participants’ usage of municipality and health care services. The participants have a BMI ≥30 but ≤45 kg/m2, and 50% of the participants have type 2 diabetes. The participants are randomized in an approximately 60:40 manner, and based on sample size calculations on weight loss and intention-to-treat statistics, 200 participants are randomized to an intervention group and 140 are randomized to a control group. The control group is offered the conventional preventive program of the municipality, and it is compared to the intervention group, which follows the LIVA 2.0 in addition to the conventional preventive program. Results: The first baseline assessments have been carried out in March 2018, and the 2-year follow-up will be carried out between March 2020 and April 2021. The hypothesis is that the trial results will demonstrate decreased body weight and that the number of patients who show normalization of their HbA 1c levels in the intervention group will be much higher than that in the control group. The participants in the intervention group are also expected to show a greater decrease in their use of glucose-lowering medication and a greater improvement in their QOL when compared with the control group. Operational costs are expected to be lower than standard care, and the intervention is expected to be cost-effective. Conclusions: This is the first time that an app and web-based eHealth lifestyle coaching program implemented in Danish municipalities will be clinically and economically evaluated. If the LIVA 2.0 eHealth lifestyle coaching program is proven to be effective, there is great potential for decreasing the rates of obesity, diabetes, and related chronic diseases.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brandt, Carl Joakim","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Lauridsen, Jørgen Trankjær","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Sortsø, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632458"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup"],"keyword":["Digital behavioral coaching","Health Behavior Change","Interactive advice","Lifestyle change","Obesity","Participant engagement","Quality of Life","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of the clinical and economic effects of a primary care anchored collaborative electronic health lifestyle coaching program in denmark protocol for a two year randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/19172","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632458","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7380992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32584260","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091510591","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ceb503d9-923c-46e3-8cef-5a8c2c205324"],"keyword":["Digital behavioral coaching","Health behavior change","Interactive advice","Lifestyle change","Obesity","Participant engagement","Quality of life","Type 2 diabetes management","Weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-40F30A5F9ABE1A3ACC80F3B7ADDD9754"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/173536401/Evaluation_of_the_Clinical_and_Economic_Effects_of_a_Primary_Care.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/19172","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Liva Healthcare"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carl J.","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"75a8dd44-4449-4163-96e5-37499194768e","name":"Brandt, Carl Joakim","name_org":"Brandt, Carl J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3268-0595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Reffstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7b0b955e-4090-479a-8bef-6fd6ad983680","name":"Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2412-5989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen T.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"9282b638-e2b9-44ce-a6f5-d8fa8cfdf674","name":"Lauridsen, Jørgen Trankjær","name_org":"Lauridsen, Jørgen T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9889-6236","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"sortsøpau","last":"Sortsø","name":"Sortsø, Camilla","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32584260"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/19172","issn":["19290748"],"issue":"6","journal":"JMIR Research Protocols","paperid":"e19172","publisher":"JMIR Publications","status":"p","title":"JMIR Research Protocols","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091510591"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","liva healthcare"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ceb503d9-923c-46e3-8cef-5a8c2c205324"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of the Clinical and Economic Effects of a Primary Care Anchored, Collaborative, Electronic Health Lifestyle Coaching Program in Denmark : Protocol for a Two-Year Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-632458","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Deprescribing is of particular importance in older adults with limited life expectancy since this population group is highly susceptible to the potential harms of inappropriate medications. Objective: This systematic review aimed to explore attitudes towards deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives. Methods: A systematic literature review was conducted in the MEDLINE and EMBASE databases from inception to October 2019. Inclusion criteria were studies specifically describing attitudes towards deprescribing among older adults (≥ 65 years) with limited life expectancy and/or their relatives regardless of study type. Results were analyzed, inspired by the Joanna Briggs Institute’s method for synthesis of qualitative data. Results: A total of 842 studies were identified and screened; 84 were full-text assessed for eligibility and 7 were ultimately included. Two studies investigated the attitudes of older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives towards deprescribing of statins and donepezil, respectively, while the five remaining studies related to attitudes towards deprescribing in general. Four main themes were identified: (1) the well-being of older adults with limited life expectancy; (2) involvement of older adults and their relatives in deprescribing; (3) the role of health care professionals in deprescribing; and (4) medication-related factors affecting deprescribing. Within each of these themes, several subthemes were identified. Conclusions: Attitudes towards deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives vary and highlight several barriers and enablers to the deprescribing process. Several of these factors must be addressed to successfully implement deprescribing initiatives in this patient group.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Burghle, Alaa","Lundby, Carina","Ryg, Jesper","Søndergaard, Jens","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","Graabæk, Trine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635790"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Burghle, Alaa"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attitudes towards deprescribing among older adults with limited life expectancy and their relatives a systematic review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086441195","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635790","identifier":[{"id":"32537682","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85086441195","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-da89004c-14d1-41da-9682-4a981fca6f5e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C4275BA2B29DDF85423FDDE2CD92D2EC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["University College Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alaa","key":"burghlepau","la