{"abstract":"Formålet med LULAB-projektet om skrivelaboratorier på læreruddannelsen er at styrke de lærerstuderendes skriftlighed inden for personlig, professionel og akademisk skrivning. Man bliver bedre til at skrive ved at skrive. Derfor er vi optaget af at øve og eksperimentere med skrivning og inddragelse af de studerende i feedbackformer i forskellige læreruddannelsesdidaktiske kontekster både i den konkrete modulundervisning og i forhold til fx modulopgaver, kompetencemålsprøver og bachelorprojekter. En væsentlig intention er at fremme de studerendes refleksive, fortællende og akademiske skrivning med interesse for udvikling af deres skrivelyst og -mod og positive skriveridentitet.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dolmer, Grete","Bock, Anne","Moesgaard, Bente Louise Krogh","Kim, Won-Chung","Hust, Jesper Ejlskov Damborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-661037"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Uddannelse professioner og erhverv"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skrivelaboratorier på læreruddannelsen i via","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.via.dk/-/media/VIA/samarbejde/lulab/dokumenter/lulab-publikation.pdf?la=da&hash=80CB586390A038370422D3381ECC16B1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-661037","ids":["via-da299f3f-601b-4e6b-9007-85eda665f48b"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8E12362F4417C999485917C95ABC6611"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.via.dk/-/media/VIA/samarbejde/lulab/dokumenter/lulab-publikation.pdf?la=da&hash=80CB586390A038370422D3381ECC16B1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Pædagogik og dannelse","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Program for sprog og literacy","VIA, Uddannelser, Læreruddannelsen, HF og FIF-kurser, Læreruddannelsen Aarhus C"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Grete","key":"dolmerpau","last":"Dolmer","locid":"7b422986-fb90-4a15-bab3-68fa8e287925","name":"Dolmer, Grete","orcid":"0000-0002-0422-1922","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"bockpau","last":"Bock","locid":"ba17444f-0bd7-4866-a90e-5ed110781714","name":"Bock, Anne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Louise Krogh","key":"moesgaardpau","last":"Moesgaard","locid":"a4c38443-ee67-4277-8479-ffa04069eb7c","name":"Moesgaard, Bente Louise Krogh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Won-Chung","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","locid":"1ec00f98-49f4-48f4-8eec-5b665d306e61","name":"Kim, Won-Chung","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Ejlskov Damborg","key":"hustpau","last":"Hust","locid":"06a20358-3f94-4f71-9b50-3f056613f8e3","name":"Hust, Jesper Ejlskov Damborg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"lundnielsenpedh","last":"Lund Nielsen","name":"Lund Nielsen, Birgitte","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788797173329"],"pages":"38-47","publisher":"VIA University College","status":"p","title":"Læreruddannelsen i VIA – udviklingslaboratorium for god undervisning og uddannelse"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-da299f3f-601b-4e6b-9007-85eda665f48b"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Skrivelaboratorier på læreruddannelsen i VIA","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-661037","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we study lower bounds for a variant of jumbled-indexing problem: given an input string S on an alphabet Σ = {σ1, . . ., σλ}, store it in a data structure such that given frequencies f1, · · ·, fλ, one can find all the substrings S0 of S where the frequency of the character σi is fi, for 1 ≤ i ≤ λ. This is a very interesting and challenging text indexing problem and it has received significant attention lately, both in the string-indexing community as well as in the theory community. It is known that when λ = 2, one can use a linear-size data structure to decide whether there exists a substring that matches the query in constant time [10]. It is also known [1] that for constant λ ≥ 3, then there exists a constant αλ such that it is not possible to achieve both O(n2−αλ) preprocessing time and O(n1−αλ) query time. We study a variant of the problem where the goal is to report all the substrings of S that match a given jumbled-indexing query. Assuming the data structure operates in the pointer machine model, we prove unconditional space lower bounds that also apply to binary alphabets: we show that if the data structure has the query time of O(n0.5−o(1) + k), where k is the output size of the query, then it must consume Ω(n2−o(1)) space. The o(1) term in our lower bound is at most log(10)1n, where log(·) notation denotes the iterative log function (i.e., log(10) n = log log log log log log log log log log n). This result has a number of interesting consequences. First, it shows that reporting all the matches is significantly harder than deciding whether a match exists, at least for the binary alphabet. This was surprising for us since we believed that in order for jumbled-indexing to be difficult, the alphabet size must be at least 3. Second, from a technical point of view, we make connections between this problem and the area of additive combinatorics as well as random walks. Previously, Chan and Lewenstein [6] had shown the connections between this problem and the area of additive combinatorics from an upper bound point of view, however, we use fundamental theorems from additive combinatorics but these tools are quite different from the theorems used in [6]. In our opinion, the fact that additive combinatorics appears in our lower bound approach as well as in the upper bound approach of Chan and Lewenstein [6] is noteworthy and demands further investigation. We believe our results open up a few new venues for research. For example, we believe it is interesting to study whether it is possible to build a data structure that uses O(n) space s.t., it can report all the matches to a jumble-indexing query in O(n2/3 + k) time; this is even interesting for a binary alphabet.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Afshani, Peyman","Duijn, Ingo van","Killmann, Rasmus","Nielsen, Jesper Sindahl"],"cuid":["S02-095.19-007195"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","end":"2020-01-08","place":"Salt Lake City, us","start":"2020-01-05","title":"31st Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a lower bound for jumbled indexing","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85084060461&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.19-007195","identifier":[{"id":"85084060461","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-94a546ca-0254-4915-bd70-12daa2986cac","au-2846d13c-0c80-4107-aa3e-e7c29765c420"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D635C3F878930B59D63758B543878AA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peyman","key":"afshanipau","last":"Afshani","locid":"83ec0afd-4428-4aaa-b748-9f10e55c98af","name":"Afshani, Peyman","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ingo","key":"vanduijnpau","last":"van Duijn","locid":"3995abc5-b4fe-413e-9eab-e727c9be5992","name":"Duijn, Ingo van","name_org":"van Duijn, Ingo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"killmannpau","last":"Killmann","locid":"5be8226c-b9c6-44ee-add6-cf685ec1a9a9","name":"Killmann, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sindahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b70668c1-8833-4c48-be91-7e3552de7773","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper Sindahl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shuchi","key":"chawlapedh","last":"Chawla","name":"Chawla, Shuchi","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611975994.36","eisbn":["9781611975994"],"pages":"592-606","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"31st Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084060461"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94a546ca-0254-4915-bd70-12daa2986cac","au-2846d13c-0c80-4107-aa3e-e7c29765c420"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A lower bound for jumbled indexing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.19-007195","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Buccal delivery of saquinavir has the advantage to bypass the gastrointestinal enzymatic degradation and the hepatic first-pass metabolism. Saquinavir has a pH-dependent solubility and is poorly soluble in human saliva at the physiological pH. Decreasing microenvironmental pH (pHM) in saliva may increase saquinavir release from buccal formulations. The present study aimed to investigate the effects of organic acids on the pHM, saquinavir release in vitro and the solid-state form of saquinavir. An UV/Vis imaging method was used to measure pHM. After 5 min of swelling of the buccal films containing malic acid, pHM was reduced from 6.8 to 5.4. The films containing malic acid were more efficient in maintaining low pHM than films containing citric acid and succinic acid. Addition of organic acids in the buccal films resulted in a faster drug release than films without acids due to the reduced pHM. However, the enhancement of saquinavir release was limited by the fast release of organic acids. Addition of malic acid and citric acid suppressed the crystallization of saquinavir during 3 months storage at the elevated temperature (40 °C) and humidity (RH 75%) respectively. These results suggest that pHM modifying film is a potential formulation strategy for buccal delivery of saquinavir.","author_count":7,"contributors":["He, Shaolong","Østergaard, Jesper","Ashna, Madina","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","Jacobsen, Jette","Mu, Huiling"],"cuid":["S02-097.51-046142"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Saquinavir","UV Vis imaging","pH modification"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microenvironmental ph modifying films for buccal delivery of saquinavir effects of organic acids on ph and drug release in vitro","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086918269","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.51-046142","identifier":[{"id":"85086918269","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32585177","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c88d61fd-71f6-4041-a14c-53afa41038d6","sdu-716d950b-efce-4d31-9323-fde416033913"],"keyword":["Buccal film","Saquinavir","UV/Vis imaging","pH modification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-49AC65684F0B6509444CD90FC371E47D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Physical and Analytical Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Shaolong","key":"hepau","last":"He","locid":"3964dff7-5e7a-4abb-a7e7-563f17c387ff","name":"He, Shaolong","orcid":"0000-0002-1533-6936","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Madina","key":"ashnapau","last":"Ashna","name":"Ashna, Madina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"uhdnielsenpau","last":"Uhd Nielsen","locid":"69a90973-6315-4248-a49e-c6e0413b526a","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","name_org":"Uhd Nielsen, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-5776-6865","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten Uhd","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"d0f28d95-ba86-4570-9caa-2f4b1f70fe27","name":"Jacobsen, Jette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Huiling","key":"mupau","last":"Mu","locid":"f112da1b-f1ab-4891-bf6a-3c799d71d4cc","name":"Mu, Huiling","orcid":"0000-0001-9246-3931","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32585177"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijpharm.2020.119567","issn":["03785173","18733476"],"issn_org":["03785173"],"journal":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","paperid":"119567","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","volume":"585"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086918269"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c88d61fd-71f6-4041-a14c-53afa41038d6","sdu-716d950b-efce-4d31-9323-fde416033913"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Microenvironmental pH modifying films for buccal delivery of saquinavir : Effects of organic acids on pH and drug release in vitro","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.51-046142","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To reveal the phenotypic differences between human ocular surface stromal cells (hOSSCs) cultured from the corneal, limbal, and scleral compartments. Methods: A comparative analysis of cultured hOSSCs derived from four unrelated donors was conducted by multichromatic flow cytometry for six distinct CD antigens, including the CD73, CD90, CD105, CD166, CD146, and CD34. Results: The hOSSCs, as well as the reference cells, displayed phenotypical profiles that were similar in high expression of the hallmark mesenchymal stem cell markers CD73, CD90, and CD105, and also the cancer stem cell marker CD166. Notably, there was considerable variation regarding the expression of CD34, where the highest levels were found in the corneal and scleral compartments. The multi-differentiation potential marker CD146 was also expressed highly variably, ranging from 9% to 89%, but the limbal stromal and endometrial mesenchymal stem cells significantly surpassed their counterparts within the ocular and reference groups, respectively. The use of six markers enabled investigation of 64 possible variants, however, just four variants accounted for almost 90% of all hOSSCs, with the co-expression of CD73, CD90, CD105, and CD166 and a combination of CD146 and CD34. The limbal compartment appeared unique in that it displayed greatest immunophenotype diversity and harbored the highest proportion of the CD146+CD34- pericyte-like forms, but, interestingly, the pericyte-like cells were also found in the avascular cornea. Conclusions: Our findings confirm that the hOSSCs exhibit an immunophenotype consistent with that of MSCs, further highlight the phenotypical heterogeneity in stroma from distinct ocular surface compartments, and finally underscore the uniqueness of the limbal region.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Liu, Lei","Yu, Ying","Peng, Qiuyue","Porsborg, Simone Riis","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Jørgensen, Annemette","Grove, Anni","Søndergaard, Chris Bath","Hjortdal, Jesper","Christiansen, Ole Bjarne","Fink, Trine","Zachar, Vladimir"],"cuid":["S02-099.63-001363"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jilin University","The First Bethune Hospital of Jilin University"],"keyword":["CD146","CD34","Flow Cytometry","Human Ocular Surface Stromal Cells","Pericytes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distribution of stromal cell subsets in cultures from distinct ocular surface compartments","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18502/jovr.v15i4.7780","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.63-001363","identifier":[{"id":"33133440","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85095715849","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7591840","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-1ad0b378-6f2f-49fe-8fba-58aff132a42c","au-a48b5092-e398-4ded-9fdd-e0aaac5547f4"],"keyword":["CD146","CD34","Flow Cytometry","Human Ocular Surface Stromal Cells","Pericytes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C71EA1B21DBBB119588C7228E14C22A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18502/jovr.v15i4.7780","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/386843948/7780_Main_Text_34387_1_10_20201025.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities",