name":"Zachar, Vladimir","orcid":"0000-0002-5279-2690","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33133440"],"pub":{"doi":"10.18502/jovr.v15i4.7780","issn":["20082010","2008322X"],"issn_org":["20082010"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Ophthalmic and Vision Research","pages":"493-501","publisher":"Knowledge E","status":"p","title":"Journal of Ophthalmic and Vision Research","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85095715849"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1ad0b378-6f2f-49fe-8fba-58aff132a42c","au-a48b5092-e398-4ded-9fdd-e0aaac5547f4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Distribution of Stromal Cell Subsets in Cultures from Distinct Ocular Surface Compartments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.63-001363","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The objective of this cross-sectional case-control study was to determine the prevalence and size of marginal and subarticular osteophytes in patients with osteoarthritis (OA), and to compare these to that of a control group. DESIGN: We investigated femoral heads from 25 patients with OA following hip replacement surgery, and 25 femoral heads from a control group obtained post-mortem. The area and boundary length of the femoral head, marginal osteophytes, and subarticular osteophytes were determined with histomorphometry. Marginal osteophytes were defined histologically as bony projections at the peripheral margin of the femoral head, while subarticular osteophytes were defined as areas of bone that expanded from the normal curvature of the femoral head into the articular cartilage. RESULTS: The prevalence of OA patients with marginal- and subarticular osteophytes were 100 and 84%, respectively. Whereas the prevalence of the participants in the control group with marginal- and subarticular osteophytes were 56 and 28%, respectively. The area and boundary length of marginal osteophytes was (median (Interquartile range)) 165.3mm2 (121.4-254.0) mm2 and 75.1 mm (50.8-99.3) mm for patients with OA compared to 0 mm2 (0-0.5) mm2 and 0 mm (0-0.5) mm for the control group (P <  0.001). For the subarticular osteophytes, the area and boundary length was 1.0 mm2 (0-4.4) mm2 and 1.4 mm (0-6.5) mm for patients with OA compared to 0 mm2 (0-0.5) mm2 and 0 mm (0-0.5) mm for the control group (P <  0.001). CONCLUSION: As expected, both marginal- and subarticular osteophytes at the femoral head, were more frequent and larger in patients with OA than in the control group. However, in the control group, subarticular osteophytes were more prevalent than expected from the minor osteophytic changes at the femoral head margin, which may suggest that subarticular osteophytes are an early degenerative phenomenon that ultimately might develop into clinical osteoarthritis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Klose-Jensen, Rasmus","Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","Hartlev, Louise Brøndt","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","Laursen, Mogens Berg","Keller, Kresten Krarup","Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe"],"cuid":["S02-099.69-007303"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Klose-Jensen, Rasmus"],"keyword":["Femoral head","Osteoarthritis","Osteophytes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histomorphometric case control study of subarticular osteophytes in patients with osteoarthritis of the hip","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-020-03648-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.69-007303","identifier":[{"id":"85092509375","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7542119","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33023570","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-96bb6d54-9370-49dd-8b09-e1c0abf1f642","au-07b19bf3-2e93-404a-9db0-80197d7dad71"],"keyword":["Femoral head","Osteoarthritis","Osteophytes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6250E01050E078107B8D67DA83394EBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-020-03648-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/381877149/Klose_Jensen_et_al_2020_Histomorphometric_case_control_study_of_subarticular_osteophytes_in_patients_with_osteoarthritis_of_the_hip.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Section for Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"klosejensenpau","last":"Klose-Jensen","locid":"23dd4b1b-5313-4ad6-8e33-00476fc5d97e","name":"Klose-Jensen, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas Wiggers","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dc3ce48a-c47a-46ef-beac-360aec95aacc","name":"Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","orcid":"0000-0001-8180-6871","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Brøndt","key":"hartlevpau","last":"Hartlev","locid":"ff30b23b-e653-4cd0-902c-04cb78f756cf","name":"Hartlev, Louise Brøndt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Skovhus","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"924ef2ac-827c-4260-9cd7-fbe300bbafeb","name":"Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0001-9386-6679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Warner Thorup","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"cf69d33f-562c-489b-9564-9a9dc15c0a16","name":"Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"26102317-00ee-41ec-ae85-c7a3bde4c391","name":"Laursen, Mogens Berg","name_org":"Laursen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-2791-3921","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kresten Krarup","key":"kellerpau","last":"Keller","locid":"a13c7405-9555-41cf-9bc3-311bb925bb9c","name":"Keller, Kresten Krarup","orcid":"0000-0003-2474-3389","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen Margrethe","key":"haugepau","last":"Hauge","locid":"6e0e979f-48d6-40bd-89ec-a2502b1cefd4","name":"Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33023570"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12891-020-03648-w","issn":["14712474"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","paperid":"653","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092509375"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-96bb6d54-9370-49dd-8b09-e1c0abf1f642","au-07b19bf3-2e93-404a-9db0-80197d7dad71"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Histomorphometric case-control study of subarticular osteophytes in patients with osteoarthritis of the hip","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.69-007303","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Data elucidating trends of community-onset extended-spectrum β-lactamase (ESBL)-producing Escherichia coli and Klebsiella pneumoniae infections remain sparse in low prevalence areas. We conducted a population-based study to determine the incidence, temporal trends and co-resistance of community-onset ESBL infections. Methods: We identified all recorded episodes of E. coli and K. pneumoniae bacteraemia and urinary tract infections in adult patients (>15 years) in the North Denmark Region between 2007–2017. Using population-based registries, we obtained information on demographics and place of acquisition, and investigated the standardized incidence rates and temporal trends of community-onset ESBL infections and the associated patterns of co-resistance. Results: A total of 3741 episodes of community-onset ESBL E. coli or K. pneumoniae infections were observed during the study period, with the annual standardized incidence rate increasing from 7.5 to 105 per 100,000 person-years between 2007–2017. The increase was conveyed primarily by a rise in E. coli urinary tract infections shifting from being mainly healthcare-associated to community-acquired. ESBL-producing isolates increased from 0.5 to 4.0% with considerable co-resistance. Conclusion: The proportion of E. coli and K. pneumoniae isolates producing ESBL have increased considerably in the North Denmark Region. The increasing incidence and frequent co-resistance should raise awareness among physicians responsible for empirical antibiotic treatment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Richelsen, Rasmus","Smit, Jesper","Anru, Pavithra Laxsen","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-006890"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bacteraemia","Escherichia coli","Extended spectrum β lactamase","Incidence","Population","Urinary tract infection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence of community onset extended spectrum β lactamase producing escherichia coli and klebsiella pneumoniae infections an 000000000011 year population based study in denmark","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085322020","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-006890","identifier":[{"id":"85085322020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32401562","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8e1dfe9f-8bb7-44ae-8cdd-a30fa4bf60cc","sdu-f41da6bb-51a7-4deb-acdb-8f082b8d5412"],"keyword":["Escherichia coli","Extended-spectrum β-lactamase","bacteraemia","incidence","population","urinary tract infection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C257EEC7FE527DC74F6AEEB916DA685F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Epidemiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"richelsenpau","last":"Richelsen","locid":"fc616b60-585b-4b71-abf7-5d2617983656","name":"Richelsen, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"smitpau","last":"Smit","locid":"29aa2e66-1f20-4693-9114-5f988949c879","name":"Smit, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pavithra Laxsen","key":"anrupau","last":"Anru","locid":"b2416d40-ddd8-4f61-9287-09274f0e5588","name":"Anru, Pavithra Laxsen","orcid":"0000-0002-7046-2556","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Carl","key":"schønheyderpau","last":"Schønheyder","locid":"d35b264a-6efc-467d-ac9d-e558542ef8a8","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32401562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/23744235.2020.1763452","issn":["23744235","23744243"],"issn_org":["23744235"],"issue":"8","journal":"Infectious Diseases","pages":"547-556","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Infectious Diseases","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085322020"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8e1dfe9f-8bb7-44ae-8cdd-a30fa4bf60cc","sdu-f41da6bb-51a7-4deb-acdb-8f082b8d5412"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Incidence of community-onset extended-spectrum β-lactamase-producing Escherichia coli and Klebsiella pneumoniae infections : an 11-year population-based study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-006890","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Our aim was to evaluate the interobserver agreement in 18F-sodium fluoride (NaF) PET/CT for the detection of bone metastases in patients with prostate cancer (PCa). Methods: 18F-NaF PET/CT scans were retrieved from all patients who participated in 4 recent prospective trials. Two experienced observers independently evaluated the 18F-NaF PET/CT scans on a patient level using a 3-category scale (no bone metastases [M0], equivocal for bone metastases, and bone metastases present [M1]) and on a dichotomous scale (M0/M1). In patients with no more than 10 lesions, the location and number of lesions were recorded. On a patient level, the diagnostic performance was calculated using a sensitivity analysis, in which equivocal lesions were handled as M0 as well as M1. Results: 18F-NaF PET/CT scans from 219 patients with PCa were included, of whom 129 patients were scanned for primary staging, 67 for biochemical recurrence, and 23 for metastatic castration-resistant PCa. Agreement between the observers was almost perfect on a patient level (3-category unweighted κ = 0.83 ± 0.05, linear weighted κ = 0.90 ± 0.06, and dichotomous κ = 0.91 ± 0.07). On a lesion level (dichotomous scale), the observers agreed on the number and location of bone metastases in 205 (93.6%) patients. In the remaining 14 patients, the readers disagreed on the number of lesions in 13 patients and the location of bone metastases in 1 patient. A final diagnosis of bone metastases was made for 211 of 219 patients. The sensitivity ranged from 0.86 to 0.92, specificity from 0.83 to 0.97, positive predictive value from 0.70 to 0.93, and negative predictive value from 0.94 to 0.96. Conclusion: The interobserver agreement on 18F-NaF PET/CT for the detection of bone metastases in patients with PCa was very high among trained observers, both on a patient level and on a lesion level. Moreover, the diagnostic performance of 18F-NaF PET/CT was satisfactory, rendering 18F-NaF PET/CT a robust tool in the diagnostic armamentarium.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zacho, Helle D","Fonager, Randi F.","Nielsen, Julie B","Haarmark, Christian","Hendel, Helle W","Johansen, Martin Berg","Mortensen, Jesper C","Petersen, Lars Jelstrup"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-004390"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms diagnostic imaging","Bone metastases","Fluorine Radioisotopes","Humans","Interobserver agreement","Male","Middle Aged","Observer Variation","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Prostate cancer","Prostatic Neoplasms pathology","Sensitivity and Specificity","Sodium Fluoride","Value"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"observer agreement and accuracy of sup 000000000018 sup f sodium fluoride pet ct in the diagnosis of bone metastases in prostate cancer","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7067525/pdf/jnm232686.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-004390","identifier":[{"id":"31481577","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85081136167","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7067525","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-59e85fcf-3776-4ebc-84f9-8bfa88890a26","ku-11f451cc-6709-4793-8ec8-df2adb372c62"],"keyword":["18F-sodium-fluoride PET/CT","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms/diagnostic imaging","Fluorine Radioisotopes","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Observer Variation","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Prostatic Neoplasms/pathology","Sensitivity and Specificity","Sodium Fluoride","bone metastases","interobserver agreement","prostate cancer","κ value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D6A85D5ADFC26092DBA14689AF9E3F75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7067525/pdf/jnm232686.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Clinical Cancer Research Center","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nuclear Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle D","key":"zachopau","last":"Zacho","locid":"951a4739-b06e-45ad-a483-c09697db4ceb","name":"Zacho, Helle D","orcid":"0000-0001-9089-288X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Randi F","key":"fonagerpau","last":"Fonager","locid":"745bed97-ed5d-49af-8866-d1f03963cd4f","name":"Fonager, Randi F.","name_org":"Fonager, Randi F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5c62fe4c-be01-4494-a214-84503b6a7e3a","name":"Nielsen, Julie B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"haarmarkpau","last":"Haarmark","name":"Haarmark, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Helle W","key":"hendelpau","last":"Hendel","locid":"0ed6dd56-8353-40da-a0d8-b1bd06e37567","name":"Hendel, Helle Westergren","name_org":"Hendel, Helle W","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin B","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"bbd320a7-9c17-4062-a6d9-76a1bbed24bf","name":"Johansen, Martin Berg","name_org":"Johansen, Martin B","orcid":"0000-0001-9790-0985","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper C","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Jesper C","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars J","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"e5cf5f25-4cff-407e-9c25-97921d98a7bc","name":"Petersen, Lars Jelstrup","name_org":"Petersen, Lars J","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31481577"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2967/jnumed.119.232686","issn":["01615505","15355667"],"issn_org":["01615505"],"issue":"3","journal":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","pages":"344-349","publisher":"Society of Nuclear Medicine Inc.","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","title_org":"Journal of Nuclear Medicine","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081136167"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-59e85fcf-3776-4ebc-84f9-8bfa88890a26","ku-11f451cc-6709-4793-8ec8-df2adb372c62"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Observer Agreement and Accuracy of <sup>18</sup>F-Sodium Fluoride PET/CT in the Diagnosis of Bone Metastases in Prostate Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-004390","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Total knee arthroplasty (TKA) is considered an effective treatment for pain relief and improved physical performances in end-stage knee osteoarthritis. However, several studies have reported less favorable outcomes after TKA with chronic pain rates of approximately 20%. Exercise might be an effective treatment strategy for chronic pain following TKA, but no randomized controlled trials have evaluated its effect. Therefore, the purpose of this randomized controlled trial is to investigate whether a 12-week neuromuscular exercise (NEuroMuscular EXercise training program for patients with knee or hip osteoarthritis assigned for total joint replacement; NEMEX-TJR) program combined with pain neuroscience education (PNE) provides greater pain relief and improvement in physical performances than PNE alone at 12 months follow-up in a population of patients with chronic pain after primary TKA. METHODS: For this randomized controlled superiority trial, 120 patients with moderate-to-severe chronic pain after TKA are recruited from Aalborg University Hospital, Denmark. Patients are randomly assigned in a 1:1 ratio to one of two interventions: (a) NEMEX-TJR twice weekly for 12 weeks combined with two sessions of PNE or (b) two sessions of PNE given over 6 weeks. Assessment is performed at baseline before intervention and at 3, 6, and 12 months after initiation of the intervention. Outcome assessors are blinded toward group allocation. The primary outcome is the change in the Knee Injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score4 (KOOS4), defined as the mean score for the KOOS subscales pain, symptoms, activities of daily living, and quality of life. Secondary outcomes include all KOOS subscale scores and scores for PainDETECT, the Fear-Avoidance Beliefs Questionnaire, Global Perceived Effect, the Pain Catastrophizing Scale, pain intensities, temporal summation, conditioned pain modulation, and pressure pain thresholds. Physical performances are measured with walking, stair climbing, and chair standing tests as well as tests of muscle strength and power. DISCUSSION: The findings will be useful in establishing effective treatment strategies for chronic pain after TKA. The randomized controlled trial involves rigorous scientific methods and uses clinically applicable interventions. The study interventions are conducted in clinical settings, thereby enhancing the possibility of future implementation of the treatments in the health care systems. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT03886259. Registered 22 March 2019. Ethics committee registration: N-20180046.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper Bie","Skou, Søren T","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Simonsen, Ole","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000464"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chronic pain","Neuromuscular exercise","Pain neuroscience education","Total knee replacement"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education compared with pain neuroscience education alone in patients with chronic pain after primary total knee arthroplasty study protocol for the nepnep randomized controlled trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-020-4126-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-000464","identifier":[{"id":"85082147316","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32197629","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7083002","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-08e5d943-60ac-44d6-8835-ccd077e0453c","sdu-f7e29394-bde0-414f-9b9f-9c8500d5df92"],"keyword":["Chronic pain","Neuromuscular exercise","Pain neuroscience education","Total knee replacement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-02BDF8C39A64CBC4D5C757C00F9E58DF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/329817134/document_10_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-020-4126-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/168923797/s13063_020_4126_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"16d35f43-63eb-473e-a466-4f5a12d5f43f","name":"Larsen, Jesper Bie","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-7913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren T","key":"skoupau","last":"Skou","locid":"656a59cf-32bc-4190-b072-4adf47d954c1","name":"Skou, Søren Thorgaard","name_org":"Skou, Søren T","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"dc7f061c-65a2-47fc-901a-38fac8019f1f","name":"Simonsen, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32197629"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-020-4126-5","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"issue":"1","journal":"Trials","paperid":"218","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082147316"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-08e5d943-60ac-44d6-8835-ccd077e0453c","sdu-f7e29394-bde0-414f-9b9f-9c8500d5df92"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education compared with pain neuroscience education alone in patients with chronic pain after primary total knee arthroplasty : study protocol for the NEPNEP randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-000464","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The control of ankle muscle force is an integral component of walking and postural control. Aging impairs the ability to produce force steadily and accurately, which can compromise functional capacity and quality of life. Here, we hypothesized that reduced force control in older adults would be associated with altered cortico-cortical communication within a network comprising the primary motor area (M1), the premotor cortex (PMC), parietal, and prefrontal regions. We examined electroencephalographic (EEG) responses from fifteen younger (20–26 yr) and fifteen older (65–73 yr) participants during a unilateral dorsiflexion force-tracing task. Dynamic Causal Modelling (DCM) and Parametric Empirical Bayes (PEB) were used to investigate how directed connectivity between contralateral M1, PMC, parietal, and prefrontal regions was related to age group and precision in force production. DCM and PEB analyses revealed that the strength of connections between PMC and M1 were related to ankle force precision and differed by age group. For young adults, bidirectional PMC-M1 coupling was negatively related to task performance: stronger backward M1-PMC and forward PMC-M1 coupling was associated with worse force precision. The older group exhibited deviations from this pattern. For the PMC to M1 coupling, there were no age-group differences in coupling strength; however, within the older group, stronger coupling was associated with better performance. For the M1 to PMC coupling, older adults followed the same pattern as young adults - with stronger coupling accompanied by worse performance - but coupling strength was lower than in the young group. Our results suggest that bidirectional M1-PMC communication is related to precision in ankle force production and that this relationship changes with aging. We argue that the observed differences reflect compensatory reorganization that counteracts age-related sensorimotor declines and contributes to maintaining performance.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Beck, Mikkel Malling","Christensen, Mark Schram","Dietz, Martin","Karabanov, Anke Ninija","Geertsen, Svend Sparre","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014992"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Ageing","Aging","Connectivity","DCM","EEG","Faculty of Science","Motor system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Elsass Institute, Charlottenlund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"directed connectivity between primary and premotor areas underlying ankle force control in young and older adults","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.116982","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-014992","identifier":[{"id":"85085945125","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32450250","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-20d16297-4ed5-493a-8339-1519e08abacb","ku-d09b1a23-73c8-4a13-88b0-fdb36e143291"],"keyword":["Ageing","Aging","Connectivity","DCM","EEG","Faculty of Science","Motor system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-71F417362446994B6C2CEF4AA0A3E95E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.116982","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/244083636/Directed_connectivity_between_primary_and_premotor_areas_underlying_ankle_force_control_in_young_and_older_adults.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised",