esponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"kristiansenkristianpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Kristian","rank":87,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32939067"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-020-2688-8","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7825","journal":"Nature","pages":"390-396","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"585"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091129874"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-778b3b91-27ef-4e2c-aad7-ed0421e0e6e1","dtu-0ae314d8-3cae-4be5-aa11-60a43e069920","ku-086ea951-1ff7-4440-8203-9f99493d1404","kum-7676ac2a-4676-46b2-ab01-84851f2058be","sdu-e91a6ec4-90a1-4c53-b09a-911db76d343d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Population genomics of the Viking world","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-095.94-021408","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Infiltration excess runoff, i.e., runoff as a result of the rainfall intensity exceeding the infiltration capacity of the soil surface, has traditionally been considered the only contributor to the surface runoff from urban pervious areas. However, recent studies show that subsurface throughflow also can be a significant contributor to urban stormwater runoff. Although rainfall-runoff from urban pervious areas can contribute with large quantities of runoff, only little knowledge exists on this topic. In this study, experimental field observations of subsurface throughflow from the literature are used to assess the capability of different models to simulate this type of runoff. It is investigated how well three new modeling approaches in urban drainage engineering (linear reservoir, regression, and shallow neural network models) performs in simulating subsurface throughflow compared to two commonly used models (the time-area and kinematic wave model). The models are compared with the measured runoff rate and evaluated by the root mean square error (RMSE), Nash-Sutcliffe efficiency (NSE), and Bayesian likelihood (L). Generally, a neural network containing 60 neurons and using up to 180 min of data back in time produces the best results (RMSE=0.59 Lmin-1, NSE=0.91, and L=0.92). However, both the kinematic wave (RMSE=1.06 L min-1, NSE=0.71, and L=0.76) and linear reservoir model (RMSE=0.98 L min-1, NSE=0.75, and L=0.78) generate reasonable results despite their significantly simpler modeling approaches.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Kristoffer","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Uggerby, Mads","Rasmussen, Michael R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076787"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Kristoffer"],"keyword":["Linear reservoir model Kinematic wave","Neural network","Pervious surfaces","Stormwater runoff","Subsurface throughflow","Urban drainage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling of subsurface throughflow in urban pervious areas","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1061/(ASCE)HE.1943-5584.0001990","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was partially funded by The Foundation for Development of Technology in the Danish Water Sector, the Innovation Fund Denmark, Aarhus Vand, EnviDan A/S, and Aalborg University."],"id":"S01-000.00-076787","identifier":[{"id":"85091480135","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5c1aeca5-a462-4931-afe1-f766663a3cb1"],"keyword":["Linear reservoir model Kinematic wave","Neural network","Pervious surfaces","Stormwater runoff","Subsurface throughflow","Urban drainage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CE0D862B5C741FC87EA71E0E7C73A04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/402003470/_ASCE_HE.1943_5584.0001990.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1061/(ASCE)HE.1943-5584.0001990","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Water and Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Envidan A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer T.","key":"nielsenkristofferpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"11dec065-32b9-41f9-b675-c73b37df10de","name":"Nielsen, Kristoffer","name_org":"Nielsen, Kristoffer T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper E.","key":"nielsenjesperellerbækpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper E.","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"uggerbymadspau","last":"Uggerby","name":"Uggerby, Mads","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael R.","key":"rasmussenmichaelrpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1061/(asce)he.1943-5584.0001990","issn":["10840699","19435584"],"issn_org":["10840699"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Hydrologic Engineering","paperid":"04020050","publisher":"American Society of Civil Engineers (ASCE)","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hydrologic Engineering","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091480135"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","envidan a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5c1aeca5-a462-4931-afe1-f766663a3cb1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling of Subsurface Throughflow in Urban Pervious Areas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076787","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim of this study was to investigate the procedural efficacy and safety of the novel Watchman FLX (Boston Scientific, Marlborough, Massachusetts) device for left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) and to assess the feasibility of intracardiac echocardiography (ICE) to guide implantation. Background: The Watchman FLX device for transcatheter LAAO was introduced for a simplified implantation in a wider range of LAA anatomies. Methods: This single-center study included consecutive patients undergoing LAAO with the Watchman FLX between March 2019 and January 2020 (N = 91). Patients underwent cardiac computed tomography (CT) imaging for pre-procedural planning. Initial procedures were guided by transesophageal echocardiography (TEE; n = 8) and thereafter by ICE (n = 83) from the left atrium. TEE and cardiac CT imaging were performed at 8 weeks’ follow-up. Results: Technical success was achieved in 90 (99%) patients, with the first device implanted in 86 (96%) procedures. Procedural success was 93.4%. Peri-procedural complications occurred in 5 (5.5%), with pericardial effusion being the most common (2.2%). Only 3.3% had a peri-device leak on TEE follow-up. No device-related thrombosis occurred. The mean device compression rate at end of procedure was 18.3 ± 7.7%, compared with 12.2 ± 7.8% by TEE at 8 weeks’ follow-up (p < 0.001) and 5.8 ± 8.8% by cardiac CT imaging at follow-up (p < 0.001). Conclusions: The Watchman FLX device was suitable for closure of a wide range of LAA anatomies, including shallow appendages. The follow-up closure rate was higher than previously reported with other devices. ICE from the left atrium was used, with high procedural success and a low complication rate, comparable to previous studies on LAAO.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Korsholm, Kasper","Samaras, Athanasios","Andersen, Asger","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146146"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"keyword":["Clinical research","LAA closure","other imaging modalities"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the watchman flx device first european experience and feasibility of intracardiac echocardiography to guide implantation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090481761","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146146","identifier":[{"id":"33334441","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090481761","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1d622e85-2ddf-4539-b6a1-0918f1833719"],"keyword":["LAA closure","clinical research","other imaging modalities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7D809C62E4C09A0EB9F16D3FB456157"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Athanasios","key":"samaraspau","last":"Samaras","locid":"6a4a79d3-94eb-48b5-9e1f-87718ebe5376","name":"Samaras, Athanasios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a87aec57-562e-4950-b4cf-6741aae86cf1","name":"Andersen, Asger","orcid":"0000-0002-9102-3130","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33334441"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacep.2020.06.028","issn":["2405500X"],"issue":"13","journal":"JACC: Clinical Electrophysiology","pages":"1633-1642","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Clinical Electrophysiology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090481761"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1d622e85-2ddf-4539-b6a1-0918f1833719"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Watchman FLX Device : First European Experience and Feasibility of Intracardiac Echocardiography to Guide Implantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146146","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Perioperative mortality and morbidity remain substantial in acute surgery. Risk factors include known cardiovascular disease, but preoperative screening is insensitive to occult cardiopulmonary conditions. Focused cardiac ultrasound (FOCUS) can disclose both structural and functional cardiac disease and provides insight into the patient’s haemodynamic status. This study aims to clarify whether preoperative FOCUS changes clinical outcomes in high-risk patients. Methods: This is a multi-centre, randomised, controlled, prospective study including patients ≥ 65 years of age scheduled for acute/emergency abdominal-or orthopaedic surgery. A total of 800 patients will be randomised to ± application of preoperative FOCUS. The primary endpoint is the proportion of patients admitted to hospital > 10 days or death within 30 days of surgery. The secondary endpoints include changes in the anaesthesia approach facilitated by FOCUS, biomarkers of organ function and perioperative complications. Conclusions: The knowledge generated from this study may facilitate changes in the anaesthesia evaluation and decision process and, consequently, in the entire perioperative anaesthesia clinical practice. The study has the potential to reduce the risk of perioperative cardiopulmonary complications which directly implies improved patient outcome and reduced hospital costs.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Pallesen, Jan","Bhavsar, Rajesh","Fjølner, Jesper","Krog, Jan","Malachauskiené, Laima","Bakke, Skule Arnesen","Andersen, Mikkel Strømgaard","Vang, Marianne L.","Andersen, Jakob Keller","Bøndergaard, Michael Helbo","Jessing, Thomas Damgaard","Thee, Carsten","Mortensen, Lone","Nielsen, Michael Bugge","Juhl-Olsen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177197"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of preoperative point of care focused cardiac ultrasound in high risk patients study protocol for a prospective randomised controlled trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85077639297","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177197","identifier":[{"id":"31908251","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077639297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-53ea3fd2-5dbd-406e-a356-b9f55a76afd7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7F224FEB5B00B911EE143C66D18BC370"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anæstesiologisk afdeling, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Hospital of Southern Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"pallesenjanpau","last":"Pallesen","locid":"a8619a0b-c0f7-4d27-ae7c-51b780623ee3","name":"Pallesen, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rajesh","key":"bhavsarrajeshpau","last":"Bhavsar","name":"Bhavsar, Rajesh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"c