of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4ff1457b-9469-47a8-860d-9e9e407bb061"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coronary CT Angiography in Patients With Non-ST-Segment Elevation Acute Coronary Syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-441180","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"On/off patch spraying based on weed maps is used in site-specific weed management. Two prerequisites for realising patch spraying are accurate weed detection and targeting of the herbicides on weed patches. There is plenty in the literature about weed detection, but little attention has been paid to the spatial accuracy of herbicide application. This study was conducted in order to assess the extent to which patch-sprayed herbicides are targeted precisely according to pre-loaded prescription maps and to evaluate a new spatial assessment method. The new method consisted of spraying with red Ponceau 4R dye, unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) imagery and spatial image analysis based on a geographic information system (GIS). The sprayed dye was clearly visible in aereal images and the locations of the sprayed areas were compared with the locations given by the prescription maps. Four different commercial sprayers with boom section width in the range of 0.5 to 3 m and driving speed in the range of 2.5 to 8 km h−1 were used in ten experiments. All the experiments were carried out in autumn in stubble fields. The results showed that the new method was fast and reliable. The incorrectly sprayed area outside targeted areas on prescription maps averaged 81% for three different sprayers with 3 m boom sections, and 5% for a sprayer with 0.5 m boom sections (individual spray nozzle control). The target areas not sprayed within the planned weed patch areas averaged 6% of the pre-defined patch area for sprayers with 3 m boom sections, and 14% for the sprayer with 0.5 m boom sections. This study revealed that the sprayer with 0.5 m boom sections had a controller that was not quick enough at opening and closing spray nozzles at normal driving speeds. Log files from the sprayer console overestimated the sprayed area by 24% and were less accurate than the spatial analysis of the sprayed areas.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Azim, Saiful","Nielsen, Jon","Mikkelsen, Birgitte Feld","Hørfarter, Rita","Christensen, Svend"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458886"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a new method to estimate the spatial correlation between planned and actual patch spraying of herbicides","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-458886","identifier":[{"id":"85074595454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6d96981a-809c-48f2-bf46-7ec030c7c68a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-303272A132B35029AD432E3CDC561DE6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["AgroTech AS"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["Seges P/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Saiful","key":"azimpau","last":"Azim","locid":"6fdcaa54-993e-45e1-9976-cfd74fac0c12","name":"Azim, Saiful","orcid":"0000-0002-2686-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d45561f-3e81-41e1-8310-03bdb7abbad0","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birgitte Feld","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Birgitte Feld","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rita","key":"hørfarterpau","last":"Hørfarter","name":"Hørfarter, Rita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c284dfaf-4015-461e-9604-bef890d95acb","name":"Christensen, Svend","orcid":"0000-0002-1112-1954","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11119-019-09691-5","issn":["13852256","15731618"],"issn_org":["15731618"],"journal":"Precision Agriculture","pages":"713-728","status":"p","title":"Precision Agriculture","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074595454"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6d96981a-809c-48f2-bf46-7ec030c7c68a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A new method to estimate the spatial correlation between planned and actual patch spraying of herbicides","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458886","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"B29N(epsilon)-lithocholyl-gamma-L-beta Glu-desB30 human insulin [NN344] belongs to a group of insulins with fatty acid or sterol modifications. These insulin analogues have been found to form subcutaneous depots upon injection and hereby have a protracted release profile in vivo. In the present study, B29N(epsilon)-lithocholyl-gamma-L-Glu-desB30 human insulin was investigated using in-solution small-angle X-ray scattering (SAXS) at chemical conditions designed to mimic three stages during treatment in vivo: in-vial/pen, postinjection, and longer times after injection. We found that the specific insulin analogue formed a mixture of mono- and dihexamers under in-vial/pen conditions of low salt and stabilizing phenol. At postinjection, conditions mimicking a subcutaneous depot, B29N(epsilon)-lithocholyl-gamma-L-Glu-desB30 human insulin, formed very long straight soluble hexamer-based rods stacked along the Zn(II)-axis. The self-assembly was triggered by an increase in salt concentration when going from vial to physiological conditions. Mimicking longer times after injection and the additional removal of phenol caused the length of the rods to decrease significantly. Finally, we found that the self-assembly could be controlled by varying the amount of modification at the interaction interface by making mixed hexamers of B29N(epsilon)-lithocholyl-gamma-L-Glu-desB30 and desB30 human insulin. This opens extra possibilities for controlling the release profile of very-long-acting insulins.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dreyer, Lasse Sander","Nygaard, Jesper","Malik, Leila","Hoeg-Jensen, Thomas","Hoiberg-Nielsen, Rasmus","Arleth, Lise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Degludec","Detemir","Insulin","Mechanism","Oligomer","PROTRACTION","SAXS","Self assembly"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural insight into the self assembly of a pharmaceutically optimized insulin analogue obtained by small angle x ray scattering","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-543069","identifier":[{"id":"000558726700005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85089613457","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32579369","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fab0e603-deb6-4ae2-aafa-296095a2225f"],"keyword":["DEGLUDEC","DETEMIR","MECHANISM","MONOMERIC INSULINS","PROTRACTION","SAXS","ZINC-BINDING DOMAINS","insulin","oligomer","prolonged action","self-assembly"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2022B5D316FC922CCFB9C3DC7EC75DB3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Xray and Neutron Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse Sander","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"b8c18cde-5f37-4f07-be0e-de761f1a06af","name":"Dreyer, Lasse Sander","orcid":"0000-0001-7852-9121","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"2f989124-c388-42b6-9fff-f1757259e52e","name":"Nygaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leila","key":"malikpau","last":"Malik","locid":"78903637-5bb9-4ba6-b3be-5f4f950fcc99","name":"Malik, Leila","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"hoegjensenpau","last":"Hoeg-Jensen","name":"Hoeg-Jensen, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus","key":"hoibergnielsenpau","last":"Hoiberg-Nielsen","name":"Hoiberg-Nielsen, Rasmus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"arlethpau","last":"Arleth","locid":"15d83378-85d7-49d2-a442-242f57f46967","name":"Arleth, Lise","orcid":"0000-0002-4694-4299","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32579369"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.molpharmaceut.0c00112","issn":["15438384","15438392"],"issn_org":["15438384"],"issue":"8","journal":"Molecular Pharmaceutics","pages":"2809-2820","status":"p","title":"Molecular Pharmaceutics","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089613457"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fab0e603-deb6-4ae2-aafa-296095a2225f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Structural Insight into the Self-Assembly of a Pharmaceutically Optimized Insulin Analogue Obtained by Small-Angle X-ray Scattering","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-543069","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Perioperative mortality and morbidity remain substantial in acute surgery. Risk factors include known cardiovascular disease, but preoperative screening is insensitive to occult cardiopulmonary conditions. Focused cardiac ultrasound (FOCUS) can disclose both structural and functional cardiac disease and provides insight into the patient’s haemodynamic status. This study aims to clarify whether preoperative FOCUS changes clinical outcomes in high-risk patients. Methods: This is a multi-centre, randomised, controlled, prospective study including patients ≥ 65 years of age scheduled for acute/emergency abdominal-or orthopaedic surgery. A total of 800 patients will be randomised to ± application of preoperative FOCUS. The primary endpoint is the proportion of patients admitted to hospital > 10 days or death within 30 days of surgery. The secondary endpoints include changes in the anaesthesia approach facilitated by FOCUS, biomarkers of organ function and perioperative complications. Conclusions: The knowledge generated from this study may facilitate changes in the anaesthesia evaluation and decision process and, consequently, in the entire perioperative anaesthesia clinical practice. The study has the potential to reduce the risk of perioperative cardiopulmonary complications which directly implies improved patient outcome and reduced hospital costs.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Pallesen, Jan","Bhavsar, Rajesh Prabhakar","Fjølner, Jesper","Krog, Jan","Malachauskiené, Laima","Bakke, Skule Arnesen","Strømgaard Andersen, Mikkel Andreas","Vang, Marianne Lauridsen","Keller Andersen, Jakob","Helbo Bøndergaard, Michael","Jessing, Thomas Damgaard","Thee, Carsten","Mortensen, Lone","Bugge Nielsen, Michael","Juhl-Olsen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-573320"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["The PreOpFOCUS Study Investigators"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of preoperative point of care focused cardiac ultrasound in high risk patients study protocol for a prospective randomised controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/159484129/a07190410_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-573320","identifier":[{"id":"85077639297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-003dc70f-41a1-48b2-a075-7532e45875cc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-59CF51E873E056B38235DF51A39A6340"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/dmj/effects-preoperative-point-care-focused-cardiac-ultrasound-high-risk-patients-study-protocol","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/159484129/a07190410_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Aabenraa)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"the preopfocus study investigators","name":"The PreOpFOCUS Study Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"pallesenpau","last":"Pallesen","name":"Pallesen, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rajesh Prabhakar","key":"bhavsarpau","last":"Bhavsar","locid":"beb303ae-3ca0-4e32-bd2b-fe6abbc41c39","name":"Bhavsar, Rajesh Prabhakar","orcid":"0000-0001-5747-5769","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"fjølnerpau","last":"Fjølner","name":"Fjølner, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laima","key":"malachauskienépau","last":"Malachauskiené","locid":"9cef14c3-813e-4d24-903d-540837ac95c5","name":"Malachauskiené, Laima","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Skule","key":"arnesenbakkepau","last":"Arnesen Bakke","locid":"5bfc758f-7e24-47f7-b976-f768c660cbc8","name":"Bakke, Skule Arnesen","name_org":"Arnesen Bakke, Skule","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Andreas","key":"strømgaardandersenpau","last":"Strømgaard Andersen","name":"Strømgaard Andersen, Mikkel Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Lauridsen","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","name":"Vang, Marianne Lauridsen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"kellerandersenpau","last":"Keller Andersen","name":"Keller Andersen, Jakob","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"helbobøndergaardpau","last":"Helbo Bøndergaard","name":"Helbo Bøndergaard, Michae