{"abstract":"Objectives The organization of night shift work affects sleep duration and quality. The aim of this study was to investigate the effects of the number of consecutive night shifts on sleep duration and quality among police officers with night shift work as part of their normal schedule. Methods This quasi-experimental, within-subject crossover study included 73 police officers. All participants performed three work schedules: two, four and seven consecutive night shifts followed by the same number of recovery days, ie, day work or days off (2+2, 4+4, and 7+7). Sleep assessed through sleep diaries and actigraphy after all night shifts and recovery days (totaling 26 days) was compared by use of repeated measures analysis. Results Participants experienced shorter sleep duration (with and without naps), more premature awakening, less difficulty falling asleep, and more non-refreshing sleep after night shifts compared with recovery days. Sleep duration and quality did not change with increasing number of consecutive night shifts. Sleep was shorter and of poorer quality after the last night shift in the 2+2 and 4+4 work schedule compared with the second and fourth night shift, respectively, in the 7+7 schedule. Conclusion Sleep duration was reduced after night shift work and did not increase with more consecutive night shifts, which leads to accumulated sleep debt. Sleep duration was shortest and sleep quality was poorest after the last night shift in a series of night shifts.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Garde, Anne Helene","Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","Kristiansen, Jesper","Sørensen, Jeppe Karl","Hansen, Åse Marie"],"cuid":["S02-099.66-768632"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Arbejdstid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of the number of consecutive night shifts on sleep duration and quality","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.3885","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.66-768632","identifier":[{"id":"85087359652","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32055864","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0a2c6f79-0851-411e-88b7-fe3ea52107ae","nfa-c33d267b-bf81-4133-abba-7c4ffa700ec7"],"keyword":["Arbejdstid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8CB8723C4A7E2AA1259CF7A252E3647D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.3885","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/244276302/The_effects_of_the_number_of_consecutive_night_shifts_on_sleep_duration_and_quality.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["National Research Center for the Working Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"64b13e21-4e8a-4454-b945-766da6180377","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"266b247f-d127-46ae-a6ab-aa16c3f010b9","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0002-4298-1420","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Marie Aarrebo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"56d55b14-b9d2-4886-8819-0a395b08846a","name":"Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Karl","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"42f8c87d-2eda-4198-9cf5-fe5d426e9eb7","name":"Sørensen, Jeppe Karl","orcid":"0000-0002-0789-8752","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5b151ef4-abb8-4673-9522-abc399e62fea","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4075-3918","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32055864"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5271/sjweh.3885","issn":["03553140","03566528"],"issn_org":["03553140"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","pages":"446-453","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087359652"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0a2c6f79-0851-411e-88b7-fe3ea52107ae","nfa-c33d267b-bf81-4133-abba-7c4ffa700ec7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"The effects of the number of consecutive night shifts on sleep duration and quality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.66-768632","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Most existing DNA methylation-based methods for detection of circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) are based on conversion of unmethylated cytosines to uracil. After conversion, the 2 DNA strands are no longer complementary; therefore, targeting only 1 DNA strand merely utilizes half of the available input DNA. We investigated whether the sensitivity of methylation-based ctDNA detection strategies could be increased by targeting both DNA strands after bisulfite conversion. METHODS: Dual-strand digital PCR assays were designed for the 3 colorectal cancer (CRC)-specific methylation markers KCNQ5, C9orf50, and CLIP4 and compared with previously reported single-strand assays. Performance was tested in tumor and leukocyte DNA, and the ability to detect ctDNA was investigated in plasma from 43 patients with CRC stages I to IV and 42 colonoscopy-confirmed healthy controls. RESULTS: Dual-strand assays quantified close to 100% of methylated control DNA input, whereas single-strand assays quantified approximately 50%. Furthermore, dual-strand assays showed a 2-fold increase in the number of methylated DNA copies detected when applied to DNA purified from tumor tissue and plasma from CRC patients. When the results of the 3 DNA methylation markers were combined into a ctDNA detection test and applied to plasma, the dual-strand assay format detected 86% of the cancers compared with 74% for the single-strand assay format. The specificity was 100% for both the dual- and single-strand test formats. CONCLUSION: Dual-strand assays enabled more sensitive detection of methylated ctDNA than single-strand assays.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Sarah Østrup","Øgaard, Nadia","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Bramsen, Jesper Bertram","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-030400"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biomarkers","Cancer","Colorectal cancer","DNA methylation","Early detection","Liquid biopsy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced performance of dna methylation markers by simultaneous measurement of sense and antisense dna strands after cytosine conversion","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/clinchem/hvaa100","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-030400","identifier":[{"id":"85088206672","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32460325","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f5cda06d-d525-471b-bc34-fcfde8da5996","ku-8c3109fc-0618-4b2f-8a2b-d0bbe57dd5a8"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","biomarkers","cancer","colorectal cancer","early detection","liquid biopsy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DC1E4D626258C1F1C91D2DFF9068172D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/220256192/hvaa100.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251019996/hvaa100.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/clinchem/hvaa100","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sarah Østrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"290a86e4-0250-4afb-94fd-5c11f86b44d7","name":"Jensen, Sarah Østrup","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-3362","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nadia","key":"øgaardpau","last":"Øgaard","locid":"b6a80700-00b7-425e-87c2-fcd01f998cdb","name":"Øgaard, Nadia","orcid":"0000-0003-0343-8369","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"87f9baf4-e29c-4104-be23-daf6d94d7124","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper B.","key":"bramsenpau","last":"Bramsen","locid":"bcaa0339-abb7-415d-9fd3-bff68766370e","name":"Bramsen, Jesper Bertram","name_org":"Bramsen, Jesper B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus L.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f97421ce-9c23-4c51-9fcd-be0843ed0c0f","name":"Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg","name_org":"Andersen, Claus L.","orcid":"0000-0002-7406-2103","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32460325"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/clinchem/hvaa100","issn":["00099147","15308561"],"issn_org":["00099147"],"issue":"7","journal":"Clinical Chemistry","pages":"925-933","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Clinical Chemistry","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088206672"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f5cda06d-d525-471b-bc34-fcfde8da5996","ku-8c3109fc-0618-4b2f-8a2b-d0bbe57dd5a8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhanced Performance of DNA Methylation Markers by Simultaneous Measurement of Sense and Antisense DNA Strands after Cytosine Conversion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-030400","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Due to a substantial first-pass metabolism of oral budesonide, systemic bioavailability is low compared to other oral corticosteroids, thereby possibly avoiding adverse effects of systemic corticosteroid use. AIM: To determine whether use of oral budesonide is associated with osteoporotic fractures in patients with microscopic colitis (MC). METHODS: Applying data from the Danish nationwide health registries, we conducted a case-control study nested within a cohort of patients with MC from 2004 to 2012. We estimated odds ratios (ORs) for the association between budesonide use and osteoporotic fractures (hip, wrist and spinal fractures). RESULTS: We identified 417 cases with a first occurrence of an osteoporotic fracture. Eighty-six per cent were women and the median age was 78 years. The OR for the overall association between ever-use of budesonide and any osteoporotic fractures did not reach statistical significance (OR 1.13, CI: 0.88-1.47). The highest risk was observed for spinal fractures (OR 1.98, CI: 0.94-4.17), where a dose-response association seemed to exist, followed by hip and wrist fractures (OR 1.17 [CI: 0.79-1.73] and OR 0.99 [CI: 0.66-1.47] respectively). We generally found modestly increased ORs across subgroups at suspected high or low risk of fractures (1.00-2.49). No overall dose-response association was evident (OR for doubling of cumulative dose 0.93 (CI: 0.84-1.03). CONCLUSION: No overall association between use of oral budesonide and osteoporotic fractures was demonstrated among individuals with MC. There seemed to be an isolated adverse effect of budesonide on the risk of spinal fractures, which appears to be dose related.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Reilev, Mette","Hallas, Jesper","Thomsen Ernst, Martin","Nielsen, Gunnar Lauge","Bonderup, Ole K"],"cuid":["S03-096.94-007639"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Bonderup, Ole K.","Bonderup, Ole Kristian"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term oral budesonide treatment and risk of osteoporotic fractures in patients with microscopic colitis","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170345459/apt.15648.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Declaration of personal interests: Ole Bonderup has received speaker fees from Tillotts and Dr Falk Pharma, is a member of an advisory board for Tillotts and has received grants from Tillotts. The study is supported by an unrestricted grant from Tillotts. Jesper Hallas, Martin Thomsen Ernst, Gunnar Lauge Nielsen and Mette Reilev declare no further conflict of interest in relation to this study."],"id":"S03-096.94-007639","identifier":[{"id":"32003028","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85079046022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9d8157da-7141-48ac-abb0-08019e0b1ac8","au-081cc59b-2af6-4df0-9dd8-8c994287c0cf","sdu-194e7811-ce80-4e9f-8361-cbcc4eb09579"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-525783E3136EAD58BDBA5978011A1E1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431652714/apt.15648.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170345459/apt.15648.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"Univers