{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Microscopic colitis (MC) is potentially induced by an inflammatory reaction to a luminal gut factor. The emerging pathogen Campylobacter concisus is associated with prolonged diarrhoea and subsequently increased risk of MC. We aimed to examine the prevalence of C. concisus in clinical samples from MC patients, analyse the subtypes collagenous colitis (CC) and lymphocytic colitis (LC), and characterise C. concisus isolates from MC patients by genomic sequencing. METHODS: Mucosal biopsies were collected by sigmoidoscopy in 55 MC patients (CC n = 34, LC n = 21). Saliva and faecal samples were also collected. A two-step cultivation method and PCR established C. concisus prevalence. Biopsy and faecal isolates were sequenced for genomic analysis. RESULTS: Cultivation revealed C. concisus in saliva 55/55, faeces 14/55 and biopsies 69/436, which was confirmed by PCR in faeces 28/55 and biopsies 215/430. Interestingly, biopsy prevalence was higher in CC patients than in LC patients both by cultivation (50/270 vs.19/166, p = .058) and by PCR (175/270 vs. 40/160, p < .0001). Long disease duration also affected biopsy prevalence both by cultivation 30/244 (<2 years) vs. 39/192 (>2 years) (p = .025) and by PCR 103/239 (<2 years) vs. 112/191 (>2 years) (p = .002). Genomic analysis on sixty biopsy and twenty faecal isolates revealed division into two clusters/genomospecies and a high presence of various, putative virulence genes (zot, exotoxin 9 and hcp). CONCLUSIONS: Campylobacter concisus was prevalent in MC patients. Interestingly, the biopsy prevalence differed in biopsies from CC and LC patients and with regard to disease duration. Further studies are needed to elucidate this possible association.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aagaard, Marta Emilie Yde","Kirk, Karina Frahm","Nielsen, Hans Linde","Tarpgaard, Irene Harder","Hansen, Jesper Bach","Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072246"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Campylobacter concisus","Collagenous colitis","Genomospecies","Inflammatory bowel disease","Lymphocytic colitis","Microscopic colitis","Saliva","Stools","Virulence genes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i campylobacter concisus i is prevalent in the gastrointestinal tract of patients with microscopic colitis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85088104653&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-072246","identifier":[{"id":"85088104653","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32667235","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-4c907e98-1e0e-4134-a886-f107b0b37d9f"],"keyword":["Campylobacter concisus","Microscopic colitis","collagenous colitis","genomospecies","inflammatory bowel disease","intestinal biopsies","lymphocytic colitis","saliva","stools","virulence genes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE6985E2722630F88319E3C728DF01D9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marta Emilie","key":"ydeaagaardpau","last":"Yde Aagaard","locid":"b04c50d2-b40e-4dda-bbc2-440a32f1f234","name":"Aagaard, Marta Emilie Yde","name_org":"Yde Aagaard, Marta Emilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karina","key":"frahmkirkpau","last":"Frahm Kirk","locid":"73ba3fb8-2ee9-4bec-ba60-3616b3116538","name":"Kirk, Karina Frahm","name_org":"Frahm Kirk, Karina","orcid":"0000-0002-7603-8422","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"lindenielsenpau","last":"Linde Nielsen","locid":"d6796338-f0fd-4638-a2d0-201ce807d6f2","name":"Nielsen, Hans Linde","name_org":"Linde Nielsen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0002-2370-417X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"hardertarpgaardpau","last":"Harder Tarpgaard","locid":"c9d5c81d-afd6-4d85-9603-eea04d4b694b","name":"Tarpgaard, Irene Harder","name_org":"Harder Tarpgaard, Irene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bachhansenpau","last":"Bach Hansen","locid":"a3a2f82f-68fa-4a90-9632-c073911950bf","name":"Hansen, Jesper Bach","name_org":"Bach Hansen, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32667235"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365521.2020.1792976","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00365521"],"issue":"8","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"924-930","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088104653"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Un