d Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Zihao","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Zihao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changchun","key":"baopau","last":"Bao","name":"Bao, Changchun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icsp48669.2020.9320929","eisbn":["9781728144801"],"isbn":["9781728144795","9781728144788","9781728144818"],"issn":["21645221"],"pages":"131-135","publisher":"IEEE Signal Processing Society","series":"IEEE International Conference on Signal Processing","status":"p","title":"2020 15th IEEE International Conference on Signal Processing (ICSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100240198"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6bbabcec-2318-4599-a904-c624887eed68"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Performance Comparison of AR Codebook Training for Speech Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081384","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background and aims: In recent years, focus on assessing descending pain modulation or conditioning pain modulation (CPM) has emerged in patients with chronic pain. This requires reliable and simple to use bed-side tools to be applied in the clinic. The aim of the present pilot study was to develop and provide proof-of-concept of a simple clinically applicable bed-side tool for assessing CPM. Methods: A group of 26 healthy volunteers participated in the experiment. Pressure pain thresholds (PPT) were assessed as test stimuli fromthe lower leg before, during and 5 min after delivering the conditioning tonic painful pressure stimulation. The tonic stimulus was delivered for 2min by a custom-made spring-loaded finger pressure device applying a fixed pressure (2.2 kg) to the index finger nail. The pain intensity provoked by the tonic stimulus was continuously recorded on a 0-10 cm Visual Analog Scale (VAS). Results: The median tonic pain stimulus intensity was 6.7 cm(interquartile range: 4.6-8.4 cm) on the 10 cmVAS. The mean PPT increased significantly (P = 0.034) by 55 ± 126 kPa from 518 ± 173 kPa before to 573 ± 228 kPa during conditioning stimulation. When analyzing the individual CPM responses (increases in PPT), a distribution of positive and negative CPM responders was observed with 69% of the individuals classified as positive CPM responders (increased PPTs = anti-nociceptive) and the rest as negative CPM responders (no or decreased PPTs = Pro-nociceptive). This particular responder distribution explains the large variation in the averaged CPM responses observed in many CPM studies. The strongest positive CPM response was an increase of 418 kPa and the strongest negative CPM response was a decrease of 140 kPa. Conclusions: The present newly developed conditioning pain stimulator provides a simple, applicable tool for routine CPM assessment in clinical practice. Further, reporting averaged CPM effects should be replaced by categorizing volunteers/patients into anti-nociceptive and pro-nociceptive CPM groups. Implications: The finger pressure device provided moderate- to-high pain intensities and was useful for inducing conditioning stimuli. Therefore, the finger pressure device could be a useful bed-side method for measuring CPM in clinical settings with limited time available. Future bedside studies involving patient populations are warranted to determine the usefulness of the method.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Larsen, Jesper Bie","Rasmussen, Stine Brock","Krogh, Malene","Borg, Laura","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"keyword":["Pain assessment","Quantitative sensory testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel clinical applicable bed side tool for assessing conditioning pain modulation proof of concept","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/385284399/_18778879_Scandinavian_Journal_of_Pain_A_novel_clinical_applicable_bed_side_tool_for_assessing_conditioning_pain_modulation_proof_of_concept_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-085713","identifier":[{"id":"85089081571","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32692710","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-7abebb70-020d-46f7-a650-891b76b123ff"],"keyword":["bed-side test","conditioning pain modulation","pain assessment","pressure pain stimulation","quantitative sensory testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F941F3F06ED7C293FF10AAA9A212499"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/385284399/_18778879_Scandinavian_Journal_of_Pain_A_novel_clinical_applicable_bed_side_tool_for_assessing_conditioning_pain_modulation_proof_of_concept_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bie","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"16d35f43-63eb-473e-a466-4f5a12d5f43f","name":"Larsen, Jesper Bie","orcid":"0000-0003-3077-7913","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"d4300693-6515-4309-a8e2-4652c69cf113","name":"Rasmussen, Stine Brock","name_org":"Rasmussen, Stine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"d192dd43-5f01-4ffe-bf2f-bfe353892bdf","name":"Krogh, Malene","orcid":"0000-0003-2790-1020","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"borgpau","last":"Borg","locid":"ea427c5b-0e32-4524-a692-56bff54c30cd","name":"Borg, Laura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32692710"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/sjpain-2020-0033","issn":["18778860","18778879"],"issn_org":["18778860"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","pages":"801-807","publisher":"De Gruyter Mouton","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Pain","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089081571"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7abebb70-020d-46f7-a650-891b76b123ff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A novel clinical applicable bed-side tool for assessing conditioning pain modulation : proof-of-concept","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-085713","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"SBi-anvisning 272, 2. udgave, forklarer og fortolker bestemmelserne i Bygningsreglement 2018 (BR18) gældende fra 1. juli 2020. Med BR18 er indført en ny kapitelstruktur. Samtidig er kravene til myndighedsbehandlingen ændret, og er for brandforhold og bærende konstruktioner erstattet af en certificeringsordning. Anvisningen har samme kapitelstruktur som bygningsreglementet, og SBi's anvisningstekst ledsages af den fulde reglementstekst samt teksten i Trafik-, Bygge- og Boligstyrelsens hovedvejledninger. Desuden henviser anvisningen til relevante standarder, andre SBi-anvisninger og andet baggrundsmateriale fra det almene tekniske fælleseje med uddybende information. Anvisningen omhandler de samme emner som BR18: administrative bestemmelser, adgangsforhold, affaldssystemer, afløbsinstallationer, brandforhold, brugerbetjente anlæg, byggepladsen, byggeret og helhedsvurdering, bygningers indretning, elevatorer, energiforbrug, energiforsyningsanlæg, forureninger, fugt og vådrum, konstruktioner, legepladser, lydforhold, lys og udsyn, termisk indeklima, ubebyggede arealer, vandinstallationer og ventilation. Anvisningen henvender sig til alle professionelle parter i byggeriet, særligt projekterende og kommunale byggesagsbehandlere.","author_count":20,"contributors":["de Place Hansen, Ernst Jan","Ginnerup, Søren","Sigbrand, Lone","Jensen, Ole Michael","Brandt, Erik","Morelli, Martin","Sørensen, Lars Schiøtt","Buch-Hansen, Thomas Cornelius","Møller, Eva B.","Kirkeby, Inge Mette","Kragh, Jesper","Aggerholm, Søren","Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","Nielsen, Rene Dahl","Gunnarsen, Lars","Rasmussen, Torben Valdbjørn","Aagaard, Niels Jørgen","Rasmussen, Birgit","Johnsen, Kjeld","Bergsøe, Niels Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090757"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bebyggelsesregulerende bestemmelser","Bygningsindretning","Dokumentation","Energiforbrug","Fugt","Indeklima","Installationer","Konstruktioner","Luftkvalitet","Lyd","Lys","Tilgængelighed","Vand","Ventilation","Vådrum","byggetilladelser"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anvisning om bygningsreglement 000000002018","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://sbi.dk/anvisninger/Pages/272-Anvisning-om-Bygningsreglement-2018-2_1.aspx","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090757","ids":["aau-8c17256f-a2dd-4f39-b197-8f595ba566e5"],"keyword":["bebyggelsesregulerende bestemmelser","byggetilladelser","bygningsindretning","dokumentation","energiforbrug","fugt","indeklima","installationer","konstruktioner","luftkvalitet","lyd","lys","tilgængelighed","vand","ventilation","vådrum"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-36864969048B368274D5DB55D649A108"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Building Physics Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Building Technology, Management and Indoor Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Den