"Jensen, Steen Solvang","orcid":"0000-0001-5923-8441","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"masslingpau","last":"Massling","locid":"5bb9394c-7de2-4cb2-a79d-a5e2af778523","name":"Massling, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-8046-2798","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo Denier","key":"vandergonpau","last":"van der Gon","name":"van der Gon, Hugo Denier","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"mandersgrootpau","last":"Manders-Groot","name":"Manders-Groot, Astrid","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8199dae1-13a6-4f5c-9800-c10b0296a33e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"LONG TERM EXPOSURE ESTIMATES OF PARTICLE NUMBER CONCENTRATIONS IN DENMARK","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-203415","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To evaluate the psychometric properties of the Danish Keratoconus Outcome Research Questionnaire (KORQ). METHODS: Phase 1: Rasch analysis assessed the original Danish KORQ. Phase 2: Reengineering of the Danish KORQ to optimize the psychometric properties and functioning of the KORQ. RESULTS: The KORQ was self-administered by 195 patients. Phase 1 displayed trouble with local dependency and poor item fit. In phase 2, local dependency was addressed, and acceptable item fit was obtained for both subscales by collapsing item pairs into superitems (A6+A7, A9+A17, and S6+S9) and deleting 2 items (S4 and S2). After these corrections, the inter-item range was 0.28 to 0.72 for activity limitation scale (AL-S) and 0.14 to 0.54 for symptoms scale (S-S). Ordered thresholds were present, except in items A11, S5, and S10. No differential item functioning was present. Person separation reliability was 0.93 for AL-S and 0.81 for S-S. The person-item maps showed that the target was slightly above the study population. The maximal corneal curvature was the clinical measure of keratoconus with the highest correlation of 0.33 for AL-S and 0.24 for S-S. Evaluating individual questions showed that patients had the most trouble seeing at distance, driving at night, and wearing rigid gas-permeable lenses, whereas the least troublesome areas were walking up/downstairs, doing household tasks, avoiding objects on their path, and doing their job. CONCLUSIONS: The revised Danish KORQ largely fulfilled the assumptions of the Rasch model and displayed satisfactory psychometric properties. The need to revise the Danish KORQ highlights that cross-cultural validation is of key importance when working with patient-reported outcomes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","Grønborg, Therese Koops","Ivarsen, Anders","Hjortdal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-217676"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bak-Nielsen, Sashia"],"keyword":["Keratoconus","MODEL","Patient reported outcomes","Quality of Life","Vision related quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the keratoconus outcome research questionnaire a cross cultural validation study of the danish version","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079093587","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-217676","identifier":[{"id":"000559736500016","type":"wos"},{"id":"85079093587","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32452989","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9b097e7a-e57f-494f-970c-2a4725c4b00e"],"keyword":["MODEL","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","keratoconus","patient-reported outcomes","vision-related quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-456DACE6D27B34933F57E891E902D2A4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sashia","key":"baknielsenpau","last":"Bak-Nielsen","locid":"4d778acb-8da2-45ce-a916-232721f4c529","name":"Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Therese K","key":"groenborgpau","last":"Groenborg","locid":"ccdac4a6-81cd-4724-b66c-dca50b9c99bf","name":"Grønborg, Therese Koops","name_org":"Groenborg, Therese K","orcid":"0000-0001-6583-3319","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"ivarsenpau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"072c0ad1-1c62-4539-8b63-868ff8422866","name":"Ivarsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1466-4804","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32452989"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ico.0000000000002354","issn":["02773740","15364798"],"issn_org":["02773740"],"issue":"8","journal":"Cornea","pages":"998-1005","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Cornea","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087531419"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9b097e7a-e57f-494f-970c-2a4725c4b00e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Keratoconus Outcome Research Questionnaire : A Cross-Cultural Validation Study of the Danish Version","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-217676","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This article is rooted in an understanding of talent as something you do rather than something you either are or have. Talent is hereby seen as a phenomenon that comes into being through actions, rather than as an individualized, inherent capacity. Our perspective is informed by new materialist concepts that analyse talent development as an assemblage. Based on a case study focusing on Jamie, an injured badminton player, we argue that talent development produces a number of affects: it translates potential into a singular talent; it enables the conversion of talent into expertise; it turns doubt into belief; and it impedes other ways of coming into being for the athlete under development. The study provides insight into the micropolitics of talent development and into the ontological, pedagogical and ethical implications for the athlete and all the other actors entangled in a talent assemblage.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stilling Olesen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Christian","Søndergaard, Dorte Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-226399"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affect","Agential Realism New Materialism","Assemblage","Micropolitics","New materialism","Talent","Talent Enactment","Talent development"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disassembling and reassembling a sports talent","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/cu.2000.1525.20200526a","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-226399","identifier":[{"id":"85104062817","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-aa2e5c3f-454f-4cf9-a8fb-ca42981733c9"],"keyword":["Affect","Agential Realism-New Materialism","Assemblage","Micropolitics","New materialism","Talent","Talent Enactment","Talent development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-93250F45F011A185B9ED750A2DF0A255"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/cu.2000.1525.20200526a","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Marie","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"c938db5d-8b6d-4c0c-98e0-c4a0800b3a3e","name":"Søndergaard, Dorte Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-8859-8590","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/cu.2000.1525.20200526a","issn":["20001525"],"issue":"2","journal":"Culture Unbound: Journal of Current Cultural Research","pages":"311-331","paperid":"5","publisher":"Linkoping University Electronic Press","status":"p","title":"Culture Unbound: Journal of Current Cultural Research","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104062817"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aa2e5c3f-454f-4cf9-a8fb-ca42981733c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Disassembling and Reassembling a Sports Talent","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-226399","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Most existing blockchains either rely on a Nakamoto-style of consensus, where the chain can fork and produce rollbacks, or on a committee-based Byzantine fault tolerant (CBFT) consensus, where no rollbacks are possible. While the latter ones offer better consistency, the former tolerate more corruptions. To achieve the best of both worlds, we initiate the formal study of finality layers. Such a finality layer can be combined with a Nakamoto-style blockchain (NSB) and periodically declare blocks as final, preventing rollbacks beyond final blocks. As conceptual contributions, we formalize the concept of a finality layer and identify the following properties to be crucial for finality layers: finalized blocks form a chain (chain-forming), all parties agree on the finalized blocks (agreement), the last finalized block does not fall too far behind the last block in the underlying blockchain (updated), and all finalized blocks at some point have been on the chain adopted by honest parties holding at least k units of the resource on which consensus is based, e.g., stake or computing power (k-support). As our main technical contribution we propose the finality layer protocol Afgjort. We prove that it satisfies all of the aforementioned requirements in the setting with less than 1/3 corruption among the finalizers and a partially synchronous network. We further show that tolerating less than 1/3 corruption is optimal for partially synchronous finality layers. Finally, we provide data from experiments ran with an implementation of our protocol; the data confirms that finality is reached much faster than without our finality layer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dinsdale-Young, Thomas","Magri, Bernardo","Matt, Christian","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Tschudi, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-227953"],"event":{"acronym":"SCN","end":"2020-09-16","place":"Amalfi, it","start":"2020-09-14","title":"12th International Conference on Security and Cryptography for Networks, SCN 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Matt, Christian"],"keyword":["Blockchain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"afgjort a partially synchronous finality layer for blockchains","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85091159353","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-227953","identifier":[{"id":"85091159353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-acf8522b-969a-4506-bedd-3f0d2bf6e09e"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Byzantine agreement","Finality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B05955CC040CC9071F73FA9DAB090394"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"dinsdaleyoungpau","last":"Dinsdale-Young","name":"Dinsdale-Young, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo","key":"magripau","last":"Magri","locid