{"abstract":"This study compared the properties of waste chars from gasification of wood chips and pyrolysis of wastewater sludge with a commercial activated carbon for the adsorption of dyes. Before the adsorption tests, sludge char was steam-activated at various temperatures between 650 and 900 °C. The activated sample with the largest porosity was chosen for further testing alongside the original sludge char. Results from adsorption tests with methylene blue (cationic dye) and amaranth (anionic dye) were analysed with equilibrium and kinetic models. Wood char showed the highest dye removal efficiency, followed by commercial activated carbon. Monolayer completion was not achieved for these materials in the tested conditions. Sludge char showed maximum adsorption capacities of 13.4 and 8.4 mg/g for the anionic and cationic dye, respectively. Steam activation improved these values to 19.6 and 12.3 mg/g. The cationic dye uptake was in all cases higher compared with the anionic dye.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ravenni, Giulia","Cafaggi, Giovanni","Sárossy, Zsuzsa","Nielsen, K. T. Rohde","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Henriksen, Ulrik Birk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313817"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ravenni, Giulia"],"keyword":["Activated carbon","Adsorption","Waste utilization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"waste chars from wood gasification and wastewater sludge pyrolysis compared to commercial activated carbon for the removal of cationic and anionic dyes from aqueous solution","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209347791/marac_waste_chars.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313817","identifier":[{"id":"85083365936","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1efd49ea-6206-422a-9d0e-5ef7928eabcb"],"keyword":["Activated carbon","Adsorption","Gasification char","Sludge char","Waste utilization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-486F0FF3504E5AC9CB14EA9D6287D51E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209347791/marac_waste_chars.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, The Hempel Foundation Coatings Science and Technology Centre (CoaST)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["AquaGreen ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"G.","key":"ravennipau","last":"Ravenni","locid":"c9296947-c635-4809-93df-75a66f0f0f49","name":"Ravenni, Giulia","name_org":"Ravenni, G.","orcid":"0000-0002-7147-8832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"cafaggipau","last":"Cafaggi","locid":"cec72ca7-6425-4657-b04b-7d75c9605721","name":"Cafaggi, Giovanni","name_org":"Cafaggi, G.","orcid":"0000-0003-3918-6175","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Z.","key":"sárossypau","last":"Sárossy","locid":"39d0a52a-2fb9-42d3-abde-a9452b7fd211","name":"Sárossy, Zsuzsa","name_org":"Sárossy, Z.","orcid":"0000-0001-5377-258X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"K. T. Rohde","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, K. T. Rohde","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","name_org":"Ahrenfeldt, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"U.B.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"e24f0587-f0e8-4ba0-93f0-9096e3a1b547","name":"Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","name_org":"Henriksen, U.B.","orcid":"0000-0003-1838-3962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biteb.2020.100421","issn":["2589014X"],"journal":"Bioresource Technology Reports","paperid":"100421","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Bioresource Technology Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083365936"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","aquagreen aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1efd49ea-6206-422a-9d0e-5ef7928eabcb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Waste chars from wood gasification and wastewater sludge pyrolysis compared to commercial activated carbon for the removal of cationic and anionic dyes from aqueous solution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313817","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The Collective Thomson Scattering (CTS) diagnostic measures the scattering spectrum of incident radiation off collective fluctuations in plasmas. In Wendelstein 7-X (W7-X) the diagnostic uses a 140 GHz heating gyrotron as a source of the probing radiation. At this frequency, the CTS spectra are heavily affected by the electron cyclotron emission, and the microwave beam propagation is restricted at typical W7-X plasma parameters. The diagnostic was successfully commissioned in the last experimental campaign and demonstrated ion temperature measurements. However, the signal-to-noise ratio was too low for measuring other quantities such as the fast-ion velocity distribution function or the fuel ion ratio. Currently, the W7-X CTS diagnostic is undergoing an upgrade to a frequency of 175 GHz. This will increase the sensitivity of the diagnostic, since the noise due to electron cyclotron emission will be reduced, and it will relax the constraints on microwave beam propagation in W7-X. Here we present the salient features of the upgraded CTS system and discuss its prospects for both thermal-ion and fast-ion measurements.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Moseev, Dmitry","Laqua, H. P.","Stange, T.","Abramovic, I.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Äkäslompolo, S.","Avramidis, K.","Braune, H.","Gantenbein, G.","Illy, S.","Jelonnek, J.","Jin, J.","Kasparek, W.","Krier, L.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Lechte, C.","Marek, Ales","Marsen, S.","Nishiura, M.","Pagonakis, I.","Salewski, Mirko","Rasmussen, Jesper","Tancetti, A.","Thumm, M.","Wolf, R. C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-336213"],"event":{"end":"2019-09-26","place":"Whitefish, us","start":"2019-09-22","title":"19th International Symposium on Laser-Aided Plasma Diagnostics","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Moseev, Dmitry"],"country":["Germany","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Institutes of Natural Sciences - National Institute for Fusion Science","University of Stuttgart"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collective thomson scattering diagnostic for wendelstein 000000000007 x at 000000000175 ghz","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/276773715/hkkr_Collective_Thomson_Scattering_Diagnostic_for_Wendelstein_7_X_at_175_GHz.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-336213","identifier":[{"id":"85085734964","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000534740600035","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-69fc8bbd-a376-41ec-a2eb-84ccd6f9a822"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC50B6E92E3E2A5BAF70F340A7BDB997"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/276773715/hkkr_Collective_Thomson_Scattering_Diagnostic_for_Wendelstein_7_X_at_175_GHz.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physic