ee279a831d05"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term exposure to PM<sub>2.5</sub> and its constituents and risk of Non-Hodgkin lymphoma in Denmark : A population-based case–control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.67-793316","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In inversion tillage systems, the mouldboard plough is fundamental for producing a desirable seedbed. The desired ploughing quality is achieved when the plough layer is inverted homogeneously. This is, however, difficult to obtain in the main-headland intersection zone where the plough is lowered and elevated, as ploughed and unploughed triangles are formed. This results in zones where the soil is inverted twice, which may result in poor residue and weed incorporation and a poor seedbed quality. The design of the three-point linkage-attached mouldboard plough has not changed since the 1950s, but the number of furrows has increased, which has increased the size of the aforementioned triangles. A novel ploughing system was introduced to meet these headland challenges, where each plough section can be lowered and elevated independently. The aim of this study was to evaluate the effects of using a section-controlled mouldboard plough. Two similarly designed, randomized, field plot experiments were conducted on two different soil types (sandy loam and loamy sand) on a stubble field and grass field. The study showed that the section-controlled plough reduced the main-headland overlap area by ~98%. The results of a range of soil physical properties measurements and seedbed quality analyses showed that the section-controlled plough created a homogeneous loosened seedbed quality, improving the incorporation of crop residues and leaving fewer residues on the soil surface. Furthermore, the section-controlled plough showed additional benefits, for example wedge operations and visual line marking.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Søren Kirkegaard","Carstensen, Hans Christian Givard","Munkholm, Lars Juhl","Nørremark, Michael","Rasmussen, Jesper","Bertl, Johanna","Labouriau, Rodrigo","Green, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-014144"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Søren Kirkegaard"],"keyword":["Compaction","Long term","Precision agriculture","Quality","Seed","improved residue and weed incorporation","mouldboard ploughing","section control"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized soil inversion in the headlands with a novel section controlled mouldboard ploughing system","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85078021184","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-014144","identifier":[{"id":"85078021184","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000506057700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-159d24e0-997e-46f7-863b-9233fae7b085","ku-ad09dd2c-27a4-40a2-8609-5eae67fff3b4"],"keyword":["COMPACTION","CROP RESIDUE MANAGEMENT","LONG-TERM","QUALITY","SEED","TILLAGE INTENSITY","improved residue and weed incorporation","mouldboard ploughing","precision agriculture","section control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-62914BCD0C11CE5B1DEC0A1CE9C691EF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Agro Intelligence Aps"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Soil Physics and Hydropedology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Kirkegaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Søren Kirkegaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Christian","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","locid":"a4ffec11-fb52-47a3-84fd-8c4bd58cd88b","name":"Carstensen, Hans Christian Givard","name_org":"Carstensen, Hans Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars J.","key":"munkholmpau","last":"Munkholm","locid":"26e39f15-e023-4f6f-8cd8-9fed2a266f71","name":"Munkholm, Lars Juhl","name_org":"Munkholm, Lars J.","orcid":"0000-0002-4506-9488","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"nørremarkpau","last":"Nørremark","locid":"2ea7128f-f041-4034-9591-b3f0dee0024d","name":"Nørremark, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanna","key":"bertlpau","last":"Bertl","locid":"c95ddcbf-3f64-4581-b47c-7a7b3e212be8","name":"Bertl, Johanna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rodrigo","key":"labouriaupau","last":"Labouriau","locid":"0dc2d839-4722-4196-b35e-1af6905b1816","name":"Labouriau, Rodrigo","orcid":"0000-0001-8713-6864","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"greenpau","last":"Green","locid":"46bf805a-3394-48b6-bd41-7ec7c1dd6d0d","name":"Green, Ole","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sum.12569","issn":["02660032","14752743"],"issn_org":["02660032"],"issue":"3","journal":"Soil Use and Management","pages":"470-481","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Soil Use and Management","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078021184"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","agro intelligence aps","agro intelligence aps (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-159d24e0-997e-46f7-863b-9233fae7b085","ku-ad09dd2c-27a4-40a2-8609-5eae67fff3b4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Optimized soil inversion in the headlands with a novel section-controlled mouldboard ploughing system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-014144","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this study, we find that the drying method is the key element in generating the well-known fresh scent of line-dried laundry, which we argue demonstrates that it is the result of physical and chemical processes occurring on the surface of the fabric. Cotton towels were rinsed with Milli-Q water and dried outdoors, indoors, and outdoors but not exposed to sunlight. The dried towels were placed in sealed Tedlar bags, and the emitted compounds were analysed by using thermal desorption-gas chromatography/mass spectrometry (TD-GC/MS) to yield qualitative gas chromatograms and mass spectra. We observed a variety of C5 to C9 oxidised carbon compounds (e.g. aldehydes such as pentanal, hexanal, heptanal, octanal, and nonanal) when the towels were dried outside. These compounds are not observed in the other conditions. Many of these compounds have smells that are subjectively found to be pleasant. The experiments indicate that both UV light and the presence of liquid water are necessary to generate the products. The polar nature of the oxidised compounds may explain why the smell of fresh laundry is relatively long-lasting because hydrogen bonds can form between these compounds and cotton fibres. We therefore propose that oxidative photochemistry on the surface of the drying laundry is responsible for the production of the fresh smell.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pugliese, Silvia","Jespersen, Malte Frydenlund","Pernov, Jakob Boyd","Shenolikar, Justin","Nygaard, Jesper","Nielsen, Ole John","Johnson, Matthew S."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013052"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Johnson, Matthew S."],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","College de France","Collège de France","Max Planck Institute for Chemistry","Universite de Namur","University of Namur"],"keyword":["Volatile organic compounds","laundry smell","odour chemistry","surface photooxidation","wet surfaces"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chemical analysis and origin of the smell of line dried laundry","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85082112991","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013052","identifier":[{"id":"85082112991","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000559812400002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-0627ca36-fe47-4426-836e-766a868cfeb4","ku-00b7d4f0-62c8-493f-816e-08e075838d30"],"keyword":["laundry smell","odour chemistry","surface photooxidation","volatile organic compounds","wet surfaces"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1262A81F408C22FEA6B3B3738AB190DD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"university of namur","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Namur","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"collège de france","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Collège de France","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for chemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Chemistry","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Silvia","key":"pugliesepau","last":"Pugliese","name":"Pugliese, Silvia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malte Frydenlund","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"7ca1fca8-d795-4437-afc9-2a98a7e05674","name":"Jespersen, Malte F.","name_org":"Jespersen, Malte Frydenlund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Boyd","key":"pernovpau","last":"Pernov","locid":"b4eddd2c-066d-4cce-b8b4-e2a2e37741d3","name":"Pernov, Jakob Boyd","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin","key":"shenolikarpau","last":"Shenolikar","name":"Shenolikar, Justin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"741afb0a-ec33-463b-ba45-828822224f78","name":"Nygaard, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole John","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5a14c7c0-570f-4c1f-9b79-fa0a5a7c84fb","name":"Nielsen, Ole John","orcid":"0000-0002-0088-3937","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthew S.","key":"johnsonpau","last":"Johnson","locid":"03bbf286-9790-4cc4-a659-4d3956486bf3","name":"Johnson, Matthew Stanley","name_org":"Johnson, Matthew S.","orcid":"0000-0002-3645-3955","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1071/en19206","issn":["14482517","14498979"],"issn_org":["14482517"],"issue":"5","journal":"Environmental Chemistry","pages":"355-363","publisher":"CSIRO Publishing","publisher_org":"C S I R O Publishing","status":"p","title":"Environmental Chemistry","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082112991"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0627ca36-fe47-4426-836e-766a868cfeb4","ku-00b7d4f0-62c8-493f-816e-08e075838d30"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chemical analysis and origin of the smell of line-dried laundry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013052","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Motor skill acquisition depends on central nervous plasticity. However, behavioural determinants leading to long lasting corticospinal plasticity and motor expertise remain unexplored. Here we investigate behavioural and electrophysiological effects of individually tailored progressive practice during long-term motor skill training. Two groups of participants practiced a visuomotor task requiring precise control of the right digiti minimi for 6 weeks. One group trained with constant task difficulty, while the other group trained with progressively increasing task difficulty, i.e. continuously adjusted to their individual skill level. Compared to constant practice, progressive practice resulted in a two-fold greater performance at an advanced task level and associated increases in corticospinal excitability. Differences were maintained 8 days later, whereas both groups demonstrated equal retention 14 months later. We demonstrate that progressive practice enhances motor skill learning and promotes corticospinal plasticity. These findings underline the importance of continuously challenging patients and athletes to promote neural plasticity, skilled performance, and recovery.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christiansen, Lasse","Larsen, Malte Nejst","Madsen, Mads","Grey, Michael James","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-041823"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Christiansen, Lasse"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of East Anglia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term motor skill training with individually adjusted progressive difficulty enhances learning and promotes corticospinal plasticity","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-72139-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-041823","identifier":[{"id":"85091444425","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32973251","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7518278","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-40be68ab-4327-408a-9a1d-ea4a6d782a3f","sdu-1774e8d8-f27b-4f25-87a3-1919a7d05112"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1FAEE6DBA151E2DDEEDE57ADFE1F203D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/249108989/Christiansen_et_al_Scientific_Reports_2020_Vol_10_e15588.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/173632837/s41598_020_72139_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-72139-8","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Danish Research Centre for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of east anglia","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of East Anglia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lasse","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bb3cbbb6-5540-42a7-8bdb-b9ded2314867","name":"Christiansen, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-9316-1529","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Malte Nejst","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c5db3b12-d024-43ad-a807-1eba8d4098c4","name":"Larsen, Malte Nejst","orcid":"0000-0002-2600-7126","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Mads Just","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"6250e1ba-c50a-468c-8657-fa4e0f8743b0","name":"Madsen, Mads","name_org":"Madsen, Mads Just","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Michael James","key":"greypau","last":"Grey","name":"Grey, Michael James","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32973251"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-72139-8","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"15588","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091444425"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-40be68ab-4327-408a-9a1d-ea4a6d782a3f","sdu-1774e8d8-f27b-4f25-87a3-1919a7d05112"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term motor skill training with individually adjusted progressive difficulty enhances learning and promotes corticospinal plasticity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-041823","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper analyzes the performance of well-known precoding schemes for massive multiple-input multiple-output (MMIMO) systems. The investigations are based on extensive measurements made with a sounding system capable of capturing the dynamic channels towards users moving in many different outdoor scenarios. Assuming ideal channel state information (CSI), results show that the mean sum-rate of the maximum ratio transmission (MRT) precoder varies considerably with the scenario, e.g., from 6.5 to 14.5 bit/s/Hz (10%- and 90%-percentiles) for a 64 element uniform linear array (ULA) at the base station (BS), while the zero-forcing (ZF) and signal to leakage and noise ratio (SLNR) precoders are more robust and higher performing with variation from 13.4 to 16.3 bit/s/Hz in the same conditions. However, when the CSI is non-ideal the performance drops. With the CSI delayed corresponding to movement of about 1/5 of a wavelength, the ZF and SLNR mean sum-rate is 60–92% of that achieved with ideal CSI (10%- and 90%-percentiles). More statistics for different massive array sizes with both delay and frequency offset CSI are given in the paper.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Karstensen, Anders","Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","De Carvalho, Elisabeth","Steinböck, Gerhard","Alm, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068063"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd."],"keyword":["Cellular communications","Channel sounding","Massive MIMO","Multi user","Precoding","Sum rate","radio propagation measurements"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"precoding for tdd and fdd in measured massive mimo channels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.3033166","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-068063","identifier":[{"id":"85096036022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3e143f97-592d-4a27-bf3a-ba19fd9c577a"],"keyword":["Cellular communications","Channel Sounding","massive MIMO","multi-user","precoding","radio propagation measurements","sum-rate","time-varying channel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5600E79C49B0FECEB685916647FA6C2D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.3033166","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/387130389/09235534.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"huawei technologies co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"karstensenpau","last":"Karstensen","locid":"0d1d4896-50a7-4849-acdb-10dc2e0b27f5","name":"Karstensen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrick Claus Friedrich","key":"eggerspau","last":"Eggers","locid":"f054cb97-cef9-4540-a4db-37441facf026","name":"Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","name_org":"Eggers, Patrick Claus Friedrich","orcid":"0000-0002-2359-9779","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"decarvalhopau","last":"De Carvalho","locid":"cd08d3bf-1c27-487e-90dc-9aafd1088da2","name":"De Carvalho, Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-5478-5531","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerhard","key":"steinböckpau","last":"Steinböck","name":"Steinböck, Gerhard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"almpau","last":"Alm","name":"Alm, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2020.3033166","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"193644-193654","paperid":"9235534","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096036022"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3e143f97-592d-4a27-bf3a-ba19fd9c577a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Precoding for TDD and FDD in Measured Massive MIMO Channels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068063","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Variations in the internal pressure distribution applied to cartilage and synovial fluid explain the spatial dependencies of the knee vibroarthrographic signals. These spatial dependencies were assessed by multi-channel recordings during activities of daily living in patients with painful knee osteoarthrosis. METHODS: Knee vibroarthrographic signals were detected using eight miniature accelerometers, and vibroarthrographic maps were calculated for the most affected knee of 20 osteoarthritis patients and 20 asymptomatic participants during three activities: (i) sit to stand, (ii) stairs descent, and (iii) stairs ascent in real life conditions. Vibroarthrographic maps of average rectified value, variance of means squared, form factor, mean power frequency, % of recurrence and, % of determinism were obtained from the eight VAG recordings. FINDINGS: Higher average rectified value and lower % of recurrence were found in knee osteoarthritis patients compared with asymptomatic participants. All vibroarthrographic parameters, except for % of recurrence, differentiated the type of activity. Average rectified value, variance of means squared, form factor, and % of determinism were lowest while mean power frequency was highest during sit-to-stand compared with stairs ascent and descent. INTERPRETATION: Distinct topographical vibroarthrographic maps underlined that the computed parameters represent unique features. The present study demonstrated that wireless multichannel vibroarthrographic recordings and the associated topographical maps highlighted differences between (i) knee osteoarthritis patients and asymptomatic participants, (ii) sit to stand, stairs descent and ascent and (iii) knee locations. The technique offers new perspectives for biomechanical assessments of physical functions of the knee joint in ecological environment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Madeleine, Pascal","Andersen, Rasmus Elbæk","Larsen, Jesper Bie","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Samani, Afshin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101634"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wireless multichannel vibroarthrographic recordings for the assessment of knee osteoarthritis during three activities of daily living","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/442690423/CLBI_2019_613_Accepted1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-101634","identifier":[{"id":"31794924","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075687043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b1adc896-66d3-43a4-ba14-d7d1eeacdc0c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5CF47A1610ECE4C8D4951565858B623"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/442690423/CLBI_2019_613_Accepted1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-4