:"10.1016/j.joca.2020.02.283","issn":["10634584","15229653"],"issn_org":["10634584"],"issue":"1","journal":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","paperid":"252","publisher":"W. B. Saunders Company","status":"p","title":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8561a6c5-0c59-4938-adc2-4604c9d8577f","sdu-8c87e687-3334-48bb-bda1-44231294a14f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Study protocol for a randomized controlled trial of neuromuscular exercise and pain neuroscience education in patients with chronic pain after total knee arthroplasty","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.19-006456","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"There is limited evidence regarding a possible association between exposure to ambient air pollutants and the risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL). Previous epidemiological studies have relied on crude estimations for air pollution exposure and/or small numbers of NHL cases. The objective of our study was to analyze this association based on air pollution modeled at the address level and NHL cases identified from the nationwide Danish Cancer Registry. We identified 20,874 incident NHL cases diagnosed between 1989 and 2014 and randomly selected 41,749 controls matched on age and gender among the entire Danish population. We used conditional logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) and adjusted for individual and neighborhood level sociodemographic variables. There was no association between exposure to PM 2.5, BC, O 3, SO 2 or NO 2 and overall risk of NHL but several air pollutants were associated with higher risk of follicular lymphoma, but statistically insignificant, for example, PM 2.5 (OR = 1.15 per 5 μg/m 3; 95% CI: 0.98–1.34) and lower risk for diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (OR = 0.92 per 5 μg/m 3; 95% CI: 0.82–1.03). In this population-based study, we did not observe any convincing evidence of a higher overall risk for NHL with higher exposure to ambient air pollutants.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Taj, Tahir","Poulsen, Aslak H.","Ketzel, Matthias","Geels, Camilla","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Puett, Robin","Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","Sørensen, Mette","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-099.21-018141"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland","University of Maryland","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Case control study","non Hodgkin lymphoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to air pollution and risk of non hodgkin lymphoma in denmark a population based case control study","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85084741569","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.21-018141","identifier":[{"id":"85084741569","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32175588","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4b37b712-f162-4b40-a68c-7089c7cdabe5","ruc-bc8433c5-a490-4c53-80a1-4ad7551fb113"],"keyword":["air pollution","case–control study","non-Hodgkin lymphoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33456A5FCDE0BEEFB26B20FEC45B3D6D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"tajpau","last":"Taj","name":"Taj, Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"puettpau","last":"Puett","name":"Puett, Robin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla A.","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla A.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32175588"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.32978","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"7","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1874-1880","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"147"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084741569"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4b37b712-f162-4b40-a68c-7089c7cdabe5","ruc-bc8433c5-a490-4c53-80a1-4ad7551fb113"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-term exposure to air pollution and risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in Denmark : A population‐based case–control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.21-018141","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Preoperative intramuscular-administered botulinum toxin A (BTA) in the lateral abdominal muscles prior to abdominal wall reconstruction has been reported to produce a flaccid paralysis and improve the primary closure rate of large ventral hernias with loss of domain. Complications to this treatment remain sparsely described. The aim of the current study was to report safety and short-term outcome of abdominal wall reconstruction aided by BTA administration. Methods: This was a retrospective two-center study including all patients undergoing abdominal wall reconstruction for ventral hernia aided by preoperative BTA administration to the lateral abdominal muscles. Data were retrieved from patient charts and included preoperative demographic and perioperative information as well as postoperative 30-day complications and readmissions. Results: A total of 37 patients underwent BTA administration prior to hernia repair. The mean age and body mass index were 59.5 (SD 10.1) years and 31.1 (SD 5.2) kg/m2. The BTA injections were administered mean 31.6 days (SD 10.0) prior to the hernia repair. One (2.7%) patient reported pain as a complication immediately after the BTA administration. Subsequent to the hernia repair, six (16.2%) patients were readmitted within 30 days. Nine patients (24.3%) had wound complications and medical complications occurred in seven (18.9%) patients. Conclusions: We found early preoperative administration of BTA a safe adjunct to large ventral hernia repair, without adverse events related to the administration preoperative. Future studies should further highlight the efficacy of preoperative BTA for reconstruction of otherwise untreatable hernias.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, M.","Bjerg, J.","Dorfelt, A.","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Jensen, K. K."],"cuid":["S02-099.83-041818"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, M. Ø."],"keyword":["Abdominal wall reconstruction","Botulinum toxin A","Loss of domain","Safety","Ventral hernia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short term safety of preoperative administration of botulinum toxin a for the treatment of large ventral hernia with loss of domain","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85065252434","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.83-041818","identifier":[{"id":"85065252434","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31041556","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-40693334-d4de-43cf-97ba-3095014d33f6","sdu-fdaa3bbb-a045-4cd1-8ebf-8a6068a1961c"],"keyword":["Abdominal wall reconstruction","Botulinum toxin A","Loss of domain","Safety","Ventral hernia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-82B7637146E1D92D76C33777C9538352"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["​Bispebjerg Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. Ø.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, M. Ø.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"bjergpau","last":"Bjerg","locid":"53301431-23bd-429f-bc51-bc850163be0a","name":"Bjerg, Jesper","name_org":"Bjerg, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"dorfeltpau","last":"Dorfelt","locid":"a347e745-ee00-460c-a934-43606a778d1e","name":"Dorfelt, Allan","name_org":"Dorfelt, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"L. N.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","name_org":"Jørgensen, L. N.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. K.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, K. K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31041556"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10029-019-01957-1","issn":["12489204","12654906"],"issn_org":["12654906"],"journal":"Hernia","pages":"295-299","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Hernia","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065252434"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-40693334-d4de-43cf-97ba-3095014d33f6","sdu-fdaa3bbb-a045-4cd1-8ebf-8a6068a1961c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Short-term safety of preoperative administration of botulinum toxin A for the treatment of large ventral hernia with loss of domain","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.83-041818","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The Fourth Universal Definition of Myocardial Infarction defines electrocardiographic Q waves as duration ≥30 ms and amplitude ≥1 mm or QS complex in 2 contiguous leads. However, current taskforce criteria may be overly restrictive. Therefore, we investigated the association of isolated, lenient, or strict Q waves with long-term outcome. METHODS: From 2001 to 2015, we included Danish primary care patients with digital electrocardiograms (ECGs) that were evaluated for Q waves. If none occurred, patients had no Q waves. If no other contiguous Q wave occurred, patients had isolated Q waves. If another contiguous Q wave occurred meeting only 1 criterion (≥30 ms and <1 mm or <30 ms and ≥1 mm), patients had lenient Q waves. If another contiguous Q wave occurred, patients had strict Q waves. RESULTS: Of 365,206 patients, 87,957 had isolated, lenient, or strict Q waves (24%; median age, 61 years; male, 48%), and 277,249 had no Q waves (76%; median age, 53 years; male, 42%). Mortality risk was increased with isolated (all-cause adjusted hazard ratio [aHR], 1.33; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.29-1.37; cardiovascular-cause aHR, 1.78; 95% CI, 1.70-1.87), lenient (all-cause aHR, 1.41; 95% CI, 1.33-1.50; cardiovascular-cause aHR, 1.78; 95% CI, 1.63-1.94), or strict (all-cause aHR, 1.64; 95% CI, 1.57-1.72; cardiovascular-cause aHR, 2.70; 95% CI, 2.52-2.89) Q waves compared with no Q waves. Highest mortality risk was associated with lenient or strict Q waves in anteroseptal leads. CONCLUSIONS: This large contemporary analysis suggests that less-stringent Q-wave criteria carry prognostic value in predicting adverse outcome among primary care patients.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Polcwiartek, Christoffer","Kragholm, Kristian","Friedman, Daniel J","Atwater, Brett D","Graff, Claus","Nielsen, Jonas B","Holst, Anders G","Struijk, Johannes","Pietersen, Adrian H","Svendsen, Jesper H","Køber, Lars","Søgaard, Peter","Jensen, Svend Eggert","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Hansen, Steen Møller"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010515"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"keyword":["Aged","Denmark","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction diagnosis","Prognosis","Registries","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term prognostic value of less stringent electrocardiographic q waves and fourth universal definition of myocardial infarction q waves","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/313240019/Polcwiartek_et_al._Electrocardiographic_Q_Wave_Criteria_and_Mortality_Risk_Pre_proof.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-010515","identifier":[{"id":"85076865324","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31647913","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-dcd3c159-a2ea-4677-a12d-30c876477bd9","ku-b40e58f2-afd5-4492-91e0-54449f75b191"],"keyword":["Aged","Denmark","Electrocardiography/standards","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction/diagnosis","Prognosis","Registries","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-260CD00E3F0624F42B810EFADA08D94D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/313240019/Polcwiartek_et_al._Electrocardiographic_Q_Wave_Criteria_and_Mortality_Risk_Pre_proof.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Forskning, Uddannelse og Innovation","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Unit of Epidemiology and Biostatistics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, De