{"abstract":"Purpose: To assess the performance of a 4-step algorithm for neurological prognostication after cardiac arrest recommended by the European Resuscitation Council (ERC) and the European Society of Intensive Care Medicine (ESICM). Methods: Retrospective descriptive analysis with data from the Target Temperature Management (TTM) Trial. Associations between predicted and actual neurological outcome were investigated for each step of the algorithm with results from clinical neurological examinations, neuroradiology (CT or MRI), neurophysiology (EEG and SSEP) and serum neuron-specific enolase. Patients examined with Glasgow Coma Scale Motor Score (GCS-M) on day 4 (72–96 h) post-arrest and available 6-month outcome were included. Poor outcome was defined as Cerebral Performance Category 3–5. Variations of the ERC/ESICM algorithm were explored within the same cohort. Results: The ERC/ESICM algorithm identified poor outcome patients with 38.7% sensitivity (95% CI 33.1–44.7) and 100% specificity (95% CI 98.8–100) in a cohort of 585 patients. An alternative cut-off for serum neuron-specific enolase, an alternative EEG-classification and variations of the GCS-M had minor effects on the sensitivity without causing false positive predictions. The highest overall sensitivity, 42.5% (95% CI 36.7–48.5), was achieved when prognosticating patients irrespective of GCS-M score, with 100% specificity (95% CI 98.8–100) remaining. Conclusion: The ERC/ESICM algorithm and all exploratory multimodal variations thereof investigated in this study predicted poor outcome without false positive predictions and with sensitivities 34.6–42.5%. Our results should be validated prospectively, preferably in patients where withdrawal of life-sustaining therapy is uncommon to exclude any confounding from self-fulfilling prophecies.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Moseby-Knappe, Marion","Westhall, Erik","Backman, Sofia","Mattsson-Carlgren, Niklas","Dragancea, Irina","Lybeck, Anna","Friberg, Hans","Stammet, Pascal","Lilja, Gisela","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Rylander, Christian","Hassager, Christian","Ullén, Susann","Nielsen, Niklas","Cronberg, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438566"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Luxembourg","Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","National Fire and Rescue Corps","Skåne University Hospital","University of Amsterdam","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Coma","Prognostic accuracy","Prognostication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance of a guideline recommended algorithm for prognostication of poor neurological outcome after cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-020-06080-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438566","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7527324","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32494928","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085936715","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4bb05353-9587-4e41-9f87-7b7ce96f4d89"],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Coma","Guideline algorithm","Prognostic accuracy","Prognostication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-855CA763E33B4CBC8C23AC451D378AD0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250382250/Moseby_Knappe2020_Article_PerformanceOfAGuideline_recomm.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00134-020-06080-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"lu","key":"national fire and rescue corps","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Fire and Rescue Corps","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marion","key":"mosebyknappepau","last":"Moseby-Knappe","name":"Moseby-Knappe, Marion","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"westhallpau","last":"Westhall","name":"Westhall, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofia","key":"backmanpau","last":"Backman","name":"Backman, Sofia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"mattssoncarlgrenpau","last":"Mattsson-Carlgren","name":"Mattsson-Carlgren, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"draganceapau","last":"Dragancea","name":"Dragancea, Irina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"lybeckpau","last":"Lybeck","name":"Lybeck, Anna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Christian","key":"rylanderpau","last":"Rylander","name":"Rylander, Christian","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Susann","key":"ullénpau","last":"Ullén","name":"Ullén, Susann","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32494928"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00134-020-06080-9","issn":["03424642","09351701"],"issn_org":["03424642"],"issue":"10","journal":"Intensive Care Medicine","pages":"1852-1862","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085936715"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4bb05353-9587-4e41-9f87-7b7ce96f4d89"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Performance of a guideline-recommended algorithm for prognostication of poor neurological outcome after cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438566","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Headdresses, as opulent markers of rank and affiliation, offer a unique opportunity to examine sociopolitical roles and offices at Teotihuacan. In particular, in light of the few surviving glyphic texts from the site, the representations of headdresses, either in isolation, as part ritual investitures, or actively worn by individuals, are in fact one of the few ways to achieve a deeper understanding of the nature, structure, and institutional aspects of social stations and in the ancient metropolis. In this paper, we will first discuss the elemental properties of headdresses in Teotihuacan iconography as well as the rites of accession upon which these symbolic markers were acquired. Thereafter, we suggest that several kinds of headdresses are also associated with specific named houses at Teotihuacan, which indicate their close affiliation with certain powerful institutions. Finally, we focus on some of the specific types of headdresses, and especially those qualified by the so-called Year Sign (Figure 1). Based on comparisons with Classic and Epiclassic calendrical records, wherein dates are also crowned by the same headdress, as well as with the diadem of the Late Postclassic Mexica rulers, the xiuhhuitzolli, we put forth a new interpretation of its meaning at Teotihuacan.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Helmke, Christophe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479570"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crowning rulers and years interpreting the year sign headdress at teotihuacan","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0956536118000585","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-479570","identifier":[{"id":"85067888322","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-901d67d8-0599-4ebd-b76a-6bade1f55ac3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88DE263E92B113A01B1B4CB5A3871B6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0956536118000585","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0956536118000585","issn":["09565361","14691787"],"issn_org":["09565361"],"issue":"2","journal":"Ancient Mesoamerica","pages":"319-334","status":"p","title":"Ancient Mesoamerica","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067888322"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-901d67d8-0599-4ebd-b76a-6bade1f55ac3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crowning Rulers and Years : Interpreting the Year Sign Headdress at Teotihuacan","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479570","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
