","key":"graakjærpau","last":"Graakjær","name":"Graakjær, Merete","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter M","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9ae5d1ed-28ad-40d0-8d33-9bea0716ca89","name":"Petersen, Peter Mosborg","name_org":"Petersen, Peter M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"ungerpau","last":"Unger","locid":"487449ca-afef-4b40-a332-10d44f135549","name":"Unger, Barbara","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren G","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"5076f30c-8b9f-4765-b494-a263c944e96b","name":"Kjær, Søren Geill","name_org":"Kjær, Søren G","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente L","key":"langdahlpau","last":"Langdahl","locid":"1c4e9957-996d-4c56-aa0d-4e57e7be12a5","name":"Langdahl, Bente Lomholt","name_org":"Langdahl, Bente L","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen M","key":"haugepau","last":"Hauge","locid":"6e0e979f-48d6-40bd-89ec-a2502b1cefd4","name":"Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","name_org":"Hauge, Ellen M","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31521790"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jbspin.2019.09.006","issn":["1297319X","17787254"],"issn_org":["1297319X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Joint Bone Spine","pages":"181-183","publisher":"Elsevier Masson","status":"p","title":"Joint Bone Spine","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85080951577"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-00572310-914f-4438-bf8a-bbef7f934a8c","sdu-92112354-5180-4443-99fd-be354f9e4abd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"One-year progression of erosive disease in patients with anti-citrullinated peptide antibodies and arthralgia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.45-012597","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Few population-based epidemiological studies of adults have examined the relationship between air pollution and leukaemias. METHODS: Using Danish National Cancer Registry data and Danish DEHM-UBM-AirGIS system-modelled air pollution exposures, we examined whether particulate matter (PM2.5), black carbon (BC), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and ozone (O3) averaged over 1, 5 or 10 years were associated with adult leukaemia in general or by subtype. In all, 14,986 adult cases diagnosed 1989–2014 and 51,624 age, sex and time-matched controls were included. Separate conditional logistic regression models, adjusted for sociodemographic factors, assessed exposure to each pollutant with leukaemias. RESULTS: Fully adjusted models showed a higher risk of leukaemia with higher 1-, 5- and 10-year-average exposures to PM2.5 prior to diagnosis (e.g. OR per 10 μg/m3 for 10-year average: 1.17, 95% CI: 1.03, 1.32), and a positive relationship with 1-year average BC. Results were driven by participants 70 years and older (OR per 10 μg/m3 for 10-year average: 1.35, 95% CI: 1.15–1.58). Null findings for younger participants. Higher 1-year average PM2.5 exposures were associated with higher risks for acute myeloid and chronic lymphoblastic leukaemia. CONCLUSION: Among older adults, higher risk for leukaemia was associated with higher residential PM2.5 concentrations averaged over 1, 5 and 10 years prior to diagnosis.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Puett, Robin","Harbo Poulsen, Aslak","Taj, Tahir","Ketzel, Matthias","Geels, Camilla","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Sørensen, Mette","Roswall, Nina","Arthur Hvidtfeldt, Ulla","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-028684"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Puett, Robin"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University System of Maryland","University of Maryland","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relationship of leukaemias with long term ambient air pollution exposures in the adult danish population","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-01058-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.78-028684","identifier":[{"id":"32939055","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091133854","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7722932","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-dce5d99f-0291-4e8f-9f4e-d5862e5fe383","ruc-321c2466-c6f0-4f82-8dfc-ea0f37e3bcab"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4B03AF7716AEF644B7E37234A55F8F91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/230082246/s41416_020_01058_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77359105/s41416_020_01058_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-01058-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"puettpau","last":"Puett","name":"Puett, Robin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak","key":"harbopoulsenpau","last":"Harbo Poulsen","name":"Harbo Poulsen, Aslak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"tajpau","last":"Taj","name":"Taj, Tahir","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"roswallpau","last":"Roswall","name":"Roswall, Nina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"arthurhvidtfeldtpau","last":"Arthur Hvidtfeldt","name":"Arthur Hvidtfeldt, Ulla","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulla","key":"hvidtfeldtpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt","name":"Hvidtfeldt, Ulla","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32939055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41416-020-01058-2","issn":["00070920","15321827"],"issn_org":["00070920"],"issue":"12","journal":"British Journal of Cancer","pages":"1818-1824","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Cancer","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091133854"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dce5d99f-0291-4e8f-9f4e-d5862e5fe383","ruc-321c2466-c6f0-4f82-8dfc-ea0f37e3bcab"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Relationship of leukaemias with long-term ambient air pollution exposures in the adult Danish population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-028684","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The focus of this study is to describe the hydraulic effects of stormwater discharge, thus sediment transport occurring as a result of increased discharge from a stormwater detention pond, based on measurements made in a small high-slope Danish stream. In order to extrapolate the findings and predict the result of larger discharge flow rates from the detention pond in this study, 11 traditional threshold equations were tested, and results were compared to the sediment transport experiment with five formulas predicting the threshold based on shear stress and six based on stream power. The sediment transport experiment was constructed as a staircase pattern, step-wise increasing the discharge. During the experiment, measurements of sediment transport in the stream were made in two stations downstream from the point of discharge. Results from those measurements showed that there was no notable correlation between suspended sediment transport and bed sediment transport, and that suspended transport peaked during the periods of low flow conditions. Bed sediment transport peaked before the maximum flow, indicating that the available sediment for transport is a limiting factor. When comparing the calculated threshold of the collected sediment particle sizes to the shear stress and stream power calculated during the experiment, all 11 tested formulas overestimated the sediment transport and particle size moved by a specific flow. This result is in correspondence with results found in other experiments, and here the expected explanation is that the form roughness of the stream bed makes less energy available for sediment transport. This implies that the hydraulic impact from discharge of stormwater into small streams has to be evaluated on a case-by-case basis, rather than relying on general threshold sediment transport models.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomsen, Anja Thrane Hejselbæk","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Riis, Tenna","Rasmussen, Michael R."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-003978"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Thomsen, Anja T.H."],"keyword":["Discharge effects","Measured sediment transport","Shear stress","Stormwater detention ponds","Stream power","Threshold formulas of sediment transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-WSP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-WSP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydraulic effects of stormwater discharge into a small stream","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85085559804&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-003978","identifier":[{"id":"32501243","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085559804","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-517763b0-1a7b-4b2a-af50-13e6af34b020","au-69e38e47-08f1-47aa-82ca-27578d4f514e"],"keyword":["Discharge effects","Measured sediment transport","Shear stress","Stormwater detention ponds","Stream power","Threshold formulas of sediment transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-86F53208640CFA2BD38BEB9BB639B66E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Water and Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"wsp danmark","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-WSP","l3nl":"WSP Danmark A/S","l3nn":"WSP Danmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"WSP Danmark","namevar":["Orbicon"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-WSP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Thrane Hejselbæk","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c09d222d-0faa-4234-8fbc-f6b2ec063677","name":"Thomsen, Anja Thrane Hejselbæk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tenna","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"63e9c033-4056-4f18-8c91-44244963ef37","name":"Riis, Tenna","orcid":"0000-0003-2501-4444","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael R.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32501243"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jenvman.2020.110793","issn":["03014797","10958630"],"issn_org":["03014797"],"issue":"September 2020","journal":"Journal of Environmental Management","paperid":"110793","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environmental Management","volume":"270"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085559804"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","WSP Danmark A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-517763b0-1a7b-4b2a-af50-13e6af34b020","au-69e38e47-08f1-47aa-82ca-27578d4f514e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hydraulic effects of stormwater discharge into a small stream","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-003978","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we show how collaboration between Danish public municipal primary and lower secondary schools (folkeskoler) and elite sports clubs to establish SportsClasses enables schools to set parameters that align student-athletes’ attitudes and behavior towards school and academic performance. Using neo-institutional theory, we show how two separate institutional domains – education and sport – come to agree on common purposes and practices for an endeavour that takes place on the “home field” of education. We apply the theoretical concepts of ‘contractualisation’ and ‘accountability’ to understand what these learning agreements or implicit social contracts involve, how they are made, and how they are enforced. These concepts capture the empirical mechanisms that produce the integration of athletes into school norms and practices. The article is based on an ethnographic study of the admissions process for SportsClasses. We discuss the benefits and risks for the publicly-funded school system in entering into such social learning contracts.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Karen, David","Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Olesen, Jesper Stilling","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006928"],"event":{"end":"2020-08-11","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2020-08-07","title":"The 115th Annual Meeting of the American Sociological Association - ASA 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bryn Mawr College"],"keyword":["Accountability","Folkeskole","Grundskole","Talent","Talent development","contractualisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"institutionalizing elite sports in danish public schools processes of contractualization and accountability","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-006928","ids":["aau-8ef44f65-4339-41ab-86da-66d069468d04","au-87a06c37-9938-47bd-b280-85c65485616e"],"keyword":["Folkeskole","Grundskole","Talent","accountability","contractualisation","elite sport and school","talent development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-A8D60A145A0A6F916EBF41C7977FFB12"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"bryn mawr college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Bryn Mawr College","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Active Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"karenpau","last":"Karen","name":"Karen, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8ef44f65-4339-41ab-86da-66d069468d04","au-87a06c37-9938-47bd-b280-85c65485616e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Institutionalizing Elite Sports in Danish Public Schools : Processes of Contractualization and Accountability","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-006928","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Vitamin K antagonists (VKA) remain the most frequently prescribed oral anticoagulants worldwide despite the introduction of non-vitamin K antagonist oral anticoagulants (NOAC). VKA interfere with the regeneration of Vitamin K1 and K2, essential to the activation of coagulation factors and activation of matrix-Gla protein, a strong inhibitor of arterial calcifications. This study aimed to clarify whether VKA treatment was associated with the extent of coronary artery calcification (CAC) in a population with no prior cardiovascular disease (CVD). METHODS: We collected data on cardiovascular risk factors and CAC scores from cardiac CT scans performed as part of clinical examinations (n = 9,672) or research studies (n = 14,166) in the period 2007-2017. Data on use of anticoagulation were obtained from the Danish National Health Service Prescription Database. The association between duration of anticoagulation and categorized CAC score (0, 1-99, 100-399, ≥400) was investigated by ordered logistic regression adjusting for covariates. RESULTS: The final study population consisted of 17,254 participants with no prior CVD, of whom 1,748 and 1,144 had been treated with VKA or NOAC, respectively. A longer duration of VKA treatment was associated with higher CAC categories. For each year of VKA treatment, the odds of being in a higher CAC category increased (odds ratio (OR) = 1.032, 95%CI 1.009-1.057). In contrast, NOAC treatment duration was not associated with CAC category (OR = 1.002, 95%CI 0.935-1.074). There was no significant interaction between VKA treatment duration and age on CAC category. CONCLUSIONS: Adjusted for cardiovascular risk factors, VKA treatment-contrary to NOAC-was associated to higher CAC category.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Hasific, Selma","Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","Gerke, Oke","Hallas, Jesper","Busk, Martin","Lambrechtsen, Jess","Urbonaviciene, Grazina","Sand, Niels Peter Rønnow","Nielsen, Jens Steen","Diederichsen, Louise","Pedersen, Kenneth Bruun","Carter-Storch, Rasmus","Ilangkovan, Nivethitha","Mickley, Hans","Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","Lindholt, Jes Sandal","Diederichsen, Axel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-012662"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hasific, Selma"],"keyword":["Aged","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Coronary Artery Disease drug therapy","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Risk Factors","Vitamin K antagonists inhibitors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extent of arterial calcification by conventional vitamin k antagonist treatment","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0241450","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-012662","identifier":[{"id":"33119722","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7595268","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85094920281","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-01255fd0-62dc-4562-9fe8-21a2d3c40275","sdu-7daf329b-7711-4f76-9469-74c4e599b31a"],"keyword":["Aged","Anticoagulants/therapeutic use","Calcinosis/drug therapy","Coronary Artery Disease/drug therapy","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Risk Factors","Vitamin K/antagonists & inhibitors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C9D50CB17F7B4A132C3644D6FDFB6955"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175053347/Hasific_2020_Extent_of_arterial_calcification_by_conventional_vitamin_K.pdf