,"volume":"141"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084695093"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6f74b209-0bc6-47be-9c40-fc30bffa34e3","ku-b248c1a0-e820-4f74-9a80-364c75bfd745","sdu-22af81b2-dd6e-4e75-9709-ef9e5edbf059"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comprehensive Evaluation of Rhythm Monitoring Strategies in Screening for Atrial Fibrillation : Insights From Patients at Risk Monitored Long Term With an Implantable Loop Recorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.40-005403","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To describe lifeworld insights into the phenomenon of caring responsibility from the perspectives of persons aged 80+ years living alone with chronic illness, physical frailty and dependency on adult children. Design: A phenomenological inquiry inspired by Reflective Lifeworld Research. Method: Semi-structured lifeworld interviews with 11 persons aged 80+ years were conducted following their discharge. The interviews lasted 35–83 min, were audio-recorded and transcribed verbatim. Both interviews and the analysis followed the epistemological and methodological principles of Reflective Lifeworld Research. Findings: We identified the essential meaning ‘It means everything’ and four constituents illuminating different aspects inherent in the complex phenomenon of caring responsibility; ‘A life-constraining transition,’ ‘Trusting the children to fill the gaps and be the glue,’ ‘Tacit responsibility, agreement and acceptance’ and ‘Depending on the children and knowing they are burdened by you.’. Conclusions: Caring responsibility is based on a trusting relationship and tacit agreements indicating an understanding of interdependence and acceptance of dependence on adult children. However, a paradox appears when older persons express a deep-rooted perception of autonomy and independence as they have difficulties with their growing dependency and feelings of being burdensome. Older persons try to balance the continuum of autonomy, their existential self-image and actual capability. The practical part of caring responsibility seems to dominate and strongly affect the parent–child relationship because the child needs to take care of practical issues related to healthcare management and instrumental activities of daily living, leaving less time for meaningful togetherness. Implications for practice: Older persons want their adult children to be involved and acknowledged when planning care and treatment because they often seem to serve as the ‘glue’ that makes it possible for the parent to remain in his/her own home.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Helle Elisabeth","Hoeck, Bente","Nielsen, Dorthe","Ryg, Jesper","Delmar, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-025060"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Helle Elisabeth"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","VID","VID Specialized University"],"keyword":["Frailty","Interviews","Phenomenology","adult children as caregivers","caring responsibility","disease health science and nursing","independence dependence","older ill persons","own home","Ældre voksne børn pleje og omsorgsansvar"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caring responsibility from the perspectives of older persons whose adult children are their caregivers","src":["au","sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/opn.12335","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-025060","identifier":[{"id":"32716593","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088585416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a9ef1200-e761-4883-b914-a1ce552f0f9d","sdu-4ef4d19f-ab3b-4899-9976-fd960ba4bbc3","ucl-b9d6cf0b-b620-4689-9263-6a682a3f85f9"],"keyword":["adult children as caregivers","caring responsibility","disease, health science and nursing","frailty","independence/dependence","interviews","older ill persons","own home","phenomenology","Ældre, voksne børn, pleje- og omsorgsansvar"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F0FEF9AE6D2420E697707AE53C4A6E3B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171912666/opn.12335.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/opn.12335","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen i Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, User Perspectives and Community-based Interventions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"vid specialized university","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VID Specialized University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"no","key":"uit the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UiT The Arctic University of Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Elisabeth","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a86bb097-e747-4baf-b509-d2770cc35b41","name":"Andersen, Helle Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-5011-2295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"hoeckpau","last":"Hoeck","locid":"ed8ce3c5-4f5e-4dba-a104-b73d77a095e5","name":"Hoeck, Bente","orcid":"0000-0001-7647-5641","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"delmarpau","last":"Delmar","locid":"7fff10d3-6f0a-4e60-aded-688d884eedf8","name":"Delmar, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-9455-4511","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32716593"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/opn.12335","issn":["17483735","17483743"],"issn_org":["17483735"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Older People Nursing","paperid":"e12335","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Older People Nursing","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088585416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a9ef1200-e761-4883-b914-a1ce552f0f9d","sdu-4ef4d19f-ab3b-4899-9976-fd960ba4bbc3","ucl-b9d6cf0b-b620-4689-9263-6a682a3f85f9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Caring Responsibility from the Perspectives of Older Persons whose Adult Children are their Caregivers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-025060","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Mass customization is a manufacturing paradigm that enables customized and personalized design at a cost near mass production. Mass customization's ability to lower unit cost, increase quality, and shorten project duration for customized offerings is considered highly relevant for tomorrow's house building industry. Therefore, through a literature review, this research investigates state-of-the-art in mass customization in the house building industry from four perspectives: (1) mass customization in the house building industry, (2) modular and off-site construction, (3) construction supply chains, and (4) customer satisfaction. It is concluded that a great potential exists for applying mass customization in the house building industry. However, despite its potential, research on mass customization in the house building industry is sparse. In particular, research on developing the solution space and choice navigation tools is limited in this industry.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Maria Stoettrup Schioenning","Lindhard, Søren Munch","Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Nielsen, Kjeld","Larsen, Jesper Kranker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065684"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Customer satisfaction","Literature review","Mass customization","Modular construction","Off site construction","Supply chains"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mass customization in the house building industry literature review and research directions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fbuil.2019.00115","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-065684","identifier":[{"id":"85074163112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-35cd7ff9-fe48-4a29-8788-2ef7e2a483fb"],"keyword":["customer satisfaction","house building industry","literature review","mass customization","modular construction","off-site construction","supply chains"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EEF9FB27FCA42621D43AF7DD33E4D0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321412557/Larsen_et_al_2019_Frontiers_in_Built_Environment.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fbuil.2019.00115","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Operations and Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Stoettrup Schioenning","key":"larsenmariastoettrupschioenningpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e29be532-9d2b-4802-9c64-16a774948f2a","name":"Larsen, Maria Stoettrup Schioenning","orcid":"0000-0003-3396-4925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Munch","key":"lindhardsørenmunchpau","last":"Lindhard","locid":"96bcf8e1-eb4d-4e72-8cbe-c98cd7ffb5b2","name":"Lindhard, Søren Munch","orcid":"0000-0001-8959-1262","rank":2,"rolecode":"pa