{"abstract":"As well established for patients with chronic pain, patients suffering from chronic itch also exhibit signs of peripheral and central sensitization. This has been linked to parallel neuroplastic sensitization processes. However, for chronic itch, sensitization has not yet been systematically assessed, studied, and hence validated. This review (Prospero CRD42016043002) summarizes and meta-analytically evaluates whether sensory aberrations including sensitization for itch occur in chronic itch. Databases PubMed, Embase, and Cochrane Library were searched for studies investigating somatosensory sensitivity assessment by quantitative sensory testing stimuli, including experimental cutaneous chemical pruritic provocations, in patients with chronic itch from skin/neurological conditions and compared with healthy controls. Outcomes were extracted for lesional and nonlesional skin, and risk of biases were assessed. Meta-analyses were performed when sufficient quantitative data were available. Of 4667 identified articles, 46 were included and 25 were eligible for meta-analyses. Patients (66% atopic dermatitis [AD]) were found more sensitive than the controls to histamine-evoked itch in lesional skin (standardized mean difference [SMD]: 0.66 confidence interval [CI]: 0.16-1.15), but not nonlesionally (SMD: -0.26 [CI: -0.58 to 0.06]). Cowhage did not evoke more itch in nonlesional skin of patients as compared to the controls (SMD: 0.38 [CI: -0.04 to 0.81]). For numerous other chemical provocations as well as for mechanical, thermal, and electrical stimulation paradigms, results were ambiguous or based on few studies. Patients with chronic itch are only robustly sensitized to various chemical pruritic stimuli when applied lesionally. More studies on somatosensory aberrations in chronic itch conditions other than AD are needed to establish whether sensitization is robustly present across chronic itch conditions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["van Laarhoven, Antoinette I. M.","Marker, Jens Broch","Elberling, Jesper","Yosipovitch, Gil","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Andersen, Hjalte Holm"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011133"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","University of Miami"],"keyword":["Alloknesis","Central sensitization","Hyperknesis","Neuroplasticity","Pain","Peripheral sensitization","Pruritus","Quantitative sensory testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"itch sensitization a systematic review of studies using quantitative sensory testing in patients with chronic itch","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309512594/00006396_900000000_98613.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011133","identifier":[{"id":"85074962404","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31408048","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e8ef3e3e-767c-4be4-a157-8e7e141424a1","ku-241b057f-463a-4e76-83f6-2645b4bde940"],"keyword":["Alloknesis","Central sensitization","Hyperknesis","Neuroplasticity","Pain","Peripheral sensitization","Pruritus","Quantitative sensory testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BB8E0009B1FC880F08E4D4E426B81F93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309512594/00006396_900000000_98613.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Pain Biomarkers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of miami","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Miami","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoinette","key":"vanlaarhovenpau","last":"van Laarhoven","locid":"e1116201-2651-4354-864b-43defef4c068","name":"van Laarhoven, Antoinette I. M.","name_org":"van Laarhoven, Antoinette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens B","key":"markerpau","last":"Marker","locid":"ea7f550b-974c-4bc8-85f0-04327d1a3bb9","name":"Marker, Jens Broch","name_org":"Marker, Jens B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gil","key":"yosipovitchpau","last":"Yosipovitch","name":"Yosipovitch, Gil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hjalte H","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5de532a5-1602-416c-96b7-20a316e28e25","name":"Andersen, Hjalte Holm","name_org":"Andersen, Hjalte H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31408048"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/j.pain.0000000000001678","issn":["03043959","18726623"],"issn_org":["03043959"],"issue":"12","journal":"Pain","pages":"2661-2678","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Pain","volume":"160"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074962404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e8ef3e3e-767c-4be4-a157-8e7e141424a1","ku-241b057f-463a-4e76-83f6-2645b4bde940"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Itch sensitization? : A systematic review of studies using quantitative sensory testing in patients with chronic itch","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011133","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate whether a 18F-FDG PET/CT (PET/CT)-based diagnostic strategy adds decisive new information compared to conventional imaging in the evaluation of salivary gland tumours and the detection of cervical lymph node metastases, distant metastases, and synchronous cancer in patients with salivary gland carcinoma. Methods: The study was a blinded prospective cohort study. Data were collected consecutively through almost 3 years. All patients underwent conventional imaging—magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and chest X-ray (CXR)—in addition to PET/CT prior to surgery. Final diagnosis was obtained by histopathology. MRI/CXR and PET/CT were interpreted separately by experienced radiologists and nuclear medicine physicians. Interpretation included evaluation of tumour site, cervical lymph node metastases, distant metastases, and synchronous cancer. Results: Ninety-one patients were included in the study. Thirty-three patients had primary salivary gland carcinoma and eight had cervical lymph node metastases. With PET/CT, the sensitivity was 92% and specificity 29% regarding tumour site. With MRI/CXR, the sensitivity and specificity were 90% and 26%, respectively. Regarding cervical lymph node metastases in patients with salivary gland carcinoma, the sensitivity with PET/CT was 100% and with MRI/CXR 50%. PET/CT diagnosed distant metastases in five patients, while MRI/CXR detected these in two patients. Finally, PET/CT diagnosed two synchronous cancers, whereas MRI/CXR did not detect any synchronous cancers. Conclusions: Compared with MRI/CXR PET/CT did not improve discrimination of benign from malignant salivary gland lesions. However, PET/CT may be advantageous in primary staging and in the detection of distant metastases and synchronous cancers.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie","Rohde, Max","Godballe, Christian","Eriksen, Jesper Grau","Larsen, Stine Rosenkilde","Gerke, Oke","Nguyen, Nina","Nielsen, Mie K.","Nielsen, Anne L.","Thomassen, Anders","Asmussen, Jon T.","Diaz, Anabel","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","Bjørndal, Kristine"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-022424"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Westergaard-Nielsen, Marie"],"keyword":["Diagnostic imaging","PET CT","Salivary gland carcinoma","Salivary gland tumours","Staging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"up front f000000000018 fdg pet ct in suspected salivary gland carcinoma","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85066025585","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-022424","identifier":[{"id":"31102059","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85066025585","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8607afd9-d1d0-4aeb-9d93-01f839a95a1a","sdu-6545db16-3354-40ba-8456-9ee35cc853cb"],"keyword":["Diagnostic imaging","PET/CT","Salivary gland carcinoma","Salivary gland tumours","Staging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-80FC5B1BBEFC931204D976E3DAB5C13F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oto Rhino Laryngology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","k