{"abstract":"In the design practice of urban hydrological systems, e.g., storm-water drainage systems, design rainfall is typically assumed spatially homogeneous over a given catchment. For catchments larger than approximately 10 km2, this leads to significant overestimation of the design rainfall intensities, and thus potentially oversizing of urban drainage systems. By extending methods from rural hydrology to urban hydrology, this paper proposes the introduction of areal reduction factors in urban drainage design focusing on temporal and spatial scales relevant for urban hydrological applications (1 min to 1 day and 0.1 to 100 km2). Storm-centred areal reduction factors are developed based on a 15-year radar rainfall dataset from Denmark. From the individual storms, a generic relationship of the areal reduction factor as a function of rainfall duration and area is derived. This relationship can be directly implemented in design with intensity–duration–frequency curves or design storms.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Rasmussen, Michael R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058569"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Areal rainfall","Areal reduction factor","Design storms","Urban drainage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of storm centred areal reduction factors from radar rainfall for design in urban hydrology","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/w11061120","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-058569","identifier":[{"id":"000475346300008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85068855935","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1d369e20-04e0-4fa5-8c49-ce1ad36bea8f"],"keyword":["Areal rainfall","Areal reduction factor","Design storms","Urban drainage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B744B38133083B13DF973FC51AB7AAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/307053540/Estimation_of_Storm_Centred_Areal_Reduction_Factors_from_Radar_Rainfall_for_Design_in_Urban_Hydrology.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/w11061120","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Environment (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Urban Water Research Group (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Liedtke","key":"thorndahlpau","last":"Thorndahl","locid":"5faa528b-e2f0-41fd-8128-9d76ed5993f0","name":"Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000