{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To describe the annual incidence rate of keratoconus in Denmark 1995-2015 and prevalence of keratoconus in the National Danish Patient Register 1977-2015. METHODS: All patients diagnosed with keratoconus in the National Danish Patient Register 1977-2015 were included in the study. The annual incidence rates and the overall prevalence of diagnosed keratoconus in the register were calculated using life tables from the general Danish population. A sub-analysis excluding immigrants and descendants was performed. RESULTS: An increase in the annual incidence rate was seen from 1.24 per 100 000 person-years in 2003 to 3.83 per 100 000 in 2011. The average incidence rate 2011-2015 was 3.60 per 100 000 person-years. A survey of primary-sector ophthalmologists supported that the register data could be considered complete from 2011. The prevalence of diagnosed keratoconus in the National Patient Register 1977-2015 was 44 per 100 000 persons. Excluding immigrants and descendants yielded an average incidence rate 2011-2015 of 2.89 per 100 000 person-years and a prevalence of diagnosed keratoconus in the National Patient Register 1977-2015 of 40 per 100 000 persons. CONCLUSION: The present incidence rate (based on 2011-2015 data) has increased 2-3-fold during the last 10-15 years. The increase is possibly largely a consequence of more complete data due to the availability of corneal cross-linking, which has changed the referral pattern from the primary sector. Other factors such as better diagnostic tools and immigration may also play a role.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia Høst","Ivarsen, Anders","Plana-Ripoll, Oleguer","Hjortdal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-168234"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cornea","Epidemiology","Incidence","Keratoconus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence and prevalence of keratoconus in denmark an update","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064055458","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-168234","identifier":[{"id":"30964230","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85064055458","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-44522343-7c54-4472-b197-a55969c334a5"],"keyword":["cornea","epidemiology","incidence","keratoconus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCB2E6550F787F5EBB1674637A8D9D7F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sashia","key":"baknielsenpau","last":"Bak-Nielsen","locid":"4d778acb-8da2-45ce-a916-232721f4c529","name":"Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cecilia H","key":"ramlauhansenpau","last":"Ramlau-Hansen","locid":"76e02a27-dc4a-4c88-968c-d82d47f9961f","name":"Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia Høst","name_org":"Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia H","orcid":"0000-0003-3296-0121","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"ivarsenpau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"072c0ad1-1c62-4539-8b63-868ff8422866","name":"Ivarsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1466-4804","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oleguer","key":"planaripollpau","last":"Plana-Ripoll","locid":"bdf4b27a-e767-49e7-9c8f-3314033a15b2","name":"Plana-Ripoll, Oleguer","orcid":"0000-0002-6470-7465","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30964230"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.14082","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"752-755","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064055458"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-44522343-7c54-4472-b197-a55969c334a5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Incidence and prevalence of keratoconus in Denmark - an update","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-168234","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Helle Elisabeth","Hoeck, Bente","Nielsen, Dorthe","Ryg, Jesper","Delmar, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-170964"],"event":{"end":"2019-01-25","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2019-01-25","title":"PhD dag ved Health Aarhus Universitet","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caring responsibility towards a frail old parent","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-170964","ids":["au-49092a5c-2447-4021-b4a8-f477d50f128c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B4C76ABF805F697FE390E82F540AC714"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Elisabeth","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a86bb097-e747-4baf-b509-d2770cc35b41","name":"Andersen, Helle Elisabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"hoeckpau","last":"Hoeck","name":"Hoeck, Bente","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","name":"Ryg, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"delmarpau","last":"Delmar","locid":"7fff10d3-6f0a-4e60-aded-688d884eedf8","name":"Delmar, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-9455-4511","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-49092a5c-2447-4021-b4a8-f477d50f128c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Caring responsibility towards a frail old parent","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-170964","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Ants possess properties that can be used to optimize plant production in agricultural systems. Ant services can be herbivore and pathogen protection and fertilization of their plant partners. They may, however, also harm plants by facilitating ant-attended herbivorous homopterans. To assess whether wood ants can be used in IPM-systems to improve apple production, we transplanted wood ants into a Danish apple plantation and tested whether ants (i) reduced the number of herbivores, (ii) led to higher amounts of leaf nutrients, (iii) controlled apple pathogens, (iv) increased homopteran abundance and (iv) whether these effects affected apple yields. During a two year study, we found that the wood ants significantly reduced the numbers of winter moth larvae, increased magnesium content in apple leaves (but did not affect 10 other nutrients), reduced the number of apples infected with apple brown rot and apple scab (on one apple variety) and increased aphid infections. In the first year, this led to higher apple production on ant trees, whereas ants had no effect on yields in the second year. It was evident that ants provided both services and disservices. If mutualistic ant-homopteran interactions can be disrupted, this would favor plant growth and open for the use of wood ants in sustainable plant management. We discuss how this may be accomplished. Alternatively, ants may be used short term to knock down pest outbreaks (before building up homopteran populations) or used in crops that do not host ant-attended homopterans.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Offenberg, Joachim","Nielsen, Jesper Stern","Damgaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-197065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ant aphid mutualism","Fertilization","Integrated pest management","Plant pathogens"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wood ant formica polyctena services and disservices in a danish apple plantation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13102/sociobiology.v66i2.4251","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-197065","identifier":[{"id":"85078514335","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7689a32f-478d-45d3-9e28-e9c7b93080d6"],"keyword":["Ant-aphid mutualism","Apple diseases","Fertilization","Integrated pest management","Plant pathogens","Winter moth"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6522B9240B8B2DD82434667F4BCA14DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/194288481/4251_19668_1_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13102/sociobiology.v66i2.4251","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joachim","key":"offenbergpau","last":"Offenberg","locid":"e6beed8f-14ca-4175-a9d8-051650c8df35","name":"Offenberg, Joachim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Stern","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ed1b0551-036f-4eb3-89f7-50baf96bb499","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Stern","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.13102/sociobiology.v66i2.4251","issn":["03616525"],"issue":"2","journal":"Sociobiology","pages":"247-256","publisher":"Universidade Estadual de Feira de Santana","status":"p","title":"Sociobiology","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078514335"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7689a32f-478d-45d3-9e28-e9c7b93080d6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Wood ant (Formica polyctena) services and disservices in a Danish apple plantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-197065","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":9,"contributors":["Ellermann, Thomas","Bossi, Rossana","Nygaard, Jesper","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Løfstrøm, Per","Monies, Christian","Geels, Camilla","Nielsen, Ingeborg Elbæk","Poulsen, Maria Bech"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-221096"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atmosfærisk deposition 000000002018 novana","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-221096","ids":["au-a1093391-8dd8-48b7-8550-5bf456b95cf4"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4348EBC9AF2F2ADD50FFC8518C0D0494"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ellermannpau","last":"Ellermann","locid":"5e5a2168-23db-4863-b6d5-bda7dcb1f662","name":"Ellermann, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rossana","key":"bossipau","last":"Bossi","locid":"34a56df6-38c9-42d4-9608-0092024d922e","name":"Bossi, Rossana","orcid":"0000-0002-6396-7222","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"741afb0a-ec33-463b-ba45-828822224f78","name":"Nygaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"løfstrømpau","last":"Løfstrøm","locid":"84f4d438-b0e8-417d-bbbd-723e71eff311","name":"Løfstrøm, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"moniespau","last":"Monies","locid":"46192369-39b7-4c79-9c2f-83219f8cdf43","name":"Monies, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingeborg Elbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"404da8d7-4b3a-499d-8be4-5ee0cc3dc427","name":"Nielsen, Ingeborg Elbæk","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Bech","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"01949cf5-5759-444f-947f-4b40ade019be","name":"Poulsen, Maria Bech","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771564501"],"issue":"351","pages":"84","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitet","repno":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 351","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a1093391-8dd8-48b7-8550-5bf456b95cf4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Atmosfærisk deposition 2018 : NOVANA","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-221096","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The control of ankle muscle force is an integral component of walking and postural control. Aging impairs the ability to produce force steadily and accurately, which can compromise functional capacity and quality of life. Here, we hypothesized that reduced force control in older adults would be associated with altered cortico-cortical communication within a network comprising the primary motor area (M1), the premotor cortex (PMC), parietal, and pre-frontal regions. We examined electroencephalographic (EEG) responses from fifteen younger (20-26 yr) and fifteen older (65-73 yr) participants during a unilateral dorsiflexion force-tracing task. Dynamic Causal Modelling (DCM) and Parametric Empirical Bayes (PEB) were used to investigate how directed connectivity between contralateral M1, PMC, parietal, and prefrontal regions was related to age group and precision in force production. DCM and PEB analyses revealed that the strength of connections between PMC and M1 were related to ankle force precision and differed by age group. For young adults, bidirectional PMC-M1 coupling was negatively related to task performance: stronger backward M1-PMC and forward PMC-M1 coupling was associated with worse force precision. The older group exhibited deviations from this pattern. For the PMC to M1 coupling, there were no age-group differences in coupling strength; however, within the older group, stronger coupling was associated with better performance. For the M1 to PMC coupling, older adults followed the same pattern as young adults - with stronger coupling accompanied by worse performance - but coupling strength was lower than in the young group. Our results suggest that bidirectional M1-PMC communication is related to precision in ankle force production and that this relationship changes with aging. We argue that the observed age-related differences reflect compensatory mechanisms whereby older adults maintain performance in the face of declines in the sensorimotor system.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Beck, Mikkel Malling","Christensen, Mark Schram","Dietz, Martin","Karabanov, Anke Ninija","Geertsen, Svend Sparre","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-241597"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Brain connectivity","DCM","EEG","Motor control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"directed connectivity between primary and premotor areas underlying ankle force control in young and older adults","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/804450","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-241597","ids":["au-c4adb2bf-a189-4873-8dc3-af95c1cb6722"],"keyword":["DCM","EEG","brain connectivity","motor control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-67E26FF8D020CB2E9A3E795C0AF10287"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/804450","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Meaghan Elizabeth","key":"speddenpau","last":"Spedden","name":"Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Malling","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Mikkel Malling","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Schram","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Mark Schram","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","locid":"a79894f4-0039-4965-a48d-f6313b627477","name":"Dietz, Martin","orcid":"0000-0003-0029-6932","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anke Ninija","key":"karabanovpau","last":"Karabanov","name":"Karabanov, Anke Ninija","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svend Sparre","key":"geertsenpau","last":"Geertsen","name":"Geertsen, Svend Sparre","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/804450","publisher":"bioRxiv","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c4adb2bf-a189-4873-8dc3-af95c1cb6722"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Directed connectivity between primary and premotor areas underlying ankle force control in young and older adults","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-241597","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
