{"abstract":"Cirsium arvense is an invasive plant normally found in cold climates that affects cereal crops. Therefore, its detection is important to improve crop production. A previous study based on the analysis of aerial photographs focused on its detection using deep learning techniques and established methods based on image processing. This study introduces an image processing technique that generates even better results than those found with machine learning algorithms; this is reflected in aspects such as the accuracy and speed of the detection of the weeds in the cereal crops. The proposed method is based on the detection of the extreme green color characteristic of this plant with respect to the crops. To evaluate the technique, it was compared to six popular machine learning methods using images taken from two different heights: 10 and 50 m. The accuracy obtained with the machine learning techniques was 97.07% at best with execution times of more than 2 min with 200 × 200-pixel subimages, while the accuracy of the proposed image processing method was 98.23% and its execution time was less than 3 s.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Forero, Manuel G.","Herrera-Rivera, Sergio","Ávila-Navarro, Julián","Franco, Camilo Andres","Rasmussen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485510"],"event":{"end":"2018-11-22","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2018-11-19","title":"23rd Iberoamerican Congress on Pattern Recognition, CIARP 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Colombia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidad de Ibagué","University of Los Andes"],"keyword":["Cereal crops","Deep learning","Image processing","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"color classification methods for perennial weed detection in cereal crops","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85063068269&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485510","identifier":[{"id":"85063068269","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9a0443ef-7ddd-49b9-af0d-649538fdc30a"],"keyword":["Automated weed classification","Cereal crops","Deep learning","Image processing","Machine learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F961DC597EAE4A5DEDBC6DF1E40716F0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"co","key":"universidad de ibagué","loc":["Colombia","America, South","OECD"],"name":"Universidad de Ibagué","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"co","key":"university of los andes","loc":["Colombia","America, South","OECD"],"name":"University of Los Andes","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Manuel G.","key":"foreropau","last":"Forero","name":"Forero, Manuel G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sergio","key":"herrerariverapau","last":"Herrera-Rivera","name":"Herrera-Rivera, Sergio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julián","key":"ávilanavarropau","last":"Ávila-Navarro","name":"Ávila-Navarro, Julián","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Camilo Andres","key":"francopau","last":"Franco","name":"Franco, Camilo Andres"