{"abstract":"Litteraturen om talentudvikling udpeger en række normative over­gange, som alle udøvere møder på deres vej mod eliten. Antagelsen er, at det i særlig grad er omkring disse overgange, at en del af dem, der på et tidspunkt var udpeget som talenter, falder fra. I dette kapitel følger vi idrætsklasseeleverne fra 8. klasse til afslutningen af 9. klasse, hvilket falder sammen med, at de udøvere, der spiller fodbold, går fra at spille U15 til U17. Overgangen til U17 kan betragtes som en aktør, der i mødet med spillerne skaber nogle afgørende translationer i ta­lentmassen, hvorved nogle talenter fremstår som evidente, og andre som mere tvivlsomme.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stilling Olesen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-134071"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Grundskole","Talent"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transitioner i sport","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-134071","ids":["au-085ae817-b980-477d-a37e-e4222021c812"],"keyword":["Grundskole","Talent"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A76166C769DCCC67A9BEE1606D62C68"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["978 87 7184 144 2"],"issn":["19042698"],"issue":"18","pages":"167-190","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","series":"Asterisk","status":"p","title":"Talentudvikling og elitesport i skolen"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-085ae817-b980-477d-a37e-e4222021c812"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Transitioner i sport","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-134071","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The purpose of the study was to investigate the role of Prolactin-Induced Protein (PIP) as a predictive biomarker for Keratoconus (KC). PARTICIPANTS: This study included one hundred and forty-seven patients with KC (105 male, 42 female), and sixty healthy controls (27 male, 33 female). METHODS: Tears, plasma and saliva samples were collected from all participants. In both KC and healthy groups all collected samples were divided into four age subgroups (15-24y), (25-34y), (35-44y) and (45y and up). Samples were analyzed using western blot (WB) and enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA). Areas under the receiver operating characteristic curves (AUROCs) were used to evaluate diagnostic accuracy for distinguishing between KC and healthy eyes. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Difference in PIP protein levels between patients with KC and healthy controls. RESULTS: Results showed significant downregulation of PIP expression in all three biological fluids on KC patients when compared to healthy controls, independent of age, sex and severity. Since PIP is a hormonal-regulated protein, we also investigated the expression of major sex hormones. We detected significant upregulation in salivary and plasma Dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEA-S) levels and significant downregulation of estrone and estriol levels, in KC patients compared to healthy controls, independent of sex, age, and KC severity stage. ROC was used to determine the overall predictive accuracy of this protein in KC. Data showed an area under the curve (AUC) for PIP in tears of 0.937 (95%CI: 0.902-0.971), in plasma of 0.928 (95%CI: 0.890-0.968) and in saliva of 0.929 (95%CI: 0.890-0.968). CONCLUSIONS: Conclusively, our results show that PIP levels are reduced in all three human biological fluids tested, and may independently or in combination with current imaging techniques aid in screening and diagnosis of KC. Our data revealed that PIP levels can potentially differentiate between disease and healthy cases, and PIP levels are stable in relation to KC severity, sex and age. Moreover, alterations in sex hormone levels in correlation with reduced PIP levels in KC provide an intriguing insight in the underlying KC pathophysiology and highlights the role of PIP as a KC biomarker.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sharif, Rabab","Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","Sejersen, Henrik","Ding, Kai","Hjortdal, Jesper","Karamichos, Dimitrios"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-160453"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oklahoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prolactin induced protein is a novel biomarker for keratoconus","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6360109/pdf/nihms-1511481.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-160453","identifier":[{"id":"30393162","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6360109","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85055910382","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-36739d84-ace2-4076-8413-0fa50198dd9b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6312A4EF40D5A73D5EAFC35ED7E1D0F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6360109/pdf/nihms-1511481.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rabab","key":"sharifpau","last":"Sharif","name":"Sharif, Rabab","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sashia","key":"baknielsenpau","last":"Bak-Nielsen","locid":"4d778acb-8da2-45ce-a916-232721f4c529","name":"Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"sejersenpau","last":"Sejersen","locid":"d367cfa0-7df1-471e-9421-257e02de62f5","name":"Sejersen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Kai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dimitrios","key":"karamichospau","last":"Karamichos","name":"Karamichos, Dimitrios","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30393162"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.exer.2018.10.015","issn":["00144835","10960007"],"issn_org":["00144835"],"journal":"Experimental Eye Research","pages":"55-63","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Experimental Eye Research","volume":"179"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055910382"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-36739d84-ace2-4076-8413-0fa50198dd9b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prolactin-Induced Protein is a novel biomarker for Keratoconus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://loc