e":"300","pages":"52","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 300","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-da92c42f-5c1f-41c0-9d80-0d8c70730eb1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Udvikling i luftkvalitet og helbredseffekter for 2020 og 2030 i relation til Nationalt program for reduktion af luftforurening (NAPCP) : Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE – Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi nr. 300","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254112","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Numerical simulation of the electric fields induced by non-invasive brain stimulation (NIBS), using realistic anatomical head models has gained interest in recent years for understanding the NIBS effects in individual subjects. Although automated tools for generating the head models and performing the electric field simulations have become available, individualized modelling is still not a standard practice in NIBS studies. This is likely partly explained by the lack of robustness and usability of the previously available software tools, and partly by the still developing understanding of the link between physiological effects and electric field distributions in the brain. To facilitate individualized modelling in NIBS, we have introduced the SimNIBS (Simulation of NIBS) software package, providing easy-to-use automated tools for electric field modelling. In this chapter, we give an overview of the modelling pipeline in SimNIBS 2.1, with step-by-step examples of how to run a simulation. Furthermore, we demonstrate a set of scripts for extracting average electric fields for a group of subjects, and finally demonstrate the accuracy of automated placement of standard electrode montages on the head model. SimNIBS 2.1 is freely available at www.simnibs.org .","author_count":6,"contributors":["Saturnino, Guilherme B.","Puonti, Oula","Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","Antonenko, Daria","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Thielscher, Axel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313037"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thielscher, Axel"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greifswald University Hospital"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simnibs 000000000002 000000000001 a comprehensive pipeline for individualized electric field modelling for transcranial brain stimulation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-21293-3_1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313037","identifier":[{"id":"85147143222","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1c52a957-b90b-4a07-b825-5f78e33c5ae4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCD54BE2A9BCD91CECAF4AC7ACD2B2E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-21293-3_1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/199152778/2019_Chapter_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"greifswald university hospital","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Greifswald University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilherme B.","key":"saturninopau","last":"Saturnino","locid":"66bcbb15-27cc-4a52-9658-596a30995d7c","name":"Saturnino, Guilherme B.","orcid":"0000-0002-3466-8725","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oula","key":"puontipau","last":"Puonti","locid":"c70fbf13-b1e6-439c-b87a-6b1ec682d60f","name":"Puonti, Oula","orcid":"0000-0003-3186-244X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper D-","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"72984c53-aee6-47e3-80d7-3f973e5aa18d","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper D-","orcid":"0000-0003-3697-1012","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daria","key":"antonenkopau","last":"Antonenko","name":"Antonenko, Daria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer Hougaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"243ae993-e526-4121-b28a-aabf62c3df84","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8606-7641","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Axel","key":"thielscherpau","last":"Thielscher","locid":"b7ae115c-6c5c-4457-b454-49b2dc26a0cd","name":"Thielscher, Axel","orcid":"0000-0002-4752-5854","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-21293-3_1","eisbn":["9783030212933"],"pages":"3-25","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Brain and Human Body Modeling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147143222"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1c52a957-b90b-4a07-b825-5f78e33c5ae4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"SimNIBS 2.1: A Comprehensive Pipeline for Individualized Electric Field Modelling for Transcranial Brain Stimulation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313037","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Detailed computational anatomical models of the entire head are needed for accurate in silico modeling in a variety of transcranial stimulation applications. Models from different subjects help to understand and account for population variability. To this end, we have developed a new library of head models of 20 individuals, segmented from co-aligned multi-modal medical image data. The acquired image modalities allow to accurately model tissues with different material properties, such as electrical conductivity or spatially varying acoustic properties. The usefulness of the models is illustrated for two example applications.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Farcito, Silvia","Puonti, Oula","Montanaro, Hazael","Saturnino, Guilherme B.","Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","Madsen, Camilla G.","Siebner, Hartwig R.","Neufeld, Esra","Kuster, Niels","Lloyd, Bryn A.","Thielscher, Axel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-338269"],"event":{"acronym":"EMBC","end":"2019-07-27","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2019-07-23","title":"41st Annual International Conference of the IEEE Engineering in Medicine and Biology Society","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Foundation for Research on Information Technologies in Society"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Research Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accurate anatomical head segmentations a data set for biomedical simulations","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85077891688","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-338269","identifier":[{"id":"31947240","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077891688","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-70e72f89-df64-4fe9-a97e-84b05eef04cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F829E5A67F8D9B32151830F714CD6A7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"foundation for research on information technologies in society","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Foundation for Research on Information Technologies in Society","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Research Center for Magnetic Resonance"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"farcitopau","last":"Farcito","name":"Farcito, Silvia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oula","key":"puontipau","last":"Puonti","locid":"c70fbf13-b1e6-439c-b87a-6b1ec682d60f","name":"Puonti, Oula","orcid":"0000-0003-3186-244X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hazael","key":"montanaropau","last":"Montanaro","name":"Montanaro, Hazael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilherme B.","key":"saturninopau","last":"Saturnino","locid":"66bcbb15-27cc-4a52-9658-596a30995d7c","name":"Saturnino, Guilherme B.","orcid":"0000-0002-3466-8725","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Duemose","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"72984c53-aee6-47e3-80d7-3f973e5aa18d","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","orcid":"0000-0003-3697-1012","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla G.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Camilla G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hartwig R.","key":"siebnerpau","last":"Siebner","name":"Siebner, Hartwig R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esra","key":"neufeldpau","last":"Neufeld","name":"Neufeld, Esra","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"kusterpau","last":"Kuster","name":"Kuster, Niels","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Bryn A.","key":"lloydpau","last":"Lloyd","name":"Lloyd, Bryn A.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Axel","key":"thielscherpau","last":"Thielscher","locid":"b7ae115c-6c5c-4457-b454-49b2dc26a0cd","name":"Thielscher, Axel","orcid":"0000-0002-4752-5854","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31947240"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/embc.2019.8857041","pages":"6118-6123","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 39th Annual International Conference of the Ieee Engineering in Medicine and Biology Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077891688"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-70e72f89-df64-4fe9-a97e-84b05eef04cf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Accurate anatomical head segmentations: a data set for biomedical simulations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-338269","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"A switch from batch to continuous manufacturing of gallium-68 (68Ga) and 68Ga-labeled pharmaceuticals can be advantageous, as it recycles isotopically-enriched zinc-68 (68Zn), removes pre- and post-irradiation target manipulations, and provides scalability via dose-on-demand production. Herein we report efficient extraction of radiogallium (66,67,68Ga = *Ga) from ZnCl2/HCl solutions in batch and in flow using a membrane-based liquid-liquid separator. From 5.6 M ZnCl2/3 M HCl, a 1/2 (v/v) diisopropyl ether (iPr2O)/trifluorotoluene (TFT) solvent extracts 76.3 ± 1.9% of *Ga and 1.9 ± 1.6% of Zn in flow using a single pass through. From 1 M ZnCl2/6 M HCl, a 1/2 (v/v) n-butyl methyl ether (n-BuOMe)/TFT solvent extracts 95.7 ± 2.0% of *Ga and 0.005 ± 0.003% of Zn in flow. TFT plays a key role in controlling the interfacial tension between the aqueous and the organic phases, ensuring clean membrane-based separation. The process did not extract Cu, Mn, and Co but did extract Fe. Using HGaCl4 and ZnCl2 as the extractable species, the COSMO-RS theory predicts the solvation-driven extraction of Ga and Zn with a mean unsigned error of prediction of 4.0% and 3.4% respectively.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Kristina Søborg","Nielsen, Karin Michaelsen","Fonslet, Jesper","Jensen, Mikael","Zhuravlev, Fedor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340769"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COSMO RS","Gallium 68"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"separation of radiogallium from zinc using membrane based liquid liquid extraction in flow experimental and cosmo rs studies","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/07366299.2019.1646982","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340769","identifier":[{"id":"85070531675","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7943aa58-4447-4aa1-aab2-6693c4836dc3"],"keyword":["COSMO-RS","Gallium-67","Gallium-68","Liquid extraction in flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6551ED52CAF958F9D3504FD646625784"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/192396632/Separation_of_Radiogallium_from_Zinc_Using_Membrane_Based_Liquid_Liquid_Extraction_in_Flow_Experimental_and_COSMO_RS_Studies.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/07366299.2019.1646982","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Center for Nuclear Technologies","Technical University of Denmark, Center for Nuclear Technologies, The Hevesy Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina Søborg","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"143ed0ee-c65d-4169-a706-9070a0923fbc","name":"Pedersen, Kristina Søborg","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-9237","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin Michaelsen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7a3dcd4b-430f-43d6-bd0c-cdb4e052a262","name":"Nielsen, Karin Michaelsen","orcid":"0000-0003-4736-8980","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"fonsletpau","last":"Fonslet","locid":"4e7c8b5c-0ca8-486a-90a2-0a43669dc729","name":"Fonslet, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-1563-0251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7a6b32c7-c6b6-4fbf-af7f-f0e64f27de43","name":"Jensen, Mikael","orcid":"0000-0002-9109-2187","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fedor","key":"zhuravlevpau","last":"Zhuravlev","locid":"36931255-67cf-464d-9e3e-7ab0b2af30f4","name":"Zhuravlev, Fedor","orcid":"0000-0001-8457-5191","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/07366299.2019.1646982","issn":["07366299","15322262"],"issn_org":["07366299"],"issue":"5","journal":"Solvent Extraction and Ion Exchange","pages":"376-391","publisher":"Taylor & Francis Inc.","status":"p","title":"Solvent Extraction and Ion Exchange","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070531675"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7943aa58-4447-4aa1-aab2-6693c4836dc3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Separation of Radiogallium from Zinc Using Membrane-Based Liquid-Liquid Extraction in Flow: Experimental and COSMO-RS Studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340769","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"A Collective Thomson Scattering (CTS) diagnostic is installed at Wendelstein 7-X for ion temperature measurements in the plasma core. The diagnostic utilizes 140 GHz gyrotrons usually used for electron cyclotron resonance heating (ECRH) as a source of probing radiation. The CTS diagnostic uses a quasi-optical transmission line covering a distance of over 40 m. The transmission line is shared between the ECRH system and the CTS diagnostic. Here we elaborate on the design, installation, and alignment of the CTS diagnostic and present the first measurements at Wendelstein 7-X.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Moseev, D.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Stange, T.","Abramovic, I.","Laqua, H. P.","Marsen, S.","Schneider, N.","Braune, H.","Hoefel, U.","Kasparek, W.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Lechte, C.","Leipold, Frank","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Salewski, Mirko","Rasmussen, Jesper","Weißgerber, M.","Wolf, R. C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352975"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Moseev, D."],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","University of Stuttgart"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collective thomson scattering diagnostic at wendelstein 000000000007 x","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.5050193","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014–2018 under Grant Agreement No. 633053. The views and opinions expressed her