{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: High Amplitude Low Frequency-Music Impulse Stimulation (HALF-MIS) is a form of Vagus Nerve Stimulation (VNS). The aim of the study was to determine the feasibility, efficacy, and potential side effects of HALF-MIS, used as an add-on treatment for depression. METHODS: This is an open randomized controlled pilot study. Patients with depressive disorder were randomly allocated to either a HALF-MIS group with eight add-on HALF-MIS sessions (over a period of 3-4 weeks) or a control group which received treatment as usual. Seated in a specially designed chair() embedded with a transducer, their central nervous system was stimulated through the abdomen, () using music and vibration. Hamilton rating was performed. Side effects were registered. RESULTS: Eighteen patients were randomized to the add-on treatment and 20 patients to the control group. Both groups show in Hamilton Depression Rating Scale (HDRS)-17 and in HDRS-6, although the HALF-MIS group had a greater decline of symptoms. This was a significant difference in intergroup analysis (p = .011, CI 95% for the HALF-MIS group 3.0588-8.5327 and CI 95% for the control group 0.2384-3.0). The (HDRS)-6 difference was also significant (p = .020, CI 95% for the HALF-MIS group 1.5911-5.0487 and for the control group -0.297 to 1.7058). No side effects were observed. CONCLUSIONS: High Amplitude Low Frequency-Music Impulse Stimulation treatment seems to give beneficial effect as an add-on treatment for depression. HALF-MIS appears to be a safe and effective add-on treatment for depression.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sigurdardóttir, Gudrun Agusta","Nielsen, Peter Michael","Rønager, Jesper","Wang, August G"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499526"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a pilot study on high amplitude low frequency music impulse stimulation as an add on treatment for depression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/brb3.1399","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-499526","identifier":[{"id":"31507100","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85072209227","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6790306","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b1a2072e-bdad-44a1-b451-290e6aec524d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FDDD947C61A1F6CCD0B5ABEEED414EC7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/brb3.1399","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/235969691/Sigurdard_ttir_et_al_2019_Brain_and_Behavior.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Gudrun Agusta","key":"sigurdardóttirpau","last":"Sigurdardóttir","name":"Sigurdardóttir, Gudrun Agusta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Michael","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Peter Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"rønagerpau","last":"Rønager","name":"Rønager, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"August Gabriel","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"6dfb1299-b15e-42dd-bf71-44f2b5f49a7c","name":"Wang, August G","name_org":"Wang, August Gabriel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31507100"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/brb3.1399","issn":["21623279"],"issue":"10","journal":"Brain and Behavior","paperid":"e01399","status":"p","title":"Brain and Behavior","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072209227"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b1a2072e-bdad-44a1-b451-290e6aec524d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A pilot study on high amplitude low frequency-music impulse stimulation as an add-on treatment for depression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499526","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Selective pharmacological tool compounds are invaluable for understanding the functions of the various ionotropic glutamate receptor subtypes. For the kainate receptors these compounds are few. Here we have synthesized 9 novel quinoxaline-2,3-diones with substitutions in the 7-position to investigate the structure-activity relationship at kainate and AMPA receptors. Compound 11 exhibited the highest binding affinity across GluK1-3 while having a 73-fold selectivity towards kainate vs. AMPA receptors. 11 potently inhibited glutamate evoked currents at homomeric GluK1 and GluK3 receptors in HEK293 cells with Kb values of 65 and 39 nM, respectively. The binding mode of 11 in the ligand binding domain of GluK1 was investigated by X-ray crystallography, revealing that 11 stabilizes the receptor in an open conformation, consistent with its demonstrated antagonism. Furthermore, 11 was tested for analgesic effects in the mouse tail flick test where it significantly increased tail flick latency at doses where NBQX was ineffective.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Møllerud, Stine","Hansen, Rikke Rie","Pallesen, Jakob S","Temperini, Piero","Pasini, Diletta","Bornholdt, Jan","Nielsen, Birgitte","Mamedova, Esmira","Chalupnik, Paulina","Paternain, Ana V","Lerma, Juan","Diaz-delCastillo, Marta","Andreasen T., Jesper","Frydenvang, Karla","Kastrup, Jette Sandholm","Johansen, Tommy Nørskov","Pickering, Darryl S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-508160"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"em n em 000000000007 000000000001 em h em imidazol 000000000001 yl 000000000002 000000000003 dioxo 000000000006 trifluoromethyl 000000000003 000000000004 dihydroquinoxalin 000000000001 000000000002 em h em yl benzamide a new kainate receptor selective antagonist and analgesic synthesis x ray crystallography structure affinity relationships in vitro and in vivo pharmacology","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-508160","identifier":[{"id":"31622082","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85074785234","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c044742c-9663-435e-abaa-40c68afcfdec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B6EC5AA2555F0B5F041077F8CB2DB32"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biostructural Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine","key":"møllerudpau","last":"Møllerud","locid":"c3bbc2d0-6465-4ce3-a1d2-6dc292a98699","name":"Møllerud, Stine","orcid":"0000-0001-6828-8539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rie B","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"f465dadd-549f-4425-ace4-7e402882e92a","name":"Hansen, Rikke Rie","name_org":"Hansen, Rie B","orcid":"0000-0002-7588-1303","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob S","key":"pallesenpau","last":"Pallesen","locid":"db051a39-ca79-46cd-9c01-fa7640118749","name":"Pallesen, Jakob S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Piero","key":"temperinipau","last":"Temperini","locid":"b77e014f-aad7-4a89-9eab-55c93a44f8b9","name":"Temperini, Piero","orcid":"0000-0003-4951-6879","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Diletta","key":"pasinipau","last":"Pasini","name":"Pasini, Diletta","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"bornholdt