try":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"buurpau","last":"Buur","locid":"e99df072-1a1e-4f65-9204-18e7f410f286","name":"Buur, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-0828-8374","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"sveegaardpau","last":"Sveegaard","locid":"ea1c364f-09ba-4d20-a1cc-9c0d6f568664","name":"Sveegaard, Signe","orcid":"0000-0002-8893-9842","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"galatiuspau","last":"Galatius","locid":"34804171-9f60-4314-a4f4-70df2c4fe2bf","name":"Galatius, Anders","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"teilmannpau","last":"Teilmann","locid":"733c70b6-2727-4145-b8d2-c8778c6bfce2","name":"Teilmann, Jonas","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b0e7f6de-90dc-4a52-aaeb-baf341279236"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bevaringsstatus for naturtyper og arter : Oversigt over Danmarks Artikel 17-rapportering til habitatdirektivet 2019","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230255","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This modeling study presents the sectoral contributions of anthropogenic emissions in the four Nordic countries (Denmark, Finland, Norway and Sweden) on air pollution levels and the associated health impacts and costs over the Nordic and the Arctic regions for the year 2015. The Danish Eulerian Hemispheric Model (DEHM) has been used on a 50 km resolution over Europe in tagged mode in order to calculate the response of a 30% reduction of each emission sector in each Nordic country individually. The emission sectors considered in the study were energy production, non-industrial/commercial heating, industry, traffic, off-road mobile sources and waste management/agriculture. In total, 28 simulations were carried out. Following the air pollution modeling, the Economic Valuation of Air Pollution (EVA) model has been used to calculate the associated premature mortality and their costs. Results showed that more than 80 % of the PM2.5 concentration was attributed to transport from outside these four countries, implying an effort outside the Nordic region in order to decrease the pollutant levels over the area. The leading emission sector in each country was found to be non-industrial combustion (contributing by more than 60 % to the total PM2.5 mass coming from the country itself), except for Sweden, where industry contributed to PM2.5 with a comparable amount to non-industrial combustion. In addition to non-industrial combustion, the next most important source categories were industry, agriculture and traffic. The main chemical constituent of PM2.5 concentrations that comes from the country itself is calculated to be organic carbon in all countries, which suggested that non-industrial wood burning was the dominant national source of pollution in the Nordic countries. We have estimated the total number of premature mortality cases due to air pollution to be around 4000 in Denmark and Sweden and around 2000 in Finland and Norway. These premature mortality cases led to a total cost of EUR 7 billion in the selected Nordic countries. The assessment of the related premature mortality and associated cost estimates suggested that non-industrial combustion, together with industry and traffic, will be the main sectors to be targeted in emission mitigation strategies in the future.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Im, Ulas","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Sand, Maria","Makkonen, Risto","Geels, Camilla","Anderson, Camilla","Kukkonen, Jaakko","Lopez-Aparicio, Susana","Brandt, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232235"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Im, Ulas"],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for International Climate and Environmental Research","Finnish Meteorological Institute","Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute","The Climate and Environmental Research Institute (NILU)","University of Helsinki"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contributions of nordic anthropogenic emissions on air pollution and premature mortality over the nordic region and the arctic","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-19-12975-2019","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-232235","identifier":[{"id":"85073726737","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b45f361f-bc59-485f-9d1c-f1678086988d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1466A5AE90B93324FFC981C07BFD3F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-19-12975-2019","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/209947741/acp_19_12975_2019.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"centre for international climate and environmental research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Centre for International Climate and Environmental Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"finnish meteorological institute","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Meteorological Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"swedish meteorological and hydrological institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"the climate and environmental research institute","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"The Climate and Environmental Research Institute (NILU)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","name_org":"Christensen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Kenneth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","name_org":"Nielsen, Ole Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","name":"Sand, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Risto","key":"makkonenpau","last":"Makkonen","name":"Makkonen, Risto","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"andersonpau","last":"Anderson","name":"Anderson, Camilla","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaakko","key":"kukkonenpau","last":"Kukkonen","name":"Kukkonen, Jaakko","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Susana","key":"lopezapariciopau","last":"Lopez-Aparicio","name":"Lopez-Aparicio, Susana","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/acp-19-12975-2019","issn":["16807316","16807324"],"issn_org":["16807316"],"issue":"20","journal":"Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics","pages":"12975-12992","publisher":"Copernicus Publications","status":"p","title":"Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073726737"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b45f361f-bc59-485f-9d1c-f1678086988d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Contributions of Nordic anthropogenic emissions on air pollution and premature mortality over the Nordic region and the Arctic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-232235","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The primary purpose of the collective Thomson scattering (CTS) diagnostic at ITER is to measure the properties of fast-ion populations, in particular those of fusion-born -particles. Based on the present design of the diagnostic, we compute and fit synthetic CTS spectra for the ITER baseline plasma scenario, including the effects of noise, refraction, multiple fast-ion populations, and uncertainties on nuisance parameters. As part of this, we developed a model for CTS that incorporates spatial effects of frequency-dependent refraction. While such effects will distort the measured ITER CTS spectra, we demonstrate that the true -particle densities can nevertheless be recovered to within  ∼10% from noisy synthetic spectra, using existing fitting methods that do not take these spatial effects into account. Under realistic operating conditions, we thus find the predicted performance of the ITER CTS system to be consistent with the ITER measurement requirements of a 20% accuracy on inferred -particle density profiles at 100 ms time resolution.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Jensen, T.","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Larsen, Axel Wright","Leipold, Frank","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Salewski, Mirko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Jesper"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","ITER","Particles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inference of α particle density profiles from iter collective thomson scattering","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196406968/cts_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331157","identifier":[{"id":"85072108830","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-596b42e0-7ce0-48b0-86cb-1354e4eb8aaf"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","ITER","α-particles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0757C763677574DE15AEA47741EC1FE3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196406968/cts_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"stejnerpau","last":"Stejner","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Stejner, M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e840242d-2592-40b7-bc0b-02995c8fe6ba","name":"Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9801-1530","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben Bryndt","key":"klinkbypau","last":"Klinkby","locid":"1a611e33-cd53-43a3-9b7c-ebdd92d302f7","name":"Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","orcid":"0000-0002-1908-5644","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Bang","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.W.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"55ff89d0-a9e8-4bd0-b3f8-1c544444c72a","name":"Larsen, Axel Wright","name_org":"Larsen, A.W.","orcid":"0000-0002-7837-717X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"leipoldpau","last":"Leipold","locid":"fb1ca27f-36e0-43a2-8779-3d8135a2a8dc","name":"Leipold, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3107-6713","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S.K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/ab2f50","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"9","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"096051","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072108830"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-596b42e0-7ce0-48b0-86cb-1354e4eb8aaf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Inference of α-particle density profiles from ITER collective Thomson scattering","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-331157","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The ASDEX Upgrade (AUG) programme, jointly run with the EUROfusion MST1 task force, continues to significantly enhance the physics base of ITER and DEMO. Here, the full tungsten wall is a key asset for extrapolating to future devices. The high overall heating power, flexible heating mix and comprehensive diagnostic set allows studies ranging from mimicking the scrape-off-layer and divertor conditions of ITER and DEMO at high density to fully noninductive operation (q95 = 5.5, βN ≤ 2.8) at low density. Higher installed electron cyclotron resonance heating power ≤ 6 MW, new diagnostics and improved analysis techniques have further enhanced the capabilities of AUG. Stable high-density H-modes with Psep/R ≤ 11 MW m−1 with fully detached strikepoints have been demonstrated. The ballooning instability close to the separatrix has been identified as a potential cause leading to the H-mode density limit and is also found to play an important role for the access to small edge-localized modes (ELMs). Density limit disruptions have been successfully avoided using a path-oriented approach to disruption handling and progress has been made in understanding the dissipation and avoidance of runaway electron beams. ELM suppression with resonant magnetic perturbations is now routinely achieved reaching transiently HH98(y,2) ≤ 1.1. This gives new insight into the field penetration physics, in particular with respect to plasma flows. Modelling agrees well with plasma response measurements and a helically localised ballooning structure observed prior to the ELM is evidence for the changed edge stability due to the magnetic perturbations. The impact of 3D perturbations on heat load patterns and fast-ion losses have been further elaborated. Progress has also been made in understanding the ELM cycle itself. Here, new fast measurements of Ti and Er allow for inter ELM transport analysis confirming that Er is dominated by the diamagnetic term even for fast timescales. New analysis techniques allow detailed comparison of the ELM crash and are in good agreement with nonlinear MHD modelling. The observation of accelerated ions during the ELM crash can be seen as evidence for the reconnection during the ELM. As type-I ELMs (even mitigated) are likely not a viable operational regime in DEMO studies of ‘natural’ no ELM regimes have been extended. Stable I-modes up to n/nGW ≤ 0.7 have been characterised using β-feedback. Core physics has been advanced by more detailed characterisation of the turbulence with new measurements such as the eddy tilt angle—measured for the first time—or the crossphase angle of Te and ne fluctuations. These new data put strong constraints on gyro-kinetic turbulence modelling. In addition, carefully executed studies in different main species (H, D and He) and with different heating mixes highlight the importance of the collisional energy exchange for interpreting energy confinement. A new regime with a hollow Te profile now gives access to regimes mimicking aspects of burning plasma conditions and lead to nonlinear interactions of energetic particle modes despite the sub-Alfvénic beam energy. This will help to validate the fast-ion codes for predicting ITER and DEMO.","author_count":400,"contributors":["Meyer, H.","Angioni, C.","Albert, C.G.","Arden, N.","Parra, R. Arredondo","Asunta, O.","Baar, M. de","Balden, M.","Bandaru, V.","Behler, K.","Bergmann, A.","Bernardo, J.","Bernert, M.","Biancalani, A.","Bilato, R.","Birkenmeier, G.","Blanken, T.C.","Bobkov, V.","Bock, A.","Bolzonella, T.","Bortolon, A.","Böswirth, B.","Bottereau, C.","Bottino, A.","Brand, H. van den","Brezinsek, S.","Brida, D.","Brochard, F.","Bruhn, C.","Buchanan, J.","Buhler, A.","Burckhart, A.","Camenen, Y.","Carlton, D.","Carr, M.","Carralero, D.","Castaldo, C.","Cavedon, M.","Cazzaniga, C.","Ceccuzzi, S.","Challis, C.","Chankin, A.","Chapman, S.","Cianfarani, C.","Clairet, F.","Coda, S.","Coelho, R.","Coenen, J.W.","Colas, L.","Conway, G.D.","Costea,