iversity of Denmark"],"title":"Dependence on plasma shape and plasma fueling for small edge-localized mode regimes in TCV and ASDEX Upgrade","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-345858","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Typically, slow steaming is adopted to lower ship’s resistance, which in turn reduces exhaust gas emissions due to lower propulsion power demands. Fine tuning of the underlying hydrodynamic models is key to the reliable forecasting of fuel consumption. Accurate knowledge of the vessel’s speedthrough- water (STW) is paramount to estimate the actual resistance of the vessel. The paper presents a feasibility study about the use of sensor fusion methods for real-time estimation of STW based on inertial measurements of ship motions and measurement of sea current. By combining a purely kinematic model together with linear Kalman filtering, the paper addresses the challenge of designing an optimal STW estimator by detailing the fundamental design choices. The proposed STW estimator is verified on simulated data and tested with measured data from an in-service container vessel.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ikonomakis, Angelos","Galeazzi, Roberto","Dietz, Jesper","Kähler Holst, Klaus","Nielsen, Ulrik Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369071"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-08","place":"Gubbio, it","start":"2019-05-06","title":"4th Hull Performance &amp; Insight Conference (HullPIC’19)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"application of sensor fusion to drive vessel performance","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/194234246/Final_HullPic_2019_word_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369071","ids":["dtu-d7e021c9-3c5b-455c-92d1-a23b7af96469"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2554D0BE8E0B19CEE391540E5D6CF0A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/194234246/Final_HullPic_2019_word_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"a p moller maersk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-MAE","l3nl":"A.P. Møller – Mærsk","l3nn":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"A.P. Moller - Maersk","namevar":["Maersk R&D"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-MAE","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Angelos","key":"ikonomakispau","last":"Ikonomakis","name":"Ikonomakis, Angelos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzipau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"dietzpau","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"kählerholstpau","last":"Kähler Holst","name":"Kähler Holst, Klaus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"106115f2-5a14-4e9b-ba17-0199c93439b5","name":"Nielsen, Ulrik Dam","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-2003","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["A.P. Møller – Mærsk","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d7e021c9-3c5b-455c-92d1-a23b7af96469"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Application of Sensor Fusion to Drive Vessel Performance","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-369071","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present the results of the R&D work that has been performed on avoiding electron cyclotron (EC) gas breakdown inside the launcher transmission line (TL) of the ITER collective Thomson scattering (CTS) diagnostic, due to encountering the fundamental EC resonance, which is located inside the port plug vacuum for the baseline ITER magnetic field scenario. If an EC breakdown occurs, this can lead to strong local absorption of the CTS gyrotron beam, as well as arcing inside the ITER vacuum vessel, which must be avoided. Due to the hostile, restrictive, and nuclear environment in ITER, it is not possible to implement the standard method for avoiding EC breakdown - a controlled atmosphere at the EC resonance. Instead, the CTS diagnostic will include a longitudinally-split electrically-biased corrugated waveguide (SBWG) in the launcher transmission line. The SBWG works by applying a transverse DC bias voltage across the two electrically-isolated waveguide halves, causing free electrons to diffuse out of the EC resonant region before they can cause an electron-impact ionisation-avalanche, and thus an EC breakdown. Due to insufficient experimental facilities, the functionality of the SBWG is validated through Monte Carlo electron modelling.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Larsen, Axel Wright","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Gonçalves, B.","Gutierrez Espinoza, Heidi Estibaliz","Henriques, E.","Infante, V.","Jensen, T.","Jessen, Martin","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Nonbøl, Erik","Luis, R.","Vale, A.","Lopes, A.","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Salewski, Mirko","Rasmussen, Jesper","Taormina, Arianna","Møllsøe, Claus","Mussenbrock, T.","Trieschmann, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-374697"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-10","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2019-05-06","title":"3rd European Conference on Plasma Diagnostics","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, 