{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-529542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crossing borders a cross disciplinary perspective on the study of mesoamerican visual culture","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-529542","identifier":[{"id":"85166763383","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e3f82f64-805f-4684-933b-7102530352b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-334373FCD4C7F50FE9702D6B1BC342B9"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1525/lavc.2019.000007c","issn":["25760947"],"issue":"1","journal":"Latin American and Latinx Visual Culture","pages":"105-110","status":"p","title":"Latin American and Latinx Visual Culture","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166763383"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e3f82f64-805f-4684-933b-7102530352b5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crossing Borders? : A Cross-Disciplinary Perspective on the Study of Mesoamerican Visual Culture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-529542","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Drug-related problems are a common complication in the transition from hospital to primary care and are associated with morbidity and increased health care costs. In this study, we evaluated the cost and consequences of a comprehensive pharmaceutical intervention compared with usual care, comprised of a medication review and patient interview before discharge and follow-up for polypharmacy patients. Methods: This economic evaluation was embedded within a randomized clinical trial. Patients were randomized to either the basic intervention group (n = 493) which received a medication review, the extended intervention group (n = 476) which received a medication review, discharge interview, and follow-up, or the control group (n = 498) which received standard care. Total health care costs were estimated over a period of 180 days at individual patient level from a health sector perspective. Results: The mean cost per patient was lower in the intervention groups (basic, €16 748; extended, €15 631) compared with the control group (€17 288), although these differences did not reach statistical significance. The costs of additional time used on medication reviews, patient interviews, and follow-ups (€88) were outweighed by a decrease in costs of readmissions. The results of the clinical study favored the extended intervention group on clinical outcomes, with statistical significance on a composite of readmissions or emergency department visits within 180 days after inclusion (hazard ratio 0.77, 95% confidence interval 0.64-0.93). Conclusions: This comprehensive pharmaceutical intervention was not costly and positive effects were seen in the clinical outcomes, thereby reaching a decrease in total cost per patient on average. The results thus indicate that the intervention is cost-effective and that the positive net effects can justify costs of the intervention.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Duckert, Marie-Louise","Lund, Mia Lolk","Henriksen, Jolene Pilegaard","Nielsen, Michelle Lyndgaard","Eriksen, Christina Skovsende","Buck, Thomas Croft","Hansen, Morten Rix","Pottegård, Anton","Hallas, Jesper","Kidholm, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584549"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical pharmacists","Cost analysis","Pharmacy Service Hospital","Polypharmacy","economics pharmaceutical"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["St Thomas Pharmacy"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cost consequence analysis evaluating multifaceted clinical pharmacist intervention targeting patient transitions of care from hospital to primary care","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170826737/jac5.1042.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584549","identifier":[{"id":"85077721326","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-279337b0-771d-4502-a666-5c4a19dd6e55"],"keyword":["clinical pharmacists","cost analysis","economics, pharmaceutical","pharmacy service, hospital","polypharmacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B49E914D4DD13D2A58F95A05A7ED57CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170826737/jac5.1042.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","E