{"abstract":"An oblivious data structure is a data structure where the memory access patterns reveals no information about the operations performed on it. Such data structures were introduced by Wang et al. [ACM SIGSAC’14] and are intended for situations where one wishes to store the data structure at an untrusted server. One way to obtain an oblivious data structure is simply to run a classic data structure on an oblivious RAM (ORAM). Until very recently, this resulted in an overhead of ω(lg n) for the most natural setting of parameters. Moreover, a recent lower bound for ORAMs by Larsen and Nielsen [CRYPTO’18] show that they always incur an overhead of at least Ω(lg n) if used in a black box manner. To circumvent the ω(lg n) overhead, researchers have instead studied classic data structure problems more directly and have obtained efficient solutions for many such problems such as stacks, queues, deques, priority queues and search trees. However, none of these data structures process operations faster than Θ(lg n), leaving open the question of whether even faster solutions exist. In this paper, we rule out this possibility by proving Ω(lg n) lower bounds for oblivious stacks, queues, deques, priority queues and search trees.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jacob, Riko","Larsen, Kasper Green","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S02-090.00-020238"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","end":"2019-01-09","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2019-01-06","title":"Thirtieth Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Data structure lower bounds","Memory access patterns","Oblivious RAM ORAM","Oblivious data structures","Untrusted servers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower bounds for oblivious data structures","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611975482.149","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.00-020238","identifier":[{"id":"85066934958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-68102b8b-3220-4def-8d7c-98dc32d32c7e","itu-5f0a648c-07e3-4728-afd7-db539373117a"],"keyword":["Data structure lower bounds","Memory access patterns","Oblivious RAM (ORAM)","Oblivious data structures","Untrusted servers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4058ED52A73D982995135D5E892B44BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611975482.149","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84740929/1810.10635.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Riko","key":"jacobpau","last":"Jacob","locid":"e6f70fb0-caf1-4736-b583-b0777bc1390f","name":"Jacob, Riko","orcid":"0000-0001-9470-1809","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper Green","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"13372598-332d-42b0-b510-3b70fefb0465","name":"Larsen, Kasper Green","orcid":"0000-0001-8841-5929","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Timothy M.","key":"chanpedh","last":"Chan","name":"Chan, Timothy M.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611975482.149","eisbn":["9781611975482"],"pages":"2439-2447","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","series":"Proceedings of the Thirtieth Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Thirtieth Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066934958"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-68102b8b-3220-4def-8d7c-98dc32d32c7e","itu-5f0a648c-07e3-4728-afd7-db539373117a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lower Bounds for Oblivious Data Structures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.00-020238","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Sound zones are valuable in scenarios where multiple people are present in the same room but want to listen to individual audio content without wearing headphones. The purpose of sound zone methods is to minimize the acoustic leakage between the zones by controlling multiple loudspeakers. This requires knowledge of how the loudspeakers interact with the room and radiate sound to the zones. That interaction is characterized by the transfer functions between the loudspeakers and microphones sampling the sound field in the zones. In this paper, the effect on the acoustic separation due to inherent noise in in situ transfer function measurements is investigated. The attainable separation is analyzed in the frequency range 20-300 Hz by means of the eigenfunctions of a rectangular room. The concept of observable degrees of freedom is introduced to indicate the number of active eigenfunctions, which are different within the zones at a given frequency. Likewise, controllable degrees of freedom indicate whether each source can excite the active eigenfunctions independently. It is argued that high separation can be achieved when the observable degrees of freedom are fewer than the controllable, and the target sound field can be described by the observable degrees of freedom. However, to attain this high separation it is a requirement that the details in the transfer functions associated with these degrees of freedom can be resolved in the presence of the measurement noise. For both simulated and experimental conditions the transfer functions are estimated using Bayesian inference and the uncertainty in the estimates is used to automatically regularize the sound field control. This regularization is seen to improve the performance when the measurement noise is correlated between the microphones and have little effect when the noise is uncorrelated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Martin Bo","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Fernandez Grande, Efren","Olesen, Søren Krarup"],"cuid":["S02-095.56-000126"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Møller, Martin Bo"],"keyword":["Personal audio","Sound field control","Sound zones"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-BOO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-BOO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the influence of transfer function noise on sound zone control in a room","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/192311460/hkkr_08732395.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-095.56-000126","identifier":[{"id":"85068203233","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-026f1c0f-d46a-43b8-bbc4-bb9769647487","dtu-8dd83767-6721-4cad-8370-11eb633dec76"],"keyword":["Personal audio","Sound field control","Sound zones"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-820F8D27DB734C1DB1CAA87D1AE59321"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/192311460/hkkr_08732395.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/335131387/hkkr_08732395.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Signal and Information Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"bang olufsen","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-BOO","l3nl":"Bang & Olufsen","l3nn":"Bang & Olufsen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bang & Olufsen","namevar":["Bang & Olufsen A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-BOO","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bo","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"cc048a47-3f70-4d96-99ac-f3d51a03e4b0","name":"Møller, Martin Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Krarup","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"215999a6-bbe8-4d92-acb8-0b35df2e6492","name":"Olesen, Søren Krarup","orcid":"0000-0002-7950-0926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/taslp.2019.2921151","issn":["23299290"],"issue":"9","journal":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","pages":"1405-1418","paperid":"8732395","publisher":"IEEE Advancing Technology for Humanity","status":"p","title":"IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068203233"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Bang & Olufsen","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-026f1c0f-d46a-43b8-bbc4-bb9769647487","dtu-8dd83767-6721-4cad-8370-11eb633dec76"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On the influence of transfer function noise on sound zone control in a room","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.56-000126","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Neurological injuries remain the leading cause of death in comatose patients resuscitated from out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Adequate blood pressure is of paramount importance to optimize cerebral perfusion and to minimize secondary brain injury. Markers measuring global cerebral ischemia caused by cardiac arrest and consecutive resuscitation and reflecting the metabolic variations after successful resuscitation are needed to assist a more individualized post-resuscitation care. Currently, no technique is available for bedside evaluation of global cerebral energy state, and until now blood pressure targets have been based on limited clinical evidence. Recent experimental and clinical studies indicate that it might be possible to evaluate cerebral oxidative metabolism from measuring the lactate-to-pyruvate (LP) ratio of the draining venous blood. In this study, jugular bulb microdialysis and immediate bedside biochemical analysis are introduced as new diagnostic tools to evaluate the effect of higher mean arterial blood pressure on global cerebral metabolism and the degree of cellular damage after OHCA. METHODS/DESIGN: This is a single-center, randomized, double-blinded, superiority trial. Sixty unconscious patients with sustained return of spontaneous circulation after OHCA will be randomly assigned in a one-to-one fashion to low (63 mm Hg) or high (77 mm Hg) mean arterial blood pressure target. The primary end-point will be a difference in mean LP ratio within 48 h between blood pressure groups. Secondary end-points are (1) association between LP ratio and all-cause intensive care unit (ICU) mortality and (2) association between LP ratio and survival to hospital discharge with poor neurological function. DISCUSSION: Markers measuring cerebral ischemia caused by cardiac arrest and consecutive resuscitation and reflecting the metabolic changes after successful resuscitation are urgently needed to enable a more personalized post-resuscitation care and prognostication. Jugular bulb microdialysis may provide a reliable global estimate of cerebral metabolic state and can be implemented as an entirely new and less invasive diagnostic tool for ICU patients after OHCA and has implications for early prognosis and treatment. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT03095742 ). Registered March 30, 2017.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Mölström, Simon","Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","Nordström, Carl H","Hassager, Christian","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Möller, Sören","Schmidt, Henrik","Toft, Palle"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-041880"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Mølstrøm, Simon"],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Brain metabolism","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Cerebral metabolism","Double Blind Method","Energy Metabolism","Humans","Lactic Acid metabolism","Microdialysis","Neuroprotection","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Pyruvic Acid metabolism","Research Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design paper of the blood pressure targets in post resuscitation care and bedside monitoring of cerebral energy state a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-019-3397-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Until now, the study has been supported by non-profit organizations, including the University of Southern Denmark, Region of Southern Denmark, and Department of Anesthesiology and Intensive Care, Odense. The study received a grant from the A.P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Science of 50.000 DKK (grant number 17-L-0030). Any additional funding will be included along with the publication of trial results."],"id":"S02-099.94-041880","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6558732","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31182135","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85067169901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-428d5f03-6506-4bd8-80c1-579ac0cca920","sdu-95522d6b-2994-47f7-a9c9-2bf622300809"],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Brain/metabolism","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Cerebral metabolism","Double-Blind Method","Energy Metabolism","Humans","Lactic Acid/metabolism","Microdialysis","Neuroprotection","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/therapy","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Pyruvic Acid/metabolism","Research Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8E3FA0571C03A2539316688C88CBD634"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151670284/Design_paper_of_the_blood_pressure_targets_in_post_resuscitation_care_and_bedside_monitoring_of_cerebral_energy_state.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236220784/document_11_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-019-3397-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"mölströmpau","last":"Mölström","locid":"197d79e9-dd07-401b-90f8-1c26dc359db2","name":"Mølstrøm, Simon","name_org":"Mölström, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2778-8075","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels Halfeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"18f40b9c-d8d6-4d6b-b3af-374f6221676a","name":"Nielsen, Troels Halfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3943-8128","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl H.","key":"nordströmpau","last":"Nordström","locid":"832530b4-9bf3-4eb3-bbda-ad9fad3cae33","name":"Nordström, Carl-Henrik","name_org":"Nordström, Carl H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","name":"Kjærgaard, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sören","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"905018dc-c6c4-4a79-b50d-d0c08618e77a","name":"Möller, Sören","orcid":"0000-0003-0858-4269","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Palle","key":"toftpau","last":"Toft","locid":"a06bd771-b511-4783-8c06-333267c94154","name":"Toft, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-3188-449X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31182135"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-019-3397-1","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"journal":"Trials","paperid":"344","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067169901"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-428d5f03-6506-4bd8-80c1-579ac0cca920","sdu-95522d6b-2994-47f7-a9c9-2bf622300809"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Design paper of the \"Blood pressure targets in post-resuscitation care and bedside monitoring of cerebral energy state: a randomized clinical trial\"","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-041880","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"I dette kapitel belyser vi, hvordan idrætseleverne i deres tilblivelsesprocesser arbejder på at leve op til idrætsklassens dobbelte udviklingsmål, og hvordan denne standard for udvikling af talent i en idrætsklasse presser dem, hvis de af den ene eller den anden grund får vanskeligheder med at udvikle sig i den rigtige takt og retning.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Olesen, Jesper Stilling"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002502"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Grundskole","Talent"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tilblivelsesmuligheder variationer og brud","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://unipress.dk/udgivelser/t/talentudvikling-og-elitesport-i-skolen/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002502","ids":["aau-324c0689-1db2-452c-a90d-42e32d92ebe2","au-dbe4d3fb-508c-42d7-9ec4-702e4c0045de"],"keyword":["Grundskole","Talent"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-48CBFA3CE9D3ABA3718F674FC8506F7F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences (SSI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Stilling","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Jesper Stilling","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpedh","last":"Stilling Olesen","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Stilling","key":"olesenpedh","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Jesper Stilling","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["978 87 7184 144 2"],"issn":["19042698"],"issue":"18","pages":"129-150","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","series":"Asterisk","status":"p","title":"Talentudvikling og elitesport i skolen"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-324c0689-1db2-452c-a90d-42e32d92ebe2","au-dbe4d3fb-508c-42d7-9ec4-702e4c0045de"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tilblivelsesmuligheder, variationer og brud","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-002502","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The primary goal was to validate a Danish translated version of the Catquest-9SF by Rasch analysis. The secondary goal was to investigate whether preoperative Catquest-9SF scores, best-corrected visual acuity, comorbidity, gender, age or corneal astigmatism could predict improvements in subjective outcome. METHODS: In a prospective trial, 250 patients eligible for cataract surgery were included. Patients filled out the translated Catquest-9SF questionnaire before surgery and again 3 months after surgery. Both preoperative and postoperative questionnaires were included in the Rasch analysis. A multiple reverse stepwise regression model was used to investigate the correlation between preoperative measurements and subjective improvement. RESULTS: The preliminary Rasch analysis showed misfit of items 4 and 6. These items were removed, and the remaining seven items demonstrated a measurement precision of 2.78, a person reliability coefficient of 0.89, ordered response categories, infit of 0.69-1.22, outfit of 0.73-1.14, observed raw variance explained by measures of 70.4% and an eigenvalue of 1.7. Item 7 showed a mild DIF for gender (0.54 logits), and person mean Rasch score targeting was -1.69 logits. Preoperative Catquest score was the only parameter with a significant correlation to a gain in subjective outcome (p < 0.001). A preoperative Catquest-9SF score of 0.5 carried a 95% likelihood of an increase in subjective outcome. CONCLUSION: The Danish version of the Catquest-9SF fit the Rasch model. Only preoperative Catquest-9SF score was correlated to subjective improvement, and a cut-off value of 0.5 predicted an improvement in subjective outcome with 95% probability.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Esben","Lundström, Mats","Pesudovs, Konrad","Hjortdal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006068"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Aged","Cataract epidemiology","Denmark epidemiology","Disability Evaluation","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Male","Morbidity trends","Prospective Studies","Psychometrics methods","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Sickness Impact Profile","Surveys and Questionnaires standards","Visual Acuity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Australian College of Optometry, Carlton, Victoria, Australia."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of catquest 000000000009sf in danish developing a revised form of the catquest 000000000009sf the danish catquest 000000000007sf","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85053692123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-006068","identifier":[{"id":"30242976","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000459637900010","type":"wos"},{"id":"85053692123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7d176990-e3a4-4a1b-aaae-af4d31708c61","au-4b5148ab-7bcd-4e17-9bc7-42a09c3f9261"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Aged","Cataract Extraction/rehabilitation","Cataract/epidemiology","Denmark/epidemiology","Disability Evaluation","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Male","Morbidity/trends","Prospective Studies","Psychometrics/methods","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Sickness Impact Profile","Surveys and Questionnaires/standards","Visual Acuity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5368EC0BCCDCA8758A68727AAA5BD893"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Ophthalmology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - University Clinic for Interdisciplinary Orthopaedic Pathways (UCOP)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Australian College of Optometry, Carlton, Victoria, Australia."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7a8107e2-2d34-4191-98cb-d87ac45f274e","name":"Nielsen, Esben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mats","key":"lundströmpau","last":"Lundström","name":"Lundström, Mats","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Konrad","key":"pesudovspau","last":"Pesudovs","name":"Pesudovs, Konrad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30242976"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.13921","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"173-177","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053692123"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7d176990-e3a4-4a1b-aaae-af4d31708c61","au-4b5148ab-7bcd-4e17-9bc7-42a09c3f9261"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Validation of Catquest-9SF in Danish : developing a revised form of the Catquest-9SF - the Danish Catquest-7SF","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-006068","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Formålet med dette dokument er at introducere nogle af de potentialer, der kan være ved en omfattende implementering af termisk pyrolyse af afgrøderester og organiske gødningsfraktioner for reduktion af drivhusgasudledning fra dansk landbrug. Pyrolyse vil have til formål 1) at lagre biogent kulstof i landbrugsjorden, 2) at øge produktionen af dansk bioenergi, 3) at reducere de direkte emissioner af lattergas og metan fra behandling, opbevaring og anvendelse af organiske gødningsfraktioner, og 4) at foranledige en række yderligere emissionsreduktioner og dyrkningsmæssige fordele via jordforbedring. Notatet vil beskrive disse fire formål og give en kvalitativ vurdering af de relaterede reduktionspotentialer.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Gadsbøll, Rasmus Østergaard","Clausen, Lasse Røngaard","Stiesdal, Henrik","Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","Müller-Stöver, Dorette Sophie","Bruun, Sander","Winding, Anne"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-019686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biochar","Biokul","Klima","Landbrug"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduktion af landbrugets klimaaftryk ved termisk pyrolyse af afgrøderester og organiske gødningsfraktioner","src":["au","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/66631371/DTU_RUC_KU_AU_2019_Reduktion_af_landbrugets_klimaaftryk_ved_pyrolyse.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-019686","ids":["au-60b0aa40-0439-43a5-ab53-3629b036c573","ruc-a3eb445f-7d34-494b-a673-326775d3e87b"],"keyword":["Biochar","Biokul","Drivhusgas","Jordforbedring","Klima","Landbrug"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-A81E122629331475C9A0D910BF90A9D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/66631371/DTU_RUC_KU_AU_2019_Reduktion_af_landbrugets_klimaaftryk_ved_pyrolyse.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/212347768/DTU_RUC_KU_AU_2019_Reduktion_af_landbrugets_klimaaftryk_ved_pyrolyse.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark (DTU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dansk Gasteknisk Center"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Birk","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Østergaard","key":"gadsbøllpau","last":"Gadsbøll","name":"Gadsbøll, Rasmus Østergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Røngaard","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Lasse Røngaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"stiesdalpau","last":"Stiesdal","name":"Stiesdal, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Tobias Pape","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"e0f8cb5c-1327-4f91-99a5-2da7ebda73e8","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"0bc8cc02-9199-4a75-9e51-7dd5ceba9583","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8929-9691","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorette Sophie","key":"müllerstöverpau","last":"Müller-Stöver","name":"Müller-Stöver, Dorette Sophie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sander","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Sander","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"windingpau","last":"Winding","locid":"143b20bd-245f-4e46-97f8-58fe24c1bda1","name":"Winding, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-7491-4548","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"12","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","dansk gasteknisk center"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-60b0aa40-0439-43a5-ab53-3629b036c573","ruc-a3eb445f-7d34-494b-a673-326775d3e87b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Reduktion af landbrugets klimaaftryk ved termisk pyrolyse af afgrøderester og organiske gødningsfraktioner","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-019686","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Rationale: Within the field of personalized medicine there is an increasing focus on designing flexible, multifunctional drug delivery systems that combine high efficacy with minimal side effects, by tailoring treatment to the individual. Methods: We synthesized a chemically stabilized ~4 nm nucleic acid nanoscaffold, and characterized its assembly, stability and functional properties in vitro and in vivo. We tested its flexibility towards multifunctionalization by conjugating various biomolecules to the four modules of the system. The pharmacokinetics, targeting capability and bioimaging properties of the structure were investigated in mice. The role of avidity in targeted liver cell internalization was investigated by flow cytometry, confocal microscopy and in vivo by fluorescent scanning of the blood and organs of the animals. Results: We have developed a nanoscaffold that rapidly and with high efficiency can self-assemble four chemically conjugated functionalities into a stable, in vivo-applicable system with complete control of stoichiometry and site specificity. The circulation time of the nanoscaffold could be tuned by functionalization with various numbers of polyethylene glycol polymers or with albumin-binding fatty acids. Highly effective hepatocyte-specific internalization was achieved with increasing valencies of tri-antennary galactosamine (triGalNAc) in vitro and in vivo. Conclusion: With its facile functionalization, stoichiometric control, small size and high serum- and thermostability, the nanoscaffold presented here constitutes a novel and flexible platform technology for theranostics.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Andersen, Veronica Liv","Vinther, Mathias","Kumar, Rajesh","Ries, Annika","Wengel, Jesper","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Kjems, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026630"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kjems, Jørgen"],"keyword":["Bioconjugation","Drug delivery","LNA","Nanomedicine","Personalized medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a self assembled modular nucleic acid based nanoscaffold for multivalent theranostic medicine","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/thno.32060","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026630","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6525989","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31131060","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85066857969","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c0351f45-7cdf-4f4d-9b93-903ca1d9e260","sdu-df49f15d-341b-42f2-9ce6-5c0524cd2244"],"keyword":["Bioconjugation","Drug delivery","LNA","Nanomedicine","Personalized medicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-38B4AA302D4ED02083850CD4541BE6A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151816522/A_self_assembled_modular_nucleic_acid_based_nanoscaffold_for_multivalent_theranostic_medicine.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/thno.32060","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronica Liv","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"de7beb69-fdb9-4569-822b-ba1a3dd1cf79","name":"Andersen, Veronica Liv","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"3a9a8008-ecaa-4865-a6bf-a99688f12c6a","name":"Vinther, Mathias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rajesh","key":"kumarpau","last":"Kumar","locid":"91cb95ad-5fbb-47ce-8554-4d49a3a99bf5","name":"Kumar, Rajesh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"riespau","last":"Ries","locid":"7eba40b2-7f55-4a1a-b1bd-b28f0f54c98d","name":"Ries, Annika","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"wengelpau","last":"Wengel","locid":"4803676b-fbaf-4593-baab-147b5465bbec","name":"Wengel, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-9835-1009","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sejrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemspau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31131060"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7150/thno.32060","issn":["18387640"],"issue":"9","journal":"Theranostics","pages":"2662-2677","publisher":"Ivyspring International Publisher","status":"p","title":"Theranostics","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066857969"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c0351f45-7cdf-4f4d-9b93-903ca1d9e260","sdu-df49f15d-341b-42f2-9ce6-5c0524cd2244"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A self-assembled, modular nucleic acid-based nanoscaffold for multivalent theranostic medicine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026630","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The prevalence of lifestyle diseases has escalated, and effective exercise training programmes are warranted. This study tested the hypothesis that regular participation in small-sided team handball training could provide beneficial health effects on cardiovascular, skeletal, and muscular parameters in young adult untrained men. Method: Twenty-six untrained 20-30-year-old men were randomly allocated to either a team handball training group (HG; n = 14), which completed 1.9 ± 0.3 training sessions per week over 12 weeks, or an inactive control group (CG; n = 12). Physiological training adaptations were assessed pre- and post interventions by DXA scans, blood samples, muscle biopsies, and physical tests. Results: The average heart rate during training was equivalent to 84 ± 4% of maximal heart rate. Compared to CG, HG displayed significant increases in VO2max (11 ± 6%), proximal femur bone mineral density (2 ± 1%), whole-body bone mineral content (2 ± 1%), intermittent endurance performance (32 ± 16%), incremental treadmill test performance (16 ± 7%) and muscle citrate synthase activity (22 ± 28%) as well as decreases in total fat mass (7 ± 7%) and total fat percentage (6 ± 7%) (all p < 0.05). There were no significant changes in muscle mass, blood pressure, resting heart rate, muscle hydroxyl-acyl-dehydrogenase activity, or blood lipids (all p > 0.05). Conclusion: Participation in regular recreational team handball training was associated with positive cardiovascular, skeletal, and muscular adaptations, including increased maximal oxygen uptake, increased muscle enzymatic activity, and improved bone mineralization as well as lower fat percentage. These findings suggest that recreational team handball training may be an effective health-promoting activity for young adult men.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hornstrup, Therese","Løwenstein, Frederik Terkildsen","Larsen, Mikkel Allerslev","Helge, Eva Wulff","Póvoas, S","Helge, Jørn Wulff","Nielsen, Jens Jung","Fristrup, Bjørn","Andersen, Jesper Løvind","Gliemann, Lasse","Nybo, Lars","Krustrup, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047078"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hornstrup, Therese"],"country":["Canada","Portugal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","McGill University","University Institute of Maia","University of Exeter","niversity Institute of Maia"],"keyword":["Ball games","Bone markers","Bone mineralization","Exercise training","Faculty of Science","Fat percentage","Maximal oxygen uptake","Muscle enzyme activity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiovascular muscular and skeletal adaptations to recreational team handball training a randomized controlled trial with young adult untrained men","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85057308831","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-047078","identifier":[{"id":"85057308831","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30474740","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ea4ee7df-9a3a-465a-a898-6c9dfc7f5841","sdu-9c563ec8-6800-43b5-8fb7-45097d27491b"],"keyword":["Ball games","Bone markers","Bone mineralization","Exercise training","Faculty of Science","Fat percentage","Maximal oxygen uptake","Muscle enzyme activity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-730F50129D1B491832039CC22BF728A2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"niversity institute of maia","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"niversity Institute of Maia","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pt","key":"university institute of maia","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Institute of Maia","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Sport and Health Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Therese","