{"abstract":"A number of studies suggest that scientific papers with women in leading-author positions attract fewer citations than those with men in leading-author positions. We report the results of a matched case-control study of 1,269,542 papers in selected areas of medicine published between 2008 and 2014. We find that papers with female authors are, on average, cited between 6.5 and 12.6% less than papers with male authors. However, the standardized mean differences are very small, and the percentage overlaps between the distributions for male and female authors are extensive. Adjusting for self-citations, number of authors, international collaboration and journal prestige, we find near-identical per-paper citation impact for women and men in first and last author positions, with self-citations and journal prestige accounting for most of the small average differences. Our study demonstrates the importance of focusing greater attention on within-group variability and between-group overlap of distributions when interpreting and reporting results of gender-based comparisons of citation impact.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andersen, Jens Peter","Schneider, Jesper Wiborg","Jagsi, Reshma","Nielsen, Mathias Wullum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255951"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Jens Peter"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Michigan"],"keyword":["GAP","Sex differences","Women"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender variations in citation distribution in medicine are very small and due to self citation and journal prestige","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.45374","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255951","identifier":[{"id":"31305239","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6677534","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000478691700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85071059592","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ddd938e8-ebb4-41ef-b4c2-8e2106214c27"],"keyword":["GAP","SCHOLARLY PRODUCTIVITY","SCIENTIFIC IMPACT","SEX-DIFFERENCES","WOMEN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A9EFDC72B56D2565AC3D8A01CB755618"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.45374","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science - Danish Centre for Studies in Research and Research Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of michigan","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Peter","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b1e70d8a-0883-480d-8c07-5a7775417377","name":"Andersen, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2444-6210","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Wiborg","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"8fcbf953-b83f-4fe7-b698-d4aec218e1f5","name":"Schneider, Jesper Wiborg","orcid":"0000-0001-5556-0919","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Reshma","key":"jagsipau","last":"Jagsi","name":"Jagsi, Reshma","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Wullum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"62286630-268a-4741-82ab-6fa4f08d5706","name":"Nielsen, Mathias Wullum","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31305239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7554/elife.45374","issn":["2050084X"],"journal":"eLife","paperid":"45374","publisher":"eLife Sciences Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"eLife","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071059592"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ddd938e8-ebb4-41ef-b4c2-8e2106214c27"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Gender variations in citation distribution in medicine are very small and due to self-citation and journal prestige","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255951","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PARAFAC2 is a widely applicable method often used for analyzing multi-way chromatographic data. We recently proposed a probabilistic framework for PARAFAC2[1]. The probabilistic formulations allow for a principled way of determining the number of latent components as well as modeling heteroscedastic noise. In this work we present a summary of the probabilistic PARAFAC2 models and their properties by revisiting the previous results of the analyzed data sets in a concise fashion.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Philip Johan Havemann","Nielsen, Søren F. V.","Hinrich, Jesper Løve","Schmidt, Mikkel Nørgaard","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Mørup, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-333822"],"event":{"acronym":"NIPS","end":"2019-12-14","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2019-12-08","title":"33rd Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of chromatographic data using the probabilistic parafac000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/200641615/NeurIPS_ML4PS_2019_143.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-333822","ids":["dtu-622f32f8-71d7-4953-98b0-996bf650d1e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D01BA782D8B75CF256CE1AFDCE632BAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/200641615/NeurIPS_ML4PS_2019_143.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Sennheiser Communications A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip Johan Havemann","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"c50537ce-d98e-475f-96f3-90db25281943","name":"Jørgensen, Philip Johan Havemann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren F. V.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Søren F. V.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Løve","key":"hinrichpau","last":"Hinrich","locid":"e3c8c713-afa8-4d6e-9071-774487e7e599","name":"Hinrich, Jesper Løve","orcid":"0000-0003-0258-7151","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Nørgaard","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"55dbf06c-c859-4324-8104-3fa649d8d140","name":"Schmidt, Mikkel Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6927-8869","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer Hougaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"243ae993-e526-4121-b28a-aabf62c3df84","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8606-7641","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","locid":"7ffdfaca-76bd-44ec-a98f-13fe4f033b71","name":"Mørup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-4985-4368","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Second Workshop on Machine Learning and the Physical Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","sennheiser communications a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-622f32f8-71d7-4953-98b0-996bf650d1e0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Analysis of Chromatographic Data using the Probabilistic PARAFAC2","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333822","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The electron cyclotron emission (ECE) in fusion devices is non-trivial to model in detail at frequencies well below the fundamental resonance where the plasma is optically thin. However, doing so is important for evaluating the background for microwave diagnostics operating in this frequency range. Here we present a general framework for estimating the ECE levels of fusion plasmas at such frequencies using ensemble-averaging of rays traced through many randomized wall reflections. This enables us to account for the overall vacuum vessel geometry, self-consistently include cross-polarization, and quantify the statistical uncertainty on the resulting ECE spectra. Applying this to ITER conditions, we find simulated ECE levels that increase strongly with frequency and plasma temperature in the considered range of 55–75 GHz. At frequencies smaller than 70 GHz, we predict an X-mode ECE level below 100 eV in the ITER baseline plasma scenario, but with corresponding intensities reaching keV levels in the hotter hybrid plasma scenario. Benchmarking against the SPECE raytracing code reveals good agreement under relevant conditions, and the predicted strength of X-mode to O-mode conversion induced by wall reflections is consistent with estimates from existing fusion devices. We discuss possible implications of our findings for ITER microwave diagnostics such as ECE, reflectometry, and collective Thomson scattering.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Figini, L.","Jensen, T.","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Larsen, Axel Wright","Leipold, Frank","Micheletti, D.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Salewski, Mirko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346051"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Jesper"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Research Council of Italy"],"keyword":["Electron cyclotron emission","ITER","Microwave diagnostics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling the electron cyclotron emission below the fundamental resonance in iter","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196407430/ece_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346051","identifier":[{"id":"85072061988","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8b177c90-802b-420d-9c71-b75de3da8140"],"keyword":["Electron cyclotron emission","ITER","Microwave diagnostics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A144D9888F5A5017B09CCF1FFE84DBFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196407430/ece_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"stejnerpau","last":"Stejner","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Stejner, M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"figinipau","last":"Figini","name":"Figini, L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e840242d-2592-40b7-bc0b-02995c8fe6ba","name":"Jensen, T.","orcid":"0000-0001-9801-1530","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E. B.","key":"klinkbypau","last":"Klinkby","locid":"1a611e33-cd53-43a3-9b7c-ebdd92d302f7","name":"Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","name_org":"Klinkby, E. B.","orcid":"0000-0002-1908-5644","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. B.","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","name_org":"Korsholm, S. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A. W.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"55ff89d0-a9e8-4bd0-b3f8-1c544444c72a","name":"Larsen, Axel Wright","name_org":"Larsen, A. W.","orcid":"0000-0002-7837-717X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"leipoldpau","last":"Leipold","locid":"fb1ca27f-36e0-43a2-8779-3d8135a2a8dc","name":"Leipold, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3107-6713","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"michelettipau","last":"Micheletti","name":"Micheletti, D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","name_org":"Nielsen, S. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","name_org":"Salewski, M.","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1361-6587/ab2f4a","issn":["07413335","13616587"],"issn_org":["07413335"],"issue":"9","journal":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","paperid":"095002","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072061988"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b177c90-802b-420d-9c71-b75de3da8140"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modeling the electron cyclotron emission below the fundamental resonance in ITER","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-346051","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The main objective of WGBFAS was to assess the status and produce a draft advice of the following stocks: • Sole in Division 3.a, SDs 20–24 • Cod in Kattegat, Cod in SDs 22–24, Cod in SDs 24–32 • Herring in SDs 25–27, 28.2, 29 and 32 • Herring in SD 28.1 (Gulf of Riga) • Herring in SDs 30-31 (Gulf of Bothnia) • Sprat in SDs 22–32 • Plaice in SDs 21–23, Plaice in SDs 24–32 • Flounder in SDs 22–23 (no catch advice) • Flounder in SDs 24–25 (no catch advice) The WG was not requested to assess the following stocks in 2019, as no advice was needed: • Flounder in SDs 26+28 • Flounder in SDs 27+29–32 • Brill in SDs 22–32 • Dab in SDs 22–32 • Turbot in SDs 22–32 It was, however, decided by the group to compile and update the input data for 2018 and thereby also conduct update assessments for these latest five stocks. In the introductory chapter of this report the WG, in agreement with the ToRs, considers and comments on the ecosystem and fisheries overviews, reviews the progress on benchmark processes, identifies the data needed for next year’s data call with some suggestions for improvements in the data call, and summarizes general and stock-specific research needs. The introduction further summarizes the work of other WGs relevant to the WGBFAS, and the assessment methods used. Finally, the introduction presents a brief overview of each stock and quite extensively discusses the ecosystem considerations of the Baltic Sea and ecosystem changes that have been analytically considered in the stock assessments. The results of the analytical stock assessment or survey trends for the species listed above are presented for all the stocks with the same species in the same sections. The analytical models used for the stock assessments were XSA, SAM and SS3. For most flatfish (data limited stocks), CPUE trends from bottom-trawl surveys were used in the assessment (except plaice in SDs 24–25 for which relative SSB from SAM was used). For cod in SDs 24–32, a full analytical assessment (using SS3) could be performed, after the compilation/benchmark work undertaken in 2018–2019. The report ends with references, annexes with the response to a special request, links to Stock Annexes, and list of Working Documents.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Amosova, Viktoriia","Bergenius, Mikaela","Boje, Jesper","Carlshamre, Sofia","Eero, Margit","Fernandez, Ruth","Gröhsler, Tomas","Gutkowska, Julita","Hommik, Kristiina","Horbowy, Jan","Jounela, Pekka","Kaljuste, Olavi","Karpushevskiy, Igor","Klinger, Richard","Krumme, Uwe","Lövgren, Johan","Mirny, Zuzanna","Albertsen, Christoffer Moesgaard","Neuenfeldt, Stefan","Plikshs, Maris","Nielsen, Anders","Öhman, Kristin","Pekcan-Hekim, Zeynep","Pönni, Jukka","Putnis, Ivars","Raid, Tiit","Raitaniemi, Jari","Rodriguez-Tress, Paco","Statkus, Romas","Stoetera, Sven","Storr-Paulsen, Marie","Ulrich, Clara","Ustups, Didzis","Zolubas, Tomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368273"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Game and Fisheries Research Institute","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","University of Hamburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["International Council for the Exploration of the Sea"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"baltic fisheries assessment working group wgbfas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17895/ices.pub.5949","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-368273","ids":["dtu-d5493805-aa19-4e5b-ba9a-a383620f0a11"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi"