{"abstract":"Ion cyclotron emission (ICE) signals whose spectral peaks match the fundamental cyclotron frequencies of hydrogen and tritium in the plasma core, near the magnetic axis, are observed in ASDEX Upgrade deuterium plasmas. In these cases the only source of energetic (⩾1 MeV) hydrogen and tritium ions is D–D fusion reactions between neutral beam injected deuterium ions and bulk deuterium ions. Hydrogen-matched core ICE is observed in a wide variety of ASDEX Upgrade plasmas, while tritium-matched core ICE is (so far) only observed in so-called H-mode density limit plasmas. In all cases ICE signals are detected directly using B-dot probes, which provide information on the emission frequency, the amplitude, and, in principle, the parallel wavenumber values. These observations support the idea of using an ICE-based diagnostic to monitor the presence of fusion-born alpha particles in tritium-burning fusion plasmas on devices such as JET, ITER, CFETR, or DEMO.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Ochoukov, R.","Bilato, R.","Bobkov, V.","Chapman, B.","Chapman, S.C.","Dendy, R.O.","Dunne, M.","Faugel, H.","García-Muñoz, M.","Geiger, B.","Kallenbach, A.","Kappatou, A.","McClements, K.G.","Moseev, D.","Nielsen, S.","Rasmussen, Jesper","Schneider, P.","Weiland, M.","Noterdaeme, J.-M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-376875"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ochoukov, R."],"country":["Germany","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Seville","University of Warwick"],"keyword":["Ion cyclotron emission"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"core plasma ion cyclotron emission driven by fusion born ions","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/216541168/Ochoukov_Core.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014–2018 under grant agreement No 633053. The views and opinions expressed herein do not necessarily reflect those of the European Commission. Rodolphe D’Inca’s contribution to the ICE diagnostic on ASDEX Upgrade is explicitly acknowledged."],"id":"S01-000.00-376875","identifier":[{"id":"85063536960","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f196efb8-561a-42b8-a9f7-0391144154d6"],"keyword":["ICRF Waves","Ion cyclotron emission","Tokamak plasmas"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7855E91FA19F9E5FEBB5432C65F8AB7F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/216541168/Ochoukov_Core.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"united kingdom atomic energy authority","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"ochoukovrpau","last":"Ochoukov","name":"Ochoukov, R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"bilatorpau","last":"Bilato","name":"Bilato, R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"bobkovvpau","last":"Bobkov","name":"Bobkov, V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"chapmanbpau","last":"Chapman","name":"Chapman, B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.C.","key":"chapmanscpau","last":"Chapman","name":"Chapman, S.C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"R.O.","key":"dendyropau","last":"Dendy","name":"Dendy, R.O.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"dunnempau","last":"Dunne","name":"Dunne, M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H.","key":"faugelhpau","last":"Faugel","name":"Faugel, H.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"garcíamuñozmpau","last":"García-Muñoz","name":"García-Muñoz, M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"geigerbpau","last":"Geiger","name":"Geiger, B.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"kallenbachapau","last":"Kallenbach","name":"Kallenbach, A.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"kappatouapau","last":"Kappatou","name":"Kappatou, A.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"K.G.","key":"mcclementskgpau","last":"McClements","name":"McClements, K.G.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"moseevdpau","last":"Moseev","name":"Moseev, D.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"nielsenspau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, S.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"rasmussenjesperpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","name_org":"Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"schneiderppau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, P.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"weilandmpau","last":"Weiland","name":"Weiland, M.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.-M.","key":"noterdaemejmpau","last":"Noterdaeme","name":"Noterdaeme, J.-M.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/aaebb0","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"014001","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063536960"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f196efb8-561a-42b8-a9f7-0391144154d6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Core plasma ion cyclotron emission driven by fusion-born ions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-376875","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Telemonitoring of cardiac implantable electronic devices (CIEDs) has many advantages. However, telemonitoring involves clinical work that is often overlooked or considered a burden, such as the work performed during telephone contact with patients. The objective of this study was to scrutinize telephone calls to and from patients to understand the clinical workload in CIED remote monitoring. The focus was on time spent, type of work, and the content of telephone contact with patients. Methods: A combined quantitative and qualitative observational study was conducted at a large CIED remote monitoring center. The unit ‘encounter’ was used to describe either a telephone call between patient and clinician and/or a complete review of a CIED data transmission. The time spent on different encounters was measured, the telephone call content was identified and described, and the different types of clinical work were described. Results: A total of 260 encounters were analyzed. Encounters that involved patient telephone contact were more time consuming. Telephone calls were mostly about the home monitoring box, CIED transmission data, and symptoms. In most telephone calls, two or more topics appeared. Five types of clinical work were performed: inclusion work, coordination work, diagnostic work, education work, and comfort work. Inclusion work and diagnostic work were the dominant types. Discussion: Patient telephone contact in CIED telemonitoring is typically described as a “burden”. This study unpacks the contents and functions of telephone calls between patients and clinicians and suggests that the function of telephone contact should be recognized as integral, rather than burdensome, to the clinical work in CIED telemonitoring.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andersen, Tariq Osman","Nielsen, Karen Dam","Moll, Jonas","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398954"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device","Telecare","Telemonitoring","Workload"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unpacking telemonitoring work workload and telephone calls to patients in implanted cardiac device care","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2019.06.021","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-398954","identifier":[{"id":"31445281","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85069640409","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0928d413-c9ad-43ba-bbb3-9e41bc92e95d"],"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device","Patient-Clinician collaboration","Remote monitoring work","Telecare","Telemonitoring","Telephone communication","Workload"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E33779F73B967FE06F72FA61BAA3962D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/227044804/OAAndersenEtAl.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2019.06.021","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tariq Osman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"dfc4b3ec-64f4-4e84-92f