{"abstract":"Formålet er at identificere udviklingen i kystfiskeriet efter revisionen af kystfiskerordningen 1. januar 2017. Ved kystfiskeri forstås fiskeri med fartøjer i kystfiskerordningen. Udviklingen identificeres som helhed for fartøjer i ordningen og for undergrupper, såvel som der sammenlignes med udviklingen for andre fartøjer. Nøgletal analyseres for fiskerflåden, fangster, fangstværdi, priser, økonomi, beskæftigelse og kvoter. Der ses primært på kommercielt aktive fartøjer. Den økonomiske og sociale udvikling identificeres, den sociale dog alene på grundlag af beskæftigelsen. Den biologiske og miljømæssige udvikling vurderes ikke.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Max","Nielsen, Rasmus","Andersen, Jesper Levring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-426537"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udviklingen i dansk kystfiskeri efter 000000002016","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/229012668/IFRO_Udredning_2019_21.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-426537","ids":["ku-37acd70c-ee1c-4a66-84b0-567b7c17ebaa"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2C84CCEF92B7A9BDE276947A7F8750DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/229012668/IFRO_Udredning_2019_21.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Environment and Natural Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Max","key":"nielsenmaxpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8d20668c-7b6b-4bf5-86e6-055001d5e015","name":"Nielsen, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-4283-1852","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenrasmuspau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f6e4af88-d330-4a75-8435-e502a8c24df7","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-7357-6965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Levring","key":"andersenjesperlevringpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"72c137de-8212-41ed-ac15-9d04635c2559","name":"Andersen, Jesper Levring","orcid":"0000-0001-6963-5053","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-37acd70c-ee1c-4a66-84b0-567b7c17ebaa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Udviklingen i dansk kystfiskeri efter 2016","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-426537","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"A nonvolatile fluorine-18 aldehyde prosthetic group was developed from [18F]SFB, and used for site-specific labeling of active site inhibited factor VII (FVIIai). FVIIai has a high affinity for tissue factor (TF), a transmembrane protein involved in angiogenesis, proliferation, cell migration, and survival of cancer cells. A hydroxylamine N-glycan modified FVIIai (FVIIai-ONH2) was used for oxime coupling with the aldehyde [18F]2 under mild and optimized conditions in an isolated RCY of 4.7 ± 0.9%, and a synthesis time of 267 ± 5 min (from EOB). Retained binding and specificity of the resulting [18F]FVIIai to TF was shown in vitro. TF-expression imaging capability was evaluated by in vivo PET/CT imaging in a pancreatic human xenograft cancer mouse model. The conjugate showed exceptional stability in plasma (>95% at 4 h) and a binding fraction of 90%. In vivo PET/CT imaging showed a mean tumor uptake of 3.8 ± 0.2% ID/g at 4 h post-injection, a comparable uptake in liver and kidneys, and low uptake in normal tissues. In conclusion, FVIIai was labeled with fluorine-18 at the N-glycan chain without affecting TF binding. In vitro specificity and a good in vivo imaging contrast at 4 h postinjection was demonstrated.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Troels E.","Kristensen, Lotte K","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Petersen, Lars C.","Kristensen, Jesper B","Behrens, Carsten","Madsen, Jacob","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444655"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxime coupling of active site inhibited factor seven with a nonvolatile water soluble fluorine 000000000018 labeled aldehyde","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-444655","identifier":[{"id":"85063164524","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30676028","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-55ba58f5-1e06-434c-8be8-b677655f78bd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7B1E4B151CBD5A95F04441874F2FD885"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Troels E.","key":"jeppesentroelsepau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"73a2a7f3-ceeb-4383-a182-9ffc08d45bc4","name":"Jeppesen, Troels E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lotte K.","key":"kristensenlottekpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"cf50f8c1-d3cd-4d46-af75-636ddcf0721f","name":"Kristensen, Lotte K","name_org":"Kristensen, Lotte K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten H","key":"nielsencarstenhaagenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aefb223a-8c5c-41c6-9e69-fade0a04bf90","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","name_org":"Nielsen, Carsten H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars C.","key":"petersenlarscpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Lars C.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper B","key":"kristensenjesperbpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Jesper B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"behrenscarstenpau","last":"Behrens","name":"Behrens, Carsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"madsenjacobpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Jacob","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerandreaspau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30676028"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.bioconjchem.8b00900","issn":["10431802","15204812"],"issn_org":["10431802"],"issue":"3","journal":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","pages":"775-784","status":"p","title":"Bioconjugate Chemistry","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063164524"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-55ba58f5-1e06-434c-8be8-b677655f78bd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Oxime Coupling of Active Site Inhibited Factor Seven with a Nonvolatile, Water-Soluble Fluorine-18 Labeled Aldehyde","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-444655","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Abnormal P-wave morphology (PWM) has been associated with a history of atrial fibrillation (AF) in earlier studies. Although lone AF is believed to have substantial genetic basis, studies on associations between single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNP) linked to lone AF and PWM have not been reported. We aimed to assess whether SNPs previously associated with lone AF (rs2200733, rs13376333, rs3807989, and rs11047543) are also linked to P-wave abnormalities. Methods: Four SNPs were studied in 176 unrelated individuals with early-onset lone AF (age at onset <50 years), median age 38 years (19–63 years), 149 men. Using sinus rhythm ECG, orthogonal PWM was classified as Type 1—positive in leads X and Y and negative in lead Z, Type 2—positive in leads X and Y and biphasic (−/+) in lead Z, Type 3—positive in lead X and biphasic in lead Y (+/−), and the remaining as atypical. Results: Two SNPs were found to be significantly associated with altered P-wave morphology distribution: rs3807989 near the gene CAV1/CAV2 and rs11047543 near the gene SOX5. Both SNPs were associated with a higher risk of non-Type 1 P-wave morphology (rs3807989: OR = 4.8, 95% CI = 2.3–10.2, p < 0.001; rs11047543: OR = 4.7, 95% CI = 1.1–20.5, p = 0.04). No association was observed for rs2200733 and rs13376333. Conclusion: In this study, the two variants rs3807989 and rs11047543, previously associated with PR interval and lone AF, were associated with altered P-wave morphology distribution in patients with early-onset lone AF. These findings suggest that common genetic variants may modify atrial conduction properties.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Seifert, Mariam B.","Olesen, Morten S","Christophersen, Ingrid E.","Nielsen, Jonas B","Carlson, Jonas","Holmqvist, Fredrik","Tveit, Arnljot","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Platonov, Pyotr G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461384"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","SNP"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variants on chromosomes 000000000007p000000000031 and 000000000012p000000000012 are associated with abnormal atrial electrical activation in patients with early onset lone atrial fibrillation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc6931409?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461384","identifier":[{"id":"85066630349","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31152482","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6931409","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-71b293cd-a206-4888-b062-51d4f4337d13"],"keyword":["P-wave morphology","SNP","atrial fibrillation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D54A97D19701FB980EAA2E90A45AD7E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc6931409?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mariam B.","key":"seifertpau","last":"Seifert","name":"Seifert, Mariam B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","name_org":"Olesen, Morten S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingrid E.","key":"christophersenpau","last":"Christophersen","name":"Christophersen, Ingrid E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"64ee18f9-f549-4a20-b501-a5a61c157cb9","name":"Nielsen, Jonas B","name_org":"Nielsen, Jonas B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"carlsonpau","last":"Carlson","name":"Carlson, Jonas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fredrik","key":"holmqvistpau","last":"Holmqvist","name":"Holmqvist, Fredrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arnljot","key":"tveitpau","last":"Tveit","name":"Tveit, Arnljot","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper H.","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","name_org":"Svendsen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pyotr G.","key":"platonovpau","last":"Platonov","name":"Platonov, Pyotr G.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31152482"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/anec.12661","issn":["1082720X","1542474X"],"issn_org":["1542474X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Annals of Noninvasive Electrocardiology","paperid":"e12661","status":"p","title":"Annals of Noninvasive Electrocardiology","title_org":"Annals of Noninvasive Electrocardiology (Online)","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066630349"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-71b293cd-a206-4888-b062-51d4f4337d13"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic variants on chromosomes 7p31 and 12p12 are associated with abnormal atrial electrical activation in patients with early-onset lone atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-461384","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Helmke, Christophe","Fenoglio, Fiorella","Saint-Charles Zetina, Juan Carlos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-517544"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","OECD"],"country":["Mexico"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INAH Queretaro"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the early classic murals of el rosario queretaro mexico description and iconographic analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-517544","ids":["ku-cfb93072-84ba-4e39-8d2e-52d8e8462bba"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-99EEC1C93EBA046761824242015BB807"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"mx","key":"inah queretaro","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"INAH Queretaro","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Fiorella","key":"fenogliopau","last":"Fenoglio","name":"Fenoglio, Fiorella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Juan Carlos","key":"saintcharleszetinapau","last":"Saint-Charles Zetina","name":"Saint-Charles Zetina, Juan Carlos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15312097"],"journal":"Ancient America","pages":"1-75","status":"p","title":"Ancient America","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cfb93072-84ba-4e39-8d2e-52d8e8462bba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Early Classic Murals of El Rosario, Queretaro, Mexico : Description and Iconographic Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-517544","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In adults, oscillatory activity in the sensorimotor cortex is coherent with contralateral muscle activity at beta frequencies (15-35 Hz) during tonic contraction. This functional coupling reflects the involvement of the sensorimotor cortex, the corticospinal pathway, and likely also ascending sensory feedback in the task at hand. However, little is known about the developmental trajectory of task-related corticomuscular connectivity relating to the voluntary control of the ankle muscles. To address this, we recorded electroencephalography (EEG) from the vertex (Cz) and electromyography (EMG) from ankle muscles (proximal and distal anterior tibial, TA; soleus, SOL; gastrocnemius medialis, GM) in 33 participants aged 7-23 yr during tonic dorsi- and plantar flexion requiring precise maintenance of a submaximal torque level. Coherence was calculated for Cz-TA, Cz-SOL, TA-TA, and SOL-GM signal pairs. We found strong, positive associations between age and beta band coherence for Cz-TA, Cz-SOL, and TA-TA, suggesting that oscillatory corticomuscular connectivity is strengthened during childhood development and adolescence. Directionality analysis indicated that the primary interaction underlying this age-related increase was in the descending direction. In addition, performance during dorsi- and plantar flexion tasks was positively associated with age, indicating more precise control of the ankle joint in older participants. Performance was also positively associated with beta band coherence, suggesting that participants with greater coherence also exhibited greater precision. We propose that these results indicate an age-related increase in oscillatory corticospinal input to the ankle muscle motoneuron pools during childhood development and adolescence, with possible implications for maturation of precision force control. Within the theoretical framework of predictive coding, we suggest that our results may reflect an age-related increase in reliance on feedforward control as the developing nervous system becomes better at predicting the sensory consequences of movement. These findings may contribute to the development of novel intervention strategies targeting improved sensorimotor control in children and adolescents with central motor disorders.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","Jensen, Peter","Terkildsen, Cecilie Ulbæk","Jensen, Nicole Jacqueline","Halliday, David M","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Geertsen, Svend Sparre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532119"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of York"],"keyword":["Coherence","Connectivity","Development","EEG","EMG","Faculty of Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Elsass Instituttet, Charlottenlund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the development of functional and directed corticomuscular connectivity during tonic ankle muscle contraction across childhood and adolescence","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248819972/The_development_of_functional_and_directed_corticomuscular_connectivity_during_tonic_ankle_muscle_contraction_across_childhood_and_adolescence_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532119","identifier":[{"id":"85062280774","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30818025","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e837d0e6-ad78-4c15-9307-1633df3d71da"],"keyword":["Coherence","Connectivity","Development","EEG","EMG","Faculty of Science"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A8C93E3BFAD7F37A9E9A2BC784E9871"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248819972/The_development_of_functional_and_directed_corticomuscular_connectivity_during_tonic_ankle_muscle_contraction_across_childhood_and_adolescence_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Elsass Instituttet, Charlottenlund"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Meaghan Elizabeth","key":"speddenmeaghanelizabethpau","last":"Spedden","locid":"e96259a8-d793-4586-903e-cbf824fa8021","name":"Spedden, Meaghan Elizabeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6854-2226","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"jensenpeterpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1b0c1122-5f72-4a02-816f-4709531f8d8e","name":"Jensen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-2597-5408","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie Ulbæk","key":"terkildsencecilieulbækpau","last":"Terkildsen","locid":"67fc2ee4-baea-4d57-af37-3501b6662ec0","name":"Terkildsen, Cecilie Ulbæk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole Jacqueline","key":"jensennicolejacquelinepau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a201203c-15a5-4289-b43a-e7dc1bc34c15","name":"Jensen, Nicole Jacqueline","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"David M","key":"hallidaydavidmpau","last":"Halliday","name":"Halliday, David M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenjesperpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","country":"dk","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenjensbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend Sparre","key":"geertsensvendsparrepau","last":"Geertsen","locid":"9b71cea0-a6d4-47bd-91ca-e969fd3e3af0","name":"Geertsen, Svend Sparre","orcid":"0000-0003-4497-3616","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30818025"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neuroimage.2019.02.054","issn":["10538119","10959572"],"issn_org":["10538119"],"journal":"NeuroImage","pages":"350-360","status":"p","title":"NeuroImage","volume":"191"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062280774"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e837d0e6-ad78-4c15-9307-1633df3d71da"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The development of functional and directed corticomuscular connectivity during tonic ankle muscle contraction across childhood and adolescence","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532119","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVE: Use of statins is considerable among older persons. We investigated factors associated with statin discontinuation in new statin users aged 70 years or older within the first 4 years of use. DESIGN: Register-based descriptive drug utilization study using data from 2008 to 2016. POPULATION/SETTING: All Danish persons, aged 70 years or older, initiating statin treatment. MEASUREMENTS: Rates and predictors of statin discontinuation after 1 year (early), 2 years, and 4 years. Predictors of discontinuation were estimated using logistic regression. RESULTS: We included 83 788 statin initiators. At 1 year, 13% had discontinued their treatment, while another 12% and 13% discontinued after 2 and 4 years, respectively. The overall discontinuation rate over 4 years was 32%. Increasing age was associated with discontinuation at all time points (adjusted odds ratio [OR] = 2.06 [95% confidence interval {CI} = 1.35-3.16] at 1 year, adjusted OR = 3.94 [95% CI, 1.83-8.49] at 4 years, comparing those aged >95 years to those aged 70-74 years). Further, higher comorbidity scores and use of more than 10 medications were modestly associated with discontinuation. Use of statins for secondary prevention was associated with decreased odds of discontinuation compared to primary prevention at 1 year (adjusted OR = 0.74; 95% CI, 0.65-0.83) and at 4 years (adjusted OR = 0.83; 95% CI, 0.72-0.95), along with concomitant use of cardiovascular (CV) therapies. The annual proportion of early discontinuers ranged from 14% to 17% for primary prevention and from 9% to 12% for secondary prevention between 2008 and 2015. DISCUSSION: Statin discontinuation within the first 4 years after initiation appeared to be influenced most strongly by age, and may also be influenced by comorbidity, polypharmacy, use for secondary prevention, and concomitant CV medication use. Future research should clarify reasons for, and discussions about, statin discontinuation and initiation among older persons, to provide additional insight on this topic.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thompson, Wade","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Haastrup, Peter","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598126"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thompson, Wade"],"keyword":["Polypharmacy","Statins","medication discontinuation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statins in older danes factors associated with discontinuation over the first 000000000004 years of use","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535004/Factors_associated_with_discontinuation_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-598126","identifier":[{"id":"85069831457","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31335968","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-56f420b1-2c73-4b9a-bbf7-d091b727553b"],"keyword":["medication discontinuation","polypharmacy","statins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7093CF3C7B58E3814D3B920E6222B677"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535004/Factors_associated_with_discontinuation_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wade","key":"thompsonpau","last":"Thompson","locid":"3d654d06-5597-4de2-9f88-e0913ad14d60","name":"Thompson, Wade","orcid":"0000-0002-8268-4092","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"03dbf65e-75df-4540-b951-0d05e7a60cde","name":"Haastrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7265-743X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31335968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jgs.16073","issn":["00028614","15325415"],"issn_org":["00028614"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of the American Geriatrics Society","pages":"2050-2057","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Geriatrics Society","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069831457"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-56f420b1-2c73-4b9a-bbf7-d091b727553b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Statins in Older Danes : Factors Associated With Discontinuation Over the First 4 Years of Use","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598126","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objectives Characterisation of worker injuries on board merchant ships is modest. Using telemedical service contacts in Denmark, we describe the worker injuries patterns and factors related to injury incidence. Methods The data for this study were based on contacts (n=1401) from ships to Telemedical Assistance Service (TMAS) in Denmark in 2004–2014, which were supplemented with data on the annual estimation of all seafarers from the Danish Maritime Authority (n=73 336). The final data included information on broad age groups, occupation and nationality. The outcomes were injuries from any cause and six broad categories of injuries characterised by anatomic location or type of injury. Results During the observation period of 11 years, there were 1401 contacts to TMAS due to injuries, of which 36% were in upper limb, 18% in lower limb and 13% in the head. Age-adjusted incidence rates for all injuries varied between 13.6 and 26.8 incidences per 1000 person-years in 2004–2014. In most types of injuries, younger and older seafarers had higher risk for injuries than seafarers aged 30–49 years. Depending on the type of injury, non-officers had threefold to fivefold increased odds of injuries compared with officers, the risk being highest for head injuries with an OR of 5.00 (95% CI 3.19 to 7.83). Non-officers from the European Union (EU) had higher risk in most types of injuries than non-officers from outside the EU, whereas the pattern of this risk was inverse among officers. Conclusions These findings suggest that non-officers and European seafarers have an increased risk for several types of injuries on board Danish-flagged merchant ships. Additionally, age affected risk with the younger (<30 years) and older (>50 years) seafarers having increased risk.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Herttua, Kimmo","Gerdøe-Kristensen, Stine","Vork, Jan","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-636784"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"age and nationality in relation to injuries at sea among officers and non officers a study based on contacts from ships to telemedical assistance service in denmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-034502","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-636784","identifier":[{"id":"85076707669","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31843856","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6924698","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-ddfd11a3-e1ac-4d66-a5ab-60a7172e5d59"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46BE769E71522D690E12CAF3DB5C5DDF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-034502","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/159194752/e034502.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Sydvestjysk Sygehus Esbjerg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kimmo","key":"herttuapau","last":"Herttua","name":"Herttua, Kimmo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"gerdøekristensenpau","last":"Gerdøe-Kristensen","name":"Gerdøe-Kristensen, Stine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"vorkpau","last":"Vork","name":"Vork, Jan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31843856"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2019-034502","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"12","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e034502","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076707669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ddfd11a3-e1ac-4d66-a5ab-60a7172e5d59"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Age and nationality in relation to injuries at sea among officers and non-officers : a study based on contacts from ships to Telemedical Assistance Service in Denmark.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-636784","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Microbial biofilms are the cause of persistent infections associated with various medical implants and distinct body sites such as the urinary tract, lungs, and wounds. Compared with their free living counterparts, bacteria in biofilms display a highly increased resistance to immune system activities and antibiotic treatment. Therefore, biofilm infections are difficult or impossible to treat with our current armory of antibiotics. The challenges associated with biofilm infections have urged researchers to pursue a better understanding of the molecular mechanisms that are involved in the formation and dispersal of biofilms, and this has led to the identification of several steps that could be targeted in order to eradicate these challenging infections. Here we describe mechanisms that are involved in the regulation of biofilm development in Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Escherichia coli, and Acinetobacter baumannii, and provide examples of chemical compounds that have been developed to specifically inhibit these processes. These compounds include (i) pilicides and curlicides which inhibit the initial steps of biofilm formation by E. coli; (ii) compounds that interfere with c-di-GMP signaling in P. aeruginosa and E. coli; and (iii) compounds that inhibit quorum-sensing in P. aeruginosa and A. baumannii. In cases where compound series have a defined molecular target, we focus on elucidating structure activity relationship (SAR) trends within the particular compound series.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Qvortrup, Katrine","Hultqvist, Louise Dahl","Nilsson, Martin","Jakobsen, Tim Holm","Jansen, Charlotte Uldahl","Uhd, Jesper","Andersen, Jens Bo","Nielsen, Thomas E.","Givskov, Michael","Tolker-Nielsen, Tim"],"cuid":["S02-087.01-036019"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Tolker-Nielsen, Tim"],"keyword":["Acinetobacter baumannii","Escherichia coli","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Quorum sensing","c di GMP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"small molecule anti biofilm agents developed on the basis of mechanistic understanding of biofilm formation","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fchem.2019.00742","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.01-036019","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6838868","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31737611","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075368407","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-95ef423f-c9b6-4bc2-9c5b-d2ad460f27ee","ku-8ee83b8b-5f34-472a-8a21-cde3461c0c13"],"keyword":["Acinetobacter baumannii","Anti-biofilm compounds","Escherichia coli","Pilicides and curlicides","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Quorum sensing","c-di-GMP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2C17A043AA6EABE59F79FDBDD017113A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196884930/fchem_07_00742_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/235587171/fchem_07_00742.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fchem.2019.00742","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Bacteriology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrine","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","locid":"cfc8ffa0-b091-4a00-8ec1-c8c43f47ea33","name":"Qvortrup, Katrine","orcid":"0000-0003-3828-2069","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise Dahl","key":"hultqvistpau","last":"Hultqvist","locid":"182681ee-548d-4d87-960d-8ce5e88b18e9","name":"Hultqvist, Louise Dahl","orcid":"0000-0003-0256-892X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"42451f7e-e9b1-49b8-ad46-3c450430a8d2","name":"Nilsson, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-6251-9842","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tim Holm","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"c4df6233-6aa5-4ff3-b95f-68f445643741","name":"Jakobsen, Tim Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-1671-2155","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Uldahl","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","locid":"09b0fd2f-9342-4f39-9e0d-338f8d2e922f","name":"Jansen, Charlotte Uldahl","orcid":"0000-0002-1168-8002","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"uhdpau","last":"Uhd","locid":"e3695412-4774-4773-9557-9d862f3ce3db","name":"Uhd, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Bo","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"20a1fab5-e1e8-44fc-9d8b-45f10aa89e29","name":"Andersen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-1720-1581","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas E","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"809d5f89-6d6a-42b5-b775-a7ea25ab9e4e","name":"Nielsen, Thomas E.","name_org":"Nielsen, Thomas E","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"givskovpau","last":"Givskov","locid":"9d3d31be-5f63-4257-a014-c86cc3100276","name":"Givskov, Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-5004-8609","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tim","key":"tolkernielsenpau","last":"Tolker-Nielsen","locid":"3cdd7c13-7576-4d34-8c3c-6b1bae91acc0","name":"Tolker-Nielsen, Tim","orcid":"0000-0002-9751-474X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31737611"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fchem.2019.00742","issn":["22962646"],"journal":"Frontiers in Chemistry","paperid":"742","publisher":"Frontiers Media","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Chemistry","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075368407"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-95ef423f-c9b6-4bc2-9c5b-d2ad460f27ee","ku-8ee83b8b-5f34-472a-8a21-cde3461c0c13"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Small Molecule Anti-biofilm Agents Developed on the Basis of Mechanistic Understanding of Biofilm Formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.01-036019","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Blood-based, cancer-associated biomarkers may detect subjects at risk of having neoplastic diseases. The aim of the present study was to evaluate whether elevated serological protein biomarker levels may identify adenoma patients, who are at increased risk of being diagnosed with subsequent primary malignancy. Methods: Levels of CEA, CA19-9, TIMP-1 and YKL-40 were determined in blood samples collected prior to diagnostic bowel endoscopy due to symptoms of colorectal neoplasia. Follow-up time was ten years, and identified adenoma patients, who were diagnosed with subsequent primary intra- or extra-colonic malignant diseases. The biomarker levels were also determined in 400 subjects, who underwent diagnostic colonoscopy, had clean colorectum and were without apparent co-morbidity; these levels were used as reference levels. In the present study, biomarkers were interpreted as elevated when levels were above the reference intervals adjusting for age and gender. The 1-year and 5-years cumulative incidences were calculated. Results: Primary malignancies were identified in 175 (19%) of the 923 subjects diagnosed with adenomas at the primary bowel endoscopy. In detail, 20 of the 175 subjects were diagnosed with colorectal cancer (CRC) and 155 subjects with extra-colonic cancers. Thirty patients were diagnosed with malignancy within the first year. Three groups were established: 0: no elevated biomarkers; 1: 1 of the 4 biomarkers elevated; and 2: ≥2 biomarkers elevated. The cumulative 5-years incidence of malignancy was: 0: 6.9%; 1: 11.8%; and 2: 17.5% (p =.0009). Conclusion: Elevated blood-based, cancer-associated protein biomarker levels in subjects diagnosed with adenomas at large bowel endoscopy identifies subjects at increased risk of being diagnosed with subsequent primary malignancy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Piper, Thomas B.","Jørgensen, Lars N.","Olsen, Jesper","Nielsen, Knud T.","Davis, Gerard","Johansen, Julia S.","Jarle Christensen, Ib","Nielsen, Hans J."],"cuid":["S02-088.62-017112"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Piper, Thomas B."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Diagnostics","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased serological cancer associated protein biomarker levels at diagnosis of large bowel adenoma risk of subsequent primary malignancy","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/0284186X.2018.1540885","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.62-017112","identifier":[{"id":"85058173690","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30523734","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3cc153a7-b258-4b01-a13e-58c4774c18ea","ku-acf8d3cb-6370-4190-8c8b-1a76e1371b92"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FA26C44E2EC737C3301940D1638506B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/0284186X.2018.1540885","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Surgical Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"abbott diagnostics","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Abbott Diagnostics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Thomas B","key":"piperthomasbpau","last":"Piper","name":"Piper, Thomas B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars N","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","name_org":"Jørgensen, Lars N","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenjesperpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud T.","key":"nielsenknudtpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"73d72739-ec40-49c4-8ad3-934fe96c994d","name":"Nielsen, Knud T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"davisgerardpau","last":"Davis","name":"Davis, Gerard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julia S","key":"johansenjuliaspau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","name_org":"Johansen, Julia S","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ib","key":"jarlechristensenibpau","last":"Jarle Christensen","name":"Jarle Christensen, Ib","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans J","key":"nielsenhansjørgenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"87f9baf4-e29c-4104-be23-daf6d94d7124","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","name_org":"Nielsen, Hans J","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30523734"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2018.1540885","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"sup1","journal":"Acta Oncologica","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058173690"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3cc153a7-b258-4b01-a13e-58c4774c18ea","ku-acf8d3cb-6370-4190-8c8b-1a76e1371b92"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increased serological, cancer-associated protein biomarker levels at diagnosis of large bowel adenoma : Risk of subsequent primary malignancy?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.62-017112","year":"2019","yearsub":2020}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To summarize available tools that can assist clinicians in identifying and reducing or stopping (deprescribing) potentially inappropriate medications and that specifically consider frailty or limited life expectancy. DESIGN: Systematic review and narrative synthesis. SETTING: We searched MEDLINE (via Ovid SP), EMBASE (via Ovid SP), and CINAHL from inception to December 2017, along with grey literature. We included articles that described a tool to guide deprescribing of medications. PARTICIPANTS: Frail older persons and older persons with limited life expectancy. MEASUREMENTS: Narrative description of tools. RESULTS: We identified 15 tools and organized them into three main categories: tools (n = 2) that described a model or framework for approaching deprescribing, tools (n = 9) that outlined a deprescribing approach for the entire medication list, and tools (n = 4) that provided medication-specific advice. The complexity of the tools ranged from simple lists to detailed, step-wise protocols. The development methodology varied widely, and the methods used to synthesize the tools were generally not well described. Most tools were based on expert opinion. Only four of the 15 tools have been tested in clinical practice (in very low-quality studies). CONCLUSION: Tools exist to help clinicians deprescribe in frail older persons and those with limited life expectancy. These tools may assist clinicians at various stages in the deprescribing process. However, it remains to be investigated whether use of such tools in practice is likely to improve clinical outcomes or reduce inappropriate medication use. J Am Geriatr Soc 67:172–180, 2019.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thompson, Wade","Lundby, Carina","Graabæk, Trine","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","Ryg, Jesper","Søndergaard, Jens","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S02-089.72-049625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Decision Support Techniques","Deprescribing","Deprescriptions","End of life","Female","Frail","Frail Elderly","Geriatric Assessment","Humans","Life Expectancy","Male","Potentially Inappropriate Medication List","Practice Patterns Physicians statistics numerical data"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tools for deprescribing in frail older persons and those with limited life expectancy a systematic review","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jgs.15616","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.72-049625","identifier":[{"id":"85054804345","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30315745","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e638a1af-8523-4ecc-b8e2-e579444fd9ad","ucl-606986d4-230d-400a-a751-a2bfee5d464f"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Decision Support Techniques","Deprescriptions","Female","Frail Elderly","Geriatric Assessment","Humans","Life Expectancy","Male","Potentially Inappropriate Medication List","Practice Patterns, Physicians'/statistics & numerical data","deprescribing","end of life","frail"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C9176E45278DD5BCF1E7DCA399DE0545"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535061/Review_of_deprescribing_tools_manuscript_June_7.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jgs.15616","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1"