,"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"21","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"2025-2027","paperid":"V08180570","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"181"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b3798463-8cf7-40f5-85a0-0c82d87af2a8","au-fcf5fbd9-5b64-43ae-900f-c2ab048af36a","sdu-ec29b134-b51c-483c-9a64-0495b52fac7e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Myalgisk encefalomyelitis eller kronisk træthedssyndrom","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.25-008647","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) is often the first manifestation of unrecognised cardiac disease. ECG abnormalities encountered in primary care settings may be warning signs of OHCA. Objective: We examined the association between common ECG abnormalities and OHCA in a primary care setting. Methods: We cross-linked individuals who had an ECG recording between 2001 and 2011 in a primary care setting with the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry and identified OHCAs of presumed cardiac cause. Results: A total of 326 227 individuals were included and 2667 (0,8%) suffered an OHCA. In Cox regression analyses, adjusted for age and sex, the following ECG findings were strongly associated with OHCA: ST-depression without concomitant atrial fibrillation (HR 2.79; 95% CI 2.45 to 3.18), left bundle branch block (LBBB; HR 3.44; 95% CI 2.85 to 4.14) and non-specific intraventricular block (NSIB; HR 3.15; 95% CI 2.58 to 3.83). Also associated with OHCA were atrial fibrillation (HR 1.89; 95% CI 1.63 to 2.18), Q-wave (HR 1.75; 95% CI 1.57 to 1.95), Cornell and Sokolow-Lyon criteria for left ventricular hypertrophy (HR 1.56; 95% CI 1.33 to 1.82 and HR 1.27; 95% CI 1.12 to 1.45, respectively), ST-elevation (HR 1.40; 95% CI 1.09 to 1.54) and right bundle branch block (HR 1.29; 95% CI 1.09 to 1.54). The association between ST-depression and OHCA diminished with concomitant atrial fibrillation (HR 1.79; 95% CI 1.42 to 2.24, p < 0.01 for interaction). Among patients suffering from OHCA, without a known cardiac disease at the time of the cardiac arrest, 14.2 % had LBBB, NSIB or ST-depression. Conclusions: Several common ECG findings obtained from a primary care setting are associated with OHCA.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Søndergaard, Marc Meller","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Mortensen, Rikke Nørmark","Gislason, Gunnar","Køber, Lars","Lippert, Freddy","Graff, Claus","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Kragholm, Kristian","Pietersen, Adrian Holger","Lind, Bent Struer","Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","Struijk, Johannes","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Hansen, Steen Møller"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-000490"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Søndergaard, Marc Meller"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Michigan"],"keyword":["Cardiac disease","ECG","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between common ecg abnormalities and out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2018-000905","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-000490","identifier":[{"id":"85066016299","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31217990","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6546195","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-09572ca5-8cc3-4dbd-ad6e-3cd5627dacff","ku-75402d0d-bb21-483e-8448-c83c82dc7fa8","sdu-18ca0f4f-cc79-41f3-873b-2c50fca49cd7"],"keyword":["ECG","cardiac disease","out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-59B82937B9A14CC47168CBBCD093D49D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"http://openheart.bmj.com/content/6/1/e000905.abstract","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/152599861/Associations_between_common_ECG_abnormalities_and_out_of_ho