igurable Manufacturing Systems for Mass Customized Products : an Industrial Survey","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-051445","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Artiklen analyserer, hvorvidt EU-Domstolen med dommene i Mangold, C-144/04, Ole Andersen, C-499/08 og/eller Ajos, C-414/14, har overskredet sin kompetence ved at fastslå en grundlæggende rettighed på EU-traktatniveau i form af et forbud mod aldersdiskriminering. Forfatteren besvarer spørgsmålet benægtende. En sådan udvikling af grundlæggende rettigheder kan rummes inden for rammerne af Domstolens retsskabende virksomhed, som er bredt accepteret, også af Danmark. Det er derfor forfatterens opfattelse, at det i Ajos også af danske domstole kunne være lagt til grund, at der består et sådant princip. Ved pådømmelsen af Ajos kunne der have været søgt inspiration i de synspunkter og observationer, som den tyske forfatningsdomstol fremførte i sin dom af 6. juli 2010 (2661/06). Der kan med rette rejses kritik af Mangold, men både dommens synspunkter om indirekte virkning via EU-konform (direktivkonform) fortolkning og ligeledes dens synspunkter om udvikling af almindelige EU-retlige grundsætninger, har ikke en sådan karakter, at der er flyttet kompetencer til EU på medlemsstaternes bekostning, og dette bør til syvende og sidst være det afgørende kriterium her. Der er næppe grundlag for at antage, at bestemthedskravet i relation til overladelse af beføjelser i medfør af Grundlovens § 20 skulle føre til, at marginen for EU-Domstolen set fra en dansk synsvinkel skulle være snævrere, end den er det fra en tysk synsvinkel, således som sidstnævnte er kommet til udtryk i forfatningsdomstolens dom af 6. juli 2016 på grundlag af det tyske bestemthedskrav (’das Prinzip der begrenzten Einzelermächtigung’). Danmark har konsekvent accepteret EU-Domstolens retsskabende virksomhed, og herunder også de grundlæggende rettigheder, der er udviklet gennem Domstolens praksis. Overfører man den margin, som den tyske forfatningsdomstol i relation til Mangold indrømmer EU-Domstolen inden for rammerne af det tyske bestemthedskrav, må det antages, at en tilsvarende margin kunne være indrømmet inden for det danske bestemthedskrav, uden at man herved kom i konflikt med Højesterets udsagn i UfR 2013.1451 H, hvorefter proceduren i Grundlovens § 20 skal iagttages, hvis der overlades ”yderligere beføjelser til at udøve lovgivende, administrativ eller dømmende myndighed med direkte virkning i Danmark, hvad enten udvidelsen angår sagsområderne eller karakteren af de overladte beføjelser”. Et forventnings- eller tillidsprincip til skrevne nationale regler har altid måttet underlægges den væsentlige modifikation, at en præjudiciel afgørelse fra EU-Domstolen kan fortolke EU-retten på en måde, som der ikke i tilstrækkelig grad er taget højde for i national ret. En sådan præjudiciel afgørelse har som udgangspunkt virkning ex tunc, og det er kun EU-Domstolen, ikke nationale domstole, der har kompetencen til at begrænse en præjudiciel afgørelses tidsmæssige virkninger.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Werlauff, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058399"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ajos","Grundlæggende rettigheder"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"national rets modtagelse af problematiske nyskabelser fra eu domstolen ajos problematikken anskuet ud fra en tysk forfatningsretlig synsvinkel","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.djoef-forlag.dk/book-info/festskrift-til-mads-bryde-andersen","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-058399","ids":["aau-1c96fec2-4e34-4f78-8094-d8dc5f1134b7"],"keyword":["Ajos","Mangol","grundlæggende rettigheder","lovfortolkning contra legem","præjudiciel doms virkning ex tunc"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BAF9FEDF096A39EB663A7889D2DD8A80"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management, Auditing, Accounting, Advice Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"werlauffpau","last":"Werlauff","locid":"51ebbc6b-e33c-4dbc-8d38-9d50edfbd27e","name":"Werlauff, Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"udsenpedh","last":"Udsen","name":"Udsen, Henrik","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Schans","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jan Schans","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Lau","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper Lau","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Torsten","key":"iversenpedh","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Torsten","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Linda","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","isbn":["9788757441130"],"pages":"313-332","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","publisher_org":"DJØF Forlag","status":"p","title":"Festskrift til Mads Bryde Andersen","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1c96fec2-4e34-4f78-8094-d8dc5f1134b7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"National rets modtagelse af problematiske nyskabelser fra EU-Domstolen : ’AJOS-problematikken’ anskuet ud fra en tysk forfatningsretlig synsvinkel","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058399","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Optimal linear filtering has been used extensively for speech enhancement. In this paper, we take a first step in trying to apply linear filtering to the decomposition of a noisy speech signal into its components. The problem of decomposing speech into its voiced and unvoiced components is considered as an estimation problem. Assuming a harmonic model for the voiced speech, we propose a Wiener filtering scheme which estimates both components separately in the presence of noise. It is shown under which conditions this optimal filtering formulation outperforms two state-of-the-art speech decomposition methods, which is also revealed by objective measures, spectrograms and informal listening tests.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Esquivel Jaramillo, Alfredo","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059442"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-07","place":"Rome, it","start":"2018-09-03","title":"26th European Signal Processing Conference","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["speech decomposition","time domain filtering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on optimal filtering for speech decomposition","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321286091/Eusipco2018RomeDecompositionAccepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059442","identifier":[{"id":"85059813729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-20289dfb-3b13-4bd0-837b-520ad6003366"],"keyword":["Wiener filter","speech decomposition","time-domain filtering","unvoiced speech","voiced speech"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5B744C56EED97DE3FC405DB5077DC79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321286091/Eusipco2018RomeDecompositionAccepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"esquiveljaramillopau","last":"Esquivel Jaramillo","locid":"a9286a43-363b-461d-adcf-9cd2b30e97ea","name":"Esquivel Jaramillo, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-8994-9479","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eusipco.2018.8553512","eisbn":["9789082797015"],"isbn":["9789082797008","9781538637364"],"issn":["20761465"],"pages":"2325-2329","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Proc. European Signal Processing Conference","status":"p","title":"2018 26th European Signal Processing Conference (EUSIPCO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059813729"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-20289dfb-3b13-4bd0-837b-520ad6003366"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"On Optimal Filtering for Speech Decomposition","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059442","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents continuous wave power measurements conducted in forest terrain with a focus on path-loss in a Device-to-Device (D2D) communication scenario. The measurements have been conducted at 917.5 MHz with measurement ranges extending to more than 2.5 kilometers using a purpose developed measurement system with a dynamic range of 180 dB. The impact of different antenna heights has been investigated by placing antennas at 1.5, 2.5 and 3.5 meters elevation over the terrain. The measurements showed that the antenna elevation in the given scenario did not have a significant impact on the received power. The measurements also showed that the dominant path of propagation is through the foliage for the first approximately 1000 meters where foliage excess loss is dominant in this region. After approximately 1000 meters the measured received power tend to follow the fourth-power law indicating that the excess loss due to foliage has to be limited. The measurement results have been compared to models proposed in the literature based on empirical data, as well as models proposed by ITU and COST. The comparison showed that only two models predicted the limit in foliage excess loss in the measurement data observed. By applying these excess loss models in combination with path-loss models it was possible to model the measured total path-loss with an RMS error of less than 10 dB. This was achieved by either applying a model proposed by Tewari or a combination between the two-ray path-loss model and the ITU-R P.2108 clutter loss model.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hejselbæk, Johannes","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Fan, Wei","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-079818"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Foliage","Forest","Internet of Things IoT","Path loss","Radio Propagation","Vegetation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"empirical study of near ground propagation in forest terrain for internet of things type device to device communication","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2871368","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-079818","identifier":[{"id":"85053634385","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000448011800001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-668a1311-b14a-4ec4-8cde-2e5a79eab29c"],"keyword":["Internet-of-Things (IoT)","Radio propagation","clutter loss","deviceto-device (D2D)","excess loss","foliage","forest","narrow band IoT (NB-IoT)","near ground propagation","path-loss","vegetation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-878565A884F50A314A3190EB478E5F02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/293132166/08468151.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2871368","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"hejselbækpau","last":"Hejselbæk","locid":"9163c39e-9747-4c12-bcb7-861a91af7c57","name":"Hejselbæk, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-3053-5474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2018.2871368","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"54052-54063","paperid":"8468151","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053634385"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-668a1311-b14a-4ec4-8cde-2e5a79eab29c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Empirical Study of Near Ground Propagation in Forest Terrain for Internet-of-Things type Device-to-Device Communication","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-079818","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Ray tracing (RT)-assisted beamforming, where beams are directly steered to dominant paths tracked by ray tracing simulations, is a promising beamforming strategy, since it avoids the time-consuming exhaustive beam searching adopted in conventional beam steering strategies. The performance of RT-assisted beamforming depends directly on how accurate the spatial profiles of the radio environment can be predicted by the RT simulation. In this paper, we investigate how ray tracingassisted beamforming performs in both poorly furnished and richly furnished indoor environments. Single user beamforming performance was investigated using both single beam and multiple beams, with two different power allocation schemes applied to multi-beamforming. Channel measurements were performed at 28-30 GHz using a vector network analyzer equipped with a Biconical antenna as the transmit antenna and a rotated horn antenna as the receive antenna. 3D ray tracing simulations were carried out in the same replicated propagation environments. Based on measurement and ray tracing simulation data, it is shown that RT-assisted beamforming performs well both for single and multi-beamforming in these two representative indoor propagation environments.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Karstensen, Anders","Fan, Wei","Zhang, Fengchun","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081665"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of simulated and measured indoor channels for mm wave beamforming applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/2642904","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081665","identifier":[{"id":"85042127930","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6cb556aa-94d9-4081-a647-67349b619ce5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E68E65D7B8A96A6314BB953BD8DAE0B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.hindawi.com/journals/ijap/aip/2642904/","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/272761200/Analysis_of_Simulated_and_Measured_Indoor_Channels_for_mmWave_Beamforming_Applications.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/2642904","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"karstensenpau","last":"Karstensen","locid":"0d1d4896-50a7-4849-acdb-10dc2e0b27f5","name":"Karstensen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fengchun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"4badb5be-83e0-446f-acc3-0744c6443cd6","name":"Zhang, Fengchun","orcid":"0000-0003-0957-1232","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2018/2642904","issn":["16875869","16875877"],"issn_org":["16875869"],"journal":"International Journal of Antennas and Propagation","pages":"2-19","paperid":"2642904","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Antennas and Propagation","volume":"2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042127930"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6cb556aa-94d9-4081-a647-67349b619ce5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analysis of Simulated and Measured Indoor Channels for mm-Wave Beamforming Applications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081665","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Managing and capitalizing on product variety, customization, personalization, decreasing batch sizes, as well as rapid new product introductions are prevailing challenges facing today’s manufacturing companies. Changeable and reconfigurable manufacturing systems have been widely accepted as means to respond to these challenges, due to their ability to accommodate continuous and cost-efficient change in functionality and capacity. However, enablers of reconfigurability that should be selected during manufacturing system design are in current research rarely regarded in terms of their inherent relations and impact on manufacturing performance. Therefore, the aim of this paper is to explore implementation relations between physical enablers of reconfigurability on system and equipment level and their effect on manufacturing performance. For this purpose, a quantitative questionnaire-based survey has been conducted in various Danish manufacturing companies. The findings suggest that most reconfigurability enablers correlate strongly in their implementation and their extent of implementation generally correlates with critical performance aspects such as profitability, ramp-up time, and life-time of production systems.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen, Ann-Louise","Nielsen, Kjeld","Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Larsen, Jesper Kranker","Ketelsen, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089388"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-30","place":"Seoul, kr","start":"2018-08-26","title":"IFIP International Conference on Advances in Production Management Systems","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Changeability","Changeable manufacturing","Reconfigurability","Reconfigurable manufacturing","Survey research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding changeability enablers and their impact on performance in manufacturing companies","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85053231387&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-089388","identifier":[{"id":"85053231387","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8710f2dd-23f2-4ea0-b50c-ba902134ff15"],"keyword":["Changeability","Changeable manufacturing","Reconfigurability","Reconfigurable manufacturing","Survey research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9287B0157960422542EEF4D56B799355"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Manufacturing Systems research group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann-Louise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"73d5c9b6-ff83-41c1-b16e-43f380f384d9","name":"Andersen, Ann-Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7923-6301","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ffae8343-8516-499e-89a3-2f0d6179a5fc","name":"Nielsen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3720-167X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas D.","key":"brunoepau","last":"Brunoe","locid":"b75a6b6d-0181-4141-b951-6f7f70bae83f","name":"Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","name_org":"Brunoe, Thomas D.","orcid":"0000-0002-9847-6562","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cfa28d79-69f2-47dc-b958-6017a1128eee","name":"Larsen, Jesper Kranker","name_org":"Larsen, Jesper K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"ketelsenpau","last":"Ketelsen","locid":"89a93b01-3bc6-4955-94c8-57e364f316fc","name":"Ketelsen, Christopher","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ilkyeong","key":"moonpedh","last":"Moon","name":"Moon, Ilkyeong","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jinwoo","key":"parkpedh","last":"Park","name":"Park, Jinwoo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gyu M.","key":"leepedh","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Gyu M.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dimitris","key":"kiritsispedh","last":"Kiritsis","name":"Kiritsis, Dimitris","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gregor","key":"voncieminskipedh","last":"von Cieminski","name":"von Cieminski, Gregor","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-99704-9_36","eisbn":["9783319997070"],"isbn":["9783319997032"],"issn":["18684238"],"pages":"297-304","publisher":"Springer","series":"IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology","status":"p","subtitle":"IFIP WG 5.7 International Conference, APMS 2018, Seoul, Korea, August 26-30, 2018, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Advances in Production Management Systems. Production Management for Data-Driven, Intelligent, Collaborative, and Sustainable Manufacturing - IFIP WG 5.7 International Conference, APMS 2018, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053231387"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8710f2dd-23f2-4ea0-b50c-ba902134ff15"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Understanding Changeability Enablers and Their Impact on Performance in Manufacturing Companies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089388","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Changeability and reconfigurability can be considered decisive factors of competitiveness in high-wage countries with pressure for cost reduction, extensive relocation of manufacturing, and growing need for product variety and customization. Despite these promising potentials, their current state in industry remains rather unexplored. Therefore, the aim of this paper is to explore requirements and implementation of changeability and reconfigurability in Danish manufacturing through an exploratory descriptive survey. The findings indicate that changeability is both relevant and important in Danish manufacturing. However, the findings also indicate a mismatch between requirements and implementation of changeability, as enablers of reconfigurability are only rudimentarily existing.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Ann-Louise","Larsen, Jesper Kranker","Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Nielsen, Kjeld","Ketelsen, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091428"],"event":{"end":"2018-05-18","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2018-05-16","title":"51st CIRP Conference on Manufacturing Systems, CIRP CMS 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Changeability","Changeable manufacturing","Reconfigurability","Survey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring requirements and implementation of changeability and reconfigurability in danish manufacturing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.078","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091428","identifier":[{"id":"85049585125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8e5d6481-a69f-45ee-94d0-714aab0421fa"],"keyword":["Changeability","Changeable manufacturing","Danish manufacturing","Reconfigurability","Survey"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7456C028B75378CD1554F391790DC5A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.078","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/284777060/1_s2.0_S2212827118301823_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Manufacturing Systems research group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann-Louise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"73d5c9b6-ff83-41c1-b16e-43f380f384d9","name":"Andersen, Ann-Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7923-6301","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kranker","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cfa28d79-69f2-47dc-b958-6017a1128eee","name":"Larsen, Jesper Kranker","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ditlev","key":"brunøpau","last":"Brunø","locid":"b75a6b6d-0181-4141-b951-6f7f70bae83f","name":"Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","orcid":"0000-0002-9847-6562","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ffae8343-8516-499e-89a3-2f0d6179a5fc","name":"Nielsen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3720-167X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"ketelsenpau","last":"Ketelsen","locid":"89a93b01-3bc6-4955-94c8-57e364f316fc","name":"Ketelsen, Christopher","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.078","issn":["22128271"],"issue":"2018","journal":"Procedia CIRP","pages":"665-670","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Procedia CIRP","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049585125"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8e5d6481-a69f-45ee-94d0-714aab0421fa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring Requirements and Implementation of Changeability and Reconfigurability in Danish Manufacturing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091428","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: During design of reconfigurable manufacturing systems, manufacturing companies need to select and implement the right enablers of reconfigurability in accordance with the specific requirements being present in the manufacturing setting. Therefore, the purpose of this paper is to investigate enablers of reconfigurability in terms of their importance in industry, current level of implementation in industry, and significant differences in their implementation and criticality across different manufacturing settings. Design/methodology/approach: A questionnaire survey is conducted, in order to provide generalizable empirical evidence across various industries and manufacturing types. Findings: The findings indicate that the level of implementation of the reconfigurability enablers is rudimentary, while their criticality is perceived higher than the current level of implementation. Moreover, significant differences regarding implementation and criticality of mobility, scalability, and convertibility were found for companies with varying degrees of manual work, make-to-stock production, and varying production volume, industry type and organization size. Research limitations/implications: Main limitations of the research cover the relatively small sample size and non-random sampling method applied, primarily limited to one country, which could be increased to further extent the findings reported in this paper. Practical implications: The findings indicate that the importance and implementation of reconfigurability enablers is contingent on the manufacturing setting. Thus, the research presented in this paper provides valuable knowledge in regard to aiding a paradigm shift in industry and help companies design manufacturing systems with the right reconfigurability enablers. Originality/value: This paper expands research on manufacturing system design for changeability and reconfigurability, by explicitly considering these as capabilities that can be enabled in various ways for various purposes in different manufacturing contexts.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Ann-Louise","Larsen, Jesper Kranker","Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Nielsen, Kjeld","Ketelsen, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091725"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Flexible manufacturing systems","Manufacturing flexibility","Modular production","Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"critical enablers of changeable and reconfigurable manufacturing and their industrial implementation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85045186839&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091725","identifier":[{"id":"85045186839","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8f6a91d6-1875-4ae7-826b-775477613fcf"],"keyword":["Flexible manufacturing systems","Manufacturing flexibility","Manufacturing management","Modular production","Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B1C12FE8B07D97FE56CF9D689B9468E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Manufacturing Systems research group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann-Louise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"73d5c9b6-ff83-41c1-b16e-43f380f384d9","name":"Andersen, Ann-Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7923-6301","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kranker","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cfa28d79-69f2-47dc-b958-6017a1128eee","name":"Larsen, Jesper Kranker","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ditlev","key":"brunøpau","last":"Brunø","locid":"b75a6b6d-0181-4141-b951-6f7f70bae83f","name":"Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","orcid":"0000-0002-9847-6562","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ffae8343-8516-499e-89a3-2f0d6179a5fc","name":"Nielsen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3720-167X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"ketelsenpau","last":"Ketelsen","locid":"89a93b01-3bc6-4955-94c8-57e364f316fc","name":"Ketelsen, Christopher","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/jmtm-04-2017-0073","issn":["1741038X","17587786"],"issn_org":["1741038X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Manufacturing Technology Management","pages":"983-1002","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing Limited","status":"p","title":"Journal of Manufacturing Technology Management","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045186839"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8f6a91d6-1875-4ae7-826b-775477613fcf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Critical enablers of changeable and reconfigurable manufacturing and their industrial implementation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091725","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This working paper analyses results from field work conducted in three case areas in the Central Region Denmark: the rural Lemvig, the suburban Horsens and the urban Aarhus. All three areas are independent municipalities within the same region. The analysis is preceded by an introduction presenting the objectives of the report and the contextual conditions that characterize the Danish case, as well as the methodological considerations. The analysis is structured along the themes of territorial capital, collective efficacy and life chances and territorial governance. In the concluding section we draw out similarities and differences between the three case areas as well as preliminary conclusions based on the qualitative data presented in this working paper.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fallov, Mia Arp","Jørgensen, Anja","Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","Hansen, Jesper Rohr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collective efficacy","Territorial capital","Territorial cohesion","Territorial governance"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"working paper on interviews denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/documents/downloadPublic?documentIds=080166e5e1f74619&appId=PPGMS","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093545","ids":["aau-95f73f6c-48d0-46ac-9dc8-6e017f132dcc"],"keyword":["Collective efficacy","Life chances","Territorial capital","Territorial cohesion","Territorial governance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1321B13620989FF155DF796E856E011B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/documents/downloadPublic?documentIds=080166e5e1f74619&appId=PPGMS","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work, SOSA - Social Work in the field of psychiatry and disability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mia","key":"arpfallovpau","last":"Arp Fallov","locid":"52c23fcf-7641-4f31-9d82-d70de307cf99","name":"Fallov, Mia Arp","name_org":"Arp Fallov, Mia","orcid":"0000-0002-2630-1982","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1075f62b-258c-43d9-90c0-5c57bdd67f42","name":"Jørgensen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0003-3864-2458","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Skovgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"125da2cb-a5a5-47e8-84ab-be518f10a19f","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0308-1275","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Rohr","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2e1430aa-5cad-4c23-9556-9575252cc7b7","name":"Hansen, Jesper Rohr","orcid":"0000-0001-9403-9296","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"50","publisher":"European Commission","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-95f73f6c-48d0-46ac-9dc8-6e017f132dcc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Working paper on interviews: DENMARK","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093545","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a Massive-MIMO measurement campaign with bi-directional angular discrimination. Aspects like non-stationarity, spatial consistency and spherical wavefronts become important for proper modeling of such channels. This campaign is designed to measure and investigate these aspects of the channel. The paper includes analyses of the angular statistics and the dual directional power angular spectrum for a few locations. Next, the paths/clusters are mapped to a 2D map for visualisation of clusters. finally, non-stationarity across the large array aperture is investigated in terms of angular statistics and power.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Karstensen, Anders","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","De Carvalho, Elisabeth","Alm, Martin","Steinbock, Gerhard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-109131"],"event":{"acronym":"EuCAP","end":"2018-04-13","place":"London, gb","start":"2018-04-09","title":"12th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dual user massive mimo measurements at 000000000003 000000000005ghz with bi directional angular discrimination","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/286339376/EuCAP2018_ak_sub.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-109131","identifier":[{"id":"85057329153","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-cba3fd48-f098-4272-9841-c32cf975342f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2