{"abstract":"Glaciers create some of Earth's steepest topography; yet, many areas that were repeatedly overridden by ice sheets in the last few million years include extensive plateaus. The distinct geomorphic contrast between plateaus and the glacial troughs that dissect them has sustained two long-held hypotheses: first, that ice sheets perform insignificant erosion beyond glacial troughs, and, second, that the plateaus represent ancient pre-glacial landforms bearing information of tectonic and geomorphic history prior to Pliocene-Pleistocene global cooling (~3.5 Myr ago). Here we show that the Fennoscandian ice sheets drove widespread erosion across plateaus far beyond glacial troughs. We apply inverse modelling to 118 new cosmogenic 10 Be and 26 Al measurements to quantify ice sheet erosion on the plateaus fringing the Sognefjorden glacial trough in western Norway. Our findings demonstrate substantial modification of the pre-glacial landscape during the Quaternary, and that glacial erosion of plateaus is important when estimating the global sediment flux to the oceans.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Andersen, Jane Lund","Egholm, D.L.","Knudsen, Mads Faurschou","Linge, Henriette","Jansen, John D.","Pedersen, Vivi K.","Nielsen, S.B.","Tikhomirov, Dmitry","Olsen, Jesper","Fabel, Derek","Xu, Sheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-248931"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Jane Lund"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bergen","University of Glasgow"],"keyword":["Climate change","Cosmogenic nuclides","Fennoscandian Ice Sheet","Landscape evolution","RATES","Sediment","Surfaces","WESTERN NORWAY"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"widespread erosion on high plateaus during recent glaciations in scandinavia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03280-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-248931","identifier":[{"id":"85043296263","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000426049100003","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5827020","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29483526","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d1481287-94db-4e0c-8998-99d3abcb1bd9"],"keyword":["AMS STANDARDS","BE-10 EXPOSURE AGES","CLIMATE-CHANGE","COSMOGENIC NUCLIDES","FENNOSCANDIAN ICE-SHEET","LANDSCAPE EVOLUTION","RATES","SEDIMENT","SURFACES","WESTERN NORWAY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78D626A2E2BC15276567064AB1773DA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03280-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/124049643/s41467_018_03280_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"aff