{"abstract":"Eutrophication events are frequent in Inner Danish waters and critical loads are exceeded for much of the Danish sensitive terrestrial ecosystems. The Danish air quality monitoring program combines measurements and model calculations to benefit from the complementarities in data from these two sources. Measurements describe actual status, seasonal variation, and temporal trends. Model calculations extrapolate the results to the entire country and determine depositions to specific ecosystems. Measurements in 2016 show annual depositions between 7.5 and 11 kg N/ha to terrestrial ecosystems, and a load to marine waters of 5.3 kg N/ha. The deposition on Danish marine waters in 2016 was calculated to be 73,000 tons N with an average deposition of 6.9 kg N/ha. For terrestrial areas, the deposition was calculated to be 57,000 tons N with an average deposition of 13 kg N/ha. This is above critical loads for sensitive ecosystems. Long-term trends show a 35% decrease since 1990 in measured annual nitrogen deposition. At two out of four stations in nature areas, measured ammonia levels exceeded critical levels for lichens and mosses. Conclusions: Nitrogen loads and levels to Danish nature is decreasing, but critical loads and levels are still exceeded for sensitive ecosystems. Combining measurements and model calculations is a strong tool in monitoring.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Ellermann, Thomas","Nygaard, Jesper","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Løfstrøm, Per","Geels, Camilla","Nielsen, Ingeborg Elbæk","Poulsen, Maria Bech","Monies, Christian","Gyldenkærne, Steen","Brandt, Jørgen","Hertel, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-268368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hertel, Ole"],"keyword":["Ammonia","Ammonium","Atmospheric transport","Critical loads","Dry deposition","Nitrate","Nitrogen budget","Nitrogen oxides","Source apportionment","Wet deposition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nitrogen deposition on danish nature","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/atmos9110447","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-268368","identifier":[{"id":"85056749181","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f3bfc8ff-b307-450d-8e71-bf426485942b"],"keyword":["Ammonia","Ammonium","Atmospheric transport","Critical loads","Dry deposition","Nitrate","Nitrogen budget","Nitrogen oxides","Sensitive ecosystems","Source apportionment","Wet deposition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F8BFAC852FCAFCB9C14822174D14BFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/atmos9110447","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/137250907/atmosphere_09_00447.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"ellermannpau","last":"Ellermann","locid":"5e5a2168-23db-4863-b6d5-bda7dcb1f662","name":"Ellermann, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"741afb0a-ec33-463b-ba45-828822224f78","name":"Nygaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"løfstrømpau","last":"Løfstrøm","locid":"84f4d438-b0e8-417d-bbbd-723e71eff311","name":"Løfstrøm, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingeborg Elbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"404da8d7-4b3a-499d-8be4-5ee0cc3dc427","name":"Nielsen, Ingeborg Elbæk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Bech","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"01949cf5-5759-444f-947f-4b40ade019be","name":"Poulsen, Maria Bech","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"moniespau","last":"Monies","locid":"46192369-39b7-4c79-9c2f-83219f8cdf43","name":"Monies, Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen","key":"gyldenkærnepau","last":"Gyldenkærne","locid":"228a6f6f-cac4-445c-86ec-de5f977ce821","name":"Gyldenkærne, Steen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","locid":"6a33f2b3-9140-4f59-a55e-e68a73c9fa32","name":"Hertel, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-0972-7735","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/atmos9110447","issn":["20734433"],"issue":"11","journal":"Atmosphere","paperid":"447","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Atmosphere","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056749181"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f3bfc8ff-b307-450d-8e71-bf426485942b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Nitrogen deposition on Danish nature","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-268368","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Understanding the determinants of public transport ridership is important in order to plan attractive public transport systems efficiently. This study analyses at a meta-level per capita public transport ridership across 48 European cities based on a rich database collected as part of this study. The dataset includes detailed mode-specific information about the public transport networks, hence extending previous research by analysing each public transport mode separately while simultaneously taking into account the main determinants of ridership identified by a thorough literature review of 36 previous studies, e.g. urban demographics and land uses. Factor analysis was deployed revealing four main composite determinants, namely i) metro coverage, network connectivity, and urban density, ii) suburban rail coverage, iii) economic inequality, and iv) light rail coverage. Subsequent multiple regression analysis confirmed the a priori hypothesis of per capita ridership being positively associated with the extent of network coverage in terms of metro, suburban rail and light rail transit. The importance of network connectivity was included with results suggesting that the number of transfer stations was more important than the cyclomatic number of the public transport network. Cities with higher economic inequality in terms of higher unemployment, lower per capita GDP and higher GINI-coefficient showed lower public transport ridership. Finally, the analyses highlighted the importance of proper definitions of urban areas in order to perform consistent analyses of data across cities. This revealed the impact on transit ridership of urban density defined as population and especially job intensity per km2. As the study is based on aggregate, cross-sectional data from a relatively small sample of European cities, it is not without limitations in terms of mainly revealing correlational structures rather than causations as well as not including all variables related to public transport ridership. Future studies should further investigate these interrelationships before drawing conclusions on the causational relationships.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss"],"keyword":["Factor analysis","Network topology","Public transport ridership","Rail factor","Urban density"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how urban density network topology and socio economy influence public transport ridership empirical evidence from 000000000048 european metropolitan areas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152927263/Ingvardson_Nielsen_2018_How_urban_density_network_topology_and_soci.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325186","identifier":[{"id":"85052322325","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-45443172-7fcc-4d9d-946e-72d967c56e9f"],"keyword":["Factor analysis","Network topology","Public transport ridership","Rail factor","Urban density"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A7089232F3294CFED677F521B372EED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152927263/Ingvardson_Nielsen_2018_How_urban_density_network_topology_and_soci.._.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtrangeo.2018.07.002","issn":["09666923","18731236"],"issn_org":["09666923"],"journal":"Journal of Transport Geography","pages":"50-63","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Transport Geography","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052322325"],"sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","11. Sustainable Cities and Production","15. Life on Land","8. Decent Work and Economic Growth","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-45443172-7fcc-4d9d-946e-72d967c56e9f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"How urban density, network topology and socio-economy influence public transport ridership: Empirical evidence from 48 European metropolitan areas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325186","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Numerical modelling is increasingly supporting the analysis and optimization of manufacturing processes in the production industry. Even if being mostly applied to multistep processes, single process steps may be so complex by nature that the needed models to describe them must include multiphysics. On the other hand, processes which inherently may seem multiphysical by nature might sometimes be modelled by considerably simpler models if the problem at hand can be somehow adequately simplified. In the present article, examples of this will be presented. The cases are chosen with the aim of showing the diversity in the field of modelling of manufacturing processes as regards process, materials, generic disciplines as well as length scales: (1) modelling of tape casting for thin ceramic layers, (2) modelling the flow of polymers in extrusion, (3) modelling the deformation process of flexible stamps for nanoimprint lithography, (4) modelling manufacturing of composite parts and (5) modelling the selective laser melting process. For all five examples, the emphasis is on modelling results as well as describing the models in brief mathematical details. Alongside with relevant references to the original work, proper comparison with experiments is given in some examples for model validation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jabbari, Masoud","Baran, Ismet","Mohanty, Sankhya","Comminal, Raphaël","Sonne, Mads Rostgaard","Nielsen, Michael Wenani","Spangenberg, Jon","Hattel, Jesper Henri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343064"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jabbari, Masoud"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Twente","University of Warwick"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LM","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiphysics modelling of manufacturing processes a review","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1687814018766188","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343064","identifier":[{"id":"85048022616","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-80dbae4b-4c94-4575-9520-f3d194ff5981"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24D860D774C66556D0C97C55A21ECF55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/148217157/1687814018766188.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1687814018766188","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of twente","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Twente","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"lm wind power","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LM","l3nn":"LM Wind Power","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LM Wind Power","namevar":["LM Wind Power"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Masoud","key":"jabbaripau","last":"Jabbari","name":"Jabbari, Masoud","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ismet","key":"baranpau","last":"Baran","name":"Baran, Ismet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sankhya","key":"mohantypau","last":"Mohanty","locid":"060a0df5-09bb-4038-b84e-848bbe3b0182","name":"Mohanty, Sankhya","orcid":"0000-0002-1142-0989","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Raphaël","key":"comminalpau","last":"Comminal","locid":"d1438993-c3aa-43b5-8f3d-d5baed49b637","name":"Comminal, Raphaël","orcid":"0000-0003-3764-5550","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Rostgaard","key":"sonnepau","last":"Sonne","locid":"90cd7f24-85a8-4b70-afdc-779b21caea85","name":"Sonne, Mads Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6320-0841","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Wenani","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Wenani","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"spangenbergpau","last":"Spangenberg","locid":"d6472dc2-035e-4d54-b7ee-96256e30814c","name":"Spangenberg, Jon","orcid":"0000-0002-5411-6821","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1687814018766188","issn":["16878132","16878140"],"issn_org":["16878132"],"issue":"5","journal":"Advances in Mechanical Engineering","pages":"1-31","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"Advances in Mechanical Engineering","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048022616"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-80dbae4b-4c94-4575-9520-f3d194ff5981"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Multiphysics modelling of manufacturing processes: A review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343064","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Waiting time at public transport stops is perceived by passengers to be more onerous than in-vehicle time, hence it strongly influences the attractiveness and use of public transport. Transport models traditionally assume that average waiting times are half the service headway by assuming random passenger arrivals. However, research agree that two distinct passenger behaviour types exist: one group arrives randomly, whereas another group actively tries to minimise their waiting time by arriving in a timely manner at the scheduled departure time. This study proposes a general framework for estimating passenger waiting times which incorporates the arrival patterns of these two groups explicitly, namely by using a mixture distribution consisting of a uniform and a beta distribution. The framework is empirically validated using a large-scale automatic fare collection system from the Greater Copenhagen Area covering metro, suburban, and regional rail stations thereby giving a range of service headways from 2 to 60 min. It was shown that the proposed mixture distribution is superior to other distributions proposed in the literature. This can improve waiting time estimations in public transport models. The results show that even at 5-min headways 43% of passengers arrive in a timely manner to stations when timetables are available. The results bear important policy implications in terms of providing actual timetables, even at high service frequencies, in order for passengers to be able to minimise their waiting times.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker","Raveau, Sebastián","Nielsen, Bo Friis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368940"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss"],"country":["Chile"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile"],"keyword":["Public policy","Scheduling","Smart cards","Waiting time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"passenger arrival and waiting time distributions dependent on train service frequency and station characteristics a smart card data analysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149170756/TRC_Review3_Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-368940","identifier":[{"id":"85044568774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d769f6c6-c7d0-458b-8e56-1d8a3cc83c7e"],"keyword":["Automated fare collection","Public policy","Scheduling","Smart cards","Subways","Waiting-time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3117AD8F132A04EFDA2EE116612E34EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149170756/TRC_Review3_Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cl","key":"pontificia universidad católica de chile","loc":["Chile","America, South","OECD"],"name":"Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonjesperbláfosspau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenottoankerpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastián","key":"raveausebastiánpau","last":"Raveau","name":"Raveau, Sebastián","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo Friis","key":"nielsenbofriispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"364b98b5-e608-4186-a566-62fa91a37d59","name":"Nielsen, Bo Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-9146-9733","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.trc.2018.03.006","issn":["0968090X","18792359"],"issn_org":["0968090X"],"journal":"Transportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies","pages":"292-306","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Transportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies","title_org":"Transportation Research. Part C: Emerging Technologies","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044568774"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d769f6c6-c7d0-458b-8e56-1d8a3cc83c7e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Passenger arrival and waiting time distributions dependent on train service frequency and station characteristics: A smart card data analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-368940","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Capturing aerial images by Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAV) allows gathering a general view of an agricultural site together with a detailed exploration of its relevant aspects for operational actions. Here we explore the challenging task of detecting cirsium arvense, a thistle-weed species, from aerial images of barley-cereal crops taken from 50 m above the ground, with the purpose of applying herbicide for site-specific weed treatment. The methods for automatic detection are based on object-based annotations, pointing out the RGB attributes of the Weed or Cereal classes for an entire group of pixels, referring to a crop area which will have to be treated if it is classified as being of the Weed class. In this way, an annotation belongs to the Weed class if more than half of its area is known to be covered by thistle weeds. Hence, based on object and pixel-level analysis, we compare the use of k-Nearest Neighbours (k-NN) and (feed-forward, one-hidden layer) neural networks, obtaining the best results for weed detection based on pixel-level analysis, based on a soft measure given by the proportion of predicted weed pixels per object, with a global accuracy of over 98%.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Franco, Camilo","Guada, Carely","Rodríguez, J. Tinguaro","Nielsen, Jon","Rasmussen, Jesper","Gómez, Daniel","Montero, Javier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405018"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-15","place":"Cadiz, es","start":"2018-06-11","title":"17th International Conference on Information Processing and Management of Uncertainty in Knowledge-Based Systems, IPMU 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Colombia","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Complutense University of Madrid","University of Los Andes"],"keyword":["Image analysis","Neural networks","Precision agriculture","Soft measures","Weed detection","k Nearest neighbours"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automatic detection of thistle weeds in cereal crops from aerial rgb images","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-405018","identifier":[{"id":"85048054602","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-13748f48-cbd9-4941-b0f8-7a78210e9d14"],"keyword":["Image analysis","Neural networks","Precision agriculture","Soft measures","Weed detection","k-Nearest neighbours"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9AEC2E7D47B17A2331387D54D1DAC203"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"co","key":"university of los andes","loc":["Colombia","America, South","OECD"],"name":"University of Los Andes","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"complutense university of madrid","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Complutense University of Madrid","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Camilo","key":"francopau","last":"Franco","name":"Franco, Camilo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Carely","key":"guadapau","last":"Guada","name":"Guada, Carely","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J. Tinguaro","key":"rodríguezpau","last":"Rodríguez","name":"Rodríguez, J. Tinguaro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d45561f-3e81-41e1-8310-03bdb7abbad0","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniel","key":"gómezpau","last":"Gómez","name":"Gómez, Daniel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Javier","key":"monteropau","last":"Montero","name":"Montero, Javier","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-91479-4_37","isbn":["9783319914787"],"issn":["18650929"],"pages":"441-452","publisher":"Springer","series":"Communications in Computer and Information Science","status":"p","title":"Information Processing and Management of Uncertainty in Knowledge-Based Systems. Applications - 17th International Conference, IPMU 2018, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048054602"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-13748f48-cbd9-4941-b0f8-7a78210e9d14"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automatic detection of thistle-weeds in cereal crops from aerial RGB images","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405018","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist","Nielsen, Jesper G.","Rasmussen, Anders Juhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bipersonerne peter seebergs romaner noveller og kortprosa","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-408964","ids":["ku-19fdeddb-3c61-43ad-8f92-3253aa4cfa20"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CBCAFBFA3C469C79467D9BC0AE938A63"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Lindquist","key":"barnwellped","last":"Barnwell","locid":"50916516-bf5a-460e-94b1-77cf4f11c535","name":"Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist","orcid":"0009-0001-8395-1818","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper G.","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper G.","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenped","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e1188ff-4cc9-42e2-86b3-59515e62f1af","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788702275667"],"pages":"299","place":"København","publisher":"Gyldendal","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-19fdeddb-3c61-43ad-8f92-3253aa4cfa20"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bipersonerne : Peter Seebergs romaner, noveller og kortprosa","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408964","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Target temperature management (TTM) at 32-36 °C is recommended in unconscious survivors of cardiac arrest. This study reports awakening in the TTM-trial. Our predefined hypotheses were that time until awakening correlates with long-term neurological outcome and is not affected by level of TTM. METHODS: Post-hoc analysis of time until awakening after cardiac arrest, its association with long-term (180-days) neurological outcome and predictors of late awakening (day 5 or later). The trial randomized 939 comatose survivors to TTM at 33 °C or 36 °C with strict criteria for withdrawal of life-sustaining therapies. Administered sedation in the treatment groups was compared. Awakening was defined as a Glasgow Coma Scale motor score 6. RESULTS: 496 patients had registered day of awakening in the ICU, another 43 awoke after ICU discharge. Good neurological outcome was more common in early (275/308, 89%) vs late awakening (142/188, 76%), p < 0.001. Awakening occurred later in TTM33 than in TTM36 (p = 0.002) with no difference in neurological outcome, or cumulative doses of sedative drugs at 12, 24 or 48 h. TTM33 (p = 0.006), clinical seizures (p = 0.004), and lower GCS-M on admission (p = 0.03) were independent predictors of late awakening. CONCLUSION: Late awakening is common and often has a good neurological outcome. Time to awakening was longer in TTM33 than in TTM36, this difference could not be attributed to differences in sedative drugs administered during the first 48 h.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Lybeck, Anna","Cronberg, Tobias","Aneman, Anders","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Hovdenes, Jan","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Wanscher, Michael","Stammet, Pascal","Wise, Matthew P","Nielsen, Niklas","Ullén, Susann","Friberg, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["TTM-Trial Investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Coma drug therapy","Female","Humans","Hypnotics and Sedatives administration dosage","Hypothermia Induced methods","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Single Blind Method","Time Factors","Withholding Treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"time to awakening after cardiac arrest and the association with target temperature management","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-440914","identifier":[{"id":"85041577290","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29371115","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4f82dd4b-3115-4e3b-b992-8af457ff648b"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Coma/drug therapy","Female","Humans","Hypnotics and Sedatives/administration & dosage","Hypothermia, Induced/methods","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/therapy","Single-Blind Method","Time Factors","Wakefulness/drug effects","Withholding Treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D74EB0CD01CAFFA336A020E6E486443"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ttm trial investigators","name":"TTM-Trial Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anna","k