,"name":"Omerzu, Heike","orcid":"0000-0001-9538-5748","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"høgenhavenpedh","last":"Høgenhaven","name":"Høgenhaven, Jesper","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"tangnielsenpedh","last":"Tang Nielsen","name":"Tang Nielsen, Jesper","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"omerzupedh","last":"Omerzu","name":"Omerzu, Heike","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783161554391"],"issn":["05121604"],"pages":"1-5","place":"Tübingen","publisher":"Mohr Siebeck","series":"Wissenschaftliche Untersuchungen zum Neuen Testament","status":"p","title":"Rewriting and Reception in and of the Bible"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-873912d0-357e-4720-b4af-81fece8976fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction: Rewriting and Reception in and of the Bible","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474322","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Dyscarbia is common in out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) patients and its association to neurological outcome is undetermined. Methods: This is an exploratory post-hoc substudy of the Target Temperature Management (TTM) trial, including resuscitated OHCA patients, investigating the association between serial measurements of arterial partial carbon dioxide pressure (PaCO2) and neurological outcome at 6months, defined by the Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) scale, dichotomized to good outcome (CPC 1 and 2) and poor outcome (CPC 3-5). The effects of hypercapnia and hypocapnia, and the time-weighted mean PaCO2 and absolute PaCO2 difference were analyzed. Additionally, the association between mild hypercapnia (6.0-7.30kPa) and neurological outcome, its interaction with target temperature (33°C and 36°C), and the association between PaCO2 and peak serum-Tau were evaluated. Results: Of the 939 patients in the TTM trial, 869 were eligible for analysis. Ninety-six percent of patients were exposed to hypocapnia or hypercapnia. None of the analyses indicated a statistical significant association between PaCO2 and neurological outcome (P=0.13-0.96). Mild hypercapnia was not associated with neurological outcome (P=0.78) and there was no statistically significant interaction with target temperature (P interaction=0.95). There was no association between PaCO2 and peak serum-Tau levels 48 or 72h after return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC). Conclusions: Dyscarbia is common after ROSC. No statistically significant association between PaCO2 in the post-cardiac arrest phase and neurological outcome at 6 months after cardiac arrest was detected. There was no significant interaction between mild hypercapnia and temperature in relation to neurological outcome.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ebner, Florian","Harmon, Matt B.A.","Aneman, Anders","Cronberg, Tobias","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Juffermans, Nicole","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Mattsson, Niklas","Pelosi, Paolo","Ullén, Susann","Undén, Johan","Wise, Matt P.","Nielsen, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524269"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Italy","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Academic Medical Centre","All Global Affiliations","Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care","Department of Anesthesia and Intensive Care","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST - Istituto Nazionale per la Ricerca sul Cancro","Leeuwarden Medical Centrum","Lund University","University Hospital of Wales","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Cerebral performance","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Serum Tau"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carbon dioxide dynamics in relation to neurological outcome in resuscitated out of hospital cardiac arrest patients an exploratory target temperature management trial substudy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-018-2119-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524269","identifier":[{"id":"30119692","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85051973001","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6098627","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-db0eb81a-3a91-41fa-9faf-0ad3fd623476"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Carbon dioxide partial pressure","Cerebral performance","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Serum Tau"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D561195469E895883A2CE348FC9882F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc"