6eebd4-6fdf-4819-bf31-6ae3c7e0b582","name":"Skovgaard, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6729-4988","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30475135"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1123/jpah.2018-0509","issn":["15433080","15435474"],"issn_org":["15433080"],"issue":"Supplement 2","journal":"Journal of Physical Activity and Health","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Activity and Health","title_org":"Journal of Physical Activity & Health","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057080678"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","UC SYD, University College South Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","the region of southern denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c534298d-8857-470f-bf3d-5d763bcf5fff","sdu-88c76a39-de35-4a8f-8e54-876346e5b6d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Results from Denmark's 2018 Report Card on Physical Activity for Children and Youth","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.19-046042","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Hydraulic conductivity (Ks) and effective porosity (ϕeff) for saturated water flow are essential hydraulic properties for describing fluid and chemical transport in soil and groundwater systems. Typically, Ks is predicted by pedotransfer functions of soil texture and total porosity or ϕeff. This study shows that a more conceptual approach that uses a volume-weighted ratio of coarser (part of the sand fraction) to finer (clay and organic matter) particles alongside total porosity could explain variations in both Ks and φeff in intact 100-cm3 samples of 20 sandy surface and subsurface soils with <10% fines (clay + organic matter). The Ks function used was a simple power-law function of the volume-weighted coarse/fine particle ratio with two calibration parameters [A and pore network connectivity (PNC)]. The value of the power-law exponent (PNC) in the calibrated function was 1.8, similar to power-law exponents for gas diffusivity and air permeability in unsaturated soil (1.5–2). The second calibration parameter (A) probably depends on the soil classes under consideration, the Ks measurement method, and the sample scale. A sensitivity analyses showed that both Ks and ϕeff (taken as the volume content of pores larger than 30 μm, that is, drained at –10 kPa of soil water matric potential) are especially sensitive to organic matter content. Besides the water transport parameters, water retention under dry conditions was also closely correlated with the volume-weighted fines content. Therefore, the volume ratio concept seems to be a promising platform for the development of simple, accurate functions for the hydraulic properties of coarse-textured soils.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Karup, Dan","De Jonge, Lis W.","Ahm, Malte","Bentzen, Thomas Ruby","Rasmussen, Michael R.","Møldrup, Per"],"cuid":["S02-097.03-006322"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can the volume ratio of coarse to fine particles explain the hydraulic properties of sandy soil","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2136/sssaj2018.02.0083","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.03-006322","identifier":[{"id":"85054827707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-829cb6d1-795f-4098-9231-a150729cdd4d","au-733767fe-9c30-4604-a516-7ea0657272f5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F398AF8839E50B0CABFC86A98329AB30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/301511689/Can_the_volume_ratio_of_coarse_to_fine_particles_explain_the_hydraulic_properties_of_sandy_soil.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2136/sssaj2018.02.0083","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/140614068/1093.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Environment (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Vandmiljø Randers A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Soil Physics and Hydropedology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper E.","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"karuppau","last":"Karup","name":"Karup, Dan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lis Wollesen","key":"dejongepau","last":"de Jonge","locid":"ba21501a-3289-4d7f-8cae-eeb7556b854a","name":"de Jonge, Lis Wollesen","orcid":"0000-0003-2874-0644","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Malte","key":"ahmpau","last":"Ahm","name":"Ahm, Malte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas R.","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","locid":"2d4c4761-75f3-4d14-adc5-06f73cd3a2d3","name":"Bentzen, Thomas Ruby","name_org":"Bentzen, Thomas R.","orcid":"0000-0002-5738-2519","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael R.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"moldruppau","last":"Moldrup","locid":"a34e3e5e-cf22-4350-9d3c-095ea3f5c014","name":"Møldrup, Per","name_org":"Moldrup, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-1619-1457","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2136/sssaj2018.02.0083","issn":["03615995","14350661"],"issn_org":["03615995"],"issue":"5","journal":"Soil Science Society of America Journal","pages":"1093-1100","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Soil Science Society of America Journal","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054827707"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","aarhus water ltd.","vandmiljø randers a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-829cb6d1-795f-4098-9231-a150729cdd4d","au-733767fe-9c30-4604-a516-7ea0657272f5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Can the Volume Ratio of Coarse to Fine Particles Explain the Hydraulic Properties of Sandy Soil?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.03-006322","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Activation of energy expenditure in thermogenic fat is a promising strategy to improve metabolic health, yet the dynamic processes that evoke this response are poorly understood. Here we show that synthesis of the mitochondrial phospholipid cardiolipin is indispensable for stimulating and sustaining thermogenic fat function. Cardiolipin biosynthesis is robustly induced in brown and beige adipose upon cold exposure. Mimicking this response through overexpression of cardiolipin synthase (Crls1) enhances energy consumption in mouse and human adipocytes. Crls1 deficiency in thermogenic adipocytes diminishes inducible mitochondrial uncoupling and elicits a nuclear transcriptional response through endoplasmic reticulum stress-mediated retrograde communication. Cardiolipin depletion in brown and beige fat abolishes adipose thermogenesis and glucose uptake, which renders animals insulin resistant. We further identify a rare human CRLS1 variant associated with insulin resistance and show that adipose CRLS1 levels positively correlate with insulin sensitivity. Thus, adipose cardiolipin has a powerful impact on organismal energy homeostasis through thermogenic fat bioenergetics. Sustarsic et al. reveal that synthesis of the mitochondrial phospholipid cardiolipin is a hallmark of brown and beige fat activation by cold temperature. This single lipid species in thermogenic fat not only shapes adipose mitochondrial bioenergetics but also exerts profound control over whole-body insulin sensitivity and metabolic flexibility.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Sustarsic, Elahu G","Ma, Tao","Lynes, Matthew D","Larsen, Michael","Karavaeva, Iuliia","Havelund, Jesper F","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Jedrychowski, Mark P","Moreno-Torres, Marta","Lundh, Morten","Plucińska, Kaja","Jespersen, Naja Z","Grevengoed, Trisha J.","Kramar, Barbara","Peics, Julia","Hansen, Jakob Bondo","Shamsi, Farnaz","Forss, Isabel","Neess, Ditte","Keipert, Susanne","Wang, Jianing","Stohlmann, Katharina","Brandslund, Ivan","Christensen, Cramer","Jørgensen, Marit E","Linneberg, Allan","Pedersen, Oluf","Kiebish, Michael A","Qvortrup, Klaus","Han, Xianlin","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Jastroch, Martin","Mandrup, Susanne","Kjaer, Andreas","Gygi, Steven P","Hansen, Torben","Gillum, Matthew P.","Grarup, Niels","Emanuelli, Brice","Nielsen, Søren","Scheele, Camilla","Tseng, Yu-Hua","Færgeman, Nils J","Gerhart-Hines, Zachary"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-043882"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gerhart-Hines, Zachary"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BERG Health","Harvard Medical School","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","The University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio"],"keyword":["Cardiolipin","Insulin Resistance","Lipid Metabolism","Mitochondria","Phospholipids","Thermogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiolipin synthesis in brown and beige fat mitochondria is essential for systemic energy homeostasis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmet.2018.05.003","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank members of the Gerhart-Hines and Tseng labs for discussions. We are grateful to Genoway for assistance in the design and generation of Crls1 floxed mice. We thank Dr. Miao Wang for technical assistance with targeted brown fat lipidomics. The Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx) Project was supported by the Common Fund of the Office of the Director of the NIH , and by NCI , NHGRI , NHLBI , NIDA , NIMH , and NINDS . The Core Facility for Integrated Microscopy (CFIM) is acknowledged for access to electron microscopes. This work was supported by funding from NIDDK grants R01DK077097 and R01DK102898 (Y.H.-T.), F32DK102320 (M.D.L.), 30DK036836 (Joslin Diabetes Center's Diabetes Research Center), the Danish Diabetes Academy (M.M.-T. and N.Z.J.), the Novo Nordisk Foundation (T.H., M.P.G., B.E., N.G., C.S., and Z.G.-H.), and the Danish Council for Independent Research-Medical Sciences (M. Lundh, N.J.F.), including Sapere Aude Starting grant 4002-00024 (Z.G.-H). In addition, this project has received funding from the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation Programme (grant agreement no. 639382 ). The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research is an independent Research Center at the University of Copenhagen partially funded by an unrestricted donation from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( http://cbmr.ku.dk/ )."],"id":"S02-097.78-043882","identifier":[{"id":"29861389","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85047218679","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6038052","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8028fe7f-422a-440b-b5d5-c67606aa09aa","sdu-ac1be669-d852-4f0c-8624-0ba53d73a566"],"keyword":["CHOP-10","CRLS1","beige adipose","brown adipose","cardiolipin","insulin resistance","lipid metabolism","mitochondria","phospholipids","thermogenesis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AC1D7BB68A365502788AC6F9609A5E78"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/199881781/1_s2.0_S1550413118303103_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141723640/1_s2.0_S1550413118303103_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa",