t":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Søren","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla","key":"scheelecamillapau","last":"Scheele","locid":"7e468840-db86-434d-b6f7-2b1c9cadb88e","name":"Scheele, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0002-6055-9709","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu Hua","key":"tsengyuhuapau","last":"Tseng","name":"Tseng, Yu Hua","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nils J.","key":"færgemannilsjpau","last":"Færgeman","locid":"448a164d-523a-4d91-923c-fc5536371b95","name":"Færgeman, Nils J.","orcid":"0000-0002-9281-5287","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zachary","key":"gerharthineszacharypau","last":"Gerhart-Hines","locid":"04fa1a49-5a2d-49c8-96ce-cb4eb14d091c","name":"Gerhart-Hines, Zachary","orcid":"0000-0003-2981-4991","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29861389"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cmet.2018.05.003","issn":["15504131","19327420"],"issn_org":["15504131"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cell Metabolism","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Cell Metabolism","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047218679"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8028fe7f-422a-440b-b5d5-c67606aa09aa","sdu-ac1be669-d852-4f0c-8624-0ba53d73a566"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cardiolipin Synthesis in Brown and Beige Fat Mitochondria Is Essential for Systemic Energy Homeostasis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-043882","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Itch and pain share numerous mechanistic similarities. Patients with chronic itch conditions (for instance atopic dermatitis or neuropathic itch) often experience symptoms such as mechanical alloknesis and hyperknesis. These dysesthesias are analogous to the pain-associated phenomena allodynia and hyperalgesia, which are often observed, for example, in neuropathic pain conditions. Mechanical itch dysesthesias represent abnormal sensory states (caused by neuroplastic changes), wherein considerable itch is evoked, for instance by light cutaneous stimuli such as from clothing (alloknesis), or where increased itch is perceived in response to normally itch-evoking stimuli (hyperknesis). These itch sensitization phenomena have been explored in experimental human studies, observed in chronic itch patients, and in animal models of itch. Limited attention has been paid to these sensory phenomena in clinical studies, and it is unknown how they respond to antipruritics. Psychophysical quantitative sensory testing can quantify the presence, severity, and spatial extent of itch dysesthesias in chronic itch patients, providing a proxy measurement of itch sensitization. This review outlines current assessment techniques, knowledge on the mechanisms of mechanical alloknesis and hyperknesis, and presents the diverse results derived from clinical studies exploring the presence of itch dysesthesias in chronic itch patients. A key role of quantitative sensory testing and neuronal sensitization in patients with chronic pain is accepted and used in clinical assessments. However, the precise mechanisms and potential clinical implications of itch sensitization in chronic itch patients remain to be evaluated.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Andersen, Hjalte Holm","Akiyama, Tasuka","Nattkemper, Leigh Ann","van Laarhoven, Antoinette I. M.","Elberling, Jesper","Yosipovitch, Gil","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-098.84-005344"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Central Nervous System Sensitization physiology","Humans","Pain physiopathology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alloknesis and hyperknesis mechanisms assessment methodology and clinical implications of itch sensitization","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/273832383/Alloknesis_and_hyperknesis_mechanisms_assessment_methodology_and_clinical_implications_of_itch_sensitization.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.84-005344","identifier":[{"id":"85055725688","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29659469","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-6e35aac8-3fda-47fc-b30f-c24ec702e093","ku-3cd397db-eccb-4223-8a64-8c153c580557"],"keyword":["Central Nervous System Sensitization/physiology","Humans","Pain/physiopathology","Pruritus/physiopathology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-68AC2CF32FD12C3F7429DC2CEC3853DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/273832383/Alloknesis_and_hyperknesis_mechanisms_assessment_methodology_and_clinical_implications_of_itch_sensitization.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Pain and Motor System Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hjalte Holm","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5de532a5-1602-416c-96b7-20a316e28e25","name":"Andersen, Hjalte Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tasuka","key":"akiyamapau","last":"Akiyama","name":"Akiyama, Tasuka","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Leigh Ann","key":"nattkemperpau","last":"Nattkemper","name":"Nattkemper, Leigh Ann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoinette I. M.","key":"vanlaarhovenpau","last":"van Laarhoven","locid":"e1116201-2651-4354-864b-43defef4c068","name":"van Laarhoven, Antoinette I. M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gil","key":"yosipovitchpau","last":"Yosipovitch","name":"Yosipovitch, Gil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29659469"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/j.pain.0000000000001220","issn":["03043959","18726623"],"issn_org":["03043959"],"issue":"7","journal":"Pain","pages":"1185-1197","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Pain","volume":"159"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055725688"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6e35aac8-3fda-47fc-b30f-c24ec702e093","ku-3cd397db-eccb-4223-8a64-8c153c580557"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Alloknesis and hyperknesis : mechanisms, assessment methodology, and clinical implications of itch sensitization","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.84-005344","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: The Osborn or J-wave, an upright deflection of the J-point on the electrocardiogram (ECG), is often observed during severe hypothermia. A possible relation between Osborn waves (OW) and increased risk of ventricular arrhythmia has been reported. We sought to determine whether the level of targeted temperature management (TTM) following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) affects the prevalence of OW and to assess the associations between OW and risk of ventricular arrhythmia and death. Methods and results: The present study is part of the TTM-trial ECG-substudy (including OHCA-patients randomized to TTM at 33 °C vs. 36 °C from 24 of 36 sites). Serial 12-lead ECGs from 680 (94%) patients were analysed and stratified by OW at predefined time-points (0, 4, 28, 36, 72-h after admission). On admission, the overall prevalence of OW was 16%, increasing to 32% at target temperature, with higher prevalence in the 33 °C-group (40% vs. 23%, p < 0.0001). No difference in prevalence was found between the 33 °C- and 36 °C-groups on admission (18% vs. 14%, p =.11) or after rewarming (13% vs. 10%, p =.44). OW were not associated with increased risk of ventricular arrhythmia (Odds ratio = 0.78 (0.51–1.20), p =.26), but associated with significantly lower 180-day mortality as compared to no OW (38% vs. 52%, p log-rank = 0.001) in univariable analyses only. Conclusion: OW are frequent during TTM, particularly in patients treated with 33 °C. OW are not associated with increased risk of ventricular arrhythmia, and may be considered a benign physiological phenomenon, associated with lower mortality in univariable analyses.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hadziselimovic, Edina","Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Køber, Lars","Graff, Claus","Pehrson, Steen","Nielsen, Niklas","Erlinge, David","Frydland, Martin","Wiberg, Sebastian","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.86-002941"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Arrhythmias Cardiac etiology","Cardiac arrest","Cardiac arrhythmia","Electrocardiography","Female","Humans","Hypothermia","Hypothermia Induced adverse effects","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest mortality","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Repolarization","Risk Factors","TTM","Targeted temperature management","Therapeutic hypothermia","Ventricular arrhythmia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"osborn waves following out of hospital cardiac arrest effect of level of temperature management and risk of arrhythmia and death","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/275085079/PIIS0300957218302090.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-099.86-002941","identifier":[{"id":"85047072104","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29723608","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-3ba7eb92-0d81-45fe-8fec-02db97a5f08e","ku-deb4cebf-935a-4f5d-89c6-52d566b21af7"],"keyword":["Aged","Arrhythmias, Cardiac/etiology","Cardiac arrest","Cardiac arrhythmia","Electrocardiography","Female","Humans","Hypothermia","Hypothermia, Induced/adverse effects","J-waves","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Osborn waves","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/mortality","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Repolarization","Risk Factors","TTM","Targeted temperature management","Therapeutic hypothermia","Ventricular arrhythmia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-579FB7DA528948CA73148754F56A5547"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/275085079/PII