e":"Abdulla, Jawdat","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"lyngbækstigpau","last":"Lyngbæk","name":"Lyngbæk, Stig","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"elminghannepau","last":"Elming","name":"Elming, Hanne","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Susette Krohn","key":"therkelsensusettekrohnpau","last":"Therkelsen","name":"Therkelsen, Susette Krohn","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"abildgaardulrikpau","last":"Abildgaard","name":"Abildgaard, Ulrik","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Skov","key":"jensenjanskovpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e29024e8-87d0-4edb-a304-f0b6393488a4","name":"Jensen, Jan Skov","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"skovjensenjanpau","last":"Skov Jensen","name":"Skov Jensen, Jan","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Gunnar","key":"gislasongunnarpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","orcid":"0000-0002-0548-402X","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars V","key":"køberlarspau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","name_org":"Køber, Lars V","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars V.","key":"køberlarsvpau","last":"Køber","name":"Køber, Lars V.","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thomas","key":"engstrømthomaspau","last":"Engstrøm","locid":"77ddb69e-092a-4c53-bbf0-409cdd3d12f7","name":"Engstrøm, Thomas","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30565996"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.118.037152","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"issue":"24","journal":"Circulation","pages":"2741-2750","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"138"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058892770"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e2eeb64e-d092-42df-9887-eb75cb3a99f6","ku-a26cd091-1b85-48b7-a94a-936a46df6ff2","sdu-1100e26a-b08a-4db4-97fb-53b666b21402"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Early Versus Standard Care Invasive Examination and Treatment of Patients With Non-ST-Segment Elevation Acute Coronary Syndrome : VERDICT Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.99-010838","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Women living with HIV (WLWH) have elevated risk of human papillomavirus (HPV) related cancers. OBJECTIVES: To assess prevalence, distribution and concordance of cervical, oral, and anal HPV infection, and predictors of oral and anal HPV in WLWH in Denmark. STUDY DESIGN: WLWH followed in the Study on HIV, cervical Abnormalities and infections in women in Denmark (SHADE) were enrolled and examined for cervical, oral, and anal HPV infection. Logistic regression models were used to identify predictors of anal and oral HPV. RESULTS: A total of 214 of 334 WLWH had sufficient DNA for analysis at all three anatomical sites and were included in analyses. Cervical, oral, and anal high-risk (hr) HPV prevalence were 28.0%, 3.7% and 39.3%. Most frequent i) cervical, ii) oral and iii) anal hrHPV genotypes were i) hrHPV58 (8.4%), 52 (5.1%), 16 (5.1%) and 51 (5.1%); ii) 52 (1.4%) and iii) 51 (9.3%), 58 (8.9%), 16 (7.0%) and 18 (7.0%). Among present cervical, oral, and anal hrHPV genotypes, 6.7%, 12.5% and 17.9% were targeted by the 2-or 4-valent HPV vaccines, whereas 50.0%, 50.0% and 42.9% of hrHPV genotypes were covered by the 9-valent HPV vaccine. Anal HPV infection was predicted by cervical HPV infection (adjusted OR 4.47 (95%CI 2.25-8.89)). CONCLUSION: Cervical and anal HPV infection were highly prevalent in WLWH. Non-16/18 hrHPV genotypes were predominant at all anatomical sites. Almost half of all hrHPV infections at the three anatomical sites could have been prevented by childhood/adolescent vaccination with the 9-valent HPV vaccine.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Thorsteinsson, Kristina","Storgaard, Merete","Katzenstein, Terese L","Ladelund, Steen","Rönsholt, Frederikke F","Johansen, Isik Somuncu","Pedersen, Gitte","Gaardsting, Anne","Nielsen, Lars Nørregård","Bonde, Jesper","Lebech, Anne-Mette"],"cuid":["S04-099.24-012074"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Thorsteinsson, Kristina"],"keyword":["Adult","Cervical cancer anal cancer","Cervix Uteri virology","Cohort Studies","Concordance","Denmark epidemiology","Epidemiological Monitoring","Female","Genotype","Genotype distribution","HIV Infections complications","HPV prevalence","HPV vaccine","Human papillomavirus","Humans","Middle Aged","Mouth virology","Oral cancer","Papillomaviridae genetics","Papillomavirus Infections epidemiology","Prevalence","Regression Analysis","Risk Factors","Women living with HIV"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Institute of Clinical Medicine, Faculty of Medicine, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of cervical oral and anal human papillomavirus infection in women living with hiv in denmark the shade cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/295080907/Prevalence_of_Cervical_Oral_and_Anal_Human_Papillomaviru_2018_Journal_of_C.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish Cancer Society and the AIDS Foundation ; the Aragon Foundation ; the Foundation of Aase and Ejnar Danielsens and the Foundation of Anna and Preben Simonsen . Grant numbers do not apply in a Danish setting. The sponsors of the study had no role in study design, data collection, data analysis, data interpretation or writing of the article. KT has received research funding from Abbott, a travel grant from Janssen-Cilag and honoraria from Janssen-Cilag, BMS and GlaxoSmithKline/Viiv. MS has received an unrestricted grant from Gilead. TLK has received research funding and/or honoraria from Bristol-Myers Squibb, Merck Sharp & Dohme, GlaxoSmithKline/Viiv, Abbott, Gilead, and Janssen-Cilag. Since the paper in question was initiated, SL, has taken up a position in Novo Nordisk A/S working within the insulin franchise. For this paper SL is affiliating Clinical Research Centre, Copenhagen University Hospital, Hvidovre. JB attended meetings with various HPV device manufacturers. JB used to serve as a paid advisor to Roche and Genomica, and has received honoraria from Hologic/Gen-probe, Roche, Qiagen, Genomica, and BD Diagnostics for lectures, and is the principal investigator on projects funded by BD Diagnostics, Genomica, and Qiagen. AML has received travel grant and/or honoraria from Bristol-Myers Squibb, Gilead and GlaxoSmithKline. SL, FR, IJ, GP, LNN, AG discloses no conflicts of interest."],"id":"S04-099.24-012074","identifier":[{"id":"29906660","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85048307929","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fdeb8fa7-d936-41e4-bcbd-8bea3699f6c6","au-08df7ccd-aba0-4731-be95-b81c5750809e","ku-468efd3b-2def-4688-845b-7c2f3073c267","sdu-e0c49079-7441-4784-b22e-096cab6c7cac"],"keyword":["Adult","Anal Canal/virology","Cervical cancer, anal cancer","Cervix Uteri/virology","Cohort Studies","Concordance","Denmark/epidemiology","Epidemiological Monitoring","Female","Genotype","Genotype distribution","HIV Infections/complications","HPV prevalence","HPV vaccine","Human papillomavirus","Humans","Middle Aged","Mouth/virology","Oral cancer","Papillomaviridae/genetics","Papillomavirus Infections/epidemiology","Prevalence","Regression Analysis","Risk Factors","Women living with HIV"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-D5889BDBC38E29A083C24283EEE4BDA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":