{"abstract":"The estimation of the noise power spectral density (PSD) forms a critical component of several existing single channel speech enhancement systems. In this paper, we evaluate one new and some of the existing and commonly used noise PSD estimation algorithms in terms of the spectral estimation accuracy and the enhancement performance for different commonly encountered background noises, which are stationary and non-stationary in nature. The evaluated algorithms include the Minimum Statistics, MMSE, IMCRA methods and a new model-based method.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kavalekalam, Mathew Shaji","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Boldt, Jesper Bünsow"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-075463"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2018-04-20","place":"Calgary, ca","start":"2018-04-15","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a study of noise psd estimators for single channel speech enhancement","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-075463","identifier":[{"id":"85054203112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-57933ca9-06d7-4d9b-9556-919d99a072b5"],"keyword":["speech enhancement, noise PSD estimation, autoregressive models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-802D49A73ACD002FB6418FD553954844"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["GN Hearing A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathew Shaji","key":"kavalekalampau","last":"Kavalekalam","locid":"6082dcd3-6e02-459e-8b51-2ac06555e654","name":"Kavalekalam, Mathew Shaji","orcid":"0000-0003-3124-3008","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bünsow","key":"boldtpau","last":"Boldt","name":"Boldt, Jesper Bünsow","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp.2018.8461703","eisbn":["9781538646588","9781538646595"],"isbn":["9781538646571"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"5464-5468","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054203112"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","gn hearing a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-57933ca9-06d7-4d9b-9556-919d99a072b5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Study of Noise PSD Estimators for Single Channel Speech Enhancement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-075463","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Sound zones are typically created using Acoustic Contrast Control (ACC), Pressure Matching (PM), or variations of the two. ACC maximizes the acoustic potential energy contrast between a listening zone and a quiet zone. Although the contrast is maximized, the phase is not controlled. To control both the amplitude and the phase, PM instead minimizes the difference between the reproduced sound field and the desired sound field in all zones. On the surface, ACC and PM seem to control sound fields differently, but we here demonstrate they are actually extreme special cases of a much more general framework. The framework is inspired by the variable span linear filtering framework for speech enhancement. Using this framework, we demonstrate that 1) ACC gives the best contrast, but the highest signal distortion in the bright zone, and 2) PM gives the smallest signal distortion in the bright zone, but the worst contrast. Aside from showing this mathematically, we also demonstrate this via a small toy example.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lee, Taewoong","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100907"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2018-04-20","place":"Calgary, ca","start":"2018-04-15","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Joint diagonalization","Personal sound","Sound zones","Speech enhancement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a unified approach to generating sound zones using variable span linear filters","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/299372143/tlee_etal_VAST_ICASSP2018.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-100907","identifier":[{"id":"85054259278","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000446384600098","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-af3aa2fd-6230-422d-a915-5128873c9aff"],"keyword":["Joint diagonalization","Personal sound","Sound zones","Speech enhancement","Variable span linear filter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30E8147532BB1C981FD690540E8718EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/299372143/tlee_etal_VAST_ICASSP2018.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Taewoong","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","locid":"d1eeade6-8e75-427d-9c1f-1a4ac5464576","name":"Lee, Taewoong","orcid":"0000-0002-6669-0820","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp.2018.8462477","eisbn":["9781538646588"],"isbn":["9781538646571"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"491-495","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054259278"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-af3aa2fd-6230-422d-a915-5128873c9aff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Unified Approach to Generating Sound Zones Using Variable Span Linear Filters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-100907","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We consider determinantal point processes on the d-dimensional unit sphere S d . These are finite point processes exhibiting repulsiveness and with moment properties determined by a certain determinant whose entries are specified by a so-called kernel which we assume is a complex covariance function defined on S d ×S d. We review the appealing properties of such processes, including their specific moment properties, density expressions and simulation procedures. Particularly, we characterize and construct isotropic DPPs models on S d , where it becomes essential to specify the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions in a spectral representation for the kernel, and we figure out how repulsive isotropic DPPs can be. Moreover, we discuss the shortcomings of adapting existing models for isotropic covariance functions and consider strategies for developing new models, including a useful spectral approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Jesper","Nielsen, Morten","Porcu, Emilio","Rubak, Ege Holger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-104131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Chile"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidad Técnica Federico Santa Maria"],"keyword":["Isotropic covariance function","Joint intensities","Quantifying repulsiveness","Spatial point process density","Spectral representation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determinantal point process models on the sphere","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.03675.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-104131","identifier":[{"id":"85034844268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ba509661-4f6b-41fd-a8db-291b20424765"],"keyword":["Schoenberg representation","isotropic covariance function","joint intensities","quantifying repulsiveness","spatial point process density","spectral representation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D30591E76EEF5B701A74A926924165E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.03675.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cl","key":"universidad técnica federico santa maria","loc":["Chile","America, South","OECD"],"name":"Universidad Técnica Federico Santa Maria","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"f4a41894-3666-409d-9242-1e37dc10e906","name":"Møller, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-0008-6890","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a2d4eb0d-db4a-4f25-924a-4a830da62f9f","name":"Nielsen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9078-0594","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilio","key":"porcupau","last":"Porcu","name":"Porcu, Emilio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ege Holger","key":"rubakpau","last":"Rubak","locid":"926a5257-f1ec-46d6-be30-bba4c80a0867","name":"Rubak, Ege Holger","orcid":"0000-0002-6675-533X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3150/16-bej896","issn":["13507265"],"issue":"2","journal":"Bernoulli","pages":"1171-1201","publisher":"Bernoulli Society for Mathematical Statistics and Probability","status":"p","title":"Bernoulli","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034844268"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ba509661-4f6b-41fd-a8db-291b20424765"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Determinantal point process models on the sphere","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-104131","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Tollund Man is one of the most famous Iron Age bog bodies due to his well-preserved head. Since he was unearthed in 1950 in Bjældskovdal, Denmark, he has been subjected to several scientific investigations, but until now no attempts to reconstruct his general diet through isotope analyses have been conducted. Furthermore, previous radiocarbon ( 14C) analyses have only been able to date him broadly to the 3rd-4th century BC. In this study, stable isotope measurements (δ 13C, δ 15N) on bone collagen from Tollund Man's femur and rib showed that the diet of Tollund Man was terrestrial-based and that the crops he ate probably were grown on manured fields. Accelerator mass spectrometry (AMS) 14C dates were obtained on both the <30kDa and >30kDa fractions of ultrafiltered collagen. Results showed that the ultrafiltration removed contamination from older substances from the burial environment. The femur was dated to 2330±23 BP, the rib to 2322±30 BP. These dates statistically agree with a previously published AMS 14C age on skin. By combining the new dates with the previous date of his skin it was possible to narrow down the age of Tollund Man to the period 405-380 cal BC (95.4% confidence interval).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Helt Nielsen, Nina","Philippsen, Bente","Kanstrup, Marie","Olsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-167750"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-23","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2017-06-20","title":"Radiocarbon and Diet","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Iron Age","Radiocarbon dating","Stable isotopes","bog bodies","collagen extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Museum Silkeborg"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diet and radiocarbon dating of tollund man new analyses of an iron age bog body from denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/open-access-policies/open-access-journals/green-open-access-policy-for-journals","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/178834594/Diet_and_Radiocarbon_Dating_of_Tollund_Man_New_Analyses_of_an_Iron_Age_Bog_Body_from_Denmark.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-167750","identifier":[{"id":"85057057784","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-436d555e-0eb0-42e6-9540-f66b7ec8bef0"],"keyword":["Iron Age","Tollund Man","bog bodies","collagen extraction","radiocarbon dating","stable isotopes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8F2C5A9D3B31D44D41C822FB698088C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/open-access-policies/open-access-journals/green-open-access-policy-for-journals","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/178834594/Diet_and_Radiocarbon_Dating_of_Tollund_Man_New_Analyses_of_an_Iron_Age_Bog_Body_from_Denmark.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Museum Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Centre for Urban Network Evolutions (UrbNet)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"heltnielsenpau","last":"Helt Nielsen","name":"Helt Nielsen, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"philippsenpau","last":"Philippsen","locid":"5824c0a3-8410-477e-b9a8-8921314d3d70","name":"Philippsen, Bente","orcid":"0000-0001-5732-3570","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"kanstruppau","last":"Kanstrup","locid":"1665c93b-b3ce-4ca7-8480-58c5082dc41b","name":"Kanstrup, Marie","orcid":"0009-0008-4680-3710","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/rdc.2018.127","issn":["00338222","19455755"],"issn_org":["00338222"],"issue":"5","journal":"Radiocarbon","pages":"1533-1545","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Radiocarbon","title_org":"Radiocarbon: An International Journal of Cosmogenic Isotope Research","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057057784"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-436d555e-0eb0-42e6-9540-f66b7ec8bef0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Diet and radiocarbon dating of Tollund Man : New analyses of an Iron Age bog body from Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-167750","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Electron transport within living cells is essential for energy conservation in all respiring and photosynthetic organisms. While a few bacteria transport electrons over micrometer distances to their surroundings, filaments of cable bacteria are hypothesized to conduct electric currents over centimeter distances. We used resonance Raman microscopy to analyze cytochrome redox states in living cable bacteria. Cable-bacteria filaments were placed in microscope chambers with sulfide as electron source and oxygen as electron sink at opposite ends. Along individual filaments a gradient in cytochrome redox potential was detected, which immediately broke down upon removal of oxygen or laser cutting of the filaments. Without access to oxygen, a rapid shift toward more reduced cytochromes was observed, as electrons were no longer drained from the filament but accumulated in the cellular cytochromes. These results provide direct evidence for long-distance electron transport in living multicellular bacteria.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","Boschker, Henricus T. S.","Larsen, Steffen","Berry, David","Schmid, Markus","Millo, Diego","Tataru, Paula","Meysman, Filip J. R.","Wagner, Michael","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Schramm, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180359"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerg, Jesper Jensen"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","University of Antwerp","University of Vienna","VU University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Cable bacteria","Conduction","Currents","Cytochrome c","Electromicrobiology","Marine sediment","Nanowires","REVEAL","Raman spectroscopy","SEA FLOOR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long distance electron transport in individual living cable bacteria","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5984516/pdf/pnas.201800367.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180359","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5984516","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85047914945","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000433283700069","type":"wos"},{"id":"29735671","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-59870c77-620e-401b-9717-608b367f128e"],"keyword":["CURRENTS","CYTOCHROME-C","GEOBACTER-SULFURREDUCENS BIOFILMS","MARINE SEDIMENT","NANOWIRES","REVEAL","Raman spectroscopy","SEA-FLOOR","cable bacteria","conduction","electromicrobiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-06927FF6493C2AD7EF1A8CDE5BEE3528"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5984516/pdf/pnas.201800367.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Electromicrobiology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Geomicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"university of antwerp","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Antwerp","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"vu university amsterdam","lo