:"Caitlin","key":"petropau","last":"Petro","locid":"8b1796d1-08fd-4801-9ab1-eefcc8b45459","name":"Petro, Caitlin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"bøggildpau","last":"Bøggild","locid":"f4ec8733-0cb2-4098-9d7b-797ae34d4875","name":"Bøggild, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0003-2130-3521","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"brokjærpau","last":"Brokjær","locid":"2c041bf0-72b0-4425-a1f1-b2a393a07e79","name":"Brokjær, Signe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b1f70e1-663b-4a12-b10c-a12dfc320c81","name":"Nielsen, Lars Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7269-4860","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e872ab8c-b926-4d7c-98d5-98ceb959e17d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cable bacteria: from single filament taxonomy to clonal enrichments in autoclaved sediment","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-261989","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The design of patient-centred e-health services embodies an inherent tension between the concerns of clinicians and those of patients. Clinicians’ concerns are related to professional issues to do with diagnosing and curing disease in accordance with accepted medical standards. In contrast, patients’ concerns typically relate to personal experience and quality of life issues. It is about their identity, their hopes, their fears and their need to maintain a meaningful life. This divergence of concerns presents a fundamental challenge for designers of patient-centred e-health services. We explore this challenge in the context of chronic illness and telecare. Based on insights from medical phenomenology as well as our own experience with designing an e-health service for patients with chronic heart disease, we emphasise the importance – and difficulty – of aligning the concerns of patients and clinicians. To deal with this, we propose a set of concepts for analysing concerns related to the design of e-health services: A concern is (1) meaningful if it is relevant and makes sense to both patients and clinicians, (2) actionable if clinicians or patients – at least in principle – are able to take appropriate action to deal with it, and (3) feasible if it is easy and convenient to do so within the organisational and social context. We conclude with a call for a more participatory and iterative approach to the design of patient-centred ehealth services.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Tariq Osman","Bansler, Jørgen P.","Kensing, Finn","Moll, Jonas","Monsted, Troels","Nielsen, Karen Dam","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Petersen, Helen Hogh","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394879"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Medical phenomenology","Participatory Design","Patient clinician interaction","Patient provider relationship"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aligning concerns in telecare three concepts to guide the design of patient centred e health","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-018-9309-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394879","identifier":[{"id":"000441232100029","type":"wos"},{"id":"85047114032","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0253ef76-2c22-4c3c-b825-38a175f1f829"],"keyword":["Alignment of concerns","Medical phenomenology","Participatory design","Patient-centred e-health","Patient-clinician interaction","Patient-provider relationship"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85324E44F3C9499EEADD066236691FF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-018-9309-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/202383063/Aligning_Concerns_in_Telecare.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tariq Osman","key":"andersentariqosmanpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"dfc4b3ec-64f4-4e84-92fe-67e3b681c85b","name":"Andersen, Tariq Osman","orcid":"0000-0002-9342-5520","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen Peter","key":"banslerjørgenppau","last":"Bansler","loci