{"abstract":"In this paper, we propose a speech enhancement method based on non-negative matrix factorization (NMF) techniques. NMF techniques allow us to approximate the power spectral density (PSD) of the noisy signal as a weighted linear combination of trained speech and noise basis vectors arranged as the columns of a matrix. In this work, we propose to use basis vectors that are parameterised by autoregressive (AR) coefficients. Parametric representation of the spectral basis is beneficial as it can encompass the signal characteristics like, e.g. the speech production model. It is observed that the parametric representation of basis vectors is beneficial while performing online speech enhancement in low delay scenarios.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kavalekalam, Mathew Shaji","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Shi, Liming","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Boldt, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081705"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-07","place":"Rome, it","start":"2018-09-03","title":"26th European Signal Processing Conference (EUSIPCO 2018)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"online parametric nmf for speech enhancement","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/300257539/eusipco_2018_paper_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081705","identifier":[{"id":"85059822235","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6cda013d-9d5e-4693-aaca-9a9a90d92b54"],"keyword":["autoregressive modelling, speech enhancement, NMF"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E8306CA087700C6340395896B0E71E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/300257539/eusipco_2018_paper_2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["GN Hearing A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathew Shaji","key":"kavalekalampau","last":"Kavalekalam","locid":"6082dcd3-6e02-459e-8b51-2ac06555e654","name":"Kavalekalam, Mathew Shaji","orcid":"0000-0003-3124-3008","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liming","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","locid":"e44b1378-1291-46be-b76a-fd0e196e2d46","name":"Shi, Liming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"boldtpau","last":"Boldt","name":"Boldt, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eusipco.2018.8553039","eisbn":["9789082797015"],"isbn":["9789082797008"],"issn":["20761465"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Proceedings of the European Signal Processing Conference","status":"p","title":"2018 26th European Signal Processing Conference (EUSIPCO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059822235"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","gn hearing a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6cda013d-9d5e-4693-aaca-9a9a90d92b54"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Online Parametric NMF for Speech Enhancement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081705","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate if attention to additional sensory information from the fingertip can improve postural stability during pain, which is known to impair balance. Methods: In 16 healthy volunteers, experimental pain was induced by intramuscular injection of hypertonic saline in the right vastus medialis muscle (isotonic saline used as nonpainful control, intramuscular injection in the same location). Pain intensity was assessed on an 11-point numeric rating scale (NRS; 0 representing \"no pain\" and 10 \"maximum pain\"). Subjects were asked to stand as still as possible on a force plate for 40 seconds with their eyes closed. Their postural stability was quantified by the area and velocity of center of pressure (CoP) displacement. The CoP was recorded with and without pain during two different conditions: 1) no touch and 2) the subjects were asked to lightly touch a curtain with their right index finger and focus their attention on keeping it as still as possible. Results: Hypertonic injections induced higher NRS scores compared with control injections (P < 0.05). During the hypertonic injection condition, the CoP area and velocity in both directions increased during no touch compared with the light touch condition (P < 0.05). No differences were found during light touch between the hypertonic and isotonic injection conditions. Although experimental knee-related pain impaired postural stability, lightly touching a curtain with the fingertip decreased postural sway during painful conditions. Conclusions: Providing additional sensory information while pain patients are performing balance exercises may improve postural stability and increase the quality of exercise, consequent rehabilitation protocols, and clinical outcomes.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","Christensen, Steffan Wittrup McPhee","Agger, Simone May","Gammelgaard, Mikkel Svindt","Røssner, Nicklas","Abildgaard, Jesper","Vuillerme, Nicolas","Graven-Nielsen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116019"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université Grenoble Alpes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"light touch contact improves pain evoked postural instability during quiet standing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/300160912/Light_touch_contact_improves_pain_evoked_postural_instability_during_quiet_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-116019","identifier":[{"id":"29481664","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000454336200017","type":"wos"},{"id":"85059255125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e2ef5609-f5a5-4fc8-a0e3-691e36881f51"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B1C8C47632DF7D3A8514F589A8B842E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/300160912/Light_touch_contact_improves_pain_evoked_postural_instability_during_quiet_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Pain and Motor System Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université grenoble alpes","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Grenoble Alpes","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rogerio P.","key":"hiratapau","last":"Hirata","locid":"a8f714d2-931d-4b16-a957-38bd1b321fe6","name":"Hirata, Rogerio Pessoto","name_org":"Hirata, Rogerio P.","orcid":"0000-0002-9943-2713","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffan W.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3b61b688-fcef-4e25-9a7b-c7aae536ec84","name":"Christensen, Steffan Wittrup McPhee","name_org":"Christensen, Steffan W.","orcid":"0000-0001-9068-0641","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simone","key":"aggerpau","last":"Agger","locid":"e2c77f5d-9cc3-4284-aec8-fb2572ce394b","name":"Agger, Simone May","name_org":"Agger, Simone","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"svindtpau","last":"Svindt","locid":"77f916a8-8732-48c0-90c0-64a717ae5abe","name":"Gammelgaard, Mikkel Svindt","name_org":"Svindt, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicklas","key":"røssnerpau","last":"Røssner","locid":"0e5fdda0-90f7-4292-ae06-0d89e558e8b7","name":"Røssner, Nicklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"abildgaardpau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"cb8a713f-011e-4f61-a11a-0cba06139e75","name":"Abildgaard, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolas","key":"vuillermepau","last":"Vuillerme","name":"Vuillerme, Nicolas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"gravennielsenpau","last":"Graven-Nielsen","locid":"474a635b-4e83-4b02-a90b-80d417d37e52","name":"Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7787-4860","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29481664"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/pm/pny015","issn":["15262375","15264637"],"issn_org":["15262375"],"issue":"12","journal":"Pain Medicine","pages":"2487-2495","publisher":"VICER Publishing","status":"p","title":"Pain Medicine","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059255125"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e2ef5609-f5a5-4fc8-a0e3-691e36881f51"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Light touch contact improves pain-evoked postural instability during quiet standing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-116019","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT) is an established treatment in patients with heart failure and prolonged QRS duration where a biventricular pacemaker is implanted to achieve faster activation and more synchronous contraction of the left ventricle (LV). Despite the convincing effect of CRT, 30-40% of patients do not respond. Among the most important correctable causes of non-response to CRT is non-optimal LV lead position. METHODS: We will enroll 122 patients in this patient-blinded and assessor-blinded, randomized, clinical trial aiming to investigate if implanting the LV lead guided by electrical mapping towards the latest LV activation as compared with imaging-guided implantation, causes an excess increase in left ventricular (LV) ejection fraction (LVEF). The patients are randomly assigned to either the intervention group: preceded by cardiac computed tomography of the cardiac venous anatomy, the LV lead is placed according to the latest LV activation in the coronary sinus (CS) branches identified by systematic electrical mapping of the CS at implantation and post-implant optimization of the interventricular pacing delay; or patients are assigned to the control group: placement of the LV lead guided by cardiac imaging. The LV lead is targeted towards the latest mechanical LV activation as identified by echocardiography and outside myocardial scar as identified by myocardial perfusion (MP) imaging. The primary endpoint is change in LVEF at 6-month follow up (6MFU) as compared with baseline measured by two-dimensional echocardiography. Secondary endpoints include relative percentage reduction in LV end-systolic volume, all-cause mortality, hospitalization for heart failure, and a clinical combined endpoint of response to CRT at 6MFU defined as the patient being alive, not hospitalized for heart failure, and experiencing improvement in NYHA functional class or/and > 10% increase in 6-minute walk test. DISCUSSION: We assume an absolute increase in LVEF of 12% in the intervention group versus 8% in the control group. If an excess increase in LVEF can be achieved by LV lead implantation guided by electrical mapping, this study supports the conduct of larger trials investigating the impact of this strategy for LV-lead implantation on clinical outcomes in patients treated with CRT. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT02346097 . Registered on 12 January 2015. Patients were enrolled between 16 February 2015 and 13 December 2017.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stephansen, Charlotte","Sommer, Anders","Kronborg, Mads Brix","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Bouchelouche, Kirsten","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130115"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CRT","Cardiac imaging","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Electrical mapping","Heart failure","LVEF","Left ventricular ejection fraction","Left ventricular lead placement","QLV"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrically guided versus imaging guided implant of the left ventricular lead in cardiac resynchronization therapy a study protocol for a double blinded randomized controlled clinical trial electrocrt","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85065349402","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130115","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6211399","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85065349402","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30382923","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0179b952-5cd4-419c-af67-79862c1eb86b"],"keyword":["CRT","Cardiac imaging","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Electrical mapping","Heart failure","LVEF","Left ventricular ejection fraction","Left ventricular lead placement","QLV"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6ABDEA6648E6F71500AC234B7920CA7B"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"stephansenpau","last":"Stephansen","locid":"bc398e00-bb58-4ef9-b28a-70f693ee6928","name":"Stephansen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3272-2115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"sommerpau","last":"Sommer","locid":"fa8add57-7165-4648-a1ef-fc71d826c899","name":"Sommer, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Brix","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"76c15c18-4786-4b38-93b3-91afbc1ea875","name":"Kronborg, Mads Brix","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"bouchelouchepau","last":"Bouchelouche","locid":"f253980f-a953-448a-bdfb-2a0fcfe82101","name":"Bouchelouche, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30382923"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-018-2930-y","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["14686708"],"issue":"1","journal":"Trials","pages":"600","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","title_org":"Current Controlled Trials in Cardiovascular Medicine (Print)","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065349402"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0179b952-5cd4-419c-af67-79862c1eb86b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Electrically guided versus imaging-guided implant of the left ventricular lead in cardiac resynchronization therapy : a study protocol for a double-blinded randomized controlled clinical trial (ElectroCRT)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-130115","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Electrochemical enzyme-linked sandwich assays on magnetic beads (MBs) refer to one of the most sensitive approaches for analysis of nonamplified nucleic acid samples, with redox enzymes being routinely used as labels. Here, we report a sensitive and inexpensive electrochemical nucleic acid sandwich assay on MBs that exploits a hydrolytic enzyme cellulase as a label, while MBs are used for preconcentration and bioseparation of analyzed samples. Binding of target DNA or RNA to capture DNA-modified MB triggers sandwich assembly and its labeling with cellulase. Application of the assembled sandwich to the electrodes covered with insulating nitrocellulose films induces film digestion by the cellulase label and pronounced changes in the electrical properties of the electrodes, the extent of the changes being proportional to the concentration of the analyzed nucleic acids. Down to 1 amol of Lactobacillus brevis specific synthetic DNA and rRNA isolated from L. brevis cells could be detected in 1 mL samples in the overall from 2 to 3 h assay. The assay is universal and can be adapted for point-of-care-testing and for in-field environmental and microbiomic analysis of unamplified samples of any DNA/RNA sequences.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fapyane, Deby","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Ferapontova, Elena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183764"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ferapontova, Elena"],"keyword":["Amplification","Biosensors","Cellulase","Electrochemical analysis","Hybridization","LAYERS","Magnetic beads","Nucleic acid detection","Nucleic acids","Pathogens","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Surface","Transduction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrochemical enzyme linked sandwich assay with a cellulase label for ultrasensitive analysis of synthetic dna and cell isolated rna","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055109274","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-183764","identifier":[{"id":"000449030300011","type":"wos"},{"id":"30257555","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055109274","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5f685614-39c0-47ef-8d69-a654851f310a"],"keyword":["AMPLIFICATION","BIOSENSORS","COPIES","HYBRIDIZATION","LAYERS","NUCLEIC-ACIDS","PATHOGENS","POLYMERASE-CHAIN-REACTION","SURFACE","TRANSDUCTION","cellulase","electrochemical analysis","enzyme-linked sandwich assay","magnetic beads","nucleic acid detection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F40E885974F9BD9AC194AE20A6E3D98"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Deby","key":"fapyanepau","last":"Fapyane","locid":"8233b882-29ff-4afc-8f0b-39fb2cb1cbbd","name":"Fapyane, Deby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elena E.","key":"ferapontovapau","last":"Ferapontova","locid":"fb776e85-d3fe-451d-ba01-40d092a0e54c","name":"Ferapontova, Elena","name_org":"Ferapontova, Elena E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30257555"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acssensors.8b00662","issn":["23793694"],"issue":"10","journal":"ACS Sensors","pages":"2104-2111","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Sensors","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055109274"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5f685614-39c0-47ef-8d69-a654851f310a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Electrochemical Enzyme-Linked Sandwich Assay with a Cellulase Label for Ultrasensitive Analysis of Synthetic DNA and Cell-Isolated RNA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183764","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Air pollutant levels over Denmark are simulated using the high resolution THOR model system for the years 1979–2015. The system employs the Danish Eulerian Hemispheric Model (DEHM), coupled to the Urban Background Model (UBM) that covers the whole of Denmark on a 1 km spatial resolution. This study evaluates the performance of the model system in simulating hourly, daily, monthly and yearly mean ozone (O 3), nitrogen oxides (NOx) and particulate matter (PM 10 and PM 2.5) concentrations using surface measurements from eight Danish monitoring stations between 1990 and 2015. The spatial and temporal variability of air pollutants and emissions are also investigated to better understand the air pollution trends over Denmark during this 37 year period.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Im, Ulas","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Ketzel, Matthias","Ellermann, Thomas","Geels, Camilla","Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","Hertel, Ole","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Brandt, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-229560"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Integrated modelling","Model evaluation","Ozone","Particulate matter","TRENDS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollutant trends over denmark over the last 000000000037 years as simulated by the integrated thor model system","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85060484901","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-229560","identifier":[{"id":"85060484901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-afaf98aa-9b94-40a0-a70a-68c69134ed1a"],"keyword":["Integrated modelling","Model evaluation","Ozone","Particulate matter","Trends"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28AFA6E38FA710756027BE622EFF284D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"ellermannpau","last":"Ellermann","locid":"5e5a2168-23db-4863-b6d5-bda7dcb1f662","name":"Ellermann, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj Mantzius","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"85f79280-93e9-4d5f-aaec-c245958a6b24","name":"Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","locid":"6a33f2b3-9140-4f59-a55e-e68a73c9fa32","name":"Hertel, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-0972-7735","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole-Kenneth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marlene Schmidt","key":"plejdruppau","last":"Plejdrup","locid":"9dede80b-ff3e-4171-9504-bf8547fec74d","name":"Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-57645-9_8","eisbn":["9783319576459"],"isbn":["9783319576442"],"pages":"49-54","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Springer Proceedings in Complexity"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060484901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-afaf98aa-9b94-40a0-a70a-68c69134ed1a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Air Pollutant Trends over Denmark over the Last 37 Years as Simulated by the Integrated THOR Model System","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-229560","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Keratoconus (KC) is the most common ectatic corneal disease, with clinical findings that include discomfort, visual disturbance and possible blindness if left untreated. KC affects approximately 1:400 to 1:2000 people worldwide, including both males and females. The aetiology and onset of KC remains a puzzle and as a result, the ability to treat or reverse the disease is hampered. Sex hormones are known to play a role in the maintenance of the structure and integrity of the human cornea. Hormone levels have been reported to alter corneal thickness, curvature, and sensitivity during different times of menstrual cycle. Surprisingly, the role of sex hormones in corneal diseases and KC has been largely neglected. Prolactin-induced protein, known to be regulated by sex hormones, is a new KC biomarker that has been recently proposed. Studies herein discuss the role of sex hormones as a control mechanism for KC onset and progression and evidence supporting the view that prolactin-induced protein is an important hormonally regulated biomarker in KC is discussed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sharif, Rabab","Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","Hjortdal, Jesper","Karamichos, Dimitrios"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238530"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oklahoma"],"keyword":["Human cornea","Keratoconus","Sex hormones"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pathogenesis of keratoconus the intriguing therapeutic potential of prolactin inducible protein","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6235698/pdf/nihms-989018.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-238530","identifier":[{"id":"85049757536","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6235698","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29758268","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bf63e3a2-c800-4795-a2fc-dddc0ea4a7d9"],"keyword":["Bodily fluids","Human cornea","Keratoconus","Prolactin-induced protein","Sex hormones"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7708B8C3ECF5F32967E57828591FB32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6235698/pdf/nihms-989018.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rabab","key":"sharifpau","last":"Sharif","name":"Sharif, Rabab","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sashia","key":"baknielsenpau","last":"Bak-Nielsen","locid":"4d778acb-8da2-45ce-a916-232721f4c529","name":"Bak-Nielsen, Sashia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dimitrios","key":"karamichospau","last":"Karamichos","name":"Karamichos, Dimitrios","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29758268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.preteyeres.2018.05.002","issn":["13509462","18731635"],"issn_org":["13509462"],"journal":"Progress in Retinal and Eye Research","pages":"150-167","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Progress in Retinal and Eye Research","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049757536"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bf63e3a2-c800-4795-a2fc-dddc0ea4a7d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pathogenesis of Keratoconus : The intriguing therapeutic potential of Prolactin-inducible protein","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-238530","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
