Tang Nielsen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"omerzupedh","last":"Omerzu","name":"Omerzu, Heike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783161554391"],"issn":["05121604"],"pages":"235-251","place":"Tübingen","publisher":"Mohr Siebeck","series":"Wissenschaftliche Untersuchungen zum Neuen Testament","status":"p","title":"Rewriting and Reception in and of the Bible"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f173b8a3-055c-48a1-bb23-842fc29a9e7f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Das Petrusevangelium als ›rewritten Gospel‹? : Eine forschungsgeschichtliche Erörterung der Rezeption der Kategorie ›rewritten Bible‹ in Bezug auf frühchristliche Texte","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-537504","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist","Nielsen, Jesper G.","Rasmussen, Anders Juhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-540551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rejsen til ribe peter seebergs romaner noveller og kortprosa","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-540551","ids":["ku-f677a746-f866-4cc7-a3b0-8cfab5a4c352"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6428FD19A31A661C33C1BAA6A4CAD446"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Lindquist","key":"barnwellped","last":"Barnwell","locid":"50916516-bf5a-460e-94b1-77cf4f11c535","name":"Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist","orcid":"0009-0001-8395-1818","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper G.","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper G.","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenped","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e1188ff-4cc9-42e2-86b3-59515e62f1af","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788702250497"],"pages":"236","place":"København","publisher":"Gyldendal","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f677a746-f866-4cc7-a3b0-8cfab5a4c352"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rejsen til Ribe : Peter Seebergs romaner, noveller og kortprosa","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-540551","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: A session of motor skill learning is accompanied by transient increases in corticospinal excitability (CSE), which are thought to reflect acute changes in neuronal connectivity associated with improvements in sensorimotor performance. Factors influencing changes in excitability and motor skill with continued practice remain however to be elucidated. Objective/Hypothesis: Here we investigate the hypothesis that progressive motor practice during consecutive days can induce repeated transient increases in corticospinal excitability and promote motor skill learning. Methods: Changes in motor performance and CSE were assessed during 4 consecutive days of skill learning and 8 days after the last practice session. CSE was assessed as area under recruitment curves (RC) using transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS). Two groups of participants (n = 12) practiced a visuomotor tracking-task with task difficulty progressively increased with individual proficiency (PPG) or with the same task level throughout all 4 days (NPPG). Results: Progressive practice resulted in superior motor learning compared to NPPG (p < 0.001). Whereas NPPG displayed increased CSE following only the first day of practice (p < 0.001), progressive motor practice was accompanied by increases in CSE on both the first and the final session of motor practice (p = 0.006). Eight days after ended practice, the groups showed similar CSE, but PPG maintained superior performance at a skilled task level and transfer task performance (p < 0.005, p = 0.029). Conclusion: The results demonstrate that progressive practice promotes both motor learning and repeated increases in CSE across multiple days. While changes in CSE did not relate to learning our results suggest that they signify successful training. Progressive practice is thus important for optimizing neurorehabilitation and motor practice protocols in general.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christiansen, Lasse","Madsen, Mads Alexander Just","Bojsen-Møller, Emil","Thomas, Richard","Nielsen, Jens Bo","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544278"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Corticospinal excitability","Faculty of Science","Learning","Plasticity","TMS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"progressive practice promotes motor learning and repeated transient increases in corticospinal excitability across multiple days","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-544278","identifier":[{"id":"29187320","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85035077416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fcba6093-8f7e-4b6c-9377-d70edcfff485"],"keyword":["Corticospinal excitability","Faculty of Science","Learning","Plasticity","TMS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E4B408167CA8D79A6A02A8E0D12EFCA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Motor Control","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Neural Control of Movement"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bb3cbbb6-5540-42a7-8bdb-b9ded2314867","name":"Christiansen, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-9316-1529","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Alexander Just","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"52f2a2a8-b89b-43a9-b868-cafb803ed7ba","name":"Madsen, Mads Alexander Just","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emil","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"7892be7c-df9f-4143-9793-f2559a7b0dea","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Richard","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","locid":"12553647-094e-422c-81e2-e8e932fc659f","name":"Thomas, Richard","orcid":"0000-0002-8745-7462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29187320"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.brs.2017.11.005","issn":["18764754","1935861X"],"issn_org":["1935861X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Brain Stimulation","pages":"346-357","status":"p","title":"Brain Stimulation","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85035077416"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fcba6093-8f7e-4b6c-9377-d70edcfff485"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Progressive practice promotes motor learning and repeated transient increases in corticospinal excitability across multiple days","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-544278","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, a simple digital model-based implementation of a carrier-based pulse width modulation (PWM) strategy is Prasented. The strategy is used to operate a 10 kW hybrid three-level three-phase voltage source PWM inverter (VSI). The topology of the VSI is active neutral point-clamped (ANPC). This hybrid inverter consists of silicon (Si) power MOSFETs and Gallium-Nitride (GaN) FETs. Since the Gan FETs are switching at high frequency for the power level (100 kHz for 10 kW), the PWM digital implementation has to be fast and accurate to avoid shoot-through issue in the inverter. Therefore, a field programmable gate array (FPGA) is used for that purpose. The digital model is designed using MATLAB/Simulink and Xilinx's System Generator. Finally, a 10 k W three-level three-phase hybrid ANPC is designed using two GaN-FETs and 4 Si MOSFETs for each leg. The carrier-based PWM is implemented in the FPGA of a micro-lab box from dSPACE. The experimental results show the performance of the 10 kW hybrid ANPC at 100 kHz of switching with different load conditions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kapino, Giorgo","Kouchaki, Alireza","Nielsen, Jesper","Nymand, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-573899"],"event":{"end":"2018-04-12","place":"Doha, qa","start":"2018-04-10","title":"12th IEEE International Conference on Compatibility, Power Electronics and Power Engineering, CPE-POWERENG 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ANPC","GaN FET","Multilevel inverter","Si MOSFET"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple digital model based design and implementation of carrier based pwm for high frequency hybrid 000000000003 l active npc inverter","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85048886606","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-573899","identifier":[{"id":"85048886606","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-025fec96-07ce-4a38-a57f-6f874b94273f"],"keyword":["ANPC","GaN FET","Hybrid topology","Model based digital implementation","Multilevel inverter","Si MOSFET"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F8E114207F7BFF3E3042590B7BCB80B8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giorgo","key":"kapinopau","last":"Kapino","name":"Kapino, Giorgo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alireza","key":"kouchakipau","last":"Kouchaki","locid":"b54c567b-3cea-4cad-adc8-0e5e067029d8","name":"Kouchaki, Alireza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a2c86e37-f396-4b5e-9e63-19af9641cc04","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1469-7684","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"nymandpau","last":"Nymand","locid":"3f0c9441-e312-42bb-bb24-490c2ab76c9d","name":"Nymand, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-1470-5621","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cpe.2018.8372519","eisbn":["9781538625088","9781538625071"],"isbn":["9781538625095"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2018 IEEE 12th International Conference on Compatibility, Power Electronics and Power Engineering, CPE-POWERENG 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048886606"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-025fec96-07ce-4a38-a57f-6f874b94273f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Simple digital model-based design and implementation of carrier-based PWM for high frequency hybrid 3-L active NPC inverter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-573899","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Type 2 diabetes (T2D) is on the rise among young adults (aged 20-39 years). A challenge for health risk communication is that young adults may not be aware or lack acknowledgement of their personal risk of developing T2D. To date, no knowledge is available on potential relationships between personality traits and T2D risk perception in this target group. This cross-sectional study aimed to investigate direct and indirect (mediated via health-related behaviours and body mass index) associations between the Five-Factor Model personality traits and T2D risk perception among university students in Denmark. METHODS: Participants included 1205 students (80% females; mean age = 25) from five major universities. All variables were assessed by means of self-report in an online questionnaire. Health-related behaviours included physical activity, sweets consumption and prior T2D screening. Covariates included socio-demographic factors and family history of T2D. RESULTS: A hierarchical multiple regression analysis revealed that higher levels of conscientiousness and emotional stability were directly negatively associated with T2D risk perception after controlling for covariates, health-related behaviours, and body mass index. Binary logistic regression analyses showed several significant associations between personality traits and health-related behaviours as well as body mass index. Sobel tests indicated that both physical activity and body mass index partially mediated the association between conscientiousness and T2D risk perception. The association between extraversion and T2D risk perception was fully mediated by PA. CONCLUSIONS: We present novel evidence suggesting that personality traits, health-related behaviours and body mass index are associated with T2D risk perception among young adults. Thus, it may be beneficial to tailor health risk communications targeting T2D to match recipients' personality characteristics instead of using the one size fits all approach.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Skøt, Lotte","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Leppin, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606139"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Five factor model","Health communication","Health related behaviours","Personality traits","Risk perception","Students","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"who perceives a higher personal risk of developing type 000000000002 diabetes a cross sectional study on associations between personality traits health related behaviours and perceptions of susceptibility among university students in denmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-018-5884-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606139","identifier":[{"id":"30075710","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6076414","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85051117791","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7311aa20-b766-4d1d-a725-638b091f041e"],"keyword":["Five-factor model","Health communication","Health-related behaviours","Personality traits","Risk perception","Students","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3004B770D9358A18AC4E1EEA85D6B105"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/143630265/Who_perceives_a_higher_personal_risk_of_developing_type_2_diabetes.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-018-5884-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu universit