ding":null,"first":"Ann Sophia","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","name":"Bertelsen, Ann Sophia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","name":"Ryg, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b004b8b4-3e62-4425-829c-7936423fc3d5","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01974572","15283984"],"issn_org":["01974572"],"journal":"Geriatric Nursing","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Geriatric Nursing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-c91fe659-20ac-46ed-9447-5acc7308aa78"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Perspectives from patients attending a Falls Clinic – A qualitative study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649293","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The two key purposes of assessment, formative and summative, often contradict each other when attempted used simultaneously. Summative assessment of learning will generally prevent formative assessment for learning. Moreover, in order to be useful and manageable, the assessment method must be easy to integrate into and should ordinary teaching. This study explores how such an assessment method, called the Structured Assessment Dialogue (SAD), could be designed and the rationale behind it. Then the study investigates the challenges and benefits perceived by teachers related to the uptake of SAD in their daily practice. The SADs were undertaking in science, technology and mathematics in primary and secondary schools in Denmark and Finland. The data used in this study include teacher-generated preparation and reflections forms, interviews with teachers,and an open-ended questionnaire.Our findings suggest that SAD holds prospects for fulfilling the purposes for both formative and summative assessment, with the highest prospects related to formative assessment purposes and characteristics. However, it needs time, change of classroom culture, and adjustments and careful implementation and routine building. In addition, teachers must be proficient in addressing the different aspects and levels of competences throughout the SAD.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Sanne Schnell","Dolin, Jens","Bruun, Jesper","Jensen, Sofie Birch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760303"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-25","start":"2017-08-21","title":"ESERA","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the design and implementation of an assessment method combining formative and summative use of assessment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/212903242/Part_11_eBook.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-760303","ids":["ku-bbadfec2-5b78-432c-83b2-ae719c64b594"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D441B562981F632B92B4B71CDA802646"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/212903242/Part_11_eBook.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Assessment, Teaching and Learning in Science Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sanne Schnell","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e2e58218-933a-44d8-af1f-cbcda52d8d1b","name":"Nielsen, Sanne Schnell","orcid":"0000-0002-9981-8288","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"dolinpau","last":"Dolin","locid":"76d1971b-6d64-4bce-b4dc-6af9cd79f81f","name":"Dolin, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1604-1846","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"d2218073-20b7-41ac-aa88-f7c4bc9fff74","name":"Bruun, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-4739-7351","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sofie Birch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Sofie Birch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1468-1479","series":"ESERA Conference Proceedings series","status":"p","title":"Evaluation and assessment of student learning and development: Part 11, Strand 11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bbadfec2-5b78-432c-83b2-ae719c64b594"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Design and Implementation of an Assessment Method Combining Formative and Summative Use of Assessment","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760303","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE Nasal continuous positive airway pressure (nCPAP) is a well-established treatment of respiratory distress syndrome in preterm infants. Suboptimal weaning from nCPAP may be associated with lung injury, pulmonary morbidity, and infant weight gain. To our knowledge, the best weaning strategy from nCPAP is unknown. OBJECTIVE To compare the effect of sudden wean and pressure wean from nCPAP in very preterm infants. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS A randomized, clinical, open-label, multicenter trial was conducted at 6 neonatal intensive care units in Denmark from September 2012 to December 2016 and included infants born before 32 weeks of gestation. INTERVENTIONS Sudden wean with discontinuation of nCPAP without a prior reduction in pressure. Pressure wean with gradual pressure reduction prior to the discontinuation of nCPAP. MAIN OUTCOME AND MEASURES The primary outcome was weight gain velocity from randomization to postmenstrual age 40 weeks. Secondary outcomes included other measures of growth, nCPAP and the duration of oxygen supplementation, postmenstrual age at successful wean and at discharge, successful wean at the first attempt, the number of attempts to wean, and the length of the hospital stay. Prespecified subgroup analyses by gestational age were performed. RESULTS Of the 372 randomized infants, 185 (49.7%) were randomized to sudden wean and 187 infants (50.3%) to pressure wean. A total of 177 infants in both groups completed the trial (median gestational age for sudden and pressure wean, 30 weeks [interquartile range, 29-31]; male: sudden wean, 89 [50%]; pressure wean, 96 [54%]). There was no difference in mean [SD] weight gain velocity from randomization to 40 weeks postmenstrual age between the 2 groups (22 [6] g/kg/day). No difference was found in any of the secondary outcomes. More infants born before 28 weeks of gestation were successfully weaned from nCPAP during the first attempt in the pressure wean group compared with the sudden wean group (risk difference, 31%; 95% CI, 13%-50%), but there was no difference in the duration of nCPAP and oxygen supplementation. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE Overall, we found no difference in weight gain velocity or any of the secondary outcomes between very preterm infants who were randomized to sudden wean or pressure wean from nCPAP. However, among infants born before 28 weeks' gestation, infants from the pressure wean group were more often successfully weaned during the first attempt without a longer total duration of nCPAP treatment.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jensen, Christina Friis","Sellmer, Anna","Ebbesen, Finn","Cipliene, Rasa","Johansen, Anders","Hansen, Rikke Monrad","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Nikitina, Olga Hogreffe","Petersen, Jesper Padkær","Henriksen, Tine Brink"],"cuid":["S02-099.85-011857"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Department of Pediatrics, Randers Regional Hospital, Randers, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sudden vs pressure wean from nasal continuous positive airway pressure in infants born before 000000000032 weeks of gestation a randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6143058/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.85-011857","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6143058","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85053010348","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30039171","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f847262b-0d5f-4144-a3b6-f02e168276ea","au-fa6f9724-7307-429b-a665-360f1e38d293"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5F766069B4245E1DE482D1D872696D0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6143058/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Perinatal epidemiologi, SKS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Paediatrics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Pediatrics, Randers Regional Hospital, Randers, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Friis","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"522abbc1-cb9a-4667-ab9b-7fd302e0eb8c","name":"Jensen, Christina Friis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"sellmerpau","last":"Sellmer","locid":"ba41341a-0df8-4154-a4c6-1b21e7f8997e","name":"Sellmer, Anna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Finn","key":"ebbesenpau","last":"Ebbesen","locid":"463d052f-dffa-449f-b5ba-1b21a1a1db02","name":"Ebbesen, Finn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasa","key":"ciplienepau","last":"Cipliene","locid":"186b6598-7fb9-45ce-94f2-7a358bf8f62f","name":"Cipliene, Rasa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Monrad","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Rikke Monrad","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e46d68f5-1ae6-4bd4-ac17-54bd5692acc2","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga Hogreffe","key":"nikitinapau","last":"Nikitina","name":"Nikitina, Olga Hogreffe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Padkær","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"80bcc09f-cd7e-4313-a2ef-37d827f3c24b","name":"Petersen, Jesper Padkær","orcid":"0000-0002-4071-0416","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Brink","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"1fbd1982-a1cb-4687-9250-60b91463b802","name":"Henriksen, Tine Brink","orcid":"0000-0001-6933-8294","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30039171"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamapediatrics.2018.2074","issn":["21686203","21686211"],"issn_org":["10724710"],"issue":"9","journal":"JAMA Pediatrics","pages":"824-831","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Pediatrics","volume":"172"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053010348"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f847262b-0d5f-4144-a3b6-f02e168276ea","au-fa6f9724-7307-429b-a665-360f1e38d293"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Sudden vs Pressure Wean From Nasal Continuous Positive Airway Pressure in Infants Born Before 32 Weeks of Gestation : A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.85-011857","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Exaggerated itch responses to pruritic chemical provocations and mechanical stimuli are evident in patients with chronic itch, for example, in atopic dermatitis. Currently used human models of itch do not account for such itch sensitization features, and the mechanisms underlying clinical itch sensitization are unknown. This study utilized two established human models of cutaneous nociceptive sensitization to explore how pre-established inflammatory hyperalgesia (ultraviolet-B-irradiation; \"UVB\") and non-inflammatory neurotrophic pain sensitization (nerve growth factor; \"NGF\") alter sensitivity to chemical and mechanically evoked itch. Twenty healthy volunteers participated in the UVB experiment. Six volar forearm areas (2 cm diameter) were UVB irradiated with ≤2 × minimal erythemal dose, and two non-irradiated areas were used as controls. Sixteen healthy volunteers participated in the NGF experiment and had 2 μg intradermally injected (4 × 50 μL in 2 cm diameter areas) into both volar forearms. Isotonic saline was applied as control. Pain sensitivity measurements (mechanical and heat pain thresholds) were conducted to validate the models. Subsequently, itch was evoked using histamine and cowhage spicules in the sensitized skin areas, and itch/pain was rated using visual analogue scales. Mechanical hyperknesis (increased itch to punctuate stimuli) was probed with von Frey filaments before/after each itch provocation. Both UVB- and NGF models induced robust primary mechanical hyperalgesia (P < .01) and hyperknesis (P < .05). Neither of the models augmented itch in response to chemical itch provocations but significant increases specifically for pain ratings were observed for both histamine and cowhage (P < .05). This suggests that these models are of limited value as proxies for itch sensitization to pruritogens observed, e.g., in inflammatory dermatoses.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Hjalte Holm","Lo Vecchio, Silvia","Elberling, Jesper","Yosipovitch, Gil","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-005593"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Miami"],"keyword":["Inflammation","Itch","Nerve Growth Factor","itch sensitization","pruriception"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uvb and ngf induced cutaneous sensitization in humans selectively augments cowhage and histamine induced pain and evokes mechanical hyperknesis","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85043342049&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-005593","identifier":[{"id":"85043342049","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29406574","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-734a87f7-0f63-404d-8fc3-38656af33d04","ku-5ca65aff-21b8-417d-8c86-9f18d02f20fa"],"keyword":["inflammation","itch","itch sensitization","nerve growth factor","pruriception"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3A353AD0689B745977F6468E5F5EBA51"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Pain and Motor System Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of miami","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Miami","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hjalte Holm","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5de532a5-1602-416c-96b7-20a316e28e25","name":"Andersen, Hjalte Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gil","key":"yosipovitchpau","last":"Yosipovitch","name":"Yosipovitch, Gil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29406574"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/exd.13508","issn":["09066705","14791250"],"issn_org":["09066705"],"issue":"3","journal":"Experimental Dermatology","pages":"258-267","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Experimental Dermatology","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043342049"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-734a87f7-0f63-404d-8fc3-38656af33d04","ku-5ca65aff-21b8-417d-8c86-9f18d02f20fa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"UVB- and NGF-induced cutaneous sensitization in humans selectively augments cowhage- and histamine-induced pain and evokes mechanical hyperknesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-005593","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Most of the subjects undergoing diagnostic colonoscopy do not have neoplastic bowel lesions. Potentially, some of the symptoms may therefore be caused by extracolonic malignancy, and subjects with persisting symptoms may need subsequent examinations. Blood-based, cancer-associated biomarkers may aid in directing the examinations for other specific malignant diseases. Methods: EDTA plasma samples available from a previous prospective study of subjects undergoing diagnostic colonoscopy were used for analysis of 18 protein biomarkers. The study population of 3732 subjects included 400 patients with colorectal cancer (CRC) and 177 patients with extracolonic malignancies. Univariable analysis of the association of specific biomarkers and extracolonic cancers included those with 10 or more cases. Subsequently, reduced models of 4 or 6 biomarkers, respectively, were established by choosing those with the highest likelihood; age and sex were included as well. Results: Univariable analyses showed that CyFra21-1 had an area under curve (AUC) of 0.87 for lung cancers (n = 33), CA19-9 had an AUC of 0.85 for pancreatic cancer (n = 22), CA125 had an AUC of 0.95 for ovary cancer (n = 16), B2M had an AUC of 0.81 for non-Hodgkin lymphoma (n = 12), and total prostate-specific antigen had an AUC of 0.99 for prostate cancer (n = 10). The multivariable analysis of 4 or 6 biomarkers plus age and sex as explanatory variables showed AUCs of 0.82 to 0.85 both for extracolonic cancers and CRC. The 4 biomarkers included in the model for detection of extracolonic cancers were CA125, hsCRP, CA19-9, and CyFra21-1; the 2 additional for the 6 biomarkers model were CEA and Galectin-3. Similarly, the 4 biomarkers included in the model for detection of CRC were CEA, CyFra21-1, Ferritin, and HE4; the two additional for the 6 biomarkers model were hsCRP and Pepsinogen 2. Conclusions: Results of this study indicate that it may be possible to detect subjects that have an increased risk of extracolonic cancer following a colonoscopy without findings of neoplastic lesions. Combinations of various protein biomarkers may direct subsequent examination after colonoscopy with clean colorectum. The results, although preliminary, may form the basis for additional research directed both for primary examinations of subjects with symptoms of malignancy and subsequent examinations after colonoscopy.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Wilhelmsen, Michael","Christensen, Ib J","Jørgensen, Lars N","Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","Vilandt, Jesper","Hillig, Thore","Klærke, Michael","Nielsen, Knud T","Laurberg, Søren","Gawel, Susan","Yang, Xiaoping","Davis, Gerard","Heijboer, Anne Meike","Martens, Frans","Nielsen, Hans J"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-017501"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Diagnostics","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clean colorectum at diagnostic colonoscopy subsequent detection of extracolonic malignancies by plasma protein biomarkers","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1179299X18776974","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-017501","identifier":[{"id":"29872358","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5977429","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-42365e32-fe91-47fd-9c92-97e240973380","ku-cc07ad76-0748-4f9b-a209-018e74eb1be0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2