{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Several studies have investigated correlations between metastatic pattern and mutation status in patients with colorectal cancer (CRC). However, most of the studies were small and heterogeneously designed and further research is needed to confirm previous results. In this study, we investigated the association between RAS (KRAS or NRAS), BRAF, PIK3CA mutations and metastatic pattern in patients with metastatic (m) CRC. MATERIAL AND METHODS: This study reviewed Danish biobank and database of patients with mCRC who received cetuximab and irinotecan, independent of RAS mutation status, after fluoropyrimidine, oxaliplatin and irinotecan treatment failure. The database contained information regarding tumor mutation status of KRAS, NRAS, BRAF and PIK3CA genes. RESULTS: Totally, 448 patients were included. On multivariate analyses, RAS mutations were significantly associated with increased odds of having lung metastases at diagnosis of mCRC (odds ratio (OR) = 2.04; 95% confidence interval (CI) = 1.32-3.17), and PIK3CA mutations with decreased odds of peritoneal metastases at diagnosis of mCRC (OR = 0.10; 95%CI = 0.01-0.79). On multivariate analyses of the hazard of developing metastases at any time during follow-up, RAS mutations were significantly associated with increased hazard of lung (hazard ratio (HR) = 1.34; 95%CI = 1.04-1.72) and ovarian metastases (HR = 3.12; 95%CI = 1.05-9.24), BRAF V600E mutation was associated with increased hazard of skin metastases (HR = 6.82; 95%CI = 1.86-25.02) and PIK3CA mutations with decreased hazard of peritoneal metastases (HR = 0.31; 95%CI = 0.11-0.86). CONCLUSIONS: This study indicated that in patients with mCRC, RAS mutations are associated with increased risk of lung and ovary metastases. BRAF V600E is associated with increased risk of skin metastases, and PIK3CA mutation with decreased risk of peritoneal metastases.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christensen, Troels Dreier","Palshof, Jesper Andreas","Larsen, Finn Ole","Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","Høgdall, Estrid","Pfeiffer, Per","Jensen, Benny Vittrup","Yilmaz, Mette Karen","Nielsen, Dorte"],"cuid":["S03-094.23-665836"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Class I Phosphatidylinositol 3 Kinases genetics","Colorectal Neoplasms drug therapy","Drug Resistance Neoplasm drug effects","Female","Humans","Lung Neoplasms genetics","Male","Middle Aged","Mutation","Ovarian Neoplasms genetics","Peritoneal Neoplasms genetics","Proto Oncogene Proteins B raf genetics","Retrospective Studies","Skin Neoplasms genetics","ras Proteins genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between primary tumor ras braf and pik000000000003ca mutation status and metastatic site in patients with chemo resistant metastatic colorectal cancer","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85041196552&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-094.23-665836","identifier":[{"id":"29380640","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85041196552","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-66c3927a-7073-4475-a961-94abcf1b7d6a","ku-46b142a5-5e3f-4052-8602-c5f040c97f79","sdu-46efde4a-78bc-4c38-ad3a-4a7fdcb9afc9"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Class I Phosphatidylinositol 3-Kinases/genetics","Colorectal Neoplasms/drug therapy","Drug Resistance, Neoplasm/drug effects","Female","Humans","Lung Neoplasms/genetics","Male","Middle Aged","Mutation","Ovarian Neoplasms/genetics","Peritoneal Neoplasms/genetics","Proto-Oncogene Proteins B-raf/genetics","Retrospective Studies","Skin Neoplasms/genetics","ras Proteins/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-52161A52CBD3BE42BC7E5FE9CD942FF7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev og Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Oncology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Kirurgi og Kræftbehandling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels Dreier","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Troels Dreier","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Andreas","key":"palshofpau","last":"Palshof","name":"Palshof, Jesper Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn Ole","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Finn Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim Svenstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6d-4a52-a3f3-deb515bdd48f","name":"Høgdall, Estrid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"37da1b83-d32a-4f6c-bde6-ca05372851a5","name":"Pfeiffer, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-2925-0586","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benny Vittrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Benny Vittrup","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Karen","key":"yilmazpau","last":"Yilmaz","locid":"a7f763fb-f3f8-403e-841c-202ee8616479","name":"Yilmaz, Mette Karen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Dorte","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e9a4f1d9-3c3d-4eba-b1db-e820b1669e47","name":"Nielsen, Dorte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29380640"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2018.1433322","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"1057-1062","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041196552"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-66c3927a-7073-4475-a961-94abcf1b7d6a","ku-46b142a5-5e3f-4052-8602-c5f040c97f79","sdu-46efde4a-78bc-4c38-ad3a-4a7fdcb9afc9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations between primary tumor RAS, BRAF and PIK3CA mutation status and metastatic site in patients with chemo-resistant metastatic colorectal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.23-665836","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) is a chronic intestinal disorder, with two main types: Crohn's disease (CD) and ulcerative colitis (UC), whose molecular pathology is not well understood. The majority of IBD-associated SNPs are located in non-coding regions and are hard to characterize since regulatory regions in IBD are not known. Here we profile transcription start sites (TSSs) and enhancers in the descending colon of 94 IBD patients and controls. IBD-upregulated promoters and enhancers are highly enriched for IBD-associated SNPs and are bound by the same transcription factors. IBD-specific TSSs are associated to genes with roles in both inflammatory cascades and gut epithelia while TSSs distinguishing UC and CD are associated to gut epithelia functions. We find that as few as 35 TSSs can distinguish active CD, UC, and controls with 85% accuracy in an independent cohort. Our data constitute a foundation for understanding the molecular pathology, gene regulation, and genetics of IBD.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Boyd, Mette","Thodberg, Malte","Vitezic, Morana","Bornholdt, Jette","Vitting-Seerup, Kristoffer","Chen, Yun","Coskun, Mehmet","Li, Yuan","Lo, Bobby Zhao Sheng","Klausen, Pia","Jan Schweiger, Pawel","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Rapin, Nicolas","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Dahlgaard, Katja","Andersson, Robin","Terkelsen, Thilde Bagger","Lilje, Berit","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","Petersen, Andreas Munk","Jensen, Kim Bak","Gögenur, Ismail","Thielsen, Peter","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","Sandelin, Albin"],"cuid":["S03-098.36-036705"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Sandelin, Albin"],"keyword":["Disease genetics","Inflammatory bowel disease","Transcriptomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of the enhancer and promoter landscape of inflammatory bowel disease from human colon biopsies","src":["dtu","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03766-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.36-036705","identifier":[{"id":"85046090244","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29695774","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5916929","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-b53772e3-55fe-4b30-a719-1e02abdf824a","ku-1d962938-4d43-41e4-b4ae-103f8ba9df9b","ruc-7c28d2eb-8565-4a0b-a781-47a7055a3098"],"keyword":["Disease genetics","Inflammatory bowel disease","Transcriptional regulatory elements","Transcriptomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-892D1F45D9E597169AFA795D3F2ADA1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/147553339/s41467_018_03766_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/197762043/Characterization_of_the_enhancer_and_promoter_landscape_of_inflammatory_bowel_disease_from_human_colon_biopsies.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-03766-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/111450027/s41467-018-03766-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU Universi