{"abstract":"The critically endangered European eel Anguilla anguilla is dependent on suitable habitat qualities over a vast geographic area. Even though a significant proportion of the population never enters fresh water, the preferred benthic habitat is largely unknown in the marine environment. Examining substratum selection in A. anguilla reveals that elvers prefer coarse gravel, suggesting that conservation efforts may benefit from targeting this type of substratum in marine coastal areas.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Mads","Svendsen, Jon Christian","Kuhn, Jesper","Nielsen, Anders","Martjanova, A.","Støttrup, Josianne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311427"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christoffersen, Mads"],"keyword":["Anguillia anguillia","Coastal management","European eel","Habitat selection","Marine sediment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"benthic habitat selection in juvenile european eel anguilla anguilla implications for coastal habitat management and restoration","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/153874525/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311427","identifier":[{"id":"85057539331","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30246412","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-16c3b18b-50a2-4a4c-8532-44a4d25ea4ba"],"keyword":["Anguillia anguillia","Coastal management","Elvers","European eel","Habitat selection","Marine sediment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0BBA5BFA15034111CEA732024A2E6E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/153874525/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M.","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"955b638f-ff31-4afe-a4aa-126372d06907","name":"Christoffersen, Mads","name_org":"Christoffersen, M.","orcid":"0000-0002-6335-7459","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon Christian","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"2208c455-c4d1-4ba7-a638-9062097f640b","name":"Svendsen, Jon Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0273-0985","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. A.","key":"kuhnpau","last":"Kuhn","locid":"eecd10a1-5c18-4556-acd0-d0a5e87dc523","name":"Kuhn, Jesper","name_org":"Kuhn, J. A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b954c930-484f-4d22-8431-f896942080ec","name":"Nielsen, Anders","name_org":"Nielsen, A.","orcid":"0000-0001-9683-9262","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"martjanovapau","last":"Martjanova","name":"Martjanova, A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josianne Gatt","key":"støttruppau","last":"Støttrup","locid":"cf999b24-fb74-420b-b42b-d48a114d16b1","name":"Støttrup, Josianne","name_org":"Støttrup, Josianne Gatt","orcid":"0000-0002-0921-8773","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30246412"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jfb.13807","issn":["00221112","10958649"],"issn_org":["00221112"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Fish Biology","pages":"996-999","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Fish Biology","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057539331"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-16c3b18b-50a2-4a4c-8532-44a4d25ea4ba"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Benthic habitat selection in juvenile European eel Anguilla anguilla : implications for coastal habitat management and restoration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311427","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aortic valve stenosis increases peak systolic velocity (PSV) and flow complexity in the ascending aorta, and is treated with either biological or mechanical implants. Vector flow imaging (VFI) is an angle independent ultrasound method for flow assessment. In contrast to conventional ultrasound, VFI can quantify complex flow patterns, e.g. the flow complexity called vector concentration (VC) in long axis and the secondary rotation (SR) in short axis view. Study aim was to evaluate flow changes only visible with VFI before and after valve implantation in patients with aortic valve stenosis. VFI on a commercial scanner (Pro Focus 2202 Ultra View, BK Medical) with a linear transducer (8670, BK Medical) was applied intraoperatively on the ascending aorta. Four patients scheduled for biological valve implants and 4 patients for mechanical valve implants were scanned before and after surgery. Four patients with normal aortic valve were scanned for comparison. VFI data of the ascending aorta were obtained in long and short axis view during the systolic phase for assessment of VC and SR. VC ranges from 0 to 1 (complex to laminar flow), and SR is measured in Hz. PSV was obtained with conventional spectral Doppler. Before surgery, patients with aortic valve stenosis scheduled for mechanical (PSV: 356.3 (64.3) cmls; SR: 15.3 (7.8) Hz; VC: 0.18 (0.03)) and biological implants (PSV: 350.0 (80.8) cmls; SR: 17.9 (2.6) Hz; VC: 0.26 (0.07)) had more complex flow with higher velocities compared with patients with normal aortic valve (PSV: 124.8 (16. 7) cmls; SR: 2.9 (1.1) Hz; VC: 0.83 (0.09)). After surgery, velocities were lower for mechanical (PSV: 214.5 (47.5) cmls; SR: 5.6 (3.0) Hz) compared with biological implants (PSV: 241.5 (39.1) cmls; SR: 13.2 (1.8) Hz). However, VC was higher for biological (0.68 (0.05)) compared with mechanical implants (0.56 (0.09)) indicating a more laminar and less complex flow despite higher systolic velocities in patients treated with biological implants. The mechanical valve has a larger opening with cusps attached centrally in the lumen opposed to the biological valve, which may explain the differences found. Normal flow was neither found for biological nor mechanical implants. VFI can provide new parameters for flow evaluation and be useful for aortic flow assessment before and after valve implantation and in the development of mechanical valves.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nguyen, Tin Quoc","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-332729"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aortic Valve Stenosis","Aortic valve implantation","Ascending aorta","Ultrasound","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flow changes after biological and mechanical aortic valve implantation measured with vfi","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197989575/new_ieee.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-332729","identifier":[{"id":"85060614420","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5e950bd3-a203-4bbd-86c9-8f39b8dc71e6"],"keyword":["Aortic valve implantation","Aortic valve stenosis","Ascending aorta","Ultrasound","Vector flow imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-0F6C4AE6D86614A4F687766BAE16D4B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197989575/new_ieee.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer Lindskov","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasse","key":"møllersørensenpau","last":"Møller-Sørensen","name":"Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tin Quoc","key":"nguyenpau","last":"Nguyen","name":"Nguyen, Tin Quoc","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ultsym.2018.8579916","eisbn":["9781538634257"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium (IUS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060614420"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5e950bd3-a203-4bbd-86c9-8f39b8dc71e6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Flow Changes after Biological and Mechanical Aortic Valve Implantation Measured with VFI","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-332729","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Non-negative matrix and tensor factorization (NMF/NTF) have become important tools for extracting part based representations in data. It is however unclear when an NMF or NTF approach is most suited for data and how reliably the models predict when trained on partially observed data. We presently extend a recently proposed variational Bayesian NMF (VB-NMF) to non-negative tensor factorization (VB-NTF) for partially observed data. This admits bi- and multi-linear structure quantification considering both model prediction and evidence. We evaluate the developed VB-NTF on synthetic and a real dataset of gene expression in the human brain and contrast the performance to VB-NMF and conventional NMF/NTF. We find that the gene expressions are better accounted for by VB-NMF than VB-NTF and that VB-NMF/VB-NTF more robustly handle partially observed data than conventional NMF/NTF. In particular, probabilistic modeling is beneficial when large amounts of data is missing and/or the model order over-specified.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hinrich, Jesper Løve","Nielsen, Søren Føns Vind","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Mørup, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-355898"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-20","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2018-09-17","title":"2018 IEEE 28th International Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Missing data","Non negative Tensor Factorization","Probabilistic modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variational bayesian partially observed non negative tensor factorization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85057018485","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-355898","identifier":[{"id":"85057018485","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-abd58193-b105-4e85-86d9-b6be4a741f25"],"keyword":["Human brain microarray data","Missing data","Non-negative tensor factorization","Probabilistic modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3177B5770E9F131480E86644C9AE9592"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Løve","key":"hinrichpau","last":"Hinrich","locid":"e3c8c713-afa8-4d6e-9071-774487e7e599","name":"Hinrich, Jesper Løve","orcid":"0000-0003-0258-7151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Føns Vind","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"82813a45-694c-483d-81ea-5ba6f2e77078","name":"Nielsen, Søren Føns Vind","orcid":"0000-0001-6713-9144","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer Hougaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"243ae993-e526-4121-b28a-aabf62c3df84","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8606-7641","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","locid":"7ffdfaca-76bd-44ec-a98f-13fe4f033b71","name":"Mørup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-4985-4368","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mlsp.2018.8516924","isbn":["9781538654774"],"pages":"1-6","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2018 IEEE 28th International Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057018485"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-abd58193-b105-4e85-86d9-b6be4a741f25"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Variational bayesian partially observed non-negative tensor factorization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-355898","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We discuss α-particle velocity-space diagnostic in ITER based on the planned collective Thomson scattering (CTS) and γ-ray spectrometry (GRS) systems as well as ASCOT simulations of the α-particle distribution function. GRS is sensitive to α-particles with energies MeV at all pitches p, and CTS for MeV and . The remaining velocity space is not observed. GRS and CTS view the plasma (almost) perpendicularly to the magnetic field. Hence we cannot determine the sign of the pitch of the α-particles and cannot distinguish co- and counter-going α-particles with the currently planned α-particle diagnostics. Therefore we can only infer the sign-insensitive 2D distribution function by velocity-space tomography for MeV. This is a serious limitation, since co- and counter-going α-particle populations are expected to have different birth rates and neoclassical transport as well as different anomalous transport due to interaction with modes such as Alfvén eigenmodes. We propose the installation of an oblique GRS system on ITER to allow us to diagnostically track such anisotropy effects and to infer the full, sign-sensitive for MeV. α-particles with MeV are diagnosed by CTS only, which does not allow velocity-space tomography on its own. Nevertheless, we show that measurements of the α-particle energy spectrum, which is an ITER measurement requirement, are now feasible for MeV using a velocity-space tomography formalism assuming isotropy in velocity space.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Salewski, Mirko","Nocente, M.","Madsen, B.","Abramovic, I.","Fitzgerald, M.","Gorini, G.","Hansen, Per Christian","Heidbrink, W.W.","Jacobsen, A.S.","Jensen, T.","Kiptily, V.G.","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Kurki-Suonio, T.","Larsen, Axel Wright","Leipold, Frank","Moseev, D.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Pinches, S.D.","Rasmussen, Jesper","Rebai, M.","Schneider, M.","Shevelev, A.","Sipilä, S.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardocchi, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-366430"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Salewski, Mirko"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Italy","Russia","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","ITER Cadarache","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Research Council of Italy","RAS - Ioffe Physico Technical Institute","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of California at Irvine","University of Milan - Bicocca"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alpha particle velocity space diagnostic in iter","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196393882/salewski2018bnf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-366430","identifier":[{"id":"85051210673","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cf3b6dce-76cb-47d7-83f5-fe1b08efca5c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0917C68C781E416557939A3F999AD6E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196393882/salewski2018bnf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","us