{"abstract":"We present a case report of a 70-year-old male patient with a giant goitre. The patient experienced recurrent episodes of syncope/fainting, when he turned his head towards to the right, and he experienced discomfort when lying on his back. A CT scan showed compression of the right carotid artery and carotid sinus from a thyroid mass. After a mass of 1,473 g of thyroid tissue had been removed by a right thyroid lobectomy, the patient experienced no further episodes of syncope. It is well known, that giant goitres can bring a wide range of symptoms including compression of arteries, veins, nerves and related structures on the neck and in the thorax.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Agger-Nielsen, Helle Elisabeth","Døssing, Helle","Sørensen, Jesper Roed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-577590"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Goiter Nodular complications","Humans","Male","Quality of Life","Syncope etiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synkope grundet monstrøs struma","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85072309465","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-577590","identifier":[{"id":"29886887","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85072309465","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-0f65ca02-60e3-45b2-a496-b63be3b6e64b"],"keyword":["Aged","Goiter, Nodular/complications","Humans","Male","Quality of Life","Syncope/etiology"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7C26769AD5BB8D5B6ECC3A0E87B159A1"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oto Rhino Laryngology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"aggernielsenpau","last":"Agger-Nielsen","locid":"f47be3a8-3391-42ee-a171-a95fae63b6aa","name":"Agger-Nielsen, Helle Elisabeth","name_org":"Agger-Nielsen, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-9394-8161","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"døssingpau","last":"Døssing","locid":"f3091fc9-8b0b-4ece-bd65-0c7b016928c1","name":"Døssing, Helle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Roed","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"df2f67c9-1538-4bd8-82fb-79cd5c6b6814","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Roed","orcid":"0000-0003-4351-8873","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29886887"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"24","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V01180048","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"180"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0f65ca02-60e3-45b2-a496-b63be3b6e64b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Synkope grundet monstrøs struma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-577590","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background Metformin constitutes first-line treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus. It is presumed to have lactic acidosis as a dangerous, but rare, side effect. Objectives To estimate the incidence rate of lactic acidosis in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus as well as to estimate the relative risk of lactic acidosis associated with metformin treatment. Methods This is a population-based combined cohort and case-control study among patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus who were acutely admitted with lactic acidosis at Odense University Hospital, Denmark; in the period from 1st June 2009 to 1st October 2013. The patients included as cases were all acutely hospitalized with lactic acidosis (pH <7.35 and lactate 2.0 mmol/l). For each case, we identified 24 age- and sex-matched controls sampled from the same cohort with type 2 diabetes mellitus. The use of metformin identified by using a prescription database. Analyses included multivariable logistic regression and adjusting for predefined confounding: renal function, HbA1c, comorbidity and diabetes duration. Results Our cohort included 10,652 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with a median age of 74 years, and 51.5% were male. During follow-up, 163 individuals were hospitalized with lactic acidosis, corresponding to an incidence rate of 391/100,000 person years. Use of metformin was not associated with lactic acidosis: adjusted odds ratio was 0.79 (95%CI 0.54–1.17)Conclusion Among patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, the incidence rate of acute hospitalization with lactic acidosis was 391/100,000 person years. Use of metformin did not increase the risk of lactic acidosis. However, comorbidity seems to be an important risk factor.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aharaz, Abdellatif","Pottegård, Anton","Henriksen, Daniel Pilsgaard","Hallas, Jesper","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Lassen, Annmarie Touborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Aharaz, Abdellatif"],"keyword":["Acidosis Lactic chemically induced","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Case Control Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 drug therapy","Female","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents adverse effects","Incidence","Male","Metformin adverse effects","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of lactic acidosis in type 000000000002 diabetes patients using metformin a case control study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0196122","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-587131","identifier":[{"id":"85046664222","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29738540","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5940216","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-3097c8b4-46df-4ca9-beff-6616c21170d9"],"keyword":["Acidosis, Lactic/chemically induced","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Case-Control Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark/epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/drug therapy","Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions/etiology","Female","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents/adverse effects","Incidence","Male","Metformin/adverse effects","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87EB5EBC6B6FA7D43268402F07A792F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0196122","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/140809831/Risk_of_lactic_acidosis_in_type_2_diabetes_patients_using_metformin.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Abdellatif","key":"aharazpau","last":"Aharaz","locid":"164a9e4c-ab59-459c-9ffa-c0b0724690a1","name":"Aharaz, Abdellatif","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Pilsgaard","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"44eb5c50-0799-4ae1-86e1-d57667563b07","name":"Henriksen, Daniel Pilsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1303-6195","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"becknielsenpau","last":"Beck-Nielsen","locid":"0e78b588-9e9c-4acc-a1b8-8bcccea0b5a5","name":"Beck-Nielsen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0002-7428-7898","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annmarie Touborg","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"80e651b5-e70f-43e0-baf8-e88335ac10b8","name":"Lassen, Annmarie Touborg","orcid":"0000-0003-4942-6152","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29738540"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0196122","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"5","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0196122","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046664222"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3097c8b4-46df-4ca9-beff-6616c21170d9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Risk of lactic acidosis in type 2 diabetes patients using metformin : A case control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-587131","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Medication errors (MEs) in neonates are frequent and associated with increased potential for harm compared with adults. The effect of learning from reported MEs is potentially lacking due to underreporting, lack of feedback and missing actions to improve medication safety. A new approach involving positive recognition of current and future strategies may facilitate greater exploration of how to improve medication safety in neonates. We aimed to explore current and potential future practices to prevent MEs in neonatal intensive care units (NICUs). Methods: Focus group interviews of physicians and nurses were conducted at three Danish NICUs. Participants were included if they had at least 1 month of working experience and provided direct patient care. A semistructured interview guide involving three questions was used: (a) how do you feel about discussing prevention of MEs? (b) how do you currently prevent MEs from occurring? and (c) how can we become better at preventing MEs in the future? Content analysis was used to identify themes in the interviews. Results: Participants commented that MEs still occur and that action must be taken to improve medication safety. Current practices to prevent MEs involved technology, procedures, education, skills and hospital pharmacy services. Potential future practices to prevent MEs included customizing the computerized physician order entry systems to support optimal prescribing, standardizing the double-check process, training of calculation skills and teamwork and increased use of hospital pharmacy services. Conclusions: Several current and potential future practices to reduce MEs in NICUs were identified, highlighting the complexity of MEs. Our findings support an interdisciplinary multifaceted intervention involving both technical and nontechnical elements to improve medication safety in NICUs.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rishoej, Rikke Mie","Lai Nielsen, Henriette","Strzelec, Stina Maria","Fritsdal Refer, Jane","Allermann Beck, Sanne","Gramstrup, Hanne Marie","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Juel Kjeldsen, Lene","Hallas, Jesper","Almarsdóttir, Anna Birna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606602"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rishoej, Rikke Mie"],"keyword":["Hospital","Medication Errors","Paediatrics","Prevention strategies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"qualitative exploration of practices to prevent medication errors in neonatal intensive care units a focus group study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151867623/2042098618771541.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606602","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6048629","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30034776","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85046632860","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-74b1fa40-9be1-404e-aea4-5ca3ae58f270"],"keyword":["hospital","medication errors","paediatrics","prevention strategies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B63FB19F715002731886C6BBC936265"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151867623/2042098618771541.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amgros"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Mie","key":"rishoejpau","last":"Rishoej","locid":"e97ad0ed-cc20-4da7-9d0c-e2ef9aa00b1b","name":"Rishoej, Rikke Mie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"lainielsenpau","last":"Lai Nielsen","name":"Lai Nielsen, Henriette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Maria","key":"strzelecpau","last":"Strz