{"abstract":"Objective: Bone formation is a hallmark of osteoarthritis (OA). It has been speculated that bone formation may occur because of ossification at the bone-cartilage unit, that is, bone formation directly involving the calcified cartilage (CC). This study aimed to investigate the thickness of the CC and subchondral bone (SCB) in relation to the severity of the overlying articular cartilage (AC) degeneration. Design: We investigated femoral heads from 20 patients with OA and 15 healthy subjects with design-based stereology using systematic uniform random sampling of the entire joint surface. This was combined with the Osteoarthritis Research Society International (OARSI) OA cartilage histopathology assessment system, thus obtaining focal OARSI grades paired with thickness measurements of AC, CC and the SCB. Results: The patients with OA had thicker CC (mean 159; 95% CI 144 to 177 µm) compared with the healthy subjects (mean 132; 95% CI 113 to 1550 µm; p=0.036), and this difference was even higher in areas without loss of AC thickness (OARSI grade ≤3); 187 (95% CI 164 to 214) µm vs 132 (95% CI 113 to 155) µm (p=0.001). In the patients with OA, a thicker SCB was observed in areas with loss of AC thickness (OARSI grade ≥4), but not in areas without loss of AC thickness (OARSI grade ≤3). Conclusion: The study showed that thicker CC is present in early stages of OA, suggesting that bone formation by endochondral ossification is an early phenomenon of OA. Thickening of the SCB was present, but only in areas with denuded bone. Suggesting that also appositional bone growth occurs and that it may be a consequence of changed biomechanics.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hartlev, Louise Brøndt","Klose-Jensen, Rasmus","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Nyengaard, Jens Randel","Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","Laursen, Mogens Berg","Laurberg, Trine Bay","Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","Steengaard-Pedersen, Kristian","Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe"],"cuid":["S02-081.82-010278"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Articular cartilage","Calcified cartilage","Hip","Osteoarthritis","Stereology","Subchondral bone"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thickness of the bone cartilage unit in relation to osteoarthritis severity in the human hip joint","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2018-000747","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.82-010278","identifier":[{"id":"30271622","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6157564","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85057599633","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d70317d9-df06-4d88-813a-1efb18677575","au-64397199-a3ec-4941-bda7-d7c1e1eba868"],"keyword":["articular cartilage","calcified cartilage","hip","osteoarthritis","stereology","subchondral bone"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-62B93441E2DDC1B9FCE763E2586F1593"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/287919350/Thickness_of_the_bone_cartilage_unit_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2018-000747","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Section for Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Brøndt","key":"hartlevpau","last":"Hartlev","locid":"ff30b23b-e653-4cd0-902c-04cb78f756cf","name":"Hartlev, Louise Brøndt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"klosejensenpau","last":"Klose-Jensen","locid":"23dd4b1b-5313-4ad6-8e33-00476fc5d97e","name":"Klose-Jensen, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Skovhus","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"924ef2ac-827c-4260-9cd7-fbe300bbafeb","name":"Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0001-9386-6679","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Randel","key":"nyengaardpau","last":"Nyengaard","locid":"8288d58c-4602-4c0c-9b76-949cc83d281b","name":"Nyengaard, Jens Randel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Warner Thorup","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"cf69d33f-562c-489b-9564-9a9dc15c0a16","name":"Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens Berg","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"26102317-00ee-41ec-ae85-c7a3bde4c391","name":"Laursen, Mogens Berg","orcid":"0000-0002-2791-3921","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Bay","key":"laurbergpau","last":"Laurberg","locid":"9b62fbc1-6542-4056-9722-914c29f223f0","name":"Laurberg, Trine Bay","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas Wiggers","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dc3ce48a-c47a-46ef-beac-360aec95aacc","name":"Nielsen, Andreas Wiggers","orcid":"0000-0001-8180-6871","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"steengaardpedersenpau","last":"Steengaard-Pedersen","locid":"cb8cd9be-ca7d-4963-86b6-31dcc273f625","name":"Stengaard-Pedersen, Kristian","name_org":"Steengaard-Pedersen, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0001-7991-2456","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen-Margrethe","key":"haugepau","last":"Hauge","locid":"6e0e979f-48d6-40bd-89ec-a2502b1cefd4","name":"Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","name_org":"Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30271622"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/rmdopen-2018-000747","issn":["20565933"],"issue":"2","journal":"RMD Open","paperid":"e000747","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"RMD Open","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057599633"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d70317d9-df06-4d88-813a-1efb18677575","au-64397199-a3ec-4941-bda7-d7c1e1eba868"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Thickness of the bone-cartilage unit in relation to osteoarthritis severity in the human hip joint","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.82-010278","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims and objectives: No validated version of the 9-item Shared Decision Making Questionnaire (SDM-Q-9) in Danish is available. The aim of the study was to translate, culturally adapt and psychometrically test a Danish version of the SDM-Q-9 in 2 patient groups: elderly patients from outpatient gynecology clinics and a group of younger patients from an outpatient sports clinic. Method: The SDM-Q-9, patient version, was translated into Danish through a standardized forward-backward translation performed by 4 independent translators, followed by cognitive interviewing of 11 outpatients from the 2 patient groups. The process was adjusted by an expert panel. The psychometric testing was performed at 5 Danish hospital departments. Reliability (internal consistency) was estimated by Cronbach’s alpha. Construct validity was determined by confirmatory and explanatory factor analysis. Results: A total of 268 patients (218 gynecological and 50 knee patients) were included. The scale had high reliability (Cronbach’s alpha of 0.94). A high ceiling effect was found (44% with the highest rating). None of the tested models in the confirmatory analysis had a good fit. The explanatory factor analysis for the whole sample yielded a unidimensional factor, which explained 91% of variances with high factor loadings of more than 0.7. Conclusion: The Danish version of the SDM-Q-9 is a well-accepted, reliable and - despite the challenges of a high ceiling effect - valid instrument in the tested populations. Further psychometrical testing in other populations is necessary as well as research with other convergent instruments to demonstrate consistency over time and between patient groups.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hulbæk, Mette","Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","Mainz, Hanne","Birkelund, Regner","Nielson, Jesper Bo","Debrabant, Birgit","Primdahl, Jette"],"cuid":["S02-085.75-025366"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Clinical Decision Making","Factor analysis","Patient involvement","Patient perspectives","Psychometric testing","Urogynecology","person centered healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish translation cultural adaptation and validation of the shared decision making questionaire patient version sdm q 000000000009 pat","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-085.75-025366","ids":["au-ae768cf6-eeb7-4c77-8c81-2d3eeeb20271","sdu-dd71b312-95bd-4d51-8749-a5be0eb9f3aa"],"keyword":["Anterior cruciate ligament injurie","clinical decision-making","factor analysis","patient involvement","patient perspectives","person-centered healthcare","psychometric testing","treatment options","urogynecology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D2E1EA2B2DD9FAA86FB64776DE0544F4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"hulbækpau","last":"Hulbæk","locid":"140af55f-92a4-4fcd-be71-f7776e32e2d3","name":"Hulbæk, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8258-3398","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Johansson","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"69bdfc6a-06a4-4473-9211-b8eed69a4cc4","name":"Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4822","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"mainzpau","last":"Mainz","name":"Mainz, Hanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Regner","key":"birkelundpau","last":"Birkelund","locid":"dedbb04e-270c-4add-a26c-87277d6caf0f","name":"Birkelund, Regner","orcid":"0000-0002-5374-0630","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsonpau","last":"Nielson","name":"Nielson, Jesper Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit","key":"debrabantpau","last":"Debrabant","locid":"bc47d3aa-9760-4139-9a72-ae553777b623","name":"Debrabant, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-1964-3204","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"primdahlpau","last":"Primdahl","locid":"e7f33410-2d7a-4869-b5e9-ed886ba48c94","name":"Primdahl, Jette","orcid":"0000-0002-1049-4150","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5750/ejpch.v6i3.1529","issn":["20525656"],"journal":"European Journal for Person Centered Healthcare","pages":"438-446","publisher":"University of Buckingham Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal for Person Centered Healthcare","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ae768cf6-eeb7-4c77-8c81-2d3eeeb20271","sdu-dd71b312-95bd-4d51-8749-a5be0eb9f3aa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Danish translation, cultural adaptation and validation of the shared decision making questionaire : patient version (SDM-Q-9-PAT)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.75-025366","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The barrier properties of cellular membranes are increasingly attracting attention as a source of inspiration for designing biomimetic membranes. The broad range of potential technological applications makes the use of lipid and lately also polymeric materials a popular choice for constructing biomimetic membranes, where the barrier properties can be controlled by the composition of the membrane constituent elements. Here we investigate the membrane properties reported by the light-induced proton pumping activity of bacteriorhodopsin (bR) reconstituted in three vesicle systems of different membrane composition. Specifically we quantify how the resulting proton influx and efflux rates are influenced by the membrane composition using a variety of membrane modulators. We demonstrate that by adding hydrocarbons to vesicles with reconstituted bR formed from asolectin lipids the resulting transmembrane proton fluxes changes proportional to the carbon chain length when compared against control. We observe a similar proportionality in single-component 1,2-Dioleoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine model membranes when using cholesterol. Lastly we investigate the effects of adding the amphiphilic di-block co-polymer polybutadiene-polyethyleneoxide (PB12-PEO10) to phospholipid membranes formed from 1,2-Dioleoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine, 1,2-Dioleoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphatidylethanolamine, and 1,2-Dioleoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphatidylserine. The proton pumping activity of bR (measured as a change in extra-vesicular pH) in mixed lipid/PB12-PEO10 lipid systems is up to six-fold higher compared to that observed for bR containing vesicles made from PB12-PEO10 alone. Interestingly, bR inserts with apparent opposite orientation in pure PB12-PEO10 vesicles as compared to pure lipid vesicles. Addition of equimolar amounts of lipids to PB12-PEO10 results in bR orientation similar to that observed for pure lipids. In conclusion our results show how the barrier properties of the membranes can be controlled by the composition of the membrane. In particular the use of mixed lipid-polymer systems may pave the way for constructing biomimetic membranes tailored for optimal properties in various applications including drug delivery systems, biosensors and energy conservation technology.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Palanco, Marta Espina","Skovgaard, Nils","Hansen, Jesper Søndergaard","Berg-Sørensen, Kirstine","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S02-097.60-033718"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Asolectin","Bacteriorhodopsin","Biomimetic membranes","Cholesterol","Diblock copolymer","Lipid membrane","Phospholipids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tuning biomimetic membrane barrier properties by hydrocarbon cholesterol and polymeric additives","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/138480160/Untitled.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-097.60-033718","identifier":[{"id":"29019793","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85047488083","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-32ef3d09-e6ee-4573-a5e2-544ccd1c2251","ku-e847ed68-88fe-4bb0-959d-cacd45d97f82"],"keyword":["Asolectin","Bacteriorhodopsin","Biomimetic membranes","Cholesterol","Diblock copolymer","Lipid membrane","Phospholipids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1493FB60A890763A37FCEF2C2205B141"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/138480160/Untitled.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Biophysics and Fluids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biostructural Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marta Espina","key":"palancopau","last":"Palanco","locid":"1ff7c268-0086-4071-83e5-964acaa52174","name":"Palanco, Marta Espina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nils","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"872dab07-af5f-49a4-9501-eddc58b8b00c","name":"Skovgaard, Nils","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Søndergaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper Søndergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirstine","key":"bergsørensenpau","last":"Berg-Sørensen","locid":"f1c10c27-0fce-408f-88a4-b6262dcb8e98","name":"Berg-Sørensen, Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-9977-3980","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"hélixnielsenpau","last":"Hélix-Nielsen","locid":"bea497c9-caba-420a-81f8-8f2730634b31","name":"Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-9392-7133","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29019793"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1748-3190/aa92be","issn":["17483182","17483190"],"issn_org":["17483182"],"issue":"1","journal":"Bioinspiration & Biomimetics","paperid":"016005","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Bioinspiration & Biomimetics","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047488083"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-32ef3d09-e6ee-4573-a5e2-544ccd1c2251","ku-e847ed68-88fe-4bb0-959d-cacd45d97f82"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tuning biomimetic membrane barrier properties by hydrocarbon, cholesterol and polymeric additives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.60-033718","year":"2018","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The aim of the present study was to investigate whether street basketball organized as 3 v 3 on either a half court (HC) with 1 basket or a full court (FC) with 2 baskets could improve fitness and health profiles of untrained men after 3 months of supervised training. Methods: Thirty-five untrained men (aged 20–42 years) completed the pre- and post-intervention testing (FC: n = 13, HC: n = 12, CO (control): n = 10). The training attendance was 2.0 ± 0.4 and 1.9 ± 0.3 times per week in FC and HC, respectively. Mean heart rate (HR) was 83.8 ± 6.0 percent of maximal heart rate (%HR max ) and 84.5 ± 2.9 %HR max in FC and HC, respectively. Results: The 3 months of street basketball training on an FC with 2 baskets increased maximal oxygen uptake (2.4 mL/min/kg (95% confidence interval (CI): 1.0–3.9)), time to exhaustion (47 s (95%CI: 26–67)), lean body mass (0.8 kg (95%CI: 0.1–1.5)), and bone mineral density (0.021 g/cm 2 (95%CI: 0.011–0.031)), whereas mean arterial pressure (–5.6 mmHg (95%CI: –7.5 to 3.7)), body fat percentage (–1.6%, (95%CI: –2.5 to –0.7)), heart rate (–18 bpm (95%CI: –24 to –12)), and blood lactate (median: –1.4 mmol/L (interquartile range: –1.5 to –0.6)) during submaximal running were lowered. The changes were less pronounced after the training period when playing on an HC with 1 basket, but increases in maximal oxygen uptake (1.6 mL/min/kg (95%CI: –0.1 to 3.3)), time to exhaustion (28 s (95%CI: 9–47)), lean body mass (1.3 kg (95%CI: 0.3–2.4)), and lower body fat percentage (–0.9% (95%CI: –1.9 to –0.1)) were observed in this group. Conclusion: Three months of 3 v 3 street basketball training improved fitness and led to broad-spectrum improvements in variables related to overall health profile, with the most marked effects observed when playing on an FC with 2 baskets.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Randers, Morten Bredsgaard","Hagman, Marie","Brix, Jonathan","Christensen, Jesper F","Pedersen, Mogens Theisen","Nielsen, Jens Jung","Krustrup, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-097.74-040845"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Body composition","Cardiovascular fitness","Maximal oxygen uptake","Muscoloskeletal fitness","Physical demands","Small sided games","Team sport"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of 000000000003 months of full court and half court street basketball training on health profile in untrained men","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jshs.2017.09.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.74-040845","identifier":[{"id":"85034439418","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30356444","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6180545","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-22fcdb54-7b86-4056-9493-f0fc95266685","sdu-3805ad75-52e9-42fd-8972-9fdddd9b809f"],"keyword":["Blood pressure","Body composition","Cardiovascular fitness","Maximal oxygen uptake","Muscoloskeletal fitness","Physical demands","Small-sided games","Team sport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FC5C0C25BF7D553FE1CBDA7E188E2F24"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jshs.2017.09.004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/196348071/Randers_et_al_Journal_of_Sport_and_Health_Science_2018_Vol_7_2_132_138.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141556793/1_s2.0_S209525461730114X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten Bredsgaard","key":"randerspau","last":"Randers","locid":"5f16a5dd-f231-48c6-bddd-cd4ec6b20ea4","name":"Randers, Morten Bredsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0192-8981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Bredsgaard Randers","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"b92f7ad7-56ca-40b1-9e2b-80e88902f8bd","name":"Randers, Morten Bredsgaard","name_org":"Thomsen, Morten Bredsgaard Randers","orcid":"0000-0002-0192-8981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie von Ahnen","key":"hagmanpau","last":"Hagman","locid":"7cece57f-3725-4f82-9a43-69eb1e94b476","name":"Hagman, Marie von Ahnen","orcid":"0000-0002-7171-4241","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonathan","key":"brixpau","last":"Brix","name":"Brix, Jonathan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper F","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jesper F","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens Theisen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5390946b-e1a6-47e1-817a-72dfb5283a42","name":"Pedersen, Mogens Theisen","orcid":"0000-0002-3178-6320","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Jung","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b6501345-ec3f-49e9-87fe-e10aea74fa41","name":"Nielsen, Jens Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-7694-3425","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"krustruppau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"466150ff-704b-461f-8004-692635d9c82b","name":"Krustrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1461-9838","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30356444"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jshs.2017.09.004","issn":["20952546","22132961"],"issn_org":["20952546"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Sport and Health Science","pages":"132-138","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Sport and Health Science","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034439418"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-22fcdb54-7b86-4056-9493-f0fc95266685","sdu-3805ad75-52e9-42fd-8972-9fdddd9b809f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of 3 months of full-court and half-court street basketball training on health profile in untrained men","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.74-040845","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Anatomically realistic volume conductor models of the human head are important for accurate forward modeling of the electric field during transcranial brain stimulation (TBS), electro- (EEG) and magnetoencephalography (MEG). In particular, the skull compartment exerts a strong influence on the field distribution due to its low conductivity, suggesting the need to represent its geometry accurately. However, automatic skull reconstruction from structural magnetic resonance (MR) images is difficult, as compact bone has a very low signal in magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Here, we evaluate three methods for skull segmentation, namely FSL BET2, the unified segmentation routine of SPM12 with extended spatial tissue priors, and the skullfinder tool of BrainSuite. To our knowledge, this study is the first to rigorously assess the accuracy of these state-of-the-art tools by comparison with CT-based skull segmentations on a group of ten subjects. We demonstrate several key factors that improve the segmentation quality, including the use of multi-contrast MRI data, the optimization of the MR sequences and the adaptation of the parameters of the segmentation methods. We conclude that FSL and SPM12 achieve better skull segmentations than BrainSuite. The former methods obtain reasonable results for the upper part of the skull when a combination of T1- and T2-weighted images is used as input. The SPM12-based results can be improved slightly further by means of simple morphological operations to fix local defects. In contrast to FSL BET2, the SPM12-based segmentation with extended spatial tissue priors and the BrainSuite-based segmentation provide coarse reconstructions of the vertebrae, enabling the construction of volume conductor models that include the neck. We exemplarily demonstrate that the extended models enable a more accurate estimation of the electric field distribution during transcranial direct current stimulation (tDCS) for montages that involve extraencephalic electrodes. The methods provided by FSL and SPM12 are integrated into pipelines for the automatic generation of realistic head models based on tetrahedral meshes, which are distributed as part of the open-source software package SimNIBS for field calculations for transcranial brain stimulation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Puonti, Oula","Siebner, Hartwig R.","Bauer, Christian","Madsen, Camilla Gøbel","Saturnino, Guilherme B.","Thielscher, Axel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033348"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Thielscher, Axel"],"keyword":["Adult","Brain anatomy histology","Cognitive neuroscience","Electroencephalography","Electroencephalography methods","Female","Forward modeling","Humans","Image Processing Computer Assisted methods","Magnetic Resonance Imaging methods","Magnetoencephalography methods","Male","Models Biological","Neurology","Pattern Recognition Automated","Reproducibility of Results","Skull anatomy histology","Skull segmentation","Software","Transcranial Direct Current Stimulation methods","Transcranial brain stimulation","Volume conductor model","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automatic skull segmentation from mr images for realistic volume conductor models of the head assessment of the state of the art","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/145259432/1_s2.0_S1053811918301800_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-033348","identifier":[{"id":"85043378835","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29518567","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-229c633e-ede3-4437-b257-0a08e2c447b5","ku-933d452a-641c-48f6-8e00-48e21cee1003"],"keyword":["Adult","Brain/anatomy & histology","Cognitive Neuroscience","Electroencephalography","Electroencephalography/methods","Female","Forward modeling","Humans","Image Processing, Computer-Assisted/methods","Magnetic Resonance Imaging/methods","Magnetoencephalography/methods","Male","Models, Biological","Neurology","Pattern Recognition, Automated","Reproducibility of Results","Skull segmentation","Skull/anatomy & histology","Software","Transcranial Direct Current Stimulation/methods","Transcranial brain stimulation","Volume conductor model","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3FCE166EFCCF62053845F80A7ECBA5FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/145259432/1_s2.0_S1053811918301800_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Duemose","key":"nielsenjesperduemosepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"72984c53-aee6-47e3-80d7-3f973e5aa18d","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Duemose","orcid":"0000-0003-3697-1012","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper D","key":"nielsenjesperdpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer Hougaard","key":"madsenkristofferhougaardpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"243ae993-e526-4121-b28a-aabf62c3df84","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8606-7641","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristoffer H","key":"madsenkristofferhpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Oula","key":"puontioulapau","last":"Puonti","locid":"c70fbf13-b1e6-439c-b87a-6b1ec682d60f","name":"Puonti, Oula","orcid":"0000-0003-3186-244X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hartwig R","key":"siebnerhartwigromanpau","last":"Siebner","locid":"d9ed8669-a16b-429a-86ed-353ef481bb72","name":"Siebner, Hartwig Roman","name_org":"Siebner, Hartwig R","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"bauerchristianpau","last":"Bauer","name":"Bauer, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla Gøbel","key":"madsencamillagøbelpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Camilla Gøbel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guilherme B","key":"saturninoguilhermebpau","last":"Saturnino","name":"Saturnino, Guilherme B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Axel","key":"thielscheraxelpau","last":"Thielscher","locid":"b7ae115c-6c5c-4457-b454-49b2dc26a0cd","name":"Thielscher, Axel","orcid":"0000-0002-4752-5854","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29518567"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neuroimage.2018.03.001","issn":["10538119","10959572"],"issn_org":["10538119"],"journal":"NeuroImage","pages":"587-598","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"NeuroImage","volume":"174"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043378835"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-229c633e-ede3-4437-b257-0a08e2c447b5","ku-933d452a-641c-48f6-8e00-48e21cee1003"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automatic skull segmentation from MR images for realistic volume conductor models of the head: Assessment of the state-of-the-art","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-033348","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"A family history of atrial fibrillation constitutes a substantial risk of developing the disease, however, the pathogenesis of this complex disease is poorly understood. We perform whole-exome sequencing on 24 families with at least three family members diagnosed with atrial fibrillation (AF) and find that titin-truncating variants (TTNtv) are significantly enriched in these patients (P = 1.76 × 10-6). This finding is replicated in an independent cohort of early-onset lone AF patients (n = 399; odds ratio = 36.8; P = 4.13 × 10-6). A CRISPR/Cas9 modified zebrafish carrying a truncating variant of titin is used to investigate TTNtv effect in atrial development. We observe compromised assembly of the sarcomere in both atria and ventricle, longer PR interval, and heterozygous adult zebrafish have a higher degree of fibrosis in the atria, indicating that TTNtv are important risk factors for AF. This aligns with the early onset of the disease and adds an important dimension to the understanding of the molecular predisposition for AF.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Ahlberg, Gustav","Refsgaard, Lena","Lundegaard, Pia R","Andreasen, Laura","Ranthe, Mattis F","Linscheid, Nora","Nielsen, Jonas B","Melbye, Mads","Haunsø, Stig","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Camp, Lu","Olesen, Søren-Peter","Rasmussen, Simon","Lundby, Alicia","Ellinor, Patrick T","Holst, Anders G","Svendsen, Jesper H","Olesen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036370"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Olesen, Morten S"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Broad Institute","Massachusetts General Hospital","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"OT":["The Lundbeck Foundation Centre for Applied Medical Genomics in Personalized Disease Prediction, Prevention and Care, Copenhagen, 2200 N, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rare truncating variants in the sarcomeric protein titin associate with familial and early onset atrial fibrillation","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-06618-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036370","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6193003","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85055120704","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30333491","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-a61f6e59-b3ab-49af-9f9f-31287827e8d4","ku-11c0e0fb-9a7c-438f-8650-96436515dccc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-15B987C41EA25030C2F384571BD58EFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/157789862/s41467_018_06618_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-06618-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209551337/Rare_truncating_variants_in_the_sarcomeric_protein_titin_associate_with_familial_and_early_onset_atrial_fibrillation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health