{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Microscopic colitis causes chronic watery diarrhoea and has previously been associated with the use of proton pump inhibitors. AIM: To explore the association between proton pump inhibitor use and microscopic colitis, including its dependency on timing, dose and choice of proton pump inhibitor. METHODS: Within a 10-year period, we identified 10 652 patients with a first-time diagnosis of microscopic colitis, including 6254 (59%) with collagenous colitis and 4398 (41%) with lymphocytic colitis. All microscopic colitis cases were histologically confirmed in the Danish Pathology Register. Information on proton pump inhibitor use was obtained from the Danish Prescription Register. In this case-control study, we estimated the adjusted odds ratios (aOR) for the association between proton pump inhibitor use and risk of microscopic colitis using conditional logistic regression while adjusting for potential confounders. RESULTS: We found strong associations between current proton pump inhibitor use and both collagenous colitis (aOR 6.98; 95% CI: 6.45-7.55) and lymphocytic colitis (aOR 3.95; 95% CI: 3.60-4.33). This association was observed with all PPIs. The strongest association was with the current use of lansoprazole for both collagenous colitis (aOR 15.74; 95% CI: 14.12-17.55) and lymphocytic colitis (aOR 6.87; 95% CI: 6.00-7.86). When considering timing, ORs were highest for current use of proton pump inhibitor and lower for recent or past exposure. No clear dose-response pattern was observed. CONCLUSIONS: We found a strong association between microscopic colitis and ongoing use of proton pump inhibitors, especially lansoprazole.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bonderup, Ole K","Nielsen, Gunnar Lauge","Dall, Michael","Pottegård, Anton","Hallas, Jesper"],"cuid":["S03-097.27-007918"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Bonderup, Ole K."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Diagnostic Centre, Regional Hospital Silkeborg, and University Research Clinic for Innovative Patient Pathways, Aarhus University, Aarhus, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"significant association between the use of different proton pump inhibitors and microscopic colitis a nationwide danish case control study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85050930359","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.27-007918","identifier":[{"id":"30039564","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85050930359","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000442338900004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-a3de92f6-b214-4e60-9086-505f15f82f1b","au-2f28ff04-aecf-4995-bc04-4f8b8b029ab0","sdu-4f648bbd-c21b-42d7-8f22-626f9c133540"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DD0AF3BDC8357E4212971E9B265E1AE5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Diagnostisk Center, Universitetsklinik for Innovative Patientforløb, Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Diagnostic Centre, Regional Hospital Silkeborg, and University Research Clinic for Innovative Patient Pathways, Aarhus University, Aarhus, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Medicinsk Afdeling, Farsø/Hobro/Thisted","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Medical Department"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole K","key":"bonderuppau","last":"Bonderup","locid":"3e60844b-3088-4834-9cec-bf43c73f3a19","name":"Bonderup, Ole Kristian","name_org":"Bonderup, Ole K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunnar L","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7e984c06-4032-4a3f-8fa7-fc532cb2549b","name":"Nielsen, Gunnar Lauge","name_org":"Nielsen, Gunnar L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"dallpau","last":"Dall","locid":"b8e03fd8-5db6-4f34-a888-1c3663878822","name":"Dall, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30039564"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apt.14916","issn":["02692813","09530673"],"issn_org":["02692813"],"issue":"6","journal":"Alimentary Pharmacology and Therapeutics","pages":"618-625","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Alimentary Pharmacology and Therapeutics","title_org":"Alimentary Pharmacology & Therapeutics","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050930359"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a3de92f6-b214-4e60-9086-505f15f82f1b","au-2f28ff04-aecf-4995-bc04-4f8b8b029ab0","sdu-4f648bbd-c21b-42d7-8f22-626f9c133540"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Significant association between the use of different proton pump inhibitors and microscopic colitis : A nationwide Danish case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.27-007918","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Chronic inflammatory diseases (CIDs) are frequently treated with biological medications, specifically tumour necrosis factor inhibitors (TNFi)). These medications inhibit the pro-inflammatory molecule TNF alpha, which has been strongly implicated in the aetiology of these diseases. Up to one-third of patients do not, however, respond to biologics, and lifestyle factors are assumed to affect treatment outcomes. Little is known about the effects of dietary lifestyle as a prognostic factor that may enable personalised medicine. The primary outcome of this multidisciplinary collaborative study will be to identify dietary lifestyle factors that support optimal treatment outcomes. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: This prospective cohort study will enrol 320 patients with CID who are prescribed a TNFi between June 2017 and March 2019. Included among the patients with CID will be patients with inflammatory bowel disease (Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis), rheumatic disorders (rheumatoid arthritis, axial spondyloarthritis, psoriatic arthritis), inflammatory skin diseases (psoriasis, hidradenitis suppurativa) and non-infectious uveitis. At baseline (pretreatment), patient characteristics will be assessed using patient-reported outcome measures, clinical assessments of disease activity, quality of life and lifestyle, in addition to registry data on comorbidity and concomitant medication(s). In accordance with current Danish standards, follow-up will be conducted 14-16 weeks after treatment initiation. For each disease, evaluation of successful treatment response will be based on established primary and secondary endpoints, including disease-specific core outcome sets. The major outcome of the analyses will be to detect variability in treatment effectiveness between patients with different lifestyle characteristics. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The principle goal of this project is to improve the quality of life of patients suffering from CID by providing evidence to support dietary and other lifestyle recommendations that may improve clinical outcomes. The study is approved by the Ethics Committee (S-20160124) and the Danish Data Protecting Agency (2008-58-035). Study findings will be disseminated through peer-reviewed journals, patient associations and presentations at international conferences. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT03173144; Pre-results.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Christensen, Robin","Heitmann, Berit L","Andersen, Karina Winther","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Sørensen, Signe Bek","Jawhara, Mohamad","Bygum, Anette","Hvid, Lone","Grauslund, Jakob","Wied, Jimmi","Glerup, Henning","Fredberg, Ulrich","Villadsen, Jan Alexander","Kjær, Søren Geill","Fallingborg, Jan","Moghadd, Seyed A G R","Knudsen, Torben","Brodersen, Jacob","Frøjk, Jesper","Dahlerup, Jens Frederik","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Thiel, Steffen","Færgeman, Nils J","Brandslund, Ivan","Bennike, Tue Bjerg","Stensballe, Allan","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Franke, Andre","Ellinghaus, David","Rosenstiel, Philip","Raes, Jeroen","Boye, Mette","Werner, Lars","Nielsen, Charlotte Lindgaard","Munk, Heidi Lausten","Nexøe, Anders Bathum","Ellingsen, Torkell","Holmskov, Uffe","Kjeldsen, Jens","Andersen, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S05-095.87-011719"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Vibeke"],"country":["Belgium","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Christian-Albrechts-University of Kiel","Kiel University","University of Leuven","VIB","Vlaams Instituut voor Biotechnologie (VIB)"],"keyword":["Ankylosing spondylitis","BOWEL DISEASE","Crohns disease","EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE COHORT","Food frequency questionnaire","Journal Article","LONG TERM INTAKE","Patient related outcome measures","Personalized medicine","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Rheumatoid arthritis","Short Health Scale","Sulfate reducing bacteria","Treatment Outcome","Ulcerative colitis","Western style diet","biomarker and lifestyle","lifestyle and chronic inflammatory disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Musculoskeletal Statistics Unit, The Parker Institute, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital, 2000 Frederiksberg, Denmark. Robin.Christensen@regionh.dk."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of red and processed meat and fibre intake on treatment outcomes among patients with chronic inflammatory diseases protocol for a prospective cohort study of prognostic factors and personalised medicine","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2017-018166","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S05-095.87-011719","identifier":[{"id":"85052169135","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29439003","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5829767","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000433129800163","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5829767","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f523cc00-4f53-4e58-b71f-8e26a9812c8b","au-34e6bcde-cd73-44c8-9813-81d33081ce41","ku-f22ff4e9-fcf9-4720-843c-3ce40e92ceef","sdu-f7121b29-dcb4-4f97-ba6f-fc7a6f8d2173","vive-84cc5722-2f63-4f5d-bd02-9457880a23a4"],"keyword":["ANKYLOSING-SPONDYLITIS","BOWEL-DISEASE","CROHNS-DISEASE","EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE COHORT","FOOD FREQUENCY QUESTIONNAIRE","Journal Article","LONG-TERM INTAKE","RHEUMATOID-ARTHRITIS","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","SHORT HEALTH SCALE","SULFATE-REDUCING BACTERIA","ULCERATIVE-COLIT