","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Impact of red and processed meat and fibre intake on treatment outcomes among patients with chronic inflammatory diseases: protocol for a prospective cohort study of prognostic factors and personalised medicine.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-095.87-011719","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present a measurement campaign conducted in forest terrain with focus on path-loss. The aim of the measurement campaign is to study the coverage in a Device-to-Device (D2D) communication scenario. The measurement campaign was conducted in the LTE band 8 at 917.5 MHz with measurement ranges extending to more than 2.5 km. The measurements have been conducted using a purpose-developed measurement system with a dynamic range of 180 dB. The measurements showed that a D2D system with transmit and receive antenna at heights of 1.5 m could achieve a range of approximately 2 km using the 164 dB path-loss limit specified for Narrow Band Internet-of-Things (NB-IoT).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hejselbæk, Johannes","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Drewes, Christian","Fan, Wei","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-052506"],"event":{"acronym":"EuCAP","end":"2018-04-13","place":"London, gb","start":"2018-04-09","title":"12th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Intel"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"propagation measurements for device to device communication in forest terrain","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266137349/EuCAP18_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-052506","identifier":[{"id":"85057316392","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-086bd49c-2620-4a23-9863-7b3ad964553e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F5F6128EE34EE792B35DF1860C160CB7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266137349/EuCAP18_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"intel","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Intel","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"hejselbækpau","last":"Hejselbæk","locid":"9163c39e-9747-4c12-bcb7-861a91af7c57","name":"Hejselbæk, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-3053-5474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"drewespau","last":"Drewes","name":"Drewes, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1049/cp.2018.0389","eisbn":["9781785618161"],"isbn":["9781785618154"],"publisher":"Institution of Engineering and Technology (IET)","status":"p","title":"12th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-086bd49c-2620-4a23-9863-7b3ad964553e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Propagation Measurements for Device-to-Device Communication in Forest Terrain","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052506","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The design of so-called sound zones is a fairly old idea which has recently gained some research attention. The idea is to control a loudspeaker array to reproduce a desired sound field in certain regions. In this paper, we show how the sound zone control problem can be solved using techniques from speech enhancement. Specifically, we first describe in detail the recently introduced variable span linear filtering (VSLF) framework which unifies the popular optimal filtering and subspace-based approaches to speech enhancement. We then show how the sound zone control problem can be solved using the VSLF framework and how a number of well-known sound zone control methods can be viewed as special cases of this solution. We also discuss in detail the differences between the speech enhancement problem and the sound zone control problem and argue that the VSLF framework is actually even better suited for controlling sound zones than for enhancing speech.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Lee, Taewoong","Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093297"],"event":{"end":"2018-10-31","place":"Pacific Grove, us","start":"2018-09-28","title":"Asilomar Conference on Signals, Systems and Computers (ACSSC 2018)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sound zones as an optimal filtering problem","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/297832680/master.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093297","identifier":[{"id":"85062958301","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-950e1f2b-f0a0-47f6-b64d-c5fd2c638b02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9437CF055D6EB3EE4EE0D824153C7095"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/297832680/master.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Taewoong","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","locid":"d1eeade6-8e75-427d-9c1f-1a4ac5464576","name":"Lee, Taewoong","orcid":"0000-0002-6669-0820","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/acssc.2018.8645268","eisbn":["9781538692165","9781538692172","9781538692196"],"isbn":["9781538692189"],"issn":["10586393"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Asilomar Conference on Signals, Systems and Computers. Conference Record","status":"p","title":"2018 52nd Asilomar Conference on Signals, Systems, and Computers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062958301"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-950e1f2b-f0a0-47f6-b64d-c5fd2c638b02"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sound Zones as an Optimal Filtering Problem","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093297","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"How can we design digital artefacts to help young adults with low self-esteem feel happier? To gain new insights into young adult’s self-esteem problems and how we might help support them with interactive technologies, we conducted a mixed method user-centred study. We used a 6-week cultural probe study with 11 young adults, including a focus group, to understand current practices in managing self-esteem with everyday technologies. We then co-designed interactive digital artefacts for helping improve self-esteem, to deploy as technology probes with 6 young adults for four weeks. Our contribution is two-fold. Firstly, we present the Self- Esteem Technology Support (SETS) framework for informing design of interactive technologies supporting young adults in managing low self-esteem. Secondly, we propose that interactive technologies designed to help young people feel happier need to be flexible, adaptable, private, available, personalisable, and have an engaging form factor to inspire feelings of fondness toward having the device as part of their daily routines.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Paay, Jeni","Nielsen, Heidi","Larsen, Helle Hyllested","Kjeldskov, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-110845"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","end":"2018-10-03","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2018-10-01","title":"NordiCHI 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Melbourne"],"keyword":["Cultural probes","Design workshop","Interaction design","Self esteem","Technology probes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"happy bits interactive technologies helping young adults with low self esteem","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/287214662/1104_paay.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-110845","identifier":[{"id":"85056607287","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d16ea40f-48de-410a-aabb-914fc28f7b6e"],"keyword":["Design workshop","Digital engagement","Technology probes","cultural probes","interaction design","self-esteem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D379E1F61BA6A5E285DCBB028B1AE334"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/287214662/1104_paay.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of melbourne","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Melbourne","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeni","key":"paaypau","last":"Paay","name":"Paay, Jeni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"771d2416-4af6-4dcd-8bb8-2e7cbd2abfa4","name":"Nielsen, Heidi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Hyllested","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c6d8ef4-51db-4986-ad03-057e0197469f","name":"Larsen, Helle Hyllested","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"kjeldskovpau","last":"Kjeldskov","locid":"90f5514b-34fa-4d01-98dd-ed6166dd1489","name":"Kjeldskov, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7990-4229","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3240167.3240180","isbn":["9781450364379"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '18 Proceedings of the 10th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056607287"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d16ea40f-48de-410a-aabb-914fc28f7b6e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Happy Bits: Interactive Technologies Helping Young Adults with Low Self-Esteem","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-110845","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Both massive multiple-input multiple-output (MIMO) technology and use of frequencies in the range 24–100 GHz are considered essential for upcoming 5G systems. Measurements of the new type of channels are needed, but this is challenging due to the large number of channels in massive MIMO and the short wavelength in the 24–100 GHz channels (so-called mmWave channels). This article describes a sounder system capable of measurements in both types of channels. While the same sounding system supports simultaneous massive MIMO and mmWave channels, the number of channels in each band and in total is in practice limited. For massive MIMO in the 300–6000 MHz band alone, arrays with up to 128 receiver (Rx) elements are possible, receiving from 16 independent mobile transmitter (Tx) antennas, where all channels are measured within 1.3 ms and in a 200 MHz bandwidth. To the authors knowledge, this is the first sounding system with this number of channels and a speed necessary for measuring the dynamic channels in typical application scenarios. For mmWave channels the sounder operates in the range 18–40 GHz. For these bands up to 2 Tx elements and 16 Rx elements can be measured. In addition, the paper describes some measurements in both a massive MIMO setup in an indoor sports arena and a mmWave setup with a handheld device containing a 7-element array.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Fan, Wei","Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-110971"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a channel sounder for massive mimo and mmwave channels","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/285308451/final_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-110971","identifier":[{"id":"85058453691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d1dfb779-903f-456b-a035-87578c650630"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B14DF76441DED35BE508A1233CABFC4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/285308451/final_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrick Claus F.","key":"eggerspau","last":"Eggers","locid":"f054cb97-cef9-4540-a4db-37441facf026","name":"Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","orcid":"0000-0002-2359-9779","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mcom.2018.1800199","issn":["01636804","15581896"],"issn_org":["01636804"],"issue":"12","journal":"IEEE Communications Magazine","pages":"67-73","paperid":"8570042","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Communications Magazine","title_org":"I E E E Communications Magazine","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058453691"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d1dfb779-903f-456b-a035-87578c650630"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Channel Sounder for Massive MIMO and mmWave Channels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-110971","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
