{"abstract":"n this paper, a numerical model is used to perform a robustness analysis of the bonding process of a joint between the two shells composing a wind turbine blade. The flow behaviour of the bonding adhesive is quantified on a rheometer and the Herschel-Bulkley material model is utilized to approximate the rheological data set. The material model parameters are implemented in the numerical model, which is validated by comparison with experimental results. The robustness analysis is focused on analysing the adhesive position and initial shape as well as the inclination angle's effect on the squeeze force and final adhesive geometry. The results illustrate that the numerical model can assist in increasing the strength of the joint, decreasing the risk of residual stress induced cracks, and minimizing cost/waste and mass of the blade.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Spangenberg, Jon","Uzal, Anil","Nielsen, M. W.","Hattel, Jesper Henri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319597"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Spangenberg, Jon"],"keyword":["Joints","Numerical modelling","Squeeze flow","Wind turbine blades"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LM","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robustness analysis of the bonding process of joints in wind turbine blades","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149728000/1_s2.0_S0143749618301647_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319597","identifier":[{"id":"85049740401","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3289a7f3-60c6-418a-837f-261339611238"],"keyword":["Herschel-Bulkley material model","Joints","Numerical modelling","Squeeze flow","Wind turbine blades"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30E2B57D1104F933F2EF56685B6EB2BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149728000/1_s2.0_S0143749618301647_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lm wind power","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LM","l3nn":"LM Wind Power","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LM Wind Power","namevar":["LM Wind Power"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J","key":"spangenbergpau","last":"Spangenberg","locid":"d6472dc2-035e-4d54-b7ee-96256e30814c","name":"Spangenberg, Jon","name_org":"Spangenberg, J","orcid":"0000-0002-5411-6821","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"uzalpau","last":"Uzal","locid":"a75282b6-6b9f-4bf6-9ac8-ff940ce5533a","name":"Uzal, Anil","name_org":"Uzal, A.","orcid":"0000-0001-8717-9813","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, M. W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. H.","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","name_org":"Hattel, J. H.","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijadhadh.2018.06.009","issn":["01437496","18790127"],"issn_org":["01437496"],"journal":"International Journal of Adhesion and Adhesives","pages":"281-285","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Adhesion and Adhesives","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049740401"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3289a7f3-60c6-418a-837f-261339611238"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A robustness analysis of the bonding process of joints in wind turbine blades","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319597","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"New product development processes are difficult to model as they are subject to high variability and are hard to monitor. In multi-project environments, one particular problem is to quantify the effects of changing the number of projects that run concurrently. In this paper, a closed queueing network model of the flow of projects in a product development system is presented. The model is evaluated using discrete-event simulation. Using a relation between a project’s monetary value and the time it spends in the system, an optimal number of concurrent projects is determined. Application of the model and results are shown for a case study of a Danish biotechnology company. Results show, that the value generated by the system can be increased by 17.5 percent by adjusting the total number of concurrent projects and by terminating low-value projects midway. Though the model is tailored to a specific system, it contains many features relevant for new product development systems in general.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Jesper Fink","Lauridsen, Carsten","Nielsen, Bo Friis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346273"],"event":{"end":"2018-12-19","place":"Bangkok, th","start":"2018-12-16","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Industrial Engineering and Engineering Management","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Jesper Fink"],"keyword":["Discrete event simulation","New product development","Project portfolio management","Time to market"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dimensioning a product development project portfolio using a closed queueing network","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85061823740","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346273","identifier":[{"id":"85061823740","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8bd0b565-47ba-406f-af0d-7b9be6685c2f"],"keyword":["Discrete-event simulation","Multi-project environment","New Product Development","Project Portfolio Management","Queueing network","Time-to-market"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9C23690ECA025DDA89BE39FC00F39526"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Fink","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b866063c-6bb9-4a46-8b75-8f054206f477","name":"Andersen, Jesper Fink","orcid":"0000-0002-3213-5853","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo Friis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"364b98b5-e608-4186-a566-62fa91a37d59","name":"Nielsen, Bo Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-9146-9733","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.