nk":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"omerzupedh","last":"Omerzu","name":"Omerzu, Heike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["05121604"],"pages":"163-180","place":"Tübingen","publisher":"Mohr Siebeck","series":"Wissenschaftliche Untersuchungen zum Neuen Testament","status":"p","title":"Rewriting and Reception in and of the Bible"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f6a2b944-576e-404e-885a-56368ee3a290"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Light to the Gentiles : The Reception of Isaiah in Luke-Acts","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-540656","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objectives Assisting patients in lifestyle change using collaborative e-health tools can be an efficient treatment for non-communicable diseases like diabetes, cardiovascular disease and chronic obstructive lung disease that are caused or aggravated by unhealthy living in the form of unhealthy diet, physical inactivity or tobacco smoking. In a prospective pilot study, we tested an online collaborative e-health tool in general practice. The aim of this study was to identify drivers of importance for long-term personal lifestyle changes from a patient perspective when using a collaborative e-health tool, including the support of peers and healthcare professionals. Setting General practice clinics in the Region of Southern Denmark. Participants 10 overweight patients who had previously successfully used a hybrid online collaborative e-health tool with both face-to-face and online consultations to lose weight. Results The main themes identified were facilitators, barriers and support from family and peers. Establishment of a trustworthy relationship with the healthcare professionals was of paramount importance. It was important for the patients to monitor the measurable outcomes with realistic goals and feedback from a trusted person. Often, significant life events were identified as catalysts for successful long-term lifestyle changes. Dominant barriers to change were perception of insurmountable obstacles, experience of lack of self-efficacy and excess eating of high-calorie food. Finally, experiencing of trustworthy person-to-person forums, need for acknowledgement from referent others and support from family and peers were important drivers for long-term lifestyle change. Conclusion The most important driver in long-term weight loss was a strong relationship with a healthcare professional. Collaborative e-health tools can support the relationship and behavioural changes through monitoring and providing relevant feedback. The support from family and peers also matters, and long-term success depends on the ability to establish strong, positive support on a day-to-day basis.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Brandt, Carl Joakim","Clemensen, Jane","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-581986"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Clemensen, Jane"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark","Diet","Exercise","Female","Health Knowledge Attitudes Practice","Humans","Internet","Interviews as Topic","Male","Middle Aged","Overweight prevention control","Pilot Projects","Prospective Studies","Qualitative Research","Risk Reduction Behavior","Telemedicine","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drivers for successful long term lifestyle change the role of e health a qualitative interview study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2017-017466","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-581986","identifier":[{"id":"29530904","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044189709","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5857693","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-1ea0ad4b-1539-4a4e-b14d-edd46603432a"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark","Diet","Exercise","Female","Health Knowledge, Attitudes, Practice","Humans","Internet","Interviews as Topic","Male","Middle Aged","Overweight/prevention & control","Pilot Projects","Prospective Studies","Qualitative Research","Risk Reduction Behavior","Telemedicine","Weight Loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A68A0F14ADE92848D3F8B65687AC7957"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2017-017466","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/137901441/Drivers_for_successful_long_term_lifestyle_change_the_role_of_e_health.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carl Joakim","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"75a8dd44-4449-4163-96e5-37499194768e","name":"Brandt, Carl Joakim","orcid":"0000-0002-3268-0595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"clemensenpau","last":"Clemensen","locid":"1a64bd2f-c3d5-4006-86ac-7e0620155800","name":"Clemensen, Jane","orcid":"0000-0002-6127-1010","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29530904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2017-017466","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"3","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e017466","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044189709"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1ea0ad4b-1539-4a4e-b14d-edd46603432a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Drivers for successful long-term lifestyle change, the role of e-health : A qualitative interview study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-581986","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Energy poverty is widespread in island countries, especially for the low-income countries. It is around 70% households in the Pacific island countries do not have access to electricity. With the fast development of renewable technologies, feasible and cost-efficient microgrid solutions are expected to mitigate this issue. This paper uses Indonesia as an example to investigate, develop and evaluate the potential microgrid solutions for the remote islands. There are six potential microgrid solutions are discussed, and two solutions (photovoltaic cells and storage; diesel generator, photovoltaic cells, and battery) are evaluated and identified as the most feasible, cheapest, and green solutions for the remote island microgrids.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ma, Zheng","Santos, Athila Quaresma","Gamborg, Filip","Fischer Nielsen, Jesper","Meinhard Johannesen, Johan","Jensen, Maria Dahl Hedegaard","Pedersen, Morten Ratzer","Jørgensen, Bo Nørregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584130"],"event":{"acronym":"ISGT NA","end":"2018-05-25","place":"Singapore, sg","start":"2018-05-22","title":"The International Conference on Innovative Smart Grid Technologies (IEEE PES ISGT Asia 2018)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energy system","Island microgrid","Microgrid Solution","remote island"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"solutions for remote island microgrids discussion and analysis of indonesia s remote island energy system","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055504499","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584130","identifier":[{"id":"85055504499","type":"sc