corresponding":null,"first":"Lars J","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"e5cf5f25-4cff-407e-9c25-97921d98a7bc","name":"Petersen, Lars Jelstrup","name_org":"Petersen, Lars J","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29876619"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-018-4058-4","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"11","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"1884-1897","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048054457"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6a42d9a3-8f5d-479d-8910-28c623105f73","au-d51b21d7-3cc5-454e-880d-81e9c3e0a7ad"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prospective comparison of <sup>68</sup>Ga-PSMA PET/CT, <sup>18</sup>F-sodium fluoride PET/CT and diffusion weighted-MRI at for the detection of bone metastases in biochemically recurrent prostate cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.05-005152","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: The aims of this study are two-fold: 1) To explore how cardiac patients experience their use of a telerehabilitation tool for recuperation from surgery, and 2) To study how the patients’ use of the interactive ‘Active Heart’ web portal affected their eHealth literacy skills. Methods: The ‘Active Heart’ telerehabilitation web portal offers patients and their relatives information and exercises for recovery from cardiac surgery. 109 cardiac patients were using the Active Heart web portal for a duration of three months. Results: 49 patients completed questionnaires that were administered both before and after their use of the portal, resulting in a 45% response rate. Respondents had a mean age of 60.64 ± 10.75 years, and 82% of the respondents were males. The respondents had a positive impression of Active Heart, reporting that it was easy to access, user-friendly, and written in an understandable language. The patients’ eHealth literacy skills increased during the trial period. Conclusion: Use of a cardiac telerehabilitation web portal can be beneficial for patient education and can increase cardiac patients’ eHealth literacy skills. Practice implications: Online telerehabilitation portals may be used as a tool in patient education and cardiac rehabilitation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Melholt, Camilla","Jønsson, Katrine","Spindler, Helle","Hansen, John","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Nielsen, Gitte","Nørgaard, Astrid Clausen","Tracey, Anita","Thorup, Charlotte Brun","Kringelholt, Rikke","Dinesen, Birthe"],"cuid":["S02-096.31-011141"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Melholt, Camilla"],"keyword":["Cardiac diseases","Patient education","Rehabilitation","Tele rehabilitation","eHealth literacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiac patients experiences with a telerehabilitation web portal implications for ehealth literacy","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85039807625&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.31-011141","identifier":[{"id":"29305064","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85039807625","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e9212f0c-9ccf-4db7-ab4f-2d471715e1b0","au-5ee2b8b8-fb6e-4b49-a365-4a3e2d80dcde"],"keyword":["Cardiac diseases","EHealth literacy","Patient education","Rehabilitation","Tele-rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5D4C390F163F6E4082FCBF9FE82F6D5E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["The North Denmark Region"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"melholtpau","last":"Melholt","locid":"af72a55a-7f9f-42ec-96e5-7020233c5b2e","name":"Melholt, Camilla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"jønssonpau","last":"Jønsson","locid":"f83d17bf-e735-4fb7-b1c6-0f33f87f7811","name":"Jønsson, Katrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"spindlerpau","last":"Spindler","locid":"c95c8b19-e4d8-4f11-acca-5212a92f3db9","name":"Spindler, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-7098-5699","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ae89da32-d0ea-4a39-8295-a7cc351013f6","name":"Hansen, John","orcid":"0000-0003-4989-8117","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Jesper","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"64f82f01-dc7b-4ed4-873a-940774d8921e","name":"Andreasen, Jan Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-2382-3734","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid Clausen","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"9f12f4a3-c184-4cb5-a147-090eb54778f2","name":"Nørgaard, Astrid Clausen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"traceypau","last":"Tracey","locid":"6bdaf7a0-94a6-46e1-890a-4f3dd2af14fa","name":"Tracey, Anita","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Brun","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"90bf6dfd-49cd-42dc-a945-c22f8561c981","name":"Thorup, Charlotte Brun","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"kringelholtpau","last":"Kringelholt","name":"Kringelholt, Rikke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birthe Irene","key":"dinesenpau","last":"Dinesen","locid":"22de2dad-03e3-4bc9-8d55-94736e7d5941","name":"Dinesen, Birthe","name_org":"Dinesen, Birthe Irene","orcid":"0000-0001-5893-9676","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29305064"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.pec.2017.12.017","issn":["07383991","18735134"],"issn_org":["07383991"],"issue":"5","journal":"Patient Education and Counseling","pages":"854-861","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Patient Education and Counseling","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039807625"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e9212f0c-9ccf-4db7-ab4f-2d471715e1b0","au-5ee2b8b8-fb6e-4b49-a365-4a3e2d80dcde"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cardiac patients’ experiences with a telerehabilitation web portal : Implications for eHealth literacy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.31-011141","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To assess the live-versus-video, intrarater interday and interrater interday reliability of the test Segmental Assessment of Trunk Control (SATCo), which seeks to estimate the degree of sitting trunk control in children with cerebral palsy (CP). Method: Thirty-one children with CP between 9 months and 16 years of age (22 males, mean age 8y 10mo [SD 3y 5mo], Gross Motor Function Classification System level I [n = 13], II [n = 4], III [n = 4], IV [n = 3], and V [n = 7]) were included. Children were tested twice by two raters and tests were video recorded. Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test, ICC [2,1] and a descriptive measure for absolute reliability were applied. Results: No systematic differences were found between live-versus-video, between raters or days (p > 0.05) except for one analysis. All ICC values were excellent (ICC ≥ 0.9) except for one analysis for which it was good (ICC = 0.73). Complete agreement between scores was seen in 75% of all cases while 22% differed by one segmental level. Only 3% showed disagreement above one segmental level. Conclusions: SATCo is a clinically applicable assessment tool. Relative reliability is excellent and absolute agreement is good. Modifications regarding testing method could potentially improve the reliability and the value of the test in research and in clinical practice.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Lisbeth","Erhardsen, Katrine Thingholm","Bencke, Jesper","Magnusson, S. Peter","Curtis, Derek John"],"cuid":["S02-096.75-038843"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","Children","Physiotherapy","Reliability"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the reliability of the segmental assessment of trunk control satco in children with cerebral palsy","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85026357642","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.75-038843","identifier":[{"id":"85026357642","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28749721","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["kp-50254053-2cd7-47c0-9e5c-e8ebd348eadd","ku-a57a128a-7980-4b99-b247-a9517242bcbb"],"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","SATCo","children","physiotherapy","reliability","trunk control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-53B23904C3E0B84BCAF1A5AE9084E366"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Skovly","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2ae7c2d6-d0cb-45b8-85e7-89647a9e323c","name":"Nielsen, Lisbeth Skovly","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Thingholm","key":"erhardsenpau","last":"Erhardsen","locid":"c743c00c-e87d-4830-ab8b-644c4e3b1008","name":"Erhardsen, Katrine Thingholm","orcid":"0000-0001-6527-8853","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"benckepau","last":"Bencke","name":"Bencke, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Stig Peter","key":"magnussonpau","last":"Magnusson","locid":"6f430caa-ac01-4dfe-9a62-e3a49afba21a","name":"Magnusson, S. Peter","name_org":"Magnusson, Stig Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Derek John","key":"curtispau","last":"Curtis","locid":"42b0cd41-9c5b-4d8c-854c-b65829b3e27f","name":"Curtis, Derek John","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28749721"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01942638.2017.1337662","issn":["01942638","15413144"],"issn_org":["01942638"],"issue":"3","journal":"Physical and Occupational Therapy in Pediatrics","pages":"291-304","status":"p","title":"Physical and Occupational Therapy in Pediatrics","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026357642"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-50254053-2cd7-47c0-9e5c-e8ebd348eadd","ku-a57a128a-7980-4b99-b247-a9517242bcbb"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Reliability of the Segmental Assessment of Trunk Control (SATCo) in Children with Cerebral Palsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.75-038843","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The purpose of the present controlled cross-sectional study was to investigate proximal femur and whole-body bone mineral density (BMD), as well as bone turnover profile, in lifelong trained elderly male football players and young elite football players compared with untrained age-matched men. Methods: One hundred and forty healthy, non-smoking men participated in the study, including lifelong trained football players (FTE, n = 35) aged 65-80 years, elite football players (FTY, n = 35) aged 18-30 years, as well as untrained age-matched elderly (UE, n = 35) and young (UY, n = 35) men. All participants underwent a regional Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry (DXA) scan of the proximal femur and a whole-body DXA scan to determine BMD. From a resting blood sample, the bone turnover markers (BTMs) osteocalcin, carboxy-terminal type-1 collagen crosslinks (CTX-1), procollagen type-1 amino-terminal propeptide (P1NP), and sclerostin were measured.  Results: FTE had 7.3%-12.9% higher (p <. 0.05) BMD of the femoral neck, wards, shaft, and total proximal femur in both legs compared to UE, and 9.3%-9.7% higher (p <. 0.05) BMD in femoral trochanter in both legs compared to UY. FTY had 24.3%-37.4% higher (p <. 0.001) BMD in all femoral regions and total proximal femur in both legs compared to UY. The whole-body DXA scan confirmed these results, with FTE showing similar whole-body BMD and 7.9% higher (p <. 0.05) leg BMD compared to UY, and with FTY having 9.6% higher (p <. 0.001) whole-body BMD and 18.2% higher (p <. 0.001) leg BMD compared to UY. The plasma concentration of osteocalcin, CTX-1, and P1NP were 29%, 53%, and 52% higher (p <. 0.01), respectively, in FTY compared to UY.  Conclusion: BMD of the proximal femur and whole-body BMD are markedly higher in lifelong trained male football players aged 65-80 years and young elite football players aged 18-30 years compared to age-matched untrained men. Elderly football players even show higher BMD in femoral trochanter and leg BMD than untrained young despite an age difference of 47 years.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hagman, Marie","Helge, Eva Wulff","Hornstrup, Therese","Fristrup, Bjørn","Nielsen, Jens Jung","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Andersen, Jesper Løvind","Helge, Jørn Wulff","Krustrup, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-098.65-044697"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Bone mass","Bone turnover markers","Dual energy X ray absorptiometry","Proximal femur bone mineral density","Soccer","Whole body bone mineral density"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone mineral density in lifelong trained male football players compared with young and elderly untrained men","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jshs.2017.09.009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.65-044697","identifier":[{"id":"30356456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85038405800","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6180542","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9ac6c492-3d63-4005-998f-c12600d681ea","sdu-a57b3f2b-4b3a-49f1-9007-92af5ecd13b2"],"keyword":["Bone mass","Bone turnover markers","Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry","Proximal femur bone mineral density","Soccer","Whole-body bone mineral density"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FD6BC86580490D2288EAF08BD705621E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://