{"abstract":"An exciting recent line of work has focused on formally investigating the core cryptographic assumptions underlying the security of Bitcoin. In a nutshell, these works conclude that Bitcoin is secure if and only if the majority of the mining power is honest. Despite their great impact, however, these works do not address an incisive question asked by positivists and Bitcoin critics, which is fuelled by the fact that Bitcoin indeed works in reality: Why should the real-world system adhere to these assumptions? In this work we employ the machinery from the Rational Protocol Design (RPD) framework by Garay et al. [FOCS 2013] to analyze Bitcoin and address questions such as the above. We show that under the natural class of incentives for the miners’ behavior—i.e., rewarding them for adding blocks to the blockchain but having them pay for mining—we can reserve the honest majority assumption as a fallback, or even, depending on the application, completely replace it by the assumption that the miners aim to maximize their revenue. Our results underscore the appropriateness of RPD as a “rational cryptography” framework for analyzing Bitcoin. Along the way, we devise significant extensions to the original RPD machinery that broaden its applicability to cryptocurrencies, which may be of independent interest.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Badertscher, Christian","Garay, Juan","Maurer, Ueli","Tschudi, Daniel","Zikas, Vassilis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-261810"],"event":{"acronym":"EUROCRYPT","end":"2018-05-03","place":"Tel Aviv, il","start":"2018-04-29","title":"EUROCRYPT 2018 - 37th Annual International Conference on the Theory and Applications of Cryptographic Techniques","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","Texas A and M University","University of Edinburgh"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"but why does it work a rational protocol design treatment of bitcoin","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045901209","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-261810","identifier":[{"id":"85045901209","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e82560d1-fa94-4502-8974-dd6f329f3f47"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50DCB16D2FA1497EB358A8F0399B3B2F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"texas a and m university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Texas A and M University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"badertscherpau","last":"Badertscher","name":"Badertscher, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan","key":"garaypau","last":"Garay","name":"Garay, Juan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ueli","key":"maurerpau","last":"Maurer","name":"Maurer, Ueli","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"tschudipau","last":"Tschudi","locid":"0ee91524-821e-4add-bb6d-ca09a03888d5","name":"Tschudi, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Vassilis","key":"zikaspau","last":"Zikas","name":"Zikas, Vassilis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"buusnielsenpedh","last":"Buus Nielsen","name":"Buus Nielsen, Jesper","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-78375-8_2","issn":["03029743"],"issue":"10821","pages":"34-65","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advances in Cryptology - EUROCRYPT 2018 - 37th Annual International Conference on the Theory and Applications of Cryptographic Techniques, 2018 Proceedings","volume":"10821"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045901209"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e82560d1-fa94-4502-8974-dd6f329f3f47"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"But Why Does It Work? : A Rational Protocol Design Treatment of Bitcoin","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-261810","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The overall goal of the project is to stimulate decision-makers in Belarus to prioritize abatement measures aimed at black carbon in their efforts to reduce emissions of PM2.5, as encouraged in the Gothenburg protocol under the UNECE CLRTAP. To reach this purpose and in order to build up scientific basis necessary for further policy development, a comprehensive analysis of PM2.5 and BC emissions, emission reduction potentials and cost-effective abatement measures in Belarus has been conducted. The report presents two main parts of the conducted analysis: a part focused on the emission inventories, and a part summarizing the results of the integrated assessment modelling. The main focus is on analysis for Belarus; however, a range of modelling results have been obtained for the three participating Nordic countries – Denmark, Finland and Sweden.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kakareka, Sergey","Malchykhina, Hanna","Krukowskaya, Olga","Yaramenka, Katarina","Kindbom, Karin","Mawdsley, Ingrid","Åström, Stefan","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Bak, Jesper Leth","Saarinen, Kristina","Savolahti, Mikko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-270529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Environment Institute","Svenska Miljoeinstitutet AB (IVL)"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"particle emissions in belarus and in the nordic countries emission inventories and integrated assessment modelling of black carbon and pm000000000002 000000000005","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6027/TN2018-544","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-270529","ids":["au-f78de79c-c609-40d6-8696-53d5f239f86e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-662F7C4274F40EE824F466F78CC2DC79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6027/TN2018-544","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://norden.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1252388/FULLTEXT01.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"svenska miljoeinstitutet ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Svenska Miljoeinstitutet AB (IVL)","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Emission modeling & environmental geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"finnish environment institute","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Environment Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergey","key":"kakarekapau","last":"Kakareka","name":"Kakareka, Sergey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna","key":"malchykhinapau","last":"Malchykhina","name":"Malchykhina, Hanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"krukowskayapau","last":"Krukowskaya","name":"Krukowskaya, Olga","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katarina","key":"yaramenkapau","last":"Yaramenka","name":"Yaramenka, Katarina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"kindbompau","last":"Kindbom","name":"Kindbom, Karin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid","key":"mawdsleypau","last":"Mawdsley","name":"Mawdsley, Ingrid","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"åströmpau","last":"Åström","name":"Åström, Stefan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole-Kenneth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marlene Schmidt","key":"plejdruppau","last":"Plejdrup","locid":"9dede80b-ff3e-4171-9504-bf8547fec74d","name":"Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Leth","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"72bda0b4-7b42-48eb-beb7-564a18e9a1d6","name":"Bak, Jesper Leth","orcid":"0000-0001-7610-7662","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"saarinenpau","last":"Saarinen","name":"Saarinen, Kristina","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"savolahtipau","last":"Savolahti","name":"Savolahti, Mikko","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.6027/tn2018-544","isbn":["9789289357661"],"pages":"110","publisher":"Nordic Council of Ministers","status":"p","volume":"544"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f78de79c-c609-40d6-8696-53d5f239f86e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Particle emissions in Belarus and in the Nordic countries : Emission inventories and integrated assessment modelling of black carbon and PM2.5","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-270529","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Cities worldwide are implementing modern transit systems to improve mobility in the increasingly congested metropolitan areas. Despite much research on the effects of such systems, a comparison of effects across transit modes and countries has not been studied comprehensively. This paper fills this gap in the literature by reviewing and comparing the effects obtained by 86 transit systems around the world, including Bus Rapid Transit (BRT), Light Rail Transit (LRT), metro and heavy rail transit systems. The analysis is twofold by analysing (i) the direct operational effects related to travel time, ridership and modal shifts, and (ii) the indirect strategic effects in terms of effects on property values and urban development. The review confirms the existing literature suggesting that BRT can attract many passengers if travel time reductions are significantly high. This leads to attractive areas surrounding the transit line with increasing property values. Such effects are traditionally associated with attractive rail-based public transport systems. However, a statistical comparison of 41 systems did not show significant deviations between effects on property values resulting from BRT, LRT and metro systems, respectively. Hence, this paper indicates that large strategic effects can be obtained by implementing BRT systems at a much lower cost.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-312186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of new bus and rail rapid transit systems an international review","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131599819/Paper_1_v10_full_rev2_v6_final_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-312186","identifier":[{"id":"85015966340","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1959e09b-b41a-4644-b3fa-766514fa5037"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D8619DD936780A0CB2C2AA83327B04DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131599819/Paper_1_v10_full_rev2_v6_final_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01441647.2017.1301594","issn":["01441647","14645327"],"issn_org":["01441647"],"issue":"1","journal":"Transport Reviews","pages":"96-116","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Transport Reviews","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015966340"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1959e09b-b41a-4644-b3fa-766514fa5037"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effects of new bus and rail rapid transit systems – an international review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-312186","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Bayesian integrated data analysis combines measurements from different diagnostics to jointly measure plasma parameters of interest such as temperatures, densities, and drift velocities. Integrated data analysis of fast-ion measurements has long been hampered by the complexity of the strongly non-Maxwellian fast-ion distribution functions. This has recently been overcome by velocity-space tomography. In this method two-dimensional images of the velocity distribution functions consisting of a few hundreds or thousands of pixels are reconstructed using the available fast-ion measurements. Here we present an overview and current status of this emerging technique at the ASDEX Upgrade tokamak and the JET toamak based on fast-ion D-alpha spectroscopy, collective Thomson scattering, gamma-ray and neutron emission spectrometry, and neutral particle analyzers. We discuss Tikhonov regularization within the Bayesian framework. The implementation for different types of diagnostics as well as the uncertainties are discussed, and we highlight the importance of integrated data analysis of all available detectors.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Salewski, Mirko","Nocente, M.","Jacobsen, A.S.","Binda, F.","Cazzaniga, C.","Eriksson, J.","Geiger, B.","Gorini, G.","Hellesen, C.","Kiptily, V. G.","Koskela, T.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Kurki-Suonio, T.","Leipold, Frank","Moseev, D.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Schneider, P. A.","Sharapov, S. E.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardocchi, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Salewski, Mirko"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Italy","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Research Council of Italy","Rutherford Appleton Laboratory","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Milan - Bicocca","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Fast ions","Tokamaks","Velocity space tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bayesian integrated data analysis of fast ion measurements by velocity space tomography","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196393991/salewski2018fst_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356286","identifier":[{"id":"85048105479","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ad22cd67-eef2-4f72-ab16-cb43ef36259c"],"keyword":["Fast ions","Tokamaks","Velocity-space tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-261266517D74184DF943E70145CD3CC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196393991/salewski2018fst_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of milan bicocca","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan - Bicocca","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"4","co