{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Hjelm, Ingrid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393841"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the coming of a prophet like you in ancient literature","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-393841","ids":["ku-009fe36e-9e7d-49a7-965e-b56dfef71cd0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-88E989EDB2067B7E7A003DAE648E9BFE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ingrid","key":"hjelmpau","last":"Hjelm","locid":"a39c5568-0635-4471-ae91-bb3ae06699a5","name":"Hjelm, Ingrid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"høgenhavenpedh","last":"Høgenhaven","name":"Høgenhaven, Jesper","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"omerzupedh","last":"Omerzu","name":"Omerzu, Heike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783161550065"],"issn":["05121604"],"pages":"33-48","place":"Tübingen","publisher":"Mohr Siebeck","series":"Wissenschaftliche Untersuchungen zum Neuen Testament","status":"p","title":"Rewriting and Reception in and out of the Bible."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-009fe36e-9e7d-49a7-965e-b56dfef71cd0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Coming of ‘a Prophet Like You’ in Ancient Literature","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-393841","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"‘Revocability’ is obviously the opposite of ‘irrevocability,’ but if we are only talking about a starting point amended by significant exceptions, it hardly much matters where we start (and end). If, to take a different example, we translate ‘unconscionable’ as ‘unreasonable’ (for lack of a better corresponding term), that would gloss over important substantive differences at the domestic level, perhaps also leading the way to inappropriate conclusions in an international ‘impracticability’ context. So, what makes the greatest impression, the common core or the differences? Maybe it depends on the direction in which we’re headed ... or on where we’re coming from.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lookofsky, Joseph"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-403092"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revocability unconscionability and impracticability in american danish and international law","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3487520","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-403092","ids":["ku-104a8170-867c-46ee-9dc3-7ea627d32c44"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F94E53C3204E36452781CAF2796EE73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3487520","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Faculty of Law Research Centres"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joseph","key":"lookofskypau","last":"Lookofsky","locid":"f4b59e6e-04ab-448b-b160-5e9ae7e7664e","name":"Lookofsky, Joseph","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"udsenpedh","last":"Udsen","name":"Udsen, Henrik","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"schanschristensenpedh","last":"Schans Christensen","name":"Schans Christensen, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"lauhansenpedh","last":"Lau Hansen","name":"Lau Hansen, Jesper","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Torsten","key":"iversenpedh","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Torsten","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Linda","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788757441130"],"pages":"575-591","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p","title":"Festskrift til Mads Bryde Andersen"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-104a8170-867c-46ee-9dc3-7ea627d32c44"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Revocability, Unconscionability and Impracticability in American, Danish and International Law","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-403092","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Rosenmeier, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415594"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"projekt jurabog ophavsretlige udfordringer og muligheder","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-415594","ids":["ku-25242384-b744-4fa3-85cd-64f431f5c3eb"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7942025FE8D8258498CCECD4EF285C11"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre for Information and Innovation Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"rosenmeierpau","last":"Rosenmeier","locid":"54c2d78b-ede1-4107-beea-6485375dde8a","name":"Rosenmeier, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"udsenpedh","last":"Udsen","name":"Udsen, Henrik","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Schans","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jan Schans","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Lau","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper Lau","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Torsten","key":"iversenpedh","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Torsten","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Linda","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788757441130"],"pages":"83-100","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p","title":"Festskrift til Mads Bryde Andersen"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-25242384-b744-4fa3-85cd-64f431f5c3eb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Projekt Jurabog. Ophavsretlige udfordringer og muligheder","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415594","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Cell-enriched fat grafting has shown promising results for improving graft survival, although many questions remain unanswered. A large animal model is crucial for bridging the gap between rodent studies and human trials. We present a step-by-step approach in using the Göttingen minipig as a model for future studies of cell-enriched large volume fat grafting. Methods: Fat grafting was performed as bolus injections and structural fat grafting. Graft retention was assessed by magnetic resonance imaging after 120 days. The stromal vascular fraction (SVF) was isolated from excised fat and liposuctioned fat from different anatomical sites and analyzed. Porcine adipose-derived stem/stromal cells (ASCs) were cultured in different growth supplements, and population doubling time, maximum cell yield, expression of surface markers, and differentiation potential were investigated. Results: Structural fat grafting in the breast and subcutaneous bolus grafting in the abdomen revealed average graft retention of 53.55% and 15.28%, respectively, which are similar to human reports. Liposuction yielded fewer SVF cells than fat excision, and abdominal fat had the most SVF cells/g fat with SVF yields similar to humans. Additionally, we demonstrated that porcine ASCs can be readily isolated and expanded in culture in allogeneic porcine platelet lysate and fetal bovine serum and that the use of 10% porcine platelet lysate or 20% fetal bovine serum resulted in population doubling time, maximum cell yield, surface marker profile, and trilineage differentiation that were comparable with humans. Conclusions: The Göttingen minipig is a feasible and cost-effective, large animal model for future translational studies of cell-enriched fat grafting.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Bo S.","Sørensen, Celine L.","Vester-Glowinski, Peter","Herly, Mikkel","Kurbegovic, Sorel","Ørholt, Mathias","Svalgaard, Jesper D.","Kølle, Stig Frederik T.","Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","Talman, Maj-Lis Møller","Drzewiecki, Krzysztof T.","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425884"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel porcine model for future studies of cell enriched fat grafting","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/GOX.0000000000001735","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-425884","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5977937","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85053867572","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29876178","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-36953fcf-48ae-47bf-a687-a11c8b837101"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1CEBBDA578688F094C28D35B0C235BD3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/GOX.0000000000001735","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/215872123/A_Novel_Porcine_Model_for_Future_Studies_of.13.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Bo S.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Bo S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Celine L.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Celine L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter V.","key":"vesterglowinskipau","last":"Vester-Glowinski","locid":"ff170014-afd2-40eb-892a-9bb0a75d1365","name":"Vester-Glowinski, Peter","name_org":"Vester-Glowinski, Peter V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"herlypau","last":"Herly","name":"Herly, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sorel","key":"kurbegovicpau","last":"Kurbegovic","name":"Kurbegovic, Sorel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias","key":"ørholtpau","last":"Ørholt","name":"Ørholt, Mathias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper D.","key":"svalgaardpau","last":"Svalgaard","name":"Svalgaard, Jesper D.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stig Frederik T.","key":"køllepau","last":"Kølle","locid":"af3f9bcd-d46e-4d8a-9d68-1a9297381ed9","name":"Kølle, Stig Frederik T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Annemarie T.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","name_org":"Kristensen, Annemarie T.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maj Lis M.","key":"talmanpau","last":"Talman","locid":"6645d585-9ef3-4f81-9af3-8baf4e9d8fdf","name":"Talman, Maj-Lis Møller","name_org":"Talman, Maj Lis M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Krzysztof T.","key":"drzewieckipau","last":"Drzewiecki","locid":"f69cac2a-d092-4294-bd80-e2fc75165ea4","name":"Drzewiecki, Krzysztof T.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","locid":"af37e8db-0c68-4da1-9b25-5625d241b9ca","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29876178"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/gox.0000000000001735","issn":["21697574"],"issue":"4","journal":"Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery - Global Open","paperid":"e1735","status":"p","title":"Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery - Global Open","title_org":"Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery, Global Open","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053867572"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-36953fcf-48ae-47bf-a687-a11c8b837101"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A novel porcine model for future studies of cell-enriched fat grafting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425884","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background and Objectives: Research has shown that dual sensory loss is a risk factor for depression in older adults. However, validated measures of depression for people with dual sensory loss are lacking. The purpose of the present study was to investigate the construct validity and reliability of the Major Depression Inventory for use among elderly persons with acquired dual sensory loss. Research Design and Methods:  A cross-sectional questionnaire survey was conducted in a national sample of people ≥50 years of age with functional acquired dual sensory loss. Of the invited participants, 302 (66%) returned the questionnaire and 207 complete cases were included for analysis. Rasch models and graphical log-linear Rasch models were used for item analysis. Lack of differential item functioning was tested relative to severity of vision and hearing impairment, mode of questionnaire completion, age, sex, comorbidity, instrumental activities of daily living, social position, and cohabitation status. Results:  The 10-item Major Depression Inventory did not fit the Rasch model. An 8-item version, excluding the items “feeling sad” and “sleep problems,” fit a graphical log-linear Rasch model. No evidence of differential item functioning was discovered, thus the 8-item Major Depression Inventory was measurement invariant across severity of impairments and mode of completing the questionnaire. The overall reliability was 0.81 and ranged from acceptable to good for all subgroups of participants, except males with severe hearing impairment and low functional status. Consequently, the 8-item version of the Major Depression Inventory was considered construct valid and reliable within the frame of reference. Discussion and Implications: An 8-item version of the Major Depression Inventory can be used to screen for depressive symptoms in elderly persons with acquired dual sensory loss.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hovaldt, Hanna Birkbak","Nielsen, Tine","Dammeyer, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503969"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Disabilities","Faculty of Social Sciences","Psychometrics","Vision"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity and reliability of the major depression inventory for persons with dual sensory loss","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/geroni/igy010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-503969","identifier":[{"id":"85101201201","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30480134","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6177090","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b92a7493-a550-4974-923b-68ed58176da2"],"keyword":["Depression and anxiety","Disabilities","Faculty of Social Sciences","Psychometrics","Vision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8CD0DE502CCE14C440C296A525842A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/210832467/igy010.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/geroni/igy010","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Department of Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hanna Birkbak","key":"hovaldtpau","last":"Hovaldt","locid":"bffd9afc-154c-4421-9e14-6be62cdc4ffe","name":"Hovaldt, Hanna Birkbak","orcid":"0000-0002-9478-6985","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"14fb3295-de48-4f81-b80e-125cb666ad07","name":"Nielsen, Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-9087-729X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"dammeyerpau","last":"Dammeyer","locid":"4e00d381-dd0b-4b42-a335-652388c7f73b","name":"Dammeyer, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30480134"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/geroni/igy010","issn":["23995300"],"issue":"1","journal":"Innovation in Aging","pages":"1-11","paperid":"igy010","status":"p","title":"Innovation in Aging","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101201201"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b92a7493-a550-4974-923b-68ed58176da2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validity and reliability of the Major Depression Inventory for persons with dual sensory loss","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503969","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-539936"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"åndsforestillinger og deres enhed i johannesevangeliet","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/dtt/article/view/106365/163253","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-539936","identifier":[{"id":"85049621851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f5712538-3f41-4cc6-b9e1-0c0cce3b3611"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C2674A46368FAE7047E9BD0D9C525C25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/dtt/article/view/106365/163253","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01053191","19023898"],"issn_org":["01053191"],"journal":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","pages":"18","status":"p","title":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049621851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f5712538-3f41-4cc6-b9e1-0c0cce3b3611"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Åndsforestillinger og deres enhed i Johannesevangeliet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-539936","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Exports of entire educational programs from countries with established universities to other countries are increasing rapidly. Scant literature exists on education exports and related educational and pedagogical knowledge transfer. Evidence in this area helps us to develop better and more cost-effective future export programs, render knowledge transfer more efficiently and enhance intercultural learning in general—all important in the current globalized world. Aim: To share the experiences and lessons learned during the educational export project of two Bachelor of Science programs in health sciences from a Danish university to a newly established Saudi Arabian university. Methods: There were two contract periods: one of 4.5 years and another 1-year extension. An accredited program from Denmark was exported with the goal of gradually transferring the knowledge of the exporting staff to the local staff. Teams of one senior and two juniors traveled from the exporting university to the receiving university to deliver courses lasting 4 weeks each. Implicit knowledge comes from the personal experiences of the authors in the preparation, collaboration, administration, management and teaching of the two BSc programs. Explicit, written data come from the evaluation reports, for which 24 students and 31 staff members were interviewed, and from a review of document filing and administrative course material. Analysis was conducted based on the Neville and Warren theory of knowledge transfer in educational settings and using SWOT analysis. Analysis and Conclusion: Opportunities for knowledge transfer were not fully implemented; however, during the contract years, exchange and collaboration between the staff groups increased. The successful and well-received education export with sustainable knowledge transfer requires thorough and collaborative preparation and needs-based implementation. Learning to know each other’s working culture and creating mutual trust and acceptance take time and readiness to exchange expectations, views and experiences on equal footing.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aro, Arja R.","Eklund Karlsson, Leena","Ikonen, Anne Leena","Palianopoulou, Maria","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-577419"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experiences with the export of education in health sciences from denmark to saudi arabia","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4236/ce.2018.96060","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-577419","ids":["sdu-0ec87a40-e917-4d6e-9f07-ad0bd785c3c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EC8A6786599BC647F47A8B3C145A02DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/145633128/Experiences_with_the_export_of_education_in_health_sciences_from_Denmark_to_Saudi_Arabia.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4236/ce.2018.96060","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Health Promotion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arja R.","key":"aropau","last":"Aro","locid":"bc933962-5ce8-47d6-b8d5-3cd3d562cf4e","name":"Aro, Arja R.","orcid":"0000-0002-5499-2848","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leena","key":"eklundkarlssonpau","last":"Eklund Karlsson","locid":"e058970c-397d-43b8-a90f-fe9ad509c964","name":"Eklund Karlsson, Leena","orcid":"0000-0003-2052-0989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Leena","key":"ikonenpau","last":"Ikonen","locid":"d0eb3734-1c0b-492d-8376-4f60125d57c6","name":"Ikonen, Anne Leena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"palianopouloupau","last":"Palianopoulou","locid":"260cc49a-93a1-495e-9453-19500c3c98ba","name":"Palianopoulou, Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-1182-5158","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4236/ce.2018.96060","issn":["21514755","21514771"],"issn_org":["21514755"],"issue":"6","journal":"Creative Education","pages":"819-830","publisher":"Scientific Research Publishing, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Creative Education","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0ec87a40-e917-4d6e-9f07-ad0bd785c3c8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Experiences with the export of education in health sciences from Denmark to Saudi Arabia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-577419","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In Sect. 4.3 “Factors Associated with Statin Use in the Oldest Old”, the second paragraph contains errors that affect the interpretation of the studies discussed with respect to the effect of co-morbidities. The paragraph currently reads: In the outpatient population, Chokshi et al. reported that a higher co-morbidity index was associated with a lower chance of receiving a statin [15]. This is in line with the findings of Noaman et al., who reported that a higher comor-bidity index increased the likelihood of receiving a statin [26]. In contrast, Gnjidic et al. found that those with a higher co-morbidity index were more likely to receive a statin in a nursing home population [14]. Further, Tija et al. studied the advanced dementia population living in a nursing home and reported that statin use was more likely in patients with comorbidities such as hypertension, diabetes mellitus, or stroke [24]. These findings suggest that the presence of multiple co-morbidities decreases the likelihood of receiving a statin in the community but increases the likelihood in persons living in nursing homes. One explanation for the discrepancy is that in the Gnjidic et al. study, 94% of statin users were receiving statins for secondary prevention at baseline [14]. Thus, even with more co-morbidities, the validity of statin use may be perceived to be greater and people would be kept on statins. It should read: In the outpatient population, Chokshi et al. reported that a higher co-morbidity index was associated with a lower chance of receiving a statin [15], while Noaman et al. reported that a higher co-morbidity index increased likelihood of receiving a statin on hospital admission [26]. Gnjidic et al. found that those with a higher co-morbidity index were more likely to receive a statin in a nursing home population [14]. Furthermore, Tija et al. studied the advanced dementia population living in a nursing home and reported that statin use was more likely in patients with co-morbidities such as hypertension, diabetes, or stroke [24]. These findings suggest conflicting evidence for the effect of co-morbidities on statin use in the community, while increasing co-morbidity appears to raise the likelihood of receiving a statin for persons living in nursing homes. One explanation is that in the Gnjidic et al. study, 94% of statin users were receiving statins for secondary prevention at baseline [14]. Thus, even with more co-morbidities, the validity of statin use may be perceived to be greater and people would be kept on statins.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thompson, Wade","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Haastrup, Peter","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-581242"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correction to how common is statin use in the oldest old drugs amp aging 000000000010 000000001007 s000000040266 000000000018 000000000567 x","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535246/How_Common_Is_Statin_Use_Correction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-581242","identifier":[{"id":"85054569128","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30284119","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-1c07f8fa-67e6-4236-90a4-ee634f2c53ff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6621F5AE3F51F946003879805F2FA7A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535246/How_Common_Is_Statin_Use_Correction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3