{"abstract":"There is a lack of evidence surrounding the efficacy of statins in the oldest old (≥ 80 years of age). As such, there is controversy surrounding use of statins in this population. We sought to evaluate the prevalence of statin use in the oldest old worldwide to understand the scope of this issue. We searched PubMed and grey literature over the last 5 years. Studies had to report the prevalence of statin use in adults ≥ 80 years of age. The first author performed screening and extracted data. Our search produced 1870 hits; 14 articles were considered eligible. We found three studies of nursing home residents, eight studies of community-dwelling patients and three studies in the combined population (i.e., both community-dwelling patients and nursing home residents). The prevalence of statin use ranged from 17 to 39% in nursing home residents, 12 to 59% for community-dwelling patients and 18 to 45% in combined populations. Beyond age 80 years, the prevalence of statin use appeared to decrease with advancing age. Statin use was more common as secondary prevention compared with primary prevention. The prevalence of statin use in the oldest old has increased over recent decades. The increase in prevalence appears to be more pronounced in the oldest old compared with younger old, as reported by two studies. Statins are widely used in the oldest old despite the lack of evidence in this population. Given how common statin use is in the oldest old, clinical evidence surrounding their efficacy in this group is urgently needed to guide appropriate use and shared decision-making.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thompson, Wade","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Haastrup, Peter","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-628152"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thompson, Wade"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how common is statin use in the oldest old","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535143/Statin_use_march_6.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-628152","identifier":[{"id":"29987758","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85049636119","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bf9fd681-b579-48fc-a7ca-6ecd05a10259"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF443E54A09B16345EA5F9E69B0F3FED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154535143/Statin_use_march_6.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wade","key":"thompsonpau","last":"Thompson","locid":"3d654d06-5597-4de2-9f88-e0913ad14d60","name":"Thompson, Wade","orcid":"0000-0002-8268-4092","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"03dbf65e-75df-4540-b951-0d05e7a60cde","name":"Haastrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7265-743X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29987758"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40266-018-0567-x","issn":["1170229X","11791969"],"issn_org":["1170229X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Drugs & Aging","pages":"679-686","publisher":"Adis","status":"p","title":"Drugs & Aging","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049636119"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bf9fd681-b579-48fc-a7ca-6ecd05a10259"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How Common is Statin Use in the Oldest Old?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-628152","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Fibrinogen C domain containing 1 (FIBCD1) is a transmembrane receptor that binds chitin and other acetylated compounds with high affinity. FIBCD1 has previously been shown to be present in the epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract. In the present study, we performed a detailed analysis of normally structured human tissues for the expression of FIBCD1 by quantitative PCR and immunohistochemistry. We find that FIBCD1 is expressed in epithelial cells derived from all three germ layers. Endodermal-derived epithelial cells throughout the gastrointestinal tract and the respiratory system showed high expression of FIBCD1 and also mesodermal-derived cells in the genitourinary system and ectodermal-derived epidermis and sebaceous glands cells expressed FIBCD1. In some columnar epithelial cells, for example, in the salivary gland and gall bladder, the FIBCD1 expression was clearly polarized with strong apical reaction, while other columnar cells, for example, in small and large intestine and in bronchi, the staining was equally strong apically and basolaterally. In keratinocytes in skin, tongue, and oral cavity, the FIBCD1 staining was granular. This expression pattern together with the known binding properties supports that FIBCD1 plays a role in innate immunity in the skin and at mucosal surfaces.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Leicht von Huth, Sebastian","Møller, Jesper Bonnet","Schlosser, Anders","Marcussen, Niels","Nielsen, Ole","Nielsen, Vicki","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Holmskov, Uffe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642092"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chitin","Digestive system","FIBCD1","Immunohistochemistry","Innate immunity","Mucosal immunity","Pattern recognition","Receptors","Respiratory System"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunohistochemical localization of fibrinogen c domain containing 000000000001 on epithelial and mucosal surfaces in human tissues","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151776875/0022155417743694.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-642092","identifier":[{"id":"29220632","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5794204","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85041461206","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f0a01eb5-994a-400d-8481-8a40a8bd0264"],"keyword":["FIBCD1","chitin","digestive system","fibrinogen-related domain","immunohistochemistry","innate immunity","mucosal immunity","pattern recognition","receptors","respiratory system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-699E48954543E76D99604F89459770AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151776875/0022155417743694.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Department of Cancer and Inflammation Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"leichtvonhuthsebastianpau","last":"von Huth","locid":"92b34897-4b26-4ad2-89af-6e78175ff320","name":"Leicht von Huth, Sebastian","name_org":"von Huth, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0001-8127-6815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper B","key":"møllerjesperbo