{"abstract":"Ubiquitination is a post-translational modification (PTM) that is essential for balancing numerous physiological processes. To enable delineation of protein ubiquitination at a site-specific level, we generated an antibody, denoted UbiSite, recognizing the C-terminal 13 amino acids of ubiquitin, which remain attached to modified peptides after proteolytic digestion with the endoproteinase LysC. Notably, UbiSite is specific to ubiquitin. Furthermore, besides ubiquitination on lysine residues, protein N-terminal ubiquitination is readily detected as well. By combining UbiSite enrichment with sequential LysC and trypsin digestion and high-accuracy MS, we identified over 63,000 unique ubiquitination sites on 9,200 proteins in two human cell lines. In addition to uncovering widespread involvement of this PTM in all cellular aspects, the analyses reveal an inverse association between protein N-terminal ubiquitination and acetylation, as well as a complete lack of correlation between changes in protein abundance and alterations in ubiquitination sites upon proteasome inhibition.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Akimov, Vyacheslav","Barrio-Hernandez, Inigo","Hansen, Sten V.F.","Hallenborg, Philip","Pedersen, Anna-Kathrine","Bekker-Jensen, Dorte B.","Puglia, Michele","Christensen, Stine D K","Vanselow, Jens T.","Nielsen, Mogens M.","Kratchmarova, Irina","Kelstrup, Christian D","Olsen, Jesper V.","Blagoev, Blagoy"],"cuid":["S02-099.57-044226"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Blagoev, Blagoy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ubisite approach for comprehensive mapping of lysine and n terminal ubiquitination sites","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85049563460","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.57-044226","identifier":[{"id":"85049563460","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29967540","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8b6c3aa1-5ba2-4dc0-87f4-8a17c284de68","sdu-e2fc9188-461b-4cd2-9f3b-e68d0d85adc6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-35F034ABD7FDF066983047AFD924C365"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vyacheslav","key":"akimovpau","last":"Akimov","locid":"e1670787-90dd-4dce-af6a-7142767ccb3a","name":"Akimov, Vyacheslav","orcid":"0000-0002-8377-1761","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inigo","key":"barriohernandezpau","last":"Barrio-Hernandez","locid":"3330a12f-27e1-452c-b78c-09cf2469bcb1","name":"Barrio-Hernandez, Inigo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sten V F","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hans