{"abstract":"Kapitlet diskuterer, hvordan brugen af \"tilblivelse\" som analytisk begreb kan ses i relation til en større teoretisk udvikling inden for børne- og barndomsforskningen. Derefter gennemgås nogle centrale antagelser i teorierne om, hvordan aktører bliver til, og afslutningsvis demonstreres begrebets analytiske anvendelse på nogle udvalgte empiriske eksempler.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stilling Olesen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-194989"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tilblivelse læring i aktør netværk","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-194989","ids":["au-72faeab5-124f-4936-97f7-92707d30cedc"],"keyword":["Læring"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-07942A8AFB43FEEB0C702D0CA2ACB177"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","name_org":"Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gritt","key":"bnielsenpedh","last":"B. Nielsen","name":"B. Nielsen, Gritt","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"gulløvpedh","last":"Gulløv","name":"Gulløv, Eva","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ida","key":"wentzelwintherpedh","last":"Wentzel Winther","name":"Wentzel Winther, Ida","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788741268521"],"isbn":["9788741263236"],"pages":"229-241","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"tilgange og begreber","title":"Pædagogisk antropologi"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-72faeab5-124f-4936-97f7-92707d30cedc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tilblivelse : læring i aktør-netværk","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-194989","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We initiate a formal investigation on the power of predictability for argument of knowledge systems for NP. Specifically, we consider private-coin argument systems where the answer of the prover can be predicted, given the private randomness of the verifier; we call such protocols Predictable Arguments of Knowledge (PAoK). Our study encompasses a full characterization of PAoK, showing that such arguments can be made extremely laconic, with the prover sending a single bit, and assumed to have only one round (i.e., two messages) of communication without loss of generality. We additionally explore PAoK satisfying additional properties (including zero-knowledge and the possibility of re-using the same challenge across multiple executions with the prover), present several constructions of PAoK relying on different cryptographic tools, and discuss applications to cryptography.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Faonio, Antonio","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Venturi, Daniele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-196714"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-31","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2017-03-28","title":"20th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public-Key Cryptography, PKC 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Faonio, Antonio"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Rome La Sapienza"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictable arguments of knowledge","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014465351","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-196714","identifier":[{"id":"85014465351","type"