{"abstract":"Light rail transit and bus rapid transit have shown to be efficient and cost-effective in improving public transport systems in cities around the world. As these systems comprise various elements, which can be tailored to any given setting, e.g. pre-board fare-collection, holding strategies and other advanced public transport systems (APTS), the attractiveness of such systems depends heavily on their implementation. In the early planning stage it is advantageous to deploy simple and transparent models to evaluate possible ways of implementation. For this purpose, the present study develops a mesoscopic model which makes it possible to evaluate public transport operations in details, including dwell times, intelligent traffic signal timings and holding strategies while modelling impacts from other traffic using statistical distributional data thereby ensuring simplicity in use and fast computational times. This makes it appropriate for analysing the impacts of improvements to public transport operations, individually or in combination, in early planning stages. The paper presents a joint measure of reliability for such evaluations based on passengers’ perceived travel time by considering headway time regularity and running time variability, i.e. taking into account waiting time and in-vehicle time. The approach was applied on a case study by assessing the effects of implementing segregated infrastructure and APTS elements, individually and in combination. The results showed that the reliability of on-street public transport operations mainly depends on APTS elements, and especially holding strategies, whereas pure infrastructure improvements induced travel time reductions. The results further suggested that synergy effects can be obtained by planning on-street public transport coherently in terms of reduced travel times and increased reliability.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Kornerup Jensen, Jonas","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-345646"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysing improvements to on street public transport systems a mesoscopic model approach","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131599937/Manuscript_Mesoscopic_modelling_of_on_street_public_transport_Revision2_v5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-345646","identifier":[{"id":"85021327854","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-89c56b63-9a84-4ffd-921c-d9c3035624ca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77324B0EDEFAFCC124A5BD5776711911"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131599937/Manuscript_Mesoscopic_modelling_of_on_street_public_transport_Revision2_v5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"kornerupjensenpau","last":"Kornerup Jensen","name":"Kornerup Jensen, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12469-016-0151-x","issn":["16137159","1866749X"],"issn_org":["1866749X"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Public Transport","pages":"385-409","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Public Transport","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021327854"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-89c56b63-9a84-4ffd-921c-d9c3035624ca"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Analysing improvements to on-street public transport systems: a mesoscopic model approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-345646","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
