{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-495193"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"review of stefan nordgaard possessions and family in the writings of luke questioning the unity of luke s ethics københavn museum tusculanum 000000002017","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djb","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-495193","ids":["ku-aa5e2467-c3c9-4567-a992-796ee1235567"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-63933D85EA999673FBADB879CC4E6F13"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01053191","19023898"],"issn_org":["01053191"],"journal":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","pages":"73-75","status":"p","title":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aa5e2467-c3c9-4567-a992-796ee1235567"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"review of: Stefan Nordgaard: Possessions and Family in the Writings of Luke. Questioning the Unity of Luke's Ethics. København: Museum Tusculanum 2017","type":"Journal Book Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-495193","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Allergic reactions to airborne allergens may have important consequences for affected individuals and are believed to be unstable through life, although evidence from longitudinal studies is limited. OBJECTIVE: To assess changes in skin prick reactivity during 20 years in a random population sample of children and adolescents in relation to symptoms of rhinitis. METHODS: A total of 983 individuals, aged 7 to 17 years, were randomly selected in 1986 and invited to 4 examinations during a 20-year period. During each examination, a skin prick test was performed using common local aeroallergens (ie, birch, grass, mugwort, horse, dog, cat, house dust mite [Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus and Dermatophagoides farinae] and 2 molds [Alternaria iridis and Cladosporium herbarum]). RESULTS: The prevalence of allergy to any tested allergen peaked at the ages of 13 to 23 years. Rates of sensitization were variable. In the group of individuals tested more than once (n = 592), 16% developed sensitization during the study period and 9% became desensitized. In the group of individuals tested at all 4 examinations (n = 148), 34% developed sensitization and 22% became desensitized. In the group who developed sensitization, 55% had rhinitis, 17% had asthma, and 70% had eczema. In the group who became desensitized, 30% had rhinitis, 10% had asthma, and 50% had eczema. CONCLUSION: This 20-year prospective study found that sensitization is common, but its prevalence in individuals is also variable over time. Furthermore, through puberty and early adulthood a large number of individuals develop sensitization and a smaller number become desensitized. In addition, we found that symptoms of rhinitis rarely preceded sensitization.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schou Nielsen, Jesper","Meteran, Howraman","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Porsbjerg, Celeste","Backer, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-513346"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Allergens immunology","Animals","Asthma immunology","Child","Desensitization Immunologic","Female","Humans","Hypersensitivity immunology","Immunization","Male","Prospective Studies","Rhinitis diagnosis","Skin Tests methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"natural history of skin prick test reactivity a 000000000020 year prospective study of a random population sample of children and adolescents","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-513346","identifier":[{"id":"28599992","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020205089","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c8d12ac9-2b42-4076-9f55-f0cc56c4e9ba"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Allergens/immunology","Animals","Asthma/immunology","Child","Desensitization, Immunologic","Female","Humans","Hypersensitivity/immunology","Immunization","Male","Particulate Matter/immunology","Prospective Studies","Rhinitis/diagnosis","Skin Tests/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-889CCE61FF0E65AE743F6C59FD3A0C9A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Respiratory Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"schounielsenpau","last":"Schou Nielsen","name":"Schou Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Howraman","key":"meteranpau","last":"Meteran","name":"Meteran, Howraman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Suppli","key":"ulrikpau","last":"Ulrik","locid":"ea578010-4d8b-498b-b9d0-8f3d8cc424df","name":"Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Celeste","key":"porsbjergpau","last":"Porsbjerg","locid":"990b2125-b509-42b3-8fde-7014125da044","name":"Porsbjerg, Celeste","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke","key":"backerpau","last":"Backer","locid":"8ea3c13b-5a32-4002-b7bb-4621659a1827","name":"Backer, Vibeke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28599992"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.anai.2017.05.001","issn":["10811206","15344436"],"issn_org":["10811206"],"issue":"2","journal":"Annals of Allergy, Asthma & Immunology","pages":"184-188","status":"p","title":"Annals of Allergy, Asthma & Immunology","title_org":"Annals of Allergy, Asthma, & Immunology","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020205089"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c8d12ac9-2b42-4076-9f55-f0cc56c4e9ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Natural history of skin prick test reactivity : A 20-year prospective study of a random population sample of children and adolescents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-513346","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Matematikkens historie de sidste 50 år. Særligt de danske bidrag og særligt bidrag af medlemmer af Videnskabernes Selskab","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lützen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516113"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Det Natur og Biovidenskabelige Fakultet","Matematik","Matematikhistorie"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"den moderne matematik","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-516113","ids":["ku-cd6470a9-4833-4a5b-b669-ee030a4d1a3b"],"keyword":["Det Natur- og Biovidenskabelige Fakultet","Matematikhistorie","matematik"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B7E4C2F2E1BA14AD8A15136DCE5AE23B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lützenpau","last":"Lützen","locid":"8665d6b0-2fc2-4cf4-b7bd-f4a842265139","name":"Lützen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3797-8569","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marita Akhøj","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Marita Akhøj","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788773044100"],"pages":"204-208","place":"København","publisher":"Det Kongelige Danske Videnskabernes Selskab","status":"p","title":"Det Kongelige Danske Videnskabernes Selskab 1742-2017. Et jubilæumsskrift"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cd6470a9-4833-4a5b-b669-ee030a4d1a3b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Den moderne matematik","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516113","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Mosses collected decades ago and stored in herbaria are often used to assess historical nitrogen deposition. This method is effectively based on the assumption that tissue N concentration remains constant during storage. The present study raises serious doubt about the generality of that assumption. We measured tissue N and C concentrations as well as δ15N, δ13C, Pb and Mg in herbarium and present day samples of seven bryophyte species from six sites across Denmark. While an increase in nitrogen deposition during the last century is well-documented for the study site, we surprisingly found foliar N concentration to be higher in historical samples than in modern samples. Based on δ15N values and Pb concentration, we find nitrogen contamination of herbarium specimens during storage to be the most likely cause, possibly in combination with dilution though growth and/or decomposition during storage. We suggest ways to assess contamination and recommend caution to be taken when using herbarium specimens to assess historical pollution if exposure during storage cannot be ruled out. Analyses of moss tissue stored in a herbarium for a century raises serious concern about the reliability of this data source to past levels of nitrogen deposition.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Tora Finderup","Larsen, Jesper Ruf","Michelsen, Anders","Bruun, Hans Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are herbarium mosses reliable indicators of historical nitrogen deposition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85017462742&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-530551","identifier":[{"id":"85017462742","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28420490","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e59d0b24-7fc8-468e-8c42-abf1cf5997a5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59A724F19A71400E80260C361C0B4B31"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tora Finderup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"146e37d6-2d54-4b3c-b84b-fba5211074c9","name":"Nielsen, Tora Finderup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Ruf","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d03015cd-ca5d-4992-aa52-fc7cbd94d0d5","name":"Larsen, Jesper Ruf","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"michelsenpau","last":"Michelsen","locid":"5f62798d-50c6-41c3-8018-18babf5e5046","name":"Michelsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-9541-8658","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Henrik","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"5d597e2b-61e5-45ea-8816-0c37431329f0","name":"Bruun, Hans Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0674-2577","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28420490"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envpol.2017.04.020","issn":["02697491","18736424"],"issn_org":["02697491"],"issue":"Part 1","journal":"Environmental Pollution","pages":"1201-1207","status":"p","title":"Environmental Pollution","volume":"231"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017462742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e59d0b24-7fc8-468e-8c42-abf1cf5997a5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Are herbarium mosses reliable indicators of historical nitrogen deposition?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530551","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Danish Translation and Cultural Adaption of the 9-Item Shared Decision Making Questionnaire (SDM-Q-9) patient version.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hulbæk, Mette","Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","Primdahl, Jette","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Birkelund, Regner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590156"],"event":{"end":"2017-07-05","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2017-07-02","title":"9th International Shared Decision Making Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Shared decision making"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish translation and cultural adaption of the 000000000009 item shared decision making questionnaire sdm q 000000000009 patient version","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-590156","ids":["sdu-3b19639f-886c-4208-8b2b-b289a0605f1b"],"keyword":["shared decision making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7A9C964818DD9A0E5386A9DB80B1B394"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Familiecentret","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"hulbækpau","last":"Hulbæk","locid":"140af55f-92a4-4fcd-be71-f7776e32e2d3","name":"Hulbæk, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8258-3398","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Johansson","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"primdahlpau","last":"Primdahl","locid":"e7f33410-2d7a-4869-b5e9-ed886ba48c94","name":"Primdahl, Jette","orcid":"0000-0002-1049-4150","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Regner","key":"birkelundpau","last":"Birkelund","locid":"dedbb04e-270c-4add-a26c-87277d6caf0f","name":"Birkelund, Regner","orcid":"0000-0002-5374-0630","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3b19639f-886c-4208-8b2b-b289a0605f1b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Danish Translation and Cultural Adaption of the 9-Item Shared Decision Making Questionnaire (SDM-Q-9) patient version.","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590156","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This report evaluates ”Afprøvning af ACT-metoden over for borgere med psykiske lidelser og samtidigt misbrug” (“Testing the ACT method on citizens with psychological problems and concurrent substance and alcohol abuse”), a project financed through the public pool of funds. The project tested the ACT method on 62 citizens with psychological problems and concurrent substance or alcohol abuse in the City of Copenhagen and Skanderborg Municipality in the period 2014 to 2017. ACT (Assertive Community Treatment) is a proactive approach providing treatment and support in the comfort of the citizen’s own home or community. The intervention is delivered by a cross-disciplinary team of staff who provide support and treatment to citizens. In this project, the municipal team consisted of staff with different professional competences and areas of expertise, e.g. social education workers, nurses, case workers, addiction consultants, employment consultants, psychologists and psychiatrists. Overall, the evaluation shows that most citizens experienced a positive effect from the ACT intervention. However, a group of citizens experienced neither a positive nor a negative effect, and a small group experienced a setback. Furthermore, the evaluation points to a number of drivers and barriers in implementation of the project, including in relation to management, organisation and competences. The evaluation was based on qualitative as well as quantitative methods and data sources. The evaluation of developments among citizens was based on regular before-and-after impact measurements, and on an impact evaluation in which people receiving ACT were compared with a control group. Furthermore, qualitative interviews were carried out with project managers, ACT team staff and the management in the two municipalities participating in the project. Finally, interviews were conducted with citizens receiving ACT.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Amilon, Anna","Birkelund, Jesper Fels","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Kirkedal Nielsen, Ian","Møller, mikkel Stamp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-665160"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluering af afprøvning af act metoden over for borgere med psykiske lidelser og samtidigt misbrug","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/1072390/evaluering_af_act_metoden_pdfa.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-665160","ids":["vive-dc3afd64-1c3e-4d08-9110-89c3756b20eb"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1746FD8479EAEA69354E27DAD89DE36A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/1072390/evaluering_af_act_metoden_pdfa.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["The Danish National Institute for Social Research, Social Policy and Welfare"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"amilonpau","last":"Amilon","locid":"39fe7edd-14c3-4c68-9c69-f829260a988a","name":"Amilon, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Fels","key":"birkelundpau","last":"Birkelund","locid":"2f7eb417-62ae-4bb7-8a14-27f2baebf245","name":"Birkelund, Jesper Fels","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"056b6180-64df-40c2-8bc8-12867660066c","name":"Bojesen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5321-6855","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ian","key":"kirkedalnielsenpau","last":"Kirkedal Nielsen","name":"Kirkedal Nielsen, Ian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"mikkel Stamp","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, mikkel Stamp","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13961810"],"pages":"86","place":"København","publisher":"VIVE - Det Nationale Forsknings- og Analysecenter for Velfærd","repno":"SFI-Rapport","series":"SFI-Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-dc3afd64-1c3e-4d08-9110-89c3756b20eb"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Evaluering af ”Afprøvning af ACT-metoden over for borgere med psykiske lidelser og samtidigt misbrug”","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-665160","year":"2017","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Segmenting tree structures is common in several image processing applications. In medical image analysis, reliable segmentations of airways, vessels, neurons and other tree structures can enable important clinical. applications. We present a framework for tracking tree structures comprising of elongated branches using probabilistic state-space models and Bayesian smoothing. Unlike most existing methods that proceed with sequential tracking of branches, we present an exploratory method, that is less sensitive to local anomalies in the data due to acquisition noise and/or interfering structures. The evolution of individual branches is modelled using a process model and the observed data is incorporated into the update step of the Bayesian smoother using a measurement model that is based on a multi-scale blob detector. Bayesian smoothing is performed using the RTS (Rauch-Tung-Striebel) smoother, which provides Gaussian density estimates of branch states at each tracking step. We select likely branch seed points automatically based on the response of the blob detection and track from all such seed points using the RTS smoother. We use covariance of the marginal posterior density estimated for each branch to discriminate false positive and true positive branches. The method is evaluated on 3D chest CT scans to track airways. We show that the presented method results in additional branches compared to a baseline method based on region growing on probability images","author_count":19,"contributors":["Selvan, Raghavendra","Petersen, Jens","Pedersen, Jesper Johannes Holst","de Bruijne, Marleen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695465"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-14","place":"Quebec, ca","start":"2017-09-10","title":"1st International Workshop on Graphs in Biomedical Image Analysis (GRAIL) / 6th International Workshop on Mathematical Foundations of Computational Anatomy (MFCA) / 3rd International Workshop on Imaging Genetics (MICGen)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Airways","CT","Segmentation","Tree segmentation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extraction of airways with probabilistic state space models and bayesian smoothing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1708.02096.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-695465","identifier":[{"id":"000463348600006","type":"wos"},{"id":"85029764213","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-13c0f3b4-9f82-431d-8ee4-d2cd9a3e9ae8"],"keyword":["Airways","Bayesian smoothing","CT","Probabilistic state-space","SEGMENTATION","Tree segmentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48661DCDBBD96C07D48126998384FEFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1708.02096.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Selvan","key":"raghavendrapau","last":"Raghavendra","locid":"f325aa0c-cfdc-4993-bb34-ef97810761c1","name":"Selvan, Raghavendra","name_org":"Raghavendra, Selvan","orcid":"0000-0003-4302-0207","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0fcef7de-bc0f-463f-b539-bc02ae09e0e5","name":"Petersen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-0138-0693","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Johannes Holst","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f87d965e-c646-421c-8804-666d39c7028b","name":"Pedersen, Jesper Johannes Holst","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marleen","key":"debruijnepau","last":"de Bruijne","locid":"988d3493-ffac-4b50-99ff-e91d85774b0d","name":"de Bruijne, Marleen","orcid":"0000-0002-6328-902X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M. Jorge","key":"cardosopedh","last":"Cardoso","name":"Cardoso, M. Jorge","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tal","key":"arbelpedh","last":"Arbel","name":"Arbel, Tal","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Enzo","key":"ferrantepedh","last":"Ferrante","name":"Ferrante, Enzo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"pennecpedh","last":"Pennec","name":"Pennec, Xavier","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Adrian V.","key":"dalcapedh","last":"Dalca","name":"Dalca, Adrian V.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah","key":"parisotpedh","last":"Parisot","name":"Parisot, Sarah","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarang","key":"joshipedh","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Sarang","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nematollah K.","key":"batmanghelichpedh","last":"Batmanghelich","name":"Batmanghelich, Nematollah K.","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Aristeidis","key":"sotiraspedh","last":"Sotiras","name":"Sotiras, Aristeidis","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Mads","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mert R.","key":"sabuncupedh","last":"Sabuncu","name":"Sabuncu, Mert R.","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tom","key":"fletcherpedh","last":"Fletcher","name":"Fletcher, Tom","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"shenpedh","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Li","rank":17,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stanley","key":"durrlemanpedh","last":"Durrleman","name":"Durrleman, Stanley","rank":18,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"sommerpedh","last":"Sommer","name":"Sommer, Stefan","rank":19,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-67675-3_6","eisbn":["9783319676753"],"isbn":["9783319676746"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"53-63","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"First International Workshop, GRAIL 2017, 6th International Workshop, MFCA 2017, and Third International Workshop, MICGen 2017, Held in Conjunction with MICCAI 2017, Québec City, QC, Canada, September 10–14, 2017, Proceedings","title":"Graphs in Biomedical Image Analysis, Computational Anatomy and Imaging Genetics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029764213"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-13c0f3b4-9f82-431d-8ee4-d2cd9a3e9ae8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extraction of Airways with Probabilistic State-Space Models and Bayesian Smoothing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695465","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To ascertain whether persons treated with statins experience a decreased risk of community-acquired Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia (CA-SAB) as compared with nonusers. PATIENTS AND METHODS: Using population-based medical registries, we conducted a case-control study including all adults with first-time CA-SAB and population controls matched on age, sex, and residence in Northern Denmark from January 1, 2000, through December 31, 2011. Statin users were categorized as current users (new or long-term use), former users, and nonusers. We used conditional logistic regression to compute odds ratios (ORs) for CA-SAB according to statin exposure, overall and stratified by intensity (<20, 20-39, ≥40 mg/d) and duration of use (<365, 365-1094, ≥1095 days). RESULTS: We identified 2638 patients with first-time CA-SAB and 26,379 matched population controls. Compared with nonusers, current statin users experienced markedly decreased risk of CA-SAB (adjusted OR, 0.73; 95% CI, 0.63-0.84). The adjusted OR was 0.96 (95% CI, 0.60-1.51) for new users, 0.71 (95% CI, 0.62-0.82) for long-term users, and 1.12 (95% CI, 0.94-1.32) for former users as compared with nonusers. The CA-SAB risk decreased with increasing intensity of statin use; thus, compared with nonusers, the adjusted OR was 0.84 (95% CI, 0.68-1.04) for current users with daily dosages of less than 20 mg/d, 0.71 (95% CI, 0.58-0.87) for 20 to 39 mg/d, and 0.63 (95% CI, 0.49-0.81) for 40 mg/d or more. Conversely, we observed no differences in the risk of CA-SAB with successive increases in the duration of statin use. CONCLUSION: Statin use was associated with a decreased risk of CA-SAB, particularly in long-term users.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Smit, Jesper","López-Cortés, Luis Eduardo","Thomsen, Reimar W","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Nielsen, Henrik","Frøslev, Trine","Rodríguez-Bãno, Jesús","Søgaard, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-089.77-003455"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Smit, Jesper"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas (CSIC)"],"keyword":["Cohort","Comorbidity","Danish","Disease","Epidemiology","Infections","Journal Article","Mortality","Nationwide","Sepsis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unidad Clínica de Enfermedades Infecciosas, Microbiología y Medicina Preventiva, Instituto de Biomedicina de Sevilla (IBiS), Hospitales Universitarios Virgen Macarena y Virgen del Rocío/CSIC/Universidad de Sevilla, Sevilla, Spain."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statin use and risk of community acquired staphylococcus aureus bacteremia a population based case control study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85030472089","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.77-003455","identifier":[{"id":"28982483","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85030472089","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000411959800006","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-469c6c2d-87d0-41f5-bbc0-a9b90f76cc34","au-307b3b8c-5fd2-481e-9934-61c9b82f0bad"],"keyword":["COHORT","COMORBIDITY","DANISH","DISEASE","EPIDEMIOLOGY","INFECTIONS","Journal Article","MORTALITY","NATIONWIDE","SEPSIS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8749D03295977526586E359F9C195541"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU