,"name":"Maeng, Michael","name_org":"Mæng, Michael","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen D","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","name_org":"Kristensen, Steen D","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars R","key":"krusellpau","last":"Krusell","locid":"660b49df-f279-4bc2-8ff9-50fe259b2d33","name":"Krusell, Lars Romer","name_org":"Krusell, Lars R","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens F","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"569ae3f1-67b8-4b02-9b3f-6469767f33e3","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens F","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper M","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper M","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28862968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.117.005587","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e005587","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030699040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-24d7d104-41e4-48c9-86cf-d0ed73adf683","sdu-c266f0c7-34cb-4a33-b696-043ee021e2d7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Myocardial Perfusion Imaging Versus Computed Tomography Angiography-Derived Fractional Flow Reserve Testing in Stable Patients With Intermediate-Range Coronary Lesions : Influence on Downstream Diagnostic Workflows and Invasive Angiography Findings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-015277","year":"2017","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Background: Transcriptomic profiling of ex vivo cultured human limbal epithelial stem cells (hLESCs) will foster better understanding of corneal physiology and novel treatment paradigms to limbal stem cell deficiency (LSCD). However, currently such profiling studies are hampered due to difficulties with producing sufficient amounts of intact mRNA for deep RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) from subpopulations sorted on the basis of co-expression of membrane and intracellular antigens by fluorescence-activated cell sorting (FACS). Methods: To address this problem, we systematically analyzed the critical steps, and found that ethanol fixation together with optimized downstream procedures provided a pipeline that yielded high quality total RNA in amounts to readily support the RNA-seq procedure, while still preserving good discrimination between the individual hLESC immunophenotypes. Results: The average RNA integrity number (RIN) was 7.7 ± 0.4, and the average yield was 4.6 ± 1.7 pg of RNA per cell. The sequencing analysis of the isolated RNA produced high quality data with more than 70% of read pairs mapping uniformly to the reference genome and 80% of bases with a Phred score of at least 30. Conclusion: In this study, we developed a reliable FACS-based procedure using ethanol as a fixative that would support accurate isolation of limbal epithelial progenitor subpopulations along with RNA yield and quality sufficient to enable deep transcriptomic profiling.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Liu, Lei","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Porsborg, Simone Riis","Emmersen, Jeppe","Fink, Trine","Hjortdal, Jesper Østergaard","Søndergaard, Chris Bath","Zachar, Vladimir"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006931"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zachar, Vladimir"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jilin University"],"keyword":["Ethanol","Fluorescence activated cell sorting","Journal Article","RNA integrity","RNA sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maintaining rna integrity for transcriptomic profiling of ex vivo cultured limbal epithelial stem cells after fluorescence activated cell sorting facs","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12575-017-0065-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-006931","identifier":[{"id":"29255379","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85038107559","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000417870200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5727887","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-8f10cb19-998a-4da6-940c-e5cc9fa2726f","au-c1365601-dce2-44ee-8e2b-d9091d7138ff"],"keyword":["Ethanol","Fluorescence-activated cell sorting","Intracellular staining","Journal Article","Limbal stem cells","RNA integrity","RNA sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F71811BB29321188AD214BC6817A0B6C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266899670/10.1186_s12575_017_0065_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12575-017-0065-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory for Stem Cell Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"c0466f4f-89d6-45c8-ac35-75e2cacc8313","name":"Liu, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frederik Mølgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d7387610-1579-4bc0-892f-a8523e6579ba","name":"Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simone Elkjær","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"46410c88-b904-4c92-a6dc-53656d7d8d4a","name":"Porsborg, Simone Riis","name_org":"Riis, Simone Elkjær","orcid":"0000-0003-0167-5408","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"emmersenpau","last":"Emmersen","locid":"f1d96f8c-182e-402d-a274-ddad81d21d3c","name":"Emmersen, Jeppe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"finkpau","last":"Fink","locid":"d03e5c33-ea86-44f7-9d8f-4ac7af2eedc2","name":"Fink, Trine","orcid":"0000-0001-7578-1137","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Østergaard","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","name_org":"Hjortdal, Jesper Østergaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chris","key":"bathpau","last":"Bath","locid":"2af42c27-be6e-490c-87bc-939e601f27af","name":"Søndergaard, Chris Bath","name_org":"Bath, Chris","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vladimir","key":"zacharpau","last":"Zachar","locid":"33eb9eb1-289c-4a1a-b4c9-d3614d239c0e","name":"Zachar, Vladimir","orcid":"0000-0002-5279-2690","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29255379"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12575-017-0065-2","issn":["14809222"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biological Procedures Online","paperid":"15","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Biological Procedures Online","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038107559"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8f10cb19-998a-4da6-940c-e5cc9fa2726f","au-c1365601-dce2-44ee-8e2b-d9091d7138ff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Maintaining RNA Integrity for Transcriptomic Profiling of Ex Vivo Cultured Limbal Epithelial Stem Cells after Fluorescence-Activated Cell Sorting (FACS)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-006931","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim was to elucidate whether levels of circulating antibodies to Actinobacillus actinomycetemcomitans and Porphyromonas gingivalis correlate to loss of attachment, as a marker for periodontitis and cardiovascular disease (CVD). Design: Sera were collected from 576 participants of the Danish Health Examination Survey (DANHES). Immunoglobulin G antibodies against lipopolysaccharide (LPS) and protein antigens from the a, b and c serotypes of A. actinomycetemcomitans and P. gingivalis were quantified by titration in ELISA plates coated with a mixture of antigens prepared by disintegration of bacteria. Results: Levels of antibodies against P. gingivalis (OR = 1.48) and A. actinomycetemcomitans (1.31) associated with periodontitis, as determined by univariable logistic regression analysis. These antibody levels also associated with CVD (1.17 and 1.37), respectively, However, after adjusting for other risk factors, including age, smoking, gender, alcohol consumption, overweight, and level of education using multivariable logistic regression analysis, only increasing body mass index (BMI; 1.09), previous smoking (1.99), and increasing age (decades) (2.27) remained associated with CVD. Increased levels of antibodies against P. gingivalis (1.34) remained associated with periodontitis after adjusting for other risk factors. Conclusions: CVD and periodontitis were associated with levels of IgG antibodies to P. gingivalis or A. actinomycetemcomitans in univariable analyses, but only the association of P. gingivalis antibody levels with periodontitis reached statistical significance after adjustment for common confounders. Age, in particular, influenced this relationship.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Damgaard, Christian","Reinholdt, Jesper","Enevold, Christian","Fiehn, Nils-Erik","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Holmstrup, Palle"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-021153"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Damgaard, Christian"],"keyword":["AGGRESSIVE PERIODONTITIS","Actinobacillus actinomycetemcomitans","Antibody","Atherosclerosis","Bacteremia","Cardiovascular disease","Cohort study","Coronary heart disease","Hypertension","IgG","Immune response","Immunoglobulin","LINKED IMMUNOSORBENT ASSAY","Myocardial Infarction","Pathogens","Periodontal disease","Periodontitis","Risk","Risk factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunoglobulin g antibodies against porphyromonas gingivalis or aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans in cardiovascular disease and periodontitis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20002297.2017.1374154","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-021153","identifier":[{"id":"29081914","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85052735332","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000410617300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5646634","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-74092c00-f08e-4bb6-a3c6-a851d020182f","ku-65adc136-82d1-4086-8b66-2a76a7846ea4"],"keyword":["ACTINOBACILLUS-ACTINOMYCETEMCOMITANS","AGGRESSIVE PERIODONTITIS","BACTEREMIA","CORONARY-HEART-DISEASE","Cardiovascular disease","IGG","IMMUNE-RESPONSE","LINKED-IMMUNOSORBENT-ASSAY","PATHOGENS","RISK","SERUM ANTIBODIES","antibody","atherosclerosis","cohort study","hypertension","immunoglobulin","myocardial infarction","periodontal disease","periodontitis","risk factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-17C4EDD831034964C2E5B632CD8D6F5D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20002297.2017.1374154","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/183832013/Immunoglobulin_G_antibodies_against_Porphyromonas_gingivalis_or_Aggregatibacter_actinomycetemcomitans_in_cardiovascular_disease_and_periodontitis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 01 - Prosthetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"166c1339-46eb-42f4-ab74-f84615ac1706","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2394-746X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"reinholdtpau","last":"Reinholdt","locid":"03ef8acb-f581-45e7-9dd2-3cb6bb520c9a","name":"Reinholdt, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"enevoldpau","last":"Enevold","name":"Enevold, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils-Erik","key":"fiehnpau","last":"Fiehn","locid":"2038d5e4-408f-4610-9482-9912dd6e8526","name":"Fiehn, Nils-Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8caf59ab-44ff-4d9a-a722-8dd317bbd8b9","name":"Nielsen, Claus Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7543-9016","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Palle","key":"holmstruppau","last":"Holmstrup","locid":"70e9b4ab-ebee-4ee2-9356-87e935612e99","name":"Holmstrup, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-1563-1089","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29081914"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/20002297.2017.1374154","issn":["20002297"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Oral Microbiology","paperid":"1374154","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Oral Microbiology","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052735332"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-74092c00-f08e-4bb6-a3c6-a851d020182f","ku-65adc136-82d1-4086-8b66-2a76a7846ea4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Immunoglobulin G antibodies against Porphyromonas gingivalis or Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans in cardiovascular disease and periodontitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-021153","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The Focused Assessment with Sonography in Trauma (FAST) protocol is considered beneficial in emergent evaluation of trauma patients with blunt or penetrating injury and has become integrated into the Advanced Trauma Life Support (ATLS) protocol. No guidelines exist as to the use of ultrasonography in trauma in Denmark. We aimed to determine the current use of ultrasonography for assessing trauma patients in Denmark. METHODS: We conducted a nation-wide cross-sectional investigation of ultrasonography usage in trauma care. The first phase consisted of an Internet-based investigation of existing guidelines, and the second phase was a series of structured interviews of orthopedic surgeons, anesthesiologists, and radiologists on call in all hospitals receiving traumatized patients in Denmark. RESULTS: Guidelines were obtained from all 22 hospitals receiving traumatized patients in Denmark. Twenty-one (95.5%) of the guidelines included and recommended FAST as part of trauma assessment. The recommended person to perform the examination was the radiologist in n = 11 (50.0%), the surgeon in n = 6 (27.3%), the anesthesiologist in n = 1 (4.5%), and unspecified in n = 3 (13.6%) facilities. FAST indications varied between circulatory instability n = 8 (36.4%), team leader's discretion n = 6 (27.3%), abdominal trauma n = 3 (13.6%), and not specified n = 6 (27.3%). Telephone interviews revealed that exams were always n = 8 (36.4%) or often n = 4 (18.2%) registered in the patients' charts. The remaining n = 10 (45.5%) facilities either never registered n = 2 (9.1%), it was not possible to register n = 1 (4.5%), or unknown by the trauma leaders n = 7 (31.8%). Images were often stored in n = 1 (4.5%), never stored in n = 10 (45.5%), not possible to store in n = 2 (9.1%), and unknown in n = 9 (40.9%) facilities. CONCLUSION: Ultrasonography was used in a non-uniform fashion by multiple specialties in Danish trauma facilities. Very few images from FAST examinations were stored and documentation was scanty. National guidelines on application and documentation of ultrasonography in trauma are called for.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Weile, Jesper","Nielsen, Klaus","Primdahl, Stine C","Frederiksen, Christian Alcaraz","Laursen, Christian B","Sloth, Erik","Kirkegaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026141"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Emergency medicine","FAST","Journal Article","Trauma","Ultrasonography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultrasonography in trauma a nation wide cross sectional investigation","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13089-017-0071-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026141","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5479771","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85021261435","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28639253","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b92f4da2-a4cc-4a63-a7ae-73dfd06b63aa","sdu-4bb8001f-95ff-42fd-bc10-0989edffe2a2"],"keyword":["Emergency Medicine","FAST","Focused Assessment with Sonography in Trauma","Journal Article","Trauma","Ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-929471DBC7FB9B2B9F9F8FC42358C805"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13089-017-0071-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125226043/Ultrasonography_in_trauma.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Re