14712334"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Infectious Diseases","pages":"376","paperid":"376","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Infectious Diseases","title_org":"B M C Infectious Diseases","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020039505"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3a507af0-30f2-40dc-93cc-65a4656909c8","au-02dd07aa-92f6-4d05-a385-a4d708ee275a","ku-26a289ec-b693-47d3-9024-45413f4a608a","sdu-2fc6bd34-5e8d-4d65-8ac8-ef99409576e6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bacterial vaginosis, human papilloma virus and herpes viridae do not predict vaginal HIV RNA shedding in women living with HIV in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.33-002887","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Chronic inflammatory diseases (CIDs), including Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis (inflammatory bowel diseases, IBD), rheumatoid arthritis, psoriasis, psoriatic arthritis, spondyloarthritides, hidradenitis suppurativa, and immune-mediated uveitis, are treated with biologics targeting the pro-inflammatory molecule tumour necrosis factor-α (TNF) (i.e., TNF inhibitors). Approximately one-third of the patients do not respond to the treatment. Genetics and lifestyle may affect the treatment results. The aims of this multidisciplinary collaboration are to identify (1) molecular signatures of prognostic value to help tailor treatment decisions to an individual likely to initiate TNF inhibitor therapy, followed by (2) lifestyle factors that support achievement of optimised treatment outcome. This report describes the establishment of a cohort that aims to obtain this information. Clinical data including lifestyle and treatment response and biological specimens (blood, faeces, urine, and, in IBD patients, intestinal biopsies) are sampled prior to and while on TNF inhibitor therapy. Both hypothesis-driven and data-driven analyses will be performed according to pre-specified protocols including pathway analyses resulting from candidate gene expression analyses and global approaches (e.g., metabolomics, metagenomics, proteomics). The final purpose is to improve the lives of patients suffering from CIDs, by providing tools facilitating treatment selection and dietary recommendations likely to improve the clinical outcome.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Andersen, Vibeke Normann","Holmskov, Uffe","Sørensen, Signe Bek","Jawhara, Mohamad","Andersen, Karina W","Bygum, Anette","Sylvester Hvid, Lone","Grauslund, Jakob","Wied, Jimmi","Glerup, Henning","Fredberg, Ulrich","Villadsen, Jan Alexander","Kjær, Søren Geill","Fallingborg, Jan","Moghadd, Seyed A G R","Knudsen, Torben","Brodersen, Jacob","Frøjk, Jesper","Dahlerup, Jens Frederik","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Christensen, Robin","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Thiel, Steffen","Færgeman, Nils J","Brandslund, Ivan","Stensballe, Allan","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Franke, Andre","Ellinghaus, David","Rosenstiel, Philip","Raes, Jeroen","Heitmann, Berit","Boye, Mette","Lindgaard Nielsen, Charlotte","Werner, Lars","Kjeldsen, Jens","Ellingsen, Torkell"],"cuid":["S05-099.47-002802"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Christian-Albrechts-University of Kiel","Kiel University","University of Leuven","VIB","Vlaams Instituut voor Biotechnologie (VIB)"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Biomarkører","CID","Exercise","Food","Journal Article","Kronisk inflammatorisk sygdom","Molecular epidemiology","Motion","Patient related outcome measures PROMs","Personalized medicine","Red meat","Rygning","Smoking","Treatment Outcome","Western style diet WSD"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Diagnostic Centre, Silkeborg Regional Hospital, University of Aarhus, 8600 Silkeborg, Denmark. Henning.Glerup@silkeborg.rm.dk."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a proposal for a study on treatment selection and lifestyle recommendations in chronic inflammatory diseases a danish multidisciplinary collaboration on prognostic factors and personalised medicine","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu9050499","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S05-099.47-002802","identifier":[{"id":"85019440395","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000402054500077","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5452229","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28505128","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-387d681e-6fe9-477d-8db0-a652e13fa218","au-ca015806-bebc-47d1-955d-b70e90d58736","ku-e2cf7fce-109f-4ff2-ad93-6f8cb473a063","sdu-fd830100-228f-4ef1-8cc5-758b0fc435ba","vive-9fb3143a-8c24-4113-b5b3-d4ae38b9f5a5"],"keyword":["CID","Food","Journal Article","Molecular epidemiology","Personalized medicine","biomarker","biomarkører","exercise","kronisk inflammatorisk sygdom","motion","patient related outcome measures (PROMs)","red meat","rygning","smoking","treatment outcome","western style diet (WSD)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-8-9A03DABA77315CDCD76F313944E87F47"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/184416822/nutrients_09_00499.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/257739062/nutrients_09_00499.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu9050499","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124947399/A_Proposal_for_a_Study_on_Treatment_Selection_and_Lifestyle_Recommendations_in_Chronic_Inflammatory_Diseases.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Researc