dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-099.47-002802","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present validation of a method for constructing a virtual omnidirectional antenna in the azimuth plane. The virtual omnidirectional antenna utilizes a combination of data from directive horn antennas. The aim is to utilize the high gain of the horn antenna to improve the dynamic range of channel sounding measurements conducted in the centimeter and millimeter wave bands. The resulting complex impulse response from the virtual omnidirectional antenna is used to find the power-delay-profile (PDP). This is then compared to measurements conducted at the same time using a real omnidirectional antenna. The validation shows that the synthesized omnidirectional is capable of predicting main components and the slope of the PDP. Further, it is shown that by choosing angular sampling steps corresponding to the half power beam width (HPBW) of the used antenna similar power levels can be achieved.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hejselbæk, Johannes","Karstensen, Anders","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Fan, Wei","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063710"],"event":{"acronym":"EuCAP","end":"2017-03-24","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2017-03-19","title":"11th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of emulated omnidirectional antenna output using directive antenna data","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/261607493/Validation_of_Emulated_Omnidirectional_Antenna_Output_Using_Directive_Antenna_Data.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-063710","identifier":[{"id":"85020230305","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000403827300028","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-2f166fde-1bd5-4257-8b2c-da958417630d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3904780439187BA0A2231771C5310A7C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/261607493/Validation_of_Emulated_Omnidirectional_Antenna_Output_Using_Directive_Antenna_Data.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"hejselbækpau","last":"Hejselbæk","locid":"9163c39e-9747-4c12-bcb7-861a91af7c57","name":"Hejselbæk, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-3053-5474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"karstensenpau","last":"Karstensen","locid":"0d1d4896-50a7-4849-acdb-10dc2e0b27f5","name":"Karstensen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eucap.2017.7928192","eisbn":["9788890701870"],"pages":"131-135","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2017 11th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020230305"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2f166fde-1bd5-4257-8b2c-da958417630d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Validation of Emulated Omnidirectional Antenna Output Using Directive Antenna Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063710","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The harmonic chirp signal model has only very recently been in- troduced for modelling approximately periodic signals with a time- varying fundamental frequency. A number of estimators for the pa- rameters of this model have already been proposed, but they are ei- ther inaccurate, non-robust to noise, or very computationally inten- sive. In this paper, we propose a fast algorithm for the harmonic chirp summation method which has been demonstrated in the liter- ature to be accurate and robust to noise. The proposed algorithm is orders of magnitudes faster than previous algorithms which is also demonstrated via timing studies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Jensen, Søren Holdt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081811"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2017-03-09","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2017-03-05","title":"2017 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing, ICASSP 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast harmonic chirp summation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/317717654/master.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081811","identifier":[{"id":"000414286200084","type":"wos"},{"id":"85023752463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6d34a11a-b16d-4724-91f5-af3eb9b5c13c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61FCD5BC6CAC66B582780FEEA37176BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/267516975/20170628_HCS_sim.zip","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/317717654/master.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Signal and Information Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenjesperkjærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Lindstrøm","key":"jensentobiaslindstrømpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a2e382fc-c4c6-4ff2-b7d2-8b012eb5160e","name":"Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","orcid":"0000-0003-4262-0577","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenjesperrindompau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenmadsgræsbøllpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Holdt","key":"jensensørenholdtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bfd2a53b-f2bd-4563-8968-9a911996215f","name":"Jensen, Søren Holdt","orcid":"0000-0002-1050-470X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp.2017.7952189","eisbn":["9781509041176"],"issn":["15206149"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2017 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85023752463"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6d34a11a-b16d-4724-91f5-af3eb9b5c13c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Fast Harmonic Chirp Summation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081811","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Respiratory-induced motions are prone to degrade the positron emission tomography (PET) signal with the consequent loss of image information and unreliable segmentations. This phantom study aims to assess the discrepancies relative to stationary PET segmentations, of widely used semiautomatic PET segmentation methods on heterogeneous target lesions influenced by motion during image acquisition. Three target lesions included dual F-18 Fluoro-deoxy-glucose (FDG) tracer concentrations as high-and low tracer activities relative to the background. Four different tracer concentration arrangements were segmented using three SUV threshold methods (Max40%, SUV40% and 2.5SUV) and a gradient based method (GradientSeg). Segmentations in static 3D-PET scans (PETsta) specified the reference conditions for the individual segmentation methods, target lesions and tracer concentrations. The motion included PET images followed a 4D-PET (PET4D) and a 3D-PET (PETmot) scan protocol. Moreover, motion-corrected PET images (PETdeb) were derived from the PETmot images. Segmentations in PET4D, PETmot and PETdeb were compared to the PETsta segmentations according to volume changes (Delta Vol) and an error estimate (lowUptake(error)) for the lesion part covering the low tracer concentration. In PET4D images, all segmentation methods provided lowUptakeerror estimates equivalent to PETsta segmentations and, except for the Max40% segmentations, a slight volume expansion. In the PET(mo)t images, the GradientSeg method results in an average 0.43 increased volume and an overestimation of 0.33 for the lowUptakeerror. The most accurate segmentations in PETmot, relative to PETsta, were accomplished by the 2.5SUV and SUV40% methods. In the PETdeb images, the GradientSeg method solitary provided segmentations equivalent to segmentation in PETsta images. The use of FDG with various tracer concentrations revealed, according to PETsta images, that the most constant segmentations for motion-corrected PET images (PET4D or PETdeb) were achieved using the GradientSeg method. In the absence of PET4D or PETdeb images, the 2.5SUV and SUV40% methods are most consistent to PETsta segmentations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Martin Skovmos","Hansen, Jesper Carl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090195"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validating pet segmentation of thoracic lesions is 000000000004d pet necessary","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/2057-1976/aa5ba9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090195","identifier":[{"id":"85139243781","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000411035000030","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-8a034519-a8c8-4218-937f-e7bc43602696"],"keyword":["FDG-PET segmentation lung cancer cell lung-cancer positron-emission-tomography respiratory motion tumor volume f-18-fdg pet radiotherapy images delineation definition phantom Radiology, Nuclear Medicine & Medical Imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-852EDB803010560D52EC6F3CA3013DA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/2057-1976/aa5ba9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/266904287/Nielsen_2017_Biomed._Phys._Eng._Express_3_015028.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Oncology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Kirurgi og Kræftbehandling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fbcf9e4e-63e5-4ae8-9b00-319148e15063","name":"Nielsen, Martin Skovmos","name_org":"Nielsen, M. S.","orcid":"0000-0002-3955-7266","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"carlpau","last":"Carl","locid":"b2b04c0e-3516-4898-aff3-b83015cfd71d","name":"Hansen, Jesper Carl","name_org":"Carl, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/2057-1976/aa5ba9","issn":["20571976"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biomedical Physics & Engineering Express","paperid":"015028","publisher":"IOP Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Biomedical Physics & Engineering Express","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139243781"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8a034519-a8c8-4218-937f-e7bc43602696"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Validating PET segmentation of thoracic lesions-is 4D PET necessary?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-090195","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Traditionally storm water detention ponds in Denmark are discharging to steams with a constant flow rate based on standard values. The discharged flow rate does not necessarily take the stream characteristics into account, thus sometimes causing flooding and erosion of the stream. Based on knowledge of the geometry and sediment characteristics in the stream it is possible to determine the maximum capacity of the steam to receive detention pond discharges without unintended erosion of the stream and flooding of the adjacent areas. Results of modelling have shown that it is possible to make a controlled discharge of storm water that is in agreement with the hydraulic capacity of the stream.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thomsen, Anja Thrane Hejselbæk","Moeslund, Thomas Baltzer","Jensen, G. P.","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Pedersen, Morten Lauge","Rasmussen, Michael R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-096382"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-15","place":"Prag, cz","start":"2017-09-10","title":"14th International Conference on Urban Drainage","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Discharge","Erosion","SWDP","Stream capacity","Stream hydraulics","Stream impact"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"controlling the hydraulic impact of discharge from storm water detention ponds into streams","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-096382","ids":["aau-9fdf17a1-02fe-4fdb-a39d-cf388fa16099"],"keyword":["Discharge","Erosion","SWDP","Stream capacity","Stream hydraulics","Stream impact"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7430757BFF3A78333D6AD2E607B33A81"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg universi