p","subtitle":"Småfagenes danske kulturhistorie i glimt","title":"Små fag, store horisonter","volume":"7"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2f70b8ab-6483-466f-a18a-ccdbb3351523"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nye verdener, andre historier : Det indianske på Københavns Universitet - og hos Ib Michael","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421713","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Clinical seizures are common after cardiac arrest and predictive of a poor neurological outcome. Seizures may be myoclonic, tonic-clonic or a combination of seizure types. This study reports the incidence and prognostic significance of clinical seizures in the target temperature management (TTM) after cardiac arrest trial. Our hypotheses were that seizures are associated with a poor prognosis and that the incidence of seizures is not affected by the target temperature. METHODS: Post-hoc analysis of reported clinical seizures during day 1-7 in the TTM-trial including their treatment, EEG-findings, and long-term neurological outcome. The trial randomised 939 comatose survivors to TTM at 33°C or 36°C with strict criteria for withdrawal of life-sustaining therapies. Sensitivity, specificity and false positive rate for poor outcome were reported for different types of seizures. RESULTS: Clinical seizures were registered in 268 patients (29%), similarly distributed in both intervention arms. Early and late seizures were equally predictive of poor outcome. Myoclonic seizures were the most common (240 patients, 26%) and the most predictive of a poor outcome (sensitivity 36.1%, false positive rate 4.3%). Two patients with status myoclonus regained consciousness, one with a good neurological outcome, generating a false positive rate of poor outcome of 0.2% (95%CI 0.0-1.0). CONCLUSION: Clinical seizures are common after cardiac arrest and indicate poor outcome with limited specificity. Prolonged seizures are a very grave sign but occasional patients may have a good outcome. The level of the target temperature does not affect the prevalence or prognostic significance of seizures.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Lybeck, Anna","Friberg, Hans","Aneman, Anders","Hassager, Christian","Horn, Janneke","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Kuiper, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Ullén, Susann","Wise, Matthew P","Westhall, Erik","Cronberg, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455688"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["TTM-trial Investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Coma","Electroencephalography","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Multicenter Study","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Randomized Controlled Trial","Risk Factors","Seizures","Sensitivity and Specificity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic significance of clinical seizures after cardiac arrest and target temperature management","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-455688","identifier":[{"id":"28163232","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85012884110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-68446bae-6353-44cc-8bdb-2e2b8b9b8155"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Coma","Electroencephalography","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Multicenter Study","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Randomized Controlled Trial","Risk Factors","Seizures","Sensitivity and Specificity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E584455F733D7E0FF7B5E63749ED1424"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns