{"abstract":"Incineration of sewage sludge is a common practice in many western countries. Gasification is an attractive option because of its high energy efficiency and flexibility in the usage of the produced gas. However, they both unavoidably produce sewage sludge ashes, a material that is rich in phosphorus, but which is commonly landfilled or used in construction materials. With current uncertainty in phosphate rock supply, phosphorus recovery from sewage sludge ashes has become interesting. In the present work, ashes from incineration and gasification of the same sewage sludge were compared in terms of phosphorus extractability using electrodialytic (ED) methods. The results show that comparable recovery rates of phosphorus were achieved with a single ED step for incineration ashes and a sequential combination of two ED steps for gasification ashes, which was due to a higher influence of iron and/or aluminium in phosphorus solubility for the latter. A product with lower level of metallic impurities and comparable to wet process phosphoric acid was eventually obtained from gasification ashes. Thus, gasification becomes an interesting alternative to incineration also in terms of phosphorus separation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Parés Viader, Raimon","Jensen, Pernille Erland","Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-097.04-037767"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Electrodialysis","Heavy metals","Incineration","Low temperature gasification","Phosphorus","Sewage sludge ash"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of phosphorus recovery from incineration and gasification sewage sludge ash","src":["dtu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/137330544/Comparison_of_phosphorus_recovery_from_incineration_and_gasification_sewage_sludge_ash.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-097.04-037767","identifier":[{"id":"wst_2016_620","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85018413442","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28272054","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-e8104f65-8b0e-4df8-9aba-f1e28b874351","ruc-4798cd0c-442c-428e-8c44-b2790c86cd51"],"keyword":["Electrodialysis","Heavy metals","Incineration","Low-temperature gasification","Phosphorus","Sewage sludge ash"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F4C856759F40B450F829D4FA3A3131BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/59945888/Comparison_of_phosphorus_recovery_from_incineration_and_gasification_sewage_sludge_ash.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/137330544/Comparison_of_phosphorus_recovery_from_incineration_and_gasification_sewage_sludge_ash.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/wst.2016.620","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, ARTEK, Section for Arctic Engineering and Sustainable Solutions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Raimon","key":"parésviaderpau","last":"Parés Viader","locid":"d5b464c6-90ab-4f44-8f76-3d0295518738","name":"Parés Viader, Raimon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Erland","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c21f7bd4-85f5-420a-b31b-51a5c58bc254","name":"Jensen, Pernille Erland","orcid":"0000-0003-4718-1630","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lisbeth M.","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","locid":"653cfe69-d98d-42ec-b241-5409bbfc951c","name":"Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","orcid":"0000-0001-7756-382X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Pape","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f75a7756-932a-4066-8a74-8955f3f30f55","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"0bc8cc02-9199-4a75-9e51-7dd5ceba9583","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8929-9691","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28272054"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2166/wst.2016.620","issn":["02731223","19969732"],"issn_org":["02731223"],"issue":"5","journal":"Water Science and Technology","pages":"1251-1260","publisher":"IWA Publishing","status":"p","title":"Water Science and Technology","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018413442"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e8104f65-8b0e-4df8-9aba-f1e28b874351","ruc-4798cd0c-442c-428e-8c44-b2790c86cd51"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Comparison of phosphorus recovery from incineration and gasification sewage sludge ash","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.04-037767","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Chronic itch is difficult to treat and associated with significantly decreased life quality. Topical low-concentration capsaicin (0.006-0.05%) has previously been investigated and applied in therapy of itch but contradictory evidence exits regarding its efficacy. OBJECTIVES: This placebo-controlled, double-blinded study investigated the effect of 8% topical capsaicin applied for 1 and 24 hours on evoked itch, neurogenic inflammation and itch-associated dysesthesia. METHODS: Sixteen healthy volunteers (22±0.5 years, 9F) were treated with capsaicin for 1h and 24hrs, and vehicle for 24hrs on each volar forearm. After capsaicin/vehicle application, histamine (1%, administered prick test lancets) and cowhage (40-45 spicules) were applied in pretreated areas. Evoked itch and pain intensities were recorded for 10 minutes using a visual analog scale (0-10 cm), while Sensitivity To Touch-evoked Itch (STTI) was evaluated using von Frey filaments before/after itch provocations (as a measure of punctuate hyperknesis). Neurogenic inflammation was assessed using perfusion-imaging. RESULTS: In the vehicle-pretreated areas peak itch responses to histamine and cowhage were 4.67±0.58 and 5.15±0.71, respectively. Capsaicin-pretreatment reduced peak itch responses to both histamine and cowhage, after 24-hour pretreatment to 1.41±0.58 (p=0.003) and 0.81±0.18, (p<0.001), respectively. 1-hour capsaicin-pretreatment only reduced cowhage-induced itch (p=0.023). Furthermore, 24-hours capsaicin-pretreatment abolished punctuate hyperknesis and lowered histamine-induced neurogenic inflammation but did not affect wheal reactions. CONCLUSIONS: Twenty-four hours of topical 8% capsaicin-pretreatment reduced histaminergic and non-histaminergic itch by ≈75%, while only significant reduction was achieved for non-histaminergic itch in a standard 1-hour treatment. Further investigations are needed to elucidate the clinical potential of high-concentration capsaicin as an antipruritic. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Hjalte Holm","Marker, Jens Broch","Hoeck, Emil August Østergaard","Elberling, J.","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-098.00-002610"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antipruritic effect of pretreatment with topical capsaicin 000000000008 on histamine and cowhage evoked itch in healthy volunteers a randomized vehicle controlled proof of concept trial","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-098.00-002610","identifier":[{"id":"28117875","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020412951","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000406036200027","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-345b75df-e46e-4b00-8e81-74c17a4b4aa5","ku-99a988e2-d3ea-445e-821d-f2f1def08762"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-544038783DA35128DB34EBB5495DF422"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Pain and Motor System Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hjalte Holm","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5de532a5-1602-416c-96b7-20a316e28e25","name":"Andersen, Hjalte Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Broch","key":"markerpau","last":"Marker","locid":"ea7f550b-974c-4bc8-85f0-04327d1a3bb9","name":"Marker, Jens Broch","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil A.","key":"hoeckpau","last":"Hoeck","locid":"6a34c578-227d-4f84-9689-7d16ca6b9aae","name":"Hoeck, Emil August Østergaard","name_org":"Hoeck, Emil A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J.","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","locid":"7aab77bb-8c61-43b3-bd29-e5db736cceef","name":"Elberling, Jesper","name_org":"Elberling, J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28117875"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bjd.15335","issn":["00070963","13652133"],"issn_org":["00070963"],"issue":"1","journal":"British Journal of Dermatology","pages":"107-116","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Dermatology","volume":"177"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020412951"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-345b75df-e46e-4b00-8e81-74c17a4b4aa5","ku-99a988e2-d3ea-445e-821d-f2f1def08762"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antipruritic effect of pretreatment with topical capsaicin 8% on histamine- and cowhage-evoked itch in healthy volunteers : a randomized, vehicle-controlled, proof-of-concept trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.00-002610","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The Bacillus Calmette-Guérin vaccine (BCG) has been associated with beneficial non-specific effects (NSEs) on infant health. Within a randomized trial on the effect of neonatal BCG on overall health, we investigated the possible immunological impact of neonatal BCG vaccination on lymphocyte subsets, determined by flow cytometry. In 118 infants blood samples were obtained 4 (±2) days post randomization to BCG vaccination or no intervention, and at 3 and 13 months of age. No effects of BCG were found at 4 days. However, BCG increased proportions of effector memory cells at 3 months (Geometric mean ratio (GMR) 1.62, 95% confidence interval (CI) (1.20-2.21), p = 0.002 for CD4(+) T cells and GMR 1.69, 95% CI (1.06-2.70), p = 0.03 for CD8(+) T cells), and reduced proportions of late differentiated CD4(+) T cells (GMR = 0.62, 95% CI (0.38-1.00), p = 0.05) and apoptotic CD4(+) T cells at 13 months (GMR = 0.55, 95% CI (0.32-0.92), p = 0.03). In conclusion, limited overall impact of neonatal BCG vaccination on lymphocyte subsets was found in healthy Danish infants within the first 13 months of life. This is in line with the limited clinical effects of BCG observed in our setting.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Birk, Nina Marie","Nissen, Thomas Nørrelykke","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Hartling, Hans Jacob","Thøstesen, Lisbeth Marianne","Kofoed, Poul-Erik","Stensballe, Lone Graff","Andersen, Andreas","Pryds, Ole","Netea, Mihai G","Benn, Christine Stabell","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Jeppesen, Dorthe Lisbeth"],"cuid":["S02-099.92-043375"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Birk, Nina Marie"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Medical Center"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of bacillus calmette guérin bcg vaccination at birth on t and b lymphocyte subsets results from a clinical randomized trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-017-11601-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.92-043375","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5622034","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28963455","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85030323578","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-70542086-1d9c-465e-9b59-7234ce62e57f","sdu-7ace8bd2-9d33-47a7-97a9-ba41ea508b8d"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-10BA3A19576E03390E9993E8F8490018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134225639/effects_of_Bacillus.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-017-11601-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/185987982/s41598_017_11601_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark"