t":"Nyholm Jørgensen","locid":"8d6c3178-b2a4-4c33-b5f9-b0ee8f679986","name":"Nyholm Jørgensen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-1329-1674","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René A.","key":"sørensenppu","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f8653b3f-bd0a-4938-ac41-26e3ca36d339","name":"Sørensen, René A.","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Stigaard","key":"laursenppu","last":"Laursen","locid":"262e6719-f46f-473a-9d3c-705a59d01e89","name":"Laursen, Morten Stigaard","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenppu","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","rank":4,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"nielsenppu","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":5,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"YouTube","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-258d22c9-90c5-4783-807d-358f886d3694"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"FutureCropping Generering af tidselkort med Pix4D, DeepLearning og QGIS 18AUG2017","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-150896","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We consider the situation where a large number n of players want to securely compute a large function f with security against an adaptive, malicious adversary which might corrupt t < cn of the parties for some given c ∈ [0, 1). In other words, only some arbitrarily small constant fraction of the parties are assumed to be honest. For any fixed c, we consider the asymptotic complexity as n and the size of f grows. We are in particular interested in the computational overhead, defined as the total computational complexity of all parties divided by the size of f. We show that it is possible to achieve poly-logarithmic computational overhead for all c < 1. Prior to our result it was only known how to get poly-logarithmic overhead for c < 1/2. We therefore significantly extend the area where we can do secure multiparty computation with polylogarithmic overhead. Since we allow that more than half the parties are corrupted, we can only get security with abort, i.e., the adversary might make the protocol abort before all parties learn their outputs. We can, however, for all c make a protocol for which there exists d > 0 such that if at most dn parties are actually corrupted in a given execution, then the protocol will not abort. Our result is solely of theoretical interest. In its current form, it has not practical implications whatsoever.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Ranellucci, Samuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-197593"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-31","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2017-03-28","title":"20th IACR International Conference on Practice and Theory of Public-Key Cryptography, PKC 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ranellucci, Samuel"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","George Mason University","University System of Maryland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the computational overhead of mpc with dishonest majority","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014438192","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-197593","identifier":[{"id":"85014438192","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-775d0e2e-d3fa-491f-a5d9-a7988642a38c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-15115B363DE6D5A0063A7A768C72B9F5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"george mason university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"George Mason University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university system of maryland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University System of Maryland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel","key":"ranelluccipau","last":"Ranellucci","name":"Ranellucci, Samuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Serge","key":"fehrpedh","last":"Fehr","name":"Fehr, Serge","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.100