{"abstract":"Paravalvular leakage (PVL) occurs in 6%-15% of cases after surgical heart valve replacement. A percutaneous approach is increasingly used to close PVLs as an alternative to repeat surgery. Computed tomography (CT) can be used for simulation of fluoroscopic cardiac anatomy. This technique allows preprocedural definition of optimal C-arm angulations and PVL localization in reference to fluoroscopic views. It is very helpful for guidewire crossing of the PVL and positioning of the closure device. We report a case with the first use of dedicated software for fluoroscopic simulation (FluoroCT) in transcatheter mitral PVL closure.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Korsholm, Kasper","Mortensen, Ulrik","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Piazza, Nicolo","Thériault-Lauzier, Pascal","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-245542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Paravalvular leak","Software"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcatheter mitral paravalvular leak closure facilitated by preprocedural cardiac ct for simulation of fluoroscopic anatomy and paravalvular defect localization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85011340655","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-245542","identifier":[{"id":"28145877","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85011340655","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cb648e9f-1380-4761-aba0-0a060d044c1d"],"keyword":["FluoroCT","Paravalvular leak","Software"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-95D17BBB9C30FC01E925967701CBBE4D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"45ade509-f8d0-479c-95a8-5c94e1cfaf65","name":"Mortensen, Ulrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolo","key":"piazzapau","last":"Piazza","name":"Piazza, Nicolo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pascal","key":"thériaultlauzierpau","last":"Thériault-Lauzier","name":"Thériault-Lauzier, Pascal","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28145877"],"pub":{"issn":["10423931","15572501"],"issn_org":["10423931"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Invasive Cardiology","publisher":"Cliggott Publishing Co.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Invasive Cardiology","title_org":"The Journal of invasive cardiology","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011340655"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cb648e9f-1380-4761-aba0-0a060d044c1d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Transcatheter Mitral Paravalvular Leak Closure Facilitated by Preprocedural Cardiac CT for Simulation of Fluoroscopic Anatomy and Paravalvular Defect Localization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-245542","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Sediments from the small lake Ilsø situated in the Illerup/Alken Enge Valley were studied in order to investigate past landscape development at the time of a probably ritual human mass burial following battle during the Roman Iron Age (ad 1–400). A pollen record from Ilsø and a number of other records from Jutland were combined using the Landscape Reconstruction Algorithm to reconstruct local vegetation changes through the last 2,800 years. These methods were supplemented by studies of catchment-related geochemistry of the Ilsø lake sediments. The results show a marked reforestation event associated with a strong decrease in erosion levels at the very beginning of the first century ad, contemporaneous with the finds of human remains at Alken Enge. Comparison with a pollen record 10 km away and with those from other sites, reveals that this reforestation occurs unusually early and rapidly, and is an unparalleled development in a Danish context. We suggest that the major landscape changes at the beginning of the Roman Iron Age and forest cover for the next few centuries comprise a possible example of ritual control of local land-use.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Søe, Niels Emil","Odgaard, Bent Vad","Nielsen, Anne Birgitte","Olsen, Jesper","Kristiansen, Søren Munch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256954"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Odgaard, Bent Vad"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Erosion rates","Iron Age","Palaeolimnology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"late holocene landscape development around a roman iron age mass grave alken enge denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84991628315","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256954","identifier":[{"id":"84991628315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-df8c766d-0732-4019-b9c0-3f4207f6e2fc"],"keyword":["Erosion rates","Iron Age","Landscape Reconstruction Algorithm","Palaeolimnology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D67C26F573CADC50080CD1BE60BDCED"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Emil","key":"søepau","last":"Søe","locid":"a7ca50c8-add2-44b5-baf5-e5780c92afaa","name":"Søe, Niels Emil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent Vad","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"4ee030b7-6e35-4a20-98aa-651fcbe39e87","name":"Odgaard, Bent Vad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Birgitte","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anne Birgitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren M.","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"96d56247-9432-4030-9387-cdb020665136","name":"Kristiansen, Søren Munch","name_org":"Kristiansen, Søren M.","orcid":"0000-0003-3128-4061","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00334-016-0591-x","issn":["09396314","16176278"],"issn_org":["09396314"],"issue":"3","journal":"Vegetation History and Archaeobotany","pages":"277-292","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Vegetation History and Archaeobotany","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991628315"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-df8c766d-0732-4019-b9c0-3f4207f6e2fc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Late Holocene landscape development around a Roman Iron Age mass grave, Alken Enge, Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-256954","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Tissue factor (TF) is related to aggressiveness and invasiveness of cancer and there is a correlation between tumor TF expression, metastatic potential, and patient outcome. The aim of the study was to test the therapeutic potential and toxicity of a novel compound for localized TF targeted radionuclide therapy. The radionuclide therapy was based on Factor VII (FVII), the natural ligand to TF. In the current study, we investigated the biodistribution, therapeutic potential and toxicity of 177Lu labeled active site inhibited FVIIa (177Lu-FVIIai) in an experimental mouse model of pancreatic cancer. Methods: p-SCN-Bn-CHX-A’’-DTPA was conjugated to FVIIai followed by radiolabeling with 177Lu (177Lu-CHX-A’’-DTPA-FVIIai). A pancreas xenograft mouse model (BxPC3) was used to assess the therapeutic potential of 177Lu-FVIIai. NMRI nude mice with subcutaneous BxPC3 tumors were used. The mice were randomized into groups receiving 177Lu-FVIIai, FVIIai, or vehicle when the tumor volumes were about 50 mm3. 177Lu-FVIIai was administered in doses of 15 MBq, 7.5 MBq or 2 x 7.5 MBq (n=8 mice/group). Tumor growth was monitored three times weekly. Biodistribution of 177Lu-FVIIai was studied ex vivo in several organs at 1, 4, 24, 72 and 168 hours after injection. The in vivo biodistribution of 177Lu-FVIIai was evaluated by SPECT/CT imaging. Furthermore, competition and dose escalation experiments (1-30 MBq) were performed. In a parallel set of NMRI mice, toxic effects of 177Lu-FVIIai were evaluated by hematology, histology and 99mTc-DMSA scintigraphy. Results: FVIIai was successfully radiolabeled with 177Lu with a specific activity of 10-25 GBq/µmol after EDTA scavenging and PD-10 purification. Treatment with FVIIai did not change tumor growth compared to the vehicle groups. The mice that received 15 MBq 177Lu-FVIIai had a significantly reduced tumor growth from day 0 to day 19 compared with mice from the control groups (425.5±44.8% versus 614.2±49.1%; p=0.02). The groups receiving 7.5 MBq or 2 x 7.5 MBq 177Lu-FVVai had no significant different tumor growth compared with controls on day 19. Tumor uptake of 177Lu-FVIIai measured ex vivo was 1.16±0.04, 1.97±0.18, 1.95±0.07, 1.01±0.06, 0.31±0.02 percent injected dose per gram (%ID/g) at 1, 4, 24, 72 and 168 hours post-injection, respectively. Injection with unlabeled FVIIai 10 minutes before 177Lu-FVIIai injection significantly reduced tumor uptake of 177Lu-FVIIai (from 2.5±0.16 %ID/g to 1.7±0.05 %ID/g; p<0.05). Escalating the dose of 177Lu-ASIS from 1-30 MBq did not change tumor uptake (%ID/g). A transient decrease in leucocyte counts was observed for the mice receiving 15 and 7.5 MBq 177Lu-FVIIai. Ten weeks after injection of 177Lu-FVIIai kidney uptake of 99mTc-DMSA was significantly decreased in all the treatment groups compared to the vehicle group when measured by SPECT imaging. Conclusion: FVIIai was successfully radiolabeled with 177Lu. 177Lu-FVIIai showed anti-tumor activity in a mouse model of human pancreatic cancer. Treatment with 177Lu-ASIS induced a transient decrease in leucocyte counts and a decreased kidney function ten weeks after injection.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Carsten","Jensen, Mette","Fonslet, Jesper","Knudsen, Camilla","Jeppesen, Troels","Jensen, Andreas","Severin, Gregory","Kjær, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313574"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radionuclide therapy with tissue factor targeting lu 000000000177 fviiai inhibits growth in an experimental mouse model of human pancreatic cancer","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-313574","identifier":[{"id":"000404949902072","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-1e1bea5e-9891-4a69-806c-877281b4711c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2054E5AC5DAEB05699EEC796175FCFC6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Center for Nuclear Technologies","Technical University of Denmark, Center for Nuclear Technologies, The Hevesy Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"nielsencarstenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Carsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"jensenmettepau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"fonsletjesperpau","last":"Fonslet","locid":"4e7c8b5c-0ca8-486a-90a2-0a43669dc729","name":"Fonslet, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-1563-0251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"knudsencamillapau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Camilla","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels","key":"jeppesentroelspau","last":"Jeppesen","name":"Jeppesen, Troels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"jensenandreaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"2c0d444b-509d-4d47-a8ea-d3818433f84b","name":"Jensen, Andreas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory","key":"severingregorypau","last":"Severin","locid":"0e92340c-c204-4cd4-a297-06bb096315e3","name":"Severin, Gregory","orcid":"0000-0003-1189-7311","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"kjærandreaspau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Andreas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01615505","15355667"],"issn_org":["01615505"],"issue":"suppl. 1","journal":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","paperid":"463","publisher":"Society of Nuclear Medicine Inc.","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Nuclear Medicine","title_org":"Journal of Nuclear Medicine","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1e1bea5e-9891-4a69-806c-877281b4711c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Radionuclide therapy with tissue factor targeting Lu-177-FVIIai inhibits growth in an experimental mouse model of human pancreatic cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313574","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Many data-driven approaches exist to extract neural representations of functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) data, but most of them lack a proper probabilistic formulation. We propose a scalable group level probabilistic sparse factor analysis (psFA) allowing spatially sparse maps, component pruning using automatic relevance determination (ARD) and subject specific heteroscedastic spatial noise modeling. For task-based and resting state fMRI, we show that the sparsity constraint gives rise to components similar to those obtained by group independent component analysis. The noise modeling shows that noise is reduced in areas typically associated with activation by the experimental design. The psFA model identifies sparse components and the probabilistic setting provides a natural way to handle parameter uncertainties. The variational Bayesian framework easily extends to more complex noise models than the presently considered.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hinrich, Jesper Løve","Nielsen, Søren Føns Vind","Riis, Nicolai Andre Brogaard","Eriksen, Casper","Frøsig, Jacob","Kristensen, Marco D. F.","Schmidt, Mikkel Nørgaard","Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","Mørup, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335425"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-09","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2017-03-05","title":"2017 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Analytical models","Correlation","Data models","Graphics processing units","Indexes","Neuroimaging","Principal component analysis","Probabilistic logic","Sparsity","Variational Bayes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scalable group level probabilistic sparse factor analysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85023774152","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335425","identifier":[{"id":"85023774152","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-674932b9-e9f3-49d3-a33c-0bb36bf1334c"],"keyword":["Analytical models","Correlation","Data models","Graphics processing units","Independent components","Indexes","Neuroimaging","Principal component analysis","Probabilistic factor analysis","Probabilistic logic","Variational Bayes","sparsity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB2E50C74840D752468DF81A359E8219"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Løve","key":"hinrichpau","last":"Hinrich","locid":"e3c8c713-afa8-4d6e-9071-774487e7e599","name":"Hinrich, Jesper Løve","orcid":"0000-0003-0258-7151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Føns Vind","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"82813a45-694c-483d-81ea-5ba6f2e77078","name":"Nielsen, Søren Føns Vind","orcid":"0000-0001-6713-9144","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicolai Andre Brogaard","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"a740c408-ea09-43fa-9ec7-45cac16af745","name":"Riis, Nicolai Andre Brogaard","orcid":"0000-0002-6883-9078","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Casper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"frøsigpau","last":"Frøsig","name":"Frøsig, Jacob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco D. F.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Marco D. F.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Nørgaard","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"55dbf06c-c859-4324-8104-3fa649d8d140","name":"Schmidt, Mikkel Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6927-8869","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer Hougaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"243ae993-e526-4121-b28a-aabf62c3df84","name":"Madsen, Kristoffer Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8606-7641","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"møruppau","last":"Mørup","locid":"7ffdfaca-76bd-44ec-a98f-13fe4f033b71","name":"Mørup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-4985-4368","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp.2017.7953371","isbn":["9781509041169"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"6314-6318","publisher":"IEEE","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2017 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85023774152"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-674932b9-e9f3-49d3-a33c-0bb36bf1334c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Scalable group level probabilistic sparse factor analysis","type":"Conference Paper","