search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-075273","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Millimeter wave (mmWave) communication works in the frequencies above 6 gigahertz (GHz), with the system bandwidth up to 500 megahertz (MHz) or wider. In this case, the channel situations are dramatically different from the existing wireless channels in Third Generation/Fourth Generation (3G/4G) communication systems, and the stationarity of mmWave channels could be very different from our former knowledge. The focus of this paper is to study the frequency and spatial stationarities of mmWave channels. For better understanding, we compare the stationarity regions between mmWave channels and the channels below 6 GHz. First, the general average power delay profile (APDP) method is introduced as a metric to determine the size of the stationarity regions in time, frequency, and spatial domains. Then, the general APDP method is applied in the data analysis of a channel measurement. We find that the frequency stationarity regions of the channels are much larger in mmWave bands above 6 GHz than those in conventional bands below 6 GHz, while the spatial stationarity regions of the channels are much smaller in mmWave bands above 6 GHz than those in conventional bands below 6 GHz","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yi, Tan","Wang, Chengxiang","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-084605"],"event":{"acronym":"IWCMC","end":"2017-06-30","place":"Valencia, es","start":"2017-06-26","title":"The 13th International Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Heriot-Watt University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of stationarity regions for wireless channels from 000000000002 ghz to 000000000030 ghz","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-084605","identifier":[{"id":"85027845469","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000426991500109","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-76fddcd1-55f4-4b34-950e-2e627f8e2715"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FDA735BBA4A68DB0EF7FBE7547AD6813"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"heriot watt university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Heriot-Watt University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tan","key":"yipau","last":"Yi","name":"Yi, Tan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chengxiang","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chengxiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iwcmc.2017.7986361","eisbn":["9781509043729"],"isbn":["9781509043736"],"pages":"647-652","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2017 13th International Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing Conference (IWCMC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027845469"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-76fddcd1-55f4-4b34-950e-2e627f8e2715"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparison of Stationarity Regions for Wireless Channels From 2 GHz to 30 GHz","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-084605","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"For mobile systems involving hand held devices, the influence of the user on system performance has to be considered. Extensive studies below 6 GHz have demonstrated large effects on system performance. However, the impact of user influence at potential higher frequency bands for upcoming 5G mobile networks is still to be investigated. This work investigates how the user affects the performance of a 5G handset mock-up. The user impact is studied by channel sounding in an indoor scenario, with and without the presence of different users. The mock-up handset has a uniform linear array of receive (Rx) antennas operated at 21.5 GHz. A dual-polarized horn antenna with a wide beamwidth is used as transmit (Tx) antenna and a fast channel sounder is used, allowing for recording dynamic and realistic channels. The results show that the mean influence of the user on the power varies considerably depending on the scenario, with more than 12 dB loss in some cases, while a gain of 4 dB is seen in other. An important finding is that the mean power among the seven Rx branches may be very different. Branch power ratios in the typical range of 2–10 dB were found, depending on the user and scenario.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hejselbæk, Johannes","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Fan, Wei","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-087057"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measured 000000000021 000000000005 ghz indoor channels with user held handset antenna array","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/261604044/Measured_21_5_GHz_Indoor_Channels_With_User_Held_Handset_Antenna_Array.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-087057","identifier":[{"id":"000417885000034","type":"wos"},{"id":"85028516260","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7f31f0f9-c7f8-46d4-b342-8c43735dff86"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BE784ACC70E9DE4B3FB1A3E97E187A62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/261604044/Measured_21_5_GHz_Indoor_Channels_With_User_Held_Handset_Antenna_Array.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"hejselbækpau","last":"Hejselbæk","locid":"9163c39e-9747-4c12-bcb7-861a91af7c57","name":"Hejselbæk, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-3053-5474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau",