{"abstract":"We demonstrate the measurement of a 2D MeV-range ion velocity distribution function by velocity-space tomography at JET. Deuterium ions were accelerated into the MeV-range by third harmonic ion cyclotron resonance heating. We made measurements with three neutron emission spectrometers and a high-resolution γ-ray spectrometer detecting the γ-rays released in two reactions. The tomographic inversion based on these five spectra is in excellent agreement with numerical simulations with the ASCOT–RFOF and the SPOT–RFOF codes. The length of the measured fast-ion tail corroborates the prediction that very few particles are accelerated above 2 MeV due to the weak wave-particle interaction at higher energies.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Salewski, Mirko","Nocente, M.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Binda, F.","Cazzaniga, C.","Ericsson, G.","Eriksson, J.","Gorini, G.","Hellesen, C.","Hjalmarsson, A.","Kiptily, V.G.","Koskela, T.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Kurki-Suonio, T.","Leipold, Frank","Madsen, Jens","Moseev, Dmitry","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Schneider, M.","Sharapov, S.E.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardocchi, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-366050"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Italy","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","ITER Cadarache","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Research Council of Italy","Rutherford Appleton Laboratory","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Milan - Bicocca","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Fast ions","Neutron emission spectrometry","Tokamak","Velocity space tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rty