":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b3c4a03c-46dd-41ae-bc6f-3c91bf24ccf8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Johannæisk filosofi?","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-500806","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The dimethoxyphenyl-N-((2-methoxyphenyl)methyl)ethanamine (NBOMe) compounds are potent serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonists and have recently been subject to recreational use due to their hallucinogenic effects. Use of NBOMe compounds has been known since 2011, and several non-fatal and fatal intoxication cases have been reported in the scientific literature. The aim of this study was to determine the importance of the different cytochrome P450 enzymes (CYP) involved in the metabolism of 2-(4-iodo-2,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-N-(2methoxybenzyl)ethanamine (25I-NBOMe) and 2-[[2-(4-iodo-2,5dimethoxyphenyl)ethylamino]methyl]phenol (25I-NBOH) and to characterize the metabolites. The following approaches were used to identify the main enzymes involved in primary metabolism: incubation with a panel of CYP and monoamine oxidase (MAO) enzymes and incubation in pooled human liver microsomes (HLM) with and without specific CYP chemical inhibitors. The study was further substantiated by an evaluation of 25I-NBOMe and 25I-NBOH metabolism in single donor HLM. The metabolism pathways of 25I-NBOMe and 25I-NBOH were NADPHdependent with intrinsic clearance values of (CLint) of 70.1 and 118.7 mL/min/kg, respectively. The biotransformations included hydroxylation, O-demethylation, N-dealkylation, dehydrogenation, and combinations thereof. The most abundant metabolites were all identified by retention time and spectrum matching with synthesized reference standards. The major CYP enzymes involved in the metabolism of 25I-NBOMe and 25INBOH were identified as CYP3A4 and CYP2D6, respectively. The compound 25I-NBOH was also liable to direct glucuronidation, which may diminish the impact of CYP2D6 genetic polymorphism. Users of 25I-NBOMe may be subject to drug-drug interactions (DDI) if 25I-NBOMe is taken with a strong CYP3A4 inhibitor. Copyright © 2016 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line Marie","Holm, Niels Bjerre","Leth-Petersen, Sebastian","Kristensen, Jesper Langgaard","Olsen, Lars","Linnet, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-517644"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of the hepatic cytochrome p000000000450 enzymes involved in the metabolism of 000000000025i nbome and 000000000025i nboh","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-517644","identifier":[{"id":"84978907397","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27400739","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cfe49316-86ef-4a0e-9639-2e9fe5ae3d81"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76F9B7DB1617B153E53D0E11D355D24B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biostructural Research","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Section of Forensic Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Marie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c206ea3f-9342-46ec-9359-0f9602fa8ef6","name":"Nielsen, Line Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels Bjerre","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"dab1d12e-3995-43ea-bef6-766c7b40a1dd","name":"Holm, Niels Bjerre","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"lethpetersenpau","last":"Leth-Petersen","locid":"b9b48b