{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Patients with normal stress perfusion have an excellent prognosis. Prospective studies on the diagnostic accuracy of stress-only scans with contemporary, independent examinations as gold standards are lacking. PATIENTS AND METHODS: A total of 109 patients with typical angina and no previous coronary artery disease underwent a 2-day stress (exercise)/rest, gated, and attenuation-corrected (AC), 99m-technetium-sestamibi perfusion study, followed by invasive coronary angiography. The stress datasets were evaluated twice by four physicians with two different training levels (expert and novice): familiar and unfamiliar with AC. The two experts also made a consensus reading of the integrated stress-rest datasets. The consensus reading and quantitative data from the invasive coronary angiography were applied as reference methods. RESULTS: The sensitivity/specificity were 0.92-1.00/0.73-0.90 (reference: expert consensus reading), 0.93-0.96/0.63-0.82 (reference: ≥1 stenosis>70%), and 0.75-0.88/0.70-0.88 (reference: ≥1 stenosis>50%). The four readers showed a high and fairly equal sensitivity independent of their familiarity with AC. The expert familiar with AC had the highest specificity independent of the reference method. The intraobserver and interobserver agreements on the stress-only readings were good (readers without AC experience) to excellent (readers with AC experience). CONCLUSION: AC stress-only images yielded a high sensitivity independent of the training level and experience with AC of the nuclear physician, whereas the specificity correlated positively with both. Interobserver and intraobserver agreements tended to be the best for physicians with AC experience.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ejlersen, June A","May, Ole","Mortensen, Jesper","Nielsen, Gitte L","Lauridsen, Jeppe Killerich","Johansen, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-634591"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stress only myocardial perfusion scintigraphy a prospective study on the accuracy and observer agreement with quantitative coronary angiography as the gold standard","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85032196458","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-634591","identifier":[{"id":"85032196458","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28885540","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-d644e4a7-367c-49eb-a6a4-819c8ed730dc"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5C5D2642D1EFC0A495F8C35F5804CB30"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Holstebro"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"June A","key":"ejlersenpau","last":"Ejlersen","name":"Ejlersen, June A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"maypau","last":"May","name":"May, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte L","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gitte L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe F","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"8fdc9a2d-e00c-45d3-aac9-3bde8cf5e73a","name":"Lauridsen, Jeppe Killerich","name_org":"Lauridsen, Jeppe F","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johansen","key":"allanpau","last":"Allan","locid":"dc7a1a61-b703-48ec-bd87-c92b55784133","name":"Johansen, Allan","name_org":"Allan, Johansen","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-057X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28885540"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mnm.0000000000000739","issn":["01433636"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nuclear Medicine Communications","pages":"904-911","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Medicine Communications","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032196458"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d644e4a7-367c-49eb-a6a4-819c8ed730dc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Stress-only myocardial perfusion scintigraphy : a prospective study on the accuracy and observer agreement with quantitative coronary angiography as the gold standard","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-634591","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Few questionnaires used in monitoring sun-related behaviour have been tested for validity. Objectives: We established the criteria validity of a questionnaire developed for monitoring population sun-related behaviour. Methods: During May–August 2013, 664 Danes wore a personal electronic ultraviolet radiation (UVR) dosimeter for 1 week that measured their outdoor time and dose of erythemal UVR exposure. In the following week, they answered a questionnaire on their sun-related behaviour in the measurement week. Results: Outdoor time measured by dosimetry correlated strongly with both outdoor time and the developed exposure scale measured in the questionnaire. Exposure measured in standard erythema dose (SED) by dosimetry correlated strongly with the exposure scale. In a linear regression model of UVR (SED) received, 41% of the variation was explained by skin type, age, week of participation and exposure scale, with exposure scale as the main contributor. The weekly sunburn fraction correlated strongly with the number of ambient sun hours (r = 0·73, P < 0·001). Conclusions: This criteria-validated questionnaire provides evidence of the exposure that the questionnaire aimed to measure. The evidence provided showed a strong link between the objectively measured behaviour and the behaviour measured by this survey construct. The questionnaire is the first validated tool to measure the UVR exposure in a national population-based sample.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Køster, Brian","Søndergaard, Jens","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Allen, M","Olsen, A.","Bentzen, J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-641833"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Canterbury"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Denmark epidemiology","Environmental Exposure analysis","Female","Health Behavior","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Radiation Dosage","Sunlight","Surveys and Questionnaires standards","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the validated sun exposure questionnaire association of objective and subjective measures of sun exposure in a danish population based sample","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bjd.14861","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-641833","identifier":[{"id":"85007137821","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27412948","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-efa01b3a-b66a-4b40-a3bd-2f91af7baeb4"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Age Distribution","Aged","Denmark/epidemiology","Environmental Exposure/analysis","Female","Health Behavior","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Radiation Dosage","Radiation Dosimeters","Sunburn/epidemiology","Sunlight","Sunscreening Agents/therapeutic use","Surveys and Questionnaires/standards","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC563D7A3CCF4872BBDA6CCB76700892"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bjd.14861","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128961875/K_ster_et_al_2017_British_Journal_of_Dermatology.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Kræftens Bekæmpelse"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nz","key":"university of canterbury","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Canterbury","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"B","key":"køsterpau","last":"Køster","locid":"b5dacba2-0e04-4301-93cc-f6c6ab09b564","name":"Køster, Brian","name_org":"Køster, B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","name_org":"Søndergaard, J","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, J B","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M","key":"allenpau","last":"Allen","name":"Allen, M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","name":"Bentzen, J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27412948"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bjd.14861","issn":["00070963","13652133"],"issn_org":["00070963"],"issue":"2","journal":"British Journal of Dermatology","pages":"446-456"