{"abstract":"Background and aims Measure instruments that measure the extent to which patients are involved in the process of decision-making are developed and validated and being used worldwide. So far, no validated self-report instrument for the shared decision making (SDM) process is available in Denmark. The German 9-item Shared Decision Making Questionnaire (SDM-Q-9, patient version) is used to measure the extent to which patients are involved in the process of decision-making. The questionnaire can be used in both research and clinical practice. It can be used when there are several treatment options for a particular disease and can be implemented for purposes of evaluation and quality improvement in health care. It has been translated into 17 languages, thus it can be suitable for comparing results internationally. The aim was to translate and cultural adapt a Danish translation of the SDM-Q-9 patient version to the context of Danish women with pelvic organ prolapse and patients with cruciate ligament injuries in the Outpatient Gynecology Clinic and the Department of Sports Traumatology. A brief description of methods In accordance with and acceptance of the German authors the original SDM-Q-9, patient version was translated from German and cultural adapted into a Danish context following WHO’s four phased recommended process; (1) Forward translation (2) Expert panel discussion – Back translation (3) Pre-testing and cognitive interviewing and (4) Final version and documentation. A brief summary of results to support conclusion A forward and backward translation were completed by four different translators and followed by an adjustment made by the expert panel. The expert panel included the three of the four translators, experts in health, instrument development and translation and an expert in the field of gynecology. Minor changes to the first Danish draft was made based on results from a cognitive pretest among six women with pelvic organ prolapse and five patients with knee injuries recruited from the outpatient clinics. The final Danish version was approved by the German author. Conclusion A Danish translated version of SDM-Q-9patient version, is now available and is currently undergoing psychometric testing for further validation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hulbæk, Mette","Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","Primdahl, Jette","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Birkelund, Regner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642639"],"event":{"end":"2017-07-05","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2017-07-02","title":"9th International Shared Decision Making Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Shared decision making"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish translation and cultural adaption of the 000000000009 item shared decision making questionnaire sdm q 000000000009 patient version","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-642639","ids":["sdu-f2793a59-0255-43d3-ab17-941e37852b0d"],"keyword":["Shared decision making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-13C49437E9F71F3EF29744D18C7F308B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Familiecentret","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"hulbækpau","last":"Hulbæk","locid":"140af55f-92a4-4fcd-be71-f7776e32e2d3","name":"Hulbæk, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8258-3398","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Johansson","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Marianne Johansson","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"primdahlpau","last":"Primdahl","locid":"e7f33410-2d7a-4869-b5e9-ed886ba48c94","name":"Primdahl, Jette","orcid":"0000-0002-1049-4150","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Regner","key":"birkelundpau","last":"Birkelund","locid":"dedbb04e-270c-4add-a26c-87277d6caf0f","name":"Birkelund, Regner","orcid":"0000-0002-5374-0630","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f2793a59-0255-43d3-ab17-941e37852b0d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Danish Translation and Cultural Adaption of the 9-Item Shared Decision Making Questionnaire (SDM-Q-9) patient version.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-642639","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"140Nd (t1/2 = 3.4 days), owing to its short-lived positron emitting daughter 140Pr (t1/2 = 3.4 min), has promise as an in vivo generator for positron emission tomography (PET). However, the electron capture decay of 140Nd is chemically disruptive to macrocycle-based radiolabeling, meaning that an in vivo redistribution of the daughter 140Pr is expected before positron emission. The purpose of this study was to determine how the delayed positron from the de-labeled 140Pr affects preclinical imaging with 140Nd. To explore the effect, 140Nd was produced at CERN-ISOLDE, reacted with the somatostatin analogue, DOTA-LM3 (1,4,7,10- tetraazacyclododecane, 1,4,7- tri acetic acid, 10- acetamide N - p-Cl-Phecyclo(D-Cys-Tyr-d-4-amino-Phe(carbamoyl)-Lys-Thr-Cys)D-Tyr-NH2) and injected into H727 xenograft bearing mice. Comparative pre- and post-mortem PET imaging at 16 h postinjection was used to quantify the in vivo redistribution of 140Pr following 140Nd decay. The somatostatin receptor-positive pancreas exhibited the highest tissue accumulation of 140Nd-DOTA-LM3 (13% ID/g at 16 h) coupled with the largest observed redistribution rate, where 56 ± 7% (n = 4, mean ± SD) of the in situ produced 140Pr washed out of the pancreas before decay. Contrastingly, the liver, spleen, and lungs acted as strong sink organs for free 140Pr3+. Based upon these results, we conclude that 140Nd imaging with a non-internalizing vector convolutes the biodistribution of the tracer with the accumulation pattern of free 140Pr. This redistribution phenomenon may show promise as a probe of the cellular interaction with the vector, such as in determining tissue dependent internalization behavior.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Severin, Gregory","Kristensen, Lotte K.","Nielsen, Carsten H.","Fonslet, Jesper","Jensen, Andreas Tue Ingemann","Frellsen, Anders Floor","Jensen, Mikael","Elema, Dennis Ringkjøbing","Maecke, Helmut","Kjær, Andreas","Johnston, Karl","Köster, Ulli"],"cuid":["S02-093.02-033640"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CERN","University Medical Center Freiburg"],"keyword":["DOTA LM3","Internalization","Positron Emission Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neodymium 000000000140 dota lm000000000003 evaluation of an i in vivo i generator for pet with a non internalizing vector","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2017.00098","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.02-033640","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5506079","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85062776091","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28748183","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-2f83b663-615b-484e-b375-6c16ccdf8786","ku-30e4920c-723a-4c41-8861-3dc43ae1556f"],"keyword":["140Nd","140Pr","DOTA-LM3","Internalization","Positron emission tomography","in vivo generator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A6B624F1B7F44BA8E6A511A7E396BB44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/195256345/fmed_04_00098.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134440158/fmed_04_00098.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2017.00098","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Center for Nuclear Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university medical center freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"cern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"CERN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory","key":"severingregorypau","last":"Severin","locid":"0e92340c-c204-4cd4-a297-06bb096315e3","name":"Severin, Gregory","orcid":"0000-0003-1189-7311","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lotte K","key":"kristensenlottekpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Lotte K","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten H","key":"nielsencarstenhaagenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aefb223a-8c5c-41c6-9e69-fade0a04bf90","name":"Ni