{"abstract":"A scenario based risk assessment method is used to evaluate how combined sewer overflow (CSO) affects a nearby bathing beach in Skanderborg, Denmark. The method combines an urban drainage model with a 3D CFD model to pre-simulate 60 different scenarios, used for assessing the risk of poor bathing water quality in a computational efficient way. The results are verified by experimental data.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Michael R.","Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Bastholm, S.","Starcke, S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088378"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-15","place":"Prag, cz","start":"2017-09-10","title":"14th International Conference on Urban Drainage","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bathing water","CFD","CSO","E coli","Scenario modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scenario based risk assessment of the dispersion of e coli from combined sewer overflow to a fresh water lake","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-088378","ids":["aau-83b618dd-67ab-400b-9fdb-32d5b0e559ef"],"keyword":["Bathing water","CFD","CSO","E-coli","Scenario modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-50BCF0B3B2C0EBCA20F8664C76BC0372"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Environment (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amphi-Bac ApS, Forskerparken NOVI, Aalborg Ø, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Robdrup","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","name_org":"Rasmussen, Michael Robdrup","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Liedtke","key":"thorndahlpau","last":"Thorndahl","locid":"5faa528b-e2f0-41fd-8128-9d76ed5993f0","name":"Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"bastholmpau","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"starckepau","last":"Starcke","name":"Starcke, S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"2366-2369","publisher":"IWA/IAHR International Conference on Urban Drainage","status":"p","subtitle":"14th IWA/IAHR International Conference on Urban Drainage","title":"Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","amphi-bac aps, forskerparken novi, aalborg ø, denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-83b618dd-67ab-400b-9fdb-32d5b0e559ef"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Scenario based risk assessment of the dispersion of E-coli from combined sewer overflow to a fresh-water lake","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088378","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Modelling signals as being periodic is common in many applications. Such periodic signals can be represented by a weighted sum of sinusoids with frequencies being an integer multiple of the fundamental frequency. Due to its widespread use, numerous methods have been proposed to estimate the fundamental frequency, and the maximum likelihood (ML) estimator is the most accurate estimator in statistical terms. When the noise is assumed to be white and Gaussian, the ML estimator is identical to the non-linear least squares (NLS) estimator. Despite being optimal in a statistical sense, the NLS estimator has a high computational complexity. In this paper, we propose an algorithm for lowering this complexity significantly by showing that the NLS estimator can be computed efficiently by solving two Toeplitz-plus-Hankel systems of equations and by exploiting the recursive-in-order matrix structures of these systems. Specifically, the proposed algorithm reduces the time complexity to the same order as that of the popular harmonic summation method which is an approximate NLS estimator. The performance of the proposed algorithm is assessed via Monte Carlo and timing studies. These show that the proposed algorithm speeds up the evaluation of the NLS estimator by a factor of 50–100 for typical scenarios.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Jensen, Søren Holdt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-108503"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-BOO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-BOO","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast fundamental frequency estimation making a statistically efficient estimator computationally efficient","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/249876060/master.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-108503","identifier":[{"id":"000395609800019","type":"wos"},{"id":"85009919903","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c9604a90-5140-40fa-b973-7feea1fa3ea7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1AEF3F7647C590DA0228DE354A384651"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/249876060/master.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320308077/ff0.zip","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"bang olufsen","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-BOO","l3nl":"Bang & Olufsen","l3nn":"Bang & Olufsen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bang & Olufsen","namevar":["Bang & Olufsen A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-BOO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenjesperkjærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Lindstrøm","key":"jensentobiaslindstrømpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a2e382fc-c4c6-4ff2-b7d2-8b012eb5160e","name":"Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","orcid":"0000-0003-4262-0577","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenjesperrindompau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenmadsgræsbøllpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Holdt","key":"jensensørenholdtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bfd2a53b-f2bd-4563-8968-9a911996215f","name":"Jensen, Søren Holdt","orcid":"0000-0002-1050-470X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.sigpro.2017.01.011","issn":["01651684","18727557"],"issn_org":["01651684"],"journal":"Signal Processing","pages":"188-197","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Signal Processing","volume":"135"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009919903"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Bang & Olufsen","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c9604a90-5140-40fa-b973-7feea1fa3ea7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Fast fundamental frequency estimation : Making a statistically efficient estimator computationally efficient","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-108503","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Fundamental frequency estimation is an important task in speech and audio analysis. Harmonic model-based methods typically have superior estimation accuracy. However, such methods usually as- sume that the fundamental frequency and amplitudes are station- ary over a short time frame. In this paper, we propose a Kalman filter-based fundamental frequency estimation algorithm using the harmonic model, where the fundamental frequency and amplitudes can be truly nonstationary by modeling their time variations as first- order Markov chains. The Kalman observation equation is derived from the harmonic model and formulated as a compact nonlinear matrix form, which is further used to derive an extended Kalman filter. Detailed and continuous fundamental frequency and ampli- tude estimates for speech, the sustained vowel /a/ and solo musical tones with vibrato are demonstrated.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shi, Liming","Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Little, Max A","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113735"],"event":{"acronym":"WASPAA","end":"2017-10-18","place":"New Paltz, us","start":"2017-10-15","title":"2017 IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aston University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a kalman based fundamental frequency estimation algorithm","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/318997509/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-113735","identifier":[{"id":"85042357059","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000426939000064","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-db174639-a732-4ddd-8c8e-decd3ced8f8d"],"keyword":["Fundamental frequency estimation, extended Kalman filter, harmonic model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BAA0892CE8EF0B19CFDC77E11204D5E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/318997509/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"aston university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Aston University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liming","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","locid":"e44b1378-1291-46be-b76a-fd0e196e2d46","name":"Shi, Liming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Max A","key":"littlepau","last":"Little","name":"Little, Max A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/waspaa.2017.8170046","eisbn":["9781538616321"],"isbn":["9781538616338"],"issn":["19471629"],"pages":"314-318","place":"New Paltz, NY, USA, USA","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics","status":"p","title":"2017 IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics (WASPAA 2017)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042357059"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-db174639-a732-4ddd-8c8e-decd3ced8f8d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Kalman-based Fundamental Frequency Estimation Algorithm","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113735","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The aim of this study was to compare the efficacy and safety of intracardiac echocardiography (ICE) from the left atrium (LA) with transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) for procedural guidance of transcatheter left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO). BACKGROUND: TEE with general anesthesia is the current gold standard to guide LAAO. By the use of ICE from the LA, LAAO can be performed in local anesthesia and may potentially have advantages over TEE. METHODS: A single-center, cohort study of patients undergoing LAAO with the Amplatzer Cardiac Plug or Amulet (St. Jude Medical, St. Paul, Minnesota). Procedures were guided by ICE from the LA with local anesthesia (n = 109) or TEE using general anesthesia (n = 107). All patients had pre-procedural cardiac computed tomography. Efficacy outcomes were technical success, procedural success, and peridevice leakage at TEE 8 weeks after LAAO. Safety outcome was a composite of periprocedural complications. RESULTS: Technical success was achieved in 99% of both the TEE and ICE group. Procedural success was similar between groups: 94.4% success rate in the TEE-guided group, and 94.5% in the ICE-guided group. Major periprocedural complications occurred in 4.7% of the TEE group and 1.8% of the ICE group. Rate and degree of peridevice leak did not differ between groups at follow-up. Turnover time in the catheter laboratory, and contrast use were reduced with ICE. CONCLUSIONS: LA ICE to guide LAAO as compared with TEE appears to be effective and safe, without increased procedure-related complications. The rate of peridevice leak is low and similar to TEE-guided procedures. Time spent in the catheterization room may decrease substantially.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Korsholm, Kasper","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-158415"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intracardiac echocardiography from the left atrium for procedural guidance of transcatheter left atrial appendage occlusion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85028614434","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-158415","identifier":[{"id":"85028614434","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28866042","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-32dd85ae-db7c-4884-8459-d0fc353318c0"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-051D465FAF008D69F22CBD84AE3DDA2F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28866042"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcin.2017.06.057","issn":["18767605","19368798"],"issn_org":["19368798"],"issue":"21","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","pages":"2198-2206","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","title_org":"JACC. Cardiovascular interventions","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028614434"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-32dd85ae-db7c-4884-8459-d0fc353318c0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Intracardiac Echocardiography From the Left Atrium for Procedural Guidance of Transcatheter Left Atrial Appendage Occlusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-158415","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Pericytes surround the endothelial cells of the microvasculature where they serve as active participants in crucial vascular functions such as angiogenesis, stability, and permeability. However, pericyte loss or dysfunction has been described in a number of pathologies. Targeting pericytes could therefore prove instrumental in the further development of vascular therapeutics. Methods: To target the pericyte, a proteomic-based approach using antibody phage display was conducted. We present a novel single-cell selection strategy, with a modified selection step to drive the selection of antibodies toward relevant pericyte epitopes. Results: Characterization of the selected antibodies revealed two antibodies with binding specificity for pericytes. The cognate antigen of one of the antibodies was identified as pericyte-expressed fibronectin. This antibody was shown to be a potent inhibitor of pericyte migration and to induce a pro-angiogenic response when included in a pericyte-endothelial cell co-culture angiogenesis assay. Conclusions: The selection method provides an efficient platform for the selection of functional antibodies which target pericytes. We obtain an antibody that interacts with a fibronectin epitope important for pericyte mobility and functionality. Targeting of this epitope in pathologies where pericytes are implicated could potentially be of therapeutic benefit.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Just, Jesper","Lykkemark, Simon","Nielsen, Charlotte Høgsbjerg","Roshenas, Ali Reza","Drasbek, Kim Ryun","Petersen, Steen Vang","Bek, Toke","Kristensen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-168450"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pericyte modulation by a functional antibody obtained by a novel single cell selection strategy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85026762639","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-168450","identifier":[{"id":"28236639","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85026762639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-44a52ce6-cf30-41c7-ae7b-f3070d781017"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1E7484528EA6770EDA714221C36A3E92"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Protein science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sino danish centre for education and research","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"justpau","last":"Just","locid":"f4ba15f6-630e-4c10-b970-c7aa51bb7ee5","name":"Just, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"lykkemarkpau","last":"Lykkemark","locid":"da548181-69fe-4ac0-af61-d60242a82f9d","name":"Lykkemark, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Høgsbjerg","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dac052bc-2d74-4ed5-9d65-82bc4724da41","name":"Nielsen, Charlotte Høgsbjerg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ali Reza","key":"roshenaspau","last":"Roshenas","name":"Roshenas, Ali Reza","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Ryun","key":"drasbekpau","last":"Drasbek","locid":"de170443-bbbb-46ff-ad6c-077e42b64468","name":"Drasbek, Kim Ryun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen Vang","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"e3b8741c-82e6-46e8-a2fe-38b29762b334","name":"Petersen, Steen Vang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"b504c3ab-64aa-4aa9-86b3-21d898c2c548","name":"Kristensen, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28236639"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/micc.12365","issn":["10739688","15498719"],"issn_org":["10739688"],"issue":"6","journal":"Microcirculation","paperid":"e12365","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Microcirculation","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026762639"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-44a52ce6-cf30-41c7-ae7b-f3070d781017"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pericyte modulation by a functional antibody obtained by a novel single cell selection strategy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-168450","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
