{"abstract":"Several lines of evidence indicate that the most primitive staphylococcal species, those of the Staphylococcus sciuri group, were involved in the first stages of evolution of the staphylococcal cassette chromosome mec (SCCmec), the genetic element carrying the β-lactam resistance gene mecA. However, many steps are still missing from this evolutionary history. In particular, it is not known how mecA was incorporated into the mobile element SCC prior to dissemination among Staphylococcus aureus and other pathogenic staphylococcal species. To gain insights into the possible contribution of several species of the Staphylococcus sciuri group to the assembly of SCCmec, we sequenced the genomes of 106 isolates, comprising S. sciuri (n = 76), Staphylococcus vitulinus (n = 18), and Staphylococcus fleurettii (n = 12) from animal and human sources, and characterized the native location of mecA and the SCC insertion site by using a variety of comparative genomic approaches. Moreover, we performed a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) analysis of the genomes in order to understand SCCmec evolution in relation to phylogeny. We found that each of three species of the S. sciuri group contributed to the evolution of SCCmec: S. vitulinus and S. fleurettii contributed to the assembly of the mec complex, and S. sciuri most likely provided the mobile element in which mecA was later incorporated. We hypothesize that an ancestral SCCmec III cassette (an element carried by one of the most epidemic methicillin-resistant S. aureus clones) originated in S. sciuri possibly by a recombination event in a human host or a human-created environment and later was transferred to S. aureus.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rolo, Joana","Worning, Peder","Nielsen, Jesper Boye","Bowden, Rory","Bouchami, Ons","Damborg, Peter Panduro","Guardabassi, Luca","Perreten, Vincent","Tomasz, Alexander","Westh, Henrik","de Lencastre, Hermínia","Miragaia, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524696"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NOVA University Lisbon","Rockefeller University","University of Bern","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Evolution","SCCmec","Staphylococci","beta Lactam Resistance","mecA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolutionary origin of the staphylococcal cassette chromosome mec sccmec","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5444190?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524696","identifier":[{"id":"85019736140","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28373201","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5444190","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000403783400055","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-dbc683d6-7886-4e9e-96f2-812b33a3bd9d"],"keyword":["SCCmec","beta-lactam resistance","evolution","mecA","staphylococci"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E4EC6F5558F0DF60EB773A4F33D04FFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5444190?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"nova university lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"NOVA University Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"rockefeller university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rockefeller University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joana","key":"rolopau","last":"Rolo","name":"Rolo, Joana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peder","key":"worningpau","last":"Worning","name":"Worning, Peder","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Boye","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Boye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rory","key":"bowdenpau","last":"Bowden","name":"Bowden, Rory","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ons","key":"bouchamipau","last":"Bouchami","name":"Bouchami, Ons","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Peter","key":"damborgpau","last":"Damborg","locid":"a8f66d07-58a8-4f3b-bbc1-869f827e08d2","name":"Damborg, Peter Panduro","name_org":"Damborg, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9932-5996","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Luca","key":"guardabassipau","last":"Guardabassi","locid":"a5c1a52b-b35b-4d24-864d-c513c79a1dd0","name":"Guardabassi, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Vincent","key":"perretenpau","last":"Perreten","name":"Perreten, Vincent","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Alexander","key":"tomaszpau","last":"Tomasz","name":"Tomasz, Alexander","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Henrik","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hermínia","key":"delencastrepau","last":"de Lencastre","name":"de Lencastre, Hermínia","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"miragaiapau","last":"Miragaia","name":"Miragaia, Maria","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28373201"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/aac.02302-16","issn":["00664804","10706283"],"issn_org":["00664804"],"issue":"6","journal":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","paperid":"e02302-16","status":"p","title":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019736140"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dbc683d6-7886-4e9e-96f2-812b33a3bd9d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolutionary Origin of the Staphylococcal Cassette Chromosome mec (SCCmec)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524696","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535509"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vanddåb og åndsdåb i markusevangeliet","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-535509","ids":["ku-ee0dc19c-3c30-4ee4-9e83-a62b39a11b1d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-23A60FA123F9A208585CB6F05511164F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13991361"],"journal":"Bibliana","pages":"28-31","status":"p","title":"Bibliana","volume":"18"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee0dc19c-3c30-4ee4-9e83-a62b39a11b1d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Vanddåb og åndsdåb i Markusevangeliet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535509","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Since the 1960s, silicone implants have been used for breast augmentations, both cosmetically and in reconstructive surgery. Tissue exposed to silicone can react with multiple adverse advents. Autoimmune/inflammatory syndrome induced by adjuvants due to silicone exposure from ruptured silicone implants can lead to different interstitial lung manifestations predominantly with granuloma evolvement, leading to the so-called silicone implant incompatibility syndrome (SIIS). This case describes a 57-year-old woman with multiple lung infiltrations and a left-sided breast implant. The implant had been replaced twice, once due to implant rupture 36 years ago. The nodular infiltrates could not be related to infection, malignancy, interstitial lung disease, vasculitis or connective tissue disorder, and it was concluded that the nodular infiltrations were of inflammatory origin due to an autoimmune response secondary to the silicone implants (SIIS). After explantation, the patient's symptoms subsided and her physical condition has remarkably improved.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schierbeck, Juliane","Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","Grindsted Nielsen, Sanne","Bille, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-597529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"silicone implant incompatibility syndrome siis in a 000000000057 year old woman with unilateral silicone breast implant","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045571363","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-597529","identifier":[{"id":"28739610","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85045571363","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-54e01617-ad70-40c8-9ffe-c3cd618c8c35"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B557D2B440C017A3D7C314AD18F90C6B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juliane","key":"schierbeckpau","last":"Schierbeck","locid":"1486a380-ef06-492f-9010-d1b3c1c43cf2","name":"Schierbeck, Juliane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rømhild","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"bfd91489-501f-49d3-aa3b-d9e8ea9a77f0","name":"Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-4014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne","key":"grindstednielsenpau","last":"Grindsted Nielsen","locid":"32082713-9c1f-40a3-ad15-3890bc8ecd7b","name":"Grindsted Nielsen, Sanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"billepau","last":"Bille","locid":"935adbe7-0d57-4668-a1ef-4d6e0b1133d7","name":"Bille, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0002-7727-462X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28739610"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bcr-2016-218709","issn":["1757790X"],"journal":"BMJ Case Reports","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Case Reports","volume":"2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045571363"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-54e01617-ad70-40c8-9ffe-c3cd618c8c35"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Silicone implant incompatibility syndrome (SIIS) in a 57-year-old woman with unilateral silicone breast implant","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-597529","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Interactions between transcriptional promoters and their distal regulatory elements play an important role in transcriptional regulation; however, the extent to which these interactions are subject to rapid modulations in response to signals is unknown. Here, we use promoter capture Hi-C to demonstrate a rapid reorganization of promoter-anchored chromatin loops within 4 hr after inducing differentiation of 3T3-L1 preadipocytes. The establishment of new promoter-enhancer loops is tightly coupled to activation of poised (histone H3 lysine 4 mono- and dimethylated) enhancers, as evidenced by the acquisition of histone H3 lysine 27 acetylation and the binding of MED1, SMC1, and P300 proteins to these regions, as well as to activation of target genes. Intriguingly, formation of loops connecting activated enhancers and promoters is also associated with extensive recruitment of corepressors such as NCoR and HDACs, indicating that this class of coregulators may play a previously unrecognized role during enhancer activation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Siersbæk, Rasmus","Madsen, Jesper Grud Skat","Javierre, Biola Maria","Nielsen, Ronni","Bagge, Emilie Kristine","Cairns, Jonathan","Wingett, Steven William","Traynor, Sofie","Spivakov, Mikhail","Fraser, Peter","Mandrup, Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603785"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Babraham Institute","Florida State University"],"keyword":["3T3 L1 Cells","Adipocytes","Adipogenesis","Animals","Cell Cycle Proteins","Chromatin","Chromatin Assembly and Disassembly","Chromatin Immunoprecipitation","Chromosomal Proteins Non Histone","E1A Associated p300 Protein","Enhancer Elements Genetic","Journal Article","Mediator Complex Subunit 1","Mice","Nucleic Acid Conformation","Promoter Regions Genetic","RNA Messenger","Sequence Analysis RNA","Time Factors","Transcription Genetic","Transcriptional Activation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic rewiring of promoter anchored chromatin loops during adipocyte differentiation","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85018727024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-603785","identifier":[{"id":"28475875","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85018727024","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6b04abea-799a-4df5-9c31-85f84390e71f"],"keyword":["3T3-L1 Cells","Adipocytes","Adipogenesis","Animals","Cell Cycle Proteins","Chromatin","Chromatin Assembly and Disassembly","Chromatin Immunoprecipitation","Chromosomal Proteins, Non-Histone","E1A-Associated p300 Protein","Enhancer Elements, Genetic","Journal Article","Mediator Complex Subunit 1","Mice","Nucleic Acid Conformation","Promoter Regions, Genetic","RNA, Messenger","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Time Factors","Transcription, Genetic","Transcriptional Activation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5EE9C236ECAA8DC608BB5FA52A28951F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"babraham institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":