{"abstract":"Macrophage migration inhibitory factor (MIF), a small conserved protein, is abundant in the immune- and central nervous system (CNS). MIF has several receptors and binding partners that can modulate its action on a cellular level. It is upregulated in neurodegenerative diseases and cancer although its function is far from clear. Here, we report the finding of a new binding partner to MIF, the serine protease HTRA1. This enzyme cleaves several growth factors, extracellular matrix molecules and is implicated in some of the same diseases as MIF. We show that the function of the binding between MIF and HTRA1 is to inhibit the proteolytic activity of HTRA1, modulating the availability of molecules that can change cell growth and differentiation. MIF is therefore the first endogenous inhibitor ever found for HTRA1. It was found that both molecules were present in astrocytes and that the functional binding has the ability to modulate astrocytic activities important in development and disease of the CNS.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Fex Svenningsen, Åsa","Loering, Svenja","Sørensen, Anna Lahn","Uyen Buu Huynh, Ha","Hjæresen, Simone","Martin, Nellie Anne","Møller, Jesper Bonnet","Elkjaer, Maria L.","Holmskov, Uffe","Illes, Zsolt","Andersson, Malin","Nielsen, Solveig Beck","Benedikz, Eirikur"],"cuid":["S02-091.61-047856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fex Svenningsen, Åsa"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["Academic Medical Center","Academic Medical Center, Tytgat Institute for Liver and Intestinal Research,, Amsterdam, The Netherland","All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Uppsala University","Weill Cornell Medicine, Cornell University, USA"],"keyword":["HTRA1","MIF","Protein interaction","Yeast 2 hybrid","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"macrophage migration inhibitory factor mif modulates trophic signaling through interaction with serine protease htra000000000001","src":["pha","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00018-017-2592-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.61-047856","identifier":[{"id":"28726057","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5663815","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85025106716","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["pha-040c4db0-28e6-4995-9dfe-3247006c5ac9","sdu-a5107b35-5b2f-4b79-a269-04345cc53d78"],"keyword":["HTRA1","MIF","Protein Interaction","Yeast-2-Hybrid","disease, health science and nursing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5A68D6A431FD9F9C72589A55F37880A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00018-017-2592-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129128554/Macrophage_migration_inhibitory_factor_MIF_modulates_trophic_signaling_through_interaction_with_serine_protease_HTRA1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"a