, H.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"sanchezpau","last":"Sanchez","name":"Sanchez, P.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Stejner","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Pedersen, Morten Stejner","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arianna","key":"taorminapau","last":"Taormina","locid":"3f2308da-3403-41e7-8210-d40228218861","name":"Taormina, Arianna","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/irmmw-thz.2016.7758537","eisbn":["9781467384858"],"isbn":["9781467384865"],"issn":["21622027"],"publisher":"IEEE","series":"International Conference on Infrared, Millimeter and Terahertz Waves","status":"p","title":"2016 41st International Conference on Infrared, Millimeter, and Terahertz waves (IRMMW-THz)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006147279"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-59c1f7e0-55d7-446c-872c-474ca3561252"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"High power microwave diagnostic for the fusion energy experiment ITER","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-331258","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"To analyze the heating and cooling phase of an induction heated injection molding tool accurately, the temperature dependent magnetic properties, namely the non-linear B-H curves, need to be accounted for in an induction heating simulation. Hence, a finite element model has been developed, including the non-linear temperature dependent magnetic data described by a three-parameter modified Frohlich equation fitted to the magnetic saturation curve, and solved with an iterative procedure. The numerical calculations are compared with experiments conducted with two types of induction coils, built in to the injection molding tool. The model shows very good agreement with the experimental temperature measurements. It is also shown that the non-linearity can be used without the temperature dependency in some cases, and a proposed method is presented of how to estimate an effective linear permeability to use with simulation codes not able to utilize a non-linear solver. (C) 2015 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Guerrier, Patrick","Nielsen, Kaspar Kirstein","Menotti, Stefano","Hattel, Jesper Henri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352081"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Axisymmetric","Induction heating","Injection molding","Non linear finite element"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an axisymmetrical non linear finite element model for induction heating in injection molding tools","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84948746492","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352081","identifier":[{"id":"84948746492","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9f403141-a114-4237-9456-fd5ee9d28f21"],"keyword":["Axisymmetric","Induction heating","Injection molding","Non-linear finite element","Temperature dependent magnetic properties"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ED9F968B0D23F3AD98B937291F9EAF76"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"guerrierpau","last":"Guerrier","locid":"269ab07e-04d3-4aa7-8a5d-f84a54653073","name":"Guerrier, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaspar Kirstein","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"82e21ae8-a61e-40c9-867b-de0b8f7c7c01","name":"Nielsen, Kaspar Kirstein","orcid":"0000-0001-7938-4577","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefano","key":"menottipau","last":"Menotti","locid":"d0f0c355-a4e1-485f-bb93-871c70fd117a","name":"Menotti, Stefano","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.finel.2015.11.001","issn":["0168874X","18726925"],"issn_org":["0168874X"],"journal":"Finite Elements in Analysis and Design","pages":"1-10","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Finite Elements in Analysis and Design","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84948746492"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9f403141-a114-4237-9456-fd5ee9d28f21"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"An axisymmetrical non-linear finite element model for induction heating in injection molding tools","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352081","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Sawtooth instabilities can modify heating and current-drive profiles and potentially increase fast-ion losses. Understanding how sawteeth redistribute fast ions as a function of sawtooth parameters and of fast-ion energy and pitch is hence a subject of particular interest for future fusion devices. Here we present the first collective Thomson scattering (CTS) measurements of sawtooth-induced redistribution of fast ions at ASDEX Upgrade. These also represent the first localized fast-ion measurements on the high-field side of this device. The results indicate fast-ion losses in the phase-space measurement volume of about 50% across sawtooth crashes, in good agreement with values predicted with the Kadomtsev sawtooth model implemented in TRANSP and with the sawtooth model in the EBdyna_go code. In contrast to the case of sawteeth, we observe no fast-ion redistribution in the presence of fishbone modes. We highlight how CTS measurements can discriminate between different sawtooth models, in particular when aided by multi-diagnostic velocity-space tomography, and briefly discuss our results in light of existing measurements from other fast-ion diagnostics.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Galdon-Quiroga, J.","Garcia-Munoz, M.","Geiger, B.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Jaulmes, F.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Lazanyi, N.","Leipold, Frank","Ryter, F.","Salewski, Mirko","Schubert, M.","Stober, J.","Wagner, D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353136"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Hungary","Netherlands","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Budapest University of Technology and Economics","Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","University of Seville"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","Fast ion velocity distribution function","Fast ions in tokamaks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collective thomson scattering measurements of fast ion transport due to sawtooth crashes in asdex upgrade","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126152750/WPMST1PR1614817.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353136","identifier":[{"id":"84993950035","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a2bc537f-e74d-4893-9eaf-6217d2136dcf"],"keyword":["Collective Thomson scattering","Fast ions in tokamaks","Fast-ion velocity distribution function","Sawtooth instabilities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F36320145C6516B98A98809E5406D880"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126152750/WPMST1PR1614817.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"dutch institute for fundamental energy research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"hu","key":"budapest university of technology and economics","loc":["Hungary","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Budapest University of Technology and Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefan Kragh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Stejner","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Pedersen, Morten Stejner","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"galdonquirogapau","last":"Galdon-Quiroga","name":"Galdon-Quiroga, J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"garciamunozpau","last":"Garcia-Munoz","name":"Garcia-Munoz, M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"geigerpau","last":"Geiger","name":"Geiger, B.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"jaulmespau","last":"Jaulmes","name":"Jaulmes, F.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","f