.0-84955188275"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","private practice - denmark (medical)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bff0470e-cbcf-413f-a3b3-47f8dade71c2","ku-647bf9b3-a229-436a-82e8-8eb05c1418d5","sdu-0ce1780f-bc10-4f13-a8d4-70c6d41d53aa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Treatment of adult patients with schizophrenia and complex mental health needs - A national clinical guideline","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-089.10-026609","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cardiac rehabilitation can reduce mortality of patients with cardiovascular disease, but a frequently low participation rate in rehabilitation programs has been found globally. The objective of the Teledialog study was to assess the cost-utility (CU) of a cardiac telerehabilitation (CTR) program. The aim of the intervention was to increase the patients' participation in the CTR program. At discharge, an individualized 3-month rehabilitation plan was formulated for each patient. At home, the patients measured their own blood pressure, pulse, weight, and steps taken for 3 months. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The analysis was carried out together with a randomized controlled trial with 151 patients during 2012-2014. Costs of the intervention were estimated with a health sector perspective following international guidelines for CU. Quality of life was assessed using the 36-Item Short Form Health Survey. RESULTS: The rehabilitation activities were approximately the same in the two groups, but the number of contacts with the physiotherapist was higher among the intervention group. The mean total cost per patient was €1,700 higher in the intervention group. The quality-adjusted life-years (QALYs) gain was higher in the intervention group, but the difference was not statistically significant. The incremental CU ratio was more than €400,000 per QALY gained. CONCLUSIONS: Even though the rehabilitation activities increased, the program does not appear to be cost-effective. The intervention itself was not costly (less than €500), and increasing the number of patients may show reduced costs of the devices and make the CTR more cost-effective. Telerehabilitation can increase participation, but the intervention, in its current form, does not appear to be cost-effective.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kidholm, Kristian","Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Hansen, John","Nielsen, Gitte","Spindler, Helle","Dinesen, Birthe"],"cuid":["S03-099.50-011980"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Blood Pressure","Body Weight","Cost Benefit Analysis","Cost utility","Economic evaluation","Female","Heart Patients","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Pulse","Quality Adjusted Life Years","Quality of Life","Randomized study","Remote sensing technology","Telerehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cost utility analysis of a cardiac telerehabilitation program the teledialog project","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4939376/pdf/tmj.2015.0194.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.50-011980","identifier":[{"id":"84978173073","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26713491","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000379447900003","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC4939376","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-fb78e3f5-ba12-4631-9d37-23dbc4668aa2","au-cba04949-87a7-4f9a-b717-e429a78e4c3f","sdu-e5cd70cf-383c-4ca0-80b3-e634287c5e5a"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Blood Pressure","Body Weight","Cardiac Rehabilitation/economics","Cost-Benefit Analysis","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Pulse","Quality of Life","Quality-Adjusted Life Years","Remote Sensing Technology","Telerehabilitation/economics","cost-utility","cost-utility heart patients telerehabilitation randomized study economic evaluation health rehabilitation Health Care Sciences & Services","economic evaluation","heart patients","randomized study","telerehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-87856E3F6AFD18A8767A7533CB61598B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4939376/pdf/tmj.2015.0194.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjerte-Lungekirurgi (Thoraxkirurgi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-N