{"abstract":"Colorectal cancers (CRC) often show activating mutations of the KRAS or BRAF genes, which stimulate the extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK) pathway, thus increasing cell proliferation and inhibiting apoptosis. However, immunohistochemical results on ERK activation in such tumors differ greatly. Recently, using a highly optimized immunohistochemical method, we obtained evidence that high levels of ERK activation in rectal adenocarcinomas were associated with resistance to radiochemotherapy. In order to determine whether KRAS and/or BRAF mutations correlate to immunohistochemically detectable increases in phosphorylation of ERK (pERK), we stained biopsies from 36 CRC patients with activating mutations in the BRAF gene (BRAFV600E: BRAF(m)), the KRAS gene (KRAS(m)) or in neither (BRAF/KRAS(n)) with this optimized method. Staining was scored in blind-coded specimens by two observers. Staining of stromal cells was used as a positive control. BRAF(m) or KRAS(m) tumors did not show higher staining scores than BRAF/KRAS(n) tumors. Although BRAFV600E staining occurred in over 90% of cancer cells in all 9 BRAF(m) tumors, 3 only showed staining for pERK in less than 10% of cancer cell nuclei. The same applied to 4 of the 14 KRAS(m) tumors. A phophorylation-insensitive antibody demonstrated that lack of pERK staining did not reflect defect expression of ERK1/2 protein. Thus, increased staining for pERK does not correlate to BRAF or KRAS mutations even with a highly optimized procedure. Further studies are required to determine whether this reflects differences in expression of counterregulatory molecules, including ERK phosphatases.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holck, Susanne","Bonde, Jesper","Pedersen, Helle","Petersen, Anja Alex","Chaube, Amita","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Larsson, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413389"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"localization of active dually phosphorylated extracellular signal regulated kinase 000000000001 and 000000000002 in colorectal cancer with or without activating i braf i and i kras i mutations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.humpath.2016.03.001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-413389","identifier":[{"id":"27036313","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84969174566","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2165493b-7aef-421d-9585-70b150ec4813"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4876822B2A4A038D5B23CE8797754B99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.humpath.2016.03.001","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","locid":"bd4aad62-7596-4684-8c7e-55dcc62b59a1","name":"Holck, Susanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Helle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anja Alex","key":"pete