nding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffclauspau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22489/cinc.2016.061-436","eisbn":["9781509008964"],"issn":["02766574"],"journal":"Computing in Cardiology","pages":"201-204","paperid":"61-436","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Computing in Cardiology","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016119562"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ad16aeee-7fcf-4405-a7b8-904aa9b6015b","ku-8205619d-3426-4b66-a766-6f07942bbd0d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A vectorcardiographic evaluation of the consensus criteria for early repolarization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.59-008333","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"CMY-2 is the most common plasmid-mediated AmpC beta-lactamase in Escherichia coli isolates of human and animal origin. The aim of this study was to elucidate the epidemiology of CMY-2-producing E. coli in Denmark. Strain and plasmid relatedness was studied in 93 CMY-2-producing clinical and commensal E. coli isolates collected from 2006 to 2012 from humans, retail poultry meat, broilers, and dogs. Multilocus sequence typing (MLST), antimicrobial susceptibility testing, and conjugation were performed in conjunction with plasmid replicon typing, plasmid multilocus sequence typing (pMLST), restriction fragment length polymorphism (RFLP), and sequencing of selected bla(CMY-2)-harboring plasmids. MLST revealed high strain diversity, with few E. coli lineages occurring in multiple host species and sample types. bla(CMY-2) was detected on plasmids in 83 (89%) isolates. Most (75%) of the plasmids were conjugative and did not (96%) cotransfer resistance to antimicrobials other than cephalosporins. The main replicon types identified were IncI1-I gamma (55%) and IncK (39%). Isolates from different host species mainly carried distinct plasmid subtypes. Seven of the 18 human isolates harbored IncI1-I gamma/sequence type 2 (ST2), IncI1-I gamma/ST12, or IncK plasmids highly similar to those found among animal isolates, even though highly related human and animal plasmids differed by nonsynonymous single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) or insertion sequence elements. This study clearly demonstrates that the epidemiology of CMY-2 can be understood only by thorough plasmid characterization. To date, the spread of this beta-lactam resistance determinant in Denmark is mainly associated with IncK and IncI1-I gamma plasmids that are generally distributed according to host-specific patterns. These baseline data will be useful to assess the consequences of the increasing human exposure to CMY-2-producing E. coli via animal sources.IMPORTANCECMY-2 is the most common plasmid-mediated AmpC beta-lactamase in Escherichia coli. This beta-lactamase is poorly inhibited by clavulanic acid and confers resistance to cephamycins, third-generation cephalosporins, and aztreonam. Furthermore, resistance to carbapenems has been reported in E. coli as a result of production of plasmid-encoded CMY-2 beta-lactamase in combination with decreased outer membrane permeability. The gene encoding CMY-2 generally resides on transferable plasmids belonging to different incompatibility groups. The prevalence of CMY-2-mediated cephalosporin resistance in E. coli varies significantly depending on the geographical region and host. This study demonstrates that the epidemiology of CMY-2 can be understood only by thorough plasmid characterization. To date, the spread of this beta-lactam resistance determinant in Denmark is mainly associated with IncK and IncI1-I gamma plasmids, which are generally distributed according to host-specific patterns. These data will be useful to assess the consequences of the increasing human exposure to CMY-2-producing E. coli via animal sources.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Katrine Hartung","Bortolaia, Valeria","Nielsen, Christine Ahl","Nielsen, Jesper Boye","Schonning, Kristian","Agersø, Yvonne","Guardabassi, Luca","Besser, T. E."],"cuid":["S02-089.97-036132"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animalia","Animals","Antimicrobial susceptibility testing","Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology","Baseline data","Biotechnology","Canis familiaris","DNA","Ecology","Escherichia coli","Food Science","Genetic diversity","Insertion sequences","Multilocus Sequence Typing","Single nucleotide polymorphisms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"host specific patterns of genetic diversity among inci000000000001 i gamma and inck plasmids encoding cmy 000000000002 beta lactamase in escherichia coli isolates from humans poultry meat poultry and dogs in denmark","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/125634764/Appl._Environ._Microbiol._2016_Hansen_4705_14.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.97-036132","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4984282","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000379772200023","type":"wos"},{"id":"27235431","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84979891759","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9b9a3e95-35bb-4227-968f-8e2fa93be605","ku-1880c425-6a0f-44c3-8774-bd0b2f28670f"],"keyword":["Animalia","Animals","Antimicrobial susceptibility testing","Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology","Baseline data","Biotechnology","Canis familiaris","DNA","Ecology","Escherichia coli","Food Science","Genetic diversity","Human exposures","Insertion sequences","Multilocus sequence typing","Restriction fragment length polymorphisms","Single nucleotide polymorphisms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-814DB115DA964DCB8D7D175DC5349E51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/125634764/Appl._Environ._Microbiol._2016_Hansen_4705_14.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine Hartung","key":"hansenkatrinehartungpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"da30d481-d3e5-4bca-b321-807db3b1651f","name":"Hansen, Katrine Hartung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Valeria","key":"bortolaiavaleriapau","last":"Bortolaia","locid":"204ced4c-fd1a-43eb-abde-7beb937d1cdf","name":"Bortolaia, Valeria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christine Karin Ahl","key":"nielsenchristinekarinahlpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ddd6aa03-8acd-4d5f-a8ac-07c924761320","name":"Nielsen, Christine Karin Ahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Boye","key":"nielsenjesperboyepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Boye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"schønningkristianpau","last":"Schønning","locid":"17301a86-39e7-44c0-bdf3-12e0c55b9b18","name":"Schønning, Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"schonningkristianpau","last":"Schonning","name":"Schonning, Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yvonne","key":"agersøyvonnepau","last":"Agersø","locid":"727ec55d-b40c-4ff2-b27e-cc347dbeb7ed","name":"Agersø, Yvonne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luca","key":"guardabassilucapau","last":"Guardabassi","locid":"a5c1a52b-b35b-4d24-864d-c513c79a1dd0","name":"Guardabassi, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27235431"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/aem.00495-16","issn":["00992240","10985336"],"issn_org":["00992240"],"issue":"15","journal":"Applied and Environmental Microbiology","pages":"4705-4714","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Applied and Environmental Microbiology","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979891759"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9b9a3e95-35bb-4227-968f-8e2fa93be605","ku-1880c425-6a0f-44c3-8774-bd0b2f28670f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Host-Specific Patterns of Genetic Diversity among IncI1-I gamma and IncK Plasmids Encoding CMY-2 beta-Lactamase in Escherichia coli Isolates from Humans, Poultry Meat, Poultry, and Dogs in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.97-036132","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Detection of immune responses is important in the diagnosis of many diseases. For example, the detection of circulating autoantibodies against double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) is used in the diagnosis of Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE). It is, however, difficult to reach satisfactory sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy with established assays. Also, existing methodologies for quantification of autoantibodies are challenging to transfer to a point-of-care setting. Here we present the use of flow-induced dispersion analysis (FIDA) for rapid (minutes) measurement of autoantibodies against dsDNA. The assay is based on Taylor dispersion analysis (TDA) and is fully automated with the use of standard capillary electrophoresis (CE) based equipment employing fluorescence detection. It is robust toward matrix effects as demonstrated by the direct analysis of samples composed of up to 85% plasma derived from human blood samples, and it allows for flexible exchange of the DNA sequences used to probe for the autoantibodies. Plasma samples from SLE positive patients were analyzed using the new FIDA methodology as well as by standard indirect immunofluorescence and solid-phase immunoassays. Interestingly, the patient antibodies bound DNA sequences with different affinities, suggesting pronounced heterogeneity among autoantibodies produced in SLE. The FIDA based methodology is a new approach for autoantibody detection and holds promise for being used for patient stratification and monitoring of disease activity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Poulsen, Nicklas N","Pedersen, Morten E.","Østergaard, Jesper","Petersen, Nickolaj J.","Nielsen, Christoffer T","Heegaard, Niels H H","Jensen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.04-041767"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flow induced dispersion analysis for probing anti dsdna antibody binding heterogeneity in systemic lupus erythematosus patients toward a new approach for diagnosis and patient stratification","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84988556807","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.04-041767","identifier":[{"id":"27571264","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84988556807","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3f27bd98-d763-47a6-b7f5-9569395c109a","sdu-8a271d8d-a132-4226-a38e-073f1491ed42"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0201242B23E7E27622A5B811F017581C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicklas N","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"53c801f6-9395-4d1f-b184-4e1c33f776fb","name":"Poulsen, Nicklas N","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten E","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f0db357e-f5c3-4919-a7d6-8b473c185b10","name":"Pedersen, Morten E.","name_org":"Pedersen, Morten E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Nickolaj J","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1327012e-b05a-43ca-8332-4001e6730d79","name":"Petersen, Nickolaj J.","name_org":"Petersen, Nickolaj J","orcid":"0000-0001-5101-3571","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer Tandrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Christoffer Tandrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels H H","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"c63c237a-51cc-4a7c-89ad-04eefa031abb","name":"Heegaard, Niels H H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"88cd8faf-69c6-46de-a355-03f93d52eeb1","name":"Jensen, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27571264"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.6b01741","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"18","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"9056-9061","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"88"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988556807"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3f27bd98-d763-47a6-b7f5-9569395c109a","sdu-8a271d8d-a132-4226-a38e-073f1491ed42"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Flow-Induced Dispersion Analysis for Probing Anti-dsDNA Antibody Binding Heterogeneity in Systemic Lupus Erythematosus Patients : Toward a New Approach for Diagnosis and Patient Stratification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.04-041767","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Exercise-based cardiac rehabilitation reduces morbidity and mortality. Walking is a convenient activity suitable for people with cardiac disease. Pedometers count steps, measure walking activity and motivate people to increase physical activity. In this study, patients participating in cardiac telerehabilitation were provided with a pedometer to support motivation for physical activity with the purpose of exploring pedometer use and self-determined motivation for walking experienced by patients and health professionals during a cardiac telerehabilitation program. Methods: A qualitative research design consisting of observations, individual interviews and patient documents made the basis for a content analysis. Data was analysed deductively using Self Determination Theory as a frame for analysis and discussion, focusing on the psychological needs of autonomy, competence and relatedness. Twelve cardiac patients, 11 health professionals, 6 physiotherapists and 5 registered nurses were included. Results: The pedometer offered independence from standardised rehabilitation since the pedometer supported tailoring, individualised walking activity based on the patient's choice. This led to an increased autonomy. The patients felt consciously aware of health benefits of walking, and the pedometer provided feedback on walking activity leading to an increased competence to achieve goals for steps. Finally, the pedometer supported relatedness with others. The health professionals' surveillance of patients' steps, made the patients feel observed, yet supported, furthermore, their next of kin appeared to be supportive as walking partners. Conclusion: Cardiac patients' motivation for walking was evident due to pedometer use. Even though not all aspects of motivation were autonomous and self determined, the patients felt motivated for walking. The visible steps and continuous monitoring of own walking activity made it possible for each individual patient to choose their desired kind of activity and perform ongoing adjustments of walking activity. The immediate feedback on step activity and the expectations of health benefits resulted in motivation for walking. Finally, pedometer supported walking made surveillance possible, giving the patients a feeling of being looked after and supported.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thorup, Charlotte Brun","Grønkjær, Mette","Spindler, Helle","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Hansen, John","Dinesen, Birthe","Nielsen, Gitte","Sørensen, Erik Elgaard"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002358"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cardiac telerehabilitation","Journal Article","Pedometer","Physical activity","Telemedicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pedometer use and self determined motivation for walking in a cardiac telerehabilitation program a qualitative study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13102-016-0048-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research were funded by: Eir Research and Business park, The European Regional Development Fund, UNIK partnership, Danish Council of Research and Innovation, Departments of Cardiothoracic Surgery and Clinical Nursing Research Unit, Aalborg University Hospital, Aalborg University and the Lundbeck foundation (FP25/2013). The Teledi@log project was approved by the Danish Ethical Committee (N-20120051) and The Danish Data Protection Agency, and the study conformed to the Helsinki declaration. The study’ Clinical Trials Registration Number is NCT01752192. All participants signed informed consent after accepting participation in this sub-study."],"id":"S02-100.00-002358","identifier":[{"id":"85026811490","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4991060","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000386705500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"27547404","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2f0ea7ff-3a94-407b-8a2e-1d8cbf622c8f","au-7cdbcb47-3fe2-41f4-bf3e-b00611d6824a"],"keyword":["Cardiac telerehabilitation","Journal Article","Pedometer","Physical activity","Telemedicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E0F1B6656D9FED1B93E32761CDAB886E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4991060/pdf/13102_2016_Article_48.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13102-016-0048-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjerte-Lungekirurgi (Thoraxkirurgi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Brun","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"90bf6dfd-49cd-42dc-a945-c22f8561c981","name":"Thorup, Charlotte Brun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"grønkjærpau","last":"Grønkjær","locid":"574b63eb-8aff-43ac-b907-12a665ace204","name":"Grønkjær, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-1558-7062","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"spindlerpau","last":"Spindler","locid":"c95c8b19-e4d8-4f11-acca-5212a92f3db9","name":"Spindler, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-7098-5699","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Jesper","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"64f82f01-dc7b-4ed4-873a-940774d8921e","name":"Andreasen, Jan Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-2382-3734","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ae89da32-d0ea-4a39-8295-a7cc351013f6","name":"Hansen, John","orcid":"0000-0003-4989-8117","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birthe Irene","key":"dinesenpau","last":"Dinesen","locid":"22de2dad-03e3-4bc9-8d55-94736e7d5941","name":"Dinesen, Birthe","name_org":"Dinesen, Birthe Irene","orcid":"0000-0001-5893-9676","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gitte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Elgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7176fcbc-7d07-4fed-9358-d12ae9e5f2f3","name":"Sørensen, Erik Elgaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27547404"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13102-016-0048-7","issn":["20521847"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Sports Science, Medicine and Rehabilitation","paperid":"24","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Sports Science, Medicine and Rehabilitation","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026811490"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2f0ea7ff-3a94-407b-8a2e-1d8cbf622c8f","au-7cdbcb47-3fe2-41f4-bf3e-b00611d6824a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pedometer use and self-determined motivation for walking in a cardiac telerehabilitation program : a qualitative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-002358","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Poor adherence to medical treatment may have considerable consequences for the patients' health and for healthcare costs to society. The need to understand the determinants for poor adherence has motivated several studies on socio-demographics and comorbidity. Few studies focus on the association between risk attitude and adherence. The aim of the present study was to estimate associations between patients' adherence to statin treatment and different dimensions of risk attitude, and to identify subgroups of patients with poor adherence. METHODS: Population-based questionnaire and register-based study on a sample of 6393 persons of the general. Danish population aged 20-79. Data on risk attitude were based on 4 items uncovering health-related as well as financial dimensions of risk attitude. They were collected through a web-based questionnaire and combined with register data on redeemed statin prescriptions, sociodemographics and comorbidity. Adherence was estimated by proportion of days covered using a cut-off point at 80 %. RESULTS: For the dimension of health-related risk attitude, \"Preference for GP visit when having symptoms\", risk-neutral and risk-seeking patients had poorer adherence than the risk-averse patients, OR 0.80 (95 %-CI 0.68-0.95) and OR 0.83 (95 %-CI 0.71-0.98), respectively. No significant association was found between adherence and financial risk attitude. Further, patients in the youngest age group and patients with no CVD were less adherent to statin treatment. CONCLUSION: We find some indication that risk attitude is associated with adherence to statin treatment, and that risk-neutral and risk-seeking patients may have poorer adherence than risk-averse patients. This is important for clinicians to consider when discussing optimal treatment decisions with their patients. The identified subgroups with the poorest adherence may deserve special attention from their GP regarding statin treatment.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Barfoed, Benedicte Lind","Paulsen, Maja Skov","Christensen, Palle Mark","Halvorsen, Peder Andreas","Kjær, Trine","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Larsen, Pia Veldt","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Søndergaard, Jens","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007366"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adherence","Cardiovascular","General practice","Journal Article","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Risk attitude","Statins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between patients risk attitude and their adherence to statin treatment a population based questionnaire and register study","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-016-0423-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007366","identifier":[{"id":"84960388582","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26956487","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000371966600002","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC4784361","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-97dc5cb0-d1ab-4ede-a05d-82dee934099f","sdu-c4bd37d7-3e40-43fc-b514-581f4f0160b0"],"keyword":["Adherence","Cardiovascular","General practice","Journal Article","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Risk attitude","Statins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DA8598D770820FAC9E147226EE74D481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-016-0423-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121934333/Associations_between_patients_risk_attitude.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/265214306/document_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedicte Marie Lind","key":"barfoedbenedictemarielindpau","last":"Barfoed","locid":"d4fff58a-9ee4-49aa-ba67-bd49cb73f420","name":"Barfoed, Benedicte Marie Lind","orcid":"0000-0002-2319-3963","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedicte Lind","key":"barfoedbenedictelindpau","last":"Barfoed","name":"Barfoed, Benedicte Lind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Skov","key":"paulsenmajaskovpau","last":"Paulsen","locid":"7288551b-43b2-4400-bdc3-b78ad9c0ccc3","name":"Paulsen, Maja Skov","orcid":"0000-0003-0360-0039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Palle Mark","key":"christensenpallemarkpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"e266e55b-be6c-4c91-ad39-392abfc547f6","name":"Christensen, Palle Mark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peder Andreas","key":"halvorsenpederandreaspau","last":"Halvorsen","locid":"6b414563-caed-41a2-910a-1ed6c929c3fe","name":"Halvorsen, Peder Andreas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"kjærtrinepau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0d94bc73-7597-4daf-bad7-b5d74ed6c2a9","name":"Kjær, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-9554-374X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens Lytken","key":"larsenmogenslytkenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4dd22edc-ce70-44c0-beff-7afe7a9c8c47","name":"Larsen, Mogens Lytken","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Veldt","key":"larsenpiaveldtpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d6c16700-b7c7-4172-a8df-3e726624dc36","name":"Larsen, Pia Veldt","orcid":"0000-0002-8730-3703","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenjesperbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardjenspau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbøldorteejgpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26956487"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12875-016-0423-1","issn":["14712296"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Family Practice","paperid":"28","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Family Practice","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960388582"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-97dc5cb0-d1ab-4ede-a05d-82dee934099f","sdu-c4bd37d7-3e40-43fc-b514-581f4f0160b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations between patients' risk attitude and their adherence to statin treatment : a population based questionnaire and register study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-007366","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Heart rate (HR) at rest is a well-known marker of cardiovascular morbidity and mortality. Results on the association between HR and incident atrial fibrillation (AF) have, however, been conflicting. Using digital electrocardiograms from 281,451 primary care patients, we aimed to describe the association between HR at rest and the hazards of incident AF. Secondary end points were death from all causes and pacemaker implantation. Data on drug use, co-morbidity, and outcomes were collected from nationwide administrative health care registries. During a median follow-up time of 8.4 years, 15,666 subjects were observed to develop AF, of which 1,631 were lone AF. A HR at rest from 30 to 51 beats/min was associated with an adjusted hazard ratio of 1.16 (95% CI 1.06 to 1.27) for AF compared with the reference group (66 to 72 beats/min). From 72 beats/min and upward, the hazard ratio of AF increased in a dose-response manner, reaching an adjusted hazard ratio of 1.36 (95% CI 1.26 to 1.46) for HR between 95 and 120 beats/min. Both for low and high HR, the associations were accentuated for the outcome lone AF (adjusted hazard ratios of 1.48, 95% CI 1.19 to 1.84 and 1.84, 95% CI 1.47 to 2.30 for HR between 30 to 51 and 95 to 120 beats/min, respectively). For death from all causes, the hazard increased almost linearly with increasing HR. A HR at rest from 30 to 51 beats/min was associated with an adjusted hazard ratio of 1.80 (95% CI 1.46 to 2.21) for pacemaker implantation. In conclusion, a U-shaped association was found between HR at rest and incident AF, and this association was strongest for the outcome lone AF.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Skov, Morten W.","Bachmann, Troels N.","Rasmussen, Peter V.","Olesen, Morten S.","Pietersen, Adrian","Graff, Claus","Lind, Bent","Struijk, Johannes","Køber, Lars","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper H.","Gerds, Thomas A.","Holst, Anders G.","Nielsen, Jonas B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010552"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between heart rate at rest and incident atrial fibrillation from the copenhagen electrocardiographic study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-010552","identifier":[{"id":"000382420400015","type":"wos"},{"id":"27394409","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84979669608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dd9a478f-82ae-4e1c-bc2b-1077525fd025","ku-a504ccc0-01f1-4248-a1b9-55a516b64fde"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-45CE66E3D40CE967B517938A457F45D8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Medical Informatics Group (CT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"