name":"Nordentoft, Steen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Lau","key":"baggesendortelaupau","last":"Baggesen","locid":"f887fd6c-b59d-46ba-960e-b91277045780","name":"Baggesen, Dorte Lau","orcid":"0000-0003-4018-1531","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"madsenmogenspau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Mogens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26842400"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13028-016-0192-9","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","paperid":"11","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","title_org":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica (Online)","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84956931267"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Novo Nordisk","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","dianova a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cfaeecba-b16a-4b4b-9765-13c60a0251d7","ku-8e1b3def-afaf-4b6d-9a7a-20126c6f9a75","sdu-b5a88fa4-4d4b-4792-9ed4-0055565dfb82"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Campylobacter jejuni and Campylobacter coli in wild birds on Danish livestock farms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.34-037273","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background The benefit of an implantable cardioverter-defibrillator (ICD) in patients with symptomatic systolic heart failure caused by coronary artery disease has been well documented. However, the evidence for a benefit of prophylactic ICDs in patients with systolic heart failure that is not due to coronary artery disease has been based primarily on subgroup analyses. The management of heart failure has improved since the landmark ICD trials, and many patients now receive cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT). Methods In a randomized, controlled trial, 556 patients with symptomatic systolic heart failure (left ventricular ejection fraction, ≤35%) not caused by coronary artery disease were assigned to receive an ICD, and 560 patients were assigned to receive usual clinical care (control group). In both groups, 58% of the patients received CRT. The primary outcome of the trial was death from any cause. The secondary outcomes were sudden cardiac death and cardiovascular death. Results After a median follow-up period of 67.6 months, the primary outcome had occurred in 120 patients (21.6%) in the ICD group and in 131 patients (23.4%) in the control group (hazard ratio, 0.87; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.68 to 1.12; P=0.28). Sudden cardiac death occurred in 24 patients (4.3%) in the ICD group and in 46 patients (8.2%) in the control group (hazard ratio, 0.50; 95% CI, 0.31 to 0.82; P=0.005). Device infection occurred in 27 patients (4.9%) in the ICD group and in 20 patients (3.6%) in the control group (P=0.29). Conclusions In this trial, prophylactic ICD implantation in patients with symptomatic systolic heart failure not caused by coronary artery disease was not associated with a significantly lower long-term rate of death from any cause than was usual clinical care. (Funded by Medtronic and others; DANISH ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT00542945 .).","author_count":29,"contributors":["Køber, Lars","Thune, Jens J","Nielsen, Jens C","Haarbo, Jens","Videbæk, Lars","Korup, Eva","Jensen, Gunnar","Hildebrandt, Per","Steffensen, Flemming H","Bruun, Niels Eske","Eiskjær, Hans","Brandes, Axel","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Gustafsson, Finn","Egstrup, Kenneth","Videbæk, Regitze","Hassager, Christian","Svendsen, Jesper H","Høfsten, Dan E","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Pehrson, Steen"],"cuid":["S04-099.01-011508"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corpau":["DANISH Investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Amiodarone","Cardiac Pacing Artificial","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Cardiovascular Diseases","Death","Death Sudden Cardiac","Defibrillators Implantable","Dilated cardiomyopathy","Electrocardiography","Female","Follow Up Studies","Heart Failure Systolic","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Mortality","Multicenter Study","Prevention","Randomized Controlled Trial","Risk","Stroke Volume","TRIAL"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"defibrillator implantation in patients with nonischemic systolic heart failure","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128446678/Defibrillator_Implantation_in_Patients_with_Nonischemic_Systolic_Heart_Failure.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.01-011508","identifier":[{"id":"27571011","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000384265000004","type":"wos"},{"id":"WOS:000384265000004","type":"wos"},{"id":"84990029434","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f0c6d4ff-f12d-4736-b2a2-199e0716511e","au-9273479b-57f2-4bc6-9e42-5bc30f6726e7","ku-252ac339-a861-4d9a-aea5-17d94012d319","sdu-6ead1446-0edd-4bc2-9903-f6309a1b28b5"],"keyword":["AMIODARONE","Aged","CARDIAC-RESYNCHRONIZATION THERAPY","CARDIOVERTER-DEFIBRILLATOR","Cardiac Pacing, Artificial","Cardiovascular Diseases","DEATH","DILATED CARDIOMYOPATHY","Death, Sudden, Cardiac","Defibrillators, Implantable","Electrocardiography","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Heart Failure, Systolic","Humans","Journal Article","MORTALITY","Male","Middle Aged","Multicenter Study","PREVENTION","RISK","Randomized Controlled Trial","Stroke Volume","TRIAL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-E4D76281E281C05C3B8157EFAF0856BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128446678/Defibrillator_Implantation_in_Patients_with_Nonischemic_Systolic_Heart_Failure.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3