{"abstract":"Garbled circuits is a cryptographic technique, which has been used among other things for the construction of two and threeparty secure computation, private function evaluation and secure outsourcing. Garbling schemes is a primitive which formalizes the syntax and security properties of garbled circuits. We define a generalization of garbling schemes called reactive garbling schemes. We consider functions and garbled functions taking multiple inputs and giving multiple outputs. Two garbled functions can be linked together: an encoded output of one garbled function can be transformed into an encoded input of the other garbled function without communication between the parties. Reactive garbling schemes also allow partial evaluation of garbled functions even when only some of the encoded inputs are provided. It is possible to further evaluate the linked garbled functions when more garbled inputs become available. It is also possible to later garble more functions and link them to the ongoing garbled evaluation. We provide rigorous definitions for reactive garbling schemes. We define a new notion of security for reactive garbling schemes called confidentiality. We provide both simulation based and indistinguishability based notions of security. We also show that the simulation based notion of security implies the indistinguishability based notion of security. We present an instantiation of reactive garbling schemes. We finally present an application of reactive garbling schemes to reactive two-party computation secure against a malicious, static adversary.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Ranellucci, Samuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130765"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-08","place":"Hanoi, vn","start":"2016-12-04","title":"22nd International Conference on the Theory and Application of Cryptology and Information Security, ASIACRYPT 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reactive garbling foundation instantiation application","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85008195174","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130765","identifier":[{"id":"85008195174","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-02a72fff-ac23-4298-aa45-c9788a12e50a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D97F5E18F6C8B862B8853B50CA70B3A1"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel","key":"ranelluccipau","last":"Ranellucci","locid":"880e9315-34fd-496c-bf58-f18b12d2de7b","name":"Ranellucci, Samuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jung Hee","key":"cheonpedh","last":"Cheon","name":"Cheon, Jung Hee","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tsuyoshi","key":"takagipedh","last":"Takagi","name":"Takagi, Tsuyoshi","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-53890-6_34","eisbn":["9783662538906"],"isbn":["9783662538890"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"1022-1052","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advances in Cryptology - ASIACRYPT 2016 - 22nd International Conference on the Theory and Application of Cryptology and Information Security, Proceedings","volume":"10032"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008195174"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-02a72fff-ac23-4298-aa45-c9788a12e50a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reactive garbling : Foundation, instantiation, application","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-130765","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
