,{"affno":"","first":"Erland Kolding","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Erland Kolding","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lundtoftepedh","last":"Lundtofte","name":"Lundtofte, Henrik","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"mariagerpedh","last":"Mariager","name":"Mariager, Rasmus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob K.","key":"meilepedh","last":"Meile","name":"Meile, Jakob K.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788763545464"],"pages":"379-393","place":"Kbh.","publisher":"Det Kongelige Bibliotek","series":"Danish Humanist Texts and Studies","status":"p","subtitle":"Historiske &amp; kulturhistoriske studier. Festskrift til John T. Lauridsen","title":"Kildekunst","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-63c26ccc-4fa7-482c-a1cc-a980f19ac8ca"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Dunkle forretninger. Karl Larsen og Emil Charlet : To intellektuelle konjunkturryttere i 1920'rnes Berlin","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-548789","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Following human mercury (Hg) exposure, the metal accumulates in considerable concentrations in kidney, liver, and brain. Although the toxicokinetics of Hg have been studied extensively, factors responsible for interindividual variation in humans are largely unknown. Differences in accumulation of renal Hg between inbred mouse strains suggest a genetic interstrain variation regulating retention or/and excretion of Hg. A.SW, DBA/2 and BALB/C mouse strains accumulate higher amounts of Hg than B10.S. Objectives: We aimed to find candidate genes associated with regulation of renal Hg concentrations. Methods: A.SW, B10.S and their F1 and F2 offspring were exposed for 6 weeks to 2.0 mg Hg/L drinking water. Genotyping with microsatellites was conducted on 84 F2 mice for genome-wide scanning with ion pair reverse-phase high-performance liquid chromatography (IP RP HPLC). Quantitative trait loci (QTL) were established. Denaturing HPLC was used to detect single nucleotide polymorphisms for haplotyping and fine mapping in 184 and 32 F2 mice, respectively. Candidate genes (Pprc1, Btrc and Nfkb2) verified by fine mapping and QTL were further inves-tigated by real-time polymerase chain reaction. Genes enhanced by Pprc1 (Nrf1 and Nrf2) were included for gene expression analysis. results: Renal Hg concentrations differed significantly between A.SW and B10.S mice and between males and females within each strain. QTL analysis showed a peak logarithm of odds ratio score 5.78 on chromosome 19 (p = 0.002). Haplotype and fine mapping associated the Hg accumulation with Pprc1, which encodes PGC-1-related coactivator (PRC), a coactivator for proteins involved in detoxification. Pprc1 and two genes coactivated by Pprc1 (Nrf1 and Nrf2) had significantly lower gene expression in the A.SW strain than in the B10.S strain. conclusions: This study supports Pprc1 as a key regulator for renal Hg excretion.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Alkaissi, Hammoudi","Ekstrand, Jimmy","Jawad, Aksa","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Havarinasab, Said","Soderkvist, Peter","Hultman, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-611551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Linköping University"],"keyword":["Animals","Gene Expression drug effects","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotype","Haplotypes","Humans","Kidney drug effects","Mercury toxicity","Mice","Mice Inbred BALB C","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Quantitative Trait Loci","Real Time Polymerase Chain Reaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association study to identify genes related to renal mercury concentrations in mice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409284","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-611551","identifier":[{"id":"84977126011","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26942574","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4937848","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-85e48ef3-2795-4621-92d7-937b909315df"],"keyword":["Animals","Gene Expression/drug effects","Genome-Wide Association Study","Genotype","Haplotypes","Humans","Kidney/drug effects","Mercury/toxicity","Mice","Mice, Inbred BALB C","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Quantitative Trait Loci","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EFBDF9453C4CD00896F303D2A10CD06A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp.1409284","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/123549492/ehp.1409284.alt.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hammoudi","key":"alkaissipau","last":"Alkaissi","name":"Alkaissi, Hammoudi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jimmy","key":"ekstrandpau","last":"Ekstrand","name":"Ekstrand, Jimmy","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aksa","key":"jawadpau","last":"Jawad","name":"Jawad, Aksa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Said","key":"havarinasabpau","last":"Havarinasab","name":"Havarinasab, Said","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"soderkvistpau","last":"Soderkvist","name":"Soderkvist, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"hultmanpau","last":"Hultman","name":"Hultman, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26942574"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp.1409284","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"7","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","pages":"920-926","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977126011"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-85e48ef3-2795-4621-92d7-937b909315df"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genome-Wide Association Study to Identify Genes Related to Renal Mercury Concentrations in Mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-611551","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Disse to artikler tilbyder pædagoger nogle centrale perspektiver på etik og dømmekraft særligt på opholdssteder. Men perspektiverne er også særdeles relevante for pædagoger, som arbejder i andre institutionstyper. Artikel 1: Behovet for flerstemmighed Den første artikel peger på, at det socialpædagogiske arbejde på opholdssteder er i hastig forandring i disse år. Forfatterne nævner to centrale forandringer, som eksempler på forhold, der potentielt sætter den socialpædagogiske praksis under pres: Der er sket et skift i målgruppen, da det er en anden type børn og unge, der bliver anbragt. Dette betyder for eksempel, at misbrug og psykiatriske diagnoser i større grad er en del af pædagogernes hverdag. Der er øgede krav til pædagogerne i forhold til at dokumentere deres pædagogiske arbejde og opnå resultater. Artiklen ønsker at vise, at forhold som disse potentielt øger risikoen for det, der i psykologien kaldes gruppetænkning. Gruppetænkning menes at kunne svække det, forfatterne kalder moralsk sensitivitet og dømmekraft. Artiklen behandler derefter ’faren ved at blive ligesom din kollega’. Under denne overskrift inddrages den amerikanske professor i psykologi Irving Janis’ forståelse af gruppetænkning. Janis arbejder i denne forståelse ud fra tre kategorier: foranledende betingelser for gruppetænkning, symptomer på gruppetænkning samt symptomer på dårlige beslutningsprocesser. Disse tre kategorier anvendes til at belyse materiale fra interview med tre pædagoger fra et opholdssted for børn og unge i Nordjylland. Derefter inddrages den russiske litteraturteoretiker og sprogfilosof Mikhal Mikhajlovitj Bakhtin for hvem dialogen, og med denne flerstemmigheden(polyfonien), er et helt grundlæggende princip for alt udvikling. Ifølge forfatterne betyder dette i en pædagogisk praksis, at forskellighed i holdninger og perspektiver er forudsætningen for en institution i udvikling. I denne sammenhæng forklares det, hvordan flerstemmighed kan udgøre et ideal for institutionskulturen. Afslutningsvis beskrives følelser som moralske indikatorer. Her forklares det, at følelser kan forstås som stemmer, der søger at komme til orde, og som bør tages alvorligt i socialpædagogisk praksis. Forfatterne mener, at når pædagoger møder forventninger om klar (entydig) tale i forhold til såvel de unge, som de anbringende myndigheder, opstår der en risiko for gruppetænkning. Det er dermed vigtigt, at pædagogerne værner om flerstemmighed for at sikre den moralske sensitivitet og dømmekraft. Artikel 2: Vidensformer på opholdssteder Den anden artikel peger på det at være pædagog på et opholdssted og bedrive pædagogik der kan være en kompleks størrelse. Det pædagogiske arbejde er kendetegnet ved, at der findes få sandheder, men mange muligheder. Derfor bliver den faglige argumentation central, understreger forfatterne. Når man som pædagog står i en konkret situation og skal afgøre, hvad der er det etisk rigtige at gøre her og nu, kan den faglige argumentation gå i mange retninger. Når pædagogen står i et etisk dilemma, spiller værdier og menneskesyn en afgørende rolle, påpeger forfatterne. Omdrejningspunktet for denne artikel er sammenhængen mellem de forskellige vidensformer, der er på spil i den pædagogiske praksis. Forfatternes tese er, at bevidsthed om forskellige vidensformer kan spille en rolle for pædagogernes dømmekraft. Her forstås dømmekraft som evnen til at identificere et etisk dilemma og derefter afgøre, hvad der er det bedste/mest rigtige at gøre i situationen. I undersøgelsen er der taget udgangspunkt i Carsten Pedersens model, i hvilken han samler Aristoteles’ forskellige vidensformer. De forskellige vidensformer beskrives kort og Pedersens model præsenteres. Derefter udfoldes en analyse af fire opholdssteders beskrivelse af dem selv på deres hjemmeside. I denne sammenhæng forsøger forfatterne at præsentere en analyse, der kan give anledning til refleksioner over sammenhænge mellem forskellige vidensformer og disses betydning for dømmekraft i institutionssammenhæng generelt. Formålet er at vise et eksempel på, hvordan man med Aristoteles’ vidensformer kan forsøge at forstå, hvad der skal være til stede for at kunne sikre en god etisk praksis på opholdssteder. Forfatterne peger blandt andet på, at medarbejdere på opholdssteder må træne deres evne til at få øje på og kunne fortolke sociale situationer ved at overveje og afveje de værdier og interesser, der er på spil. Udover at vælge de mest brugbare metoder med et særligt mål for øje, må medarbejderne også tilegne sig viden om, hvilken videnskabelig viden, der ligger bag ved metoderne, for at kunne vurdere hvorvidt og hvordan disse stemmer overens med institutionens værdier og menneskesyn.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lisbeth","Boll, Brian Harring","Munksgaard, Jesper","Kjærgaard, Holger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-651975"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dømmekraft","Etik","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Vidensformer","flerstemmighed"],"level":"pop","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"etik på opholdssteder perspektiver på etik og dømmekraft på opholdssteder","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucn.dk/ws/files/37890777/Publikation_etik_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-651975","ids":["ucn-b4777a27-c0f7-4582-8c20-2518453e92aa"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","dømmekraft","etik","flerstemmighed","opholdssteder","vidensformer"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-F4E4D6A7CD506379121E6646AD766A28"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucn.dk/ws/files/37890777/Publikation_etik_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Pædagoguddannelsen Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8ab6f3a4-8fd4-4c4d-9177-237f7183502a","name":"Nielsen, Lisbeth","orcid":"0000-0002-1855-826X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian Harring","key":"bollpau","last":"Boll","locid":"b425372e-db35-430f-a714-97be6ecc1074","name":"Boll, Brian Harring","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"munksgaardpau","last":"Munksgaard","locid":"3109898e-bc7e-4c74-956a-462fd0bc11c6","name":"Munksgaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"94f0f892-342e-4815-83f6-8e60c3b0cedb","name":"Kjærgaard, Holger","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-b4777a27-c0f7-4582-8c20-2518453e92aa"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Etik på opholdssteder : Perspektiver på etik og dømmekraft på opholdssteder","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-651975","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Programs for population screening of colorectal cancer (CRC) have been implemented in several countries with fecal immunochemical testing (FIT) as the preferred platform. However, the major obstacle for a feces-based testing method is the limited compliance that reduces the clinical sensitivity for detection of participants with non-symptomatic CRC. Therefore, research approaches have been initiated to develop screening concepts based on biomarkers in blood. Preliminary results show that protein, genetic, epigenetic, and metabolomic components may be valuable in blood-based screening concepts, particularly when combinations of the various components appear to lead to significant improvements. OBJECTIVES: The protocol described in this paper focuses on the validation of concepts based on biomarkers in blood in a major population screened by FIT. METHODS: In Part 1, participants will be identified and included through the Danish CRC Screening Program comprising initial FIT and subsequent colonoscopy to those with a positive result. Blood samples will be collected from 8000 FIT-positive participants, who are offered subsequent colonoscopy. Findings and interventions at colonoscopy together with personal data including co-morbidity will be recorded. Blood samples and data will also be collected from 6000 arbitrarily chosen participants with negative FIT. In Part 2, blood samples and data will be collected from 30,000 FIT-negative participants three times within 4 years. The blood samples will be analyzed using various in-house and commercially available manual and automated analysis platforms. RESULTS: We anticipate Part 1 to terminate late August 2016 and Part 2 to terminate late September 2022. The results from Parts 1 and 2 will be presented within 12 to 18 months from termination. CONCLUSIONS: The purpose of this study is to improve the efficacy of identifying participants with neoplastic bowel lesions, to identify false negative participants, to identify participants at risk of interval neoplastic lesions, to improve the compliance in screening sessions, and to establish guidelines for out-patient follow-up of at-risk participants based on combinations of blood-based biomarkers.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Louise","Wilhelmsen, Michael","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Andersen, Jens","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Rasmussen, Morten","Hendel, Jakob W","Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","Vilandt, Jesper","Hillig, Thore","Klærke, Michael","Münster, Anna-Marie Bloch","Andersen, Lars M","Andersen, Berit","Hornung, Nete","Erlandsen, Erland Jørn","Khalid, Ali","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-091.22-028481"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol outlines for parts 000000000001 and 000000000002 of the prospective endoscopy iii study for the early detection of colorectal cancer validation of a concept based on blood biomarkers","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/resprot.6346","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.22-028481","identifier":[{"id":"27624815","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5039335","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d9e5f522-4b9d-4a9a-a8e7-aca4c0b73e53","ku-6ab1afab-af7f-467b-b94b-4d9f3d6d037f"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31A872C8BF1693C3B49DE4E7D7473A20"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/resprot.6346","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Mave- og Tarmkirurgi, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"rasmussenlouisepau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"wilhelmsenmichaelpau","last":"Wilhelmsen","name":"Wilhelmsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenibjarlepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b8f0594e-4a73-4cf7-9117-a9eb69323873","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"andersenjenspau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Nannestad","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenmortenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob W","key":"hendeljakobwpau","last":"Hendel","name":"Hendel, Jakob W","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens R","key":"madsenmogensrørbækpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"5591f71f-23fb-4bb3-b656-8718aa84819b","name":"Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","name_org":"Madsen, Mogens R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens R.","key":"madsenmogensrpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Mogens R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"vilandtjesperpau","last":"Vilandt","name":"Vilandt, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thore","key":"hilligthorepau","last":"Hillig","name":"Hillig, Thore","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"klærkemichaelpau","last":"Klærke","name":"Klærke, Michael","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna-Marie Bloch","key":"münsterannamarieblochpau","last":"Münster","locid":"f3549a60-dc15-4d2a-93c4-d9c10789581b","name":"Münster, Anna-Marie Bloch","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars M","key":"andersenlarsmpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lars M","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Berit","key":"andersenberitpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4f64dc11-e5ca-4037-bbad-8ca533d841e4","name":"Andersen, Berit","orcid":"0000-0003-4074-6504","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nete","key":"hornungnetepau","last":"Hornung","locid":"0bdfd3fe-c5d8-472a-831e-bc8519e68814","name":"Hornung, Nete","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Erland J","key":"erlandsenerlandjørnpau","last":"Erlandsen","locid":"3b933505-c002-4644-8a49-d2b7a977e37d","name":"Erlandsen, Erland Jørn","name_org":"Erlandsen, Erland J","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erland J.","key":"erlandsenerlandjpau","last":"Erlandsen","name":"Erlandsen, Erland J.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ali","key":"khalidalipau","last":"Khalid","locid":"f4783aa9-b40c-45b2-bbdd-9b3548921e4a","name":"Khalid, Ali","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"phw435","key":"nielsenhansjørgenpau","last":"phw435","locid":"87f9baf4-e29c-4104-be23-daf6d94d7124","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","name_org":"phw435, phw435","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27624815"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/resprot.6346","issn":["19290748"],"issue":"3","journal":"JMIR Research Protocols","paperid":"e182","status":"p","title":"JMIR Research Protocols","title_org":"J M I R Research Protocols","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d9e5f522-4b9d-4a9a-a8e7-aca4c0b73e53","ku-6ab1afab-af7f-467b-b94b-4d9f3d6d037f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protocol Outlines for Parts 1 and 2 of the Prospective Endoscopy III Study for the Early Detection of Colorectal Cancer : Validation of a Concept Based on Blood Biomarkers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.22-028481","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The prognostic value of the metabolic syndrome (MetS) is believed to vary with age. With an elderly population expecting to triple by 2060, it is important to evaluate the validity of MetS in this age group. We examined the association of MetS risk factors with later risk of type 2 diabetes (T2DM) and cardiovascular disease (CVD) in elderly Caucasian women. We further investigated if stratification of individuals not defined with MetS would add predictive power in defining future disease prevalence of individuals with MetS. The Prospective Epidemiological Risk Factor Study, a community-based cohort study, followed 3905 Danish women since 2000 (age: 70.1±6.5) with no previous diagnosis of T2DM or CVD, holding all measurements used for MetS definition; central obesity, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and hyperglycemia combined with register-based follow-up information. Elderly women with defined MetS presented a 6.3-fold increased risk of T2DM (95% confidence interval: [3.74-10.50]) and 1.7-fold increased risk of CVD (1.44-2.05) compared to women with no MetS risk factors. Subdividing the control group without defined MetS revealed that both centrally obese controls and controls holding other MetS risk factors also had increased risk of T2DM (hazard ratio (HR)=2.21 [1.25-3.93] and HR=1.75 [1.04-2.96]) and CVD (HR=1.51 [1.25-1.83] and HR=1.36 [1.15-1.60]) when compared to controls with no MetS risk factors. MetS in elderly Caucasian women increased risk of future T2DM and CVD. While not defined with MetS, women holding only some risk factors for MetS were also at increased risk of T2DM or CVD compared to women with no MetS risk factors.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Møller, Katrine Dragsbæk","Neergaard, Jesper","Laursen, Janne Marie","Hansen, Henrik B.","Christiansen, Claus","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Karsdal, Morten A.","Brix, Susanne","Henriksen, Kim"],"cuid":["S02-093.55-033574"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-1