":"Associations between patients' adherence and GPs' attitudes towards risk, statin therapy and management of non-adherence : a survey and register-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011349","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this article we show how a hybridisation of elite sport and school in lower-secondary education in Denmark produces a particular kind of learning subject with dual tracks for development, and we ask what kind of actions the students apply in order to stay becoming along both tracks. We apply theoretical conceptions of ‘becoming’ inspired by Brembeck and Johansson that allow us to understand how the sports students live up to the code of conduct of the sports classes. The article is based on an ethnographic study carried out in four schools located in four regions of Denmark. We argue that the hybrid obliges students to follow a narrow developmental track with an ambitious goal of performing in both sport and school, and that the hybrid is threatened when a sports student prioritises either sport or school while he/she is still enrolled in the class.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Olesen, Jesper Stilling","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011381"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard"],"keyword":["Becoming","Development","Education","Ethnography","Sport","Talent","Ungdomsuddannelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to stay becoming living up to the code of conduct in a sports class","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84948145116","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011381","identifier":[{"id":"84948145116","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000388410700010","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-ee54e513-6297-435c-8aba-040d7de862a2","au-955bc71e-481c-4e61-989c-3aae8604d4fb"],"keyword":["Talent","Ungdomsuddannelse","becoming","development","education","ethnography","sport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7EDF9908F54A0064DDAC2C86668A7DA6"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Education Policy Research (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Centre for Health Science Education and Problem-based Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Physical Activity and Human Performance","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences (SSI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","name_org":"Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17457823.2015.1109467","issn":["17457823","17457831"],"issn_org":["17457823"],"issue":"3","journal":"Ethnography and Education","pages":"371-387","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Ethnography and Education","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84948145116"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ee54e513-6297-435c-8aba-040d7de862a2","au-955bc71e-481c-4e61-989c-3aae8604d4fb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How to stay becoming : living up to the code of conduct in a sports class","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011381","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"It is well established that lncRNAs are aberrantly expressed in cancer where they have been shown to act as oncogenes or tumor suppressors. RNA profiling of 314 colorectal adenomas/adenocarcinomas and 292 adjacent normal colon mucosa samples using RNA-sequencing demonstrated that the snoRNA host gene 16 (SNHG16) is significantly up-regulated in adenomas and all stages of CRC. SNHG16 expression was positively correlated to the expression of Wnt-regulated transcription factors, including ASCL2, ETS2, and c-Myc. In vitro abrogation of Wnt signaling in CRC cells reduced the expression of SNHG16 indicating that SNHG16 is regulated by the Wnt pathway. Silencing of SNHG16 resulted in reduced viability, increased apoptotic cell death and impaired cell migration. The SNHG16 silencing particularly affected expression of genes involved in lipid metabolism. A connection between SNHG16 and genes involved in lipid metabolism was also observed in clinical tumors. Argonaute CrossLinking and ImmunoPrecipitation (AGO-CLIP) demonstrated that SNHG16 heavily binds AGO and has 27 AGO/miRNA target sites along its length, indicating that SNHG16 may act as a competing endogenous RNA (ceRNA) “sponging” miRNAs off their cognate targets. Most interestingly, half of the miRNA families with high confidence targets on SNHG16 also target the 3′UTR of Stearoyl-CoA Desaturase (SCD). SCD is involved in lipid metabolism and is down-regulated upon SNHG16 silencing. In conclusion, up-regulation of SNHG16 is a frequent event in CRC, likely caused by deregulated Wnt signaling. In vitro analyses demonstrate that SNHG16 may play an oncogenic role in CRC and that it affects genes involved in lipid metabolism, possible through ceRNA related mechanisms.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Christensen, Lise Lotte","True, Kirsten Kallesøe","Hamilton, M.P.","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Djodji Damas, Nkerorema","Damgaard, Christian Kroun","Ongen, Halit","Dermitzakis, Emmanouil T","Bramsen, Jesper","Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Lund, Anders Henrik","Vang, Søren","Stribolt, Katrine","Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","Laurberg, Søren","McGuire, Sean","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023063"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","University of Geneva"],"keyword":["Colorectal cancer","Functional analyses","Long non coding RNAs","Wnt pathway"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snhg000000000016 is regulated by the wnt pathway in colorectal cancer and affects genes involved in lipid metabolism","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molonc.2016.06.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023063","identifier":[{"id":"84992707538","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5423192","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27396952","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8ea66dc4-cce1-40c2-9d0b-65f51bdf6287","ku-9a81db3e-88ac-422b-9fbd-77649a2c72e9"],"keyword":["AGO-CLIP","Colorectal cancer","Functional analyses","Long non-coding RNAs","SNHG16","Wnt pathway"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-276C2F1891B44CBBC6620CAF81B62A42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molonc.2016.06.003","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/