{"abstract":"Flooding produced by high-intensive local rainfall and drainage system capacity exceedance can have severe impacts in cities. In order to prepare cities for these types of flood events – especially in the future climate – it is valuable to be able to simulate these events numerically both historically and in real-time. There is a rather untested potential in real-time prediction of urban floods. In this paper radar data observations with different spatial and temporal resolution, radar nowcasts of 0–2 h lead time, and numerical weather models with lead times up to 24 h are used as inputs to an integrated flood and drainage systems model in order to investigate the relative difference between different inputs in predicting future floods. The system is tested on a small town Lystrup in Denmark, which has been flooded in 2012 and 2014. Results show it is possible to generate detailed flood maps in real-time with high resolution radar rainfall data, but rather limited forecast performance in predicting floods with lead times more than half an hour.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Jensen, David Getreuer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-111492"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Numerical weather models","Pluvial flood modelling","Radar nowcasting","Real time modelling of drainage systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urban pluvial flood prediction a case study evaluating radar rainfall nowcasts and numerical weather prediction models as model inputs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-111492","identifier":[{"id":"85014956028","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000391264900009","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d39ba409-b52d-42a9-a555-c49831f8c2f8"],"keyword":["Numerical weather models","Pluvial flood modelling","Radar nowcasting","Real-time modelling of drainage systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-310C1F10C8FEE1205EAA713623D12DFA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Environment (CIVIL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Envidan A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Liedtke","key":"thorndahlpau","last":"Thorndahl","locid":"5faa528b-e2f0-41fd-8128-9d76ed5993f0","name":"Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jes