:"Nielsen","locid":"6dee8124-9f7e-40a3-baa8-8dd5138e691d","name":"Nielsen, Agnete Hedemann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Torkell","key":"ellingsenpau","last":"Ellingsen","name":"Ellingsen, Torkell","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dbb0a9f1-daf5-4b1a-b23d-57b067ffd062"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Left ventricular function at 2-year follow-up in treatment-naive rheumatoid arthritis - patients is associated with anti-CCP status: A cohort study","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254727","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In 2004, as a response to increased competition in the world of elite sports (and of Denmark’s perceived lagging), the Danish Ministry of Culture lowered the age of recruitment for athletes for the Danish elite sport association (Team Danmark) from 15 to 12. In 2005, the first sports classes were introduced and, as of 2015, SportsClasses were available for talented athletes in Grades 7-9 in designated public schools. The SportsClasses attempt to balance collaboration between two different organizations: Danish public schools and sports clubs. The sports clubs’ main purpose is to develop talented youth who can compete nationally and internationally, while the purpose of the Danish schools is to educate all students and enable their versatile – i.e. athletic AND academic - development. To evaluate this program, in 2013, the largest survey of SportsClass students was undertaken (N=1206) with a follow-up survey in 2015. In this paper, we explore the social backgrounds and experiences of students in order to examine their likelihood of retention during the first few years of the program. Focusing on socioeconomic status, the role of having parents in elite sports, and type of sport, we study what key experiences and relationships lead students to abandon or sustain their interest in careers related to sports and how this differs for boys and girls. By applying Pierre Bourdieu’s concepts of habitus and types of capital, we conclude that there are elements of both reproduction and opportunity revealed by this new program but that the patterns differ significantly by gender.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","Karen, David","Nielsen, Jens Christian","Stilling Olesen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-262982"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bryn Mawr College"],"keyword":["Bourdieu","Gender","Grundskole","Køn","Opportunities","Social reproduction","Sports classes","Talent","Talent development"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reproduction or opportunity talent development in danish sports classes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-262982","ids":["au-ea2d31ac-0aae-48fd-ab47-8b7dab46fa4f"],"keyword":["Bourdieu","Grundskole","Køn","Sports classes","Talent","Talent development","gender","opportunities","social opportunities","social reproduction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1738A329DA11D62C2559C4FA0CA45340"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University (AAU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"bryn mawr college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Bryn Mawr College","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"karenpau","last":"Karen","name":"Karen, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","name_org":"Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ea2d31ac-0aae-48fd-ab47-8b7dab46fa4f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reproduction or opportunity : Talent development in Danish Sports Classes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-262982","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Fusion energy research is moving to the next stage with the well progressed construction of one of the largest research infrastructures ever – ITER. The goal of ITER is to produce 500 MW of fusion power while heating the fuel –deuterium/tritium plasma – by 50 MW. This will confirm fusion energy to be a viable energy source. Fusion energy power plants will be safe and can be operated to supply the baseload of an energy system. The fuel resources are inexhaustible, and can be derived from sea water. Fusion energy is based on the nuclear reaction fusing hydrogen isotopes into helium – like in the Sun – and thus no CO2 is released in the energy production. The waste of the energy production is the irradiated steel of the core of the reactor, but this radioactivity will only last for about 100 years and no long-term radioactive waste storage is needed. While the promise of safe, clean and abundant energy is the ultimate goal of fusion energy, the path towards this is challenging. A fusion plasma has a temperature of 200 mio. degrees (15 times that of the core of the Sun), and this is confined by a magnetic field generated by powerful superconducting magnets in a vacuum chamber of 1000 m3. Operating diagnostic systems in the environment of ITER is a challenge for many technologies, but due to robustness, microwave diagnostics will play an increasingly important role in burning plasma fusion energy experiments like ITER and beyond. The Collective Thomson Scattering (CTS) diagnostic to be installed at ITER is an example of such a diagnostic with great potential in present and future experiments. The ITER CTS diagnostic will inject a 1 MW 60 GHz beam of electromagnetic radiation from a gyrotron into the ITER plasma and observe the scattering off fluctuations in the plasma – to monitor the dynamics of the fast ions generated in the fusion reactions. This will provide important physics understanding of the behavior of the fusion plasma that can be used for optimizing future fusion power plants. A research team at DTU (DTU Physics and DTU Nutech) has been tasked by Fusion for Energy (the European coordinator for supplies to ITER) to develop the ITER CTS diagnostic in collaboration with Instituto Superior Técnico in Portugal. It is a 5 year effort of more than 50 man year total effort. This presentation will outline the prospects and the status of the development of fusion energy research and the CTS diagnostic system for ITER.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Gutierrez Espinoza, Heidi Estibaliz","Jensen, T.","Jessen, Martin","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Larsen, Axel Wright","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Nonbøl, Erik","Rasmussen, Jesper","Salewski, Mirko","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Taormina, Arianna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311553"],"event":{"end":"2016-11-30","place":"Kgs. Lyngby, dk","start":"2016-11-30","title":"Sustain-ATV Conference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing diagnostic systems for iter the next step fusion energy experiment","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sustain.dtu.dk/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311553","ids":["dtu-17318209-8154-4849-815b-e4c875ff5240"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4C3F9C45900BC86B60D434888799C0C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sustain.dtu.dk/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark",