{"abstract":"Concurrent data structures synchronized with locks do not scale well with the number of threads. As more scalable alternatives, concurrent data structures and algorithms based on widely available, however advanced, atomic operations have been proposed. These data structures allow for correct and concurrent operations without any locks. In this paper, we present a new fully lock-free open addressed hash table with a simpler design than prior published work. We split hash table insertions into two atomic phases: first inserting a value ignoring other concurrent operations, then in the second phase resolve any duplicate or conflicting values. Our hash table has a constant and low memory usage that is less than existing lock-free hash tables at a fill level of 33% and above. The hash table exhibits good cache locality. Compared to prior art, our hash table results in 16% and 15% fewer L1 and L2 cache misses respectively, leading to 21% fewer memory stall cycles. Our experiments show that our hash table scales close to linearly with the number of threads and outperforms, in throughput, other lock-free hash tables by 19%","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Puge","Karlsson, Sven"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-362390"],"event":{"end":"2016-03-16","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2016-03-12","title":"ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles and Practice of Parallel Programming","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a scalable lock free hash table with open addressing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963778133","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-362390","identifier":[{"id":"84963778133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c168c107-d01d-4c98-ab0a-905c87b26ea9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-05B7A753C0E41CCF8B0BA2655BAE0350"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Puge","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Puge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sven","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"0994c73f-6656-4260-b54d-3f9f426c4edb","name":"Karlsson, Sven","orcid":"0000-0003-0737-9992","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3016078.2851196","isbn":["9781450340922"],"issn":["03621340"],"pages":"1-2","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM SIGPLAN Notices","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 21st ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles and Practice of Parallel Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963778133"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c168c107-d01d-4c98-ab0a-905c87b26ea9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A scalable lock-free hash table with open addressing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-362390","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Fra arkitekturens tidligste barndom har der været tætte forbindelser mellem byggekunst og alkohol. I denne artikel skal vi se nærmere på, hvordan alkohol er blevet inddraget i arkitekturens planlægnings-, beslutnings- og byggeprocesser, og vi skal præsenteres for prominente eksempler på alkotektur – fra den jordbundne vinkælder til den æteriske cocktailsky","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kinzel, Moritz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417310"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Architectural Analysis","Building history","Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Heritage","Typology"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alkotektur byggeri arkitekter og alkohol","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://e-pages.dk/ku/1205/2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417310","ids":["ku-27ed89a7-bcac-42f7-ac2e-eab9fde899c9"],"keyword":["Building history","Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Heritage","Typology","architectural analysis"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A10DD3BFBCA89E46B4665826606B73D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://e-pages.dk/ku/1205/2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Moritz","key":"kinzelpau","last":"Kinzel","locid":"c509397f-b9ce-4534-8379-35bc1c5645f3","name":"Kinzel, Moritz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ditte Maria","key":"søgaardpedh","last":"Søgaard","name":"Søgaard, Ditte Maria","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788789221250"],"issn":["19042957"],"issue":"6","pages":"111-126","place":"København","publisher":"Institut for Tværkulturelle og Regionale Studier, Københavns Universitet","series":"Tværkultur","status":"p","subtitle":"Årbog for ToRS 2015","title":"Alkohol"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-27ed89a7-bcac-42f7-ac2e-eab9fde899c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Alkotektur : byggeri, arkitekter og alkohol","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-417310","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: In the recently updated clinical guidelines from the European Society of Cardiology on the management of stable coronary artery disease (CAD), the updated Diamond Forrester score has been included as a pretest probability (PTP) score to select patients for further diagnostic testing. We investigated the validity of the new guidelines in a population of patients with acute-onset chest pain. METHODS: We examined 527 consecutive patients with either an exercise-ECG stress test or single-photon emission computed tomography, and subsequently coronary computed tomography angiography (CCTA). We compared the diagnostic accuracy of PTP and stress testing assessed by the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC) to identify significant CAD, defined as at least 1 coronary artery branch with >70% diameter stenosis identified by CCTA. RESULTS: The diagnostic accuracy of PTP was significantly higher than the stress test (AUC 0.80 vs. 0.69; p = 0.009), but the diagnostic accuracy of the combination of PTP and a stress test did not significantly increase when compared to PTP alone (AUC 0.86 vs. 0.80; p = 0.06). CONCLUSIONS: PTP using the updated Diamond and Forrester Score is a very useful tool in risk-stratifying patients with acute-onset chest pain at a low-to-intermediate risk of having CAD. Adding a stress test to PTP does not appear to offer significant diagnostic benefit.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørgaard, Mathias","Linde, Jesper James","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Kühl, Jørgen Tobias","Kelbæk, Henning Skov","Nielsen, Walter Bjørn","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-424039"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Chest Pain","Cohort Studies","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Stenosis","Coronary Vessels","Coronary artery disease","Exercise Test","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Predictive Value of Tests","ROC Curve","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Risk Assessment","Severity of Illness Index","Tomography Emission Computed Single Photon","Validation Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic value of the updated diamond and forrester score to predict coronary artery disease in patients with acute onset chest pain","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-424039","identifier":[{"id":"26389728","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84942279374","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3373ad21-ec4c-488e-aba3-96840390f5c6"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Chest Pain","Cohort Studies","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Coronary Stenosis","Coronary Vessels","Exercise Test","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Predictive Value of Tests","ROC Curve","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Risk Assessment","Severity of Illness Index","Tomography, Emission-Computed, Single-Photon","Validation Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3415E459807CC37817374798A8BA15D8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","c