{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Patients with diabetes may experience higher risk of Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia (SAB) than patients without diabetes due to decreased immunity or coexisting morbidities. We investigated the risk of community-acquired (CA) SAB in persons with and without diabetes. DESIGN: Using population-based medical databases, we conducted a case-control study of all adults with first-time CA-SAB and matched population controls in Northern Denmark, 2000-2011. METHODS: Based on conditional logistic regression, we computed odds ratios (ORs) of CA-SAB according to diabetes. We further assessed whether the risk of CA-SAB differed according to various diabetes-related characteristics (e.g. duration of diabetes, glycemic control, and presence of diabetes complications). RESULTS: We identified 2,638 patients with incident CA-SAB of which 713 (27.0%) had diabetes, and 26,379 matched population controls (2,495 or 9.5% with diabetes). Individuals with diabetes had a substantially increased risk of CA-SAB compared with population controls (adjusted OR=2.8 (95% confidence interval (CI), 2.5-3.1)). Diabetes duration of ≥10 years and poor glycemic control conferred higher risk estimates, with an adjusted OR=2.3 (95% CI, 1.9-2.7) for diabetes with Hba1c <7% (<53 mmol/mol) and an adjusted OR=5.7 (95% CI, 4.2-7.7) for diabetes with Hba1c ≥9% (≥75 mmol/mol). The risk of CA-SAB was particularly high in patient with diabetes complications: adjusted OR=5.5 (95% CI, 4.2-7.2) with presence of microvascular complications and OR=7.0 (95% CI, 5.4-9.0) with combined macro- and microvascular complications. CONCLUSIONS: Diabetes is associated with substantially increased risk of CA-SAB, particularly among patients with diabetes of long duration, poor glycemic control, and diabetes complications.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Smit, Jesper","Søgaard, Mette","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Nielsen, Henrik","Frøslev, Trine","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich"],"cuid":["S02-086.93-665939"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bacteremia","Case Control Studies","Community Acquired Infections","Denmark","Diabetes Complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Risk","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetes and risk of community acquired staphylococcus aureus bacteremia a population based case control study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84970024159","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.93-665939","identifier":[{"id":"26966175","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000375653400013","type":"wos"},{"id":"84970024159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b9621fdf-bad1-48eb-b913-b86197335995","au-da2399e5-1bbc-4217-8685-55e394050105"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Bacteremia","Case-Control Studies","Community-Acquired Infections","Denmark","Diabetes Complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Risk","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-526DCC39543B28F051A352FF7E597950"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Infektionsmedicin [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"smitpau","last":"Smit","locid":"29aa2e66-1f20-4693-9114-5f988949c879","name":"Smit, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","loci