{"abstract":"The literature has traditionally considered commitment as an individual characteristic or condition of the individual. This means that one is inclined to think that it is those who have commitment who have the opportunity to become excellent performers within their sport. But what if commitment is not something you have, or are, but something you do, and commitment is not an individual property but a relationship in which athletes relate to talent developers to become talents. If that is so talent development may not be as much about spotting and selecting as about forging relationships and building commitment.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Stilling Olesen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-204143"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-17","place":"Trollhättan, se","start":"2016-06-15","title":"Nordic Youth Research Symposium (NYRIS),","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Becoming","Commitment","Idrætselever","Talent","Talentudvikling"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"building commitment in a sports class","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-204143","ids":["au-83078bcd-c105-4d04-aa57-9ee6e1ccf1e2"],"keyword":["Talent","aktør-netværk","becoming","commitment","idrætselever","relationel udvikling","talentudvikling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9280EA87713F05E0E4AAA2D30C6F46F5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Anthropology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","name_org":"Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-83078bcd-c105-4d04-aa57-9ee6e1ccf1e2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Building commitment in a sports class","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-204143","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The migration strategy of many capital breeders is to garner body stores along the flyway at distinct stopover sites. The rate at which they can fuel is likely to be strongly influenced by a range of factors, such as physiology, food availability, time available for foraging and perceived predation. We analysed the foraging behaviour and fuel accumulation of pink-footed geese, an Arctic capital breeder, at their mid-flyway spring stopover site and evaluated to what extent their behaviour and fuelling were related to physiological and external factors and how it differed from other stopovers along the flyway. We found that fuel accumulation rates of geese at the mid-flyway site were limited by habitat availability rather than by digestive constraints. However, as the time available for foraging increased over the stopover season, geese were able to keep constant fuelling rate. Putting this in perspective, geese increased their daily net energy intake along the flyway corresponding to the increase in time available for foraging. The net energy intake per hour of foraging remained the same. Geese showed differences in their reaction to predators/disturbance between the sites, taking higher risks particularly at the final stopover site. Hence, perceived predation along the flyway may force birds to postpone the final fuel accumulation to the last stopover along the flyway. Flexibility in behaviour appears to be an important trait to ensure fitness in this capital breeder. Our findings are based on a new, improved method for estimating fuel accumulation of animals foraging in heterogeneous landscapes based on data obtained from satellite telemetry and habitat specific intake rates.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Chudzińska, Magda Ewa","Nabe-Nielsen, Jacob","Nolet, Bart, A.","Madsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-206067"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Netherlands Institute of Ecology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foraging behaviour and fuel accumulation of capital breeders during spring migration as derived from a combination of satellite and ground based observations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84959449263","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-206067","identifier":[{"id":"84959449263","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-866fe387-d4e0-4866-8cfb-7f1bb2eeb94d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF4AC91E9B84B22E9E52FC2DFD26191E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Mammal Research 1"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"netherlands institute of ecology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Netherlands Institute of Ecology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magda Ewa","key":"chudzińskapau","last":"Chudzińska","locid":"faa4c400-68a5-4a5b-a6fd-6e0244e4bb5b","name":"Chudzińska, Magda Ewa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"96cc4583-5bb9-464a-9718-535c82041193","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-071