{"abstract":"The project focussed on validating RNA based methods as potential genomic tools in assessment of agricultural soil ecosystems. It was shown that the mRNA based technique was very sensitive and the effects was seen in the same situations as when the OECD nitrification assay showed an effect. 16S rRNA based pyrosequencing of bacterial communities in soil was shown to report different than just DNA based analysis and indicated unlike the DNA measurement that the community was developing. Finally microarray analysis was compared to traditional test for toxicity testing of Folsomia candida and showed a more sensitive response to the pesticide exposure.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Carsten Suhr","Feld, Louise","Hjelmsø, Mathis Hjort","Nielsen, Morten Schostag","Rønn, Regin","Ekelund, Flemming","Johnsen, Anders","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Krogh, Paul Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253527"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genepease genomic tools for assessment of pesticide effects on the agricultural soil ecosystem","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www2.mst.dk/Udgiv/publications/2016/06/978-87-93283-27-5.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253527","ids":["au-d9975dea-35dd-4980-ab20-931eea8c4fa7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-96189F80A8C145DD2D560EC01A3152A2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Suhr","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"133780bc-c017-4476-9545-8e1ce69c200a","name":"Jacobsen, Carsten Suhr","orcid":"0000-0003-1041-0823","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"feldpau","last":"Feld","name":"Feld, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathis Hjort","key":"hjelmsøpau","last":"Hjelmsø","name":"Hjelmsø, Mathis Hjort","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Schostag","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schostag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Regin","key":"rønnpau","last":"Rønn","name":"Rønn, Regin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"ekelundpau","last":"Ekelund","name":"Ekelund, Flemming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J G","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","name_org":"Sørensen, J G","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Paul Henning","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"afaf03ea-44d9-4c45-b081-ce7e524cad38","name":"Krogh, Paul Henning","orcid":"0000-0003-2033-553X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793283275"],"pages":"53","publisher":"Bekæmpelsesmiddelforskning fra Miljøstyrelsen","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d9975dea-35dd-4980-ab20-931eea8c4fa7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"GENEPEASE Genomic tools for assessment of pesticide effects on the agricultural soil ecosystem","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253527","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Many information-theoretic secure protocols are known for general secure multi-party computation, in the honest majority setting, and in the dishonest majority setting with preprocessing. All known protocols that are efficient in the circuit size of the evaluated function follow the same “gate-by-gate” design pattern: we work through an arithmetic (boolean) circuit on secret-shared inputs, such that after we process a gate, the output of the gate is represented as a random secret sharing among the players. This approach usually allows non-interactive processing of addition gates but requires communication for every multiplication gate. Thus, while information-theoretic secure protocols are very efficient in terms of computational work, they (seem to) require more communication and more rounds than computationally secure protocols. Whether this is inherent is an open and probably very hard problem. However, in this work we show that it is indeed inherent for protocols that follow the “gate-by-gate” design pattern. We present the following results: – In the honest majority setting, as well as for dishonest majority with preprocessing, any gate-by-gate protocol must communicate Ω(n) bits for every multiplication gate, where n is the number of players. – In the honest majority setting, we show that one cannot obtain a bound that also grows with the field size. Moreover, for a constant number of players, amortizing over several multiplication gates does not allow us to save on the computational work, and – in a restricted setting – we show that this also holds for communication. All our lower bounds are met up to a constant factor by known protocols that follow the typical gate-by-gate paradigm. Our results imply that a fundamentally new approach must be found in order to improve the communication complexity of known protocols, such as BGW, GMW, SPDZ etc.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Polychroniadou, Antigoni","Raskin, Mikhail"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255718"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-18","place":"Santa Barbara, us","start":"2016-08-14","title":"36th International Cryptology Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the communication required for unconditionally secure multiplication","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979517512","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255718","identifier":[{"id":"84979517512","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dd6a654e-5c07-4f77-9cbf-1f8b72671bd9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CA67322CA30C656908AA679FFD998DB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan Bjerre","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antigoni","key":"polychroniadoupau","last":"Polychroniadou","locid":"8d946260-2eb4-4513-bd35-bfb4087ca61d","name":"Polychroniadou, Antigoni","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikhail","key":"raskinpau","last":"Raskin","locid":"af3e30a1-11f4-4ae6-9d64-419d8af909ee","name":"Raskin, Mikhail","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-53008-5_16","eisbn":["9783662530085"],"isbn":["9783662530078"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"459-488","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advances in Cryptology - 36th Annual International Cryptology Conference, CRYPTO 2016, Proceedings","volume":"9815"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979517512"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dd6a654e-5c07-4f77-9cbf-1f8b72671bd9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"On the Communication Required for Unconditionally Secure Multiplication","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255718","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":10,"contributors":["Im, Ulas","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Ketzel, Matthias","Ellermann, Thomas","Geels, Camilla","Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","Hertel, Ole","Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","Brandt, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263094"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-25","place":"Chania, Crete, gr","start":"2016-08-25","title":"35th International Technical Meeting on Air Pollution Modelling and its Application","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"air pollutant trends over denmark over the last 000000000036 years as simulated by the integrated thor model system","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-263094","ids":["au-ea5e1633-4bab-41dd-9b64-e34497ec7fb7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-670D95290BF48F2C49546D08983DED04"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulas","key":"impau","last":"Im","locid":"e2356d82-8e7b-49c9-b660-76e719a4058e","name":"Im, Ulas","orcid":"0000-0001-5177-5306","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Heile","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5d084fe1-5909-4b7f-ac1a-907f4a30089e","name":"Christensen, Jesper Heile","orcid":"0000-0002-6741-5839","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"ellermannpau","last":"Ellermann","locid":"5e5a2168-23db-4863-b6d5-bda7dcb1f662","name":"Ellermann, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"geelspau","last":"Geels","locid":"fbcefbda-1f0a-4649-8234-28012f2714d6","name":"Geels, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2549-1750","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj Mantzius","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"85f79280-93e9-4d5f-aaec-c245958a6b24","name":"Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","locid":"6a33f2b3-9140-4f59-a55e-e68a73c9fa32","name":"Hertel, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-0972-7735","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole-Kenneth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"17ec76bb-7916-4024-867b-3aca60ca0c40","name":"Nielsen, Ole-Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0003-4350-0956","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marlene Schmidt","key":"plejdruppau","last":"Plejdrup","locid":"9dede80b-ff3e-4171-9504-bf8547fec74d","name":"Plejdrup, Marlene Schmidt","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"5f570c62-a5a5-4760-b7c7-8755b6e37ebf","name":"Brandt, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-7580-9547","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ea5e1633-4bab-41dd-9b64-e34497ec7fb7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Air pollutant trends over Denmark over the last 36 years as simulated by the integrated THOR model system","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263094","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Left ventricular (LV) lead position at the latest mechanically activated non-scarred myocardial LV region confers improved response to cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT). We conducted a double-blind, randomized controlled trial to evaluate the clinical benefit of multimodality imaging-guided LV lead placement in CRT. Methods and results: Patients were allocated (1:1) to imaging-guided LV lead placement using cardiac computed tomography (CT) venography, 99mTechnetium myocardial perfusion imaging, and speckle-tracking echocardiography radial strain to target the optimal coronary sinus (CS) branch closest to the non-scarred myocardial segment with latest mechanical activation (imaging group, n = 89) or to routine LV lead implantation in a posterolateral region with late electrical activation (control group, n = 93). The primary endpoint was clinical non-response to CRT [≥1 of the following after 6 months: (1) death, (2) heart failure hospitalization, or (3) no improvement in New York Heart Association class and <10% increase in 6-min walk distance]. Secondary outcomes included LV remodelling and the combination of all-cause mortality and hospitalization owing to heart failure during 1.8 ± 0.9 years. Analysis was intention-to-treat. In the imaging group, fewer patients reached the primary endpoint (26% vs. 42%, P = 0.02). More patients in the imaging group had the LV lead placed in the optimal CS branch (83% vs. 65%, P = 0.01). There were no between-group differences in reverse LV remodelling or the combined endpoint of death or hospitalizations for heart failure. Conclusions: Multimodality imaging-guided LV lead placement towards the CS branch closest to latest mechanically activated non-scarred myocardial LV segment reduces the proportion of clinical non-responders to CRT. Larger long-term multicentre studies are needed.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Sommer, Anders","Kronborg, Mads Brix","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","Bouchelouche, Kirsten","Böttcher, Morten","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Kristensen, Jens","Gerdes, Christian","Mortensen, Peter Thomas","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-270550"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Left ventricular lead placement","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Speckle tracking echocardiography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimodality imaging guided left ventricular lead placement in cardiac resynchronization therapy a randomized controlled trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963558385","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-270550","identifier":[{"id":"27087019","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84963558385","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f79652c8-133e-4ba0-9bed-f7441ecf5467"],"keyword":["Cardiac computed tomography","Cardiac resynchronization therapy","Left ventricular lead placement","Myocardial perfusion imaging","Speckle-tracking echocardiography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7BEFADEE2027F72912387B0261E451A9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}]