{"abstract":"Phosphorus scarcity requires improved recover and reuse of urban sources; the recycling of this nutrient from sewage sludge has become increasingly important in the last years. Using an innovative electrodialytic process, the present study shows the potential for P separation from Fe and Al precipitated sewage sludge ash using this technique, with a recovery rate of around 70%. Furthermore, heavy metals were removed from the phosphorous fraction, producing a pure and safe phosphorus source in the end.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Parés Viader, Raimon","Jensen, Pernille Erland","Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311067"],"event":{"end":"2015-09-02","place":"Ghent, be","start":"2015-08-30","title":"1st IWA Resource Recovery Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrodialytic recovery of phosphorus from chemically precipitated sewage sludge ashes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124961922/Poster_draft.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311067","ids":["dtu-15835a3f-e9a5-4eed-8169-ec2751d5fdd0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F151ACD64C6FF55B85082C55CED5E1FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/124961922/Poster_draft.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, ARTEK, Section for Arctic Engineering and Sustainable Solutions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Raimon","key":"parésviaderpau","last":"Parés Viader","locid":"d5b464c6-90ab-4f44-8f76-3d0295518738","name":"Parés Viader, Raimon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Erland","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c21f7bd4-85f5-420a-b31b-51a5c58bc254","name":"Jensen, Pernille Erland","orcid":"0000-0003-4718-1630","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lisbeth M.","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","locid":"653cfe69-d98d-42ec-b241-5409bbfc951c","name":"Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","orcid":"0000-0001-7756-382X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"ccc14efd-163a-46ec-865c-cdfd086c15fe","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-15835a3f-e9a5-4eed-8169-ec2751d5fdd0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Electrodialytic recovery of phosphorus from chemically precipitated sewage sludge ashes","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311067","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Velocity-space tomography has been used to infer 2D fast-ion velocity distribution functions. Here we compare the performance of five different tomographic inversion methods: truncated singular value decomposition, maximum entropy, minimum Fisher information and zeroth and first-order Tikhonov regularization. The inversion methods are applied to fast-ion Dα measurements taken just before and just after a sawtooth crash in the ASDEX Upgrade tokamak as well as to synthetic measurements from different test distributions. We find that the methods regularizing by penalizing steep gradients or maximizing entropy perform best. We assess the uncertainty of the calculated inversions taking into account photon noise, uncertainties in the forward model as well as uncertainties introduced by the regularization which allows us to distinguish regions of high and low confidence in the tomographies. In high confidence regions, all methods agree that ions with pitch values close to zero, as well as ions with large pitch values, are ejected from the plasma center by the sawtooth crash, and that this ejection depletes the ion population with large pitch values more strongly.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Stagner, L.","Salewski, Mirko","Geiger, B.","Heidbrink, W.W.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Thomsen, H.","Weiland, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-336451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","University of California at Irvine"],"keyword":["Fast ion D alpha spectroscopy","Fast ions","Sawtooth crash","Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inversion methods for fast ion velocity space tomography in fusion plasmas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.euro-fusionscipub.org/wp-content/uploads/eurofusion/WPMST1PR15_14314_submitted.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-336451","identifier":[{"id":"84955270050","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6ac2e511-eb0c-4ffa-85ae-9d9ecfec34b5"],"keyword":["Fast ions","Fast-ion D-alpha spectroscopy","Sawtooth crash","Tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02E00549D0EE5CDC8CE54DD43B2E0967"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.euro-fusionscipub.org/wp-content/uploads/eurofusion/WPMST1PR15_14314_submitted.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at irvine","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Irvine","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7