{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A lateral ankle sprain is the most prevalent musculoskeletal injury in sports. Exercises that aim to improve balance are a standard part of the ankle rehabilitation process. In an optimal progression model for ankle rehabilitation and prevention of future ankle sprains, it is important to characterize different balance exercises based on level of difficulty and sensori-motor training stimulus. PURPOSE: The purpose of this study was to investigate frontal-plane ankle kinematics and associated peroneal muscle activity during single-legged balance on stable surface (floor) and three commonly used balance devices (Airex®, BOSU® Ball and wobble board). DESIGN: Descriptive exploratory laboratory study. METHODS: Nineteen healthy subjects performed single-legged balance with eyes open on an Airex® mat, BOSU® Ball, wobble board, and floor (reference condition). Ankle kinematics were measured using reflective markers and 3-dimensional recordings and expressed as inversion-eversion range of motion variability, peak velocity of inversion and number of inversion-eversion direction changes. Peroneus longus EMG activity was averaged and normalized to maximal activity during maximum voluntary contraction (MVC), and in addition amplitude probability distribution function (APDF) between 90 and 10% was calculated as a measure of muscle activation variability. RESULTS: Balancing on BOSU® Ball and wobble board generally resulted in increased ankle kinematic and muscle activity variables, compared to the other surfaces. BOSU® Ball was the most challenging in terms of inversion-eversion variability while wobble board was associated with a higher number of inversion-eversion direction changes. No differences in average muscle activation level were found between these two surfaces, but the BOSU® Ball did show a more variable activation pattern in terms of APDF. CONCLUSION: The results showed large kinematic variability among different balance training devices and these differences are also reflected in muscle activation variability. The two most challenging devices were BOSU® Ball and Wobble board compared to Airex® and floor. This study can serve as guidance for clinicians who wish to implement a gradual progression of ankle rehabilitation and prevention exercises by taking the related ankle kinematics and muscle activity into account. LEVEL OF EVIDENCE: Level 3.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Strøm, Mark","Thorborg, Kristian","Bandholm, Thomas","Tang, Lars","Zebis, Mette","Nielsen, Kristian","Bencke, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-098.44-039304"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ankle joint control during single legged balance using common balance training devices implications for rehabilitation strategies","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4886807/pdf/ijspt-11-388.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.44-039304","identifier":[{"id":"27274425","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4886807","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["kp-b3076f67-e30d-4fba-ad2f-97022b179150","ku-23198904-3d51-4f45-9afd-082f6bf8a958"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-20828CCD31B6820D16EB6D6C93BAA80B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4886807/pdf/ijspt-11-388.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Metropol (ophørt), Fysioterapeutuddannelsen (ophørt)"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"strømpau","last":"Strøm","name":"Strøm, Mark","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kristian","key":"thorborgpau","last":"Thorborg","locid":"7c1f3592-61a0-469e-b376-7adea54a0fa9","name":"Thorborg, Kristian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"bandholmpau","last":"Bandholm","name":"Bandholm, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hermann","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","locid":"c7bdb48c-35ab-4b64-ac18-b6fe9812b61e","name":"Tang, Lars Hermann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"zebispau","last":"Zebis","locid":"9af38beb-ccaf-45a7-89b3-d6a28bddcede","name":"Zebis, Mette Kreutzfeldt","name_org":"Zebis, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-5301-3241","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kristian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"benckepau","last":"Bencke","name":"Bencke, Jesper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27274425"],"pub":{"issn":["15586162","21592896"],"issn_org":["21592896"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","pages":"388-99","publisher":"American Physical Therapy Association, Sports Physical Therapy Section","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-b3076f67-e30d-4fba-ad2f-97022b179150","ku-23198904-3d51-4f45-9afd-082f6bf8a958"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ANKLE JOINT CONTROL DURING SINGLE-LEGGED BALANCE USING COMMON BALANCE TRAINING DEVICES - IMPLICATIONS FOR REHABILITATION STRATEGIES","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.44-039304","year":"2016","yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate whether the use of systemic glucocorticoids is a risk factor for community-acquired Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia (CA-SAB). PATIENTS AND METHODS: We used population-based medical registries in Northern Denmark to conduct a case-control study including all adults with first-time CA-SAB and matched population controls from January 1, 2000, through December 31, 2011. Glucocorticoid users were categorized as current users (new or long-term use), former users, and nonusers. Using conditional logistic regression, we computed odds ratios (ORs) of CA-SAB according to glucocorticoid exposure, overall and by 90-day prednisolone-equivalent cumulative dose. RESULTS: We identified 2638 patients with first-time CA-SAB and 26,379 matched population controls. Current glucocorticoid users experienced considerably increased risk of CA-SAB compared with nonusers (adjusted OR=2.48; 95% CI, 2.12-2.90). The adjusted OR was 2.73 (95% CI, 2.17-3.45) in new users, 2.31 (95% CI, 1.90-2.82) in long-term users, and much lower at 1.33 (95% CI, 0.98-1.81) in former users of glucocorticoids compared with nonusers. The risk of CA-SAB increased with higher 90-day cumulative doses. Compared with nonusers of glucocorticoids, the adjusted OR was 1.32 (95% CI, 1.01-1.72) for persons with a cumulative dose of 150 mg or less, 2.42 (95% CI, 1.76-3.33) for persons whose cumulative dose was greater than 500 to 1000 mg, and 6.25 (95% CI, 4.74-8.23) for persons with a cumulative dose greater than 1000 mg. CONCLUSION: Glucocorticoid use was associated with a substantially increased risk of CA-SAB. The risk increased with higher cumulative dose, revealing a distinct dose-response relation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Smit, Jesper","Kaasch, Achim","Søgaard, Mette","Thomsen, Reimar W","Nielsen, Henrik","Frøslev, Trine","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl"],"cuid":["S02-099.00-009950"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cologne"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of glucocorticoids and risk of community acquired staphylococcus aureus bacteremia a population based case control study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84973534368","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.00-009950","identifier":[{"id":"84973534368","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27289410","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000379572200013","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-cf737faf-dd19-4c6b-99d8-7b3107e7adf2","au-97195000-aff8-4b75-b841-f7b34c7fafa6"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8F8255345CA206075A3D8AAF8A882750"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Infektionsmedicin [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cologne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"smitpau","last":"Smit","locid":"29aa2e66-1f20-4693-9114-5f988949c879","name":"Smit, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Achim J","key":"kaaschpau","last":"Kaasch","name":"Kaasch, Achim J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5550d2b5-320f-4f20-82aa-3bd98f0fe3dd","name":"Søgaard, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reimar W","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"36e7af2c-e02f-48d4-b124-0f1bd95b1748","name":"Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","name_org":"Thomsen, Reimar W","orcid":"0000-0001-9135-3474","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Ib","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","name_org":"Nielsen, Henrik Ib","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"frøslevpau","last":"Frøslev","locid":"796f4ce4-c427-483a-a529-89ba3e66e284","name":"Frøslev, Trine","orcid":"0000-0003-1594-9959","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik C","key":"schønheyderpau","last":"Schønheyder","locid":"d35b264a-6efc-467d-ac9d-e558542ef8a8","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","name_org":"Schønheyder, Henrik C","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27289410"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mayocp.2016.04.023","issn":["00256196","19425546"],"issn_org":["00256196"],"issue":"7","journal":"Mayo Clinic Proceedings","pages":"873-80","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Mayo Clinic Proceedings","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84973534368"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cf737faf-dd19-4c6b-99d8-7b3107e7adf2","au-97195000-aff8-4b75-b841-f7b34c7fafa6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Use of Glucocorticoids and Risk of Community-Acquired Staphylococcus aureus Bacteremia : A Population-Based Case-Control Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.00-009950","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Stenosis of the aortic valve gives rise to more complex blood flows with increased velocities. The angleindependent vector flow ultrasound technique transverse oscillation was employed intra-operatively on the ascending aorta of (I) 20 patients with a healthy aortic valve and 20 patients with aortic stenosis before (IIa) and after (IIb) valve replacement. The results indicate that aortic stenosis increased flow complexity (p , 0.0001), induced systolic backflow (p , 0.003) and reduced systolic jet width (p , 0.0001). After valve replacement, the systolic backflow and jet width were normalized (p , 0.52 and p , 0.22), but flow complexity was not (p , 0.0001). Flow complexity (p , 0.0001), systolic jet width (p , 0.0001) and systolic backflow (p , 0.001) were associated with peak systolic velocity. The study found that aortic stenosis changes blood flow in the ascending aorta and valve replacement corrects some of these changes. Transverse oscillation may be useful for assessment of aortic stenosis and optimization of valve surgery. (E-mail: lindskov@gmail.com) 2016 World Federation for Ultrasound in Medicine & Biology","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Jensen, Maiken Brit","Lund, Jens Teglgaard","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Lange, Theis","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann"],"cuid":["S02-099.18-033232"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aortic Valve Stenosis","Flow complexity","Intraoperative ultrasound","Journal Article","Secondary flow","Systolic backflow","Transverse oscillation","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intra operative vector flow imaging using ultrasound of the ascending aorta among 000000000040 patients with normal stenotic and replaced aortic valves","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979680252","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.18-033232","identifier":[{"id":"84979680252","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27471116","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1db67788-5835-4023-879a-0ad0424858cd","ku-81a84421-6f59-42f1-9e6a-01a23dbb64d5"],"keyword":["Aortic valve stenosis","Flow complexity","Intraoperative ultrasound","Journal Article","Secondary flow","Systolic backflow","Transverse oscillation","Vector flow imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7A51B34C20E11F8E7624CCA5135AC79F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kristoffer Lindskov","key":"hansenkristofferlindskovpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hasse","key":"møllersørensenhassepau","last":"Møller-Sørensen","name":"Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardjesperpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maiken Brit","key":"jensenmaikenbritpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Maiken Brit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Teglgaard","key":"lundjensteglgaardpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Jens Teglgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads Møller","key":"pedersenmadsmøllerpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Mads Møller","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Theis","key":"langetheispau","last":"Lange","locid":"e4664578-01fc-4a93-8efd-1dbffb72cdd6","name":"Lange, Theis","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-8347","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenjørgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenmichaelbachmannpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27471116"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ultrasmedbio.2016.06.009","issn":["03015629","1879291X"],"issn_org":["03015629"],"issue":"10","journal":"Ultrasound in Medicine & Biology","pages":"2414-2422","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ultrasound in Medicine & Biology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979680252"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1db67788-5835-4023-879a-0ad0424858cd","ku-81a84421-6f59-42f1-9e6a-01a23dbb64d5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intra-Operative Vector Flow Imaging Using Ultrasound of the Ascending Aorta among 40 Patients with Normal, Stenotic and Replaced Aortic Valves","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.18-033232","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In Denmark, both influenza A(H1N1)pdm09 and influenza B co-circulated in the 2015/16 season. We estimated the vaccine effectiveness (VE) of the trivalent influenza vaccine in patients 65 years and older using the test-negative case-control design. The adjusted VE against influenza A(H1N1)pdm09 was 35.0% (95% confidence interval (CI): 11.1-52.4) and against influenza B 4.1% (95% CI: -22.0 to 24.7). The majority of influenza A(H1N1)pdm09 circulating in 2015/16 belonged to the new genetic subgroup subclade 6B.1.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Emborg, H.","Krause, T. G.","Nielsen, L.","Thomsen, M. K.","Christiansen, C. B.","Skov, M. N.","Nielsen, X. C.","Sandborg Weinreich, Lenette","Fischer, T. K.","Rønn, J.","Trebbien, R."],"cuid":["S03-092.57-004950"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influenza vaccine effectiveness in adults 000000000065 years and older denmark 000000002015 000000000016 a rapid epidemiological and virological assessment","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2016.21.14.30189","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-092.57-004950","identifier":[{"id":"84963612106","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27101732","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000373738500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-66