{"abstract":"From 4 to 7 April 2016, 24 researchers from 8 countries and from a variety of academic disciplines gathered in Snekkersten, Denmark, to reach evidence-based consensus about physical activity in children and youth, that is, individuals between 6 and 18 years. Physical activity is an overarching term that consists of many structured and unstructured forms within school and out-of-school-time contexts, including organised sport, physical education, outdoor recreation, motor skill development programmes, recess, and active transportation such as biking and walking. This consensus statement presents the accord on the effects of physical activity on children's and youth's fitness, health, cognitive functioning, engagement, motivation, psychological well-being and social inclusion, as well as presenting educational and physical activity implementation strategies. The consensus was obtained through an iterative process that began with presentation of the state-of-the art in each domain followed by plenary and group discussions. Ultimately, Consensus Conference participants reached agreement on the 21-item consensus statement.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Bangsbo, Jens","Krustrup, Peter","Duda, Joan","Hillman, Charles","Andersen, Lars Bo","Weiss, Maureen","Williams, Craig A.","Lintunen, Taru","Green, Ken","Hansen, Peter Riis","Naylor, Patti Jean","Ericsson, Ingegerd","Nielsen, Glen","Froberg, Karsten","Bugge, Anna","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Schipperijn, Jasper","Dagkas, Symeon","Agergaard, Sine","von Seelen, Jesper","Østergaard, Charlotte","Skovgaard, Thomas","Busch, Henrik","Elbe, Anne Marie"],"cuid":["S05-093.32-025110"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-07","place":"Snekkersten, dk","start":"2016-04-04","title":"The Copenhagen Consensus Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Krustrup, Peter"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Finland","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Kinesiology and Community Health, University of Illinois, Urbana, Illinois, USA.","Faculty of Sport and Health Sciences, University of Jyväskylä, Jyväskylä, Finland.","Health Sport and Biosciences, London","Health Sport and Biosciences, London, UK.","Malmo University","Malmö University","Sogn og Fjordane University College","University of Birmingham","University of British Columbia","University of Chester","University of Chester, Chester, UK.","University of East London","University of Exeter","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Jyväskylä","University of Minnesota","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of Victoria","University of Victoria BC","Victoria University","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Children","Cognition physiology","Congresses as Topic","Consensus","Denmark","Exercise","Health","Health promotion","Humans","Interpersonal Relations","Leisure Activities","Mental health","Physical activity","Schools","Well being"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCS"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the copenhagen consensus conference 000000002016 children youth and physical activity in schools and during leisure time","src":["au","ku","sdu","ucsyd"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bjsports-2016-096325","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S05-093.32-025110","identifier":[{"id":"27354718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5036221","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84994634533","type":"scopus"},{"id":"84979080398","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-aaa0f2d0-94f6-4c30-aa01-659a147acf03","ku-cdf33c09-a96e-4203-b41f-31f2fc66248a","sdu-21948a66-0575-40f1-a4f8-c03adfbb9dc7","sdu-873fc472-0ab1-4962-ad16-7fde3acb9f9c","ucsyd-911f1851-b7b4-4f07-b336-5004ce1ab494"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Children","Cognition/physiology","Congresses as Topic","Consensus","Denmark","Exercise","Health","Health Promotion","Humans","Interpersonal Relations","Leisure Activities","Mental Health","Physical activity","Schools","Well-being"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-8-712B1650BEE7745FA6CCE4ACC83B4FBC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5036221/pdf/bjsports-2016-096325.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/165741701/Bangsbo_et_al_British_Journal_of_Sports_Medicine_2016_Vol_50_19_1177_1178.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bjsports-2016-096325","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.teamsport-health.ku.dk/hb_statements/14831_KU_Haefte_UK-versionering-Print.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Center for Ho