irst":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenjespermøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenhenrikkjærulfpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Grethe","key":"andersengrethepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"97e157c9-4cb4-4690-a971-06e4699b50fe","name":"Andersen, Grethe","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-2500","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskjenserikpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27969609"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacc.2016.09.047","issn":["07351097","15583597"],"issn_org":["07351097"],"issue":"18S","journal":"Journal of the American College of Cardiology","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American College of Cardiology","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-843f5a82-08e2-4585-98e8-4d66f40c2427"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"TCT-27 Transcatheter Left Atrial Appendage Occlusion Using Aspirin Alone for Post-implant Antithrombotic Therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-204838","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Primary objective Utilizing the detailed vascular network obtained from micro-computed tomography (μCT) to establish a mathematical model of the temporal molecular distribution within a murine C3H mammary carcinoma. Procedures Female CDF1 mice with a C3H mammary carcinoma on the right rear foot were used in this study. Dynamic information for each tumour was achieved by Dynamic Contrast Enhanced-Magnetic Resonance Imaging (DCE-MRI) on a 16.4 T system. Detailed morphologic information on the tumour vasculature was obtained by ex vivo μCT and compared to CD34 immunohistochemical staining of tissue sections. The reconstructed vascular network served as origin for the diffusion (described by the apparent diffusion coefficient) within the tumour (the restricted volume described by the interstitial volume fraction derived from DCE-MRI). The resulting partial differential equation was solved using Finite-Element and a combined mathematical graph describing molecular distribution within the tumour was obtained. Results The established molecular distribution model predicted a heterogeneous distribution throughout the tumour related to the layout of the vascular network. Central tumour section concentration-time curves estimated from the established molecular distribution model were compared with physical measurements obtained by DCE-MRI of the same tumours and showed excellent correlation. Conclusions A mathematical model describing temporal molecular distribution based on detailed vascular network structures was established and compared to DCE-MRI. The improved morphological insight will enhance future studies of heterogeneous tumours.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wittenborn, Thomas R.","Nielsen, Thomas","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Horsman, Michael R","Nygaard, Jens Vinge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-219411"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Finite element modeling","Magnetic resonance imaging MRI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulation of heterogeneous molecular delivery in tumours using μct reconstructions and mri validation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84983543815","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-219411","identifier":[{"id":"84983543815","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27569845","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9e277953-7976-49ac-94a2-cc4ae50a5182"],"keyword":["Animal models and imaging","Finite element modeling","Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)","X-ray imaging and computed tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65DCDCDF0192355BD8B4F8B53AE20B0C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Experimental Clinical Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Rea","key":"wittenbornpau","last":"Wittenborn","locid":"563cd85d-66a7-410d-a66b-fee9daa9fccf","name":"Wittenborn, Thomas R.","name_org":"Wittenborn, Thomas Rea","orcid":"0000-0002-6361-542X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a892a177-3001-4c39-959d-ddfdd25a4f11","name":"Nielsen, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country"