{"abstract":"Unravelling of disulfide linkage patterns is a crucial part of protein characterization, whether it is for a previously uncharacterized protein in basic research or a recombinant pharmaceutical protein. In the biopharmaceutical industry, elucidation of the cysteine connectivities is a necessity to avoid disulfide scrambled and incorrectly folded forms in the final product. Mass spectrometry (MS) is a highly utilized analytical tool for this due to fast and accurate characterization. However, disulfide bonds being an additional covalent bond in the protein structure represent a challenge in protein sequencing by tandem MS (MS/MS). Electrochemical (EC) reduction of disulfide bonds has recently been demonstrated to provide efficient reduction efficiencies, significantly enhancing sequence coverages in online coupling with MS characterization. In this study, the potential use of EC disulfide reduction in combination with MS characterization for disulfide mapping was assessed. We employed two approaches based on (1) the high flexibility and instant information about the degree of reduction in infusion EC-MS to generate partially reduced species on the intact protein level and (2) the preserved link between parent disulfide-linked fragments and free reduced peptides in an LC-EC-MS platform of nonreduced proteolytic protein digestions. Here we report the successful use of EC as a partial reduction approach in mapping of disulfide bonds of intact human insulin (HI) and lysozyme. In addition, we established a LC-EC-MS platform advantageous in disulfide characterization of complex and highly disulfide-bonded proteins such as human serum albumin (HSA) by online EC reduction of nonreduced proteolytic digestions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cramer, Christian N","Haselmann, Kim F","Olsen, Jesper V.","Nielsen, Peter Kresten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393854"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disulfide linkage characterization of disulfide bond containing proteins and peptides by reducing electrochemistry and mass spectrometry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-393854","identifier":[{"id":"84957584750","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26695097","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-00a76b96-d64b-48ad-a85d-7ccc9f9fbbe5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24AFE1BA733C54B58C1627916381D9F7"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, CPR publication list","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian N","key":"cramerpau","last":"Cramer","name":"Cramer, Christian N","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kim F","key":"haselmannpau","last":"Haselmann","name":"Haselmann, Kim F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper V","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"16f5cd56-244f-4fe8-bebd-13ee7bd17822","name":"Olsen, Jesper V.","name_org":"Olsen, Jesper V","orcid":"0000-0002-4747-4938","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Kresten","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Peter Kresten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26695097"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.5b03148","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"3","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"1585-1592","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"88"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957584750"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-00a76b96-d64b-48ad-a85d-7ccc9f9fbbe5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Disulfide Linkage Characterization of Disulfide Bond-Containing Proteins and Peptides by Reducing Electrochemistry and Mass Spectrometry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-393854","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The origin of carbapenem-hydrolyzing metallo-β-lactamases (MBLs) acquired by clinical bacteria is largely unknown. We investigated the frequency, host range, diversity, and functionality of MBLs in the soil microbiota. Twenty-five soil samples of different types and geographical origins were analyzed by antimicrobial selective culture, followed by phenotypic testing and expression of MBL-encoding genes in Escherichia coli, and whole-genome sequencing of MBL-producing strains was performed. Carbapenemase activity was detected in 29 bacterial isolates from 13 soil samples, leading to identification of seven new MBLs in presumptive Pedobacter roseus (PEDO-1), Pedobacter borealis (PEDO-2), Pedobacter kyungheensis (PEDO-3), Chryseobacterium piscium (CPS-1), Epilithonimonas tenax (ESP-1), Massilia oculi (MSI-1), and Sphingomonas sp. (SPG-1). Carbapenemase production was likely an intrinsic feature in Chryseobacterium and Epilithonimonas, as it occurred in reference strains of different species within these genera. The amino acid identity to MBLs described in clinical bacteria ranged between 40 and 69%. Remarkable features of the new MBLs included prophage integration of the encoding gene (PEDO-1), an unusual amino acid residue at a key position for MBL structure and catalysis (CPS-1), and overlap with a putative OXA β-lactamase (MSI-1). Heterologous expression of PEDO-1, CPS-1, and ESP-1in E. coli significantly increased the MICs of ampicillin, ceftazidime, cefpodoxime, cefoxitin, and meropenem. Our study shows that MBL producers are widespread in soil and include four genera that were previously not known to produce MBLs. The MBLs produced by these bacteria are distantly related to MBLs identified in clinical samples but constitute resistance determinants of clinical relevance if acquired by pathogenic bacteria.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gudeta, Dereje Dadi","Bortolaia, Valeria","Amos, Greg","Wellington, Elizabeth M H","Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","Poirel, Laurent","Nielsen, Jesper Boye","Westh, Henrik","Guardabassi, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394116"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the soil microbiota harbors a diversity of carbapenem hydrolyzing β lactamases of potential clinical relevance","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aac.asm.org/content/60/4/2599","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394116","identifier":[{"id":"26482314","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4704184","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84957886265","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0113f4c4-6eda-46e6-98a1-57fca35e5a3f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A43EE74E1BC171AA5CF564B2173A5A1D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Dereje Dadi","key":"gudetapau","last":"Gudeta","locid":"fb648089-42ba-4bea-aa75-c5dd949a32af","name":"Gudeta, Dereje Dadi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Valeria","key":"bortolaiapau","last":"Bortolaia","locid":"204ced4c-fd1a-43eb-abde-7beb937d1cdf","name":"Bortolaia, Valeria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Greg","key":"amospau","last":"Amos","name":"Amos, Greg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elizabeth M H","key":"wellingtonpau","last":"Wellington","name":"Wellington, Elizabeth M H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Koefoed","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"c196f0ea-2378-4bc3-bf49-2e64410cbabf","name":"Brandt, Kristian Koefoed","orcid":"0000-0001-7886-9708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laurent","key":"poirelpau","last":"Poirel","name":"Poirel, Laurent","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Boye","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"be47b1a6-e531-464c-b0c8-3a2e54d7fa93","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Boye","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luca","key":"guardabassipau","last":"Guardabassi","locid":"a5c1a52b-b35b-4d24-864d-c513c79a1dd0","name":"Guardabassi, Luca","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26482314"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/aac.01424-15","issn":["00664804","10706283"],"issn_org":["00664804"],"issue":"1","journal":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","pages":"151-160","status":"p","title":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957886265"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0113f4c4-6eda-46e6-98a1-57fca35e5a3f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The soil microbiota harbors a diversity of carbapenem-hydrolyzing β-lactamases of potential clinical relevance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394116","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A method for quantification of a pharmaceutical peptide in human plasma was developed using gradient elution LC-ICP-MS. A membrane desolvation (MD) system was applied to remove organic solvents from the eluent prior to the detection as SO+ in the dynamic reaction cell (DRC) of the ICP-DRC-MS instrument and subsequent quantification by post-column isotope dilution (IDA). Plasma proteins were precipitated prior to analysis. Analytical figures of merit including linearity, precision, LOD, LOQ and accuracy were considered satisfactory for analysis of plasma samples. The selectivity of the developed method was demonstrated for five pharmaceutically relevant peptides: desmopressin, penetratin, substance P, PTH (1-34) and insulin. Preliminary experiments on an ICP-MS/MS system using oxygen to reduce the effect of organic solvents were also performed to compare sensitivity. The results of the study demonstrated that LC-ICP-MS post-column IDA may constitute a valuable additional tool in quantification of non-labelled peptides in the early drug development offering absolute quantification without need of species specific standards.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Møller, Laura Hyrup","Macherius, André","Hansen, Thomas Hesselhøj","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","Cornett, Claus","Østergaard, Jesper","Stürup, Stefan","Gammelgaard, Bente"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425719"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantification of pharmaceutical peptides in human plasma by lc icp ms sulfur detection","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/C6JA00132G","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-425719","identifier":[{"id":"84984706979","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-364a8cab-7781-4f48-9eb9-f875ce7d9f2e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0DF4C04A6D57561909CE01ECC7659B1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/165309387/JAAS_sulfur_detection.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/C6JA00132G","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Analytical Biosciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Laura Hyrup","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"68d4b77a-c0d9-4a6b-b42a-3bd23b231890","name":"Møller, Laura Hyrup","orcid":"0000-0002-7987-344X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"André","key":"macheriuspau","last":"Macherius","locid":"8b218ff4-9be6-4e26-a4ac-a9ed7a7c17f9","name":"Macherius, André","orcid":"0000-0003-1229-511X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Hesselhøj","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"f3995053-12c0-4056-8eef-800cb8fb104e","name":"Hansen, Thomas Hesselhøj","orcid":"0000-0003-3511-2806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Hanne Mørck","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b0450b3-f634-47ec-912c-b07ecd943be8","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","orcid":"0000-0002-7285-9100","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"cornettpau","last":"Cornett","locid":"c65adbed-6ecf-48d1-940c-2514741cb798","name":"Cornett, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-6991-5362","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefan","key":"stüruppau","last":"Stürup","locid":"b45dc4f0-7473-4e3a-be67-4d129a710e3c","name":"Stürup, Stefan","orcid":"0000-0002-6856-9207","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"gammelgaardpau","last":"Gammelgaard","locid":"4ba048dd-88f5-4a5f-8556-10c9a5bd45d3","name":"Gammelgaard, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-1014","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c6ja00132g","issn":["02679477","13645544"],"issn_org":["02679477"],"journal":"Journal of Analytical Atomic Spectrometry","pages":"1877-1884","status":"p","title":"Journal of Analytical Atomic Spectrometry","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84984706979"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-364a8cab-7781-4f48-9eb9-f875ce7d9f2e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantification of pharmaceutical peptides in human plasma by LC-ICP-MS sulfur detection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425719","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
