{"abstract":"Ouzo is a symbol of modern Greek identity. But where does the word \"ouzo\" actually come from? Is it originally Greek or borrowed from Italian or Turkish? And what do the various explanations of the word's origin tell us about the Greeks' self-image?","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lucas, Sandra"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-441208"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvor kommer ouzo fra et studie i national identitet","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://e-pages.dk/ku/1205/2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-441208","ids":["ku-4ffe01ac-963c-474a-aa0b-0fb34d61c855"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C1CB58FFB7DF9B44212E4D2F98709C53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://e-pages.dk/ku/1205/2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sandra","key":"lucaspau","last":"Lucas","locid":"39c21214-f907-4fd0-812f-9447f22f7339","name":"Lucas, Sandra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ditte Maria","key":"søgaardpedh","last":"Søgaard","name":"Søgaard, Ditte Maria","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788789221250"],"issn":["19042957"],"issue":"6","pages":"67-75","place":"København","publisher":"Institut for Tværkulturelle og Regionale Studier, Københavns Universitet","series":"Tværkultur","status":"p","subtitle":"Årbog for ToRS 2015","title":"Alkohol"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4ffe01ac-963c-474a-aa0b-0fb34d61c855"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hvor kommer 'ouzo' fra? : et studie i national identitet","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-441208","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"P-type ATPases catalyze the active transport of cations and phospholipids across biological membranes. Members of this large family are involved in a range of fundamental cellular processes. To date, a substantial number of P-type ATPase inhibitors have been characterized, some of which are used as drugs. In this work a library of natural compounds was screened and we first identified curcuminoids as plasma membrane H+-ATPases inhibitors in plant and fungal cells. We also found that some of the commercial curcumins contain several curcuminoids. Three of these were purified and, among the curcuminoids, demethoxycurcumin was the most potent inhibitor of all tested P-type ATPases from fungal (Pma1p; H+-ATPase), plant (AHA2; H+-ATPase) and animal (SERCA; Ca2+-ATPase) cells. All three curcuminoids acted as non-competitive antagonist to ATP and hence may bind to a highly conserved allosteric site of these pumps. Future research on biological effects of commercial preparations of curcumin should consider the heterogeneity of the material.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Dao, Trong Tuan","Sehgal, Pankaj","Thanh Tung, Truong","Møller, Jesper Vuust","Nielsen, John","Palmgren, Michael","Christensen, Søren Brøgger","Fuglsang, Anja Thoe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"demethoxycurcumin is a potent inhibitor of p type atpases from diverse kingdoms of life","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0163260","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-443528","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5028038","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84992387981","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27644036","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-53e1e7e3-ac20-4dbe-879e-b52a5ebb523a"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D8CF9E6BF04C60D79B5823A8031185D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/166196702/journal.pone.0163260.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0163260","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Natural Products and Peptides"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Trong Tuan","key":"daopau","last":"Dao","locid":"946dc8e5-696a-4df8-9b40-62bca4ace781","name":"Dao, Trong Tuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pankaj","key":"sehgalpau","last":"Sehgal","name":"Sehgal, Pankaj","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Truong","key":"thanhtungpau","last":"Thanh Tung","locid":"61a6697c-016d-4fc9-9303-f58fd43b5478","name":"Thanh Tung, Truong","orcid":"0000-0002-5263-203X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Vuust","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jesper Vuust","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"John","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b927452e-5c62-49fb-93f6-76877c08e407","name":"Nielsen, John","orcid":"0000-0002-2854-8188","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Broberg","key":"palmgrenpau","last":"Palmgren","locid":"28d7c382-c542-4a79-83e5-b479c3fe763e","name":"Palmgren, Michael","name_org":"Palmgren, Michael Broberg","orcid":"0000-0002-9982-6114","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Brøgger","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7fa2901b-af37-44dc-bc6d-c1a674738eb7","name":"Christensen, Søren Brøgger","orcid":"0000-0002-5773-6874","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja Thoe","key":"fuglsangpau","last":"Fuglsang","locid":"3445d1a8-92a8-46ee-b57a-c373263a4d60","name":"Fuglsang, Anja Thoe","orcid":"0000-0003-1153-8394","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27644036"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0163260","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"9","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0163260","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84992387981"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-53e1e7e3-ac20-4dbe-879e-b52a5ebb523a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Demethoxycurcumin is a potent inhibitor of P-type ATPases from diverse kingdoms of life","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443528","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
