{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To investigate the impact of common anesthetic techniques on postoperative opioid consumption in ankle fracture surgery. MATERIALS AND METHODS: We performed a retrospective cohort study on 622 patients with isolated ankle fractures undergoing primary reconstructive surgery. Patients were identified by consecutive screening in the years 2008 to 2011. Our primary endpoint was the difference in the 24-hour postoperative opioid consumption after general anesthesia (GA) compared with different regional anesthesia modalities. Secondary endpoints were length of stay in the postanesthesia care unit, risk of postoperative nausea and vomiting, and postoperative length of hospital stay. RESULTS: Opioid consumption in 4 anesthesia groups (equipotent doses of IV morphine) was as follows: GA: 21.9 mg (95% confidence interval [CI]±1.2), GA+peripheral nerve block (PNB): 16.3 mg (95% CI±1.1), spinal anesthesia (SA): 17.1 mg (95% CI±0.9), and SA+PNB: 14.6 mg (95% CI±1.0). We found significant differences between \"GA\" and all other groups (P≤0.01). The most pronounced difference is seen when GA is compared with SA+PNB, with a 33.4% opioid reduction in the latter group. DISCUSSION: Regional anesthesia modalities reduce postoperative opioid consumption in ankle fracture surgery in comparison with GA. A benefit of PNBs is possibly due to an improved pain profile. Our study is retrospective and cannot predict the exact magnitude of this benefit.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christensen, Kristian P","Møller, Ann Merete","Nielsen, Jesper K.","Klausen, Tobias W","Sort, Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-445032"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of anesthetic technique on postoperative opioid consumption in ankle fracture surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-445032","identifier":[{"id":"84949437060","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26633690","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-565e1e01-6272-4a4e-a653-f5a6db4bff1c"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E570831BC817305674B236CF7174D906"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kristian P","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Kristian P","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ann M.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"75bf0134-ea9c-4496-908d-56c8e51aed96","name":"Møller, Ann Merete","name_org":"Møller, Ann M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias W","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","name":"Klausen, Tobias W","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rune","key":"sortpau","last":"Sort","name":"Sort, Rune","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26633690"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ajp.0000000000000335","issn":["07498047","15365409"],"issn_org":["07498047"],"issue":"10","journal":"The Clinical Journal of Pain","pages":"870-874","status":"p","title":"The Clinical Journal of Pain","title_org":"Clinical Journal of Pain","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949437060"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-565e1e01-6272-4a4e-a653-f5a6db4bff1c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Effects of Anesthetic Technique on Postoperative Opioid Consumption in Ankle Fracture Surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-445032","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Atrial fibrillation has been associated with increased mortality in the general population and mixed populations of critical ill. Atrial fibrillation can also affect patients during post-cardiac arrest care. We sought to assess the prognostic implications of atrial fibrillation following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, including relation to the level of targeted temperature management. Design: A post hoc analysis of a prospective randomized trial. Setting: Thirty-six ICUs. Patients: We included 897 (96%) of the 939 comatose out-of-hospital cardiac arrest survivors from the targeted temperature management trial (year, 2010-2013) with data on heart rhythm on day 2. Interventions: Targeted temperature management at 33°C or 36°C. Measurements and Main Results: Endpoints included cumulative proportion of atrial fibrillation following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest and 180-day all-cause mortality and specific death causes stratified by atrial fibrillation. Atrial fibrillation on day 2 was used as primary endpoint analyses to exclude effects of short-term atrial fibrillation related to resuscitation and initial management. The cumulative proportions of atrial fibrillation were 15% and 11% on days 1 and 2, respectively. Forty-three percent of patients with initial atrial fibrillation the first day were reported with sinus rhythm on day 2. No difference was found between the groups treated with targeted temperature management at 33°C and 36°C. Patients affected by atrial fibrillation had significantly higher 180-day mortality (atrial fibrillation: 66% vs no-atrial fibrillation: 43%; plogrank < 0.0001 and unadjusted hazard ratio, 1.75 [1.35-2.30]; p < 0.0001). The association between atrial fibrillation and higher mortality remained significant (adjusted hazard ratio, 1.34 [1.01-1.79]; p < 0.05) adjusted for potential confounders. Atrial fibrillation was independently associated with increased risk of cardiovascular death and multiple-organ failure (adjusted hazard ratio, 2.07 [1.39-3.09]; p < 0.001), whereas no association with higher risk of death from cerebral causes was found. Conclusions: Atrial fibrillation was independently associated with higher mortality, primarily driven by cardiovascular causes and multiple-organ failure, and may thus identify a vulnerable subpopulation. Whether treatment to prevent atrial fibrillation is associated with an improved prognosis remains to be established.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Hassager, Christian","Erlinge, David","Nielsen, Niklas","Horn, Janneke","Hovdenes, Jan","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Wanscher, Michael","Pehrson, Steen","Køber, Lars","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458268"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Comatose","Mortality","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Therapeutic hypothermia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atrial fibrillation following out of hospital cardiac arrest and targeted temperature management are we giving it the attention it deserves","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-458268","identifier":[{"id":"84995575849","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27513534","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6c8adac0-b0e3-4ba9-a398-ee3a22679809"],"keyword":["atrial fibrillation","cardiopulmonary resuscitation","comatose","mortality","out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","therapeutic hypothermia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0915E79F9E20A7C79DE921CF67D55E5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Hartvig","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen","key":"pehrsonpau","last":"Pehrson","locid":"081e7ed3-5467-4c96-9471-1519871354db","name":"Pehrson, Steen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27513534"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ccm.0000000000001958","issn":["00903493","10637389"],"issn_org":["00903493"],"issue":"12","journal":"Critical Care Medicine","pages":"2215-2222","status":"p","title":"Critical Care Medicine","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995575849"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6c8adac0-b0e3-4ba9-a398-ee3a22679809"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Atrial Fibrillation Following Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest and Targeted Temperature Management - Are We Giving It the Attention it Deserves?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458268","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Left atrial volume (LAV) estimation with 3D echocardiography has been shown to be more accurate than 2D volume calculation. However, little is known about the possible effect of respiratory movements on the accuracy of the measurement. METHODS: 100 consecutive patients admitted with chest pain were examined with 3D echocardiography and LAV was quantified during inspiratory breath hold, expiratory breath hold and during free breathing. RESULTS: Of the 100 patients, only 65 had an echocardiographic window that allowed for 3D echocardiography in the entire respiratory cycle. Mean atrial end diastolic volume was 45.4 ± 14.5 during inspiratory breath hold, 46.4 ± 14.8 during expiratory breath hold and 45.6 ± 14.3 during free respiration. Mean end systolic volume was 17.6 ± 7.8 during inspiratory breath hold, 18.8 ± 8.0 during expiratory breath hold and 18.3 ± 8.0 during free respiration. No significant differences were seen in any of the measured parameters. CONCLUSIONS: The present study adds to the feasibility of 3D LAV quantitation. LAV estimation by 3D echocardiography may be performed during either end-expiratory or end-inspiratory breath-hold without any significant difference in the calculated volume. Also, the LAV estimation may be performed during free breathing.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sørgaard, Mathias","Linde, Jesper J","Ismail, Hafsa","Risum, Niels","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Kühl, Jørgen T","Tittle, Benjamin","Nielsen, Walter B","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470176"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Artifacts","Echocardiography Three Dimensional","Female","Heart Atria","Humans","Image Enhancement","Image Interpretation Computer Assisted","Imaging Three Dimensional","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Motion","Organ Size","Reproducibility of Results","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Respiratory Mechanics","Sensitivity and Specificity","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"respiratory influence on left atrial volume calculation with 000000000003d echocardiography","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12947-016-0054-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-470176","identifier":[{"id":"84960494207","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26970904","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4789267","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8027de53-10a2-4ae3-8f55-97b6f4cc9dd3"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Artifacts","Echocardiography, Three-Dimensional","Female","Heart Atria","Humans","Image Enhancement","Image Interpretation, Computer-Assisted","Imaging, Three-Dimensional","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Motion","Organ Size","Reproducibility of Results","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Respiratory Mechanics","Sensitivity and Specificity","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22C260354FDC507491C2141C267A9CF5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12947-016-0054-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/177190102/art_3A10.1186_2Fs12947_016_0054_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"sørgaardpau","last":"Sørgaard","name":"Sørgaard, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper J","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Jesper J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hafsa","key":"ismailpau","last":"Ismail","name":"Ismail, Hafsa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"risumpau","last":"Risum","name":"Risum, Niels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus F","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","name_org":"Kofoed, Klaus F","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen T","key":"kühlpau","last":"Kühl","name":"Kühl, Jørgen T","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Benjamin","key":"tittlepau","last":"Tittle","name":"Tittle, Benjamin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Walter B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Walter B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","name_org":"Hove, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26970904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12947-016-0054-7","issn":["14767120"],"journal":"Cardiovascular Ultrasound","paperid":"11","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Ultrasound","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960494207"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8027de53-10a2-4ae3-8f55-97b6f4cc9dd3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Respiratory influence on left atrial volume calculation with 3D-echocardiography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-470176","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Well-collected and well-documented sample repositories are necessary for disease biomarker development. The availability of significant numbers of samples with the associated patient information enables biomarker validation to proceed with maximum efficacy and minimum bias. The creation and utilization of such a resource is an important step in the development of blood-based biomarker tests for colorectal cancer.Methods: We have created a subject data and biological sample resource, Endoscopy II, which is based on 4698 individuals referred for diagnostic colonoscopy in Denmark between May 2010 and November 2012. Of the patients referred based on 1 or more clinical symptoms of colorectal neoplasia, 512 were confirmed by pathology to have colorectal cancer and 399 were confirmed to have advanced adenoma. Using subsets of these sample groups in case-control study designs (300 patients for colorectal cancer, 302 patients for advanced adenoma), 2 panels of plasma-based proteins for colorectal cancer and 1 panel for advanced adenoma were identified and validated based on ELISA data obtained for 28 proteins from the samples.Results: One of the validated colorectal cancer panels was comprised of 8 proteins (CATD, CEA, CO3, CO9, SEPR, AACT, MIF, and PSGL) and had a validation ROC curve area under the curve (AUC) of 0.82 (CI 0.75textendash0.88). There was no significant difference in the performance between early- and late-stage cancer. The advanced adenoma panel was comprised of 4 proteins (CATD, CLUS, GDF15, SAA1) and had a validation ROC curve AUC of 0.65 (CI 0.56textendash0.74).Conclusions: These results suggest that the development of blood-based aids to colorectal cancer detection and diagnosis is feasible.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Blume, John E.","Wilhelmsen, Michael","Benz, Ryan W.","Brünner, Nils","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Croner, Lisa J.","Dillon, Roslyn","Hillig, Thore","Jones, Jeffrey J.","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Kao, Athit","Klaerke, Michael","Laurberg, Søren","Madsen, Mogens R.","Nielsen, Knud T.","Vilandt, Jesper","Wilcox, Bruce E.","You, Jia","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479946"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovery and validation of plasma protein biomarker panels for the detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenoma in a danish collection of samples from patients referred for diagnostic colonoscopy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jalm.aaccjnls.org/content/early/2016/08/12/jalm.2016.020271","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-479946","identifier":[{"id":"85025596175","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-90c97884-a450-493c-96f4-7b19aeda65d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5CB0B742373453390EB608A6C6CCBF6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jalm.aaccjnls.org/content/early/2016/08/12/jalm.2016.020271","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Molecular Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"John E.","key":"blumejohnepau","last":"Blume","name":"Blume, John E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wilhelmsenmichaelpau","last":"Wilhelmsen","name":"Wilhelmsen, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ryan W.","key":"benzryanwpau","last":"Benz","name":"Benz, Ryan W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils","key":"brünnernilspau","last":"Brünner","locid":"0e935a59-f9ff-4d0d-8c60-8a74a558e6aa","name":"Brünner, Nils","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenibjarlepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b8f0594e-4a73-4cf7-9117-a9eb69323873","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisa J.","key":"cronerlisajpau","last":"Croner","name":"Croner, Lisa J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Roslyn","key":"dillonroslynpau","last":"Dillon","name":"Dillon, Roslyn","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thore","key":"hilligthorepau","last":"Hillig","name":"Hillig, Thore","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeffrey J.","key":"jonesjeffreyjpau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Jeffrey J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Nannestad","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ae2a79a1-5374-4e92-84c9-3af55ef5712e","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Athit","key":"kaoathitpau","last":"Kao","name":"Kao, Athit","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"klaerkemichaelpau","last":"Klaerke","name":"Klaerke, Michael","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren","key":"laurbergsørenpau","last":"Laurberg","name":"Laurberg, Søren","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens R.","key":"madsenmogensrpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Mogens R.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Knud T.","key":"nielsenknudtpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Knud T.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"vilandtjesperpau","last":"Vilandt","name":"Vilandt, Jesper","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bruce E.","key":"wilcoxbruceepau","last":"Wilcox","name":"Wilcox, Bruce E.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jia","key":"youjiapau","last":"You","name":"You, Jia","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans J.","key":"nielsenhansjørgenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"87f9baf4-e29c-4104-be23-daf6d94d7124","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","name_org":"Nielsen, Hans J.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1373/jalm.2016.020271","issn":["24757241"],"issue":"2","journal":"The Journal of Applied Laboratory Medicine","pages":"181-193","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Applied Laboratory Medicine","title_org":"The journal of applied laboratory medicine","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025596175"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-90c97884-a450-493c-96f4-7b19aeda65d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovery and validation of plasma-protein biomarker panels for the detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenoma in a Danish collection of samples from patients referred for diagnostic colonoscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479946","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: We investigated whether comorbidity burden of comatose survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) affects outcome and if comorbidity modifies the effect of target temperature management (TTM) on final outcome. DESIGN: The TTM trial randomized 939 patients to 24 h of TTM at either 33 or 36 °C with no difference regarding mortality and neurological outcome. This post-hoc study of the TTM-trial formed a modified comorbidity index (mCI), based on available comorbidities from the Charlson comorbidity index (CCI). RESULTS: Bystander cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) decreased with higher comorbidity group, p = 0.01. Comorbidity groups were univariately associated with higher mortality compared to mCI0 (HRmCI1: 1.55, CI: 1.25-1.93, p < 0.001, HRmCI2: 2.01, CI: 1.55-2.62, p < 0.001, HRmCI ≥ 3: 2.16, CI: 1.57-2.97, p < 0.001). When adjusting for confounders there was a consistent, nonsignificant association between level of comorbidity and mortality (HRmC11: 1.17, CI: 0.92-1.48, p = 0.21, HRmCI2: 1.28, CI: 0.96-1.71, p = 0.10, HRmCI ≥ 3: 1.37, CI: 0.97-1.95, p = 0.08). There was no interaction between comorbidity burden and level of TTM on outcome, p = 0.61. CONCLUSION: Comorbidity burden was associated with higher mortality following OHCA, but when adjusting for confounders, the influence was no longer significant. The association between mCI and mortality was not modified by TTM. Comorbidity burden is associated with lower rates of bystander cardiopulmonary resuscitation after OHCA.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nielsen, Niklas","Kuiper, Michael","Friberg, Hans","Søholm, Helle","Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Frydland, Martin","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485095"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comorbidity burden is not associated with higher mortality after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-485095","identifier":[{"id":"84980022394","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27385408","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-994d0dfe-350a-48fa-8dc4-cb70c51eab4f"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D63A19CEA3D674884883251F5023360"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"søholmpau","last":"Søholm","name":"Søholm, Helle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Hartvig","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"T