{"abstract":"We construct the first UC commitment scheme for binary strings with the optimal properties of rate approaching 1 and linear time complexity (in the amortised sense, using a small number of seed OTs). On top of this, the scheme is additively homomorphic, which allows for applications to maliciously secure 2-party computation. As tools for obtaining this, we make three contributions of independent interest: we construct the first (binary) linear time encodable codes with non-trivial distance and rate approaching 1, we construct the first almost universal hash function with small seed that can be computed in linear time, and we introduce a new primitive called interactive proximity testing that can be used to verify whether a string is close to a given linear code.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cascudo, Ignacio","Damgård, Ivan","David, Bernardo Machado","Döttling, Nico","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S02-083.45-004111"],"event":{"acronym":"CRYPTO","end":"2016-08-18","place":"Santa Barbara, us","start":"2016-08-14","title":"36th Annual International Cryptology Conference, CRYPTO 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["David, Bernardo Machado"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at Berkeley"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rate 000000000001 linear time and additively homomorphic uc commitments","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979608655","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-083.45-004111","identifier":[{"id":"84979608655","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-53ff9b81-82d6-412e-903a-71034286e05d","au-94ba7314-9070-4987-ab25-dbea530290ef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5D4A0B8D44767ADD339C54381629A859"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ignacio","key":"cascudopau","last":"Cascudo","locid":"2f2ded74-b364-4a8d-ada1-189dad083eea","name":"Cascudo, Ignacio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","name_org":"Damgård, Ivan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo Machado","key":"davidpau","last":"David","locid":"e39dd946-3171-4c2c-acc2-0990fe5230b3","name":"David, Bernardo Machado","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nico","key":"döttlingpau","last":"Döttling","name":"Döttling, Nico","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew","key":"robshawpedh","last":"Robshaw","name":"Robshaw, Matthew","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonathan","key":"katzpedh","last":"Katz","name":"Katz, Jonathan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-53015-3_7","eisbn":["9783662530153"],"isbn":["9783662530146"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"179-207","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"36th Annual International Cryptology Conference, Santa Barbara, CA, USA, August 14-18, 2016, Proceedings, Part III","title":"Advances in Cryptology - CRYPTO 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979608655"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-53ff9b81-82d6-412e-903a-71034286e05d","au-94ba7314-9070-4987-ab25-dbea530290ef"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Rate-1, linear time and additively homomorphic UC commitments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.45-004111","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The Greenland shark (Somniosus microcephalus), an iconic species of the Arctic Seas, grows slowly and reaches >500 centimeters (cm) in total length, suggesting a life span well beyond those of other vertebrates. Radiocarbon dating of eye lens nuclei from 28 female Greenland sharks (81 to 502 cm in total length) revealed a life span of at least 272 years. Only the smallest sharks (220 cm or less) showed signs of the radiocarbon bomb pulse, a time marker of the early 1960s. The age ranges of prebomb sharks (reported as midpoint and extent of the 95.4% probability range) revealed the age at sexual maturity to be at least 156 ± 22 years, and the largest animal (502 cm) to be 392 ± 120 years old. Our results show that the Greenland shark is the longest-lived vertebrate known, and they raise concerns about species conservation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nielsen, Julius","Hedeholm, Rasmus B.","Heinemeier, Jan","Bushnell, Peter G.","Christiansen, Jorgen S.","Olsen, Jesper","Ramsey, Christopher Bronk","Brill, Richard W.","Simon, Malene","Steffensen, Kirstine F.","Steffensen, John F."],"cuid":["S02-090.43-020703"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Julius"],"country":["Greenland","Norway","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","College of William and Mary","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Indiana University South Bend","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Age validation","Calibration","Feeding ecology","Food web","Journal Article","Otoliths","Research Support Non U S Gov t","delta N 15"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["National Aquarium Denmark - Den Blå Planet"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eye lens radiocarbon reveals centuries of longevity in the greenland shark i somniosus microcephalus i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84982174967","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.43-020703","identifier":[{"id":"84982174967","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000381561200041","type":"wos"},{"id":"27516602","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6dead7a7-70b3-4e9d-92b2-2231ff6ae179","ku-ffbea06a-a98f-4e3d-9c1f-8047b3669b5d"],"keyword":["AGE VALIDATION","CALIBRATION","DELTA-N-15","FEEDING ECOLOGY","FOOD-WEB","Greenland shark somniosus longevity ageing","Journal Article","LAMNA-NASUS","NORTHWEST ATLANTIC","OTOLITHS","POST-BOMB RADIOCARBON","PRE-BOMB","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D069705D6F764CEE4A36B52C6D107EFD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Marine Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["National Aquarium Denmark - Den Blå Planet"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"4","c