{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The purpose of this review is to summarize the current knowledge from field studies on how many consecutive night shifts are required for adaptation of diurnal rhythms in cortisol, melatonin and heart rate variability (HRV) to night work. METHODS: A systematic search of the databases PubMed and Web of Science resulted in 18 studies selected for review. RESULTS: Cortisol was measured in five studies, melatonin in 11 studies and HRV in four studies. Diurnal rhythms were assessed by use of several different measures based on three to eight samples per day for cortisol and melatonin and 24-h recordings for HRV. Most of the studies in the review were small studies with less than 30 participants, and most studies evaluated diurnal rhythms after only two consecutive night shifts whereas only six studies used seven or more consecutive night shifts. The majority of studies found that adaptation to night work had not occurred after two consecutive night shifts, whereas a small number found evidence for full adaptation after seven consecutive night shifts based on diurnal rhythms in cortisol and melatonin. CONCLUSION: There are methodological differences in the field studies analyzing diurnal rhythms and large diversity in the occupational fields studied. Nevertheless, we conclude that diurnal rhythms in cortisol, melatonin and HRV are not adapted to night work after 1-3 consecutive night shifts. Studies are needed to establish how many consecutive night shifts are needed for full adaptation of diurnal rhythms to night work.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","Garde, Anne Helene","Kristiansen, Jesper","Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","Hansen, Åse Marie"],"cuid":["S02-094.79-769076"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of the number of consecutive night shifts on diurnal rhythms in cortisol melatonin and heart rate variability hrv a systematic review of field studies","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84944571874","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.79-769076","identifier":[{"id":"26464315","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84944571874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-98e61c20-bb9b-4bee-913e-cbb935daf2f9","nfa-5dd73aa7-1693-44a8-80a9-33cfd50fc6fc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5EF52FFE6F71BA66E2EC8368EC578259"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nl":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Aarrebo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"56d55b14-b9d2-4886-8819-0a395b08846a","name":"Jensen, Marie Aarrebo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Helene","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"266b247f-d127-46ae-a6ab-aa16c3f010b9","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0002-4298-1420","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5b151ef4-abb8-4673-9522-abc399e62fea","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4075-3918","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26464315"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00420-015-1093-3","issn":["03400131","14315777"],"issn_org":["03400131"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","pages":"531-545","status":"p","title":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944571874"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-98e61c20-bb9b-4bee-913e-cbb935daf2f9","nfa-5dd73aa7-1693-44a8-80a9-33cfd50fc6fc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"The effect of the number of consecutive night shifts on diurnal rhythms in cortisol, melatonin and heart rate variability (HRV) : a systematic review of field studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.79-769076","year":"2016","yearsub":2016}
{"abstract":"Background: The important cereal crop Sorghum bicolor (L.) Moench biosynthesize and accumulate the defensive compound dhurrin during development. Previous work has suggested multiple roles for the compound including a function as nitrogen storage/buffer. Crucial for this function is the endogenous turnover of dhurrin for which putative pathways have been suggested but not confirmed. Results: In this study, the biosynthesis and endogenous turnover of dhurrin in the developing sorghum grain was studied by metabolite profiling and time-resolved transcriptome analyses. Dhurrin was found to accumulate in the early phase of grain development reaching maximum amounts 25 days after pollination. During the subsequent maturation period, the dhurrin content was turned over, resulting in only negligible residual dhurrin amounts in the mature grain. Dhurrin accumulation correlated with the transcript abundance of the three genes involved in biosynthesis. Despite the accumulation of dhurrin, the grains were acyanogenic as demonstrated by the lack of hydrogen cyanide release from macerated grain tissue and by the absence of transcripts encoding dhurrinases. With the missing activity of dhurrinases, the decrease in dhurrin content in the course of grain maturationrepresents the operation of hitherto uncharacterized endogenous dhurrin turnover pathways. Evidence for theoperation of two such pathways was obtained by metabolite profiling and time-resolved transcriptome analysis. By combining cluster- and phylogenetic analyses with the metabolite profiling, potential gene candidates of glutathione S-transferases, nitrilases and glycosyl transferases involved in these pathways were identified. The absence of dhurrin in the mature grain was replaced by a high content of proanthocyanidins. Cluster- and phylogenetic analyses coupled with metabolite profiling, identified gene candidates involved in proanthocyanidin biosynthesis in sorghum. Conclusions: The results presented in this article reveal the existence of two endogenous dhurrin turnover pathways in sorghum, identify genes putatively involved in these transformations and show that dhurrin in additionto its insect deterrent properties may serve as a storage form of reduced nitrogen. In the course of sorghum grainmaturation, proanthocyanidins replace dhurrin as a defense compound. The lack of cyanogenesis in the developingsorghum grain renders this a unique experimental system to study CNglc synthesis as well as endogenous turnover.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lasse Janniche","Stuart, Peter","Pičmanová, Martina","Rasmussen, Simon","Olsen, Carl Erik","Harholt, Jesper","Møller, Birger Lindberg","Bjarnholt, Nanna"],"cuid":["S02-096.38-034166"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Seedtek"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CARL"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CARL","DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dhurrin metabolism in the developing grain of i sorghum bicolor i l moench investigated by metabolite profiling and novel clustering analyses of time resolved transcriptomic data","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12864-016-3360-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.38-034166","identifier":[{"id":"27964718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5154151","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85003583755","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-45968deb-6357-4c37-98d4-058bccca35d9","ku-b4eb81d0-d501-4de9-af79-8df201e604b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E9D7B75600421B4797616CB5ADBBD6C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/173394390/art_10.1186_s12864_016_3360_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12864-016-3360-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127820301/Nielsen_Dhurrin_BMCGenomics_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"seedtek","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Seedtek","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"carlsberg foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CARL","l3nn":"Carlsberg Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Carlsberg Foundation","namevar":["Carlsberg Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CARL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Janniche","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lasse Janniche","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","name":"Stuart, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Martina","key":"picmanovapau","last":"Picmanova","locid":"76cfbbb8-cd14-4870-a691-49cc456c9b86","name":"Picmanova, Martina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7dcb9d6e-8054-4bcf-a087-82517b291a32","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carl Erik","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"abcd3923-e43e-4a0e-b104-4b6238e5afc8","name":"Olsen, Carl Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-2275-0596","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"harholtpau","last":"Harholt","name":"Harholt, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Birger Lindberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"54d5ec55-f24e-4492-9e76-2c5478d312e0","name":"Møller, Birger Lindberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3252-3119","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Nanna","key":"bjarnholtpau","last":"Bjarnholt","locid":"e90f6c69-b328-49e5-ad2f-26c9b6914bf1","name":"Bjarnholt, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5301-5885","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27964718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12864-016-3360-4","issn":["14712164"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Genomics","paperid":"1021","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"BMC Genomics","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85003583755"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-45968deb-6357-4c37-98d4-058bccca35d9","ku-b4eb81d0-d501-4de9-af79-8df201e604b5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dhurrin metabolism in the developing grain of Sorghum bicolor (L.) Moench investigated by metabolite profiling and novel clustering analyses of time-resolved transcriptomic data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.38-034166","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"I artikel belyses, hvordan unge potentielle idrætstalenter i folkeskolens idrætsklasser arbejder på at leve op til repræsentationen af det at være et talent. Analysen fokuserer på, hvad der sker, hvis potentielle talenter af forskellige grunde har vanskeligt ved at leve op til de forventninger, der rettes mod dem. I analyser tages der afsæt i et poststrukturalistisk begreb om becoming der tilfører analysen centrale perspektiver på, hvordan potentielle idrætstalenter gør og praktiserer talent, og på de forventninger til udvikling de søges forpligtiget på. Det anvendte begreb om becoming henter i særlig grad inspiration fra den Deleuze’ begrebsverden og fra poststrukturalistiske etnografiske analyser, der trækker på denne eller tilsvarende begrebssæt. Deleuze skelner mellem tilblivelse, hvor individet lever op til forventede repræsentationer og normer og (for)bliver den samme, becoming-the-same, og tilblivelse, hvor individet bliver en anden, becoming-other. Becoming kan således, som del af et udviklingsbegreb, bidrage til at undersøge mødet mellem herskende talentforståelser og potentielle idrætstalenter subjektivering igennem disse – og dermed hvad de unge skal gøre for at passere som et talent i udvikling. Endeligt præsentere artiklen inspireret af Bronwyn Davies et begreb om emergent lytning, der i praksisfeltets møde med talenter kan skabe rum for bredere og alternative former for talentgørelsen.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Olesen, Jesper Stilling","Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard"],"cuid":["S02-098.15-008068"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Emergent lytning","Gilles Deleuze","Idrætsklasser","Læring","Talent","Talentgørelse","Talentudvikling","Tilblivelse","Ungdomsuddannelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tilblivelse af talenter og ikke talenter om unges arbejde med at blive til som idrætstalenter","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.skolepsykologi.dk/53--%c3%a5rgang---2016","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.15-008068","ids":["aau-a6c5b85d-be94-4f98-805c-6d5fc26bde00","au-421dec2e-a6f9-48fc-9212-01710d4b2740"],"keyword":["Bronwyn Davies","Emergent lytning","Gilles Deleuze","Idrætsklasser","Læring","Talent","Talentgørelse","Talentudvikling","Tilblivelse","Ungdomsuddannelse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-F5635EC66C1CF33EC0C45754555C99A2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Education Policy Research (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Centre for Health Science Education and Problem-based Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Physical Activity and Human Performance","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences (SSI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","name_org":"Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Stausgaard","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","locid":"aa7165f7-cae8-472d-a248-99070c7f941a","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte Stausgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7419-1856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0906690X","19030002"],"issn_org":["19030002"],"issue":"2","journal":"Pædagogisk Psykologisk Tidsskrift","pages":"90-104","paperid":"9","publisher":"Forlaget Skolepsykologi","status":"p","title":"Pædagogisk Psykologisk Tidsskrift","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a6c5b85d-be94-4f98-805c-6d5fc26bde00","au-421dec2e-a6f9-48fc-9212-01710d4b2740"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tilblivelse af talenter og ikke-talenter : om unges arbejde med at blive til som idrætstalenter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.15-008068","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with diabetes (DM) experience increased risk of Staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia (SAB), but the prognostic impact of diabetes in patients with SAB remain unclear. Therefore, we investigated 30-day all-cause mortality in patients with and without DM. METHODS: Population-based medical databases were used to conduct a cohort study of all adult patients with community-acquired SAB in Northern Denmark, 2000-2011. Using Cox proportional hazards regression, we computed hazard ratios as estimates of 30-day mortality rate ratios (MRRs) among patients with and without DM. We further investigated whether the prognostic impact of DM differed among patients with and without recent preadmission healthcare contacts (within 30 days of the current hospitalization) and by age, sex, marital status, level of comorbidity, and DM-related characteristics (e.g., duration of DM and presence of DM complications). RESULTS: Among 2638 SAB patients, 713 (27.0%) had DM. Thirty-day cumulative mortality was 25.8% in patients with DM and 24.3% in patients without DM, for an adjusted MRR (aMRR) of 1.01 (95% confidence interval (CI), 0.84-1.20). In analyses with and without recent healthcare contacts, the corresponding aMRRs were 0.84 (95% CI, 0.62-1.14) and 1.13 (95% CI, 0.91-1.41), respectively. Compared to patients without DM, the aMRR was 0.94 (95% CI, 0.74-1.20) for male patients with DM and 1.13 (95% CI, 0.87-1.47) for female patients with DM. The prognostic influence of DM on mortality did not differ notably with age, level of comorbidity, or characteristics of patients with DM. CONCLUSION: Patients with DM and community-acquired SAB did not experience higher 30-day mortality than patients without DM.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Smit, Jesper","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Nielsen, Henrik","Frøslev, Trine","Søgaard, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002845"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bacteremia","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark","Diabetes Complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Risk Factors","Staphylococcal Infections","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcome of community acquired staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia in patients with diabetes a historical population based cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0153766","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002845","identifier":[{"id":"000374291800051","type":"wos"},{"id":"84977663774","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4833306","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27082873","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-395227f1-56dd-4a0f-8c1c-35765347efde","au-b9a199e1-f4a8-4390-8c71-d977384f0e57"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Bacteremia","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark","Diabetes Complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Risk Factors","Staphylococcal Infections","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9B4A775BE222580A84191CB48B452B75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0153766","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Infektionsmedicin [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"smitpau","last":"Smit","locid":"29aa2e66-1f20-4693-9114-5f988949c879","name":"Smit, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"RW","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"36e7af2c-e02f-48d4-b124-0f1bd95b1748","name":"Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","name_org":"Thomsen, RW","orcid":"0000-0001-9135-3474","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Carl","key":"schønheyderpau","last":"Schønheyder","locid":"d35b264a-6efc-467d-ac9d-e558542ef8a8","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Ib","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f0dd5aa7-1ea7-4567-9595-b60afb486088","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","name_org":"Nielsen, Henrik Ib","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine","key":"frøslevpau","last":"Frøslev","locid":"796f4ce4-c427-483a-a529-89ba3e66e284","name":"Frøslev, Trine","orcid":"0000-0003-1594-9959","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5550d2b5-320f-4f20-82aa-3bd98f0fe3dd","name":"Søgaard, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27082873"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0153766","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0153766","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977663774"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-395227f1-56dd-4a0f-8c1c-35765347efde","au-b9a199e1-f4a8-4390-8c71-d977384f0e57"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Outcome of Community-Acquired Staphylococcus aureus Bacteraemia in Patients with Diabetes : A Historical Population-Based Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-002845","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This study compares the details and performance of fisheries management between the EU and a selection of other countries worldwide: Iceland, New Zealand, and Australia, which are considered in many respects to be among the most advanced in the world in fisheries management. Fisheries management in the EU, Iceland, Australia, and New Zealand has developed following different paths, despite being based on similar instruments and principles. Iceland, Australia, and New Zealand have been at the forefront of developing management practices such as stakeholder involvement, legally binding management targets (Australia, New Zealand), individual transferable quotas, and discard bans (Iceland, New Zealand). The EU has since the beginning of the 21st century taken significant steps to better involve stakeholders and establish quantitative targets through management plans, and a landing obligation is gradually being implemented from 2015 onward. The management of domestic fisheries resources in Australia, New Zealand, and Iceland has, overall, performed better than in the EU, in terms of conservation and economic efficiency. It should, however, be stressed that, compared to Australia, New Zealand, and Iceland, (i) initial over‐capacity was more of an issue in the EU when management measures became legally binding and also that (ii) EU has been progressive in developing common enforcement standards, on stocks shared by sovereign nations. The situation of EU fisheries has substantially improved over the period 2004–2013 in the northeast Atlantic, with fishery status getting close to that in the other jurisdictions, but the lack of recovery for Mediterranean fish stocks remains a concern.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Marchal, Paul","Andersen, Jesper Levring","Aranda, Martin","Fitzpatrick, Mike","Goti, Leyre","Guyader, Olivier","Haraldsson, Gunnar","Hatcher, Aaron","Hegland, Troels Jacob","Le Floc’h, Pascal","Macher, Claire","Malvarosa, Loretta","Maravelias, Christos","Mardle, Simon","Murillas, Arantza","Nielsen, J. Rasmus","Sabatella, Rosaria","D M Smith, Anthony","Stokes, Kevin","Thøgersen, Thomas T.","Ulrich, Clara"],"cuid":["S03-098.78-011324"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","France","Germany","Greece","Iceland","Ireland","Italy","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AZTI","All Global Affiliations","Azti-Tecnalia Food Research Institute","CSIRO","CSIRO Oceans and Atmosphere","Fishery and Aquaculture Research Organisation","Hellenic Centre for Marine Research","Institut français de recherche pour l'exploitation de la mer","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","NISEA, Fishery and Aquaculture Research Organisation","National University of Ireland","The Institute for Economic Research in Fishery and Acquaculture, IREPA","Thunen-Institut","University of Galway","University of Iceland","University of Portsmouth","Université de Bretagne Occidentale"],"keyword":["Australia","Comparative review","European Union","Fisheries management","Iceland","New Zealand"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["rue de Kergoat, B^at. B, CS 93837, 29238, Brest Cedex 3, France"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparative review of fisheries management experiences in the european union and in other countries worldwide iceland australia and new zealand","src":["aau","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146594650/Postprint.doc.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-098.78-011324","identifier":[{"id":"00038249460001