{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Helmke, Christophe","Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457595"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the defeat of the great bird in myth and royal pageantry a mesoamerican myth in a comparative perspective","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/151344857/8_16_1_SM.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-457595","ids":["ku-6b70c7ad-6171-4b11-bac3-15db95fae1ec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E452BD65A60038B99DAE0AF2FE3733F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/151344857/8_16_1_SM.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christophe","key":"helmkepau","last":"Helmke","locid":"b726201f-2e3a-4217-a929-548e07b4aa7e","name":"Helmke, Christophe","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-7075","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c4f316cc-ab4e-4a04-9c3f-a4a1a4249ad1","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["24099899"],"issue":"1","journal":"Comparative Mythology","pages":"23-60","status":"p","title":"Comparative Mythology","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b70c7ad-6171-4b11-bac3-15db95fae1ec"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Defeat of the Great Bird in Myth and Royal Pageantry : A Mesoamerican Myth in a Comparative Perspective","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457595","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Jagtturisme giver høj indtjening til lokalsamfundene, og det kan skabe incitament til at passe bedre på de vilde dyr og til at forvalte områderne fornuftigt. Et forbud mod trofæjagt kan medføre det omvendte.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schou, Jesper Sølver","Lundhede, Thomas","Nielsen, Martin Reinhardt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471515"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trofæjagt kan være god fornuft","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ifro.ku.dk/debatindlaeg/trofaejagt-kan-vaere-god-fornuft/","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471515","ids":["ku-828055f5-a967-42d9-96e7-555a88dd7fab"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6C90820154A61F167296F6E84FCBD339"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ifro.ku.dk/debatindlaeg/trofaejagt-kan-vaere-god-fornuft/","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Sølver","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"e9d20fb4-4b3f-40ce-9fba-acfb58217c0b","name":"Schou, Jesper Sølver","orcid":"0000-0001-5030-4035","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"lundhedepau","last":"Lundhede","locid":"0c4f5b4a-ec81-45ec-bde0-90c871b56a42","name":"Lundhede, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-3226-8338","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Reinhardt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c723a39f-eb05-4fba-9493-2b18ba7b5a43","name":"Nielsen, Martin Reinhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-8941-6031","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01064142","09057633"],"issn_org":["01064142"],"newspaper":"Weekendavisen","pages":"12","status":"p","title":"Weekendavisen"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-828055f5-a967-42d9-96e7-555a88dd7fab"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trofæjagt kan være god fornuft","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471515","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate the hemodynamic profile associated with different target temperatures and to assess the prognostic implication of inotropic/vasopressor support and mean arterial pressure after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. There is a lack of information how different target temperatures may affect hemodynamics. DESIGN: Post hoc analysis of a prospective randomized study. SETTING: Thirty-six ICUs in 10 countries. PATIENTS: Nine hundred twenty patients (97%) with available vasopressor data out of 950 patients from the Target Temperature Management trial randomly assigned patients to a targeted temperature management at 33 °C or 36 °C. INTERVENTIONS: None. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: Mean arterial pressure, heart rate, and lactate were registered at prespecified time points. The population was stratified according to cardiovascular Sequential Organ Failure Assessment = 4 defining the high vasopressor group and cardiovascular Sequential Organ Failure Assessment less than or equal to 3 defining the low vasopressor group. The targeted temperature management 33 (TTM33) group had a hemodynamic profile with lower heart rate (-7.0 min(-1) [95% confidence limit, -8.7, -5.1]; p(group) < 0.0001), similar mean arterial pressure (-1.1 mm Hg [95% confidence limit, -2.3, 0.2]; p(group) = 0.10), and increased lactate (0.6 mmol/L [95% confidence limit, 0.3, 0.8]; p(group) < 0.0001) compared with the targeted temperature management 36 (TTM36) group. A cardiovascular Sequential Organ Failure Assessment score = 4 was recorded in 54% versus 45%, p = 0.03 in the TTM33 and the TTM36 group, respectively. The high vasopressor group carried a 53% mortality rate when compared with a 34% in the low vasopressor group, p(log-rank) less than 0.0001, with an adjusted hazard ratio of 1.38 (95% CI, 1.11-1.71; p = 0.004). There was no interaction between vasopressor group and allocated target temperature group (p = 0.40). An inverse relationship between mean arterial pressure and mortality was identified (p = 0.0008). CONCLUSIONS: Targeted temperature management at 33 °C was associated with hemodynamic alterations with decreased heart rate, elevated levels of lactate, and need for increased vasopressor support compared with targeted temperature management at 36 °C. Low mean arterial pressure and need for high doses of vasopressors were associated with increased mortality independent of allocated targeted temperature management.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bro-Jeppesen, John","Annborn, Martin","Hassager, Christian","Wise, Matt P","Pelosi, Paolo","Nielsen, Niklas","Erlinge, David","Wanscher, Michael","Friberg, Hans","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472685"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["TTM Investigators"],"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Body Temperature","Comorbidity","Dose Response Relationship Drug","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Intensive Care Units","Lactic Acid","Male","Middle Aged","Organ Dysfunction Scores","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Sex Factors","Single Blind Method","Vasoconstrictor Agents"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hemodynamics and vasopressor support during targeted temperature management at 000000000033 c versus 000000000036 c after out of hospital cardiac arrest a post hoc study of the target temperature management trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-472685","identifier":[{"id":"25365723","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925348426","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-846a17bb-8d0f-49b3-bdc6-f3cb54b207ec"],"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Body Temperature","Comorbidity","Dose-Response Relationship, Drug","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Intensive Care Units","Lactic Acid","Male","Middle Aged","Organ Dysfunction Scores","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Sex Factors","Single-Blind Method","Vasoconstrictor Agents"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-308A3F7ECA9F6C2D8ADF5C64463EB494"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ttm investigators","name":"TTM Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"annbornpau","last":"Annborn","name":"Annborn, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matt P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt P","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paolo","key":"pelosipau","last":"Pelosi","name":"Pelosi, Paolo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25365723"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ccm.0000000000000691","issn":["00903493","10637389"],"issn_org":["00903493"],"issue":"2","journal":"Critical Care Medicine","pages":"318-27","status":"p","title":"Critical Care Medicine","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925348426"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-846a17bb-8d0f-49b3-bdc6-f3cb54b207ec"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hemodynamics and vasopressor support during targeted temperature management at 33°C Versus 36°C after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest : a post hoc study of the target temperature management trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472685","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"To assess the relationship between epicardial coronary artery stenosis severity and the corresponding regional transmural perfusion at rest and during adenosine stress, using multidetector computed tomography (MDCT). We evaluated the relationship between the severity of coronary artery diameter stenosis assessed by MDCT angiography and semi-quantitative myocardial MDCT perfusion in 200 symptomatic patients. The perfusion index (PI = mean myocardial attenuation density/mean left ventricular lumen attenuation density) at rest and during adenosine stress, the myocardial perfusion reserve (MPR = stress - PI/rest - PI), and the transmural perfusion ratio (TPR = subendocardium/subepicardium) were calculated. A coronary artery stenosis ≥50 % was present in 49 patients (25 %). Rest-PI and rest-TPR values were similar in patients with and without a coronary artery stenosis ≥50 %, whereas stress-PI, stress-TPR and MPR were significantly reduced in patients with a stenosis ≥50 % (p < 0.001, p < 0.0001 and p = 0.02, respectively). Subendocardial PI was significantly higher than subepicardial PI at rest and during stress for patients without a significant stenosis, whereas this difference was blurred during stress in patients with ≥50 % stenosis. In a broad spectrum of stenosis severity groups, TPR at rest remained unchanged until the group of patients with total occlusions, whereas TPR during stress decreased progressively when a threshold of 50 % was superseded. In this study we establish the relationship between semi-quantitative perfusion measurements by MDCT and severity of coronary artery stenoses and find the transmural myocardial perfusion ratio to be a potential strong functional index of the hemodynamic significance of coronary artery atherosclerotic lesions.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Linde, Jesper James","Kühl, Jørgen Tobias","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Sørgaard, Mathias","Kelbæk, Henning","Nielsen, Walter Bjørn","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482678"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adenosine","Adult","Aged","Coronary Circulation","Coronary Stenosis","Coronary Vessels","Denmark","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Hyperemia","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Observer Variation","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Reproducibility of Results","Severity of Illness Index","Vasodilator Agents"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transmural myocardial perfusion gradients in relation to coronary artery stenoses severity assessed by cardiac multidetector computed tomography","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-482678","identifier":[{"id":"25194436","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84921060767","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-95605f8a-432e-49aa-933e-5b00a8484fd8"],"keyword":["Adenosine","Adult","Aged","Coronary Circulation","Coronary Stenosis","Coronary Vessels","Denmark","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Hyperemia","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Observer Variation","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Reproducibility of Results","Severity of Illness Index","Vasodilator Agents"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8555C8BE424ADD118A80B86DA4051314"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jesper James","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Jesper James","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen Tobias","key":"kühlpau","last":"Kühl","name":"Kühl, Jørgen Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Dahlgaard","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"sørgaardpau","last":"Sørgaard","name":"Sørgaard, Mathias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henning","key":"kelbækpau","last":"Kelbæk","name":"Kelbæk, Henning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Walter Bjørn","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Walter Bjørn","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus Fuglsang","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25194436"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10554-014-0530-9","issn":["15695794","15730743"],"issn_org":["15695794"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"171-180","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921060767"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-95605f8a-432e-49aa-933e-5b00a8484fd8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transmural myocardial perfusion gradients in relation to coronary artery stenoses severity assessed by cardiac multidetector computed tomography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482678","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Comparing the outcome after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) in men and women and to determine whether sex modifies the effect of targeted temperature management (TTM) at 33 or 36°C. METHODS: The TTM trial randomized 950 patients to TTM at 33 or 36°C for 24h. This predefined sub-study of the TTM trial assessed survival and neurological outcome defined as Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) and modified Rankin Scale (mRS) using female sex as main predictor of outcome, in relation to level of TTM and other confounding factors. RESULTS: Compared to men, women more often had OHCA at home, p=0.04 and less often had bystander defibrillation, p=0.01. No other differences in arrest circumstances were found. Coronary angiography (CAG) and percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) <24h after ROSC was less often performed in women, both: p=0.02. Female sex was associated with higher mortality in univariate analysis, hazard ratio (HR)=1.29, CI=1.04-1.61, p=0.02 compared to men. Adjusting for demographic factors (age and comorbidity), arrest circumstances, pre-hospital findings, inclusion sites, treatments and status at admission reduced this: HR=1.11, CI=0. 87-1.41, p=0.42, and sex was no longer an independent risk factor for death. The effect of sex did not modify the effect of TTM at 33 and 36°C, pinteraction=0.73. CONCLUSION: Female sex seems associated with adverse outcome, but this association is largely explained by differences in arrest circumstances and in-hospital treatment. Our data shows no interaction between sex and the effect of targeting 33 vs. 36°C.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Wanscher, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Wetterslev, Jørn","Cronberg, Tobias","Erlinge, David","Friberg, Hans","Gasche, Yvan","Horn, Janneke","Hovdenes, Jan","Kuiper, Michael","Pellis, Tommaso","Stammet, Pascal","Wise, Matthew P","Åneman, Anders","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485498"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no difference in mortality between men and women after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-485498","identifier":[{"id":"26215480","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84944897104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-99ffd8ec-9357-44f5-81d7-875b44b0c38a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-361430DE1E48B4AF436CB854F327A3AC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"gaschepau","last":"Gasche","name":"Gasche, Yvan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matthew P","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ånemanpau","last":"Åneman","name":"Åneman, Anders","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26215480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2015.06.030","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"78-84","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944897104"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-99ffd8ec-9357-44f5-81d7-875b44b0c38a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"No difference in mortality between men and women after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485498","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"For decades, infectious endometritis has been a major cause of infertility in mares and an inflammatory response secondary to uterine infection appears to be a major contributor to a suboptimal uterine environment. The aim of the present study was to characterize the endometrial gene expression of the glycoprotein lactoferrin in brood mares and to evaluate if the expression was associated with infectious endometritis. Endometrial biopsies were obtained from broodmares at a Danish AI-center during the 2014 breeding season by the use of a guarded approach as described by Nielsen (Nielsen, 2005). Mares with clinical signs of endometritis and/or a history of previous un-successful breeding were selected for the study. Two biopsies were obtained from each mare. One biopsy was used for bacterial culture and cytology and one biopsy was used for RNA extraction. Relative gene-expression analyses were performed by quantitative reverse transcriptase PCR (qRT-PCR) using validated primers and SYBR green detection. Infectious endometritis was diagnosed in 49% of the mares (29/59) with S. zooepidemicus isolated most frequently (45%). Data was analysed using the non-parametric Kruskal-Wallis test. Expression of lactoferrin was significantly increased in mares with infectious endometritis compared to mares with no growth of uterine pathogens. Lactoferrin expression was also associated with positive cytology (>0.5% PMNs) (Nielsen, 2005). The results indicate that lactoferrin plays a role in the innate immune response and emphasizes its ability to function as a bacteristatic and bactericidal agent.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Mette","Møller Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507221"],"event":{"end":"2015-09-30","place":"Gdansk, pl","start":"2015-09-28","title":"2nd International Conference on Biology and Pathology of Reproduction in Domestic Animals","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 con