{"abstract":"Andersen-Tawil syndrome (ATS) is a rare hereditary multi--system disorder consisting of a triad of symptoms, ventricular arrhythmias, periodic paralysis and dysmorphic features. The syndrome is associated with a loss of function mutation in the gene KCNJ2, which encodes the Kir2.1 inward rectifier potassium channel. We represent a case story of a 15-year-old girl who had unexplained arrhythmias for six years. Molecular genetic screening with a 75-heart-panel revealed a pathogenic KCNJ2 missense mutation. The patient was diagnosed with ATS.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Broendberg, Anders Krogh","Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-170761"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular genetic diagnostics of the cause of ventricular arrhythmias in children","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85037697838","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-170761","identifier":[{"id":"85037697838","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26376421","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-48adc9df-3eee-4733-8545-29ad400c6f85"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B1BD3CAF5553B0BA0ACB604914E58FE5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Krogh","key":"brøndbergpau","last":"Brøndberg","locid":"4a65d3cf-b7b4-4fab-b53f-47e1b6e9d64c","name":"Broendberg, Anders Krogh","name_org":"Brøndberg, Anders Krogh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Vandborg","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"88b6b510-516e-4eb2-a040-91ea40ee55ae","name":"Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26376421"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"38","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"177"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-48adc9df-3eee-4733-8545-29ad400c6f85"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Molecular genetic diagnostics of the cause of ventricular arrhythmias in children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-170761","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Universally composable secure computation was assumed to require trusted setups, until it was realized that parties exchanging (untrusted) tamper-proof hardware tokens allow an alternative approach (Katz; EUROCRYPT 2007). This discovery initialized a line of research dealing with two different types of tokens. Using only a single stateful token, one can implement general statistically secure two-party computation (Döttling, Kraschewski, Müller-Quade; TCC 2011); though all security is lost if an adversarial token receiver manages to physically reset and rerun the token. Stateless tokens, which are secure by definition against any such resetting-attacks, however, do provably not suffice for statistically secure computation in general (Goyal, Ishai, Mahmoody, Sahai; CRYPTO 2010). We investigate the natural question of what is possible if an adversary can reset a token at most a bounded number of times (e.g., because each resetting attempt imposes a significant risk to trigger a self-destruction mechanism of the token). Somewhat surprisingly, our results come close to the known positive results with respect to non-resettable stateful tokens. In particular, we construct polynomially many instances of statistically secure and universally composable oblivious transfer, using only a constant number of tokens. Our techniques have some abstract similarities to previous solutions, which we grasp by defining a new security property for protocols that use oracle access. Additionally, we apply our techniques to zero-knowledge proofs and obtain a protocol that achieves the same properties as bounded-query zero-knowledge PCPs (Kilian, Petrank, Tardos; STOC 1997), even if a malicious prover may issue stateful PCP oracles.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Döttling, Nico Marcel","Kraschewski, Daniel","Müller-Quade, Jörn","Nilges, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-220564"],"event":{"acronym":"TCC","end":"2015-03-25","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2015-03-23","title":"Theory of Cryptography Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","TNG Technology Consulting GmbH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"general statistically secure computation with bounded resettable hardware tokens","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84924689911","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-220564","identifier":[{"id":"84924689911","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a01b69f5-4041-435e-b4c1-036aebf648ce"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14BA53EB9F2A5B10A1657D3504EF6238"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"tng technology consulting gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TNG Technology Consulting GmbH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nico","key":"döttlingpau","last":"Döttling","locid":"3d5f5967-e1e1-41bc-89a2-7cc2e040412a","name":"Döttling, Nico Marcel","name_org":"Döttling, Nico","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"kraschewskipau","last":"Kraschewski","name":"Kraschewski, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"müllerquadepau","last":"Müller-Quade","name":"Müller-Quade, Jörn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"nilgespau","last":"Nilges","name":"Nilges, Tobias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yevgeniy","key":"dodispedh","last":"Dodis","name":"Dodis, Yevgeniy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"buusnielsenpedh","last":"Buus Nielsen","name":"Buus Nielsen, Jesper","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-46494-6_14","eisbn":["9783662464946"],"isbn":["9783662464939"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"319-344","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"12th Theory of Cryptography Conference, TCC 2015, Warsaw, Poland, March 23-25, 2015, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Theory of Cryptography"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924689911"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a01b69f5-4041-435e-b4c1-036aebf648ce"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"General statistically secure computation with bounded-resettable hardware tokens","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220564","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The proceedings contain 26 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Foundations, Multiparty Computation, Resettable Security, Non-malleable Codes and Tampering. The topics include: On basing size-verifiable one-way functions on NP-hardness; the power of negations in cryptography; from weak to strong zero-knowledge and applications; an efficient transform from sigma protocols to NIZK with a CRS and non-programmable random oracle; the two-tier model for secure multiparty computation; secure physical computation using disposable circuits; complete characterization of fairness in secure two-party computation of Boolean functions; round-efficient concurrently composable secure computation via a robust extraction lemma; an alternative approach to non-black-box simulation in fully concurrent setting; general statistically secure computation with bounded-resettable hardware tokens; leakage-resilient non-malleable codes; locally decodable and updatable non-malleable codes and their applications; tamper detection and continuous non-malleable codes; optimal algebraic manipulation detection codes in the constant-error model; from single-bit to multi-bit public-key encryption via non-malleable codes; improved bounds and applications to padding-based encryption and tightly-secure authenticated key exchange.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dodis, Yevgeniy","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-226836"],"event":{"end":"2015-03-25","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2015-03-23","title":"Theory of Cryptography Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","New York University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"theory of cryptography 000000000012th theory of cryptography conference tcc 000000002015 warsaw poland march 000000000023 000000000025 000000002015 proceedings part ii","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84924733608","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-226836","identifier":[{"id":"84924733608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-aaef5c36-2b93-443e-b42c-0104d1bdab37"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-A013F78A9F71296B7A8FA4CF15252EB7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yevgeniy","key":"dodisped","last":"Dodis","name":"Dodis, Yevgeniy","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-46497-7","eisbn":["9783662464977"],"isbn":["9783662464960"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"659","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924388036","2-s2.0-84924699431"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aaef5c36-2b93-443e-b42c-0104d1bdab37"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Theory of Cryptography : 12th Theory of Cryptography Conference, TCC 2015, Warsaw, Poland, March 23-25, 2015, Proceedings, Part II","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-226836","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Adaptively secure Multi-Party Computation (MPC) first studied by Canetti, Feige, Goldreich, and Naor in 1996, is a fundamental notion in cryptography. Adaptive security is particularly hard to achieve in settings where arbitrary number of parties can be corrupted and honest parties are not trusted to properly erase their internal state. We did not know how to realize constant round protocols for this task even if we were to restrict ourselves to semi-honest adversaries and to the simpler two-party setting. Specifically the round complexity of known protocols grows with the depth of the circuit the parties are trying to compute. In this work, using indistinguishability obfuscation, we construct a UC two-round Multi-Party computation protocol secure against any active, adaptive adversary corrupting an arbitrary number of parties.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Garg, Sanjam","Polychroniadou, Antigoni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239207"],"event":{"acronym":"TCC","end":"2015-03-25","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2015-03-23","title":"Theory of Cryptography Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at Berkeley"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"two round adaptively secure mpc from indistinguishability obfuscation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84924359034","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239207","identifier":[{"id":"84924359034","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c08e35d6-e60d-4004-b7c6-b7f0d38a22ec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific",