Martin","key":"schubertpau","last":"Schubert","name":"Schubert, Martin","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"stoberpau","last":"Stober","name":"Stober, J.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"W.","key":"suttroppau","last":"Suttrop","name":"Suttrop, W.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"tardinipau","last":"Tardini","name":"Tardini, G.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, D.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/0741-3335/57/3/035009","issn":["07413335","13616587"],"issn_org":["07413335"],"issue":"3","journal":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","pages":"035009","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923240026"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bbccbdb5-fc7c-4a82-afb2-c61253d406fb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Measurements of the fast-ion distribution function at ASDEX upgrade by collective Thomson scattering (CTS) using active and passive views","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360705","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: Genome-wide assocn. studies have shown that the common single nucleotide polymorphism rs6800541 located in SCN10A, encoding the voltage-gated Nav1.8 sodium channel, is assocd. with PR-interval prolongation and atrial fibrillation (AF). Single nucleotide polymorphism rs6800541 is in high linkage disequil. with the nonsynonymous variant in SCN10A, rs6795970 (V1073A, r2=0.933). We therefore sought to det. whether common and rare SCN10A variants are assocd. with early onset AF. Methods and Results: SCN10A was sequenced in 225 AF patients in whom there was no evidence of other cardiovascular disease or dysfunction (lone AF). In an assocn. study of the rs6795970 single nucleotide polymorphism variant, we included 515 AF patients and 2 control cohorts of 730 individuals free of AF and 6161 randomly sampled individuals. Functional characterization of SCN10A variants was performed by whole-cell patch-clamping. In the lone AF cohort, 9 rare missense variants and 1 splice site donor variant were detected. Interestingly, AF patients were found to have higher G allele frequency of rs6795970, which encodes the alanine variant at position 1073 (described from here on as A1073, odds ratio =1.35 [1.16-1.54]; P=2.3×10). Both of the common variants, A1073 and P1092, induced a gain-of-channel function, whereas the rare missense variants, V94G and R1588Q, resulted in a loss-of-channel function. Conclusions: The common variant A1073 is assocd. with increased susceptibility to AF. Both rare and common variants have effect on the function of the channel, indicating that these variants influence susceptibility to AF. Hence, our study suggests that SCN10A variations are involved in the genesis of AF.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jabbari, Javad","Olesen, Morten S","Yuan, Lei","Nielsen, Jonas B","Liang, Bo","Macri, Vincenzo","Christophersen, Ingrid E.","Nielsen, Nikolaj","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Ellinor, Patrick T.","Grunnet, Morten","Haunsø, Stig","Holst, Anders G","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Jespersen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419016"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"common and rare variants in i scn000000000010a i modulate the risk of atrial fibrillation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-419016","identifier":[{"id":"25085921","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84924539336","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2aee225d-863d-4d06-81e9-f6902984f9dc"],"keyword":["SCN10A atrial fibrillation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-2794CB7B1F69D0620BFBBADAA51381C5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Javad","key":"jabbarijavadpau","last":"Jabbari","locid":"3c7f307b-30cb-4fb2-b8b5-8368ccc83e7a","name":"Jabbari, Javad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S.","key":"olesenmortenspau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","name_org":"Olesen, Morten S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"yuanleipau","last":"Yuan","locid":"89fca32c-7fca-4448-a2ff-6a0354839255","name":"Yuan, Lei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas B.","key":"nielsenjonasbpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"64ee18f9-f549-4a20-b501-a5a61c157cb9","name":"Nielsen, Jonas B","name_org":"Nielsen, Jonas B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"liangbopau","last":"Liang","locid":"2c35b5a6-249a-4022-b09b-8c6b3b14c1ce","name":"Liang, Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vincenzo","key":"macrivincenzopau","last":"Macri","name":"Macri, Vincenzo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingrid E.","key":"christopherseningridepau","last":"Christophersen","name":"Christophersen, Ingrid E.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nikolaj","key":"nielsennikolajpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bc559080-989d-4a3f-8f14-bbceb1490bf8","name":"Nielsen, Nikolaj","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehahmadpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patrick T.","key":"ellinorpatricktpau","last":"Ellinor","name":"Ellinor, Patrick T.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"grunnetmortenpau","last":"Grunnet","locid":"b17b3f5b-0621-42a0-9870-a5921c3ee2b9","name":"Grunnet, Morten","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøstigpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders G.","key":"holstandersgpau","last":"Holst","locid":"8676b11a-536a-4ada-906e-c39eaac492f3","name":"Holst, Anders G","name_org":"Holst, Anders G.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper H.","key":"svendsenjesperhastruppau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","name_org":"Svendsen, Jesper H.","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"jespersenthomaspau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"db23d6cb-3abe-4ba2-b1d3-44f918c72e51","name":"Jespersen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6575-360X","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25085921"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circgenetics.113.000442","issn":["1942325X","19423268"],"issn_org":["1942325X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Circulation: Cardiovascular Genetics","pages":"64-73","status":"p","title":"Circulation: Cardiovascular Genetics","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924539336"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2aee225d-863d-4d06-81e9-f6902984f9dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Common and rare variants in <i>SCN10A</i> modulate the risk of atrial fibrillation.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-419016","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Time to Return of Spontaneous Circulation (ROSC) has a plausible relation to severity of hypoxic injury before and during resuscitation in Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest (OHCA), and has consistently been associated with adverse outcome. The effect of Targeted Temperature Management (TTM) may not be similar over the full spectrum of time to ROSC. This study investigated the possible beneficial effect of targeting 33°C over 36°C on the prognostic importance of time to ROSC. METHODS: In predefined sub-study of the TTM-trial (NEJM 2013) we investigated the relationship between time to ROSC, level of TTM and mortality and neurological outcome as assessed by the Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) scale and modified Rankin Scale (mRS) after 180 days. RESULTS: Prolonged time to ROSC was significantly associated with increased mortality with a hazard ratio (HR) of 1.02 per minute (95% CI 1.01-1.02). Level of TTM did not modify the association of time to ROSC and mortality, pinteraction=0.85. Prolonged time to ROSC was associated with reduced odds of surviving with a favorable neurological outcome for CPC (p=0.008 for CPC 1-2) and mRS (p=0.17, mRS 0-3) with no significant interaction with level of TTM. CONCLUSION: Time to ROSC remains a significant prognostic factor in comatose OHCA patients with regards to risk of death and risk of adverse neurological outcome. For any time to ROSC, targeting 33°C in TTM was not associated with benefit with regards to reducing mortality or risk of adverse neurological outcome compared to targeting 36°C.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nielsen, Niklas","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Wanscher, Michael","Pellis, Tommaso","Kuiper, Michael","Hartvig Thomsen, Jakob","Wetterslev, Jørn","Cronberg, Tobias","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Erlinge, David","Friberg, Hans","Søholm, Helle","Gasche, Yvan","Horn, Janneke","Hovdenes, Jan","Stammet, Pascal","Wise, Matthew P","Åneman, Anders","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428946"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of time to return of spontaneous circulation on neuroprotective effect of targeted temperature management at 000000000033 or 000000000036 degrees in comatose survivors of out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-428946","identifier":[{"id":"84945451471","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26159609","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3b7f9f92-3224-4d4b-aa9b-83d3144d1cc4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-080CED2789FA7809142B3778FD5E434C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"a