en","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","rank":64,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristian","key":"kristiansenkristianpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Kristian","rank":65,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eske","key":"willersleveskepau","last":"Willerslev","locid":"21d2e042-0513-44fe-8acd-56b0d00a603e","name":"Willerslev, Eske","orcid":"0000-0002-7081-6748","rank":66,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nature14507","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["15461718"],"issue":"7555","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"167-172","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"522"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930940396"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c76dbfab-24d3-4f23-969b-3049174c282d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Population genomics of bronze age Eurasia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-512454","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Activated factor VII blocked in the active site with Phe-Phe-Arg-chloromethyl ketone (active site inhibited factor VII (ASIS)) is a 50-kDa protein that binds with high affinity to its receptor, tissue factor (TF). TF is a transmembrane glycoprotein that plays an important role in, for example, thrombosis, metastasis, tumor growth, and tumor angiogenesis. The aim of this study was to develop an 18F-labeled ASIS derivative to assess TF expression in tumors. Active site inhibited factor VII was labeled using N-succinimidyl-4-[18F]fluorobenzoate, and the [18F]ASIS was purified on a PD-10 desalting column. The radiochemical yield was 25 ± 6%, the radiochemical purity was >97%, and the pseudospecific radioactivity was 35 ± 9 GBq/µmol. The binding efficacy was evaluated in pull-down experiments, which monitored the binding of unlabeled ASIS and [18F]ASIS to TF and to a specific anti-factor VII antibody (F1A2-mAb). No significant difference in binding efficacy between [18F]ASIS and ASIS could be detected. Furthermore, [18F]ASIS was relatively stable in vitro and in vivo in mice. In conclusion, [18F]ASIS has for the first time been successfully synthesized as a possible positron emission tomography tracer to image TF expression levels. In vivo positron emission tomography studies to evaluate the full potential of [18F]ASIS are in progress.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Erlandsson, Maria","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Jeppesen, Troels E.","Kristensen, Jesper B.","Petersen, Lars C.","Madsen, Jacob","Kjaer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516357"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthesis and characterization of sup 000000000018 sup f labeled active site inhibited factor vii asis