{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To investigate the suitability of three antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) as cell-penetrating antimicrobial peptides. METHODS: Cellular uptake of three AMPs (PK-12-KKP, SA-3 and TPk) and a cell-penetrating peptide (penetratin), all 5(6)-carboxytetramethylrhodamine-labeled, were tested in HeLa WT cells and analyzed by flow cytometry and confocal microscopy. Furthermore, the effects of the peptides on eukaryotic cell viability as well as their antimicrobial effect were tested. In addition, the disrupting ability of the peptides in the presence of bilayer membranes of different composition were analyzed. RESULTS: AMP uptake relative to penetratin was ~13% (PK-12-KKP), ~66% (SA-3) and ~50% (TPk). All four peptides displayed a punctate uptake pattern in HeLa WT cells with co-localization to lysosomes and no indication that clathrin-mediated endocytosis was the predominant uptake mechanism. TPk showed the highest antibacterial activity. SA-3 exhibited selective disruption of liposomes mimicking Gram-positive and Gram-negative membranes. CONCLUSION: PK-12-KKP is an unlikely candidate for targeting intracellular bacteria, as the eukaryotic cell-penetrating ability is poor. SA-3, affected the cellular viability to an unacceptable degree. TPk showed acceptable uptake efficiency, high antimicrobial activity and relatively low toxicity, and it is the best potential lead peptide for further development.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bahnsen, Jesper S","Franzyk, Henrik","Sayers, Edward J","Jones, Arwyn T","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438954"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell penetrating antimicrobial peptides prospectives for targeting intracellular infections","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-438954","identifier":[{"id":"84939961839","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25777610","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4c51746d-782f-465f-a4f2-0e57fda51375"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33B0BB6AE401E341C631386A4A32C094"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Natural Products and Peptides"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jesper S","key":"bahnsenpau","last":"Bahnsen","name":"Bahnsen, Jesper S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"franzykpau","last":"Franzyk","locid":"5120ce68-6886-4ac8-8178-310a47d19261","name":"Franzyk, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2822-1927","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Edward J","key":"sayerspau","last":"Sayers","name":"Sayers, Edward J","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arwyn T","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Arwyn T","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne M","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b0450b3-f634-47ec-912c-b07ecd943be8","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","name_org":"Nielsen, Hanne M","orcid":"0000-0002-7285-9100","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25777610"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11095-014-1550-9","issn":["07248741","1573904X"],"issn_org":["07248741"],"issue":"5","journal":"Pharmaceutical Research","pages":"1546-56","status":"p","title":"Pharmaceutical Research","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939961839"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4c51746d-782f-465f-a4f2-0e57fda51375"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cell-penetrating antimicrobial peptides - prospectives for targeting intracellular infections","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438954","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patient crowding in emergency departments (ED) is a common challenge and associated with worsened outcome for the patients. Previous studies on biomarkers in the ED setting has focused on identification of high risk patients, and and the ability to use biomarkers to identify low-risk patients has only been sparsely examined. The broader aims of the TRIAGE study are to develop methods to identify low-risk patients appropriate for early ED discharge by combining information from a wide range of new inflammatory biomarkers and vital signs, the present baseline article aims to describe the formation of the TRIAGE database and characteristize the included patients. METHODS: We included consecutive patients ≥ 17 years admitted to hospital after triage staging in the ED. Blood samples for a biobank were collected and plasma stored in a freezer (-80 °C). Triage was done by a trained nurse using the Danish Emergency Proces Triage (DEPT) which categorizes patients as green (not urgent), yellow (urgent), orange (emergent) or red (rescusitation). Presenting complaints, admission diagnoses, comorbidities, length of stay, and 'events' during admission (any of 20 predefined definitive treatments that necessitates in-hospital care), vital signs and routine laboratory tests taken in the ED were aslo included in the database. RESULTS: Between September 5(th) 2013 and December 6(th) 2013, 6005 patients were included in the database and the biobank (94.1 % of all admissions). Of these, 1978 (32.9 %) were categorized as green, 2386 (39.7 %) yellow, 1616 (26.9 %) orange and 25 (0.4 %) red. Median age was 62 years (IQR 46-76), 49.8 % were male and median length of stay was 1 day (IQR 0-4). No events were found in 2658 (44.2 %) and 158 (2.6 %) were admitted to intensive or intermediate-intensive care unit and 219 (3.6 %) died within 30 days. A higher triage acuity level was associated with numerous events, including acute surgery, endovascular intervention, i.v. treatment, cardiac arrest, stroke, admission to intensive care, hospital transfer, and mortality within 30 days (p < 0.001). CONCLUSION: The TRIAGE database has been completed and includes data and blood samples from 6005 unselected consecutive hospitalized patients. More than 40 % experienced no events and were therefore potentially unnecessary hospital admissions.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Plesner, Louis Lind","Iversen, Anne Kristine Servais","Langkjær, Sandra","Nielsen, Ture Lange","Østervig, Rebecca","Warming, Peder Emil","Salam, Idrees Ahmad","Kristensen, Michael","Schou, Morten","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Forberg, Jakob Lundager","Køber, Lars","Rasmussen, Lars S","Sölétormos, György","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457004"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the formation and design of the triage study baseline data on 000000006005 consecutive patients admitted to hospital from the emergency department","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-015-0184-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-457004","identifier":[{"id":"84949293745","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4667414","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26626588","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6a6b8756-f935-414f-9627-4ed15cfe20bb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-675F4A61EC6BF4DFF7243AF2CEE09559"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-015-0184-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louis Lind","key":"plesnerlouislindpau","last":"Plesner","name":"Plesner, Louis Lind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Kristine Servais","key":"iversenannekristineservaispau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Anne Kristine Servais","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sandra","key":"langkjærsandrapau","last":"Langkjær","name":"Langkjær, Sandra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ture Lange","key":"nielsenturelangepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Ture Lange","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rebecca","key":"østervigrebeccapau","last":"Østervig","name":"Østervig, Rebecca","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peder Emil","key":"warmingpederemilpau","last":"Warming","name":"Warming, Peder Emil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Idrees Ahmad","key":"salamidreesahmadpau","last":"Salam","name":"Salam, Idrees Ahmad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kristensenmichaelpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"schoumortenpau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenjesperpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Lundager","key":"forbergjakoblundagerpau","last":"Forberg","name":"Forberg, Jakob Lundager","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"køberlarspau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars S","key":"rasmussenlarsspau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37e36b99-34dd-471f-b09b-d93e72940ec0","name":"Rasmussen, Lars S","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"György","key":"sölétormosgyörgypau","last":"Sölétormos","name":"Sölétormos, György","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bente Klarlund","key":"pedersenbenteklarlundpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d38d54e-e0d1-4397-98ca-6d8c9b78606d","name":"Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenkasperpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26626588"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13049-015-0184-1","issn":["17577241"],"journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","pages":"1-9","paperid":"23:106","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949293745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6a6b8756-f935-414f-9627-4ed15cfe20bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The formation and design of the TRIAGE study--baseline data on 6005 consecutive patients admitted to hospital from the emergency department","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457004","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"A cliff exposure of the Eocene Lillebælt Clay Formation, on the Røsnæs peninsula of Zealand, Denmark, has yielded a diverse trace-fossil assemblage. The trace fossils are described formally for the first time and assigned to Phymatoderma melvillensis, unnamed clusters of small burrows, Ophiomorpha nodosa, Spongeliomorpha isp., Dreginozoum beckumensis, Bichordites isp., Chondrites isp., Atollites zitteli? and ?Rhizocorallium isp. The preservation of the trace fossils is strongly related to early diagenetic enhancement. The trace-fossil assemblage is dominated by a combination of dwelling and feeding burrows. The bioturbation took place in very clean clay of a shelf setting far offshore. The trace-fossil assemblage is indicative of the distal Cruziana ichnofacies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jan Kresten","Milàn, Jesper","Mesfun, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494406"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","VNG Norge"],"keyword":["Bioturbation","Ethology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["GXU -Gladsaxe 10. Klasse og Ungdomsskole"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trace fossils from the eocene lillebælt clay formation røsnæs peninsula denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14241/asgp.2015.020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-494406","identifier":[{"id":"84944740547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a90971d1-2477-4007-b084-304068c99f68"],"keyword":["Bioturbation","Ethology","Ichnofacies","Ichnotaxonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B8C7A4CE908FE00D13F0FBC8A9026ADC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14241/asgp.2015.020","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161190763/Nielsen_2015_Trace_fossils.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"vng norge","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VNG Norge","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["GXU -Gladsaxe 10. Klasse og Ungdomsskole"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Kresten","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jan Kresten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"milànpau","last":"Milàn","locid":"bd8be89e-1386-4a3b-adc6-350b299d7b69","name":"Milàn, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Daniel","key":"mesfunpau","last":"Mesfun","name":"Mesfun, Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14241/asgp.2015.020","issn":["02089068"],"issue":"3","journal":"Annales Societatis Geologorum Poloniae","pages":"493-505","status":"p","title":"Annales Societatis Geologorum Poloniae","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944740547"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a90971d1-2477-4007-b084-304068c99f68"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trace fossils from the eocene Lillebælt clay formation, Røsnæs Peninsula, Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494406","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Target temperature management is recommended as a neuroprotective strategy after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Potential effects of different target temperatures on cognitive impairment commonly described in survivors have not been investigated sufficiently. The primary aim of this study was to evaluate whether a target temperature of 33°C compared with 36°C was favorable for cognitive function; the secondary aim was to describe cognitive impairment in cardiac arrest survivors in general. METHODS AND RESULTS: Study sites included 652 cardiac arrest survivors originally randomized and stratified for site to temperature control at 33°C or 36°C within the Target Temperature Management trial. Survival until 180 days after the arrest was 52% (33°C, n=178/328; 36°C, n=164/324). Survivors were invited to a face-to-face follow-up, and 287 cardiac arrest survivors (33°C, n=148/36°C, n=139) were assessed with tests for memory (Rivermead Behavioural Memory Test), executive functions (Frontal Assessment Battery), and attention/mental speed (Symbol Digit Modalities Test). A control group of 119 matched patients hospitalized for acute ST-segment-elevation myocardial infarction without cardiac arrest performed the same assessments. Half of the cardiac arrest survivors had cognitive impairment, which was mostly mild. Cognitive outcome did not differ (P>0.30) between the 2 temperature groups (33°C/36°C). Compared with control subjects with ST-segment-elevation myocardial infarction, attention/mental speed was more affected among cardiac arrest patients, but results for memory and executive functioning were similar. CONCLUSIONS: Cognitive function was comparable in survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest when a temperature of 33°C and 36°C was targeted. Cognitive impairment detected in cardiac arrest survivors was also common in matched control subjects with ST-segment-elevation myocardial infarction not having had a cardiac arrest. CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION: URL: http://www.clinicaltrials.gov. Unique identifier: NCT01946932.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Lilja, Gisela","Nielsen, Niklas","Friberg, Hans","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nilsson, Fredrik","Pellis, Tommaso","Wetterslev, Jørn","Wise, Matt P","Bosch, Frank","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Brunetti, Iole","Buratti, Azul Forti","Hassager, Christian","Hofgren, Caisa","Insorsi, Angelo","Kuiper, Michael","Martini, Alice","Palmer, Nicki","Rundgren, Malin","Rylander, Christian","van der Veen, Annelou","Wanscher, Michael","Watkins, Helen","Cronberg, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507210"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cognition","Electrocardiography","Europe","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Patient Outcome Assessment","Risk Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cognitive function in survivors of out of hospital cardiac arrest after target temperature management at 000000000033 c versus 000000000036 c","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.114.014414","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-507210","identifier":[{"id":"25681466","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84929278828","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bea0e14b-993d-48c5-bea7-141664cd06bf"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cognition","Electrocardiography","Europe","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Patient Outcome Assessment","Risk Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D8DA05C1C9E4E084AA453699C074155C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.114.014414","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fredrik","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Fredrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matt P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt P","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frank","key":"boschpau","last":"Bosch","name":"Bosch, Frank","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Iole","key":"brunettipau","last":"Brunetti","name":"Brunetti, Iole","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Azul Forti","key":"burattipau","last":"Buratti","name":"Buratti, Azul Forti","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Caisa","key":"hofgrenpau","last":"Hofgren","name":"Hofgren, Caisa","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Angelo","key":"insorsipau","last":"Insorsi","name":"Insorsi, Angelo","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alice","key":"martinipau","last":"Martini","name":"Martini, Alice","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicki","key":"palmerpau","last":"Palmer","name":"Palmer, Nicki","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Malin","key":"rundgrenpau","last":"Rundgren","name":"Rundgren, Malin","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"rylanderpau","last":"Rylander","name":"Rylander, Christian","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annelou","key":"vanderveenpau","last":"van der Veen","name":"van der Veen, Annelou","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helen","key":"watkinspau","last":"Watkins","name":"Watkins, Helen","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25681466"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.114.014414","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"journal":"Circulation","pages":"1340-9","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"131"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929278828"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bea0e14b-993d-48c5-bea7-141664cd06bf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cognitive function in survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest after target temperature management at 33°C versus 36°C","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-507210","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Bradycardia is a common finding in patients undergoing therapeutic hypothermia (TH) following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA), presumably as a normal physiological response to low body temperature. We hypothesized that a normal physiological response with sinus bradycardia (SB) indicates less neurological damage and therefore would be associated with lower mortality. METHODS: We studied 234 consecutive comatose survivors of OHCA with presumed cardiac etiology and shockable primary rhythm, who underwent a full 24-h TH-protocol (33°C) at a tertiary heart center (years: 2004-2010). Primary endpoint was 180-day mortality; secondary endpoint was favorable neurological outcome (180-day cerebral performance category: 1-2). RESULTS: SB, defined as sinus rhythm <50 beats per minute during TH, was present in 115 (49%) patients. Baseline characteristics including sex, witnessed arrest, bystander cardiopulmonary resuscitation and time to return of spontaneous circulation were not different between SB- and no-SB patients. However, SB-patients were younger, 57±14 vs. 63±14 years, p<0.001 and less frequently had known heart failure (7% vs. 20%, p<0.01). Patients experiencing SB during the hypothermia phase of TH had a 17% 180-day mortality rate compared to 38% in no-SB patients (p<0.001), corresponding to a 180-day hazard ratio (HRadjusted=0.45 (0.23-0.88, p=0.02)) in the multivariable analysis. Similarly, SB during hypothermia was directly associated with lower odds of unfavorable neurological outcome (ORunadjusted=0.42 (0.23-0.75, p<0.01). CONCLUSION: Sinus bradycardia during therapeutic hypothermia is independently associated with a lower 180-day mortality rate and may thus be a novel, early marker of favorable outcome in comatose survivors of OHCA.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Hassager, Christian","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Søholm, Helle","Nielsen, Niklas","Wanscher, Michael","Køber, Lars","Pehrson, Steen","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-520960"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Bradycardia","Coma","Denmark","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Outcome Assessment Health Care","Prevalence","Retrospective Studies","Survival Rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sinus bradycardia during hypothermia in comatose survivors of out of hospital cardiac arrest a new early marker of favorable outcome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-520960","identifier":[{"id":"25619443","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84927647060","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d5780fd9-f609-4623-85f3-4d267a495c1a"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Bradycardia","Coma","Denmark","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Outcome Assessment (Health Care)","Prevalence","Retrospective Studies","Survival Rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39EB5CD5C8668A36EC6876A78CED6092"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Hartvig","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"søholmpau","last":"Søholm","name":"Søholm, Helle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen","key":"pehrsonpau","last":"Pehrson","locid":"081e7ed3-5467-4c96-9471-1519871354db","name":"Pehrson, Steen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25619443"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.12.031","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"36-42","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927647060"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d5780fd9-f609-4623-85f3-4d267a495c1a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sinus bradycardia during hypothermia in comatose survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest : a new early marker of favorable outcome?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-520960","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Brain injury affects neurologic function and quality of life in survivors after cardiac arrest. OBJECTIVE: To compare the effects of 2 target temperature regimens on long-term cognitive function and quality of life after cardiac arrest. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: In this multicenter, international, parallel group, assessor-masked randomized clinical trial performed from November 11, 2010, through January 10, 2013, we enrolled 950 unconscious adults with cardiac arrest of presumed cardiac cause from 36 intensive care units in Europe and Australia. Eleven patients were excluded from analysis for a total sample size of 939. INTERVENTIONS: Targeted temperature management at 33°C vs 36°C. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: Cognitive function was measured by the Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE) and assessed by observers through the Informant Questionnaire on Cognitive Decline in the Elderly (IQCODE). Patients reported their activities in daily life and mental recovery through Two Simple Questions and their quality of life through the Medical Outcomes Study 36-Item Short Form Health Survey, version 2. RESULTS: In the modified intent-to-treat population, including nonsurvivors, the median MMSE score was 14 in the 33°C group (interquartile range [IQR], 0-28) vs 17 in the 36°C group (IQR, 0-29) (P = .77), and the IQCODE score was 115 (IQR, 79-130) vs 115 (IQR, 80-130) (P = .57) in the 33°C and 36°C groups, respectively. The median MMSE score for survivors was within the reference range and similar (33°C group median, 28; IQR, 26-30; vs 36°C group median, 28; IQR, 25-30; P = .61). The median IQCODE score was within the minor deficit range (33°C group median, 79.5; IQR, 78.0-85.9; vs 36°C group median, 80.7; IQR, 78.0-86.9; P = .04). A total of 18.8% vs 17.5% of survivors reported needing help with everyday activities (P = .71), and 66.5% in the 33°C group vs 61.8% in the 36°C group reported that they thought they had made a complete mental recovery (P = .32). The mean (SD) mental component summary score was 49.1 (12.5) vs 49.0 (12.2) (P = .79), and the mean (SD) physical component summary score was 46.8 (13.8) and 47.5 (13.8) (P = .45), comparable to the population norm. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: Quality of life was good and similar in patients with cardiac arrest receiving targeted temperature management at 33°C or 36°C. Cognitive function was similar in both intervention groups, but many patients and observers reported impairment not detected previously by standard outcome scales. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01020916.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Cronberg, Tobias","Lilja, Gisela","Horn, Janneke","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Wise, Matt P","Pellis, Tommaso","Hovdenes, Jan","Gasche, Yvan","Åneman, Anders","Stammet, Pascal","Erlinge, David","Friberg, Hans","Hassager, Christian","Kuiper, Michael","Wanscher, Michael","Bosch, Frank","Cranshaw, Julius","Kleger, Gian-Reto","Persson, Stefan","Undén, Johan","Walden, Andrew","Winkel, Per","Wetterslev, Jørn","Nielsen, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-539783"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["TTM Trial Investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cognition Disorders","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Outcome Assessment Health Care","Quality of Life","Single Blind Method"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neurologic function and health related quality of life in patients following targeted temperature management at 000000000033 c vs 000000000036 c after out of hospital cardiac arrest a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-539783","identifier":[{"id":"25844993","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84931057233","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f52f56a6-b0bc-434a-88f4-51fc6cd9648c"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cognition Disorders","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Outcome Assessment (Health Care)","Quality of Life","Single-Blind Method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E74A4F3CF364151725C0CDAEA3722813"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ttm trial investigators","name":"TTM Trial Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gisela","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Gisela","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matt P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matt P","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"gaschepau","last":"Gas