{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In 2007, a national skin cancer prevention campaign was launched to reduce the UV exposure of the Danish population. To improve campaign evaluation a questionnaire validation using UV-dosimeters was initiated. AIM: To show the feasibility of dosimeters for national representative studies and of smartphones as a data collection tool. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Participants were sent a dosimeter which they wore for 7 days, received a short diary questionnaire by text message each day and subsequently a longer questionnaire. Correlation between responses from questionnaire, smartphone diaries and dosimeters were examined. RESULTS: This study shows a 99.5% return rate (n = 205) of the dosimeters by ordinary mail and high response-rates for a smartphone questionnaire dairy. Correlation coefficients for outdoor-time reported through smartphones and dosimeters as average by week 0.62 (0.39-0.77), P < 0.001 (n = 40). Correlation coefficient for outdoor time estimated by questionnaire and dosimeters were 0.42 (0.11-0.64), P = 0.008. The subjective perception of the weather was the only covariate significantly influencing questionnaire estimates of actual outdoor exposure. We showed that dosimeter studies are feasible in national settings and that smartphones are a useful tool for monitoring and collecting UV behavior data. CONCLUSION: We found diary data reported on a daily basis through smartphones more strongly associated with actual outdoor time than questionnaire data. Our results demonstrate tools and possible considerations for executing a UV behavior questionnaire validation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Køster, Brian","Søndergaard, Jens","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Allen, Martin","Bjerregaard, Mette","Olsen, Anja","Bentzen, Joan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632052"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Feasibility study","Personal UV dosimetry","Ultraviolet radiation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of smartphone diaries and personal dosimeters to quantitatively study exposure to ultraviolet radiation in a small national sample","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/phpp.12179","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632052","identifier":[{"id":"25850335","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84940787037","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-cd4e0ce1-730e-473a-b8e5-5e2936dcdf77"],"keyword":["Feasibility study","Personal UV-dosimetry","Skin cancer prevention","Smartphone diary","Ultraviolet radiation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8F8453C61ACDB323B7B922779BA8ADA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/phpp.12179","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"køsterpau","last":"Køster","locid":"b5dacba2-0e04-4301-93cc-f6c6ab09b564","name":"Køster, Brian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper B","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"allenpau","last":"Allen","name":"Allen, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Anja","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joan","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","name":"Bentzen, Joan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25850335"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/phpp.12179","issn":["09054383","16000781"],"issn_org":["09054383"],"issue":"5","journal":"Photodermatology, Photoimmunology & Photomedicine","pages":"252-260","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Photodermatology, Photoimmunology & Photomedicine","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940787037"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cd4e0ce1-730e-473a-b8e5-5e2936dcdf77"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feasibility of smartphone diaries and personal dosimeters to quantitatively study exposure to ultraviolet radiation in a small national sample","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-632052","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Many patients experience acute or chronic pain. The options for treating these pain conditions are many, and particularly products for topical application are gaining ground. NSAID for topical use is a good alternative to NSAID administered orally due to less systemic side effects. Transdermally delivered opioids have proven to be as effective as morphine in pain management of chronic, moderate to severe pain. The steady delivery and lower risk of breakthrough pain overweigh the higher cost and risk of adverse events compared to the orally delivered opioids.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Niels Martin","Holmgaard, Rikke","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Sørensen, Jens Ahm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-633212"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["English Abstract","Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visse analgetika kan med fordel anvendes transdermalt","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85016501854","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-633212","identifier":[{"id":"85016501854","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25749289","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-d1610016-a332-4476-ade9-8a7ea321ec74"],"keyword":["English Abstract","Journal Article"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC2D5C0E0B16506F6128FCC43E7828E4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Martin","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"859d1db6-e5ba-4534-8316-eaae5c2fc948","name":"Jensen, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-1725-4096","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"holmgaardpau","last":"Holmgaard","locid":"7d4c8fb0-ed6b-42f4-913c-dde65ee144d1","name":"Holmgaard, Rikke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25749289"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"9","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"2-6","paperid":"V09140487","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"177"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016501854"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d1610016-a332-4476-ade9-8a7ea321ec74"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Visse analgetika kan med fordel anvendes transdermalt","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-633212","year":"2015","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"'Symbolic violence' is committed, however well-intentionally, by the imposition of particular conceptualizations of what information, in what form and quality, is needed in order to make an 'informed choice' and hence - by questionable segue - a high quality decision. The social and cultural forms of relevant cognitive capital possessed by those who fail, because of their low general literacy, professionally-set knowledge tests of functional health literacy, are being ignored. Failing to recognise and exploit a particular form of functional decision literacy, in fact leads to symbolic violence being experienced by individuals at any and all levels of general literacy. It leads many to adopt the same range of avoidant and other undesirable strategies within healthcare situations observed in those of low basic literacy. The alternative response we propose exploits the alternative generic decision literacy which comes in the form of the ability to access and use the decision-relevant resources provided for many consumer services and products on comparison websites and magazines. The methodology is the simple form of multi-criteria analysis in which the products' ratings on multiple criteria are combined with criterion weights (supplied by the site) to produce scores and 'best buys' and 'good value for money' verdicts. Our alternative approach extends this approach to healthcare options and permits the incorporation of personal criterion weights in furtherance of person-centred care. Health informaticians, especially those in the decision support field, should build on this widespread generic competence. The fact that it is generic, far from implying context insensitivity, can be seen as a necessary basis for achieving context-sensitivity and sensitivisation at the level of the individual person as they experience a lifelong sequence of healthcare decisions.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Salkeld, Glenn","Dowie, Jack"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638196"],"event":{"end":"2015-08-16","place":"Curitiba, br","start":"2015-08-15","title":"http://cshi2015.org/","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Empowerment","Health literacy","Informed choice","Person centred care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health informatics can avoid committing symbolic violence by recognizing and supporting generic decision making competencies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/978-1-61499-574-6-172","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-638196","identifier":[{"id":"84952043098","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26262547","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e2e1506c-88fe-4396-a20e-114339edfbed"],"keyword":["Empowerment","Health literacy","Informed choice","Person-centred care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3FC051445F2856EC4643A6FD14C80FD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/978-1-61499-574-6-172","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Medicine (Svendborg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Kjer","key":"kaltoftpau","last":"Kaltoft","locid":"6f7d182a-c64a-413a-84e7-40365be224fe","name":"Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-8297","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Glenn","key":"salkeldpau","last":"Salkeld","name":"Salkeld, Glenn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack","key":"dowiepau","last":"Dowie","locid":"4c165795-2471-415a-9a87-aa348af42431","name":"Dowie, Jack","orcid":"0000-0002-4572-9562","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elizabeth M.","key":"boryckipedh","last":"Borycki","name":"Borycki, Elizabeth M.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andre W.","key":"kushnirukpedh","last":"Kushniruk","name":"Kushniruk, Andre W.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Craig E.","key":"kuziemskypedh","last":"Kuziemsky","name":"Kuziemsky, Craig E.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"nøhrpedh","last":"Nøhr","name":"Nøhr, Christian","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pmid":["26262547"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/978-1-61499-574-6-172","eisbn":["9781614995739"],"issn":["09269630"],"pages":"172-177","series":"Studies in Health Technology and Informatics","status":"p","subtitle":"Many Places, Many Users, Many Contexts, Many Uses","title":"Context Sensitive Health Informatics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952043098"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e2e1506c-88fe-4396-a20e-114339edfbed"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Health Informatics Can Avoid Committin