{"abstract":"We consider determinantal point processes on the d-dimensional unit sphere Sd . These are finite point processes exhibiting repulsiveness and with moment properties determined by a certain determinant whose entries are specified by a so-called kernel which we assume is a complex covariance function defined on Sd × Sd . We review the appealing properties of such processes, including their specific moment properties, density expressions and simulation procedures. Particularly, we characterize and construct isotropic DPPs models on Sd , where it becomes essential to specify the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions in a spectral representation for the kernel, and we figure out how repulsive isotropic DPPs can be. Moreover, we discuss the shortcomings of adapting existing models for isotropic covariance functions and consider strategies for developing new models, including a useful spectral approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Jesper","Nielsen, Morten","Porcu, Emilio","Rubak, Ege"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180025"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Chile"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidad Tecnica Federico Santa Maria"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determinantal point process models on the sphere","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/97725724/math_csgb_2015_13.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180025","ids":["au-58e2734e-a400-4e7e-b83b-a4648f1d67a8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-387F14B5025F0F55915E2EAFCCF15373"],"oa_link":[{"access":"