Multi-Party Computation for Binary Circuits Based on Oblivious Transfer","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-254115","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Doppler tomography is a well-known method in astrophysics to image the accretion flow, often in the shape of thin discs, in compact binary stars. As accretion discs rotate, all emitted line radiation is Doppler-shifted. In fast-ion Dα (FIDA) spectroscopy measurements in magnetically confined plasma, the Dα-photons are likewise Doppler-shifted ultimately due to gyration of the fast ions. In either case, spectra of Doppler-shifted line emission are sensitive to the velocity distribution of the emitters. Astrophysical Doppler tomography has lead to images of accretion discs of binaries revealing bright spots, spiral structures and flow patterns. Fusion plasma Doppler tomography has led to an image of the fast-ion velocity distribution function in the tokamak ASDEX Upgrade. This image matched numerical simulations very well. Here we discuss achievements of the Doppler tomography approach, its promise and limits, analogies and differences in astrophysical and fusion plasma Doppler tomography and what can be learned by comparison of these applications.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Salewski, Mirko","Geiger, B.","Heidbrink, W. W.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Madsen, Jens","Moseev, D.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stagner, L.","Steeghs, D.","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardini, G.","Weiland, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309173"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute","University of California at San Diego","University of Warwick"],"keyword":["Accretion discs","Fast ion D alpha spectroscopy","Fast ions","Spectroscopy","Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"doppler tomography in fusion plasmas and astrophysics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0741-3335/57/1/014021","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309173","identifier":[{"id":"84914706451","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0f3ce70f-6adb-48e1-ab54-be39927a9412"],"keyword":["Accretion discs","Fast ion D-alpha spectroscopy","Fast ions","Spectroscopy","Tomamak","Tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A0567FBF7F0DDA316963B4469D124F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0741-3335/57/1/014021","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/105300015/salewski2015ppcf.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california at san diego","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at San Diego","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"geigerpau","last":"Geiger","name":"Geiger, B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"W. W.","key":"heidbrinkpau","last":"Heidbrink","name":"Heidbrink, W. W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Bang","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank","key":"leipoldpau","last":"Leipold","locid":"fb1ca27f-36e0-43a2-8779-3d8135a2a8dc","name":"Leipold, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3107-6713","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"moseevpau","last":"Moseev","name":"Moseev, D.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefan Kragh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"stagnerpau","last":"Stagner","name":"Stagner, L.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"steeghspau","last":"Steeghs","name":"Steeghs, D.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"stejnerpedersenpau","last":"Stejner Pedersen","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"tardinipau","last":"Tardini","name":"Tardini, G.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"weilandpau","last":"Weiland","name":"Weiland, M.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/0741-3335/57/1/014021","issn":["07413335","13616587"],"issn_org":["07413335"],"issue":"1","journal":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","pages":"014021","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84914706451"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0f3ce70f-6adb-48e1-ab54-be39927a9412"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Doppler tomography in fusion plasmas and astrophysics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309173","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the ascending aorta, atherosclerotic plaque formation, which is a risk factor for cerebrovascular events, most often occurs along the inner curvature. Atherosclerosis is a multifactorial disease, but the predilection site for the aortic vessel degradation is probably flow dependent. To better understand the aortic flow and especially the complex flow patterns, the ascending aorta was scanned intraoperatively in patients undergoing heart surgery using the angle-independent vector velocity ultrasound method Transverse Oscillation (TO). The primary aim of the study was to analyze systolic backflow in relation to atherosclerosis. Thirteen patients with normal aortic valves were included in to the study. TO implemented on a conventional US scanner (ProFocus 2202 UltraView, BK Medical, Herlev, Denmark) with a linear array transducer (8670, BK Medical, Herlev, Denmark) was used intraoperatively on the ascending aorta in long axis view. The presence of systolic backflow, visualized with TO, was correlated to aortic atherosclerosis, to systolic velocities obtained with transesophageal echocardiography and cardiac output obtained with pulmonary artery catheter thermodilution, to gender, age, aortic diameter, left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) and previous myocardial infarctions (MI). Systolic backflow in the ascending aorta was present for 38% (n=5) of the patients. The location of the backflow was strongly associated to the location of the plaques (p<0.005), and backflow was associated to high systolic velocities (p<0.05). The other obtained parameters were not associated to systolic backflow. It was shown that systolic backflow is a common flow feature in the ascending aorta, and that backflow is associated to atherosclerotic plaques and systolic velocities. The study indicates that vector flow imaging using TO can provide important blood flow information in the assessment of atherosclerosis.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Jensen, Maiken Brit","Lund, Jens Teglgaard","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-322418"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-24","place":"Taipei, tw","start":"2015-10-21","title":"2015 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ascending aorta","Atherosclerosis","Systolic backflow","Transverse oscillation","Vector velocity imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vector flow imaging of the ascending aorta are systolic backflow and atherosclerosis related","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/117487151/hansen_kl_ieee2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-322418","identifier":[{"id":"84962030137","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3beb8d0a-3e17-4c11-adbb-cfe94327f8e6"],"keyword":["Ascending aorta","Atherosclerosis","Systolic backflow","Transverse Oscillation","Vector velocity imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6081071314C92289D9AE86E3B8C62CAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/117487151/hansen_kl_ieee2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ULTSYM.2015.0069","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic",