":"Dorette Sophie","key":"müllerstöverpau","last":"Müller-Stöver","locid":"61683248-325a-49da-846c-76bb595a24b4","name":"Müller-Stöver, Dorette Sophie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"ccc14efd-163a-46ec-865c-cdfd086c15fe","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5ca0a43f-9663-4139-8ff3-d8ad6bd33efb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Forgasning og fremstilling af halmkoks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-332112","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"High-resolution γ-ray spectroscopy (GRS) measurements resolve spectral shapes of Dopplerbroadened γ-rays. We calculate weight functions describing velocity-space sensitivities of any two-step reaction GRS measurements in magnetized plasmas using the resonant nuclear reaction 9Be(α, nγ)12C as an example. The energy-dependent cross sections of this reaction suggest that GRS is sensitive to alpha particles above about 1.7 MeV and highly sensitive to alpha particles at the resonance energies of the reaction. Here we demonstrate that highresolution two-step reaction GRS measurements are not only selective in energy but also in pitch angle. They can be highly sensitive in particular pitch angle ranges and completely insensitive in others. Moreover, GRS weight functions allow rapid calculation of γ-ray energy spectra from fast-ion distribution functions, additionally revealing how many photons any given alpha-particle velocity-space region contributes to the measurements in each γ-ray energy bin.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Salewski, Mirko","Nocente, M.","Gorini, G.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Kiptily, V.G.","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Madsen, Jens","Moseev, D.","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardocchi, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348919"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Research Council of Italy","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Milan - Bicocca"],"keyword":["Energetic particles","Gamma ray spectroscopy","Tokamaks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"velocity space observation regions of high resolution two step reaction gamma ray spectroscopy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/116642473/salewski2015nf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-348919","identifier":[{"id":"84941584933","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-94bdadbc-3576-46e4-b6dd-4f773d2be2b7"],"keyword":["Energetic particles","Gamma-ray spectroscopy","Tokamaks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A0FF1FE36B60A9B00D0664755557A8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0029-5515/55/9/093029","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/116642473/salewski2015nf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of milan bicocca","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan - Bicocca","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"united kingdom atomic energy authority","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"national research council of italy","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Research Council of Italy","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"nocentepau","last":"Nocente","name":"Nocente, M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"gorinipau","last":"Gorini","name":"Gorini, G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"V.G.","key":"kiptilypau","last":"Kiptily","name":"Kiptily, V.G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Bang","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank","key":"leipoldpau","last":"Leipold","locid":"fb1ca27f-36e0-43a2-8779-3d8135a2a8dc","name":"Leipold, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3107-6713","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"moseevpau","last":"Moseev","name":"Moseev, D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefan Kragh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Stejner","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","name_org":"Pedersen, Morten Stejner","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"tardocchipau","last":"Tardocchi","name":"Tardocchi, M.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/0029-5515/55/9/093029","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"9","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","pages":"093029","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941584933"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-94bdadbc-3576-46e4-b6dd-4f773d2be2b7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Velocity-space observation regions of high-resolution two-step reaction gamma-ray spectroscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348919","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"GPS data collection has become an important means of investigating travel behaviour. This is because such data ideally provide far more detailed information on route choice and travel patterns over a longer time period than possible from traditional travel survey methods. Wearing a GPS unit is furthermore less requiring for the respondents than filling out (large) questionnaires. It places however high requirements to the post-processing of the data. This study developed and tested a combined fuzzy logic and GIS-based algorithm to process raw GPS data. The algorithm is applied to GPS data collected in the highly complex large-scale multi-modal transport network of the Greater Copenhagen area. It detects trips, trip legs and distinguishes between five modes of transport. The algorithm was validated by comparing with a control questionnaire collected among the same persons and a sensitivity analysis was performed. This showed that the algorithm (i) identified corresponding trip legs for 82% of the reported trip legs, (ii) avoided classifying non-trips such as scatter around activities as trip legs, (iii) identified the correct mode of transport for more than 90% of trip legs, and (iv) were robust towards the specification of the model parameters and thresholds. The method thus makes it possible to use GPS for travel surveys in large-scale multi-modal networks.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Thomas Kjær","Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Halldórsdóttir, Katrín","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-366616"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithms","Complex networks","Data handling","Fuzzy logic","GIS","GPS data","Geographic Information Systems","Global Positioning System","Multimodal transport","Revealed preference data","Sensitivity analysis","Surveys","Transportation","Transportation routes","Travel behaviour","Wearable technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved methods to deduct trip legs and mode from travel surveys using wearable gps devices a case study from the greater copenhagen area","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compenvurbsys.2015.04.001","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-366616","identifier":[{"id":"84949726330","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cfc2668a-a7ca-4bbb-8f2e-52361cf95deb"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Complex networks","Data handling","Fuzzy logic","GIS","GPS data","GPS data processing","Geographic information systems","Global positioning system","Handheld GPS","Mode of transport","Multi-modal travel survey","Multi-modal travels","Multimodal network","Multimodal transport","Revealed preference data","Revealed preference datum","Sensitivity analysis","Surveys","Transportation","Transportation routes","Travel behaviour","Wearable technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-060A09E00BE0B64AFDE0E5F3822DEA2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compenvurbsys.2015.04.001","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport, Traffic modelling and planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Kjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6499d80a-6f70-4824-91c8-d34b630c2e24","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-0979-9667","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrín","key":"halldórsdóttirpau","last":"Halldórsdóttir","locid":"4f8d1a3d-f76a-4afb-81a0-bf96bec9c97c","name":"Halldórsdóttir, Katrín","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.compenvurbsys.2015.04.001","issn":["01989715","18737587"],"issn_org":["01989715"],"journal":"Computers, Environment and Urban Systems","pages":"301-313","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Computers, Environment and Urban Systems","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949726330"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cfc2668a-a7ca-4bbb-8f2e-52361cf95deb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved methods to deduct trip legs and mode from travel surveys using wearable GPS devices: A case study from the Greater Copenhagen area","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-366616","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We develop a wavefunction approach to describe the scattering of two photons on a quantum emitter embedded in a one-dimensional waveguide. Our method allows us to calculate the exact dynamics of the complete system at all times, as well as the transmission properties of the emitter. We show that the nonlinearity of the emitter with respect to incoming photons depends strongly on the emitter excitation and the spectral shape of the incoming pulses, resulting in transmission of the photons which depends crucially on their separation and width. In addition, for counter-propagating pulses, we analyze the induced level of quantum correlations in the scattered state, and we show that the emitter behaves as a nonlinear beam-splitter when the spectral width of the photon pulses is similar to the emitter decay rate.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nysteen, Anders","Kristensen, Philip Trøst","McCutcheon, Dara","Nielsen, Per Kær","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379607"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Decay organic","Optical waveguide","Optical waveguides","Photons","Quant ph cond mat mes hall","Quantum Theory","Quantum correlations","Quantum emitters","Waveguides"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scattering of two photons on a quantum emitter in a one dimensional waveguide exact dynamics and induced correlations","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/106931509/1367_2630_17_2_023030.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379607","identifier":[{"id":"84924261088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-faca4e17-32d2-4679-bef4-0a6b6e36cd8b"],"keyword":["Counterpropagating","Decay (organic)","Few-photon scattering","One-dimensional waveguides","Optical waveguide","Optical waveguides","Photon correlation","Photon correlations","Photon scattering","Photons","Quant-ph cond-mat.mes-hall","Quantum correlations","Quantum emitters","Quantum theory","Transmission property","Two-level emitter","Waveguides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-251D42DF48E3968CDEB17193F00BF76E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/106931509/1367_2630_17_2_023030.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/17/2/023030","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nysteenpau","last":"Nysteen","locid":"feb12213-6336-4444-bc91-486323195b3a","name":"Nysteen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip Trøst","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"1f8487dd-eb6e-4260-a533-315a5d05c79c","name":"Kristensen, Philip Trøst","orcid":"0000-0001-5804-1989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dara","key":"mccutcheonpau","last":"McCutcheon","locid":"a31f29f9-266d-4152-9553-7e81c5497fe4","name":"McCutcheon, Dara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1367-2630/17/2/023030","issn":["13672630"],"issue":"2","journal":"New Journal of Physics","paperid":"023030","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"New Journal of Physics","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924261088"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-faca4e17-32d2-4679-bef4-0a6b6e36cd8b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Scattering of two photons on a quantum emitter in a one-dimensional waveguide: exact dynamics and induced correlations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379607","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The aim of the CATCH (CArdiac cT in the treatment of acute CHest pain) trial was to investigate the long-term clinical impact of a coronary computed tomographic angiography (CTA)-guided treatment strategy in patients with recent acute-onset chest pain compared to standard care. BACKGROUND: The prognostic implications of a coronary CTA-guided treatment strategy have not been compared in a randomized fashion to standard care in patients referred for acute-onset chest pain. METHODS: Patients with acute chest pain but normal electrocardiograms and troponin values were randomized to treatment guided by either coronary CTA or standard care (bicycle exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial perfusion imaging). In the coronary CTA-guided group, a functional test was included in cases of nondiagnostic coronary CTA images or coronary stenoses of borderline severity. The primary endpoint was a composite of cardiac death, myocardial infarction (MI), hospitalization for unstable angina pectoris (UAP), late symptom-driven revascularizations, and readmission for chest pain. RESULTS: We randomized 299 patients to coronary CTA-guided strategy and 301 to standard care. After inclusion, 24 patients withdrew their consent. The median (interquartile range) follow-up duration was 18.7 (range 16.8 to 20.1) months. In the coronary CTA-guided group, 30 patients (11%) had a primary endpoint versus 47 patients (16%) in the standard care group (p = 0.04; hazard ratio [HR]: 0.62 [95% confidence interval: 0.40 to 0.98]). A major adverse cardiac event (cardiac death, MI, hospitalization for UAP, and late symptom-driven revascularization) was observed in 5 patients (2 MIs, 3 UAPs) in the coronary CTA-guided group versus 14 patients (1 cardiac death, 7 MIs, 5 UAPs, 1 late symptom-driven revascularization) in the standard care group (p = 0.04; HR: 0.36 [95% CI: 0.16 to 0.95]). Differences in cardiac death and MI (8 vs. 2) were insignificant (p = 0.06). CONCLUSIONS: A coronary CTA-guided treatment strategy appears to improve clinical outcome in patients with recent acute-onset chest pain and normal electrocardiograms and troponin values compared to standard care with a functional test. (Cardiac-CT in the Treatment of Acute Chest Pain [CATCH]; NCT01534000).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Linde, Jesper J","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Sørgaard, Mathias","Kelbæk, Henning","Jensen, Gorm B","Kühl, Jørgen T","Hindsø, Louise","Køber, Lars","Nielsen, Walter B","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-423847"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term clinical impact of coronary ct angiography in patients with recent acute onset chest pain the randomized controlled catch trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-423847","identifier":[{"id":"84959208227","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26577263","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-331b2cc1-75ba-40cd-8cb3-4ba1dc229918"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7EF5E3C4BE7B63ECC0934EECC8CF9035"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jesper J","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Jesper J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","name_org":"Hove, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"sørgaardpau","last":"Sørgaard","name":"Sørgaard, Mathias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henning","key":"kelbækpau","last":"Kelbæk","locid":"6b4d4aaf-2b8e-4614-8cdd-41bb2577b701","name":"Kelbæk, Henning","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gorm B","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Gorm B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen T","key":"kühlpau","last":"Kühl","name":"Kühl, Jørgen T","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"hindsøpau","last":"Hindsø","name":"Hindsø, Louise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Walter B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Walter B","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus F","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","name_org":"Kofoed, Klaus F","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26577263"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcmg.2015.07.015","issn":["18767591","1936878X"],"issn_org":["1936878X"],"issue":"12","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"1404-13","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","title_org":"J A C C: Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959208227"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-331b2cc1-75ba-40cd-8cb3-4ba1dc229918"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-Term Clinical Impact of Coronary CT Angiography in Patients With Recent Acute-Onset Chest Pain : The Randomized Controlled CATCH Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-423847","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT Neuroscience has fundamentally changed the understanding of learning and memory within recent years. Here, the authors discuss a number of specific areas where they believe new understanding of the CNS from basic science is having a fundamental impact on neurorehabilitation and is leading to new therapeutic approaches. These areas have constituted a basis for development of some basic principles for neurorehabilitation: Optimal rehabilitation should involve (a) active (patient) participation in the training, (b) training that does not only involve many repetitions, but also continues to challenge the skill of the training person, (c) motivation and reward, (d) intensive training and practice over a long time, (e) careful organization of the training in relation to other activities, and (f) incorporation of other potentially beneficial parameters such as sleep and diet. It should in this relation also be pointed out that albeit neurorehabilitation may be predicted to have the most optimal effect early in life and as soon after injury as possible, there is no reason to believe that beneficial effects of training may not be obtained late in life or several years after injury.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Bo","Willerslev-Olsen, Maria","Christiansen, Lasse","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Lorentzen, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437668"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Helene Elsass Center, Charlottenlund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"science based neurorehabilitation recommendations for neurorehabilitation from basic science","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-437668","identifier":[{"id":"25575219","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84920848743","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4a0bd4f3-bf2a-4b50-9973-e535400742b3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77ABD983808B38744E569B0B4CCBDD4A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Motor Control","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Neural Control of Movement"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Helene Elsass Center, Charlottenlund"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"willerslevolsenpau","last":"Willerslev-Olsen","locid":"58638ef9-1900-4f20-8a44-899fdf6dae22","name":"Willerslev-Olsen, Maria","orcid":"0000-0001-7817-6610","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"bb3cbbb6-5540-42a7-8bdb-b9ded2314867","name":"Christiansen, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-9316-1529","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"lundbyejensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jakob","key":"lorentzenpau","last":"Lorentzen","name":"Lorentzen, Jakob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25575219"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00222895.2014.931273","issn":["00222895","19401027"],"issn_org":["00222895"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Motor Behavior","pages":"7-17","status":"p","title":"Journal of Motor Behavior","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920848743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4a0bd4f3-bf2a-4b50-9973-e535400742b3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Science-based neurorehabilitation : Recommendations for neurorehabilitation from basic science","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437668","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Despite a lack of randomized trials in comatose survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) with an initial non-shockable rhythm (NSR), guidelines recommend induced hypothermia to be considered in these patients. We assessed the effect on outcome of two levels of induced hypothermia in comatose patient resuscitated from NSR. METHODS: Hundred and seventy-eight patients out of 950 in the TTM trial with an initial NSR were randomly assigned to targeted temperature management at either 33°C (TTM33, n=96) or 36°C (TTM36, n=82). We assessed mortality, neurologic function (Cerebral Performance Score (CPC) and modified Rankin Scale (mRS)), and organ dysfunction (Sequential Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score). RESULTS: Patients with NSR were older, had longer time to ROSC, less frequently had bystander CPR and had higher lactate levels at admission compared to patients with shockable rhythm, p<0.001 for all. Mortality in patients with NSR was 84% in both temperature groups (unadjusted HR 0.92, adjusted HR 0.75; 95% CI 0.53-1.08, p=0.12). In the TTM33 group 3% survived with poor neurological outcome (CPC 3-4, mRS 4-5), compared to 2% in the TTM36 group (adjusted OR 0.67; 95% CI 0.08-4.73, p=0.69 for both). Thirteen percent in the TTM33 group and 15% in the TTM36 group had good neurologic outcome (CPC 1-2, mRS 0-3, OR 1.5, CI 0.21-12.5, p=0.69). The SOFA-score did not differ between temperature groups. CONCLUSION: Comatose patients after OHCA with initial NSR continue to have a poor prognosis. We found no effect of targeted temperature management at 33°C compared to 36°C in these patients.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Frydland, Martin","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Erlinge, David","Wanscher, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Pellis, Tommaso","Åneman, Anders","Friberg, Hans","Hovdenes, Jan","Horn, Janneke","Wetterslev, Jørn","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Wise, Matthew P","Kuiper, Michael","Stammet, Pascal","Cronberg, Tobias","Gasche, Yvan","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446277"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Electric Countershock","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Organ Failure","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Recovery of Function","Survival Rate","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"target temperature management of 000000000033 c and 000000000036 c in patients with out of hospital cardiac arrest with initial non shockable rhythm a ttm sub study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-446277","identifier":[{"id":"25629544","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84927594039","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5853b79b-69a4-49b9-b3de-d9ea66385eda"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Temperature","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Electric Countershock","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Organ Failure","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Recovery of Function","Survival Rate","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBC6BA787A1F5979A29C2381358CDA58"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Center of Epidemiology and Screening"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"frydlandpau","last":"Frydland","name":"Frydland, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ånemanpau","last":"Åneman","name":"Åneman, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matthew P","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"gaschepau","last":"Gasche","name":"Gasche, Yvan","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25629544"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.12.033","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"142-8","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927594039"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5853b79b-69a4-49b9-b3de-d9ea66385eda"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Target temperature management of 33°C and 36°C in patients with out-of-hospital cardiac arrest with initial non-shockable rhythm : a TTM sub-study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446277","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) is associated with a poor prognosis. As comorbidity and frailty increase with age; ethical dilemmas may arise when OHCA occur in the very old. OBJECTIVES: We aimed to investigate mortality, neurological outcome and post resuscitation care in octogenarians (≥80) to assess whether resuscitation and post resuscitation care should be avoided. METHODS: During 2007-2011 consecutive OHCA-patients were attended by the physician-based Emergency Medical Services-system in Copenhagen. Pre-hospital data based on Utstein-criteria, and data on post resuscitation care were collected. Primary outcome was successful resuscitation; secondary endpoints were 30-day mortality and neurological outcome (Cerebral Performance Category (CPC)). RESULTS: 2509 OHCA-patients with attempted resuscitation were recorded, 22% (n=558) were octogenarians/nonagenarians. 166 (30% of all octogenarians with resuscitation attempted) octogenarians were successfully resuscitated compared to 830 (43% with resuscitation attempted) patients <80 years. 30-day mortality in octogenarians was significantly higher after adjustment for prognostic factors (HR=1.61 CI: 1.22-2.13, p<0.001). Octogenarians received fewer coronary angiographies (CAG) (14 vs. 37%, p<0.001), and had lower odds of receiving CAG by multivariate logistic regression (OR: 0.19, CI: 0.08-0.44, p<0.001). A favorable neurological outcome (CPC 1/2) in survivors to discharge was found in 70% (n=26) of octogenarians compared to 86% (n=317, p=0.03) in the younger patients. CONCLUSION: OHCA in octogenarians was associated with a significantly higher mortality rate after adjustment for prognostic factors. However, the majority of octogenarian survivors were discharged with a favorable neurological outcome. Withholding resuscitation and post resuscitation care in octogenarians does not seem justified.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Hassager, Christian","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Nielsen, Niklas","Lippert, Freddy","Køber, Lars","Wanscher, Michael","Søholm, Helle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453103"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resuscitation and post resuscitation care of the very old after out of hospital cardiac arrest is worthwhile","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-453103","identifier":[{"id":"84943530631","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26340128","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-63ca99d9-f4ac-41ff-8823-cd8b53559021"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3249A0C42871DAE877253DD8CEB067F6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Freddy K","key":"lippertpau","last":"Lippert","locid":"48ac5d81-3437-4345-b6c3-394683a09d5d","name":"Lippert, Freddy","name_org":"Lippert, Freddy K","orcid":"0000-0002-2356-8809","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"søholmpau","last":"Søholm","name":"Søholm, Helle","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26340128"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2015.08.143","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"616-23","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"201"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84943530631"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63ca99d9-f4ac-41ff-8823-cd8b53559021"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resuscitation and post resuscitation care of the very old after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest is worthwhile","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453103","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
