 Tønnes","orcid":"0000-0003-4628-5411","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rainer","key":"czichonpau","last":"Czichon","name":"Czichon, Rainer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"høgelpau","last":"Høgel","locid":"337cd941-81a2-4faa-96fc-99a9d6255289","name":"Høgel, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3192-0961","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bünyamin","key":"kıvrakpau","last":"Kıvrak","name":"Kıvrak, Bünyamin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Majbom","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"e32f502a-9dd2-4f29-8a66-7c4f54049f11","name":"Madsen, Jesper Majbom","orcid":"0000-0003-0997-2730","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vera","key":"sauerpau","last":"Sauer","locid":"e62a41c8-a685-43a1-b719-a2fc2bd33e61","name":"Sauer, Vera","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Lund","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3c0cb1a6-129c-40f6-bd95-315c7f00bcd7","name":"Sørensen, Søren Lund","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"wintherjacobsenpau","last":"Winther-Jacobsen","name":"Winther-Jacobsen, Kristina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9786053963394"],"pages":"96","place":"Istanbul","publisher":"Arkeoloji ve Sanat Yayınları","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ea572163-b238-46b3-902c-ae63211d21a0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ancient Neoklaudiopolis (Vezirköprü in Samsun province) : A Historical and Archaeological Guide","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640315","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The vector velocity method Transverse Oscillation (TO) implemented on a conventional ultrasound (US) scanner (ProFocus, BK Medical, Herlev, Denmark) can provide real-time, angle-independent estimates of the cardiac blood flow. During cardiac surgery, epicardial US examination using TO was performed on (A) 3 patients with healthy aortic valve and (B) 3 patients with aortic valve stenosis. In group B, the systolic flow of the ascending aorta had higher velocities, was more aliased and chaotic. The jet narrowed to 44% of the lumen compared to 75% in group A and with a vector concentration, a measure of flow complexity, of 0.41 compared to 0.87 in group A. The two groups had similar secondary flow of the ascending aorta with an average rotation frequency of 4.8 Hz. Simultaneous measurements were obtained with spectral Doppler (SD) and a thermodilution technique (TD). The mean difference in peak systolic velocity compared to SD in group A was 22% and 45% in B, while the mean difference in volume flow compared to TD in group A was 30% and 32% in B. TO can potentially reveal new information of cardiac blood flow, and may become a valuable diagnostic tool in the evaluation of patients with cardiovascular diseases.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Hansen, Peter Møller","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Lund, Jens Teglgaard","Nilsson, Jens Christian","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann"],"cuid":["S02-095.56-034544"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aortic Valve","Cardiac flow","Stenosis","Transverse oscillation","Vector flow imaging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"first report on intraoperative vector flow imaging of the heart among patients with healthy and diseased aortic valves","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ultras.2014.07.015","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.56-034544","identifier":[{"id":"84912011669","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25128079","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-56831651-c743-4383-bce3-3fac4b5cd41d","ku-2de78c62-df4d-4ce8-a906-33cbd8912f1c"],"keyword":["Aortic valve","Cardiac flow","Stenosis","Transverse oscillation","Vector flow imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4B91487BA88BBB9733C7F30DD8DE23E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ultras.2014.07.015","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2"