"pmid":["25597749"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1158/1055-9965.epi-13-1281","issn":["10559965","15387755"],"issn_org":["10559965"],"issue":"3","journal":"Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers & Prevention","pages":"621-626","status":"p","title":"Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers & Prevention","title_org":"Cancer epidemiology, biomarkers & prevention : a publication of the American Association for Cancer Research, cosponsored by the American Society of Preventive Oncology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927760273"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6fafea1f-1a7a-46b9-92ad-eddf2600c66d","ku-82f28604-4888-4d99-889e-3ce4128363d2","sdu-2d39301e-78c4-476a-b9ca-35889c41561b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Serum YKL-40 in risk assessment for colorectal cancer : a prospective study of 4,496 subjects at risk of colorectal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.48-020839","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Thermal gasification of various biomass residues is a promising technology for combining bioenergy production with soil fertility management through the application of the resulting biochar as soil amendment. In this study, we investigated gasification biochar (GB) materials originating from two major global biomass fuels: straw gasification biochar (SGB) and wood gasification biochar (WGB), produced by a Low Temperature Circulating Fluidized Bed gasifier (LT-CFB) and a TwoStage gasifier, respectively, optimized for energy conversion. Stability of carbon in GB against microbial degradation was assessed in a shortterm soil incubation study and compared to the traditional practice of direct incorporation of cereal straw. The GBs were chemically and physically characterized to evaluate their potential to improve soil quality parameters. After 110 days of incubation, about 3% of the added GB carbon was respired as CO2, compared to 80% of the straw carbon added. The stability of GB was also confirmed by low H/C and O/C atomic ratios with lowest values for WGB (H/C 0.12 and O/C 0.10). The soil application of GBs exhibited a liming effect increasing the soil pH from ca 8 to 9. Results from scanning electron microscopy and BET analyses showed high porosity and specific surface area of both GBs, indicating a high potential to increase important soil quality parameters such as soil structure, nutrient and water retention, especially for WGB. These results seem promising regarding the possibility to combine an efficient bioenergy production with various soil aspects such as carbon sequestration and soil quality improvements.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Veronika","Müller-Stöver, Dorette Sophie","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Holm, Jens Kai","Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-038145"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Biochar soil amendment","Bioenergy efficiency","Carbon sequestration","Gasification","Soil quality improvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gasification biochar as a valuable by product for carbon sequestration and soil amendment","src":["dtu","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/56705674/pdf_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-038145","identifier":[{"id":"84921535835","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000349724100031","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-fadd0cab-83fb-4eb0-bacb-ccbc838895ad","ku-f815c157-2161-4159-b653-ced4e19a5a72","ruc-aa24c155-6f06-4b9d-b35d-1db10d9f403e"],"keyword":["Biochar soil amendment","Bioenergy efficiency","Carbon sequestration","Gasification","Soil quality improvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F72E9B7C6E8785ADA6A41C7FE3A71B33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2014.10.013","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/56705674/pdf_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Ecosystems Programme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["Ørsted A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, The Department of Environmental, Social and Spatial Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Veronika","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ae632c9d-96e3-4b62-aa62-c88b8cd37a16","name":"Hansen, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0090-0984","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorette Sophie","key":"müllerstöverpau","last":"Müller-Stöver","locid":"61683248-325a-49da-846c-76bb595a24b4","name":"Müller-Stöver, Dorette Sophie","orcid":"0000-0001-7921-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Kai","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jens Kai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Birk","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"e24f0587-f0e8-4ba0-93f0-9096e3a1b547","name":"Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","orcid":"0000-0003-1838-3962","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"0bc8cc02-9199-4a75-9e51-7dd5ceba9583","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8929-9691","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2014.10.013","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","pages":"300-308","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921535835"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fadd0cab-83fb-4eb0-bacb-ccbc838895ad","ku-f815c157-2161-4159-b653-ced4e19a5a72","ruc-aa24c155-6f06-4b9d-b35d-1db10d9f403e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Gasification biochar as a valuable by-product for carbon sequestration and soil amendment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-038145","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The article asks the research question whether the ephemeral affordance of Snapchat can be characterized as a product of the panopticon or of the synopticon. To seek to answer this question a threefold approach is employed. The first is historical and it investigates the relationship between the snapshot tied to leisure (“the Kodak moment”) and Snapchat. The second is empirical, and it uses pre-existing statistics about Snapchat and a questionnaire survey carried out for this article. Finally, the article sees the Snapchat phenomenon in the light of pertinent schools of cultural theory and in the context of new social media, e.g. research about selfies, and it considers the concepts of the panopticon and the more recent concept of the synopticon.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Jørgen Riber","Hansen, Julie Cecilie","Larsen, Frederik Holm","Nielsen, Jesper Sig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055216"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["SNaPshot","Selfies","Snapchat"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from snapshot to snapchat panopticon or synopticon","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.akademiskkvarter.hum.aau.dk/pdf/vol11/6_JoergenRiberChristesenJulieCecilieHansenFrederikHolmlarsenJesperSigNielsen_FromSnapshotToSnapchat.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-055216","ids":["aau-11b50557-af46-431c-a7df-089591d6f667"],"keyword":["#Snapchat, #panopticon, #synopticon, # the gaze, #the snapshot","Panopticon","Selfies","Snapchat","Snapshot","Synopticon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C37624F9AB0A5582E7262A0C64698D79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.akademiskkvarter.hum.aau.dk/pdf/vol11/6_JoergenRiberChristesenJulieCecilieHansenFrederikHolmlarsenJesperSigNielsen_FromSnapshotToSnapchat.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Global Studies (CL), IRGiC - The Interdisciplinary Research Group in Culture (CGS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, InDiMedia (Centre for Interactive Digital Media & Experience Design)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, MÆRKK (Markedskommunikation og Æstetik: Reception ift. Kognition og Kultur)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Reklame og medieæstetik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Riber","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"8046fe82-3c29-474e-8798-1deed17dcd66","name":"Christensen, Jørgen Riber","orcid":"0000-0002-0782-1421","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Cecilie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Julie Cecilie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Holm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Frederik Holm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sig","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sig","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19040008"],"issue":"June","journal":"Akademisk Kvarter","pages":"69-84","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Akademisk Kvarter","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-11b50557-af46-431c-a7df-089591d6f667"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"From Snapshot to Snapchat : Panopticon or Synopticon?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055216","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The multi-probe anechoic chamber method is promising for OTA testing. The reason can be attributed to its potential for enabling evaluating MIMO terminals in realistic environments. The focus of the paper is on investigating how to create desired spatial channel models with the multi-probe anechoic chamber setups. Simulation results have shown that with the discussed methods, the number of probes and probe power weights determine to which level the spatial characteristics of the target channel models can be accurately approximated. With the optimized weights, better agreement is achieved for all scenarios compared with the direct sampling methods.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fan, Wei","Kyösti, Pekka","Nuutinen, Jukka-Pekka","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057230"],"event":{"end":"2015-12-09","place":"Nanjing, cn","start":"2015-12-06","title":"2015 Asia-Pacific Microwave Conference (APMC)","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anite Telecoms Oy","Intel"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on probe weighting for mimo ota testing in anechoic chamber setups","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-057230","identifier":[{"id":"84979010965","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1881afa9-4893-4c15-92e9-4edbe33e4c83"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E853935F3954B1A6BC06A3C9D0F704C1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU A