{"abstract":"In the present study, the impact on peptide properties of labelling peptides with the fluorophore TAMRA or the selenium (Se) containing amino acid SeMet was evaluated. Three differently labelled variants of the cell-penetrating peptide (CPP) penetratin (Pen) were synthesized, PenMSe, TAMRA-PenMSe and TAMRA-Pen. The labelled peptides were characterized in terms of hydrodynamic radius, secondary structure during peptide–membrane interaction, effect on membrane leakage induction, uptake efficiency in HeLa cells. Furthermore, stability of peptides and identities of degradation products in cell media and cell lysate were evaluated. TAMRA-labelling increased the hydrodynamic radius of Pen and PenMSe significantly. Labelling with Se caused no or minimal changes in size, secondary structure and membrane leakage induction in concentration levels relevant for cellular uptake studies. Similar degradation patterns of all labelled peptides were observed in HBSS media; degradation was mainly due to oxidation. Cellular uptake was significantly higher for the TAMRA labelled peptides as compared to Se-labelled Pen. Extensive degradation was observed in media during cellular uptake studies, however, in all cell lysates, primarily the intact peptide (PenMSe, TAMRA-PenMSe or TAMRA-Pen) was observed. Selenium labelling caused minimal alteration of the physicochemical properties of the peptide and allowed for absolute quantitative determination of cellular uptake by inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry. Selenium is thus proposed as a promising alternative label for quantification of peptides in general, altering the properties of the peptide to a minor extent as compared to commonly used peptide labels.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Møller, Laura Hyrup","Bahnsen, Jesper Søborg","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","Østergaard, Jesper","Stürup, Stefan","Gammelgaard, Bente"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-519733"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"selenium as an alternative peptide label comparison to fluorophore labelled penetratin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-519733","identifier":[{"id":"25447743","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84913533883","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d3670331-0fca-49ff-9955-d2e23729cc91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CF783A2913501CF29575030B88441400"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Analytical Biosciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"hyrupmøllerpau","last":"Hyrup Møller","locid":"68d4b77a-c0d9-4a6b-b42a-3bd23b231890","name":"Møller, Laura Hyrup","name_org":"Hyrup Møller, Laura","orcid":"0000-0002-7987-344X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Søborg","key":"bahnsenpau","last":"Bahnsen","locid":"0f1c83cc-a6e0-485c-854a-0642ae7d51e3","name":"Bahnsen, Jesper Søborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Hanne Mørck","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b0450b3-f634-47ec-912c-b07ecd943be8","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","orcid":"0000-0002-7285-9100","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefan","key":"stüruppau","last":"Stürup","locid":"b45dc4f0-7473-4e3a-be67-4d129a710e3c","name":"Stürup, Stefan","orcid":"0000-0002-6856-9207","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"gammelgaardpau","last":"Gammelgaard","locid":"4ba048dd-88f5-4a5f-8556-10c9a5bd45d3","name":"Gammelgaard, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-1014","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25447743"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejps.2014.11.001","issn":["09280987","18790720"],"issn_org":["09280987"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","pages":"76-84","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84913533883"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d3670331-0fca-49ff-9955-d2e23729cc91"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selenium as an alternative peptide label - comparison to fluorophore-labelled penetratin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-519733","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: We studied whether variants previously associated with congenital long QT syndrome (cLQTS) have an effect on the QTc interval in a Danish population sample. Furthermore, we assessed whether carriers of variants in cLQTS-associated genes are more prone to experience syncope compared with non-carriers and whether carriers have an increased mortality compared with non-carriers. METHODS AND RESULTS: All genetic variants previously associated with cLQTS were surveyed using the Human Gene Mutation Database. We screened a Danish population-based sample with available whole-exome sequencing data (n = 870) and genotype array data (n = 6161) for putative cLQTS genetic variants. In total, 33 of 1358 variants previously reported to associate with cLQTS were identified. Of these, 10 variants were found in 8 or more individuals. Electrocardiogram results showed normal mean QTc intervals in carriers compared with non-carriers. Syncope data analysis between variant and non-variant carriers showed that 4 of 227 (1.8%) and 95 of 5861 (1.6%) individuals, respectively, had experienced syncope during follow-up (P = 0.80). There was no significant difference in overall mortality rates between carriers [7/217 (3.2%)] and non-carriers [301/6453 (4.7%)] (P = 0.24). CONCLUSION: We present QTc data and register data, indicating that 26 cLQTS-associated variants neither had any effect on the QTc intervals nor on syncope propensity or overall mortality. Based on the frequency of individual gene variants, we suggest that the 10 variants frequently identified, assumed to relate to cLQTS, are less likely to associate with a dominant monogenic form of the disease.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Ghouse, Jonas","Have, Christian Theil","Weeke, Peter","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Ahlberg, Gustav","Balslev-Harder, Marie","Appel, Emil Vincent Rosenbaum","Skaaby, Tea","Olesen, Søren-Peter","Grarup, Niels","Linneberg, Allan","Pedersen, Oluf","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Hansen, Torben","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Salling Olesen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543393"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rare genetic variants previously associated with congenital forms of long qt syndrome have little or no effect on the qt interval","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-543393","identifier":[{"id":"26159999","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84943559303","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fb367ee6-9283-45de-82ec-82a5efbcb8dc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65DFBF036B85D4BFB817A9E7A6C453CE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"ghousepau","last":"Ghouse","name":"Ghouse, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"aff