{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Whole-body ischemia during out-of-hospital cardiac arrest triggers immediate activation of inflammatory systems leading to a sepsis-like syndrome. The aim was to investigate the association between level of systemic inflammation and mortality in survivors after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest treated with targeted temperature management. DESIGN: Post hoc analysis. SETTING: Single-center study of a prospective multicenter randomized study. PATIENTS: One hundred sixty-nine patients (99%) with available blood samples out of 171 patients included in the Target -Temperature Management trial, randomly assigning patients to targeted temperature management at 33°C or 36°C. INTERVENTION: None. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: At baseline and 24, 48, and 72 hours after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, blood samples were obtained and screened for a battery of inflammatory markers. Level of interleukin-1β, interleukin-2, interleukin-4, interleukin-5, interleukin-6, interleukin-9, interleukin-10, interleukin-12, interleukin-13, tumor necrosis factor-α, interferon-γ, C-reactive protein, and procalcitonin were measured. Mortality at 30 days was evaluated by Cox analysis, and the predictive capability of inflammatory markers was evaluated by area under the curve. Level of all inflammatory markers changed significantly within 72 hours after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (all p values < 0.001), but only procalcitonin levels showed overall differences between nonsurvivors and survivors (p = 0.0002). At baseline, interleukin-6 was independently associated with mortality, whereas both interleukin-6 levels (hazard ratio = 1.23 [1.01-1.49]; p = 0.04) and procalcitonin levels (hazard ratio = 1.20 [1.03-1.39]; p = 0.02) 24 hours after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest were associated with 30-day mortality with no interactions between targeted temperature management group and levels of interleukin-6 (p = 0.25) or procalcitonin (p = 0.85). None of the other inflammatory markers were independently associated with mortality. Area under the curve for procalcitonin and interleukin-6, 24 hours after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, were 0.74 and 0.63, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: Level of inflammation, assessed by interleukin-6 and procalcitonin, was independently associated with increased mortality with the highest discriminative value obtained 24 hours after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Interventions aiming at decreasing level of inflammation as a way to improve outcome may be investigated in future studies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bro-Jeppesen, John","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Wanscher, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Friberg, Hans","Bjerre, Mette","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-012965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Biomarkers","C Reactive Protein","Calcitonin","Cytokines","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Inflammation Mediators","Male","Middle Aged","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prognosis","Protein Precursors","Severity of Illness Index"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systemic inflammatory response and potential prognostic implications after out of hospital cardiac arrest a substudy of the target temperature management trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/CCM.0000000000000937","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-012965","identifier":[{"id":"25756419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84931578363","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-04f93216-f5c0-4bcd-a5b2-d87f4f568f30","ku-08833afc-88a6-40a5-8faa-4f9eb300203f"],"keyword":["Aged","Biomarkers","C-Reactive Protein","Calcitonin","Cytokines","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Inflammation Mediators","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Prognosis","Protein Precursors","Severity of Illness Index"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-167EE0D31EE16C0EAB1BF9510F34C199"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/CCM.0000000000000937","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"1337eaca-a3a1-4837-a772-261478be9f37","name":"Bjerre, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25756419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ccm.0000000000000937","issn":["00903493","10637389"],"issn_org":["00903493"],"issue":"6","journal":"Critical Care Medicine","pages":"1223","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Critical Care Medicine","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84931578363"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-04f93216-f5c0-4bcd-a5b2-d87f4f568f30","ku-08833afc-88a6-40a5-8faa-4f9eb300203f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systemic Inflammatory Response and Potential Prognostic Implications After Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest : A Substudy of the Target Temperature Management Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-012965","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Fungal keratitis is a severe sight-threatening condition. The aim of this study was to investigate the incidence and clinical characteristics of fungal keratitis patients living in a temperate climate. Methods: By reviewing medical records from 2000 to July 2013, patients with fungal keratitis were identified. Risk factors, clinical signs and outcome were registered. Results: Twenty-five patients were identified: 52% with Candida, 20% with Fusarium, 16% with Aspergillus and 12% with mixed filamentous fungi. A minimum incidence of fungal keratitis of 0.6 cases per million per year was estimated. Prior topical steroid treatment was commonly found in our cases (44%). Trauma including contact lens wear was associated with infection with filamentous fungi, whereas in patients with Candida infection, ocular surface disease was a prominent feature. Median time from onset of symptoms to diagnosis was 24 days. Only a few patients exhibited classical clinical features such as endothelial plaques (28%), satellite lesions (24%) and feathery edges (16%). The final visual outcome was poor with an average best-corrected logMAR of (mean, 95% CI) 0.70 (0.4-1.0). A total of 52% were treated with corneal transplantation. Patients with Candida infections had a significantly worse visual outcome. Conclusion: We found that patients with fungal keratitis had a poor visual outcome. However, knowledge of risk factors and clinical signs leading to early treatment can improve the prognosis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Stine E.","Nielsen, Esben","Julian, Hanne Olsen","Lindegaard, Jens","Højgaard, Klavs","Ivarsen, Anders","Hjortdal, Jesper","Heegaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018308"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Stine E."],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Antifungal Agents","Aspergillus","Candida","Climate","Corneal Transplantation","Corneal Ulcer","Culture","Denmark","Diagnosis","Epidemiology","Eye","Eye Enucleation","Female","Fungal keratitis","Fungus","Fusarium","Humans","Incidence","Male","Microbial keratitis","Middle Aged","Mycoses","Risk Factors","South India","Spectrum","Ulceration","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence and clinical characteristics of fungal keratitis in a danish population from 000000002000 to 000000002013","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12440","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018308","identifier":[{"id":"84921593828","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000348500500032","type":"wos"},{"id":"24836583","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4d5a0350-029e-419a-9584-85e327a4fd07","ku-c9b61f0a-0123-4e80-ba49-2fec7e3df9a9"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Antifungal Agents","Aspergillus","CLIMATE","CORNEAL ULCERS","Candida","Corneal Transplantation","Corneal Ulcer","DIAGNOSIS","Denmark","EYE","Eye Enucleation","Eye Infections, Fungal","Female","Fusarium","Humans","Incidence","MICROBIAL KERATITIS","Male","Middle Aged","Mycoses","Risk Factors","SOUTH-INDIA","SPECTRUM","ULCERATION","Young Adult","culture","epidemiology","fungal keratitis","fungus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-51EB480F16396CBB77B8D5ABA9F0DA24"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12440","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine E.","key":"nielsenstineepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a59b0122-1b20-4624-9547-47341f7eea45","name":"Nielsen, Stine E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"nielsenesbenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"242d1c56-f540-479d-87ad-68df850f2587","name":"Nielsen, Esben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Olsen","key":"julianhanneolsenpau","last":"Julian","locid":"91fa26d0-853d-4a22-a466-8c314cc15a6c","name":"Julian, Hanne Olsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens","key":"lindegaardjenspau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"029ccd5f-9c1f-49de-97ff-4ad7541d7172","name":"Lindegaard, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klavs","key":"højgaardklavspau","last":"Højgaard","name":"Højgaard, Klavs","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"ivarsenanderspau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"072c0ad1-1c62-4539-8b63-868ff8422866","name":"Ivarsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1466-4804","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corres