{"abstract":"This paper discusses generating three dimensional (3D) spatial channel models with emphasis on the angular sampling methods. Three angular sampling methods, i.e. modified uniform power sampling, modified uniform angular sampling, and random pairing methods are proposed and investigated in detail. The random pairing method, which uses only twenty sinusoids in the ray-based model for generating the channels, presents good results if the spatial channel cluster is with a small elevation angle spread. For spatial clusters with large elevation angle spreads, however, the random pairing method would fail and the other two methods should be considered.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fan, Wei","Jämsä, Tommi","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-122269"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anite Telecoms Oy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on angular sampling methods for 000000000003 d spatial channel models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/206008376/final_manuscript.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-122269","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000349396300031","type":"wos"},{"id":"84923247515","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f89d2289-ad04-43a5-b5d3-7273313d222c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57A1885F8C629D547AF59137BF8C8040"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/206008376/final_manuscript.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.i