"Bavngaard","name":"Bavngaard, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779037366"],"pages":"66","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Institut for Geovidenskab og Naturforvaltning, Københavns Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","hededanmark a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-46df425e-5f8c-4df8-96fa-c6241d6fbaf3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kvalitetsbeskrivelser for drift af grønne områder 2015 : Branchestandard","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-435747","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To examine contemporary rates of severe hypoglycemia (SH) and identify the effect of predictors of SH in a pediatric type 1 diabetes population. Methods: The national diabetes register provided data on children residing in Denmark from 2008 to 2013 in this register-based population study. Robust Poisson regression models were applied. Results: The study population [n = 2,715 (50.9 % boys), mean (SD) age at onset; 8.1 (4.0) years, diabetes duration; 5.6 (4.9) years] comprised 7,390 person-years of data and 561 events of SH. The overall incidence of SH was 7.6 per 100 person-years. The incidence rate peaked with 16.0 per 100 person-years in 2008 reaching a nadir of 4.9 in 2011. Overall, insulin pump reduced the rate of SH with 27 % compared to any pen treatment (P = 0.003). When stratifying pen treatment, premixed insulin increased the rate of SH by 1.9-fold (P = 0.0015) and NPH increased the rate by 1.6-fold (P = 0.003) versus pump treatment, whereas long-acting insulin analogues were comparable with pump treatment (P = 0.1485). We found no association of SH with glycemic control (P > 0.05). Conclusions: A nationwide halving in rates of severe hypoglycemia was observed during the study period independent of the prevailing average HbA1c level. Changes in diabetes care and successful educational programs may have influenced the lower incidence rate of severe hypoglycemia.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Fredheim, Siri","Johansen, A.","Thorsen, Steffen Ullitz","Kremke, B.","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Olsen, Bo Sanderhoff","Lyngsøe, Lene","Sildorf, S. M.","Pipper, Christian Bressen","Mortensen, Henrik B","Johannesen, Jesper","Svensson, Jannet"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-454915"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children","Hypoglycemia","Insulin therapy","Register","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nationwide reduction in the frequency of severe hypoglycemia by half","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/record/display.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84930081623&origin=resultslist&sort=plf-f&src=s&st1=Nationwide+reduction+in+the+frequency+of+severe+hypoglycemia+by+half&st2=&sid=095E7B63AB04ACB9147B6682EE127391.euC1gMODexYlPkQec4u1Q%3a280&sot=b&sdt=b&sl=75&s=TITLE%28Nationwide+reduction+in+the+frequency+of+severe+hypoglycemia+by+half%29&relpos=0&citeCnt=3&searchTerm=","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-454915","identifier":[{"id":"84930081623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25528006","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-66f3b798-2999-4259-ae86-ac46be7306e2"],"keyword":["Children","Hypoglycemia","Insulin therapy","Register","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C31769E782907A35CB15B22438F665D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"S.","key":"fredheimpau","last":"Fredheim","locid":"834b9d9f-0f77-498e-bd73-0210623e3ddf","name":"Fredheim, Siri","name_org":"Fredheim, S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"S. U.","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"e3dc0db2-8ac8-454b-83ec-bbb85a8b4100","name":"Thorsen, Steffen Ullitz","name_org":"Thorsen, S. U.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"B.","key":"kremkepau","last":"Kremke","name":"Kremke, B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L. B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, L. B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"B. S.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"6389a284-e556-4971-9a2f-a7392e591320","name":"Olsen, Bo Sanderhoff","name_org":"Olsen, B. S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L.","key":"lyngsøepau","last":"Lyngsøe","locid":"4405194d-c6f8-46da-8c68-366119e29d7b","name":"Lyngsøe, Lene","name_org":"Lyngsøe, L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S. M.","key":"sildorfpau","last":"Sildorf","name":"Sildorf, S. M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Bressen","key":"pipperpau","last":"Pipper","locid":"c002fade-f477-46eb-aa1f-34702fdd3746","name":"Pipper, Christian Bressen","orcid":"0000-0003-0261-616X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H. B.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f1a10f64-1be6-42df-b4ee-7df370fcc9d0","name":"Mortensen, Henrik B","name_org":"Mortensen, H. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-9231-8363","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J.","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"f8330122-dfc2-46b6-823b-95cdf4efab03","name":"Johannesen, Jesper","name_org":"Johannesen, J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J.","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"404145c9-3f7a-4360-81ae-2ee5a9ca2173","name":"Svensson, Jannet","name_org":"Svensson, J.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25528006"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00592-014-0697-5","issn":["09405429","14325233"],"issn_org":["09405429"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Diabetologica","pages":"591-599","status":"p","title":"Acta Diabetologica","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930081623"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-66f3b798-2999-4259-ae86-ac46be7306e2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nationwide reduction in the frequency of severe hypoglycemia by half","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-454915","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"TL1A is a TNF-like cytokine which has been shown to co-stimulate TH1 and TH17 responses during chronic inflammation. The expression of this novel cytokine has been investigated in inflammatory disorders like rheumatoid arthritis and inflammatory bowel disease, but little is known about expression and induction in psoriasis. Indeed, the pathogenesis in psoriasis is still not fully understood and it is speculated that cytokines other than TNF-α are important in subsets of patients. Also, for patients with severe disease that are treated with systemic anti-TNF-α blockade, novel candidates to be used as disease and response biomarkers are of high interest. Here, we demonstrate TL1A expression in biopsies from psoriatic lesions. Also, we investigated spontaneous and induced TL1A secretion from PBMCs and blood levels from a cohort of psoriasis patients. Here, increased spontaneous secretion from PBMCs was observed as compared to healthy controls and a small subset of patients had highly elevated TL1A in the blood. Interestingly, activation of PBMCs with various cytokines showed a decreased sensitivity for TL1A activation in psoriasis patients compared to healthy controls.TL1A levels in blood and biopsies could not be correlated with disease activity with this patient cohort. Thus, additional large-scale studies are warranted to investigate TL1A as a biomarker.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Pedersen, Anders Elm","Schmidt, Esben Gjerløff Wedebye","Sørensen, Jesper Freddie","Faber, Carsten","Nielsen, Boye Schnack","Holmstrøm, Kim","Omland, Silje Haukali","Tougaard, Peter","Skov, Søren","Bang, Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455510"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Case Control Studies","Cytokines","Female","Healthy Volunteers","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Leukocytes Mononuclear","Male","Middle Aged","Pilot Projects","Psoriasis","Skin","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-BION"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-BION","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"secretion blood levels and cutaneous expression of tl000000000001a in psoriasis patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-455510","identifier":[{"id":"84932196146","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25908025","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-67f6195c-ffd1-47b5-9438-3c386e09e628"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Case-Control Studies","Cytokines","Female","Healthy Volunteers","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Leukocytes, Mononuclear","Male","Middle Aged","Pilot Projects","Psoriasis","Skin","Tumor Necrosis Factor Ligand Superfamily Member 15","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D911461C3D51F09911BEE95C735948BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"bioneer","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-BION","l3nn":"Bioneer","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bioneer","namevar":["Bioneer"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-BION","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Elm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dcd1cfb9-0ba1-4151-897d-f04233bd6c91","name":"Pedersen, Anders Elm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Esben Gjerløff Wedebye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c807aea5-557c-4473-874b-de212d3e5a69","name":"Schmidt, Esben Gjerløff Wedebye","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Freddie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"13ccc199-ed59-4f07-ae96-ded6ba6978a5","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Freddie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"989bdc3e-2cd9-4feb-9875-f746afb3fe89","name":"Faber, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Boye Schnack","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Boye Schnack","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kim","key":"holmstrømpau","last":"Holmstrøm","name":"Holmstrøm, Kim","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Silje Haukali","key":"omlandpau","last":"Omland","name":"Omland, Silje Haukali","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"tougaardpau","last":"Tougaard","locid":"7ebf3728-8bdd-42ba-a7e6-129b0b6e8092","name":"Tougaard, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"c1c333fb-a9e9-4c7b-8d50-ef83a755fa41","name":"Skov, Søren","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bo","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Bo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25908025"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apm.12385","issn":["09034641","0903465X"],"issn_org":["09034641"],"issue":"7","journal":"APMIS","pages":"547-555","status":"p","title":"APMIS","title_org":"APMIS : acta pathologica, microbiologica, et immunologica Scandinavica","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84932196146"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-67f6195c-ffd1-47b5-9438-3c386e09e628"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Secretion, blood levels and cutaneous expression of TL1A in psoriasis patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455510","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Neuron-specific enolase (NSE) is a widely-used biomarker for prognostication of neurological outcome after cardiac arrest, but the relevance of recommended cutoff values has been questioned due to the lack of a standardized methodology and uncertainties over the influence of temperature management. OBJECTIVES: This study investigated the role of NSE as a prognostic marker of outcome after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) in a contemporary setting. METHODS: A total of 686 patients hospitalized after OHCA were randomized to targeted temperature management at either 33°C or 36°C. NSE levels were assessed in blood samples obtained 24, 48, and 72 h after return of spontaneous circulation. The primary outcome was neurological outcome at 6 months using the cerebral performance category score. RESULTS: NSE was a robust predictor of neurological outcome in a baseline variable-adjusted model, and target temperature did not significantly affect NSE values. Median NSE values were 18 ng/ml versus 35 ng/ml, 15 ng/ml versus 61 ng/ml, and 12 ng/ml versus 54 ng/ml for good versus poor outcome at 24, 48, and 72 h, respectively (p < 0.001). At 48 and 72 h, NSE predicted neurological outcome with areas under the receiver-operating curve of 0.85 and 0.86, respectively. High NSE cutoff values with false positive rates ≤5% and tight 95% confidence intervals were able to reliably predict outcome. CONCLUSIONS: High, serial NSE values are strong predictors of poor outcome after OHCA. Targeted temperature management at 33°C or 36°C does not significantly affect NSE levels. (Target Temperature Management After Cardiac Arrest [TTM]; NCT01020916).","author_count":19,"contributors":["Stammet, Pascal","Collignon, Olivier","Hassager, Christian","Wise, Matthew P","Hovdenes, Jan","Åneman, Anders","Horn, Janneke","Devaux, Yvan","Erlinge, David","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Gasche, Yvan","Wanscher, Michael","Cronberg, Tobias","Friberg, Hans","Wetterslev, Jørn","Pellis, Tommaso","Kuiper, Michael","Gilson, Georges","Nielsen, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518113"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["TTM-Trial Investigators"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Brain Ischemia","Europe","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Phosphopyruvate Hydratase","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Temperature","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuron specific enolase as a predictor of death or poor neurological outcome after out of hospital cardiac arrest and targeted temperature management at 000000000033 c and 000000000036 c","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-518113","identifier":[{"id":"25975474","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84929207083","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d0ab4c0a-596b-442e-8b80-50487199873d"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Brain Ischemia","Europe","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Phosphopyruvate Hydratase","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Temperature","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BB0ECD4DBE4979F8F7C8D0F63768FD7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ttm trial investigators","name":"TTM-Trial Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olivier","key":"collignonpau","last":"Collignon","name":"Collignon, Olivier","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matthew P","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ånemanpau","last":"Åneman","name":"Åneman, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"devauxpau","last":"Devaux","name":"Devaux, Yvan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"gaschepau","last":"Gasche","name":"Gasche, Yvan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","locid":"e79b2031-27ca-4c44-94de-211b8963848a","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Georges","key":"gilsonpau","last":"Gilson","name":"Gilson, Georges","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25975474"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacc.2015.03.538","issn":["07351097","15583597"],"issn_org":["07351097"],"issue":"19","journal":"Journal of the American College of Cardiology","pages":"2104-14","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American College of Cardiology","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929207083"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d0ab4c0a-596b-442e-8b80-50487199873d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neuron-Specific Enolase as a Predictor of Death or Poor Neurological Outcome After Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest and Targeted Temperature Management at 33°C and 36°C","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518113","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Depression and anxiety often co-occur, and conventional monoamine-facilitating antidepressants show efficacy against symptoms in both disorders. Rodent studies indicate that antidepressant effects of monoamine-based antidepressants involve increased α-amino-3-hydroxy-5- methyl-4-isoxazolepropionic acid glutamate receptor (AMPAR) neurotransmission, and positive allosteric modulators (PAMs) at AMPARs produced antidepressant-like effects in rodents. While this suggests that increased AMPAR-mediated neurotransmission is beneficial in depression management, preclinical studies addressing AMPARs in relation to anxiety have given ambiguous results with both anxiolytic-like and anxiogenic-like effects observed after AMPAR blockade. This study systematically compared the effects of the AMPAR potentiator LY451646 and the AMPAR antagonist GYKI-53655 on depression-related behaviour using the mouse forced swim (FST) and tail suspension tests (TST), and anxiety-related behaviour using the elevated zero maze (EZM), marble burying (MB) and novelty-induced hypophagia (NIH) tests. The serotonin-selective antidepressant citalopram was included for comparison. Due to the importance of AMPARs in learning and memory we also tested if GYKI-53655 disrupted performance in the V-maze test for attention-dependent behaviour, and the social transmission of food preference (STFP) test of long-term memory. LY451646 (3 mg/kg) showed an antidepressant-like profile in the FST and TST, and GYKI-53655 (≥ 5 mg/kg) had a depressogenic-like effect in the TST but no effect in the FST. Conversely, GYKI-53655 produced marked anxiolytic-like effects in the EZM (≥ 2.5 mg/kg), MBT (≥ 2.5 mg/kg), and NIH tests (≥ 5 mg/kg), while LY451646 (≥ 3 mg/kg) increased anxiety-like behaviour in the EZM. Citalopram showed an antidepressant-like effect in the FST (≥ 10 mg/kg), but not TST, an anxiolytic-like effect in the EZM (≥ 3 mg/kg) and MB test (≥ 2.5 mg/kg), and an anxiogenic-like effect in the NIH test (≥ 30 mg/kg). GYKI-53655 did not affect cognitive performance in the V-maze or STFP tests. Collectively, these findings suggest a differential role of AMPARs in depression and anxiety, with AMPAR activation promoting antidepressant responses and AMPAR inhibition promoting anxiolytic responses. The potential of AMPARs as a novel target in depression and anxiety pharmacotherapy is discussed.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andreasen T., Jesper","Fitzpatrick, Ciarán M","Larsen, Maria","Skovgaard, Lars","Nielsen, Simon D","Clausen, Rasmus Prætorius","Troelsen, Karin de Linde Lind","Pickering, Darryl S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541538"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Anti Anxiety Agents","Antidepressive Agents","Anxiety","Behavior Animal","Benzodiazepines","Depressive Disorder","Female","Maze Learning","Mice","Motor Activity","Receptors AMPA","Sulfonamides"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differential role of ampa receptors in mouse tests of antidepressant and anxiolytic action","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-541538","identifier":[{"id":"25578259","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84924439661","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f8112864-84b9-4284-a842-832a1ac5e83e"],"keyword":["Animals","Anti-Anxiety Agents","Antidepressive Agents","Anxiety","Behavior, Animal","Benzodiazepines","Depressive Disorder","Female","Maze Learning","Mice","Motor Activity","Receptors, AMPA","Sulfonamides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E2E0A31E1B4BFD2AE83A1513E187104"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Experimental Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper T","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"bc66d36f-6969-4fa0-9b43-ac503a438a8a","name":"Andreasen T., Jesper","name_org":"Andreasen, Jesper T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ciaran M","key":"fitzpatrickpau","last":"Fitzpatrick","locid":"882de932-ff04-42a8-828b-a361baa48114","name":"Fitzpatrick, Ciarán M","name_org":"Fitzpatrick, Ciaran M","orcid":"0000-0002-9996-4541","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Simon D","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Simon D","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus P","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"46680ca4-b09b-4a7b-b497-2306b14c78c6","name":"Clausen, Rasmus Prætorius","name_org":"Clausen, Rasmus P","orcid":"0000-0001-9466-9431","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karin","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"4fad120b-c63f-4195-a282-96b41df82eb5","name":"Troelsen, Karin de Linde Lind","name_org":"Troelsen, Karin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Darryl S","key":"pickeringpau","last":"Pickering","locid":"7f3e2ef6-0c80-45fd-932e-92ec257a25d4","name":"Pickering, Darryl S","orcid":"0000-0001-8687-6094","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25578259"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.brainres.2015.01.001","issn":["00068993","18726240"],"issn_org":["00068993"],"journal":"Brain Research","pages":"117-26","status":"p","title":"Brain Research","volume":"1601"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924439661"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f8112864-84b9-4284-a842-832a1ac5e83e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Differential role of AMPA receptors in mouse tests of antidepressant and anxiolytic action","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541538","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To assess older age as a prognostic factor in patients resuscitated from out-of-hospital-cardiac arrest (OHCA) and the interaction between age and level of target temperature management. METHODS AND RESULTS: 950 patients included in the target temperature management (TTM) trial were randomly allocated to TTM at 33 or 36 °C for 24h. We assessed survival and cerebral outcome (cerebral performance category, CPC and modified Rankin scale, mRS) using age as predictor, dividing patients into 5 age groups: ≤ 65 (median), 66-70, 71-75, 76-80 and >80 years of age. Shockable rhythm decreased with higher age groups, p = 0.001, the same was true for ST segment elevation on ECG at admission, p < 0.01. Increasing age was associated with a higher mortality rate (HR = 1.04 per year, 95% CI = 1.03-1.06, p < 0.001) after adjusting for confounders. Octogenarians had an increased mortality (HR = 3.5, CI: 2.5-5.0, p < 0.001) compared to patients ≤ 65 years of age. Favorable vs. unfavorable outcome measured by CPC and mRS in survivors was different between age groups with adverse outcomes more prevalent in higher age groups (CPC: p = 0.04, mRS: p = 0.001). The interaction between age and target temperature allocation was not statistically significant for either mortality or neurological outcome. CONCLUSION: Increasing age is associated with significantly increased mortality after OHCA, but mortality rate is not influenced by level of target temperature. Risk of poor neurological outcome also increases with age, but is not modified by level of target temperature.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Pellis, Tommaso","Kuiper, Michael","Koopmans, Matty","Hassager, Christian","Nielsen, Niklas","Wetterslev, Jørn","Cronberg, Tobias","Erlinge, David","Friberg, Hans","Gasche, Yvan","Horn, Janneke","Hovdenes, Jan","Stammet, Pascal","Wanscher, Michael","Wise, Matthew P","Åneman, Anders","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545490"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Female","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Prognosis","Regression Analysis","Survival Analysis","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mortality and neurological outcome in the elderly after target temperature management for out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-545490","identifier":[{"id":"84929262467","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25597506","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fed57a37-a695-42aa-b85a-50ac463d5b27"],"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Female","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","Prognosis","Regression Analysis","Survival Analysis","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-961D53A025BA3AE2BD960C3568060A18"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommaso","key":"pellispau","last":"Pellis","name":"Pellis, Tommaso","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kuiperpau","last":"Kuiper","name":"Kuiper, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matty","key":"koopmanspau","last":"Koopmans","name":"Koopmans, Matty","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"cronbergpau","last":"Cronberg","name":"Cronberg, Tobias","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"erlingepau","last":"Erlinge","name":"Erlinge, David","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvan","key":"gaschepau","last":"Gasche","name":"Gasche, Yvan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Janneke","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Janneke","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"hovdenespau","last":"Hovdenes","name":"Hovdenes, Jan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pascal","key":"stammetpau","last":"Stammet","name":"Stammet, Pascal","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew P","key":"wisepau","last":"Wise","name":"Wise, Matthew P","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ånemanpau","last":"Åneman","name":"Åneman, Anders","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25597506"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.12.030","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"92-8","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929262467"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fed57a37-a695-42aa-b85a-50ac463d5b27"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mortality and neurological outcome in the elderly after target temperature management for out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-545490","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background and Objectives Medication adherence is often suboptimal among patients with hypertension. Non-adherence is a multi-dimensional problem and a successful adherence intervention requires multiple components to address the underlying reason for non-adherence. The objective of the present study was to describe the content and process outcomes of an adherence program developed for hypertensive patients in a hospital setting. Methods The intervention development was based on adherence and behavioral theories, and evidence of effective interventions. The intervention was pharmacist-led and included three components: a focused medication review, a patient interview and follow-up telephone calls. Two tools were used to identify and address non-adherence: The DRAW©-tool and an adherence questionnaire. A study carried out at, three out clinics at Odense University Hospital, Denmark was used to evaluate process outcomes. Results In total, 240 patients with hypertension were invited to participate in the study. Among these, 156 patients (65%) accepted participation and received the intervention. The focused medication review revealed 91 drug-related problems categorized into eight types. According to the questionnaire, 44.2% of the patients had at least one item indicated an adherence problem. The DRAW©-tool used at the interview, identified 416 problems, 60% medication-related and 40% life style-related. In total 528 actions were taken divided into 8 categories. Motivational interviewing was the most frequent action (60%) and was exercised in 94% of the patients. All participants gave informed consent and the study was approved by The Regional Scientific Ethical Committee for Southern Denmark and the Danish Registry Board Conclusions A pharmacist-led multifaceted tailored adherence intervention has been developed to be used in patients with hypertension. The intervention was feasible for identifying and addressing a large range of potential medication- adherence and life style problems. Motivational interviewing was the most frequent action taken and used in nearly all patients. Implications to practice This study could serve as a guide for development of similar interventions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hedegaard, Ulla","Hallas, Jesper","Nielsen, Lene Ravn-Vestergaard","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-594892"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-05","place":"Tartu, ee","start":"2015-06-03","title":"Nordic Social Pharmacy and Health Services Researh Conference &amp; The Nordic Networking Group of Clinical Pharmacy","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multifaceted medication adherence intervention for patients with hypertension in secondary care","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-594892","ids":["sdu-4ba320ff-a465-49b9-b36d-197bf6332da1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5EAB3E99EAA1AFADD419D27C1A2CDB82"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Dept. Clinical Biochemistry and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amgros"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla","key":"hedegaardpau","last":"Hedegaard","locid":"82b24eb2-1cc9-49b6-bd97-07f2cb6a6d2b","name":"Hedegaard, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0002-8958-2187","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Ravn-Vestergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ravn-Vestergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","amgros"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4ba320ff-a465-49b9-b36d-197bf6332da1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multifaceted medication adherence intervention for patients with hypertension in secondary care","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-594892","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background The aim of the project was to assess the definitions of hazard, risk, and their assessment used in different scientific disciplines and to give examples of the potential implications in the scientific discussions as well as in risk communication. Method The following disciplines were involved: public health, psychology, environmental health, occupational health, engineering, sociology and medicine. From each discipline a scientist was asked to present their own views on the given topics. Questions were developed together to get comparable responses from participants. Result: The surprising result was that, when working together, pre-given major differences disappeared. Hazard is an adverse event or condition, mostly expressed in qualitative terms. For most risk definitions probability and severity are both important aspects and often a quantification of risk is desired, whereas risk perception is seen as a subjective appraisal and a cognitive construct. Discussion Risk perceptions are based on a combination of knowledge and individual values and affects; therefore risk perceptions may not provide a reliable guidance for risk management decisions on a societal level. The subjective and value laden risk perception raises the question how to objectively assess risk, in spite of the fact that the hazard may have been established. Main messages Discipline differences are small and mainly connected to the usage of terminology and interpretation of key concepts. For dealing with controversies in science, a common terminology and standardized and transparent risk assessment framework are important. Key message Differences in risk definitions between disciplines are small and mainly connected to the usage of terminology. Common terminology and standardized and transparent risk assessment are important","author_count":7,"contributors":["Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","Wiedemann, Peter","Adam, Balazs","Breum Ølgaard, Kristian","Andersen, Pernille Tanggaard","Kabwama, Steven Ndugwa","Nielsen, Jesper Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606826"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-17","place":"Milano, it","start":"2015-10-14","title":"European Public Health Conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","United Arab Emirates University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk definitions risk research is done in multiple disciplines but is it multidisciplinary","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurpub/ckv176.086","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606826","ids":["sdu-757613b2-4c4d-4750-ba5e-428159dbac7e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D9ED438C392E18E58CFEB977D874AF0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurpub/ckv176.086","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Health Promotion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ae","key":"united arab emirates university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"United Arab Emirates University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriele","key":"bergbeckhoffpau","last":"Berg-Beckhoff","locid":"df22cacd-c8b4-440c-8c16-aecbc139d9b6","name":"Berg-Beckhoff, Gabriele","orcid":"0000-0003-1614-938X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"wiedemannpau","last":"Wiedemann","name":"Wiedemann, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Balazs","key":"adampau","last":"Adam","name":"Adam, Balazs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"breumølgaardpau","last":"Breum Ølgaard","name":"Breum Ølgaard, Kristian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Tanggaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3ab68877-26af-4d94-8efb-fa63ce8ae714","name":"Andersen, Pernille Tanggaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7334-761X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven Ndugwa","key":"kabwamapau","last":"Kabwama","locid":"bf8ac2e0-5891-4947-a617-5c8fd0d21593","name":"Kabwama, Steven Ndugwa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurpub/ckv176.086","issn":["11011262","1464360X"],"issn_org":["11011262"],"issue":"suppl 3","journal":"European Journal of Public Health","pages":"405","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Public Health","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-757613b2-4c4d-4750-ba5e-428159dbac7e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Risk definitions - risk research is done in multiple disciplines; but is it multidisciplinary?:","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-606826","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
