nd Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"MA","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, MA","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","name_org":"Kristiansen, J","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"AH","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"8e894baf-467c-45d3-8abe-41a805b30b22","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","name_org":"Garde, AH","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-fd9ec055-4e6c-4b9a-a644-2719a0c5107c"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"What is the preferred number of consecutive night shifts? Results from the \"In the Middle of the Night\" project","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782232","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Purpose – The purpose of this article is to investigate how facilities management (FM) units navigate Energy Service Company (ESCO) collaborations, here defined as examples of public collaborative innovation within the context of FM. The driving motivation is to inform and inspire internal FM units of local institutions on how to navigate and manage collaboration of different, intra- and inter-organisational actors throughout ESCO projects. Design/methodology/approach – A deductive research methodology was applied based on the first ten ESCO projects in Danish municipalities between 2008 and 2012. Findings – A model of FM roles in FM public innovation is proposed. The internal FM unit coordinates between clients and end users by acting as translator and demonstrator and collaborates with the ESCO company to implement the energy renovation (FM processor). Research limitations/implications – The data were collected from a limited sample of ESCO collaborations in Denmark. Future research should thus investigate collaborative innovation in ESCO (and other forms of private–public) collaborations outside of Denmark. Practical implications – Not only should FM units clarify what different stakeholders expect from an ESCO collaboration, but also they should translate stakeholders’ expectations into actual goals and objectives; process them together with the ESCO company; demonstrate their execution to all stakeholders throughout the process, not just when closing the collaboration. Originality/value – This paper contributes to FM innovation research by exploring FM innovation in the public sector and by depicting the coordinating role of local governments’ internal FM units engaging in public–private collaborative innovation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nardelli, Giulia","Jensen, Jesper Ole","Balslev Nielsen, Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-088.77-000457"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Energy optimisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"facilities management innovation in public private collaborations danish esco projects","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128934217/s1_ln18158766_1844153331_1939656818Hwf_1905882071IdV_62166603718158766PDF_HI0001.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-088.77-000457","identifier":[{"id":"85019695388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-08aee14b-b751-4f73-af9a-6a287cbe011b","dtu-bbae8435-a09f-4840-9351-94b3a53e97ea"],"keyword":["ESCO","Energy optimisation","FM innovation","FM roles","Public FM","Sustainable FM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CBC7FB4CE3372D315A6355D61E528C97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128934217/s1_ln18158766_1844153331_1939656818Hwf_1905882071IdV_62166603718158766PDF_HI0001.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1108/JFM-04-2014-0012","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.emeraldinsight.com/doi/abs/10.1108/JFM-04-2014-0012","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Forskningsgruppen for integreret byudvikling","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Regional udvikling og bosætning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Research Group on Sustainable Cities and Housing","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Town, Housing and Property (THP)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management, Centre for Facilities Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giulia","key":"nardellipau","last":"Nardelli","name":"Nardelli, Giulia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba9f81ea-c5a0-4b37-a1ef-bcf1bc98535e","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3730-0619","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Balslev","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"37d6b355-4468-4f72-8256-afc593b8426e","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","orcid":"0000-0002-8269-6771","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/jfm-04-2014-0012","issn":["14725967","17410983"],"issn_org":["14725967"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Facilities Management","pages":"185-203","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing Limited","status":"p","title":"Journal of Facilities Management","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019695388"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-08aee14b-b751-4f73-af9a-6a287cbe011b","dtu-bbae8435-a09f-4840-9351-94b3a53e97ea"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Facilities management innovation in public-private collaborations : Danish ESCO projects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.77-000457","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Objectives Direct health provider to patient presentation of coronary computed tomography angiography findings may increase adherence to preventive therapy and risk modification. The purpose of this study was to assess the influence of visualization of coronary artery calcification and lifestyle recommendations on cholesterol concentrations and other risk variables in symptomatic patients with nonobstructive coronary artery disease and hyperlipidemia. Methods We performed a prospective 2-center randomized controlled trial. Patients were randomized 1:1 to intervention or standard follow-up in general practice. The primary end point was change in plasma total cholesterol concentration at 6 months follow-up. Results We included 189 patients (mean [± standard deviation] age 61 [12] years, 57% were male). Median (range) Agatston score was 166 (70-2054). The reduction in plasma total cholesterol concentrations tended to be higher in the intervention group than in the control group, 51.04 mg/dL versus 45.63 mg/dL (P =.181). In a subgroup including patients continuing statin therapy during follow-up (n = 147), the reduction in plasma total cholesterol concentrations was more pronounced in the intervention group than in the control group, 66.13 mg/dL versus 55.68 mg/dL (P =.027). In the intervention group, there was a higher degree of statin adherence and a higher proportion of patients who stopped smoking and commenced healthier dietary behavior than in the control group. Conclusions Visualization of coronary artery calcification and brief recommendations about risk modification after coronary computed tomography angiography in symptomatic patients with nonobstructive coronary artery disease and hyperlipidemia may have a favorable influence on plasma total cholesterol concentration, adherence to statin therapy, and risk behavior. Further investigations are needed.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Mols, Rikke Elmose","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Sand, Niels Peter","Fuglesang, Charlotte","Bagdat, Døne","Vedsted, Peter","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Nielsen, Lene Hüche","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S02-095.78-017566"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Angina pectoris","Atherosclerosis","Calcinosis diagnostic imaging","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary artery calcification","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl CoA Reductase Inhibitors therapeutic use","Hypercholesterolemia drug therapy","Lifestyle behavior","Male","Medication Adherence","Middle Aged","Patient Education as Topic","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Risk Reduction Behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visualization of coronary artery calcification influence on risk modification","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjmed.2015.03.033","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.78-017566","identifier":[{"id":"84940459947","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25910787","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-43394203-d614-47b5-8b51-b5447b59556b","sdu-a6d1885c-2a8d-442d-b646-5196de68de5e"],"keyword":["Adherence preventive therapy","Angina pectoris","Atherosclerosis","Calcinosis/diagnostic imaging","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Disease/diagnostic imaging","Coronary artery calcification","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA Reductase Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Hypercholesterolemia/drug therapy","Lifestyle behavior","Male","Medication Adherence","Middle Aged","Patient Education as Topic","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Risk Reduction Behavior","Risk factor modification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4147B8E79D7B034772C2CEC580268104"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjmed.2015.03.033","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Cardiology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nord