{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: The influence of glucagon on glycaemic control in type 1 diabetes is debated. We investigated the relationship between postprandial glucagon levels and HbA1c during a period up to 60 months after diagnosis of childhood type 1 diabetes. METHODS: The Danish remission phase cohort comprised 129 children (66 boys) with type 1 diabetes whose mean (SD) age at onset was 10.0 (3.9) years. Liquid mixed-meal tests were performed prospectively at 1, 3, 6 and 12 months and a subset of 40 patients completed follow-up at 60 months. Postprandial (90 min) plasma levels of glucagon, glucose (PG), C-peptide, total glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1), glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) and HbA1c were analysed. Multivariate regression (repeated measurements with all five visits included) was applied and results expressed as relative change (95% CI). RESULTS: Postprandial glucagon levels increased 160% from 1 to 60 months after diagnosis (p < 0.0001). A doubling in postprandial PG corresponded to a 21% increase in postprandial glucagon levels (p = 0.0079), whereas a doubling in total GLP-1 levels corresponded to a 33% increase in glucagon levels (p < 0.0001). Postprandial glucagon associated negatively with postprandial C-peptide (p = 0.017). A doubling in postprandial glucagon corresponded to a 3% relative increase in HbA1c levels (p = 0.0045). CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: Postprandial glucagon levels were associated with deterioration of glycaemic control and declining beta cell function in the first 5 years after diagnosis of type 1 diabetes. The positive association of glucagon with total GLP-1 and PG suggests that physiological regulation of alpha cell secretion in type 1 diabetes is seriously disturbed.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fredheim, Siri","Andersen, Marie-Louise M","Pörksen, Sven","Nielsen, Lotte B","Pipper, Christian Bressen","Hansen, Lars","Holst, Jens Juul","Thomsen, Jane","Johannesen, Jesper","Mortensen, Henrik B","Svensson, Jannet"],"cuid":["S02-098.57-047488"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Alpha cell regulation","Children","Glucagon","Glucagon Like Peptide 1","Glucose dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","Glycaemic control","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the influence of glucagon on postprandial hyperglycaemia in children 000000000005 years after onset of type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84925465190","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.57-047488","identifier":[{"id":"25541633","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925465190","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f77802b6-6c96-407b-ba0f-89d54f0b57fa","sdu-d25ebfc5-3b52-4f9f-9660-94f4d6d2fb57"],"keyword":["Alpha cell regulation","Children","Glucagon","Glucagon-like peptide-1","Glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide","Glycaemic control","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C4DC9390424E982C094E74E0CCEA9CBB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Paediatrics (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Siri","key":"fredheimpau","last":"Fredheim","locid":"834b9d9f-0f77-498e-bd73-0210623e3ddf","name":"Fredheim, Siri","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marie-Louise M","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Marie-Louise M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sven","key":"pörksenpau","last":"Pörksen","name":"Pörksen, Sven","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lotte B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lotte B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"pipperpau","last":"Pipper","locid":"c002fade-f477-46eb-aa1f-34702fdd3746","name":"Pipper, Christian Bressen","name_org":"Pipper, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-0261-616X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"7be933b9-8685-4e2f-90b2-5aebacecfb0f","name":"Thomsen, Jane","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"f8330122-dfc2-46b6-823b-95cdf4efab03","name":"Johannesen, Jesper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik B","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f1a10f64-1be6-42df-b4ee-7df370fcc9d0","name":"Mortensen, Henrik B","orcid":"0000-0001-9231-8363","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jannet","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"404145c9-3f7a-4360-81ae-2ee5a9ca2173","name":"Svensson, Jannet","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25541633"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-014-3486-3","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"828-834","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925465190"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f77802b6-6c96-407b-ba0f-89d54f0b57fa","sdu-d25ebfc5-3b52-4f9f-9660-94f4d6d2fb57"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The influence of glucagon on postprandial hyperglycaemia in children 5 years after onset of type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.57-047488","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To determine how often cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT) pacing systems generate visible pace spikes in the electrocardiogram (ECG). METHODS: In 46 patients treated with CRT pacing systems, we recorded ECGs during intrinsic rhythm, atrial pacing and ventricular pacing. ECGs were analysed for atrial and ventricular pace spikes by two experienced ECG readers blinded to the pacing therapy and to the study purpose. RESULTS: Atrial pacing generated visible pace spikes in less than 70% of the ECGs, whereas ventricular pacing generated visible pace spikes in about 90% of ECGs. The sensitivity of manual ECG interpretation for pace spikes was low for atrial pacing (Reader 1: 0.62 [95% confidence interval (CI) 0.50-0.74]; Reader 2: 0.65 [95% CI 0.53-0.77]) and moderate for ventricular pacing (Reader 1: 0.88 [95% CI 0.81-0.93]; Reader 2: 0.93 [95% CI 0.87-0.97]). CONCLUSIONS: In patients with CRT pacing systems, the absence of visible pace spikes in the ECG does not rule out paced rhythm.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersson, Hedvig","Hansen, Marco Bo","Thorsberger, Mads","Biering-Sørensen, Tor","Nielsen, Jonas Bille","Graff, Claus","Pehrson, Steen","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S02-098.72-001746"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic accuracy of pace spikes in the electrocardiogram to diagnose paced rhythm","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-098.72-001746","identifier":[{"id":"84941313849","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000362617000016","type":"wos"},{"id":"26278651","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-229b3045-dfdb-4cb6-9e6f-ec28ea0b5116","ku-3158634f-603f-4e31-a843-45079934493b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-207B3D6C8C8849071401E98F1C9545B0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Pleje, Observation og Førstehjælp"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Medical Informatics Group (CT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hedvig","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Hedvig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marco Bo","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b089f3da-89ef-4453-8948-ab7284cc888f","name":"Hansen, Marco Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"thorsbergerpau","last":"Thorsberger","name":"Thorsberger, Mads","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tor","key":"bieringsørensenpau","last":"Biering-Sørensen","name":"Biering-Sørensen, Tor","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Bille","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Bille","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"pehrsonpau","last":"Pehrson","name":"Pehrson, Steen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26278651"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2015.07.005","issn":["00220736","15328430"],"issn_org":["00220736"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Electrocardiology","pages":"834-839","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Electrocardiology","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941313849"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-229b3045-dfdb-4cb6-9e6f-ec28ea0b5116","ku-3158634f-603f-4e31-a843-45079934493b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diagnostic accuracy of pace spikes in the electrocardiogram to diagnose paced rhythm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.72-001746","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Soluble cancer-related protein biomarker levels may be increased in subjects without findings at large bowel endoscopy performed due to symptoms associated with colorectal cancer. The present study focused on a possible association between increased biomarker levels in such subjects and subsequent development of malignant diseases. In a major study of 4,990 subjects undergoing large bowel endoscopy, 691 were without pathology and comorbidity. Plasma levels of TIMP-1, CEA, CA19-9, and YKL-40 were determined in samples collected just before endoscopy and compared with subsequent development of a malignant disease within a period of 7-8 years. The upper 90% limits of the reference levels of every single protein were used to differentiate between normal and increased levels. The levels were separated into three groups: 0, none of the biomarkers increased; 1, one biomarker increased; 2, two or more biomarkers increased. A total of 43 subjects developed a primary malignant disease in the observation period. Univariatly, increase of all four biomarkers was significantly associated with subsequent development of a malignant disease. A multivariate analysis showed that increased biomarker levels were associated with subsequent development of a malignant disease (P = 0.002). The cumulative risk of developing malignant disease within the first 5 years after endoscopy was group 0, 3.3%; group 1, 5.8%; group 2, 7.8%. It is concluded that increased levels of plasma TIMP-1, CEA, CA19-9, and serum YKL-40 at large bowel endoscopy without findings may be associated with an increased risk of developing a subsequent malignant disease.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Kring, Thomas S","Piper, Thomas B","Jørgensen, Lars N","Olsen, Jesper","Rahr, Hans B","Nielsen, Knud T","Laurberg, Søren","Davis, Gerard","Dowell, Barry","Johansen, Julia S","Christensen, Ib J","Brünner, Nils","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-030824"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Diagnostics Division R&D","All Global Affiliations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood based biomarkers at large bowel endoscopy and prediction of future malignancies","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4137/BIC.S31330","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-030824","identifier":[{"id":"26526637","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4620935","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-fc9e2dab-58c4-4469-84ca-303d37774c4c","ku-4797b60a-d751-4866-98bb-bfaf9d78794c","sdu-2022eddc-3460-4812-8e1f-d8f8bc167150"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BDB790D1024D1268F08B8935C9ABBE49"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4137/BIC.S31330","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129608919/Blood_based_Biomarkers_at_Large_Bowel_Endoscopy_and_Prediction_of_Future_Malignancies.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/159106246/Blood_based_biomarkers_at_large_bowel_endoscopy_and_prediction_of_future_malignancies.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospi