{"abstract":"We investigate the effect of electron-phonon interactions on the coherence properties of single photons emitted from a semiconductor cavity QED (quantum electrodynamics) system, i.e., a quantum dot embedded in an optical cavity. The degree of indistinguishability, governing the quantum mechanical interference between two single photons, is calculated as a function of important parameters describing the cavity QED system and the phonon reservoir, e.g., cavity quality factor, light-matter coupling strength, temperature, and phonon lifetime. We show that non-Markovian effects play an important role in determining the coherence properties for typical parameter values and establish the conditions under which a Markovian approximation may be applied. The calculations are performed using a recently developed second-order perturbation theory, and the limits of validity are established by comparing to an exact diagonalization approach. We find that for large cavity decay rates the perturbation theory may break down.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Per Kær","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350781"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Semiconductors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decoherence in semiconductor cavity qed systems due to phonon couplings","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/100216719/PhysRevB.90.035312.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350781","identifier":[{"id":"84904638888","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9aef7a1a-54a9-46e3-9590-5ecbd3de0a16"],"keyword":["SEMICONDUCTORS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D77B28EF5F52DA03A2F772094F14AC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/100216719/PhysRevB.90.035312.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.90.035312","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.90.035312","issn":["01631829","1550235X"],"issn_org":["01631829"],"issue":"3","journal":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","paperid":"035312","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","title_org":"Physical Review B","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904638888"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9aef7a1a-54a9-46e3-9590-5ecbd3de0a16"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Decoherence in semiconductor cavity QED systems due to phonon couplings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350781","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Dense wavelength division multiplexing lasers play a major role in today's long-haul broadband communication. Typical distributed feedback laser cavities consist of long half-pitch gratings in InGaAsP on InP substrates with grating periods of around 240 nm. The lasers include a quarter wavelength shift in the grating, and are single mode with high side-mode suppression. Typically, such lasers are patterned using e-beam lithography (EBL). We present a fabrication method based on patterning by thermal nanoimprint lithography, which is potentially less costly and faster than EBL. Thermal nanoimprint lithography of laser gratings raises two types of challenges: (1) The imprint process itself is delicate due to the mechanical fragility of indium phosphide substrates and the thermal mismatch between the substrate and the silicon stamp. (2) The subsequent processing puts requirements on the imprint resist thickness after patterning, and the alignment between the crystallographic direction of the substrate and the grating pattern. Working laser arrays were produced, with >40 mW optical power and side mode suppression ratios of more than 50 dB in all 12 channels.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Smistrup, Kristian","Nørregaard, Jesper","Mironov, Andrej","Bro, Tobias H.","Bilenberg, Brian","Nielsen, Theodor","Eriksen, Johan","Thilsted, Anil Haraksingh","Hansen, Ole","Kristensen, Anders","Rishton, Stephen","Khan, ferdous","Emanuel, Mark","Ma, Young","Zhang, Yin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365634"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NeoPhotonics Corporation"],"keyword":["DFB","Dense wavelength division multiplexing","Distributed feedback lasers","Nanoimprint lithography","Process integration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nanoimprinted dwdm laser arrays on indium phosphide substrates","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mee.2014.07.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365634","ids":["dtu-cc850155-79bc-4c20-ac59-8fce8583a9cb"],"keyword":["D-WDM","DFB","Dense wavelength division multiplexing","Distributed feedback lasers","Nanoimprint lithography","Process integration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1B8217D5E74E71BCD4346E614079D144"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mee.2014.07.004","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["NIL Technology ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Optofluidics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"neophotonics corporation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NeoPhotonics Corporation","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"smistruppau","last":"Smistrup","name":"Smistrup, Kristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nørregaardpau","last":"Nørregaard","name":"Nørregaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrej","key":"mironovpau","last":"Mironov","name":"Mironov, Andrej","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias H.","key":"bropau","last":"Bro","name":"Bro, Tobias H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"bilenbergpau","last":"Bilenberg","name":"Bilenberg, Brian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Theodor","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Theodor","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"23bbe886-a6f9-4524-bfdb-0307c16e49bc","name":"Eriksen, Johan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anil Haraksingh","key":"thilstedpau","last":"Thilsted","locid":"c633f02a-963d-47d2-95e6-1ad3fbbcab59","name":"Thilsted, Anil Haraksingh","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8d678857-a721-4f7f-9a33-1dadb7401ce4","name":"Hansen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-6090-8323","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3c79a020-2c73-4e30-ac42-aee3ff272bcd","name":"Kristensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9567-1656","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephen","key":"rishtonpau","last":"Rishton","name":"Rishton, Stephen","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"ferdous","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","name":"Khan, ferdous","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"emanuelpau","last":"Emanuel","name":"Emanuel, Mark","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Young","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Young","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yin","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mee.2014.07.004","issn":["01679317","18735568"],"issn_org":["01679317"],"journal":"Microelectronic Engineering","pages":"149-153","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Microelectronic Engineering","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904969880","2-s2.0-84904997195"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","nil technology aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cc850155-79bc-4c20-ac59-8fce8583a9cb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Nanoimprinted DWDM laser arrays on indium phosphide substrates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365634","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Nuclear fusion – the process from which the Sun derives its energy – holds the potential to become a clean,safe, highly efficient, and virtually inexhaustible energy source for the future. To mimic this process on earth, experimental fusion devices seek to heat gas to millions of degrees (creating a fusion plasma) and to confine it within magnetic fields. Learning how such plasmas behave and can be controlled is a crucial step towards realizing fusion as a sustainable energy source.At the Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy (PPFE) section at DTU Physics, we are exploring these issues,focusing on areas of high priority on the way towards a working fusion power plant. On the theoreticalfront, we are simulating plasma turbulence and transport of heat and particles in fusion plasmas (Fig. 1a). These issues play a key role in determining how the plasma behaves globally and how well it remains confined in the magnetic field of the fusion device. Understanding this is important for optimizing plasmaperformance and for controlling the heat load onto the walls of the confining vessel.Experimentally, we operate equipment to measure key plasma properties in experimental fusion devices such as ASDEX Upgrade in Germany (Fig. 1b+c). Using a technique called collective Thomson scattering(CTS), we can infer the plasma composition and the dynamics of energetic ions in the plasma. Control of these parameters is vital for achieving a high fusion yield in future power plants. We are also designing CTS equipment for the next-step fusion device ITER (Fig. 1d), in which plasma temperatures will exceed 200million C. This machine is currently being built in France in a large international effort to experimentally demonstrate fusion as a viable energy source and pave the way for the first fusion power plant.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Thrysøe, Alexander Simon","Dam, Magnus","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Jensen, T.","Jessen, Martin","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Le