Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783110384154"],"isbn":["9783110349788"],"pages":"145-168","publisher":"De Gruyter","status":"p","title":"Cognitive Linguistic Explorations in Biblical Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979156027"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fe4416bc-4bc0-4457-9484-44b8f1ea0bbd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Cognitive Structures in Galatians 1:4","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-545154","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Nursing informatics, ethics and decisions: implications for translational research Objective: To introduce, in the multi-disciplinary contexts of clinical decision making and policy formation, a theory-based decision-analytic framework for the transparent forward translation of research into practice which can simultaneously identify and communicate the needs for backward translation from practice to research. Method: Web-based decision analytic software is used to demonstrate how the weights for multiple person/patient-important criteria can be combined in an expected value-calculation with evidence-based ratings for option performance on those criteria to produce a preference-sensitive assessment or opinion. Results: The first example shows the framework connecting nursing informatics and nursing ethics in the clinical context of a nurse’s decision to disclose or not disclose information to a near relative (criteria: beneficence, non-maleficence, autonomy, justice, veracity, confidentiality). The second shows it being used in a systematic review for a mini-Health Technology Assessment (HTA) on whether to invest in nurse handheld computers (criteria are patient-related (effectiveness, safety, satisfaction, Quality of Life), organization-related (staff and work environment, internal and external communication and relationships) and economics-related (start-up costs, financial implications and externalities)). Conclusion: Web-based decision support can provide nursing with a template, technique and tool for translating research findings into practice. It also can identify weaknesses in the current evidence base in order to influence research priorities. The optimal decision in each case depends on both the weights attached to the selected criteria and the performance ratings for the options for those criteria. Inevitable trade-offs can be communicated interactively in the decision-analytic framework to aid multi-disciplinary collaboration.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Dowie, Jack"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-619548"],"event":{"end":"2014-06-12","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2014-06-10","title":"Nordic Conference in Nursing Research","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","The University of Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nursing informatics ethics and decisions implications for translational research","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/108764347/kaltoft_nurses_odense_6QR_ok.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-619548","ids":["sdu-a1f78864-8996-4bc1-bb14-3785232b8456"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A53BAC776EEFD6F50FC5F6AA55C8DE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sygeplejekonference.dk/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/108764347/kaltoft_nurses_odense_6QR_ok.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"the university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"london school of hygiene and tropical medicine","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Kjer","key":"kaltoftpau","last":"Kaltoft","locid":"6f7d182a-c64a-413a-84e7-40365be224fe","name":"Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-8297","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack","key":"dowiepau","last":"Dowie","name":"Dowie, Jack","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a1f78864-8996-4bc1-bb14-3785232b8456"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Nursing informatics, ethics and decisions: implications for translational research","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-619548","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To explore the feasibility and potential of a prescriptive, web-based, decomposable measure of decision quality (MyDecisionQuality (MDQ)); to assess and enhance patient-clinician decision concordance, thereby facilitating more transparent shared decision making and documentation of better informed consent. Methods: Data presented are from patient-clinician dyads in an Inflammatory Bowel Disease decision aid study: web (log, MDQ scores, patient comments), interviews (with patients), presentations of the MDQ and concordance measures. Matched sets of MDQ data (Weightings (W) and Ratings (R) of the 8 MDQ criteria (options, effects, importance, chances; trust, support, control, commitment) were elicited and fed back in decomposed formats, along with concordance measures (Mean Squared Difference (MSD), Mean Absolute Difference (MAD)). The Incremental Values of Perfect Ratings were calculated to quantify, document, and suggest how future dyadic decisions can be enhanced by criterion prioritisation. Associations between patient’s MDQ-W before, and MDQ-R after consultation with their clinician were analysed along with patient scores from the Satisfaction With Decision (SWD) instrument. Results: Patient’s online feedback quotes and face-to-face interviews suggested that the MDQ instrument prompted increased decision thought. The 8 MDQ criteria were interpreted as providing an acceptable decision quality instrument. Of the illustrative results for two dyads, the first displayed perfect concordance on both W and R for options and control, but otherwise a discordant W distribution. The other dyad showed more discordant W and R. The MSDs of W and R were .0275 and .0175 for the former patient and .0150 and .0025 for the latter. The MADs of W and R were .1250 and .1000 for the former and .1000 and .0250 for the latter. The patient’s MDQ scores were .886 and .954 with SWD scores of 1.0 and .8 respectively. (The correlation between MDQ and SWD instruments for the initial 29 patients was 0.70.) Conclusion: Proof of concept and method is presented in relation to the degree of concordance between patient and clinician using the dually-personalised decomposable MyDecisionQuality (MDQ) instrument. This has the potential to guide future work on optimising dyad-specific patient-clinician communication for shared decision making and informed consent.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","Selby, Warwick","Salkeld, Glenn","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Dowie, Jack"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627629"],"event":{"end":"2014-06-10","place":"Antwerpen, be","start":"2014-06-08","title":"15th Biennial European Meeting","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","The University of Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing shared decision making through assessment of patient clinician concordance on decision quality","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://smdm.org/meeting/15th-biennial-european-meeting","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627629","ids":["sdu-bdc84dcb-3b22-43aa-98a3-dd834ea96f78"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-22F545BA40CC49549BB68B17CFB14F57"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://smdm.org/meeting/15th-biennial-european-meeting","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"the university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"london school of hygiene and tropical medicine","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Kjer","key":"kaltoftpau","last":"Kaltoft","locid":"6f7d182a-c64a-413a-84e7-40365be224fe","name":"Kaltoft, Mette Kjer","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-8297","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Warwick","key":"selbypau","last":"Selby","name":"Selby, Warwick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Glenn","key":"salkeldpau","last":"Salkeld","name":"Salkeld, Glenn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack","key":"dowiepau","last":"Dowie","name":"Dowie, Jack","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bdc84dcb-3b22-43aa-98a3-dd834ea96f78"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Enhancing shared decision making through assessment of patient-clinician concordance on decision quality","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627629","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The study investigated the noise exposure in a group of Danish school teachers. The aims were to investigate if noise posed a risk of impairment of hearing and to study the association between classroom acoustical conditions, noise exposure, vocal symptoms, and cognitive fatigue. METHODS: Background noise levels, vocal load and speaking time were measured on 35 teachers during actual classroom teaching. The classrooms were characterized acoustically by measurements of reverberation time. Before and after the workday, the teachers answered a questionnaire on fatigue symptoms and carried out two cognitive test tasks sensitive to mental fatigue. RESULTS: The average noise level during the lessons was 72 dB(A), but during indoor sports activities the average noise level increased 6.6 dB(A). Room reverberation time (range 0.39-0.83 s) had no significant effect on the noise level. The teachers were talking with a raised voice in 61 % of the time, and the vocal load increased 0.65 dB(A) per dB(A) increase in the average lesson noise level. An increase in voice symptoms during the workday correlated significantly with individual average noise exposure, and a decrease in performance in the two-back test correlated significantly with individual average vocal load. CONCLUSIONS: Noise exposure in general classrooms posed no risk of noise-induced hearing impairment in school teachers. However, the results provide evidence for an association between noise exposure and vocal load and development of vocal symptoms and cognitive fatigue after work","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kristiansen, Jesper","Lund, Søren Peter","Persson, Stig Roger","Shibuya, Hitomi","Nielsen, P.M.","Scholz, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-781865"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a study of classroom acoustics and school teachers noise exposure voice load and speaking time during teaching and the effects on vocal and mental fatigue","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84919496023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-781865","identifier":[{"id":"84919496023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["nfa-d6554b87-90d4-4ccf-bca6-89b0671f6107"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-248EC55E9B632CBFEFBC2E984443C96D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Peter","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Søren Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Roger","key":"perssonpau","last":"Persson","locid":"119c15fc-ec5e-4c8a-a017-bf96d5148ebf","name":"Persson, Stig Roger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hitomi","key":"shibuyapau","last":"Shibuya","locid":"7e393310-d5ce-4aa8-8159-c8c36dfb0b81","name":"Shibuya, Hitomi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"P.M.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, P.M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"scholzpau","last":"Scholz","name":"Scholz, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00420-014-0927-8","issn":["03400131","14315777"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","pages":"851-860","status":"p","title":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84919496023"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-d6554b87-90d4-4ccf-bca6-89b0671f6107"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"A study of classroom acoustics and school teachers' noise exposure, voice load and speaking time during teaching, and the effects on vocal and mental fatigue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-781865","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"spa typing of methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) has traditionally been done by PCR amplification and Sanger sequencing of the spa repeat region. At Hvidovre Hospital, Denmark, whole-genome sequencing (WGS) of all MRSA isolates has been performed routinely since January 2013, and an in-house analysis pipeline determines the spa types. Due to national surveillance, all MRSA isolates are sent to Statens Serum Institut, where the spa type is determined by PCR and Sanger sequencing. The purpose of this study was to evaluate the reliability of the spa types obtained by 150-bp paired-end Illumina WGS. MRSA isolates from new MRSA patients in 2013 (n = 699) in the capital region of Denmark were included. We found a 97% agreement between spa types obtained by the two methods. All isolates achieved a spa type by both methods. Nineteen isolates differed in spa types by the two methods, in most cases due to the lack of 24-bp repeats in the whole-genome-sequenced isolates. These related but incorrect spa types should have no consequence in outbreak investigations, since all epidemiologically linked isolates, regardless of spa type, will be included in the single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) analysis. This will reveal the close relatedness of the spa types. In conclusion, our data show that WGS is a reliable method to determine the spa type of MRSA.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Bartels, Mette Damkjaer","Petersen, Andreas","Worning, Peder","Nielsen, Jesper Boye","Larner-Svensson, Hanna","Johansen, Helle Krogh","Andersen, Leif Percival","Jarlov, Jens Otto","Boye, Kit","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Westh, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-085.50-032826"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparing whole genome sequencing with sanger sequencing for spa typing of methicillin resistant staphylococcus aureus","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.01979-14","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-085.50-032826","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4313303","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84910145816","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25297335","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-0a6735d6-1e64-48d0-967c-ec98824093a3","ku-0c1ff3c6-34b4-430b-b784-1197df2e42be"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D16D5A08982BB4BA8F547EDB39A1E3D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.01979-14","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability, Bacterial Cell Factories"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Damkjær","key":"bartelspau","last":"Bartels","name":"Bartels, Mette Damkjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peder","key":"worningpau","last":"Worning","name":"Worning, Peder","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Boye","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Boye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanna","key":"larnersvenssonpau","last":"Larner-Svensson","name":"Larner-Svensson, Hanna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Krogh","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"7d64ceb7-6c81-415d-ab2b-f7f607a6570a","name":"Johansen, Helle Krogh","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leif Percival","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Leif Percival","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Otto","key":"jarløvpau","last":"Jarløv","name":"Jarløv, Jens Otto","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kit","key":"boyepau","last":"Boye","name":"Boye, Kit","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Rhod","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Rhod","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Henrik","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25297335"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/jcm.01979-14","issn":["00951137","1070633X"],"issn_org":["00951137"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","pages":"4305-4308","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84910145816"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0a6735d6-1e64-48d0-967c-ec98824093a3","ku-0c1ff3c6-34b4-430b-b784-1197df2e42be"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparing Whole-Genome Sequencing with Sanger Sequencing for spa Typing of Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.50-032826","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"To evaluate the diagnostic accuracy of aortic valve area (AVA) assessment with 320-detector Computed Tomography (MDCT) compared to transthoracic echocardiography (TTE) in a population with mild to severe aortic valve stenosis. AVA was estimated in 169 patients by planimetry on MDCT images (AVA(MDCT)) and by the continuity equation with TTE (AVA(TTE)). To generate a reference AVA (AVA(REF)) we used the stroke volume from MDCT divided by the velocity time integral from CW Doppler by TTE (according to the continuity equation: stroke volume in LVOT = stroke volume passing the aortic valve). AVA(REF) was used as the reference to compare both measures against, since it bypasses the assumption of LVOT being circular in the continuity equation and the potential placement error of PW Doppler in the LVOT. The mean (±SD) age of the patients was 71 (±9) years, 113 (67%) were males. Mean AVA(TTE) was 0.93 (±0.33) cm(2), mean AVA(MDCT) was 0.99 (±0.36) cm(2) and mean AVA(REF) was 1.00 (±0.39) cm(2). The mean difference between AVA(TTE) and AVA(MDCT) was -0.06 cm(2), p = 0.001, mean difference between AVA(TTE) and AVA(REF) was -0.06 cm(2), p < 0.001, and mean difference between AVA(MDCT) and AVA(REF) was -0.01 cm(2), p = 0.60. Calcification of the aortic valve quantified by Agatston score, significantly decreased the correlation between AVA(MDCT) and AVA(REF), (r low Agatston = 0.90, r high Agatston = 0.57). MDCT measured AVA is slightly larger than AVA measured by TTE (0.06 cm(2)). The accuracy and precision errors on AVA measurements are comparable for MDCT and TTE. Valvular calcification may primarily affect the accuracy of AVA(MDCT).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Linnea Hornbech","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Carstensen, Helle Gervig","Mejdahl, Mads Rams","Andersen, Mads Jønsson","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Køber, Lars","Møgelvang, Rasmus","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-088.60-030788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Aortic Valve","Aortic Valve Stenosis","Calcinosis","Comparative Study","Echocardiography Doppler","Evaluation Studies","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Predictive Value of Tests","Radiographic Image Interpretation Computer Assisted","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Severity of Illness Index"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aortic valve area assessed with 000000000320 detector computed tomography comparison with transthoracic echocardiography","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10554-013-0295-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.60-030788","identifier":[{"id":"84898900558","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24126620","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-fc0b8a92-d022-40ee-b74b-9c7f8d8805c5","ku-de18d048-26a9-4571-bb1d-8b9a6a51ce52"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Aortic Valve","Aortic Valve Stenosis","Calcinosis","Comparative Study","Echocardiography, Doppler","Evaluation Studies","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Predictive Value of Tests","Radiographic Image Interpretation, Computer-Assisted","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Severity of Illness Index"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7CE8249D4BDF610DECE17EB13C935271"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10554-013-0295-6","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Linnea Hornbech","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Linnea Hornbech","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus Fuglsang","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Gervig","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","name":"Carstensen, Helle Gervig","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Rams","key":"mejdahlpau","last":"Mejdahl","name":"Mejdahl, Mads Rams","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Jønsson","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"19d72cda-3d6c-4f48-9d4b-6fe5dee888ba","name":"Andersen, Mads Jønsson","orcid":"0000-0002-9320-8227","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olav Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"møgelvangpau","last":"Møgelvang","name":"Møgelvang, Rasmus","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24126620"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10554-013-0295-6","issn":["15695794","18758312"],"issn_org":["15695794"],"issue":"1","journal":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"165-73","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84898900558"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fc0b8a92-d022-40ee-b74b-9c7f8d8805c5","ku-de18d048-26a9-4571-bb1d-8b9a6a51ce52"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aortic valve area assessed with 320-detector computed tomography : comparison with transthoracic echocardiography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.60-030788","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The potential gains from a regulatory change allowing for reallocation of marketable nitrogen emission permits under a cap and trade system are analyzed in a dynamic context using Data Envelopment Analysis to formulate linear programming models. In these models new, more environmental friendly farms are gradually introduced to the industry over 10 years. The new industry structure, production, and profitability gains are investigated, and the effect of changing the overall level of nitrogen emission is analyzed. Our results show that there is scope for a more efficient allocation of resources to either increase the production level or to reduce the emission level. This article adds to the literature by extending previous static reallocation models to a dynamic model, which allows for a gradual introduction of new firms. This makes it possible for managers to analyze the effects of reallocating production across firms and time.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rasmus","Levring Andersen, Jesper","Bogetoft, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-095.71-031323"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aquaculture"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic reallocation of marketable nitrogen emission permits in danish freshwater aquaculture","src":["cbs","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1086/677758","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.71-031323","identifier":[{"id":"84928790759","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-2fbfff77-03f2-4a25-b945-117c5ab01292","ku-e53cd703-1d70-4104-938e-98636681c4fa"],"keyword":["Aquaculture","Data development analysis","Dynamic reallocation","Marketable nitrogen emission permits"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3917F03EECF33EDA08F01A6431C59E03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1086/677758","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Environment and Natural Resources"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f6e4af88-d330-4a75-8435-e502a8c24df7","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-7357-6965","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Levring","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"72c137de-8212-41ed-ac15-9d04635c2559","name":"Andersen, Jesper Levring","orcid":"0000-0001-6963-5053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"bogetoftpau","last":"Bogetoft","locid":"a44168f7-050b-4094-8df4-c341d55837aa","name":"Bogetoft, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-2173-2791","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1086/677758","issn":["07381360","23345985"],"issn_org":["07381360"],"issue":"3","journal":"Marine Resource Economics","pages":"219-239","publisher":"University of Chicago Press","status":"p","title":"Marine Resource Economics","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928790759"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-2fbfff77-03f2-4a25-b945-117c5ab01292","ku-e53cd703-1d70-4104-938e-98636681c4fa"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic Reallocation of Marketable Nitrogen Emission Permits in Danish Freshwater Aquaculture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.71-031323","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Survivors after cardiac arrest (CA) exhibits a systemic inflammatory response as part of post-cardiac arrest syndrome (PCAS). We investigated the association between systemic inflammation and severity of PCAS and whether level of targeted temperature management (TTM) modifies level of the inflammatory response. METHODS: We studied 169 patients included at a single center in the TTM-trial, randomly assigned to TTM at 33 °C or 36 °C for 24 h. Plasma samples were analyzed for inflammatory markers including interleukin (IL) IL-1β,IL-4,IL-6,IL-10, tumor necrosis factor-α (TNF-α), C-reactive protein (CRP) and procalcitonin (PCT) at randomization and 24, 48 and 72 h after CA. Severity of PCAS was assessed by Sequential Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score. RESULTS: Plasma levels of both IL-6 and IL-10 determined at randomization correlated with severity of PCAS at day 2 (r=0.36 and r=0.27, p<0.001) and day 3 (r=0.32 and r=0.22, p<0.001). IL-6 at randomization was an independent predictor of severity of PCAS at day 2 (p=0.003) and day 3 (p<0.0001) and was a significantly stronger predictor of severity of PCAS at day 3 compared to CRP (p=0.04) and PCT (p=0.03). Level of TTM did not modify level of the inflammatory markers IL-1β, IL-6, TNF-α, IL-4, IL-10, CRP and PCT, (p=NS for each inflammatory marker). CONCLUSIONS: Level of inflammatory response was associated with severity of PCAS with IL-6 being consistently and more strongly associated with severity of PCAS than the inflammatory markers CRP and PCT. The systemic inflammatory response after CA was not modified by TTM at 33 °C or 36 °C.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bro-Jeppesen, John","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Wanscher, Michael","Nielsen, Niklas","Friberg, Hans","Bjerre, Mette","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-098.91-017306"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the inflammatory response after out of hospital cardiac arrest is not modified by targeted temperature management at 000000000033 c or 000000000036 c","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.08.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.91-017306","identifier":[{"id":"25150183","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84908238128","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3f48ce75-88ca-425d-accd-b46c9fa3dbb5","ku-14ce75d6-b4de-40c4-9b28-5360648dac91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7CA82AA243B7D00FD3F48E3212676870"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.08.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"brojeppesenpau","last":"Bro-Jeppesen","name":"Bro-Jeppesen, John","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"d2d434a4-221d-4c1a-a9c6-466340d150e0","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Hans","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"1337eaca-a3a1-4837-a772-261478be9f37","name":"Bjerre, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25150183"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2014.08.007","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"issue":"11","journal":"Resuscitation","pages":"1480-7","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84908238128"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3f48ce75-88ca-425d-accd-b46c9fa3dbb5","ku-14ce75d6-b4de-40c4-9b28-5360648dac91"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The inflammatory response after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest is not modified by targeted temperature management at 33 °C or 36 °C","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.91-017306","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Knowledge regarding knee and ankle joint load across a range of running speeds is important, if running related injuries are to be prevented. The purpose of the present study was to test the hypothesis that peak plantar flexion moment increases relatively more than peak knee extension moment when running speed is increased. METHODS: Kinematic and ground reaction force data were collected from 33 recreational runners during steady-state running at three different speeds: 7.96km·h(-1) (SD 0.18), 11.92km·h(-1) (SD 0.25) and 15.91km·h(-1) (SD 0.36). Peak plantar flexion moment and peak knee extension moment were calculated using a standard three-dimensional inverse dynamics approach. FINDINGS: There was a significant interaction between the joint location and the running speed (P=0.03): When running speed increased from 7.96 to 15.91km·h(-1), mean peak plantar flexion moment increased by 0.74N·m·kg(-1) (95% CI: 0.64; 0.85) which was more than the 0.52N·m·kg(-1) (95% CI: 0.42; 0.63) increase in mean peak knee extension moment. INTERPRETATION: A greater increase in biomechanical load occurs for the plantar flexors of the ankle joint than for the extensors of the knee joint when running speed increases. This may indicate that at an excessive running speed, the structures at the posterior part of the lower leg and underneath the foot are relatively more vulnerable to injury compared with the structures at the anterior part of the knee. As a considerable load reduction is achieved, a decrease in running speed may benefit rearfoot striking recreational runners experiencing pain in the posterior lower leg or underneath the foot.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Petersen, Jesper Hansen","Nielsen, Rasmus Østergaard","Rasmussen, Sten","Sørensen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002966"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparisons of increases in knee and ankle joint moments following an increase in running speed from 000000000008 to 000000000012 to 000000000016km h sup 000000000001 sup","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2014.09.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002966","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000346222100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84913552765","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25242200","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-3c63ab11-a101-4c01-8445-70265784c8f1","au-1e524982-58a9-471d-9f56-a8513e206f18"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3896535943095D12084598BFCA848E58"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2014.09.003","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Hansen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9ce6b4dc-b9b3-48d6-9ae1-4b0f4613d31f","name":"Petersen, Jesper Hansen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus O","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6f7c8db1-3883-45ae-9517-48f086dce130","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus Østergaard","name_org":"Nielsen, Rasmus O","orcid":"0000-0001-5757-1806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"29717b7b-a132-446a-a12b-23cc9f139476","name":"Sørensen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25242200"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2014.09.003","issn":["02680033","18791271"],"issn_org":["02680033"],"issue":"9","journal":"Clinical Biomechanics","pages":"959-964","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Clinical Biomechanics","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84913552765"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3c63ab11-a101-4c01-8445-70265784c8f1","au-1e524982-58a9-471d-9f56-a8513e206f18"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Comparisons of increases in knee and ankle joint moments following an increase in running speed from 8 to 12 to 16km·h <sup>-1</sup>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-002966","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Screening programmes for colorectal cancer (CRC) are being implemented in various countries worldwide including Denmark. The majority of programmes rely on faecal occult blood testing with subsequent colonoscopy. This approach is challenged by limited compliance, which reduces the efficiency of the screening programme. Current research into improve-ments of screening of CRC includes biological markers identified in blood. Combining blood-based biological markers with clinical and demographical parameters have shown promising results, which may improve the present approach to screening.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Louise","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Madsen, Mogens Rørbæk","Vilandt, Jesper","Klærke, Michael","Andersen, Jens","Nielsen, Knud T","Khalid, Ali","Laurberg, Søren","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Brünner, Nils","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024426"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metoder til screening for kolorektal cancer kan forbedres","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84903761523","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024426","identifier":[{"id":"25350810","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84903761523","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a0a1766e-acb8-45a4-ac1a-ff7924ef2522","ku-b9debe63-abcd-457b-b1b8-65ad74897740"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8D8FC445E81EFE61B11C6666113F97ED"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","k