{"abstract":"In the last few years garbled circuits (GC) have been elevated from being merely a component in Yao’s protocol for secure two-party computation, to a cryptographic primitive in its own right, following the growing number applications that use GCs. Zero-Knowledge (ZK) protocols is one of these examples: In a recent paper Jawurek et al. [JKO13] showed that GCs can be used to construct efficient ZK for unstructured languages. In this work we show that due to the property of this particular scenario (i.e., one of the party knows all the secret input bits, and therefore all intermediate values in the computation), we can construct more efficient garbled schemes specifically tailored to this goal. As a highlight of our result, in one of our constructions only one encryption per gate needs to be communicated and XOR gates never require any cryptographic operation. In addition to making a step forward towards more practical ZK, we believe that our contribution is also interesting from a conceptual point of view: in the terminology of Bellare et al. [BHR12] our garbling schemes achieve authenticity, but no privacy nor obliviousness, therefore representing the first natural separation between those notions","author_count":3,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Tore Kasper","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Orlandi, Claudio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239749"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"privacy free garbled circuits with applications to efficient zero knowledge","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://eprint.iacr.org/2014/598.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239749","ids":["au-c17d4c16-a750-447b-8c3d-5ee7cf8fd01e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F2026A2CC935F9F1AF7AF1C74EDC3EA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://eprint.iacr.org/2014/598.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tore Kasper","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"b96bd502-b384-44c2-9a99-2386d87d22b8","name":"Frederiksen, Tore Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claudio","key":"orlandipau","last":"Orlandi","locid":"393c3898-d32f-431e-aea6-ee1e79c535ef","name":"Orlandi, Claudio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Cryptology ePrint Archive","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c17d4c16-a750-447b-8c3d-5ee7cf8fd01e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Privacy-Free Garbled Circuits with Applications To Efficient Zero-Knowledge","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239749","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Filamentous Desulfobulbaceae have been reported to conduct electrons over centimetre-long distances, thereby coupling oxygen reduction at the surface of marine sediment to sulphide oxidation in sub-surface layers. To understand how these /`cable bacteria/' establish and sustain electric conductivity, we followed a population for 53 days after exposing sulphidic sediment with initially no detectable filaments to oxygen. After 10 days, cable bacteria and electric currents were established throughout the top 15[thinsp]mm of the sediment, and after 21 days the filament density peaked with a total length of 2[thinsp]km[thinsp]cm-2. Cells elongated and divided at all depths with doubling times over the first 10 days of <20[thinsp]h. Active, oriented movement must have occurred to explain the separation of O2 and H2S by 15[thinsp]mm. Filament diameters varied from 0.4-1.7[thinsp][mu]m, with a general increase over time and depth, and yet they shared 16S rRNA sequence identity of >98%. Comparison of the increase in biovolume and electric current density suggested high cellular growth efficiency. While the vertical expansion of filaments continued over time and reached 30[thinsp]mm, the electric current density and biomass declined after 13 and 21 days, respectively. This might reflect a breakdown of short filaments as their solid sulphide sources became depleted in the top layers of the anoxic zone. In conclusion, cable bacteria combine rapid and efficient growth with oriented movement to establish and exploit the spatially separated half-reactions of sulphide oxidation and oxygen consumption.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schauer, Regina","Risgaard-Petersen, Nils","Kjeldsen, Kasper Urup","Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","Jørgensen, Bo Barker","Schramm, Andreas","Nielsen, Lars Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cable bacteria Desulfobulbaceae electric currents filament growth marine sediment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"succession of cable bacteria and electric currents in marine sediment","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ismej.2013.239","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239942","identifier":[{"id":"84901283551","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4030233","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24451206","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c1d4e2ca-bbc9-4d1d-8a71-b22da7a04b6d"],"keyword":["cable bacteria; Desulfobulbaceae; electric currents; filament growth; marine sediment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16737C5DDC35EB04A2F88CAA0FCC6292"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nature.com/doifinder/10.1038/ismej.2013.239","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ismej.2013.239","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Geomicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Regina","key":"schauerpau","last":"Schauer","locid":"b1a71cf8-aef9-441f-9620-7902d5440b6f","name":"Schauer, Regina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"risgaardpetersenpau","last":"Risgaard-Petersen","locid":"f722845a-947c-4408-bedc-7a338f234420","name":"Risgaard-Petersen, Nils","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper Urup","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"70f809ce-0110-40e4-ad60-77e80799c7e9","name":"Kjeldsen, Kasper Urup","orcid":"0000-0002-7805-5605","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Jensen","key":"bjergpau","last":"Bjerg","locid":"682ae3d8-d830-4101-b5a3-494ea2e4e0be","name":"Bjerg, Jesper Jensen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo Barker","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9a3b819c-1b8e-4d4d-8d87-998f4aa91ef1","name":"Jørgensen, Bo Barker","orcid":"0000-0001-9398-8027","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b1f70e1-663b-4a12-b10c-a12dfc320c81","name":"Nielsen, Lars Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7269-4860","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24451206"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ismej.2013.239","issn":["17517362","17517370"],"issn_org":["17517362"],"journal":"ISME Journal","pages":"1314-1322","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"ISME Journal","title_org":"I S M E Journal","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901283551"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c1d4e2ca-bbc9-4d1d-8a71-b22da7a04b6d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Succession of cable bacteria and electric currents in marine sediment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239942","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Purpose:  To evaluate indications for paediatric keratoplasty in recipients aged ≤16 years and assess long-term clinical outcome. Method:  Recipients were identified from records of the Danish Cornea Bank. Data were collected from patient journals, clinical follow-up examinations and questionnaires and stratified into pre-, peri- and postoperative variables. Diagnoses were classified into acquired traumatic, acquired nontraumatic and congenital groups. Recipients were divided into groups of","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hovlykke, Maria","Hjortdal, Jesper","Ehlers, Niels","Nielsen, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-250987"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical results of 000000000040 years of paediatric keratoplasty in a single university eye clinic","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12198x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-250987","identifier":[{"id":"84901372184","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23879323","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d5146826-1416-41f1-89c9-6f838f27ea7b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9DB44304A823397602E617D50CA82A0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12198x","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"hovlykkepau","last":"Hovlykke","name":"Hovlykke, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"ehlerspau","last":"Ehlers","name":"Ehlers, Niels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23879323"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.12198x","issn":["17553768"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Ophthamologica","pages":"370-7","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthamologica","title_org":"Acta Ophthalmologica (Online)","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901372184"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d5146826-1416-41f1-89c9-6f838f27ea7b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Clinical results of 40 years of paediatric keratoplasty in a single university eye clinic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-250987","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"During the last decade selecting and developing talent has been an increasing focus in the Danish school system. An indication of this is the new tendency in the Danish educational system, where schools are able to create thematic tracks for students who show a special interest in or a talent for a certain activity. Among some of the thematic tracks are Sports Classes; a combined school and sport program developed for talented young athletes in grade 7th-9th in the public elementary schools by The Sports Confederation of Denmark (DIF) and Team Danmark (The Danish elite sport organization). The sport classes build upon collaboration between the Danish public schools and sports clubs. They are traditionally driven by different institutional logics and purposes. The sports clubs’ main purpose is to select and develop talents who can compete nationally and internationally, while the purpose of the Danish schools is to educate all students and secure their versatile development. In this paper we focus on how students applying for the sports classes are selected through a sport specific entrance examination. The selection process for the sports classes is different from the general way students enter the Danish public schools. Traditionally students enter local schools and are put in randomly assembled classes. In contrast, students in the sports classes are applicants from a larger regional area and they are chosen because of their talent in sport. The selection process ensures that the sports classes form an elite environment that stimulates the students’ dedication to their formation as potential elite athletes. Thus the maintenance of the elite environment depends on the student ability and willingness to stick to a rather narrow learning track towards an ambitious goal. In order to ensure that the students comply with the sports classes’ code of conduct, it seems that the schools try to oblige the individual student to a particular personal development. By applying Brembeck and Johanssons (2010) use of the Deleuzian concepts ‘I-am’ and ‘I-do, we will be able to analyse how sports classes distribute talent representations to students and the different ways students choose to perform talent. The ethnographic methods applied are a combination of observations of different sport specific entrance examinations and interviews with coaches, athletes, parents and teachers. The empirical study is carried out in four different cities in Denmark and it is part of a national research project focusing on Sports Classes. The analysis shows that the students are obliged to follow a particular development towards the elite. The paper discuss whether and how this highly focused learning trail as an effect excludes alternative ways of becoming and doing talent.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Skrubbeltrang, Lotte","Stilling Olesen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-251086"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Childhood studies","Deleuze","Dual becoming","Grundskole","Idrætsklasser","Kultur","Talent","Talent development"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to stay becoming living up to the code of conduct in a sport class","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-251086","ids":["au-d53ff630-43d0-4772-8ecf-d311f3ded837"],"keyword":["Childhood Studies","Deleuze","Dual becoming","Grundskole","Idrætsklasser","Kultur","Talent","Talent Development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BDE7882E33785F0A063946FBE49AC940"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University (AAU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Research Programme for Diversity, Culture and Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"skrubbeltrangpau","last":"Skrubbeltrang","name":"Skrubbeltrang, Lotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"25","place":"København","publisher":"Institut for Uddannelse og Pædagogik (DPU), Aarhus Universitet","publisher_org":"Institut for Uddannelse og Pædagogik (DPU) Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d53ff630-43d0-4772-8ecf-d311f3ded837"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How to stay becoming : living up to the code of conduct in a sport class","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-251086","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","David, Bernardo Machado","Giacomelli, Irene","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253113"],"event":{"end":"2014-12-11","place":"Kaoshiung , tw","start":"2014-12-07","title":"International Conference on the Theory and Application of Cryptology and Information Security","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"compact vss and efficient homomorphic uc commitments","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-45608-8_12","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253113","identifier":[{"id":"84916230072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d8d78078-2445-458e-a21d-4d7a99875123"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9561D3D4957C1DB806788B2078F6987A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-45608-8_12","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007%2F978-3-662-45608-8_12#","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan Bjerre","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernardo Machado","key":"davidpau","last":"David","locid":"e39dd946-3171-4c2c-acc2-0990fe5230b3","name":"David, Bernardo Machado","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"giacomellipau","last":"Giacomelli","locid":"7cc44141-fd00-4611-9623-f209b88c750b","name":"Giacomelli, Irene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Palash","key":"sarkarpedh","last":"Sarkar","name":"Sarkar, Palash","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tetsu","key":"iwatapedh","last":"Iwata","name":"Iwata, Tetsu","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-45608-8_12","eisbn":["9783662456088"],"isbn":["9783662456071"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"213-232","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th International Conference on the Theory and Application of Cryptology and Information Security, Kaoshiung, Taiwan, R.O.C., December 7-11, 2014, Proceedings, Part II","title":"Advances in Cryptology – ASIACRYPT 2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84916230072"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d8d78078-2445-458e-a21d-4d7a99875123"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Compact VSS and Efficient Homomorphic UC Commitments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253113","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Understanding the behaviour of the confined fast ions is important in both current and future fusion experiments. These ions play a key role in heating the plasma and will be crucial for achieving conditions for burning plasma in next-step fusion devices. Microwave-based Collective Thomson Scattering (CTS) is well suited for reactor conditions and offers such an opportunity by providing measurements of the confined fast-ion distribution function resolved in space, time and 1D velocity space. We currently operate a CTS system at ASDEX Upgrade using a gyrotron which generates probing radiation at 105 GHz. A new setup using two independent receiver systems has enabled improved subtraction of the background signal, and hence the first accurate characterization of fast-ion properties. Here we review this new dual-receiver CTS setup and present results on fast-ion measurements based on the improved background characterization. These results have been obtained both with and without NBI heating, and with the measurement volume located close to the centre of the plasma. The measurements agree quantitatively with predictions of numerical simulations. Hence, CTS studies of fast-ion dynamics at ASDEX Upgrade are now feasible. The new background subtraction technique could be important for the design of CTS systems in other fusion experiments.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Salewski, Mirko","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Meo, Fernando","Michelsen, Poul","Moseev, Dmitry","Schubert, M.","Stober, J.","Tardini, G.","Wagner, D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334482"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-13","place":"Varenna, it","start":"2013-09-09","title":"International Conference on Fusion Reactor Diagnostics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","Max Planck Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved collective thomson scattering measurements of fast ions at asdex upgrade","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/88348805/1310.2406v1_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-334482","identifier":[{"id":"84907385627","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-645630aa-b447-45ee-aa07-2a6c5ed9219f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-383EA8D5FB40A542818250B0EDB3251D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/88348805/1310.2406v1_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"dutch institute for fundamental energy research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dutch Institute for Fundamental Energy Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","firs