 Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781784910518"],"isbn":["9781784910501"],"pages":"51-64","place":"Oxford","publisher":"Archaeopress","series":"Archaeopress Pre-Columbian Archaeology","status":"p","title":"Palaces and Courtly Culture in Ancient Mesoamerica"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-41d6b5f0-d314-4fb1-9ab5-bd2da94d25f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Center of Power : Tasks and Strategies of the Mexica Court","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432795","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Atrial fibrillation (AF) is the most common cardiac arrhythmia affecting 1-2% of the general population. A number of studies have demonstrated that AF, and in particular lone AF, has a substantial genetic component. Monogenic mutations in lone and familial AF, although rare, have been recognized for many years. Presently, mutations in 25 genes have been associated with AF. However, the complexity of monogenic AF is illustrated by the recent finding that both gain- and loss-of-function mutations in the same gene can cause AF. Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have indicated that common single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) have a role in the development of AF. Following the first GWAS discovering the association between PITX2 and AF, several new GWAS reports have identified SNPs associated with susceptibility of AF. To date, nine SNPs have been associated with AF. The exact biological pathways involving these SNPs and the development of AF are now starting to be elucidated. Since the first GWAS, the number of papers concerning the genetic basis of AF has increased drastically and the majority of these papers are for the first time included in a review. In this review, we discuss the genetic basis of AF and the role of both common and rare genetic variants in the susceptibility of developing AF. Furthermore, all rare variants reported to be associated with AF were systematically searched for in the Exome Sequencing Project Exome Variant Server.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Olesen, Morten S","Nielsen, Morten W","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438490"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Genetic Loci","Homeodomain Proteins","Humans","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Transcription Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atrial fibrillation the role of common and rare genetic variants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejhg.2013.139","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438490","identifier":[{"id":"23838598","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84894387715","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3925267","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4b8c67f5-cd61-4282-a7ff-3a39688433fa"],"keyword":["Atrial Fibrillation","Genetic Loci","Homeodomain Proteins","Humans","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Transcription Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB20FD57314FC8CAD4233A0380768517"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejhg.2013.139","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten W","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bfd09d1f-fd5c-4259-9ae5-3ccc48c85386","name":"Nielsen, Morten W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper H","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","name_org":"Svendsen, Jesper H","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23838598"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ejhg.2013.139","issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"297-306","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84894387715"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4b8c67f5-cd61-4282-a7ff-3a39688433fa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Atrial fibrillation : the role of common and rare genetic variants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438490","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Several studies have shown an overlap between genes involved in the pathophysiological mechanisms of atrial fibrillation (AF) and Brugada Syndrome (BrS). We investigated whether three single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) (rs11708996; G>C located intronic to SCN5A, rs10428132; T>G located in SCN10A, and rs9388451; T>C located downstream to HEY2) at loci associated with BrS in a recent genome-wide association study (GWAS) also were associated with AF. A total of 657 patients diagnosed with AF and a control group comprising 741 individuals free of AF were included. The three SNPs were genotyped using TaqMan assays. The frequencies of risk alleles in the AF population and the control population were compared in two-by-two models. One variant, rs10428132 at SCN10A, was associated with a statistically significant decreased risk of AF (odds ratio (OR)=0.77, P=0.001). A meta-analysis was performed by enriching the control population with allele frequencies from controls in the recently published BrS GWAS (2230 alleles). In this meta-analysis, both rs10428132 at SCN10A (OR=0.73, P=5.7 × 10(-6)) and rs11708996 at SCN5A (OR=0.80, P=0.02) showed a statistically significant decreased risk of AF. When assessing the additive effect of the three loci, we found that the risk of AF decreased in a dose-responsive manner with increasing numbers of risk alleles (OR=0.50, P=0.001 for individuals carrying ≥4 risk alleles vs ≤1 allele). In conclusion, the prevalence of three risk alleles previously associated with BrS was lower in AF patients than in patients free of AF, suggesting a protective role of these loci in developing AF.European Journal of Human Genetics advance online publication, 26 March 2014; doi:10.1038/ejhg.2014.46.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Andreasen, Laura","Nielsen, Jonas B","Darkner, Stine","Christophersen, Ingrid E","Jabbari, Javad","Refsgaard, Lena","Thiis, Jens J","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Tveit, Arnljot","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Schmitt, Nicole","Olesen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460757"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vestre Viken Hospital Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brugada syndrome risk loci seem protective against atrial fibrillation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejhg.2014.46","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460757","identifier":[{"id":"24667784","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4231412","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85027956970","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-70b4517e-bd4b-4510-a970-ecfe2f0902cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F8D4400F9A658C67BB68B6D0742CE8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejhg.2014.46","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"vestre viken hospital trust","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Vestre Viken Hospital Trust","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Laura","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"058fca60-48be-4703-beca-c144879aa2d0","name":"Andreasen, Laura","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stine","key":"darknerpau","last":"Darkner","name":"Darkner, Stine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ingrid E","key":"christophersenpau","last":"Christophersen","name":"Christophersen, Ingrid E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Javad","key":"jabbaripau","last":"Jabbari","locid":"3c7f307b-30cb-4fb2-b8b5-8368ccc83e7a","name":"Jabbari, Javad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lena","key":"refsgaardpau","last":"Refsgaard","name":"Refsgaard, Lena","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens J","key":"thiispau","last":"Thiis","locid":"f51a5442-8c30-401b-a34d-33a47aa9a5b6","name":"Thiis, Jens J","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Arnljot","key":"tveitpau","last":"Tveit","name":"Tveit, Arnljot","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper H","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","name_org":"Svendsen, Jesper H","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole","key":"schmittpau","last":"Schmitt","locid":"942c887c-32b0-4e89-812f-a11edf2505a5","name":"Schmitt, Nicole","orcid":"0000-0001-9482-9749","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"60e76597-44c1-4838-bb63-9b8568adb06f","name":"Olesen, Morten S","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24667784"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ejhg.2014.46","issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"1357-1361","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027956970"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-70b4517e-bd4b-4510-a970-ecfe2f0902cf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Brugada syndrome risk loci seem protective against atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460757","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
