{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Åse Marie","Jensen, MA","Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","Kristiansen, Jesper","Garde, Anne Helene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-781210"],"event":{"end":"2014-10-22","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2014-10-22","title":"WINC Working Hours in the Nordic Countries","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"number of consecutive nights and sleep","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-781210","ids":["nfa-9211bfa2-a8bb-4e4c-a9a7-6141d7df7ed1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C990DE7731606876CA0367A8FE35639B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Åse Marie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Åse Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"MA","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, MA","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"2b90a97c-15d6-468c-a8d6-1362e731d2bc","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","name_org":"Kristiansen, J","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"AH","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"8e894baf-467c-45d3-8abe-41a805b30b22","name":"Garde, Anne Helene","name_org":"Garde, AH","orcid":"0000-0002-1553-2291","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-9211bfa2-a8bb-4e4c-a9a7-6141d7df7ed1"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Number of consecutive nights and sleep","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-781210","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background: Fibulin-1, a circulating extracellular matrix glycoprotein, has been associated with arterial disease and elevated N-terminal prohormone B-type natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) in diabetes. Soluble urokinase plasminogen activator receptor (suPAR), a marker of inflammation, has been associated with subclinical atherosclerosis. Therefore, we aimed to explore the interplay between these biomarkers and mild to moderate aortic valve stenosis (AS). Methods: In 374 patients with mild to moderate AS, we investigated the relationship of fibulin-1 with NT-proBNP, levels of suPAR and the degree of AS at baseline and after one and four years of treatment with Simvastatin 40 mg and Ezetimibe 10 mg or placebo. Results: During treatment, fibulin-1 became more closely associated with NT-proBNP (β year0 = 0.10, p = 0.08, β year1 = 0.16, p = 0.005, β year4 = 0.22, p<0.001) and suPAR (β year0 = 0.05, p = 0.34, β year1 = 0.16, p = 0.006, β year4 = 0.13, p = 0.03) at the expense of the association to aortic valve area index (AVAI) (β year0 = 20.14, p = 0.005, β year1 = 20.08, p = 0.11, β year4 = 20.06, p = 0.22) independently of age, gender, creatinine, and serum aspartate aminotransferase (Adj. R year0 2 = 0.19, Adj.R year1 2 = 0.22, Adj.R year4 2 = 0.27). Fibulin-1 was unrelated to aortic regurgitation, left ventricular mass, and ejection fraction. In patients with baseline AVAI<0.58 cm 2/m 2 (median value), fibulin-1 was more closely associated to NT-proBNP (β year0 = 0.25, β year1 = 0.21, β year4 = 0.22, all p<0.01), and suPAR (β year0 = 0.09, p = 0.26, β year1 = 0.23, β year4 = 0.21, both p< 0.01) independently of age, gender, AST and treatment allocation. Conclusions: Increased levels of fibulin-1 were independently associated with higher levels of suPAR and NT-proBNP especially in patients with lower AVAI, suggesting that fibulin-1 may be an early marker of AS as well as cardiac fibrosis secondarily to elevated left ventricular hemodynamic load.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kruger, Ruan","Rasmussen, Lars M","Argraves, William S","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Nielsen, Olav W","Blyme, Adam","Willenheimer, Ronnie","Wachtell, Kristian","Olsen, Michael H"],"cuid":["S02-086.76-041803"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Aortic Valve Stenosis","Biological Markers","Calcium Binding Proteins","Echocardiography","Extracellular matrix","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Natriuretic Peptide Brain","Peptide Fragments","Prospective Studies","Receptors Urokinase Plasminogen Activator"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extracellular matrix biomarker fibulin 000000000001 is closely related to nt probnp and soluble urokinase plasminogen activator receptor in patients with aortic valve stenosis the seas study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0101522","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.76-041803","identifier":[{"id":"84904212843","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25014213","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4094491","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4025e91a-f2c3-4218-a904-2073b10ff5c1","sdu-83b26014-7c47-4a6c-9fd4-e31a7d7fb286"],"keyword":["Aged","Aortic Valve Stenosis","Biological Markers","Calcium-Binding Proteins","Echocardiography","Extracellular Matrix","Female","Hemodynamics","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Natriuretic Peptide, Brain","Peptide Fragments","Prospective Studies","Receptors, Urokinase Plasminogen Activator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E134919460C439E5FBA740743F831215"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0101522","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cardiovascular and Renal Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ruan","key":"krugerpau","last":"Kruger","name":"Kruger, Ruan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars M","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"bf5d4e3b-cb51-4e61-a6d1-e22445213324","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars M","orcid":"0000-0001-5795-4794","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"William S","key":"argravespau","last":"Argraves","name":"Argraves, William S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olav W","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Olav W","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Adam","key":"blymepau","last":"Blyme","name":"Blyme, Adam","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ronnie","key":"willenheimerpau","last":"Willenheimer","name":"Willenheimer, Ronnie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristian","key":"wachtellpau","last":"Wachtell","locid":"70ec2ee4-bbde-412e-b5f0-ca50c8097c2c","name":"Wachtell, Kristian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael H","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8ff309b5-8760-45c3-9bc6-41599369c816","name":"Olsen, Michael Hecht","name_org":"Olsen, Michael H","orcid":"0000-0003-2230-5780","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25014213"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0101522","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"7","journal":"PLOS ONE","pages":"1-8","paperid":"e101522","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"PloS one","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904212843"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4025e91a-f2c3-4218-a904-2073b10ff5c1","sdu-83b26014-7c47-4a6c-9fd4-e31a7d7fb286"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Extracellular Matrix Biomarker, Fibulin-1, Is Closely Related to NT-proBNP and Soluble Urokinase Plasminogen Activator Receptor in Patients with Aortic Valve Stenosis (The SEAS Study)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.76-041803","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Design is increasingly becoming a part of the university curriculum and research agenda. A theory about the pro-cess and practice of design might be important to estab-lish design as a main subject at universities. We believe it is in the interest of many design communities – not least the Participatory Design (PD) community – to engage in theorizing design, on the basis of our understanding of design and design practices. This theory could be posi-tioned as an alternative to other attempts to theorize design, for example the influential efforts of the Information Systems (IS) community. We urge the PD community to engage in collective theory building, and we present a framework intended to support our shared reflections on the design of human technologies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Simonsen, Jesper","Hertzum, Morten","Nielsen, Jørgen Lerche","Riis, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-093.01-041601"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","end":"2014-12-05","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2014-12-02","title":"Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design","Epistemology","Faculty of Humanities","Framework","Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Brugerdreven IT Innovation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward a theory for the design of human technologies","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/138764952/DesignTheory_OZCHI2014.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.01-041601","identifier":[{"id":"84945429162","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3a90afdc-bda3-4018-880a-0a0e59b973