{"abstract":"Standardization work for over-the-air (OTA) testing of multiple-input–multiple-output (MIMO) capable terminals is currently ongoing in COST IC1004, 3GPP, and CTIA, where a multiprobe anechoic chamber based method is a promising candidate. Setting up a multiprobe configuration with channel emulators is costly, so finding ways to limit the number of probes while still reproducing the target channels accurately could make the test system both cheaper and simpler to implement. Several probe selection algorithms are presented in this paper to address this issue. The proposed techniques provide a probe selection framework for the channel emulation techniques published in the literature. Simulation results show that good channel emulation accuracy can be achieved with the selected subset of probes for the considered target channel models. The probe selection algorithm is further supported by measurement results in a practical multiprobe setup","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fan, Wei","Sun, Fan","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Carreño, Xavier","Ashta, Jagjit Singh","Knudsen, Mikael Bergholz","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092201"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Intel"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probe selection in multiprobe ota setups","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/181562601/06716023.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-092201","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000334744700035","type":"wos"},{"id":"84940227385","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-910cf37d-98d6-4d25-a512-d38b86a929ae"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E294F7923EDC19DBCE91CF0A9DF1497"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/181562601/06716023.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"intel","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Intel","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fan","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","locid":"0593f460-9081-4a41-8abb-c5bf8bdb4026","name":"Sun, Fan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xavier","key":"carreñopau","last":"Carreño","name":"Carreño, Xavier","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jagjit Singh","key":"ashtapau","last":"Ashta","name":"Ashta, Jagjit Singh","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael Bergholz","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Mikael Bergholz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert Frølund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tap.2014.2301179","issn":["0018926X"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","pages":"2109-2120","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Antennas and Propagation","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940227385"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-910cf37d-98d6-4d25-a512-d38b86a929ae"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Probe Selection in Multiprobe OTA Setups","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092201","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Parameter estimation from compressively sensed signals has recently received some attention. We here also consider this problem in the context of frequency sparse signals which are encountered in many application. Existing methods perform the estimation using finite dictionaries or incorporate various interpolation techniques to estimate the continuous frequency parameters. In this paper, we show that solving the problem in a probabilistic framework instead produces an asymptotically efficient estimator which outperforms existing methods in terms of estimation accuracy while still having a low computational complexity. Moreover, the proposed algorithm is also able to make inference about the sparsity level of the measured signal. The simulation code is available online.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Jensen, Søren Holdt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102012"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2014-05-09","place":"Firenze, it","start":"2014-05-04","title":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"joint sparsity and frequency estimation for spectral compressive sensing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/206071688/20140314_ICASSP14A.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-102012","identifier":[{"id":"84905270216","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000343655301012","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-b2f1b328-6bb4-4cf0-96bf-930c9995aa5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CC3D13F54F2143DC6D2988FFB25E1EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/206071688/20140314_ICASSP14A.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://kom.aau.dk/~jkn/publications/simulations/20140314_ICASSP14A.zip","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Signal and Information Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Holdt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bfd2a53b-f2bd-4563-8968-9a911996215f","name":"Jensen, Søren Holdt","orcid":"0000-0002-1050-470X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp.2014.6853754","isbn":["9781479928927"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"1035-1039","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905270216"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b2f1b328-6bb4-4cf0-96bf-930c9995aa5f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Joint Sparsity and Frequency Estimation for Spectral Compressive Sensing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102012","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The EU Directive on the Energy Performance of Buildings requires that energy certification of buildings should be implemented in Denmark so that houses that are sold or let should have an energy performance certificate. The result is that only a small part of existing houses has an energy performance certificate. The Danish Building Research Institute has described a method that can be applied for estimating the energy demand of dwellings. This is based on the information in the Danish Building and Dwelling Register and requirements in the Danish Building Regulations from the year of construction of the house. The result is an estimate of the energy demand of each building with a variation. This makes it possible to make an automatic classification of all buildings. The paper discusses the uncertainties and makes a sensitivity analysis to find the important parameters. The variations are compared with measured energy demand. The method can be applied in other countries with modifications for local building requirements, climate and building registers.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anker","Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","Bertelsen, Niels Haldor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114270"],"event":{"acronym":"NSB","end":"2014-06-19","place":"Lund , se","start":"2014-06-15","title":"10th Nordic Symposium on Building Physics","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energibesparelse","Renovering","beregningsmetode"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sensitivity analysis of the energy demand of existing buildings based on the danish building and dwelling register bbr","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-114270","ids":["aau-dcda3a48-0408-472d-b454-227c259ae928"],"keyword":["Energibesparelse","beregningsmetode","renovering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C7954C84903F14DA0E8373FF1D764346"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Construction and health (CH)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"218dfaef-8c2b-4ec5-a965-af8a4382b15d","name":"Nielsen, Anker","orcid":"0000-0002-7130-6432","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Bjarne","key":"wittchenpau","last":"Wittchen","locid":"4cf412e5-ace3-40f6-8f0c-dfef37eac83d","name":"Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","orcid":"0000-0002-3305-5409","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Haldor","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"e39ec4b4-5ae5-4793-99e4-3be87a28aafd","name":"Bertelsen, Niels Haldor","orcid":"0000-0001-6247-4218","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"arfvidssonpedh","last":"Arfvidsson","name":"Arfvidsson, Jesper","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars-Erik","key":"harderuppedh","last":"Harderup","name":"Harderup, Lars-Erik","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"kumlinpedh","last":"Kumlin","name":"Kumlin, Anders","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bitte","key":"rosencrantzpedh","last":"Rosencrantz","name":"Rosencrantz, Bitte","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789188722515"],"pages":"46","place":"Lund, Sweden","publisher":"Lunds Tekniska Högskola, LTH. Institutionen för Byggnadsteknik","status":"p","subtitle":"Abstract book","title":"NSB 2014: 10th Nordic Symposium on Building Physics 15-19 June 2014 Lund, Sweden"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dcda3a48-0408-472d-b454-227c259ae928"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sensitivity analysis of the energy demand of existing buildings based on the Danish Building and Dwelling Register (BBR)","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-114270","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"\"Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser\" præsenterer resultaterne af en stor videnskabelig undersøgelse om idrætsklasser og talentudvikling blandt 7., 8. og 9. klasses idrætselever. Undersøgelsen bygger på registerdata og elektroniske spørgeskemaer med skoleelever i udskolingen, der går i særlige idrætsklasser på folkeskoler i 15 elitekommuner. Rapporten indgår i det treårige forskningsprojekt \"Idrætsklasser – plads til idrætstalenter i den danske folkeskole\" om idrætsklasser i udskolingen, hvis overordnede formål er at undersøge, hvordan idrætsklasserne fungerer som ramme både for elevernes skolegang og for deres udvikling som idrætstalenter med fokus på hvad idrætsklasserne giver eleverne personligt, fagligt og socialt, herunder hvordan idrætsklassen som ramme/støtte for deres skolegang og idræt kobler sig til deres motivation for videre uddannelse og talentudvikling. Nærværende forskningsrapport er baseret på survey- og registerdata. Således belyser rapporten primært idrætsklasseeleverne og idrætsklasserne i tal og tabeller, der er lavet med udgangspunkt i statistiske analyser af vores spørgeskemaundersøgelse og registerdata. Rapporten indeholder bl.a. analyser af, hvor udbredt tilfredsheden er med idrætsklasserne blandt eleverne, hvordan de vurderer idrætsklassernes betydning for deres sportslige udvikling, hvordan de ser på det faglige miljø og undervisningen, hvordan de ser på klassefællesskabet og det sociale læringsmiljø og hvilke fremtidsperspektiver de har på deres skolegang og idræt. Der er også foretaget analyser af, om idrætselevernes erfaringer hænger sammen med hvilket klassetrin de går på, hvilken sportsgren de dyrker, deres køn og deres socioøkonomiske baggrund. Endeligt er der på baggrund af karakterdata fra folkeskolens afgangsprøver i dansk (læsning) og matematik (problemløsning) foretaget analyser af idrætselevernes skolepræstationer i disse fag. Denne del af analysen baserer sig alene på 9. klasses eleverne.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Stilling Olesen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-132559"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Folkeskole","Fællesskab","Grundskole","Læring og læringsmiljøer","Motivation","Talentudvikling","Udskoling","eliteidræt"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/75146625/Idr_tselevers_erfaringer_med_idr_tsklasser_JCN_og_JEO_DPU_AU_22_01_2014.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-132559","ids":["au-05b6ea35-8aa4-4595-8c5c-02b5fd3d59a6"],"keyword":["Folkeskole","Fællesskab","Grundskole","Læring og læringsmiljøer","Motivation","eliteidræt","konkurrence og fællesskab","socialt læringsmiljø","talentudvikling","udskoling"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-91913B930FF580BD1C6E035EFE4B9D86"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/75146625/Idr_tselevers_erfaringer_med_idr_tsklasser_JCN_og_JEO_DPU_AU_22_01_2014.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.emu.dk/sites/default/files/Rapport%20Idraetselevers%20erfaringer%20med%20idraetsklasser.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Research Programme for Diversity, Culture and Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"142","place":"København","publisher":"Institut for Uddannelse og Pædagogik (DPU), Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-05b6ea35-8aa4-4595-8c5c-02b5fd3d59a6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-132559","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser - et blik på Roskilde Kommune er et tillæg til og skal læses i sammenhæng med rapporten Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser, der blev offentliggjort i begyndelsen af 2014. Rapporten og dens tillæg er del af et 3-årigt forskningsprojekt om idrætsklasser og talentudvikling i folkeskolernes 7. til 9. klassetrin i landets elitekommuner. Rapporten er baseret på data fra en survey blandt 1.170 idrætselever og tilkoblede registerdata fra Danmarks Statistik om elevernes socioøkonomiske baggrund. Nærværende rapporttillæg indeholder særkørsler af disse data med fokus på idrætseleverne i Roskilde Kommune. I tillægget er der fokus på fem områder: 1) Idrætsklassernes sammensætning – beskriver idræts-elevernes kønsfordeling, etnicitet og socioøkonomiske baggrund, 2) Fællesskabet og kulturen i idrætsklasserne – belyser fællesskabet og undervisningsmiljøet i idrætsklasserne, 3) Samspil mellem skole og idræt – belyser skolens tilpasning til elevernes idrætsudøvelse, 4) Idrætsklassen på skolen – belyser forholdet til de øvrige elever på skolen og 5) To spor – uddannelse og sport – belyser vægtning af sport og uddannelse og deres fremtidsplaner efter 9. klasse.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Stilling Olesen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-132998"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Folkeskolen","Udskoling","elevsammensætning","idræt og uddannelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser et blik på roskilde kommune","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-132998","ids":["au-06710527-f991-4a98-af90-fbe8d0e3e18b"],"keyword":["Folkeskolen","Udskoling","elevsammensætning","idræt og uddannelse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8426AA063F2FC4A73AEE9CC15FC21219"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Research Programme for Diversity, Culture and Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8fee80e-c33e-467c-9afd-8462e0bf571e","name":"Nielsen, Jens Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"stillingolesenpau","last":"Stilling Olesen","locid":"bb840c08-e692-4000-8a96-d541f03bb9f4","name":"Stilling Olesen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-7536-4544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"17","place":"København","publisher":"Institut for Uddannelse og Pædagogik (DPU), Aarhus Universitet","publisher_org":"Institut for Uddannelse og Pædagogik (DPU) Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-06710527-f991-4a98-af90-fbe8d0e3e18b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser – et blik på Roskilde Kommune","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-132998","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Non-malleable codes are a natural relaxation of error correcting/ detecting codes that have useful applications in the context of tamper resilient cryptography. Informally, a code is non-malleable if an adversary trying to tamper with an encoding of a given message can only leave it unchanged or modify it to the encoding of a completely unrelated value. This paper introduces an extension of the standard non-malleability security notion - so-called continuous non-malleability - where we allow the adversary to tamper continuously with an encoding. This is in contrast to the standard notion of non-malleable codes where the adversary only is allowed to tamper a single time with an encoding. We show how to construct continuous non-malleable codes in the common split-state model where an encoding consist of two parts and the tampering can be arbitrary but has to be independent with both parts. Our main contributions are outlined below: We propose a new uniqueness requirement of split-state codes which states that it is computationally hard to find two codewords X = (X 0,X 1) and X′ = (X 0,X 1′) such that both codewords are valid, but X 0 is the same in both X and X′. A simple attack shows that uniqueness is necessary to achieve continuous non-malleability in the split-state model. Moreover, we illustrate that none of the existing constructions satisfies our uniqueness property and hence is not secure in the continuous setting. We construct a split-state code satisfying continuous non-malleability. Our scheme is based on the inner product function, collision-resistant hashing and non-interactive zero-knowledge proofs of knowledge and requires an untamperable common reference string. We apply continuous non-malleable codes to protect arbitrary cryptographic primitives against tampering attacks. Previous applications of non-malleable codes in this setting required to perfectly erase the entire memory after each execution and required the adversary to be restricted in memory. We show that continuous non-malleable codes avoid these restrictions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Faust, Sebastian","Mukherjee, Pratyay","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Venturi, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137505"],"event":{"end":"2014-02-26","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2014-02-24","title":"Theory of Cryptography Conference","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Rome La Sapienza"],"keyword":["Non malleable codes","Split state"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continuous non malleable codes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-54242-8_20","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137505","identifier":[{"id":"84894254935","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0e46875c-6caa-4c8c-b0a2-172c720f5e03"],"keyword":["non-malleable codes","split-state","tamper resilience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC471D874E56355A6F092540FFD246FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-54242-8_20","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of rome la sapienza","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rome La Sapienza","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"faustpau","last":"Faust","locid":"a159659b-6f11-4ff6-92dc-1d680e0caa9c","name":"Faust, Sebastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pratyay","key":"mukherjeepau","last":"Mukherjee","locid":"105d3bfa-ce11-4ee6-a8c6-311de435888b","name":"Mukherjee, Pratyay","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"venturipau","last":"Venturi","name":"Venturi, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yehuda","key":"lindellpedh","last":"Lindell","name":"Lindell, Yehuda","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-54242-8_20","eisbn":["9783642542428"],"isbn":["9783642542411"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"465-488","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"11th Theory of Cryptography Conference, TCC 2014, San Diego, CA, USA, February 24-26, 2014. Proceedings","title":"Theory of Cryptography"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84894254935"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0e46875c-6caa-4c8c-b0a2-172c720f5e03"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Continuous Non-malleable Codes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137505","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser - et blik på Haderslev Kommune er et tillæg til og skal læses i sammenhæng med rapporten Idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser, der blev offentliggjort i begyndelsen af 2014. Rapporten og dens tillæg er del af et 3-årigt forskningsprojekt om idrætsklasser og talentudvikling i folkeskolernes 7. til 9. klassetrin i landets elitekommuner. Rapporten er baseret på data fra en survey blandt 1.170 idrætselever og tilkoblede registerdata fra Danmarks Statistik om elevernes socioøkonomiske baggrund. Nærværende rapporttillæg indeholder særkørsler af disse data med fokus på idrætseleverne i Haderslev Kommune. I tillægget er der fokus på fem områder: 1) Idrætsklassernes sammensætning – beskriver idræts-elevernes kønsfordeling, etnicitet og socioøkonomiske baggrund, 2) Fællesskabet og kulturen i idrætsklasserne – belyser fællesskabet og undervisningsmiljøet i idrætsklasserne, 3) Samspil mellem skole og idræt – belyser skolens tilpasning til elevernes idrætsudøvelse, 4) Idrætsklassen på skolen – belyser forholdet til de øvrige elever på skolen og 5) To spor – uddannelse og sport – belyser vægtning af sport og uddannelse og deres fremtidsplaner efter 9. klasse.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Christian","Stilling Olesen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-150118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Folkeskolens udskoling","Talentudvikling","elevsammensætning","eliteidræt og uddannelse","klassefællesskab"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"idrætselevers erfaringer med idrætsklasser et blik på haderslev kommune","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-150118","ids":["au-2439d484-7458-4e8f-8cae-c423