{"abstract":"This compendium is intended as a handbook for teachers who wish to incorporate inquiry-based teaching into their didactic repertoire. It is aimed at those who, on the one hand, seek a didactic foundation for their work, and on the other, want to see how other educators have designed inquiry-based sequences in various science subjects and in mathematics. The main section of the compendium provides a brief overview of the key concepts and ideas relevant to implementing Inquiry-Based Science Education (IBSE), or in Danish, Undersøgelsesbaseret Naturfagsundervisning (UBNU). The appendices include concrete descriptions of various teaching sequences and links to a large number of additional examples available online. The compendium serves two main purposes. First, it offers a shared language for teachers involved in IBSE teaching. Second, it emphasizes that the use of the 6F model in planning IBSE sequences highlights the teacher’s role in guiding instruction, whereas problem-oriented project work places greater emphasis on the student’s role.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Frisdahl, Klavs Kokseby","Dolin, Jens","Nielsen, Jan Alexis","Jacobsen, Lærke Bang","Bruun, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818683"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kompendium inquiry based science education ibse termer metoder tankegange og erfaringer undersøgelsesbaseret undervisning i naturfag og matematik","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dln","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456706402/36-Kompendie-IBSE_ny_web2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818683","ids":["ku-2044acf0-e669-4ffe-9bc2-c244497c672f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F55DD6B97F88C5EF01D68D5FBA15D14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456706402/36-Kompendie-IBSE_ny_web2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Assessment, Teaching and Learning in Science Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Klavs Kokseby","key":"frisdahlpau","last":"Frisdahl","locid":"373b9fe6-a3d9-438b-9a59-e894f5ff6542","name":"Frisdahl, Klavs Kokseby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"dolinpau","last":"Dolin","locid":"76d1971b-6d64-4bce-b4dc-6af9cd79f81f","name":"Dolin, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1604-1846","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Alexis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cef45857-ae6d-43b5-9fa4-4a34e36c31f4","name":"Nielsen, Jan Alexis","orcid":"0000-0002-2596-4880","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lærke Bang","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"310b0aac-971e-41ea-b3cc-5aa1f7c65812","name":"Jacobsen, Lærke Bang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"d2218073-20b7-41ac-aa88-f7c4bc9fff74","name":"Bruun, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-4739-7351","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16022149"],"issue":"36","pages":"132","series":"IND's Skriftserie","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2044acf0-e669-4ffe-9bc2-c244497c672f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kompendium: Inquiry Based Science Education - IBSE : Termer, metoder, tankegange og erfaringer - Undersøgelsesbaseret undervisning i naturfag og matematik","type":"Lecture Notes","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818683","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Patients were identified from a population-based prospective study of 4990 individuals with symptoms associated with colorectal cancer (CRC). A total of 244 CRC tissue samples were available for immunohistochemical staining of uPAR, semiquantitatively scored at the invasive front, and in the tumor core on cancer cells, macrophages, and myofibroblasts. In addition, the levels of the intact and cleaved uPAR-forms in blood from the same patients are evaluated in this study. In a univariate analysis, the number of uPAR-positive versus uPAR-negative macrophages (HR = 2.26, [95% CI: 1.39-3.66, P = 0.0009]) and cancer cells (HR=1.49, [95% CI: 1.01-2.20, P = 0.047]) located in the tumor core were significantly associated to overall survival. In a multivariate analysis, uPAR-positive versus uPAR-negative macrophages located in the tumor core showed the best separation of patients with positive score associated to poor prognosis (HR = 1.84 [95% CI: 1.12-3.04, P = 0.017]). In a multivariate analysis including clinical covariates and soluble uPAR(I), the latter was significantly associated to overall survival (HR = 2.68 [95% CI: 1.90-3.79, P < 0.0001]) and uPAR-positive macrophages in the tumor core remained significantly associated to overall survival (HR = 1.81 [95% CI: 1.08-3.01, P = 0.023]). Membrane-bound uPAR showed additive effects with the circulating uPAR(I) and stage, giving a hazard ratio of 12 between low and high scores. Thus, combining stage, uPAR(I) in blood and uPAR on macrophages in the tumor core increase the prognostic precision more than tenfold, as compared to stage alone.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Illemann, Martin","Laerum, Ole Didrik","Hasselby, Jane Preuss","Thurison, Tine","Høyer-Hansen, Gunilla","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Olsen, Jesper","Rahr, Hans B","Nielsen, Knud T","Laurberg, Søren","Christensen, Ib Jarle"],"cuid":["S02-093.47-046329"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Danish Study Group on Early Detection of Colorectal Cancer"],"corresponding_author":["Illemann, Martin"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma blood","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Antigens CD metabolism","Antigens Differentiation Myelomonocytic metabolism","Biomarkers Tumor blood","Colorectal Neoplasms blood","Colorectal cancer","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Invasion","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Macrophages metabolism","Male","Middle Aged","Multivariate Analysis","Prognosis","Receptors Urokinase Plasminogen Activator blood","Survival","uPAR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urokinase type plasminogen activator receptor upar on tumor associated macrophages is a marker of poor prognosis in colorectal cancer","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cam4.242","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.47-046329","identifier":[{"id":"24889870","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4303153","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84929142910","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cee9ce48-0d66-4054-8b77-0db9180379b9","sdu-75894c1a-b981-4f46-8409-edbb3669fcc7"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma/blood","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Antigens, CD/metabolism","Antigens, Differentiation, Myelomonocytic/metabolism","Biomarkers, Tumor/blood","Colorectal Neoplasms/blood","Colorectal cancer","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Invasion","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Macrophages/metabolism","Male","Middle Aged","Multivariate Analysis","Prognosis","Receptors, Urokinase Plasminogen Activator/blood","Survival","uPAR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B2ECBFEE9F64932D0B85AA29C6A413DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/189350982/Illemann_et_al_2014_Cancer_Medicine.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cam4.242","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, BRIC, BRIC Research Groups, Høyer-Hansen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Institut for Grænseregionsforskning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":5,"key":"danish study group on early detection of colorectal cancer","name":"Danish Study Group on Early Detection of Colorectal Cancer","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Martin","key":"illemannmartinpau","last":"Illemann","locid":"f3650240-6fea-4f9f-b6d4-1663c5dd483f","name":"Illemann, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole Didrik","key":"laerumoledidrikpau","last":"Laerum","name":"Laerum, Ole Didrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Preuss","key":"hasselbyjanepreusspau","last":"Hasselby","name":"Hasselby, Jane Preuss","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tine","key":"thurisontinepau","last":"Thurison","name":"Thurison, Tine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunilla","key":"høyerhansengunillapau","last":"Høyer-Hansen","locid":"0a238034-5893-44b7-87dd-27669e1e32dd","name":"Høyer-Hansen, Gunilla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"nielsenhansjørgenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f2980a61-e4e2-4879-8930-1535bc4f720e","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Nannestad","key":"jørgensenlarsnannestadpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"b2b91c8d-1f1e-4a45-a37f-290785ac9447","name":"Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"olsenjesperpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans B.","key":"rahrhansbpau","last":"Rahr","locid":"941e7830-92a2-42c8-a6d4-93a9fa3235e4","name":"Rahr, Hans B","name_org":"Rahr, Hans B.","orcid":"0000-0002-4571-7852","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud T","key":"nielsenknudtpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Knud T","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenibjarlepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"e7a3f6c5-8088-42dd-a87a-15e0dfc9a79e","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24889870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cam4.242","issn":["20457634"],"issue":"4","journal":"Cancer Medicine","pages":"855-864","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Cancer Medicine","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929142910"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cee9ce48-0d66-4054-8b77-0db9180379b9","sdu-75894c1a-b981-4f46-8409-edbb3669fcc7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Urokinase-type plasminogen activator receptor (uPAR) on tumor-associated macrophages is a marker of poor prognosis in colorectal cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.47-046329","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Tumor necrosis factor-α (TNF-α) is highly upregulated in inflammation and reduces the expression of the intestinal transcription factor, Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2 (CDX2). Wnt/β-catenin signaling is critical for intestinal cell proliferation, but a decreased CDX2 expression has influence on the Wnt signaling-related genes and progression of colorectal cancer. Although several inflammatory signaling pathways, including TNF-α, have been reported to promote Wnt/β-catenin activity and development of cancer, the underlying molecular mechanisms remain unclear. The aim was to investigate the signaling pathways involved in the TNF-α-mediated downregulation of CDX2, and its influence on Wnt/β-catenin signaling components in colon cancer cells. The expression of TNF-α and CDX2 at the invasive front were evaluated by immunohistochemical staining and showed reduced CDX2-positive cells in tumor buddings in areas with TNF-α expression in the surrounding inflammatory cells. In vitro studies revealed that TNF-α treatment showed a dose-dependent decrease of CDX2 messenger RNA (mRNA) and protein expression in Caco-2 cells. Inhibition of nuclear factor-kappaB or p38 pathways showed that these are involved in the TNF-α-dependent downregulation of CDX2. Furthermore, TNF-α-mediated downregulation of CDX2 was found to significantly decrease the mRNA levels of adenomatous polyposis coli (APC), axis inhibition protein 2 (AXIN2) and glycogen synthase kinase-3 beta (GSK3β), whereas the mRNA levels of Wnt targets were significantly elevated in TNF-α-treated Caco-2 cells. These findings were associated with reduced binding of CDX2 to promoter or enhancer regions of APC, AXIN2 and GSK3β. In conclusion, it was found that TNF-α induces the expression of Wnt signaling components through a downregulation of the CDX2 expression that might have a tumor-promoting effect on colon cancer cells.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Olsen, Anders Krüger","Bzorek, Michael","Holck, Susanne","Engel, Ulla Højholt","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S02-094.57-046617"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Caco 2 Cells","Colonic Neoplasms","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Gene expression","Homeodomain Proteins","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","MAP Kinase Signaling System","NF kappa B","Protein Binding","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha","Wnt Signaling Pathway","beta Catenin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"involvement of cdx000000000002 in the cross talk between tnf α and wnt signaling pathway in the colon cancer cell line caco 000000000002","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/carcin/bgu037","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.57-046617","identifier":[{"id":"84902012810","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24501326","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d9a96eab-0c82-46ca-acc8-b3c5af07ec55","ruc-64352a62-3a1d-4811-bbb6-d6e325d81770"],"keyword":["Caco-2 Cells","Colonic Neoplasms","Gene Expression","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Homeodomain Proteins","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","MAP Kinase Signaling System","NF-kappa B","Protein Binding","Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha","Wnt Signaling Pathway","beta Catenin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1C62EB74446117DDBC010F0A6B7C2151"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/carcin/bgu037","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"