st":"J.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, J.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"S.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, S.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"H.","key":"nordmeyerpau","last":"Nordmeyer","name":"Nordmeyer, H.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"G.","key":"peteinatospau","last":"Peteinatos","name":"Peteinatos, G.","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"A.","key":"papadopoulospau","last":"Papadopoulos","name":"Papadopoulos, A.","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J.","key":"svensgaardpau","last":"Svensgaard","name":"Svensgaard, J.","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M.","key":"weispau","last":"Weis","name":"Weis, M.","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c284dfaf-4015-461e-9604-bef890d95acb","name":"Christensen, Svend","orcid":"0000-0002-1112-1954","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/wre.12079","issn":["00431737","13653180"],"issn_org":["00431737"],"issue":"3","journal":"Weed Research","pages":"223-233","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Weed Research","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84898778040"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5f5805ff-2b55-40f6-bdc6-8121cc1d3a54","sdu-6b8de776-8ae5-46c0-a511-5f931b4f1f1e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sensor-based assessment of herbicide effects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.55-042834","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: An injury to the hamstring muscle complex is the most common injury in soccer. Ultrasound of acute hamstring injuries is often used as a clinical tool for diagnosing hamstring injuries and guiding players in when they can return to play. PURPOSE: To (1) investigate the characteristic sonographic findings of acute hamstring injuries in soccer players, (2) compare the mean injury severity (time to return to play) in injured players with and without sonographically verified abnormalities, and (3) correlate the length of the injured area and absence from soccer play (time to return to play) to investigate if ultrasonography can be used as a prognostic indicator of time to return to play. STUDY DESIGN: Case series; Level of evidence, 4. METHODS: Players from 50 teams participating in 1 of the top 5 Danish soccer divisions were followed in the period from January to December 2008. Of 67 players with acute hamstring injuries, 51 underwent ultrasonographic examination of the injured thigh and were included in this study. RESULTS: Ultrasonographic examinations were performed 1 to 10 days after injury (mean, 5.2 ± 3.0 days), and sonographic findings were present in 31 of 51 cases (61%). Two thirds of the injuries were to the biceps femoris muscle and one third to the semitendinosus muscle. No total ruptures were documented. The 51 acute hamstring injuries resulted in absence from soccer of a mean 25.4 ± 15.7 days per injury, with no significant difference between players with and without sonographically verified abnormalities (P = .41). No correlation existed between the length of the injured area and injury severity (r = 0.19, P = .29). CONCLUSION: The biceps femoris is the most commonly injured hamstring muscle detected by ultrasound, and more than half of the injuries are intramuscular. Because neither the presence of sonographic findings nor the size of the findings was correlated with time to return to play in injured soccer players, the prognosis of hamstring injuries should not be guided by these findings alone.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Petersen, Jesper","Thorborg, Kristian","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Skjødt, Thomas","Bolvig, Lars","Bang, Niels","Hölmich, Per"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-015393"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Acute Disease","Denmark","Humans","Injury Severity Score","Leg Injuries","Male","Muscle Skeletal","Physical Examination","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Recovery of Function","Recurrence","Soccer","Thigh","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the diagnostic and prognostic value of ultrasonography in soccer players with acute hamstring injuries","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0363546513512779","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-015393","identifier":[{"id":"24335495","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84893539596","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-267bc664-d599-4baa-8f52-be91f1013bc4","ku-229785ea-bbd8-4b53-9918-ed717decc42f"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Denmark","Humans","Injury Severity Score","Leg Injuries","Male","Muscle, Skeletal","Physical Examination","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Recovery of Function","Recurrence","Soccer","Thigh","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-14257672551BA469F52B836932468839"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0363546513512779","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Radiologisk afdeling, THG","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"thorborgpau","last":"Thorborg","locid":"7c1f3592-61a0-469e-b376-7adea54a0fa9","name":"Thorborg, Kristian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"skjødtpau","last":"Skjødt","name":"Skjødt, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"bolvigpau","last":"Bolvig","locid":"9ed75aac-ec1f-40b2-9f4d-4ab094eb165f","name":"Bolvig, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","locid":"0363dcf8-fa4b-41e2-bdc5-0f2efb7803d9","name":"Bang, Niels","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"hölmichpau","last":"Hölmich","locid":"dbb82dee-c9f9-47c8-b3d8-f810ae75ee69","name":"Hölmich, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24335495"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0363546513512779","issn":["03635465","15523365"],"issn_org":["03635465"],"issue":"2","journal":"American Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"399-404","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Sports Medicine","title_org":"The American Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893539596"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-267bc664-d599-4baa-8f52-be91f1013bc4","ku-229785ea-bbd8-4b53-9918-ed717decc42f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Diagnostic and Prognostic Value of Ultrasonography in Soccer Players With Acute Hamstring Injuries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-015393","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background: Numerous studies on seasonality of birth and schizophrenia risk have been published but it is uncertain whether, among those with schizophrenia, refractory illness exhibits any predilection for birth month. We hypothesized and examined whether a season of birth effect was present in patients with schizophrenia with a history of clozapine treatment. Method: Using record linkage with Danish registers, we examined patients with schizophrenia born between 1950 and 1970, and between 1995 and 2009 and Cox regression analysis was used to examine season of birth in relation to history of clozapine treatment. Results: In a study population corresponding to 60,062 person-years from 5328 individuals with schizophrenia of which 1223 (23%) received at least one clozapine prescription, birth in the autumn (September-November) was associated with clozapine treatment (HR = 1.24; 95% CI 1.07-1.46) when compared with birth in the spring (March-May). Conclusion: Although replication studies are needed, this is the first evidence from a nationwide study suggesting a possible season-associated risk of clozapine treatment in schizophrenia. The reasons for this relationship remain to be further investigated but might be partially explained by early exposures such as winter flu season and low vitamin D levels.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Holger J","Foldager, Leslie","Røge, Rasmus","Pristed, Sofie Gry","Andreasen, Jesper T","Nielsen, Jimmi"],"cuid":["S03-097.90-002399"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adult","Antipsychotic Agents","Clozapine","Drug Utilization","Female","Humans","Male","Medical Record Linkage","Middle Aged","Risk Assessment","Schizophrenia","Seasons"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an association between autumn birth and clozapine treatment in patients with schizophrenia a population based analysis","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/08039488.2013.854408","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.90-002399","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000340099300007","type":"wos"},{"id":"24228775","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84904417164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2ff79afe-1fe8-4dc8-bcb3-c8895dcbbef0","au-c75a97b0-32d6-4040-b38f-a7facb56db53","ku-a909b4b5-6a49-42f6-b8f8-e292ba98b277"],"keyword":["Adult","Antipsychotic Agents","Clozapine","Drug Utilization","Female","Humans","Male","Medical Record Linkage","Middle Aged","Risk Assessment","Schizophrenia","Seasons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-28CA4DA7F05C3CF494C3386A87782745"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/08039488.2013.854408","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger J","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"db089eef-09e3-4f8a-869f-e9f6ee4c504c","name":"Sørensen, Holger J","orcid":"0000-0003-2268-1735","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leslie","key":"foldagerpau","last":"Foldager","locid":"a815b9b5-4778-40b7-9686-3020f664195f","name":"Foldager, Leslie","orcid":"0000-0002-2639-826X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"røgepau","last":"Røge","locid":"e38b5e69-6b92-478d-b072-ae461fdbf6b6","name":"Røge, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-6452-1599","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Gry","key":"pristedpau","last":"Pristed","locid":"871611e1-8aa7-4e05-b1b2-c8cf77cad0c8","name":"Pristed, Sofie Gry","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper T","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"bc66d36f-6969-4fa0-9b43-ac503a438a8a","name":"Andreasen T., Jesper","name_org":"Andreasen, Jesper T","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jimmi","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e666518b-f6a4-4adb-849e-b6544de3e312","name":"Nielsen, Jimmi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24228775"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/08039488.2013.854408","issn":["08039488","08039496"],"issn_org":["08039488"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"428-432","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904417164"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2ff79afe-1fe8-4dc8-bcb3-c8895dcbbef0","au-c75a97b0-32d6-4040-b38f-a7facb56db53","ku-a909b4b5-6a49-42f6-b8f8-e292ba98b277"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An association between autumn birth and clozapine treatment in patients with schizophrenia : A population-based analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.90-002399","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Clovis, with its distinctive biface, blade and osseous technologies, is the oldest widespread archaeological complex defined in North America, dating from 11,100 to 10,700 (14)C years before present (bp) (13,000 to 12,600 calendar years bp). Nearly 50 years of archaeological research point to the Clovis complex as having developed south of the North American ice sheets from an ancestral technology. However, both the origins and the genetic legacy of the people who manufactured Clovis tools remain under debate. It is generally believed that these people ultimately derived from Asia and were directly related to contemporary Native Americans. An alternative, Solutrean, hypothesis posits that the Clovis predecessors emigrated from southwestern Europe during the Last Glacial Maximum. Here we report the genome sequence of a male infant (Anzick-1) recovered from the Anzick burial site in western Montana. The human bones date to 10,705 ± 35 (14)C years bp (approximately 12,707-12,556 calendar years bp) and were directly associated with Clovis tools. We sequenced the genome to an average depth of 14.4× and show that the gene flow from the Siberian Upper Palaeolithic Mal'ta population into Native American ancestors is also shared by the Anzick-1 individual and thus happened before 12,600 years bp. We also show that the Anzick-1 individual is more closely related to all indigenous American populations than to any other group. Our data are compatible with the hypothesis that Anzick-1 belonged to a population directly ancestral to many contemporary Native Americans. Finally, we find evidence of a deep divergence in Native American populations that predates the Anzick-1 individual.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Morten","Anzick, Sarah L.","Waters, Michael R.","Skoglund, Pontus","Degiorgio, Michael","Stafford, Thomas W.","Rasmussen, Simon","Moltke, Ida","Albrechtsen, Anders","Doyle, Shane M.","Poznik, G. David","Gudmundsdottir, Valborg","Yadav, Rachita","Malaspinas, Anna Sapfo","Samuel Stockton White, V.","Allentoft, Morten E.","Cornejo, Omar E.","Tambets, Kristiina","Eriksson, Anders","Heintzman, Peter D.","Karmin, Monika","Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","Meltzer, David J.","Pierre, Tracey L.","Stenderup, Jesper","Saag, Lauri","Warmuth, Vera M.","Lopes, Margarida C.","Malhi, Ripan S.","Brunak, Søren","Sicheritz-Ponten, Thomas","Barnes, Ian","Collins, Matthew","Orlando, Ludovic","Balloux, Francois","Manica, Andrea","Gupta, Ramneek","Metspalu, Mait","Bustamante, Carlos D.","Jakobsson, Mattias","Nielsen, Rasmus","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S03-098.62-019310"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Willerslev, Eske"],"country":["Estonia","Kenya","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anzick Family","Imperial College London","Montana State University","Southern Methodist University","Stanford University","Texas A&M University","University College London","University of California","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at San Diego","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Cambridge","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of London","University of Montana","University of Nairobi","University of Tartu","University of York","Uppsala University","Washington State University Misc. Campuses","Washington State University Pullman"],"keyword":["Archaeology","Asia","Bone and Bones","Burial","Chromosomes Human Y","DNA Mitochondrial","Emigration and Immigration","Europe","Gene flow","Genome Human","Haplotypes","History Ancient","Humans","Indians North American","Infant","Male","Models Genetic","Molecular Sequence Data","Phylogeny","Population dynamics","Radiometric Dating"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","o