{"abstract":"Language acquisition in the bodily-tactile modality is difficult to understand, describe, and support. This chapter advocates a reinterpretation of the gestural and idiosyncratic bodily-tactile communication of people with congenital deafblindness (CDB) in terms of early language acquisition towards Tactile Sign Language (TSL). The access to participation in complex TSL culture is crucial for language acquisition. We already know how to transfer the patterns of social interaction into the bodily-tactile modality. This is the fundation on which to build actual linguistic participation. TSL as a first language is presently a theoretic possibility. We need more research on how to accommodate TSL to language Development and on how to fit TSL into participation in complex cultural activities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ask Larsen, Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485729"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acquisition of a bodily tactile language as first language","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-485729","ids":["ku-9a622a92-216a-48b0-aab8-7862c6a5c1b7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4D76D2A068A62F3DF7AE097E1B76FF8F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Department of Psychology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Psykologisk studienævn - fordelingssted"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"asklarsenpau","last":"Ask Larsen","locid":"4e4c1ada-3aa1-4fea-8250-9856667bacb7","name":"Ask Larsen, Flemming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"dammeyerpedh","last":"Dammeyer","name":"Dammeyer, Jesper","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anja","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anja","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788792574220"],"pages":"91-119","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Materialecentret","status":"p","title":"Kropslig og Taktil Sprogudvikling"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9a622a92-216a-48b0-aab8-7862c6a5c1b7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Acquisition of a bodily-tactile language as first language","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485729","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The sense of force is critical in the control of movement and posture. Multiple factors influence our perception of exerted force, including inputs from cutaneous afferents, muscle afferents and central commands. Here, we studied the influence of cutaneous feedback on the control of ankle force output. We used repetitive electrical stimulation of the superficial peroneal (foot dorsum) and medial plantar nerves (foot sole) to disrupt cutaneous afferent input in 8 healthy subjects. We measured the effects of repetitive nerve stimulation on (1) tactile thresholds, (2) performance in an ankle force-matching and (3) an ankle position-matching task. Additional force-matching experiments were done to compare the effects of transient versus continuous stimulation in 6 subjects and to determine the effects of foot anesthesia using lidocaine in another 6 subjects. The results showed that stimulation decreased cutaneous sensory function as evidenced by increased touch threshold. Absolute dorsiflexion force error increased without visual feedback during peroneal nerve stimulation. This was not a general effect of stimulation because force error did not increase during plantar nerve stimulation. The effects of transient stimulation on force error were greater when compared to continuous stimulation and lidocaine injection. Position-matching performance was unaffected by peroneal nerve or plantar nerve stimulation. Our results show that cutaneous feedback plays a role in the control of force output at the ankle joint. Understanding how the nervous system normally uses cutaneous feedback in motor control will help us identify which functional aspects are impaired in aging and neurological diseases.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Choi, Julia T","Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","Leukel, Christian","Nielsen, Jens Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493101"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Freiburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cutaneous mechanisms of isometric ankle force control","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00221-013-3570-9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-493101","identifier":[{"id":"84879844331","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23702971","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a6e33176-8715-474b-b664-51209ea3c9db"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63FECADC3A73B138B1AD0A6842C997D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00221-013-3570-9","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Neural Control of Movement"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Julia T","key":"choipau","last":"Choi","locid":"1c26c04f-6d4a-4b69-80d8-4ac865b20961","name":"Choi, Julia T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Lundbye","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"337846ab-970f-43ed-907d-a3f06b03ce2d","name":"Lundbye-Jensen, Jesper","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper Lundbye","orcid":"0000-0003-3144-861X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"leukelpau","last":"Leukel","name":"Leukel, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8b75713d-f9df-4123-8a0c-53b387d60776","name":"Nielsen, Jens Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-5568-2916","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23702971"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00221-013-3570-9","issn":["00144819","14321106"],"issn_org":["00144819"],"issue":"3","journal":"Experimental Brain Research","pages":"377-384","status":"p","title":"Experimental Brain Research","volume":"228"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879844331"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a6e33176-8715-474b-b664-51209ea3c9db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cutaneous mechanisms of isometric ankle force control","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493101","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
