ku-20faae45-da1a-4fe5-a253-782c5cc84d68"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association of National Initiatives to Improve Cardiac Arrest Management With Rates of Bystander Intervention and Patient Survival After Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011355","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"CONTEXT:Uncoupling protein 2 (UCP2) is involved in regulating ATP synthesis, generation of reactive oxygen species and glucose-stimulated insulin secretion in β-cells. Polymorphisms in UCP2 may be associated with obesity and type 2 diabetes mellitus.OBJECTIVE:To determine the influence of a functional UCP2 promoter polymorphism (-866G>A, rs659366) on obesity, type 2 diabetes and intermediary metabolic traits. Furthermore, to include these and previously published data in a meta-analysis of this variant with respect to its impact on obesity and type 2 diabetes.DESIGN:We genotyped UCP2 rs659366 in a total of 17 636 Danish individuals and established case-control studies of obese and non-obese subjects and of type 2 diabetic and glucose-tolerant subjects. Meta-analyses were made in own data set and in publicly available data sets. Quantitative traits relevant for obesity and type 2 diabetes were analysed within separate study populations.RESULTS:We found no consistent associations between the UCP2 -866G-allele and obesity or type 2 diabetes. Yet, a meta-analysis of data from 12 984 subjects showed an association with obesity (GA vs GG odds ratio (OR) (95% confidence interval (CI)): 0.894(0.826-0.968) P=0.00562, and AA vs GG OR(95% CI): 0.892(0.800-0.996), P=0.0415. Moreover, a meta-analysis for type 2 diabetes of 15 107 individuals showed no association. The -866G-allele was associated with elevated fasting serum insulin levels (P=0.002) and HOMA insulin resistance index (P=0.0007). Insulin sensitivity measured during intravenous glucose tolerance test in young Caucasian subjects (n=377) was decreased in carriers of the GG genotype (P=0.05).CONCLUSIONS:The UCP2 -866G-allele is associated with decreased insulin sensitivity in Danish subjects and is associated with obesity in a combined meta-analysis.International Journal of Obesity advance online publication, 21 February 2012; doi:10.1038/ijo.2012.22.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Andersen, G","Dalgaard, L T","Justesen, J M","Anthonsen, S","Nielsen, T","Thørner, L W","Witte, D","Jørgensen, T","Clausen, J O","Lauritzen, Torsten","Holmkvist, J","Hansen, T","Pedersen, Oluf"],"cuid":["S03-096.77-020869"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Genetics","Insulin Resistance","Obesity","UCP2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-NP-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the frequent ucp000000000002 000000000866g gt a polymorphism protects against insulin resistance and is associated with obesity a study of obesity and related metabolic traits among 000000000017 000000000636 danes","src":["au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/37528419/Andersen_G_2012.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S03-096.77-020869","identifier":[{"id":"22349573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84873712711","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-70039887-b6df-4b1d-aa83-1d09c3e68d27","ku-cc81429b-a98a-4252-bb5f-ac0e14b63a11","ruc-a7107424-bee7-46b0-8caa-9875b1ece946"],"keyword":["Obesity","UCP2","genetics","insulin resistance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-54C8023F3B52A5197812C8700F747AFD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/37528419/Andersen_G_2012.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ijo.2012.22","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"}