{"abstract":"Background. We compared the immunogenicity and reactogenicity of Cervarix or Gardasil human papillomavirus (HPV) vaccines in adults infected with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV).Methods. This was a double-blind, controlled trial randomizing HIV-positive adults to receive 3 doses of Cervarix or Gardasil at 0, 1.5, and 6 months. Immunogenicity was evaluated for up to 12 months. Neutralizing anti-HPV-16/18 antibodies were measured by pseudovirion-based neutralization assay. Laboratory tests and diary cards were used for safety assessment. The HPV-DNA status of the participants was determined before and after immunization.Results. Ninety-two participants were included in the study. Anti-HPV-18 antibody titers were higher in the Cervarix group compared with the Gardasil group at 7 and 12 months. No significant differences in anti-HPV-16 antibody titers were found among vaccine groups. Among Cervarix vaccinees, women had higher anti-HPV-16/18 antibody titers compared to men. No sex-specific differences in antibody titers were found in the Gardasil group. Mild injection site reactions were more common in the Cervarix group than in the Gardasil group (91.1% vs 69.6%; P = .02). No serious adverse events occurred.Conclusion. Both vaccines were immunogenic and well tolerated. Compared with Gardasil, Cervarix induced superior vaccine responses among HIV-infected women, whereas in HIV-infected men the difference in immunogenicity was less pronounced.Clinical Trials Registration. NCT01386164.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lars Toft","Storgaard, Merete","Müller, Martin","Sehr, Peter","Bonde, Jesper","Tolstrup, Martin","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-203007"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of the immunogenicity and reactogenicity of cervarix and gardasil human papillomavirus vaccines in hiv infected adults a randomized double blind clinical trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jit657","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-203007","identifier":[{"id":"84897394406","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24273179","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-80e0c36c-96d1-4e11-82bb-d825a1026826"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A639766E37FACE7628CD291751813DF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jit657","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Toft","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"57593d7e-a6df-4659-a4c9-08c8c7e155aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Toft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merete","key":"storgaardpau","last":"Storgaard","locid":"2c2b23fe-581a-47b7-9194-ab66b60773d3","name":"Storgaard, Merete","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5963","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"sehrpau","last":"Sehr","name":"Sehr, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","locid":"4b12f240-d09e-4563-8035-d3cbbe4601bf","name":"Bonde, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"tolstruppau","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"36e9f1d5-608c-46b7-8d41-2505c02086fc","name":"Tolstrup, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7020-5173","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Jørgen","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"fb8358a6-187a-4d5f-8187-06051ed74173","name":"Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-2459-0511","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole S","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"1939f653-c3a3-482e-a947-b1a7501b3986","name":"Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","name_org":"Søgaard, Ole S","orcid":"0000-0001-9107-2023","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24273179"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jit657","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","title_org":"Journal of Infectious Diseases"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897394406"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-80e0c36c-96d1-4e11-82bb-d825a1026826"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Comparison of the Immunogenicity and Reactogenicity of Cervarix and Gardasil Human Papillomavirus Vaccines in HIV-Infected Adults : A Randomized, Double-Blind Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-203007","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper examines how agile software development can be implemented in an offshore setting by introducing and testing the dual-shore approach. The topic is further enlightened by an analysis and discussion of an autoethnographic study proposing three specific suggestions for improvements of a particular agile offshoring process. Furthermore, the discussion leads to a modification of the original dual-shore approach to fit the characteristics of low-budget development projects. The article explains agile development and elaborates the four basic principles associated with it. The four principles are then used as a framework throughout the article. A short introduction to the terms outsourcing and offshoring is given, and it is illuminated how agile processes can be implemented into offshored development. The most common difficulties regarding agile offshoring are described and the dual-shore model is introduced as a tool to improve communication in an agile offshore setting. Key findings are that the dual-shore model is suggested to be supplemented with Exemplary Business Process Models extended beyond the onshore team and partially presented to the offshore development team, the metaphorical layers of the dual-shore approach is specifically included, and a design of an online start-up meeting is proposed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Riber","Hovmøller, Harald","Jørgensen, Michael Thorkild Nørgaard","Tambo, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-224582"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","end":"2013-08-15","place":"Gran, Oslo, no","start":"2013-08-12","title":"Informations Systems Research in Scandinavia","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile development","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving offshoring of low budget agile software development using the dual shore approach an autoethnographic study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mn.uio.no/ifi/english/research/news-and-events/events/conferences-and-seminars/iris2013/proceedings/iris36-proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-224582","ids":["au-a71e037a-b459-4a64-aa49-5240e92c9591"],"keyword":["Software Development","agile development","agile offshoring","dual-shore","exemplary business process model","low-budget projects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-183D4F51BA62D2B347681ECF1BC98B12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mn.uio.no/ifi/english/research/news-and-events/events/conferences-and-seminars/iris2013/proceedings/iris36-proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Business Development and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Riber","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b68b2808-48c5-4027-b759-634394d757f5","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Riber","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harald","key":"hovmøllerpau","last":"Hovmøller","locid":"94382949-7907-4e4f-945d-f79dae471fe5","name":"Hovmøller, Harald","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Thorkild Nørgaard","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"63fd4e86-8890-4d33-9446-b5d4f9fe5bed","name":"Jørgensen, Michael Thorkild Nørgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","correspond