{"abstract":"The renal distal nephron plays an important role in the maintenance of sodium balance, extra cellular volume and blood pressure. The degree of water transport, via aquaporin2 water channels (AQP2), and sodium transport, via epithelial sodium channels (ENaC) in renal collecting duct principal cells are reflected by the level of urinary excretion of AQP2 (u-AQP2) and the γ-fraction of ENaC (u-ENaCγ). The effects of an acute intravenous volume load with isotonic saline, hypertonic saline and glucose on u-AQP2, u-ENaCγ and underlying mechanisms have never been studied in a randomized, placebo-controlled trial in healthy humans.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Janni Majgaard","Mose, Frank Holden","Bech, Jesper N.","Nielsen, Søren","Pedersen, Erling Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180251"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of volume expansion with hypertonic and isotonic saline and isotonic glucose on sodium and water transport in the principal cells in the kidney","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2369-14-202","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180251","identifier":[{"id":"84884540838","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3849534","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24067081","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-59528717-b509-4398-8e4d-53be0897d9a8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26A333F98795EE2B250BB05F2E2C890C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2369-14-202","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"o