oi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0068166","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"7","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879834261"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3f0aa66-3a55-4bb5-acf4-7d2c3780e5ff"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Quantification of collagen ultrastructure after penetrating keratoplasty - implications for corneal biomechanics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222732","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"50 years ago, no lexicographer used a database in the work process. Today, almost all dictionary projects incorporate databases. In our opinion, the optimal lexicographical database should be planned in cooperation between a lexicographer and a database specialist in each specific lexicographic project. Such cooperation will reach the highest level of success if the lexicographer has at least a basic knowledge of the topic presented in this paper: What is a database? This type of knowledge is also needed when the lexicographer describes an ongoing or a finished project. In this article, we provide the description of this type of cooperation, using the most important theoretical terms relevant in the planning of a database. It will be made clear that a lexicographical database is like any other database. The only difference is that an optimal lexicographical database is constructed to fulfil the requirements for a specific lexicographical project.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bergenholtz, Henning","Skovgård Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230346"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Database","Database structure","Lexicographical database","Management","RECORD","Schema","User Interface"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what is a lexicographical database","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.statsbiblioteket.dk/au/showrecord.jsp?record_id=etss_ssj0035912","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230346","identifier":[{"id":"84892490254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b119905c-8b76-4ca0-9b3f-3c0abf651584"],"keyword":["DATABASE","DATABASE STRUCTURE","DATAB