{"abstract":"We study the fundamental limit on single-photon indistinguishability imposed by decoherence due to phonon interactions in semiconductor quantum dot-cavity quantum electrodynamics systems. Employing an exact diagonalization approach we find large differences compared to standard methods. An important finding is that short-time non-Markovian effects limit the maximal attainable indistinguishability. The results are explained using a polariton picture that yields valuable insight into the phonon-induced dephasing dynamics.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Per Kær","Lodahl, Peter","Jauho, Antti-Pekka","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378596"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microscopic theory of indistinguishable single photon emission from a quantum dot coupled to a cavity the role of non markovian phonon induced decoherence","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53340650/PhysRevB.87.081308.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378596","identifier":[{"id":"84874530613","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f77b5de7-725d-4927-a3c3-048597519705"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-ADDF84F752F5131BDB6CF6F3920475E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53340650/PhysRevB.87.081308.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.87.081308","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpau","last":"Lodahl","locid":"1228c48c-978c-45f6-a482-284ece371a8f","name":"Lodahl, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Antti-Pekka","key":"jauhopau","last":"Jauho","locid":"72495773-3ad7-4387-86a1-7757b6a46a1b","name":"Jauho, Antti-Pekka","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-7859","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.87.081308","issn":["01631829","1550235X"],"issn_org":["01631829"],"issue":"8","journal":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","paperid":"081308","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874530613"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f77b5de7-725d-4927-a3c3-048597519705"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Microscopic theory of indistinguishable single-photon emission from a quantum dot coupled to a cavity: The role of non-Markovian phonon-induced decoherence","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-378596","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Small unmanned aerial systems (UAS) with cameras have not been adopted in weed research, but offer low-cost sensing with high flexibility in terms of spatial resolution. A small rotary-wing UAS was tested as part of a search for an inexpensive, user-friendly and reliable aircraft for practical applications in UAS imagery weed research. In two experiments with post-emergence weed harrowing in barley, the crop resistance parameter, which reflects the crop response to harrowing, was unaffected by image capture altitude in the range from 1 to 50 m. This corresponded to image spatial resolution in the range from 0.3 to 17.1 mm per pixel. This finding is important because spatial resolution is inversely related to sensing capacity. We captured 20 plots comprising a total of about 0.2 ha in one image at 50 m altitude without losing information about the cultivation impacts on vegetation compared with ground truth data. UAS imagery also gave excellent results in logarithmic sprayer experiments in oilseed rape, where we captured 37 m long plots in each image from an altitude of 35 m. Furthermore, perennial weeds could be mapped from UAS images. These first experiences with a small rotary-wing UAS show that it is relatively easy to integrate as a tool in weed research and offers great potential for site-specific weed management.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Nielsen, Jon","Garcia Ruiz, Francisco Jose","Christensen, Svend","Streibig, Jens Carl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413103"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential uses of small unmanned aircraft systems uas in weed research","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/wre.12026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-413103","identifier":[{"id":"84879886461","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-20f6f3cc-6c27-413b-9030-594baefaf63f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01A85FE008D13CCC25BE2DE79FB9B944"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/wre.12026","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d45561f-3e81-41e1-8310-03bdb7abbad0","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Francisco Jose","key":"garciaruizpau","last":"Garcia Ruiz","locid":"5c1e1448-bdf1-4ee6-bc61-903233e51af1","name":"Garcia Ruiz, Francisco Jose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Svend","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c284dfaf-4015-461e-9604-bef890d95acb","name":"Christensen, Svend","orcid":"0000-0002-1112-1954","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Carl","key":"streibigpau","last":"Streibig","locid":"ed70ae10-cb37-444b-b7dd-3d8addfa248d","name":"Streibig, Jens Carl","orcid":"0000-0002-6204-4004","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/wre.12026","issn":["00431737","13653180"],"issn_org":["00431737"],"issue":"4","journal":"Weed Research","pages":"242-248","status":"p","title":"Weed Research","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879886461"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-20f6f3cc-6c27-413b-9030-594baefaf63f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Potential uses of small unmanned aircraft systems (UAS) in weed research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-413103","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
