{"abstract":"As affective and cognitive disturbances frequently co-occur in psychiatric disorders, research into opportunities to simultaneously target both entities is warranted. These disorders are typically treated with monoamine reuptake inhibitors (MRIs), whereas ongoing research suggests that symptoms also improve by nicotinic acetylcholine receptor (nAChR) activation. Preclinical studies have corroborated this and also demonstrated a synergistic antidepressant-like action when nAChR agonists and MRIs are combined. Here, we present the in vitro and in vivo profile of NS9775, a combined full α7 nAChR agonist and triple MRI. NS9775 potently inhibited [(3)H]α-bungarotoxin binding in vitro (Ki: 1.8 nM), and ex vivo (ED₅₀: 3.6 mg/kg), showing negligible activity at α4β2-(Ki: 1720 nM) or α1-containing nAChRs (Ki: 12,200 nM). In α7-expressing oocytes, NS9775 displayed an EC₅₀ value of 280 nM, with a maximal response of 77% relative to a saturating acetylcholine concentration. Furthermore, NS9775 inhibited cortical [(3)H]5-HT, [(3)H]NA and [(3)H]DA uptake equipotently (14-43 nM), and inhibited striatal [(3)H]WIN35,428 binding (ED₅₀: 9.1 mg/kg). Behaviourally in mice, NS9775 (0.3-3.0 mg/kg) reversed scopolamine-induced deficits in a modified Y-maze and MK-801-induced learning deficits in 5-trial inhibitory avoidance. Swim distance in the forced swim test was increased by 30 mg/kg NS9775, and 10 and 30 mg/kg NS9775 reduced digging behaviour in the marble burying paradigm and increased the number of punished crossings in the four plate test. This pro-cognitive, antidepressant-like and anxiolytic-like effect of NS9775 suggests that combining α7 nAChR agonism and triple monoamine reuptake inhibition could be a step in the evolution of pharmacological treatments of affective and/or cognitive disturbances.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andreasen T., Jesper","Redrobe, John P","Nielsen, Elsebet Ø","Christensen, Jeppe K","Olsen, Gunnar M","Peters, Dan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527964"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Symptoms","Animals","Avoidance Learning","Behavior Animal","Brain","Bungarotoxins","Cognition Disorders","Drug Evaluation Preclinical","Female","Male","Maze Learning","Mice","Naphthalenes","Nicotinic Agonists","Punishment","Radioligand Assay","Tritium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a combined α000000000007 nicotinic acetylcholine receptor agonist and monoamine reuptake inhibitor ns000000009775 represents a novel profile with potential benefits in emotional and cognitive disturbances","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527964","identifier":[{"id":"23748055","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84885091106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e1231cca-691a-461b-a6aa-f1dc021ee9c8"],"keyword":["Affective Symptoms","Animals","Avoidance Learning","Behavior, Animal","Brain","Bungarotoxins","Cognition Disorders","Drug Evaluation, Preclinical","Female","Male","Maze Learning","Mice","Naphthalenes","Neurotransmitter Uptake Inhibitors","Nicotinic Agonists","Punishment","Radioligand Assay","Tritium"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9AE9EEB73755910164872D036E8DB7A4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Experimental Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper T","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"bc66d36f-6969-4fa0-9b43-ac503a438a8a","name":"Andreasen T., Jesper","name_org":"Andreasen, Jesper T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John P","key":"redrobepau","last":"Redrobe","name":"Redrobe, John P","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elsebet Ø","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Elsebet Ø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeppe K","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jeppe K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunnar M","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Gunnar M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","name":"Peters, Dan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23748055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neuropharm.2013.04.060","issn":["00283908","18737064"],"issn_org":["00283908"],"journal":"Neuropharmacology","pages":"183-191","status":"p","title":"Neuropharmacology","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84885091106"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1231cca-691a-461b-a6aa-f1dc021ee9c8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A combined α7 nicotinic acetylcholine receptor agonist and monoamine reuptake inhibitor, NS9775, represents a novel profile with potential benefits in emotional and cognitive disturbances","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527964","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
