y bowel disease is associated with increased risk of myocardial infarction, stroke and cardiovascular death--a Danish nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.23-666140","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents current research on Danish municipalities’ use of Energy Service Companies (ESCO) as a way to improve the standard of public buildings and to increase energy efficiency. In recent years more and more municipalities have used ESCO-contracts to retrofit existing public buildings, and to make them more energy efficient. At the moment 30 municipalities (of the 98 municipalities in Denmark) are involved in, or preparing, ESCO contracts. Nevertheless, ESCO-contracting still faces many challenges on the Danish market, as there is a widespread skepticism towards the concept amongst many stakeholders. The purpose of this paper is to discuss the various experience gained so far by municipalities use of ESCO-contracting, the different approached to ESCO-contracting being used in practice, as well as the different viewpoints drivers and barriers behind the development. The strong growth in ESCO-contracts reflects that the ESCO-concept fits well with a number of present problems that municipalities are facing, as well as a flexible adaptation to the local context in different municipalities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Ole","Balslev Nielsen, Susanne","Hansen, Jesper Rohr"],"cuid":["S02-095.71-003622"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Energy Service Companies ESCO","Energy savings","Municipalities","Public buildings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greening public buildings esco contracting in danish municipalities","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en6052407","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.71-003622","identifier":[{"id":"84880433541","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000319443200005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-4a610623-9bf5-4517-9ab6-18859bd55ed7","dtu-65f71ffd-b5b2-48dc-9bbd-cfd4b1087018"],"keyword":["Energy Service Companies (ESCO)","energy savings","municipalities","public buildings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D7EA7504EB7CFAF33D22B5D2CF9B8702"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en6052407","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/76197647/energies_06_02407.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/54638128/Greening_Public_Buildings.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/6/5/2407","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Housing and Urban Renewal","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Research Group on Sustainable Cities and Housing","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Town, Housing and Property (THP)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management, Centre for Facilities Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba9f81ea-c5a0-4b37-a1ef-bcf1bc98535e","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3730-0619","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Balslev","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"37d6b355-4468-4f72-8256-afc593b8426e","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","orcid":"0000-0002-8269-6771","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rohr","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2e1430aa-5cad-4c23-9556-9575252cc7b7","name":"Hansen, Jesper Rohr","orcid":"0000-0001-9403-9296","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en6052407","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"5","journal":"Energies","pages":"2407-2427","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880433541"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4a610623-9bf5-4517-9ab6-18859bd55ed7","dtu-65f71ffd-b5b2-48dc-9bbd-cfd4b1087018"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Greening Public Buildings: ESCO-Contracting in Danish Municipalities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.71-003622","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"To implement rational pharmacotherapy in hospitals, it is important to develop, implement and evaluate hospital drug formularies (HDFs). A report from Denmark recommended standardizing activities of the drug and therapeutics committees (DTCs) in Denmark, but little is known about their current organization. The aim of the study was to describe the organization of DTCs in Denmark, how HDFs are developed and implemented, and to what extent policies that support the use of HDFs exist. A questionnaire was developed based on previous research and guidelines and contained 20 questions, which were divided into the following subjects: structure, activities, drug selection and implementation. The questionnaire was sent to the chairmen of the nine DTCs in Denmark. The response rate was 100% (9/9). The DTCs varied in structure and activities; meetings were held between 2 and 6 times annually, and the duration of the meetings lasted between 1 and 2.5 hr. Eight (89%) DTCs developed HDFs, policies and guidelines (P&Gs) that supported the use of HDFs. Eight (89%) had established criteria for inclusion of drugs on the HDFs, and seven had developed criteria for generic substitution and therapeutic interchange. The number of trade names on the HDFs varied between 116 and 1195. The nine DTCs in Denmark varied considerably regarding structure and activity. The main activity was to develop formularies, and most of the committees developed policies that supported medication use.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Plet, Hanne T.","Hallas, Jesper","Nielsen, Gitte S","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel"],"cuid":["S02-096.84-666015"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cross Sectional Studies","Denmark","Drug Substitution","Drug therapy","Guidelines as Topic","Humans","Organizational Policy","Pharmacy and Therapeutics Committee","Questionnaires","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug and therapeutics committees in danish hospitals a survey of organization activities and drug selection procedures","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.12028","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.84-666015","identifier":[{"id":"23107106","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84875058741","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000316217100008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-efdfbd04-e2f4-432d-8e29-981d690a6a56","sdu-c298253e-4a30-4aa9-b09d-047c36402a21"],"keyword":["Cross-Sectional Studies","Cross-Sectional Studies Denmark Drug Substitution Drug Therapy/*standards *Formularies, Hospital *Guidelines as Topic Humans Organizational Policy Pharmacy and Therapeutics Committee/*organization & administration Questionnaires Time Factors","Denmark","Drug Substitution","Drug Therapy","Formularies, Hospital","Guidelines as Topic","Humans","Organizational Policy","Pharmacy and Therapeutics Committee","Questionnaires","Time Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2F8896E57D5CC68C9C0D62A89984DD0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.12028","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinisk Farmakologi [Klinik Akut]"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Klinisk Farmakologi"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne T","key":"pletpau","last":"Plet","locid":"0df2aaa5-9380-43ba-b749-febb40cb7e1c","name":"Plet, Hanne T.","name_org":"Plet, Hanne T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","name_org":"Hallas, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte S","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gitte S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"L. J.","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"b3d44e3d-440c-41f1-b52d-838b0338bf55","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","name_org":"Kjeldsen, L. J.","orcid":"0009-0008-2559-9319","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23107106"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.12028","issn":["17427835"],"issn_org":["17427843"],"issue":"4","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"264-9","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","title_org":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology Online","volume":"112"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875058741"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","klinisk farmakologi"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-efdfbd04-e2f4-432d-8e29-981d690a6a56","sdu-c298253e-4a30-4aa9-b09d-047c36402a21"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Drug and therapeutics committees in Danish hospitals : a survey of organization, activities and drug selection procedures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.84-666015","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To study the influence of chronological age on fentanyl permeation through human skin in vitro using static diffusion cells. Elderly individuals are known to be more sensitive to opioids and obtain higher plasma concentrations following dermal application of fentanyl compared to younger individuals. The influence of age - as an isolated pharmacokinetic term - on the absorption of fentanyl has not been previously studied. METHOD: Human skin from 30 female donors was mounted in static diffusion cells, and samples were collected during 48 h. Donors were divided into three age groups: <30 years of age (n = 6), ≥30 and <60 years of age (n = 18) and ≥60 years of age (n = 6). RESULTS: The youngest group had a significantly higher mean absorption (3,100 ng/cm(2)) than the two other groups (2,000 and 1,475 ng/cm(2), respectively) and a significant larger AUC (young age group: 9,393 ng; middle and old age groups: 5,922 and 4,050 ng, respectively). Furthermore, the lag time and absorption rate were different between the three groups, with a significantly higher rate in the young participants versus the oldest participants. CONCLUSION: We demonstrate that fentanyl permeates the skin of young individuals in greater amounts and at a higher absorption rate than in middle-aged and old individuals in vitro.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Holmgaard, R","Benfeldt, Eva","Sorensen, J A","Nielsen, J B"],"cuid":["S02-098.16-046413"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Age","Aged","Aging","Analgesics Opioid","Female","Fentanyl","Human skin","Humans","Middle Aged","Penetration","Skin","Skin Absorption","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronological age affects the permeation of fentanyl through human skin in vitro","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000348876","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.16-046413","identifier":[{"id":"23736084","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84878362520","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d1d83bfb-2cec-4667-8a18-c661f59cf652","sdu-9821ac02-63ac-4c28-9a8c-ddebe4332b12"],"keyword":["Adult","Age","Aged","Aging","Analgesics, Opioid","Female","Fentanyl","Human skin","Humans","Middle Aged","Penetration","Skin","Skin Absorption","Static diffusion cells","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B87C89CD925B5211DCB66C935C39CF02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000348876","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"R","key":"holmgaardpau","last":"Holmgaard","name":"Holmgaard, R","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"E","key":"benfeldtpau","last":"Benfeldt","locid":"7c7d625b-398b-4c53-9762-02669d007af8","name":"Benfeldt, Eva","name_org":"Benfeldt, E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J A","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","name_org":"Sorensen, J A","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, J B","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23736084"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000348876","issn":["16605527","16605535"],"issn_org":["16605527"],"issue":"3","journal":"Skin Pharmacology and Physiology","pages":"155-9","status":"p","title":"Skin Pharmacology and Physiology","title_org":"Skin Pharmacology and Physiology (Print)","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878362520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d1d83bfb-2cec-4667-8a18-c661f59cf652","sdu-9821ac02-63ac-4c28-9a8c-ddebe4332b12"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Chronological age affects the permeation of fentanyl through human skin in vitro","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.16-046413","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Purpose:  This study aims to clarify the existence of and to map the localization of different proposed stem cell niches in the corneal limbal region. Materials and methods:  One human eye was cut into 2200 consecutive sections. Every other section was stained with haematoxylin and eosin, digitized at low and high magnification, aligned, 3D reconstructed and visualized using interactive 3D visualization software. The visualization software has interactive tools that make free rotations in all directions possible and makes it possible to create virtual sections independent of the original cutting plan. In all, one low-magnification and 24 high-magnification interactive 3D models were created. Immunohistochemistry against stem cell markers p63 and ΔNp63α was performed as a supplement to the 3D models. Results:  Using the interactive 3D models, we identified three types of stem cell niches in the limbal region: limbal epithelial crypts (LECs), limbal crypts (LCs) and focal stromal projections (FSPs). In all, eight LECs, 25 LCs and 105 FSPs were identified in the limbal region. The LECs, LCs and FSPs were predominantly located in the superior limbal region with seven LECs, 19 LCs and 93 FSPs in the superior limbal region and one LEC, six LCs and 12 FSPs in the inferior limbal region. Only few LECs, LCs and FSPs were localized nasally and temporally. Conclusion:  Interactive 3D models are a powerful tool that may help to shed more light on the existence and spatial localization of the different stem cell niches (LECs, LCs and FSPs) in the corneal limbal region.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Molvaer, Rikke Kongshaug","Andreasen, Arne","Heegaard, Steffen","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Hjortdal, Jesper","Urbak, Steen Fiil","Nielsen, Kim"],"cuid":["S03-086.23-015949"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cell Proliferation","Computer Simulation","Humans","Imaging Three Dimensional","Immunohistochemistry","Limbus Corneae","Male","Middle Aged","Stem cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Øjenlæge"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive 000000000003d computer model of the human corneolimbal region crypts projections and stem cells","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2012.02446.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-086.23-015949","identifier":[{"id":"84880255252","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22682073","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2df766de-0b0f-446c-bbf0-d1f009a087eb","ku-2e533217-4088-45ff-a085-cad0b24a2584","ku-dcb2a83a-241d-495e-8809-c3266ff6010d"],"keyword":["Cell Proliferation","Computer Simulation","Humans","Imaging, Three-Dimensional","Immunohistochemistry","Limbus Corneae","Male","Middle Aged","Stem Cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-6C93EE7D5A13A4C35CABC438B802F28D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2012.02446.x","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Øjenlæge"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Syd"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Øjenafdelingen (Oftalmologi), NBG"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"R.K.","key":"molvaerpau","last":"Molvaer","name":"Molvaer, R.K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"e60f073e-4e38-4dfc-94b4-d92fcadd319e","name":"Andreasen, Arne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Steffen","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"e1720fc3-b9d4-4664-8bcc-2394fd476fdd","name":"Heegaard, Steffen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Skovhus","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"924ef2ac-827c-4260-9cd7-fbe300bbafeb","name":"Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0001-9386-6679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Fiil","key":"urbakpau","last":"Urbak","locid":"ad1f1cbb-6bfb-46f1-904b-c5d3822b02dc","name":"Urbak, Steen Fiil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fd36656a-1aa7-48bb-9135-b85808617582","name":"Nielsen, Kim","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22682073"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1755-3768.2012.02446.x","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"457-462","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880255252"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","øjenafdelingen (oftalmologi), nbg"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2df766de-0b0f-446c-bbf0-d1f009a087eb","ku-2e533217-4088-45ff-a085-cad0b24a2584","ku-dcb2a83a-241d-495e-8809-c3266ff6010d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive 3D computer model of the human corneolimbal region : crypts, projections and stem cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-086.23-015949","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"During the last decade, a total of three student satellites have been developed by engineering students in a Problem and Project-Based Learning (PBL) environment at Aalborg University (AAU), Denmark. As solving such a complex project, we emphasize that a high level of motivation is needed for the students. Thus some efforts have been done on project management style with this aim. However, it is necessary continuous to discuss this issue from the students’ perspective for a better PBL environment. This leads to the research question of how the students perceive their motivation in developing satellite projects in a PBL environment. Empirically, a total of 12 student participants were interviewed. The results show that students’ motivation is highly stimulated by the project management with a series of factors, such as the task characteristics, support of peers, help of supervisors, and openness, etc. However, the time schedule is a barrier to motivation. Thus, the supervisors are suggested to be more aware of the complex relationships between student, teacher, tasks and the students’ response.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper Abildgaard","Nielsen, Jens Frederik Dalsgaard","Zhou, Chunfang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-073704"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motivating students to develop satellites in a problem and project based learning environment","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3991%2Fijep.v3i3.2529","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-073704","ids":["aau-516e00c8-4fdd-4178-af2e-6bb0cc23a69b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-23541451D6CEC18EABA4A7A7C8806BBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3991%2Fijep.v3i3.2529","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://online-journals.org/i-jep/article/view/2529","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Automation & Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Abildgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c2132fab-0da3-4eac-a19c-ff7f57345bb6","name":"Larsen, Jesper Abildgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4164-4913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Frederik Dalsgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1aa2e772-694f-4788-be3a-0b340af051fe","name":"Nielsen, Jens Frederik Dalsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1765-5551","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chunfang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"a0a4138c-09c9-425a-a228-963e343a5840","name":"Zhou, Chunfang","orcid":"0000-0001-5128-3950","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3991/ijep.v3i3.2529","issn":["21924880"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Engineering Pedagogy","pages":"11-17","publisher":"International Federation of Engineering Education Societies (IFEES)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Engineering Pedagogy","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-516e00c8-4fdd-4178-af2e-6bb0cc23a69b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Motivating Students to Develop Satellites in a Problem and Project-Based Learning Environment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-073704","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses over the air (OTA) testing for multiple input multiple output (MIMO) capable terminals with emphasis on channel spatial characteristics emulation. A novel technique to obtain optimum power weights for the OTA probes based on convex optimization is proposed. The proposed technique emulates spatial correlation as well as introduces constraints on the maximum deviation between the target power azimuth spectrum (PAS) and the emulated PAS in terms of mean angle of arrival (AoA) and azimuth spread (AS). Simulation results show that the proposed emulation technique present better performance compared with existing techniques in the literature. This improvement is further demonstrated by measurement results in a practical MIMO OTA setup.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fan, Wei","Carreño, Xavier","Sun, Fan","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Knudsen, Mikael B.","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-079109"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"emulating spatial characteristics of mimo channels for ota testing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/76111517/Emulating_Spatial_Characteristics_of_MIMO_Channels_for_OTA_Testing.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-079109","identifier":[{"id":"84881282003","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000322716900042","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-6410bf94-74f8-475f-9d38-e5810ef47396"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D8513FEBBE18723034DA697203E6514"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/76111517/Emulating_Spatial_Characteristic