{"abstract":"This paper presents current research on Danish municipalities' use of ESCOs (Energy Service Companies) as a way to improve the standard of public buildings and to increase energy efficiency. ESCO has for many years been known as a way to realise energy efficiency in buildings. In Denmark, it has mainly been used in the industry so far, but in recent years more and more municipalities have taken up ESCO initiatives, in order to retrofit existing public buildings, and to make them more energy efficient. ESCO is in many ways a new way of collaboration for Danish municipalities, and therefore include many challenges. At the moment 15 municipalities (of 98 municipalities in Denmark) are involved in ESCO contracting. The purpose of this paper is to discuss the various experience gained so far by municipalities, and to discuss the drivers and barriers behind the development. We also discuss whether ESCO might lead to new ways of working with energy efficiency in public buildings, and possibly generate innovation in the public sector. There is already some evidence from the municipalities that on-going ESCO projects have led to new ambitious initiatives and plans for energy savings in municipalities ESCOs have received much attention in different Danish energy-.efficiency policies, where ESCOs are often described as a promising way to achieve energy savings in existing housing and to overcome barriers encountered by other attempts at energy savings. Instead of assessing ESCO only on the amount of energy saved, we suggest that ESCO contracting could potentially become a learning process for municipalities, enabling and encourage public administrations to work in other ways with public-private and public-public partnerships on energy savings. Theoretically, it will compare the Danish development with international ESCO experience as well as refer to public innovation literature. Combined with empirical case studies on ESCO contracting, we discuss factors and conditions that influence decisions on ESCO, the flexibility of ESCO contracts and whether it implies an innovative process, or as a possible contrast, a 'once in a lifetimeexperience' for municipalities. The paper is based on an on-going research project, which aims to identify the opportunities and barriers of applying ESCO in the Danish housing market. The results are therefore preliminary.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Ole","Hansen, Jesper Rohr","Nielsen, Susanne Balslev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310167"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-26","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2011-05-24","title":"6th International Conference on Energy Efficiency in Domestic Appliances and Lighting","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esco in danish municipalities experience innovations potential","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5822446/Jensen%20Hansen%20and%20Balslev_EnergyServices%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310167","ids":["dtu-128f6d1f-f8c5-4d79-ab36-237b162273a6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EA6290DF2DD3DA21446EC0EF2DC32357"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5822446/Jensen%20Hansen%20and%20Balslev_EnergyServices%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management, Centre for Facilities Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Rohr","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper Rohr","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Balslev","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"37d6b355-4468-4f72-8256-afc593b8426e","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","orcid":"0000-0002-8269-6771","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"EEDAL - Energy Efficiency in Domestic Appliances and Lighting"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-128f6d1f-f8c5-4d79-ab36-237b162273a6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ESCO in Danish municipalities : Experience, innovations, potential","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310167","year":"2013","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Fast ions play an important role in heating the plasma in a magnetic confinement fusion device. Fast-ion Dα(FIDA) spectroscopy diagnoses fast ions in small measurement volumes. Spectra measured by a FIDA diagnostic can be related to the 2D fast-ion velocity distribution function. A single FIDA view probes certain regions in velocity-space, determined by the geometry of the set-up. Exploiting this, the fast-ion distribution function can be inferred using a velocity-space tomography method. This poster contains a tomography calculated from measured spectra from three different FIDA views at ASDEX Upgrade. The quality of the tomography improves with the number of FIDA views simultaneously measuring the same volume. To investigate the potential benefits of including additional views (up to 18), tomographies are inferred from synthetic spectra calculated from a simulated distribution function. The number of experimentally available views can be increased by combining different types of diagnostics in a joint velocity-space tomography. Using this, up to 7 views are available at ASDEX Upgrade from 2014.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Salewski, Mirko","Geiger, Benedikt","Garcia-Munoz, Manuel","Heidbrink, William","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Leipold, Frank","Madsen, Jens","Michelsen, Poul","Moseev, Dmitry","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Rasmussen, Jesper","Stejner Pedersen, Morten","Tardini, Giovanni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341848"],"event":{"end":"2013-11-15","place":"Denver, us","start":"2013-11-11","title":"55th Annual Meeting of the APS Division of Plasma Physics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute","University of California at Irvine","University of Seville"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"velocity space tomography of the fast ion distribution function","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-341848","ids":["dtu-7ce75819-e123-4fb3-ab19-0c4bc07bb07b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A294EEA1543E170C8872162DCF5117E1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california at irvine","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Irvine","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Schou","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2cf25f5f-7ac3-4206-b331-68303e95a7f8","name":"Jacobsen, Asger Schou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mirko","key":"salewskipau","last":"Salewski","locid":"38100e3a-6385-47d3-aa2d-6fc5608a8649","name":"Salewski, Mirko","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-679X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedikt","key":"geigerpau","last":"Geiger","name":"Geiger, Benedikt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel","key":"garciamunozpau","last":"Garcia-Munoz","name":"Garcia-Munoz, Manuel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"heidbrinkpau","last":"Heidbrink","name":"Heidbrink, William","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Bang","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"cc3d86b6-81c5-4e9b-99dd-3933c1d56f7d","name":"Korsholm, Søren Bang","orcid":"0000-0001-7160-8361","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank","key":"leipoldpau","last":"Leipold","locid":"fb1ca27f-36e0-43a2-8779-3d8135a2a8dc","name":"Leipold, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3107-6713","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul","key":"michelsenpau","last":"Michelsen","locid":"c713423a-38b4-4aef-93e1-c79449baf091","name":"Michelsen, Poul","orcid":"0000-0001-7409-0131","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dmitry","key":"moseevpau","last":"Moseev","name":"Moseev, Dmitry","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefan Kragh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"185da313-7f9e-45e7-9ee7-83306c90e806","name":"Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","orcid":"0000-0003-4175-3829","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"64e646b9-b8d3-4a78-ad01-598d07290029","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3947-1518","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"stejnerpedersenpau","last":"Stejner Pedersen","locid":"5e16534e-b167-4a1f-a316-ea12e478d879","name":"Stejner Pedersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-1300-8135","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"tardinipau","last":"Tardini","name":"Tardini, Giovanni","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00030503"],"issue":"16","journal":"American Physical Society. Bulletin","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"American Physical Society. Bulletin","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7ce75819-e123-4fb3-ab19-0c4bc07bb07b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Velocity-space tomography of the fast-ion distribution function","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341848","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We show that Auger processes involving wetting layer transitions mediate emission from a cavity that is detuned from a quantum dot by even tens of meV. The wetting layer thus acts as a reservoir, which by Coulomb scattering can supply or absorb the energy difference between emitter and cavity. We perform microscopic calculations of the effect treating the wetting layer as a non-Markovian reservoir interacting with the coupled quantum dot-cavity system through Coulomb interactions. Experimentally, cavity feeding has been observed in the asymmetric detuning range of -10 to +45 meV. We show that this asymmetry arises naturally from the quasiequilibrium properties of the wetting layer reservoir. Furthermore, we present numerical calculations of both photoluminescence spectra and photon correlations, demonstrating good qualitative agreement with experiments.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Settnes, Mikkel","Nielsen, Per Kær","Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347329"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"auger processes mediating the nonresonant optical emission from a semiconductor quantum dot embedded inside an optical cavity","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57771718/PhysRevLett.111.067403.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-347329","identifier":[{"id":"23971611","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84881527053","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8f514905-4da1-46a4-b0c7-1001b5c9f11c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E68A73F6793386843BE8D7B0E265734"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57771718/PhysRevLett.111.067403.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.111.067403","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Theoretical Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"settnespau","last":"Settnes","locid":"c6a5329d-a7a8-44c2-953d-a3fcb2cff6cf","name":"Settnes, Mikkel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Mølbjerg","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1bf57cde-4fad-4c3b-8fe1-c2be836414eb","name":"Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23971611"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.111.067403","issn":["00319007","10797114"],"issn_org":["00319007"],"issue":"6","journal":"Physical Review Letters","paperid":"067403","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Letters","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881527053"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8f514905-4da1-46a4-b0c7-1001b5c9f11c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Auger Processes Mediating the Nonresonant Optical Emission from a Semiconductor Quantum Dot Embedded Inside an Optical Cavity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347329","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Differences in the confinement of electrons and holes in quantum dots are shown to profoundly impact the magnitude of scattering with acoustic phonons. Using an extensive model that includes the non-Markovian nature of the phonon reservoir, we show how the effect may be addressed by photoluminescence excitation spectroscopy of a single quantum dot. We also investigate the implications for cavity QED, i.e., a coupled quantum dot-cavity system, and demonstrate that the phonon scattering may be strongly quenched. The quenching is explained by a balancing between the deformation potential interaction strengths and the carrier confinement and depends on the quantum dot shape. Numerical examples suggest a route towards engineering the phonon scattering.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nysteen, Anders","Nielsen, Per Kær","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348957"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proposed quenching of phonon induced processes in photoexcited quantum dots due to electron hole asymmetries","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.110.087401","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-348957","identifier":[{"id":"23473200","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84874130003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-94e2005e-32fe-4eb5-8217-3e70b017c795"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11BDB46A3105D81A66A6A084F710CBF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.110.087401","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nysteenpau","last":"Nysteen","locid":"feb12213-6336-4444-bc91-486323195b3a","name":"Nysteen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23473200"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.110.087401","issn":["00319007","10797114"],"issn_org":["00319007"],"issue":"8","journal":"Physical Review Letters","paperid":"087401","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Letters","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874130003"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-94e2005e-32fe-4eb5-8217-3e70b017c795"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Proposed Quenching of Phonon-Induced Processes in Photoexcited Quantum Dots due to Electron-Hole Asymmetries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348957","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In the present study, a coupled 3D transient Eulerian thermo-chemical analysis together with a 2D plane strain Lagrangian mechanical analysis of the pultrusion process, which has not been considered until now, is carried out. The development of the process induced residual stresses and strains together with the distortions are predicted during the pultrusion in which the cure hardening instantaneous linear elastic (CHILE) approach is implemented. At the end of the process, tension stresses prevail for the inner region of the composite since the curing rate is higher here as compared to the outer regions where compression stresses are obtained. The separation between the heating die and the part due to shrinkage is also investigated using a mechanical contact formulation at the die-part interface. The proposed approach is found to be efficient and fast for the calculation of the residual stresses and distortions together with the temperature and the cure distributions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Baran, Ismet","Tutum, Cem Celal","Nielsen, Michael Wenani","Hattel, Jesper Henri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353208"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["C Finite element analysis FEA","E Pultrusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"process induced residual stresses and distortions in pultrusion","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compositesb.2013.03.031","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353208","identifier":[{"id":"84877814177","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a2fffebf-91be-477b-afd1-c6802f288c1c"],"keyword":["A. Theromosetting resin","B. Residual/internal stress","C. Finite element analysis (FEA)","E. Pultrusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76C753AC59A70D673CB6B889C44621BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compositesb.2013.03.031","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ismet","key":"baranpau","last":"Baran","locid":"e2cf909e-6bb4-4050-9e1e-e92d58052ab3","name":"Baran, Ismet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cem Celal","key":"tutumpau","last":"Tutum","locid":"eb2f53c9-d215-44f4-973e-e005a7962db4","name":"Tutum, Cem Celal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Wenani","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6f04228d-8fbe-4940-8fba-6b7dd9e8df6c","name":"Nielsen, Michael Wenani","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.compositesb.2013.03.031","issn":["13598368"],"journal":"Composites Part B: Engineering","pages":"148-161","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Composites Part B: Engineering","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877814177"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a2fffebf-91be-477b-afd1-c6802f288c1c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Process induced residual stresses and distortions in pultrusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353208","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Denne artikel omhandler anbefalinger til opstilling af en geologisk og hydrogeologisk konceptuel model ved forureningsundersøgelser og er en del af en række korte artikler /1, som udspringer af et samarbejdsprojekt om vurdering/bestemmelse af DNAPL mellem DTU Miljø og Region Hovedstaden. Det samlede projekt er beskrevet i detaljer i Janniche et al. /2/. Artiklen tager udgangspunkt i en geologisk/hydrogeologisk feltundersøgelse af Naverland-lokaliteten /3, hvor der optræder chlorerede opløsningsmidler som DNAPL. Der er tale om en lerlokalitet med underliggende kalk.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Damgaard, Jesper","Grosen, Bernt","Martinez, Kerim","Fritz Nielsen, Ole","Kerrn-Jespersen, Henriette","Janniche, Gry Sander","Broholm, Mette Martina","Wealthall, Gary","Jørgensen, Torben H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357051"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GeoSyntec Consultants"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"geologisk og hydrogeologisk konceptuel modeludvikling for moræneler og kalk","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/56405520/Jordforurening_2_2013_net_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357051","ids":["dtu-afb45602-f28d-4137-bd8d-a0ffa96766b3"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-15CB1A887357BA888BF1BAE36A97A9D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.jordforurening.info/filer/avjinfo/98/Jordforurening_2_2013_net_2.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/56405520/Jordforurening_2_2013_net_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Region Hovedstaden"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Water Resources Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"geosyntec consultants","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GeoSyntec Consultants","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","name":"Damgaard, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernt","key":"grosenpau","last":"Grosen","name":"Grosen, Bernt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kerim","key":"martinezpau","last":"Martinez","name":"Martinez, Kerim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"fritznielsenpau","last":"Fritz Nielsen","name":"Fritz Nielsen, Ole","rank":4,"r