{"abstract":"I mange europæiske storbyer er el-drevne, støjsvage og hurtige letbaner på vej frem. De moderne ”sporvogne” er både erstatning for busser, men også et supplement til metro, S-tog og regionaltog. I hovedstadsregionen er letbanen langs med Ring 3 fra Lundtofte til Ishøj tæt på at blive til virkelighed med et passagergrundlag, der bliver større end kystbanen. Det viser den netop fremlagte udredning fra Ringby – Letbanesamarbejdet. I Trængselskommissionens idékatalog lægges der op til, at et sammenhængende letbanenet i Hovedstadsområdet skal undersøges. Denne rapport analyserer potentialet for flere letbaner i hovedstadsregionen – eventuelt suppleret af hurtige højklassede buslinjer (såkaldte Bus Rapid Transit, BRT). Rapporten viser, at man vil kunne anlægge et helt net af letbaner til samme pris som en metrolinje, og at en række linjer har stort passagerpotentiale.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Otto Anker","Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","Andersen, Jonas Lohmann Elkjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357705"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyse af potentialet for flere letbaner i hovedstadregionen rapport 000000000006","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/69844835/Analyse%20af%20potentialet%20for%20flere%20letbaner%20i%20Hovedstadsregionen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357705","ids":["dtu-b1db1633-551d-4ec6-9f99-c44ceb6a9f04"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2C06A11121F9FC0059354DAA9C166AF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/69844835/Analyse%20af%20potentialet%20for%20flere%20letbaner%20i%20Hovedstadsregionen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport, Traffic modelling and planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bláfoss","key":"ingvardsonpau","last":"Ingvardson","locid":"910e3f5c-3100-4005-82a4-8d3253d4d89b","name":"Ingvardson, Jesper Bláfoss","orcid":"0000-0002-0609-5165","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Lohmann Elkjær","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"0f1c058d-30ea-40ca-8bed-319bf28bdcee","name":"Andersen, Jonas Lohmann Elkjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788773272435"],"pages":"122","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"DTU Transport","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b1db1633-551d-4ec6-9f99-c44ceb6a9f04"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Analyse af potentialet for flere letbaner i Hovedstadregionen : Rapport 6","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357705","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper outlines results of a proposed layout of a light 2-bladed rotor, with a driving torque constraint matching the generator design, and shows details of the pultruded blade – and rotor geometry. In comparison with the 1st baseline design of a 5 MW VAWT concept this present development provides during standstill and operation significant less mass with a comparable level of loading strain in the blades and in the junctions between blade and tower. Optimized blade profile having a low weight and high stiffness is obtained according to the design evaluations based on the standstill calculations in ANSYS software. The selected profiles are used in the aero dynamic simulation. Furthermore the simulation code will be demonstrated to show the fully development model, integrating the simulation of turbulent wind inflow, actuator cylinder flow model, power controls, hydraulic floater - and mooring line systems implementation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schmidt Paulsen, Uwe","Aagaard Madsen, Helge","Hattel, Jesper Henri","Baran, Ismet","Nielsen, Per Hørlyk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378152"],"event":{"end":"2013-01-25","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2013-01-24","title":"10th Deep Sea Offshore Wind R &amp; D Conference","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Pultrusion","Structural design","vertical axis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design optimization of a 000000000005 mw floating offshore vertical axis wind turbine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57600487/Design_Optimization.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378152","identifier":[{"id":"84897530002","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f5f722cd-e9e7-4e15-80af-10bbe6352618"],"keyword":["floating offshore wind turbine ;submerged generator ;optimization","pultrusion","structural design","vertical axis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5BDF0C8C43486CD0462A1D8723DAF99C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57600487/Design_Optimization.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.egypro.2013.07.155","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Test and Measurements"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uwe","key":"schmidtpaulsenpau","last":"Schmidt Paulsen","locid":"1ca05d05-ae00-49ee-8355-7f76690a269e","name":"Schmidt Paulsen, Uwe","orcid":"0000-0002-8991-5658","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"aagaardmadsenpau","last":"Aagaard Madsen","locid":"4fac772e-0130-46b6-b3d5-9ee867002814","name":"Aagaard Madsen, Helge","orcid":"0000-0002-4647-3706","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ismet","key":"baranpau","last":"Baran","locid":"e2cf909e-6bb4-4050-9e1e-e92d58052ab3","name":"Baran, Ismet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Hørlyk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f1bac13c-b951-45c8-9718-1a5c783cbc04","name":"Nielsen, Per Hørlyk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.egypro.2013.07.155","issn":["18766102"],"journal":"Energy Procedia","pages":"22-32","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy Procedia","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897530002"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f5f722cd-e9e7-4e15-80af-10bbe6352618"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Design Optimization of a 5 MW Floating Offshore Vertical-axis Wind Turbine","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-378152","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Cell-penetrating peptides (CPPs) and antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) show great potential as drug delivery vectors and new antibiotic drug entities, respectively. The current study deals with the properties of a variety of peptide analogs derived from the well-known CPP penetratin as well as octaarginine and different Tat sequences. The effects of peptide length, guanidinium content, and sequence of non-cationic residues were assessed in mammalian and bacterial cells. The arginine (Arg) content in the penetratin analogs was found to influence eukaryotic cell uptake efficiency, antimicrobial activity towards both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria as well as eukaryotic cell viability. All examined analogs retained the ability to cross eukaryotic membranes giving rise to a distribution within the vacuolar apparatus. Interestingly, a series of shuffled analogs of penetratin with the cationic residues in conserved positions, attain the same a-helical conformation as native penetratin in the presence of cholesterol-containing liposomes, while conformational differences were observed in the presence of highly anionic liposomes. While the antibacterial effect of the two groups of peptides was similar, the eukaryotic cellular uptake of the shuffled analogs was noticeably lower than for native penetratin. Moreover, a point substitution of Met to Leu in native penetratin had no influence on eukaryotic cellular uptake and antimicrobial effect, and only a minor effect on cytotoxicity, in contrast to the fact that the same substitution in the shuffled analog gave rise to reduced eukaryotic cellular uptake while increasing the antibacterial effect and cytotoxicity.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bahnsen, Jesper Søborg","Franzyk, Henrik","Sandberg-Schaal, Anne","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400884"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Acces