ner-Møller, Asger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"stobbepau","last":"Stobbe","locid":"ca5f4de5-9547-4d43-b6b1-f78e8adc914d","name":"Stobbe, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-0991-041X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nysteenpau","last":"Nysteen","locid":"feb12213-6336-4444-bc91-486323195b3a","name":"Nysteen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpau","last":"Lodahl","locid":"fa2dbf58-7de5-4c4c-a7fc-6c96dc6d6937","name":"Lodahl, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9348-9591","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.88.045316","issn":["01631829","1550235X"],"issn_org":["01631829"],"issue":"4","journal":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","paperid":"045316","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","volume":"88"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883204921"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d2b4cdb6-5a29-4f5b-9657-d9a85ef69325","ku-dbf2d20f-0d48-43f7-8c17-ef6ae739153f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measuring the effective phonon density of states of a quantum dot in cavity quantum electrodynamics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.17-037350","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The cardiac flow is complex and multidirectional, and difficult to measure with conventional Doppler ultrasound (US) methods due to the one-dimensional and angle-dependent velocity estimation. The vector velocity method Transverse Oscillation (TO) has been proposed as a solution to this. TO is implemented on a conventional US scanner (Pro Focus 2202 UltraView, BK Medical) using a linear transducer (8670, BK Medical) and can provide real-time, angle-independent vector velocity estimates of the cardiac blood flow. During cardiac surgery, epicardiac US examinations using TO were performed on three patients. Antegrade central jet and retrograde flow near the vessel wall in the ascending aorta and the pulmonary artery were seen during systole, while stable vortices were seen in the aortic sinuses and complex flow patterns were seen around the valves during diastole. In the right atrium, a stable vortex was seen during the entire heart cycle. For comparison, simultaneous Measurements were obtained with conventional spectral Doppler (SD) and intravenous catheter thermodilution technique (TD). Peak systolic velocities were underestimated by 18% compared to SD and cardiac output was underestimated by 16% compared to TD. This is the first time TO measurements have been obtained of cardiac flow. TO can potentially reveal new information of cardiovascular physiology and blood flow dynamics, and become a valuable tool in cardiology.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Nilsson, Jens Christian","Lund, Jens Teglgaard","Bachmann Nielsen, Michael","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S02-084.50-035931"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-25","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2013-07-21","title":"2013 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood flow","Cardiology","Intraoperative ultrasound","Transverse oscillation","Vector velocity estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraoperative vector flow imaging of the heart","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57407156/Hansen_ieee_2013.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-084.50-035931","identifier":[{"id":"84894375094","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-929086aa-c613-4ed3-91f4-83b9cdd194e6","ku-19743db9-4a53-4af2-a834-871b22a87304"],"keyword":["Blood flow","Cardiology","Intraoperative ultrasound","Transverse Oscillation","Vector velocity estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-480EB707B39CEE131DBFA6DAF9587DC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57407156/Hansen_ieee_2013.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ULTSYM.2013.0445","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l