as Aalexander","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick Thomas","key":"ellinorpau","last":"Ellinor","name":"Ellinor, Patrick Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Gaarsdal","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23608590"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hrthm.2013.04.012","issn":["15475271","15563871"],"issn_org":["15475271"],"issue":"9","journal":"Heart Rhythm","pages":"1249-1256","status":"p","title":"Heart Rhythm","title_org":"Heart rhythm : the official journal of the Heart Rhythm Society","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883246516"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-037abc79-185b-4695-84bb-9d383de9acbb","ku-8580cd32-6f05-42b4-89ec-4e8ab6916a78"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of atrial fibrillation as a function of the electrocardiographic PR interval : Results from the Copenhagen ECG Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.00-000180","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: To investigate the indications for system upgrade with single lead atrial pacing (AAIR), complications associated with these re-interventions, and possible predictors for system upgrade among patients included in the Danish Multicenter Randomized Trial on AAIR vs. dual-chamber pacing (DDDR) in sick sinus syndrome (DANPACE).METHODS AND RESULTS: A total of 707 of 1415 patients were randomized to AAIR pacing. Mean follow-up was 5.5 ± 2.6 years. Information on indications for system upgrade and complications were collected by reviewing patient charts. Multiple logistic regression was used to estimate adjusted odds ratios (aOR) with 95% confidence intervals (CI) for the association between predictors and system upgrade. Sixty-six patients (9.3%) in the AAIR group underwent system upgrade. Fifty-nine of these patients (89.3%) had a documented class I indication for system upgrade. Age (aOR 0.98 for each 1-year increase in age; 95% CI 0.6-1.0), and left atrial enlargement (aOR 1.9; 95% CI 1.0-3.8) were predictors for system upgrade. No single clinically applicable predictor for upgrade was identified. A total of 11 patients (16.7%) experienced at least one major complication after system upgrade.CONCLUSION: The majority of patients with AAIR pacing who underwent system upgrade had a class I indication. The incidence of major complications after system upgrade was high. The present data support the use of DDDR pacing rather than AAIR pacing in sick sinus syndrome.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kirkfeldt, Rikke Esberg","Andersen, Henning Rud","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Investigators, DANPACE","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S02-096.59-013001"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["on behalf of the DANPACE Investigators"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"system upgrade and its complications in patients with a single lead atrial pacemaker data from the danpace trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/eut039","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.59-013001","identifier":[{"id":"23449923","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880929847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-05834eb4-5920-4826-a373-c5fd21d34ff7","ku-f22c4bb7-17d3-4b89-a18e-56475beb8d20"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-40869B6A9EDF93F94D146516F5BA0FB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/eut039","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"on behalf of the danpace investigators","name":"on behalf of the DANPACE Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Esberg","key":"kirkfeldtpau","last":"Kirkfeldt","locid":"929b9a19-9b99-41a9-a8c3-6558e74c5117","name":"Kirkfeldt, Rikke Esberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning Rud","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b10137fd-6f42-4108-8ab6-f4c14c6157e7","name":"Andersen, Henning Rud","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"DANPACE","key":"investigatorspau","last":"Investigators","name":"Investigators, DANPACE","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23449923"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/eut039","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"8","journal":"Europace","pages":"1166-1173","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880929847"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-05834eb4-5920-4826-a373-c5fd21d34ff7","ku-f22c4bb7-17d3-4b89-a18e-56475beb8d20"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"System upgrade and its complications in patients with a single lead atrial pacemaker : data from the DANPACE trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.59-013001","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To use microarray-based miRNA profiling of colonic mucosal biopsies from patients with ulcerative colitis (UC), Crohn's disease (CD), and controls in order to identify new potential miRNA biomarkers in inflammatory bowel disease. METHODS: Colonic mucosal pinch biopsies from the descending part were obtained endoscopically from patients with active UC or CD, quiescent UC or CD, as well as healthy controls. Total RNA was isolated and miRNA expression assessed using the miRNA microarray Geniom Biochip miRNA Homo sapiens (Febit GmbH, Heidelberg, Germany). Data analysis was carried out by principal component analysis and projection to latent structure-discriminant analysis using the SIMCA-P+12 software package (Umetrics, Umea, Sweden). The microarray data were subsequently validated by quantitative real-time polymerase chain reaction (qPCR) performed on colonic tissue samples from active UC patients (n = 20), patients with quiescent UC (n = 19), and healthy controls (n = 20). The qPCR results were analyzed with Mann-Whitney U test. In silico prediction analysis were performed to identify potential miRNA target genes and the predicted miRNA targets were then compared with all UC associated susceptibility genes reported in the literature. RESULTS: The colonic mucosal miRNA transcriptome differs significantly between UC and controls, UC and CD, as well as between UC patients with mucosal inflammation and those without. However, no clear differences in the transcriptome of patients with CD and controls were found. The miRNAs with the strongest differential power were identified (miR-20b, miR-99a, miR-203, miR-26b, and miR-98) and found to be up-regulated more than a 10-fold in active UC as compared to quiescent UC, CD, and controls. Two miRNAs, miR-125b-1* and let-7e*, were up-regulated more than 5-fold in quiescent UC compared to active UC, CD, and controls. Four of the seven miRNAs (miR-20b, miR-98, miR-125b-1*, and let-7e*) were validated by qPCR and found to be specifically upregulated in patients with UC. Using in silico analysis we found several predicted pro-inflammatory target genes involved in various pathways, such as mitogen-activated protein kinase and cytokine signaling, which are both key signaling pathways in UC. CONCLUSION: The present study provides the first evidence that miR-20b, miR-98, miR-125b-1*, and let-7e* are deregulated in patients with UC. The level of these miRNAs may serve as new potential biomarkers for this chronic disease.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Troelsen, Jesper","Olsen, Jørgen","Nielsen, Ole Haagen"],"cuid":["S02-098.84-047149"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Biopsy","Case Control Studies","Colitis Ulcerative","Crohn Disease","Female","Gene Expression Regulation","Humans","MAP Kinase Signaling System","Male","MicroRNAs","Middle Aged","Oligonucleotide Array Sequence Analysis","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Software"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mir 000000000020b mir 000000000098 mir 000000000125b 000000000001 and let 000000000007e as new potential diagnostic biomarkers in ulcerative colitis","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3748/wjg.v19.i27.4289","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.84-047149","identifier":[{"id":"23885139","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880437626","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3718896","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ec68657e-2c3d-4fb7-8056-9f17ea1f5a44","ruc-b218150a-7e0b-4f61-bb8b-3834f7f8516b"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Biopsy","Case-Control Studies","Colitis, Ulcerative","Crohn Disease","Female","Gene Expression Regulation","Humans","MAP Kinase Signaling System","Male","MicroRNAs","Middle Aged","Oligonucleotide Array Sequence Analysis","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Software"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-08FD21152076C8721F65563C17DD1CCF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3748/wjg.v19.i27.4289","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, ICMM Section 8"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Eukaryot Cellebiologi","Roskilde University, The Department of Science, Systems and Models"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Tveiten","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","locid":"fe4b37d0-7b36-4636-925f-e1d395b9e573","name":"Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"dd6747c2-2376-4486-a000-1b4f1222eaaf","name":"Olsen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-1974-6446","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23885139"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3748/wjg.v19.i27.4289","issn":["10079327","10093079"],"issn_org":["10079327"],"issue":"27","journal":"World Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"4289-4299","status":"p","title":"World Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880437626"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ec68657e-2c3d-4fb7-8056-9f17ea1f5a44","ruc-b218150a-7e0b-4f61-bb8b-3834f7f8516b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"miR-20b, miR-98, miR-125b-1*, and let-7e* as new potential diagnostic biomarkers in ulcerative colitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.84-047149","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Multiple Chemical Sensitivity (MCS) is a chronic condition characterized by recurrent, non-specific symptoms in response to chemically unrelated exposures in non-toxic concentrations. Although the pathophysiology of MCS remains unknown, central sensitization may be an important factor contributing to the clinical manifestations. PURPOSE: To use quantitative sensory testing (QST) to study central hyperexcitability and multiple aspects of central sensory processing in MCS patients without comorbid overlapping disorders and to compare the results with those among matched controls. METHODS: 15 MCS patients and 15 healthy matched controls underwent QST to assess the following aspects of pain: capsaicin-induced secondary punctate hyperalgesia, stimulus response function (SRF) to punctate mechanical stimuli before and after capsaicin injection, temporal summation to punctate stimuli post capsaicin injection, pressure pain thresholds, heat pain thresholds, tonic heat stimulation and conditioning pain modulation (CPM: formerly known as diffuse noxious inhibitory control or DNIC). RESULTS: The mean area of capsaicin-induced secondary punctate hyperalgesia was significantly larger in MCS patients than in controls at 5, 30 and 60 min post capsaicin injection (p=0.01). In addition MCS patients reported higher ratings in response to punctate mechanical stimuli assessed by SRF compared with controls (p<0.001). The CPM test induced significantly higher pain ratings in patients than in controls (p=0.002). We found no group differences in pressure pain and heat pain thresholds, temporal summation to punctate stimuli post capsaicin injection, capsaicin and tonic heat pain ratings or CPM effect. CONCLUSION: Increased capsaicin-induced secondary punctate hyperalgesia was demonstrated in MCS patients without comorbid, overlapping disorders, suggesting facilitated central sensitization in MCS.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tran, Marie Thi Dao","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Kupers, Ron","Elberling, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-098.96-007355"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Capsaicin","Central Nervous System Sensitization","Cold Temperature","Female","Hot Temperature","Humans","Hyperalgesia","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple chemical sensitivity","Pain Measurement","Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiple chemical sensitivity on the scent of central sensitization","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheh.2012.02.010","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.96-007355","identifier":[{"id":"22487274","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84873059212","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000316438900013","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-97a80fde-9800-431b-8a79-bba06a1f1c30","ku-f04d05e5-d5dc-4f09-8e8d-ede18591804b"],"keyword":["Adult","Capsaicin","Central Nervous System Sensitization","Cold Temperature","Female","Hot Temperature","Humans","Hyperalgesia","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Chemical Sensitivity","Pain Measurement","Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5041AF2BEC4C90AEB379C2145ECBDD6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijheh.2012.02.010","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, BRAIN Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Thi Dao","key":"tranpau","last":"Tran","name":"Tran, Marie Thi Dao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ron","key":"kuperspau","last":"Kupers","locid":"8dffd6cf-3925-4283-aca4-8e51f3691c90","name":"Kupers, Ron","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22487274"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijheh.2012.02.010","issn":["14384639","1618131X"],"issn_org":["14384639"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal of Hygiene and Environmental Health","pages":"202-210","publisher":"Elsevier GmbH","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hygiene and Environmental Health","volume":"216"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873059212"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-97a80fde-9800-431b-8a79-bba06a1f1c30","ku-f04d05e5-d5dc-4f09-8e8d-ede18591804b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multiple chemical sensitivity : on the scent of central sensitization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.96-007355","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Forecast-based flow prediction in drainage systems can be used to implement real-time control of drainage systems. This study compares two different types of rainfall forecast - a radar rainfall extrapolation-based nowcast model and a numerical weather prediction model. The models are applied as input to an urban runoff model predicting the inlet flow to a waste water treatment plant. The modelled flows are auto-calibrated against real-time flow observations in order to certify the best possible forecast. Results show that it is possible to forecast flows with a lead time of 24 h. The best performance of the system is found using the radar nowcast for the short lead times and the weather model for larger lead times.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","Poulsen, Troels Sander","Bøvith, Thomas","Borup, Morten","Ahm, Malte","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","Grum, Morten","Rasmussen, Michael R.","Gill, Rasphall","Mikkelsen, Peter Steen"],"cuid":["S02-099.39-011615"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["DMI HIRLAM","Drainage","Forecast","Forecasting","Numerical Weather Model","Radar","Real time control","Runoff Model","Sewage","Weather forecasting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DMI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-KVWT","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DMI","DI-PR-KVWT","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of short term rainfall forecasts for modelbased flow prediction in urban drainage systems","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/wst.2013.274","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.39-011615","identifier":[{"id":"84881191169","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000322886600028","type":"wos"},{"id":"23863443","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f3257e53-4f64-4fd8-a7da-b239323a1fab","dtu-aebf099d-66ba-4c4b-a02d-f9be7fb26a35"],"keyword":["DMI-HIRLAM","Drainage","Forecast","Forecasting","Numerical Weather Model","Radar","Real time control","Runoff Model","Sewage","Weather forecasting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-52B37B41854AA7FD63D305B1646BB716"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/wst.2013.274","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Soil","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Urban Water and Environment Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Water and Environment Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Water and Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","