":"Ahm, Malte","orcid":"0000-0002-9257-6765","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"grumpau","last":"Grum","name":"Grum, Morten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael R.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"boruppau","last":"Borup","locid":"bddb33a7-54ad-492e-a40c-d47a0e71b77e","name":"Borup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-6531-9464","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasphall","key":"gillpau","last":"Gill","name":"Gill, Rasphall","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Steen","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"5d6db083-1bf0-4341-bc4c-ac2f83e29354","name":"Mikkelsen, Peter Steen","orcid":"0000-0003-3799-0493","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23863443"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2166/wst.2013.274","issn":["02731223","19969732"],"issn_org":["02731223"],"issue":"2","journal":"Water Science and Technology","pages":"472-478","publisher":"IWA Publishing","status":"p","title":"Water Science and Technology","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881191169"],"sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Krüger A/S Veolia Water Technologies, Denmark","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","krüger a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f3257e53-4f64-4fd8-a7da-b239323a1fab","dtu-aebf099d-66ba-4c4b-a02d-f9be7fb26a35"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of short-term rainfall forecasts for modelbased flow prediction in urban drainage systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.39-011615","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: Multiple chemical sensitivity (MCS) is a chronic condition of unknown etiology. MCS is characterized by recurrent nonspecific symptoms from multiple organ systems in response to chemical exposures in concentrations that are normally tolerated by the majority of the population. The symptoms may have severe impact on patients' lives, but an evidence-based treatment for the condition is nonexisting. The pathophysiology is unclarified, but several indicators point towards abnormal processing of sensory signals in the central nervous system. Pulsed electromagnetic fields (PEMF) offer a promising new treatment for refractory depression and can be targeted at the brain, thereby activating biochemical cell processes.Methods/Design: In a parallel, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial conducted at the Danish Research Centre for Chemical Sensitivities, the effects of PEMF in MCS patients will be assessed using the Re5 Independent System. Based on sample size estimation, 40 participants will be randomized to either PEMF therapy or placebo. The allocation sequence will be generated by computer. All involved parties (that is, participants, investigators, the research nurse, and the statistician) will be blinded to group allocation. The participants will receive PEMF therapy or placebo applied transcranially 30 minutes twice a day for 7 days a week over 6 consecutive weeks. Outcomes will be measured at baseline, once weekly during treatment, post treatment, and at 2.5-month and 4.5-month follow-up according to a predefined timetable. The primary outcome will be a measurement of the impact of MCS on everyday life. The secondary outcomes will be measurements of MCS symptoms, psychological distress (stress, anxiety or depressive symptoms), capsaicin-induced secondary punctate hyperalgesia, immunological markers in serum, and quality of life.Discussion: This trial will assess the effects of PEMF therapy for MCS. Currently, there is no treatment with a documented effect on MCS, and in terms of healthcare there is very little to offer these patients. There is thus a great need for well-conducted randomized trials aimed at assessing possible treatment effects. A positive outcome will pave the way for improved healthcare and understanding of this very disabling and overlooked condition.Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT01834781.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tran, Marie Thi Dao","Skovbjerg, Sine","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Christensen, Karl Bang","Elberling, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009097"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Multiple chemical sensitivity","Pulsed electromagnetic fields","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["The Danish Research Centre for Chemical Sensitivities"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcranial pulsed electromagnetic fields for multiple chemical sensitivity study protocol for a randomized double blind placebo controlled trial","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1745-6215-14-256","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009097","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000323391100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC3765111","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23947742","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84881530261","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bca72ab5-0982-4668-a6c2-44fb25922b1d","ku-af3b7e21-0dfd-437c-933b-3dbb944c3d17"],"keyword":["Multiple chemical sensitivity","Pulsed electromagnetic fields","Randomized controlled trial","Re5 independent system","Re5 therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB0A0AB64E86E78B1A290092CE9BCCD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84881530261&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1745-6215-14-256","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The Danish Research Centre for Chemical Sensitivities"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marie Thi Dao","key":"tranpau","last":"Tran","locid":"49488d09-4796-4b5f-a55a-f6b6fb945582","name":"Tran, Marie Thi Dao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sine","key":"skovbjergpau","last":"Skovbjerg","name":"Skovbjerg, Sine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Bang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"850a805f-c580-4858-822c-8e5c72ac780c","name":"Christensen, Karl Bang","orcid":"0000-0003-4518-5187","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"elberlingpau","last":"Elberling","name":"Elberling, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23947742"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1745-6215-14-256","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"journal":"Trials","paperid":"256","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881530261"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bca72ab5-0982-4668-a6c2-44fb25922b1d","ku-af3b7e21-0dfd-437c-933b-3dbb944c3d17"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transcranial pulsed electromagnetic fields for multiple chemical sensitivity: Study protocol for a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009097","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Chronic stress is prevalent in patients with ischemic heart disease (IHD) and worsens the long-term prognosis. Chronic stress is vaguely defined, but is associated with depressive symptoms, reduced psychological wellbeing, and reduced quality of life (QOL). Stress seems to induce hyperalgesia. The aim of the present study was to evaluate hyperalgesia by pressure pain sensitivity (PPS) in patients with IHD, and compare PPS to questionnaires measuring depressive symptoms, reduced psychological wellbeing, and QOL as markers of stress. Design. A cross-sectional study of 361 subjects with IHD. Methods. PPS was measured on the sternum, and compared to the questionnaires: Clinical stress symptoms score (CSS), Major Depression Inventory (MDI), WHO-5 Wellbeing Index, and SF-36 QOL score. Results. PPS correlated to CSS (r = 0.20, p <0.001), MDI (r = 0.14, p = 0.02), SF-36 mental component summary score (MCS) (r = - 0.10, p = 0.049), SF-36 physical component summary score (PCS) (r = - 0.17, p = 0.001), and self-perceived stress level (r = 0.15, p = 0.006). CSS correlated similarly (r = 0.5-0.7, all p <0.001). Comparing subjects within the lowest vs. highest tertiles of PPS and CSS, the mean MDI score was 4 vs. 15, WHO-5 was 77 vs. 53, SF-36 PCS was 53 vs. 43, and SF-36 MCS was 58 vs. 46; all p <0.001. Conclusions. PPS reflected to a modest degree markers of chronic stress in IHD. PPS and CSS together might be useful as easy-to use tools for evaluating these markers in IHD patients","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bergmann, Natasha","Ballegaard, Søren","Holmager, Pernille","Kristiansen, Jesper","Gyntelberg, Finn","Andersen, Lars J.","Hjalmarson, Åke","Bech, Per","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Faber, Jens"],"cuid":["S03-097.83-766968"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pressure pain sensitivity a new method of stress measurement in patients with ischemic heart disease","src":["aau","ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2013.785588","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.83-766968","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000323106700003","type":"wos"},{"id":"84882310729","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23607612","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b62913e8-102c-432d-bfb0-aa4df1059dd2","ku-b5b93f93-f910-4655-8917-ef7c9e137671","nfa-c024368c-d9d6-4ee3-bb1b-fba7bb9f114f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-005B7DFB84160C58B31BD737CF5D3418"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2013.785588","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://informahealthcare.com/doi/abs/10.3109/00365513.2013.785588","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nl":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Natasha","key":"bergmannpau","last":"Bergmann","name":"Bergmann, Natasha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"ballegaardpau","last":"Ballegaard","name":"Ballegaard, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"holmagerpau","last":"Holmager","name":"Holmager, Pernille","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-8900","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn","key":"gyntelbergpau","last":"Gyntelberg","name":"Gyntelberg, Finn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars J.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lars J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Åke","key":"hjalmarsonpau","last":"Hjalmarson","name":"Hjalmarson, Åke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","locid":"b586a6d5-0293-47f7-bacb-7d8c7f4e3d46","name":"Bech, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-4948-6115","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23607612"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365513.2013.785588","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"5","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"373-379","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882310729"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b62913e8-102c-432d-bfb0-aa4df1059dd2","ku-b5b93f93-f910-4655-8917-ef7c9e137671","nfa-c024368c-d9d6-4ee3-bb1b-fba7bb9f114f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Pressure pain sensitivity: A new method of stress measurement in patients with ischemic heart disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.83-766968","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: All five Nordic countries have nationwide prescription databases covering all dispensed drugs, with potential for linkage to outcomes. The aim of this review is to present an overview of therapeutic areas studied and methods applied in pharmacoepidemiologic studies using data from these databases. METHODS: The study consists of a Medline-based structured literature review of scientific papers published during 2005-2010 using data from the prescription databases in Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway, and Sweden, covering 25 million inhabitants. Relevant studies were analyzed in terms of pharmacological group, study population, outcomes examined, type of study (drug utilization vs. effect of drug therapy), country of origin, and extent of cross-national collaboration. RESULTS: A total of 515 studies were identified. Of these, 262 were conducted in Denmark, 97 in Finland, 4 in Iceland, 87 in Norway, and 61 in Sweden. Four studies used data from more than one Nordic country. The most commonly studied drugs were those acting on the nervous system, followed by cardiovascular drugs and gastrointestinal/endocrine drugs. A total of 228 studies examined drug utilization and 263 focused on the effects and safety of drug therapy. Pregnant women were the most commonly studied population in safety studies, whereas prescribers' adherence to guidelines was the most frequent topic of drug utilization studies. CONCLUSIONS: The Nordic prescription databases, with their possibility of record-linkage, represent an outstanding resource for assessing the beneficial and adverse effects of drug use in large populations, under routine care conditions, and with the potential for long-term follow-up. Copyright (c) 2013 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd","author_count":20,"contributors":["Wettermark, B","Zoëga, H","Furu, K","Korhonen, M","Hallas, Jesper","Nørgaard, M","Almarsdottir, Ab","Andersen, Mette","Andersson Sundell, K","Bergman, Ulf Michael","Helin-Salmivaara, A","Hoffmann, M","Kieler, H","Martikainen, Je","Mortensen, M","Petzold, M","Wallach-Kildemoes, H","Wallin, C","Sørensen, Ht","Almarsdóttir, Anna Birna"],"cuid":["S03-099.46-022209"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Wettermark,B.; Zoega,H.; Furu,K.; Korhonen,M.; Hallas,J.; Norgaard,M.; Almarsdottir,A.; Andersen,M.; Andersson,Sundell K.; Bergman,U.; Helin-Salmivaara,A.; Hoffmann,M.Kieler,H.; Martikainen,J.; Mortensen,M.; Petzold,M.; Wallach-Kildemoes,H.; Wallin,C.; Sorensen,H."],"keyword":["Cross national comparison","Drug Utilization","Effectiveness","Observational studies","Pharmacoepidemiology","Record linkage","Safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the nordic prescription databases as a resource for pharmacoepidemiological research a literature review","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pds.3457","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.46-022209","identifier":[{"id":"84880046715","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23703712","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-828b1055-1367-4c93-ac8a-f59d156e51a4","ku-4cb0069e-2cab-4fd6-b0ba-a8a809034b45","sdu-39d778fd-815b-47e4-b22e-0d15219faee8"],"keyword":["Cross-national comparison","Drug utilization","Effectiveness","Observational studies","Pharmacoepidemiology","Prescription databases","Record-linkage","Safety"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-7975CD6C9BCCE07F0A3337B489F679FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pds.3457","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unuse