{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Christian","Sort, Jesper Chrautwald","Bentsen, Martin Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100550"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"levers of management in university industry collaborations how project management affects value creation at different life cycle stages of a collaboration","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/13583883.2013.795603","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-100550","identifier":[{"id":"84882250095","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ae14dbe8-6b71-443b-b60b-f5f5a1d53e1d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-947F60A95BB8D2A0B4E43B7890B211A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/13583883.2013.795603","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/13583883.2013.795603","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Aalborg University Business School, Business Design Center","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management, Management Accounting and Control, MAC"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5ce07766-d99e-45a5-84b3-0267fca84453","name":"Nielsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-5050-5793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Chrautwald","key":"sortpau","last":"Sort","locid":"11418beb-d40c-40bf-af69-55b47598cc45","name":"Sort, Jesper Chrautwald","orcid":"0000-0003-0468-6209","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Juul","key":"bentsenpau","last":"Bentsen","locid":"f7a7a631-c1fe-41fc-8412-321ca83586b3","name":"Bentsen, Martin Juul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/13583883.2013.795603","issn":["13583883","15731936"],"issn_org":["13583883"],"issue":"3","journal":"Tertiary Education and Management","pages":"246-266","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Tertiary Education and Management","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882250095"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ae14dbe8-6b71-443b-b60b-f5f5a1d53e1d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Levers of Management in University–Industry Collaborations : How project management affects value creation at different life-cycle stages of a collaboration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-100550","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The topic of this thesis is weather radar precipitation measurements. Measuring the spatial and temporal variations of the precipitation by weather radars has significant advantages compared to point measurements from rain gauges within urban drainage applications. Knowledge on how the rainfall is distributed between the rain gauges is in itself valuable for retrospective analysis of urban drainage systems. In addition, on-line distributed weather radar precipitation measurements facilitate radar based now-casts of the precipitation. As the radar detects the precipitation before it reaches the urban area of interest, the radar measurements can be used in the process of predicting the near future loads and state of the urban drainage system. Such information is a necessity for real-time control decision support. The action possibilities within real-time control rely greatly on accurate prediction of future system state. Accurate and reliable weather radar measurements are, therefore, important for future developments and achievements within urban drainage. This PhD study investigates two types of weather radars. Both systems are in operational use in Denmark today. A network of meteorological C-band weather radars provides a basic coverage of almost the entire country. In addition, the larger cities are also covered by small Local Area Weather Radars (LAWR). Whereas the large C-band network is operated and owned by the Danish Meteorological Institute (DMI), the smaller urban radars are operated individually and owned by local water utility companies. Although the two radar systems use similar working principles, the systems have significant differences regarding technology, temporal resolution, spatial resolution, range and scanning strategy. The focus of the research was to combine the precipitation measurements from the two radar systems into a single radar data product, which utilises strengths and compensates for weaknesses of the individual radar system. The core of the research has thereby been to investigate the consequences of the differences of the two radar systems in order to understand the strengths and weaknesses for the best possible combination strategy. The project has resulted in developments and methods, which improve the radar based precipitation measurements from both radar systems. Moreover, a better understanding has been gained on how the radar measurement represents the precipitation at the ground and how proper comparisons are conducted. It was discovered, that the LAWR (prior the project) was performing poorly and the low performance challenged any meaningful combination. This finding was unexpected, and great effort was made in order to improve the LAWR performance. The improvements have made LAWR measurements comparable with C-band measurements, thus meaningful combination is in principle possible today. The LAWR is, however, still the Achilles’ heel of the combination. A temporal interpolation method was developed for increasing the temporal resolution of the C-band measurements, with the result of significant improvements. It is concluded that temporal interpolated C-band measurements perform significantly better than the combination of the two radar systems.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-111788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["C Band","Precipitation Measurements","Rain Gauges","Rainfall Estimates","Urban areas","Urban drainage systems","Weather Radars","X Band"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combining c and x band weather radars for improving precipitation estimates over urban areas","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-111788","ids":["aau-d48ca76a-c02c-4300-93bc-d517bf1c1d61"],"keyword":["C-Band","Precipitation Measurements","Rain Gauges","Rainfall Estimates","Urban Areas","Urban Drainage Systems","Weather Radars","X-Band"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E44A3283DC943C4055C7F5D5E2343D75"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Division of Water and Soil","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Urban Water and Environment Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering, Water and Environment Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Water and Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Water Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19017294"],"issue":"53","pages":"187","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Department of Civil Engineering, Aalborg University","series":"DCE Thesis","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d48ca76a-c02c-4300-93bc-d517bf1c1d61"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Combining C- and X-band Weather Radars for Improving Precipitation Estimates over Urban Areas","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-111788","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Attention towards the optimization of mitral valve repair methods is increasing. Patch augmentation is one strategy used to treat functional ischemic mitral regurgitation (FIMR). The study aim was to investigate the force balance changes in specific chordae tendineae emanating from the posterior papillary muscle in a FIMR-simulated valve, following posterior leaflet patch augmentation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rahmani, Azadeh","Rasmussen, Ann Qvist","Hønge, Jesper Langhoff","Ostli, Bjorn","Levine, Robert A.","Hagège, Albert","Nygaard, Hans","Nielsen, Sten Lyager","Jensen, Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-178479"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Universite Paris 5"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mitral valve mechanics following posterior leaflet patch augmentation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.icr-heart.com.ez.statsbiblioteket.dk:2048/?cid=3591","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-178479","identifier":[{"id":"84880173090","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23610985","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5626193e-8659-4ffb-b256-337085ccd5c3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-705F050DB1410E9432B52F901F15E2D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.icr-heart.com.ez.statsbiblioteket.dk:2048/?cid=3591","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"universite paris 5","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Paris 5","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Azadeh","key":"rahmanipau","last":"Rahmani","name":"Rahmani, Azadeh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann Qvist","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Ann Qvist","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Langhoff","key":"høngepau","last":"Hønge","locid":"4c24e711-2c28-4064-81ba-c1cbabe56ebf","name":"Hønge, Jesper Langhoff","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjorn","key":"ostlipau","last":"Ostli","name":"Ostli, Bjorn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert A.","key":"levinepau","last":"Levine","name":"Levine, Robert A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert","key":"hagègepau","last":"Hagège","name":"Hagège, Albert","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"4cb12a02-6ad5-448b-8ece-dccb3f5b92da","name":"Nygaard, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sten L","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d28acbea-1e2e-4dcc-8fb6-a1402771d89f","name":"Nielsen, Sten Lyager","name_org":"Nielsen, Sten L","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1d0d7d42-4da2-44a4-8c5b-081a366c8825","name":"Jensen, Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23610985"],"pub":{"issn":["09668519"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Heart Valve Disease","pages":"28-35","publisher":"ICR Publishers Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Heart Valve Disease","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880173090"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5626193e-8659-4ffb-b256-337085ccd5c3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mitral valve mechanics following posterior leaflet patch augmentation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-178479","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Introducing a simple image grading system to support the interpretation of in vivo confocal microscopy (IVCM) images in filamentous fungal keratitis. SETTING: Clinical and confocal studies took place at the Department of Ophthalmology, Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark. Histopathological analysis was performed at the Eye Pathology Institute, Department of Neuroscience and Pharmacology, University of Copenhagen, Denmark. METHODS: A recent series of consecutive patients with filamentous fungal keratitis is presented to demonstrate the results from in-house IVCM. Based upon our experience with IVCM and previously published images, we composed a grading system for interpreting IVCM images of filamentous fungal keratitis. RESULTS: A recent case series of filamentous fungal keratitis from 2011 to 2012 was examined. There were 3 male and 3 female patients. Mean age was 44.5 years (range 12-69), 6 out of 17 (35%) cultures were positive and a total of 6/7 (86%) IVCM scans were positive. Three different categories of IVCM results for the grading of diagnostic certainty were formed. CONCLUSION: IVCM is a valuable tool for diagnosing filamentous fungal keratitis. In order to improve the reliability of IVCM, we suggest implementing a simple and clinically applicable grading system for aiding the interpretation of IVCM images of filamentous fungal keratitis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Esben","Heegaard, Steffen","Prause, J U","Ivarsen, Anders","Mortensen, Klaus Leth","Hjortdal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-252943"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fungal keratitis improving diagnostics by confocal microscopy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000357558","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-252943","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3901632","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84893028431","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24474933","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d87e18c6-5bc7-46b9-86d4-514aeceeba19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-513209155DE7F3973209372EC1AA1FA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000357558","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"242d1c56-f540-479d-87ad-68df850f2587","name":"Nielsen, Esben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"7688b675-066f-4a0f-bf64-8bba69216c51","name":"Heegaard, Steffen","name_org":"Heegaard, S","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J U","key":"prausepau","last":"Prause","name":"Prause, J U","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A","key":"ivarsenpau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"072c0ad1-1c62-4539-8b63-868ff8422866","name":"Ivarsen, Anders","name_org":"Ivarsen, A","orcid":"0000-0003-1466-4804","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K L","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"ebe93177-a46f-4c14-a9bf-aa8e5e426530","name":"Mortensen, Klaus Leth","name_org":"Mortensen, K L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","name_org":"Hjortdal, J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24474933"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000357558","issn":["16632699"],"issue":"3","journal":"Case Reports in Ophthalmology","pages":"303-10","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Case Reports in Ophthalmology","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893028431"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d87e18c6-5bc7-46b9-86d4-514aeceeba19"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fungal keratitis - improving diagnostics by confocal microscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-252943","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Pearce, Christof","Seidenkrantz, Marit-Solveig","Massé, Guillaume","Kuijpers, Antoon","Olsen, Jesper","Nielsen, Ole Bjørslev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259742"],"event":{"end":"2013-05-03","place":"Blair Atholl, gb","start":"2013-04-27","title":"Integrating Ice core, Marine and Terrestrial records (INTIMATE) 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ocean circulation as driver for the younger dryas holocene transition","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-259742","ids":["au-e465c16d-ea37-450b-86e7-82ff71f6e37e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FB5C0D9F4BA0C1367660FACFA4E532B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christof","key":"pearcepau","last":"Pearce","locid":"e17d2158-c52c-4a02-b3bf-35df387b922a","name":"Pearce, Christof","orcid":"0000-0002-4866-3204","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marit-Solveig","key":"seidenkrantzpau","last":"Seidenkrantz","locid":"6a284409-8bc3-475a-b664-e3064e0c8f93","name":"Seidenkrantz, Marit-Solveig","orcid":"0000-0002-1973-5969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Guillaume","key":"massépau","last":"Massé","name":"Massé, Guillaume","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoon","key":"kuijperspau","last":"Kuijpers","name":"Kuijpers, Antoon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Bjørslev","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"038b4a82-6863-49a3-beba-14377c09d137","name":"Nielsen, Ole Bjørslev","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e465c16d-ea37-450b-86e7-82ff71f6e37e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ocean circulation as driver for the Younger Dryas – Holocene transition","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259742","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Purpose. Dynamic contrast enhanced (DCE) imaging has gained interest as an imaging modality for assessment of tumor characteristics and response to cancer treatment. However, for DCE-magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) tissue contrast enhancement may vary depending on imaging sequence and temporal resolution. The aim of this study is to compare DCE-MRI to DCE-computed tomography (DCE-CT) as the gold standard. Material and methods. Thirteen patients with advanced cervical cancer were scanned once prior to chemo-radiation and during chemo-radiation with DCE-CT and -MRI in immediate succession. A total of 22 paired DCE-CT and -MRI scans were acquired for comparison. Kinetic modeling using the extended Tofts model was applied to both image series. Furthermore the similarity of the spatial distribution was evaluated using a Γ analysis. The correlation between the two imaging techniques was evaluated using Pearson's correlation and the parameter means were compared using a Student's t-test (p <0.05). Results. A significant positive correlation between DCE-CT and -MRI was found for all kinetic parameters. The results showing the best correlation with the DCE-CT-derived parameters were obtained using a population-based input function for MRI. The median Pearson's correlations were: volume transfer constant K(trans) (r = 0.9), flux rate constant kep (r = 0.77), extracellular volume fraction ve (r = 0.58) and blood plasma volume fraction vp (r = 0.83). All quantitative parameters were found to be significantly different as estimated by DCE-CT and -MRI. The Γ analysis in normalized maps revealed that 45% of the voxels failed to find a voxel with the corresponding value allowing for an uncertainty of 3 mm in position and 3% in value (Γ3,3). By reducing the criteria, the Γ-failure rates were: Γ3,5 (37% failure), Γ3,10 (26% failure) and at Γ3,15 (19% failure). Conclusion. Good to excellent correlations but significant bias was found between DCE-CT and -MRI. Both the Pearson's correlation and the Γ analysis proved that the spatial information was similar when analyzing the two sets of DCE data using the extended Tofts model. Improvement of input function sampling is needed to improve kinetic quantification using DCE-MRI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kallehauge, Jesper Folsted","Nielsen, Thomas","Haack, Søren","Peters, David Alberg","Mohamed, Sandy","Fokdal, Lars","Lindegaard, Jacob Christian","Hansen, David Christoffer","Rasmussen, Finn","Tanderup, Kari","Pedersen, Erik Morre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263029"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voxelwise comparison of perfusion parameters estimated using dynamic contrast enhanced dce computed tomography and dce magnetic resonance imaging in locally advanced cervical cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2013.813637","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263029","identifier":[{"id":"84884578277","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24003852","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ea3fe2ff-3ffb-44be-8fcb-cef0d49f9be2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D39FB3D54D938D59B8AEC92E2FEE73D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24003852","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2013.813637","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc