6d-409d-b4e4-10a9c32f0dbb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Velocity-space tomography using many-view CTS or FIDA systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350992","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the dynamical properties of nanolasers comprising a few two-level emitters coupled to an optical cavity. A set of rate equations is derived, and is shown to agree very well with a solution of the full master equation model. Using a linearized version of these rate equations, we can analytically express the response of the nanolaser to a modulation of the pumping rate. These results are compared with the modulation response obtained directly from the master equation using a novel method. We show that contrary to conventional semiconductor lasers, the nanolaser is typically over-damped and displays a dip in the modulation bandwidth as the two-level systems become inverted. Both these features can be traced back to the use of discrete emitters that are incoherently pumped.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","Nielsen, Per Kær","Lorke, Michael","Tromborg, Bjarne","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364888"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atom lasers","Laser theory","Nanoscale devices","Quantum dot lasers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamical properties of nanolasers based on few discrete emitters","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/JQE.2013.2282464","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364888","identifier":[{"id":"84885588932","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c9e908ed-a83c-4979-9efa-9fd73d999c90"],"keyword":["Atom lasers","Laser theory","Nanoscale devices","Quantum dot lasers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE40DBA26569A4DF166C3BF317415DCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi"