{"abstract":"We revisit the question of whether cryptographic protocols can replace correlated equilibria mediators in two-player strategic games. This problem was first addressed by Dodis, Halevi and Rabin (CRYPTO 2000), who suggested replacing the mediator with a secure protocol and proved that their solution is stable in the Nash equilibrium (NE) sense, provided that the players are computationally bounded. We show that there exist two-player games for which no cryptographic protocol can implement the mediator in a sequentially rational way; that is, without introducing empty threats. This explains why all solutions so far were either sequentially unstable, or were restricted to a limited class of correlated equilibria (specifically, those that do not dominate any NE, and hence playing them does not offer a clear advantage over playing any NE). In the context of computational NE, we classify necessary and sufficient cryptographic assumptions for implementing a mediator that allows to achieve a given utility profile of a correlated equilibrium. The picture that emerges is somewhat different than the one arising in semi-honest secure two-party computation. Specifically, while in the latter case every functionality is either “complete” (i.e., implies Oblivious Transfer) or “trivial” (i.e., can be securely computed unconditionally), in the former there exist some “intermediate” utility profiles whose implementation is equivalent to the existence of one-way functions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hubacek, Pavel","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Rosen, Alon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-192973"],"event":{"acronym":"CRYPTO","end":"2013-08-22","place":"Santa Barbara, CA, us","start":"2013-08-18","title":"Advances in Cryptology – CRYPTO 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Reichman University (RUNI)"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"limits on the power of cryptographic cheap talk","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-40041-4_16","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-192973","identifier":[{"id":"84884489948","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6f7bebb8-c6e3-41dc-b39f-faa80d4a1bce"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9DD255F31B3507642124C586519319FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-40041-4_16","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007%2F978-3-642-40041-4_16","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"reichman university","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Reichman University (RUNI)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pavel","key":"hubacekpau","last":"Hubacek","locid":"d055bd78-1fa3-479e-a0fc-6cf054b12771","name":"Hubacek, Pavel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alon","key":"rosenpau","last":"Rosen","name":"Rosen, Alon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ran","key":"canettipedh","last":"Canetti","name":"Canetti, Ran","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan A.","key":"garaypedh","last":"Garay","name":"Garay, Juan A.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-40041-4_16","eisbn":["9783642400414"],"isbn":["9783642400407"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"277-297","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"33rd Annual Cryptology Conference, Santa Barbara, CA, USA, August 18-22, 2013. Proceedings, Part I","title":"Advances in Cryptology – CRYPTO 2013"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884489948"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f7bebb8-c6e3-41dc-b39f-faa80d4a1bce"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Limits on the Power of Cryptographic Cheap Talk","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192973","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We consider applications involving a number of servers in the cloud that go through a sequence of online periods where the servers communicate, separated by offline periods where the servers are idle. During the offline periods, we assume that the servers need to securely store sensitive information such as cryptographic keys. Applications like this include many cases where secure multiparty computation is outsourced to the cloud, and in particular a number of online auctions and benchmark computations with confidential inputs. We consider fully autonomous servers that switch between online and offline periods without communicating with anyone from outside the cloud, and semi-autonomous servers that need a limited kind of assistance from outside the cloud when doing the transition. We study the levels of security one can – and cannot – obtain in this model, propose light-weight protocols achieving maximal security, and report on their practical performance.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","Jakobsen, Thomas Pelle","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Pagter, Jakob Illeborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-216594"],"event":{"acronym":"IMA","end":"2013-12-19","place":"Oxford, gb","start":"2013-12-17","title":"IMA Conference on Cryptography and Coding","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cloud computing","Information security","Secure multiparty computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"secure key management in the cloud","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-45239-0_16","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-216594","identifier":[{"id":"84893376194","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9925a10c-9002-4a57-81c4-9a5507d40b43"],"keyword":["Information security","cloud computing","cloud cryptography","secure distributed storage","secure key management","secure multiparty computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F17480C4DF34C6A605D8A58EEB85E7A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-45239-0_16","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan Bjerre","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Pelle","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"03cea827-2da0-4861-92c1-4162551c38c3","name":"Jakobsen, Thomas Pelle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Illeborg","key":"pagterpau","last":"Pagter","locid":"c9a48d4d-9bb8-483a-b0c