{"abstract":"In patients with chronic functional ischemic mitral regurgitation (FIMR), papillary muscle relocation has the potential to induce reverse left ventricular remodeling. However, in order to optimize function and durability, the forces imposed on the left ventricular myocardium by papillary muscle relocation should be assessed.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Henrik","Jensen, Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup","Vind-Kezunovic, Stefan","Vestergaard, Rikke","Ringgaard, Steffen","Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","Hønge, Jesper Langhoff","Hasenkam, J. Michael","Nielsen, Sten Lyager"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-258729"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surgical relocation of the papillary muscles in functional ischemic mitral regurgitation what are the forces of the relocation stitches acting on the myocardium","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84891551255","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-258729","identifier":[{"id":"84891551255","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24224415","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e2b84db9-30ba-4b22-afd5-0df8d0f5f7e5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAB053D63135B0C26856228F5611C217"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medi