{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To fabricate microcontainers in biodegradable polylactic acid (PLLA) polymer films using hot embossing, and investigate the application of fabricated microcontainers as an oral drug delivery system for a poorly soluble drug. METHODS: For fabrication of the PLLA microcontainers, a film of PLLA was produced by spin coating. The film was heated above the polymer glass transition temperature (Tg), and a stamp was forced into the film. Following cooling of the film the stamp was removed, exposing the formed microcontainers. Microcontainers were filled with amorphous furosemide sodium salt (produced by spray drying) using a simplified version of a screen printing technique. An enteric-resistant lid of Eudragit L-100 was subsequently spray coated onto the cavity of the microcontainers. Release of amorphous furosemide salt from the coated microcontainers was investigated using a μ-Diss profiler. Release experiments were carried out in biorelevant gastric medium (pH 1.6) for 2 h, followed by 3 h in a biorelevant intestinal medium (pH 6.5). Moreover, biorelevant flow through dissolution was also carried out in conjunction with UV imaging to visualize the release of amorphous furosemide salt from the coated microcontainers. RESULTS: Fabricated PLLA microcontainers had an inner diameter of 220 μm and a height of 100 μm. The screen printing technique was shown to be an optimized set-up to fill the microcontainers with drug. From the release experiments it was observed that the Eudragit layer prevented drug release in biorelevant gastric medium, while an immediate release of the amorphous furosemide salt was seen in the biorelevant intestinal medium. The same trend was observed in the UV imaging experiments –negligible drug release was observed in gastric medium, whereas following re-equilibration of the dissolution cell with the intestinal medium, a release of furosemide was observed after 1 min with an increased release after 5 min of dissolution. CONCLUSIONS: Biodegradable microcontainers were successfully fabricated and loaded with drug. Coating with Eudragit L-100 proved to be useful for protecting drug release from microcontainers in gastric medium, and facilitated an immediate release in the intestinal medium. The fabricated microcontainers therefore show considerable future potential as oral drug delivery systems.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line Hagner","Nagstrup, Johan","Keller, Stephan Sylvest","Gordon, Sarah","Østergaard, Jesper","Rades, Thomas","Müllertz, Anette","Boisen, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365682"],"event":{"end":"2013-11-14","place":"San Antonio, us","start":"2013-11-10","title":"2013 AAPS Annual Meeting","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Saarland University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biodegradable microcontainers as an oral drug delivery system for poorly soluble drugs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/97771136/Biodegradable_microcontainers_as_an_oral_drug_delivery_system_for_poorly_soluble_drugs_2.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365682","ids":["dtu-ccad3355-217f-4ee8-b1d9-db57136ec12f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-20E7B0BEFC3DE2D2EAFF29AE0BAB36BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/97771136/Biodegradable_microcontainers_as_an_oral_drug_delivery_system_for_poorly_soluble_drugs_2.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Hagner","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Line Hagner","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"nagstruppau","last":"Nagstrup","locid":"70d9f1d3-9676-43a6-87dc-c0e6b25d8890","name":"Nagstrup, Johan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stephan Sylvest","key":"kellerpau","last":"Keller","locid":"892abdb1-3523-4896-a00d-4e3b2cd78538","name":"Keller, Stephan Sylvest","orcid":"0000-0003-4108-1305","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"gordonpau","last":"Gordon","name":"Gordon, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"radespau","last":"Rades","name":"Rades, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"müllertzpau","last":"Müllertz","name":"Müllertz, Anette","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2013 AAPS Annual Meeting"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ccad3355-217f-4ee8-b1d9-db57136ec12f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Biodegradable microcontainers as an oral drug delivery system for poorly soluble drugs.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365682","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A holistic approach to strain monitoring in fibre-reinforced polymer composites is presented using embedded fibre Bragg grating sensors. Internal strains are monitored in unidirectional E-glass/epoxy laminate beams during vacuum infusion, curing, post-curing and subsequent loading in flexure until failure. The internal process-induced strain development is investigated through use of different cure schedules and tool/part interactions. The fibre Bragg grating sensors successfully monitor resin flow front progression during infusion, and strain development during curing, representative of the different cure temperatures and tool/part interfaces used. Substantial internal process-induced strains develop in the transverse fibre direction, which should be taken into consideration when designing fibre-reinforced polymer laminates. Flexure tests indicate no significant difference in the mechanical properties of the differently cured specimens, despite the large differences in measured residual strains. This indicates that conventional flexure testing may not reveal residual strain or stress effects at small specimen scale levels. The internal stresses are seen to influence the accuracy of the fibre Bragg gratings within the loading regime. This study confirms the effectiveness of composite life cycle strain monitoring for developing consistent manufacturing processes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Michael Wenani","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Høgh, Jacob Herold","Waldbjørn, Jacob Paamand","Hattel, Jesper Henri","Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","Markussen, Christen Malte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380688"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Composite","Curing","Fibre Bragg grating sensors","Life cycle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"life cycle strain monitoring in glass fibre reinforced polymer laminates using embedded fibre bragg grating sensors from manufacturing to failure","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/52890727/Journal_of_Composite_Materials_2013_Nielsen_0021998312472221.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380688","identifier":[{"id":"84892929604","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fe4df6d3-ed24-4e1c-b94c-446e27cb0185"],"keyword":["Composite","Curing","Fibre Bragg grating sensors","Life cycle","Process-induced strains","Strain monitoring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CF65907BE9243145D8C5085913D769B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0021998312472221","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/52890727/Journal_of_Composite_Materials_2013_Nielsen_0021998312472221.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Composites Mechanics and Materials Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Wenani","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6f04228d-8fbe-4940-8fba-6b7dd9e8df6c","name":"Nielsen, Michael Wenani","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2a187e49-ed7b-44eb-a0d4-f9d00cc245ce","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Herold","key":"høghpau","last":"Høgh","locid":"56aa09df-44cd-4b50-897e-298cad97ef04","name":"Høgh, Jacob Herold","orcid":"0000-0002-5288-1255","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Paamand","key":"waldbjørnpau","last":"Waldbjørn","locid":"fc8d8dab-f1a5-4f8c-8483-6d03a507e0cb","name":"Waldbjørn, Jacob Paamand","orcid":"0000-0003-1398-4814","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"løgstrupandersenpau","last":"Løgstrup Andersen","locid":"a3b0c1b2-d918-4f62-813c-87ade730ab3e","name":"Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","orcid":"0000-0002-4998-6603","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christen Malte","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","locid":"a780ae37-79fd-4b1c-a26b-852eed6032ca","name":"Markussen, Christen Malte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0021998312472221","issn":["00219983","1530793X"],"issn_org":["00219983"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Composite Materials","pages":"365-381","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Composite Materials","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892929604"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fe4df6d3-ed24-4e1c-b94c-446e27cb0185"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Life cycle strain monitoring in glass fibre reinforced polymer laminates using embedded fibre Bragg grating sensors from manufacturing to failure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380688","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Biorelevant dissolution behaviour of the amorphous sodium salt and amorphous acid forms of furosemide was evaluated, together with investigations of the solid state changes during in vitro dissolution in medium simulating the conditions in the small intestine. UV imaging of the two amorphous forms, as well as of crystalline furosemide salt and acid showed a higher rate of dissolution of the salt forms in comparison with the two acid forms. The measured dissolution rates of the four furosemide forms from the UV imaging system and from eluted effluent samples were consistent with dissolution rates obtained from micro dissolution experiments. Partial least squares-discriminant analysis of Raman spectra of the amorphous acid form during flow through dissolution showed that the amorphous acid exhibited a fast conversion to the crystalline acid. Flow through dissolution coupled with Raman spectroscopy showed a conversion of the amorphous furosemide salt to a more stable polymorph. It was found by thermogravimetric analysis and hot stage microscopy that the salt forms of furosemide converted to a trihydrate during dissolution. It can be concluded that during biorelevant dissolution, the amorphous and crystalline furosemide salt converted to a trihydrate, whereas the amorphous acid exhibited fast conversion to the crystalline acid.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line Hagner","Gordon, Sarah","Pekka Pajander, Jari","Østergaard, Jesper","Rades, Thomas","Müllertz, Anette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-406753"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biorelevant characterisation of amorphous furosemide salt exhibits conversion to a furosemide hydrate during dissolution","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2013.08.029","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-406753","identifier":[{"id":"84884919663","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24050989","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-164f5220-b63e-4d1e-adde-b42f4b8734cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9606AE137098F367CEECDD31A0059CC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2013.08.029","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Hagner","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"611fd738-d02e-4b6e-8d46-586833db3adf","name":"Nielsen, Line Hagner","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"gordonpau","last":"Gordon","locid":"1177312d-342f-4d1b-9c8a-9a77ae9e14f4","name":"Gordon, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jari Pekka","key":"pajanderpau","last":"Pajander","locid":"f8c6d919-f9dd-4322-8ff2-99338e30828b","name":"Pekka Pajander, Jari","name_org":"Pajander, Jari Pekka","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"718ffee9-f57d-4060-9440-4ade85c29600","name":"Østergaard, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3448-4237","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"radespau","last":"Rades","locid":"e3c9db98-a0f8-4161-911f-d6ffdccbfdc6","name":"Rades, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7521-6020","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette","key":"müllertzpau","last":"Müllertz","locid":"fe5aaa8a-5f9a-4d7f-a70c-114f266db6c6","name":"Müllertz, Anette","orcid":"0000-0003-3020-8892","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24050989"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijpharm.2013.08.029","issn":["03785173","18733476"],"issn_org":["03785173"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","pages":"14-24","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","volume":"457"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884919663"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-164f5220-b63e-4d1e-adde-b42f4b8734cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Biorelevant characterisation of amorphous furosemide salt exhibits conversion to a furosemide hydrate during dissolution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406753","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
