{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Dammeyer, Jesper","Nielsen, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-542820"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Center for Døvblindhed og Høretab"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"døvblindfødte personers sproglige udvikling om muligheder og umuligheder for taktilsproglig udvikling hos personer med medfødt døvblindhed","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-542820","ids":["ku-fa4e0dc0-83eb-4b28-b25e-10adde5f0b85"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3B826257D1F14F063D6AF8B0B69B53F7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Center for Døvblindhed og Høretab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Herup","key":"dammeyerpau","last":"Dammeyer","locid":"4e00d381-dd0b-4b42-a335-652388c7f73b","name":"Dammeyer, Jesper","name_org":"Dammeyer, Jesper Herup","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anja","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"dammeyerpedh","last":"Dammeyer","name":"Dammeyer, Jesper","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anja","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anja","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788792574220"],"pages":"81-90","place":"København","publisher":"Materialecentret","status":"p","subtitle":"En antologi om forskellige sprogmodaliteters muligheder og umuligheder, undersøgt med afsæt i personer med medfødt døvblindhed","title":"Kropslig og taktil sprogudvikling"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fa4e0dc0-83eb-4b28-b25e-10adde5f0b85"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Døvblindfødte personers sproglige udvikling : om muligheder og umuligheder for taktilsproglig udvikling hos personer med medfødt døvblindhed","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542820","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of the present study is to explore the progression of type 1 diabetes (T1D) in Danish children 12 months after diagnosis using Latent Factor Modelling. We include three data blocks of dynamic paraclinical biomarkers, baseline clinical characteristics and genetic profiles of diabetes related SNPs in the analyses. This method identified a model explaining 21.6% of the total variation in the data set. The model consists of two components: (1) A pattern of declining residual β-cell function positively associated with young age, presence of diabetic ketoacidosis and long duration of disease symptoms (P = 0.0004), and with risk alleles of WFS1, CDKN2A/2B and RNLS (P = 0.006). (2) A second pattern of high ZnT8 autoantibody levels and low postprandial glucagon levels associated with risk alleles of IFIH1, TCF2, TAF5L, IL2RA and PTPN2 and protective alleles of ERBB3 gene (P = 0.0005). These results demonstrate that Latent Factor Modelling can identify associating patterns in clinical prospective data--future functional studies will be needed to clarify the relevance of these patterns.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Andersen, Marie Louise Max","Rasmussen, Morten Arendt","Pörksen, Sven","Svensson, Jannet","Vikre-Jørgensen, Jennifer","Thomsen, Jane","Hertel, Niels Thomas","Johannesen, Jesper","Pociot, Flemming","Petersen, Jacob Sten","Hansen, Lars","Mortensen, Henrik Bindesbøl","Nielsen, Lotte Brøndum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588174"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Age of Onset","Alleles","Autoantibodies","C Peptide","Cation Transport Proteins","Child","Diabetes Mellitus Type 1","Disease Progression","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin Secreting Cells","Male","Models Biological","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Prospective Studies","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complex multi block analysis identifies new immunologic and genetic disease progression patterns associated with the residual β cell function 000000000001 year after diagnosis of type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0064632","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-588174","identifier":[{"id":"84878748010","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3674006","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23755131","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-344a5579-7e65-4c75-9f76-fc2d8bc4e944"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Age of Onset","Alleles","Autoantibodies","C-Peptide","Cation Transport Proteins","Child","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1","Disease Progression","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Hemoglobin A, Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin-Secreting Cells","Male","Models, Biological","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Prospective Studies","Risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-D375434534850209C0A054709C91C2BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0064632","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Paediatrics (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise Max","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Marie Louise Max","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Arendt","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten Arendt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sven","key":"pörksenpau","last":"Pörksen","name":"Pörksen, Sven","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannet","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","name":"Svensson, Jannet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer","key":"vikrejørgensenpau","last":"Vikre-Jørgensen","name":"Vikre-Jørgensen, Jennifer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"7be933b9-8685-4e2f-90b2-5aebacecfb0f","name":"Thomsen, Jane","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Thomas","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","locid":"ee81c290-3387-439a-8450-3b2097f91ba3","name":"Hertel, Niels Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Jesper","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"pociotpau","last":"Pociot","name":"Pociot, Flemming","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Sten","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jacob Sten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bindesbøl","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Henrik Bindesbøl","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Brøndum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lotte Brøndum","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23755131"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0064632","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"6","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878748010"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-344a5579-7e65-4c75-9f76-fc2d8bc4e944"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Complex multi-block analysis identifies new immunologic and genetic disease progression patterns associated with the residual β-cell function 1 year after diagnosis of type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-588174","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Most ecological networks are analysed as static structures, where all observed species and links are present simultaneously. However, this is over-simplified, because networks are temporally dynamical. We resolved an arctic, entire-season plant-flower visitor network into a temporal series of 1-day networks and compared the properties with its static equivalent based on data pooled over the entire season. Several properties differed. The nested link pattern in the static network was blurred in the dynamical version, because the characteristic long nestedness tail of flower-visitor specialists got stunted in the dynamical networks. This tail comprised a small food web of pollinators, parasitoids and hyper-parasitoids. The dynamical network had strong time delays in the transmission of direct and indirect effects among species. Twenty percent of all indirect links were impossible in the dynamical network. Consequently, properties and thus also robustness of ecological networks cannot be deduced from the static topology alone.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Claus","Dupont, Yoko Luise","Mosbacher, Jesper B","Nielsen, Kristian Trøjelsgaard","Olesen, Jens M."],"cuid":["S02-083.26-666586"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strong impact of temporal resolution on the structure of an ecological network","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/98434314/Strong_impact_of_temporal_resolution_on_the_structure_of_an_ecological_network.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.26-666586","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3852737","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24324718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891868587","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000327949300104","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-f7e79827-002e-4fab-bbe7-e51f6e47cc53","ku-8ecaa7be-407e-4846-b592-78187ec9ba3a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-338B560D9D6C268F6B61207D97BAC283"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/98434314/Strong_impact_of_temporal_resolution_on_the_structure_of_an_ecological_network.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0081694","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Genetics, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"24ea7809-dde1-44f9-ac17-63b508b998f7","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-1529-6548","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yoko L","key":"dupontpau","last":"Dupont","locid":"2a165175-a558-448c-9b2e-8fe1150a0fac","name":"Dupont, Yoko Luise","name_org":"Dupont, Yoko L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper B.","k