{"abstract":"Very few studies have attributed a direct, active, functional role to N-linked glycans. We describe here an N-linked glycan with a unique role for maintaining the active conformation of a protein of the serpin family. The distinguishing feature of serpins is the \"stressed-to-relaxed\" transition, in which the reactive centre loop (RCL) inserts as a β-strand into the central β-sheet A. This transition forms the basis for the conversion of serpins to the inactive latent state. We demonstrate that plasminogen activator inhibitor-1 (PAI-1) from zebrafish converts to the latent state about 5-fold slower than human PAI-1. In contrast to human PAI-1, fish PAI-1 carries a single N-linked glycan at Asn185 in the gate region through which the RCL passes during latency transition. While the latency transition of human PAI-1 is unaffected by deglycosylation, deglycosylated zebrafish PAI-1 goes latent about 50-fold faster than the glycosylated zebrafish PAI-1 and about 25-fold faster than non-glycosylated human PAI-1. X-ray crystal structure analysis of glycosylated fish PAI-1 confirmed the presence of an N-linked glycan in the gate region and a lack of glycan-induced structural changes. Thus, latency transition of zebrafish PAI-1 is delayed by steric hindrance from the glycan in the gate region. Our findings reveal a previously unknown mechanism for inhibition of protein conformational changes by steric hindrance from N-linked glycans.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bager, René","Johansen, Jesper Sanderhoff","Jensen, Jan K.","Stensballe, Allan","Jendroszek, Agnieszka","Buxbom, Linette","Sørensen, Hans Peter","Andreasen, Kristian Peter"],"cuid":["S02-097.16-007049"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institut for Molekylærbiologi og Genetik - Molekylær intervention"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein conformational change delayed by steric hindrance from an n linked glycan","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmb.2013.05.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.16-007049","identifier":[{"id":"23702291","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880924777","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000323094000004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-9153f5d8-e0c1-423a-a9d0-92d61348cbe7","au-9707f343-ca21-49b0-9ea2-f70a890c0bb1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8B93D143A48CC08B96E000319CC13055"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmb.2013.05.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Intervention"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut for Molekylærbiologi og Genetik - Molekylær intervention"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, EcoDesign","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"bagerpau","last":"Bager","locid":"0f414afc-174f-4aca-ad8a-1a02c8a70ff6","name":"Bager, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sanderhoff","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"fcf1e65e-81cc-43aa-946c-3ef1a856126e","name":"Johansen, Jesper Sanderhoff","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"50b6e2ae-af89-4715-91b6-49237fee720a","name":"Jensen, Jan Kristian","name_org":"Jensen, Jan K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"stensballepau","last":"Stensballe","locid":"31ce2dbc-d5bc-4266-8c26-1b38838c7346","name":"Stensballe, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-9888-1955","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Agnieszka","key":"jendroszekpau","last":"Jendroszek","locid":"09428f6e-7994-4901-a3e1-5d059fcb3daf","name":"Jendroszek, Agnieszka","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Linette Buxbom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"913ec509-ec66-431e-bacc-75b80c04342e","name":"Nielsen, Linette Buxbom","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Linette","key":"buxbompau","last":"Buxbom","name":"Buxbom, Linette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Peter","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"bcab9ca7-425e-47e6-a4b9-154e6a126cde","name":"Sørensen, Hans Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter A","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"fa59daee-38c4-418f-a93f-b48229438570","name":"Andreasen, Peter A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23702291"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmb.2013.05.007","issn":["00222836","10898638"],"issn_org":["00222836"],"issue":"16","journal":"Journal of Molecular Biology","pages":"2867-2877","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Molecular Biology","volume":"425"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880924777"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9153f5d8-e0c1-423a-a9d0-92d61348cbe7","au-9707f343-ca21-49b0-9ea2-f70a890c0bb1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Protein Conformational Change Delayed by Steric Hindrance from an N-Linked Glycan","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.16-007049","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Risk communication is an integral part of shared decision-making in health care. In the context of interventions for chronic diseases it represents a particular challenge for all health practitioners. By using two different quantitative formats to communicate risk level and effectiveness of a cholesterol-lowering drug, we posed the research question: how does the format of risk information influence patients' decisions concerning therapy, patients' satisfaction with the communication as well as confidence in the decision. We hypothesise that patients are less prone to accept therapy when the benefits of long-term intervention are presented in terms of prolongation of life (POL) in months compared to the absolute risk reduction (ARR). We hypothesise that patients presented with POL will be more satisfied with the communication and confident in their decision, suggesting understanding of the time-related term. METHODS: In 2009 a sample of 328 general practitioners (GPs) in the Region of Southern Denmark was invited to participate in a primary care-based clinical trial among patients making real-life clinical decisions together with their GP. Interested GPs were cluster-randomised to inform patients about cardiovascular disease (CVD) risk and the effectiveness of statin therapy using either POL or ARR. The GPs attended a training session before informing their patients. Before training and after the trial period they received a questionnaire about their attitudes to risk communication and the use of numerical information. Patients' redemptions of statin prescriptions will be registered in a regional prescription database to evaluate a possible association between redemption rates and effectiveness format. The Combined Outcome Measure for Risk Communication And Treatment Decision Making Effectiveness (COMRADE) questionnaire will be used to measure patients' confidence and satisfaction with the risk communication immediately after the conversation with their GPs. DISCUSSION: This randomised clinical trial compares the impact of two effectiveness formats on real-life risk communication between patients and GPs, including affective patient outcomes and actual choices about acceptance of therapy. Though we found difficulties in recruiting GPs, according to the study protocol we have succeeded in engaging sufficient GPs for the trial, enabling us to perform the planned analyses.Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Protocol Registration System NCT01414751.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Harmsen, Charlotte Gry","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Nexøe, Jørgen","Støvring, Henrik","Gyrd-Hansen, Dorte","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Edwards, Adrian","Kristiansen, Ivar Sønbø"],"cuid":["S02-099.70-020378"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiff University","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases","Choice Behavior","Chronic Disease","Cluster Analysis","Communication","Denmark","General Practitioners","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl CoA Reductase Inhibitors","Hypercholesterolemia","Middle Aged","Patient Participation","Patient Satisfaction","Physician Patient Relations","Questionnaires","Risk Assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of effectiveness information format on patient choice of therapy and satisfaction with decisions about chronic disease medication the influence of intervention methodologies on patient choice of therapy impact cluster randomised trial in general practice","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/53407260/1472_6963_13_76.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.70-020378","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3599428","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23442351","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84874170534","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6a05a8ba-298f-44d0-8b5c-1eb827520040","sdu-d7129ad2-03d0-474c-9ed2-f82027510e38"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases","Choice Behavior","Chronic Disease","Cluster Analysis","Communication","Denmark","General Practitioners","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA Reductase Inhibitors","Hypercholesterolemia","Middle Aged","Patient Participation","Patient Satisfaction","Physician-Patient Relations","Questionnaires","Risk Assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-86BD88056E7F51AB24E9383BFE943907"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/53407260/1472_6963_13_76.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1472-6963-13-76","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice","University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Publ