{"abstract":"A closed room environment is viewed as a lossy cavity, characterized by possibly a line of sight (LOS) component and diffuse scattering parts from walls and internal obstacles. A theory used in acoustics and reverberation chambers is applied for the electromagnetics case, and main issues related to measurement systems, antennas characteristics, diffuse energy properties, and human exposure are investigated. The goal of this paper aims first towards validation of the assessment of the reverberation time in an environment using a virtual MIMO channel system. Secondly, the reverberation time in an adjacent room is investigated and hence a measurement based method is readily developed to assess the absorption cross section and the whole-body specific absorption rate of humans at 2.3 GHz in a realistic closed environment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bamba, Aliou","Joseph, Wout","Andersen, Jørgen Bach","Tanghe, Emmeric","Vermeeren, Günther","Plets, David","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Martens, Luc"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-098650"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghent University"],"keyword":["Diffuse scattering","Power density","Reverberation time","SAR","Specific absorption rate","absorption cross section","room electromagnetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental assessment of specific absorption rate using room electromagnetics","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61436249/EMC_journal_paper_Aliou_Bamba.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-098650","identifier":[{"id":"84897583843","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000310147600004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-a78b8cfb-0e38-4642-bf7a-9945e502d99f"],"keyword":["SAR","absorption cross section","diffuse scattering","power density","reverberation time","room electromagnetics","specific absorption rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A85E1D19A5B5E69C772C135F8165691A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61436249/EMC_journal_paper_Aliou_Bamba.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TEMC.2012.2189572","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"ghent university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aliou","key":"bambapau","last":"Bamba","name":"Bamba, Aliou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wout","key":"josephpau","last":"Joseph","name":"Joseph, Wout","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Bach","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"64828c54-b67d-4e86-a6c4-02321b2be1a9","name":"Andersen, Jørgen Bach","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmeric","key":"tanghepau","last":"Tanghe","name":"Tanghe, Emmeric","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Günther","key":"vermeerenpau","last":"Vermeeren","name":"Vermeeren, Günther","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"pletspau","last":"Plets","name":"Plets, David","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luc","key":"martenspau","last":"Martens","name":"Martens, Luc","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/temc.2012.2189572","issn":["00189375","1558187X"],"issn_org":["00189375"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Electromagnetic Compatibility","pages":"747-757","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Electromagnetic Compatibility","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Electromagnetic Compatibility","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897583843"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a78b8cfb-0e38-4642-bf7a-9945e502d99f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental Assessment of Specific Absorption Rate Using Room Electromagnetics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-098650","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The current paper presents statistics on the mean effective gain (MEG) for mobile handsets. The results are based on a large measurement campaign in an urban environment where the propagation channel from two different base stations to seven different handsets were measured in two bands (776 MHz and 2300 MHz). The handsets were of different types (bar, clamshell, smartphone), all had two antennas and were used in data (browsing) mode. All handsets were measured with twelve different users with both one-hand and two-hand grips. The body loss, the mean difference between the MEG in free space and with a user, was found to be up to about 15 dB with typical values below 6 dB. Further results are given in terms of mean values, standard deviations, and analyses for differences due to antenna location and user grip style. Finally, the body loss distribution is modeled and used for estimation of confidence intervals.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Yanakiev, Boyan Radkov","Bonev, Ivan Bonev","Christensen, Morten","Pedersen, Gert Frølund","Luxey, Cyril","Diallo, A.","Dioum, I"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113479"],"event":{"acronym":"EuCAP","end":"2012-03-30","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2012-03-26","title":"6th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EUCAP 2012)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Senegal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Département Génie Informatique, Ecole Supérieure Polytechnique, Université Cheikh Anta Diop de Dakar","LEAT-CNRS, University of Nice-Sophia Antipolis"],"keyword":["Body loss","MEG","Mean Effective Gain","Propagation measurements","User interaction","dual band propagation","optical link"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Molex, Antenna Business Unit"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user influence on the mean effective gain for data mode operation of mobile handsets","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/65340263/EuCAP2012_UserMEG.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113479","identifier":[{"id":"84862846250","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-da47837d-d3fc-4097-b27a-1d6be27976da"],"keyword":["Body loss","MEG","MIMO channel","Mean Effective Gain","Propagation measurements","User interaction","dual-band propagation","optical link"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7249B3792CA2BC1E346656DD9F2171B2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EuCAP.2012.6206085","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/65340263/EuCAP2012_UserMEG.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Molex, Antenna Business Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"leat cnrs university of nice sophia an