{"abstract":"A prospective cross-sectional study was designed to test if total levels of TIMP-1 in saliva and plasma correlated with the diagnosis of colorectal cancer (CRC) in a population with symptoms consistent with this disease.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Holten-Andersen, Lars","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Jensen, Siri Beier","Reibel, Jesper","Laurberg, Søren","Nauntofte, Birgitte","Brünner, Nils","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228865"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"saliva and plasma timp 000000000001 in patients with colorectal cancer a prospective study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365521.2012.711855","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228865","identifier":[{"id":"22871105","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84866616117","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ae7e4017-0fd1-4269-846e-b0696e82d5d3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-9A00FE325F9AF73D4FA923D302767D91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365521.2012.711855","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Maxillofacial Surgery and Oral Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"holtenandersenpau","last":"Holten-Andersen","name":"Holten-Andersen, Lars","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"f312d9af-1e97-49ce-9450-57ac52d3a481","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Siri Beier","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Siri Beier","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"reibelpau","last":"Reibel","locid":"455bbe13-0f0c-404b-a967-8bb3f6f40919","name":"Reibel, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"laurbergpau","last":"Laurberg","locid":"fde493d2-685c-4530-8791-614babb5ff72","name":"Laurberg, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"nauntoftepau","last":"Nauntofte","name":"Nauntofte, Birgitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"brünnerpau","last":"Brünner","name":"Brünner, Nils","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22871105"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365521.2012.711855","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00855928"],"issue":"10","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"1234-41","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology. Supplement","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866616117"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ae7e4017-0fd1-4269-846e-b0696e82d5d3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Saliva and plasma TIMP-1 in patients with colorectal cancer : a prospective study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228865","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"During spring migration, Pink-footed Geese Anser brachyrhynchus stop in mid Norway to refuel before their onward flight to the Svalbard breeding grounds. In mid Norway, geese feed on pastures, stubble as well as newly sown grain fields. The aim of the paper is to describe diurnal variations in the behaviour of geese and to examine whether these variations are driven by digestibility of food geese feed on or also by external factors such as distance to the roost, disturbance and flock size. Based on diurnal flock scans of activity budgets (observations carried out between 05h00 and 22h00 hrs) in each habitat type, we fitted a model containing all predictors we believe may influence geese behaviour. The number of feeding and alert geese on fields displayed a strong diurnal trend, which varied among habitat types, frequent and sporadic disturbance, but not flock size. On roost sites, geese also showed diurnal variation in resting and alertness. The observed diurnal variation differed from what has been found on the wintering grounds indicating that during spring, birds increase their foraging intensity in order to meet energetic and nutritional demands in a short time. Seasonal availability of habitats as well as density dependence due to a rapidly growing population size may also shape diurnal variations in goose behaviour. This study, in combination with diurnal variation in habitat choice derived from a combination of flock scanning and detailed GPS satellite telemetry, may give an input for establishing detailed energy budgets for geese at studied stopover sites.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Chudzińska, Magda Ewa","Madsen, Jesper","Nabe-Nielsen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237710"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-22","place":"Steinkjer, no","start":"2012-04-17","title":"The 14th meeting of the Goose Specialist Group","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diurnal variation in behaviour of pink footed geese anser brachyrhynchus during spring migration in trøndelag norway","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-237710","ids":["au-bdce327c-46d4-4a69-9d36-ca581e6e33e6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-325C11036D79FAD20CCC8508FCEE762E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magda Ewa","key":"chudzińskapau","last":"Chudzińska","locid":"faa4c400-68a5-4a5b-a6fd-6e0244e4bb5b","name":"Chudzińska, Magda Ewa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"d68f4bd0-2909-4a5c-b687-e62a33fb5cfb","name":"Madsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3246-0215","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"96cc4583-5bb9-464a-9718-535c82041193","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-0716-9525","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bdce327c-46d4-4a69-9d36-ca581e6e33e6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Diurnal Variation In Behaviour Of Pink-Footed Geese (Anser Brachyrhynchus) During Spring Migration In Trøndelag, Norway","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-237710","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: It has previously been reported that patients who suffer from Fuchs’ endothelial dystrophy (Fuchs’ ED) have decreased contrast sensibility threshold. The removal of endothelial guttata by Descemet’s Stripping Automated Endothelial Keratoplasty (DSAEK) surgery has also been demonstrated to decrease intraocular light scatter and improve contrast thresholds. The purpose of this study was to compare different visual qualities in patients that had undergone DSAEK surgery in one eye while having untreated Fuchs’ dystrophy in the other eye. Methods: Thirty-two eyes of 16 patients with bilateral Fuchs’ ED who had DSAEK surgery performed in one eye were enrolled. Visual acuity at 100% contrast and contrast sensitivity (CS) as evaluated by a modified simulation of the Freiburg Acuity and Contrast Test, was measured in both eyes of each patient. Results: Snellen visual acuity improved in treated eyes from 0.66 ± 0.35 (SD) before surgery to 0.38 ± 0.18 after surgery (log MAR units; p < 0.01). In eyes with untreated Fuchs’ dystrophy, visual acuity was 0.46 ± 0.14. In a pairwise comparison, there was no difference in Snellen visual acuity between treated and nontreated eyes (p = 0.12). Contrast sensitivity was significantly better in DSAEK-treated eyes compared with untreated eyes. Mean log CS in DSAEK-treated eyes was 1.06 ± 0.25 compared with a mean log CS of 0.84 ± 0.16 in untreated eyes (p < 0.01). Fourteen of 16 patients (88%) reported that vision in their DSAEK-treated eye had the best visual quality. Conclusion: In this study, using a paired design, we demonstrate improved CS in DSAEK-operated eyes when compared with the other eye that had untreated Fuchs’ ED despite the fact that no difference in visual quality was detected with standard Snellen visual acuity. Contrast sensitivity appears to be superior to normal visual acuity measurements in the evaluation of overall visual quality after DSAEK.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Esben","Hjortdal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-265927"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visual acuity and contrast sensitivity after posterior lamellar keratoplasty","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.02218.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-265927","identifier":[{"id":"21834927","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84870556766","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ef54d7c1-33cd-4be7-9006-82b6b84d57fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-773E72F513FFDFD2B48D39FA272807FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.02218.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"242d1c56-f540-479d-87ad-68df850f2587","name":"Nielsen, Esben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"b69f284e-e209-49a7-9d0d-9eeff6a8feb3","name":"Hjortdal, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21834927"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.02218.x","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"756-60","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84870556766"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ef54d7c1-33cd-4be7-9006-82b6b84d57fb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Visual acuity and contrast sensitivity after posterior lamellar keratoplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-265927","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We describe algorithms for automated quality assurance on content of audio files in context of preservation actions and access. The algorithms use cross correlation to compare the sound waves. They are used to do overlap analysis in an access scenario, where preserved radio broadcasts are used in research and annotated. They have been applied in a migration scenario, where radio broadcasts are to be migrated for long term preservation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jurik, Bolette Ammitzbøll","Nielsen, Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-270233"],"event":{"end":"2012-10-05","place":"Toronto, ca","start":"2012-10-01","title":"Preservation of Digital Objects","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"audio quality assurance an application of cross correlation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scape-project.eu/publication/audio-quality-assurance","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-270233","ids":["au-f701362f-ee95-4acd-961d-c3c4aae8a350"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-885E0F49D9454DBB0F3A0E45A6EB4406"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scape-project.eu/publication/audio-quality-assurance","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science - Center for Massive Data Algoritmics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bolette Ammitzbøll","key":"jurikpau","last":"Jurik","name":"Jurik, Bolette Ammitzbøll","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b70668c1-8833-4c48-be91-7e3552de7773","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780991799701"],"pages":"144-149","publisher":"Digital Curation Institute, University of Toronto","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Conference on Preservation of Digital Objects, iPRES"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f701362f-ee95-4acd-961d-c3c4aae8a350"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Audio Quality Assurance : An Application of Cross Correlation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-270233","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We show that the resonance fluorescence spectrum of a quantum dot excited by a strong optical pulse contains multiple peaks beyond those of the Mollow triplet. We show that as the area of the optical pulse is increased, new side peaks split off the central peak and shift in frequency. A simple analytical theory has been derived, which quantitatively accounts for the appearance and position of the peaks. This theory explains the physics responsible for the multiple peaks. By considering the time-dependent spectrum we demonstrate a time ordering of the side peaks, which is further evidence for the suggested physical explanation. © 2012 American Physical Society.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","Nielsen, Per Kær","Lorke, Michael","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328612"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resonance fluorescence from semiconductor quantum dots beyond the mollow triplet","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6453654/D4D3Ad01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328612","identifier":[{"id":"84855481971","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22304288","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-50e924c9-485a-4093-9035-bf0803eac16a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3112E4B92C419EDA43EF970788EF76B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6453654/D4D3Ad01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.108.017401","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Mølbjerg","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1bf57cde-4fad-4c3b-8fe1-c2be836414eb","name":"Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"lorkepau","last":"Lorke","locid":"3c7a6163-8340-4232-844d-6ec362ef4116","name":"Lorke, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22304288"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.108.017401","issn":["00319007","10797114"],"issn_org":["00319007"],"issue":"1","journal":"Physical Review Letters","pages":"017401","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Letters","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855481971"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-50e924c9-485a-4093-9035-bf0803eac16a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Resonance Fluorescence from Semiconductor Quantum Dots: Beyond the Mollow Triplet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.f