{"abstract":"This study presents a fully automatic, data-driven approach for texture-based quantitative analysis of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in pulmonary computed tomography (CT) images. The approach uses supervised learning where the class labels are, in contrast to previous work, based on measured lung function instead of on manually annotated regions of interest (ROIs). A quantitative measure of COPD is obtained by fusing COPD probabilities computed in ROIs within the lung fields where the individual ROI probabilities are computed using a k nearest neighbor (kNN ) classifier. The distance between two ROIs in the kNN classifier is computed as the textural dissimilarity between the ROIs, where the ROI texture is described by histograms of filter responses from a multi-scale, rotation invariant Gaussian filter bank. The method was trained on 400 images from a lung cancer screening trial and subsequently applied to classify 200 independent images from the same screening trial. The texture-based measure was significantly better at discriminating between subjects with and without COPD than were the two most common quantitative measures of COPD in the literature, which are based on density. The proposed measure achieved an area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC) of 0.713 whereas the best performing density measure achieved an AUC of 0.598. Further, the proposed measure is as reproducible as the density measures, and there were indications that it correlates better with lung function and is less influenced by inspiration level.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Lauge","Nielsen, Mads","Lo, Pechin Chien Pau","Ashraf, Haseem","Pedersen, Jesper Johannes Holst","de Bruijne, Marleen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433082"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"texture based analysis of copd a data driven approach","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.diku.dk/lauges/publications/Sorensen2012.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-433082","identifier":[{"id":"84855397195","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21859615","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4257146e-983b-44f8-a31f-2458c0926ac2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35DFA3B4C1EACC687347101D3A7726BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.diku.dk/lauges/publications/Sorensen2012.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lauge","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"330d1478-c602-4767-8d45-30063bff33ea","name":"Sørensen, Lauge","orcid":"0000-0002-1181-7150","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52f8d6fb-fd83-4d11-ad65-3e183ca401f2","name":"Nielsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-1535-068X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Pechin Chien Pau","key":"lopau","last":"Lo","locid":"db112c42-3bce-46a6-abb7-9ad4acada3da","name":"Lo, Pechin Chien Pau","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Haseem","key":"ashrafpau","last":"Ashraf","name":"Ashraf, Haseem","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Johannes Holst","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jesper Johannes Holst","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Marleen","key":"debruijnepau","last":"de Bruijne","locid":"988d3493-ffac-4b50-99ff-e91d85774b0d","name":"de Bruijne, Marleen","orcid":"0000-0002-6328-902X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21859615"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tmi.2011.2164931","issn":["02780062","1558254X"],"issn_org":["02780062"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging","pages":"70-78","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Medical Imaging","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855397195"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4257146e-983b-44f8-a31f-2458c0926ac2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Texture-based analysis of COPD : a data-driven approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433082","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Metabotropic glutamate receptor subtype 5 (mGluR5) is a potential drug target in neurological and psychiatric disorders, and subtype-selective allosteric modulators have attracted much attention as potential drug candidates. In this study, the binding sites of three novel 2-methyl-6-(phenylethynyl)pyridine (MPEP)-derived negative allosteric modulators, 2-, 3-, and 4-BisPEB, have been characterized. 2-, 3-, and 4-BisPEB are 1,3-bis(pyridinylethynyl)-benzenes and differ only by the position of the nitrogen atoms in the pyridine rings. Despite their high structural similarity, 2-BisPEB [1,3-bis(pyridin-2-ylethynyl)-benzene, nitrogen atoms in ortho positions], with an IC(50) value in the nanomolar range, is significantly more potent than the 3- and 4-pyridyl analogs. Mutational analysis, directed by a previously published mGluR5 homology model, was used to determine key residues for the ligand-receptor interactions that may explain the potency differences of 2-, 3-, and 4-BisPEB. Residues Ile651, Pro655, Tyr659, Asn747, Trp785, Phe788, Tyr792, Ser809, and Ala810 were found to have critical roles for the activity of one or more of the three BisPEBs and the reference compound MPEP. The mutagenesis data suggest that the higher potency of 2-BisPEB is due to hydrogen bonding to Ser809 because the S809A mutation made 2-BisPEB equipotent to 3- and 4-BisPEB (IC(50), 1-2.5 µM). The potency of MPEP was also greatly affected by S809A (52-fold), suggesting that a Ser809-mediated hydrogen bond is also a key interaction between MPEP and mGluR5. Potential binding modes of 2-, 3-, and 4-BisPEB obtained by molecular docking to the mGluR5 homology model provide a structural context for the reported major mutational effects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Mølck, Christina","Harpsøe, Kasper","Gloriam, David E","Clausen, Rasmus Prætorius","Madsen, Ulf","Pedersen, Lars","Jimenez, Hermogenes N","Nielsen, Søren M","Mathiesen, Jesper M.","Bräuner-Osborne, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434418"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pharmacological characterization and modeling of the binding sites of novel 000000000001 000000000003 bis pyridinylethynyl benzenes as metabotropic glutamate receptor 000000000005 selective negative allosteric modulators","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1124/mol.112.078808","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434418","identifier":[{"id":"22899869","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84867805089","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-449ca5fb-c1e1-4197-a4dc-6e3867eb64b7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D87217E1EF87B239CFF5532D3E9778F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1124/mol.112.078808","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry Research","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used"