{"abstract":"DMUs konklusioner vedr. den økologiske risikovurdering af den genmodificerede MON87708 sojabønne i Danmark Den genmodificerede MON87708-sojabønne adskiller sig fra konventionelle sojabønner ved at have indsat gener der gør planterne tolerante over for herbicidet Dicamba. Sojabønnen søges kun godkendt til import og viderebearbejdning til bl.a. dyrefoder og fødevarer, men ikke til dyrkning eller opformering. Da importen formentlig vil foregå som levende frø er en spredning og formering potentielt mulig ved import- og bearbejdningssteder. DMU vurderer at MON87708-sojabønnen som alle andre sojabønner ikke kan etableres, spredes eller krydse med andre plantearter i dyrkede arealer eller i naturen i Danmark, da de klimatiske forhold udelukker dette. En markedsføring af sojabønnen kan derfor ikke have nogen uønskede økologiske konsekvenser i Danmark. I dyrkningsområderne i Sydeuropa kan der ved uheld ske en iblanding af GM-sojabønnefrø i frø til udsæd af ikke-GM soja. En eventuel tilfældig spredning af GM-soja vurderes dog ikke at få nogen uønskede økologiske konsekvenser. DMU vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for dyre- og planteliv ved markedsføring af den genmodificerede herbicidtolerante MON87708-sojabønne til andre formål end dyrkning. Kommentarer til EFSA: DMU har ingen kommentarer til den foreliggende anmeldelse, der inkluderer import og industriel forarbejdning til foder og fødevarer, men ikke dyrkning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjellsson, Gøsta","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Damgaard, Christian","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-083.80-015727"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af genmodificeret herbicidtolerant sojabønne linje mon000000087708 i anmeldelse vedr markeds føring under forordning 000000001829 000000002003 ef era efsa gmo nl 000000002011 000000000093","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-083.80-015727","ids":["au-2ad96600-61c5-4638-9cce-0bc248de0369","au-64b14c57-32f2-42fc-80be-fcf0d0e44786"],"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-BAC047E85EE70755CB13378028F5388B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj-Britt Uhd","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8212e441-2e87-482f-ad06-184f50830cec","name":"Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2ad96600-61c5-4638-9cce-0bc248de0369","au-64b14c57-32f2-42fc-80be-fcf0d0e44786"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Økologisk risikovurdering af genmodificeret herbicidtolerant sojabønne linje MON87708 i anmeldelse vedr. markeds¬føring under Forordning 1829/2003/EF : ERA: EFSA/GMO/NL/2011/93","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.80-015727","year":2012,"yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The prevalence, prognostic importance, and factors that predict the presence and degree of pulmonary hypertension (PH) diagnosed with right heart catheterization (RHC) in patients with end-stage chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) remain unclear. METHODS: This retrospective study included 409 patients (61% women) with COPD/emphysema or α-1-antitrypsin deficiency who underwent lung transplant evaluation during 1991 to 2010. We analyzed the occurrence and degree of PH and compared demographics, oxygenation, lung function, hemodynamics, functional capacity, and survival in patients with and without PH. Prediction of PH was assessed using univariate and multivariate regression analysis. RESULTS: The mean age at evaluation was 54 ± 7 years. All patients were in New York Heart Association functional class III-IV, with forced expiratory volume in 1 second of 23% ± 7% and total lung capacity of 126% ± 21% of predicted. PH was present in 146 (36%). The analysis excluded 53 (13%) with pulmonary venous hypertension (PVH). The distribution of the mean pulmonary artery pressure (mPAP) in patients with or without PH showed a unimodal normally distributed population, with a mean of 23.8 ± 6.0 mm Hg. Predictors of PH were partial pressures of oxygen and carbon dioxide. The 5-year survival rate was 37% in COPD patients with PH vs 63% in patients without PH (p = 0.016). Survival after lung transplantation did not differ (p = 0.37). CONCLUSIONS: RHC verified PH in 36% of COPD patients. Hypoxemia and hypercapnia were associated with mPAP. PH is associated with worse survival in COPD, but PH does not influence the prognosis after lung transplantation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersen, Kasper Hasseriis","Iversen, Martin Jes","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Mortensen, Jann","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Bendstrup, Elisabeth","Videbaek, Regitze","Carlsen, Jørn"],"cuid":["S02-084.91-015677"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence predictors and survival in pulmonary hypertension related to end stage chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.healun.2011.11.020","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-084.91-015677","identifier":[{"id":"22226804","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84858335339","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2a4fb112-6d2d-402a-b713-1f286dfe569e","ku-b17dc5d5-4d3b-4a9c-bc04-90eb1223586b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3C01AEE67AF0E6AF783E57E98AADB015"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.healun.2011.11.020","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Hjertemedicinsk Afdeling B, SKS"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Diagnostic Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Hasseriis","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kasper Hasseriis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Jes","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Martin Jes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jann","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Jann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth","key":"bendstruppau","last":"Bendstrup","locid":"be043b5b-018b-48e2-8020-9cc943355a94","name":"Bendstrup, Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-4238-6963","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Regitze","key":"videbaekpau","last":"Videbaek","name":"Videbaek, Regitze","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","name":"Carlsen, Jørn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22226804"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.healun.2011.11.020","issn":["10532498","15573117"],"issn_org":["10532498"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Heart and Lung Transplantation","pages":"373-380","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Heart and Lung Transplantation","title_org":"The Journal of heart and lung transplantation : the official publication of the International Society for Heart Transplantation","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84858335339"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","hjertemedicinsk afdeling b, sks","institut for klinisk medicin - lungemedicinsk afdeling, nbg"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2a4fb112-6d2d-402a-b713-1f286dfe569e","ku-b17dc5d5-4d3b-4a9c-bc04-90eb1223586b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence, predictors, and survival in pulmonary hypertension related to end-stage chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.91-015677","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The aim of this paper is to discuss the possible benefits of involving Energy Service Companies (ESCO) in realising energy savings in municipalities, and how ESCO projects can be formulated very differently in the various municipalities, according to building volume, use of technologies, energy savings, type of collaboration etc. Background: Since 2008, several Danish municipalities have started energy retrofitting of municipal buildings, based on contracts with Energy Service Companies. In spite of the strong growth of ESCOs, there is also widespread scepticism about ESCO, as many municipalities see an in-house approach as a better alternative. Approach (Theory/Methodology): Our research is based on literature studies and on qualitative interviews with Danish municipalities carrying out ESCO projects, as well as with ESCO providers. Results: Our studies suggest that different ESCO approaches are being used in Danish municipalities, which we label the basic, the integrated and the strategic ESCO approaches. The three approaches include different ambitions, technologies, economies and innovation potentials. Whereas the basic approach implies a ‘traditional’ guarantee-based model, with relatively few buildings, energy retrofitting and low investments, the integrative and strategic approach include a higher degree of partnership, a more ambitious building renovation approach, and more innovative understandings of facilities management. We also compare ESCO with energy retrofitting as an in-house approach, which many municipalities are considering. Practical Implications: We suggest the practical implications of our findings, as a short characteristic of the different approaches, intended for municipalities to start up energy retrofitting of municipal buildings.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Ole","Hansen, Jesper Rohr","Balslev Nielsen, Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-085.71-008328"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["ESCO Energy Service Companies","Energy retrofitting","Facilities management","Innovation","municipal buildings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esco in danish municipalities basic integrative or strategic approaches","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61411560/revised_Jensen_Hansen_Balslev.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-085.71-008328","ids":["aau-ad04a44e-0207-434e-baf8-da221e8af18e","dtu-823716fd-be51-4263-bac2-9c6da2910792"],"keyword":["ESCO (Energy Service Companies)","energy retrofitting","facilities management","innovation","municipal buildings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-4207E735CF0BE320EA919510258D027C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.cfm.dtu.dk/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61411560/revised_Jensen_Hansen_Balslev.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Town, Housing and Property (THP)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Transformation of Housing and Places Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba9f81ea-c5a0-4b37-a1ef-bcf1bc98535e","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3730-0619","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rohr","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2e1430aa-5cad-4c23-9556-9575252cc7b7","name":"Hansen, Jesper Rohr","orcid":"0000-0001-9403-9296","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Balslev","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"37d6b355-4468-4f72-8256-afc593b8426e","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","orcid":"0000-0002-8269-6771","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Anker","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Per Anker","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"balslevnielsenpedh","last":"Balslev Nielsen","name":"Balslev Nielsen, Susanne","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788750210337"],"pages":"144-158","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"Polyteknisk Boghandel og Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Past, present and future","title":"Facilities management research in the Nordic countries"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ad04a44e-0207-434e-baf8-da221e8af18e","dtu-823716fd-be51-4263-bac2-9c6da2910792"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ESCO in Danish municipalities: Basic, integrative or strategic approaches?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-008328","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BIOSCIENCE konklusioner vedr. den økolo-giske risikovurdering af den genmodifice-rede MON 88302-raps i Danmark Den genmodificerede raps, MON88302, adskiller sig fra konventionel raps ved at have indsat et gen der gør planten tolerant over for herbicidet glyfosat. Rapsen søges kun godkendt til import til foder og fødevarer for human konsumtion. DCE, Bioscience anser det for sandsynligt at MON 88302-rapsen og dens gener kan blive spredt utilsigtet i forbindelse med uheld med iblanding i konventionel raps ved fx håndtering under import, lagring og transport. Spredningen forventes dog at kunne begrænses ved den generelle overvågning foreslået af anmelderen samt ved de specielle forholdsregler der gælder vedrørende sameksistens mellem GM-afgrøder og økologiske og konventionelle afgrøder (Tolstrup et al., 2007). Set over et længere tidsperspektiv er det dog sandsynligt at genet for glyfosat-tolerance bliver spredt til vilde slægtninge af raps, mest sandsynligt agerkål. DCE, Bioscience har foretaget en analyse af de forskellige mulige uøn-skede økologiske konsekvenser for plante- og dyreliv ved en eventuel tilfældig spredning af den genmodificerede raps til landbrugsarealer og naturnære områder. Konsekvenserne må vurderes at være små og begrænsede til de dyrkningsarealer, hvor der anvendes glyfosat. Her kan den glyfosat-tolerante raps have en konkurrencemæssig fordel. Da rapsen ikke skal dyrkes forventes det dog ikke at medføre påvirkninger af biodiversitet eller miljø. DCE, Bioscience vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes væsentlige uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for miljøet samt dyre- og plantelivet ved markedsføring af MON 88302-rapsen når den kun godkendes til import til foder og fødevareanvendelse. Der findes desuden metoder til at overvåge en eventuel utilsigtet spredning via frøspild under transport og/eller hybridisering med slægtninge til GM-rapsen. BIOSCIENCE kommentarer til EFSA: DCE, Bioscience concludes, that accidental dispersal, hybridisation and persistence of the MON 88302-oilseed rape is likely to take place over time. The consequences to the environment are likely to be small. Fur-thermore, there are methods to monitor such dispersal of the GMO-plant into cultivated fields and surroundings. Although, not directly an environmental issue, we find that dispersal of the MON 88302 oilseed rape could result in problems for co-existence with non-GMO-cultivation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjellsson, Gøsta","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Damgaard, Christian","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-087.22-017508"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","Økologisk risikovurdering","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af en genmo dificeret glyfosat tolerant raps mon 000000088302 i anmeldelse til godkendelse vedr import til markedsføring under forordning 000000001829 000000002003 ef efsa gmo be 000000002011 000000000101","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-087.22-017508","ids":["au-426f2baf-a884-43b4-9752-6218d078605e","au-615b653b-5d74-45f2-b8de-8a2f09ff460f"],"keyword":["Risikovurdering","gmo","Økologisk risikovurdering","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-E3F9EC7A227004531C9B1F8E01B6DCED"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, National Environmental Research Institute, Department of Terrestrial Ecology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj-Britt Uhd","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8212e441-2e87-482f-ad06-184f50830cec","name":"Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"pages":"13","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-426f2baf-a884-43b4-9752-6218d078605e","au-615b653b-5d74-45f2-b8de-8a2f09ff460f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Økologisk risikovurdering af en genmo-dificeret glyfosat-tolerant raps MON 88302 i anmeldelse til godkendelse vedr. import til markedsføring under Forordning 1829/2003/EF. : EFSA-GMO-BE-2011-101","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.22-017508","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Resuscitation guidelines for the treatment of accidental hypothermia are based primarily on isolated cases. Mortality rates are high despite aggressive treatment aimed at restoring spontaneous circulation and normothermia.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Wanscher, Michael Christopher J","Sørensen, Lisbeth Agersnap","Ravn, Jesper Bohsen","Yndgaard, Stig","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Danielsen, Else Rubæk","Hassager, Christian","Romner, Bertil Roland","Thomsen, Carsten","Barnung, Steen Krøyer","Lorentzen, Anne Grethe","Høgenhaven, Hans","Davis, Matthew","Eifer Møller, Jakob"],"cuid":["S02-092.93-021201"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcome of accidental hypothermia with or without circulatory arrest experience from the danish præstø fjord boating accident","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2012.05.009","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.93-021201","identifier":[{"id":"84865303396","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22634431","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-74b31f85-2da6-463c-a34b-146b8efd9118","ku-ae9a2f29-5fa2-45c1-b5a5-c18b7e1e0084"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EE18FD4E681F8598E745C7CF43902171"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2012.05.009","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Hammel Neurocenter"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Christopher J","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael Christopher J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Agersnap","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"546db40a-fc8c-4211-b0a3-c76c75703ec2","name":"Sørensen, Lisbeth Agersnap","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisbeth","key":"agersnappau","last":"Agersnap","name":"Agersnap, Lisbeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Bohsen","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Jesper Bohsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"yndgaardpau","last":"Yndgaard","name":"Yndgaard, Stig","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,