 Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-74b31f85-2da6-463c-a34b-146b8efd9118","ku-ae9a2f29-5fa2-45c1-b5a5-c18b7e1e0084"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Outcome of accidental hypothermia with or without circulatory arrest. Experience from the Danish Præstø Fjord boating accident","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.93-021201","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This study examined the effect of 12 weeks of small-sided street soccer (2.2 ± 0.7 sessions/week) and fitness center training (0.5 ± 0.2 sessions/week) on physical fitness and cardiovascular health profile for homeless men. Exercise capacity, maximal oxygen uptake (VO(2max)), body composition (DXA scans), blood pressure (BP), and blood lipid profile were determined before and after the intervention period for 22 soccer-group subjects (SG) and 10 waiting list controls (CO). In addition, time-motion analyses, HR measurements, and pedometer recordings were performed during street soccer training and daily-life activities. During a 60 min 4 versus 4 street soccer session 182 ± 62 intense running bouts were performed; mean HR was 82 ± 4% HR(max) and HR was >90% HR(max) for 21 ± 12% (±SD) of total time. On a day without training the participants performed 10,733 ± 4,341 steps and HR was >80% HR(max) for 2.4 ± 4.3 min. In SG, VO(2max) was elevated (p < 0.05) from 36.7 ± 7.6 to 40.6 ± 8.6 ml/min/kg after 12 weeks and incremental cycle test performance was improved (p < 0.05) by 81 s (95% CI: 47-128 s). After 12 weeks, fat percentage (19.4 ± 8.5 to 17.5 ± 8.6%) and LDL cholesterol (3.2 ± 1.1 to 2.8 ± 0.8 mmol L(-1)) were lowered (p < 0.05) in SG. The observed changes in SG were different (p < 0.05) from CO and no intra-group changes occurred for CO (p > 0.05). BP was unaltered after 12 weeks (p > 0.05), but diastolic BP was lowered for all SG subjects with pre-values >75 mmHg (83 ± 6 to 76 ± 6 mmHg, n = 8, p < 0.05). In conclusion, the exercise intensity is high during street soccer and regular street soccer training can be used as an effective activity to promote physical fitness and cardiovascular health status for homeless men.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Randers, Morten Bredsgaard","Petersen, Jesper","Andersen, Lars Juel","Krustrup, Birgitte Rejkjær","Hornstrup, Therese","Nielsen, Jens Jung","Nordentoft, Merete","Krustrup, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-095.49-043314"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Blood Pressure","Body composition","Cardiovascular Physiological Phenomena","Cholesterol LDL","Controlled Clinical Trial","Exercise","Heart Rate","Homeless Persons","Humans","Journal Article","Lipoproteins","Male","Oxygen Consumption","Physical Fitness","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Soccer","Task Performance and Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short term street soccer improves fitness and cardiovascular health status of homeless men","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00421-011-2171-1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.49-043314","identifier":[{"id":"84861532145","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21956486","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6ecb2471-8c7f-423b-b833-c55f16d4a822","sdu-690d6bc1-b9d3-40bf-ae2f-6b1c00726869"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Blood Pressure","Body Composition","Cardiovascular Physiological Phenomena","Cholesterol, LDL","Controlled Clinical Trial","Exercise","Heart Rate","Homeless Persons","Humans","Journal Article","Lipoproteins","Male","Oxygen Consumption","Physical Fitness","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Soccer","Task Performance and Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CF3E19761CB5CC5528B88CC8F9F9F40F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00421-011-2171-1","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Department of Exercise and Sport Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Bredsgaard","key":"randersmortenbredsgaardpau","last":"Randers","locid":"5f16a5dd-f231-48c6-bddd-cd4ec6b20ea4","name":"Randers, Morten Bredsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-0192-8981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"petersenjesperpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"4732e02e-975d-47f9-8146-a202f1eabb08","name":"Petersen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Juel","key":"andersenlarsjuelpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"70b128f4-6991-46fe-a52f-a8c5cb0803b8","name":"Andersen, Lars Juel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte Rejkjær","key":"krustrupbirgitterejkjærpau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"d10d8ff1-12e2-4cf0-9bf2-c5a517216358","name":"Krustrup, Birgitte Rejkjær","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte R","key":"krustrupbirgitterpau","last":"Krustrup","name":"Krustrup, Birgitte R","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Therese","key":"hornstruptheresepau","last":"Hornstrup","locid":"a44d0bc0-e622-481b-ba67-4527d7ad6519","name":"Hornstrup, Therese","orcid":"0000-0001-6937-958X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Jung","key":"nielsenjensjungpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b6501345-ec3f-49e9-87fe-e10aea74fa41","name":"Nielsen, Jens Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-7694-3425","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"nielsenjenspau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftmeretepau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"krustruppeterpau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"9b334221-94f3-4a68-a2de-ee9f419704d8","name":"Krustrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9843-7320","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21956486"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00421-011-2171-1","issn":["14396319","14396327"],"issn_org":["14396319"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Journal of Applied Physiology","pages":"2097-106","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Applied Physiology","volume":"112"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861532145"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6ecb2471-8c7f-423b-b833-c55f16d4a822","sdu-690d6bc1-b9d3-40bf-ae2f-6b1c00726869"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Short-term street soccer improves fitness and cardiovascular health status of homeless men","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.49-043314","year":"2012","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"Two houses in the same street can be built in the same year, they can look the same, and still they might provide very different support for sustainable living. This article points to the Strategic Facilities Management Organisation (SFMO) as the most important concept, to understand and manage implementation of sustainable facilities management in housing administration. The concept provides a frame for understanding the roles and relations of tenants, owners, administrators and operators. The paper is based on a Danish research project on environmentally sound building operation including literature studies, workshops, questionnaire and case studies. The article offers an analysis of the strengths and weaknesses of 3 different constellations of SFMO, reflecting 3 different types of ownership: Social housing, owner occupied/private co-ops and private rented. It is a contribution to the expanding literature on sustainable facilities management, where it fills a gap as it deals with housing and strategic FM. Intended readers are those interested in housing administration and especially the transition of existing housing into more sustainable housing. Intended readers include building owners, policy makers, building administrators and FM-providers and others interested in process management and sustainability.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","Jensen, Per Anker","Jensen, Jesper Ole"],"cuid":["S02-096.82-001300"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the strategic facilities management organisation in housing implications for sustainable facilities management","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7701876/The_strategic_facilities_management.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.82-001300","ids":["aau-1936e8af-9fb0-419c-9245-394c94d3b598","dtu-06c7a3ab-e7f2-470a-a9cc-fe68c3e8caeb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-BA79D88B2B1FDA6C2AD6DD6E3DBD7769"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7701876/The_strategic_facilities_management.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ejournals.library.gatech.edu/ijfm/index.php/ijfm/article/view/43/57","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Production and Service Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Research Group on Sustainable Cities and Housing","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Danish Building Research Institute, Town, Housing and Property (THP)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Transformation of Housing and Places Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Balslev","key":"nielsensusannebalslevpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"37d6b355-4468-4f72-8256-afc593b8426e","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Balslev","orcid":"0000-0002-8269-6771","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Anker","key":"jensenperankerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"252a00d0-cdcb-473a-a764-55074c608bdb","name":"Jensen, Per Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-6980-0506","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenjesperolepau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba9f81ea-c5a0-4b37-a1ef-bcf1bc98535e","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3730-0619","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21503303"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Facility Management","pages":"1-15","publisher":"Georgia Tech Library","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Facility Management","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1936e8af-9fb0-419c-9245-394c94d3b598","dtu-06c7a3ab-e7f2-470a-a9cc-fe68c3e8caeb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The strategic facilities management organisation in housing : Implications for sustainable facilities management","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.82-001300","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE:: Detection of coronary artery calcification (CAC) has been proposed for population screening. It remains unknown whether such a strategy would result in unnecessary concern among participants. Therefore, we set out to assess whether CAC screening affects the psychological well-being of screening participants. MATERIALS AND METHODS:: A random sample of 1825 middle-aged subjects (men and women, 50 or 60 y old) were invited for health screening. The European HeartScore was calculated, and a CAC score was measured using a cardiac computed tomography scanner. Therapeutic interventions as a result of the observations were at the discretion of the individual general practitioner. Before screening and at 6-month follow-up a depression test (Major Depression Inventory) was conducted, and the use of psychoactive medication was recorded. RESULTS:: A total of 1257 (69%) subjects agreed to participate. Because of known cardiovascular disease or diabetes mellitus, 88 persons were excluded. Of the remaining 1169, 47% were men, and one half were 50 years old. At 6-month follow-up, significant reductions were observed in the Major Depression Inventory score from 5.3 to 3.9 (P","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders Daldorph","Videbech, Poul","Gerke, Oke","Petersen, Henrik","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Sand, Niels Peter","Egstrup, Kenneth","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Mickley, Hans","Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt"],"cuid":["S02-098.72-022308"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Daldorph Nielsen, Anders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"population screening for coronary artery calcification does not increase mental distress and the use of psychoactive medication","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/RTI.0b013e31824752bd","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.72-022308","identifier":[{"id":"22336666","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860010825","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-844f4d34-7e32-4115-b913-9535a074250c","sdu-11a2f487-a034-4f65-951d-e9aa484ced68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AABB7688BA4FAAA1D209C23CAC9CA616"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/RTI.0b013e31824752bd","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of General Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Daldorph","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"41273198-772a-4897-bec1-31feee63cd48","name":"Daldorph Nielsen, Anders","name_org":"Nielsen, Anders Daldorph","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"videbehpau","last":"Videbeh","locid":"5133ad1e-4d6c-49f3-9d2d-86c4cd33870a","name":"Videbech, Poul","name_org":"Videbeh, Poul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"videbechpau","last":"Videbech","name":"Videbech, Poul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Peter Rønnow","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","locid":"167f1566-1eb7-495f-be19-63a30a43aff1","name":"Sand, Niels Peter","name_org":"Sand, Niels Peter Rønnow","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"egstruppau","last":"Egstrup","locid":"12389a61-a119-4ff8-ba31-4b0accb0bbc5","name":"Egstrup, Kenneth","orcid":"0000-0002-6214-8751","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0b7868d1-86b5-490e-bcf2-95fc4e33319f","name":"Larsen, Mogens Lytken","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"mickleypau","last":"Mickley","locid":"f6789f9a-e23b-4ab8-bd7d-a3c168107cdb","name":"Mickley, Hans","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel Cosmus Pyndt","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"d84be6bc-52bf-4710-9f66-0209cfab4f54","name":"Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-1285-4826","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22336666"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/rti.0b013e31824752bd","issn":["08835993","15360237"],"issn_org":["08835993"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Thoracic Imaging","pages":"202-206","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thoracic Imaging","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860010825"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-844f4d34-7e32-4115-b913-9535a074250c","sdu-11a2f487-a034-4f65-951d-e9aa484ced68"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Population Screening for Coronary Artery Calcification Does Not Increase Mental Distress and the Use of Psychoactive Medication","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.72-022308","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Conventional coronary artery bypass grafting performed with the use of cardiopulmonary bypass is a well-validated treatment for patients with ischemic heart disease. Off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting (OPCAB) has been suggested to reduce the number of perioperative complications, especially in elderly patients. METHODS AND RESULTS: In a multicenter, randomized trial, we assigned 900 patients >70 years of age to conventional coronary artery bypass grafting or OPCAB surgery. After 30 days, a blinded end-point committee assessed whether a combined end point of death, stroke, or myocardial infarction had occurred. At baseline and 6 months postoperatively, self-assessed quality of life was measured with the Medical Outcomes Study Short Form-36 and EuroQol-5D questionnaires. A 6-month follow-up of mortality was performed through the Danish National Registry. The proportion of patients experiencing the combined end point within 30 days was 10.2% for conventional coronary artery bypass grafting and 10.7% for OPCAB. Implied risk difference of 0.4% (with a 95% confidence interval, -3.6 to 4.4) showed nonsignificance in a standard test for equality (P=0.83) and for noninferiority with an inferiority margin of 0.5% (P=0.49). At the 6-month follow-up, mortality was 4.7% compared with 4.2% (P=0.75). Both groups showed significant improvement in self-assessed health-related quality of life. CONCLUSIONS: Both conventional coronary artery bypass grafting and OPCAB are safe procedures that improved the quality of life when performed in elderly patients. No major differences in intermediate-term outcomes were found. However, the noninferiority of OPCAB with the prespecified margin could not be confirmed. CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION: URL: http://www.clinicaltrials.gov. Unique identifier: NCT00123981.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Houlind, Kim","Kjeldsen, Bo Juul","Madsen, Susanne Nørgaard","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Holme, Susanne Juel","Nielsen, Per Hostrup","Mortensen, Poul Erik","Madsen, Susanne Nørgaard","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Modrau, Boris","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Haahr, Poul Erik","Grønlund, Jens","Ravkilde, Jan","Aarøe, Jens","Ehlers, Lars Holger"],"cuid":["S03-094.09-012037"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["for the DOORS Study Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Studienævnene på Health - Kandidatuddannelse i Biomedicinsk Teknik"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on pump versus off pump coronary artery bypass surgery in elderly patients results from the danish on pump versus off pump randomization study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.111.052571","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-094.09-012037","identifier":[{"id":"22523305","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84861334959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fcd164f9-5765-4877-ba82-8da58f2a5635","au-383cfc7e-672b-48da-8f19-fe40dedcac84","sdu-f84a9aa4-6722-409a-8ab7-8791370de819"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-5C29D6A566A7C463E39C26D6D74D4590"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.111.052571","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":