"],"journal":"Biodiversity & Ecology","pages":"375-375","status":"p","title":"Biodiversity & Ecology","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-210a583e-49ae-4969-b958-18b4c31a3653"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"NATURDATA.DK – Danish monitoring program of vegetation and chemical plant and soil data from non-forested terrestrial habitat types","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-148259","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We report observations of disappearance of Erica tetralix in wet heathland, which is unlikely to be caused by competition, as E. tetralix is dying before its place is taken up by other species. To investigate the causes, we used both old and new data. Results showed that presence of Molinia caerulea and Calluna vulgaris were substantial in the former E. tetralix dominated areas. Measurements of the C/N ratio in the morlayer were between 21 and 26 under the E. tetralix stands. As the expected C/N ratio in a healthy nutrient poor ecosystem like the E. tetralix wet heathland is around 30, this indicates that the ratio is probably decreasing and, correspondingly, the probability of nitrogen leaching from the ecosystem is increasing. The morlayer pH was extremely low—between 3.03 and 3.78. This represents a pH decline since the 1960s, where pH values generally were above 4. This supports the hypothesis that the decrease in morlayer pH is the major factor explaining the disappearance of E. tetralix and that measures to increase pH should be considered as part of","author_count":5,"contributors":["Strandberg, Morten Tune","Damgaard, Christian","Degn, Hans Jørgen","Bak, Jesper Leth","Nielsen, Knud Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-148417"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evidence for acidification driven ecosystem collapse of danish wet heathland","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13280-012-0251-z","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-148417","identifier":[{"id":"84863714047","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22351597","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3393059","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-214ceac1-da03-4170-8d66-f021d85a73c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD7194ACE3FCA6799245BFDAD3AA1A42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13280-012-0251-z","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"degnpau","last":"Degn","name":"Degn, Hans Jørgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Leth","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"72bda0b4-7b42-48eb-beb7-564a18e9a1d6","name":"Bak, Jesper Leth","orcid":"0000-0001-7610-7662","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Erik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b349ca79-38d0-4c9b-84d2-7eb4defb1240","name":"Nielsen, Knud Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22351597"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13280-012-0251-z","issn":["00447447","03010325"],"issn_org":["00447447"],"issue":"4","journal":"Ambio","pages":"393-401","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"Ambio","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863714047"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-214ceac1-da03-4170-8d66-f021d85a73c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Evidence for acidification-driven ecosystem collapse of Danish wet heathland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-148417","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We provide the first two-party protocol allowing Alice and Bob to evaluate privately even against active adversaries any completely positive, trace-preserving map , given as a quantum circuit, upon their joint quantum input state . Our protocol leaks no more to any active adversary than an ideal functionality for provided Alice and Bob have the cryptographic resources for active secure two-party classical computation. Our protocol is constructed from the protocol for the same task secure against specious adversaries presented in [4].","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dupuis, Frédéric","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Salvail, Louis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-156150"],"event":{"acronym":"CRYPTO","end":"2012-08-23","place":"Santa Barbara, us","start":"2012-08-19","title":"Annual International Cryptology Conference","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","University of Montreal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"actively secure two party evaluation of any quantum operation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-32009-5_46","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-156150","identifier":[{"id":"84865463623","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2eeb63b0-9b2e-4d93-ae0e-f0f8ff9cf287"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B095503E73235049B83AE6C1DD495B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-32009-5_46","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"eth züric