{"abstract":"AIMS: The aim of this study was to investigate in patients with stable angina the effects on costs of frontline diagnostics by exercise-stress testing (ex-test) vs. coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA). METHODS AND RESULTS: In two coronary units at Lillebaelt Hospital, Denmark, 498 patients were identified in whom either ex-test (n = 247) or CTA (n = 251) were applied as the frontline diagnostic strategy in symptomatic patients with a low-intermediate pre-test probability of coronary artery disease (CAD). During 12 months of follow-up, death, myocardial infarction and costs associated with downstream diagnostic utilization (DTU), treatment, ambulatory visits, and hospitalizations were registered. There was no difference between cohorts in demographic characteristics or the pre-test probability of significant CAD. The mean (SD) age was 56 (11) years; 52% were men; and 96% were at low-intermediate pre-test probability of CAD. All serious cardiac events (n = 3) during follow-up occurred in patients with a negative ex-test result. Mean costs per patient associated with DTU, ambulatory visits, and cardiovascular medication were significantly higher in the ex-test than in the CTA group. The mean (SD) total costs per patient at the end of thefollow-up were 14% lower in the CTA group than in the ex-test group, € 1510 (3474) vs. €1777 (3746) (P = 0.03). CONCLUSION: Diagnostic assessment of symptomatic patients with a low-intermediate probability of CAD by CTA incurred lower costs when compared with the ex-test. These findings need confirmation in future prospective trials.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene H","Olsen, Jens","Markenvard, John","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-236176"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects on costs of frontline diagnostic evaluation in patients suspected of angina coronary computed tomography angiography vs conventional ischaemia testing","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jes166","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-236176","identifier":[{"id":"22922828","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84876572732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bb1c2ff4-873e-42ff-8f64-e7c7d62f18f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-9B6BF01F6AD992A9DEF4E25F48A7FFF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jes166","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afd., Fredericia"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"b141cf98-8c32-4956-bb6e-5ab1424d59be","name":"Olsen, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"markenvardpau","last":"Markenvard","locid":"1464f2af-2504-4a8d-8b53-438b4f36f5d4","name":"Markenvard, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22922828"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/jes166","issn":["15695794","18758312"],"issn_org":["15695794"],"journal":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"813-823","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","title_org":"International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876572732"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bb1c2ff4-873e-42ff-8f64-e7c7d62f18f1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects on costs of frontline diagnostic evaluation in patients suspected of angina : coronary computed tomography angiography vs. conventional ischaemia testing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-236176","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To investigate the accuracy and potential limitations of MV image-based dynamic multileaf collimator (DMLC) tracking in a porcine model on a linear accelerator. METHODS AND MATERIALS: A thermo-expandable NiTi stent designed for kilovoltage (kV) X-ray visualization of lung lesions was inserted into the bronchia of three anaesthetized Göttingen minipigs. A four-dimensional computed tomography scan was used for planning a five-field conformal treatment with circular multileaf collimator (MLC) apertures. A 22.5 Gy single fraction treatment was delivered to the pigs. The peak-to-peak stent motion was 3 to 8 mm, with breathing periods of 1.2 to 4 s. Before treatment, X-ray images were used for image-guided setup based on the stent. During treatment delivery, continuous megavoltage (MV) portal images were acquired at 7.5 Hz. The stent was segmented in the images and used for continuous adaptation of the MLC aperture. Offline, the tracking error in beam's eye view of the treatment beam was calculated for each MV image as the difference between the MLC aperture center and the segmented stent position. The standard deviations of the systematic error Σ and the random error σ were determined and compared with the would-be errors for a nontracking treatment with pretreatment image-guided setup. RESULTS: Reliable stent segmentation was obtained for 11 of 15 fields. Segmentation failures occurred when image contrast was dominated by overlapping anatomical structures (ribs, diaphragm) rather than by the stent, which was designed for kV rather than MV X-ray visibility. For the 11 fields with reliable segmentation, Σ was 0.5 mm/0.4 mm in the two imager directions, whereas σ was 0.5 mm/1.1 mm. Without tracking, Σ and σ would have been 1.7 mm/1.4 mm and 0.8 mm/1.4 mm, respectively. CONCLUSION: For the first time, in vivo DMLC tracking has been demonstrated on a linear accelerator showing the potential for improved targeting accuracy. The study mimicked the envisioned patient workflow of future patient treatments. Clinical implementation of MV image-based tracking would require markers designed for MV visibility.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Poulsen, Per Rugaard","Carl, Jesper Hansen","Nielsen, Jane","Nielsen, Martin Skovmos","Thomsen, Jakob Borup","Jensen, Henrik Kirstein","Kjærgaard, Benedict","Rose Zepernick, Peter","Worm, Esben Schjødt","Fledelius, Walther","Cho, Byungchul","Sawant, Amit","Ruan, Dan","Keall, Paul J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240639"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"megavoltage image based dynamic multileaf collimator tracking of a niti stent in porcine lungs on a linear accelerator","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijrobp.2011.03.023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240639","identifier":[{"id":"21605944","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84855841957","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3162131","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-c31c88aa-a4b0-4ee2-afee-95f78500016d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-154478059497BC7C26951FF48EC9180E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijrobp.2011.03.023","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per R","key":"poulsenperrugaardpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"e01c4971-0cef-4306-93d2-f6938cb8034a","name":"Poulsen, Per Rugaard","name_org":"Poulsen, Per R","orcid":"0000-0001-9940-7609","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"carljesperhansenpau","last":"Carl","locid":"39f05ca5-35f7-4251-ad47-442a087b2400","name":"Carl, Jesper Hansen","name_org":"Carl, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"nielsenjanepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dd468c6d-cd86-4689-8819-21424503294e","name":"Nielsen, Jane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin S","key":"nielsenmartinskovmospau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7535e4aa-ccdc-4002-a13b-77b05b923fbf","name":"Nielsen, Martin Skovmos","name_org":"Nielsen, Martin S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"thomsenjakobboruppau","last":"Borup Thomsen","locid":"53892cdc-f69c-4973-9d83-971bea1b0cd2","name":"Thomsen, Jakob Borup","name_org":"Borup Thomsen, Jakob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik K","key":"jensenhenrikkirsteinpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a407eb46-2de1-4c21-96c1-ceb1f1050129","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kirstein","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedict","key":"kjærgaardbenedictpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"d635f93e-c34a-4726-8250-82a4f90d414e","name":"Kjærgaard, Benedict","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"rosezepernickpeterpau","last":"Rose Zepernick","locid":"3cde3930-da32-42d1-9a77-876b1c262bf7","name":"Rose Zepernick, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"wormesbenschjødtpau","last":"Worm","locid":"b6d17f89-28c5-43c7-9f44-8677747317f7","name":"Worm, Esben Schjødt","name_org":"Worm, Esben","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Walther","key":"fledeliuswaltherpau","last":"Fledelius","locid":"bd1897aa-dd36-4152-a228-b6450606ac4e","name":"Fledelius, Walther","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Byungchul","key":"chobyungchulpau","last":"Cho","name":"Cho, Byungchul","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Amit","key":"sawantamitpau","last":"Sawant","name":"Sawant, Amit","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"ruandanpau","last":"Ruan","name":"Ruan, Dan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul J","key":"keallpauljpau","last":"Keall","name":"Keall, Paul J","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21605944"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijrobp.2011.03.023","issn":["03603016","1879355X"],"issn_org":["03603016"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal of Radiation Oncology, Biology, Physics","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Radiation Oncology, Biology, Physics","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855841957"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c31c88aa-a4b0-4ee2-afee-95f78500016d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Megavoltage Image-Based Dynamic Multileaf Collimator Tracking of a NiTi Stent in Porcine Lungs on a Linear Accelerator","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240639","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"It is well-known that decoherence deteriorates the efficiency of cavity QED systems containing quantum dots (QDs), and that a major contribution stems from the coupling between the electrical carriers in the QD and acoustic phonons [1]. Employing a recently published model [2], we demonstrate how a proper matching between the electronic wavefuntion and the phonon-induced energy shift of valence and conduction band may be exploited to change the decoherence and decay properties of the QD by suppressing the phonon-induced processes. This effect may be addressed in a photoluminescence experiment, where a CW laser excites a two-level QD which interacts with a non-Markovian reservoir of acoustical phonons, see Fig. 1a. We assume a simple harmonic confinement of the electronic carriers, resulting in Gaussian wavefunctions, (r) / exp[−r2/(2W2 )], withWe (Wg) being the width of the electron (hole) wavefunction. In Fig. 1b we plot the stationary QD population vs. the laser frequency. We observe that for non-equal electron and hole wavefunction, the phonon-induced effect on the population surprisingly is fully suppressed at specific detunings. In a coupled QD–cavity system [2, 3], see Fig. 2a, this effect causes the QD lifetime to be unaffected by phonon processes at specific QD-cavity detunings. Furthermore, as shown in Fig. 2b, a proper choice of the QD wavefunction minimizes the phonon-induced pure dephasing rate, both in terms of the short-time magnitude and the long-time constant value. Furthermore we show, that even for realistic QDs, where We and Wg are determined by the QD shape and material composition, a significant suppression of phonon-induced processes is possible. Thus, more efficient quantum systems may be obtained if the QD wavefunctions are properly matched with the phononic properties of the surroundings.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nysteen, Anders","Nielsen, Per Kær","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350516"],"event":{"end":"2012-09-27","place":"Stuttgart, de","start":"2012-09-23","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors (NOEKS)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"suppressing electron phonon interactions in semiconductor quantum dot systems by engineering the electronic wavefunctions","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.uni-stuttgart.de/noeks11/NOEKS11_booklet_web_optimiert.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350516","ids":["dtu-9a2a5759-341a-4e91-9723-32db3c7aadb1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-437BFBADE969813347875D33420AE20D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.uni-stuttgart.de/noeks11/NOEKS11_booklet_web_optimiert.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nysteenpau","last":"Nysteen","locid":"feb12213-6336-4444-bc91-486323195b3a","name":"Nysteen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"64","status":"p","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9a2a5759-341a-4e91-9723-32db3c7aadb1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Suppressing electron-phonon interactions in semiconductor quantum dot systems by engineering the electronic wavefunctions","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350516","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Pedersen, Michael Jønch","Lønberg Holm, Thomas","Pram Nielsen, Jesper","Skovby, Tommy","Mealy, Michael J.","Dam-Johansen, Kim","Kiil, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373583"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fuldskala kontinuert farmaceutisk produktion i minireaktorer","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://techmedia.swiflet.com/tm/dak/54/1/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373583","ids":["dtu-e6d696c6-cc12-406f-beb2-df90df7f3801"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A7F25E5C72524D15FE3707A7FCE7788A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://techmedia.swiflet.com/tm/dak/54/1/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["H. Lundbeck A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Jønch","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7652e811-ca29-4b18-b7a7-d4e8daa62f61","name":"Pedersen, Michael Jønch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"lønbergholmpau","last":"Lønberg Holm","name":"Lønberg Holm, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"pramnielsenpau","last":"Pram Nielsen","name":"Pram Nielsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tommy","key":"skovbypau","last":"Skovby","name":"Skovby, Tommy","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael J.","key":"mealypau","last":"Mealy","name":"Mealy, Michael J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"damjohansenpau","last":"Dam-Johansen","locid":"ca095f0d-81ca-4127-b341-7d3578a38976","name":"Dam-Johansen, Kim","orcid":"0000-0003-1658-6176","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"kiilpau","last":"Kiil","locid":"080ff861-7fa8-4b37-a0a7-ee3a7cacb037","name":"Kiil, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-9013-6870","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00116335"],"issue":"6/7","journal":"Dansk Kemi","pages":"8-10","publisher":"TechMedia AS","publisher_org":"TechMedia A/S","status":"p","title":"Dansk Kemi","volume":"93"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e6d696c6-cc12-406f-beb2-df90df7f3801"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fuldskala kontinuert farmaceutisk produktion i minireaktorer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373583","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"There is much research on technical aspects related to sensor and mapping techniques, which enable so-called intelligent cultivators to target the intra-row spaces within crop rows. This study investigates (i) an expected advantage of an intelligent rotor tine cultivator (the cycloid hoe) in terms of crop-weed selectivity and (ii) an expected synergistic effect between punch planting and post-emergence weed harrowing, in terms of improved crop-weed selectivity. Selectivity is defined as the relationship between weed density decline and associated crop density decline 1 week after cultivation. Punch planting is a sowing technique where holes are created in the ground with a minimum of soil disturbance, and seeds are inserted into them, without soil disturbance outside the holes. Two experiments were carried out with the cycloid hoe in organic sugar beet. The rotation tines were guided by RTK-GPS relative to geo-referenced sugar beets. Tines were moved into the row when there was enough space between crop plants to cultivate and kept outside when they were predicted to strike a crop plant. The selectivity of the cycloid hoe was tested against two machine variants without intelligent guidance: the rotor tine cultivator in a locked mode, where tines rotate within the crop row without taking crop plants into consideration, and an ordinary flex tine weed harrow. The experiments showed no differences between the three machine variants in terms of selectivity. Five experiments with punch planting in sugar beet and carrot crops showed no synergistic effects between plant establishment procedures and selectivity of post-emergence weed harrowing. Even if punch planting and automated intelligent rotor tine cultivation were not combined, the results indicated that there was no reason to believe that a combination contributes significantly in mechanical intra-row weed control in direct sown crops to the solution of the main problem of low selectivity, which still remains a major challenge. Future studies on precision intra-row cultivation should focus on cutting implements, instead of tine implements that mainly work through soil burial.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper","Griepentrog, Hans W.","Nielsen, Jon","Henriksen, Christian Bugge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443109"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automated intelligent rotor tine cultivation and punch planting to improve the selectivity of mechanical intra row weed control","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-3180.2012.00922.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-443109","identifier":[{"id":"84863500896","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5334570a-a0ab-43b9-adef-42a938519f62"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-53993E1FD70DBB2750013C51AB907367"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-3180.2012.00922.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Agriculture & Ecology, Department of Agriculture & Ecology, Crop Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6e727782-369c-42e4-aebe-9dad2410956c","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-7496-983X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans W.","key":"griepentrogpau","last":"Griepentrog","locid":"49fc5154-120f-4423-baf0-b5742ded2058","name":"Griepentrog, Hans W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d45561f-3e81-41e1-8310-03bdb7abbad0","name":"Nielsen, Jon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Bugge","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"bd67e28c-5466-439a-a716-946fb14e8816","name":"Henriksen, Christian Bugge","orcid":"0000-0003-2890-4522","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1365-3180.2012.00922.x","issn":["00431737","13653180"],"issn_org":["00431737"],"issue":"4","journal":"Weed Research","pages":"327-337","status":"p","title":"Weed Research","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863500896"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5334570a-a0ab-43b9-adef-42a938519f62"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automated intelligent rotor tine cultivation and punch planting to improve the selectivity of mechanical intra-row weed control","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443109","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452940"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"encyclopedia of the bible and its reception vol 000000000003 000000000004","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djb","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-452940","ids":["ku-63794a26-b94a-4c2c-868f-6e3fb60a660f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5DE481F0B0A87B30C004BFC441A03AC5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01053191","19023898"],"issn_org":["01053191"],"issue":"3","journal":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","pages":"231-233","status":"p","title":"Dansk Teologisk Tidsskrift","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63794a26-b94a-4c2c-868f-6e3fb60a660f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Encyclopedia of the Bible and Its Reception. (Vol. 3-4)","type":"Journal Book Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452940","year":"2