t":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik Kjaerulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte","key":"bannerpau","last":"Banner","locid":"9d2aead6-d3bf-46f7-b967-ef864b0748ec","name":"Banner, Jytte","orcid":"0000-0002-7559-1285","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22882672"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1540-8167.2012.02371.x","issn":["10453873","15408167"],"issn_org":["10453873"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","pages":"1092-8","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867742485"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e6af5bf0-0a17-4a3b-a62e-a4cc80e46d45","ku-8fca984f-5e15-41a3-a662-032186ebb13a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The prevalence of mutations in KCNQ1, KCNH2, and SCN5A in an unselected national cohort of young sudden unexplained death cases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.30-029386","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The purpose of this study is to compare two sampling methods--dermal Open-Flow Microperfusion (dOFM) and dermal Microdialysis (dMD) in an international joint experiment in a single-laboratory setting. We used human ex-vivo skin and sampled topically administered Fentanyl and Benzoic Acid. The second purpose was to provide guidance to researchers in choosing the most efficient method for a given penetrant and give suggestions concerning critical choices for successful dermal sampling. METHODS: The dOFM and dMD techniques are compared in equal set-ups using three probe-types (one dOFM probe and two dMD probe-types) in donor skin (n = 9)--27 probes of each type sampling each penetrant in solutions applied in penetrationchambers glued to the skin surface over a time range of 20 h. RESULTS: Pharmacokinetic results demonstrated concordance between dOFM and dMD sampling technique under the given experimental conditions. The methods each had advantages and limitations in technical, practical and hands-on comparisons. CONCLUSION: When planning a study of cutaneous penetration the advantages and limitations of each probe-type have to be considered in relation to the scientific question posed, the physico-chemical characteristics of the substance of interest, the choice of experimental setting e.g. ex vivo/in vivo and the analytical skills available.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Holmgaard, R","Benfeldt, Eva","Nielsen, J B","Gatschelhofer, C","Sorensen, J A","Höfferer, C","Bodenlenz, M","Pieber, T R","Sinner, F"],"cuid":["S02-094.31-044654"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Administration Topical","Analgesics Opioid","Benzoic acid","Dermis","Equipment Design","Female","Fentanyl","Humans","Microdialysis","Perfusion","Skin Absorption"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of open flow microperfusion and microdialysis methodologies when sampling topically applied fentanyl and benzoic acid in human dermis ex vivo","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11095-012-0705-9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.31-044654","identifier":[{"id":"85027951692","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22419258","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-995fcf65-4c41-4cdd-bc4a-5a76c5e9ca82","sdu-24cd36a3-07d3-4ebf-a994-c182f47ac2a3"],"keyword":["Administration, Topical","Analgesics, Opioid","Benzoic Acid","Dermis","Equipment Design","Female","Fentanyl","Humans","Microdialysis","Perfusion","Skin Absorption"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-568ACF15C841AE732B45E53E89D316D3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11095-012-0705-9","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2012","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R","key":"holmgaardpau","last":"Holmgaard","locid":"7d4c8fb0-ed6b-42f4-913c-dde65ee144d1","name":"Holmgaard, Rikke","name_org":"Holmgaard, R","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"E","key":"benfeldtpau","last":"Benfeldt","locid":"7c7d625b-398b-4c53-9762-02669d007af8","name":"Benfeldt, Eva","name_org":"Benfeldt, E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, J B","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C","key":"gatschelhoferpau","last":"Gatschelhofer","name":"Gatschelhofer, C","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J A","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","name_org":"Sorensen, J A","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C","key":"höffererpau","last":"Höfferer","name":"Höfferer, C","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"bodenlenzpau","last":"Bodenlenz","name":"Bodenlenz, M","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T R","key":"pieberpau","last":"Pieber","name":"Pieber, T R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"F","key":"sinnerpau","last":"Sinner","name":"Sinner, F","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22419258"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11095-012-0705-9","issn":["07248741","1573904X"],"issn_org":["07248741"],"issue":"7","journal":"Pharmaceutical Research","pages":"1808-20","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Pharmaceutical Research","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027951692"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-995fcf65-4c41-4cdd-bc4a-5a76c5e9ca82","sdu-24cd36a3-07d3-4ebf-a994-c182f47ac2a3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of open-flow microperfusion and microdialysis methodologies when sampling topically applied fentanyl and benzoic Acid in human dermis ex vivo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.31-044654","year":"2012","yearsub":2013}
{"abstract":"BIOSCIENCE konklusioner vedr. den økolo-giske risikovurdering af den genmodifice-rede GT73-raps i Danmark Den genmodificerede raps, GT73, adskiller sig fra konventionel raps ved at have indsat gener der gør planten tolerant over for herbicidet glyfosat. Rapsen søges kun godkendt til import til foder og fødevarer for human konsumtion. DCE, Bioscience anser det for sandsynligt at GT73-rapsen og dens gener kan blive spredt utilsigtet i forbindelse med uheld med iblanding i konventionel raps ved fx håndtering under import, lagring og transport. Spredningen forventes dog at kunne begrænses ved den generelle overvågning foreslået af anmelderen samt ved de specielle forholdsregler der gælder vedrørende sameksistens mellem GM-afgrøder og økologiske og konventionelle afgrøder (Tolstrup et al., 2007). Set over et længere tidsperspektiv er det sandsynligt at genet for glyfosat-tolerance bliver spredt til vilde slægtninge af raps, mest sandsynligt agerkål. DCE, Bioscience har foretaget en analyse af de forskellige mulige uøn-skede økologiske konsekvenser for plante- og dyreliv ved en eventuel tilfældig spredning af den genmodificerede raps til landbrugsarealer og naturnære områder. Konsekvenserne må vurderes at være små og begrænsede til de dyrkningsarealer, hvor der anvendes glyfosat. Her kan den glyfosat-tolerante raps have en konkurrencemæssig fordel. Da rapsen ikke skal dyrkes forventes det dog ikke at medføre påvirkninger af biodiversitet eller miljø. DCE, Bioscience vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes væsentlige uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for miljøet samt dyre- og plantelivet ved markedsføring af GT73-rapsen til import til foder og fødevareanvendelse. Der findes desuden metoder til at overvåge en eventuel utilsigtet spredning via frøspild under transport og/eller hybridisering med slægtninge til GM-rapsen. BIOSCIENCE kommentarer til EFSA: DCE, Bioscience find, that accidental dispersal, hybridisation and persistence of the GT73-oilseed rape is likely to take place over time. The consequences to the environment are likely to be small. Furthermore, there are methods to monitor such dispersal of the GMO-plant into cultivated fields and surroundings. Although, not directly an environmental issue, dispersal of the GT73 could result in problems for co-existence with non-GMO-cultivation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Damgaard, Christian","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Kjellsson, Gøsta","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-094.79-012565"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af en genmodificeret glyfosat tolerant raps gt000000000073 i anmeldelse til godkendelse vedr import til markedsføring under forordning 000000001829 000000002003 ef efsa gmo nl 000000002010 000000000087","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-094.79-012565","ids":["au-00122dc1-3236-440e-bd8a-c29a2158d5ec","au-80786c4b-b8f7-4147-aa67-de287a0a16ce"],"keyword":["Risikovurdering","gmo","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-A7504FF5FA14981927CD9371A5482593"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj-Britt Uhd","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8212e441-2e87-482f-ad06-184f50830cec","name":"Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-00122dc1-3236-440e-bd8a-c29a2158d5ec","au-80786c4b-b8f7-4147-aa67-de287a0a16ce"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Økologisk risikovurdering af en genmodificeret glyfosat-tolerant raps GT73 i anmeldelse til godkendelse vedr. import til markedsføring under Forordning 1829/2003/EF. : EFSA-GMO-NL-2010-87","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.79-012565","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Antimicrobial peptides are a new class of antibiotics that are promising for pharmaceutical applications because they have retained efficacy throughout evolution. One class of antimicrobial peptides are the defensins, which have been found in different species. Here we describe a new fungal defensin, eurocin. Eurocin acts against a range of Gram-positive human pathogens but not against Gram-negative bacteria. Eurocin consists of 42 amino acids, forming a cysteine-stabilized α/β-fold. The thermal denaturation data point shows the disulfide bridges being responsible for the stability of the fold. Eurocin does not form pores in cell membranes at physiologically relevant concentrations; it does, however, lead to limited leakage of a fluorophore from small unilamellar vesicles. Eurocin interacts with detergent micelles, and it inhibits the synthesis of cell walls by binding equimolarly to the cell wall precursor lipid II.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Øemig, Jesper Skøttegaard","Lynggaard, Carina","Knudsen, Daniel Højberg","Hansen, Frederik Teilfeldt","Nørgaard, Kent Dahm","Schneider, Tanja","Vad, Brian Stougaard","Sandvang, Dorthe","Nielsen, Line A.","Neve, Søren","Kristensen, Hans-Henrik","Sahl, Hans-Georg","Otzen, Daniel","Wimmer, Reinhard"],"cuid":["S02-097.10-008093"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eurocin a new fungal defensin structure lipid binding and its mode of action","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M112.382028","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.10-008093","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3516779","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84871338911","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23093408","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000312103000071","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC3516779","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-a74a97ca-fbd8-4392-87a7-a6f77d66d463","au-da7844f6-523d-4a53-9402-505cd66c521a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D691F4E6F28742972A1C1B9150D0692B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M112.382028","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","use