s-Georg","key":"sahlpau","last":"Sahl","name":"Sahl, Hans-Georg","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","locid":"0ec06c22-1f74-4dd2-a894-af30b6565766","name":"Otzen, Daniel E","name_org":"Otzen, Daniel","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Reinhard","key":"wimmerpau","last":"Wimmer","locid":"1d80e9f3-a391-40e6-a73a-84194aecbb6a","name":"Wimmer, Reinhard","orcid":"0000-0001-6942-5056","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23093408","PMC3516779"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m112.382028","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"50","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"42361-42372","publisher":"American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871338911"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a74a97ca-fbd8-4392-87a7-a6f77d66d463","au-da7844f6-523d-4a53-9402-505cd66c521a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Eurocin, a New Fungal Defensin : Structure, lipid binding and its mode of action","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.10-008093","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The aim of the present randomized clinical study was to evaluate histologically whether the addition of cultivated, autogenous bone cells to a composite graft of deproteinized bovine bone mineral (DBBM) and autogenous bone (AB) for sinus floor augmentation (SFA) enhance bone formation compared with what achieved after SFA with DBBM + AB alone. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Twenty patients with remaining posterior maxillary alveolar crest height of less than 3 mm received SFA after randomization either with an DBBM and AB composite in a 1 : 1 ratio or with DBBM + AB supplemented with autogenous bone cells, which were cultivated from a bone biopsy harvested earlier from the tuberosity area. Four months after SFA, two cylindrical biopsies were taken from the augmented sinuses concomitantly with the implant site preparation by means of a trephine bur. An additional biopsy was taken from the tuberosity area. Bone density at the augmented sinus and the tuberosity area and the height of augmentation were estimated on non-decalcified histological sections prepared from the biopsies. A relative bone density index (RBD) was also calculated by dividing bone density at the augmented sinus with bone density at the tuberosity area. RESULTS: All patients but one could receive two implants after SFA; in one patient, only one implant could be placed. All implants were osseointegrated and could be loaded. Median bone density in the sinus was 30% and 25% in the cell seeded and no-cells added DBBM + AB groups, respectively. Bone augmentation height averaged 6.0 and 5.4 mm and RBD averaged 0.48 and 0.73 in the cell seeded and no-cells added DBBM + AB groups, respectively. None of the differences between groups was statistically significant. CONCLUSIONS: Cultivated autogenous bone cell seeded to a DBBM + AB composite did not significantly improve bone formation (density and height) after SFA, compared with what was achieved with DBBM + AB alone. Both approaches resulted into enough bone to support implant placement and osseointegration.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hermund, Niels Ulrich","Stavropoulos, Andreas","Donatsky, Ole","Nielsen, Henrik","Clausen, Christian","Reibel, Jesper","Pakkenberg, Bente","Holmstrup, Palle"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reimplantation of cultivated human bone cells from the posterior maxilla for sinus floor augmentation histological results from a randomized controlled clinical trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0501.2011.02251.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-029031","identifier":[{"id":"22092973","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84865278990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e1ab376b-1f6b-4eaf-9a03-118c797eb85f","ku-4525f973-c793-4069-a8e1-a14c5cf173b1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CFE2F1B3A8032911642ED08FF6E0D6D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0501.2011.02251.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Periodontology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 02 - Paediatric Dentistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"N.U.","key":"hermundpau","last":"Hermund","name":"Hermund, N.U.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"stavropoulospau","last":"Stavropoulos","locid":"e06a80ba-43fc-4f6d-acc5-ef8b7bf18138","name":"Stavropoulos, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"O","key":"donatskypau","last":"Donatsky","name":"Donatsky, O","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"reibelpau","last":"Reibel","locid":"c72c1380-d82c-43d5-8d78-73c435cf2158","name":"Reibel, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-5644-7707","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"pakkenbergpau","last":"Pakkenberg","name":"Pakkenberg, Bente","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Palle","key":"holmstruppau","last":"Holmstrup","name":"Holmstrup, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-1563-1089","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22092973"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1600-0501.2011.02251.x","issn":["09057161","16000501"],"issn_org":["09057161"],"issue":"9","journal":"Clinical Oral Implants Research","pages":"1031-1037","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Clinical Oral Implants Research","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865278990"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e1ab376b-1f6b-4eaf-9a03-118c797eb85f","ku-4525f973-c793-4069-a8e1-a14c5cf173b1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reimplantation of cultivated human bone cells from the posterior maxilla for sinus floor augmentation : Histological results from a randomized controlled clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-029031","year":"2012","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"Testicular germ cell tumours (TGCTs) of young adult men, seminoma (SE) and nonseminoma (NS), develop from a precursor cell, carcinoma in situ (CIS), which resembles foetal gonocytes and retains embryonic pluripotency. We used microarrays to analyse microRNA (miRNA) expression in 12 human testis samples with CIS cells and compared it to the miRNA expression profiles of normal adult testis, testis with Sertoli-cell-only (SCO) that lack germ cells, testis tumours (SE and embryonal carcinoma (EC), an undifferentiated component of NS) and foetal male and female gonads. Principal component analysis revealed distinct miRNA expression profiles characteristic for each of the different tissue types. We identified several miRNAs that were unique to testis with CIS cells, foetal gonads, and testis tumours. These included miRNAs from the hsa-miR-371~373 and -302~367 clusters that have previously been reported in germ cell tumours and three miRNAs (hsa-miR-96, -141 and -200c) that were also expressed in human epididymis. We found several miRNAs that were upregulated in testis tumours: hsa-miR-9, -105 and the hsa-miR-182~183~96 cluster were highly expressed in SE, while the hsa-miR-515~526 cluster was high in EC. We conclude that miRNA expression profile changes during testis development and that the miRNA profile of adult testis with CIS cells shares characteristic similarities with the expression in foetal gonocytes.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Novotny, Guy Waine","Belling, Kirstine Christensen","Bramsen, Jesper Bertram","Nielsen, John E","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Almstrup, Kristian","Sonne, Si Brask","Kjems, Jørgen","Rajpert-De Meyts, Ewa","Leffers, Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-097.39-013370"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microrna expression profiling of carcinoma em in situ em cells of the testis","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/ERC-11-0271","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.39-013370","identifier":[{"id":"84862671863","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22420006","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0a9fd2a7-f79c-4946-9aa0-68b076e17c8b","dtu-98dd72da-3ec1-4a2f-acb7-ebcf22bb24a5","ku-63885071-56d6-4415-92e7-b5aeee1505ba"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1A07E72F8739C66C429107455F3465D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/ERC-11-0271","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denm