{"abstract":"We address the problem of creating a dictionary with the finger search property in the strict implicit model, where no information is stored between operations, except the array of elements. We show that for any implicit dictionary supporting finger searches in q(t) = Ω(logt) time, the time to move the finger to another element is Ω(q− 1(logn)), where t is the rank distance between the query element and the finger. We present an optimal implicit static structure matching this lower bound. We furthermore present a near optimal implicit dynamic structure supporting search, change-finger, insert, and delete in times $\\mathcal{O}(q(t))$, $\\mathcal{O}(q^{-1}(\\log n)\\log n)$, $\\mathcal{O}(\\log n)$, and $\\mathcal{O}(\\log n)$, respectively, for any q(t) = Ω(logt). Finally we show that the search operation must take Ω(logn) time for the special case where the finger is always changed to the element returned by the last query","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brodal, Gerth Stølting","Nielsen, Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","Truelsen, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-264486"],"event":{"acronym":"ISAAC","end":"2012-12-21","place":"Taipei, tw","start":"2012-12-19","title":"International Symposium Algorithms and Computation","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"finger search in the implicit model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35261-4_55","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-264486","identifier":[{"id":"84871561876","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ecccbdf2-4d27-435d-8212-18381f6dfde7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F731770510EE1D99AC9E022E6746048"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35261-4_55","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science - Center for Massive Data Algoritmics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gerth Stølting","key":"brodalpau","last":"Brodal","locid":"49025d08-41c9-48eb-aed4-80979f26e0b1","name":"Brodal, Gerth Stølting","orcid":"0000-0001-9054-915X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b70668c1-8833-4c48-be91-7e3552de7773","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Asbjørn Sindahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"truelsenpau","last":"Truelsen","locid":"6d60baea-4289-4193-ba81-f5e804b74354","name":"Truelsen, Jakob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-35261-4_55","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"527-536","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7676"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871561876"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ecccbdf2-4d27-435d-8212-18381f6dfde7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Finger Search in the Implicit Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-264486","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Single quantum dots (QDs) can be embedded in nanocavities in order to enhance the interaction with a single mode of the electromagnetic field, thereby making them candidates for applications in quantum information systems. In this work [1], we investigate the coupling between single QDs and localized modes in photonic crystal (PC) cavities. From measurements of the detuning-dependent decay rate of a QD embedded in an L3 PC cavity we find a surprisingly broadband enhancement of the decay rate, cf. Fig. 1, which cannot be explained using the standard approach of a dissipative Jaynes-Cummings (JC) model. Similar measurements on a single QD tuned through an Anderson localized (AL) mode [2] in a PC waveguide show that in this system the decay rates closely follow the JC model. We introduce a novel microscopic model taking the interaction with longitudinal-acoustic (LA) phonons into account. Using this model, we are able to explain the broadband enhancement in an L3 cavity, and the quantitative difference compared to the AL-cavity arises from a larger background decay rate in the AL-cavity due to the presence of leaky radiation modes. The concept of the effective phonon density of states (DOS) is introduced, which determines the rate of phonon-assisted spontaneous emission. If, e.g., the QD is blue-detuned from the cavity mode, the QD can emit a photon into the cavity mode by emitting the residual energy as a phonon [3]. Our microscopic model allows us to extract the effective phonon DOS, that turns out to agree with a model for bulk phonons.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Madsen, Kristian Høeg","Nielsen, Per Kær","Kreiner-Møller, Asger","Stobbe, Søren","Nysteen, Anders","Mørk, Jesper","Lodahl, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-320145"],"event":{"end":"2012-09-27","place":"Stuttgart, de","start":"2012-09-23","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors (NOEKS)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non markovian phonon dephasing of a quantum dot in a photonic crystal nanocavity","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/12484783/NOEKS11_abstract_submitted.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-320145","ids":["dtu-344a3fdb-ebe4-49fb-bd4e-8cedf2f3498c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-659EABF8F1287BB32DB278AF3B37C857"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/12484783/NOEKS11_abstract_submitted.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Høeg","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"22f5717e-6379-4f43-98ce-227c03a7679c","name":"Madsen, Kristian Høeg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger","key":"kreinermøllerpau","last":"Kreiner-Møller","locid":"651ccc08-dff5-4b0d-8612-c427a430b9fd","name":"Kreiner-Møller, Asger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"stobbepau","last":"Stobbe","name":"Stobbe, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"nysteenpau","last":"Nysteen","locid":"feb12213-6336-4444-bc91-486323195b3a","name":"Nysteen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpau","last":"Lodahl","name":"Lodahl, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"82","status":"p","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-344a3fdb-ebe4-49fb-bd4e-8cedf2f3498c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Non-Markovian phonon dephasing of a quantum dot in a photonic-crystal nanocavity","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-320145","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"For large composite structures, such as wind turbine blades, thick laminates are required to withstand large in-service loads. During the manufacture of thick laminates, one of the challenges met is avoiding process-induced shape distortions and residual stresses. In this paper, embedded fibre Bragg grating sensors are used to monitor process-induced strains during vacuum infusion of a thick glass/epoxy laminate. The measured strains are compared with predictions from a cure hardening instantaneous linear elastic (CHILE) thermomechanical numerical model where different mechanical boundary conditions are employed. The accuracy of the CHILE model in predicting process-induced internal strains, in what is essentially a viscoelastic boundary value problem, is investigated. A parametric study is furthermore performed to reveal the effect of increasing the laminate thickness. The numerical model predicts the experimental transverse strains well when a tied boundary condition at the tool/part interface is used and the tool thermal expansion is taken into account. However, the CHILE approach is shown to overestimate residual strains after demoulding because of the shortcomings of the model in considering viscoelastic effects. The process-induced strain magnitude furthermore increases when the laminate thickness was increased, owing mainly to a decrease in through-thickness internal transverse stresses.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Michael Wenani","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Hattel, Jesper Henri","Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","Markussen, Christen Malte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-320764"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blades","Composites","Curing","Distortions","Manufacturing","Numerical analysis","Process monitoring"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in situ measurement using fbgs of process induced strains during curing of thick glass epoxy laminate plate experimental results and numerical modelling","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/we.1550","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-320764","identifier":[{"id":"84888339792","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3675c2f7-96bd-4cea-ae72-2ddb5e490579"],"keyword":["Blades","Composites","Curing","Distortions","Manufacturing","Numerical analysis","Process monitoring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-470579D8593C1099CAEC8E48216541F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/we.1550","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Wenani","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6f04228d-8fbe-4940-8fba-6b7dd9e8df6c","name":"Nielsen, Michael Wenani","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2a187e49-ed7b-44eb-a0d4-f9d00cc245ce","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hattelpau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"løgstrupandersenpau","last":"Løgstrup Andersen","locid":"a3b0c1b2-d918-4f62-813c-87ade730ab3e","name":"Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","orcid":"0000-0002-4998-6603","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christen Malte","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","locid":"a780ae37-79fd-4b1c-a26b-852eed6032ca","name":"Markussen, Christen Malte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/we.1550","issn":["10954244","10991824"],"issn_org":["10954244"],"issue":"8","journal":"Wind Energy","pages":"1241-1257","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Wind Energy","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84888339792"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3675c2f7-96bd-4cea-ae72-2ddb5e490579"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"In situ measurement using FBGs of process-induced strains during curing of thick glass/epoxy laminate plate : experimental results and numerical modelling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-320764","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In this work, a cure hardening instantaneous linear elastic (CHILE) model and a path dependent (PD) constitutive approach are compared, for the case of modelling strain build-up during curing of a thick composite laminate part. The PD approach is a limiting case of viscoelasticity with path dependency on temperature and cure degree. Model predictions are compared to experimentally determined in-situ strains, determined using FBG sensors. It was found that both models offer good approximations of internal strain build-up. A general shortcoming is the lack of capturing rate-dependent effects such as creep.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Michael Wenani","Hattel, Jesper Henri","Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","Branner, Kim","Nielsen, Per Hørlyk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334819"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-28","place":"Venica, it","start":"2012-06-24","title":"ECCM15","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Curing","Numerical modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental determination and numerical modelling of process induced strains and residual stresses in thick glass epoxy laminate","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84904016051","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334819","identifier":[{"id":"84904016051","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-656d11f0-f2b7-4b45-a025-7d34b8234db3"],"keyword":["Curing","FBG sensoring","Numerical modeling","Shape distortions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E38F12BF96AD742898ED9108473E261A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Wenani","key":"nielsenmichaelwenanipau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6f04228d-8fbe-4940-8fba-6b7dd9e8df6c","name":"Nielsen, Michael Wenani","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Henri","key":"hatteljesperhenripau","last":"Hattel","locid":"cc43ac84-8b15-435d-a8b8-343c75c257db","name":"Hattel, Jesper Henri","orcid":"0000-0001-5687-4581","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"løgstrupandersentompau","last":"Løgstrup Andersen","locid":"a3b0c1b2-d918-4f62-813c-87ade730ab3e","name":"Løgstrup Andersen, Tom","orcid":"0000-0002-4998-6603","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"brannerkimpau","last":"Branner","locid":"2b4e488e-7201-4f77-a01b-5507897273e8","name":"Branner, Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-9601-6343","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Hørlyk","key":"nielsenperhørlykpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f1bac13c-b951-45c8-9718-1a5c783cbc04","name":"Nielsen, Per Hørlyk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"ECCM15 - 15th European Conference On Composite Materials"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-656d11f0-f2b7-4b45-a025-7d34b8234db3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Experimental Determination and Numerical Modelling of Process Induced Strains and Residual Stresses in Thick Glass/Epoxy Laminate","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334819","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
