{"abstract":"We investigate the influence of the electron-phonon interaction on the decay dynamics of a quantum dot coupled to an optical microcavity. We show that the electron-phonon interaction has important consequences on the dynamics, especially when the quantum dot and cavity are tuned out of resonance, in which case the phonons may add or remove energy leading to an effective nonresonant coupling between quantum dot and cavity. The system is investigated using two different theoretical approaches: (i) a second-order expansion in the bare phonon coupling constant, and (ii) an expansion in a polaron-photon coupling constant, arising from the polaron transformation which allows an accurate description at high temperatures. In the low-temperature regime, we find excellent agreement between the two approaches. An extensive study of the quantum dot decay dynamics is performed, where important parameter dependencies are covered. We find that in general the electron-phonon interaction gives rise to a greatly increased bandwidth of the coupling between quantum dot and cavity. At low temperature, an asymmetry in the quantum dot decay rate is observed, leading to a faster decay when the quantum dot has a larger energy than to the cavity. We explain this as due to the absence of phonon absorption processes. Furthermore, we derive approximate analytical expressions for the quantum dot decay rate, applicable when the cavity can be adiabatically eliminated. The expressions lead to a clear interpretation of the physics and emphasize the important role played by the effective phonon density, describing the availability of phonons for scattering, in quantum dot decay dynamics. Based on the analytical expressions, we present the parameter regimes where phonon effects are expected to be important. Also, we include all technical developments in appendixes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Per Kær","Nielsen, Torben Roland","Lodahl, P.","Jauho, Antti-Pekka","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-081.54-032638"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microscopic theory of phonon induced effects on semiconductor quantum dot decay dynamics in cavity qed","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/10493208/C752Fd01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.54-032638","identifier":[{"id":"84865072857","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-02d355c9-63dc-4617-8e66-6be5066c229a","ku-66dbe812-2d80-423d-95cb-efd18d775bd5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9BFF72F0FB438303CFDE955B827AA7DF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/10493208/C752Fd01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.86.085302","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Quantop"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenperkærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P.","key":"kaerppau","last":"Kaer","name":"Kaer, P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Roland","key":"nielsentorbenrolandpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d00af887-eee2-4b25-9c31-ff4893a61c4b","name":"Nielsen, Torben Roland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T.R.","key":"nielsentrpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, T.R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A.-P","key":"jauhoappau","last":"Jauho","name":"Jauho, A.-P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Antti-Pekka","key":"jauhoanttipekkapau","last":"Jauho","locid":"72495773-3ad7-4387-86a1-7757b6a46a1b","name":"Jauho, Antti-Pekka","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-7859","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J.","key":"mørkjpau","last":"Mørk","name":"Mørk, J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkjesperpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpeterpau","last":"Lodahl","locid":"fa2dbf58-7de5-4c4c-a7fc-6c96dc6d6937","name":"Lodahl, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9348-9591","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.86.085302","issn":["01631829","1550235X"],"issn_org":["01631829"],"issue":"8","journal":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","pages":"085302","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B Condensed Matter","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865072857"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-02d355c9-63dc-4617-8e66-6be5066c229a","ku-66dbe812-2d80-423d-95cb-efd18d775bd5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microscopic theory of phonon-induced effects on semiconductor quantum dot decay dynamics in cavity QED","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.54-032638","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Analyzing data obtained from genome-wide gene expression experiments is challenging due to the quantity of variables, the need for multivariate analyses, and the demands of managing large amounts of data. Here we present the R package pcaGoPromoter, which facilitates the interpretation of genome-wide expression data and overcomes the aforementioned problems. In the first step, principal component analysis (PCA) is applied to survey any differences between experiments and possible groupings. The next step is the interpretation of the principal components with respect to both biological function and regulation by predicted transcription factor binding sites. The robustness of the results is evaluated using cross-validation, and illustrative plots of PCA scores and gene ontology terms are available. pcaGoPromoter works with any platform that uses gene symbols or Entrez IDs as probe identifiers. In addition, support for several popular Affymetrix GeneChip platforms is provided. To illustrate the features of the pcaGoPromoter package a serum stimulation experiment was performed and the genome-wide gene expression in the resulting samples was profiled using the Affymetrix Human Genome U133 Plus 2.0 chip. Array data were analyzed using pcaGoPromoter package tools, resulting in a clear separation of the experiments into three groups: controls, serum only and serum with inhibitor. Functional annotation of the axes in the PCA score plot showed the expected serum-promoted biological processes, e.g., cell cycle progression and the predicted involvement of expected transcription factors, including E2F. In addition, unexpected results, e.g., cholesterol synthesis in serum-depleted cells and NF-κB activation in inhibitor treated cells, were noted. In summary, the pcaGoPromoter R package provides a collection of tools for analyzing gene expression data. These tools give an overview of the input data via PCA, functional interpretation by gene ontology terms (biological processes), and an indication of the involvement of possible transcription factors.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Morten","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","Olsen, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-081.74-044252"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pcagopromoter an r package for biological and regulatory interpretation of principal components in genome wide gene expression data","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/37574682/pcaGoPromoter.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.74-044252","identifier":[{"id":"84857600074","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3288097","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22384239","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8c62a4e3-40e1-46c4-ad7a-ef579d9edda9","ruc-b5709517-152e-411f-b127-ca4420367bf2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FAEDD9F2AF4695A3A9E6C3C460DF6980"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/37574682/pcaGoPromoter.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0032394","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Eukaryot Cellebiologi","Roskilde University, The Department of Science, Systems and Models"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"69e70182-dd43-43b4-a913-fd53023748a9","name":"Hansen, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas Alexander","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","locid":"b87ed711-194a-48dc-b83a-3c7aad18a00d","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob Benedikt","key":"sedelinpau","last":"Sedelin","name":"Sedelin, Jacob Benedikt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Thorvald","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"555180dd-5ada-4311-8be9-88685cec10a0","name":"Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"dd6747c2-2376-4486-a000-1b4f1222eaaf","name":"Olsen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-1974-6446","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22384239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0032394","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"2","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857600074"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8c62a4e3-40e1-46c4-ad7a-ef579d9edda9","ruc-b5709517-152e-411f-b127-ca4420367bf2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"pcaGoPromoter - An R Package for Biological and Regulatory Interpretation of Principal Components in Genome-Wide Gene Expression Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.74-044252","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"DMUs konklusioner vedr. den økologiske risikovurdering af den genmodificerede, insektresistente 5307-majs i Danmark Den genmodificerede majs 5307, adskiller sig fra konventionel majs ved at have indsat gener der gør planterne tolerante over for insektangreb fra larverne af nogle bestemte arter af biller (Diabrotica virgifera og D. longicornis). Desuden indeholder majsen et mannose-markørgen. Majsens evne til at udnytte mannose som kulstofkilde forventes dog ikke at påvirke dens etableringsevne i naturen. GM-majsen søges kun godkendt til import til brug som dyrefoder eller viderebearbejdning til fødemidler. Der kan derfor potentielt kun ske uønskede effekter på miljøet ved en tilfældig, utilsigtet spredning. Den foreslåede overvågningsplan samt den landbrugs¬mæssige kontrol af frøudsæd vil formentlig kunne påvise en sådan spredning. Hvis der skulle ske en tilfældig spredning af frø fra 5307-majsen i Danmark, vil disse, som al anden majs, ikke kunne krydse med vilde arter eller etablere vedvarende bestande i naturen eller på dyrknings¬arealerne, da frø og spirer normalt ikke kan overleve vinterperioden. Mannose er et essentielt monosaccharid der er nødvendig for opbygningen af dyreceller. Derfor er forekomst af uønskede effekter af PMI-proteinet på ikke-målorganismer næppe sandsynlige. Anvendelsen af mannose til markørgen må vurderes som miljømæssigt mindre problematisk og dermed miljømæssigt positivt i forhold til anvendelsen af HT-markører. DMU vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes nogen væsentlige uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for dyre- og planteliv ved markedsføring af den genmodificerede 5307-majs til import og anvendelse til videreforarbejdning og dyrkning. Kommentarer til EFSA: D.3: The use of a mannose-insert as a marker-gene is to be complemented on, as this is a more environmentally friendly procedure than the conventional use of herbicide-resistance markers.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjellsson, Gøsta","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Damgaard, Christian","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-088.61-022839"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af genmodificeret majs event 000000005307 i anmeldelse vedr markedsføring under forordning 000000001829 000000002003 ef era efsa gmo de 000000002011 000000000095","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-088.61-022839","ids":["au-8b8c4f5d-59ba-459b-9396-5cb188b3ff49","au-ad09fd29-0ac8-44f1-81ca-f548833bbad8"],"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-6945417AA4B36BD82AF928359E10901F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","c