{"abstract":"Når det drejer sig om radikale innovationer så er der et markant innovationpotentiale i universitets-virksomheds-samarbejde. Baseret på en innovationscase vedrørende udvikling af et radikalt nyt diagnose instrument fremhæver kapitlet en række faktorer, der er henholdsvist fremmende og hæmmende for samarbejdsprocessen, og som indeholder flere mulige implikationer for innovationsfremme via tiltag på universiteter, hos virksomheder og i erhvervsfremmepolitikken.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gertsen, Frank","Nielsen, René Nesgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"universitet virksomheds samarbejde om radikal innovation et casestudie om procesfremmende og hæmmende faktorer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-071964","ids":["aau-4b9c6fa4-c147-429b-b7af-fb12e810a089"],"keyword":["Radikal Innovation, universitets-virksomhedssamarbejde"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3358E90E32EB1889144B415B1058E03"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG), Center for Industrial Production (department)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank","key":"gertsenpau","last":"Gertsen","locid":"fd5aa05d-ea40-4068-b735-6059c0862cc6","name":"Gertsen, Frank","orcid":"0000-0002-9554-1242","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Nesgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"74df64b0-7daa-471f-ad04-20b1253a0909","name":"Nielsen, René Nesgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper L","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jesper L","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771120455"],"issn":["22455086"],"pages":"73-97","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Nordjyske Udviklingsperspektiver","status":"p","subtitle":"-afvikling eller udvikling?","title":"Nordjyske Udviklingsperspektiver"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4b9c6fa4-c147-429b-b7af-fb12e810a089"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Universitet-virksomheds-samarbejde om radikal innovation : Et casestudie om procesfremmende og -hæmmende faktorer","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071964","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Assessing experimentally the whole-body specific absorption rate (SARwb) in a complex indoor environment is very challenging. An experimental method based on room electromagnetics theory (accounting only the Line-Of-Sight as specular path) to assess the whole-body SAR is validated by numerical simulations with the Finite-Difference Time-Domain method. Furthermore, the method accounts for the diffuse multipath components (DMC) in the total absorption rate by considering the reverberation time of the investigated room, which describes all the losses in a complex indoor environment. The advantage of the proposed method is that it allows discarding the computation burden because it does not use any discretizations. Results show good agreement between measurement and computation at 2.8 GHz, as long as the plane wave assumption is valid, i.e., for high distances from the transmitter. Relative deviations 0.71% and 4% have been obtained for far-field scenarios, and 77.5% for the near field-scenario. The contribution of the DMC in the total absorption rate is also quantified here, which has never been investigated earlier. It is found that the DMC may represent an important part of the total absorption rate; its contribution may reach up to 90% for certain scenarios in an indoor environment.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bamba, Aliou","Joseph, Wout","Vermeeren, Gunter","Tanghe, Emmeric","Gaillot, Davy P.","Andersen, Jørgen Bach","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Lienard, Martine","Martens, Luc"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-079920"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghent University","Group TELICE, IEMN, University of Lille"],"keyword":["Line of sight","Power density","Reverberation time","Specific absorption rate","absorption cross section","room electromagnetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of experimental whole body sar assessment method in a complex indoor environment","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/bem.21749","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-079920","identifier":[{"id":"84872402229","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000313596000005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-66dd4d12-4cea-47a9-953f-1010a2da6df4"],"keyword":["Reverberation time","absorption cross section","diffuse multipath components","line-of-sight","power density","room electromagnetics","specific absorption rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-303D067B076547835A71045AE4B30CC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1521-186X%20","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/bem.21749","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"ghent university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"group telice iemn university of lille","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Group TELICE, IEMN, University of Lille","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio netwo