{"abstract":"Protective gloves are used to reduce dermal exposure when managing chemical exposures at the work place. Different glove materials may offer different degrees of protection. The present study combined the traditional ASTM (American Society for Testing and Materials) model with the Franz diffusion cell to evaluate overall penetration through glove and skin as well as the deposition in the different reservoirs. Benzoic acid was applied on latex or nitrile gloves placed on top of human skin. The amounts of chemical were quantified in the glove material, between glove and skin, within the skin, and in the receptor chamber. Both glove materials reduce total penetration of benzoic acid, but nitrile gloves offer a significantly better protection than latex gloves. This difference was less pronounced at the higher of the two concentrations of benzoic acid applied. Thus, glove types that offer relevant protection at low concentrations does not necessarily give appropriate protection at high concentrations. Significant amounts of benzoic acid could be extracted from the glove materials after exposure. If a chemical is accumulated in the glove material, reuse of single-use gloves should be cautioned. The reuse of gloves is generally not to be recommended without effective decontamination.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Sørensen, Jens Ahm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614772"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Benzoic acid","Female","Gloves Protective","Humans","Latex","Middle Aged","Nitriles","Skin Absorption"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glove material reservoir formation and dose affect glove permeation and subsequent skin penetration","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2011.12.037","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-614772","identifier":[{"id":"22264917","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84857033945","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-910f143b-1cc4-41fd-98f9-2d24cc8aa60f"],"keyword":["Adult","Benzoic Acid","Female","Gloves, Protective","Humans","Latex","Middle Aged","Nitriles","Skin Absorption"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA1F57C20B3C29D328CE15C7D69A591F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2011.12.037","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Environmental Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22264917"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2011.12.037","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"87-91","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"417-418"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857033945"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-910f143b-1cc4-41fd-98f9-2d24cc8aa60f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Glove material, reservoir formation, and dose affect glove permeation and subsequent skin penetration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614772","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"AU-Biosciences konklusioner vedr. den økologiske risikovurdering af de genmodificerede raps Ms8, Rf3 og Ms8xRf3 i Danmark. Den genmodificerede rapshybrid, Ms8xRf3, adskiller sig kun fra konventionel raps ved at have indsat gener der gør planten tolerant over for sprøjtning med herbicidet glufosinat og ved at være delvis han-steril. GM-rapsen søges kun godkendt til import for anvendelse til fødevarer såsom oliefremstilling til human konsum, men ikke til dyrkning. AU-Bioscience anser for sandsynligt at Ms8, Rf3 og Ms8xRf3-rapsen og dens gener kan blive spredt i forbindelse med distribution eller at der kan ske uheld med iblanding i konventionel raps i forbindelse med håndtering under import samt transport og lagring. Dette kan medføre at den genmodificerede raps og de indsatte gener med tiden vil spredes til marker med konventionel eller økologisk dyrket raps, ligesom genet vil blive spredt til vilde slægtninge af raps, mest sandsynligt agerkål. Konsekvenserne for plante- og dyrelivet ved selv en betydelig spredning af Ms8xRf3 til naturnære områder og landbrugsområder må dog vurderes at være små og begrænsede til de dyrkningsarealer, hvor der anvendes glufosinat. AU-Bioscience vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes væsentlige uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for dyre- og plantelivet ved markedsføring af Ms8, Rf3 og Ms8xRf3-rapsen til andre formål end dyrkning. Der bør dog foretages en overvågning af eventuel utilsigtet spredning af levende frø af GM-rapsen ved importstederne og langs transportruterne. Kommentarer til EFSA: D.11.3 and D.11.4: Because there is a risk of accidental dispersal and possible adventitious presence of Ms8, Rf3 and Ms8xRf3-oilseed rape at import areas and along transport routes, these areas should be monitored for GM oilseed rape-plants from seed-spill. Furthermore GM-oilseed plants may cause potential problems for co-existence with conventional oilseed rape crops in case of admixture which should be addressed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjellsson, Gøsta","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Damgaard, Christian","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-090.82-014108"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af de genmodificerede raps ms000000000008 rf000000000003 og ms000000000008xrf000000000003 i anmeldelse til markedsføring under forordning 000000001829 000000002003 ef era efsa gmo be 000000002010 000000000081","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-090.82-014108","ids":["au-15048ec7-4c7a-4c76-ad80-51055d626c43","au-7cc89519-391f-4734-b0a8-5cce0a3ffc92"],"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-C3F42A785D330E1B6CC92D165EE826B7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj-Britt Uhd","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8212e441-2e87-482f-ad06-184f50830cec","name":"Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-15048ec7-4c7a-4c76-ad80-51055d626c43","au-7cc89519-391f-4734-b0a8-5cce0a3ffc92"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Økologisk risikovurdering af de genmodificerede raps MS8, RF3 og MS8xRF3 i anmeldelse til markedsføring under Forordning 1829/2003/EF. : ERA: EFSA/GMO/BE/2010/81","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.82-014108","year":2012,"yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"The lessons learned from a review of thirteen existing European bio-economic models used in the evaluation of EU policies are presented. How these models compare and differ in terms of their biological and economic components, the integration between the components, which indicators are selected and how they are used, are described and analysed. The article concludes that the multitude of construction differences reflects the necessity of adapting the modelling approach to answer different questions. Since real life questions in fisheries are so diverse, answering them requires a diversity of models","author_count":12,"contributors":["Prellezo, Raúl","Accadia, Paolo","Andersen, Jesper L.","Andersen, Bo Sølgaard","Buisman, Erik","Little, Alyson","Nielsen, J. Rasmus","Poos, Jan Jaap","Powell, J.","Röckmann, C."],"cuid":["S02-098.48-034049"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Prellezo, Raúl"],"country":["Italy","Netherlands","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AZTI","All Global Affiliations","Azti-Tecnalia Food Research Institute","CEFAS","Centre for the Environment Fisheries and Aquaculture Science","IREPA Onlus Via S. Leonardo","Irepa Onlus","Wageningen University & Research"],"keyword":["Bio economic models","European region","Review"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Section for Management Systems"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a review of eu bio economic models for fisheries the value of a diversity of models","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2011.08.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.48-034049","identifier":[{"id":"81255176944","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-40a43e4b-317f-477a-8d82-1fadbfdce64a","ku-705cb13c-f51c-441b-be2b-804bf08fa54b"],"keyword":["Bio-economic models","European region","Model characteristics","Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E01AB034EF515779E2153ECA6A1E896B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2011.08.003","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"es","key":"azti","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"AZTI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"azti tecnalia food research institute","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Azti-Tecnalia Food Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"irepa onlus","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Irepa Onlus","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"irepa onlus via s leonardo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"IREPA Onlus Via S. Leonardo","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Institute of Food and Resource Economics, Environmental and Natural Resource Economics Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Management Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Section for Management Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"nl","key":"wageningen university research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Wageningen University & Research","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"gb","key":"centre for the environment fisheries and aquaculture science","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Centre for the Environment Fisheries and Aquaculture Science","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"gb","key":"cefas","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"CEFAS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Raúl","key":"prellezoraúlpau","last":"Prellezo","name":"Prellezo, Raúl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"accadiapaolopau","last":"Accadia","name":"Accadia, Paolo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Jesper Levring","key":"andersenjesperlevringpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"72c137de-8212-41ed-ac15-9d04635c2559","name":"Andersen, Jesper Levring","orcid":"0000-0001-6963-5053","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo S.","key":"andersenbosølgaardpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"9eb28429-875c-4e35-8780-8dc7b6e93220","name":"Andersen, Bo Sølgaard","name_org":"Andersen, Bo S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"buismanerikpau","last":"Buisman","name":"Buisman, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 10","corresponding":null,"first":"Alyson","key":"littlealysonpau","last":"Little","name":"Little, Alyson","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. Rasmus","key":"nielsenjrasmuspau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cf76e759-57d4-406d-8978-7cb20563cdec","name":"Nielsen, J. Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-2833-3873","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Jaap","key":"poosjanjaappau","last":"Poos","name":"Poos, Jan Jaap","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"powelljpau","last":"Powell","name":"Powell, J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Jeff","key":"powelljeffpau","last":"Powell","name":"Powell, Jeff","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"röckmanncpau","last":"Röckmann","name":"Röckmann, C.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Christine","key":"röckmannchristinepau","last":"Röckmann","name":"Röckmann, Christine","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marpol.2011.08.003","issn":["0308597X","18729460"],"issn_org":["0308597X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Marine Policy","pages":"423-431","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Marine Policy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-81255176944"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-40a43e4b-317f-477a-8d82-1fadbfdce64a","ku-705cb13c-f51c-441b-be2b-804bf08fa54b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A review of EU bio-economic models for fisheries: The value of a diversity of models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.48-034049","year":"2012","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"Attomole (10 mol) levels of RNA and DNA isolated from beer spoilage bacterial cells Lactobacillus brevis have been detected by the electrochemical sandwich DNA hybridization assay exploiting enzymatic activity of lipase. DNA sequences specific exclusively to L. brevis DNA and RNA were selected and used for probe and target DNA design. The assay employs magnetic beads (MB) modified with a capture DNA sequence and a reporter DNA probe labeled with the enzyme, both made to be highly specific for L. brevis DNA. Lipase-labeled DNAs captured on MBs in the sandwich assay were collected on gold electrodes modified with a ferrocene (Fc)-terminated SAM formed by aliphatic esters. Lipase hydrolysis of the ester bond released a fraction of the Fc redox active groups from the electrode surface, decreasing the electrochemical signal from the surface-confined Fc. The assay, shown to be efficient for analysis of short synthetic DNA sequences, was ineffective with genomic double stranded bacterial DNA, but it allowed down to 16amole detection of 1563nts long RNA, isolated from bacterial ribosomes without the need for PCR amplification, and single DNA strands produced from ribosomal RNA. No interference from E. coli RNA was registered. The assay allowed analysis of 400 L. brevis cells isolated from 1L of beer, which fits the \"alarm signal\" range (from 1 to 100 cells per 100mL).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Shipovskov, Stepan","Saunders, Aaron Marc","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Hansen, Majken H.","Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","Ferapontova, Elena"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-005532"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrochemical sandwich assay for attomole analysis of dna and rna from beer spoilage bacteria lactobacillus brevis","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bios.2012.05.001","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-005532","identifier":[{"id":"84861721204","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000306209300016","type":"wos"},{"id":"22633494","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-71e9f614-b87e-4701-b27f-1e9217de289b","au-1f75e4bc-e5f8-46ae-b517-849f9d37db47"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-25D153F833215C0670CD43520E93AA43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bios.2012.05.001","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stepan","key":"shipovskovpau","last":"Shipovskov","locid":"7f5e9630-87ee-422d-8bde-61bd5c7336c5","name":"Shipovskov, Stepan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.M.","key":"saunderspau","last":"Saunders","locid":"b1ecc07f-e39c-4610-89ed-c1847fb729ea","name":"Saunders, Aaron Marc","name_org":"Saunders, A.M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sejrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Majken Nørgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c4b10caa-726f-4792-8b00-99f056f2afdb","name":"Hansen, Majken Nørgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kurt Vesterager","key":"gothelfpau","last":"Gothelf","locid":"8ca43d09-e887-432e-8775-ab2f38db1e6d","name":"Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2399-3757","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"ferapontovapau","last":"Ferapontova","locid":"fb776e85-d3fe-451d-ba01-40d092a0e54c","name":"Ferapontova, Elena","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22633494"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bios.2012.05.001","issn":["09565663","18734235"],"issn_org":["09565663"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biosensors and Bioelectronics","pages":"99-106","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biosensors and Bioelectronics","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861721204"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-71e9f614-b87e-4701-b27f-1e9217de289b","au-1f75e4bc-e5f8-46ae-b517-849f9d37db47"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Electrochemical sandwich assay for attomole analysis of DNA and RNA from beer spoilage bacteria Lactobacillus brevis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-005532","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The effect of flow maldistribution on the performance of microchannel parallel plate heat exchangers is investigated using an established single blow numerical model and cyclic steady-state regenerator experiments. It is found that as the variation of the individual channel thickness in a particular stack (heat exchanger) increases the actual performance of the heat exchanger decreases significantly, deviating from the expected nominal performance. We show that this is due to both the varying fluid flow velocities in each individual channel and the thermal cross talk between the channels transverse to the direction of the flow.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Kaspar Kirstein","Engelbrecht, Kurt","Christensen, Dennis Valbjørn","Jensen, Jesper Buch","Smith, Anders","Bahl, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035521"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Flow maldistribution","Microchannels","Parallel plates","Thermal cross talk"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"degradation of the performance of microchannel heat exchangers due to flow maldistribution","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.02.019","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-035521","identifier":[{"id":"84857679708","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7f63ca6d-718d-4cf7-a658-34625608e8b3","ku-2b37ba95-4f1d-4344-bdce-48135749b3ad"],"keyword":["Flow maldistribution","Microchannels","Parallel plates","Thermal cross talk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9A1C894C1879F99BD353021EA3D4B363"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7590721/Degradation.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.02.019","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Electrofunctional materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaspar Kirstein","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"82e21ae8-a61e-40c9-867b-de0b8f7c7c01","name":"Nielsen, Kaspar Kirstein","orcid":"0000-0001-7938-4577","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kurt","key":"engelbrechtpau","last":"Engelbrecht","locid":"7ad5c8a4-c7bd-4cab-908c-a034fb241527","name":"Engelbrecht, Kurt","orcid":"0000-0002-3713-9415","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dennis","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"8e3aff3f-3fd1-413f-9c23-00927ee285c7","name":"Christensen, Dennis Valbjørn","name_org":"Christensen, Dennis","orcid":"0000-0003-0048-7595","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Buch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"2570786d-d428-4cee-b3a8-d79343db70ce","name":"Jensen, Jesper Buch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","locid":"0e57cd2b-adc6-46b8-b0bd-41ed5da4a4d4","name":"Smith, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-2723-8812","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"bahlpau","last":"Bahl","locid":"93d82dbc-38f6-496f-bdf3-a3b0c0c94a69","name":"Bahl, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1153-7183","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2012.02.019","issn":["13594311"],"journal":"Applied Thermal Engineering","pages":"236-247","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Thermal Engineering","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857679708"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7f63ca6d-718d-4cf7-a658-34625608e8b3","ku-2b37ba95-4f1d-4344-bdce-48135749b3ad"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Degradation of the performance of microchannel heat exchangers due to flow maldistribution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-035521","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"AimsIn the recently published DANPACE trial, incidence of atrial fibrillation (AF) was significantly higher with single-lead atrial (AAIR) pacing than with dual-chamber (DDDR) pacing. The present analysis aimed to evaluate the importance of baseline PQ-interval and percentage of ventricular pacing (VP) on AF.Methods and resultsWe analysed data on AF during follow-up in 1415 patients included in the DANPACE trial. In a subgroup of 650 patients with DDDR pacemaker, we studied whether %VP, baseline PQ-interval, and programmed atrio-ventricular interval (AVI) was associated with AF burden measured as time in mode-switch (MS) detected by the pacemaker. In the entire DANPACE study population, the incidence of AF was significantly higher in patients with baseline PQ-interval >180 ms (P<0.001). Among 650 patients with DDDR pacemaker, telemetry data were available for 1.337 ± 786 days, %VP was 66 ± 33%, AF was detected at planned follow-up in 160 patients (24.6%), MS occurred in 422 patients (64.9%), and AF burden was marginally higher with baseline PQ-interval >180 ms (P= 0.028). No significant association was detected between %VP and %MS (Spearman's ρ 0.056, P= 0.154). %MS was not different between minimal-paced programmed AVI ≤ 100 and >100 ms (median value), respectively (P= 0.60).ConclusionsThe present study indicates that a longer baseline PQ-interval is associated with an increased risk of AF in patients with sick sinus syndrome. Atrial fibrillation burden is not associated with the percentage of VP or the length of the programmed AVI.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Thomsen, Poul Erik B","Højberg, Søren","Møller, Mogens","Riahi, Sam","Dalsgaard, Dorthe","Mortensen, Leif","Nielsen, Tonny","Asklund, Mogens","Friis, Elsebeth V","Christensen, Per","Simonsen, Paul Erik","Eriksen, Ulrik H","Jensen, Gunnar","Svendsen, Jesper H","Toff, William D","Healey, Jeffrey S","Andersen, Henning Rud"],"cuid":["S03-097.09-021654"],"filters":{"add