 Abildgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4164-4913","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John-Josef","key":"lethpau","last":"Leth","locid":"3457cc55-3f53-4cbb-a1a5-eaa67a34863e","name":"Leth, John-Josef","orcid":"0000-0001-6043-1687","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cca.2012.6402708","eisbn":["9781467345040"],"isbn":["9781467345033"],"issn":["10851992"],"pages":"859-864","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"IEEE International Conference on Control Applications. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2012 International Conference on Control, Automation and Information Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873110019"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-93b0e084-6730-4f86-8aa4-a0e651c61fd1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Implementing Force-Feedback in a Telesurgery Environment, Using Parameter Estimation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092878","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper reports a longitudinal multi-case research project encompassing 72 semi-structured interviews carried out in 2011 and 2012. The interviews covered topics of the collaboration between university and industry, why they were engaged, who benefitted from it, the initial motives and final results. In addition the interviews tried to focus on whether the industry understood the motives of the university to engage in collaboration and vice versa. Focusing on whether the performance measurements used by politicians and universities today enhances the collaborations or obstruct them. The paper concludes that the performance management used today in universities in form of publications is overlooking the industries’ need of growth from the university knowledge. Hence motivating the scientists to engage in collaborations only from the university point of view and only to a limited extent concerning about the companies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anja Birch","Sort, Jesper Chrautwald","Nielsen, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115331"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from traditional to modern universities the ambiguousness of researcher incentives in a university industry collaboration perspective","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/71901193/KASK7_20121221.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-115331","ids":["aau-e087906f-486c-4fad-8d2d-1a7ac2ef9e88"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-17E5D682DCC329C9795E0030157C9D6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/71901193/KASK7_20121221.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ssrn.com/abstract=2192409","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja Birch","key":"nielsenanjabirchpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f3cc27d5-7b47-460b-8eaf-eee3003fe8bf","name":"Nielsen, Anja Birch","orcid":"0000-0002-5901-6053","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Chrautwald","key":"sortjesperchrautwaldpau","last":"Sort","locid":"11418beb-d40c-40bf-af69-55b47598cc45","name":"Sort, Jesper Chrautwald","orcid":"0000-0003-0468-6209","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"nielsenchristianpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5ce07766-d99e-45a5-84b3-0267fca84453","name":"Nielsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-5050-5793","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"15","publisher":"SSRN: Social Science Research Network","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e087906f-486c-4fad-8d2d-1a7ac2ef9e88"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"From Traditional to Modern Universities : The Ambiguousness of Researcher Incentives in a University-Industry Collaboration Perspective","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115331","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses design issues in the development of playful outdoor interactive installations featuring kinesthetic interaction and immersive music experiences. The research is based on the development and evaluation of the novel SwingScape installation, which is a permanent installation at an urban playground. The objectives of SwingScape are to encourage physical activity as well as creating a playful and social experience in an urban space. The interaction techniques include movement sensors built into swings, LED lights, and an ambient loudspeaker system covering approx. 180 square meters. The design issues include: creating playful and collective interaction, making a familiar swing interaction simulate the experience of a music mixing board, providing gentle integration of multimedia (light and sound) in the atmosphere of an urban space, and finally making installations robust and safe for an urban outdoor setting. The SwingScape installation has been developed in three phases for quite different urban settings, and the experiences from these are generalised to contribute to a foundation for design of interactive urban installations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Grønbæk, Kaj","Kortbek, Karen Johanne","Christensen, Claus Møller","Nielsen, Jesper Sindahl","Stenfeldt, Liselott"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-166804"],"event":{"acronym":"ACE","end":"2012-11-04","place":"Katmandu, np","start":"2012-11-01","title":"Advances in Computer Entertainment","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing playful interactive installations for urban environments the swingscape experience","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-34292-9_16","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-166804","identifier":[{"id":"84868015381","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-41d64d27-767b-43b0-8314-4d5c6278d6bd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F5E7C4512A9F001A7C4423CDDDA8F95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-34292-9_16","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"c7b908c7-ad69-4b60-bfb2-f6d7f490bb4f","name":"Grønbæk, Kaj","orcid":"0000-0002-3752-6714","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen Johanne","key":"kortbekpau","last":"Kortbek","locid":"01e6fa3c-6abd-490e-be7a-862879bf9971","name":"Kortbek, Karen Johanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Møller","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"e0ee4dcc-af94-4ad5-9318-8b7faf5e7308","name":"Christensen, Claus Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9db76efc-49ba-4329-b2ca-3c1397909536","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sindahl","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Liselott","key":"stenfeldtpau","last":"Stenfeldt","locid":"abf7deb6-29ee-4f9b-a719-738c2b112d2c","name":"Stenfeldt, Liselott","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-34292-9_16","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"230-245","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7624"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84868015381"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-41d64d27-767b-43b0-8314-4d5c6278d6bd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Designing Playful Interactive Installations for Urban Environments - The SwingScape Experience.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-166804","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the impact of financial crises on two fundamental features of stock returns, namely, the risk-return tradeoff and the leverage effect. We apply the fractionally integrated exponential GARCH-in-mean (FIEGARCH-M) model for daily stock return data, which includes both features and allows the co-existence of long memory in volatility and short memory in returns. We extend this model to allow the financial parameters governing the volatility-in-mean effect and the leverage effect to change during financial crises. An application to the daily U.S. stock index return series from 1926 through 2010 shows that both …financial effects increase significantly during crises. Strikingly, the risk-return tradeoff is significantly positive only during financial crises, and insignificant during non-crisis periods. The leverage effect is negative throughout, but increases significantly by about 50% in magnitude during …financial crises. No such changes are observed during NBER recessions, so in this sense …financial crises are special. Applications to a number of major developed and emerging international stock markets confirm the increase in the leverage effect, whereas the international evidence on the risk-return tradeoff is mixed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christensen, Bent Jesper","Nielsen, Morten Ørregaard","Zhu, Jie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-212050"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai University of Finance and Economics"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of financial crises on the risk return tradeoff and the leverage effect","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/45389761/rp12_19.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-212050","ids":["au-910e318d-5b69-4606-8ab5-42af3c4b2d72"],"keyword":["FIEGARCH-M, financial crises, financial leverage, international markets, long memory, risk-return tradeoff, stock returns, volatility feedback"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1996282BC5721DD38B67D4BD875654DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/45389761/rp12_19.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Economics and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai university of finance and economics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai University of Finance and Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent Jesper","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"bbacbd2c-0350-430f-8190-189bab4c87de","name":"Christensen, Bent Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8448-9752","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Ørregaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5f9a0ff6-05a6-4a61-8bab-4d5bd71ba1d6","name":"Nielsen, Morten Ørregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1337-9844","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Jie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"26","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Institut for Økonomi, Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-910e318d-5b69-4606-8ab5-42af3c4b2d72"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The impact of financial crises on the risk-return tradeoff and the leverage effect","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-212050","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This roundtable discusses embodiment in consumer judgment and decision-making to (1) assess the state of knowledge, (2) bring clarity to the interaction of cognitive appraisals and bodily perceptions of emotion and its effect on cognitive representations, and (3) develop directions for research on the role of embodiment in consumer behaviors.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Reimann, Martin","Ackerman, Josh","Castaño, Raquel","Garg, Nitika","Kreuzbauer, Robert","Labroo, Aparna A.","Lee, Angela Y.","Lee, Spike W. S.","Malter, Alan J.","Morrin, Maureen","Nenkov, Gergana Y.","Nielsen, Jesper H.","Perez, Maria","Pol, Gratiana","Rosa, José Antonio","Yoon, Carolyn","Zaichkowsky, Judith","Zhong, Chen-Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-283213"],"event":{"end":"2011-10-16","place":"St. Louis, us","start":"2011-10-13","title":"39th Annual Conference of the Association for Consumer Research. ACR 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Mexico","Singapore","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston College","Kellogg School of Management","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","National University of Singapore","Rotman School of Management. University of Toronto","Rutgers University","Stephen M. Ross School of Business","Tecnológico de Monterrey","University of Arizona","University of Chicago","University of Chicago Booth School of Business","University of Michigan","University of Mississippi","University of Wyoming"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"embodiment in consumer judgment and decision making behavioral psychological and neural perspectives","src":["cbs"],"src-cod