,"last":"Yoon","name":"Yoon, Carolyn","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Judith","key":"zaichkowskyjudithpau","last":"Zaichkowsky","locid":"ddb55ad6-ce39-40f5-a16c-4b023c160591","name":"Zaichkowsky, Judith","orcid":"0000-0002-8887-5308","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16","corresponding":null,"first":"Chen-Bo","key":"zhongchenbopau","last":"Zhong","name":"Zhong, Chen-Bo","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00989258"],"journal":"Advances in Consumer Research","pages":"686-688","publisher":"Association for Consumer Research","status":"p","title":"Advances in Consumer Research","volume":"39"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-52558acc-2ca2-4605-b8d4-93b2066fddcd"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Embodiment in Consumer Judgment and Decision-Making : Behavioral, Psychological, and Neural Perspectives","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-283213","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Plaice in Kattegat and Skagerrak have traditionally been considered as one stock unit. However the collected information on biology and fishery in areas between the North and Baltic Seas suggest changes are needed in assessment units as well as in management areas. Plaice in Skagerrak (Division 20) is now considered to be closely associated with plaice in the North Sea and is proposed to be included in the North Sea plaice stock assessment, although it is recognized that local populations are present in the area. Therefore, specific management of the Skagerrak plaice is suggested. Plaice in Kattegat (Division 21), the Belts (Division 22), and the Sound (Division 23) is considered a stock unit and is proposed to be assessed as such. However, separate management by area is also suggested to assure the preservation of the local populations. Plaice in the Baltic (Divisions 24–32) is considered a stock unit and is proposed to be assessed and managed as such. Pragmatic options are suggested for empirical harvest control rules accounting for the dynamic of local abundance, using a survey‐based biomass indicator. For the future, new scientific analyses should be developed to better inform the origin of the catches, provided that additional resources are allocated to the annual monitoring of different stocks and components. Such information would provide on‐going quantitative information on the degree of mixing of the various components, potentially allowing a more accurate assessment, management, and conservation of the status of these","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ulrich, Clara","Boje, Jesper","Cardinale, Massimiliano","Gatti, Paul","le Bras, Quentin","Andersen, Michael","Hansen, Jakob Hemmer","Hintzen, Niels T.","Jacobsen, Jonathan B.","Jonsson, Patrik","Miller, David C.M.","Eg Nielsen, Einar","Rijnsdorp, Adriaan","Svedäng, Henrik","Wennhage, Håkan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving the assessment and management of the plaice stock complex between the north sea and the baltic sea","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123045227/Ulrich_et_al_ICES_ASC_2012_N02.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316571","ids":["dtu-28520d6d-0d2a-4d47-b9ae-f4ac5e156a69"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0D60C5C34225893EFF91EA5E9B613908"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ices.dk/products/CMdocs/CM-2012/N/N0212.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123045227/Ulrich_et_al_ICES_ASC_2012_N02.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Management Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Clara","key":"ulrichpau","last":"Ulrich","locid":"4698ddee-30e4-4ac9-9c05-a0aacb1b8620","name":"Ulrich, Clara","orcid":"0000-0001-7598-2051","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"bojepau","last":"Boje","locid":"06dba873-ab1b-4838-9d60-25ae7de754c8","name":"Boje, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-9034-4605","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimiliano","key":"cardinalepau","last":"Cardinale","name":"Cardinale, Massimiliano","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"gattipau","last":"Gatti","locid":"d87874d8-8666-47a5-b598-3c33229c947a","name":"Gatti, Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Quentin","key":"lebraspau","last":"le Bras","locid":"ff7b3ddb-e03b-437a-abe3-4ffcb3e2a463","name":"le Bras, Quentin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Hemmer","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a9fbe122-035f-40d7-b5af-d1ed7caf2d2b","name":"Hansen, Jakob Hemmer","orcid":"0000-0002-1033-2565","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels T.","key":"hintzenpau","last":"Hintzen","name":"Hintzen, Niels T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan B.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Jonathan B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrik","key":"jonssonpau","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Patrik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David C.M.","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","name":"Miller, David C.M.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Einar","key":"egnielsenpau","last":"Eg Nielsen","locid":"b76eaaaa-879f-4118-94dd-429ea3baac67","name":"Eg Nielsen, Einar","orcid":"0000-0002-7009-9814","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Adriaan","key":"rijnsdorppau","last":"Rijnsdorp","name":"Rijnsdorp, Adriaan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"svedängpau","last":"Svedäng","name":"Svedäng, Henrik","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Håkan","key":"wennhagepau","last":"Wennhage","name":"Wennhage, Håkan","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-28520d6d-0d2a-4d47-b9ae-f4ac5e156a69"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improving the assessment and management of the plaice stock complex between the North Sea and the Baltic Sea","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316571","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Inline near-infrared (NIR) spectroscopy has been used to monitor a continuous synthesis of an active pharmaceutical ingredient (API) intermediate by a Grignard alkylation reaction. The reaction between a ketone substrate and allylmagnesium chloride may form significant impurities with excess feeding of the Grignard reagent beyond the stoichiometric ratio. On the other hand, limiting this reagent would imply a loss in yield. Therefore, accurate dosing of the two reactants is essential. A feedforward–feedback control loop was conceived in order to maintain the reaction as closely as possible to the stoichiometric ratio, leading the path to full process automation. The feedback control loop relies on NIR transmission measurements performed in a flow cell where, in contrast to labor-intensive offline HPLC analytical methods, the whole reaction product can be scanned in real time without sample dilution. A robust PLS (projection to latent structures) model was developed with a satisfactory standard error of prediction, providing quantification of the ketone substrate in solutions with a high variability of the major solution component - the alkoxide product. In addition, model performance supervision tools such as the spectral residuals or simple plots of pretreated spectra can assist in the identification of spectral outliers, which in this case could be related to Grignard reagent excess. If the sampling time of the NIR instrument is short enough, manipulating the inputs to the reactor may be used to obtain information about its dynamic behavior. This information is very useful for process control design, assessment of analytical tools and definition of sampling times. In this work, a systematic procedure for chemometric model building is followed, after which a discussion is made on some of the potential applications that can be found when exploiting the fast and rich information provided by NIR spectroscopy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cervera Padrell, Albert Emili","Nielsen, Jesper","Pedersen, Michael Jønch","Müller Christensen, Kim","Mortensen, Asmus R.","Skovby, Tommy","Dam-Johansen, Kim","Kiil, Søren","Gernaey, Krist"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-342910"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monitoring and control of a continuous grignard reaction for the synthesis of an active pharmaceutical ingredient intermediate using inline nir spectroscopy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/9824678/PRO12_03.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-342910","identifier":[{"id":"84861627122","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-806dd535-e291-42d7-8716-5a380d1db4c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4066BB4D1E607D98FA91D8FD180233EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/op2002563","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/op2002563","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/9824678/PRO12_03.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and 