{"abstract":"Torrefaction is a mild thermal treatment in an inert atmosphere, which is known to increase the energy density of biomass on a mass basis (MJ kg-1). By combining the torrefaction process and pelletization the specific energy density on volume basis is further increased would thus allow for more cost effective volume limited transport. There are two ways of combining torrefaction and pelletization: pelletize torrefied biomass and torrefy regular pellets. The former is the one used for producing commercial torrefied pellets, while the latter one could be relevant for power plant which has facility to do torrefaction before co-firing. In this study, both ways were utilized to produce torrefied pellets. The quality of these pellets have been characterized for higher heating value (HHV), energy consumption during grinding, mechanical durability and equilibrium moisture content (EMC) under different humidity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Shang, Lei","Dahl, Jonas","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Holm, Kens Kai","Nielsen, Niels Peter K.","Stelte, Wolfgang","Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Bach, Lars Stougaard","Henriksen, Ulrik Birk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348983"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-22","place":"Milan, it","start":"2012-06-17","title":"2012 EU BC&amp;E","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of pellets from torrefied biomass and pellets torrefied at different temperatures","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-348983","ids":["dtu-94fac862-a250-401e-a8fa-61ddc70536f5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-39DF60EC70DCF45E13977CAA9F379718"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"shangpau","last":"Shang","locid":"bbededa9-f22f-49fe-b873-8d18146105a1","name":"Shang, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","name":"Dahl, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kens Kai","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Kens Kai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Peter K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niels Peter K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wolfgang","key":"steltepau","last":"Stelte","locid":"f83e64eb-158e-4e6d-8eb4-45be0683d650","name":"Stelte, Wolfgang","orcid":"0000-0003-2424-4010","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f75a7756-932a-4066-8a74-8955f3f30f55","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","name_org":"Thomsen, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Stougaard","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"c9785d52-f13f-4f03-8917-b7dc901a2d8a","name":"Bach, Lars Stougaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Birk","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"e24f0587-f0e8-4ba0-93f0-9096e3a1b547","name":"Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","orcid":"0000-0003-1838-3962","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-94fac862-a250-401e-a8fa-61ddc70536f5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quality of pellets from torrefied biomass and pellets torrefied at different temperatures","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348983","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The laser has evolved from table size apparatuses to truly nano sized devices, in much the same way that computer chips have been continuously minimized. The few-emitter nanolaser represents an extreme in terms of size. The emitters can be either atoms or quantum dots, and they are coupled to a high-Q optical cavity. This system has previously been studied for the one and two emitters case, see e.g. [1, 2]. The emitters and cavity are modelled as two-level systems and a harmonic oscillator, respectively. The coupled system is modelled using the Jaynes-Cummings Hamiltonian and the two-level systems are pumped incoherently by a rate P. Solutions are found using the corresponding master equation. However, with cavity populations exceeding 100 and several emitters, the dimension of the Hilbert space of the system becomes too large to handle efficiently on a conventional computer. E.g. for four emitters and 100 photon states the density matrix has more than 2.5 × 106 elements. We have been able to simplify the problem significantly by adiabatically eliminating the photon-assisted polarizations and the correlations between emitters and cavity [3]. This results in a set of rate equations for the population of the cavity, na, and the occupation of the emitters. Fig. 1a) shows na for up to 4 emitters coupled to a cavity, as a function of the pumping rate P. The figure also shows results from a full master equation solution, and the correspondence is very good for large values of P. In Fig. 1b) the second order correlation functions g(2)(0) are shown, as obtained using the full model. The second order correlation functions become 1 for sufficiently large values of P signifying the onset of lasing. However, for larger values of P the laser quenches and the emission becomes chaotic (g(2)(0) = 2). This quenching effect is well-known in two-level models [3], but might not be realistic for semiconductor quantum dots. A proposed application for these nanolasers is in on-chip optical interconnects. In this application the modulation bandwidth is important. We have calculated the modulation bandwidth using a small-signal analysis of the rate equations, which has the advantage compared the full model of yielding a semianalytical result. The results are shown in Fig. 1c). The nanolaser has a high bandwidth, which is mostly limited by the cavity lifetime (/ 1/), but shows a prominent drop during the lasing regime. The modulation bandwidth again becomes limited by as the output becomes chaotic.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","Nielsen, Per Kær","Lorke, Michael","Tromborg, Bjarne","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357124"],"event":{"end":"2012-09-27","place":"Stuttgart, de","start":"2012-09-23","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors (NOEKS)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bremen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"properties of nanolasers based on few discrete emitters","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.uni-stuttgart.de/noeks11/NOEKS11_booklet_web_optimiert.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357124","ids":["dtu-aff039d5-5b70-4099-b35a-8b6432d7bf6c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CD674F04749B640F6FF7263EED982B8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.uni-stuttgart.de/noeks11/NOEKS11_booklet_web_optimiert.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of bremen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bremen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Mølbjerg","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1bf57cde-4fad-4c3b-8fe1-c2be836414eb","name":"Lund, Anders Mølbjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"lorkepau","last":"Lorke","name":"Lorke, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne","key":"tromborgpau","last":"Tromborg","locid":"b2ce3147-cbb6-4062-af3a-22dbf18ae873","name":"Tromborg, Bjarne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"89","status":"p","title":"11th International Workshop on Nonlinear Optics and Excitation Kinetics in Semiconductors"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-aff039d5-5b70-4099-b35a-8b6432d7bf6c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Properties of nanolasers based on few discrete emitters","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357124","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
