","pages":"533-45","status":"p","title":"Neurobiology of Disease","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865416193"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4828f4e7-ba59-4a90-ab5c-85fb7f918c3b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neuroprotective and memory enhancing properties of a dual agonist of the FGF receptor and NCAM","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436531","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Although much data have accumulated on sessile serrated adenoma/polyp/lesion (SSA/P/L) in general, its characteristics in specified contexts are less well elucidated. This lack of knowledge is even more conspicuous concerning its borderline counterpart, referred to as BSSA/P/L. The previous histological observations of the authors on SSA/P/L and BSSA/P/L in general are here extended to encompass attributes of these polyps in the context of synchronous colorectal carcinoma (SCRC), with a focus on the place of BSSA/P/L in the spectrum of non-dysplastic serrated polyps.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mohammadi, Mahin","Kristensen, Michael Holmsgaard","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Bonde, Jesper Hansen","Holck, Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459309"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"qualities of sessile serrated adenoma polyp lesion and its borderline variant in the context of synchronous colorectal carcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jclinpath-2012-200803","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-459309","identifier":[{"id":"84866934676","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22782936","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6e40f419-066b-4356-9a57-635b4134e140"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4CDEB295CC331AD56870CBAE20F2FD0D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jclinpath-2012-200803","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Re