{"abstract":"The purpose of the study was to investigate the influence of torrefaction on the quality of Scots pine pellets. Pellet samples were torrefied at 230, 250 and 270°C for 1h in nitrogen atmosphere. Higher heating value (HHV) was increased from 18.37MJkg−1 to 24.34MJkg−1. The energy to crush a pellet by mechanical compression was determined using a material tester and results showed a rapid decrease before torrefaction temperature reached 250°C. Slightly further decrease was observed when increasing the temperature up to 270°C. The strength loss was confirmed by determining the energy required for grinding the pellet samples in a bench scale disc mill. Particle size distribution measurements after grinding indicated a significant increase of small particles (diameterca. 2mm). To further analyze the effect on strength, the mechanical durability of pellets was tested according to wood pellet standards, EN 15210-1. The results have shown a good correlation between pellet durability and compression strength, and indicated that the pellet durability can be estimated based on compression strength data of about 25 pellets.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Shang, Lei","Nielsen, Niels Peter K.","Dahl, Jonas","Stelte, Wolfgang","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","Holm, Jens Kai","Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Henriksen, Ulrik Birk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356322"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Durability","Grinding","Strength","Torrefaction","Wood pellets"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality effects caused by torrefaction of pellets made from scots pine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.03.013","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356322","identifier":[{"id":"84860160598","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ad41609f-a070-460c-bd45-4f5af49f11c6"],"keyword":["Durability","Grinding","Strength","Torrefaction","Wood pellets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E87665CDD82A2A041E0BAC429795F9AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.03.013","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ørsted","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ØR","l3nl":"Ørsted","l3nn":"Ørsted","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ørsted","namevar":["Ørsted A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ØR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"shangpau","last":"Shang","locid":"bbededa9-f22f-49fe-b873-8d18146105a1","name":"Shang, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Peter K.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Niels Peter K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","name":"Dahl, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wolfgang","key":"steltepau","last":"Stelte","locid":"f83e64eb-158e-4e6d-8eb4-45be0683d650","name":"Stelte, Wolfgang","orcid":"0000-0003-2424-4010","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Kai","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jens Kai","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f75a7756-932a-4066-8a74-8955f3f30f55","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","name_org":"Thomsen, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik B.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"e24f0587-f0e8-4ba0-93f0-9096e3a1b547","name":"Henriksen, Ulrik Birk","name_org":"Henriksen, Ulrik B.","orcid":"0000-0003-1838-3962","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuproc.2012.03.013","issn":["03783820","18737188"],"issn_org":["03783820"],"journal":"Fuel Processing Technology","pages":"23-28","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel Processing Technology","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860160598"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ad41609f-a070-460c-bd45-4f5af49f11c6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quality effects caused by torrefaction of pellets made from Scots pine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356322","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A series of compounds based on the mGluR5-selective ligand 2-methyl-6-(phenylethynyl)pyridine (MPEP) were designed and synthesized. The compounds were found to be either structural analogues of MPEP, substituted monomers, or dimeric analogues. All compounds retained mGluR5 selectivity with only weak or no activity at other mGluRs or iGluRs. The substituted analogue, 1,3-bis(pyridin-2-ylethynyl)benzene (19), is a potent negative modulator at mGluR5, whereas all other compounds lost potency relative to MPEP and showed that activity is highly dependent on the position of the nitrogen atom in the pyridine moieties. A homology modeling and ligand docking study was used to understand the binding mode and the observed selectivity of compound 19.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kaae, Birgitte H","Harpsøe, Kasper","Kvist, Trine","Mathiesen, Jesper M.","Mølck, Christina","Gloriam, David E","Jimenez, Hermogenes N","Uberti, Michelle A","Nielsen, Søren M","Nielsen, Birgitte","Bräuner-Osborne, Hans","Sauerberg, Per","Clausen, Rasmus Prætorius","Madsen, Ulf"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432669"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lundbeck Research USA"],"keyword":["Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structure activity relationships for negative allosteric mglur000000000005 modulators","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cmdc.201100578","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-