{"abstract":"Background/aims: High levels of pro-inflammatory cytokines are linked to inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). The transcription factor Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2 (CDX2) plays a crucial role in differentiation of intestinal epithelium and regulates IBD-susceptibility genes, including meprin 1A (MEP1A). The aim was to investigate the expression of CDX2 and MEP1A in colitis; to assess if they are regulated by tumor necrosis factor-a (TNF-a), and finally to reveal if CDX2 is involved in a TNF-a-induced down-regulation of MEP1A. Methods: Expression of CDX2 and MEP1A was investigated in colonic biopsies of ulcerative colitis (UC) patients and in dextran sodium sulfate (DSS)-induced colitis. CDX2 protein expression was investigated by immunoblotting and immunohistochemical procedures. CDX2 and MEP1A regulation was examined in TNF-a-treated Caco-2 cells by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction and with reporter gene assays, and the effect of anti-TNF-a treatment was assessed using infliximab. Finally, in vivo CDX2-DNA interactions were investigated by chromatin immunoprecipitation. Results: The CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA expression was significantly decreased in active UC patients and in DSS-colitis. Colonic biopsy specimens from active UC showed markedly decreased CDX2 staining. TNF-a treatment diminished the CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA levels, a decrease which, was counteracted by infliximab treatment. Reporter gene assays showed significantly reduced CDX2 and MEP1A activity upon TNF-a stimulation. Finally, TNF-a impaired the ability of CDX2 to interact and activate its own, as well as the MEP1A expression. Conclusions: The present results indicate that a TNF-a-mediated down-regulation of CDX2 can be related to suppressed expression of MEP1A during intestinal inflammation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Olsen, Anders Krüger","Holm, Thomas Lindebo","Kvist, Peter Helding","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Olsen, Jørgen","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-483384"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tnf a induced down regulation of cdx000000000002 suppresses mep000000000001a expression in colitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbadis.2012.01.012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-483384","identifier":[{"id":"22326557","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84858984691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-967bbe3f-c1fa-4d6c-a281-c2cd56706b53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-C83E615F7BA274B5572248484B275860"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbadis.2012.01.012","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunmehmetpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Krüger","key":"olsenanderskrügerpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"af701802-1145-4e46-94ff-1fc07a549b94","name":"Olsen, Anders Krüger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Lindebo","key":"holmthomaslindebopau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Thomas Lindebo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pa