{"abstract":"Atrial fibrillation (AF) is the most common arrhythmia. The potassium current IKs is essential for cardiac repolarization. Gain-of-function mutations in KV7.1, the pore-forming α-subunit of the IKs channel, have been associated with AF. We hypothesized that early-onset lone AF is associated with mutations in the IKs channel regulatory subunit KCNE1.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Olesen, Morten Sig","Bentzen, Bo Hjorth","Nielsen, Jonas Bjerregaard","Steffensen, Annette Buur","David, Jens-Peter","Jabbari, Javad","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Haunsø, Stig","Svendsen, Jesper H","Schmitt, Nicole"],"cuid":["S02-091.30-014166"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Age of Onset","Atrial fibrillation","Base Sequence","Cohort Studies","DNA Mutational Analysis","Denmark","Electric conductivity","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Humans","Ion Channel Gating","Kinetics","Male","Molecular Sequence Data","Mutant Proteins","Mutation","Pedigree","Potassium Channels Voltage Gated","Protein Subunits"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mutations in the potassium channel subunit kcne000000000001 are associated with early onset familial atrial fibrillation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2350-13-24","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.30-014166","identifier":[{"id":"22471742","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3359244","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84859183376","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-15d238a1-db2f-43ed-9c8e-eadf70c61120","ku-1b0b5da0-92a9-4855-881e-2fe51bdf556b"],"keyword"