{"abstract":"The room electromagnetics (RE) theory describes the radio propagation in a single room assuming diffuse scat- tering. A main characteristic is the exponential power-delay profile (PDP) decaying with the so-called reverberation time (RT) parameter, depending only on the wall area, the volume of the room and an absorption coefficient. The PDP is independent on the location in the room, except for the arrival time. Based on measurements in a room with a spherical array of 16 dual- polarized wideband horn antennas, the current work studies how the RE parameters depend on the receiver (Rx) antenna polarization and orientation. Also the frequency dependence is investigated, with measurements done at both 2.3 GHz and 5.8 GHz center frequencies. The RE theory was found to fit well to the measurements with a RT in the range 22-25 ns. Only small differences were found due to the polarization and the channel gain was depending approximately as expected with frequency.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Andersen, Jørgen Bach","Pedersen, Gert Frølund","Pelosi, Mauro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118007"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on polarization and frequency dependence of diffuse indoor propagation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/63091521/VTC2011_JNI_REM_Horn.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-118007","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000298891500094","type":"wos"},{"id":"83755219554","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e9c58ec7-93c3-4361-a2fb-9f44fa95cd65"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8AAA7828B84994A5F45E88FC7F95640F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?arnumber=6092906","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/VETECF.2011.6092906","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/63091521/VTC2011_JNI_REM_Horn.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Bach","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"64828c54-b67d-4e86-a6c4-02321b2be1a9","name":"Andersen, Jørgen Bach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert Frølund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mauro","key":"pelosipau","last":"Pelosi","locid":"8bb317b0-1caa-4396-90be-cb837e16c874","name":"Pelosi, Mauro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vetecf.2011.6092906","issn":["15502252"],"journal":"IEEE VTS Vehicular Technology Conference. Proceedings","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE VTS Vehicular Technology Conference. Proceedings","title_org":"I E E E V T S Vehicular Technology Conference. Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-83755219554"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e9c58ec7-93c3-4361-a2fb-9f44fa95cd65"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"On Polarization and Frequency Dependence of Diffuse Indoor Propagation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118007","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This book demonstrates how the WWII bunkers can serve as an important study object for students of Architecture. The presented assignment is for 1. year students at the Aarhus school of Architecture. The overall scheme of the book falls in two categories. One being the documentations of the bunkers. The other being the translation and architectural respond to the bunker. The book i coherent with a new strategy at the Aarhus school of Architecture where research methods are implemented in teaching at an early stage of the study.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Gammelgaard Nielsen, Anders","Diaz, Pauline","Bernstorff Aagaard, Tine","Hansen, Ann Busch","Aagaard, Eva","Koch, Trine","Jensen, Kasper","Holt, Lars","Danø, Jesper","Gregersen, Trine","Krag, Mo Michelsen Stochholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-125579"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Assignment","Bunker","Dokumentation","Drawing","Translation","architecture students"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-AAA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bunker documentation and translation of a wwii bunker a first year assignment aarhus school of architecture","src":["arka"],"src-code":["DI-ART-AAA"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/34080457/BUNKER.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-125579","ids":["arka-d2bf7291-5b4b-44aa-8aa8-0137f6a33cf8"],"keyword":["No","analytic models","architectural potential","architecture students","assignment","bunker","dokumentation","drawing","translation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-62B315A8ED3562324FE2F99505AA7D37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/3408