{"abstract":"The use of serotonine reuptake inhibitors (SRIs) is increasing among Danish pregnant women. This systematic review addresses the potential adverse effects on the foetus and child of maternal SRI medication. The literature indicates a slightly increased risk of cardiovascular malformations and persistent pulmonary hypertension of the new-born, while evidence regarding the risk of preterm labour, low birth weight, low Apgar score, prolonged QT interval and miscarriage is less clear. An estimated 20-30% of infants will have neonatal symptoms following intrauterine SRI exposure. The symptoms may be caused by SRI withdrawal, toxicity or their overlap, but symptom aetiology basically remains controversial. The infants may exhibit neurological, gastrointestinal, autonomic, endocrine or respiratory symptoms. Although the symptoms are self-limited, the families may be seriously affected. In general, studies do not address this important aspect. Evidence concerning long-term effects is surprisingly sparse and many studies have important methodological limitations. However, present evidence does not convincingly indicate detrimental long-term effects. Until sufficient safety studies have been carried out, SRI must be used with caution in pregnancy and every treatment of the pregnant woman should be thoroughly considered.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fenger-Grøn, Jesper","Thomsen, Morten","Andersen, Kristian Skytte","Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580726"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paediatric outcomes following intrauterine exposure to serotonin reuptake inhibitors a systematic review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80052533818","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580726","identifier":[{"id":"21893008","type":"pmid"},{"id":"80052533818","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1a3af035-2ffc-42f3-a016-8a3cf19df444"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F5AB07EE8D77E884C48E68CEE8EF06D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Paediatrics (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"fengergrønpau","last":"Fenger-Grøn","locid":"eaeed626-b8c5-4904-8707-c31d7eba126c","name":"Fenger-Grøn, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Skytte","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristian Skytte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Gaardskær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1bfc1ab1-a1de-4993-8f2c-535fe756143b","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus Gaardskær","orcid":"0009-0000-5912-003X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21893008"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","16039629"],"issn_org":["09078916"],"issue":"9","journal":"Danish Medical Bulletin","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Bulletin","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1a3af035-2ffc-42f3-a016-8a3cf19df444"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Paediatric outcomes following intrauterine exposure to serotonin reuptake inhibitors: a systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580726","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Objective. The combination of plasma tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases-1 (TIMP-1) and carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) may be valuable biomarkers for early detection of colorectal cancer (CRC). A prospective, population based study was performed to validate this hypothesis. Material and methods. Individuals (n = 4509) referred for large bowel endoscopy due to symptoms of CRC were prospectively included. Baseline data and concurrent diseases were recorded. The primary endpoint was detection of CRC and findings at examinations were recorded using International Classification of Diseases-10 codes. Plasma was obtained before endoscopy and TIMP-1 and CEA levels were determined after the inclusion of all individuals. Results. Findings were based on sigmoidoscopy in 1766 and colonoscopy in 2743 individuals. Colon cancer (CC) was detected in 184 and rectal cancer in 110 individuals. Ten individuals with other cancers, 856 with adenomas and 1176 with non-neoplastic findings were also detected. The biomarker levels were increased in a variety of diseases including CRC compared to individuals without any findings at endoscopy. A multivariable analysis demonstrated that both markers were significant and independent detectors of CRC. Combining both biomarkers, independent contributions from each (TIMP-1, odds ratio (OR) = 1.8 (95% confidence interval (CI): 1.4-2.2), p <0.0001; CEA <5 ng/ml, OR = 1.6, 1.3-1.9, or >= 5 ng/ml, OR = 2.3, 95% CI: 1.9-2.7 (p <0.0001)) were obtained. Subgroup analysis of individuals examined by colonoscopy with CC as the endpoint showed that combining both biomarkers, independent contributions from each (TIMP-1, OR = 2.5, 95% CI: 1.8-3.4, p <0.0001; CEA <5 ng/ml, OR = 1.4, 95% CI: 1.1-1.8, and CEA 5 ng/ml, OR = 2.3, 95% CI: 1.8-3.0 (p <0.0001)) were obtained. Conclusions. This prospective validation study supports the use of the combination of plasma TIMP-1 and CEA protein measurements as a potential aid in early detection of CRC and specifically of CC.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Nielsen, Hans J","Brünner, Nils","Jorgensen, Lars N","Olsen, Jesper","Rahr, Hans B","Thygesen, Knud","Hoyer, Ute","Laurberg, Søren","Stieber, Petra","Blankenstein, Marinus A","Davis, Gerard","Dowell, Barry L","Christensen, Ib J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-631283"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Danish Endoscopy Study Group on Colorectal Cancer Detection"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Biomarkers","Carcinoembryonic antigen","Colorectal Neoplasms","Early Detection of Cancer","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Tissue Inhibitor of Metalloproteinase 1","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma timp 000000000001 and cea in detection of primary colorectal cancer a prospective population based study of 000000004509 high risk individuals","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/78651360473","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-631283","identifier":[{"id":"20799911","type":"pmid"},{"id":"78651360473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ca8df476-01a3-4612-9eec-23584a10b58c"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Biomarkers","Carcinoembryonic Antigen","Colorectal Neoplasms","Early Detection of Cancer","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Tissue Inhibitor of Metalloproteinase-1","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-365CFC7701176793ABF20DBBDDAA288E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Organ and Plastic Surgery (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"danish endoscopy study group on colorectal cancer detection","name":"Danish Endoscopy Study Group on Colorectal Cancer Detection","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans J","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Hans J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"brünnerpau","last":"Brünner","name":"Brünner, Nils","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars N","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, Lars N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans B","key":"rahrpau","last":"Rahr","locid":"941e7830-92a2-42c8-a6d4-93a9fa3235e4","name":"Rahr, Hans B","orcid":"0000-0002-4571-7852","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","name":"Thygesen, Knud","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ute","key":"hoyerpau","last":"Hoyer","name":"Hoyer, Ute","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"laurbergpau","last":"Laurberg","name":"Laurberg, Søren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Petra","key":"stieberpau","last":"Stieber","name":"Stieber, Petra","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marinus A","key":"blankensteinpau","last":"Blankenstein","name":"Blankenstein, Marinus A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","name":"Davis, Gerard","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Barry L","key":"dowellpau","last":"Dowell","name":"Dowell, Barry L","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib J","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ib J","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20799911"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365521.2010.513060","issn":["00855928","17511895"],"issn_org":["00855928"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology. Supplement","pages":"60-9","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology. Supplement","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78651360473"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ca8df476-01a3-4612-9eec-23584a10b58c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Plasma TIMP-1 and CEA in detection of primary colorectal cancer : a prospective, population based study of 4509 high-risk individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-631283","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Aims In patients with sick sinus syndrome, bradycardia can be treated with a single-lead pacemaker or a dual-chamber pacemaker. Previous trials have revealed that pacing modes preserving atrio-ventricular synchrony are superior to single-lead ventricular pacing, but it remains unclear if there is any difference between single-lead atrial pacing (AAIR) and dual-chamber pacing (DDDR). Methods and results We randomly assigned 1415 patients referred for first pacemaker implantation to AAIR (n = 707) or DDDR (n = 708) pacing and followed them for a mean of 5.4 ± 2.6 years. The primary outcome was death from any cause. Secondary outcomes included paroxysmal and chronic atrial fibrillation, stroke, heart failure, and need for pacemaker reoperation. In the AAIR group, 209 patients (29.6%) died during follow-up vs. 193 patients (27.3%) in the DDDR group, hazard ratio (HR) 1.06, 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.88-1.29, P = 0.53. Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation was observed in 201 patients (28.4%) in the AAIR group vs. 163 patients (23.0%) in the DDDR group, HR 1.27, 95% CI 1.03-1.56, P = 0.024. A total of 240 patients underwent one or more pacemaker reoperations during follow-up, 156 (22.1%) in the AAIR group vs. 84 (11.9%) in the DDDR group (HR 1.99, 95% CI 1.53-2.59, P <0.001). The incidence of chronic atrial fibrillation, stroke, and heart failure did not differ between treatment groups. Conclusion In patients with sick sinus syndrome, there is no statistically significant difference in death from any cause between AAIR pacing and DDDR pacing. AAIR pacing is associated with a higher incidence of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and a two-fold increased risk of pacemaker reoperation. These findings support the routine use of DDDR pacing in these patients. Clinical Trial Registration: URL http://www.clinicaltrials.gov. Unique identifier: NCT00236158.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Thomsen, Poul Erik B","Højberg, Søren","Møller, Mogens","Vesterlund, Thomas","Dalsgaard, Dorthe","Mortensen, Leif","Nielsen, Tonny","Asklund, Mogens","Friis, Elsebeth V","Christensen, Per D","Simonsen, Erik","Eriksen, Ulrik H","Jensen, Gunnar Vagn Hagemann","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Toff, William D","Healey, Jeffrey S","Andersen, Henning Rud"],"cuid":["S02-089.12-019843"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["DANPACE Investigators","on behalf of the DANPACE Investigators"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac Pacing Artificial","Cardiotonic Agents","Cause of Death","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pacemaker Artificial","Reoperation","Sick sinus syndrome","Stroke","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparison of single lead atrial pacing with dual chamber pacing in sick sinus syndrome","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehr022","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.12-019843","identifier":[{"id":"79952834203","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21300730","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-62fc064f-0779-416b-ab90-0f7736553c4c","sdu-80e6137e-8780-4975-9ac1-e5dbe0c1d6a4"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Atrial Fibrillation","Cardiac Pacing, Artificial","Cardiotonic Agents","Cause of Death","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pacemaker, Artificial","Reoperation","Sick Sinus Syndrome","Stroke","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-02E8DC6319A7689430D1EBCB020D94FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehr022","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"on behalf of the danpace investigators","name":"on behalf of the DANPACE Investigators","role":"oau"},{"affno":4,"key":"danpace investigators","name":"DANPACE Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenjenscosedispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Erik B","key":"thomsenpoulerikbpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Poul Erik B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"højbergsørenpau","last":"Højberg","name":"Højberg, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"møllermogenspau","last":"Møller","locid":"13f88f34-8461-4bf6-8f81-06a8d2b799b8","name":"Møller, Mogens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"vesterlundthomaspau","last":"Vesterlund","locid":"687409b7-3c04-466d-a378-29f853aff8