ectronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Multimedia Information and Signal Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"tr","key":"bogazici university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Bogazici University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Kjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3d21c73c-3aa1-4590-870f-8be578634702","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-2586-7925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ali","key":"taylancemgilpau","last":"Taylan Cemgil","name":"Taylan Cemgil, Ali","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"godsillpau","last":"Godsill","name":"Godsill, Simon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Holdt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bfd2a53b-f2bd-4563-8968-9a911996215f","name":"Jensen, Søren Holdt","orcid":"0000-0002-1050-470X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tasl.2011.2108285","issn":["15587916"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing","pages":"1986-1998","publisher":"IEEE Advancing Technology for Humanity","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960672762"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fbc1c592-6ff0-408e-8662-700e6b295629"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Bayesian Interpolation and Parameter Estimation in a Dynamic Sinusoidal Model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123148","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Purpose. A clinical feasibility study using a removable prostate stent as fiducial for image-guided radiotherapy (IGRT) of localized prostate cancer (PC). Material and methods. The study included patients with local or locally advanced PC. The clinical target volume (CTV) was outlined on magnetic resonance (MR) images co-registered to planning computer tomography (CT) images. Daily online IGRT was delivered using the stent as fiducial. Risk of migration was estimated using multiple MR. Acute urinary toxicity was scored using the international prostate symptom score (IPSS). Late gastro-intestinal (GI) and genito-urinary (GU) toxicity was scored using the Radio Therapy Oncology Group (RTOG) score, biochemical failure (BF) was defined as an elevation of prostate specific antigen (PSA) above nadir plus 2 ng/ml after radiotherapy. Results. One hundred men were enrolled in the study. Ninety completed radiotherapy with the stent as fiducial. No migration of the stent was seen, but three cases of dislocation of the stent to the bladder were observed. Acute urinary toxicity based on IPSS was comparable to toxicity in patients who had gold markers (GM) as fiducials. Removal of the stent was associated with a high frequency of urinary retention. Late GI and GU toxicity and BF were comparable to those of other studies, but longer observation time is needed. Conclusions. This study reports the first clinical results of using a prostate stent as fiducial. No migration of the stent observed. Dislocation of the stent to the urinary bladder was observed in three cases, requiring removal of the stent and insertion of a new fiducial. Acute toxicity during radiotherapy evaluated from IPSS was comparable to toxicity in patients with GM. Removal of the stent was associated with a high frequency of post procedural urinary retention. Late toxicity and BF were comparable to those of other studies, though longer observation time is needed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Carl, Jesper Hansen","Nielsen, Jane","Holmberg, Mats","Larsen, Erik Højkjær","Fabrin, Knud","Fisker, Rune Vincents"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177741"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical results from first use of prostate stent as fiducial for radiotherapy of prostate cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2010.541935","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177741","identifier":[{"id":"21174520","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955624423","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-54e19135-1530-4b2c-8a5a-026b342eaeac"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1207CA34C5D857B2FA46553B80299A18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2010.541935","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Onkologisk Afdeling, Aalborg Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"carlpau","last":"Carl","locid":"39f05ca5-35f7-4251-ad47-442a087b2400","name":"Carl, Jesper Hansen","name_org":"Carl, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dd468c6d-cd86-4689-8819-21424503294e","name":"Nielsen, Jane","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mats","key":"holmbergpau","last":"Holmberg","locid":"8aeb5363-ea26-4f33-b9c8-d6922beec785","name":"Holmberg, Mats","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Hoejkjaer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"45e5f0a7-a970-4540-8a5e-6906df0e9bc3","name":"Larsen, Erik Højkjær","name_org":"Larsen, Erik Hoejkjaer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud","key":"fabrinpau","last":"Fabrin","locid":"179817c4-3acf-4255-807f-a4a6459a18aa","name":"Fabrin, Knud","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Vincents","key":"fiskerpau","last":"Fisker","locid":"a51c5246-2f4f-404a-8d3e-3ffc345c9d17","name":"Fisker, Rune Vincents","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21174520"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/0284186x.2010.541935","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"547-54","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955624423"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-54e19135-1530-4b2c-8a5a-026b342eaeac"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Clinical results from first use of prostate stent as fiducial for radiotherapy of prostate cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177741","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Askov, Jesper Brink","Hønge, Jesper Langhoff","Nygaard, Hans","Hasenkam, J. Michael","Nielsen, Sten Lyager","Jensen, Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-193787"],"event":{"end":"2011-02-05","place":"Geilo, no","start":"2011-02-03","title":"21st Annual Meeting of the Scandinavian Society of Research in Cardiothoracic Surgery","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel papillary muscle force transducer tests and results","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-193787","ids":["au-70e3b4fd-09ab-4375-8856-e921e0ec97b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CFAB0B9BC095E4E8B49C6E499917403A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, The Department of Thoracic and Cardiovascular Surgery T"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Brink","key":"askovpau","last":"Askov","locid":"8bfafdd4-0cbc-4260-8560-f94d0be9d50e","name":"Askov, Jesper Brink","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Langhoff","key":"høngepau","last":"Hønge","locid":"4c24e711-2c28-4064-81ba-c1cbabe56ebf","name":"Hønge, Jesper Langhoff","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"4cb12a02-6ad5-448b-8ece-dccb3f5b92da","name":"Nygaard, Hans","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Michael","key":"hasenkampau","last":"Hasenkam","locid":"401f4417-fe32-4195-b22c-aaae9eb1eb3a","name":"Hasenkam, J. Michael","name_org":"Hasenkam, John Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-7960-1172","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sten Lyager","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d28acbea-1e2e-4dcc-8fb6-a1402771d89f","name":"Nielsen, Sten Lyager","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1d0d7d42-4da2-44a4-8c5b-081a366c8825","name":"Jensen, Morten Ølgaard Jegstrup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70e3b4fd-09ab-4375-8856-e921e0ec97b5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Novel papillary muscle force transducer: Tests and results","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-193787","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"We propose a coin-flip protocol which yields a string of strong, random coins and is fully simulatable against poly-sized quantum adversaries on both sides. It can be implemented with quantum-computational security without any set-up assumptions, since our construction only assumes mixed commitment schemes which we show how to construct in the given setting. We then show that the interactive generation of random coins at the beginning or during outer protocols allows for quantum-secure realizations of classical schemes, again without any set-up assumptions. As example applications we discuss quantum zero-knowledge proofs of knowledge and quantum-secure two-party function evaluation. Both applications assume only fully simulatable coin-flipping and mixed commitments. Since our framework allows to construct fully simulatable coin-flipping from mixed commitments, this in particular shows that mixed commitments are complete for quantum-secure two-party function evaluation. This seems to be the first completeness result for quantum-secure two-party function evaluation from a generic assumption.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lunemann, Carolin","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-206851"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-07","place":"Dakar, sn","start":"2011-07-05","title":"4th International Conference on Cryptology in Africa","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully simulatable quantum secure coin flipping and applications","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-21969-6_2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-206851","identifier":[{"id":"79960089255","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-87d5d370-b4d7-11df-8c1a-000ea68e967b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A88C5B5A75FE460D8F0FFC9E5F4BB58A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-21969-6_2","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carolin","key":"lunemannpau","last":"Lunemann","locid":"72920c12-201f-4c2c-99a1-2aaf30dc42fb","name":"Lunemann, Carolin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-21969-6_2","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"21-40","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"6737"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960089255"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-87d5d370-b4d7-11df-8c1a-000ea68e967b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fully simulatable quantum-secure coin-flipping and applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-206851","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
