{"abstract":"The ever growing size of chemical data bases calls for the development of novel methods for representing and comparing molecules. One such method called LINGO is based on fragmenting the SMILES string representation of molecules. Comparison of molecules can then be performed by calculating the Tanimoto coefficient which is called the LINGOsim when used on LINGO multisets. This paper introduces a verbose representation for storing LINGO multisets which makes it possible to transform them into sparse fingerprints such that fingerprint data structures and algorithms can be used to accelerate queries. The previous best method for rapidly calculating the LINGOsim similarity matrix required specialised hardware to yield a significant speedup over existing methods. By representing LINGO multisets in the verbose representation and using inverted indices it is possible to calculate LINGOsim similarity matrices roughly 2.6 times faster than existing methods without relying on specialised hardware.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kristensen, Thomas Greve","Nielsen, Jesper","Pedersen, Christian Nørgaard Storm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228320"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Virtual screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using inverted indices for accelerating lingo calculations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ci100437e","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228320","identifier":[{"id":"79953166860","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21332133","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ad9c6430-71e9-4e0b-ba29-a276204334d9"],"keyword":["virtual screening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3233BCB0841018F5C8A120CA247C2A2D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ci100437e","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Greve","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"7442e985-c1b7-43b7-be77-89e43c63f977","name":"Kristensen, Thomas Greve","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"81bd45f3-9a63-4c7c-9e55-bb00c43a907f","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Nørgaard Storm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c36d6c36-4b4c-453f-9f0d-9e9110ddbb1a","name":"Pedersen, Christian Nørgaard Storm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21332133"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/ci100437e","issn":["15499596","1549960X"],"issn_org":["15499596"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling","pages":"597-600","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953166860"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ad9c6430-71e9-4e0b-ba29-a276204334d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Using Inverted Indices for Accelerating LINGO Calculations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://loca