{"abstract":"De sidste mange år har vælgerbefolkningen været vidne til, at medierne har søgt bag om det politiske, ved at politiske kommentatorer analyserer, hvordan det politiske spil bør spilles, og hvem der bør spille med hvornår. En debat og debatten. Hvad betyder dette politiske teater for vælgeren? Denne artikel anlægger en alternativ tolkning på den akademiske diskurs. Ved at bruge et nyt analyseredskab – en associationsanalyse – anskueliggøres det, at befolkningen tager ved lære af eliternes diskussioner, og integrerer det i deres egen forståelse af det politiske landskab. Dette implicerer, at mange vælgere selv bliver politiske kommentatorer, i deres søgen efter en måde at skabe orden i en kompleks politisk virkelighed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Sigge Winther","Egeberg, Jesper de Hemmer","Larsen, Martin Vinæs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-498585"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vi er alle spindoktorer om konceptualisering og måling af andenordensvælgeren","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-498585","ids":["ku-b0061485-966c-4d7c-8005-dcbf11a8b5ba"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5CE27722589C5D195015031003995B08"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Sigge Winther","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5d11370f-e8bc-410e-83b2-34879c7c7745","name":"Nielsen, Sigge Winther","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper de Hemmer","key":"egebergpau","last":"Egeberg","locid":"e99da511-71b6-4b2e-b818-53eaaa218930","name":"Egeberg, Jesper de Hemmer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin Vinæs","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1a08c3-864c-4369-b58f-db4e5328818a","name":"Larsen, Martin Vinæs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00301906"],"issue":"1","journal":"Oekonomi og Politik","pages":"19-33","status":"p","title":"Oekonomi og Politik","volume":"84"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b0061485-966c-4d7c-8005-dcbf11a8b5ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Vi er alle spindoktorer : Om konceptualisering og måling af andenordensvælgeren","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-498585","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Tang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503121"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gud og mammon kristendom og rigdom","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-503121","ids":["ku-b7b25113-b85d-40eb-ad9c-2d1ec063fa19"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7B6E7F0CDF762C56AFBCA614E3CE5051"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Sections on Theology - Technical area, Section of Biblical Exegesis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Tang","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1ac9f31d-217b-44d0-a29a-4034f49f415b","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Tang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01066749"],"issue":"124","journal":"Kritisk Forum for Praktisk Teologi","pages":"16-25","status":"p","title":"Kritisk Forum for Praktisk Teologi"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b7b25113-b85d-40eb-ad9c-2d1ec063fa19"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gud og Mammon : Kristendom og rigdom","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503121","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The protein MOG1 is a cofactor of the cardiac sodium channel, Nav1.5. Overexpression of MOG1 in Nav1.5-expressing cells increases sodium current markedly. Mutations in the genes encoding Nav1.5 and its accessory proteins have been associated with cardiac arrhythmias of significant clinical impact. We sought to investigate whether MOG1 is implicated in cardiac arrhythmias. METHODS: We performed a genetic screening of the MOG1-encoding gene (gene symbol RANGRF, alias MOG1) in 220 Danish patients with cardiac arrhythmia. Of the 220, 197 were young patients with lone atrial fibrillation and 23 were patients with Brugada syndrome. The effect of one variant was investigated functionally by patch-clamping CHO-K1 cells coexpressing Nav1.5 with MOG1. RESULTS: We uncovered a novel heterozygous nonsense variant, c.181G>T (p.E61X), that, however, was also present in control subjects, albeit at a lower frequency (1.8% vs 0.4%, P = 0.078). Electrophysiological investigation showed that the p.E61X variant completely eliminates the sodium current-increasing effect of MOG1 and thereby causes loss of function in the sodium current. When mimicking heterozygosity by coexpression of Nav1.5 with wild-type MOG1 and p.E61X-MOG1, no current decrease was seen. CONCLUSIONS: Our screening of Nav1.5 cofactor MOG1 uncovered a novel nonsense variant that appeared to be present at a higher frequency among patients than control subjects. This variant causes MOG1 loss of function and therefore might be disease causing or modifying under certain conditions.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Olesen, Morten S","Jensen, Niels F","Holst, Anders G","Nielsen, Jonas B","Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","Jespersen, Thomas","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Haunsø, Stig","Lund, Jens T","Calloe, Kirstine","Schmitt, Nicole","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527819"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel nonsense variant in nav000000000001 000000000005 cofactor mog000000000001 eliminates its sodium current increasing effect and may increase the risk of arrhythmias","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cjca.2011.01.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-527819","identifier":[{"id":"80955179504","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21621375","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e0eb587b-9a06-4e0c-9859-a5d418f66c64"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-717C6A86E38DCE0CC14E626587382C91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cjca.2011.01.003","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Morten S","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Morten S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels F","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Niels F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders G","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"8676b11a-536a-4ada-906e-c39eaac492f3","name":"Holst, Anders G","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","locid":"bdd29054-7062-428a-a97d-e32cb8d80d38","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-3895-9316","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"db23d6cb-3abe-4ba2-b1d3-44f918c72e51","name":"Jespersen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6575-360X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig","key":"haunsøpau","last":"Haunsø","locid":"2d7a08cf-874a-4f9e-8964-e9c473cecd38","name":"Haunsø, Stig","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens T","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Jens T","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine","key":"calloepau","last":"Calloe","locid":"9fc39d74-d0ac-4774-b837-de97103c87f0","name":"Calloe, Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-1777-7938","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole","key":"schmittpau","last":"Schmitt","locid":"942c887c-32b0-4e89-812f-a11edf2505a5","name":"Schmitt, Nicole","orcid":"0000-0001-9482-9749","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Hastrup","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"d80910cf-2f9c-457c-9e85-34b4b258bb81","name":"Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-8515","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21621375"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cjca.2011.01.003","issn":["0828282X","19167075"],"issn_org":["0828282X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Canadian Journal of Cardiology","status":"p","title":"Canadian Journal of Cardiology","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80955179504"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e0eb587b-9a06-4e0c-9859-a5d418f66c64"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Novel Nonsense Variant in Nav1.5 Cofactor MOG1 Eliminates Its Sodium Current Increasing Effect and May Increase the Risk of Arrhythmias","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527819","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
