,"name":"Birgens, Henrik Sverre","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claus Henrik","key":"nielsenclaushenrikpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8caf59ab-44ff-4d9a-a722-8dd317bbd8b9","name":"Nielsen, Claus Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7543-9016","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ove Juul","key":"nielsenovejuulpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4fab2337-a477-4451-82f1-033699fd8fba","name":"Nielsen, Ove Juul","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"stentoftjesperpau","last":"Stentoft","name":"Stentoft, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans Carl","key":"hasselbalchhanscarlpau","last":"Hasselbalch","name":"Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","orcid":"0000-0003-3936-8032","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21262171"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"4","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"271-4","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"173"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79551516947"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9359555e-ca57-4dad-9aaa-e3bed79f756a","sdu-2d7abbf5-3f7c-42bf-b596-a7f2b75d115d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Nye behandlingsmuligheder ved primær immun trombocytopeni","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.68-044474","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"We present a method with fusion of images of three modalities 18F-FDG PET, CT, and 3-D ultrasound (US) applied to imaging of the anal canal and the rectum. To obtain comparable geometries in the three imaging modalities, a plexiglas rod, with the same dimensions as the US transducer, is placed in the anal canal prior to the PET-CT examination. The method is based on manual co-registration of PET-CT images and 3-D US images. The three-modality imaging of the rectum-anal canal may become useful as a supplement to conventional imaging in the external radiation therapy in the treatment of anal cancer, where the precise delineation of a tumor is crucial to avoid damage from radiation therapy to the healthy tissue surrounding it. The technique is still in a phase of development, and the demands for integration different company software systems are significant before commercial application. Three-modality imaging may also be used in certain other diagnostic or therapeutic fields.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Udesen, Jesper","Ewertsen, Caroline","Gran, Fredrik","Fogh Christensen, Anders","Kjaer-Kristoffersen, Flemming","Engelholm, Svend Aage","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann"],"cuid":["S02-093.32-033208"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Image fusion","PET CT","Ultrasound"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultrasonography fused with pet ct hybrid imaging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2174/157340511796411159","version":"Other Version"},"id