{"abstract":"Two of the most important algorithms for Hidden Markov Models are the forward and the Viterbi algorithms. We show how formulating these using linear algebra naturally lends itself to parallelization. Although the obtained algorithms are slow for Hidden Markov Models with large state spaces, they require very little communication between processors, and are fast in practice on models with a small state space. We have tested our implementation against two other imple- mentations on artificial data and observe a speed-up of roughly a factor of 5 for the forward algorithm and more than 6 for the Viterbi algorithm. We also tested our algorithm in the Coalescent Hidden Markov Model framework, where it gave a significant speed-up.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Sand, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237603"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithms for a parallel implementation of hidden markov models with a small state space","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/IPDPS.2011.181","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-237603","identifier":[{"id":"83455249877","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bda59ab8-faa2-4833-863b-7fc7ab68ddef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26FA498721F24FC2F56E02B9BCE99C55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/IPDPS.2011.181","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"81bd45f3-9a63-4c7c-9e55-bb00c43a907f","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","locid":"1ab8312b-c404-4d3a-9ca6-e07df9317abe","name":"Sand, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ipdps.2011.181","pages":"447-454","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"2011 IEEE IPDPS Workshops &amp; PhD Forum"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-83455249877"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bda59ab8-faa2-4833-863b-7fc7ab68ddef"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Algorithms for a parallel implementation of Hidden Markov Models with a small state space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-237603","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Fredshavn, Jesper Reinholt","Ejrnæs, Rasmus","Damgaard, Christian","Nielsen, Knud Erik","Nygaard, Bettina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253362"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"terrestriske habitatnaturtyper 000000002004 000000002010 novana","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www2.dmu.dk/Pub/SR7.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253362","ids":["au-d9474066-f583-4925-a9b6-2476af1d1a01"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E4EF47456CE6AB524DE86675F9B5FF93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www2.dmu.dk/Pub/SR7.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Biodiversity and Conservation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Reinholt","key":"fredshavnpau","last":"Fredshavn","locid":"9f888959-fcb1-4488-94f0-7faffc1a3303","name":"Fredshavn, Jesper Reinholt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"ejrnæspau","last":"Ejrnæs","locid":"de0d0e9b-b9f3-46a7-9a70-ed6e45dba8d8","name":"Ejrnæs, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Erik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b349ca79-38d0-4c9b-84d2-7eb4defb1240","name":"Nielsen, Knud Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bettina","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"68c147bf-e9bf-4693-8da5-69f0faac544c","name":"Nygaard, Bettina","orcid":"0000-0003-3335-9397","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"7","pages":"168","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 7","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d9474066-f583-4925-a9b6-2476af1d1a01"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Terrestriske habitatnaturtyper 2004-2010 : NOVANA","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253362","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The Hidden Markov Model (HMM) is a probabilistic model used widely in the fields of Bioinformatics and Speech Recognition. Efficient algorithms for solving the most common problems are well known, yet they all have a running time that is quadratic in the number of hidden states, which can be problematic for models with very large state spaces. The Viterbi algorithm is used to find the maximum likelihood hidden state sequence, and it has earlier been shown that a coarse-to-fine modification can significantly speed up this algorithm on some models. We propose combining work on a k-best version of Viterbi algorithm with the coarse-to-fine framework. This algorithm may be used to approximate the total likelihood of the model, or to evaluate the goodness of the Viterbi path on very large models.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-257025"],"event":{"end":"2011-06-29","place":"Palermo, it","start":"2011-06-27","title":"22nd Annual Symposium on Combinatorial Pattern Matching. CPM 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hidden Markov models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a coarse to fine approach to computing the em k em best viterbi paths","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-21458-5_32","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-257025","identifier":[{"id":"79960102165","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dfb53ca2-caa3-4399-8c8c-810530e4b6e4"],"keyword":["Hidden Markov Models","Viterbi","coarse-to-fine","k-best"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-19BD70E1FC61072F8ECEF2BEB500AB96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-21458-5_32","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"81bd45f3-9a63-4c7c-9e55-bb00c43a907f","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-21458-5_32","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"376-387","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"6661"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960102165"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dfb53ca2-caa3-4399-8c8c-810530e4b6e4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Coarse-to-Fine Approach to Computing the <em>k</em>-best Viterbi Paths","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-257025","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
