{"abstract":"A photonic nanowire single-photon source design incorporating an inverted conical tapering is proposed. The inverted taper allows for easy electrical contacting and a high photon extraction efficiency of 89 %. Unlike cavity-based approaches, the photonic nanowire features broadband spontaneous emission control and an improved tolerance towards fabrication imperfections.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gregersen, Niels","Nielsen, Torben Roland","Mørk, Jesper","Claudon, Julien","Gérard, Jean-Michel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335278"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-08","place":"Rome, it","start":"2011-09-05","title":"11th International Conference on Numerical Simulation of Optoelectronic Devices","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CNRS"],"keyword":["Electrical pumping","Inverted conical tapering","Photonic nanowire","Single photon source"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high efficiency photonic nanowire single photon source featuring an inverted conical taper","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/NUSOD.2011.6041136","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335278","identifier":[{"id":"80054958045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-66d14437-9094-4b00-9a4e-81a547c61863"],"keyword":["Electrical pumping","Inverted conical tapering","Photonic nanowire","Single-photon source"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BBA6DF9311BE191D8CCF419E0970DDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5830452/Version%201.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nusod.org/2011/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/NUSOD.2011.6041136","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"cnrs","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CNRS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"9cfafcdc-b007-48d7-aba2-caae5fedc1e6","name":"Gregersen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-8252-8989","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Roland","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d00af887-eee2-4b25-9c31-ff4893a61c4b","name":"Nielsen, Torben Roland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julien","key":"claudonpau","last":"Claudon","name":"Claudon, Julien","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean-Michel","key":"gérardpau","last":"Gérard","name":"Gérard, Jean-Michel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/nusod.2011.6041136","isbn":["9781612848761"],"pages":"5-6","status":"p","title":"2011 11th International Conference on Numerical Simulation of Optoelectronic Devices (NUSOD)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054958045"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-66d14437-9094-4b00-9a4e-81a547c61863"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A High-Efficiency Photonic Nanowire Single-Photon Source Featuring An Inverted Conical Taper","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335278","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A microscopic theory is used to study the dynamical properties of semiconductor quantum dot based nanocavity laser systems. The carrier kinetics and photon populations are determined using a fully quantum mechanical treatment of the light‐matter coupling. In this work, we investigate the dependency of the modulation response in such devices on the number of emitters coupled to the cavity mode. (© 2011 WILEY‐VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim)","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lorke, Michael","Nielsen, Torben Roland","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339164"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nanocavity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dependence of the modulation response of quantum dot based nanocavity devices on the number of emitters","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pssc.201000820","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339164","identifier":[{"id":"79953742956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-73f2d8f7-5dae-4e53-88b4-1f69c536af82"],"keyword":["Modulation bandwidth","Nanocavity","Quantum dot laser"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96B2178C03A091ACD5361F913CEBF613"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pssc.201000820","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/pssc.201000820/abstract","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"lorkepau","last":"Lorke","locid":"3c7a6163-8340-4232-844d-6ec362ef4116","name":"Lorke, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Roland","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d00af887-eee2-4b25-9c31-ff4893a61c4b","name":"Nielsen, Torben Roland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pssc.201000820","issn":["16101642","18626351"],"issn_org":["18626351"],"issue":"4","journal":"Physica Status Solidi. C: Current Topics in Solid State Physics","pages":"1145-1148","publisher":"Wiley - VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","publisher_org":"Wiley - V C H Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","status":"p","title":"Physica Status Solidi. C: Current Topics in Solid State Physics","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953742956"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-73f2d8f7-5dae-4e53-88b4-1f69c536af82"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dependence of the modulation response of quantum dot based nanocavity devices on the number of emitters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-339164","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Theoretical investigations of the switch-on behavior of semiconductor quantum dot based nanocavity laser devices are presented. From a microscopic treatment of the carrier-carrier and carrier-photon interaction, we find a fast switch-on of the laser device that is enabled by ultrafast carrier dynamics and heavily damped relaxation oscillations. We show that the timescales of the dynamics within the continuum states and the quantum dot states are strongly coupled and investigate the time dependence of the non-equilibrium scattering rates in detail. (C) 2011 American Institute of Physics. [doi:10.1063/1.3651765]","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lorke, Michael","Nielsen, Torben Roland","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347319"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"switch on dynamics of nanocavity laser devices","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6232873/2D498d01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-347319","identifier":[{"id":"80055010564","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8f4ca49b-0c7b-4c47-b983-ee9411397e6e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6810CFC624FB53CC924AC6619393C76B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.3651765","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6232873/2D498d01.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Quantum and Laser Photonics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"lorkepau","last":"Lorke","locid":"3c7a6163-8340-4232-844d-6ec362ef4116","name":"Lorke, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Roland","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d00af887-eee2-4b25-9c31-ff4893a61c4b","name":"Nielsen, Torben Roland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/1.3651765","issn":["00036951","10773118"],"issn_org":["00036951"],"issue":"15","journal":"Applied Physics Letters","pages":"151110","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Applied Physics Letters","volume":"99"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80055010564"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8f4ca49b-0c7b-4c47-b983-ee9411397e6e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Switch-on dynamics of nanocavity laser devices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347319","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
