{"abstract":"Generalized polarization (GP) microscopy represents an excellent tool to study lipid–lipid and lipid–protein interactions in situ and in vitro. Here, we present an efficient and cost effective method to perform GP microscopy using a standard light-emitting diode (LED) epifluorescence microscope equipped with a digital color camera.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Jesper Søndergaard","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-374467"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Epifluorescence","Generalized polarization","Giant unilamellar vesicles","Microscopy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an epifluorescence microscopy method for generalized polarization imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.10.138","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-374467","identifier":[{"id":"84855883155","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e99cdfe3-83f8-45c7-a1a4-d91d783388a4"],"keyword":["Epifluorescence","Generalized polarization","Giant unilamellar vesicles","Microscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A346D136B613D38E92436B128F075AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.10.138","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Søndergaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c5652107-7bb4-420d-86cf-520d1eba7924","name":"Hansen, Jesper Søndergaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"helixnielsenpau","last":"Helix Nielsen","locid":"bea497c9-caba-420a-81f8-8f2730634b31","name":"Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","name_org":"Helix Nielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-9392-7133","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.10.138","issn":["0006291X","10902104"],"issn_org":["0006291X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications","pages":"686-690","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications","volume":"415"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855883155"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e99cdfe3-83f8-45c7-a1a4-d91d783388a4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"An epifluorescence microscopy method for generalized polarization imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-374467","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Reconstitution of functionally active membrane protein into artificially made lipid bilayers is a challenge that must be overcome to create a membrane-based biomimetic sensor and separation device. In this study we address the efficacy of proteoliposome fusion with planar membrane arrays. We establish a protein incorporation efficacy assay using the major non-specific porin of Fusobacterium nucleatum (FomA) as reporter. We use electrical conductance measurements and fluorescence microscopy to characterize proteoliposome fusion with an array of planar membranes. We show that protein reconstitution in biomimetic membrane arrays may be quantified using the developed FomA assay. Specifically, we show that FomA vesicles are inherently fusigenic. Optimal FomA incorporation is obtained with a proteoliposome lipid-to-protein molar ratio (LPR)=50 more than 105 FomA proteins could be incorporated in a bilayer array with a total membrane area of 2mm2 within 20min. This novel assay for quantifying protein delivery into lipid bilayers may be a useful tool in developing biomimetic membrane applications.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pszon-Bartosz, Kamila Justyna","Hansen, Jesper S.","Stibius, Karin B.","Groth, Jesper S.","Emnéus, Jenny","Geschke, Oliver","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379193"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fusion","Membranes","Outer membrane protein","Vesicles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessing the efficacy of vesicle fusion with planar membrane arrays using a mitochondrial porin as reporter","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.02.001","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379193","identifier":[{"id":"79952191783","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f9688343-1b5b-497d-8e5a-fd8dc26428ac"],"keyword":["Fusion","Membranes","Outer membrane protein","Vesicles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D99302C99043DDD0D6929203BAAC19E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.02.001","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Polymer Micro and Nano Engineering Section","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Polymer Micro and Nano Engineering Section, Polymeric Enabling Microsystems Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Aquaporin A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kamila Justyna","key":"pszonbartoszpau","last":"Pszon-Bartosz","locid":"da32bc51-e274-4b05-a91d-63017d439c4a","name":"Pszon-Bartosz, Kamila Justyna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin B.","key":"stibiuspau","last":"Stibius","name":"Stibius, Karin B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S.","key":"grothpau","last":"Groth","name":"Groth, Jesper S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jenny","key":"emnéuspau","last":"Emnéus","locid":"43e43e53-3691-442c-9aca-2793521452e5","name":"Emnéus, Jenny","orcid":"0000-0002-8061-201X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"geschkepau","last":"Geschke","locid":"1a8f261f-b013-4046-92f8-82086d82329d","name":"Geschke, Oliver","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"helixnielsenpau","last":"Helix Nielsen","locid":"bea497c9-caba-420a-81f8-8f2730634b31","name":"Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","name_org":"Helix Nielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-9392-7133","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.02.001","issn":["0006291X","10902104"],"issn_org":["0006291X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications","pages":"96-100","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications","volume":"406"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952191783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","aquaporin a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f9688343-1b5b-497d-8e5a-fd8dc26428ac"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assessing the efficacy of vesicle fusion with planar membrane arrays using a mitochondrial porin as reporter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379193","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The purpose of the study was to evaluate unenhanced Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) for the diagnosis of appendicitis or another surgery-requiring condition in an adult population scheduled for emergency appendectomy based on a clinical diagnosis of suspected acute appendicitis. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The prospective study included 48 consecutive patients (29 female, 19 male, 18-70 years old, mean age=37.1 years). MRI examination was designed to be comfortable and fast; no contrast was administered. The sequences were performed during quiet respiration. The MRI findings were reviewed by two radiologists and one surgeon independent of each other and compared with surgical and pathological records. RESULTS: According to the surgical and histopathological findings 30 of 48 patients (63%) had acute appendicitis. Of the remaining 18 patients, 4 patients had no reasons for the clinical symptoms and 14 patients had other pathology. For the three reviewers the performance of MRI in the diagnosis of acute appendicitis showed the following sensitivity, specificity and accuracy ranges: 83-93%, 50-83% and 77-83%. Moderate (kappa=0.51) and fair (kappa=0.31) interobserver agreements in the MR diagnosis of acute appendicitis were found between the reviewers. Sensitivity, specificity and accuracy values for overall performance of MRI in detecting pelvic abnormalities were 100%, 75% (3 of 4 healthy patients were identified by MRI) and 98%, respectively. CONCLUSION: Unenhanced fast MRI is feasible as an additional fast screening before the appendectomy. It may prevent unnecessary surgeries. The fast MRI examination can be adequately performed on an MRI unit of broad range of field strengths","author_count":10,"contributors":["Chabanova, Elizaveta","Balslev, Ingegerd","Achiam, Michael Patrick","Nielsen, Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","Adamsen, S","Gocht-Jensen, Peter","Brisling, Steffen K","Løgager, Vibeke Berg","Thomsen, Henrik S","Logager, Vibeke B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434492"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unenhanced mr imaging in adults with clinically suspected acute appendicitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2010.03.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434492","identifier":[{"id":"80052147207","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-44bcfedd-57d5-41d0-91ca-7525681dc3f4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-70EB70A429537B3D53E87DEEFAA9D010"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejrad.2010.03.007","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Diagnostic Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Elizaveta","key":"chabanovapau","last":"Chabanova","name":"Chabanova, Elizaveta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingegerd","key":"balslevpau","last":"Balslev","locid":"df50ab09-a9f1-4142-a2a4-8a0060e5ddbc","name":"Balslev, Ingegerd","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"achiampau","last":"Achiam","locid":"dfd48120-815f-4309-a218-ca71a476dfda","name":"Achiam, Michael Patrick","name_org":"Achiam, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yousef Jesper Wirenfeldt","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"41cd192