{"abstract":"We report the synthesis of two C4'-modified DNA analogues and characterize their structural impact on dsDNA duplexes. The 4'-C-piperazinomethyl modification stabilizes dsDNA by up to 5°C per incorporation. Extension of the modification with a butanoyl-linked pyrene increases the dsDNA stabilization to a maximum of 9°C per incorporation. Using fluorescence, ultraviolet and nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy, we show that the stabilization is achieved by pyrene intercalation in the dsDNA duplex. The pyrene moiety is not restricted to one intercalation site but rather switches between multiple sites in intermediate exchange on the NMR timescale, resulting in broad lines in NMR spectra. We identified two intercalation sites with NOE data showing that the pyrene prefers to intercalate one base pair away from the modified nucleotide with its linker curled up in the minor groove. Both modifications are tolerated in DNA:RNA hybrids but leave their melting temperatures virtually unaffected. Fluorescence data indicate that the pyrene moiety is residing outside the helix. The available data suggest that the DNA discrimination is due to (i) the positive charge of the piperazino ring having a greater impact in the narrow and deep minor groove of a B-type dsDNA duplex than in the wide and shallow minor groove of an A-type DNA:RNA hybrid and (ii) the B-type dsDNA duplex allowing the pyrene to intercalate and bury its apolar surface.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Skov, Joan","Bryld, Torsten","Lindegaard, Dorthe","Nielsen, Katrine E","Højland, Torben","Wengel, Jesper","Petersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598226"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Department of Physics and Chemistry"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthesis and structural characterization of piperazino modified dna that favours hybridization towards dna over rna","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkq1123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-598226","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3061067","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"79953132000","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21062815","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-575c13fa-55c5-4775-a9d1-efefd0d1cf5e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3A69CF3CEF8843E814E06F8171ECCA6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkq1123","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Physics and Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy, Nucleic Acid Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joan","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Joan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Torsten","key":"bryldpau","last":"Bryld","locid":"20218ff1-7490-4c64-8c03-1aa9e1c8231b","name":"Bryld, Torsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"77d00c20-3c42-45d5-b568-7bd8f857e4cc","name":"Lindegaard, Dorthe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine E","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a53981eb-9501-4dac-afbe-e9dd342b3191","name":"Nielsen, Katrine E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"højlandpau","last":"Højland","locid":"f7fa7213-531a-49ad-bee0-fd6bf9038d7e","name":"Højland, Torben","orcid":"0000-0003-3087-4262","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"wengelpau","last":"Wengel","locid":"4803676b-fbaf-4593-baab-147b5465bbec","name":"Wengel, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-9835-1009","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"8d2f15c4-0741-4268-9425-dec4e02e37a6","name":"Petersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-0997-7657","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21062815"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkq1123","issn":["03051048","13624962"],"issn_org":["03051048"],"issue":"5","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","pages":"1953-65","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nucleic Acids Research","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953132000"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-575c13fa-55c5-4775-a9d1-efefd0d1cf5e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Synthesis and structural characterization of piperazino-modified DNA that favours hybridization towards DNA over RNA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598226","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Storage of skin at low temperatures may affect its structure. There is no report in the literature on the correlation between spatially resolved skin structure and percutaneous penetration after different storage conditions. The present study applies imaging techniques (multiphoton excitation fluorescence microscopy) and in vitro percutaneous penetration of caffeine under four different storage conditions using skin samples from the same donors: fresh skin, skin kept at -20°C for 3 weeks (with or without the use of polyethylene glycol) and at -80°C. Our results show a correlation between increasing permeation of caffeine and tissue structural damage caused by the storage conditions, most so after skin storage at -80°C. The presented approach, which combines imaging techniques with studies on percutaneous penetration, enables the link between tissue damage at selected depths and penetration into the upper layers of the epidermis to be investigated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Plasencia Gil, Maria Inés","Sørensen, Jens Ahm","Bagatolli, Luis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616332"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Caffeine","Human skin","Percutaneous penetration","Skin structure","Storage conditions"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"storage conditions of skin affect tissue structure and subsequent in vitro percutaneous penetration","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000322304","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-616332","identifier":[{"id":"78650661958","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21196813","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-96975a90-ebfa-49f1-a858-2fe3683186e2"],"keyword":["Caffeine","Human skin","Percutaneous penetration","Skin structure","Storage conditions","Teo-photon excitation flourescence microscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D30C6F8804D9BF377229B73DCD268E64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000322304","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Inés","key":"plasenciagilpau","last":"Plasencia Gil","locid":"e3ccd9b3-dd70-499b-91ef-9129a60c49f2","name":"Plasencia Gil, Maria Inés","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"bagatollipau","last":"Bagatolli","locid":"5c7b925a-6819-41b0-b533-ab27a1d56277","name":"Bagatolli, Luis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21196813"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000322304","issn":["16605527","16605535"],"issn_org":["16605527"],"issue":"2","journal":"Skin Pharmacology and Physiology","pages":"93-102","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Skin Pharmacology and Physiology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78650661958"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-96975a90-ebfa-49f1-a858-2fe3683186e2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Storage Conditions of Skin Affect Tissue Structure and Subsequent in vitro Percutaneous Penetration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616332","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Holten-Andersen L, Thaysen-Andersen M, Jensen SB, Buchwald C, Højrup P, Offenberg H, Nielsen HJ, Brünner N, Nauntofte B, Reibel J. Salivary tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases-1 localization and glycosylation profile analysis. APMIS 2011; 119: 741-9. Salivary tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases-1 (TIMP-1) has been associated with pathological conditions in the oral cavity, but the origin of TIMP-1 in saliva remains unknown. Hence, we studied the localization of TIMP-1 in salivary gland tissue and also investigated if TIMP-1 found in blood and saliva is identical. Human salivary gland tissue samples (four parotid gland and four submandibular gland biopsies) were analysed for the presence of TIMP-1 mRNA and protein expression. To assess TIMP-1 glycosylation profiles in blood and saliva, the protein was isolated from plasma and unstimulated and stimulated whole saliva as well as stimulated parotid and submandibular saliva and analysed by MALDI-TOF mass spectrometry. TIMP-1 protein was demonstrated in mucous acinar cells of the submandibular gland and in ductal cells of both the parotid and submandibular gland. However, no TIMP-1 mRNA was detected in any of these cells. The glycosylation profiles of TIMP-1 isolated from whole saliva and saliva from the major glands were highly similar. In contrast, a significant difference was found between the glycoprofiles of salivary TIMP-1 and plasma TIMP-1. Although no clear evidence of TIMP-1 transcription in major salivary glands was demonstrated our results suggest that TIMP-1 in saliva does not originate from plasma.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Holten-Andersen, Lars","Thaysen-Andersen, Morten","Jensen, Siri Beier","von Buchwald, Christian","Højrup, Peter","Offenberg, Hanne Kjær","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Brünner, Nils","Nauntofte, Birgitte","Reibel, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-081.63-666956"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salivary tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases 000000000001 localization and glycosylation profile analysis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0463.2011.02796.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.63-666956","identifier":[{"id":"21995626","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860406723","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bed38827-5314-4711-997f-4eb28bb874b0","sdu-87b21b30-4dca-4568-97dd-f54153e03bd5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C59C6121B60C676DCC2A4D53E331BC2B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0463.2011.02796.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"holtenandersenpau","last":"Holten-Andersen","locid":"5fb32793-18a4-41bf-a893-93397b7de131","name":"Holten-Andersen, Lars","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"thaysenandersenpau","last":"Thaysen-Andersen","name":"Thaysen-Andersen, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Siri Beier","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ddb01352-fd78-4715-9ae7-38f2b9625814","name":"Jensen, Siri Beier","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"buchwaldpau","last":"Buchwald","name":"Buchwald, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"højruppau","last":"Højrup","locid":"1dc527ba-e681-4af1-88fb-6383c95d07b7","name":"Højrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7838-6180","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Kjær","key":"offenbergpau","last":"Offenberg","locid":"cfcc26d2-97f3-4fb0-aba4-fc60ea0da3ba","name":"Offenberg, Hanne Kjær","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils","key":"brünnerpau","last":"Brünner","locid":"0e935a59-f9ff-4d0d-8c60-8a74a558e6aa","name":"Brünner, Nils","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"nauntoftepau","last":"Nauntofte","locid":"941090d0-de49-41a8-8ad7-abed7ab86175","name":"Nauntofte, Birgitte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"reibelpau","last":"Reibel","locid":"c72c1380-d82c-43d5-8d78-73c435cf2158","name":"Reibel, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-5644-7707","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21995626"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1600-0463.2011.02796.x","issn":["09034641","0903465X"],"issn_org":["09034641"],"issue":"11","journal":"APMIS","pages":"741-749","status":"p","title":"APMIS","title_org":"A P M I S. Acta Pathologica, Microbiologica et Immunologica Scandinavica","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860406723"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bed38827-5314-4711-997f-4eb28bb874b0","sdu-87b21b30-4dca-4568-97dd-f54153e03bd5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Salivary tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases-1 localization and glycosylation profile analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.63-666956","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, more than 60 small RNAs (sRNAs) have been identified in the gram-positive human pathogen Listeria monocytogenes, but their putative roles and mechanisms of action remain largely unknown. The sRNA LhrA was recently shown to be a post-transcriptional regulator of a single gene, lmo0850, which encodes a small protein of unknown function. LhrA controls the translation and degradation of the lmo0850 mRNA by an antisense mechanism, and it depends on the RNA chaperone Hfq for efficient binding to its target. In the present study, we sought to gain more insight into the functional role of LhrA in L. monocytogenes. To this end, we determined the effects of LhrA on global-wide gene expression. We observed that nearly 300 genes in L. monocytogenes are either positively or negatively affected by LhrA. Among these genes, we identified lmo0302 and chiA as direct targets of LhrA, thus establishing LhrA as a multiple target regulator. Lmo0302 encodes a hypothetical protein with no known function, whereas chiA encodes one of two chitinases present in L. monocytogenes. We show here that LhrA acts as a post-transcriptional regulator of lmo0302 and chiA by interfering with ribosome recruitment, and we provide evidence that both LhrA and Hfq act to down-regulate the expression of lmo0302 and chiA. Furthermore, in vitro binding experiments show that Hfq stimulates the base pairing of LhrA to chiA mRNA. Finally, we demonstrate that LhrA has a negative effect on the chitinolytic activity of L. monocytogenes. In marked contrast to this, we found that Hfq has a stimulating effect on the chitinolytic activity, suggesting that Hfq plays multiple roles in the complex regulatory pathways controlling the chitinases of L. monocytogenes.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper S","Larsen, Marianne Halberg","Lillebæk, Eva Maria Sternkopf","Bergholz, Teresa M.","Christiansen, Mie H.G.","Boor, Kathryn J.","Wiedmann, Martin","Kallipolitis, Birgitte H."],"cuid":["S02-081.82-666808"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a small rna controls expression of the chitinase chia in em listeria monocytogenes em","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/37614605/journal.pone.0019019.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.82-666808","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3078929","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"21533114","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955156794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2d4d9845-f89f-47a8-ade8-3a6686b323b9","sdu-87229a28-2629-4abe-a74f-1d756d91defa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-24FC21C8E5990C587382E54A9ED53C64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0019019","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/37614605/journal.pone.0019019.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Sejrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a2d7d80-1252-4bf8-8a2a-651838e9464d","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne Halberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"da445e7f-59a6-4e1c-ad17-57e0e317ce6a","name":"Larsen, Marianne Halberg","orcid":"0000-0001-6242-6937","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Maria Sternkopf","key":"lillebækpau","last":"Lillebæk","locid":"03a71f8c-4e77-4b95-bcde-1d54020987ab","name":"Lillebæk, Eva Maria Sternkopf","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Teresa M.","key":"bergholzpau","last":"Bergholz","name":"Bergholz, Teresa M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie H. G.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Mie H. G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kathryn J.","key":"boorpau","last":"Boor","name":"Boor, Kathryn J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Martin","key":"wiedmannpau","last":"Wiedmann","name":"Wiedmann, Martin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte H.","key":"kallipolitispau","last":"Kallipolitis","locid":"642f37f4-0a2d-459b-8092-0f1b21bebb6d","name":"Kallipolitis, Birgitte H.","orcid":"0000-0003-1233-9776","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21533114"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0019019","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955156794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2d4d9845-f89f-47a8-ade8-3a6686b323b9","sdu-87229a28-2629-4abe-a74f-1d756d91defa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Small RNA Controls Expression of the Chitinase ChiA in <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.82-666808","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Biologic and clinical observations suggest that combining imatinib with IFN-α may improve treatment outcome in chronic myeloid leukemia (CML). We randomized newly diagnosed chronic-phase CML patients with a low or intermediate Sokal risk score and in imatinib-induced complete hematologic remission either to receive a combination of pegylated IFN-α2b (Peg-IFN-α2b) 50 μg weekly and imatinib 400 mg daily (n = 56) or to receive imatinib 400 mg daily monotherapy (n = 56). The primary endpoint was the major molecular response (MMR) rate at 12 months after randomization. In both arms, 4 patients (7%) discontinued imatinib treatment (1 because of blastic transformation in imatinib arm). In addition, in the combination arm, 34 patients (61%) discontinued Peg-IFN-α2b, most because of toxicity. The MMR rate at 12 months was significantly higher in the imatinib plus Peg-IFN-α2b arm (82%) compared with the imatinib monotherapy arm (54%; intention-to-treat, P = .002). The MMR rate increased with the duration of Peg-IFN-α2b treatment (<12-week MMR rate 67%, > 12-week MMR rate 91%). Thus, the addition of even relatively short periods of Peg-IFN-α2b to imatinib markedly increased the MMR rate at 12 months of therapy. Lower doses of Peg-IFN-α2b may enhance tolerability while retaining efficacy and could be considered in future protocols with curative intent.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Simonsson, Bengt","Gedde-Dahl, Tobias","Markevärn, Berit","Remes, Kari","Stentoft, Jesper","Almqvist, Anders","Björeman, Mats","Flogegård, Max","Koskenvesa, Perttu","Lindblom, Anders","Malm, Claes","Mustjoki, Satu","Myhr-Eriksson, Kristina","Ohm, Lotta","Räsänen, Anu","Sinisalo, Marjatta","Själander, Anders","Strömberg, Ulla","Bjerrum, Ole Weiss","Ehrencrona, Hans","Gruber, Franz","Kairisto, Veli","Olsson, Karin","Sandin, Fredrik","Nagler, Arnon","Nielsen, Johan Lanng","Hjorth-Hansen, Henrik","Porkka, Kimmo"],"cuid":["S02-087.68-013058"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Nordic CML Study Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combination of pegylated ifn α000000000002b with imatinib increases molecular response rates in patients with low or intermediate risk chronic myeloid leukemia","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1182/blood-2011-02-336685","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-087.68-013058","identifier":[{"id":"80053130415","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21685374","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0640b77d-9e79-4f9b-bdc6-889f4e9c2898","ku-aae2a11c-bcc5-456e-ad0a-ee669ad8f31d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FE17EDDA58D10AA7FFBA63544B00B09A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1182/blood-2011-02-336685","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"},{"affno":3,"key":"