,"first":"Kimmo","key":"porkkapau","last":"Porkka","name":"Porkka, Kimmo","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21685374"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1182/blood-2011-02-336685","issn":["00064971","15280020"],"issn_org":["00064971"],"issue":"12","journal":"Blood","pages":"3228-35","status":"p","title":"Blood","volume":"118"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80053130415"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0640b77d-9e79-4f9b-bdc6-889f4e9c2898","ku-aae2a11c-bcc5-456e-ad0a-ee669ad8f31d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combination of pegylated IFN-α2b with imatinib increases molecular response rates in patients with low- or intermediate-risk chronic myeloid leukemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.68-013058","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"DMUs konklusioner vedr. den økologiske risikovurdering af den genmodificerede DAS-68416-4 sojabønne i Danmark Den genmodificerede DAS-68416-4-sojabønne adskiller sig fra konventionelle sojabønner ved at have indsat gener der gør planterne tolerante over for herbiciderne 2,4-D og glufosinat. Sojabønnen søges kun godkendt til import og viderebearbejdning til bl.a. dyrefoder og fødevarer, men ikke til dyrkning eller opformering. Da importen formentlig vil foregå som levende frø er en spredning og formering potentielt mulig ved import- og bearbejdningssteder. DMU vurderer at DAS-68416-4-sojabønnen som alle andre sojabønner ikke kan etableres, spredes eller krydse med andre plantearter i dyrkede arealer eller i naturen i Danmark, da de klimatiske forhold udelukker dette. En markedsføring af sojabønnen kan derfor ikke have nogen uønskede økologiske konsekvenser i Danmark. I dyrkningsområderne i Sydeuropa kan der ved uheld ske en iblanding af GM-sojabønnefrø i frø til udsæd af ikke-GM soja. En eventuel tilfældig spredning af GM-soja vurderes dog ikke at få nogen uønskede økologiske konsekvenser. DMU vurderer samlet, at der ikke kan forventes nogen uønskede økologiske konsekvenser for dyre- og planteliv ved markedsføring af den genmodificerede herbicidtolerante DAS-68416-4-sojabønne til andre formål end dyrkning. Kommentarer til EFSA: DMU har ingen kommentarer til den foreliggende anmeldelse, der inkluderer import og industriel forarbejdning til foder og fødevarer, men ikke dyrkning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjellsson, Gøsta","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Strandberg, Morten Tune","Damgaard, Christian","Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd"],"cuid":["S02-090.82-026837"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"økologisk risikovurdering af genmodificeret dobbelt herbicidtolerant sojabønne linje das 000000068416 000000000004 i anmeldelse vedr markeds føring under forordning 000000000829 000000002003 ef era efsa gmo nl 000000002011 000000000091","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-090.82-026837","ids":["au-c319a9e9-0375-4fbb-b5ef-04331ccb877b","au-e2cb13c8-c44a-4dab-b68c-4f0c3d91fa70"],"keyword":["GMO","Risikovurdering","genmodificerede planter","Økologisk risikovurdering af GMO"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-95F39A16FDD4A2035F792689B1E3C185"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Soil Fauna Ecology and Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gøsta","key":"kjellssonpau","last":"Kjellsson","locid":"fded3903-57d2-4f72-ab5c-36d55e496537","name":"Kjellsson, Gøsta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Givskov","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Tune","key":"strandbergpau","last":"Strandberg","locid":"1408a1c4-4357-441c-9f3b-1e823aa69880","name":"Strandberg, Morten Tune","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-2350","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj-Britt Uhd","key":"nielsenped","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8212e441-2e87-482f-ad06-184f50830cec","name":"Nielsen, Maj-Britt Uhd","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c319a9e9-0375-4fbb-b5ef-04331ccb877b","au-e2cb13c8-c44a-4dab-b68c-4f0c3d91fa70"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Økologisk risikovurdering af genmodificeret dobbelt herbicidtolerant sojabønne linje DAS-68416-4 i anmeldelse vedr. markeds¬føring under Forord-ning 1829/2003/EF. : ERA: EFSA-GMO-NL-2011-91","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.82-026837","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Despite decades of research, the roles of climate and humans in driving the dramatic extinctions of large-bodied mammals during the Late Quaternary period remain contentious. Here we use ancient DNA, species distribution models and the human fossil record to elucidate how climate and humans shaped the demographic history of woolly rhinoceros, woolly mammoth, wild horse, reindeer, bison and musk ox. We show that climate has been a major driver of population change over the past 50,000 years. However, each species responds differently to the effects of climatic shifts, habitat redistribution and human encroachment. Although climate change alone can explain the extinction of some species, such as Eurasian musk ox and woolly rhinoceros, a combination of climatic and anthropogenic effects appears to be responsible for the extinction of others, including Eurasian steppe bison and wild horse. We find no genetic signature or any distinctive range dynamics distinguishing extinct from surviving species, emphasizing the challenges associated with predicting future responses of extant mammals to climate and human-mediated habitat change.","author_count":63,"contributors":["Lorenzen, Eline D","Nogués-Bravo, David","Orlando, Ludovic","Weinstock, Jaco","Binladen, Jonas","Marske, Katharine A","Ugan, Andrew","Borregaard, Michael Krabbe","Gilbert, M Thomas P","Nielsen, Rasmus","Ho, Simon Y W","Goebel, Ted","Graf, Kelly E","Byers, David","Stenderup, Jesper","Rasmussen, Morten Schnack","Campos, Paula","Leonard, Jennifer A","Koepfli, Klaus-Peter","Froese, Duane","Zazula, Grant","Stafford, Thomas W","Aaris-Sørensen, Kim","Batra, Persaram","Haywood, Alan M","Singarayer, Joy S","Valdes, Paul J","Boeskorov, Gennady","Burns, James A","Davydov, Sergey P","Haile, James","Jenkins, Dennis L","Kosintsev, Pavel","Kuznetsova, Tatyana","Lai, Xulong","Martin, Larry D","McDonald, H Gregory","Mol, Dick","Meldgaard, Morten","Munch, Kasper","Stephan, Elisabeth","Sablin, Mikhail","Sommer, Rob