{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Busch, Thomas","Christensen, Bent Jesper","Nielsen, Morten Ørregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-143337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of implied volatility in forecasting future realized volatility and jumps in foreign exchange stock and bond markets","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2010.03.014","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-143337","identifier":[{"id":"78649729950","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-18636a70-6cc1-11de-b2cc-000ea68e967b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-14A5C41C1D629DFACF0233E73E8D6541"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2010.03.014","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Danske Bank Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Social Sciences, School of Economics and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"buschpau","last":"Busch","name":"Busch, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bent Jesper","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"bbacbd2c-0350-430f-8190-189bab4c87de","name":"Christensen, Bent Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8448-9752","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Ørregaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5f9a0ff6-05a6-4a61-8bab-4d5bd71ba1d6","name":"Nielsen, Morten Ørregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1337-9844","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jeconom.2010.03.014","issn":["03044076","18726895"],"issn_org":["03044076"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Econometrics","pages":"48-57","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Econometrics","volume":"160"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78649729950"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","danske bank group"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-18636a70-6cc1-11de-b2cc-000ea68e967b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Role of Implied Volatility in Forecasting Future Realized Volatility and Jumps in Foreign Exchange, Stock, and Bond Markets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-143337","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A deniable cryptosystem allows a sender and a receiver to communicate over an insecure channel in such a way that the communication is still secure even if the adversary can threaten the parties into revealing their internal states after the execution of the protocol. This is done by allowing the parties to change their internal state to make it look like a given ciphertext decrypts to a message different from what it really decrypts to. Deniable encryption was in this way introduced to allow to deny a message exchange and hence combat coercion. Depending on which parties can be coerced, the security level, the flavor and the number of rounds of the cryptosystem, it is possible to define a number of notions of deniable encryption. In this paper we prove that there does not exist any non-interactive receiver-deniable cryptosystem with better than polynomial security. This also shows that it is impossible to construct a non-interactive bi-deniable public-key encryption scheme with better than polynomial security. Specifically, we give an explicit bound relating the security of the scheme to how efficient the scheme is in terms of key size. Our impossibility result establishes a lower bound on the security. As a final contribution we give constructions of deniable public-key encryption schemes which establishes upper bounds on the security in terms of key length. There is a gap between our lower and upper bounds, which leaves the interesting open problem of finding the tight bounds.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bendlin, Rikke","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Nordholt, Peter Sebastian","Orlandi, Claudio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-190400"],"event":{"end":"2011-12-08","place":"Seoul, kr","start":"2011-12-04","title":"17th International Conference on the Theory and Application of Cryptology and Information Security","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower and upper bounds for deniable public key encryption","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-25385-0_7","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-190400","identifier":[{"id":"82955177034","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6b02831d-ac71-48b8-8efd-bf0b7f514ca4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65618EAEF4C560DC00BCD891F49CA2D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-25385-0_7","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bendlinpau","last":"Bendlin","locid":"9a599417-e72a-429e-8103-9a3facc06253","name":"Bendlin, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Sebastian","key":"nordholtpau","last":"Nordholt","locid":"45ed0f2e-3f58-4839-b089-4ba3cd802323","name":"Nordholt, Peter Sebastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudio","key":"orlandipau","last":"Orlandi","locid":"393c3898-d32f-431e-aea6-ee1e79c535ef","name":"Orlandi, Claudio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-25385-0_7","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"125-142","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7073"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-82955177034"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6b02831d-ac71-48b8-8efd-bf0b7f514ca4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Lower and Upper Bounds for Deniable Public-Key Encryption","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-190400","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Attacks on classical cryptographic protocols are usually modeled by allowing an adversary to ask queries from an oracle. Security is then defined by requiring that as long as the queries satisfy some constraint, there is some problem the adversary cannot solve, such as compute a certain piece of information. In this paper, we introduce a fundamentally new model of quantum attacks on classical cryptographic protocols, where the adversary is allowed to ask several classical queries in quantum superposition. This is a strictly stronger attack than the standard one, and we consider the security of several primitives in this model. We show that a secret-sharing scheme that is secure with threshold $t$ in the standard model is secure against superposition attacks if and only if the threshold is lowered to $t/2$. We use this result to give zero-knowledge proofs for all of NP in the common reference string model. While our protocol is classical, it is sound against a cheating unbounded quantum prover and computational zero-knowledge even if the verifier is allowed a superposition attack. Finally, we consider multiparty computation and show that for the most general type of attack, simulation based security is not possible. However, putting a natural constraint on the adversary, we show a non-trivial example of a protocol that can indeed be simulated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","Funder, Jakob Løvstad","Nielsen, Jesper Buus","Salvail, Louis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-196942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"superposition attacks on cryptographic protocols","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.6313v1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-196942","ids":["au-765b4937-422b-409c-b85b-3c79cf231d30"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-707E74E4C376605504346D9EA506D117"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.6313v1","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://eprint.iacr.org/2011/421","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan Bjerre","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Løvstad","key":"funderpau","last":"Funder","locid":"805d727a-a998-4b0f-b236-9c77c306de1d","name":"Funder, Jakob Løvstad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis","key":"salvailpau","last":"Salvail","locid":"6521efa7-be6f-4031-9fb2-752d3944200b","name":"Salvail, Louis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"29","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-765b4937-422b-409c-b85b-3c79cf231d30"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Superposition Attacks on Cryptographic Protocols","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-196942","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This report investigates whether or not it would be possible to produce carbon-negative energy from pyrolysis of wheat straw in a series of Danish agricultural scenarios. A combination of process simulation in SuperPro Designer software, correlations derived from literature studies and experimental work, and overall balance calculations has been applied in the process. The study deviates from other studies of pyrolysis and biochar production by the inclusion of substitution energy impact on the overall carbon-balance. Substitution energy is integrated to account for the gap between the energy production from the pyrolysis and the full energy potential of the biomass, quantified by complete conversion in either combustion or gasification systems. It was concluded that it is feasible to produce carbon-negative energy under a variation of different settings, but also that the negative carbon-balance is only robust for the slow pyrolysis scenario. The CO2 benefit of the most carbon-negative slow pyrolysis process is estimated to be around 10 % of the atmospheric carbon stored in the original biomass when natural gas is applied for energy substitution. This process avoids the emission of around 150-200 kg CO2/ton wheat straw with substitution energy with a Denmark 2007 average carbon-intensity. This result is weighted against the net emissions of the carbon-“neutral” process of conventional combustion. This emission is in this report estimated to be around 50 – 150 kg CO2/ton straw depending on scenario settings. The final results of the study have been compared to another study with convincing results. Results concluded that the primary force of the pyrolysis technology is the recalcitrant char product and not the pyrolysis oil. Based on this, the study suggests that despite the trend in commercial pyrolysis technology that focuses on fast pyrolysis processes with maximized bio-oil production, the twin challenge of climate mitigation and sustainable energy production is most efficiently addressed with a combination of slow pyrolysis and complete biomass conversion through combustion or gasification instead.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","Bruun, Esben","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio systems","Biosystemer","Termisk forgasning af biomasse","Thermal gasification of biomass"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the potential of pyrolysis technology in climate change mitigation influence of process design and parameters simulated in superpro designer software","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5238026/ris-r-1764.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309337","ids":["dtu-0fc03a18-77f7-4d1f-a439-e27d002609af"],"keyword":["Bio systems","Biosystemer","Risø-R-1764","Risø-R-1764(EN)","Termisk forgasning af biomasse","Thermal gasification of biomass"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F624E616F0979830557B94C7E07EDFD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5238026/ris-r-1764.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division, Biomass Gasification"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f75a7756-932a-4066-8a74-8955f3f30f55","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","name_org":"Thomsen, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"hauggaardnielsenpau","last":"Hauggaard-Nielsen","locid":"ccc14efd-163a-46ec-865c-cdfd086c15fe","name":"Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"05e96380-5fac-440c-bff8-2c66a29b9d8b","name":"Bruun, Esben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788755038776"],"issn":["01062840"],"issue":"1764(EN)","pages":"115","place":"Roskilde","publisher":"Danmarks Tekniske Universitet, Risø Nationallaboratoriet for Bæredygtig Energi","repno":"Denmark. Forskningscenter Risoe. Risoe-R, 1764(EN)","series":"Denmark. Forskningscenter Risoe. Risoe-R","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0fc03a18-77f7-4d1f-a439-e27d002609af"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The potential of pyrolysis technology in climate change mitigation – influence of process design and –parameters, simulated in SuperPro Designer Software","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309337","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Multiple independent sensors are used in security and military applications in order to increase sensitivity, selectivity and data reliability. The Xsense project has been initiated at the Technical University of Denmark in collaboration with a number of partners in an effort to produce a handheld sensor for trace detection of explosives. We are using micro- and nano technological approaches for integrating four sensing principles into a single device. At the end of the project, the consortium aims at having delivered a sensor platform consisting of four independent detector principles capable of identifying concentrations of TNT, DNT, HMX and RDX at sub parts-per-billion (ppb) levels and with a false positive rate less than 1 parts-per-thousand. The specificity, sensitivity, reliability and the speed of responses are ensured by the use of advanced data processing, surface functionalization and nanostructured sensors and sensor design.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kostesha, Natalie","Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","Bosco, Filippo","Olsen, Jesper Kenneth","Johnsen, Carsten","Nielsen, Kent A","Jeppesen, Jan Oskar","Alstrøm, Tommy Sonne","Larsen, Jan","Thundat, Thomas","Jakobsen, Mogens Havsteen","Boisen, Anja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335860"],"event":{"end":"2011-02-24","place":"San Antonio, TX, us","start":"2011-02-22","title":"2011 IEEE Sensors Applications Symposium","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Alberta"],"keyword":["Chemical sensors","Explosives","Sensor arrays","Surface treatment","Temperature sensors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the xsense project the application of an intelligent sensor array for high sensitivity handheld explosives detectors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5624525/05739782%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335860","identifier":[{"id":"84884629123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-68ca0000-a091-41ea-ba31-d7b74f767adc"],"keyword":["Chemical sensors","Explosives","Sensor arrays","Surface treatment","Temperature sensors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A28C1880962BF44CFDAC2B27872486D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5624525/05739782%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SAS.2011.5739782","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, NanoSystemsEngineering Section","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, NanoSystemsEngineering Section, Nanoprobes Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of alberta","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Alberta","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"kosteshapau","last":"Kostesha","locid":"564c1c85-18e6-4d95-be56-25c8bfcae69d","name":"Kostesha, Natalie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stenbæk","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c47946d3-04a1-42d3-98f6-62ef38222262","name":"Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Filippo","key":"boscopau","last":"Bosco","locid":"e33b40d4-116a-4fe3-b581-6af81aef0039","name":"Bosco, Filippo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Kenneth","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"27588355-87f2-4792-af37-74e56dcbc862","name":"Olsen, Jesper Kenneth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kent A","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kent A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Oskar","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","name":"Jeppesen, Jan Oskar","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tommy Sonne","key":"alstrømpau","last":"Alstrøm","locid":"2c1b856d-1052-4f55-9980-0610fbb49cce","name":"Alstrøm, Tommy Sonne","orcid":"0000-0003-0941-3146","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"172b79ba-ccb1-4bea-8cd3-30dfd62f4624","name":"Larsen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-1880-1810","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"thundatpau","last":"Thundat","name":"Thundat, Thomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens Havsteen","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"2e09303d-f3ed-46f8-9124-272437651149","name":"Jakobsen, Mogens Havsteen","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-718X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/sas.2011.5739782","isbn":["9781424480630"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of IEEE Sensors Applications Symposium"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884629123"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-68ca0000-a091-41ea-ba31-d7b74f767adc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Xsense project: The application of an intelligent sensor array for high sensitivity handheld explosives detectors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335860","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Black lipid membrane (BLM) formation across apertures in an ethylene tetra-fluoroethylene (ETFE) partition separating two aqueous compartments is an established technique for the creation of biomimetic membranes. Recently multi-aperture BLM arrays have attracted interest and in order to increase BLM array stability we studied the effect of covalently modifying the partition substrate using surface plasma polymerization with hydrophobic n-hexene, 1-decene and hexamethyldisiloxane (HMDSO) as modification groups. Average lifetimes across singlesided HMDSO modified partitions or using 1-decene modified partitions were similar and significantly lower than for arrays formed using untreated ETFE partitions. For single side n-hexene modification average membrane array lifetimes were not significantly changed compared to untreated ETFE. Double-sided n-hexene modification greatly improved average membrane array lifetimes compared to membrane arrays formed across untreated ETFE partitions. n-hexene modifications resulted in BLM membrane arrays which over time developed significantly lower conductance (Gm) and higher capacitance (Cm) values compared to the other membranes with the strongest effect for double sided modification. n-hexene modification is evident as a change in surface energy whereas the surface roughness does not change significantly. The concomitant low Gm and high Cm values for BLM arrays formed using double-sided n-hexene modification enable transmembrane ionic current recordings with a high signal-to-noise (s/n) ratio. We demonstratesd this by reconstituting gA and α-hemolysin (α-HL) into BLM arrays. The improvement in membrane array lifetime and s/n ratio demonstrates that surface plasma polymerization of the supporting partition can be used to increase the stability of biomimetic membrane arrays.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Perry, Mark","Hansen, Jesper Schmidt","Jensen, Karin Bagger Stibius","Vissing, Thomas","Pszon-Bartosz, Kamila Justyna","Rein, Christian","Eshtehardi, Bahram","Benter, Maike","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346169"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surface modifications of support partitions for stabilizing biomimetic membrane arrays","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6353269/2155-9589-S1-001.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346169","ids":["dtu-8b704cad-6356-4528-ac72-e2d76ed917c6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D2EDB50BC117FFBC50ED0D51176A6857"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4172/2155-9589.S1-001","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.omicsonline.org/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6353269/2155-9589-S1-001.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Aquaporin A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of 