al.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350792","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Concerns that raisins may be contaminated by fumonisins stem from the persistent occurrence of Aspergillus niger spores on raisins and the recent discovery of fumonisin production by A. niger on grapes, which leads to the widespread occurrence of fumonisin B-2 in wine. This study presents an LC-MS/MS survey of fumonisins in retail raisins. In 10 of 21 brands collected in Denmark, Germany, and The Netherlands, fumonisins B-2 and B-4 were detected at levels up to 13 and 1.3 mu g/kg, respectively. Only fumonisin B-2 has been detected in wine, so the presence of fumonisin B-4 in raisins suggests that the fumonisins are produced mainly during the drying process concomitant with the decreasing water activity. Analysis of multiple packages from one manufacturer showed a 3-fold package-to-package variation, suggesting that a few raisins per package are contaminated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","Mogensen, Jesper Mølgaard","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Nielsen, Kristian Fog"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-361334"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cation exchange","Grapes","SPE","Solid phase extraction","Wine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"occurrence of furnonisins b000000000002 and b000000000004 in retail raisins","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/jf103855x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-361334","identifier":[{"id":"78751520953","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-be04233a-9246-46db-8f21-68b24fee42d2"],"keyword":["Cation exchange","Fumonisins B2 and B4","Grapes","SPE","Solid-phase extraction","Wine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A849F2F5428A871300982AF7BAD5C4C9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pubs.acs.org/journal/jafcau","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/jf103855x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Boldsen","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"991df7f2-a085-49ce-a926-da127ba3b28b","name":"Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Mølgaard","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"fe4663cc-9de6-4062-8273-37e893024049","name":"Mogensen, Jesper Mølgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Fog","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d2067ee9-e48c-4cf4-ac8f-ee775d8aff5a","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Fog","orcid":"0000-0002-5848-0911","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/jf103855x","issn":["00218561","15205118"],"issn_org":["00218561"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","pages":"772-776","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78751520953"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-be04233a-9246-46db-8f21-68b24fee42d2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Occurrence of Furnonisins B2 and B4 in Retail Raisins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-361334","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A number of methods for ultrasound vector velocity imaging are presented in the paper. The transverse oscillation (TO) method can estimate the velocity transverse to the ultrasound beam by introducing a lateral oscillation in the received ultrasound field. The approach has been thoroughly investigated using both simulations, flow rig measurements, and in-vivo validation against MR scans. The TO method obtains a relative accuracy of 10% for a fully transverse flow in both simulations and flow rig experiments. In-vivo studies performed on 11 healthy volunteers comparing the TO method with magnetic resonance phase contrast angiography (MRA) revealed a correlation between the stroke volume estimated by TO and MRA of 0.91 (p<;0.01) with an equation for the line of regression given as: MRA = 1.1 · TO-0.4 ml. Several clinical examples of complex flow in e.g. bifurcations and around valves have been acquired using a commercial implementation of the method (BK Medical ProFocus Ultraview scanner). A range of other methods are also presented. This includes synthetic aperture imaging using either spherical or plane waves with velocity estimation performed with directional beamforming or speckle tracking. The key advantages of these techniques are very fast imaging that can attain an order of magnitude higher precision than conventional methods. SA flow imaging was implemented on the experimental scanner RASMUS using an 8-emission spherical emission sequence and reception of 64 channels on a BK Medical 8804 transducer. This resulted in a relative standard deviation of 1.2% for a fully transverse flow. Plane wave imaging was also implemented on the RASMUS scanner and a 100 Hz frame rate was attained. Several vector velocity image sequences of complex flow were acquired, which demonstrates the benefits of fast vector flow imaging. A method for extending the 2D TO method to 3D vector velocity estimation is presented and the implications for future vector velocity imagi- g is indicated.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nikolov, Svetoslav","Udesen, Jesper","Munk, Peter","Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Hansen, Peter Møller","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Oddershede, Niels","Kortbek, Jacob","Pihl, Michael Johannes","Li, Ye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365312"],"event":{"end":"2011-10-21","place":"Orlando, us","start":"2011-10-18","title":"2011 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Apertures","Estimation","Image color analysis","Imaging","Oscillators","Ultrasonic imaging","Vectors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recent advances in blood flow vector velocity imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5865570/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-365312","identifier":[{"id":"84869022028","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cb698814-1279-4ee5-adbd-f686e222cad0"],"keyword":["Apertures","Estimation","Image color analysis","Imaging","Oscillators","Ultrasonic imaging","Vectors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3D956EC2902B659D888B5BB32E2FA64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ewh.ieee.org/conf/ius_2011/index.html","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ULTSYM.2011.0064","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5865570/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno"