{"abstract":"A case of X-linked hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia (XHED) was identified in a family of Danish Red Holstein cattle. The ectodysplasin-signalling protein (EDA) is known to be central in the normal development of ectodermal structures, and mutations in the ectodysplasin A (EDA) gene have been reported to cause XHED. In this study, we analysed different EDA transcript variants in affected and unaffected cattle and identified a new transcript variant including a LINE1-derived pseudoexon between EDA exons 1 and 2. The 161-bp-long pseudoexon introduces a shift in reaing frame and a premature stop codon early in EDA exon 2 and is probably the cause of XHED in this Danish Red Holstein family.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Karlskov-Mortensen, Peter","Cirera Salicio, Susanna","Nielsen, Ole Lerberg","Arnbjerg, Jens","Reibel, Jesper","Fredholm, Merete","Agerholm, Jørgen Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480440"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bos taurus","Former LIFE faculty"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exonization of a line000000000001 fragment implicated in x linked hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia in cattle","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2052.2011.02192.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-480440","identifier":[{"id":"80255122657","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22034998","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-91958ccc-571f-402d-9051-e4bb93251378"],"keyword":["Bos taurus","Former LIFE faculty","LINE1","X-linked hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia","etodysplasin A"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86B98E9CC1B2EB240C320116E0643FD9"