ection for classical orchestra musicians","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-619116","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: Insulin-mediated glucose disposal rates (R (d)) are reduced in type 2 diabetic patients, a process in which intrinsic signalling defects are thought to be involved. Phosphorylation of TBC1 domain family, member 4 (TBC1D4) is at present the most distal insulin receptor signalling event linked to glucose transport. In this study, we examined insulin action on site-specific phosphorylation of TBC1D4 and the effect of exercise training on insulin action and signalling to TBC1D4 in skeletal muscle from type 2 diabetic patients. METHODS: During a 3 h euglycaemic-hyperinsulinaemic (80 mU min(-1) m(-2)) clamp, we obtained M. vastus lateralis biopsies from 13 obese type 2 diabetic and 13 obese, non-diabetic control individuals before and after 10 weeks of endurance exercise-training. RESULTS: Before training, reductions in insulin-stimulated R (d), together with impaired insulin-stimulated glycogen synthase fractional velocity, Akt Thr(308) phosphorylation and phosphorylation of TBC1D4 at Ser(318), Ser(588) and Ser(751) were observed in skeletal muscle from diabetic patients. Interestingly, exercise-training normalised insulin-induced TBC1D4 phosphorylation in diabetic patients. This happened independently of increased TBC1D4 protein content, but exercise-training did not normalise Akt phosphorylation in diabetic patients. In both groups, training-induced improvements in insulin-stimulated R (d) (~20%) were associated with increased muscle protein content of Akt, TBC1D4, a2-AMP-activated kinase (AMPK), glycogen synthase, hexokinase II and GLUT4 (20-75%). CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: Impaired insulin-induced site-specific TBC1D4 phosphorylation may contribute to skeletal muscle insulin resistance in type 2 diabetes. The mechanisms by which exercise-training improves insulin sensitivity in type 2 diabetes may involve augmented signalling of TBC1D4 and increased skeletal muscle content of key insulin signalling and effector proteins, e.g., Akt, TBC1D4, AMPK, glycogen synthase, GLUT4 and hexokinase II.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Vind, B. F.","Pehmøller, Christian","Treebak, Jonas T.","Birk, Jesper Bratz","Hey-Mogensen, M.","Beck-Nielsen, H.","Zierath, J. R.","Wojtaszewski, Jørgen","Højlund, K."],"cuid":["S02-093.73-046571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet"],"keyword":["Blood Glucose","Blotting Western","C Peptide","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Electrophoresis Polyacrylamide Gel","Exercise","GTPase Activating Proteins","Glucose Clamp Technique","Glycogen synthase","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin","Male","Middle Aged","Muscle Skeletal","Phosphorylation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired insulin induced site specific phosphorylation of tbc000000000001 domain family member 000000000004 tbc000000000001d000000000004 in skeletal muscle of type 000000000002 diabetes patients is restored by endurance exercise training","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-010-1924-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.73-046571","identifier":[{"id":"20938636","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79953767747","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d7d3bac0-f25a-11df-b6d2-000ea68e967b","sdu-d304c0a3-a0be-4560-b43f-537673201db8"],"keyword":["Blood Glucose","Blotting, Western","C-Peptide","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Electrophoresis, Polyacrylamide Gel","Exercise","GTPase-Activating Proteins","Glucose Clamp Technique","Glycogen Synthase","Hemoglobin A, Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin","Male","Middle Aged","Muscle, Skeletal","Phosphorylation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-249ADB9A39F4B87B7C4D95B17ECFAFAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-010-1924-4","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Department of Exercise and Sport Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B F","key":"vindpau","last":"Vind","locid":"30b7c375-e22b-4930-8549-4a911b74e7aa","name":"Vind, Birgitte F","name_org":"Vind, B F","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"pehmøllerpau","last":"Pehmøller","locid":"d77e478f-c5fe-4b97-9237-1b5cef3819de","name":"Pehmøller, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas Thue","key":"treebakpau","last":"Treebak","locid":"a648ef82-ccb3-4add-83c1-384e0d90952b","name":"Treebak, Jonas T.","name_org":"Treebak, Jonas Thue","orcid":"0000-0003-1488-7012","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Bratz","key":"birkpau","last":"Birk","locid":"03b94e42-79b2-4498-9c5b-cfb4e38e17c8","name":"Birk, Jesper Bratz","orcid":"0000-0001-9775-4789","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M","key":"heymogensenpau","last":"Hey-Mogensen","locid":"b06de061-9407-4abf-8879-4d6cc3ee270b","name":"Hey-Mogensen, Martin","name_org":"Hey-Mogensen, M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H","key":"becknielsenpau","last":"Beck-Nielsen","locid":"0e78b588-9e9c-4acc-a1b8-8bcccea0b5a5","name":"Beck-Nielsen, Henning","name_org":"Beck-Nielsen, H","orcid":"0000-0002-7428-7898","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J. R.","key":"zierathpau","last":"Zierath","name":"Zierath, J. R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen","key":"wojtaszewskipau","last":"Wojtaszewski","locid":"06441180-44ed-4f23-b077-4d90876cc68b","name":"Wojtaszewski, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0001-8185-3408","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K","key":"højlundpau","last":"Højlund","locid":"de11c7e6-25a6-4e23-95bb-fe86d3d775ab","name":"Højlund, Kurt","name_org":"Højlund, K","orcid":"0000-0002-0891-4224","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20938636"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-010-1924-4","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"157-167","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953767747"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d7d3bac0-f25a-11df-b6d2-000ea68e967b","sdu-d304c0a3-a0be-4560-b43f-537673201db8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impaired insulin-induced site-specific phosphorylation of TBC1 domain family, member 4 (TBC1D4) in skeletal muscle of type 2 diabetes patients is restored by endurance exercise-training","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.73-046571","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Background: SoPIP2;1 constitutes one of the major integral proteins in spinach leaf plasma membranes and belongs to the aquaporin family. SoPIP2;1 is a highly permeable and selective water channel that has been successfully overexpressed and purified with high yields. In order to optimize reconstitution of the purified protein into biomimetic systems, we have here for the first time characterized the structural stability of SoPIP2;1. Methodology/Principal Finding: We have characterized the protein structural stability after purification and after reconstitution into detergent micelles and proteoliposomes using circular dichroism and fluorescence spectroscopy techniques. The structure of SoPIP2;1 was analyzed either with the protein solubilized with octyl-beta-D-glucopyranoside (OG) or reconstituted into lipid membranes formed by E. coli lipids, diphytanoylphosphatidylcholine (DPhPC), or reconstituted into lipid membranes formed from mixtures of 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-phosphatidylcholine (POPE), 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-phosphatidylethanolamine (POPE), 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-phosphatidylserine (POPS), and ergosterol. Generally, SoPIP2;1 secondary structure was found to be predominantly a-helical in accordance with crystallographic data. The protein has a high thermal structural stability in detergent solutions, with an irreversible thermal unfolding occurring at a melting temperature of 58 degrees C. Incorporation of the protein into lipid membranes increases the structural stability as evidenced by an increased melting temperature of up to 70 degrees C. Conclusion/Significance: The results of this study provide insights into SoPIP2;1 stability in various host membranes and suggest suitable choices of detergent and lipid composition for reconstitution of SoPIP2;1 into biomimetic membranes for biotechnological applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Plasencia, Ines","Survery, Sabeen","Ibragimova, Sania","Hansen, Jesper Søndergaard","Kjellbom, Per","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","Johanson, Urban","Mouritsen, Ole G."],"cuid":["S03-086.00-666652"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Center for Molecular Protein Science","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structure and stability of the spinach aquaporin sopip000000000002 000000000001 in detergent micelles and lipid membranes","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0014674","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-086.00-666652","identifier":[{"id":"79951926849","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3038850","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"21339815","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-57cd2a90-ac35-484e-8b9e-a824d7bae59c","ku-b8e5e3ba-e595-4cd5-8e50-b547da46504b","sdu-bd47bb07-661c-43b9-9b18-fd03ca08c707"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4E83926BED4848C0AB73612F3B6AF3C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5549660/0014674.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0014674","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.plosone.org/article/info%3Adoi%2F10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0014674","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern 