{"abstract":"Growing evidence exists that living with an ICD can lead to fear and avoidance behaviour including the avoidance of physical activity. It has been suggested that psychological stress can increase the risk of shock and predict death. Small studies have indicated a beneficial effect arising from exercise training and psychological intervention, therefore a large-scale rehabilitation programme was set up.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","Svendsen, Jesper H","Zwisler, Ann-Dorthe","Pedersen, Birthe D","Preisler, Pernille","Siersbæk-Hansen, Lone","Hansen, Mette B","Nielsen, Rune H","Pedersen, Preben Ulrich"],"cuid":["S03-096.77-021159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adaptation Psychological","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arrhythmias Cardiac","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark","Electric Countershock","Equipment Failure","Exercise","Fear","Female","Health Behavior","Health Knowledge Attitudes Practice","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Education as Topic","Quality of Life","Research Design","Sexual Dysfunctions Psychological","Stress Psychological","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cope icd a randomised clinical trial studying the effects and meaning of a comprehensive rehabilitation programme for icd recipients design intervention and population","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2261-11-33","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-096.77-021159","identifier":[{"id":"21682864","type":"pmid"},{"id":"799588