, Morten Balle","name_org":"Hansen, Mette B","orcid":"0000-0003-1144-2747","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette B","key":"hansenmettebpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Mette B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rune","key":"nielsenrunepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rune","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Preben Ulrich","key":"pedersenprebenulrichpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"69459fe9-d432-4dc0-b2d7-c38a0dace26b","name":"Pedersen, Preben Ulrich","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21682864"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2261-11-33","issn":["14712261"],"issue":"33","journal":"BMC Cardiovascular Disorders","pages":"33","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Cardiovascular Disorders","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79958806315"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7413f3aa-ae46-430c-ac25-9284e768c0dd","ku-7ee49f1a-8ce4-4ae2-b575-65b1c562afb1","sdu-56641d57-27c9-43e7-a80b-65e7cf3edcf6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"COPE-ICD: A randomised clinical trial studying the effects and meaning of a comprehensive rehabilitation programme for ICD recipients -design, intervention and population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.77-021159","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates the problem of spectrally efficient operation of a multi-user uplink cognitive radio system in the presence of a single primary link. The secondary system applies opportunistic interference cancelation (OIC) and decode the primary signal when such an opportunity is created. We derive the achievable rate in the secondary system when OIC is used. This scheme has a practical significance, since it enables rate adaptation without requiring any action from the primary system. The approximated formulas and tight lower and upper bounds for the ergodic sum-rate capacity of the secondary network are found. Next, the power allocation is investigated in the secondary system for maximizing the sumrate under an interference constraint at the primary system and it is shown that the optimal solution leads to a opportunistic user selection strategy. We propose a simple user selection strategy combined with OIC which achieves the optimal capacity given an interference constraint at the primary system. Finally, the analytical results are confirmed by simulations, indicating the fact that the low-complexity, spectral-efficient, flexible, and high-performing cognitive radio can be designed based on the proposed scheme.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yanakiev, Boyan Radkov","Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","Christensen, Morten","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-124182"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-15","place":"Rome, it","start":"2011-04-11","title":"5th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation EuCAP 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Molex Interconnect"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antennas in real environments","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?tp=&arnumber=5782152&contentType=Conference+Publications&searchField%3DSearch_All%26queryText%3DAntennas+In+Real+Environments","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-124182","identifier":[{"id":"79959655928","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ff60470a-8101-42b0-9c7c-b8ac99dc54c3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-21CAD62B206A2520421BAE1E5766C8AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?tp=&arnumber=5782152&contentType=Conference+Publications&searchField%3DSearch_All%26queryText%3DAntennas+In+Real+Environments","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Molex Interconnect"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Boyan Radkov","key":"yanakievpau","last":"Yanakiev","locid":"6de284ae-908b-4652-8ad8-e1eab05c5983","name":"Yanakiev, Boyan Radkov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ødum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"12489268-4402-4c17-8487-76a4323ee983","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ødum","orcid":"0000-0002-8505-853X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781457702501"],"pages":"2766-2770","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2011 Proceedings of the Fifth European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ff60470a-8101-42b0-9c7c-b8ac99dc54c3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Antennas In Real Environments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-124182","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Dose escalation in prostate radiotherapy is limited by normal tissue toxicities. The aim of this study was to assess the impact of margin size on tumor control and side effects for intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT) and 3D conformal radiotherapy (3DCRT) treatment plans with increased dose. Eighteen patients with localized prostate cancer were enrolled. 3DCRT and IMRT plans were compared for a variety of margin sizes. A marker detectable on daily portal images was presupposed for narrow margins. Prescribed dose was 82 Gy within 41 fractions to the prostate clinical target volume (CTV). Tumor control probability (TCP) calculations based on the Poisson model including the linear quadratic approach were performed. Normal tissue complication probability (NTCP) was calculated for bladder, rectum and femoral heads according to the Lyman-Kutcher-Burman method. All plan types presented essentially identical TCP values and very low NTCP for bladder and femoral heads. Mean doses for these critical structures reached a minimum for IMRT with reduced margins. Two endpoints for rectal complications were analyzed. A marked decrease in NTCP for IMRT plans with narrow margins was seen for mild RTOG grade 2/3 as well as for proctitis/necrosis/stenosis/fistula, for which NTCP <7% was obtained. For equivalent TCP values, sparing of normal tissue was demonstrated with the narrow margin approach. The effect was more pronounced for IMRT than 3DCRT, with respect to NTCP for mild, as well as severe, rectal complications.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Ingelise","Carl, Jesper Hansen","Lund, Bente","Larsen, Erik Højkjær","Nielsen, Jane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144483"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radiobiological impact of reduced margins and treatment technique for prostate cancer in terms of tumor control probability tcp and normal tissue complication probability ntcp","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.meddos.2010.02.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144483","identifier":[{"id":"20488692","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955470532","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1a6b6700-753f-11df-8c1a-000ea68e967b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-67E076B78C9D860BD118A8C6347D00B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.meddos.2010.02.004","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Urologisk afdeling, Aalborg Sygehus Nord"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingelise","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Ingelise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"carlpau","last":"Carl","locid":"39f05ca5-35f7-4251-ad47-442a087b2400","name":"Carl, Jesper Hansen","name_org":"Carl, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1049d2bf-7baa-4e58-bde3-05fef0f5682a","name":"Lund, Bente","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik H","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"45e5f0a7-a970-4540-8a5e-6906df0e9bc3","name":"Larsen, Erik Højkjær","name_org":"Larsen, Erik H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane N","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"dd468c6d-cd86-4689-8819-21424503294e","name":"Nielsen, Jane","name_org":"Nielsen, Jane N","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20488692"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.meddos.2010.02.004","issn":["09583947","18734022"],"issn_org":["09583947"],"issue":"2","journal":"Medical Dosimetry","pages":"130-7","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Medical Dosimetry","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955470532"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1a6b6700-753f-11df-8c1a-000ea68e967b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Radiobiological impact of reduced margins and treatment technique for prostate cancer in terms of tumor control probability (TCP) and normal tissue complication probability (NTCP)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-144483","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
