{"abstract":"We present an algorithm for implementing a secure oblivious RAM where the access pattern is perfectly hidden in the information theoretic sense, without assuming that the CPU has access to a random oracle. In addition we prove a lower bound on the amount of randomness needed for implementing an information theoretically secure oblivious RAM.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","Meldgaard, Sigurd Torkel","Nielsen, Jesper Buus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-155374"],"event":{"end":"2011-03-30","place":"Providence, RI, us","start":"2011-03-28","title":"8th Theory of Cryptography Conference. TCC 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perfectly secure oblivious ram without random oracles","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-19571-6_10","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-155374","identifier":[{"id":"79953223285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2d8b6c1e-4cfc-4919-9b1d-e29494e8083f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2B2B35C8BDF8265081F17734A86CF8A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-19571-6_10","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan Bjerre","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","locid":"70603eb5-52fd-41e3-8752-15d803c3af5c","name":"Damgård, Ivan Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigurd Torkel","key":"meldgaardpau","last":"Meldgaard","locid":"6e95c0a8-6e6a-4d07-9de7-16ccf3417ad2","name":"Meldgaard, Sigurd Torkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Buus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f428c4b3-80b3-403a-ada6-9ecb0fad97b2","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-19571-6_10","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"144-163","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"6597"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953223285"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2d8b6c1e-4cfc-4919-9b1d-e29494e8083f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Perfectly Secure Oblivious RAM without Random Oracles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-155374","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This Ph.D. dissertation presents contributions to a wide range of topics within the field of bioinformatics. In particular it contains work on the computation of molecule similarity, on association mapping, on analysis of molecular biological data, on Hidden Markov Models and on the computation of the quartet distance between trees. The common denominator is the interest in the design of both theoretically and practically fast algorithms. Related to molecular similarity we show how arranging a set of bitstrings into a tree can significantly speed up searches for bitstrings similar to a query bitstring. Similarity is measured by the Tanimoto coefficient, and the speed-up is achieved by pruning subtrees, if it can be shown that any leaf fingerprint in the subtree will be dissimilar to the query. Furthermore we demonstrate how an inverted index can improve the computation time of a matrix of LINGOsim similarity scores. Association mapping is a technique based on using large amounts of data on Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms (SNPs) to statistically infer associations between segments of DNA and effects in the host. Within the area of association mapping we develop an efficient file format and software library, called SNPFile. The file format is able to store both large amounts of SNP data and associated metadata, such as ids and affected-status of samples. Thus the file format can both speed-up SNP data access and simplify data management significantly. On the topic of molecular biological data, we analyze data from an experiment on exosome knockout. The exosome is a complex with a role in RNA degradation. We find that knockout of the exosome stabilize hitherto unknown RNA transcripts upstream active transcription start sites. With respect to Hidden Markov Models we develop two fast algorithms. We show that formulating the Hidden Markov Model framework using linear algebra allows one to solve the traditional problems using parallel reduction. This approach increases the total amount of work, but can still lead to significant speed-ups on Hidden Markov Models with a small state space. For Hidden Markov Models with a large state space we demonstrate a coarse-to-fine k-best Viterbi algorithm that might be used to approximate the forward algorithm. Finally we present work on the computation of the quartet distance. There are many algorithms for generating trees, and for the systematic study of differences between these algorithms, a way to measure the distance between trees is useful. The quartet distance is such a measure, based on counting dissimilar quartet substructures between two trees. We present a new algorithm for computing the quartet distance and show that it is fast in theory and practice.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-169280"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineering algorithms for finding patterns in biological data","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dtd","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/428942658/phd_dissertation_jn.final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-169280","ids":["au-46042cf3-1038-488a-8e08-26e3ac29732a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F9F69A0F0858482430F4F2FCEEB5D5D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/428942658/phd_dissertation_jn.final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"81bd45f3-9a63-4c7c-9e55-bb00c43a907f","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"187","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-46042cf3-1038-488a-8e08-26e3ac29732a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Engineering Algorithms for Finding Patterns in Biological Data","type":"Thesis Doctoral","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-169280","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Background When inferring phylogenetic trees different algorithms may give different trees. To study such effects a measure for the distance between two trees is useful. Quartet distance is one such measure, and is the number of quartet topologies that differ between two trees. Results We have derived a new algorithm for computing the quartet distance between a pair of general trees, i.e. trees where inner nodes can have any degree ≥ 3. The time and space complexity of our algorithm is sub-cubic in the number of leaves and does not depend on the degree of the inner nodes. This makes it the fastest algorithm so far for computing the quartet distance between general trees independent of the degree of the inner nodes. Conclusions We have implemented our algorithm and two of the best competitors. Our new algorithm is significantly faster than the competition and seems to run in close to quadratic time in practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jesper","Kristensen, Anders Kabell","Mailund, Thomas","Pedersen, Christian Nørgaard Storm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-188186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sub cubic time algorithm for computing the quartet distance between two general trees","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/39769049/1748_7188_6_15.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-188186","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3141660","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"21639882","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79957832529","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-670e799a-f43a-480e-9248-0bc55c58e2f7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-145DE393EE6B4C208E886FE83FEFA930"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/39769049/1748_7188_6_15.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1748-7188-6-15","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.almob.org/content/6/1/15","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"81bd45f3-9a63-4c7c-9e55-bb00c43a907f","name":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Kabell","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"0ee5b51c-9e53-4ade-8b0d-3f16b002273f","name":"Kristensen, Anders Kabell","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"mailundpau","last":"Mailund","locid":"ca9c028d-13b6-445f-b6a0-beeed6aadb56","name":"Mailund, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Nørgaard Storm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c36d6c36-4b4c-453f-9f0d-9e9110ddbb1a","name":"Pedersen, Christian Nørgaard Storm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21639882"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1748-7188-6-15","issn":["17487188"],"issue":"15","journal":"Algorithms for Molecular Biology","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Algorithms for Molecular Biology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79957832529"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-670e799a-f43a-480e-9248-0bc55c58e2f7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A sub-cubic time algorithm for computing the quartet distance between two general trees","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-188186","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes a method to create giant protein vesicles (GPVs) of ≥10 μm by solvent‐driven fusion of large vesicles (0.1–0.2 μm) with reconstituted membrane proteins. We found that formation of GPVs proceeded from rotational mixing of protein‐reconstituted large unilamellar vesicles (LUVs) with a lipid‐containing solvent phase. We made GPVs by using n‐decane and squalene as solvents, and applied generalized polarization (GP) imaging to monitor the polarity around the protein transmembrane region of aquaporins labeled with the polarity‐sensitive probe Badan. Specifically, we created GPVs of spinach SoPIP2;1 and E. coli AqpZ aquaporins. Our findings show that hydrophobic interactions within the bilayer of formed GPVs are influenced not only by the solvent partitioning propensity, but also by lipid composition and membrane protein isoform.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Jesper S.","Vararattanavech, Ardcharaporn","Vissing, Thomas","Torres, Jaume","Emnéus, Jenny","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350400"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanyang Technological University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formation of giant protein vesicles by a lipid cosolvent method","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cbic.201100537","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350400","identifier":[{"id":"83355175579","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22069223","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-99cc1f9c-7261-48ba-a7b4-5ac962a3a980"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A71303F5F6D8716CADA4E62BAC50F56D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cbic.201100537","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Aquaporin A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jesper S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ardcharaporn","key":"vararattanavechpau","last":"Vararattanavech","name":"Vararattanavech, Ardcharaporn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"vissingpau","last":"Vissing","name":"Vissing, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaume","key":"torrespau","last":"Torres","name":"Torres, Jaume","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jenny","key":"emnéuspau","last":"Emnéus","locid":"43e43e53-3691-442c-9aca-2793521452e5","name":"Emnéus, Jenny","orcid":"0000-0002-8061-201X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"helixnielsenpau","last":"Helix Nielsen","locid":"bea497c9-caba-420a-81f8-8f2730634b31","name":"Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","name_org":"Helix Nielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-9392-7133","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22069223"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cbic.201100537","issn":["14394227","14397633"],"issn_org":["14394227"],"issue":"18","journal":"ChemBioChem","pages":"2856-2862","publisher":"Wiley - VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","publisher_org":"Wiley - V C H Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","status":"p","title":"ChemBioChem","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-83355175579"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","aquaporin a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-99cc1f9c-7261-48ba-a7b4-5ac962a3a980"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Formation of Giant Protein Vesicles by a Lipid Cosolvent Method","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350400","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Semiconductor cavity quantum electrodynamical (CQED) devices are believed to be important components for future quantum information technologies. Being composed of a single quantum dot (QD) embedded in a cavity, semiconductor CQED systems resemble atomic CQED systems. However, recent experiments [1] have demonstrated that the physics of such all-solid-state systems is much richer than their atomic counterparts. In the regime of small detuning between the QD and cavity resonance, interactions with acoustical phonons are considered [2] to be the most important effect of the solid-state environment. Phonons introduce pure dephasing and other renormalization phenomena [3], which are inherently non-Markovian in nature.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Per Kær","Nielsen, Torben Roland","Lodahl, Peter","Jauho, Antti-Pekka","Mørk, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353716"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-26","place":"Munich, de","start":"2011-05-22","title":"European Conference on Lasers and Electro-Optics and the European Quantum Electronics Conference 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"role of the lightmatter coupling strength on nonmarkovian phonon effects in semiconductor cavity qed","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CLEOE.2011.5943373","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353716","identifier":[{"id":"80052275038","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a4a5325d-4288-4fd8-a9b8-6a3604a9b862"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AFE94BA59B0BB99558CADC417B7BBFCA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.cleoeurope.org/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CLEOE.2011.5943373","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Kær","key":"nielsenperkærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0d2d70-b57e-4f6c-98aa-1574ce6c7d23","name":"Nielsen, Per Kær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Roland","key":"nielsentorbenrolandpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d00af887-eee2-4b25-9c31-ff4893a61c4b","name":"Nielsen, Torben Roland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"lodahlpeterpau","last":"Lodahl","locid":"1228c48c-978c-45f6-a482-284ece371a8f","name":"Lodahl, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Antti-Pekka","key":"jauhoanttipekkapau","last":"Jauho","locid":"72495773-3ad7-4387-86a1-7757b6a46a1b","name":"Jauho, Antti-Pekka","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-7859","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"mørkjesperpau","last":"Mørk","locid":"6621c7d8-77e3-4e53-a34d-b330e59262c6","name":"Mørk, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-8498-661X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cleoe.2011.5943373","isbn":["9781457705335"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2011 Conference on and 12th European Quantum Electronics Conference Lasers and Electro-Optics Europe (CLEO EUROPE/EQEC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052275038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a4a5325d-4288-4fd8-a9b8-6a3604a9b862"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Role of the lightmatter coupling strength on nonMarkovian phonon effects in semiconductor cavity QED","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353716","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Tolypocladium inflatum is known primarily for its production of the cyclosporines that are used as an immunosuppressive drug. However, we report here the production of the carcinogenic fumonisins B2 and B4 by this biotechnologically relevant fungal genus. These mycotoxins were detected in 11 strains tested from three species: Tolypocladium inflatum, T. cylindrosporum, and T. geodes. Production of fumonisins by Fusarium spp. and Aspergillus niger is highly medium- and temperature-dependent, so the effect of these parameters on fumonisin production by three T. inflatum strains was studied. Maximum production was achieved on media with high sugar content incubated at 25–30°C. Since these results demonstrate that fumonisin production could be widespread within the genus Tolypocladium, the potential contamination of commercial cyclosporine preparations with fumonisins needs to be investigated.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Mogensen, Jesper Mølgaard","Møller, Kirsten Amalie","von Freiesleben, Pernille","Labuda, Roman","Varga, Elisabeth","Sulyok, Michael","Kubátová, Alena","Thrane, Ulf","Andersen, Birgitte","Nielsen, Kristian Fog"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charles University","Romer Labs Division Holding GmbH","University of Natural Resources and Life Sciences, Vienna"],"keyword":["Fumonisin","Mycotoxin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"production of fumonisins b000000000002 and b000000000004 in tolypocladium species","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10295-010-0916-1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360186","identifier":[{"id":"80052478130","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ba0d3cc5-48d8-4d0d-83e3-7c0f1f820111"],"keyword":["Cyclosporin","Elaphocordyceps subsessilis","Fumonisin","Mycotoxin","Tolypocladium inflatum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-490ECE65D658D7E2D999BBCF07B6B0AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10295-010-0916-1","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"romer labs division holding gmbh","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Romer Labs Division Holding GmbH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of natural resources and life sciences vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Natural Resources and Life Sciences, Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cz","key":"charles university","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charles University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Mølgaard","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"fe4663cc-9de6-4062-8273-37e893024049","name":"Mogensen, Jesper Mølgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten Amalie","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"831e15b1-c3a7-4806-8ea8-ee07e49d1cba","name":"Møller, Kirsten Amalie","orcid":"0000-0002-6825-9647","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"fir